his surveying equipment.$B$BIt seems as though we have quite the situation on our hands here with these bugs.  They're way too cunning for their own good, and the research we've done so far is shaping up to indicate that they might even be under the controlling influence of a third party!  If this is the case, then it bodes ill for not only Gadgetzan, but the whole desert!\030Oh, this is just terrible!  I sent out my top assistant, Junior Surveyor Scrimshank, into the desert southeast of here.  That's an area we call the Gaping Chasm.  Well, he's gone missing, and his last report had more of those weird bugs where he was.  Could it be that they've infested two major regions of the desert now?$B$BI need you to head into the Gaping Chasm and look for Scrimshank, please!  That... or at least find his surveying equipment.  I fear that may be all that is left of the poor sod.\030Discover the fate of Junior Surveyor Scrimshank, and bring either him or his surveying equipment to Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser in Gadgetzan.\030Well, what news do you have?  You look like you've been in quite the fight... is Scrimshank alive?\030The Scrimshank Redemption\0312,1,26,2,257,1,7724\0302,29,119,2,257,1,7724\0302,122,161,2,257,1,7724\0302,164,250,2,261,1,7724\0302,253,322,2,257,4,7724\0302,327,399,2,259,1,7724\0302,402,408,2,257,1,7724\0302,410,450,2,257,1,7724\0302,453,504,2,257,1,7724\0303,1,142,2,384,1,7724\0301,1,39,4,272,1,7724\0301,42,143,4,272,3,7724\0301,148,228,4,272,4,7724\0301,231,408,4,272,4,7724\0301,411,494,4,272,4,7724\0304,1,28,3,256,2,7724\0304,31,77,3,260,1,7724\0304,79,98,3,256,2,7724\0317724,2,10,Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser\0312,440,1446,0,\0302,0,0,10,Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser\0302,0,0,10,Gadgetzan\03182,19,82,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030110,23,110,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,8593,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[100]="PARTIAL\031loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thanks to you. Thanks to the shamans.$B$BCorruption ebbs but life continues to wane. Up to shamans to protect life.\030Light explodes as you finish the incantation. The sounds of the water drops hitting the flame have died down and your senses are overcome as the corrupt spirits around you are destroyed.\030Speak to the Minor Manifestation of Water in Silverpine Forest.\030\030Call of Water\0312,1,45,2,257,1,0\0302,47,186,2,261,1,0\0303,1,63,2,384,1,0\0301,1,14,4,304,1,5895\0301,16,37,4,304,1,5895\0301,42,84,4,276,1,5895\0301,86,115,4,286,1,5895\0315895,2,3,Minor Manifestation of Water\03011256,2,3,Manifestation of Water\0312,0,0,3,Minor Manifestation of Water\0302,0,0,3,Silverpine Forest\03163,19,63,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\03096,23,96,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,113791,GIVER,?,9,Brazier of Everfount",[1000]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Greetings, $C.$B$BI am pleased to see the likes of you taking an interest in the well being of nature; tales of your mighty deeds precede you, and you are welcomed here. Seeing you before me instills the feeling of confidence that the Cenarion Circle will get the proper aid it needs.$B$BOur connection with the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade transcends racial and political divides. Remember this as you work on behalf of the Circle, and you will do well.\030Attention, heroes!$B$BThe Cenarion Circle seeks able bodied individuals to assist them in exploring the vast new frontiers of Kalimdor!  A forbidden wasteland of unimaginable dangers lies far to the west of Tanaris and Gadgetzan, and the Circle needs willing and honorable proxies to act in their stead.$B$BAll interested individuals should seek audience with the Cenarion Circle.  Speak with the Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem on the Elder's Rise of Thunder Bluff for more information!\030Speak with Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem on the Elder Rise of Thunder Bluff about the Cenarion Circle's call to explore the frontiers of Kalimdor.\030\030The New Frontier\0312,1,18,2,257,1,10881\0302,23,135,2,323,1,10881\0302,138,303,2,259,1,10881\0302,308,380,2,323,1,10881\0302,383,483,2,257,1,10881\0303,1,144,2,448,1,10881\0301,1,14,4,272,1,5769\0301,19,169,4,272,1,5769\0301,171,284,4,338,3,5769\0301,289,381,4,336,1,5769\0301,383,454,4,272,3,5769\0315769,2,5,Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem\0305769,2,6,Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem\0312,1638,1456,0,\0302,0,0,3,Tanaris\0304,0,0,10,Moonglade\0311004,22,1004,UNKNOWN\0301018,22,1018,UNKNOWN\0301123,23,1123,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1001]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The Buzzbox hums to life soon after you place the Thresher Eyes inside. There is a moment of static before you hear a familiar tiny voice call out.$B$B\"Crawler wine is the best...\" *hic*$B$B\"What? Oh, you fixed it already? Wow, you're a fasht one. Sho, would ya like to fix another?\"$B$BYou believe you hear a liquid being poured into a cup, followed by loud gulping sounds.\030A tiny voice crackles from deep within the machine.$B$B\"Wizbang here! The next Buzzbox is north of Auberdine, on the beach$B$BSo, that Buzzbox is number 411 and it needs 3 Thresher Eyes for its repairs. They're just off the coast! The darkshore threshers... *Hic*... Sorry about that...$B$BJust like last time, when you give the Buzzbox the goods, it'll spit out your reward. *Hic*... What? No, I'm fine!\"\030Collect 3 Thresher Eyes from Darkshore Threshers in the deep sea near Buzzbox 411.\030The machine's hatch is open and it seems to wait expectantly for 3 Thresher Eyes to be placed inside.\030Buzzbox 411\0312,1,51,2,257,1,0\0302,56,69,2,257,1,0\0302,71,122,2,257,1,0\0302,127,202,2,259,1,0\0302,204,230,2,257,1,0\0302,232,257,2,257,1,0\0302,259,266,2,257,1,0\0302,268,286,2,257,1,0\0302,291,375,2,257,1,0\0302,377,384,2,257,1,0\0302,386,390,2,257,2,0\0302,392,405,2,257,1,0\0303,1,82,2,384,1,0\0301,1,71,4,272,1,0\0301,73,147,4,272,1,0\0301,152,186,4,272,1,0\0301,191,196,4,272,2,0\0301,198,222,4,272,2,0\0301,224,247,4,272,1,0\0301,249,283,4,272,4,0\0301,288,374,4,272,4,0\0304,1,101,3,256,4,0\0316250,4,16,Crawler\0312,148,1439,0,\0302,0,0,3,Auberdine\0302,0,0,13,Darkshore Threshers\0302,0,0,13,Buzzbox\031983,19,983,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301002,23,1002,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,17182,GIVER,?,9,Buzzbox 827\030OBJECT,17183,FINISHER,?,12,Buzzbox 411\030ITEM,5412,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[1002]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The Buzzbox suddenly leaps into action, and you can hear the distinct sounds of teeth being ground to dust coming from within.$B$B\"Sho, ya made it! Thatsh exshellent newsh... Sho... Why doncha move along? Oh! Unless you want another job!\"\030The Buzzbox gives a burst of static as you hear Wizbang begin to speak.$B$B\"The next Buzzbox is number 323. Ish north of Auberdine but... where's the ale? Wha? Oh, ish on the road sho ya shouldn't have trouble finding it near the bridge.\"$B$BWizbang mumbles something incoherent before you hear a loud gulping sound.$B$B\"Thish one needs Moonstalker Fangs... 6 of 'em.\"\030Collect 6 Moonstalker Fangs and place them in Buzzbox 323.\030Though you have yet to place the 6 Moonstalker Fangs inside, you believe you hear the sounds of static and incoherent gnome ramblings coming from within. Could someone else have fixed the machine already?\030Buzzbox 323\0312,1,71,2,257,1,0\0302,76,107,2,257,1,0\0302,109,137,2,257,1,0\0302,139,154,2,257,2,0\0302,156,159,2,257,2,0\0302,161,238,2,257,1,0\0302,243,316,2,257,1,0\0302,321,357,2,259,1,0\0303,1,58,2,384,1,0\0301,1,126,4,272,1,0\0301,131,147,4,272,1,0\0301,149,174,4,272,1,0\0301,176,181,4,272,1,0\0301,183,204,4,272,2,0\0301,210,238,4,282,4,0\0304,1,153,3,256,4,0\0304,155,204,3,256,4,0\0312069,2,8,Moonstalker\0302069,2,9,Moonstalker\0302069,3,16,Moonstalker\0312,148,1439,0,\0302,0,0,3,Auberdine\0302,0,0,9,Buzzbox\0311001,19,1001,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301003,23,1003,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,17183,GIVER,?,9,Buzzbox 411\030OBJECT,17184,FINISHER,?,12,Buzzbox 323\030ITEM,5413,OBJECTIVE,6,15,",[1003]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\"Sho yash gotsh the scalps in? That'sh sho great... Wha? Well, yesh I shuppose ya have realized that I can speaksh to ya without the materials in the machine. But I was telling the truth when I shaid they were broken!$B$BSee, in addition to being communimacation toolsh, the Buzzboxes also brew and distill fine liquor. Shorry for any deceptshion, but the nightelves do not apprecimerate my liquor trade in their townsh. I put shomething special in thish box to show my gratitude for yer effortsh. Enjoy!\"\030Over the boiling noises and dripping sounds coming from the machine, you hear Wizbang's wavering voice call out.$B$B\"Nexsht onesh far south down the road. Shouldn't be hard to find... jusht off to the shide... near a fensh. I think I hid it in shum bushesh... Bushessh. Hehehe... Yesh, Buzzbox 525 takes grizzled scalps from thoshe grizzled thistle bears. Boy thash a mouthful. Grizzshled... Hehehe...\"$B$BYou hear more gulping sounds as the machine cuts out. Then, suddenly, it bursts back to life.$B$B\"4!\"\030Collect 4 Grizzled Scalps from Grizzled Thistle Bears to the south of Auberdine and place them in Buzzbox 525.\030You hear singing coming from Buzzbox 525.$B$B\"Though crawler wine's shweet, and thresher ale fine, and moonstalker moonshine ish grand. There's nothing sho dear, as a thistle bear beer, and shoon I shall have shome on hand!\"$B$BThe hatch is open and awaits the 4 grizzled scalps as you hear the song repeated over and over.\030Buzzbox 525\0312,1,112,2,257,1,0\0302,117,154,2,257,1,0\0302,156,183,2,257,1,0\0302,185,209,2,257,1,0\0302,211,223,2,257,1,0\0302,225,259,2,257,1,0\0302,261,269,2,257,1,0\0302,271,279,2,257,1,0\0302,281,355,2,257,1,0\0302,357,377,2,257,1,0\0302,379,391,2,257,1,0\0302,393,402,2,257,1,0\0302,407,459,2,257,1,0\0302,461,499,2,257,1,0\0303,1,110,2,384,1,0\0301,1,30,4,272,2,0\0301,32,51,4,272,1,0\0301,53,56,4,272,2,0\0301,58,158,4,272,1,0\0301,160,217,4,272,1,0\0301,222,319,4,272,1,0\0301,321,420,4,272,1,0\0301,422,497,4,272,1,0\0301,499,505,4,272,1,0\0304,1,41,3,256,1,0\0304,46,135,3,256,1,0\0304,137,224,3,256,3,0\0304,229,323,3,256,1,0\0316250,3,26,Crawler\0302069,3,26,Moonstalker\0302163,3,27,Thistle Bear\0312,148,1439,0,\0302,0,0,15,Grizzled Thistle Bears\0302,0,0,15,Auberdine\0302,0,0,15,Buzzbox\0303,0,0,25,Buzzbox\0311002,19,1002,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,17184,GIVER,?,9,Buzzbox 323\030OBJECT,17185,FINISHER,?,12,Buzzbox 525\030ITEM,5414,OBJECTIVE,4,15,",[1004]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Greetings, $C.$B$BI am pleased to see the likes of you taking an interest in the well being of nature; tales of your mighty deeds precede you, and you are welcomed here. Seeing you before me instills the feeling of confidence that the Cenarion Circle will get the proper aid it needs.$B$BOur connection with the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade transcends racial and political divides. Remember this as you work on behalf of the Circle, and you will do well.\030Attention, heroes!$B$BThe Cenarion Circle seeks able bodied individuals to assist them in exploring the vast new frontiers of Kalimdor!  A forbidden wasteland of unimaginable dangers lies far to the west of Tanaris and Gadgetzan, and the Circle needs willing and honorable proxies to act in their stead.$B$BAll interested individuals should seek audience with the Cenarion Circle.  Speak with the Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem on the Elder's Rise of Thunder Bluff for more information!\030Speak with Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem on the Elder Rise of Thunder Bluff about the Cenarion Circle's call to explore the frontiers of Kalimdor.\030\030The New Frontier\0312,1,18,2,257,1,10879\0302,23,135,2,323,1,10879\0302,138,303,2,259,1,10879\0302,308,380,2,323,1,10879\0302,383,483,2,257,1,10879\0303,1,144,2,448,1,10879\0301,1,14,4,272,1,5769\0301,19,169,4,272,1,5769\0301,171,284,4,338,3,5769\0301,289,381,4,336,1,5769\0301,383,454,4,272,3,5769\0315769,2,5,Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem\0305769,2,6,Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem\0312,1497,1458,0,\0302,0,0,3,Tanaris\0304,0,0,10,Moonglade\0311000,22,1000,UNKNOWN\0301018,22,1018,UNKNOWN\0301123,23,1123,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1007]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You found it! Thank you, $N!$B$BThe old city of Zoram holds many secrets, and this statuette may be the key to many of them.\030I would charge you with a task, $N.$B$BI was on my small vessel, skimming over the submerged ruins of Zoram, when naga attacked me, surging from the water and tearing at me with their claws!  I fled, carrying what supplies I could to make this meager camp.$B$BBut when I reached the shore and ran... my prized possession was lost.$B$BPlease, $N, find the site of my ambush, along the coast to the north, and search for an ancient statuette.  It is the reason I have braved the dangers of the Zoram Strand.\030Bring the Ancient Statuette to Talen, in his camp near the Zoram Strand.\030Have you found the statuette, $N?\030The Ancient Statuette\0312,1,35,2,257,4,3846\0302,40,190,2,325,1,3846\0302,193,256,2,257,4,3846\0302,261,299,2,257,1,3846\0302,301,330,2,261,1,3846\0302,335,440,2,325,1,3846\0302,443,505,2,257,1,3846\0303,1,72,2,448,1,3846\0301,1,13,4,272,1,3846\0301,15,28,4,272,1,3846\0301,33,124,4,272,1,3846\0304,1,33,3,256,2,3846\0313846,2,8,Talen\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,8,Talen\0302,0,0,8,Zoram Strand\0311009,23,1009,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5424,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1008]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very well done, $N.  Your actions in the Zoram Strand against the naga are commendable.$B$BI know your feat was not easily accomplished, for the strength and guile of the naga is well known to the night elves.  We know this, for we share a history with them.$B$BIt is a history I care not to repeat.\030There is evil lurking on our northwestern coast, known as the Zoram Strand.$B$BIt is the resting place of the doomed city of Zoram, destroyed during the Sundering and submerged beneath the seas.  It has been lost to the night elves for ages.  Lost, and nearly forgotten.$B$BNow, the naga have returned, and for what reason we do not know.  But reason matters little; we must slay these fiends and throw them back to the depths!$B$BReturn to me when your mission is complete.\030Bring 20 Wrathtail Heads to Shindrell Swiftfire in Astranaar.\030We cannot allow the naga to invade our coasts, $N.  It is vital that you go to the Zoram Strand and complete your mission.\030The Zoram Strand\0312,1,75,2,257,1,3845\0302,80,194,2,325,1,3845\0302,197,241,2,261,1,3845\0302,244,270,2,261,1,3845\0302,275,338,2,257,1,3845\0302,341,427,2,257,1,3845\0302,432,474,2,257,1,3845\0303,1,61,2,384,1,3845\0301,1,19,4,272,1,3845\0301,22,87,4,272,1,3845\0301,92,209,4,272,1,3845\0301,212,258,4,336,1,3845\0301,263,299,4,336,1,3845\0304,1,50,3,268,1,3845\0304,53,122,3,256,1,3845\0313845,2,8,Shindrell Swiftfire\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,8,Shindrell Swiftfire\0302,0,0,8,Astranaar\0304,0,0,10,Zoram Strand\0303,0,0,15,Zoram Strand\0311134,23,1134,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5490,OBJECTIVE,20,15,",[1009]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You found the ring! Thank you, $N. Please take this as payment, and know that your deeds today will remain forever in my memory.\030I fear the ancient statuette's secrets will remain forever hidden unless you find the key to its ancient lock.$B$BThat key is a ring, the Ring of Zoram.  It belonged to the rulers of this city before the waves of the Sundering drowned it.$B$BFor years the ring was lost, but the naga have recently found it.$B$BTheir leader, Ruuzel, dwells on an isle on the northern edge of Zoram.  Please, $N, retrieve the ring for me!\030Bring the Ring of Zoram to Talen near the Zoram Strand.\030It is said that the Ring of Zoram is the key to any lock within the city. Do you have it, $N?\030Ruuzel\0312,1,110,2,329,4,3846\0302,115,152,2,257,1,3846\0302,155,238,2,321,1,3846\0302,243,307,2,261,1,3846\0302,312,381,2,257,1,3846\0302,384,420,2,257,1,3846\0303,1,55,2,384,1,3846\0301,1,19,4,272,1,3846\0301,21,34,4,272,1,3846\0301,36,128,4,272,3,3846\0304,1,73,3,256,1,3846\0304,75,93,3,256,2,3846\0313943,2,5,Ruuzel\0303846,2,7,Talen\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,7,Talen\0302,0,0,7,Zoram Strand\0311007,19,1007,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5445,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[101]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very wise of you, $N. This Totem of Infliction will help to protect you against the evil which lurks throughout Azeroth and beyond. When you feel threatened, hold this totem and take comfort in its magical aura. Be brave, fair $C. You will need all the courage you can muster for I see much bloodshed in your future.\030As the mystical taint creeps through the forest, the need for self-protection is undeniable, $N.  The winds whisper to me and they speak of a great danger which waits patiently for you in the near future.$B$BIf you wish to protect yourself, noble $c, bring to me 10 ghoul fangs, 10 skeleton fingers and 5 vials of spider venom.  For you I shall enchant a Totem of Infliction which will harm those who attempt violent acts against you.\030Bring 10 Ghoul Fangs, 10 Skeleton Fingers and 5 Vials of Spider Venom to Madame Eva in Darkshire.\030Bring to me 10 ghoul fangs, 10 skeleton fingers and 5 vials of spider venom. For you I shall enchant a Totem of Infliction which will harm those who attempt violent acts against you.\030The Totem of Infliction\0312,1,96,2,259,1,265\0302,99,204,2,261,1,265\0302,209,327,2,271,4,265\0302,330,434,2,257,3,265\0303,1,97,2,384,1,265\0301,1,21,4,272,1,265\0301,23,131,4,286,3,265\0301,133,211,4,276,1,265\0301,213,230,4,272,1,265\0301,232,316,4,274,3,265\0304,1,76,3,256,1,265\0304,78,182,3,256,3,265\031846,2,3,Ghoul\0306412,2,3,Skeleton\03014881,2,3,Spider\030846,2,5,Ghoul\0306412,2,5,Skeleton\03014881,2,5,Spider\030265,2,5,Madame Eva\030846,3,11,Ghoul\0306412,3,11,Skeleton\03014881,3,11,Spider\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,5,Madame Eva\0302,0,0,5,Darkshire\031\031ITEM,1129,OBJECTIVE,10,15,\030ITEM,1130,OBJECTIVE,5,15,\030ITEM,2378,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[1010]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, you have the hair!  Now I will mix a cure for the child, and pray my concoction works.$B$BAnd... Forsaken are at Bathran's Haunt?  Very troubling to hear, that is.  Very troubling indeed...\030There is a plant that once grew in the old ruins of Bathran's Haunt to the north.  The plant was called Bathran's Hair and was known to cure ailments of the spirit.$B$BThere is a sick child in the village, and I believe it is more than just a physical illness.  Will you go to Bathran's Haunt and search it for Bathran's Hair?  I may need it to properly treat the child.$B$BBathran's Haunt lies north of Maestra's Post and just south of the border to Darkshore.\030Bring 5 Bathran's Hair to Orendil Broadleaf in Ashenvale.\030Have you gathered the Bathran's Hair, $N?  The child's health grows weaker by the hour...\030Bathran's Hair\0312,1,81,2,321,1,3847\0302,84,164,2,257,1,3847\0302,169,260,2,257,4,3847\0302,263,326,2,257,2,3847\0302,329,370,2,259,1,3847\0302,375,461,2,257,1,3847\0303,1,57,2,384,1,3847\0301,1,22,4,272,1,3847\0301,25,90,4,272,3,3847\0301,95,100,4,272,1,3847\0301,102,133,4,272,2,3847\0301,136,167,4,272,1,3847\0301,170,193,4,272,1,3847\0304,1,41,3,256,2,3847\0304,44,89,3,256,1,3847\0313847,2,7,Orendil Broadleaf\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,4,Bathran's Haunt\0302,0,0,6,Maestra's Post\0302,0,0,6,Darkshore\0302,0,0,7,Orendil Broadleaf\0302,0,0,7,Ashenvale\0304,0,0,11,Bathran's Haunt\0311020,23,1020,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5437,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[1011]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very good, $N. Now... by testing the contents of this bottle, the goals of the Forsaken will be revealed!\030The Forsaken, the undead arm of the Horde, have crept into Ashenvale, lurking at our ruins and our barrows.  We believe their goal is to spread disease amongst the lands of the night elves.  We must confirm this!$B$BThe Forsaken have a camp south of here, near the Dor'Danil Barrow Den, where they create poisons and diseases and place them in bottles.  Fight your way into that camp and steal a bottle of disease.  Return with such a bottle.  I will test it and find its purpose.\030Bring a Bottle of Disease to Kayneth Stillwind in Forest Song.\030Did you find the camp, $N? Do you have a bottle of disease?\030Forsaken Diseases\0312,1,107,2,321,1,3848\0302,110,189,2,257,4,3848\0302,192,212,2,257,1,3848\0302,217,352,2,257,1,3848\0302,355,414,2,261,1,3848\0302,417,442,2,257,1,3848\0302,445,480,2,257,3,3848\0303,1,62,2,384,1,3848\0301,1,14,4,272,1,3848\0301,16,21,4,272,1,3848\0301,23,105,4,272,3,3848\0304,1,26,3,256,2,3848\0304,28,59,3,256,2,3848\0313848,2,8,Kayneth Stillwind\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,4,Dor'Danil Barrow Den\0302,0,0,8,Kayneth Stillwind\0302,0,0,8,Forest Song\0311012,23,1012,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5440,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1012]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I felt the anguish of the Dor'danil Barrows lessen, and knew you had completed your task.$B$BIt was grim work you did, $N, for the spirits you destroyed were merely victims of the Forsaken's evil. But with their destruction, let us hope the other maddened spirits find peace.\030When I struggled with the Forsaken's poisons, I had a vision.  I had a vision of the druids in the Dor'danil Barrow Den, poisoned... murdered by the undead!  They are now errant ghosts, severed from their bodies and driven mad.$B$BSo that the druids' spirits might some day find peace, you must enter the Dor'danil Barrow Den and destroy its once great leaders: Taneel Darkwood, Uthil Mooncall and Mavoris Cloudsbreak.$B$BDo this, then return to me.\030Kill the druids: Taneel Darkwood, Uthil Mooncall, Mavoris Cloudsbreak; then return to Kayneth Stillwind in Forest Song.\030The anguish of the Dor'danil druids still haunt my dreams, $N. You must destroy their leaders!\030Insane Druids\0312,1,61,2,257,1,3848\0302,64,132,2,261,1,3848\0302,134,156,2,261,1,3848\0302,159,227,2,257,1,3848\0302,232,418,2,271,4,3848\0302,423,449,2,257,1,3848\0303,1,119,2,384,1,3848\0301,1,89,4,272,1,3848\0301,94,196,4,276,1,3848\0301,198,275,4,282,3,3848\0304,1,62,3,256,1,3848\0304,64,94,3,260,1,3848\0313940,2,5,Taneel Darkwood\0303941,2,5,Uthil Mooncall\0303942,2,5,Mavoris Cloudsbreak\0303940,2,7,Taneel Darkwood\0303941,2,7,Uthil Mooncall\0303942,2,7,Mavoris Cloudsbreak\0303848,2,7,Kayneth Stillwind\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,2,Dor'danil Barrow Den\0302,0,0,7,Kayneth Stillwind\0302,0,0,7,Forest Song\0311011,19,1011,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,3940,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Taneel Darkwood\030NPC,3941,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Uthil Mooncall\030NPC,3942,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Mavoris Cloudsbreak",[1013]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very good. This book will add nicely to my collections of the workings of Ur. His knowledge was great, but his conscience held him from true power. And so when the Scourge came and his strength was tested, it failed.$B$BWe of the Forsaken cannot afford such weakness, if we are to survive...\030$N, Shadowfang Keep holds a book, the Book of Ur, which would be much prized in my collection.  Ur was a great mage of Dalaran before the coming of the Scourge, his studies in other worlds are of much value to ... certain parties among the Forsaken.$B$BEnter Shadowfang Keep and find the book.  Bring it to me, and I will report your service to our Dark Lady...\030Bring the Book of Ur to Keeper Bel'dugur at the Apothecarium in the Undercity.\030Did you find the book, $N?\030The Book of Ur\0312,1,94,2,257,4,2934\0302,97,213,2,321,1,2934\0302,215,249,2,257,1,2934\0302,254,293,2,257,1,2934\0302,296,361,2,257,3,2934\0303,1,78,2,384,1,2934\0301,1,10,4,272,1,2934\0301,12,77,4,272,3,2934\0301,79,147,4,272,1,2934\0301,149,216,4,336,1,2934\0301,221,291,4,280,4,2934\0304,1,26,3,256,2,2934\03115065,2,5,Lady\0302934,2,6,Keeper Bel'dugur\0312,209,0,0,\0302,0,0,6,Keeper Bel'dugur\0302,0,0,6,Apothecarium\0302,0,0,6,Undercity\031\031ITEM,6283,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1014]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Silverpine Forest is finally free from the vice of that wretch Arugal. You have done the Dark Lady a great service, $N. Your tenacity shall be rewarded.\030Arugal still resides in Shadowfang Keep. We cannot claim Silverpine as a strategic stronghold for the Dark Lady until Arugal is slain.$B$BI shall see to it that his magic is eradicated, $n. But I leave it in your hands to see that Arugal meets the death he so deserves.$B$BTravel to Shadowfang Keep and put an end to Arugal's foul spells once and for all. Bring to me the vile wizard's head!\030Kill Arugal and bring his head to Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher.\030With Arugal's death we stand to increase the Dark Lady's stronghold on Lordaeron.\030Arugal Must Die\0312,1,40,2,257,1,1938\0302,42,134,2,261,1,1938\0302,139,189,2,257,3,1938\0302,191,269,2,257,1,1938\0302,274,355,2,257,1,1938\0302,357,391,2,257,1,1938\0303,1,68,2,384,1,1938\0301,1,70,4,272,1,1938\0301,72,119,4,272,1,1938\0301,121,152,4,272,3,1938\0304,1,81,3,256,1,1938\03110000,2,1,Arugal\03015065,2,2,Lady\03010000,2,2,Arugal\03010000,2,4,Arugal\03010000,2,7,Arugal\0301938,2,7,Dalar Dawnweaver\03010000,4,8,Arugal\03015065,4,9,Lady\0312,209,0,0,\0302,0,0,1,Shadowfang Keep\0302,0,0,5,Shadowfang Keep\0302,0,0,5,Arugal's\0302,0,0,7,Dalar Dawnweaver\0302,0,0,7,Sepulcher\031\031ITEM,5442,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1015]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031What makes you think I wish to be pestered by the likes of you, $C? Wait - let me stop the important duties I attend to on a daily basis so I can help you locate a doodad somewhere. By all means, the welfare of Darnassus - nay, all of Teldrassil - should come second to the acquisition of a bauble for your collection.$B$BThe fools in Moonglade waste my time with their call for assistance, and now I must endure this?\030Attention, heroes!$B$BThe Cenarion Circle seeks able bodied individuals to assist them in exploring the vast new frontiers of Kalimdor!  A forbidden wasteland of unimaginable dangers lies far to the west of Tanaris and Gadgetzan, and the Circle needs willing and honorable proxies to act in their stead.$B$BAll interested individuals should seek audience with the Cenarion Circle.  Speak with the Arch Druid in Darnassus, Fandral Staghelm, for more information!\030Speak with Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm at the Cenarion Enclave of Darnassus about the Cenarion Circle's call to explore the frontiers of Kalimdor.\030\030The New Frontier\0312,1,18,2,257,1,2198\0302,23,135,2,323,1,2198\0302,138,303,2,259,1,2198\0302,308,380,2,323,1,2198\0302,383,461,2,257,1,2198\0303,1,146,2,448,1,2198\0301,1,67,4,274,2,3516\0301,69,181,4,272,1,3516\0301,183,318,4,272,1,3516\0301,323,418,4,272,2,3516\03115382,2,5,Fandral Staghelm\0303516,2,6,Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm\03015382,2,6,Fandral Staghelm\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,3,Tanaris\0302,0,0,5,Darnassus\0302,0,0,6,Cenarion Enclave of Darnassus\0304,0,0,10,Moonglade\0311019,22,1019,UNKNOWN\0301047,22,1047,UNKNOWN\0306761,23,6761,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1016]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $N, this should give us the information we need to have the culprit discovered. How would you feel about taking out the mage who fills our pools with corrupt elementals? The corruption of Ashenvale and beyond makes my stomach turn on its own--to have a wizard actively attempting to destroy it further sickens me to no end. We shall make him pay.\030Take this divining scroll--it can determine the creator of these elementals. But you will need something from them to use as a reagent to focus scroll's magic--their bracers should do nicely.$B$BA few intact bracers from the creatures should be enough. The other bracers will be useless for our purposes, but they may be worth something to a merchant if you wish to sell them. Once you have the intact bracers attempt to use the scroll. Return to me with the results and we shall proceed from there.\030Collect 5 Intact Elemental Bracers and use the Divining Scroll on them. Afterwards, bring the Divined Scroll to Sentinel Velene Starstrike at the Silverwind Refuge.\030Since you must destroy the bracers to kill the elementals, it will probably be difficult to find the specific ones that contain the information the divining scroll needs. You can trade bracers with others in order to obtain the ones you need, or perhaps you have the divined paper already?\030Elemental Bracers\0312,1,76,2,257,1,3885\0302,78,191,2,259,3,3885\0302,196,252,2,257,1,3885\0302,254,376,2,259,4,3885\0302,378,436,2,257,1,3885\0302,438,499,2,257,3,3885\0303,1,71,2,384,1,3885\0303,73,164,2,384,1,3885\0301,1,90,4,274,1,3885\0301,92,180,4,276,4,3885\0301,182,334,4,276,1,3885\0301,336,357,4,272,3,3885\0304,1,170,3,262,3,3885\0304,172,289,3,258,4,3885\0313885,2,8,Sentinel Velene Starstrike\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,8,Sentinel Velene Starstrike\0302,0,0,8,Silverwind Refuge\0311017,23,1017,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5455,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1017]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Now I can see that repugnant smile wiped from his face forever. You have done very well, $N. Take this, the Light of Elune, drink of it when all seems lost and death is near. It may save you, Goddess willing.\030There's only one undead mage in the Barrens capable of defiling this many water elementals. He's also the only one foolish enough to try. Sarilus Foulborne is probably sitting at the top of Dreadmist Peak, laughing at me.$B$B$n, you must go into enemy territory and destroy this miscreant. I have had enough of his idiocy and we must show him what happens to those who annoy the Sentinels.$B$BDestroy him and bring me his head. Be wary though, the Horde may be watching for you.\030Slay Sarilus Foulborne and bring his head to Sentinel Velene Starstrike in Silverwind Refuge.\030Is it done? Is Sarilus Foulborne dead?\030Mage Summoner\0312,1,91,2,257,1,3885\0302,93,137,2,257,1,3885\0302,139,221,2,257,1,3885\0302,226,289,2,261,1,3885\0302,291,389,2,257,1,3885\0302,394,427,2,261,1,3885\0302,429,478,2,257,1,3885\0303,1,93,2,384,1,3885\0301,1,63,4,272,1,3885\0301,65,92,4,272,1,3885\0301,94,174,4,276,4,3885\0301,176,208,4,280,1,3885\0304,1,11,3,256,2,3885\0304,13,38,3,256,2,3885\0313986,2,3,Sarilus Foulborne\0303986,2,8,Sarilus Foulborne\0303885,2,8,Sentinel Velene Starstrike\0303986,3,14,Sarilus Foulborne\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,1,Barrens\0302,0,0,8,Sentinel Velene Starstrike\0302,0,0,8,Silverwind Refuge\0311016,19,1016,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5537,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1018]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Greetings, $C.$B$BI am pleased to see the likes of you taking an interest in the well being of nature; tales of your mighty deeds precede you, and you are welcomed here. Seeing you before me instills the feeling of confidence that the Cenarion Circle will get the proper aid it needs.$B$BOur connection with the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade transcends racial and political divides. Remember this as you work on behalf of the Circle, and you will do well.\030Attention, heroes!$B$BThe Cenarion Circle seeks able bodied individuals to assist them in exploring the vast new frontiers of Kalimdor!  A forbidden wasteland of unimaginable dangers lies far to the west of Tanaris and Gadgetzan, and the Circle needs willing and honorable proxies to act in their stead.$B$BAll interested individuals should seek audience with the Cenarion Circle.  Speak with the Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem on the Elder's Rise of Thunder Bluff for more information!\030Speak with Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem on the Elder Rise of Thunder Bluff about the Cenarion Circle's call to explore the frontiers of Kalimdor.\030\030The New Frontier\0312,1,18,2,257,1,10880\0302,23,135,2,323,1,10880\0302,138,303,2,259,1,10880\0302,308,380,2,323,1,10880\0302,383,483,2,257,1,10880\0303,1,144,2,448,1,10880\0301,1,14,4,272,1,5769\0301,19,169,4,272,1,5769\0301,171,284,4,338,3,5769\0301,289,381,4,336,1,5769\0301,383,454,4,272,3,5769\0315769,2,5,Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem\0305769,2,6,Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem\0312,1637,1454,0,\0302,0,0,3,Tanaris\0304,0,0,10,Moonglade\0311000,22,1000,UNKNOWN\0301004,22,1004,UNKNOWN\0301123,23,1123,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1019]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031What makes you think I wish to be pestered by the likes of you, $C? Wait - let me stop the important duties I attend to on a daily basis so I can help you locate a doodad somewhere. By all means, the welfare of Darnassus - nay, all of Teldrassil - should come second to the acquisition of a bauble for your collection.$B$BThe fools in Moonglade waste my time with their call for assistance, and now I must endure this?\030Attention, heroes!$B$BThe Cenarion Circle seeks able bodied individuals to assist them in exploring the vast new frontiers of Kalimdor!  A forbidden wasteland of unimaginable dangers lies far to the west of Tanaris and Gadgetzan, and the Circle needs willing and honorable proxies to act in their stead.$B$BAll interested individuals should seek audience with the Cenarion Circle.  Speak with the Arch Druid in Darnassus, Fandral Staghelm, for more information!\030Speak with Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm at the Cenarion Enclave of Darnassus about the Cenarion Circle's call to explore the frontiers of Kalimdor.\030\030The New Frontier\0312,1,18,2,257,1,10877\0302,23,135,2,323,1,10877\0302,138,303,2,259,1,10877\0302,308,380,2,323,1,10877\0302,383,461,2,257,1,10877\0303,1,146,2,448,1,10877\0301,1,67,4,274,2,3516\0301,69,181,4,272,1,3516\0301,183,318,4,272,1,3516\0301,323,418,4,272,2,3516\03115382,2,5,Fandral Staghelm\0303516,2,6,Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm\03015382,2,6,Fandral Staghelm\0312,1537,1455,0,\0302,0,0,3,Tanaris\0302,0,0,5,Darnassus\0302,0,0,6,Cenarion Enclave of Darnassus\0304,0,0,10,Moonglade\0311015,22,1015,UNKNOWN\0301047,22,1047,UNKNOWN\0306761,23,6761,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[102]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $N. With valiant adventurers such as yourself fighting alongside The People's Militia, Westfall just might return to the prosperous breadbasket it once was. Please accept this in recognition of your tireless efforts.\030Stormwind has abandoned us.  A foul wind of depravity rustles through the plains of Westfall.  This was my homeland and I will not turn my back on the citizens who choose to remain here.  We, the former farmers, shall make our stand.$B$BYour task, should you choose to accept, is to patrol the grasslands of Westfall.  Track down and slay the vile Gnolls that seem to be working in conjunction with the Deadmines thieves. Bring me eight Gnoll Paws and I will reward your bravery.\030Bring 8 Gnoll Paws to Captain Danuvin on Sentinel Hill.\030Have you collected 8 paws from those treacherous Gnolls yet?\030Patrolling Westfall\0312,1,27,2,257,1,821\0302,30,93,2,257,1,821\0302,96,186,2,257,3,821\0302,189,233,2,257,3,821\0302,238,317,2,257,1,821\0302,320,421,2,257,4,821\0302,423,479,2,257,3,821\0303,1,55,2,384,1,821\0301,1,14,4,272,1,821\0301,16,167,4,340,4,821\0301,169,227,4,272,1,821\0304,1,60,3,256,2,821\031821,2,8,Captain Danuvin\0312,40,1436,0,\0302,0,0,8,Captain Danuvin\031\031ITEM,725,OBJECTIVE,8,15,",[1020]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is from Orendil?$B$BHis skill with herbs and healing is great.  This cure gives me hope, when before I had little...\030$N, I have created a cure that I believe will help the afflicted child.  Take it to Astranaar and give it to the child's parent, Pelturas Whitemoon.$B$BTo reach Astranaar, follow the road south, then east.\030Bring Orendil's Cure to Pelturas Whitemoon in Astranaar.\030I must apologize, for I have no time to speak.  My child, Relara, is deathly ill!\030Orendil's Cure\0312,1,71,2,257,4,3847\0302,74,148,2,257,1,3847\0302,153,205,2,257,1,3847\0303,1,56,2,384,1,3847\0301,1,21,4,272,2,3894\0301,26,67,4,272,1,3894\0301,70,121,4,274,3,3894\0304,1,46,3,256,1,3894\0304,49,81,3,256,1,3894\0313894,2,2,Pelturas Whitemoon\0303894,2,4,Pelturas Whitemoon\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,2,Astranaar\0302,0,0,4,Pelturas Whitemoon\0302,0,0,4,Astranaar\0304,0,0,5,Orendil\0311010,19,1010,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301033,23,1033,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1021]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Judging by the gaping wound in her side, Anilia is on the verge of death.\030Listen, I don't know who you are, but I need your help. My sisters went to take back the Branch of Cenarius from the satyr. They said they'd be back soon, but it's been two whole days!$B$B$n, you have to find them! They were looking for the ruins of a night elf temple in Xavian to the northwest. I don't know what to think. Look for Anilia, she was leading them on the search.\030Find Anilia in Xavian.\030\030Vile Satyr! Dryads in Danger!\0312,1,55,2,259,1,3901\0302,57,123,2,257,1,3901\0302,125,184,2,257,1,3901\0302,189,214,2,257,1,3901\0302,216,296,2,321,1,3901\0302,298,324,2,257,1,3901\0302,326,377,2,257,1,3901\0303,1,22,2,384,1,3901\0301,1,73,4,272,1,3920\0313920,2,7,Anilia\0303920,2,8,Anilia\0303920,4,9,Anilia\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,5,Xavian\0302,0,0,8,Xavian\0311031,23,1031,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1022]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030requestItems\030title\031The Tome of Mel'Thandris works in strange ways. The events it records, the events it shows... No one truly understands why it does what it does.$B$BNonetheless, it is clear that what Priestess Starsong received--this Scythe of Elune--bears further investigation.\030Though we have put many resources and much effort into driving the remaining demons from the Felwood to the north, our successes have been few. We have been able to keep much of the demonic presence from Ashenvale.$B$BTo the north, near the Felwood border, the ruined shrine of Mel'Thandris has been overtaken by mysterious wolf-men. Their chilling calls have led the area to be known as the Howling Vale. The Tome of Mel'Thandris kept at the shrine may shed some light on why these wolf-men have come.\030Go to the Howling Vale and study the Tome of Mel'Thandris, then return to Sentinel Melyria Frostshadow at Forest Song.\030\030View the Tome of Mel'Thandris\030The tome of the shrine is a mysterious object. It is not a book in the traditional sense. The leaves of the tome were blessed by Mel'Thandris herself, and records events of import in its pages.$B$BIt is hard for me to explain. If you go to the shrine, you will understand.\030The Howling Vale\0312,1,143,2,257,1,3880\0302,145,214,2,257,1,3880\0302,219,333,2,257,1,3880\0302,335,405,2,257,1,3880\0302,407,502,2,257,1,3880\0303,1,118,2,384,1,3880\0301,1,47,4,272,1,3880\0301,49,93,4,272,1,3880\0301,95,144,4,272,1,3880\0301,149,262,4,272,1,3880\0306,1,46,3,256,1,3880\0306,48,89,3,256,1,3880\0306,91,193,3,256,1,3880\0306,198,226,3,256,1,3880\0306,228,272,3,256,4,3880\0305,1,29,3,384,1,3880\0313880,2,6,Sentinel Melyria Frostshadow\030112,4,10,Priestess\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,1,Felwood\0302,0,0,2,Ashenvale\0302,0,0,3,Felwood\0302,0,0,6,Howling Vale\0302,0,0,6,Sentinel Melyria Frostshadow\0302,0,0,6,Forest Song\0311037,23,1037,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,19027,OBJECTIVE,1,14,Tome of Mel'Thandris",[1023]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is terrible, $N. Teronis is dead?!$B$BThe time for mourning will come, but for now we must focus our efforts. I shall send some of the Sentinels to recover Teronis' body as soon as possible.$B$BYou have Teronis' journal and the gem he was seeking. Do you think you're capable of completing his task? I would rest much better knowing his death was not in vain.\030As you rummage through Teronis' belongings, you find a journal that is still in good condition.$B$BYou take the journal and leave Teronis' corpse as is.$B$BThe only thing left to do is find the gem Teronis was seeking. Raene mentioned it being in the area. Perhaps the murlocs have it...\030Find the Glowing Gem and return to Raene Wolfrunner in Astranaar with Teronis' Journal.\030Ah, welcome back, $N.\030Raene's Cleansing\0312,1,95,2,257,1,3891\0302,100,152,2,257,1,3891\0302,157,218,2,257,1,3891\0302,220,256,2,257,1,3891\0302,258,287,2,257,4,3891\0303,1,87,2,384,1,3891\0301,1,21,4,272,1,3691\0301,23,39,4,272,2,3691\0301,44,114,4,272,3,3691\0301,116,195,4,272,3,3691\0301,200,252,4,272,1,3691\0301,254,304,4,272,2,3691\0301,306,364,4,272,4,3691\0304,1,21,3,256,1,3691\0313891,2,2,Teronis' Corpse\0303691,2,6,Raene Wolfrunner\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,6,Raene Wolfrunner\0302,0,0,6,Astranaar\031991,19,991,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5463,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1024]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh, Raene sent you? It must be serious indeed. What can I help you with?\030You'll have to do the research yourself, but from what notes Teronis has made, it sounds like your next course of action is to find the other pieces of the rod Dartol created. I would start by heading to the moonwell east of Iris Lake. When you're ready, follow the road and turn north when you reach a small sitting area on your left.$B$BA dryad there named Shael'dryn is better suited to guide you. Seek her out.$B$BKeep the gem with you--Shael'dryn will need it if she's to help you recreate the rod.\030Find Shael'dryn at the moonwell to the northeast.\030Hello. How are you?\030Raene's Cleansing\0312,1,175,2,257,1,3691\0302,177,235,2,257,4,3691\0302,237,335,2,257,1,3691\0302,340,400,2,257,1,3691\0302,402,414,2,257,1,3691\0302,419,503,2,259,4,3691\0303,1,49,2,384,1,3691\0301,1,19,4,272,2,3916\0301,21,46,4,272,1,3916\0301,48,72,4,272,2,3916\0304,1,6,3,256,1,3916\0304,8,19,3,256,2,3916\0313916,2,4,Shael'dryn\0303916,2,7,Shael'dryn\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,2,Iris Lake\0311023,19,1023,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301026,23,1026,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1025]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have done well, $N. Thank you.\030Before you travel to the moonwell I have another task that will aid the people of Ashenvale if you would like to test your skills.$B$BAlong the road heading east before the Falfarren River, furbolgs have been attacking travelers. Their tortured minds feeding upon fear, and their appetites satiated by the blood of innocents.$B$BAid the Sentinels in protecting the lands by showing those monsters the same mercy they have shown our kind.$B$BI believe their camps are south of the road... be careful.\030Kill 1 Den Watcher, 2 Ursas, 10 Totemics, and 12 Warriors of the Foulweald tribe, and then return to Raene Wolfrunner in Astranaar.\030The furbolg were not always our enemy, $N. But times change, and it is no longer a time of peace here in these dark woods.\030An Aggressive Defense\0312,1,130,2,257,4,3691\0302,135,229,2,261,1,3691\0302,231,325,2,257,1,3691\0302,330,437,2,257,1,3691\0302,442,487,2,257,4,3691\0302,489,499,2,257,1,3691\0303,1,131,2,384,1,3691\0301,1,23,4,272,1,3691\0301,25,34,4,272,1,3691\0304,1,42,3,260,1,3691\0304,44,122,3,264,1,3691\0313691,2,7,Raene Wolfrunner\03031,3,10,Furbolg\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,7,Raene Wolfrunner\0302,0,0,7,Astranaar\0311023,19,1023,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,3746,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Foulweald Den Watcher\030NPC,3749,OBJECTIVE,2,13,Foulweald Ursa\030NPC,3750,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Foulweald Totemic\030NPC,3743,OBJECTIVE,12,13,Foulweald Warrior",[1026]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I'm pleased to see you're back, $N.\030I wish your tidings were better.$B$BRaene is correct, I know about Dartol's creation and the treants in the area--at least I did once. They've become corrupted now, their nature twisted.$B$BIf your goal is to find the next piece of the rod, then you'll have to find the key to open the chest it's in.$B$BThe wooden key is on one of the treants northeast of here, near Felwood. Once you have it, look for a small glade west of the road near the Felwood border... the chest should be hidden around there.\030Find the Wooden Key and a piece of Dartol's Rod before returning to Shael'dryn at the moonwell.\030It upsets me so that the treants have become corrupt. I wish I could do more to help them.\030Raene's Cleansing\0312,1,32,2,259,3,3916\0302,37,134,2,257,1,3916\0302,136,186,2,261,1,3916\0302,191,300,2,257,4,3916\0302,305,376,2,257,1,3916\0302,378,461,2,257,1,3916\0302,463,502,2,257,1,3916\0303,1,95,2,384,1,3916\0301,1,35,4,272,1,3916\0304,1,53,3,262,1,3916\0304,55,90,3,258,4,3916\0313916,2,8,Shael'dryn\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,5,Felwood\0302,0,0,6,Felwood\0302,0,0,8,Shael'dryn\0311024,19,1024,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301027,23,1027,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5464,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1027]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You found the final piece? Wonderful for you... and for Raene.$B$BI guess we'll have to see about repairing it, won't we?\030The final piece of the rod was given to the druids of Dor'danil for safekeeping. I have no idea where they hid it. I'm sorry I can't help you more than that.$B$BAll I can tell you is to follow the road that leads towards the Barrens. The druids took shelter to the east of that road, but they won't be of much help to you: they were killed recently... it's something I don't like to think about much.$B$BWhen you find the final piece, bring it to me and I will help you reconstruct the rod.\030Find the final piece of Dartol's Rod and return to Shael'dryn at the moonwell.\030Did you find the final piece of the rod, $N?\030Raene's Cleansing\0312,1,80,2,257,1,3916\0302,82,114,2,257,1,3916\0302,116,157,2,257,1,3916\0302,162,233,2,257,1,3916\0302,235,351,2,257,1,3916\0302,353,400,2,257,1,3916\0302,405,490,2,257,3,3916\0303,1,78,2,384,1,3916\0301,1,26,4,272,2,3916\0301,28,47,4,272,1,3916\0301,49,62,4,272,1,3916\0301,67,121,4,272,2,3916\0304,1,44,3,256,2,3916\0313916,2,8,Shael'dryn\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,8,Shael'dryn\0311026,19,1026,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301028,23,1028,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5519,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1028]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031After the glow dies, you can see the re-enchanted rod within the shrine's basin.\030Here is the completed rod, $N. Reconstructing it was simple... it's finding the shrine that has the power to recharge it that will be the hard part.$B$BWith some focus and effort it shouldn't be too hard for someone like you, who's already accomplished so much.$B$BHead southeast of here--there are very few paths, so be careful--and keep your eyes to the north. The shrine is hidden within the mountains that surround this glade.$B$BOnce there, place the rod within the shrine... the rest is magic. Hehe.\030Find the hidden shrine and re-enchant Dartol's Rod.\030You can sense a subtle yet powerful force within the shrine and surrounding trees.$B$BYou begin placing the rod within the shrine and a soft thrumming noise emits from around you as the shrine begins to glow...\030Raene's Cleansing\0312,1,30,2,257,1,3916\0302,32,62,2,257,1,3916\0302,64,148,2,257,3,3916\0302,153,261,2,257,1,3916\0302,266,362,2,257,1,3916\0302,364,430,2,257,1,3916\0302,435,480,2,257,1,3916\0302,482,499,2,257,1,3916\0302,501,505,2,257,1,3916\0303,1,51,2,384,1,3916\0301,1,80,4,272,1,0\0304,1,82,3,256,1,0\0304,87,210,3,256,1,0\031\0312,331,1440,0,\0311027,19,1027,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301055,23,1055,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,19024,FINISHER,?,12,Hidden Shrine",[1029]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You've recreated the rod Teronis had set out to find? That's wonderful to hear.$B$BTeronis would be proud to see his quest is continuing even after his tragic passing.\030I suggest you find Raene and let her know the rod is finished. I'm sure she'll know what your next course should be.$B$BGood luck, $N.\030Return to Raene Wolfrunner in Astranaar.\030\030Raene's Cleansing\0312,1,62,2,257,1,3916\0302,64,116,2,257,1,3916\0302,121,134,2,257,1,3916\0303,1,40,2,384,1,3916\0301,1,53,4,272,2,3691\0301,55,79,4,272,1,3691\0301,84,167,4,272,4,3691\0313691,2,4,Raene Wolfrunner\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,4,Raene Wolfrunner\0302,0,0,4,Astranaar\0311055,19,1055,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301030,23,1030,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[103]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Praise you, brave $C. The rocks of the Westfall Coast shall be lit thanks to your hard work. Many lives will be spared so long as the torch is kept lit.$B$BI died needlessly on this very shore. My afterlife plight is to see that no others follow my destiny.\030The night the Lighthouse Keeper's family died was horrible.  I watched, helpless, as Old Murk-Eye led the attack.  But what's done is done and now my concern is for the lives of the sailors on The Great Sea whose ships come close to the perilous rocks of the coastline.  With no one to keep watch on the flame the responsibility has fallen upon me.$B$BHelp me keep the torch lit by bringing me 5 flasks of oil from the Harvest Monsters.\030Bring 5 Flasks of Oil to Captain Grayson at the Westfall Lighthouse.\030The flame will not burn for long without oil, $N.\030Keeper of the Flame\0312,1,59,2,257,1,392\0302,62,113,2,261,1,392\0302,116,269,2,257,1,392\0302,272,348,2,257,1,392\0302,353,436,2,257,1,392\0303,1,68,2,384,1,392\0301,1,21,4,272,1,392\0301,23,92,4,272,3,392\0301,94,152,4,272,3,392\0301,157,193,4,272,1,392\0301,195,257,4,272,1,392\0304,1,49,3,256,3,392\031391,2,2,Old Murk-Eye\030392,2,6,Captain Grayson\0312,40,1436,0,\0302,0,0,5,Harvest Monsters\0302,0,0,6,Captain Grayson\0302,0,0,6,Westfall Lighthouse\031\031ITEM,814,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[1030]="PARTIAL\031loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes, yes... you are one of my kind, but still whole. Still clean.$B$BI am unsure how you have escaped the atrocities the night elves have visited upon our people, but I am glad to know that I am no longer alone.$B$BCorruption now runs through the veins of our kin, young one, corruption brought down upon us by the prideful night elves. They are the ones who did this to our people... They are the ones I blame for being cast out of my tribe.$B$BAt night I can still see the campfires burning in the darkness.\030Alas, I'm not completely certain what he had in mind next.$B$BIf what he said was true about the rod's power, then it will allow you to take on another form altogether. Which form, I do not know.$B$BPerhaps he meant to use its powers to get closer to the tainted furbolgs, but even the uncorrupted creatures would slaughter him were he not careful. Transformed by the rod, Dartol would have to speak to a furbolg who was safe from the effects of Fel Moss.$B$BI would start your search southeast of Mystral Lake.\030Find an uncorrupted furbolg, and using the power of Dartol's Rod of Transformation, speak to him.\030\030Raene's Cleansing\0312,1,58,2,257,1,3691\0302,63,168,2,257,4,3691\0302,170,195,2,257,1,3691\0302,200,348,2,257,4,3691\0302,350,455,2,257,4,3691\0302,460,511,2,257,4,3691\0303,1,97,2,384,1,3691\0301,1,11,4,272,1,3897\0301,13,52,4,272,1,3897\0301,54,65,4,272,1,3897\0301,70,211,4,304,1,3897\0301,216,336,4,276,1,3897\0301,338,384,4,272,1,3897\0301,386,442,4,272,1,3897\0301,447,509,4,272,1,3897\03131,2,5,Furbolg\03031,2,7,Furbolg\0312,331,1440,0,\0311029,19,1029,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301045,23,1045,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1031]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Anilia died? No... that can't be! It was just yesterday that we were running and playing together in the woods.$B$BI guess those days are over...\030Anilia puts her hands on your shoulders and draws you close. Gasping, she points towards the arch to the north, before her eyes close and her last wheezing breath leaves her body. \"He has taken it... Geltharis...\" You know in your heart that Anilia's dying wish is to see the Branch of Cenarius back in dryad hands.\030Kill Geltharis and return the Branch of Cenarius to Illiyana at Forest Song.\030Have you found them? What did Anilia say? Where is she?\030The Branch of Cenarius\0312,1,60,2,257,1,3920\0302,62,179,2,257,1,3920\0302,181,199,2,257,1,3920\0302,201,315,2,259,3,3920\0303,1,76,2,384,1,3920\0301,1,12,4,272,2,3901\0301,20,33,4,272,1,3901\0301,35,111,4,272,1,3901\0301,116,145,4,272,1,3901\0304,1,20,3,256,2,3901\0304,22,41,3,256,2,3901\0304,43,55,3,256,2,3901\0313920,2,1,Anilia\0304619,2,4,Geltharis\0304619,2,5,Geltharis\0303901,2,5,Illiyana\0303920,4,6,Anilia\0303920,3,11,Anilia\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,5,Illiyana\0302,0,0,5,Forest Song\0311021,19,1021,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301032,23,1032,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5461,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1032]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, kind $R. My sister's spirit is gladdened by your efforts.\030I can't believe that Anilia is gone... We used to play together in the forests all the time. I almost feel... sad.$B$BI know something that might make me feel better. Please, slay the satyrs that took Anilia from me! Bring me their horns as proof of your actions and you will forever have my gratitude.$B$B\030Bring 16 Satyr Horns to Illiyana in Forest Song.\030Please, help me avenge Anilia's death.\030Satyr Slaying!\0312,1,38,2,257,4,3901\0302,40,92,2,257,1,3901\0302,94,109,2,257,1,3901\0302,111,114,2,257,1,3901\0302,119,166,2,257,4,3901\0302,168,216,2,257,1,3901\0302,218,302,2,257,3,3901\0303,1,48,2,384,1,3901\0301,1,19,4,272,1,3901\0301,21,68,4,272,1,3901\0304,1,38,3,256,1,3901\0313920,2,1,Anilia\0303920,2,6,Anilia\0303901,2,8,Illiyana\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,8,Illiyana\0302,0,0,8,Forest Song\0311031,19,1031,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5481,OBJECTIVE,16,15,",[1033]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh, you found it! I will place the tear in a stew, and pray that it will cure her.$B$BThank you! Thank you, $N!\030I had hoped Orendil's cure would save Relara, but I fear it only slowed the disease running through my child.  We must find more powerful medicine!  Thankfully, Orendil spoke to me of further remedies to try should his first one fail.$B$BElune's Tear is a type of stone that rests in only one place: the isle on Iris Lake, east of Astranaar.  Orendil said the stone will wash away corruption... please, $N, bring me Elune's Tear and pray it will end my child's sickness!\030Bring Elune's Tear to Pelturas in Astranaar.\030$N, did you find Iris Lake? Do you have the Tear?\030Elune's Tear\0312,1,109,2,265,4,3894\0302,112,147,2,257,1,3894\0302,150,234,2,257,1,3894\0302,239,341,2,257,1,3894\0302,344,394,2,261,3,3894\0302,396,470,2,257,3,3894\0303,1,44,2,384,1,3894\0301,1,17,4,272,1,3894\0301,19,82,4,272,3,3894\0301,87,96,4,272,1,3894\0301,98,111,4,272,1,3894\0304,1,27,3,256,2,3894\0304,29,49,3,256,2,3894\031\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,4,Astranaar\0302,0,0,7,Pelturas\0302,0,0,7,Astranaar\0311020,19,1020,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301034,23,1034,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5493,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1034]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You gathered the dust! I will create a poultice from these -- it should bring down Relara's fever.$B$BThank you again, $N. Without your help, my child would surely perish.\030Elune's Tear washed clear some of my daughter's sickness.  Her nightmares are lessened and I thank the goddess for her blessing.  But ... fever still rages within her.$B$BOrendil told me of a frosted dust found among the Ruins of Stardust.  Perhaps it will abate Relara's fever.  Gather some of the dust, then please return to me.$B$BThe Ruins of Stardust lie to the south, $N.  May Elune speed your journey.\030Bring 5 Handfuls of Stardust to Pelturas in Astranaar.\030Do you yet have the Stardust, $N?\030The Ruins of Stardust\0312,1,57,2,257,1,3894\0302,60,128,2,257,1,3894\0302,131,137,2,257,1,3894\0302,139,167,2,257,1,3894\0302,172,239,2,321,1,3894\0302,242,278,2,257,4,3894\0302,281,330,2,257,1,3894\0302,335,377,2,321,1,3894\0302,380,408,2,257,1,3894\0303,1,54,2,384,1,3894\0301,1,22,4,272,1,3894\0301,24,98,4,272,3,3894\0301,103,122,4,272,1,3894\0301,124,171,4,272,4,3894\0304,1,33,3,256,2,3894\031\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,10,Pelturas\0302,0,0,10,Astranaar\0311033,19,1033,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301035,23,1035,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5494,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[1035]="PARTIAL\031loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh, $N, you have saved my daughter! I know the power of the moonstone will give back my daughter her strength!$B$BI can never repay you fully for the aid you have given me, but... please, take this. Other than Relara, it is my most dear possession.\030Relara's fever has passed, but she is still very weak.  I do not believe time alone will give her back the strength she has lost.  I believe it will take the power of a moonstone.$B$BWe used to gather moonstones at Fallen Sky Lake to the southeast... until the Shadethickets came.$B$BTheir leader, a Shadethicket Oracle, gathered up all the fallen moonstones and hoards them.  Now, you must retrieve a moonstone from the Oracle.$B$BAnd to do that, I fear that you must slay him.\030Retrieve a Fallen Moonstone from the Shadethicket Oracle, then bring it to Pelturas in Astranaar.\030Did you face the Shadethicket Oracle, $N? If so, then please hand me the fallen moonstone. Relara has strength left for only a few more breaths!\030Fallen Sky Lake\0312,1,54,2,257,1,3894\0302,57,129,2,261,4,3894\0302,132,179,2,257,4,3894\0302,184,250,2,257,1,3894\0302,252,280,2,257,1,3894\0302,285,375,2,257,1,3894\0302,378,428,2,257,1,3894\0302,433,478,2,257,1,3894\0303,1,97,2,384,1,3894\0301,1,35,4,304,1,3894\0301,37,110,4,272,3,3894\0301,115,179,4,272,1,3894\0301,181,198,4,272,1,3894\0301,200,248,4,272,1,3894\0304,1,41,3,256,2,3894\0304,43,90,3,256,4,3894\0304,92,144,3,256,1,3894\0313931,2,6,Shadethicket Oracle\0303931,2,9,Shadethicket Oracle\0303931,3,15,Shadethicket Oracle\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,4,Fallen Sky Lake\0302,0,0,7,Oracle\0302,0,0,9,Shadethicket Oracle\0302,0,0,9,Pelturas\0302,0,0,9,Astranaar\0311034,19,1034,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5508,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1036]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Avast ye, scallywag. I hears that ye be the type for a bit o' the skullduggery. Well, if yer no friend of Booty Bay, then ye might have a special place with the Bloodsail Buccaneers.$B$BArrrrr...\030$N... yeah, I've heard of you.  I've heard that you're no friend of Booty Bay - just like us Bloodsail Buccaneers.  Fleet Master Firallon is looking for hale and hearty $g men : women; just like you for a special mission.$B$BIf you're interested, head on out to the Crimson Veil and speak with him below decks.  She's anchored off the Wild Coast east of here, next to the Riptide and the Damsel's Luck.\030Speak with Fleet Master Firallon aboard the Crimson Vale off the coast of Stranglethorn Vale.\030\030Avast Ye, Scallywag\0312,7,30,2,257,1,2545\0302,33,114,2,257,1,2545\0302,117,221,2,257,1,2545\0302,226,310,2,257,4,2545\0302,313,402,2,257,1,2545\0303,1,93,2,384,1,2545\0301,1,20,4,272,1,2546\0301,22,79,4,272,1,2546\0301,81,182,4,272,4,2546\0301,187,195,4,272,1,2546\0312546,2,3,Fleet Master Firallon\0302546,2,6,Fleet Master Firallon\0312,33,1434,0,\0302,0,0,4,Crimson Veil\0302,0,0,5,Riptide\0314621,23,4621,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031REPUTATION,87,OBJECTIVE,3000,16,",[1037]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Velinde Starsong? That the priestess disappeared some time ago is almost certainly common knowledge. As to further details about the events that surrounded her departure... it would take good reason for me to divulge such information.\030Velinde Starsong was my predecessor here in Ashenvale Forest. At first it seemed she had the situation in Felwood under control, but little by little her efforts faltered. One day, she simply disappeared.$B$BI was sent here to continue her work. I'm afraid I know nothing of the priestess, however. Perhaps Thyn'tel Bladeweaver, one of the commanders of the Sentinels, knows further details of her disappearance that I was not a party to.$B$BSurely she will understand the import of such information.\030Speak with Thyn'tel Bladeweaver at the Warrior's Terrace in Darnassus.\030\030Velinde Starsong\0312,1,61,2,257,1,3880\0302,63,171,2,257,1,3880\0302,173,204,2,257,1,3880\0302,209,245,2,257,1,3880\0302,247,298,2,257,1,3880\0302,300,438,2,257,4,3880\0302,443,500,2,257,3,3880\0303,1,70,2,384,1,3880\0301,1,17,4,272,2,8026\0301,19,100,4,272,1,8026\0301,102,172,4,272,1,8026\0301,174,234,4,272,4,8026\0313946,2,1,Velinde Starsong\030112,2,5,Priestess\0308026,2,6,Thyn'tel Bladeweaver\0308026,2,8,Thyn'tel Bladeweaver\0303946,4,9,Velinde Starsong\030112,4,10,Priestess\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,1,Ashenvale Forest\0302,0,0,2,Felwood\0302,0,0,8,Warrior's Terrace\0302,0,0,8,Darnassus\0311022,19,1022,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301038,23,1038,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1038]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It seems that Velinde's disappearance is more troubling than it originally appeared. Even still, I cannot believe that she has come to a bad end. Perhaps it would be beneficial for us to make contact with her.$B$B$N, since you have shown a vested interest in this matter, I would like to enlist your aid.\030The Tome of Mel'Thandris showed you this? I suppose there would be little harm in allowing you to examine her belongings. This key will allow you to open the chest where we stored her things in the Sentinels' bunkhouse. She kept a journal of her duties, if there is anything to be learned, it will be from that.$B$BI should tell you, the Sentinels believe that she had her own reasons for leaving, and expect that she could return at any time. The priestess has done much in the past to earn our trust.\030Search through Velinde's chest for her journal, then return it along with the key to Thyn'tel Bladeweaver in Darnassus.\030What'd you find out?\030Velinde's Effects\0312,1,41,2,257,2,8026\0302,43,121,2,257,4,8026\0302,123,219,2,257,3,8026\0302,221,311,2,257,4,8026\0302,316,443,2,257,4,8026\0302,445,502,2,257,1,8026\0303,1,119,2,384,1,8026\0301,1,84,4,272,4,8026\0301,86,145,4,272,4,8026\0301,147,209,4,272,4,8026\0301,214,304,4,274,4,8026\0304,1,20,3,256,2,8026\031112,2,6,Priestess\0308026,2,7,Thyn'tel Bladeweaver\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,3,Sentinels'\0302,0,0,7,Thyn'tel Bladeweaver\0302,0,0,7,Darnassus\0311037,19,1037,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301039,23,1039,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5520,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1039]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031$R, eh? Must admit, we don't get much of your type out here. Looking for someone, eh? Just give me a moment, I'm sure I have it written in one of my ledgers.$B$BLot of people travel through here, though, so just give me a moment.\030Ratchet is the only port in the Barrens. Most likely Velinde found a trading vessel in Ratchet to take her to Blackwater Cove in Azeroth. We've had limited dealings with the goblins that run the port, but the master of the dock should have information about the comings and goings of ship passengers.$B$BFollow the road southeast through Ashenvale and you will find yourself in the Barrens. Watch your step, $n, warriors of the Horde patrol the land. You will be safe at the port, though.\030Speak with Wharfmaster Dizzywig in Ratchet.\030\030The Barrens Port\0312,1,40,2,257,1,8026\0302,42,137,2,257,1,8026\0302,139,300,2,257,1,8026\0302,305,390,2,257,3,8026\0302,392,450,2,257,1,8026\0302,452,488,2,257,3,8026\0303,1,43,2,384,1,8026\0301,9,60,4,272,1,3453\0301,62,85,4,272,2,3453\0301,87,157,4,272,1,3453\0301,162,229,4,272,1,3453\0313453,2,7,Wharfmaster Dizzywig\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,1,Barrens\0302,0,0,2,Ratchet\0302,0,0,2,Blackwater Cove\0302,0,0,2,Azeroth\0302,0,0,4,Barrens\0302,0,0,7,Ratchet\0311038,19,1038,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301040,23,1040,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[104]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031So the foul heathen, Murk-Eye is dead. Well done, $N. By your hands one life was laid to rest but perhaps many more were saved. The Great Sea, wrought with danger as it is, shall be a wee bit safer this night thanks to your heroics.\030When my life was ended upon the rocks, I had no clue what the afterlife held for me.  The Lighthouse was black that night because Old Murk-Eye had scared the keeper's family off.  They returned and re-lit the flame but Old Murk-Eye coerced the weaker minded murlocs to raid the Lighthouse with him once again.  The second time the family was not so lucky and before my eyes they perished helplessly.$B$BSlay Old Murk-Eye if you see him along the shore and bring me one of his scales and I shall reward you.\030Bring a scale of Old Murk-Eye to Captain Grayson at the Westfall Lighthouse.\030Have you laid waste to the menace known as Old Murk-Eye yet? He has been spotted roaming the coastline of Westfall.$B$BReturn to me when the foul beast is dead.\030The Coastal Menace\0312,1,84,2,257,1,392\0302,87,178,2,259,1,392\0302,181,309,2,257,1,392\0302,312,399,2,257,1,392\0302,404,506,2,257,4,392\0303,1,76,2,384,1,392\0301,1,38,4,272,1,392\0301,40,53,4,272,1,392\0301,55,127,4,272,4,392\0301,129,232,4,276,3,392\0304,1,60,3,256,2,392\0304,62,115,3,256,1,392\0304,120,160,3,256,1,392\031391,2,2,Old Murk-Eye\030391,2,3,Old Murk-Eye\030391,2,5,Old Murk-Eye\030391,2,6,Old Murk-Eye\030392,2,6,Captain Grayson\030391,3,11,Old Murk-Eye\0312,40,1436,0,\0302,0,0,6,Captain Grayson\0302,0,0,6,Westfall Lighthouse\031\031ITEM,3636,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1040]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes? Now, it doesn't look to me like you're the sort with goods that need shipping, so either you're looking for a job with my caravan--and there's no jobs to be had now--or you're probably talking to the wrong goblin.$B$BSo which one is it?\030Ah yes, finally found it. Should have told me she passed through here that long ago. Let's see.$B$BVelinde. Booked passage to Booty Bay on the Black Osprey. I don't have anything here saying otherwise, so I'd assume it arrived in port safely.$B$BNot much more help I can be to you, but she asked about overland travel over on that side of the world, and I mentioned Ruzzgot, a caravan driver based out of Booty Bay. Might be that this Velinde traveled with him.$B$BMove along, now. I haven't all day for you.\030Take a boat to Booty Bay and speak with Caravaneer Ruzzgot.\030\030Passage to Booty Bay\0312,1,25,2,257,1,3453\0302,27,84,2,321,1,3453\0302,86,95,2,257,1,3453\0302,100,107,2,257,1,3453\0302,109,156,2,257,1,3453\0302,158,242,2,265,4,3453\0302,247,415,2,257,1,3453\0302,417,461,2,257,4,3453\0302,466,481,2,257,1,3453\0302,483,508,2,257,1,3453\0303,1,59,2,384,1,3453\0301,1,4,4,272,2,3945\0301,6,218,4,274,1,3945\0301,223,241,4,272,2,3945\0313945,2,11,Caravaneer Ruzzgot\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,5,Booty Bay\0302,0,0,11,Booty Bay\0311039,19,1039,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301041,23,1041,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1041]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031With all the strange happenings of the last few years, I keep as good records of strangers as I can. Never know when it might come in handy... though it's usually not pleasant business when it does. Not to suggest anything about this Velinde you're looking for.\030Turns out I was wrong about you, and that isn't something that happens everyday.$B$BIt just so happens that I remember this Velinde you're looking for. Isn't every day that a night elf priestess that wants to travel with a dirty old--but great for your shipping needs!--caravan like my own.$B$BWe split up on the way north, she was headed for Darkshire. The clerk there keeps all sorts of records. Might know something useful.$B$BBe careful in the jungle, it is a deadly place even at the best of times.\030Speak with Clerk Daltry in Darkshire.\030\030The Caravan Road\0312,1,80,2,257,1,3945\0302,85,151,2,257,1,3945\0302,153,290,2,259,1,3945\0302,295,353,2,257,1,3945\0302,355,397,2,257,1,3945\0302,399,426,2,257,4,3945\0302,431,503,2,257,1,3945\0303,1,37,2,384,1,3945\0301,1,100,4,272,1,267\0301,102,142,4,272,4,267\0301,144,198,4,272,1,267\0301,200,261,4,272,1,267\031112,2,3,Priestess\030267,2,8,Clerk Daltry\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,8,Darkshire\0311040,19,1040,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301042,23,1042,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1042]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Dark times these are. Ill news is whispered from every swaying branch, and evil can be found under every rock.$B$BAnd in such times an unknown stranger enters my home and asks of worgen... I'll ask no forgiveness for my suspicions, only answers.$B$BAnd answers, I will have.\030No, I don't have any records of a Velinde Starsong staying in Darkshire... though, if you don't mind me saying, I can hardly imagine a night elf priestess taking a room in the inn, if you get my meaning?$B$BThese wolf-men you mentioned though, that's something I've heard about. Just the other day, Calor came into town with a string of their heads. He works with the Carevin family. Hunters of demons, undead, and other monstrosities. Speak with Jonathan, he's the head of the household.\030Speak with Jonathan Carevin in Darkshire.\030\030The Carevin Family\0312,1,74,2,257,1,267\0302,76,203,2,257,4,267\0302,208,278,2,257,1,267\0302,280,349,2,257,1,267\0302,351,383,2,257,1,267\0302,385,435,2,257,1,267\0302,437,488,2,257,1,267\0303,1,41,2,384,1,267\0301,1,21,4,272,1,661\0301,23,110,4,272,1,661\0301,115,188,4,272,1,661\0301,190,245,4,272,1,661\0301,250,274,4,272,3,661\0313946,2,1,Velinde Starsong\030112,2,2,Priestess\030663,2,4,Calor\030661,2,8,Jonathan Carevin\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,1,Darkshire\0302,0,0,8,Darkshire\0311041,19,1041,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301043,23,1043,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1043]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030requestItems\030title\031It is an interesting story you tell, $N. Though the Carevin family's influence is not large enough that we might find the root of these troubles and finish them once and for all, we will do what we can to contain the worgens' numbers in Duskwood.$B$BAlready I have instructed Calor to make this his first priority.\030Your story rings true... I do not entirely understand your motives, but if your business here in Duskwood involves ridding the forest of worgen in any number, then I can forgo understanding for results.$B$BThere is a mine to the south that has been overrun with worgen... They appeared out of nowhere, but from what we know, that is where they first were found.$B$BGo about your business, but I would ask that if you find anything of import, you share it with me. We will accept any aid in our war against evil.\030Look for signs of the Scythe of Elune then return to Jonathan Carevin in Darkshire.\030\030Find evidence of the Scythe of Elune\030The woods are perilous for the unprepared. Keep your weapons close at hand and your wits even closer, or your next journey into the haunted forest may be your last.\030The Scythe of Elune\0312,1,24,2,257,1,661\0302,26,202,2,257,4,661\0302,207,271,2,257,1,661\0302,273,361,2,257,1,661\0302,366,463,2,257,4,661\0302,465,511,2,261,3,661\0303,1,83,2,384,1,661\0301,1,40,4,272,1,661\0301,42,246,4,272,4,661\0301,251,314,4,272,1,661\0306,1,42,3,256,1,661\0306,44,164,3,256,1,661\0305,1,36,3,384,1,661\031661,2,7,Jonathan Carevin\030663,4,10,Calor\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,2,Duskwood\0302,0,0,7,Jonathan Carevin\0302,0,0,7,Darkshire\0304,0,0,9,Duskwood\0311042,19,1042,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301044,23,1044,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,19030,OBJECTIVE,1,14,Mound of Dirt",[1044]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031So this is the fate of Velinde, is it? The high priestess will be disappointed to hear of this, they were good friends before her disappearance. Still, the Scythe of Elune was surely granted to her as a boon by our goddess, and it is unsettling to me that it has fallen out of her servants' hands.$B$BAnother matter for another time, however. I owe you my thanks in no small amount for what you have accomplished.\030We shall rein in the worgen problem, have no worry of that. This evil that your friend introduced to our woods will be contained, and I bear her no ill will for her actions. Strange events are afoot in these times, $n, and the darkness knows no respite.$B$BI will keep you no longer. I suspect that there are others that should hear of what you have found in the mines of Duskwood.\030Return to Thyn'tel Bladeweaver in Darnassus.\030\030Answered Questions\0312,1,59,2,261,3,661\0302,61,173,2,257,3,661\0302,175,253,2,257,1,661\0302,258,283,2,257,3,661\0302,285,381,2,257,4,661\0303,1,44,2,384,1,661\0301,1,38,4,272,2,8026\0301,40,144,4,272,3,8026\0301,146,297,4,272,1,8026\0301,302,342,4,272,1,8026\0301,344,413,4,272,1,8026\0318026,2,6,Thyn'tel Bladeweaver\030112,4,8,Priestess\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,6,Thyn'tel Bladeweaver\0302,0,0,6,Darnassus\0311043,19,1043,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1045]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have done well, my friend.$B$BThe forest is still tainted, but at least we know we have done a small part to return it to its former glory. If you wish to return to me again, I would enjoy the company of my own kind.$B$BBe well. Perhaps our tribes will meet again under less violent times.\030The night elves are as old as time, but their arrogance destroys their very world. And now it destroys our lives too. But that can no longer be controlled...$B$BI blame the elves for much, but we are still responsible for our actions. Even beyond the corruption, we are capable of great evil.$B$BRan Bloodtooth is one such evil. Power hungry, lusting... the corruption has only made him stronger. My hatred for the elves burns, but I do not wish ill upon their children, so we must police our own.\030Kill Ran Bloodtooth and 4 Bloodtooth Guards and return to Krolg near Lake Mystral.\030Have you slain Ran yet, my friend?$B$BEven the Night elves do not truly deserve his wrath. His hatred burns even brighter than my own, but his mind is no longer his own. He is a threat to all the natural creatures of this forest.\030Raene's Cleansing\0312,1,82,2,257,1,3897\0302,84,117,2,257,1,3897\0302,119,157,2,257,1,3897\0302,162,234,2,257,1,3897\0302,236,292,2,261,1,3897\0302,297,328,2,257,1,3897\0302,330,353,2,257,1,3897\0302,355,396,2,261,1,3897\0302,398,497,2,259,3,3897\0303,1,82,2,384,1,3897\0301,1,30,4,272,1,3897\0301,35,143,4,272,1,3897\0301,145,220,4,274,4,3897\0301,225,232,4,272,1,3897\0301,234,293,4,272,4,3897\0304,1,34,3,260,2,3897\0304,39,90,3,256,1,3897\0304,92,169,3,256,1,3897\0304,171,229,3,260,1,3897\0313696,2,6,Ran Bloodtooth\03011045,2,9,Burns\0303696,2,10,Ran Bloodtooth\0303897,2,10,Krolg\03011045,3,18,Burns\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,10,Krolg\0302,0,0,10,Lake Mystral\0311030,19,1030,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301046,23,1046,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,3696,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Ran Bloodtooth\030NPC,3932,OBJECTIVE,4,13,Bloodtooth Guard",[1046]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031So, this is the skull of the fiercest furbolg threat in Ashenvale?$B$BI am more than pleased with your abilities, $N. The Sentinels cannot thank you enough. I hope we can rely on you again in the future to help our people.$B$BI shall put this skull and Dartol's Rod in a place of reverence for others to see.$B$BTeronis would be proud. Thank you again.\030Return to your own tribe and let them know of your victory here.$B$BShow them your trophy, and bask in the glory...\030Bring Ran Bloodtooth's Skull and Dartol's Rod of Transformation to Raene Wolfrunner in Astranaar.\030The Sentinels do what they can here in Ashenvale, but it's thanks to $rs like you that we have gained the ground we have.\030Raene's Cleansing\0312,1,64,2,257,1,3897\0302,69,115,2,257,1,3897\0303,1,97,2,384,1,3897\0301,1,66,4,276,2,3691\0301,71,117,4,272,1,3691\0301,119,156,4,272,1,3691\0301,158,222,4,274,3,3691\0301,227,308,4,272,3,3691\0301,313,335,4,272,4,3691\0301,337,352,4,272,1,3691\0304,1,121,3,256,1,3691\0313696,2,3,Ran Bloodtooth\0303691,2,3,Raene Wolfrunner\03031,4,4,Furbolg\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,3,Raene Wolfrunner\0302,0,0,3,Astranaar\0304,0,0,4,Ashenvale\0303,0,0,11,Ashenvale\0311045,19,1045,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5462,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1047]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031What makes you think I wish to be pestered by the likes of you, $C? Wait - let me stop the important duties I attend to on a daily basis so I can help you locate a doodad somewhere. By all means, the welfare of Darnassus - nay, all of Teldrassil - should come second to the acquisition of a bauble for your collection.$B$BThe fools in Moonglade waste my time with their call for assistance, and now I must endure this?\030Attention, heroes!$B$BThe Cenarion Circle seeks able bodied individuals to assist them in exploring the vast new frontiers of Kalimdor!  A forbidden wasteland of unimaginable dangers lies far to the west of Tanaris and Gadgetzan, and the Circle needs willing and honorable proxies to act in their stead.$B$BAll interested individuals should seek audience with the Cenarion Circle.  Speak with the Arch Druid in Darnassus, Fandral Staghelm, for more information!\030Speak with Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm at the Cenarion Enclave of Darnassus about the Cenarion Circle's call to explore the frontiers of Kalimdor.\030\030The New Frontier\0312,1,18,2,257,1,10878\0302,23,135,2,323,1,10878\0302,138,303,2,259,1,10878\0302,308,380,2,323,1,10878\0302,383,461,2,257,1,10878\0303,1,146,2,448,1,10878\0301,1,67,4,274,2,3516\0301,69,181,4,272,1,3516\0301,183,318,4,272,1,3516\0301,323,418,4,272,2,3516\03115382,2,5,Fandral Staghelm\0303516,2,6,Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm\03015382,2,6,Fandral Staghelm\0312,1657,1457,0,\0302,0,0,3,Tanaris\0302,0,0,5,Darnassus\0302,0,0,6,Cenarion Enclave of Darnassus\0304,0,0,10,Moonglade\0311015,22,1015,UNKNOWN\0301019,22,1019,UNKNOWN\0306761,23,6761,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1048]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have served the Dark Lady well, $c. 'Twas no small task I asked of you.$B$BYour loyalty to the Forsaken has been noted. And your tenacity in combat will be remembered.\030Whilst the Dark Lady tends to the pressing issue of the Lich King's advance to the north, I am seeing to it that matters closer to home are being taken care of accordingly.$B$BNo doubt, the human pests who call themselves the Scarlet Crusade are proving to be the sharpest thorn in our side domestically. Tirisfal Glades is literally crawling with the little red ants.$B$BTravel to the Monastery, $c, and lay waste to High Inquisitor Whitemane and her top lieutenants.\030Kill High Inquisitor Whitemane, Scarlet Commander Mograine, Herod, the Scarlet Champion and Houndmaster Loksey and then report back to Varimathras in the Undercity.\030Perhaps I was not explicit in my orders, $c. I want High Inquisitor Whitemane killed once and for all. And while you're at it, take out her top brass as well.$B$BKill that zealot, Scarlet Commander Mograine. Lay waste to Herod, the Scarlet Champion. And slaughter Houndmaster Loksey and his filthy mutts too.$B$BNow begone!\030Into The Scarlet Monastery\0312,1,172,2,321,1,2425\0302,177,304,2,257,1,2425\0302,306,368,2,257,1,2425\0302,373,468,2,257,1,2425\0303,1,164,2,384,1,2425\0301,1,39,4,272,1,2425\0301,41,75,4,272,1,2425\0301,80,123,4,272,1,2425\0301,125,171,4,272,3,2425\0304,1,44,3,256,4,2425\0304,46,102,3,258,1,2425\0304,104,158,3,256,1,2425\0304,163,207,3,256,1,2425\0304,209,249,3,256,1,2425\0304,251,308,3,256,1,2425\0304,313,323,3,256,1,2425\03115065,2,1,Lady\03016980,2,1,The Lich King\0303977,2,4,High Inquisitor Whitemane\0303977,2,5,High Inquisitor Whitemane\0303976,2,5,Scarlet Commander Mograine\0303975,2,5,Herod\0304302,2,5,Scarlet Champion\0303974,2,5,Houndmaster Loksey\0302425,2,5,Varimathras\03015065,4,6,Lady\0303977,3,11,High Inquisitor Whitemane\0303976,3,13,Scarlet Commander Mograine\0303975,3,14,Herod\0304302,3,14,Scarlet Champion\0303974,3,15,Houndmaster Loksey\0312,796,0,0,\0302,0,0,4,Monastery\0302,0,0,4,High Inquisitor Whitemane\0302,0,0,5,Varimathras\0302,0,0,5,Undercity\0304,0,0,8,Forsaken\0303,0,0,14,Herod\031\031NPC,3977,OBJECTIVE,1,13,High Inquisitor Whitemane\030NPC,3976,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Scarlet Commander Mograine\030NPC,3975,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Herod\030NPC,3974,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Houndmaster Loksey",[1049]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The Compendium of the Fallen! I was beginning to wonder if the very book existed!$B$BYou have served the Tauren of Thunder Bluff well, $N. Your dedication shall not be forgotten.\030The Earthen Ring had pure intentions towards our plagued brethren. But who is to know the motivations of those whispering in the ears of the Elder Council?$B$BThe Forsaken whom we have allied with have a history wrought with deceit. Too hasty was our pact. Perhaps Cairne would have been wise to heed the warnings from Orgrimmar.$B$BDeep within the Scarlet Monastery lies the Compendium of the Fallen, guarded by crazed human zealots. Their method is forged from insanity but their research might prove useful.\030Retrieve the Compendium of the Fallen from the Monastery in Tirisfal Glades and return to Sage Truthseeker in Thunder Bluff.\030Cairne is a brave and noble leader and I would trust him with my own life. But it is others that I do not trust in this political climate.$B$BOnce I have a chance to gather all the knowledge available I can provide sound council to the Chieftain.$B$BHave you had a chance to travel to Tirisfal Glades? To the Scarlet Monastery? The Compendium of the Fallen is just one piece in this complicated puzzle...\030Compendium of the Fallen\0312,1,66,2,257,1,3978\0302,68,155,2,257,2,3978\0302,160,232,2,321,1,3978\0302,234,256,2,257,1,3978\0302,258,329,2,257,4,3978\0302,334,434,2,257,1,3978\0302,436,510,2,257,4,3978\0303,1,124,2,384,1,3978\0301,1,29,4,272,1,3978\0301,31,81,4,272,4,3978\0301,86,138,4,272,1,3978\0301,140,178,4,272,3,3978\0304,1,74,3,256,4,3978\0304,76,138,3,256,1,3978\0304,143,246,3,256,1,3978\0304,251,301,3,256,2,3978\0304,303,327,3,256,2,3978\0304,329,404,3,256,1,3978\0313978,2,8,Sage Truthseeker\0312,796,0,0,\0302,0,0,5,Orgrimmar\0302,0,0,6,Scarlet Monastery\0302,0,0,8,Monastery\0302,0,0,8,Tirisfal Glades\0302,0,0,8,Sage Truthseeker\0302,0,0,8,Thunder Bluff\0303,0,0,15,Chieftain\0303,0,0,16,Tirisfal Glades\031\031ITEM,5535,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[105]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You've done it! Araj... the lich is finally defeated!$B$BYou've done a tremendous service to the Horde on this day, $N. Your bravery and perseverance are a testament to what it means to be a true hero. Please - accept this as a token for all to see and know that you have delivered the Horde a victory for the ages!\030Alas, the time to attack Andorhal and drive out the lich that controls it is upon us!$B$BInside the ruins of the city is where the lich - Araj the Summoner - holds dominion.  He is guarded by numerous Scourge surrounding the remains of city's center, and his personal retinue of guardians attached to him directly is formidable.  You will need numerous allies to even stand a chance of facing him successfully.$B$BDestroy Araj, $N, and bring me a shard from his phylactery as proof!\030Bring Araj's Phylactery Shard to High Executor Derrington at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands.\030Your task has been given to you, $N. Do you have a shard from the lich's phylactery as proof of the task being accomplished?\030Alas, Andorhal\0312,1,85,2,261,1,10837\0302,90,173,2,321,1,10837\0302,176,328,2,321,1,10837\0302,331,410,2,259,3,10837\0302,415,482,2,261,1,10837\0303,1,94,2,384,1,10837\0301,1,15,4,272,1,10837\0301,17,23,4,272,1,10837\0301,25,53,4,272,1,10837\0301,58,119,4,272,1,10837\0301,121,201,4,272,1,10837\0301,203,315,4,272,1,10837\0304,1,36,3,256,1,10837\0304,38,124,3,256,2,10837\0311852,2,2,Araj the Summoner\03010837,2,6,High Executor Derrington\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,6,High Executor Derrington\0302,0,0,6,Bulwark\0304,0,0,10,Horde\0315098,19,5098,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,17114,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1050]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have rescued the sacred text!$B$BYour journey was long and acquiring the book was undoubtedly no easy task. But the dwarves of Ironforge stand to benefit from your success.$B$BThank you, $N, on behalf of the Explorers' League.\030The future is inevitable! We hurl ourselves towards it like falling raindrops to the Great Sea.$B$BBut perhaps, by studying the past, we can know what to expect and be better prepared for the unknown.$B$BBefore dire troubles fell upon Lordaeron, there was a bastion of knowledge tucked away in the Tirisfal Glades. It is rumored that a book called Mythology of the Titans was housed in the library of the old Monastery.$B$BBring it to me and perhaps together we can unlock the secrets of the past!\030Retrieve Mythology of the Titans from the Monastery and bring it to Librarian Mae Paledust in Ironforge.\030The Monastery was a seminary for Paladins-in-training. Once a stronghold of the Light, it fell into the hands of the crazed zealots of the Scarlet Crusade.$B$BThe Crusade believed their goal a noble one: to purify the land of the undead plague. But insanity tainted their plight and now they stand enemies to all.$B$BBring Mythology of the Titans to me so I can study it and house it here in Ironforge.$B$BThe corrupt halls of the Monastery are no place for such a historical treasure.\030Mythology of the Titans\0312,1,25,2,257,1,3979\0302,27,95,2,257,1,3979\0302,100,200,2,257,4,3979\0302,205,314,2,257,1,3979\0302,316,419,2,321,1,3979\0302,424,497,2,257,4,3979\0303,1,104,2,448,1,3979\0301,1,33,4,272,1,3979\0301,38,111,4,272,1,3979\0301,113,176,4,272,1,3979\0301,181,230,4,272,1,3979\0304,1,54,3,256,1,3979\0304,56,155,3,256,1,3979\0304,160,244,3,260,1,3979\0304,246,313,3,260,1,3979\0304,318,402,3,320,1,3979\0304,407,485,3,324,1,3979\0313979,2,7,Librarian Mae Paledust\0312,796,0,0,\0302,0,0,2,Great Sea\0302,0,0,4,Tirisfal Glades\0302,0,0,7,Monastery\0302,0,0,7,Librarian Mae Paledust\0302,0,0,7,Ironforge\0303,0,0,16,Ironforge\031\031ITEM,5536,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1051]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Vorrel led such a troubled existence. And what a good mate he was...$B$BDamn those filthy humans!$B$BVorrel is gone, never to enjoy undeath again. At least I can take solace in the revenge you took in his name. For that I thank you.$B$BNow let me be to mourn....\030Even though my will is free, I can serve the Dark Lady no more. I feel my time on Azeroth has come to an end. My life force is shattered.$B$BInterrogator Vishas did this to me! Tortured me for weeks! Took my wedding ring and gave it to his wife. The bastard!$B$BRevenge... I want revenge!$B$BThe pompous fool bragged about his precious wife, Nancy, who lived along Lake Lordamere. Track the wench down, slay her and return my wedding ring to my wife, Monika in Tarren Mill.$B$BHeed my last wishes....\030Return Vorrel Sengutz's wedding ring to Monika Sengutz in Tarren Mill.\030What do you want, stranger?\030Vorrel's Revenge\0312,1,63,2,257,3,3981\0302,65,109,2,257,1,3981\0302,111,137,2,257,1,3981\0302,142,176,2,257,1,3981\0302,178,199,2,257,1,3981\0302,201,245,2,257,1,3981\0302,247,258,2,257,1,3981\0302,263,272,2,259,1,3981\0302,274,288,2,259,1,3981\0302,293,380,2,257,1,3981\0302,382,473,2,257,1,3981\0302,478,500,2,259,1,3981\0303,1,70,2,384,1,3981\0301,1,37,4,272,1,3982\0301,39,68,4,272,1,3982\0301,73,97,4,272,1,3982\0301,102,146,4,272,1,3982\0301,148,210,4,274,1,3982\0301,212,232,4,272,1,3982\0301,237,262,4,272,1,3982\0304,1,27,3,258,2,3982\03115065,2,1,Lady\0303983,2,4,Interrogator Vishas\03014528,2,10,Precious\0303981,2,13,Vorrel Sengutz\0303982,2,13,Monika Sengutz\0312,796,0,0,\0302,0,0,11,Tarren Mill\0302,0,0,13,Monika Sengutz\0302,0,0,13,Tarren Mill\031\031ITEM,5538,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1052]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Brother Anton still spreads the word of the Scarlet Crusade? Oh my....\030We of the Scarlet Crusade lay claim to strongholds from Hearthglen to Tirisfal Glades. We are quite proud of our bastions of cleansing throughout Lordaeron.$B$BYou have proven yourself against the undead in Desolace. But the true threat of the plague lies in Lordaeron.$B$BTravel to the town of Southshore, in the Eastern Kingdoms. Seek out a crusader named Raleigh the Devout. Give him this letter of commendation bearing my seal and he will escort you to a place of honor in our Scarlet Monastery.\030Take Brother Anton's Letter of Commendation to Raleigh the Devout in Southshore.\030Who goes there? What do you want from me?\030Down the Scarlet Path\0312,1,86,2,257,1,1182\0302,88,156,2,257,1,1182\0302,161,216,2,257,1,1182\0302,218,269,2,261,1,1182\0302,274,331,2,257,1,1182\0302,333,377,2,257,1,1182\0302,379,499,2,257,3,1182\0303,1,80,2,384,1,1182\0301,1,60,4,272,2,3980\0304,1,15,3,256,2,3980\0304,17,41,3,258,2,3980\0313980,2,6,Raleigh the Devout\0301182,2,8,Brother Anton\0303980,2,8,Raleigh the Devout\0301182,4,9,Brother Anton\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,1,Hearthglen\0302,0,0,1,Tirisfal Glades\0302,0,0,3,Desolace\0302,0,0,4,Lordaeron\0302,0,0,5,Eastern Kingdoms\0302,0,0,8,Raleigh the Devout\0302,0,0,8,Southshore\031261,19,261,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301053,23,1053,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1053]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031While disciples of the Light never revel in the loss of life, we must accept that on occasion, such sacrifices must happen for the greater good of the Kingdom and the planet.$B$BThrough your deeds in the Monastery you have spared many innocent lives, $N. I salute your tenacity.\030I once served the Scarlet Crusade with honor, loyalty and pride. I believed their cause to be a noble one: to rid Azeroth of the undead.$B$BBut as I spent time at the Monastery in Tirisfal Glades I realized that their grasp on reality was slipping. They now think everyone is plagued who doesn't wear the tabard of the Crusade. Innocent men and women were tortured because they were supposedly plagued. $B$BThe Scarlet Crusade must be crushed in the name of the Light. You, $n, must destroy the deranged regime.\030Kill High Inquisitor Whitemane, Scarlet Commander Mograine,  Herod, the Scarlet Champion and Houndmaster Loksey and then report back to Raleigh the Devout in Southshore.\030The corruption in the Monastery will not end until the highest ranking officials have been removed.$B$BIn the name of the Light, slay High Inquisitor Whitemane, Scarlet Commander Mograine,  Herod, the Scarlet Champion and Houndmaster Loksey. Once they have fallen, perhaps the true cause can be rekindled. Until then, anyone who crosses the path of the Crusade lies in peril.$B$BVenture forth from Southshore and make it so!\030In the Name of the Light\0312,1,64,2,257,1,3980\0302,66,136,2,257,1,3980\0302,141,248,2,257,1,3980\0302,250,327,2,257,1,3980\0302,329,402,2,259,1,3980\0302,408,468,2,257,1,3980\0302,470,511,2,261,1,3980\0303,1,169,2,384,1,3980\0301,1,174,4,280,1,3980\0301,179,254,4,272,1,3980\0301,256,278,4,272,1,3980\0304,1,99,3,260,3,3980\0304,104,241,3,256,1,3980\0304,243,305,3,256,4,3980\0304,307,375,3,256,1,3980\0304,380,424,3,256,1,3980\0313977,2,8,High Inquisitor Whitemane\0303976,2,8,Scarlet Commander Mograine\0303975,2,8,Herod\0304302,2,8,Scarlet Champion\0303974,2,8,Houndmaster Loksey\0303980,2,8,Raleigh the Devout\0303977,3,13,High Inquisitor Whitemane\0303976,3,13,Scarlet Commander Mograine\0303975,3,13,Herod\0304302,3,13,Scarlet Champion\0303974,3,13,Houndmaster Loksey\0312,796,0,0,\0302,0,0,3,Monastery\0302,0,0,3,Tirisfal Glades\0302,0,0,8,Raleigh the Devout\0302,0,0,8,Southshore\0304,0,0,10,Monastery\0303,0,0,12,Monastery\0303,0,0,16,Southshore\0311052,19,1052,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,3977,OBJECTIVE,1,13,High Inquisitor Whitemane\030NPC,3976,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Scarlet Commander Mograine\030NPC,3975,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Herod\030NPC,3974,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Houndmaster Loksey",[1054]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $N.$B$BWe are under constant threat from the furbolg. Hopefully this will keep them at bay for a bit longer.\030Directly to the north of Astranaar are the Thistlefur furbolg. My scouts report that their numbers have grown greatly over the past few months. If they grow too great, they may find the courage to attack Astranaar directly.$B$BKill as many of their kind as you can, but bring me their chieftain's skull as proof that their efforts have been stifled... for now.$B$BI shall remain here in Astranaar and await word from you. Elune be with you.\030Bring Dal Bloodclaw's Skull to Raene Wolfrunner in Astranaar.\030The furbolgs' corruption has caused Ashenvale to become a fraction of its former glory.\030Culling the Threat\0312,1,62,2,257,1,3691\0302,64,143,2,257,1,3691\0302,145,223,2,261,4,3691\0302,228,351,2,257,1,3691\0302,353,360,2,257,1,3691\0302,365,421,2,257,3,3691\0302,423,440,2,257,1,3691\0303,1,61,2,384,1,3691\0301,1,14,4,272,1,3691\0301,19,64,4,276,1,3691\0301,66,119,4,272,3,3691\0304,1,87,3,260,1,3691\03131,2,1,Furbolg\0303987,2,8,Dal Bloodclaw\0303691,2,8,Raene Wolfrunner\03031,4,10,Furbolg\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,1,Astranaar\0302,0,0,6,Astranaar\0302,0,0,8,Raene Wolfrunner\0302,0,0,8,Astranaar\031\031ITEM,5544,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1055]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You've done it, $N! Well done!\030The rod, now complete, lies in your hands. Shael'dryn will want to hear of your success.\030Return to Shael'dryn at the moonwell.\030\030Raene's Cleansing\0312,1,42,2,257,1,0\0302,44,88,2,259,3,0\0303,1,37,2,384,1,0\0301,1,19,4,272,1,3916\0301,21,30,4,272,1,3916\0313916,2,2,Shael'dryn\0303916,2,3,Shael'dryn\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,3,Shael'dryn\0311028,19,1028,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301029,23,1029,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,19024,GIVER,?,9,Hidden Shrine",[1056]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Alas, you arrive. I see Faldreas has listened to the forest spirits...\030The forest spirits tell me you are brave and willing to travel.$B$BTo the south, not far from Mystral Lake, there lies a tunnel named The Talondeep Path. Through this tunnel you will come to an area known as Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains. Once there, journey to the southwest past Cragpool Lake and then north, up the steep slope until you reach Stonetalon Peak.$B$BThere awaits Keeper Albagorm. Heed his bidding, $r.$B$BThe journey will be perilous.\030Travel to Keeper Albagorm on Stonetalon Peak.\030\030Journey to Stonetalon Peak\0312,1,63,2,257,1,3996\0302,68,153,2,257,1,3996\0302,155,251,2,257,3,3996\0302,253,375,2,257,1,3996\0302,380,408,2,257,1,3996\0302,410,430,2,257,1,3996\0302,435,463,2,257,3,3996\0303,1,45,2,384,1,3996\0301,1,17,4,272,1,3994\0301,19,70,4,272,1,3994\0313994,2,5,Keeper Albagorm\0303994,2,8,Keeper Albagorm\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,2,Mystral Lake\0302,0,0,3,Stonetalon Mountains\0302,0,0,8,Keeper Albagorm\0311057,23,1057,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301057,24,1057,UNKNOWN\031",[1057]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Now that the Bloodfuries have suffered such a great loss, perhaps the true work of restoring the land can begin....\030As a protector of the forest spirits you can undoubtedly guess why I am alarmed.$B$BYou have traveled through these mountains to reach this peak. Surely you have seen the travesty which has befallen the land. Greed has led to the destruction of these sacred hills.$B$BThe Charred Vale to the south was set afire by the greedy mechanized army of industrialists. Worse yet, the Bloodfuries that have encroached on the land refuse us passage in to begin regrowth.$B$BDrive the wretched harpies out, $n!\030Keeper Albagorm on Stonetalon Peak wants you to slay 7 Bloodfury Harpies, 7 Bloodfury Ambushers, 7 Bloodfury Slayers and 7 Bloodfury Roguefeathers.\030There is much work to be done before the Charred Vale can be restored to the lush forest it once was.$B$BClear the area of those foul menaces, $N! Only then can we begin to reclaim what belongs to nature.\030Reclaiming the Charred Vale\0312,1,80,2,257,1,3994\0302,85,145,2,257,1,3994\0302,147,208,2,257,1,3994\0302,210,264,2,257,1,3994\0302,269,360,2,257,1,3994\0302,362,460,2,257,1,3994\0302,465,499,2,257,1,3994\0303,1,147,2,386,1,3994\0301,1,115,4,272,4,3994\0304,1,101,3,320,1,3994\0304,106,146,3,256,1,3994\0304,148,204,3,256,1,3994\0313994,2,8,Keeper Albagorm\0312,406,1442,0,\0311059,23,1059,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,4022,OBJECTIVE,7,13,Bloodfury Harpy\030NPC,4025,OBJECTIVE,7,13,Bloodfury Ambusher\030NPC,4024,OBJECTIVE,7,13,Bloodfury Slayer\030NPC,4023,OBJECTIVE,7,13,Bloodfury Roguefeather",[1058]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh how happy these little woodland nymphs shall be! We'll make them feel right at home with this special concoction!\030So excited I am!$B$BThree little cages for three little elves! But what shall we do with our lovely tree-hugging friends? Why, let's give them a taste of... what do they call it... forest magic!$B$BI'll need a good mess of Stonetalon sap. From those horrid felines, bring me some twilight whiskers. This calls for plenty of courser eyes, of course -- can never have enough eyes. Oh, and lest we forget, a precious scale from a fey dragon.$B$BHurry to Stonetalon Peak, $n, so I can brew some forest magic!\030Witch Doctor Jin'Zil at Malaka'jin wants 5 portions of Stonetalon Sap, 5 Twilight Whiskers, 30 Courser Eyes and a Fey Dragon Scale.\030Look at our poor little elf friends. All caged up with no forest to frolic in!$B$BNow were you able to find me some sap? How about the whiskers from the twilight runners? Don't suppose you have that fey dragon scale on you?$B$BAnd eyes! I'll need so many eyes! You just can't mix up a fierce forest magic brew without a good helping of eyes!\030Jin'Zil's Forest Magic\0312,1,16,2,257,1,3995\0302,21,62,2,257,1,3995\0302,64,121,2,257,2,3995\0302,123,156,2,257,1,3995\0302,158,180,2,257,1,3995\0302,182,194,2,257,1,3995\0302,199,238,2,259,1,3995\0302,240,298,2,257,1,3995\0302,300,378,2,257,1,3995\0302,380,438,2,257,1,3995\0302,443,504,2,257,1,3995\0303,1,131,2,386,1,3995\0301,1,51,4,272,3,3995\0301,53,116,4,272,1,3995\0304,1,36,3,256,1,3995\0304,38,78,3,256,1,3995\0304,83,120,3,256,2,3995\0304,122,170,3,256,2,3995\0304,172,223,3,256,2,3995\0304,228,236,3,256,1,3995\0304,238,260,3,258,1,3995\0304,262,341,3,256,1,3995\03114528,2,10,Precious\0304016,2,10,Fey Dragon\0303995,2,12,Witch Doctor Jin'Zil\0304016,2,12,Fey Dragon\0304016,3,19,Fey Dragon\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,11,Stonetalon Peak\0302,0,0,12,Malaka'jin\031\031ITEM,5582,OBJECTIVE,5,15,\030ITEM,5584,OBJECTIVE,5,15,\030ITEM,5585,OBJECTIVE,30,15,\030ITEM,5583,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1059]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Keeper Albagorm was wise to send you with such urgency.$B$BLet us see if we cannot call forth aid from the great forest to travel to the Charred Vale before it is too late.\030The Bloodfuries have been subdued. But they will regroup soon enough if action is not taken.$B$BFar south of the Barrens lies a land known as Thousand Needles. If you travel west in Thousand Needles until you reach the lush forest's edge of Feralas, you will find a druid named Falfindel Waywarder.$B$BThis great and wise druid is capable of calling forth great forest spirits which can aid in the reclamation of the Charred Vale.$B$BSend word of our need! Seek him out at once!\030Travel to Falfindel Waywarder on the border of Thousand Needles and Feralas.\030\030Reclaiming the Charred Vale\0312,1,34,2,257,1,3994\0302,36,92,2,257,4,3994\0302,97,159,2,257,1,3994\0302,161,298,2,257,4,3994\0302,303,430,2,257,1,3994\0302,435,456,2,259,1,3994\0302,458,478,2,257,1,3994\0303,1,76,2,384,1,3994\0301,1,55,4,272,1,4048\0301,60,172,4,280,4,4048\0314048,2,4,Falfindel Waywarder\0304048,2,8,Falfindel Waywarder\0303994,4,9,Keeper Albagorm\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,3,Barrens\0302,0,0,4,Thousand Needles\0302,0,0,8,Falfindel Waywarder\0304,0,0,10,Charred Vale\0311057,19,1057,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[106]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah! I can't stand us being apart. I have to see her!!\030Oh, I'm cursed!  My heart belongs to Tommy Joe Stonefield, but our families are bitter enemies.  So I can't see him, even though my eyes ache to gaze upon that handsome face!$B$BPlease, take this letter and give it to Tommy Joe.  He's usually at the river to the west of the Stonefield Farm, which is due west of here.\030Give Maybell's Love Letter to Tommy Joe Stonefield.\030You have what?? Maybell is the light of my dull life. Hurry, let me see her letter!\030Young Lovers\0312,1,15,2,261,1,251\0302,18,95,2,261,1,251\0302,98,174,2,257,1,251\0302,179,228,2,257,1,251\0302,231,318,2,257,1,251\0303,1,51,2,384,1,251\0301,5,33,4,272,1,252\0301,35,53,4,272,1,252\0304,1,15,3,256,2,252\0304,17,53,3,256,1,252\0304,55,83,3,256,1,252\031252,2,2,Tommy Joe Stonefield\030252,2,6,Tommy Joe Stonefield\0312,12,1429,0,\0302,0,0,2,Tommy Joe Stonefield\0302,0,0,4,Tommy Joe\0302,0,0,5,Stonefield Farm\0302,0,0,6,Tommy Joe Stonefield\031111,23,111,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1060]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ahh, a letter from Darsok. I have not heard from him in many years.$B$BSo the last of the Bloodfeathers are dead, eh? That is good news, I can remember when my friend Rokhan went with that crazy mok'nathal to kill her older sister. Ah, to be young again, like you.\030You've done so well for me, $n. You're a regular lucky rabbit's foot and there's something I want you to see.$B$BThe harpies are not from around the Barrens. They come from a place called Stonetalon, far to the northwest of here. Though it is probably a dangerous place for you, I need this letter delivered to an old friend of mine who lives there, a witch doctor by the name of Jin'Zil.$B$BHe'll be happy to know that Serena Bloodfeather is dead, and I think you'll find Stonetalon an interesting place.\030Deliver Darsok's letter to Jin'Zil within his cave in Malaka'Jin, in Stonetalon.\030You seem a shady character. You have something for me to see?\030Letter to Jin'Zil\0312,1,31,2,257,1,3449\0302,33,109,2,259,1,3449\0302,114,157,2,257,1,3449\0302,159,229,2,257,1,3449\0302,231,388,2,259,1,3449\0302,393,505,2,257,1,3449\0303,1,80,2,384,1,3449\0301,1,26,4,272,1,3995\0301,28,67,4,272,1,3995\0301,72,117,4,272,2,3995\0301,119,231,4,272,1,3995\0301,233,264,4,272,1,3995\0304,1,27,3,256,4,3995\0304,29,61,3,256,2,3995\0313452,2,6,Serena Bloodfeather\0312,17,1413,0,\0302,0,0,7,Jin'Zil\0302,0,0,7,Malaka'Jin\0302,0,0,7,Stonetalon\0304,0,0,8,Darsok\031876,19,876,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1061]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, a $C. Very good. We will need your skills to deal with these plunderers!\030The spirits of the Stonetalon Mountains are angered, for goblins and their servants are plundering and burning the land.  So the land has cried out, and those who listen for such things... have heard.$B$BSeereth Stonebreak, a promising shaman of the Horde, was sent to Stonetalon.  She reports massive deforestation at the hands of the goblins, and requests aid.$B$BMeet Seereth in Stonetalon.  To reach her, follow the road west of the Barrens' Crossroads.  She is camped near the Greatwood Vale.\030Speak with Seereth Stonebreak in the Stonetalon Mountains.\030\030The Spirits of Stonetalon\0312,1,120,2,257,1,4047\0302,123,188,2,257,1,4047\0302,190,200,2,257,1,4047\0302,205,280,2,257,1,4047\0302,283,362,2,257,1,4047\0302,367,393,2,257,1,4047\0302,396,457,2,257,1,4047\0302,460,497,2,257,1,4047\0303,1,58,2,384,1,4047\0301,11,20,4,272,1,4049\0301,22,76,4,274,3,4049\0314049,2,4,Seereth Stonebreak\0304049,2,9,Seereth Stonebreak\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,4,Stonetalon\0302,0,0,6,Stonetalon\0302,0,0,7,Barrens' Crossroads\0302,0,0,8,Greatwood Vale\0302,0,0,9,Stonetalon Mountains\031\031",[1062]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Bravely done, $N.$B$BWe may ultimately need the wisdom of tauren elders to calm the spirits of Stonetalon, but...$B$BRidding the Venture Company of its personnel is a good first move against them.\030The goblin-run Venture Company moved into the Stonetalon Mountains, chopping down trees and burning huge stretches of forest.  The spirits of this place are nearly blind with pain and rage.  We must stop the Venture Company!$B$BHead northwest, beyond the Greatwood Vale and into the Windshear Crag.  You will find the goblins and their servants at work--show them the Horde will not allow the exploitation of Stonetalon.  Show them in the language they best understand...$B$BViolence.\030Kill 15 Venture Co. Loggers, then return to Seereth Stonebreak on the border of Stonetalon and the Barrens.\030The Greatwood Vale lies to the northwest, $N. Go. Strike fear into those who would pillage this land!\030Goblin Invaders\0312,1,125,2,257,1,4049\0302,128,189,2,257,1,4049\0302,192,224,2,257,1,4049\0302,229,298,2,257,1,4049\0302,301,420,2,257,3,4049\0302,423,471,2,257,1,4049\0302,476,484,2,257,1,4049\0303,1,19,2,384,1,4049\0303,21,107,2,384,1,4049\0301,1,17,4,272,1,4049\0301,22,113,4,274,1,4049\0301,118,196,4,272,1,4049\0304,1,45,3,256,1,4049\0304,51,101,3,256,4,4049\0314049,2,9,Seereth Stonebreak\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,9,Seereth Stonebreak\031\031NPC,3989,OBJECTIVE,15,13,Venture Co. Logger",[1063]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I bid you greetings. You are here seeking council?\030To truly tend the spirits of Stonetalon we must consult the tauren elders.$B$BI do not know many of their leaders' names, but I do know of one: Magatha.  I have heard that she is very old, and she knows much.  If anyone can marshal spiritual aid from the tauren, it is she.$B$BMagatha resides in the tauren capital of Thunder Bluff, on Elder Rise -- the city's northeastern bluff.  Speak with Magatha, and tell her of the peril of Stonetalon Mountains.\030Speak with Magatha in Thunder Bluff.\030\030The Elder Crone\0312,1,74,2,257,1,4049\0302,79,152,2,257,1,4049\0302,155,208,2,257,1,4049\0302,211,273,2,257,4,4049\0302,278,380,2,257,1,4049\0302,383,452,2,257,1,4049\0303,1,36,2,384,1,4049\0301,1,20,4,272,1,4046\0301,22,50,4,272,2,4046\031\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,7,Thunder Bluff\0311062,19,1062,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301064,23,1064,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1064]="PARTIAL\031conflict,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Magatha sent word of your coming, $N. Although my heart beats no longer, I still feel sorrow for the spirits of Stonetalon.$B$BThe Forsaken are eager to offer what help we can.\030The tauren have a bond with the land, and it pains me to hear of Stonetalon's plight.  But I fear that to heal the land, we must first remove the disease upon it.$B$BIs it not fortunate, then, that the Forsaken are allied with us?  They know much of disease.  I believe they can aid us, and by doing so they will strengthen the trust between our people.$B$BSpeak with Apothecary Zamah.  She is a scholar and an emissary of the Forsaken.  You will find her in the Pools of Vision below the Spirit Rise.\030Speak with Apothecary Zamah in the Pools of Vision in Thunder Bluff.\030\030Forsaken Aid\0312,1,85,2,257,1,4046\0302,88,162,2,257,1,4046\0302,167,230,2,257,2,4046\0302,233,258,2,257,1,4046\0302,261,353,2,257,4,4046\0302,358,385,2,257,1,4046\0302,388,436,2,257,1,4046\0302,439,501,2,257,3,4046\0303,1,68,2,384,1,4046\0301,1,37,4,272,1,3419\0301,39,123,4,304,1,3419\0301,128,176,4,272,1,3419\0313419,2,6,Apothecary Zamah\0303419,2,9,Apothecary Zamah\0312,1638,1456,0,\0302,0,0,8,Pools of Vision\0302,0,0,9,Pools of Vision\0302,0,0,9,Thunder Bluff\0311063,19,1063,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301065,23,1065,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1065]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A note from Zamah? Her needs must be great to send word from so far. Let us see what she says...$B$BAh, splendid! I know exactly what to do!\030To rid Stonetalon of the Venture Company, we must take extreme measures.  Extreme, but without bloodshed.$B$BA colleague of mine may have just the tool we need.  His name is Lydon; he dwells in the town of Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills, in the distant land of Lordaeron.$B$BTo reach Hillsbrad, travel by zeppelin to our capital, the Undercity.  Then go north to Tirisfal Glades, southwest to Silverpine, and south to Hillsbrad.$B$BSeek Lydon and bring him this note.  It details our needs to him.\030Bring Zamah's Note to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill.\030Ah, are you here with my new test subjects?\030Journey to Tarren Mill\0312,1,72,2,257,1,3419\0302,75,105,2,257,1,3419\0302,110,160,2,259,1,3419\0302,163,279,2,257,1,3419\0302,284,352,2,257,1,3419\0302,355,436,2,257,1,3419\0302,441,475,2,257,1,3419\0302,478,505,2,259,1,3419\0303,1,54,2,384,1,3419\0301,1,18,4,272,2,2216\0301,20,68,4,274,1,2216\0301,70,96,4,272,1,2216\0301,101,113,4,272,1,2216\0301,115,140,4,272,1,2216\0304,1,43,3,256,2,2216\0312216,2,9,Apothecary Lydon\0312,1638,1456,0,\0302,0,0,4,Hillsbrad Foothills\0302,0,0,6,Tirisfal Glades\0302,0,0,6,Silverpine\0302,0,0,6,Hillsbrad\0302,0,0,9,Apothecary Lydon\0302,0,0,9,Tarren Mill\0304,0,0,10,Zamah\0311064,19,1064,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301066,23,1066,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1066]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very good!  I trust the Syndicate gave you little trouble?$B$BAs I mentioned, the blood of innocents is not an easy thing to obtain.  We are lucky the Syndicate shadow mages did the difficult work for us.$B$BNow hold a moment while I create my concoction...\030I will create a toxin to bleed the violence from the Venture Company, rendering them weak and docile.  That should fix the Horde's problem in Stonetalon, yes?$B$BBut to create the toxin, I will need the blood of innocents, a difficult ingredient to obtain.$B$BFortunately the Syndicate, a group of human brigands in this area, employ shadow mages... and those mages collect innocent blood for their own, unsavory purposes.$B$BYou can find the Syndicate shadow mages in Durnholde Keep to the southeast.\030Bring 5 Vials of Innocent Blood to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill.\030Did you find the Syndicate Shadow Mages, and collect from them the blood?\030Blood of Innocents\0312,1,101,2,257,3,2216\0302,104,158,2,261,2,2216\0302,163,256,2,259,3,2216\0302,261,349,2,257,1,2216\0302,351,422,2,257,1,2216\0302,427,501,2,257,1,2216\0303,1,67,2,384,1,2216\0301,1,10,4,272,1,2216\0301,13,58,4,272,2,2216\0301,63,132,4,272,1,2216\0301,135,204,4,272,1,2216\0301,209,257,4,272,1,2216\0304,1,73,3,256,2,2216\0314244,2,4,Shadow\0304244,2,6,Shadow\0302216,2,7,Apothecary Lydon\0304244,4,11,Shadow\0304244,3,13,Shadow\0312,1638,1456,0,\0302,0,0,1,Venture Company\0302,0,0,2,Stonetalon\0302,0,0,6,Durnholde Keep\0302,0,0,7,Apothecary Lydon\0302,0,0,7,Tarren Mill\0311065,19,1065,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301067,23,1067,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5620,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[1067]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A toxin from Apothecary Lydon? Very good. If I know Lydon, then this toxin will be quite effective against the Venture Company...\030Here is the toxin.  If you use it against the Venture Company it should produce favorable, perhaps even contagious, results.  I must say, it is quite exciting to see my work applied in the field!$B$BBut before using it, take it to Apothecary Zamah.  She must create a delivery method for the toxin to maximize its effect.\030Bring Lydon's Toxin to Apothecary Zamah in Thunder Bluff.\030You have returned, $N. Do you bring aid from Apothecary Lydon?\030Return to Thunder Bluff\0312,1,18,2,257,1,2216\0302,21,124,2,257,4,2216\0302,127,195,2,257,1,2216\0302,200,248,2,257,1,2216\0302,251,321,2,257,1,2216\0303,1,57,2,384,1,2216\0301,1,30,4,272,2,3419\0301,32,41,4,272,1,3419\0301,43,129,4,272,4,3419\0304,1,22,3,256,1,3419\0304,24,62,3,256,2,3419\0313419,2,4,Apothecary Zamah\0303419,2,6,Apothecary Zamah\0302216,4,7,Apothecary Lydon\0302216,3,11,Apothecary Lydon\0312,1638,1456,0,\0302,0,0,4,Apothecary Zamah\0302,0,0,6,Apothecary Zamah\0302,0,0,6,Thunder Bluff\0304,0,0,7,Apothecary Lydon\0303,0,0,11,Apothecary Lydon\0311066,19,1066,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301086,23,1086,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1068]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The destruction of the machines XT:4 and XT:9 have soothed many of the spirits of Stonetalon, $N. With their loss, let us hope the Venture Company will remove itself from these mountains.$B$BFor if they do not, then I fear the atrocities this place has suffered will pale to what lies ahead.\030There is a relation to the spiritual magic of shaman and the natural magic of druids.  This is why we shaman can hear the plea of the spirits of Stonetalon.  Many of their whisperings are lost to me, but one message, one vision, is clear...$B$BI saw a vision of two man-shaped machines in Windshear Crag, northwest of Greatwood Vale, felling trees with impossible speed.  These metal beasts must be stopped!$B$BIn my vision, the machines were marked with strange symbols:$B$BXT:4 and XT:9.\030Kill the shredders XT:4 and XT:9, then return to Seereth Stonebreak at the border of the Stonetalon Mountains and the Barrens.\030The tree spirits wail at the loss of their brethren, $N. You must destroy the shredders XT:4 and XT:9, or I fear Stonetalon will never be healed.\030Shredding Machines\0312,1,85,2,257,1,4049\0302,88,156,2,257,1,4049\0302,159,240,2,261,1,4049\0302,245,370,2,257,1,4049\0302,373,407,2,257,1,4049\0302,412,471,2,257,1,4049\0302,476,489,2,257,1,4049\0303,1,126,2,384,1,4049\0301,1,97,4,272,1,4049\0301,99,187,4,274,3,4049\0301,192,291,4,272,4,4049\0304,1,56,3,256,1,4049\0304,58,145,3,260,3,4049\0314049,2,8,Seereth Stonebreak\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,4,Windshear Crag\0302,0,0,8,Seereth Stonebreak\0311062,19,1062,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,4073,OBJECTIVE,1,13,XT:4\030NPC,4074,OBJECTIVE,1,13,XT:9",[1069]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You got them! Thank you!$B$BI'll have these sent to Dizzywig and get them shipped to Booty Bay. I can already taste the profits!$B$BHere is your cut, $N. I couldn't have made this deal without you.\030Spider egg omelettes are a new fad in Booty Bay!  The problem is... Booty Bay's got no eggs.$B$BI smell an opportunity!$B$BIn Windshear Crag and Sishir Canyon, in the Stonetalon Mountains to the northwest, lives the deepmoss spider.  Bring me its eggs and I'll pay a bundle!$B$BIn Windshear Crag, the eggs will be clustered under what trees remain.$B$BIn Sishir Canyon... well, if you have a weak stomach then maybe you should just collect the eggs at Windshear Crag...\030Bring 15 Deepmoss Eggs to Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet.\030Did you get the eggs, $N? I already made a shipping deal with Wharfmaster Dizzywig!\030Deepmoss Spider Eggs\0312,1,48,2,257,1,3446\0302,51,67,2,261,1,3446\0302,69,92,2,257,1,3446\0302,97,119,2,257,1,3446\0302,124,232,2,257,1,3446\0302,235,274,2,257,1,3446\0302,279,348,2,257,3,3446\0302,353,371,2,257,1,3446\0302,373,469,2,257,4,3446\0303,1,52,2,384,1,3446\0301,1,13,4,272,1,3446\0301,15,24,4,272,1,3446\0301,29,95,4,272,1,3446\0301,97,128,4,272,1,3446\0301,133,153,4,272,1,3446\0301,155,197,4,272,1,3446\0304,1,25,3,256,2,3446\0304,27,83,3,256,1,3446\03114881,2,1,Spider\03014881,2,5,Spider\0303446,2,10,Mebok Mizzyrix\0303453,3,18,Wharfmaster Dizzywig\0312,17,1413,0,\0302,0,0,1,Booty Bay\0302,0,0,5,Stonetalon Mountains\0302,0,0,9,Windshear Crag\0302,0,0,10,Mebok Mizzyrix\0302,0,0,10,Ratchet\0304,0,0,13,Dizzywig\0304,0,0,13,Booty Bay\031\031ITEM,5570,OBJECTIVE,15,15,",[107]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031My heart goes out to those two poor souls, Maybell and Tommy Joe. I remember being young and in love, once.$B$BThere must be something I can do to help them! Let me think...\030I bet William Pestle has a potion to unite our two young lovers!$B$BHere, take this note to William.  He's staying at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire.\030Take Gramma Stonefield's Note to William Pestle.\030You have a note from \"Gramma\" Stonefield, eh? I haven't seen Mildred in years! I wonder what she has to say...\030Note to William\0312,1,64,2,257,1,248\0302,69,100,2,257,1,248\0302,103,152,2,257,1,248\0303,1,48,2,384,1,248\0301,1,65,4,272,1,253\0301,67,107,4,272,1,253\0301,112,157,4,272,1,253\0301,159,173,4,272,1,253\0304,1,45,3,256,2,253\0304,47,78,3,256,1,253\0304,80,110,3,256,1,253\031253,2,1,William Pestle\0302533,2,2,William\030248,2,4,Gramma Stonefield\030253,2,4,William Pestle\0312,12,1429,0,\0302,0,0,2,William\0302,0,0,3,Lion's Pride Inn\0302,0,0,3,Goldshire\0302,0,0,4,William Pestle\031111,19,111,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030112,23,112,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1070]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, you've come from Ashenvale at the behest of Thenysil -- how I miss her, my homeland and friends. She must be doing well with the Sentinels to be sequestering adventurers for other tasks. I'm proud of her.$B$BIt is a pleasure to meet you, $N.\030Hello, $N.$B$BYou seem to be full of wanderlust by the looks of you. Have you been to the Stonetalon Mountains? It is a land plagued by the Venture Co. and other enemies of the night elves.$B$BRecently, Sentinel Wolfrunner sent my friend Kaela Shadowspear there to investigate what's happening to the land, but I have yet to hear word back from her. I'm even more concerned because the Alliance sent a gnome mage along with her... a sign of trouble for sure.$B$BWould you find her and report back to me?\030Find Kaela Shadowspear overlooking the valley entering Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains.\030\030On Guard in Stonetalon\0312,1,10,2,257,1,4079\0302,15,68,2,257,4,4079\0302,70,111,2,257,2,4079\0302,113,151,2,257,1,4079\0302,153,189,2,261,1,4079\0302,194,349,2,257,1,4079\0302,351,430,2,259,1,4079\0302,432,458,2,257,1,4079\0302,463,503,2,257,4,4079\0303,1,98,2,384,1,4079\0301,1,100,4,272,1,4080\0301,102,190,4,272,1,4080\0301,192,208,4,272,1,4080\0301,213,245,4,272,1,4080\0314080,2,6,Kaela Shadowspear\0304080,2,10,Kaela Shadowspear\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,3,Stonetalon Mountains\0302,0,0,10,Stonetalon Mountains\0304,0,0,11,Ashenvale\0311085,23,1085,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301085,24,1085,UNKNOWN\031",[1071]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thanks so much for your help, $N. You're actually back just in time.$B$BI think I've got the perfect plan. Explosives. No, that's not the plan, but it's part of the plan.$B$BSee, I've been using high explosives--don't worry, they're not as dangerous as everyone thinks--to scare the goblins back a bit. I can herd 'em pretty good with a few key detonations along the mountains' edges, but I've been low on supplies now for a few days.\030You see, $N, I'm a member of the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences, and it's my goal... nay, my DUTY! to show the night elves that a blend of magic, mixtures, and mechanisms can help save their forests.$B$BBut it's a hard fought war, and the goblins reproduce like rabbits it seems. I haven't even had time to build my newest inventions!$B$BI need some time to plan and organize. But to do that, I need your help keeping the goblins at bay in Windshear Crag to the east...\030Kill 10 Venture Co. Loggers, and 10 Venture Co. Deforesters and return to Gaxim Rustfizzle in Stonetalon.\030How goes the battle on your end, $N?\030A Gnome's Respite\0312,1,122,2,259,1,4077\0302,124,136,2,257,1,4077\0302,138,237,2,265,1,4077\0302,242,317,2,261,4,4077\0302,319,372,2,257,1,4077\0302,377,414,2,259,1,4077\0302,416,507,2,259,1,4077\0303,1,19,2,384,1,4077\0303,21,47,2,384,1,4077\0303,49,105,2,384,1,4077\0301,1,33,4,272,1,4077\0301,35,68,4,272,1,4077\0301,73,106,4,272,1,4077\0301,108,118,4,272,1,4077\0301,120,170,4,272,1,4077\0301,175,302,4,272,1,4077\0301,304,434,4,272,1,4077\0304,1,36,3,260,2,4077\0314077,2,10,Gaxim Rustfizzle\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,7,Windshear Crag\0302,0,0,10,Gaxim Rustfizzle\0302,0,0,10,Stonetalon\0311085,19,1085,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,3989,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Venture Co. Logger\030NPC,3991,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Venture Co. Deforester",[1072]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ahhh. Gaxim sent you, huh? How do I know you're not lying to me?! Hmm? Hmm?\030The device I'm thinking about is my most advanced version to date. But we'll need a special potion if it's to work. I'm thinking we might as well get the good stuff since this mission could be your last.$B$BAnd for that, we're going to need some potent explosives: Nitromirglyceronium.$B$BThe only person who can make NG-5 is an old friend of mine: Lomac Gearstrip. Look for him in Tinker Town.$B$BYou talk him into making us some NG-5, I'll get to work on placement for my devices.\030Speak to Lomac Gearstrip in Ironforge.\030\030An Old Colleague\0312,1,66,2,257,1,4077\0302,68,115,2,259,4,4077\0302,117,203,2,257,4,4077\0302,208,285,2,259,3,4077\0302,290,365,2,257,1,4077\0302,367,394,2,257,1,4077\0302,399,482,2,257,1,4077\0303,1,38,2,384,1,4077\0301,1,5,4,272,1,4081\0301,7,26,4,272,2,4081\0301,28,65,4,272,2,4081\0301,67,70,4,272,2,4081\0301,72,75,4,272,2,4081\0314081,2,5,Lomac Gearstrip\0304081,2,8,Lomac Gearstrip\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,6,Tinker Town\0302,0,0,8,Lomac Gearstrip\0302,0,0,8,Ironforge\0311071,19,1071,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301073,23,1073,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1073]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This'll do nicely.$B$BIf I didn't know better, stranger, I'd say you knew somethin' about alchemy. Good, good... the world's not all about swords and sorcery, you know?\030Hahaha... you need Nitromirglyceronium to stop goblins from destroying a forest?!$B$BI don't care if you know Gaxim or not... I'll give you the stuff just to see you or them explode into itty bitty pieces.$B$BThere's a problem though: I'm all out.$B$BBut I'll tell you what, you bring me the correct potions, and I'll make some up for you right away.$B$BThe least you can do is prove you've got some skill as an alchemist before I just give you a sample of my greatest creation.\030Bring 4 Minor Mana Potions and 2 Elixirs of Minor Fortitude to Lomac Gearstrip in Ironforge.\030I can't make any Nitromirglyceronium if I don't have the potions... they're vital to its creation.\030Ineptitude + Chemicals = Fun\0312,1,9,2,257,1,4081\0302,11,81,2,263,2,4081\0302,86,125,2,257,4,4081\0302,127,205,2,257,1,4081\0302,210,247,2,261,1,4081\0302,252,350,2,257,1,4081\0302,355,478,2,257,1,4081\0303,1,92,2,384,1,4081\0301,1,18,4,272,1,4081\0301,23,98,4,272,4,4081\0301,100,112,4,272,1,4081\0301,114,168,4,272,2,4081\0304,1,67,3,256,4,4081\0304,69,98,3,256,1,4081\0314081,2,8,Lomac Gearstrip\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,8,Lomac Gearstrip\0302,0,0,8,Ironforge\0311072,19,1072,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301074,23,1074,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,2455,OBJECTIVE,4,15,\030ITEM,2458,OBJECTIVE,2,15,",[1074]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Your task has been done flawlessly, $N.$B$BNG-5 is the unequivocal component in the recipe to ignite the wagons of dynamite.$B$BWhat? Yes, dynamite... wagons of it. It's the perfect distraction, I tell you... just wait and see.\030Here you go, stranger. Take heed with it though... it's volatile stuff.$B$BIf you're really a friend of Gaxim's, then tell him I say hello. If you're not, then have fun blowin' yerself up.\030Bring the Nitromirglyceronium back to Gaxim Rustfizzle in Stonetalon.\030Ah, goodie goodie, you're back.\030Ineptitude + Chemicals = Fun\0312,1,22,2,257,1,4081\0302,24,50,2,257,1,4081\0302,52,71,2,257,1,4081\0302,76,139,2,257,4,4081\0302,141,188,2,257,4,4081\0303,1,69,2,384,1,4081\0301,1,39,4,272,1,4077\0301,44,124,4,272,1,4077\0301,129,133,4,272,2,4077\0301,135,150,4,272,1,4077\0301,152,164,4,272,1,4077\0301,166,208,4,272,1,4077\0301,210,227,4,272,1,4077\0304,1,31,3,256,1,4077\0314077,2,6,Gaxim Rustfizzle\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,6,Gaxim Rustfizzle\0302,0,0,6,Stonetalon\0311073,19,1073,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301079,23,1079,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1075]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Now, this spell you need; one that will allow you detonate explosives from a distance... hmmm.\030Okay, now for the remote detonation part of my plan... oh, I haven't explained that yet, have I?$B$BOkay, so the short of it is this: with a little magic, I can make it so the explosives go off while you're not around. I'm putting together a device that'll allow you to push just one button and have the NG-5 explode when you're ready.$B$BBut I need a spell from a friend in Stormwind--Collin Mauren is his name. You can find him in the mage quarter there. He's human, so he shouldn't be hard to miss.\030Find Collin Mauren in Stormwind.\030\030A Scroll from Mauren\0312,1,54,2,257,1,4077\0302,56,96,2,257,2,4077\0302,101,218,2,257,1,4077\0302,220,335,2,257,1,4077\0302,340,412,2,259,1,4077\0302,414,456,2,257,1,4077\0302,458,501,2,257,1,4077\0303,1,32,2,384,1,4077\0301,1,88,4,274,3,4078\0301,90,94,4,272,1,4078\0314078,2,8,Collin Mauren\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,5,Stormwind--Collin Mauren\0302,0,0,8,Stormwind\0311071,19,1071,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301076,23,1076,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1076]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Allow me just a few moments and I shall have your scroll ready for you.\030Ah, I think I have it. A messaging spell... I believe that's the effect he's looking for.$B$BI'll have to create a scroll with the spell impressed upon it. To do that I'll need debris from a dust devil.$B$BWhile I gather the rest of the components, why don't you head to Westfall and find one of the foul creatures? They are dangerous, but I'm sure it's nothing you can't handle if you're willing to subject yourself to one of Gaxim's experiments.$B$BI'll be here when you return.\030Bring Dust Devil Debris to Collin Mauren in Stormwind.\030Hello, $N. Have you found the component I need?\030Devils in Westfall\0312,1,22,2,257,1,4078\0302,24,43,2,257,1,4078\0302,45,89,2,257,4,4078\0302,94,155,2,257,1,4078\0302,157,202,2,259,1,4078\0302,207,315,2,257,2,4078\0302,317,447,2,257,4,4078\0302,452,480,2,257,1,4078\0303,1,54,2,384,1,4078\0301,1,71,4,272,3,4078\0304,1,10,3,256,1,4078\0304,12,47,3,258,2,4078\031832,2,5,Dust Devil\030832,2,9,Dust Devil\0304078,2,9,Collin Mauren\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,6,Westfall\0302,0,0,9,Collin Mauren\0302,0,0,9,Stormwind\0311075,19,1075,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301077,23,1077,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5669,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1077]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is perfect, $N! Well done.$B$BThis spell, mixed with the NG-5, shall make the perfect remote explosive.$B$BWe'll be able to create the perfect distraction for you so you can sneak in and steal the Venture Co.'s letters and engineering plans.$B$BThat will surely slow down their deforestation acts.\030Here you are, $N. This should do nicely.$B$BPlease give my regards to Gaxim when next you see him. I look forward to hearing about this adventure when it sees its completion.$B$BFare well.\030Bring the Scroll of Messaging to Gaxim Rustfizzle in Stonetalon.\030Haha! you're back! Do you have it? Do you have the spell?\030Special Delivery for Gaxim\0312,1,17,2,257,1,4078\0302,19,40,2,257,1,4078\0302,45,98,2,257,1,4078\0302,100,174,2,257,1,4078\0302,179,188,2,257,1,4078\0303,1,64,2,384,1,4078\0301,1,20,4,272,1,4077\0301,22,31,4,272,1,4077\0301,36,108,4,272,3,4077\0301,113,246,4,276,1,4077\0301,251,302,4,272,3,4077\0304,1,5,3,256,1,4077\0304,7,18,3,256,1,4077\0304,20,34,3,256,2,4077\0304,36,57,3,256,2,4077\0314077,2,6,Gaxim Rustfizzle\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,3,Gaxim\0302,0,0,6,Gaxim Rustfizzle\0302,0,0,6,Stonetalon\0311076,19,1076,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301080,23,1080,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1078]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is perfect, $N. Thank you greatly.$B$BPerhaps one day in the future I'll be able to help you as you have helped me.\030Travelers keep asking me about the Stonetalon Mountains. It seems to be a popular place for adventure--it doesn't matter if you're seeking wyvern, elementals, or you have business with the Venture Co.$B$BWithin the Charred Vale, deep in Stonetalon, there used to be a species of basilisks whose scales, when ground to dust, made a wonderful reagent for some spells I've created.$B$BIf those basilisks still live, I would love to have a few of their scales.$B$BTake your time, it is no rush, but I can pay well.\030Bring 8 Crystalized Scales to Collin Mauren in Stormwind.\030Hello again, $N.$B$BHave you already returned from the Vale in Stonetalon with those scales?\030Retrieval for Mauren\0312,1,56,2,257,1,4078\0302,58,200,2,257,4,4078\0302,205,378,2,321,1,4078\0302,383,456,2,257,4,4078\0302,461,510,2,257,1,4078\0303,1,57,2,384,1,4078\0301,1,20,4,272,1,4078\0301,22,39,4,272,1,4078\0301,44,120,4,272,4,4078\0304,1,16,3,256,1,4078\0304,21,92,3,256,2,4078\0314078,2,6,Collin Mauren\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,3,Stonetalon\0302,0,0,6,Collin Mauren\0302,0,0,6,Stormwind\0303,0,0,11,Vale\0303,0,0,11,Stonetalon\031\031ITEM,5675,OBJECTIVE,8,15,",[1079]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Truly amazing! This is a huge blow to the Venture Co.$B$BWe'll be able to find weaknesses in their machines and also incorporate their designs into our own creations. This is a wonderful day, indeed.\030This is it, $N. Pay close attention. The devices are done, and ready to be used.$B$BTake these pages--they'll explain more about the detonators and explosives, and where you should place them.$B$BRemember, the success of your mission doesn't depend on how much destruction you cause. Plan Alpha's success depends on you bringing back the Venture Co.'s engineering plans from inside the lumber mill south of Cragpool Lake.\030Retrieve the Venture Co.'s Engineering Plans from the lumber mill in Windshear Crag.\030Did you get the plans, $N?\030Covert Ops - Alpha\0312,1,15,2,257,1,4077\0302,17,36,2,257,1,4077\0302,38,80,2,257,1,4077\0302,85,192,2,257,1,4077\0302,197,283,2,257,1,4077\0302,285,421,2,257,1,4077\0303,1,84,2,384,1,4077\0301,1,14,4,272,1,4077\0301,16,53,4,272,1,4077\0301,58,166,4,272,1,4077\0301,168,199,4,272,1,4077\0304,1,26,3,256,2,4077\031\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,6,Cragpool Lake\0302,0,0,7,Windshear Crag\0304,0,0,9,Venture Co\0311074,19,1074,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5718,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1080]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Incredible, $N! Kaela and the Sentinels will be so happy. With your skill and my creations, we're unstoppable.\030Plan Beta's just like Plan Alpha, $N.$B$BWe cause a distraction and then steal their precious letters.$B$BThe key is to get their letters... remember that.$B$BThe pages I gave you already will tell you where to plant the explosives. Just get back here alive and with those letters....\030Retrieve the Venture Co. Letters from Windshear Mine at the east end of Windshear Crag.\030How'd it go, $N?\030Covert Ops - Beta\0312,1,37,2,257,1,4077\0302,42,102,2,261,1,4077\0302,107,140,2,257,1,4077\0302,142,155,2,257,1,4077\0302,160,232,2,257,3,4077\0302,234,284,2,257,1,4077\0303,1,24,2,384,1,4077\0303,26,87,2,384,1,4077\0301,1,15,4,272,1,4077\0301,17,57,4,272,3,4077\0301,59,110,4,272,1,4077\0304,1,16,3,256,2,4077\03114528,2,2,Precious\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,8,Windshear Mine\0311077,19,1077,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5717,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1081]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hello, $N. I have indeed heard your name before, and although you are still full of youth, I am pleased to see the path you have set for yourself.$B$BYou would do me a great honor if you would accept this as a gift of appreciation.\030$N, I am sure Tyrande Whisperwind herself would like to thank you for taking part in this mission.$B$BIt may not appear so on the surface, but what you've helped start could very well strengthen our foothold in the Stonetalon Mountains.$B$BIf you consider yourself our ally against these atrocities, go see Tyrande in the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.\030Find Tyrande Whisperwind in Darnassus.\030\030Reception from Tyrande\0312,1,98,2,257,4,4079\0302,103,236,2,257,4,4079\0302,241,354,2,257,4,4079\0303,1,38,2,384,1,4079\0301,1,10,4,272,1,7999\0301,12,146,4,272,1,7999\0301,151,231,4,272,4,7999\0317999,2,1,Tyrande Whisperwind\03015633,2,3,Tyrande\0307999,2,4,Tyrande Whisperwind\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,2,Stonetalon Mountains\0302,0,0,3,Temple of the Moon\0302,0,0,3,Darnassus\0302,0,0,4,Darnassus\0311082,19,1082,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1082]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, $N. You have done a service to the Sentinels.$B$BI'm glad to see Kaela... and even Gaxim, are doing well.$B$BYou've earned our appreciation.\030$N, you have done a great deed by lending a hand here.$B$BThe Sentinels of Ashenvale will reward you well if you informed them that Gaxim and I are alive. Tell them we are well on our way to stopping the Venture Co. and healing the lands.$B$BFind Tara Thenysil in Astranaar; she will be pleased to see you've returned with good news.\030Return to Sentinel Thenysil in Ashenvale.\030\030Update for Sentinel Thenysil\0312,1,54,2,257,1,4080\0302,59,154,2,257,4,4080\0302,156,215,2,257,1,4080\0302,217,238,2,257,1,4080\0302,243,333,2,257,3,4080\0303,1,41,2,384,1,4080\0301,1,14,4,272,1,4079\0301,16,56,4,272,1,4079\0301,61,84,4,272,1,4079\0301,86,116,4,272,1,4079\0301,121,151,4,272,1,4079\0314079,2,6,Sentinel Thenysil\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,5,Astranaar\0302,0,0,6,Sentinel Thenysil\0302,0,0,6,Ashenvale\0304,0,0,8,Sentinels\0311083,21,1083,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301084,21,1084,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301081,23,1081,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1083]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The remains of our enemy... your strength serves us well, $N. Thank you.\030I'm unsure what the Venture Co. did to the Vale, but it's obvious they were overpowered by the creatures there.$B$BThey set the forest aflame, and used their inventions of destruction to decimate as much of the Vale as possible.$B$BBut in their ignorance they also released something else: burning spirits, elementals of flame, stone and rage.$B$BThe land has no chance to see Elune's smile while these creatures roam free.$B$BBring me their smoldering embers to show you've reduced their numbers.\030Bring 8 Smoldering Embers from any of the fire elementals in the Charred Vale to Kaela Shadowspear in Stonetalon.\030The first time I saw the Charred Vale I almost wept, $N.\030Enraged Spirits\0312,1,31,2,257,1,4080\0302,33,111,2,257,1,4080\0302,116,228,2,257,1,4080\0302,233,343,2,257,1,4080\0302,348,423,2,257,1,4080\0302,428,497,2,257,1,4080\0303,1,113,2,384,1,4080\0301,1,27,4,276,1,4080\0301,29,61,4,272,1,4080\0301,63,72,4,272,1,4080\0304,1,56,3,256,1,4080\0314080,2,7,Kaela Shadowspear\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,2,Vale\0302,0,0,7,Charred Vale\0302,0,0,7,Kaela Shadowspear\0302,0,0,7,Stonetalon\0311091,19,1091,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5659,OBJECTIVE,8,15,",[1084]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, $N.$B$BThis should be more than sufficient for Gaxim to figure out how the treants were corrupted. I shall give this to him right away.\030It seems obvious to me that the protectors of the Vale--the treants--had something to do with the Venture Co. being driven back. Unfortunately, even those once great guardians have now become corrupt.$B$BGaxim thinks their corruption is somehow linked to the weapons the goblins used during their retreat.$B$BI told him I'd collect a sample from a wounded treant and allow him to study it in order to figure out if that's true.$B$BBring me some of the shrapnel so the gnome can tell me more...\030Bring a piece of Corroded Shrapnel to Kaela Shadowspear in Stonetalon.\030I have a feeling Gaxim will find a use for the shrapnel regardless of how the Venture Co. has used it in the past.\030Wounded Ancients\0312,1,109,2,257,4,4080\0302,111,128,2,257,1,4080\0302,130,200,2,261,1,4080\0302,205,305,2,261,1,4080\0302,310,427,2,259,4,4080\0302,432,493,2,257,1,4080\0303,1,70,2,384,1,4080\0301,1,14,4,272,1,4080\0301,19,109,4,276,1,4080\0301,111,146,4,272,3,4080\0304,1,89,3,256,3,4080\0304,91,114,3,256,1,4080\0311964,2,5,Treant\0304080,2,7,Kaela Shadowspear\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,7,Kaela Shadowspear\0302,0,0,7,Stonetalon\0311091,19,1091,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5664,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1085]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Treacherous...treacherous and dangerous, that's what this land is.$B$BBut I'm here to show the night elves that it's a little safer with the help of good ole engineering and a dash of magic.$B$BSee, swearing off magic completely won't help the night elves -- they need it. The world needs it. And with engineering and alchemy to boot, you can't go wrong. The possibilities are endless.\030The situation here in Stonetalon is obviously grave for a night elf and gnome to be working together.$B$BThe Venture Co. has devastated these lands and I've spent most of my time putting an end to the destruction.$B$BDo not judge Gaxim prematurely; he understands the need for us to work together.$B$BIf you wish to aid us, then start by speaking to Gaxim.$B$BI'm sorry I cannot send you back to Tara with good news yet. Perhaps soon.\030Speak to Gaxim.\030\030On Guard in Stonetalon\0312,1,101,2,257,1,4080\0302,106,120,2,257,1,4080\0302,122,213,2,257,1,4080\0302,218,297,2,259,1,4080\0302,302,356,2,259,4,4080\0302,361,420,2,257,1,4080\0302,422,434,2,257,4,4080\0303,1,15,2,384,1,4080\0301,1,66,4,272,1,4077\0301,71,190,4,272,1,4077\0301,195,272,4,274,1,4077\0301,274,292,4,274,1,4077\0301,294,354,4,272,1,4077\0301,356,385,4,272,1,4077\031\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,1,Stonetalon\0302,0,0,5,Gaxim\0302,0,0,6,Tara\0302,0,0,8,Gaxim\0311071,23,1071,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1086]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031You found the port? Well done, $N! I am sure the goblins were quite surprised from your delivery! Let us hope that toxin finds its way to their headquarters.$B$BYou have served your people well, and I advise you to ignore any guilt you might harbor for poisoning the Venture Company. They are deserving of far worse.$B$BAnd if there is one mote of wisdom the Forsaken might teach its allies, it is this:$B$BDo not shy from dark paths... if those paths lead to victory.\030The toxin is ready.  All that remains is its delivery.  You, $N, must make that delivery.$B$BThe Venture Company must have a means of sending messages and light cargo between its headquarters and its operations in Stonetalon.  It is likely a small sky port -- not big enough for a zeppelin, but perhaps for a flying machine.  You must search the areas in Stonetalon under control of the Venture Company and find this sky port, if it exists.  If you find it, then place the toxin there.$B$BPlace it, and run.\030Bring the Toxic Fogger to the Venture Co. sky port, then return to Apothecary Zamah.\030Place the Toxic Fogger\030You must find the Venture Company airport if it exists, $N.\030The Flying Machine Airport\0312,1,19,2,257,1,3419\0302,22,54,2,257,1,3419\0302,57,89,2,257,1,3419\0302,94,225,2,257,1,3419\0302,228,324,2,257,4,3419\0302,327,440,2,257,4,3419\0302,443,485,2,257,4,3419\0302,490,507,2,257,1,3419\0303,1,41,2,384,1,3419\0303,43,84,2,384,1,3419\0301,1,19,4,272,2,3419\0301,21,34,4,272,1,3419\0301,36,97,4,272,1,3419\0301,99,157,4,274,3,3419\0301,162,283,4,272,4,3419\0301,285,316,4,272,1,3419\0301,321,403,4,272,4,3419\0301,408,436,4,272,1,3419\0301,438,468,4,272,4,3419\0305,1,59,3,256,4,3419\0304,1,22,3,384,1,3419\0313419,2,10,Apothecary Zamah\0312,1638,1456,0,\0302,0,0,4,Stonetalon\0302,0,0,6,Stonetalon\0302,0,0,9,Venture Co\0302,0,0,10,Apothecary Zamah\0311067,19,1067,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1087]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Already I can feel it... yes... power so sweet... the rushing flood. The kaldorei are foolish to spurn the gifts of this world, to reject the coursing of magic as it flows singing through your veins.$B$BWhat a pale mockery life is without its burning embrace!\030You cannot imagine the hatred I possess for this wretched land. The ilk of Cenarius and the kaldorei druids at the peak employ their pathetic powers to stifle the flow of magic, even so far south of their pathetic holdings... their beloved forests.$B$BWould that I could return to Jaedenar and exult in the flow of magic, but my master will not allow me to return until my work is done.$B$BI have no doubt you love the night elves and their allies as little as I. Aid me, and both our ends might be satisfied.\030Kill 4 Sons of Cenarius, 4 Daughters of Cenarius and 4 Cenarion Botanists for Braelyn Firehand near Sun Rock Retreat.\030Here, channeling magic is like drawing water from a well with a bucket full of holes.\030Cenarius' Legacy\0312,1,63,2,257,1,4198\0302,65,225,2,257,1,4198\0302,227,248,2,257,1,4198\0302,253,386,2,257,4,4198\0302,391,463,2,257,1,4198\0302,465,509,2,257,4,4198\0303,1,117,2,384,1,4198\0301,1,24,4,272,1,4198\0301,26,31,4,272,1,4198\0301,33,49,4,272,1,4198\0301,51,68,4,272,1,4198\0301,70,199,4,272,1,4198\0301,204,259,4,272,1,4198\0304,1,85,3,256,1,4198\0314198,2,7,Braelyn Firehand\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,4,Jaedenar\0302,0,0,7,Sun Rock Retreat\0311088,23,1088,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,4057,OBJECTIVE,4,13,Son of Cenarius\030NPC,4053,OBJECTIVE,4,13,Daughter of Cenarius\030NPC,4051,OBJECTIVE,4,13,Cenarion Botanist",[1088]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I knew Ordanus once, long ago. He had the arrogance of his kind, holding himself above even the Highborne.$B$BHis head does not rise so high now, does it, $N?$B$BI promised you a reward, and you shall have it. Attend to me.\030They thought that they could halt the flow of magic. They were mistaken. They thought that they could hide Ordanus, but I will have his head!$B$BMagic grants me true sight. Yes... there he is. A crossroads... At the top of a great tree in Ashenvale Forest. A name... Raynewood. One of the eldest sons of the forest god. They spirited him away from the peak before I could find him, but his time runs short.$B$BBring it to me and I will share with you a mighty gift.\030Bring Ordanus' head to Braelyn Firehand near Sun Rock Retreat.\030When my master bade me to the peak of Stonetalon, I expected that all I would need was to lay waste to the night elves that crawled the sacred ruins of our ancient temple of Azshara, their touch despoiling its sanctity... but Ordanus had slipped my grasp.\030Ordanus\0312,1,52,2,257,4,4198\0302,54,72,2,257,1,4198\0302,74,141,2,257,4,4198\0302,146,172,2,257,1,4198\0302,174,179,2,257,1,4198\0302,181,192,2,257,1,4198\0302,194,208,2,257,1,4198\0302,210,256,2,257,1,4198\0302,258,266,2,257,1,4198\0302,268,277,2,257,1,4198\0302,279,319,2,257,1,4198\0302,321,406,2,257,4,4198\0302,411,465,2,257,3,4198\0303,1,62,2,384,1,4198\0301,1,30,4,336,1,4198\0301,32,106,4,336,1,4198\0301,111,158,4,272,2,4198\0301,163,209,4,272,3,4198\0301,211,223,4,272,1,4198\0304,1,221,3,322,4,4198\0304,223,255,3,256,1,4198\0314198,2,14,Braelyn Firehand\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,8,Ashenvale Forest\0302,0,0,14,Braelyn Firehand\0302,0,0,14,Sun Rock Retreat\0311087,19,1087,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301089,23,1089,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5686,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1089]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031As the three keys are slid into their matching openings, in the middle of the glowing light a number of items appear.\030The druids built the Talon Den on Stonetalon Peak, where they keep many powerful items.$B$BThey devised a complex scheme to keep them from falling into the wrong hands.$B$BLuckily, I managed to... extract some details from one of them.$B$BHidden in a small lantern at the entrance of the Den, you will find the Gatekeeper's Key--with it you will be able to open caches around the Den. The items from these caches will allow you to open their hoard, located in one of the central areas.\030Travel to the Den on Stonetalon Peak. Using the Gatekeeper's Key, obtain the druids' hidden items. Use these items to open the Talon Den Hoard.\030Three keyholes are carved into the stone.\030The Den\0312,1,87,2,257,1,4198\0302,92,168,2,257,1,4198\0302,173,196,2,257,1,4198\0302,198,235,2,257,1,4198\0302,240,384,2,257,3,4198\0302,386,485,2,257,3,4198\0303,1,37,2,384,1,4198\0303,39,98,2,384,1,4198\0303,100,143,2,384,1,4198\0301,1,117,4,272,1,0\0304,1,41,3,256,1,0\031\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,7,Den\0311088,19,1088,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,19599,FINISHER,?,12,Talon Den Hoard\030ITEM,5689,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,5690,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,5691,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[109]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, so my friend sent you here? How kind. $B$BWell the Stormwind Monarchy has abandoned our cause. Now it is up to the People's Militia to keep the land free from corruption. If our cause interests you, I can put your combat skills to use in the name of freedom.\030Looks to me you've seen quite a bit of combat in your time, $c.  If you haven't already, you should report to Gryan Stoutmantle.  He heads up the People's Militia, aimed at protecting the farmlands of Westfall.  I bet he could use your help.  You can usually find him in the stone tower on Sentinel Hill, just off the road in the middle of Westfall.\030Talk to Gryan Stoutmantle.  He usually can be found in the stone tower on Sentinel Hill, just off the road, in the middle of Westfall.\030\030Report to Gryan Stoutmantle\0312,1,63,2,257,1,0\0302,66,128,2,257,4,0\0302,131,210,2,257,1,0\0302,213,241,2,257,4,0\0302,244,349,2,257,1,0\0303,1,26,2,384,1,0\0303,29,134,2,384,1,0\0301,1,31,4,272,2,234\0301,33,41,4,272,1,234\0301,47,98,4,272,1,234\0301,100,174,4,276,1,234\0301,176,262,4,280,4,234\031234,2,2,Gryan Stoutmantle\030234,2,6,Gryan Stoutmantle\0312,12,1429,0,\0302,0,0,2,Gryan Stoutmantle\0302,0,0,6,Gryan Stoutmantle\0304,0,0,11,People's Militia\031\031",[1090]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Thanks, $N. It was looking a little dicey there for a second and we've probably drawn far too much attention to ourselves.$B$BThe important part is that we have the ore sample, though, and we should get it to Ziz as soon as possible.\030You know, I was once the second most important person here at this site. That all changed when Gerenzo took over. Fired my boss, Ziz Fizziks, and sent me down to work in the mines. Ziz told me to stay here and gather information, though. His new boss will pay us well if we can find out what Gerenzo's plans are.$B$BAnyways, what I do know is that Gerenzo has ordered large amounts of this gold-green ore to be mined. I can get you a sample to bring to Ziz, but you'll have to watch for patrols while I get it.\030Get the mysterious ore from Piznik after he finishes mining it.\030Keep Piznik safe while he mines the mysterious ore\030\030Gerenzo's Orders\0312,1,72,2,257,1,4276\0302,74,113,2,257,1,4276\0302,115,180,2,257,1,4276\0302,182,237,2,257,1,4276\0302,239,312,2,257,4,4276\0302,317,417,2,257,1,4276\0302,419,510,2,257,1,4276\0303,1,63,2,384,1,4276\0301,1,11,4,272,1,4276\0301,13,122,4,272,1,4276\0301,127,233,4,272,1,4276\0304,1,50,3,384,1,4276\0314201,2,3,Ziz Fizziks\0304276,2,8,Piznik\0304276,3,12,Piznik\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,7,Ziz\0302,0,0,8,Piznik\0304,0,0,11,Ziz\0311092,23,1092,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1091]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is interesting indeed.$B$BYou and Gaxim have done very well, $N. Thank you.\030$N, take these letters to Kaela. I'm sure she'll want to know about this. Or at least the Sentinels will.$B$BMake sure you tell her how successful we were and how we couldn't have done it without a little bit of magic.\030Bring the Venture Co. Letters to Kaela Shadowspear.\030Yes, $N? What can I do for you?\030Kaela's Update\0312,1,32,2,257,1,4077\0302,34,73,2,259,1,4077\0302,75,105,2,257,3,4077\0302,110,218,2,257,1,4077\0303,1,21,2,384,1,4077\0303,23,51,2,384,1,4077\0301,1,27,4,272,1,4080\0301,32,69,4,272,1,4080\0301,71,80,4,272,1,4080\0304,1,8,3,256,2,4080\0304,10,31,3,256,2,4080\0314080,2,6,Kaela Shadowspear\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,1,Kaela\0302,0,0,6,Kaela Shadowspear\0311079,21,1079,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301080,21,1080,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1092]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ahhh, I knew that I did the right thing by telling Piznik to stay behind. I'm sure the engineers in Undermine will be most interested to look at this...$B$BOf course I'll want to keep a little piece for myself, but what they don't know won't hurt them, yes?\030I guess I'd better think about getting out of here, also. It won't take long for word of what happened here to spread to the higher ups, and I'm sure they wouldn't take too kindly to meeting me again.$B$BI'll sneak out and meet with Ziz. Hopefully, he'll be able to find me a new job!$B$BI'll try and clean up this mess a little, but you should take the ore sample to Ziz right away. He told me that he'd set up camp somewhere on the western side of Windshear Crag. Good luck.\030Deliver the Unidentified Ore to Ziz Fizziks in the Stonetalon Mountains.\030Something I can help you with?\030Gerenzo's Orders\0312,1,57,2,257,1,4276\0302,59,200,2,257,1,4276\0302,205,237,2,257,1,4276\0302,239,284,2,257,3,4276\0302,289,383,2,257,1,4276\0302,385,465,2,257,1,4276\0302,467,476,2,257,1,4276\0303,1,72,2,384,1,4276\0301,1,73,4,272,1,4201\0301,75,152,4,272,3,4201\0301,157,257,4,274,2,4201\0304,1,30,3,256,2,4201\0314201,2,8,Ziz Fizziks\0304276,4,9,Piznik\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,5,Ziz\0302,0,0,8,Ziz Fizziks\0302,0,0,8,Stonetalon Mountains\0304,0,0,10,Undermine\0311090,19,1090,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1093]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hey, is that what I think it is? Great!$B$BNow, let's see. Ugh... how am I supposed to understand this stuff... can't figure out the way gnomes think. Lemme tell you, I'm surprised they could build the wheel, let alone those flying machines they like so much.\030Terrible what the Venture Company has done here, eh? What were they thinking? Goblin company hiring a gnome!$B$BLucky for me, Sputtervalve knows a genius when he sees one. Hired me just after I'd been kicked out!$B$BTells me they built some enormous woodcutting machine, and Sput' wants me to steal the plans for him. Unfortunately, Gerenzo--bloody gnome--wants me dead on sight... maybe you could steal the plans for me? You should be able to find them on one of their operators.\030Get the Super Reaper 6000 Blueprints for Ziz Fizziks in the Stonetalon Mountains.\030Did you find those plans? I'm eager to impress the new boss. Hopefully, once he's convinced of my loyalty--well, as much as he can be convinced... goblin's honor, you know?--he'll feel comfortable making use of my rather impressive genius.\030Super Reaper 6000\0312,1,52,2,257,2,4201\0302,54,77,2,257,2,4201\0302,79,108,2,257,1,4201\0302,113,171,2,257,1,4201\0302,173,212,2,257,1,4201\0302,217,317,2,261,1,4201\0302,319,381,2,257,1,4201\0302,383,421,2,261,4,4201\0302,423,480,2,257,1,4201\0303,1,81,2,384,1,4201\0301,1,32,4,272,2,4201\0301,34,39,4,272,1,4201\0301,44,58,4,272,1,4201\0301,60,65,4,272,1,4201\0301,67,111,4,272,1,4201\0301,113,150,4,272,1,4201\0301,152,259,4,272,4,4201\0304,1,25,3,256,2,4201\0304,27,60,3,256,1,4201\0304,62,146,3,256,3,4201\0304,148,239,3,256,2,4201\0313442,2,4,Sputtervalve\0304201,2,10,Ziz Fizziks\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,10,Stonetalon Mountains\0311094,23,1094,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5734,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1094]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Fizziks, eh? Can't say I trust him, but this information seems good enough. What I wouldn't give to have the Venture Company out of my hair.$B$BThey do come up with some good machines though... I can't deny that we've benefited from using some of the improvements they've devised.\030This envelope has all the information I was able to snatch as they booted me out the door... Venture Company internal documents, some manuals, technical things... Oh, and of course the Super Reaper 6000 blueprints.$B$BSputtervalve has taken up residence at Ratchet in the Barrens. Shouldn't have much trouble finding him, he's a little green fellow.\030Deliver the Sealed Envelope to Sputtervalve in the Barrens.\030Hello there! How can I help you?\030Further Instructions\0312,1,92,2,257,1,4201\0302,94,162,2,257,1,4201\0302,164,214,2,257,1,4201\0302,219,280,2,257,1,4201\0302,282,349,2,257,1,4201\0303,1,59,2,384,1,4201\0301,1,12,4,272,2,3442\0301,14,75,4,272,4,3442\0301,77,140,4,272,1,3442\0301,145,193,4,272,1,3442\0301,195,280,4,272,1,3442\0304,1,12,3,256,1,3442\0304,14,32,3,256,2,3442\0313442,2,4,Sputtervalve\0303442,2,6,Sputtervalve\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,4,Ratchet\0302,0,0,4,Barrens\0302,0,0,6,Sputtervalve\0302,0,0,6,Barrens\0311093,19,1093,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301095,23,1095,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1095]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Eliminate Gerenzo? Now there is a prospect that I have no objections to.$B$BGnomes are bad enough as it is, but what I learned about Gerenzo only makes it worse. Apparently, he was one of the head engineers in Gnomeregan, where he was working on their secret project--we could never infiltrate Dun Morogh well enough to find out specific details. It was a failure. Our reports say that whatever it was literally exploded in their faces.\030The matter of this gnome that has been hired by the Venture Company has caused a bit of a stir in Undermine. The trade princes do not approve of Razdunk's consorting with this Gerenzo.$B$BRiddlevox has asked me to take care of the problem, and I'm sure he was instructed to do so by one or more of the trade princes. Of course, the Director didn't tell me that. Let's just say I have a hunch.$B$BWhatever the case, Gerenzo must be removed, and it would be a fitting test to have Fizziks take care of him.\030Bring the new orders to Ziz Fizziks in the Stonetalon Mountains.\030\030Further Instructions\0312,1,108,2,257,1,3442\0302,110,184,2,257,1,3442\0302,189,316,2,261,1,3442\0302,318,361,2,257,1,3442\0302,363,392,2,257,1,3442\0302,397,504,2,257,4,3442\0303,1,64,2,384,1,3442\0301,1,18,4,272,2,4201\0301,20,72,4,272,1,4201\0301,77,161,4,272,1,4201\0301,163,346,4,272,4,4201\0301,348,364,4,272,1,4201\0301,366,436,4,272,1,4201\0314201,2,7,Ziz Fizziks\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,1,Undermine\0302,0,0,7,Ziz Fizziks\0302,0,0,7,Stonetalon Mountains\0304,0,0,11,Gnomeregan\0311094,19,1094,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301096,23,1096,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1096]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Look at that thing... it'd take a gnome to come up with something like that. I can't understand why you'd cut off an arm, and replace it with that, when you could just keep both arms and add a third!$B$BGnomes, I tell you...$B$BAt least Gerenzo's out of commission. Hopefully that'll be enough proof, and Sputtervalve will assign me to one of the Tinkers' Union workshops in Gadgetzan or maybe even Undermine.\030I met Gerenzo once, but let me tell you, he's not easy on the eyes. His flesh looks like it's rotting away, and he's grafted metal and gears onto his body, replaced some of his limbs with mechanical ones.$B$BNortheast of here, far above Cragpool Lake, up near the water wheel is where Gerenzo watches over the entire site. There's no way I could fight my way up there, not to mention take on Gerenzo... But you look like you might be able to make it.$B$BIf you kill him for me, I'll make it worth your while!\030Bring Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle's Mechanical Arm to Ziz Fizziks in the Stonetalon Mountains.\030Sputtervalve will want some sort of proof that Gerenzo's dead. I think his mechanical arm will probably do.\030Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle\0312,1,67,2,257,1,4201\0302,69,204,2,257,1,4201\0302,209,322,2,257,1,4201\0302,324,402,2,261,4,4201\0302,404,450,2,257,4,4201\0302,455,508,2,257,4,4201\0303,1,88,2,384,1,4201\0301,1,21,4,272,1,4201\0301,23,76,4,272,1,4201\0301,78,199,4,272,4,4201\0301,204,224,4,272,1,4201\0301,229,265,4,272,1,4201\0301,267,409,4,272,4,4201\0304,1,62,3,258,3,4201\0304,64,107,3,256,3,4201\0314202,2,7,Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle\0304201,2,7,Ziz Fizziks\0303442,4,13,Sputtervalve\0303442,3,14,Sputtervalve\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,7,Ziz Fizziks\0302,0,0,7,Stonetalon Mountains\0304,0,0,13,Gadgetzan\0311095,19,1095,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5736,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1097]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You're here to help with my delivery? Very good!\030There's a dwarven weaponsmith in Stormwind, Grimand Elmore, who sent word that he needs help with a delivery.  I believe he wants a package sent to his homeland in the north.$B$BYou have a sturdy pair on you!  So if you're interested in some legwork then speak with Grimand.  We could use you down here, but we must also keep our ties strong with the dwarves.$B$BYou can find Grimand Elmore at the weapon shop in the Dwarven District of Stormwind, in the northeast section of town.\030Speak with Grimand Elmore.\030\030Elmore's Task\0312,1,109,2,259,1,514\0302,112,174,2,259,4,514\0302,179,208,2,257,1,514\0302,211,274,2,257,4,514\0302,277,359,2,257,4,514\0302,364,481,2,257,1,514\0303,1,26,2,384,1,514\0301,1,37,4,272,2,1416\0301,39,48,4,272,1,1416\0311416,2,1,Grimand Elmore\0301416,2,6,Grimand Elmore\0301416,2,7,Grimand Elmore\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,1,Stormwind\0302,0,0,6,Dwarven District of Stormwind\031353,23,353,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030353,24,353,UNKNOWN\031",[1098]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Vincent's body lies broken, and still.$B$BAlthough Deathstalker Adamant will send his report to Hadrec... whatever additional details Vincent gained must remain with him.$B$BBut clutched in his hand is a small trinket...\030In preparation for an assault on Shadowfang, two deathstalkers were sent to the keep to gather intelligence.  It has been many days and they have not returned, but we must receive their report if we're to have any hope of a successful attack!$B$BSo here is your task, $N.  Go to Shadowfang Keep to the south and find the Deathstalkers Adamant and Vincent.  Find them, and if they require aid then give it.$B$BThis mission is as dangerous as is it critical, $N.  Do not fail.\030Find the Deathstalker Adamant and Deathstalker Vincent.\030\030Deathstalkers in Shadowfang\0312,1,108,2,257,1,1952\0302,111,242,2,263,4,1952\0302,247,271,2,257,1,1952\0302,274,355,2,257,1,1952\0302,358,405,2,257,4,1952\0302,410,460,2,257,1,1952\0302,463,474,2,257,1,1952\0303,1,55,2,384,1,1952\0301,1,38,4,272,1,4444\0301,43,105,4,272,3,4444\0301,107,170,4,272,1,4444\0301,175,220,4,272,1,4444\0313849,2,8,Deathstalker Adamant\0304444,2,8,Deathstalker Vincent\0303849,4,10,Deathstalker Adamant\0312,209,0,0,\0302,0,0,4,Shadowfang Keep\0304,0,0,10,Hadrec\031\031",[11]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I see you've been busy! You have our thanks, $N.\030Gnolls, brutish creatures with no decent business in these lands, have been seen along the borders of Elwynn Forest.  A large pack of them, many more than we can handle alone, have infested the woods south of the guard tower yonder.  Another group has infested the areas near Stone Cairn Lake to the east.$B$BThe Stormwind Army will commend whomever helps kill them.  Bring me their painted gnoll armbands as proof of your deed.\030Bring 8 Painted Gnoll Armbands to Deputy Rainer at the Barracks.\030Hail, $N. Have you been killing Gnolls...?\030Riverpaw Gnoll Bounty\0312,1,116,2,257,1,963\0302,119,232,2,257,1,963\0302,235,305,2,257,1,963\0302,310,366,2,257,3,963\0302,369,428,2,257,1,963\0303,1,64,2,384,1,963\0301,1,23,4,272,1,963\0301,25,48,4,272,1,963\0304,1,9,3,256,1,963\0304,11,42,3,256,2,963\031963,2,6,Deputy Rainer\0312,12,1429,0,\0302,0,0,3,Stone Cairn Lake\0302,0,0,6,Deputy Rainer\0302,0,0,6,Barracks\031\031ITEM,782,OBJECTIVE,8,15,",[110]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes, I have the results right here.  They are... unsettling, to say the least$B$BOur initial suspicion that the bugs are being controlled by an outside force, we believe, is correct.  If this is the case, then we are dealing with not only a very powerful unknown force, but also a malignant one.  These bugs have been changed to be pure ravagers.  I've never seen anything quite like it.\030I'm going to spend some time taking a look at Scrimshank's surveying gear... as well as putting his personal effects in order.  I get the sneaking feeling behind my ears that this isn't the last loss we'll be facing against these bugs.$B$BI'd like for you to check in with Alchemist Pestlezugg to see if he has had a chance to process the insect parts we sent him.  If they're ready, bring them to me.\030Check in Gadgetzan for Alchemist Pestlezugg and his analysis of the insect parts.\030\030Insect Part Analysis\0312,1,76,2,257,3,7724\0302,78,126,2,257,1,7724\0302,129,235,2,257,1,7724\0302,240,364,2,259,4,7724\0302,367,401,2,257,4,7724\0303,1,81,2,384,1,7724\0301,1,35,4,272,1,5594\0301,38,48,4,272,1,5594\0301,50,77,4,272,1,5594\0301,82,182,4,272,4,5594\0301,185,295,4,272,4,5594\0301,298,346,4,272,1,5594\0301,349,387,4,272,1,5594\0315594,2,4,Alchemist Pestlezugg\0305594,2,6,Alchemist Pestlezugg\0312,440,1446,0,\0302,0,0,1,Scrimshank's\0302,0,0,6,Gadgetzan\03110,19,10,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030113,23,113,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1100]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You say you found this journal on a deceased dwarf? Give me but a moment to peruse the pages...\030You slowly open the weathered journal of Henrig Lonebrow....\030Read Henrig Lonebrow's Journal.\030From your look of concern, I can tell that something is amiss....\030Lonebrow's Journal\0312,1,60,2,257,1,0\0303,1,31,2,384,1,0\0301,1,51,4,272,2,4048\0301,53,95,4,272,1,4048\0304,1,65,3,256,1,4048\031\0312,400,1441,0,\0311101,23,1101,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5791,STARTER,?,10,",[1101]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The crone has been laid to rest. This is fantastic news, $N.$B$BIn these times of peril, it is refreshing to see one as brave as yourself.$B$BWith Razorflank's minions taken care of, our studies in the area can continue. Perhaps now we can gain further knowledge of exactly what happened to corrupt the resting place of Agamaggan.$B$BHowever, I fear the answer to that question lies in treachery as well...\030Poor Heralath! And this dwarf... Lonebrow. What a brave soul he was.$B$BWe must not let their valiance go for naught. This crone... Charlga Razorflank ... must be stopped.$B$BSurely, infiltrating the Kraul will be perilous. There isn't time to send word to Darnassus. $n, assemble a party to slay the crone.$B$BBring me Razorflank's Medallion as proof of demise.\030Bring Razorflank's Medallion to Falfindel Waywarder in Thalanaar.\030So long as Charlga Razorflank is mustering a force in Razorfen Kraul, these lands are in great danger.\030The Crone of the Kraul\0312,1,14,2,257,1,4048\0302,16,32,2,257,1,4048\0302,34,42,2,257,1,4048\0302,44,68,2,257,1,4048\0302,73,117,2,265,1,4048\0302,119,131,2,257,1,4048\0302,133,154,2,257,1,4048\0302,156,171,2,257,1,4048\0302,176,223,2,257,3,4048\0302,225,267,2,257,1,4048\0302,269,307,2,257,1,4048\0302,312,362,2,257,1,4048\0303,1,65,2,384,1,4048\0301,1,32,4,272,1,4048\0301,34,60,4,272,1,4048\0301,65,138,4,272,1,4048\0301,143,220,4,272,1,4048\0301,222,330,4,276,4,4048\0301,335,406,4,272,1,4048\0304,1,102,3,260,1,4048\0314421,2,7,Charlga Razorflank\0304048,2,13,Falfindel Waywarder\0304421,3,20,Charlga Razorflank\0312,1717,1413,0,\0302,0,0,10,Darnassus\0302,0,0,13,Falfindel Waywarder\0302,0,0,13,Thalanaar\0303,0,0,20,Razorfen Kraul\0311100,19,1100,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5792,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1102]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I see the nasty tribe of Razorfen Kraul now knows the pain of my people. Serves the foul beasts right.$B$BTo drive one from a holy land is a sin worthy of the most severe revenge.$B$BThank you, $N, for aiding me in my plight.\030Cairne is a noble leader for uniting our people here on Thunder Bluff.$B$BBut I cannot forgive those who drove us from our ancestral lands as easily as some. My people inhabited the southern Barrens for decades. The land was holy to us. But we were driven off by numerous foes.$B$BA vengeful fate awaits the crone, Charlga Razorflank, who musters a foul army from within Razorfen Kraul.$B$BBring me Razorflank's heart and I can die in peace, $n.\030Bring Razorflank's Heart to Auld Stonespire in Thunder Bluff.\030Once I know the foul beasts of Razorfen Kraul have been driven from their foul lair, I will be able to rest in peace, knowing that revenge has been served.$B$BHave you the driven the quilboar from the Kraul? Do you bring to me good news in the form of Razorflank's heart?\030A Vengeful Fate\0312,1,70,2,257,1,4451\0302,75,157,2,257,1,4451\0302,159,211,2,257,1,4451\0302,213,236,2,257,1,4451\0302,238,277,2,257,1,4451\0302,282,386,2,257,1,4451\0302,391,445,2,265,1,4451\0303,1,61,2,384,1,4451\0301,1,72,4,272,1,4451\0301,74,102,4,272,1,4451\0301,107,179,4,274,1,4451\0301,184,225,4,272,1,4451\0304,1,155,3,266,3,4451\0304,160,207,3,256,2,4451\0304,209,271,3,256,2,4451\0314421,2,6,Charlga Razorflank\0304451,2,8,Auld Stonespire\0312,1717,1413,0,\0302,0,0,6,Razorfen Kraul\0302,0,0,8,Auld Stonespire\0302,0,0,8,Thunder Bluff\0303,0,0,14,Kraul\031\031ITEM,5793,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1103]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ahhh, den yur ready...$B$BI'll put me items in the brazier den, and you c'n talk wit' da spirit too.$B$BAn' dontchu worry none 'bout seein' into da spirit world wit' da sapta... ol' Tiev know a trick or two 'bout how da sapta magic works.$B$BCome now, head down wit' me to the shrine and let's speak to da spirits together, brotha.\030Greetin's, $g brotha:sista;! Have you too come to purify the waters here and prove your understandin' to Islen?$B$BI've just defeated the corrupt water spirit meself, and I'm just 'bout to put da bracers and remaining drops o' water on the brazier.$B$BWhat's dat? Ahhh. Tiev understan' all too well when somethin' goes wrong. Well, Tiev can help you plenty if you be needin' to see the pure water spirit again.$B$BBring me a water sapta from Islen as proof that you be ready, an' I'll wait to turn in me parts.\030Bring a Water Sapta to Tiev Mordune in Silverpine Forest if you failed to speak to the Minor Manifestation of Water.\030Ya have the sapta, brotha?$B$BI know another that had trouble after defeating da corrupt water spirit--seems he waited too long and he came out of the spirit world too quick fer his taste. Hate to see dat happen to another, so I'll just wait here fer a bit to make sure no one else be needin' me help.\030Call of Water\0312,1,28,2,257,1,7007\0302,30,111,2,257,2,7007\0302,116,248,2,261,1,7007\0302,253,263,2,257,2,7007\0302,265,269,2,257,1,7007\0302,271,325,2,257,1,7007\0302,327,410,2,257,4,7007\0302,415,510,2,257,1,7007\0303,1,116,2,384,4,7007\0301,1,22,4,272,1,7007\0301,27,100,4,272,1,7007\0301,105,177,4,272,1,7007\0301,179,238,4,272,1,7007\0301,243,331,4,272,1,7007\0304,1,26,3,256,2,7007\0304,31,188,3,260,4,7007\0304,190,301,3,256,1,7007\0315897,2,3,Corrupt Water Spirit\0306748,2,3,Water Spirit\0306748,2,7,Water Spirit\0307007,2,9,Tiev Mordune\0305895,2,9,Minor Manifestation of Water\03011256,2,9,Manifestation of Water\0305897,3,16,Corrupt Water Spirit\0306748,3,16,Water Spirit\0312,0,0,2,Islen\0302,0,0,8,Islen\0302,0,0,9,Tiev Mordune\0302,0,0,9,Silverpine Forest\0302,0,0,9,Minor Manifestation of Water\031100,19,100,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6637,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1104]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031All right! This venom is going to work great! Thanks, $N!$B$BNow I just need to boil it down, apply skipper-otomer, add a nega-catalyst, and... Drat! Where are my notes!?\030I have so many designs for our rocket car!  So many!  And I must try them all!!$B$BI'm working on a new type of fuel.  One that burns really really really hot!!  I haven't gotten the mixture perfect, but I think I know what I need...$B$BThe scorpids who wander the Shimmering Flats have a venom with lots and lots of salt in it.  It's very unique!  And it's just what I need!$B$BBring me venom and trust me -- our car will fly!!\030Bring 6 Salty Scorpid Venoms to Fizzle Brassbolts in the Shimmering Flats.\030Hi hi hi! Did you get that venom??\030Salt Flat Venom\0312,1,42,2,257,1,4454\0302,45,52,2,257,1,4454\0302,55,79,2,257,1,4454\0302,84,117,2,257,1,4454\0302,120,160,2,257,1,4454\0302,163,233,2,259,1,4454\0302,238,328,2,257,1,4454\0302,331,347,2,257,1,4454\0302,350,375,2,259,1,4454\0302,380,428,2,257,3,4454\0303,1,74,2,384,1,4454\0301,1,10,4,272,1,4454\0301,12,45,4,272,3,4454\0301,47,57,4,272,1,4454\0301,62,143,4,274,1,4454\0301,145,149,4,272,1,4454\0301,151,170,4,272,2,4454\0304,11,34,3,256,2,4454\03111045,2,5,Burns\0304454,2,11,Fizzle Brassbolts\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,11,Fizzle Brassbolts\0302,0,0,11,Shimmering Flats\031\031ITEM,5794,OBJECTIVE,6,15,",[1105]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You got them! Thanks, $N!\030My brother is working on a new fuel for his rocket car.  He's brilliant, he really is.  So brilliant that... I think that new fuel he's designing is strong enough to eat right through the car's chassis!$B$BI want to reinforce its fuel tanks before that happens.$B$BThe tortoises out on the flats have very hard shells.  I want to use them to create new tanks for our rocket car.  Tanks that can hold my brother's new fuel.$B$BYou look responsible enough.  Will you get me those shells?\030Bring 9 Hardened Tortoise Shells to Wizzle Brassbolts in the Shimmering Flats.\030My brother is making progress with his new fuel design, and that has me worried. I need to start work on a tortoise shell fuel tank as soon as possible!\030Hardened Shells\0312,1,55,2,257,1,4453\0302,58,86,2,257,1,4453\0302,89,108,2,257,1,4453\0302,110,202,2,257,1,4453\0302,207,261,2,259,1,4453\0302,266,318,2,257,1,4453\0302,321,378,2,259,1,4453\0302,381,422,2,257,1,4453\0302,427,454,2,257,1,4453\0302,457,485,2,257,2,4453\0303,1,78,2,384,1,4453\0301,1,13,4,272,1,4453\0301,15,25,4,272,1,4453\0304,1,80,3,256,1,4453\0304,82,152,3,258,1,4453\0314453,2,11,Wizzle Brassbolts\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,11,Wizzle Brassbolts\0302,0,0,11,Shimmering Flats\0311107,23,1107,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5795,OBJECTIVE,9,15,",[1106]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Fizzle sent you? Well that changes things! Of course I'll help you. Fizzle and his brother are two of the few people who don't want me dead!$B$BSo Fizzle wants to make pistons, eh? Pistons strong enough to take whatever stresses he has planned, and if I know Fizzle, then this new car of his is a volcano on wheels!\030I'm developing a new engine that'll make the car go so fast!  Fast enough to fly, I know it!  I just need to make pistons that can handle very very heavy stress.  All my trials have failed because I can't make pistons hard enough!$B$BBut there is someone who might know how.$B$BHis name is Martek the Exiled.  He is a great smith and knows more about metal than anyone.  Take him this letter, I know he can help!$B$BBut he's far far away -- in Azeroth, in the Badlands, in a camp, with a goblin!$B$BFind him!\030Bring Fizzle's Letter to Martek the Exiled in the Badlands.\030Well, you found me. Good for you.$B$BAre you here about that axe I made for Gath'Ilzogg? Or are you here to reclaim Duchess Pamay's honor?$B$BActually, I don't care which it is. If you're here to fight, then let's get it over with...\030Martek the Exiled\0312,1,60,2,257,1,4454\0302,63,92,2,257,1,4454\0302,95,161,2,259,1,4454\0302,164,230,2,259,1,4454\0302,235,274,2,257,4,4454\0302,279,308,2,257,1,4454\0302,311,369,2,257,1,4454\0302,372,412,2,257,1,4454\0302,417,495,2,257,1,4454\0302,500,508,2,257,1,4454\0303,1,59,2,384,1,4454\0301,1,16,4,272,2,4618\0301,18,42,4,272,1,4618\0301,44,67,4,272,1,4618\0301,69,140,4,272,1,4618\0301,145,180,4,274,2,4618\0301,182,315,4,272,4,4618\0304,1,19,3,256,1,4618\0304,21,33,3,256,1,4618\0304,38,88,3,256,2,4618\0304,90,138,3,256,2,4618\0304,143,177,3,256,1,4618\0304,179,233,3,260,4,4618\0314618,2,6,Martek the Exiled\0304618,2,11,Martek the Exiled\030334,3,20,Gath'Ilzogg\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,9,Azeroth\0302,0,0,9,Badlands\0302,0,0,11,Martek the Exiled\0302,0,0,11,Badlands\0311108,23,1108,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1107]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, $N! After I grind these down and fuse them with a few other ingredients, the composite will be ready. And after that, the car will be safe from its own speed.$B$BSafe, as long as it doesn't hit anything...\030Our rocket car is the fastest thing on the flats!  So fast that ... I'm afraid friction is going to tear it apart!$B$BTo prevent that I need to create a composite to coat the car's moving parts.  It must be hard but not brittle, and must be resistant to salt corrosion, or time spent on the Shimmering Flats will eat it away.$B$BHave you heard of the Vile Reef, $N?  It's off the coast of Stranglethorn Vale.  Saltscale murlocs live there, and their tail fins are a crucial ingredient of my composite.\030Bring 10 Encrusted Tail Fins to Wizzle Brassbolts in the Shimmering Flats.\030Do you have the tail fins?  If I can't protect our car from its own speed, then it won't last long in these races.\030Encrusted Tail Fins\0312,1,49,2,257,1,4453\0302,52,67,2,257,1,4453\0302,69,114,2,257,3,4453\0302,119,194,2,267,1,4453\0302,197,325,2,257,3,4453\0302,330,365,2,257,2,4453\0302,368,408,2,257,1,4453\0302,411,501,2,257,1,4453\0303,1,74,2,384,1,4453\0301,1,14,4,272,1,4453\0301,16,112,4,272,3,4453\0301,114,169,4,272,3,4453\0301,174,216,4,272,1,4453\0304,1,26,3,256,2,4453\0304,29,114,3,268,4,4453\0314453,2,9,Wizzle Brassbolts\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,9,Wizzle Brassbolts\0302,0,0,9,Shimmering Flats\0311105,19,1105,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5796,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[1108]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah yes, these will do fine. Now let's put them in some heat and see how they fare...\030I'm not out here just to stay away from people.  There is a wealth of metal in the Badlands, $N, if you have the guts to get it.$B$BThe metal's called indurium and as luck would have it, it is rumored to possess high resistance to heat and stress.  It might work for Fizzle's car.$B$BBut let's make sure.  Get me samples of indurium and I'll test its properties.$B$BTrue indurium ore lies deep in Uldaman, but the Stonevault troggs of the Badlands sometimes have flakes of it on them.  Bring me those flakes.\030Bring 10 Indurium Flakes to Martek the Exiled in the Badlands.\030Did you find any indurium flakes, $N. I have my forge heated up and ready to test them.\030Indurium\0312,1,47,2,257,1,4618\0302,50,128,2,257,4,4618\0302,133,247,2,257,4,4618\0302,250,280,2,257,4,4618\0302,285,304,2,257,1,4618\0302,307,362,2,257,1,4618\0302,367,484,2,257,1,4618\0302,487,508,2,257,1,4618\0303,1,62,2,384,1,4618\0301,1,27,4,272,3,4618\0301,29,84,4,272,1,4618\0304,1,37,3,256,1,4618\0304,39,87,3,256,1,4618\0314618,2,9,Martek the Exiled\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,2,Badlands\0302,0,0,7,Uldaman\0302,0,0,9,Martek the Exiled\0302,0,0,9,Badlands\0311106,19,1106,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301137,23,1137,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5797,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[1109]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Splendid! This is just the start we needed, $N.\030As you can see, $n, we're up to some very.... interesting experiments at the Royal Apothecary Society.$B$BAs the Master here, it is my job to oversee the most ambitious of our alchemical attempts. So much work and so little time!$B$BYou look well traveled for a $c. Perhaps you can aid me.$B$BI'm in need of a rare substance. It's foul material; it comes from a rare species of bats only found in the muck-hole known as Razorfen Kraul. Bring to me the guano from the Kraul Bats so we can begin our work...\030Bring 1 pile of Kraul Guano to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity.\030Ah, I see you have returned. Were you able to procure any Kraul Guano?\030Going, Going, Guano!\0312,1,45,2,257,1,2055\0302,47,102,2,257,1,2055\0302,107,196,2,257,1,2055\0302,198,229,2,257,1,2055\0302,234,265,2,257,1,2055\0302,267,289,2,257,4,2055\0302,294,325,2,259,1,2055\0302,327,435,2,257,1,2055\0302,437,505,2,257,1,2055\0303,1,75,2,384,1,2055\0301,1,9,4,272,1,2055\0301,11,47,4,272,1,2055\0304,1,28,3,256,1,2055\0304,30,70,3,256,2,2055\0312055,2,10,Master Apothecary Faranell\0312,1717,1413,0,\0302,0,0,2,Royal Apothecary Society\0302,0,0,9,Kraul Bats\0302,0,0,10,Master Apothecary Faranell\0302,0,0,10,Undercity\0311113,23,1113,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5801,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[111]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031While our families are feuding, Tommy Joe and Maybell don't have much of a future, but... maybe we can get them together for just a little while.$B$BHm, what can we do...\030Please, $N, talk with my Gramma.  If anyone can find a way to bring me together with Maybell, she can.$B$BShe's inside our house east of here.\030Speak with Gramma Stonefield.\030\030Speak with Gramma\0312,1,32,2,257,1,252\0302,35,102,2,257,4,252\0302,107,142,2,257,1,252\0303,1,29,2,384,1,252\0301,1,89,4,272,1,248\0301,91,145,4,272,4,248\0301,150,170,4,272,1,248\031248,2,4,Gramma Stonefield\0312,12,1429,0,\031106,19,106,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030107,23,107,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1110]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Whoa, look at all that! There's some good stuff in that heap of junk. I'm sure I can pawn it off for a hefty sum.$B$BAnd... is that an ear I see squashed between those two sheets of metal?? Ouch! Heh, I sure wouldn't want to be that pilot!$B$BThanks, $N. Here's your pay. And here's some advice, free of charge...$B$BIf you look hard enough, you can always find profit in someone else's tragedy.\030Heh heh, with all the races they're running here, it's no surprise that a few mishaps happen along the way.  If you look around the Shimmering Flats then you'll see evidence of past crashes -- scraps of rocket car parts are littered everywhere!$B$BAnd those parts are worth money to the gnomes and goblins.  They're always looking for more contraptions to slap onto their cars.$B$BSo go out and get me parts.  Bring me a heap and I'll pay you well.\030Bring 30 Rocket Car Parts to Kravel Koalbeard in the Shimmering Flats.\030$N, have you been out into the Flats? Did you bring back that load of parts I wanted?\030Rocket Car Parts\0312,1,107,2,257,1,4452\0302,110,244,2,257,4,4452\0302,249,306,2,257,1,4452\0302,309,377,2,257,1,4452\0302,382,408,2,257,1,4452\0302,411,448,2,257,1,4452\0303,1,70,2,384,1,4452\0301,1,23,4,272,1,4452\0301,25,69,4,272,1,4452\0301,71,113,4,272,1,4452\0301,118,123,4,272,1,4452\0301,125,189,4,272,2,4452\0301,191,195,4,272,1,4452\0301,197,239,4,272,1,4452\0301,244,254,4,272,1,4452\0301,256,271,4,272,1,4452\0301,273,313,4,272,1,4452\0301,318,395,4,272,4,4452\0304,1,37,3,256,2,4452\0304,39,85,3,256,2,4452\0314452,2,7,Kravel Koalbeard\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,7,Kravel Koalbeard\0302,0,0,7,Shimmering Flats\031\031ITEM,5798,OBJECTIVE,30,15,",[1111]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh yes. Parts for Kravel. I'm glad you're here. These things have been sitting out here for days, and I was afraid they'd rust!\030I make it my job to get people what they need, and the gnomes over there need a parts order filled.  Their parts were shipped to Ratchet a week ago, but I haven't been able to make the trip.$B$BSo, are you ready for some legwork?  Go to Ratchet and give this parts order to Wharfmaster Dizzywig -- he'll probably be at the docks.$B$BDo this for me, and I'll have more jobs for you.$B$BJobs, my friend, with serious profit potential...\030Bring Kravel's Parts Order to Wharfmaster Dizzywig in Ratchet.\030Speak up! Tell me, are you dropping off or picking up?\030Wharfmaster Dizzywig\0312,1,99,2,259,1,4452\0302,102,190,2,257,1,4452\0302,195,229,2,257,2,4452\0302,232,329,2,257,1,4452\0302,334,381,2,257,1,4452\0302,386,434,2,257,1,4452\0303,1,62,2,384,1,4452\0301,1,7,4,272,1,3453\0301,9,25,4,272,1,3453\0301,27,47,4,272,1,3453\0301,49,127,4,272,1,3453\0304,1,9,3,256,1,3453\0304,11,54,3,256,2,3453\0313453,2,4,Wharfmaster Dizzywig\0303453,2,7,Wharfmaster Dizzywig\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,2,Ratchet\0302,0,0,4,Ratchet\0302,0,0,4,Wharfmaster Dizzywig\0302,0,0,7,Wharfmaster Dizzywig\0302,0,0,7,Ratchet\0311112,23,1112,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1112]="PARTIAL\031conflict,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Great, you got them! Now we need to get them to the gnomes. But first...$B$BLet's take out one small item...\030Here's Kravel's package, $N.  And when you deliver it, tell him... if he wants more special orders, then he'll have to pay his tab!\030Bring Kravel's Parts to Kravel Koalbeard in the Shimmering Flats.\030Did you make it to Ratchet and get those parts?\030Parts for Kravel\0312,1,28,2,257,1,3453\0302,31,66,2,257,1,3453\0302,68,131,2,259,4,3453\0303,1,65,2,384,1,3453\0301,1,20,4,272,1,4452\0301,22,59,4,306,1,4452\0301,61,72,4,272,1,4452\0301,77,108,4,272,1,4452\0304,1,47,3,256,2,4452\0314452,2,4,Kravel Koalbeard\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,4,Kravel Koalbeard\0302,0,0,4,Shimmering Flats\0303,0,0,9,Ratchet\0311111,19,1111,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301114,23,1114,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1113]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031My what an abundance of gore you have brought me, $N! Your efforts have been most excellent!\030Why do I need a rare type of guano, you might ask. Well, for this experiment I want to see what effect two diametrically opposed chemical substances can have on each other, especially when both are combined with an ever-toxic agent to ensure the most... ghastly results.$B$BIn the northeastern peaks of Tirisfal Glades lies the Scarlet Monastery. There the crazed disciples of the Scarlet Crusade congregate, both inside and outside the halls. Which you slay matters not, any of them may have the heart I need.\030Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity wants 20 Hearts of Zeal.\030Have you returned from the Scarlet Monastery? I'll need many hearts for this delightful experiment!$B$BNo doubt, Varimathras and the Dark Lady will be pleased to be rid of the Scarlet Scum as well...\030Hearts of Zeal\0312,1,50,2,259,4,2055\0302,52,253,2,259,1,2055\0302,255,270,2,257,1,2055\0302,275,346,2,257,1,2055\0302,348,443,2,257,1,2055\0302,445,510,2,259,1,2055\0303,1,68,2,386,1,2055\0301,1,53,4,272,1,2055\0301,55,92,4,272,1,2055\0304,1,45,3,256,2,2055\0304,47,99,3,258,1,2055\0304,104,199,3,256,3,2055\0312055,2,7,Master Apothecary Faranell\0302425,3,12,Varimathras\03015065,3,12,Lady\0312,796,0,0,\0302,0,0,7,Undercity\0303,0,0,10,Scarlet Monastery\0311109,19,1109,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5805,OBJECTIVE,20,15,",[1114]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031There they are! My hydro ratchets and repeater bolts! These will do just fine. Thank you!\030Now that I have what I need, give these parts to Fizzle Brassbolts.  He's been waiting a long time for them -- I'm sure he won't miss the little piece I removed from his order...$B$BAnd I wouldn't bother mentioning it to him.  It was small and worthless.$B$BTrust me.\030Bring the Delicate Car Parts to Fizzle Brassbolts in Shimmering Flats.\030You have something for me? That's great! let's see it!\030Delivery to the Gnomes\0312,1,67,2,259,1,4452\0302,70,178,2,257,1,4452\0302,183,225,2,257,1,4452\0302,228,254,2,257,1,4452\0302,259,267,2,257,1,4452\0303,1,70,2,384,1,4452\0301,1,15,4,272,1,4454\0301,17,53,4,272,1,4454\0301,55,78,4,272,3,4454\0301,80,89,4,272,1,4454\0304,1,26,3,256,2,4454\0304,28,40,3,256,1,4454\0304,42,54,3,256,1,4454\0314454,2,1,Fizzle Brassbolts\0304454,2,6,Fizzle Brassbolts\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,1,Fizzle Brassbolts\0302,0,0,6,Fizzle Brassbolts\0302,0,0,6,Shimmering Flats\0311112,19,1112,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301115,23,1115,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1115]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You want to know about Nazz Steamboil? He's a racer pilot out in the Shimmering Flats, isn't he?$B$BYeah, I might be able to find something out about him... but it won't be easy. Or fast.$B$BOr cheap.\030Now that we've done a service for the gnomes, it's time to do the goblins a favor!  $B$BI hear that the goblin racer pilot, Nazz Steamboil, didn't always use that name.  I wonder why he changed it.  I wonder if it's a secret, and... I wonder if he values that secret.$B$BIf anyone knows the truth, then it's Krazek of Booty Bay, on the southern tip of Stranglethorn.  Speak with Krazek and ask him about our goblin pilot.$B$BIf you can get useful information from him, then we might just turn a profit from it.\030Talk to Krazek in Booty Bay.\030\030The Rumormonger\0312,1,82,2,257,1,4452\0302,89,168,2,257,1,4452\0302,171,197,2,257,1,4452\0302,200,232,2,257,4,4452\0302,234,267,2,257,4,4452\0302,272,366,2,257,4,4452\0302,369,421,2,257,1,4452\0302,426,510,2,257,4,4452\0303,1,28,2,384,1,4452\0301,1,38,4,274,2,773\0301,40,96,4,272,2,773\0301,101,156,4,272,4,773\0301,158,178,4,272,1,773\0301,180,187,4,272,1,773\0301,192,200,4,272,1,773\0314251,2,2,Goblin Racer\030773,2,6,Krazek\030773,2,7,Krazek\030773,2,9,Krazek\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,9,Krazek\0302,0,0,9,Booty Bay\0304,0,0,11,Shimmering Flats\0311114,19,1114,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301116,23,1116,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1116]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well, look at that. You found the dream dust!$B$BAnd how did you like the swamp, $N? It's not easy to get a hot meal there, is it?\030Getting the information on Nazz is quite a favor, $N.  Yes, quite a favor.  But you've come all the way from the Shimmering Flats to get it... are you willing to travel some more?$B$BWhile I contact my sources, why don't you gather something for me, eh?$B$BHm... what will it be?  How about dream dust, from the dragon whelps of the Swamp of Sorrows.  Yes, I'd love some dream dust for my snuff pouch!$B$BGet it for me, $N, and I'll give you the information you seek.\030Bring 10 Specks of Dream Dust to Krazek in Booty Bay.  Dream Dust is gathered from the dragon whelps of the Swamp of Sorrows.\030Back so soon? Do you have my dream dust?\030Dream Dust in the Swamp\0312,1,53,2,257,1,773\0302,56,74,2,257,1,773\0302,77,142,2,257,1,773\0302,144,179,2,257,2,773\0302,184,253,2,257,2,773\0302,264,279,2,257,2,773\0302,282,350,2,257,1,773\0302,353,401,2,257,1,773\0302,406,467,2,259,1,773\0303,1,53,2,384,1,773\0303,56,125,2,384,1,773\0301,1,19,4,272,1,773\0301,21,45,4,272,1,773\0301,50,84,4,272,2,773\0301,86,130,4,272,2,773\0304,1,13,3,256,2,773\0304,15,40,3,256,2,773\031773,2,10,Krazek\0312,8,1435,0,\0302,0,0,3,Shimmering Flats\0302,0,0,10,Krazek\0302,0,0,10,Booty Bay\0311115,19,1115,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301117,23,1117,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5803,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[1117]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well well! This is interesting... very interesting. Heh, perhaps I should bow to the goblin pilot the next time I see him.$B$BThis is worth plenty, $N. I'm sure Nazz will pay a small fortune to keep his secret... a secret.\030I had to use some of my favors, and gave away a rare bottle of elven wine, and did some heavy deducing myself!  But I found the information you seek.$B$BHere, I wrote a letter with some very interesting bits on our friend, Nazz Steamboil.  Do with it what you will -- it's too dangerous for me to use.$B$BJust don't tell anyone where you got it!\030Bring the Goblin Rumors to Kravel Koalbeard in the Shimmering Flats.\030Did you get anything on Nazz Steamboil? Anything he might want to keep a secret??\030Rumors for Kravel\0312,1,110,2,257,1,773\0302,113,149,2,259,1,773\0302,154,238,2,257,1,773\0302,241,301,2,257,3,773\0302,306,345,2,257,1,773\0303,1,68,2,384,1,773\0301,1,10,4,272,1,4452\0301,12,33,4,272,1,4452\0301,35,51,4,272,1,4452\0301,53,122,4,272,4,4452\0301,127,151,4,272,1,4452\0301,153,212,4,272,3,4452\0301,214,222,4,272,1,4452\0304,1,39,3,256,2,4452\0304,41,81,3,258,4,4452\0314452,2,6,Kravel Koalbeard\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,6,Kravel Koalbeard\0302,0,0,6,Shimmering Flats\0311116,19,1116,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301118,23,1118,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1118]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I see. Kravel has a big scheme planned. He has a sinister mind -- I like that about him.$B$BSo you'll need something to addle wits, eh? Something powerful...$B$BI wonder if the mixture Zanzil feeds his zombies could be used...\030$N, you're a $c I can trust, both to get the job done and to keep your mouth shut while doing it.$B$BI've been brewing up a new scheme.  It's risky, but if it works then we could both make a bundle!  And I think you're just the person to see it through.$B$BTo start, you must go back to Booty Bay.  I apologize, good $N.  I know my last task took you there.  But this time, speak with Crank Fizzlebub.$B$BGive him this letter.  And if he requires aid, do your best to help him.  It will be worth the effort.\030Bring Kravel's Scheme to Crank Fizzlebub in Booty Bay.\030Hello hello. And what brings a noble $R such as you down to Booty Bay?\030Back to Booty Bay\0312,1,97,2,257,1,4452\0302,102,135,2,257,1,4452\0302,138,198,2,257,4,4452\0302,201,253,2,257,1,4452\0302,258,297,2,257,1,4452\0302,300,320,2,257,1,4452\0302,323,357,2,257,1,4452\0302,360,401,2,257,1,4452\0302,406,426,2,257,1,4452\0302,429,477,2,257,4,4452\0302,480,507,2,257,3,4452\0303,1,54,2,384,1,4452\0301,1,6,4,272,1,2498\0301,8,39,4,272,1,2498\0301,41,88,4,272,1,2498\0301,93,135,4,274,2,2498\0301,137,157,4,272,1,2498\0301,162,226,4,272,4,2498\0304,1,12,3,256,1,2498\0304,14,70,3,256,2,2498\0312498,2,8,Crank Fizzlebub\0302498,2,12,Crank Fizzlebub\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,5,Booty Bay\0302,0,0,12,Crank Fizzlebub\0302,0,0,12,Booty Bay\0303,0,0,20,Booty Bay\0311117,19,1117,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1119]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Wonderful! Fizzlebub came through! I'll remember that next time I see him.$B$BAnd thank you, $N. You're doing a great job, and we both stand to make a lot of money from this...\030I figured out how to use Zanzil's mixture with stout to make a powerful libation.  A Fool's Stout.  I think it'll be just what Kravel needs, but try it out and let me know how it works.$B$BAnd $N, don't keep this stuff too long without using it.  Zanzil's mixture has a weird effect on the stout's yeast, kicking it into high gear.  So it won't stay fresh forever.\030Bring the Fool's Stout back to Kravel in the Shimmering Flats.\030Hello, $N. Was Fizzlebub able to help us?\030Zanzil's Mixture and a Fool's Stout\0312,1,81,2,257,1,2498\0302,84,98,2,257,1,2498\0302,101,185,2,259,1,2498\0302,190,245,2,257,1,2498\0302,248,331,2,257,1,2498\0302,334,364,2,257,1,2498\0303,1,62,2,384,1,2498\0301,1,10,4,272,1,4452\0301,12,34,4,272,1,4452\0301,36,74,4,272,1,4452\0301,79,96,4,272,1,4452\0301,98,176,4,272,1,4452\0304,1,10,3,256,1,4452\0304,12,41,3,256,2,4452\031\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,7,Kravel\0302,0,0,7,Shimmering Flats\031621,21,621,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301118,21,1118,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[112]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You got them. Good show! Now, just one moment while I concoct the potion...\030I can make an invisibility liquor for Maybell, so she can slip away from the Maclure Vineyards and go to Tommy Joe.  But to make the Liquor, I need some crystal kelp.$B$BAlthough the kelp usually grows in the ocean... sometimes murlocs collect it.  See if the murlocs near Crystal Lake have any.  Crystal Lake is just east of Goldshire.\030Bring 4 Crystal Kelp Fronds to William Pestle in Goldshire.\030Do you have that crystal kelp? I'm sure Maybell is anxious to see her beau...\030Collecting Kelp\0312,1,115,2,257,1,253\0302,118,166,2,259,1,253\0302,171,217,2,257,1,253\0302,219,247,2,257,1,253\0302,250,295,2,257,4,253\0302,298,336,2,257,1,253\0303,1,59,2,384,1,253\0301,1,13,4,272,1,253\0301,15,24,4,272,1,253\0301,26,75,4,272,1,253\0304,1,30,3,256,2,253\0304,32,77,3,256,1,253\031253,2,7,William Pestle\0312,12,1429,0,\0302,0,0,1,Maclure Vineyards\0302,0,0,1,Tommy Joe\0302,0,0,5,Crystal Lake\0302,0,0,6,Goldshire\0302,0,0,7,William Pestle\0302,0,0,7,Goldshire\031107,19,107,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030114,23,114,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,1256,OBJECTIVE,4,15,",[1120]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Stout? How considerate! Thank you!$B$BWe shouldn't be drinking with the race coming up, but... maybe my boys could do with just a little. Besides, it can't be that strong, can it?\030We need to try the Fool's Stout on one of the pit crews.  If you want to try it on the gnomes, then here -- take the stout and give it to the gnome pit boss.$B$BAnd don't wait too long.  This stout will go bad eventually.\030Bring the Fool's Stout to the Gnome Pit Boss.\030Hi! You have something for me?\030Get the Gnomes Drunk\0312,1,56,2,259,1,4452\0302,59,157,2,259,4,4452\0302,162,185,2,257,1,4452\0302,188,221,2,257,3,4452\0303,1,45,2,384,1,4452\0301,1,6,4,272,2,4495\0301,8,23,4,272,1,4495\0301,25,34,4,272,1,4495\0301,39,94,4,272,1,4495\0301,96,137,4,272,4,4495\0301,139,179,4,272,2,4495\0304,5,30,3,256,2,4495\0314495,2,2,Gnome Pit Boss\0304495,2,5,Gnome Pit Boss\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,5,Gnome Pit Boss\0311119,19,1119,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301121,22,1121,UNKNOWN\031",[1121]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031What do we have here? Booze, eh?$B$BWell, I don't mind if we have just a little...\030We need to try the Fool's Stout on one of the pit crews.  If you want to try it on the goblins, then here -- take the stout and give it to the goblin pit boss.$B$BAnd don't wait too long.  This stout will go bad eventually.\030Bring the Fool's Stout to the Goblin Pit Boss.\030What are you looking at?\030Get the Goblins Drunk\0312,1,56,2,259,1,4452\0302,59,159,2,259,4,4452\0302,164,187,2,257,1,4452\0302,190,223,2,257,3,4452\0303,1,46,2,384,1,4452\0301,1,21,4,272,2,4496\0301,23,32,4,272,2,4496\0301,37,82,4,272,4,4496\0304,1,24,3,256,2,4496\0314496,2,2,Goblin Pit Boss\0304496,2,5,Goblin Pit Boss\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,5,Goblin Pit Boss\0311119,19,1119,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301120,22,1120,UNKNOWN\031",[1122]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It says here that the fool's stout was a success. That's good news!$B$BIf you ever want more of the stuff, then let me know and I'll have you gather more of Zanzil's Mixture.\030That Fool's Stout worked great!  I placed a bet on the next race, and... let's hope the crew you got drunk did a number on their car!$B$BThere's only one more task for you -- take this note back to Crank Fizzlebub in Booty Bay.  He'll want to know of the successful test.$B$BAnd hopefully we can get more of that Fool's Stout for future races!\030Bring the Fool's Stout report to Crank Fizzlebub in Booty Bay.\030Hello $N. How'd that stout work out? It's strong stuff, isn't it?\030Report Back to Fizzlebub\0312,1,31,2,257,1,4452\0302,34,72,2,257,1,4452\0302,74,133,2,257,3,4452\0302,138,227,2,257,1,4452\0302,230,271,2,259,1,4452\0302,276,343,2,257,3,4452\0303,1,62,2,384,1,4452\0301,1,49,4,272,1,2498\0301,51,67,4,272,1,2498\0301,72,174,4,274,4,2498\0304,1,9,3,256,1,2498\0304,11,36,3,256,2,2498\0304,38,65,3,256,2,2498\0312498,2,4,Crank Fizzlebub\0302498,2,7,Crank Fizzlebub\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,4,Crank Fizzlebub\0302,0,0,4,Booty Bay\0302,0,0,7,Crank Fizzlebub\0302,0,0,7,Booty Bay\0311127,23,1127,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1123]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I am Rabine Saturna, and on behalf of Keeper Remulos and all of the denizens of this sacred glade I bid you welcome.$B$BI appreciate your interest and eagerness to assist the Cenarion Circle. The tauren have shown an incredible propensity to the tenets of Cenarius, and by their proxy the Horde is welcomed within the safety of this glade. The preservation of Azeroth is a common goal we both share.$B$BYou are among friends here, $N.\030For this task, Keeper Remulos' majordomo in Moonglade - Rabine Saturna - seeks aid in exploring the vast wastelands far to the west of Tanaris and Un'Goro.  He is located in Nighthaven, the main village of Moonglade.$B$BI want to impart on you the importance of your presence.  There are growing tensions between the night elves of Darnassus and the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade.  Look beyond racial boundaries and tap into the wisdom of your ancestors in dealings with the Circle there, $N.  Good luck.\030Speak with Rabine Saturna in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade.  Moonglade lies between Felwood and Winterspring, accessible through a path out of Timbermaw Hold.\030\030Rabine Saturna\0312,1,155,2,257,1,5769\0302,158,216,2,257,1,5769\0302,221,276,2,259,1,5769\0302,279,379,2,321,1,5769\0302,382,491,2,257,1,5769\0302,494,503,2,257,1,5769\0303,1,66,2,384,1,5769\0303,69,165,2,384,1,5769\0301,1,116,4,272,1,11801\0301,121,191,4,336,1,11801\0301,193,339,4,280,1,11801\0301,341,399,4,272,1,11801\0301,404,434,4,272,1,11801\03111832,2,1,Keeper Remulos\03011801,2,1,Rabine Saturna\03011801,2,7,Rabine Saturna\03011801,4,9,Rabine Saturna\03011832,4,9,Keeper Remulos\0312,1638,1456,0,\0302,0,0,1,Moonglade\0302,0,0,1,Tanaris\0302,0,0,2,Nighthaven\0302,0,0,4,Moonglade\0311124,23,1124,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1124]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Rabine sent you, did he? Well, consider yourself welcomed here... as much as this desolate and forsaken land can welcome someone.$B$BI wasn't alive during the time of the great tribulations that took place here, but there are parts of this desert that might as well be eerie pictures of that forgotten past. With your help, the Cenarion Circle might be able to bring finality to a threat that was supposed to have died generations ago.\030West of Un'Goro Crater, via the northwestern ridge, is a harsh wasteland - Silithus.  Few know that an ancient war was waged there between the night elves and a malign, alien power.  The evil was sealed, but now we suspect that forces work to stir this... unspeakable horror.$B$BSeek out Layo Starstrike, one of our agents in Silithus; look for him at Valor's Rest, the final resting spot for the fallen of the wastes.  Give him this letter, and he will give you his trust accordingly.\030Speak with Layo Starstrike near the Valor's Rest graveyard of Silithus, showing him Rabine's Letter.\030This is a dangerous land to be so casual, $C. What brings you to the wastes of Silithus?\030Wasteland\0312,1,84,2,257,1,11801\0302,87,181,2,325,1,11801\0302,184,255,2,257,4,11801\0302,257,275,2,257,1,11801\0302,280,418,2,257,1,11801\0302,421,485,2,257,3,11801\0303,1,100,2,384,1,11801\0301,1,24,4,272,2,13220\0301,26,65,4,272,1,13220\0301,67,129,4,272,1,13220\0301,134,307,4,272,4,13220\0301,309,435,4,340,4,13220\0304,1,45,3,256,1,13220\0304,47,88,3,256,2,13220\03113220,2,5,Layo Starstrike\0304950,2,5,Spot\03013220,2,7,Layo Starstrike\0312,493,1450,0,\0302,0,0,5,Silithus\0302,0,0,5,Valor's Rest\0302,0,0,7,Valor's Rest\0311125,23,1125,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1125]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I had thought that maybe the huge swirling hive near the ruins of the village had played a part in its demise. It would seem that your work has proven this to be correct; the proximity of the hive poses a threat to any future work we may do here.$B$BI thank you for your benevolence in freeing the souls of the fallen; such work is never easy, I know. When you're ready, however, I'd like to ask for your assistance once more...\030To our southwest lies a tragic site - the ruins of Southwind Village.  This is where our work should begin, $N.$B$BFrom what we've learned, this village was once a night elf base of operations for Silithus.  It's long since overrun by the silithid hives that infest the wastes.  I can only imagine the horror of the village's initial sundering...$B$BThe tortured spirits of fallen druids and sentinels wander the ruins aimlessly.  Explore this locale, freeing the souls of these wretched beings as needed.\030Free the spirits of 8 Tortured Druids and 8 Tortured Sentinels in Southwind Village, and then return to Layo Starstrike at the Valor's Rest graveyard of Silithus.\030Alliance or Horde, it doesn't matter - no being deserves to be trapped on this world as a tortured spirit.  The freeing of these souls will make things right, $N.\030The Spirits of Southwind\0312,1,69,2,321,1,13220\0302,72,111,2,257,1,13220\0302,116,206,2,257,1,13220\0302,209,277,2,257,1,13220\0302,280,346,2,321,1,13220\0302,351,429,2,321,1,13220\0302,432,505,2,257,1,13220\0303,1,162,2,384,1,13220\0301,1,110,4,336,4,13220\0301,112,246,4,276,4,13220\0301,251,351,4,272,1,13220\0301,353,428,4,274,1,13220\0304,1,106,3,256,1,13220\0304,109,162,3,256,3,13220\03113220,2,8,Layo Starstrike\0312,1377,1451,0,\0302,0,0,8,Southwind Village\0302,0,0,8,Layo Starstrike\0302,0,0,8,Valor's Rest\0311124,19,1124,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301126,23,1126,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,12178,OBJECTIVE,8,13,Tortured Druid\030NPC,12179,OBJECTIVE,8,13,Tortured Sentinel",[1126]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031What the... what is it?$B$BIt has the shape of a... box, maybe? It's encrusted over something fierce. Wait, there a portion here that's exposed... is that a book underneath all this gunk?$B$BI think you've stumbled across quite the find here, $N... well, at least I hope it is. Perhaps it is a journal or a log from ancient times, preserved in this shell.$B$BI think I know a way to find out what this is.\030The hive needs to be addressed in Southwind Village, and I think I know a way to get at them.  It's been my experience that the silithid hives are very sensitive to their environment; this explains their attacks when hearing the death wails of the spirits.$B$BThe silithid are strongest in the tower - the one with the mass of wasps circling it.  Scale the tower and jostle the hive into activity.  Report back what you learn, but be careful!  If you uncover anything that might help, bring it to me.\030Scale the tower of Southwind Village and locate a means to stir the silithid hive into activity.  Bring back anything unusual you may uncover when doing so to Layo Starstrike at the Valor's Rest graveyard of Silithus.\030Well, did it work? You're still in one piece, which is good news. Did you find anything?\030Hive in the Tower\0312,1,93,2,259,1,13220\0302,96,256,2,261,1,13220\0302,261,345,2,257,1,13220\0302,348,397,2,257,1,13220\0302,400,442,2,257,1,13220\0302,445,500,2,257,4,13220\0303,1,96,2,384,1,13220\0303,99,217,2,384,1,13220\0301,1,11,4,272,1,13220\0301,13,23,4,272,2,13220\0301,28,51,4,272,1,13220\0301,53,63,4,272,4,13220\0301,65,101,4,272,1,13220\0301,103,146,4,272,1,13220\0301,148,187,4,272,2,13220\0301,192,248,4,272,1,13220\0301,250,277,4,274,3,13220\0301,279,355,4,336,4,13220\0301,360,405,4,272,1,13220\0304,1,18,3,256,2,13220\0304,20,65,3,256,1,13220\0304,67,88,3,256,2,13220\03113220,2,8,Layo Starstrike\0312,1377,1451,0,\0302,0,0,1,Southwind Village\0302,0,0,8,Layo Starstrike\0302,0,0,8,Valor's Rest\0311125,19,1125,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306844,23,6844,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,17346,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1127]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, very good! Here is your pay.$B$BAnd here is a little something extra... for your discretion.\030So you want some Fool's Stout, eh?  Thinking of heading back to the races...?$B$BAll right, bring me more of Zanzil's mixture and I'll make some more stout for you.\030Bring 12 of Zanzil's Mixture to Crank Fizzlebub in Booty Bay.\030Do you have those Zanzil mixtures yet, $N?\030Fool's Stout\0312,1,34,2,259,2,2498\0302,37,77,2,257,2,2498\0302,82,164,2,257,1,2498\0303,1,61,2,384,1,2498\0301,1,14,4,272,1,2498\0301,16,32,4,272,1,2498\0301,37,75,4,272,1,2498\0301,77,96,4,272,1,2498\0304,1,42,3,256,2,2498\0312498,2,4,Crank Fizzlebub\0312,33,1434,0,\0302,0,0,4,Crank Fizzlebub\0302,0,0,4,Booty Bay\0311122,19,1122,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4016,OBJECTIVE,12,15,",[113]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you for delivering the report, Junior Surveyor $n; here is your pay for your diligent service to the Gadgetzan Water Company.$B$BWhile I am usually not thrilled about handing out our valuable information carte blanche to those who would otherwise pay good coin for it, I've known Pestlezugg for a number of years now.  If he recommends letting everyone know about it, then so be it.  Give me a moment and I'll make you a copy.\030Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser needs to see this report immediately.  Actually... everyone who can read needs to see this report.  We are facing a grave and serious threat to not only Tanaris and Gadgetzan, but if left unchecked, the entirety of southern Kalimdor.  Heck, even quite possible the whole of Azeroth; this thing has given no indication it will subside.$B$BHave Fizzledowser make a duplicate of the report for you to distribute freely to your allegiance. Everyone must know about this threat!\030Deliver the report to Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser in Gadgetzan.  Be sure he gives you a copy of the report, as Alchemist Pestlezugg has requested.\030Well Junior Surveyor $n, has ol' Pestlezugg got that report ready yet?\030Insect Part Analysis\0312,1,66,2,259,1,5594\0302,69,79,2,257,1,5594\0302,81,127,2,259,1,5594\0302,130,262,2,261,4,5594\0302,265,363,2,257,3,5594\0302,368,464,2,257,1,5594\0302,466,502,2,261,1,5594\0303,1,64,2,384,1,5594\0303,67,147,2,384,1,5594\0301,1,131,4,272,1,7724\0301,136,323,4,280,4,7724\0301,326,388,4,272,4,7724\0301,391,432,4,272,1,7724\0304,1,70,3,256,2,7724\0317724,2,1,Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser\0307724,2,8,Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser\0305594,2,9,Alchemist Pestlezugg\0312,440,1446,0,\0302,0,0,8,Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser\0302,0,0,8,Gadgetzan\0304,0,0,10,Gadgetzan Water Company\031110,19,110,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1130]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031So, $N, you have come. Now, are you prepared to journey through distant lands?$B$BIf so, young $C, then listen on...\030$N, Melor Stonehoof has heard of your deeds, and has set a path before you.$B$BIf you wish to take it, then go to Thunder Bluff and speak with Melor.  You will find him on Hunter's Rise.\030Speak with Melor Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff.\030\030Melor Sends Word\0312,1,75,2,257,1,3387\0302,80,149,2,259,4,3387\0302,152,186,2,257,3,3387\0303,1,44,2,384,1,3387\0301,1,22,4,272,1,3441\0301,24,78,4,272,2,3441\0301,83,116,4,272,4,3441\0313441,2,1,Melor Stonehoof\0303441,2,4,Melor Stonehoof\0312,1638,1456,0,\0302,0,0,2,Thunder Bluff\0302,0,0,4,Thunder Bluff\0311131,23,1131,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1131]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031In defeating the creature Steelsnap, you have cleansed the Thousand Needles of a horrible taint.$B$BAnd that, $N, is your lesson this day.\030At times we hunt for food.  At times we hunt for honor.  And at times we hunt to earn the Earthmother's teachings.$B$BBut the hunt I now set upon you is none of these things.  It is to slay a creature outside the Earthmother's blessing.$B$BThe hyena Steelsnap roams the Thousand Needles, south of the Barrens.  He is a tyrant, attracting other hyenas to him and spreading fear and bloodshed among more peaceful beasts.$B$BFind Steelsnap, $N.  Find him, and defeat him.\030Bring Steelsnap's Rib to Melor Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff.\030Have you defeated the foul Steelsnap, $N?\030Steelsnap\0312,1,26,2,257,1,3441\0302,29,55,2,257,1,3441\0302,58,114,2,257,1,3441\0302,119,174,2,257,1,3441\0302,177,236,2,257,1,3441\0302,241,309,2,257,1,3441\0302,312,418,2,257,1,3441\0302,423,441,2,257,1,3441\0302,444,468,2,257,1,3441\0303,1,58,2,384,1,3441\0301,1,96,4,272,1,3441\0301,101,138,4,272,1,3441\0304,1,41,3,256,2,3441\0314548,2,6,Steelsnap\0304548,2,8,Steelsnap\0303441,2,10,Melor Stonehoof\0304548,4,11,Steelsnap\0304548,3,13,Steelsnap\0312,1638,1456,0,\0302,0,0,5,Earthmother's\0302,0,0,6,Barrens\0302,0,0,10,Melor Stonehoof\0302,0,0,10,Thunder Bluff\0311130,19,1130,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301136,23,1136,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5837,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1132]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Good day to you! You were sent by Mr. Flint in Menethil Harbor? Well Mr. Flint is a strong judge of character. If he sent you, then there's no doubt you belong here in Kalimdor!\030Oh, to be at sea once again!  To feel the kiss of the wind, and to have the waves rock me like my blessed mother, long ago!$B$BOh, I wish I had your fortune, good $c, for I see the sea in your future!$B$BIt's my job to tell eager souls of the land of Kalimdor, the land of opportunity!  If you're willing to try your luck across the sea, then take a ship from here to the lovely port of Theramore.  Speak there with my partner, the elf, Fiora Longears.$B$BShe'll start you on your Kalimdor adventure!\030Speak with Fiora Longears on the docks at Theramore in Dustwallow Marsh.\030\030Fiora Longears\0312,1,28,2,257,1,4455\0302,31,123,2,321,1,4455\0302,128,200,2,259,3,4455\0302,205,285,2,257,1,4455\0302,288,397,2,257,4,4455\0302,400,452,2,257,1,4455\0302,457,500,2,257,1,4455\0303,1,72,2,384,1,4455\0301,1,16,4,272,1,4456\0301,18,37,4,272,1,4456\0301,39,63,4,272,2,4456\0301,65,72,4,272,1,4456\0301,74,110,4,272,1,4456\0301,112,177,4,272,4,4456\0314456,2,6,Fiora Longears\0304456,2,8,Fiora Longears\0312,11,1437,0,\0302,0,0,8,Theramore\0302,0,0,8,Dustwallow Marsh\0304,0,0,11,Menethil Harbor\0304,0,0,14,Kalimdor\0311133,23,1133,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1133]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You are here to offer your services to the Alliance, $N? We welcome the aid, for although its beauty remains... Ashenvale Forest is not the peaceful place it once was.\030If you're fresh off the boat from Menethil, then the first thing you should do is... go to Astranaar.  I'm sure an eager member of the Alliance such as you can do some real good there.  Speak with Shindrell Swiftfire and offer your services.$B$BBut don't bother mentioning who sent you.  Shindrell does not know me...\030Speak with Shindrell Swiftfire in Astranaar.\030\030Journey to Astranaar\0312,1,84,2,257,4,4456\0302,86,101,2,257,1,4456\0302,104,184,2,257,1,4456\0302,187,241,2,257,1,4456\0302,246,286,2,257,1,4456\0302,289,317,2,257,1,4456\0303,1,44,2,384,1,4456\0301,1,56,4,272,2,3845\0301,58,111,4,272,1,3845\0301,113,167,4,336,1,3845\0313845,2,4,Shindrell Swiftfire\0303845,2,7,Shindrell Swiftfire\0312,148,1439,0,\0302,0,0,1,Menethil\0302,0,0,2,Astranaar\0302,0,0,7,Astranaar\0304,0,0,8,Alliance\0311132,19,1132,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1134]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, $N. It saddens me to order the slaughter of creatures who may not willingly aid our enemies, yet it is my duty to do so.$B$BYour heart might weep for the pridewings you slew, my friend, but may your heart then swell in knowing that your allies are safe from the pridewings' venom.\030We are not in open war with the Horde, but our peace is fragile.  We often find their agents moving against us, but they do so covertly.$B$BOne such advance was revealed to us from hidden sources in Theramore, claiming that the orcs collect venom from the pridewings near Mirkfallon Lake, in the Stonetalon Mountains to the south.  Orc assassins then use the venom on their secret death raids against the Alliance!$B$BIf this is true, then we must stop them, $N.  We must deny them their source of venom.\030Bring 12 Pridewing Venom Sacs to Shindrell Swiftfire in Astranaar.\030Do you have the pridewing venom sacs, $N? We cannot allow the orcs to use the beasts' poisons against us!\030Pridewings of Stonetalon\0312,1,64,2,269,1,3845\0302,67,136,2,257,1,3845\0302,141,330,2,257,1,3845\0302,333,414,2,257,1,3845\0302,419,462,2,257,4,3845\0302,465,504,2,257,1,3845\0303,1,66,2,384,1,3845\0301,1,14,4,272,1,3845\0301,16,131,4,276,1,3845\0301,136,291,4,272,4,3845\0304,1,41,3,256,2,3845\0304,43,105,3,264,1,3845\0313845,2,7,Shindrell Swiftfire\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,3,Theramore\0302,0,0,3,Mirkfallon Lake\0302,0,0,3,Stonetalon Mountains\0302,0,0,7,Shindrell Swiftfire\0302,0,0,7,Astranaar\0311008,19,1008,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5808,OBJECTIVE,12,15,",[1135]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, most of these are nearly bursting with venom, $N. Such are normally only gathered from young wyverns, or fertile females. It must have been quite a slaughter up there in Highperch!\030As you may know, wyverns are often tamed by orcs for use as mounts.  But what is less known is that the venom of a wyvern, in some circles, is more valuable than the beast itself.  So if you're not afraid to do a little wyvern hunting, then... I have a job for you.$B$BThere is a place called Highperch in the land of a Thousand Needles, west of here.  The Highperch wyverns have a potent venom.  Potent, and valuable.\030Bring 10 Highperch Venom Sacs to Fiora Longears in Theramore.\030Did you find Highperch, $N? Any luck with the wyverns there?\030Highperch Venom\0312,1,67,2,257,1,4456\0302,70,179,2,257,1,4456\0302,182,243,2,257,4,4456\0302,245,265,2,257,1,4456\0302,270,351,2,257,1,4456\0302,354,395,2,257,1,4456\0302,398,418,2,257,1,4456\0303,1,61,2,384,1,4456\0301,1,53,4,272,1,4456\0301,55,125,4,272,1,4456\0301,127,184,4,272,1,4456\0304,1,27,3,256,2,4456\0304,29,60,3,256,2,4456\03110430,2,2,The Beast\0304456,2,8,Fiora Longears\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,8,Fiora Longears\0302,0,0,8,Theramore\0304,0,0,11,Highperch\031\031ITEM,5809,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[1136]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Both strength and cunning were needed to find and defeat Frostmaw, $N. You have both.$B$BYour path has taken you to the valleys of Thousand Needles and to the high mountains of Alterac. It will one day lead you through all the Earthmother's lands, for such is the way of the hunter.\030$N, it is now time for you to travel to far-off lands.  You are ready.$B$BYou now hunt Frostmaw, a yeti in the Alterac Mountains.  He is elusive, his white coat blending into the snows of his mountain home.  He rarely shows himself.$B$BBut I will show you how to entice a creature such as he.  Here, take this scroll.  On it I have written how Frostmaw may be lured.$B$BNow go, $N.  Your journey is long and many challenges lay waiting.  When you return with Frostmaw's mane, only then is your task complete.\030Bring Frostmaw's Mane to Melor Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff.\030Have you been to the Alterac Mountains, $N? Did you face the elusive Frostmaw?\030Frostmaw\0312,1,54,2,257,1,3441\0302,57,70,2,257,1,3441\0302,75,129,2,257,1,3441\0302,132,206,2,257,1,3441\0302,209,232,2,257,1,3441\0302,237,292,2,257,3,3441\0302,295,317,2,257,1,3441\0302,320,366,2,257,1,3441\0302,371,381,2,257,1,3441\0302,384,436,2,257,1,3441\0302,439,508,2,257,1,3441\0303,1,58,2,384,1,3441\0301,1,70,4,272,1,3441\0301,72,85,4,272,1,3441\0301,90,185,4,272,1,3441\0301,187,282,4,272,3,3441\0304,1,43,3,256,2,3441\0304,45,78,3,256,2,3441\0314504,2,3,Frostmaw\0304504,2,8,Frostmaw\0303441,2,12,Melor Stonehoof\0304504,4,13,Frostmaw\0304504,3,18,Frostmaw\0312,1638,1456,0,\0302,0,0,3,Alterac Mountains\0302,0,0,12,Melor Stonehoof\0302,0,0,12,Thunder Bluff\0303,0,0,17,Alterac Mountains\0311131,19,1131,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5811,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1137]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031$N, you're back! You found Martek? You spoke with him? What did he say? Can he help??$B$BTell me, tell me, tell me!!\030Indurium has an amazing resistance to heat!  I'm sure it will work for Fizzle's pistons.  But he'll need true indurium ore, not just the flakes.$B$BTo get the ore, it must be mined from deep within Uldaman, on the northern borders of the Badlands.  That is the true source of indurium.$B$BSend Fizzle Brassbolts my regards, and tell him what I told you.$B$BSafe travels, $N.  And it won't surprise me if we meet again -- once Fizzle learns of indurium he'll probably send you to Uldaman to acquire it!\030Speak with Fizzle Brassbolts in the Shimmering Flats.\030\030News for Fizzle\0312,1,43,2,257,1,4618\0302,46,88,2,257,3,4618\0302,91,144,2,259,1,4618\0302,149,247,2,257,1,4618\0302,250,285,2,257,1,4618\0302,290,353,2,257,1,4618\0302,358,374,2,257,1,4618\0302,377,501,2,257,4,4618\0303,1,53,2,384,1,4618\0301,1,16,4,272,1,4454\0301,18,34,4,272,2,4454\0301,36,54,4,272,2,4454\0301,56,71,4,272,2,4454\0301,73,85,4,272,2,4454\0301,90,116,4,272,1,4454\0314454,2,6,Fizzle Brassbolts\0304454,2,9,Fizzle Brassbolts\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,4,Uldaman\0302,0,0,8,Uldaman\0302,0,0,9,Shimmering Flats\0311108,19,1108,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301190,23,1190,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1138]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Wow, these fine crab chunks are what I need.  Thanks $N!  I found this while I was fishing a while ago, and I have no use for it.  Maybe you can do something with it.  It sure don't make any good crab dishes.$B$BI told you all about crabs, right?\030I love crab.  Crabs are the fruit of the sea!  You can bake it, barbecue it, boil it, and broil it.  They're pan fried, deep fried, and stir fried.  There's crab salad, crab soup, crab stew, pepper crab, lemon crab, whipper root crab, and Ironforge surprise crab.  That's... that's about it.$B$BI'm here fishing right now, so I can't get any fine crab chunks.  You can pick them out of reef crawlers and encrusted tide crawlers.  You can make a lot with it.  You can bake it, barbecue it, boil it...\030Collect 6 Fine Crab Chunks for Gubber Blump in Auberdine.\030...lemon crab, whipper root crab, and Ironforge surprise crab.  That's about it.$B$BOh, hello there $N.  Do you have them fine crab chunks I was telling you about?\030Fruit of the Sea\0312,1,12,2,257,1,10216\0302,15,45,2,257,1,10216\0302,48,99,2,257,1,10216\0302,102,147,2,257,1,10216\0302,150,263,2,257,1,10216\0302,266,274,2,257,1,10216\0302,276,291,2,257,1,10216\0302,296,359,2,257,1,10216\0302,362,428,2,257,1,10216\0302,431,457,2,257,1,10216\0302,460,499,2,257,1,10216\0303,1,57,2,384,1,10216\0301,1,44,4,274,1,10216\0301,47,56,4,272,1,10216\0301,59,129,4,272,1,10216\0301,132,166,4,272,4,10216\0301,169,208,4,272,1,10216\0301,213,246,4,272,2,10216\0304,1,62,3,256,1,10216\0304,65,80,3,256,1,10216\0304,85,103,3,256,1,10216\0304,106,163,3,256,2,10216\0316827,2,1,Crab\0306827,2,5,Crab\0306827,2,8,Crab\0306827,2,12,Crab\03010216,2,12,Gubber Blump\0306827,4,13,Crab\0306827,4,17,Crab\0306827,3,19,Crab\0306827,3,22,Crab\0312,148,1439,0,\0302,0,0,12,Auberdine\031\031ITEM,12237,OBJECTIVE,6,15,",[1139]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Advisor Belgrum shakes his head in disbelief as you hand him the stone shard.>$B$B$N, this is amazing. I shall have this brought to the king's mages as soon as possible. They will want to study it to find out if the legends are true. But that is a discussion for another time: you have aided our people more than I would have ever expected--thank you.\030We've slowed the Shadowforge clan by cutting them off from Blackrock Spire, but Hammertoe's quest is still unfulfilled. His death must not be in vain. He dreamt of finding the Tablet of Will: a stone shard inscribed with magic by the titans themselves to help imbue their creations with life--making them have a will of their own, or so the legends say.$B$BWe must still recover the Tablet before the Shadowforge clan finds it.$B$BReturn to Uldaman, find the tablet, and return here immediately.\030Find the Tablet of Will, and return them to Advisor Belgrum in Ironforge.\030Hammertoe's quest must be actualized, $N. I owe him that much.$B$BYour return to Uldaman is imperative not only to that goal, but also to the safety of all dwarven kind. With the tablet in the hands of the Dark Irons who knows how powerful their army of golems would become.\030The Lost Tablets of Will\0312,1,119,2,257,1,2918\0302,121,150,2,265,1,2918\0302,152,353,2,321,3,2918\0302,358,427,2,257,1,2918\0302,432,495,2,257,1,2918\0303,1,73,2,384,3,2918\0301,1,79,4,272,1,2918\0301,84,103,4,272,1,2918\0301,105,170,4,272,3,2918\0301,172,234,4,274,4,2918\0301,236,352,4,272,4,2918\0304,1,41,3,256,1,2918\0304,43,62,3,256,1,2918\0304,67,169,3,264,1,2918\0304,171,274,3,256,4,2918\0312918,2,6,Advisor Belgrum\0302918,4,7,Advisor Belgrum\0312,1517,1418,0,\0302,0,0,1,Blackrock Spire\0302,0,0,5,Uldaman\0302,0,0,6,Advisor Belgrum\0302,0,0,6,Ironforge\0303,0,0,14,Uldaman\031762,19,762,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5824,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[114]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh...my! I feel guilty deceiving my family, but my feelings for Tommy Joe are too strong to ignore.$B$BThank you, $N. I'll drink this liquor as soon as I have the chance and sneak away to my love.$B$BAnd for you... please take this.\030Take this invisibility liquor to young Maybell.  It should last long enough for her to visit Tommy Joe.\030Take the Invisibility Liquor to Maybell Maclure.\030Did you deliver my letter to Tommy Joe? What did he say??\030The Escape\0312,1,47,2,257,1,253\0302,50,103,2,257,1,253\0303,1,48,2,384,1,253\0301,10,99,4,272,1,251\0301,104,117,4,272,1,251\0301,119,196,4,272,1,251\0301,201,214,4,272,1,251\0301,216,232,4,272,1,251\0304,1,39,3,256,2,251\0304,41,57,3,256,2,251\031251,2,3,Maybell Maclure\0312,12,1429,0,\0302,0,0,3,Maybell Maclure\0303,0,0,9,Tommy Joe\031112,19,112,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1140]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030objectiveLabel3\030requestItems\030title\031Perhaps the satyrs have been allowed to persist in the forest for too long. I will speak with Elissa about it when next I travel to Auberdine.$B$BNonetheless, with the soulgems destroyed, Athrikus' power will be greatly diminished. We must seize on this opportunity to eliminate him and his cult.\030The writing of the orcs is little better than the scribblings of a child. Many of my order scoffed when I chose to learn their tongue, but I have found it beneficial to gain further understanding of my enemies.$B$BFrom Ilkrud's scribblings, it appears that Athrikus still possesses two soulgems, and they are being held in Night Run and Satyrnaar, satyr-held areas in northeast Ashenvale.$B$BBe careful out there, $n, the satyrs' blood-soaked temples can be unsettling even for a seasoned $c such as yourself.\030Free the trapped Highborne souls in Night Run and Satyrnaar, then return to Delgren the Purifier at Maestra's Post.\030\030Free the Highborne soul in Night Run\030Free the Highborne soul in Satyrnaar\030I heard whisper once that the satyrs' history is somehow related to that of the night elves, but I have found my esteemed hosts reticent to speak of the matter.\030The Tower of Althalaxx\0312,1,73,2,257,1,3663\0302,75,210,2,261,1,3663\0302,215,388,2,257,1,3663\0302,393,509,2,257,1,3663\0303,1,115,2,448,1,3663\0301,1,75,4,272,4,3663\0301,77,142,4,272,3,3663\0301,147,231,4,276,3,3663\0301,233,296,4,272,1,3663\0307,1,160,3,320,1,3663\0305,1,36,3,448,1,3663\0306,1,36,3,448,1,3663\0313663,2,5,Delgren the Purifier\0312,148,1439,0,\0302,0,0,3,Night Run\0302,0,0,5,Night Run\0302,0,0,5,Delgren the Purifier\0302,0,0,5,Maestra's Post\0304,0,0,7,Auberdine\0303,0,0,11,Night Run\0303,0,0,12,Satyrnaar\031973,19,973,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301167,23,1167,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,19901,OBJECTIVE,1,14,Circle of Imprisonment\030OBJECT,20352,OBJECTIVE,1,14,Circle of Imprisonment",[1141]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Them's some real nice groupers, $N!  Thanks for helping me out!$B$BYou're at least as good of a fisherman as my cousin, Graun Blump.  She also has a beard and she smells kinda funny, but that don't do nothing to stop her fishing.  I reckon you have what it takes to use a Blump Family Fishing Pole.\030I love fishing.  The Blump family is known for fishing.  My name is Gubber Blump; I fish.$B$BThere's a kind of fish I like to catch around these parts called Darkshore grouper.  I used to go out on a boat to fish for grouper, but no boats have been going out since them mean ol' murlocs moved in.  I bet they been eating up all the grouper too.$B$BSay, you wanna help me catch Darkshore grouper?  I'd give you a bona fide Blump Family Fishing Pole if you did!  It's a real good pole to catch fish with.\030Catch 6 Darkshore Grouper for Gubber Blump in Auberdine.\030There's plenty of good dishes you use Darkshore groupers for.  They're good to eat, but I think it's more fun catching them.$B$BYou caught any Darkshore groupers yet?\030The Family and the Fishing Pole\0312,1,15,2,257,1,10216\0302,18,55,2,257,1,10216\0302,58,89,2,257,1,10216\0302,94,176,2,257,1,10216\0302,179,296,2,257,1,10216\0302,299,344,2,257,1,10216\0302,349,395,2,257,2,10216\0302,398,459,2,257,4,10216\0302,462,502,2,257,1,10216\0303,1,56,2,384,1,10216\0301,1,35,4,272,1,10216\0301,38,63,4,272,1,10216\0301,68,132,4,272,1,10216\0301,135,229,4,272,1,10216\0301,232,298,4,272,1,10216\0304,1,61,3,256,1,10216\0304,64,124,3,256,1,10216\0304,129,166,3,256,2,10216\03110216,2,3,Gubber Blump\03010216,2,10,Gubber Blump\0312,148,1439,0,\0302,0,0,10,Auberdine\031\031ITEM,12238,OBJECTIVE,6,15,",[1142]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031No!$B$B'Tis not fair. Oh, cruel and intolerable world!$B$BI must now carry this burden of grief and not let Heralath's work die with him.$B$BYou were brave to journey from such a dangerous place, $N. But please leave me now.$B$BIn solitude I shall mourn.\030I have not long to live... so... so... weak.$B$B...the b-b-brave dwarf, Lonebrow, has been sent to w-w-warn Falfindel...$B$BBut before I... d-d-die...$B$B...my wife, Treshala... her pendant of bonding to me... stolen... by one of the f-f-foul aggressors...$B$BFind it p-p-please... and return it to Treshala in Darnassus...$B$B...along with w-w-word of my lonely... death.\030Find and return Treshala's Pendant to Treshala Fallowbrook in Darnassus.\030What brings you to my home, $R?\030Mortality Wanes\0312,1,26,2,257,1,4510\0302,40,44,2,257,1,4510\0302,49,120,2,257,1,4510\0302,125,139,2,257,1,4510\0302,141,150,2,257,1,4510\0302,155,177,2,257,1,4510\0302,179,209,2,257,1,4510\0302,211,219,2,261,1,4510\0302,221,256,2,257,1,4510\0302,261,281,2,257,1,4510\0302,283,323,2,257,1,4510\0302,328,365,2,257,1,4510\0302,367,372,2,257,1,4510\0303,1,72,2,384,1,4510\0301,8,21,4,272,1,4521\0301,23,54,4,272,1,4521\0301,59,137,4,272,1,4521\0301,142,199,4,272,1,4521\0301,201,224,4,272,1,4521\0301,229,254,4,272,3,4521\0304,1,31,3,256,2,4521\0314521,2,14,Treshala Fallowbrook\0312,1717,1413,0,\0302,0,0,11,Treshala\0302,0,0,11,Darnassus\0302,0,0,14,Treshala Fallowbrook\0302,0,0,14,Darnassus\031\031ITEM,5825,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1143]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031With the death of Athrikus, I hope that the demonic forces in this area will be driven back. I have no doubt that they will regroup and return, but then we shall be even more prepared to meet their threat.\030I see. Well, if what you say is true, then now is the time to strike. I believe Athrikus resides at the top of the tower. Be careful though, he is surrounded by many powerful warlocks, much more deadly than the ones you faced before.\030Kill Athrikus Narassin and bring his head to Balthule Shadowstrike near the Tower of Althalaxx.\030Athrikus Narassin is an ancient and powerful warlock. Perhaps we should wait for Delgren's assistance, but he obviously had much faith in you to send you alone.\030The Tower of Althalaxx\0312,1,6,2,257,1,3661\0302,8,69,2,257,4,3661\0302,71,121,2,257,4,3661\0302,123,233,2,257,1,3661\0303,1,95,2,384,1,3661\0301,1,92,4,274,3,3661\0301,94,205,4,276,3,3661\0304,1,53,3,320,1,3661\0304,55,160,3,256,4,3661\0313660,2,5,Athrikus Narassin\0303661,2,5,Balthule Shadowstrike\0303660,3,8,Athrikus Narassin\0312,148,1439,0,\0302,0,0,5,Balthule Shadowstrike\0302,0,0,5,Tower of Althalaxx\0311167,19,1167,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030981,23,981,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5383,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1144]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Thanks again, friend! I told you I'd make it worth your while.\030At last, help has arrived!$B$BYou have no clue how long I've been held prisoner here. I can't remember the last time I saw the outside of this place.$B$BYou see, I am an entrepreneur. Always out for a copper, as they say. I caught wind that Mebok Mizzyrix was paying well for Blueleaf Tuber from this here pig pen. I figured it would be an easy in, easy out kind of affair. As you can see, I was a bit wrong!$B$BAnyway, if you'd be so kind as to help me get out of here, I'll make it worth your while.\030Escort Willix the Importer out of Razorfen Kraul.\030Help Willix the Importer escape from Razorfen Kraul\030\030Willix the Importer\0312,1,26,2,257,1,4508\0302,31,85,2,257,1,4508\0302,87,149,2,257,1,4508\0302,154,183,2,257,1,4508\0302,185,221,2,257,1,4508\0302,223,314,2,257,1,4508\0302,316,373,2,257,4,4508\0302,375,408,2,257,1,4508\0302,413,501,2,257,4,4508\0303,1,49,2,384,1,4508\0301,1,21,4,272,1,4508\0301,23,62,4,272,1,4508\0304,1,51,3,384,1,4508\0313446,2,6,Mebok Mizzyrix\0304508,2,10,Willix the Importer\0304508,3,13,Willix the Importer\0312,1717,1413,0,\0303,0,0,13,Razorfen Kraul\031\031",[1145]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, a note from Korran. He has been a loyal servant for some time now. I was wondering how his duties were going in the Crossroads.\030Many travelers who've come through the Crossroads helped me gather eggs from the Field of Giants, and many of them have tales of how deadly the creatures are. I've heard enough to consider them insects a much larger threat than my masters first thought.$B$BI need a courier to travel to Orgrimmar to meet Belgrom Rockmaul. It be no simple matter, and someone who would take the task seriously should go.$B$BBelgrom usually be found outside the warriors' guild house.\030Deliver Korran's Sealed Note to Belgrom Rockmaul in Orgrimmar.\030I envy you, $C. You have the look of someone who's been outside the walls of Orgrimmar for a while.$B$BI myself would travel in the name of the Warchief if Thrall didn't have need of my skills here in the city. But he leads us well, and I trust his judgement - I remain here for as long as he needs me.\030The Swarm Grows\0312,1,158,2,257,1,3428\0302,160,253,2,261,1,3428\0302,258,322,2,259,1,3428\0302,324,403,2,257,4,3428\0302,408,466,2,257,1,3428\0303,1,62,2,384,1,3428\0301,1,23,4,272,1,4485\0301,25,70,4,272,1,4485\0301,72,131,4,272,1,4485\0304,1,15,3,256,1,4485\0304,17,99,3,256,1,4485\0304,104,210,3,258,4,4485\0304,212,302,3,258,1,4485\0314485,2,3,Belgrom Rockmaul\0304485,2,6,Belgrom Rockmaul\0303428,4,7,Korran\0304949,3,12,Thrall\0312,17,1413,0,\0302,0,0,1,Field of Giants\0302,0,0,3,Orgrimmar\0302,0,0,6,Belgrom Rockmaul\0302,0,0,6,Orgrimmar\0304,0,0,7,Korran\0304,0,0,9,Crossroads\0311146,23,1146,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1146]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Don't mind the thundering echoes off the mountains' walls. The goblins and gnomes are out among the Flats racing one another in atrocities created by what they call science. There are bigger threats here in Thousand Needles, one of which killed more than half my war party.$B$BBut we remain here until we hear word from Belgrom in Orgrimmar. Until then, we hold our position here, and stay vigilant.\030So, Korran has come to a similar conclusion about these insects--they seem to be a larger threat than we assumed.$B$BA few days ago a hunter returned to me from Thousand Needles nearly dead. He was with a raiding party sent to drive a dwarven excavation team out of the Shimmering Flats. During the attack, more of these insects erupted from a cave in the dig site and nearly killed the party.$B$BThey were led by Moktar Krin, and they've taken refuge on the border of the Shimmering Flats. Bring him this note.\030Deliver Belgrom's Sealed Note to Moktar Krin in Thousand Needles.\030War brings my group and I to the Shimmering Flats, $C. What brings you here?\030The Swarm Grows\0312,1,113,2,261,4,4485\0302,118,190,2,257,1,4485\0302,192,287,2,257,1,4485\0302,289,393,2,261,1,4485\0302,398,490,2,257,1,4485\0302,492,511,2,257,1,4485\0303,1,65,2,384,1,4485\0301,1,58,4,272,1,4483\0301,60,173,4,272,1,4483\0301,175,273,4,276,1,4483\0301,278,341,4,272,1,4483\0301,343,399,4,272,1,4483\0304,1,54,3,260,1,4483\0304,56,76,3,256,2,4483\0313428,2,1,Korran\0304483,2,5,Moktar Krin\0304483,2,7,Moktar Krin\0312,1637,1454,0,\0302,0,0,2,Thousand Needles\0302,0,0,7,Moktar Krin\0302,0,0,7,Thousand Needles\0304,0,0,10,Thousand Needles\0304,0,0,11,Belgrom\0304,0,0,11,Orgrimmar\0303,0,0,13,Shimmering Flats\0311145,19,1145,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301147,23,1147,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1147]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ha! That ichor you're covered in actually makes you prettier, $N! It certainly does make you reek at the same time though. Don't stand too close to the kodo; you'll either start a stampede or cause them to go into heat.$B$BI think my companions would agree that your smell alone is proof you've done your part to help us against those insect creatures. Thank you, $N.\030Hmm. Seems Belgrom thinks those monsters are a threat. He wants them pushed back into whatever depths they crawled up out of.$B$BI guess killing the dwarves sent by the Explorers' League wasn't enough--now I have to send a half-dead war party into another battle. We won't be able to do it ourselves; not while we're in this condition. The dig site's to the south of here. There shouldn't be anymore dwarves to deal with. Feel up to wielding a blade or staff and doing your part to aid us?\030Kill 5 Silithid Searchers, 5 Silithid Hive Drones, and 5 Silithid Invaders and return to Moktar Krin in Thousand Needles.\030With the amount of travelers heading out to the Flats for those races, I'm sure we can convince enough adventure seekers to help push back those insects. My party and I won't be able to leave until we do.\030The Swarm Grows\0312,1,4,2,257,1,4483\0302,6,54,2,261,4,4483\0302,56,125,2,259,1,4483\0302,130,263,2,261,1,4483\0302,265,335,2,257,1,4483\0302,337,372,2,257,1,4483\0302,374,421,2,257,1,4483\0302,423,489,2,257,2,4483\0303,1,121,2,388,1,4483\0301,5,65,4,272,1,4483\0301,67,122,4,272,1,4483\0301,124,219,4,272,1,4483\0301,224,352,4,272,4,4483\0301,354,367,4,272,1,4483\0304,1,153,3,256,1,4483\0304,155,204,3,256,1,4483\0314483,2,9,Moktar Krin\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,9,Moktar Krin\0302,0,0,9,Thousand Needles\0303,0,0,15,Flats\0311146,19,1146,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,4130,OBJECTIVE,5,13,Silithid Searcher\030NPC,4133,OBJECTIVE,5,13,Silithid Hive Drone\030NPC,4131,OBJECTIVE,5,13,Silithid Invader",[1148]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ahh, you've seen Moktar recently? He always be lookin' out for me. I'm sorry to hear he spends his time watching over his little war band instead of seeing battle, but I'm sure he be takin' great joy in killing members of the Explorers' League.$B$BYou be smart to bring me these specimens, $N. Along with the eggs we be findin' in the Field of Giants, these should give me a good start in figuring out what these insects are, and what they be wantin'.\030You inspect the carapace carefully. As you turn it over in your hands you realize that the chitinous plating is interlaced in such a way that makes it incredibly strong. It's unlike anything you've ever seen. You inspect the rest of the corpse further and realize that these creatures are very powerful and highly evolved.$B$BLooking down at the carapace again, you think that Korran would enjoy studying more of these creatures. It could help him figure out what these creatures are, and where they come from.\030Bring 1 Silithid Heart, 5 Silithid Talons, and 3 Intact Silithid Carapaces, to Korran at the Crossroads.\030Ah, it been a long time since you've come to see me, $N. What can I do for you today? You be looking like you've seen the face of battle recently. Good... good for the Horde and good for you. The more battle you've seen, the more helpful you'll be; stronger, too.\030Parts of the Swarm\0312,1,35,2,257,1,0\0302,37,169,2,257,1,0\0302,171,208,2,257,1,0\0302,210,322,2,257,1,0\0302,327,429,2,257,4,0\0302,431,510,2,257,4,0\0303,1,104,2,384,1,0\0301,1,33,4,272,2,3428\0301,35,66,4,272,1,3428\0301,68,244,4,276,1,3428\0301,249,293,4,272,1,3428\0301,295,451,4,272,1,3428\0304,1,56,3,256,1,3428\0304,58,85,3,256,2,3428\0304,87,146,3,260,1,3428\0304,148,154,3,256,1,3428\0304,156,191,3,256,1,3428\0304,193,263,3,260,1,3428\0313428,2,5,Korran\0303428,2,7,Korran\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,7,Korran\0302,0,0,7,Crossroads\0304,0,0,12,Field of Giants\0311184,23,1184,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5877,STARTER,?,10,\030ITEM,5855,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,5854,OBJECTIVE,5,15,\030ITEM,5853,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[1149]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It is not until faced with unforeseen adversity that we begin to see how strong our spirits are. You took the leap of faith even though you had no guarantees that you would survive. Your mind is open, and your spirit is prepared for what is to come.$B$BIf you are willing, then the next of your tests is ready.\030So, you have sought me out, or perhaps destiny brings you to me? No matter. You are here now, and so your journey will begin anew.$B$BMany facets make up a being: the spirit, the body, the mind. Some of these can be measured by a culture's traditions. Others we can only hope exist within ourselves. If you agree, I shall test some of the facets within you.$B$BIf you pass, then you shall become stronger. If you fail, then you will realize the vastness of the Nether.$B$BThe first is a Test of Faith.\030If you have faith, leap from the planks overlooking Thousand Needles.\030Faith. It is far more important than some realize.$B$BIt does not matter what you believe sometimes. It is just important that you believe in something.\030Test of Faith\0312,1,64,2,257,4,2986\0302,66,75,2,257,1,2986\0302,77,130,2,257,3,2986\0302,135,194,2,257,1,2986\0302,196,251,2,257,1,2986\0302,253,299,2,259,3,2986\0302,301,357,2,257,4,2986\0302,362,405,2,257,4,2986\0302,407,468,2,257,4,2986\0302,473,501,2,257,1,2986\0303,1,69,2,384,4,2986\0301,1,96,4,272,1,2986\0301,98,181,4,280,4,2986\0301,183,249,4,272,1,2986\0301,254,310,4,272,4,2986\0304,1,6,3,256,1,2986\0304,8,50,3,256,1,2986\0304,55,100,3,256,4,2986\0304,102,152,3,256,4,2986\031\0312,400,1441,0,\0311150,23,1150,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[115]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, $N. I'll send these to be destroyed immediately.\030The Blackrock orcs enlisted shadowcasters to aid their attacks in Redridge, and they have brought with them devices of dark power--midnight orbs.  These orbs have struck telling blows against Redridge's defenders, and it's imperative we remove the demon-tainted items from the conflict.$B$BFind and deliver to me midnight orbs from slain Blackrock shadowcasters.  I will then have them disposed of, for this world would be a better place without them!\030Bring 3 Midnight Orbs to Marshal Marris in Lakeshire.\030How goes your conflict with the shadowcasters? Did you find the midnight orbs?\030Shadow Magic\0312,1,145,2,261,1,382\0302,148,286,2,257,1,382\0302,291,362,2,261,1,382\0302,365,451,2,257,4,382\0303,1,53,2,384,1,382\0301,1,14,4,272,1,382\0301,16,59,4,276,1,382\0304,1,46,3,256,2,382\0304,48,78,3,256,2,382\031382,2,5,Marshal Marris\0312,44,1433,0,\0302,0,0,1,Redridge\0302,0,0,5,Marshal Marris\0302,0,0,5,Lakeshire\03120,19,20,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,1261,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[1150]="PARTIAL\031loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Grenka was powerful, even by troll standards. You should be proud of your accomplishment this day.$B$BDuring your test of faith you displayed strength of spirit, and now you have shown endurance in battle by taking on the Roguefeather harpies, but the time has come for a new test.\030I'm pleased to see your courage remains steadfast in light of what you've already done. Since your faith is intact, the time has come to test your body.$B$BFirst is a test of endurance. Go to the Roguefeather Den west of Freewind Post. Make your way to the depths of their lair and destroy their foodstuffs. By then you should have provoked their fury, and if you are able to survive long enough, Grenka Bloodscreech herself will come for you--kill her and bring me her claw to complete your test.\030Bring Grenka's Claw to Dorn Plainstalker in Thousand Needles.\030You must be prepared spiritually, physically and mentally for the challenges that lie ahead of you.$B$BToo often do we rush forward before we are ready. I consider it my duty to the youth, no matter which tribe they belong to, to prepare them for the dangers they may face after they leave the sanctity of their home.\030Test of Endurance\0312,1,87,2,257,1,2986\0302,89,152,2,257,1,2986\0302,157,185,2,257,1,2986\0302,187,235,2,257,1,2986\0302,237,307,2,261,1,2986\0302,309,497,2,265,4,2986\0303,1,61,2,384,1,2986\0301,1,45,4,272,1,2986\0301,47,98,4,272,1,2986\0301,103,281,4,308,1,2986\0304,1,99,3,256,1,2986\0304,104,152,3,264,1,2986\0304,154,317,3,256,1,2986\0314490,2,6,Grenka Bloodscreech\0302986,2,7,Dorn Plainstalker\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,4,Roguefeather Den\0302,0,0,4,Freewind Post\0302,0,0,7,Dorn Plainstalker\0302,0,0,7,Thousand Needles\0311149,19,1149,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301151,23,1151,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5843,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1151]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The Test of Strength is done. You have shown strength and bravery, and you are now prepared for the final test before these rites are completed.\030During the time of the Old Gods, elementals inhabited much of this world. They worshipped the Old Gods, and the Gods, through their power, kept the elementals bound to this world. When the Old Gods were banished, the elementals faded from our world and now only return at the bidding of powerful mages.$B$BThere are exceptions though. Some elementals were powerful enough to remain here on their own. One such elemental is Rok'Alim.$B$BTo test your strength, find Rok'Alim in Thousand Needles and slay him.\030Bring Fragments of Rok'Alim to Dorn Plainstalker in Thousand Needles.\030Rok'Alim is also called the Pounder by the centaur tribes in Thousand Needles because of the thundering his fists make as he pummels the creatures brave, or stupid, enough to stand in his path.\030Test of Strength\0312,1,73,2,321,1,2986\0302,75,179,2,325,1,2986\0302,181,302,2,321,1,2986\0302,307,334,2,257,1,2986\0302,336,400,2,257,1,2986\0302,402,432,2,257,1,2986\0302,437,506,2,257,1,2986\0303,1,69,2,384,1,2986\0301,1,29,4,272,1,2986\0301,31,144,4,272,1,2986\0304,1,193,3,258,1,2986\0312986,2,8,Dorn Plainstalker\03093,3,11,Centaur\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,7,Thousand Needles\0302,0,0,8,Dorn Plainstalker\0302,0,0,8,Thousand Needles\0303,0,0,11,Thousand Needles\0311150,19,1150,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301152,23,1152,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5844,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1152]="PARTIAL\031conflict,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The days and nights grow colder throughout the world as goblins rape the land, and the night elves point fingers at the younger races. The Forsaken and orcs are not the only ones to blame for the hardships found throughout Kalimdor and Lordaeron. Many of the intelligent races have contributed to the world's pain. Dorn knows this, and he has sent you to me because you have shown the attributes necessary to realize it also.$B$BNow you stand before Braug.\030Your time with me is just about finished. I am knowledgeable, but the Test of Lore is not mine to give. There are lessons to be learned and places to visit that others claim domain over.$B$BIf you are prepared, then seek out Braug Dimspirit--he is a shaman of great wisdom. He will test you further, so heed his words, $N.$B$BWhen you are ready, find the tunnel that connects the Stonetalon Mountains with Ashenvale: Braug dwells near there. And be careful, $N, the night elves may wish to impede your test.\030Find Braug Dimspirit near the entrance to Talondeep Path in Stonetalon Mountains.\030\030Test of Lore\0312,1,41,2,257,1,2986\0302,43,103,2,257,1,2986\0302,105,186,2,257,1,2986\0302,191,273,2,259,4,2986\0302,275,322,2,257,3,2986\0302,327,441,2,257,1,2986\0302,443,507,2,259,3,2986\0303,1,81,2,384,1,2986\0301,1,134,4,272,1,4489\0301,136,246,4,272,1,4489\0301,248,314,4,272,1,4489\0301,316,425,4,274,1,4489\0301,430,456,4,304,1,4489\0314489,2,4,Braug Dimspirit\0304489,2,8,Braug Dimspirit\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,8,Talondeep Path\0302,0,0,8,Stonetalon Mountains\0311151,19,1151,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301154,23,1154,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1153]="PARTIAL\031loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A good sample, $N. A good sample indeed.$B$BThose travelers can no longer lord over me the ore they found, now that you have been successful.$B$BI shall get to work on it immediately. If it proves strong enough, I will send a weapon crafted from the material back to the warchief to show him our success.$B$BI shall not forget your help, $C.\030$C, you have done well in helping me in the past. The warchief is pleased thus far with what I've accomplished, and asks me to continue with renewed determination. My honor dictates that I give you proper recognition to the warchief for all you have done, but first I would ask you for your help again.$B$BTravelers recently came from the south from a place called Thousand Needles. There they killed a kobold who had an unusual ore sample, but they would not sell it. I want a sample of that ore to examine.\030Find an Unrefined Ore Sample on a Gravelsnout Digger or Surveyor and bring it to Tatternack Steelforge at Camp Taurajo in the Barrens.\030I saw the travelers again - the ones that would not sell me a sample of the ore. I spit at them for not helping the warchief.$B$BMay they die in battle like cowards and not like warriors as should be the right of all people who ally themselves with the Horde.\030A New Ore Sample\0312,1,49,2,257,1,3433\0302,51,163,2,257,1,3433\0302,165,302,2,257,4,3433\0302,307,382,2,257,1,3433\0302,384,468,2,257,4,3433\0302,470,508,2,259,1,3433\0303,1,134,2,384,1,3433\0301,1,18,4,272,1,3433\0301,20,40,4,272,1,3433\0301,45,141,4,304,1,3433\0301,146,183,4,272,3,3433\0301,185,304,4,272,4,3433\0301,309,341,4,272,3,3433\0304,1,80,3,256,4,3433\0304,82,125,3,256,1,3433\0304,130,259,3,260,1,3433\0314113,2,7,Gravelsnout Digger\0303433,2,7,Tatternack Steelforge\0312,17,1413,0,\0302,0,0,7,Tatternack Steelforge\0302,0,0,7,Camp Taurajo\0302,0,0,7,Barrens\031893,19,893,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5842,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1154]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is the book I named. There is hope you will answer my question correctly then... unless you've forgotten to study its contents.$B$BWhen you are prepared, speak to me again and I shall ask a question of you.\030You have passed Dorn's tests, and now you seek to pass your next trial. Very good. But up until now, your challenges have been childish. It is easy to test your body--your mind is another matter completely.$B$BI shall explain it simply: find the book I name, study it, and answer my question about its contents.$B$BWhat book, you must be asking? The Legacy of the Aspects. It can be found at the bottom of Dor'danil in southern Ashenvale, protected by the dead druids and their slayers.\030Find the Legacy of the Aspects and return it to Braug Dimspirit near the entrance to Talondeep Path in Stonetalon Mountains.\030Bring me the book after you've studied it. I will not ask you your question until after you have given me the book.\030Test of Lore\0312,1,71,2,259,1,4489\0302,73,82,2,257,1,4489\0302,84,136,2,257,1,4489\0302,138,206,2,257,1,4489\0302,211,311,2,257,3,4489\0302,316,345,2,257,2,4489\0302,347,372,2,257,1,4489\0302,374,486,2,257,1,4489\0303,1,124,2,384,1,4489\0301,1,25,4,272,1,4489\0301,27,85,4,274,3,4489\0301,87,132,4,280,4,4489\0301,137,211,4,272,3,4489\0304,1,42,3,256,1,4489\0304,44,115,3,256,3,4489\0314489,2,9,Braug Dimspirit\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,9,Braug Dimspirit\0302,0,0,9,Talondeep Path\0302,0,0,9,Stonetalon Mountains\0311152,19,1152,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306627,23,6627,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5860,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1159]="PARTIAL\031loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Braug sent you? Impossible.$B$B<Parqual looks you up and down.>$B$BBraved Dor'Danil, took a leap of faith, fought and overpowered a powerful elemental? Bah! You're probably a farce; some adventurer that overheard talk in a tavern. And now you think you have what it takes to pass my test. So be it... $C.\030Well done, $N. You have passed the first portion of the Test of Lore, but there is still another question to be answered. But that question is not mine to ask.$B$BSeek out Parqual Fintallas in Lordaeron City. He was a great historian for the humans before the Plague overtook him. Now he continues to seek enlightenment, but of a different nature.$B$BHe will have another requirement of you before he asks you anything, but you have done masterfully thus far--I'm sure you will overcome his obstacle.\030Find Parqual Fintallas in Undercity.\030\030Test of Lore\0312,1,14,2,257,1,4489\0302,16,121,2,257,1,4489\0302,123,159,2,257,1,4489\0302,164,208,2,257,1,4489\0302,210,280,2,261,1,4489\0302,282,347,2,259,1,4489\0302,352,500,2,265,3,4489\0303,1,36,2,384,1,4489\0301,1,15,4,272,2,4488\0301,17,27,4,272,1,4488\0301,32,63,4,272,1,4488\0301,68,151,4,272,2,4488\0301,153,156,4,272,1,4488\0301,158,230,4,272,1,4488\0301,232,288,4,304,1,4488\0314488,2,4,Parqual Fintallas\0304488,2,8,Parqual Fintallas\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,4,Lordaeron City\0302,0,0,8,Undercity\0316627,19,6627,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301160,23,1160,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[116]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A job well done, $N! I know well the roads you had to journey to procure this fine array of liquor. But my patrons will be happy once again! $B$BMy wife is quite a seamstress. Please accept this cloak she made in return for your services.\030I find myself in quite a pinch here, $N.  The bottles are close to running dry.  The latest booze shipment is long overdue.  The orc invasion has been hell.$B$BPerhaps you can go to work for me?$B$BI need you to pick up a keg of Thunderbrew Lager from Grimbooze Thunderbrew in the Westfall hills, a cask of Merlot from Stormwind, a bottle of Moonshine from Darkshire and a skin of Sweet Rum from Goldshire.  Bring those back to me and I will see to it you are rewarded.\030Barkeep Daniels of Lakeshire needs a keg of Thunderbrew Lager, a cask of Merlot, a bottle of Moonshine and a skin of Sweet Rum.\030I need you to pick up a keg of Thunderbrew Lager from Grimbooze Thunderbrew in the Westfall hills, a cask of Merlot from Stormwind, a bottle of Moonshine from Darkshire and a skin of Sweet Rum from Goldshire. Bring those back to me and I will see to it you are rewarded.\030Dry Times\0312,1,40,2,257,1,346\0302,43,79,2,257,1,346\0302,82,123,2,257,1,346\0302,126,156,2,261,1,346\0302,161,194,2,257,4,346\0302,199,406,2,259,1,346\0302,409,469,2,257,3,346\0303,1,127,2,386,1,346\0301,1,20,4,272,1,346\0301,22,99,4,272,1,346\0301,101,140,4,272,3,346\0301,146,175,4,272,1,346\0301,177,238,4,272,1,346\0304,1,208,3,258,1,346\0304,210,270,3,256,3,346\031239,2,6,Grimbooze Thunderbrew\030346,2,8,Barkeep Daniels\030239,3,14,Grimbooze Thunderbrew\0312,44,1433,0,\0302,0,0,6,Grimbooze Thunderbrew\0302,0,0,6,Westfall\0302,0,0,6,Stormwind\0302,0,0,6,Darkshire\0302,0,0,6,Goldshire\0303,0,0,14,Grimbooze Thunderbrew\0303,0,0,14,Westfall\0303,0,0,14,Stormwind\0303,0,0,14,Darkshire\0303,0,0,14,Goldshire\031\031ITEM,1262,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,1941,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,1942,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,1939,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1160]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is the book I sent you to search for.$B$B<Parqual slowly caresses his hand over the top of the book as he stares down at it.>$B$BSo now you wish a question to prove your mind is as powerful as your body and spirit. If you have studied the book long enough, then I shall ask you your question and you can be done with these tests!\030I will tell you what you must seek, and I will even ask you my question, but not because you wish to prove yourself. Knowledge is far more important than strength. Even as others seem to pass you by in ability, your knowledge of the world will be more valuable.$B$BGo to the Monastery in the north of Tirisfal Glades. In the library there, a book called Beginnings of the Undead Threat resides. It was used by the now-corrupt paladins there to train them to fight my kind.$B$BBring it to me.\030Find The Beginnings of the Undead Threat, and return it to Parqual Fintallas in Undercity.\030I hope you made the Scarlet Crusade suffer some before stealing the book from them.$B$BMy views of their kind are not unwarranted. The Crusade may have been followers of the Light at one time, but now, they seek to destroy any creatures that have not sided with their religion. They believe all undead, Forsaken or otherwise, must be cleansed, and those traveling in their lands must either be insane, or subject to the undead's powerful magics. Idiots. Idiots and fools; all of them.\030Test of Lore\0312,1,116,2,259,3,4488\0302,118,163,2,257,1,4488\0302,165,261,2,257,4,4488\0302,266,317,2,257,1,4488\0302,319,394,2,261,1,4488\0302,396,472,2,261,1,4488\0302,477,491,2,257,1,4488\0303,1,90,2,388,1,4488\0301,1,42,4,272,1,4488\0301,47,130,4,272,1,4488\0301,135,219,4,274,3,4488\0301,221,334,4,272,4,4488\0304,1,83,3,262,3,4488\0304,88,130,3,256,1,4488\0304,132,277,3,262,1,4488\0304,279,445,3,264,4,4488\0304,447,453,3,256,1,4488\0304,455,484,3,256,1,4488\0314488,2,8,Parqual Fintallas\0312,796,0,0,\0302,0,0,4,Monastery\0302,0,0,4,Tirisfal Glades\0302,0,0,8,Parqual Fintallas\0302,0,0,8,Undercity\0311159,19,1159,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306628,23,6628,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5861,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1164]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You stand before me as a figure of vengeance, and I bow down before you in thanks.$B$BWith that cow's death, and knowing that their seed will no longer spread over the face of Azeroth, I can put my energy into something more lucrative. I hope you looted their farmstead after you finished them off.\030The harlot! The swine! Kenata still lives; her family healthy and prospering while I suffer. Forsaken indeed!$B$BMy family is gone, taken by the plague. Our estate also forfeit; looted and burned during the war. And after all that, her and her lousy children had the audacity to steal the only precious belongings I had left.$B$BI don't care about the things they stole any more. What I want now are their heads!$B$BKill them for me! Go to the Dabyrie Farmstead in Arathi, northeast of Refuge Point.\030Bring Kenata, Fardel, and Marcel Dabyrie's Heads to Genavie Callow in Undercity.\030Kill them all and bring me their heads!\030To Steal From Thieves\0312,1,11,2,257,1,4486\0302,13,22,2,257,1,4486\0302,24,92,2,261,1,4486\0302,94,109,2,257,1,4486\0302,114,152,2,261,1,4486\0302,154,211,2,261,1,4486\0302,213,325,2,261,1,4486\0302,330,379,2,257,1,4486\0302,381,412,2,259,1,4486\0302,417,433,2,257,1,4486\0302,435,499,2,257,1,4486\0303,1,80,2,384,1,4486\0301,1,82,4,274,1,4486\0301,87,235,4,272,3,4486\0301,237,298,4,274,3,4486\0304,1,39,3,256,1,4486\03110685,2,2,Swine\03014528,2,7,Precious\0304481,2,12,Marcel Dabyrie\0304486,2,12,Genavie Callow\0312,1497,1458,0,\0302,0,0,11,Dabyrie Farmstead\0302,0,0,11,Arathi\0302,0,0,12,Genavie Callow\0302,0,0,12,Undercity\031\031ITEM,5830,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,5832,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,5831,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1166]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You good $r. Me miss things very much. Me like you now.\030Bow before Overlord Mok'Morokk!$B$BRexxar make me mighty leader of Stonemaul Clan!$B$BMe good leader. Me keep clan safe.$B$BBig dragons come and make fire at old home. Me smart ogre. Find new home for clan here.$B$BLeave old home so fast, me forget stuff. Tiny $r, go get my things. Go south and find my yummy grog, my snuff and my strongbox. Me like you after you do that. You look in Den of Flame and Stonemaul Ruins... they be there, me sure!\030Overlord Mok'Morokk in Brackenwall Village wants you to retrieve his grog, snuff and strongbox in Dustwallow Swamp.\030Me thirsty for grog. Me miss snuff too. Where is strongbox? You go get for Overlord Mok'Morokk.$B$BGo find south in old home. Me too busy leading ogres to get.\030Overlord Mok'Morokk's Concern\0312,1,31,2,257,1,4500\0302,36,82,2,257,1,4500\0302,87,101,2,257,1,4500\0302,103,120,2,257,1,4500\0302,125,167,2,257,1,4500\0302,169,182,2,257,1,4500\0302,184,211,2,257,1,4500\0302,216,255,2,257,1,4500\0302,257,282,2,257,1,4500\0302,284,342,2,257,1,4500\0302,344,373,2,257,1,4500\0302,375,421,2,321,1,4500\0302,423,445,2,257,1,4500\0303,1,115,2,386,1,4500\0301,1,12,4,272,1,4500\0301,14,38,4,272,1,4500\0301,40,55,4,272,1,4500\0304,1,20,3,256,1,4500\0304,22,39,3,256,1,4500\0304,41,59,3,256,2,4500\0304,61,95,3,256,1,4500\0304,100,125,3,256,1,4500\0304,127,159,3,256,1,4500\0314500,2,1,Overlord Mok'Morokk\03010182,2,2,Rexxar\030211,2,6,Ogre\0304500,2,14,Overlord Mok'Morokk\0304500,3,21,Overlord Mok'Morokk\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,12,Den of Flame\0302,0,0,14,Brackenwall Village\0302,0,0,14,Dustwallow Swamp\031\031ITEM,5834,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,5835,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,5836,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1167]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, it's good to see you again, $N! The strangest things have been happening around here, I'm glad you showed up!$B$BIt was very strange, $N. Everything seemed normal--well, as normal as things get around here--and then suddenly there was a blinding flash of light from the upper room of the tower. Then came the screams. The cries split the air, and lightning struck the ground from time to time. What's going on?\030Before confronting Athrikus, it would probably be wise for you to consult with Balthule. I have no doubt he has been vigilant in his watch of the Tower, and he may have information about recent developments.\030Speak with Balthule Shadowstrike near the Tower of Althalaxx.\030\030The Tower of Althalaxx\0312,1,88,2,257,4,3663\0302,90,207,2,257,1,3663\0303,1,61,2,384,1,3663\0301,1,35,4,272,1,3661\0301,37,113,4,272,1,3661\0301,118,141,4,272,1,3661\0301,143,298,4,272,1,3661\0301,300,321,4,272,1,3661\0301,323,397,4,272,1,3661\0301,399,414,4,272,2,3661\0313661,2,3,Balthule Shadowstrike\0312,148,1439,0,\0302,0,0,3,Tower of Althalaxx\0311140,19,1140,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301143,23,1143,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1168]="PARTIAL\031consequences,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You kill many of the black dragon army. You brave $r.$B$BMake Tharg happy.\030Mok'Morokk was made Overlord by Rexxar. He care more for power than he care for ogres.$B$BBlack dragons kill many ogre. Kill Tharg's wife. Mok'Morokk tell us to run. Make us come here.$B$BOgre should fight. Ogres not good at running. Mok'Morokk care only about Mok'Morokk.$B$BMe call Stonemaul Ruins home. Me like it in the south. This place not home.$B$BHelp ogres fight army of the black dragon. Me want revenge. Me want to go home.\030Tharg in Brackenwall Village wants you to kill 10 Firemane Scouts, 10 Firemane Ash Tails, and 5 Firemane Scalebanes.\030Mok'Morokk tell all ogres to stay and keep this place safe. Me think ogres need to kill black dragon army and get old home back.$B$BYou help ogres get home back. Help ogres get revenge.\030Army of the Black Dragon\0312,1,39,2,257,1,4502\0302,41,86,2,257,1,4502\0302,91,119,2,257,1,4502\0302,121,138,2,257,1,4502\0302,140,165,2,257,1,4502\0302,167,184,2,257,1,4502\0302,189,206,2,261,1,4502\0302,208,233,2,257,1,4502\0302,235,272,2,257,1,4502\0302,277,305,2,321,1,4502\0302,307,330,2,257,1,4502\0302,332,351,2,257,1,4502\0302,356,397,2,261,1,4502\0302,399,414,2,259,1,4502\0302,416,434,2,259,1,4502\0303,1,116,2,386,1,4502\0301,1,39,4,272,1,4502\0301,41,53,4,272,1,4502\0301,58,74,4,272,1,4502\0304,1,59,3,256,1,4502\0304,61,128,3,258,1,4502\0304,133,161,3,256,1,4502\0304,163,185,3,258,1,4502\03110182,2,1,Rexxar\030211,2,3,Ogre\030211,2,7,Ogre\0304502,2,16,Tharg\0304502,4,19,Tharg\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,16,Brackenwall Village\031\031NPC,4329,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Firemane Scout\030NPC,4331,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Firemane Ash Tail\030NPC,4328,OBJECTIVE,5,13,Firemane Scalebane",[1169]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031'Twas a perilous affair, no doubt, collecting all of these hearts and tongues. I shall delve into the depths of the arcane to trace the origin of the black menace which has descended upon our former home.\030Whilst that craven fool, Mok'Morokk, wallows in power and Tharg wrestles the demons of sorrow and vengeance and vies for leadership of the clan, I seem to be the only one concerned with identifying the source of aggression on our old home.$B$BWhy the puzzled stare, $n? Expecting me to speak like an uncouth ruffian merely because I am an ogre?$B$BNow back to business, bring to me the hearts and tongues from the whelps and hatchlings. I shall trace the root of this evil...\030Draz'Zilb in Brackenwall Village would like you to bring him 15 Searing Tongues and 15 Searing Hearts.\030With the hearts and tongues of scorched offspring of the black dragon army, I can decipher what wretched beast introduced her spawn into our home. Perhaps with a greater knowledge of our aggressors, we can seek to destroy them once and for all and reclaim Stonemaul Village from ruin.$B$BOf course, convincing Mok'Morokk to move his lethargic, fat mass out of this muck hole is going to be an epic quest in and of itself...\030Identifying the Brood\0312,1,239,2,259,4,4501\0302,244,269,2,257,2,4501\0302,271,344,2,259,2,4501\0302,349,436,2,257,1,4501\0302,438,475,2,257,3,4501\0303,1,102,2,384,4,4501\0301,1,78,4,272,1,4501\0301,80,204,4,272,3,4501\0304,1,146,3,256,1,4501\0304,148,284,3,262,4,4501\0304,289,423,3,256,3,4501\0314502,2,1,Tharg\030211,2,3,Ogre\0304501,2,6,Draz'Zilb\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,6,Brackenwall Village\0311170,23,1170,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5840,OBJECTIVE,15,15,\030ITEM,5841,OBJECTIVE,15,15,",[117]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hops and Barley, yeast and malt $BThe taste-buds feel a virtual assault, $BNo need to plead, no need to beg $BFor Thunderbrew Lager comes in a keg!\030Hurry, my friend, move with haste $BIn order for our rich lager to taste $BMore like beer and less like stew, $BHops are needed to make the brew.\030Bring Grimbooze Thunderbrew 5 hops to complete his special brew.\030Hurry, my friend, move with haste $BIn order for our rich lager to taste $BMore like beer and less like stew, $BHops are needed to make the brew.\030Thunderbrew Lager\0312,1,34,2,257,1,239\0302,37,73,2,257,1,239\0302,76,110,2,257,1,239\0302,113,145,2,257,1,239\0303,1,64,2,384,1,239\0301,1,32,4,272,1,239\0301,35,73,4,272,1,239\0301,76,108,4,274,1,239\0301,111,147,4,272,1,239\0304,1,34,3,256,1,239\0304,37,73,3,256,1,239\0304,76,110,3,256,1,239\0304,113,145,3,256,1,239\031239,2,5,Grimbooze Thunderbrew\0312,40,1436,0,\031\031ITEM,1274,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[1170]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Why you tell me 'bout dragons? Me no like dragons. Me like it here. No dragons here.\030Stonemaul Village was invaded by the brood of Onyxia. But why would the daughter of the black dragonlord, Deathwing, descend upon our lands?$B$BThis is most troubling. Surely, Onyxia was driven here for a purpose beyond laying siege to a small band of ogres.$B$BNotify Mok'Morokk at once! Action must be taken.\030Speak with Overlord Mok'Morokk in Brackenwall Village.\030\030The Brood of Onyxia\0312,1,53,2,261,1,4501\0302,55,140,2,257,4,4501\0302,145,167,2,257,1,4501\0302,169,258,2,257,1,4501\0302,263,288,2,257,1,4501\0302,290,310,2,257,1,4501\0303,1,54,2,384,1,4501\0301,1,30,4,272,2,4500\0301,32,50,4,272,1,4500\0301,52,67,4,272,1,4500\0301,69,84,4,272,1,4500\03110184,2,1,Onyxia\03010184,2,4,Onyxia\0304500,2,7,Overlord Mok'Morokk\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,7,Brackenwall Village\0311169,19,1169,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301171,23,1171,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1171]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031That lazy coward!$B$BMok'Morokk displayed strength when Rexxar was our leader. But soon after Rexxar's departure Mok'Morokk fell prey to temptations of power. Rather than lead, he demanded. He does not serve his people but rather expects us to serve him.$B$BSomething must be done.\030You leave me alone now. Go tell Draz'Zilb we stay here. No black dragon here.\030Speak with Draz'Zilb in Brackenwall Village.\030\030The Brood of Onyxia\0312,1,23,2,257,1,4500\0302,25,55,2,257,1,4500\0302,57,77,2,257,1,4500\0303,1,44,2,384,1,4500\0301,1,17,4,272,1,4501\0301,22,78,4,272,1,4501\0301,80,158,4,272,1,4501\0301,160,189,4,272,1,4501\0301,191,254,4,272,1,4501\0301,259,281,4,272,1,4501\0314501,2,2,Draz'Zilb\0304501,2,4,Draz'Zilb\03010182,4,6,Rexxar\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,4,Brackenwall Village\0311170,19,1170,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301172,23,1172,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1172]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030requestItems\030title\031Splendid! It will be sometime before Onyxia can produce more eggs.$B$BOn behalf of my people, I thank you, $n.$B$BI have asked much of you so far. Perhaps you can do the Stonemaul Clan one last service.$B$BMok'Morokk is not fit to lead us. Tharg would make an excellent leader but is hindered by his injuries and age. Drive Mok'Morokk from this place by force. Only then can we appoint a new leader to return us to our proper home in the south.\030Onyxia's brood has been scattered across the Dragonmurk. It is imperative that no more whelps be permitted to hatch.$B$BMake haste to Wyrmbog in the south of Dustwallow Marsh. Surely, she has made her lair there. Track down the evil dragon's eggs and destroy them.$B$BWe will never reclaim Stonemaul Village if the surrounding area remains a breeding ground.$B$BAs for Mok'Morokk... I have other plans for the sod.\030Draz'Zilb in Brackenwall Village wants you to destroy 5 Eggs of Onyxia.\030\030Egg of Onyxia destroyed\030You must hurry to the Dragonmurk, $n. With Onyxia's eggs riddled around the Wyrmbog, we face overwhelming numbers unless something is done quickly.$B$BDestroy her eggs! Don't let the black dragon plague spread across our homeland!\030The Brood of Onyxia\0312,1,56,2,257,1,4501\0302,58,116,2,257,1,4501\0302,121,175,2,257,1,4501\0302,177,212,2,257,1,4501\0302,214,264,2,261,1,4501\0302,269,358,2,257,4,4501\0302,363,382,2,257,1,4501\0302,384,414,2,257,1,4501\0303,1,71,2,390,1,4501\0301,1,9,4,272,1,4501\0301,11,66,4,272,3,4501\0301,71,110,4,272,1,4501\0301,115,146,4,272,1,4501\0301,148,202,4,272,4,4501\0301,207,239,4,272,1,4501\0301,241,317,4,272,4,4501\0301,319,360,4,272,1,4501\0301,362,444,4,272,1,4501\0306,1,37,3,256,1,4501\0306,39,147,3,264,4,4501\0306,152,168,3,260,1,4501\0306,170,230,3,260,1,4501\0305,1,23,3,388,1,4501\0314501,2,9,Draz'Zilb\03010184,2,9,Onyxia\03010184,4,11,Onyxia\0304502,4,16,Tharg\03010184,3,23,Onyxia\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,3,Wyrmbog\0302,0,0,3,Dustwallow Marsh\0302,0,0,9,Brackenwall Village\0303,0,0,19,Dragonmurk\0311171,19,1171,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301173,23,1173,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,20359,OBJECTIVE,5,14,Egg of Onyxia",[1173]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031That cowardly fat mass Mok'Morokk fled like a scared child. You have done a great service, $N.$B$BNow my people can appoint a new leader, one who will help us reclaim our old home once and for all.\030You dare challenge Overlord Mok'Morokk?$B$BHaw!$B$BMe crush tiny $r!$B$BYou tell me when ready for good beating.\030Defeat Mok'Morokk and report the news to Draz'Zilb in Brackenwall Village.\030Drive Overlord Mok'Morokk from Brackenwall Village\030I thought you were going to attempt to drive Mok'Morokk out of the village. Instead you have come to me to chat?\030Challenge Overlord Mok'Morokk\0312,1,39,2,257,2,4500\0302,44,47,2,257,1,4500\0302,52,68,2,257,1,4500\0302,73,112,2,257,1,4500\0303,1,74,2,384,1,4500\0301,1,59,4,272,1,4501\0301,61,94,4,272,1,4501\0301,99,197,4,272,3,4501\0305,1,75,3,256,3,4501\0305,77,112,3,256,2,4501\0304,1,50,3,384,1,4500\0314500,2,1,Overlord Mok'Morokk\0304501,2,5,Draz'Zilb\0304500,3,11,Overlord Mok'Morokk\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,5,Draz'Zilb\0302,0,0,5,Brackenwall Village\0303,0,0,11,Brackenwall Village\0311172,19,1172,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1175]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I hope you didn't kill any of the basilisks on the tracks themselves! It takes a long time for the carcasses to decay in the sun, and I'd rather not have to take a shovel out to clean up.\030After the big crash with the goblins' Red Thunder racer and a basilisk, Kronkrider hired me on to take care of the track. I don't know what all the animals out on the flats are feeding on to grow so big, but we have to be careful to thin them out so they won't wander onto the track when a race is going on.$B$BTell you what. If you want to go out and make a little profit, go out and remove the basilisks from the area.\030Kill 10 Saltstone Basilisks, 10 Saltstone Crystalhides and 6 Saltstone Gazers for Trackmaster Zherin on the Shimmering Flats.\030It's bad enough having to clear out the wreckage of the racers without having to pick them out of burnt animal parts.\030A Bump in the Road\0312,1,121,2,257,1,4629\0302,123,307,2,257,1,4629\0302,312,325,2,257,1,4629\0302,327,420,2,259,4,4629\0303,1,125,2,384,1,4629\0301,1,69,4,274,3,4629\0301,71,187,4,272,1,4629\0304,1,117,3,256,1,4629\0314629,2,5,Trackmaster Zherin\0312,400,1441,0,\031\031NPC,4147,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Saltstone Basilisk\030NPC,4151,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Saltstone Crystalhide\030NPC,4150,OBJECTIVE,6,13,Saltstone Gazer",[1176]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Great! I can get the crew working on this right away. Thanks, $n!\030When it comes to racing, every bit counts! Whether it's a minor tweaking on the power output, a slight slackening on the tension coils, or lightening the weight of the frame, you have to take everything into account.$B$BWe use vulture bones for a lot of the minor structural tweaks we make to our racers, which offer the perfect balance of strength and weight. Even better, it's easy for us to get more, as the salt flats are littered with vultures.$B$BBring me some and I'll give you a good price on them.\030Get 10 Hollow Vulture Bones for Pozzik in the Shimmering Flats.\030Do you have those bones for me? I was just about to start working on lightening the steering rig, but I don't want to open her up without all the parts I need.\030Load Lightening\0312,1,42,2,257,1,4630\0302,44,216,2,257,1,4630\0302,221,360,2,265,1,4630\0302,362,449,2,257,1,4630\0302,454,506,2,257,1,4630\0303,1,63,2,384,1,4630\0301,1,6,4,272,1,4630\0301,8,53,4,272,1,4630\0301,55,65,4,272,1,4630\0304,1,31,3,256,2,4630\0304,33,159,3,258,1,4630\0314630,2,6,Pozzik\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,6,Shimmering Flats\0311178,23,1178,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5848,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[1177]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Me like fishy head!$B$BMe no eat you now.\030Mud big ogre.$B$BMe hungry.$B$BGo bash fishy. Bring Mud food.$B$BYou feed Mud or Mud eat you.\030Mudcrush Durtfeet in northern Dustwallow wants 8 Mirefin Heads.\030Gimme food or me eat you.\030Hungry!\0312,1,13,2,257,1,4503\0302,18,27,2,257,1,4503\0302,32,45,2,257,1,4503\0302,47,61,2,257,1,4503\0302,66,93,2,257,1,4503\0303,1,63,2,386,1,4503\0301,1,19,4,272,1,4503\0301,24,41,4,272,1,4503\0304,1,25,3,256,1,4503\031211,2,1,Ogre\0304503,2,6,Mudcrush Durtfeet\0312,15,1445,0,\031\031ITEM,5847,OBJECTIVE,8,15,",[1178]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Pozzik sent you, huh? You know, Pozzik was one of the most respected tinkerers in Undermine before he retired to start working on the racers.$B$BThe first thing he did when he joined the team was develop the two engine model racers. Could be that the businesses will suffer without him working with the Tinkers' Union, but who cares, right? There's nothing like the races!\030Our racing team is the pride of goblins everywhere. You'd be surprised at some of the people who contribute in one way or another to our team.$B$BYou know Gazlowe? He tracks down parts from around the world for us. He even came down to work on one of our rigs once!$B$BA few weeks ago, he said he'd send us a new prototype fuel regulator but it hasn't come yet. He's usually very prompt... Maybe you wouldn't mind going to Ratchet to ask him about it? I wouldn't be so pushy, but the gnomes are gaining on us!\030Speak to Gazlowe in Ratchet.\030\030Goblin Sponsorship\0312,1,51,2,257,1,4630\0302,53,142,2,257,1,4630\0302,147,163,2,257,2,4630\0302,165,214,2,257,1,4630\0302,216,265,2,257,1,4630\0302,270,361,2,257,1,4630\0302,363,389,2,257,1,4630\0302,391,451,2,257,4,4630\0302,453,509,2,257,1,4630\0303,1,28,2,384,1,4630\0301,1,21,4,272,2,3391\0301,23,141,4,280,1,3391\0301,146,232,4,272,1,3391\0301,234,340,4,276,4,3391\0301,342,372,4,272,1,3391\0313391,2,3,Gazlowe\0303391,2,10,Gazlowe\0304630,4,11,Pozzik\0304630,4,12,Pozzik\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,8,Ratchet\0302,0,0,10,Gazlowe\0302,0,0,10,Ratchet\0304,0,0,12,Undermine\0311176,19,1176,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301180,23,1180,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1179]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah! Longbeard sent you with a load of helmets! Hooray!$B$BNow maybe we can talk a pilot into driving our car...\030You ever heard of the Shimmering Flats?  It's a stretch of salt flats way over in Kalimdor, just south of the Thousand Needles canyon.  It's a great place for racing because, well, it's so flat!$B$BA couple of gnome brothers are out there, friends of mine, trying out their new rocket car, and from what I hear it's fast!  Heh, so fast that their pilots keep crashing.  Giving themselves concussions.$B$BSo they asked me for some Siege Engine helmets, but I have duties here.  I can't make the trip!$B$BCan you?\030Bring the crate of crash helmets to Wizzle Brassbolts in the Shimmering Flats.\030Watch where you're stepping! Watch watch watch!! This is delicate stuff you see here, and if we're to win then it must all work perfectly!\030The Brassbolts Brothers\0312,1,39,2,257,2,2092\0302,42,134,2,257,1,2092\0302,137,194,2,259,1,2092\0302,199,321,2,257,1,2092\0302,324,368,2,257,1,2092\0302,371,400,2,257,1,2092\0302,405,475,2,257,1,2092\0302,478,499,2,257,1,2092\0302,504,511,2,257,2,2092\0303,1,78,2,384,1,2092\0301,5,46,4,272,1,4453\0301,48,54,4,272,1,4453\0301,59,111,4,272,4,4453\0304,1,28,3,256,1,4453\0304,30,48,3,256,1,4453\0304,50,138,3,256,4,4453\0314453,2,10,Wizzle Brassbolts\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,2,Kalimdor\0302,0,0,2,Thousand Needles\0302,0,0,10,Wizzle Brassbolts\0302,0,0,10,Shimmering Flats\031\031",[118]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Heh, so old Verner needs some shoes, does he!?!\030I've been using so much iron keeping the Stormwind Guards outfitted, I don't have enough to supply the stable's horses with shoes!$B$BTake this note to Blacksmith Argus in Goldshire.  It explains to him my problem and requests a shipment of horseshoes.\030Take Verner's Note to Smith Argus in Goldshire.\030What's that? Verner sent you, you say? Well give me his note. And SPEAK UP!\030The Price of Shoes\0312,1,130,2,257,1,415\0302,135,182,2,257,1,415\0302,185,252,2,261,1,415\0303,1,47,2,384,1,415\0301,1,47,4,274,2,514\0304,1,12,3,256,2,514\0304,14,38,3,256,2,514\0304,40,61,3,256,1,514\0304,63,75,3,256,1,514\031514,2,4,Smith Argus\0312,44,1433,0,\0302,0,0,2,Blacksmith Argus\0302,0,0,2,Goldshire\0302,0,0,4,Smith Argus\0302,0,0,4,Goldshire\031119,23,119,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1180]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Shipments to Ratchet? Let me just check the logbooks...$B$BNo, the most recent shipment I have on record of going out to Ratchet were boots from Drizzlik. Hasn't been much else, other than building supplies and tools. Definitely no race parts.\030Back to what you came here about. I know I promised Pozzik that I'd deliver a new fuel regulator for him, but I still haven't received it yet. Revilgaz over in Booty Bay said he'd have it shipped over, but it might be it slipped through the cracks somehow.$B$BIf that's true, there's not much we can do about it. We can at least find out if it was dispatched from Booty Bay.$B$BCheck in with Wharfmaster Lozgil over there, he should be able to check the cargo records.\030Speak with Wharfmaster Lozgil in Booty Bay.\030\030Goblin Sponsorship\0312,1,33,2,257,1,3391\0302,35,142,2,257,1,3391\0302,144,256,2,257,4,3391\0302,261,312,2,257,4,3391\0302,314,374,2,257,4,3391\0302,379,468,2,257,1,3391\0303,1,43,2,384,1,3391\0301,1,21,4,272,2,4631\0301,23,55,4,272,1,4631\0301,60,154,4,272,1,4631\0301,156,217,4,272,1,4631\0301,219,243,4,272,1,4631\0314630,2,2,Pozzik\0304631,2,6,Wharfmaster Lozgil\0304631,2,7,Wharfmaster Lozgil\0302495,4,10,Drizzlik\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,3,Booty Bay\0302,0,0,5,Booty Bay\0302,0,0,7,Booty Bay\0304,0,0,8,Ratchet\0304,0,0,10,Ratchet\0304,0,0,10,Drizzlik\0311178,19,1178,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301181,23,1181,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1181]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh, sure of course I know what you're talking about. Nope, can't help you though. Some of my men were supposed to go track down the blueprints for the fuel regulator, but they came back empty-handed.\030I'm afraid I can't be of much more help to you, $n. If you'd like to follow up on it more, I'd suggest you go hit up the Baron himself. If there's anyone who knows Revilgaz's business, it's Revilgaz.$B$BYou'll find him at the tavern across the harbor, top floor.\030Speak with Baron Revilgaz in Booty Bay.\030\030Goblin Sponsorship\0312,1,51,2,257,1,4631\0302,53,135,2,257,4,4631\0302,137,199,2,257,4,4631\0302,204,262,2,257,1,4631\0303,1,39,2,384,1,4631\0301,1,52,4,272,1,2496\0301,54,81,4,272,1,2496\0301,83,199,4,272,1,2496\0312496,2,5,Baron Revilgaz\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,5,Booty Bay\0311180,19,1180,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301182,23,1182,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1182]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Now, let me just get a copy of these blueprints for my own notes and you can bring these straight to Pozzik. Wouldn't want him to think that one of his sponsors was abandoning him.\030See, the Venture Company shredders out in Lake Nazferiti (in northern Stranglethorn) have been equipped with a new model fuel regulator. I was thinking that Pozzik would be able to take advantage of it, if he could get some details. Unfortunately, Cozzle, the foreman out there, appears to be a little more clever than I gave him credit for.$B$BYou seem like you might have more luck finding the blueprints though. I know he keeps them in his house, but they're almost certainly under lock and key.\030Bring the Fuel Regulator Blueprints to Baron Revilgaz in Booty Bay.\030Much as I hate to admit it, that gnome team they have out there is pretty good. Our boys need every edge they can get.\030Goblin Sponsorship\0312,1,136,2,257,1,2496\0302,138,232,2,257,4,2496\0302,234,341,2,257,1,2496\0302,346,414,2,257,4,2496\0302,416,498,2,257,1,2496\0303,1,67,2,384,1,2496\0301,1,108,4,272,1,2496\0301,110,180,4,272,1,2496\0304,1,79,3,256,1,2496\0304,81,118,3,258,1,2496\0314630,2,2,Pozzik\0302496,2,6,Baron Revilgaz\0304630,4,7,Pozzik\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,1,Lake Nazferiti\0302,0,0,6,Baron Revilgaz\0302,0,0,6,Booty Bay\0304,0,0,7,Pozzik\0311181,19,1181,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301183,23,1183,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5852,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1183]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I was hoping that it would be already assembled, but this does present the unique opportunity to improve on the design from the ground up. Thanks, $N. I'll be able to sketch up some improved schematics, build the thing, and have it installed real soon.\030You should be all set to go. Give Pozzik my regards and tell him that if he ever needs anything, not to hesitate to ask. I'll be waiting for the news that he breaks the track record soon!\030Deliver the Fuel Regulator Blueprints to Pozzik on the Shimmering Flats.\030$N! Did you manage to track down the fuel regulator?\030Goblin Sponsorship\0312,1,28,2,257,1,2496\0302,30,120,2,259,4,2496\0302,122,187,2,257,1,2496\0303,1,72,2,384,1,2496\0301,1,138,4,272,4,4630\0301,140,150,4,272,1,4630\0301,152,252,4,272,1,4630\0304,5,52,3,256,2,4630\0314630,2,2,Pozzik\0304630,2,4,Pozzik\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,4,Pozzik\0311182,19,1182,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301186,23,1186,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1184]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I'm appreciative of your efforts, $c. The warchief will enjoy hearing how tenacious you have been in your duties.$B$BOh, of course I will mention your name to him. He speaks to me often and values my opinions greatly.$B$BGo now, I have much to do. And if you speak to Korran soon, and he has news of these creatures, then return to me--I would think they are a threat that must be taken seriously.\030Head back to Belgrom in Orgrimmar and tell him Moktar be doing his bidding well out in the Thousand Needles. Tell him also, that me studies progress, and I hope to be havin' learned more soon. That should please him greatly.\030Return to Belgrom Rockmaul in Orgrimmar.\030\030Parts of the Swarm\0312,1,108,2,257,1,3428\0302,110,192,2,259,3,3428\0302,194,224,2,257,1,3428\0303,1,40,2,384,1,3428\0301,1,37,4,272,1,4485\0301,39,113,4,272,3,4485\0301,118,163,4,272,3,4485\0301,165,217,4,272,1,4485\0301,222,247,4,272,1,4485\0301,249,397,4,276,4,4485\0314485,2,4,Belgrom Rockmaul\0303428,4,10,Korran\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,1,Belgrom\0302,0,0,1,Orgrimmar\0302,0,0,1,Thousand Needles\0302,0,0,4,Belgrom Rockmaul\0302,0,0,4,Orgrimmar\0304,0,0,10,Korran\0311148,19,1148,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1185]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hey, it's you again! Well, I mean you - as in the you that is $N! Yes - that you!$B$BHey, let me start over!$B$BThat object you found in Silithus - it was in fact a book. It was a journal written in a very ancient dialect of what we now call the Darnassian tongue. It'll take a while, but I'm going to go over it very thoroughly. I thought you should know that what you found was extremely valuable for the Circle.$B$BThe den mother's all excited and everything!\030\030\030\030Under the Chitin Was...\0311,1,20,4,272,1,11939\0301,22,65,4,272,1,11939\0301,67,81,4,272,1,11939\0301,86,108,4,272,1,11939\0301,113,170,4,272,1,11939\0301,172,264,4,336,1,11939\0301,266,329,4,272,3,11939\0301,331,414,4,272,1,11939\0301,419,462,4,272,1,11939\0316788,4,9,Den Mother\0312,493,1450,0,\0304,0,0,5,Silithus\0316845,19,6845,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1186]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You're the $R that's been helping Pozzik out, right? I was like you once, running around the pit area, helping with whatever work the mechanics would let me do.$B$BNow look at me! The goblin racing team's pilot extraordinaire!\030I'm going to be busy with working on integrating this new fuel regulator to our racer designs, but if you'd like to help out the team some more, talk to Razzeric. He's our pilot--well, our eighteenth pilot, to be exact--and he likes to add his own little modifications to the racers.$B$BHe's a little off his rocker, though, so try not to act too surprised.\030Speak with Razzeric on the Shimmering Flats.\030\030The Eighteenth Pilot\0312,1,162,2,257,4,4630\0302,164,283,2,257,1,4630\0302,288,357,2,257,1,4630\0303,1,44,2,384,1,4630\0301,1,52,4,272,2,4706\0301,54,160,4,272,4,4706\0301,165,179,4,272,1,4706\0301,181,226,4,272,1,4706\0314706,2,1,Razzeric\0304706,2,4,Razzeric\0304630,4,5,Pozzik\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,1,Razzeric\0311183,19,1183,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301187,23,1187,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1187]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Just take a look at this beauty! Fifteen pounds of solid seaforium power! Once I get this strapped on to the side of my racer, I'll be around the track so fast I'll beat the gnomes twice!\030Pozzik's a great mechanic, I know that, but he's afraid to just load on the firepower and grab on for the ride. Not me, though.$B$BAfter Pozzik finishes with a racer, I take a little time to put my own modifications on--you know, loosening up the controls, removing parts of the frame, and adding more juice!$B$BI ordered a seaforium booster from Shreev at the Gizmorium in Gadgetzan, but apparently the zeppelin it was being sent on crashed in Dustwallow Marsh! I gotta have it, $n!\030Retrieve the Seaforium Booster for Razzeric in the Shimmering Flats.\030How'm I supposed to show my face around the track without a little extra kick to get me going? It's a travesty, I tell you.\030Razzeric's Tweaking\0312,1,111,2,257,1,4706\0302,113,127,2,257,1,4706\0302,132,308,2,257,1,4706\0302,313,462,2,257,4,4706\0302,464,483,2,257,1,4706\0303,1,68,2,384,1,4706\0301,1,32,4,272,1,4706\0301,34,73,4,272,1,4706\0301,75,187,4,272,1,4706\0304,1,94,3,256,2,4706\0304,96,123,3,256,1,4706\0314630,2,3,Pozzik\0304708,2,4,Shreev\0304706,2,6,Razzeric\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,4,Shreev\0302,0,0,4,Gizmorium\0302,0,0,4,Gadgetzan\0302,0,0,4,Dustwallow Marsh\0302,0,0,6,Shimmering Flats\0311186,19,1186,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301188,23,1188,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5862,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1188]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Only Razzeric would take a look at this and say that I'd somehow put some sort of safety lock on it. This booster is almost completely seaforium explosives. I already modified it so that more of its payload would be delivered upon use, but Razzeric is never content unless he goes to eleven!\030But wait, what's this? Shreev left the safety on. That will limit the amount of power I can draw from the booster at any time. I told him I wanted it off! This is no good.$B$BYou have to take this to the Gadgetzan Gizmorium in the Tanaris Desert and have Shreev remove this.\030Bring the Seaforium Booster to Shreev in Gadgetzan.\030As I'm sure you know, the Gizmorium can service all of your tinkering needs! How can I help you?\030Safety First\0312,1,22,2,257,2,4706\0302,24,49,2,265,1,4706\0302,51,126,2,257,3,4706\0302,128,154,2,257,1,4706\0302,156,171,2,257,1,4706\0302,176,274,2,257,1,4706\0303,1,51,2,384,1,4706\0301,1,100,4,280,4,4708\0301,102,156,4,272,1,4708\0301,158,291,4,282,4,4708\0304,1,76,3,258,1,4708\0304,78,96,3,256,2,4708\0314708,2,2,Shreev\0304708,2,6,Shreev\0304708,2,7,Shreev\0304706,4,8,Razzeric\0304706,4,10,Razzeric\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,6,Gadgetzan Gizmorium\0302,0,0,6,Tanaris Desert\0302,0,0,7,Shreev\0302,0,0,7,Gadgetzan\0311187,19,1187,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301189,23,1189,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1189]="PARTIAL\031conflict,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Now that's more like it! I wish I could see the look on the gnomes' eyes when they see me set this baby off.$B$BToo bad I'll be too busy pulling off a new course record!\030There, I did what Razzeric wanted. Just tell him to be careful when he sets this off. If he makes the slightest mistake, he won't be moving forward, he'll just be a burnt spot on the track.$B$BWould be a shame, too, if that happened. Who knows if our nineteenth driver would be any good?\030Return the Modified Seaforium Booster to Razzeric on the Shimmering Flats.\030Can you believe Pozzik put a bucket of sand on the racer? How am I supposed to hit my maximum speed with a bucket of sand under the seat?\030Safety First\0312,1,34,2,257,1,4708\0302,36,85,2,257,1,4708\0302,87,189,2,257,4,4708\0302,194,233,2,257,4,4708\0302,235,287,2,257,4,4708\0303,1,74,2,384,1,4708\0301,1,24,4,304,1,4706\0301,26,108,4,274,4,4706\0301,113,169,4,272,1,4706\0304,1,57,3,256,4,4706\0304,59,137,3,256,2,4706\0314706,2,1,Razzeric\0304950,2,3,Spot\0304706,2,6,Razzeric\0304630,3,10,Pozzik\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,6,Razzeric\0311188,19,1188,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[119]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, this really helps me out.$B$BBut what's this? Argus sent a note with the crate...What?? Argus wants me to PAY him? Bah!$B$BWell, $N, thank you for your help.\030Ok, I'll give him his 50 horseshoes...$B$BHere they are, all boxed up and ready to go!  Tell Verner it was a pleasure doing business, and be sure he reads the note attached to this crate!\030Return to Verner Osgood in Redridge.  Give him the Crate of Horseshoes.\030Great, you're back! Did you get the shoes?\030Return to Verner\0312,1,38,2,257,1,514\0302,43,86,2,257,1,514\0302,89,187,2,257,1,514\0303,1,36,2,384,1,514\0303,39,71,2,384,1,514\0301,1,36,4,272,1,415\0301,41,56,4,272,2,415\0301,58,98,4,272,2,415\0301,100,125,4,274,2,415\0301,127,130,4,272,1,415\0301,135,168,4,272,1,415\0304,1,19,3,256,1,415\0304,21,42,3,256,2,415\031415,2,4,Verner Osgood\0312,44,1433,0,\0302,0,0,4,Verner Osgood\0302,0,0,4,Redridge\0304,0,0,9,PAY\031118,19,118,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1190]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Scribbled in a hasty, hurried hand, a scroll of notes and designs for the refinement of some raw material.\030The Brassbolts brothers have discovered a new building material, that's the only explanation that makes sense. Their cars have been operating faster than before, but their designs, and all the other data we've gathered from their runs is identical.$B$BWhat we do know, is that Rizzle Brassbolts has been focused on the plans for this new discovery almost constantly.$B$BZamek can create a diversion for you, so that you can steal those plans from them.\030Have Zamek create a diversion, then steal Rizzle's plans for Pozzik on the Shimmering Flats.\030\030Keeping Pace\0312,1,110,2,257,1,4630\0302,112,248,2,257,1,4630\0302,253,366,2,257,1,4630\0302,371,452,2,263,1,4630\0303,1,92,2,388,1,4630\0301,1,106,4,272,1,0\0314720,2,3,Rizzle Brassbolts\0304709,2,4,Zamek\0304709,2,5,Zamek\0304630,2,5,Pozzik\0312,400,1441,0,\0311137,19,1137,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301194,23,1194,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,20805,FINISHER,?,12,Rizzle's Unguarded Plans",[1191]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Let's go!\030\030\030\030Zamek's Distraction\0311,1,9,4,272,1,4709\031\0312,400,1441,0,\031\031",[1192]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Excellent! I'll get the crew to work right away on the parts we'll need for the next race.\030\030\030I'd like to integrate indurium into different parts of our racers, but I need large amounts of raw indurium to create these parts.$B$BYou can find indurium ore in the Uldaman excavation in the Badlands, across the sea in Khaz Modan.$B$BThe gnomes are getting their own supply of it, so it's important we get our own to keep pace with them.\030Indurium Ore\0311,1,10,4,272,1,4630\0301,12,90,4,274,1,4630\0304,1,130,3,258,1,4630\0304,135,232,3,256,1,4630\0304,237,339,3,256,1,4630\031\0312,400,1441,0,\0303,0,0,4,Uldaman\0303,0,0,4,Badlands\0303,0,0,4,Khaz Modan\0311194,19,1194,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5833,OBJECTIVE,4,15,",[1193]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The thorium widget slides effortlessly into place, creating a conduit to pour the frost oil down. Once the last drops of oil have been emptied into it, the trap snaps into position.$B$BWoe be to any unwary ogre that should just so happen to wander by!\030\030\030A large, broken trap lies before you. From the looks of it, the ogres have tried to repair the trap but to no avail. A hastily written note lies next to the trap, and strangely enough it details exactly what is needed to repair it: a thorium widget and some frost oil. Were the trap repaired, an ogre passing near it might get trapped, and could be avoided.$B$BClearly, it would seem fortuitous that very few ogres know how to read.$B$BClearly.\030A Broken Trap\0311,1,97,4,272,1,0\0301,99,181,4,272,1,0\0301,186,251,4,272,1,0\0304,1,37,3,256,1,0\0304,39,116,3,256,1,0\0304,118,268,3,256,1,0\0304,270,357,3,256,4,0\0304,362,432,3,256,4,0\0304,437,444,3,256,1,0\031211,4,3,Ogre\030211,3,7,Ogre\0312,2557,0,0,\031\031OBJECT,179485,GIVER,?,9,Broken Trap\030OBJECT,179485,FINISHER,?,12,Broken Trap\030ITEM,15994,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,3829,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1194]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Indurium? Interesting... If it is capable of resisting heat to the degree that you say, it would explain the performance increase the gnomes have displayed of late.$B$BThis sample you've brought to me will be invaluable, also. I will be able to perform some tests on this, but I'll need more for this to actually be of any use to us.\030Rizzle's schematics describe the process of the refinement of indurium ore. From his scrawls, it is apparent that indurium ore is being obtained from the dwarven excavation site of Uldaman in the Badlands.$B$BMuch of the other notes relate to the heat resistant properties.$B$BUsed as a paperweight for the plans is a hunk of what appears to be unrefined indurium ore.\030Bring the Sample of Indurium Ore to Pozzik on the Shimmering Flats.\030\030Rizzle's Schematics\0312,1,75,2,257,1,0\0302,77,205,2,257,1,0\0302,210,273,2,257,1,0\0302,278,368,2,257,1,0\0303,1,67,2,384,1,0\0301,1,9,4,272,2,4630\0301,11,24,4,272,1,4630\0301,26,164,4,272,4,4630\0301,169,226,4,272,3,4630\0301,228,333,4,274,3,4630\0314630,2,5,Pozzik\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,2,Badlands\0302,0,0,5,Pozzik\0311190,19,1190,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301192,23,1192,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,20805,GIVER,?,9,Rizzle's Unguarded Plans",[1195]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very good. This should fill Rau's request just fine. Could you deliver this to him? You might enjoy spending some time out in the Needles.\030The Galak centaur in the Thousand Needles are protecting an artifact from the time of the centaurs' creation.$B$BWe would like to retrieve it, but we require a phial of water from one of the night elves' moonwells.$B$BTo collect the water, you will first need to obtain one of the phials carried by the dryads near the Raynewood Retreat in the heart of Ashenvale Forest. There is a moonwell near the western bank of the Falfarren River, south of the main road, where you can fill the phial.\030Return a Filled Etched Phial to Zangen Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff.\030Once we have the filled phial, we can send it along to my associate, Rau, in the Thousand Needles. He was the one who requested the phial of water, so he'll better know how we can make use of it.\030The Sacred Flame\0312,1,109,2,257,1,4721\0302,114,214,2,257,4,4721\0302,219,370,2,259,3,4721\0302,372,490,2,257,1,4721\0303,1,66,2,384,1,4721\0301,1,10,4,272,1,4721\0301,12,52,4,272,1,4721\0301,54,83,4,272,4,4721\0301,85,138,4,272,4,4721\0304,1,98,3,256,1,4721\0304,100,195,3,256,1,4721\0312967,2,1,Galak Centaur\03093,2,1,Centaur\0304721,2,5,Zangen Stonehoof\0312,1638,1456,0,\0302,0,0,1,Thousand Needles\0302,0,0,3,Raynewood Retreat\0302,0,0,5,Zangen Stonehoof\0302,0,0,5,Thunder Bluff\0304,0,0,9,Needles\0303,0,0,10,Thousand Needles\0311196,23,1196,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5868,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1196]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hm, yes, this phial of water will serve our purposes perfectly. Because of the shared ancestry of the dryads and the centaurs, the water of the moonwells will enable us to breach the protection of the eternal flame surrounding the centaur relic.\030Bring the filled phial to Rau Cliffrunner at the Freewind Post in southeastern Thousand Needles. You can get to the Thousand Needles by taking the Great Lift at the southern edge of the Barrens.$B$BI wouldn't be surprised if you can help us out further.\030Deliver the Filled Etched Phial to Rau Cliffrunner at the Freewind Post.\030I don't suppose you've been sent by Zangen, hm?\030The Sacred Flame\0312,1,96,2,257,1,4721\0302,98,194,2,257,1,4721\0302,199,253,2,257,4,4721\0303,1,72,2,384,1,4721\0301,1,63,4,272,3,4722\0301,65,245,4,274,3,4722\0304,1,47,3,256,2,4722\0314722,2,1,Rau Cliffrunner\0304722,2,4,Rau Cliffrunner\03093,4,6,Centaur\0312,1638,1456,0,\0302,0,0,1,Rau Cliffrunner\0302,0,0,1,Freewind Post\0302,0,0,2,Thousand Needles\0302,0,0,4,Rau Cliffrunner\0302,0,0,4,Freewind Post\0311195,19,1195,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301197,23,1197,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1197]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I sense a strange energy emanating from the Hoof... I have no doubt that we will discover surprising new information about the centaur from its study.$B$BMy thanks, $N. Now I must begin to decipher the mysteries you have brought to me.\030Using the water you brought, you will be able to temporarily douse the flame that holds the centaur relic. It will not work permanently, however, so you will have to be quick about it.$B$BYou will find Splithoof Crag, the centaurs' stronghold, to the north of here. The flame is kept in Splithoof Hold, a heavily guarded part of the crag.$B$BBe careful, though, the Galak centaur have great numbers here, and will be rather reluctant to surrender something so dear to them.\030Retrieve the Cloven Hoof for Rau Cliffrunner at the Freewind Post.\030I am eager to put my hands upon the Cloven Hoof. Have you taken it yet?\030The Sacred Flame\0312,1,106,2,257,3,4722\0302,108,184,2,257,3,4722\0302,189,265,2,257,3,4722\0302,267,338,2,257,1,4722\0302,343,473,2,257,3,4722\0303,1,66,2,384,1,4722\0301,1,51,4,272,1,4722\0301,53,150,4,272,3,4722\0301,155,168,4,272,1,4722\0301,170,235,4,272,1,4722\0304,1,48,3,256,1,4722\0304,50,71,3,256,2,4722\03193,2,1,Centaur\0302967,2,5,Galak Centaur\03093,2,5,Centaur\0304722,2,6,Rau Cliffrunner\03093,4,8,Centaur\0312,1638,1456,0,\0302,0,0,4,Splithoof Hold\0302,0,0,6,Freewind Post\0304,0,0,7,Hoof\0311196,19,1196,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5869,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1198]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Dawnwatcher Shaedlass was good to send you. There is indeed a wicked plot underway in this corrupted place.\030Many rumors circulate these days about the union of the Twilight's Hammer and the naga in Blackfathom Deeps on the coasts of Ashenvale.$B$BMy role here with the Argent Dawn is to collect as much information as I can, so we know when and where help is needed.$B$BIt has been weeks now since I sent a scout to check on the activity at Blackfathom Deeps. Argent Guard Thaelrid has not yet reported back.$B$BMy other scouts are preoccupied with pressing matters.$B$BSeek out and aid Thaelrid for me, $n.\030Seek out Argent Guard Thaelrid in Blackfathom Deeps.\030\030In Search of Thaelrid\0312,1,135,2,257,1,4786\0302,140,258,2,257,1,4786\0302,263,351,2,257,1,4786\0302,353,400,2,257,1,4786\0302,405,458,2,257,1,4786\0302,463,499,2,257,1,4786\0303,1,52,2,384,1,4786\0301,1,43,4,272,1,4787\0301,45,107,4,276,1,4787\0314787,2,4,Argent Guard Thaelrid\0304787,2,7,Argent Guard Thaelrid\0304786,4,8,Dawnwatcher Shaedlass\0312,719,0,0,\0302,0,0,1,Blackfathom Deeps\0302,0,0,3,Blackfathom Deeps\0302,0,0,7,Blackfathom Deeps\0311200,23,1200,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1199]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You are no doubt of brave and noble blood, $N. The Argent Dawn commends you for your efforts against evil.\030Empowered by the ancient rites of the chaotic Old Gods the members of the Twilight's Hammer strive to bring about the return of their dark patrons and spread death and terror across the world.$B$BWe believe that the Twilight's Hammer has allied with the naga and are amassing in Blackfathom Deeps on the coast of Ashenvale.$B$BWhatever evil plan brews in the depths of the old temple must be thwarted.$B$BWage war on the Hammer and bring back proof of your deeds. Your efforts will be rewarded handsomely.\030Bring 10 Twilight Pendants to Argent Guard Manados in Darnassus.\030Blackfathom Deeps was once an ancient night elf temple. It once housed a most powerful moonwell. Who knows what evil brews there now at the hands of the Twilight's Hammer.$B$BHave you made any progress in ridding their presence?\030Twilight Falls\0312,1,192,2,321,1,4784\0302,197,323,2,257,4,4784\0302,328,401,2,257,1,4784\0302,406,463,2,261,1,4784\0302,465,505,2,257,3,4784\0303,1,64,2,384,1,4784\0301,1,46,4,272,1,4784\0301,48,106,4,272,1,4784\0304,1,55,3,320,1,4784\0304,57,96,3,256,1,4784\0304,98,171,3,256,1,4784\0304,176,228,3,256,2,4784\0314784,2,6,Argent Guard Manados\0312,719,0,0,\0302,0,0,2,Blackfathom Deeps\0302,0,0,6,Argent Guard Manados\0302,0,0,6,Darnassus\031\031ITEM,5879,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[12]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $N. My scout witnessed your valiant acts. You are proving yourself quite well so far.\030The People's Militia has but one goal:  To defend the lands of Westfall and return peace to our surroundings.  Unfortunately, the price of peace is often blood. $B$BOne of my scouts has brought word of a band of Defias Trappers wreaking havoc nearby.  I have reports of Defias Trapper sightings near the Jangolode Mine to the Northwest as well as at the Molsen Farm and Furlbrow's Pumpkin Farm. If you seek to join our ranks, slay 15 Defias Trappers and 15 Defias Smugglers then return to me.\030Gryan Stoutmantle wants you to kill 15 Defias Trappers and 15 Defias Smugglers then return to him on Sentinel Hill.\030Perhaps I did not make myself clear, pledge. In order to prove your worth as a servant to The People's Militia and to the Light you need to slay 15 Defias Trappers and 15 Defias Smugglers then return to me when the deed is done.\030The People's Militia\0312,1,109,2,271,1,234\0302,112,160,2,265,1,234\0302,166,250,2,257,1,234\0302,253,394,2,257,1,234\0302,396,492,2,259,4,234\0303,1,115,2,386,1,234\0301,1,14,4,272,1,234\0301,16,52,4,272,1,234\0301,54,96,4,272,1,234\0304,1,44,3,256,4,234\0304,46,228,3,258,1,234\031504,2,4,Defias Trapper\030234,2,6,Gryan Stoutmantle\0312,40,1436,0,\0302,0,0,4,Jangolode Mine\0302,0,0,4,Northwest\0302,0,0,4,Molsen Farm\0303,0,0,11,The People's Militia\0303,0,0,11,Light\03113,23,13,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,504,OBJECTIVE,15,13,Defias Trapper\030NPC,95,OBJECTIVE,15,13,Defias Smuggler",[120]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031At ease, $C.$B$BMagistrate Solomon is a noble leader. His words carry great weight with me. I shall seek the counsel of the King and make the situation clear to him. Assure the good judge that he has the Stormwind Army's support. Reinforcements will be sent as soon as word is given from His Majesty.\030These are trying times, $c.  The township is under constant siege.  Without reinforcements, we will certainly face defeat.  The message I now entrust to you is of utmost importance.  Get this report to General Marcus Jonathan of Stormwind immediately.  Once your delivery is made, return to me at once with any news, be it good or bad. $B$BNow make haste!\030Magistrate Solomon has given you a report which must be delivered to General Marcus Jonathan in Stormwind.  The judge wants you to return to him as soon as the delivery has been made.\030What have you there?\030Messenger to Stormwind\0312,1,27,2,257,1,344\0302,30,66,2,257,1,344\0302,69,122,2,257,3,344\0302,125,181,2,257,1,344\0302,184,251,2,257,1,344\0302,254,335,2,257,1,344\0302,341,355,2,257,1,344\0303,1,106,2,384,1,344\0303,109,183,2,386,1,344\0301,1,12,4,272,1,466\0301,17,53,4,272,1,466\0301,55,91,4,272,1,466\0301,93,165,4,274,3,466\0301,167,229,4,272,1,466\0301,231,300,4,272,3,466\0304,1,20,3,256,2,466\031466,2,5,General Marcus Jonathan\030344,2,8,Magistrate Solomon\030798,2,8,Solomon\030466,2,8,General Marcus Jonathan\030344,4,11,Magistrate Solomon\030798,4,11,Solomon\0312,44,1433,0,\0302,0,0,5,General Marcus Jonathan of Stormwind\0302,0,0,8,General Marcus Jonathan\0302,0,0,8,Stormwind\0304,0,0,15,His Majesty\031121,23,121,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1200]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Kelris has eluded us for quite some time.$B$BIt seems as though whenever evil made its presence known in these parts, Kelris had played a role. For some time we considered him dead or missing.$B$BBut this makes perfect sense. By ending his reign you have spared the lives of many innocent people.$B$BBy the light! To sacrifice someone to a servant of an Old God for one's personal gain is beyond reproachful!$B$BYou have done a great deed, $N. I salute you on behalf of the Argent Dawn.\030Strength has left me. Your help is needed!$B$BLong ago this site was a great temple of Elune. But misfortune led to ruin when the corruption of an Old God seeped up from beneath the earth and tainted the sacred Moon Well.$B$BAku'Mai, servant of the Old God, rose from the waters.$B$BThe Twilight's Hammer cultists have allied with the naga to occupy these grounds. The cultists, led by Kelris, sacrifice innocents to Aku'Mai for power.$B$BSlay Kelris and bring his head to Selgorm in Darnassus, $N, please.\030Bring the head of Twilight Lord Kelris to Dawnwatcher Selgorm in Darnassus.\030Time is a precious commodity, $C.$B$BMy role here in Darnassus is to ensure that the Argent Dawn thrives and that the evil forces encroaching upon Kalimdor are thwarted.$B$BState your business quickly or be on your way.\030Blackfathom Villainy\0312,1,21,2,257,1,4787\0302,23,42,2,257,1,4787\0302,47,93,2,321,1,4787\0302,95,221,2,261,1,4787\0302,226,279,2,257,1,4787\0302,284,364,2,257,1,4787\0302,366,435,2,257,1,4787\0302,440,506,2,257,1,4787\0303,1,75,2,384,1,4787\0301,1,41,4,272,1,4783\0301,46,143,4,272,4,4783\0301,145,192,4,276,1,4783\0301,197,225,4,272,1,4783\0301,227,296,4,272,1,4783\0301,301,313,4,272,1,4783\0301,315,408,4,272,1,4783\0301,413,443,4,272,1,4783\0301,445,486,4,272,1,4783\0304,1,33,3,256,1,4783\0304,38,169,3,258,1,4783\0304,174,219,3,256,1,4783\0314829,2,5,Aku'mai\0304829,2,7,Aku'mai\0304832,2,9,Twilight Lord Kelris\0304783,2,9,Dawnwatcher Selgorm\03014528,3,19,Precious\0312,719,0,0,\0302,0,0,7,Aku'Mai\0302,0,0,8,Selgorm\0302,0,0,8,Darnassus\0302,0,0,9,Dawnwatcher Selgorm\0302,0,0,9,Darnassus\0303,0,0,20,Darnassus\0311198,19,1198,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5881,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1201]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Good work.  Their infiltrators are skilled, but they're not good enough to escape the watchful eye of the Horde!\030The Horde and Alliance hold an uneasy truce.  Outlying skirmishes and covert actions are taken by one side against the other, and it is our duty to ensure the Horde is on top!$B$BNow is the chance to do just that.$B$BAlliance infiltrators have taken positions east of Brackenwall Village.  They spy on the village and report our movements to Theramore, which we cannot allow.$B$BHunt down the infiltrators and slay them.  Send a clear message to their superiors that we will not tolerate their spies' presence!\030Kill 9 Theramore Infiltrators, then return to Nazeer Bloodpike in Brackenwall Village.\030Did you find the infiltrators, $N?\030Theramore Spies\0312,1,44,2,257,1,4791\0302,47,175,2,259,1,4791\0302,180,213,2,257,1,4791\0302,218,288,2,257,1,4791\0302,291,375,2,265,1,4791\0302,380,420,2,257,1,4791\0302,423,510,2,257,3,4791\0303,1,86,2,384,1,4791\0301,1,10,4,272,1,4791\0301,13,112,4,272,1,4791\0304,1,34,3,256,2,4791\0314791,2,8,Nazeer Bloodpike\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,4,Brackenwall Village\0302,0,0,5,Theramore\0302,0,0,8,Nazeer Bloodpike\0302,0,0,8,Brackenwall Village\0311202,23,1202,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,4834,OBJECTIVE,9,13,Theramore Infiltrator",[1202]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I commend you, $N. This was not an easy mission. But the documents you gained are valued greatly by our superiors.\030$N, two of our spies were sent to steal documents from a ship at the Theramore docks.  They gained the papers but were discovered, and were forced to throw the documents into the sea.$B$BOne spy later escaped, but was unable to recover the prize.  He reported his failure to me, and I now charge the task to you.$B$BThe documents are in a footlocker, in the waters somewhere beneath the Theramore docks.  Find those documents, $N, and bring them to me.\030Bring the Captain's Documents to Nazeer Bloodpike in Brackenwall Village.\030Did you find the documents, $N?  They hold information vital to the stability of the Alliance and, hence, vital to the security of the Horde.\030The Theramore Docks\0312,1,85,2,261,1,4791\0302,88,183,2,257,1,4791\0302,188,246,2,257,1,4791\0302,249,312,2,257,1,4791\0302,317,403,2,257,1,4791\0302,406,452,2,257,1,4791\0303,1,73,2,384,1,4791\0301,1,18,4,272,1,4791\0301,20,48,4,272,1,4791\0301,50,114,4,272,1,4791\0304,1,31,3,256,2,4791\0304,34,141,3,264,1,4791\0314791,2,7,Nazeer Bloodpike\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,1,Theramore\0302,0,0,7,Nazeer Bloodpike\0302,0,0,7,Brackenwall Village\0311201,19,1201,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5882,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1203]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031That's a good blade. It has a good swing. It's a good swing blade. Thank you. Thank you, thank you, thank you!!! Now I want to try it....$B$BLater. I'll try it later. But like I was saying... thanks.\030I have cutting to do.  I can't tell you what I'm going to cut, but... I need myself a blade.  A certain blade...$B$BSome people call it a moonsteel broadsword.  I call it a swing blade.$B$BYou help me?  Maybe you find it in town, maybe you talk to a blacksmith and he'll make it special.$B$BBut don't sleep on this.  What I'm cutting won't keep forever...\030Bring a Moonsteel Broadsword to Jarl in Dustwallow Marsh.\030You have my blade??\030Jarl Needs a Blade\0312,1,21,2,257,1,4792\0302,24,69,2,257,3,4792\0302,71,92,2,259,1,4792\0302,95,112,2,257,1,4792\0302,117,159,2,257,1,4792\0302,162,185,2,257,1,4792\0302,190,201,2,257,2,4792\0302,204,287,2,257,4,4792\0302,292,315,2,257,1,4792\0302,318,355,2,257,1,4792\0303,1,57,2,384,1,4792\0301,1,20,4,272,1,4792\0301,22,41,4,272,1,4792\0301,43,66,4,272,1,4792\0301,68,77,4,272,1,4792\0301,79,112,4,272,1,4792\0301,114,137,4,274,1,4792\0301,142,147,4,272,1,4792\0301,149,166,4,272,1,4792\0301,168,191,4,272,1,4792\0301,193,199,4,272,1,4792\0304,1,19,3,256,2,4792\031\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,11,Jarl\0302,0,0,11,Dustwallow Marsh\0311206,19,1206,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3853,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1204]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031These will do fine! Thank you, $N!$B$BNow I'll try different cooking techniques on these tongues to find the best way to bring out their flavor.$B$BEventually I'll have a dish worthy of serving at the Blue Recluse in Stormwind!\030I'm working on a dish I call \"Mudrock Soup and Bugs.\"  I still need the major ingredients, and... well, I don't think I'd last long trudging through Dustwallow Marsh!$B$BSo, $N, can you do some hunting for me?  First, I need the tongues of Mudrock turtles.  You can find Mudrocks along the coast, mostly around the bay.$B$BBut I don't want just any tongues!  I hear that the tongues of some Mudrocks are forked...$B$BThey say the forked tongues have a distinct flavor, and I want that flavor in my dish...\030Bring 8 Forked Mudrock Tongues to Morgan Stern in Theramore.\030Did you get the forked tongues?\030Mudrock Soup and Bugs\0312,1,97,2,259,1,4794\0302,99,166,2,257,1,4794\0302,171,209,2,257,2,4794\0302,212,256,2,259,1,4794\0302,259,319,2,257,1,4794\0302,324,357,2,257,1,4794\0302,360,413,2,257,1,4794\0302,418,505,2,259,1,4794\0303,1,60,2,384,1,4794\0301,1,19,4,272,3,4794\0301,21,34,4,272,1,4794\0301,39,144,4,272,1,4794\0301,149,227,4,272,1,4794\0304,1,31,3,256,2,4794\0314794,2,9,Morgan Stern\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,9,Morgan Stern\0302,0,0,9,Theramore\0304,0,0,13,Blue Recluse\0304,0,0,13,Stormwind\0311258,23,1258,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5883,OBJECTIVE,8,15,",[1205]="PARTIAL\031motivations,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very good, $N.$B$BI am sure the hunt was not easy, but it is good to know the beast's pain has finally ended.\030Deadmire is an ancient crocolisk in Dustwallow marsh.  And it is his time to die.$B$BOld bones grind as he pulls his huge body through the swamp, and although he still moves with the strength and speed of youth, his aging body tortures the great spirit within it, a spirit whose flame will not waver.$B$BYet now he lives in constant, maddening pain.  You must end the life of this noble creature, $N.  You must lead Deadmire to peace.\030Bring Deadmire's Tooth to Melor in Thunder Bluff.\030Do you have the tooth of Deadmire, $N?  Have you ended the creature's suffering?\030Deadmire\0312,1,53,2,321,1,3441\0302,56,81,2,257,1,3441\0302,86,300,2,257,3,3441\0302,305,349,2,257,1,3441\0302,352,400,2,257,1,3441\0302,403,434,2,265,1,3441\0303,1,49,2,384,1,3441\0301,1,14,4,272,1,3441\0301,19,109,4,304,1,3441\0304,1,38,3,256,2,3441\0304,41,80,3,260,2,3441\0314841,2,1,Deadmire\0304841,2,6,Deadmire\03010430,4,9,The Beast\0304841,3,10,Deadmire\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,1,Dustwallow\0302,0,0,7,Melor\0302,0,0,7,Thunder Bluff\031\031ITEM,5945,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1206]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You got the eyes! You got the eyes! Tasty, tasty spider eyes!$B$BSome eyes... when you stare at them they stare back. Eat those last. They keep you company... out in the swamp.$B$BHello, little spider eyes. Hello! You taste like chicken. Gooey, salty chicken!$B$BMmmh.\030Eye juice is good juice for drinking.  Too bad most critters only have two eyes.$B$BBut spiders have lots of eyes.  Lots and lots.  And Darkmist eye juice is tasty.  Smooth and salty!  Unpopped spider eyes... I taste them already.$B$BDarkmist spiders are west of here, in the Darkmist Cavern.  You figure the spiders are named after the cave... or is it the other way around?\030Bring 20 Unpopped Darkmist Eyes to \"Swamp Eye\" Jarl at the Swamplight Manor.\030Where are those eyes?\030Jarl Needs Eyes\0312,1,37,2,257,1,4792\0302,40,80,2,257,1,4792\0