0,1,Magistrate Solomon\0302,0,0,3,Magistrate Solomon\0302,0,0,3,Lakeshire\0304,0,0,5,Lakeshire\031120,19,120,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030143,23,143,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1218]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, that's the spice! Now here's some swampy good stew.\030I like cooking.  Good swamp cooking.  Fried green frog legs and the like.$B$BAnd for cooking, I need spice.  Soothing spice.  Then I'll make a stew and stew it up and suck it down and give you some too.$B$BDo you like stew?\030Bring 3 Soothing Spices to \"Swamp Eye\" Jarl in Dustwallow Marsh.\030Spice. We could all use some spice in our life. You agree?\030Soothing Spices\0312,1,15,2,257,1,4792\0302,18,36,2,257,1,4792\0302,39,73,2,257,1,4792\0302,78,107,2,259,1,4792\0302,110,124,2,257,1,4792\0302,127,202,2,257,1,4792\0302,207,223,2,257,2,4792\0303,1,64,2,384,1,4792\0301,1,21,4,272,1,4792\0301,23,55,4,272,1,4792\0304,1,6,3,256,1,4792\0304,8,47,3,256,4,4792\0304,49,58,3,256,2,4792\03113321,2,3,Frog\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,8,Dustwallow Marsh\0311206,23,1206,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3713,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[1219]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hm... I can't read orcish very well, but this looks like a report... written by an orc spy!\030Sifting through the loose dirt, the severed hand of an orc is found.  And clutched in the hand is a bone-carved tube.  And in the tube is a dirt-stained parchment.$B$BThe parchment is written in orcish... and it looks important.\030Bring the Spy's Report to a Theramore Lieutenant.\030Do you have a report to make?\030The Orc Report\0312,1,68,2,257,1,0\0302,71,117,2,257,1,0\0302,120,163,2,257,1,0\0302,168,204,2,257,1,0\0302,206,228,2,257,1,0\0303,1,49,2,384,1,0\0301,7,68,4,272,1,4947\0301,70,91,4,272,1,4947\0304,1,29,3,256,2,4947\0314947,2,6,Theramore Lieutenant\0312,15,1445,0,\0311220,23,1220,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,20985,GIVER,?,9,Loose Dirt",[122]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thanks! These will get me out of debt to Argus...\030I need some underbelly scales from black dragon whelps to pay for the shoes Argus sent me from Goldshire.  If you can get 6 of them for me, then I can pay Argus with some... and have enough left to fashion something for you.$B$BBlack dragon whelps are often flying around south of Lakeshire, but they like to wander.  You might have to just keep an eye out and hunt them when you see them.\030Gather 6 Underbelly Whelp Scales from Black Dragon Whelps, and bring them to Verner Osgood in Redridge.\030I know that greedy Argus will send someone to collect his scales if I don't give them to him soon. Have you found those scales yet?\030Underbelly Scales\0312,1,105,2,259,1,415\0302,108,173,2,257,4,415\0302,175,224,2,257,1,415\0302,229,316,2,257,1,415\0302,319,389,2,257,4,415\0303,1,103,2,384,1,415\0301,1,7,4,272,1,415\0301,9,49,4,272,3,415\0304,1,98,3,256,4,415\0304,100,131,3,256,2,415\031415,2,6,Verner Osgood\0312,44,1433,0,\0302,0,0,1,Goldshire\0302,0,0,4,Lakeshire\0302,0,0,6,Black Dragon Whelps\0302,0,0,6,Verner Osgood\0302,0,0,6,Redridge\0304,0,0,8,Argus\031119,19,119,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,1221,OBJECTIVE,6,15,",[1220]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A report from an orc spy! How did you find this? No matter -- let's see what it says...\030Captain Vimes should see the orc report you found, $N.  He knows the orcish language better than most.  And he should know that there are Horde spies near Theramore!$B$BThe captain is in the barracks, on the northeastern side of Theramore Isle.\030Bring the Spy's Report to Captain Garran Vimes.\030You have something for me?\030Captain Vimes\0312,1,54,2,257,1,4947\0302,57,102,2,257,1,4947\0302,105,165,2,257,1,4947\0302,170,244,2,257,1,4947\0303,1,47,2,384,1,4947\0301,1,25,4,272,1,4944\0301,27,48,4,272,2,4944\0301,50,87,4,272,1,4944\0304,1,26,3,256,2,4944\0314944,2,5,Captain Garran Vimes\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,3,Theramore\0302,0,0,5,Captain Garran Vimes\0311219,19,1219,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1221]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Great, you got them! I can sell these to my contacts for a bundle!$B$BThanks for the delivery, $N! You are a great partner.\030Blueleaf tubers are a delicacy around the world!  But they're rare, very rare.  The only place to find them is here in the Barrens, deep in the earth, in Razorfen Kraul.$B$BAnd even then, they're impossible to find unless you know just where to look!  That's why I've trained these snufflenose gophers to find them for me.  They have great noses and can smell a tuber from fifty paces away.$B$BIt won't be easy, but if you get me some tubers I'll pay you handsomely.\030Grab a Crate with Holes.$BGrab a Snufflenose Command Stick.$BGrab and read the Snufflenose Owner's Manual.$B$BIn Razorfen Kraul, use the Crate with Holes to summon a Snufflenose Gopher, and use the Command Stick on the gopher to make it search for Tubers.$B$BBring 6 Blueleaf Tubers, the Snufflenose Command Stick and the Crate with Holes to Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet.\030Do you have the tubers, $N?\030Blueleaf Tubers\0312,1,48,2,257,1,3446\0302,51,78,2,257,1,3446\0302,81,169,2,257,1,3446\0302,174,250,2,265,4,3446\0302,253,322,2,257,1,3446\0302,325,390,2,257,1,3446\0302,395,466,2,257,4,3446\0303,1,24,2,384,1,3446\0303,27,59,2,384,1,3446\0303,62,106,2,384,1,3446\0303,111,255,2,384,1,3446\0303,260,368,2,384,1,3446\0301,1,20,4,272,1,3446\0301,22,66,4,272,1,3446\0301,71,98,4,272,1,3446\0301,100,123,4,272,1,3446\0304,1,27,3,256,2,3446\0314781,2,11,Snufflenose Gopher\0303446,2,12,Mebok Mizzyrix\0312,1717,1413,0,\0302,0,0,3,Barrens\0302,0,0,3,Razorfen Kraul\0302,0,0,12,Mebok Mizzyrix\0302,0,0,12,Ratchet\031\031ITEM,5876,OBJECTIVE,6,15,\030ITEM,5880,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,5897,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,6684,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1222]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Mr. Ignatz was just here with the bogbean leaves, and he told me you helped him out of some real trouble.$B$BThank you, $N. I will ask my uncle to treat you to a feast the next time you visit the Blue Recluse in Stormwind.\030Great, finally something that doesn't want to eat me!$B$BI need help handling the critters around here, and you fit the mold, $gbuddy:lady;.$B$BThe cook Morgan Stern is researching a new recipe, and he sent me out here to gather bogbean leaves.  I guess he thinks they're tasty.$B$BAnyway, while looking for a bogbean plant... I got myself surrounded!  Can you help me out of here, and watch my back as I look for the bogbean?\030Escort \"Stinky\" Ignatz, then speak with Morgan Stern in Theramore.\030Help Stinky find Bogbean Leaves\030Have you seen Mr. Ignatz? I sent him into the swamp some time ago and he hasn't returned!\030Stinky's Escape\0312,1,53,2,257,1,4880\0302,58,140,2,259,1,4880\0302,145,244,2,257,1,4880\0302,247,278,2,257,1,4880\0302,283,326,2,257,1,4880\0302,328,351,2,257,1,4880\0302,354,426,2,257,2,4880\0303,1,66,2,384,1,4880\0301,5,105,4,272,1,4794\0301,110,123,4,272,1,4794\0301,125,222,4,272,3,4794\0305,1,17,3,256,1,4794\0305,19,25,3,256,2,4794\0305,27,89,3,256,1,4794\0304,1,31,3,384,1,4880\03115065,2,2,Lady\0304794,2,3,Morgan Stern\0304794,2,8,Morgan Stern\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,8,Theramore\0304,0,0,11,Stormwind\031\031",[123]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hm... I have heard of this \"Collector\" but I don't know whom he's working for. Thank you for the schedule. It will help us solve this mystery.\030This note is a schedule with a list of days and times when a person -- described only as \"The Collector\" -- will receive a shipment of gold from the mines in Elwynn Forest.$B$BFrom the schedule, it looks as if the Collector resides near the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch in eastern Elwynn.$B$BThis sounds important.  You should report it to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire.\030Go to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire and give him The Collector's Schedule.\030What?!? We haven't had our people working the Elwynn mines for months!$B$BLet me see that note you have...\030The Collector\0312,1,172,2,257,3,0\0302,177,283,2,257,4,0\0302,288,309,2,257,1,0\0302,312,363,2,257,1,0\0303,1,72,2,384,1,0\0301,7,78,4,272,1,240\0301,80,106,4,272,1,240\0301,108,142,4,272,3,240\0304,1,7,3,256,2,240\0304,9,70,3,256,1,240\0304,75,106,3,256,1,240\031240,2,4,Marshal Dughan\030240,2,5,Marshal Dughan\0312,12,1429,0,\0302,0,0,1,Elwynn Forest\0302,0,0,2,Brackwell Pumpkin Patch\0302,0,0,4,Marshal Dughan\0302,0,0,4,Goldshire\0302,0,0,5,Marshal Dughan\0302,0,0,5,Goldshire\031147,23,147,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,1307,STARTER,?,10,",[1238]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Good work, $N. Our agent, Marg Nighteye, was stationed outside Theramore. He was charged to spy on the city. $B$BThis is his latest report, and it may be his last -- from your testimony, I fear that Marg met his end in the swamp...\030Sifting through the loose dirt, the severed hand of an orc is found.  And clutched in the hand is a bone-carved tube.  And in the tube is a dirt-stained parchment.$B$BThe parchment is a report made by an orc who spent weeks spying on the city of Theramore.$B$BAfter scanning the parchment, it is clear that it must be brought to the orc spymaster in Brackenwall Village.\030Bring the Spy's Report to Nazeer Bloodpike in Brackenwall Village.\030You have something for me?\030The Lost Report\0312,1,68,2,257,1,0\0302,71,117,2,257,1,0\0302,120,163,2,257,1,0\0302,168,256,2,257,1,0\0302,261,370,2,257,1,0\0303,1,66,2,384,1,0\0301,1,14,4,272,1,4791\0301,16,73,4,272,1,4791\0301,75,108,4,272,1,4791\0301,114,231,4,272,1,4791\0304,1,26,3,256,2,4791\0314791,2,6,Nazeer Bloodpike\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,5,Brackenwall Village\0302,0,0,6,Nazeer Bloodpike\0302,0,0,6,Brackenwall Village\0304,0,0,8,Theramore\0311239,23,1239,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,20985,GIVER,?,9,Loose Dirt",[1239]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is the head of Marg Nighteye! As I feared, he is dead.$B$BLook at the wound on his neck! Could a weapon have made that ragged cut, or did some beast slay our agent?$B$BThis is a mystery we must solve, $N. We must discover if Marg's death was at the hands of the Alliance!\030Vigorous digging reveals the head of a male orc, raggedly severed at the neck.  His lips are frozen in a snarl, and its dark eyes stare defiantly.\030Bring the Defiant Orc Head to Nazeer Bloodpike in Brackenwall Village.\030You have another matter to report, $N?\030The Severed Head\0312,1,78,2,257,1,0\0302,81,146,2,257,1,0\0303,1,70,2,384,1,0\0301,1,34,4,272,1,4791\0301,36,59,4,272,1,4791\0301,64,93,4,272,1,4791\0301,95,169,4,272,4,4791\0301,174,209,4,272,1,4791\0301,211,276,4,272,4,4791\0304,1,38,3,256,2,4791\0311383,2,2,Snarl\0304791,2,3,Nazeer Bloodpike\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,3,Nazeer Bloodpike\0302,0,0,3,Brackenwall Village\0311238,19,1238,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301240,23,1240,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,20985,GIVER,?,9,Loose Dirt",[124]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you for all your help, $N.\030As if the attacking orcs weren't enough!  Now I have gnoll brutes and mystics prowling along the ridge north of my stable, taking my horses when they stray...$B$BIf you can get rid of those gnolls, my horses and I would be very grateful.\030Kill 10 Redridge Brutes and 8 Redridge Mystics, then return to Verner Osgood.\030Yes? Is there something I can do for you?\030A Baying of Gnolls\0312,1,40,2,261,4,415\0302,43,158,2,257,1,415\0302,163,237,2,257,4,415\0303,1,77,2,384,1,415\0301,1,32,4,272,1,415\0304,1,4,3,256,2,415\0304,6,41,3,256,2,415\031415,2,4,Verner Osgood\0312,44,1433,0,\0302,0,0,4,Verner Osgood\031119,19,119,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030126,23,126,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,426,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Redridge Brute\030NPC,430,OBJECTIVE,8,13,Redridge Mystic",[1240]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, I now see. The spirit of this orc is bound in our world, boiling with rage from a task yet undone.$B$BWell, let us have words with this angry orc...\030We must know the events surrounding Marg's death!  And the only way to do that, $N, is through the witch-magic of trolls.$B$BBring Marg's head to Kin'weelay in Stranglethorn Vale, at the Grom'gol Base Camp.$B$BKin'weelay is the most powerful witchdoctor of the Darkspear trolls.  If anyone can speak to Marg Nighteye's spirit, it is he.\030Take the Defiant Orc Head to Kin'weelay in the Grom'gol Base Camp in Stranglethorn Vale.\030There is an angry spirit about you, $gbrother:sister;. What brings you to Kin'weelay?\030The Troll Witchdoctor\0312,1,49,2,257,1,4791\0302,52,121,2,257,1,4791\0302,126,206,2,257,1,4791\0302,211,278,2,257,1,4791\0302,281,336,2,257,4,4791\0303,1,88,2,384,1,4791\0301,1,14,4,272,1,2519\0301,16,102,4,276,1,2519\0301,107,152,4,272,1,2519\0304,1,54,3,256,1,2519\0304,56,85,3,256,2,2519\0312519,2,3,Kin'weelay\0302519,2,4,Kin'weelay\0302519,2,6,Kin'weelay\0302519,3,11,Kin'weelay\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,3,Kin'weelay\0302,0,0,3,Stranglethorn Vale\0302,0,0,3,Grom'gol Base Camp\0302,0,0,5,Marg Nighteye's\0302,0,0,6,Kin'weelay\0302,0,0,6,Grom'gol Base Camp\0302,0,0,6,Stranglethorn Vale\0303,0,0,11,Kin'weelay\0311239,19,1239,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301261,23,1261,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1241]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hmm... <Jorgen looks up at you through squinted eyes.>$B$BAll right. I'll help ya, but not because I want to, but because I'm obligated.$B$BAnd let's get one thing straight: you're knowin' far more than you should to begin with. Let's keep this our little secret, and don't go blabbin' at any taverns about anything you find out. Understand?\030Recently a diplomat was sent to Theramore to meet with Jaina Proudmoore. That diplomat never arrived.$B$BI believe the Defias are involved in this plot, but I'm not sure how. The diplomat's disappearance still eludes public attention, but it can't remain that way for long.$B$BAgents of the king are already scouring the city for clues, but I have my own contacts I would like involved.$B$BIn the Valley of Heroes is an old friend of mine named Jorgen. Find him, give him this note, and follow his instructions.\030Find Jorgen in Stormwind City.\030Hmph, you better have good reason to interrupt a man and his fishin'. I don't take kindly to peddlers, let alone beggars.\030The Missing Diplomat\0312,1,72,2,257,1,4960\0302,74,101,2,257,1,4960\0302,106,174,2,257,4,4960\0302,176,273,2,257,1,4960\0302,278,386,2,259,4,4960\0302,391,452,2,257,1,4960\0302,454,511,2,257,1,4960\0303,1,30,2,384,1,4960\0301,1,6,4,272,1,4959\0301,8,54,4,272,1,4959\0301,59,68,4,272,1,4959\0301,70,136,4,274,1,4959\0301,141,228,4,272,1,4959\0301,230,329,4,272,1,4959\0301,331,341,4,272,2,4959\0304,1,69,3,256,1,4959\0304,71,121,3,256,1,4959\0314959,2,6,Jorgen\0304959,2,8,Jorgen\0304959,4,10,Jorgen\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,1,Theramore\0302,0,0,8,Stormwind City\0311274,19,1274,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301242,23,1242,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1242]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I'm sorry, a letter for me? Well, I'll be... not often you get a delivery that's not a crate or barrel when all you do is work. Let's see what this is about.$B$B<Elling looks up at you while he opens the letter.>$B$BYou look a little tense, you okay, $N?\030Take this here note to Elling Trias. Don't say nothin' else to him. Just be polite and wait for him to respond. And don't worry, he will.$B$BI'm gonna only impress this on ya once more, $N: treat this matter seriously, and keep your yapper shut.$B$BYa can find Trias at his cheese shop, Trias' Cheese, in the Trade District. Good luck.\030Delivery Jorgen's Sealed Note to Elling Trias in Stormwind City.\030Hello, $N. Is there something I can do for you? Perhaps you'd like to try some of our special Trias cheddar? Or a block of Darnassian bleu?\030The Missing Diplomat\0312,1,36,2,257,1,4959\0302,38,67,2,257,1,4959\0302,69,111,2,257,1,4959\0302,113,137,2,257,3,4959\0302,142,245,2,257,1,4959\0302,250,324,2,257,1,4959\0302,326,335,2,257,1,4959\0303,1,64,2,384,1,4959\0301,1,27,4,272,2,482\0301,29,44,4,272,1,482\0301,46,127,4,272,1,482\0301,129,157,4,272,1,482\0301,162,212,4,272,1,482\0301,217,254,4,272,2,482\0304,1,10,3,256,1,482\0304,12,47,3,256,2,482\0304,49,108,3,256,4,482\0304,110,139,3,256,2,482\031482,2,1,Elling Trias\030482,2,8,Elling Trias\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,1,Elling Trias\0302,0,0,6,Trade District\0302,0,0,8,Elling Trias\0302,0,0,8,Stormwind City\0311241,19,1241,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301243,23,1243,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1243]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh, Trias sent you, huh? That's a little different.$B$BFeel free to fight whatever monstrosities come at you from the darkness. I'm sure you'll be able to handle it pretty easily if you're the type to be hanging around with the likes of him.$B$BSo, what does my friend need of me on such a gloomy day as this?\030Jorgen, you ol' sonuva.... So, that's how it's going to be, huh?$B$BAll right, I can deal with that. I hope he finds the Twisting Nether that much sooner!$B$BHere's what's gonna happen, $N. I'll start using my contacts here, but you're doing most of the footwork so I save some coin.$B$BHead to Darkshire in Duskwood and find Watcher Backus--he usually patrols the north road right outside of town. Just tell him you're looking into any Defias activity for me and he'll help you out with any information he can.\030Give the Sealed Note to Watcher Backus in Duskwood.\030Not too safe to be traveling about in the woods, $N. Be careful, and if you see anything suspicious or dangerous, contact the Watchers immediately. Don't try and take anything on yourself. We're not responsible for anything terrible that might happen to you.$B$BBut we both know you're gonna ignore me and fight whatever comes out of the darkness anyway, don't we? Haha, yeah, you adventurer types... all the same.\030The Missing Diplomat\0312,1,26,2,257,1,482\0302,28,64,2,257,2,482\0302,69,100,2,257,1,482\0302,102,154,2,259,3,482\0302,159,189,2,257,1,482\0302,191,283,2,265,1,482\0302,288,398,2,257,1,482\0302,400,511,2,257,1,482\0303,1,51,2,384,1,482\0301,1,24,4,272,2,840\0301,26,51,4,272,1,840\0301,56,127,4,276,1,840\0301,129,241,4,272,4,840\0301,246,309,4,274,2,840\0304,1,52,3,256,1,840\0304,54,147,3,256,4,840\0304,149,188,3,256,1,840\0304,190,258,3,256,4,840\0304,263,364,3,260,2,840\0304,366,400,3,256,1,840\0304,402,414,3,256,1,840\0314959,2,1,Jorgen\030840,2,7,Watcher Backus\030840,2,9,Watcher Backus\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,7,Darkshire\0302,0,0,7,Duskwood\0302,0,0,9,Watcher Backus\0302,0,0,9,Duskwood\0311242,19,1242,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301244,23,1244,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1244]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You're back safe and sound. Couldn't ask for much more than that, could you?$B$BNow, let's see what we have here. This looks pretty official as far as any Defias documents I've seen. But it could be a dupe just to throw you off track of whatever it is you're looking for.\030Defias activity? Well, there's always some activity; even if they keep to themselves we consider them a threat.$B$BBut now that I think about it, there was a recent sighting that seemed odd. It must have been a couple weeks ago, but some of their agents had gathered around Addle's Stead. From the report, I'd guessed something big went down.$B$BWhy don't you check there first and bring me back anything you find?$B$BThe farmstead is south of the road from Westfall just as you enter Duskwood.\030Find the Defias Docket and return it to Watcher Backus in Duskwood.\030Be careful out there, $N. I know Trias was the one to send you here, but that doesn't mean there isn't anything lurking out in the woods that couldn't cause you some trouble... especially with you investigating the Defias.\030The Missing Diplomat\0312,1,16,2,257,2,840\0302,18,111,2,261,4,840\0302,116,190,2,257,1,840\0302,192,288,2,257,1,840\0302,290,342,2,257,1,840\0302,347,414,2,257,2,840\0302,419,494,2,257,1,840\0303,1,67,2,384,1,840\0301,1,27,4,272,1,840\0301,29,76,4,272,4,840\0301,81,113,4,272,1,840\0301,115,182,4,272,1,840\0301,184,271,4,272,4,840\0304,1,25,3,256,1,840\0304,27,176,3,256,1,840\0304,178,222,3,256,1,840\031840,2,8,Watcher Backus\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,7,Westfall\0302,0,0,8,Watcher Backus\0302,0,0,8,Duskwood\0311243,19,1243,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301245,23,1245,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5947,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1245]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yeah... this is an interesting read. Jorgen and DeLavey were smart to bring me in on this.$B$BSeems the Defias have been trying pretty hard to complete this plan of theirs. Hmm... what's this? Fist? That's a familiar name.\030Whoa, this looks way too complex to be something to just lead you astray. I shouldn't even be looking at this stuff. Take it to Trias--he'll be able to make sense of it. And DON'T let anyone get in your way. This is bigger than me. It might even be bigger than him, but we'll see.$B$BAnd do me a favor, $N, don't tell anyone I helped you. If my superiors found out I knew about any of this and didn't share it with them they'd probably hang me.\030Bring the Defias Docket to Elling Trias in Stormwind.\030I see you're back, and in one piece. We both know you're not here for cheese, so let's cut out the pleasantries. Was Backus any help, or have you even left for Duskwood yet?\030The Missing Diplomat\0312,1,73,2,257,1,840\0302,75,116,2,257,1,840\0302,118,169,2,257,1,840\0302,171,207,2,257,1,840\0302,209,231,2,257,1,840\0302,233,280,2,257,4,840\0302,285,338,2,257,1,840\0302,340,444,2,257,4,840\0303,1,53,2,384,1,840\0301,1,7,4,272,1,482\0301,9,36,4,272,1,482\0301,38,90,4,272,1,482\0301,95,172,4,272,4,482\0301,174,179,4,272,1,482\0301,181,192,4,272,2,482\0301,194,198,4,272,2,482\0301,200,222,4,272,1,482\0304,1,36,3,256,1,482\0304,38,112,3,256,1,482\0304,114,173,3,256,2,482\031482,2,9,Elling Trias\0304959,4,12,Jorgen\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,3,Trias--he'll\0302,0,0,9,Elling Trias\0302,0,0,9,Stormwind\0311244,19,1244,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301246,23,1246,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1246]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031What?!$B$BYou come into me alley and ask questions about me personal business? Business which you obviously have nothing to do with.\030Yeah, now that I think about it... Dashel... Dashel something... What was his name? FIST! Dashel Stonefist. They call him Fist in some circles--probably on account that he likes to get in brawls.$B$BYou can find him in Old Town usually--right smack dab in the center of it. Go talk to him. If you have to, use a sword or something heavy and blunt to persuade him to open up some. And don't hesitate. If he's in this as deep as these papers suggest, then he's not going to give you any information willingly.\030Speak to Dashel Stonefist in Stormwind.\030\030The Missing Diplomat\0312,1,34,2,257,1,482\0302,36,44,2,257,1,482\0302,46,64,2,257,1,482\0302,66,83,2,257,2,482\0302,85,89,2,257,1,482\0302,91,107,2,257,1,482\0302,109,195,2,257,1,482\0302,200,273,2,257,1,482\0302,275,289,2,257,1,482\0302,291,379,2,257,4,482\0302,381,399,2,257,1,482\0302,401,507,2,257,4,482\0303,1,39,2,384,1,482\0301,1,6,4,272,2,4961\0301,11,78,4,272,2,4961\0301,80,132,4,272,1,4961\0314961,2,6,Dashel Stonefist\0304961,2,13,Dashel Stonefist\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,8,Old Town\0302,0,0,13,Dashel Stonefist\0302,0,0,13,Stormwind\0311245,19,1245,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301447,23,1447,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1247]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Good to see you're still alive, $N. So, it went well with Dashel then, huh?$B$BI've been reading up more on this plan of theirs, and although it doesn't state the name of the diplomat they were after, it does talk about this plan B they enacted after failing on their first attempt to capture him.$B$BThis Slim that Dashel mentioned doesn't have any other name written here, but if you say he's in Menethil, then that's a start.\030So yeah... um... I might know something 'bout that meeting at Addle's Stead. Happened a few weeks back I think. I really didn't have any part in it. Me part was done when plan A failed... damn adventurers.$B$BThe guy we got on the inside for plan B came out of Menethil; guy called Slim. That's all I know regarding their backup plan.\030Speak to Elling Trias in Stormwind.\030\030The Missing Diplomat\0312,1,10,2,257,1,4961\0302,18,76,2,257,4,4961\0302,78,111,2,257,1,4961\0302,113,148,2,257,1,4961\0302,150,187,2,257,1,4961\0302,189,205,2,257,1,4961\0302,210,287,2,257,1,4961\0302,289,334,2,257,1,4961\0303,1,35,2,384,1,4961\0301,1,35,4,272,1,482\0301,37,75,4,272,2,482\0301,80,297,4,272,1,482\0301,302,428,4,272,4,482\031482,2,9,Elling Trias\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,2,Addle's Stead\0302,0,0,9,Elling Trias\0302,0,0,9,Stormwind\0304,0,0,13,Menethil\0311447,19,1447,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301248,23,1248,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1248]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Welcome, welcome, welcome, $N. Good of you to join us. Perhaps an ale today? Or some mutton?$B$BName your pleasure and I'll see to it that you're taken care of. My name is Mikhail, and I look forward to serving you.$B$BHmm? What's that? Trias? Keep your voice down, my friend. This isn't something for the whole tavern to hear about.\030A contact of mine retired in the Wetlands at the harbor city of Menethil. He should be willing to help on your word alone if you tell him you're working for me. His name is Mikhail. He mentioned becoming a bartender before leaving Stormwind a few years ago.$B$BSpeak to him, find this Slim, and find out if there's anything else to know about this kidnapped diplomat. We need to find out where they've taken him, or at least who he is. The docket doesn't mention anything about their plans after he's captured.\030Speak to Mikhail in the Wetlands.\030\030The Missing Diplomat\0312,1,73,2,257,1,482\0302,75,160,2,257,4,482\0302,162,181,2,257,1,482\0302,183,257,2,321,1,482\0302,262,367,2,261,4,482\0302,369,435,2,259,1,482\0302,437,510,2,257,1,482\0303,1,33,2,384,1,482\0301,1,30,4,272,1,4963\0301,32,54,4,272,1,4963\0301,56,76,4,272,4,4963\0301,78,92,4,272,2,4963\0301,97,160,4,272,1,4963\0301,162,215,4,272,1,4963\0301,220,223,4,272,2,4963\0301,225,236,4,272,2,4963\0301,238,243,4,272,2,4963\0301,245,276,4,272,1,4963\0301,278,333,4,272,1,4963\0314963,2,3,Mikhail\0304963,2,8,Mikhail\0304963,4,14,Mikhail\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,1,Wetlands\0302,0,0,8,Mikhail\0302,0,0,8,Wetlands\0311247,19,1247,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301249,23,1249,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1249]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Caught him, huh? Good for you. I'm surprised that was Slim.$B$BI'll be honest, I never thought I'd miss the excitement of some of the more devious underground activities. I guess old habits die hard. Don't mention that to Elling--he'd probably try and get me to come back to Stormwind if he heard I missed the action.$B$BI'm glad I could at least be of a little service to you while you were in Menethil. If you need anything else, just ask.\030You say Elling sent you here? Well then, the hospitality I expressed is now tenfold. Anything you need, just ask. I will do my best to aid you.$B$BHmm, Slim, you say? Not sure the name sounds familiar, but I'll keep my eyes out for him.$B$BDon't look now, $N, but the gentleman over by the exit is looking over here. He's listening to our conversation a little too intently if you catch my meaning? If I were you, I'd do what you can to subdue him before he makes a break for the door.\030Subdue Tapoke Jahn before he escapes, and then return to Mikhail in Menethil.\030Defeat Tapoke Jahn\030Did he slip away? He looked a little shady the way he was watching us.\030The Missing Diplomat\0312,1,29,2,257,2,4963\0302,31,84,2,257,1,4963\0302,86,113,2,259,1,4963\0302,115,143,2,257,3,4963\0302,148,166,2,257,2,4963\0302,168,236,2,257,1,4963\0302,241,316,2,257,1,4963\0302,318,398,2,257,4,4963\0302,400,485,2,265,4,4963\0303,1,77,2,392,1,4963\0301,1,16,4,272,2,4963\0301,18,30,4,272,1,4963\0301,32,59,4,272,1,4963\0301,64,170,4,272,1,4963\0301,172,199,4,272,1,4963\0301,201,317,4,272,4,4963\0301,322,404,4,272,4,4963\0301,406,441,4,274,4,4963\0305,1,17,3,256,2,4963\0305,19,70,3,256,1,4963\0304,1,18,3,384,1,4963\0314963,2,10,Mikhail\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,10,Mikhail\0302,0,0,10,Menethil\0304,0,0,16,Elling--he'd\0304,0,0,16,Stormwind\0304,0,0,17,Menethil\0311248,19,1248,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301250,23,1250,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[125]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Excellent recovery, $N! I never thought I'd see these tools again.\030I could really use a hand here, $N.  With the town under siege, it's been hard to get supplies.  My tools were being delivered from Goldshire by wagon but the bridge was blown out.  We put the tools in a boat but the orcs hit it with a catapult.  Just my luck, my toolbox sank right to the bottom of the lake.$B$BRetrieve my toolbox, $N, and I'll make it worth your while.\030Foreman Oslow of Lakeshire wants you to retrieve his toolbox from the bottom of Lake Everstill.\030Were you able to find my tools?\030The Lost Tools\0312,1,35,2,257,4,341\0302,38,95,2,257,1,341\0302,98,180,2,257,1,341\0302,183,245,2,257,1,341\0302,248,309,2,257,1,341\0302,314,372,2,257,1,341\0303,1,95,2,386,1,341\0301,1,23,4,272,1,341\0301,25,66,4,272,1,341\0304,1,31,3,256,2,341\031341,2,7,Foreman Oslow\0312,44,1433,0,\0302,0,0,3,Goldshire\03189,23,89,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,1309,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1250]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031THE KING?! I mean... the king? The real king? Are you joking? You didn't mention you were looking for the king's kidnappers. I didn't even hear he was missing--that would explain his son being crowned some.$B$BI'll send word to Elling right away. He'll want to know you're on the trail.$B$BI would never have guessed Jahn would sell out Stormwind for some lousy coin. Even a rogue's got to have honor when it comes to some things.$B$BThe key now is to find this Hendel. And I think I can help with that.\030The Defias didn't pay me well enough to die for their cause. They took the king. Yeah, the king of Stormwind, not some lowly diplomat. He was on his way to Theramore to meet with Jaina Proudmore--it was a big deal apparently, and a big secret. But it's not just the Defias that are involved. They're working with someone. I think they knew this was bigger than them.$B$BMy part was just to get their man on board the king's ship while it was in the harbor. The guy's name was Hendel. That's all I know. I swear!\030Speak to Mikhail in the Wetlands.\030\030The Missing Diplomat\0312,1,60,2,257,1,4962\0302,62,80,2,257,1,4962\0302,82,134,2,257,1,4962\0302,136,243,2,257,4,4962\0302,245,291,2,257,1,4962\0302,293,321,2,257,1,4962\0302,323,366,2,257,1,4962\0302,371,456,2,257,1,4962\0302,458,483,2,257,1,4962\0302,485,502,2,257,1,4962\0302,504,511,2,257,1,4962\0303,1,33,2,384,1,4962\0301,1,10,4,272,2,4963\0301,12,20,4,272,1,4963\0301,22,30,4,272,2,4963\0301,32,45,4,272,2,4963\0301,47,61,4,272,2,4963\0301,63,124,4,272,1,4963\0301,126,206,4,276,4,4963\0301,211,246,4,272,1,4963\0301,248,286,4,274,1,4963\0301,291,367,4,272,4,4963\0301,369,430,4,272,1,4963\0301,435,469,4,272,1,4963\0301,471,503,4,272,1,4963\0314963,2,12,Mikhail\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,4,Theramore\0302,0,0,12,Mikhail\0302,0,0,12,Wetlands\0304,0,0,20,Elling\0311249,19,1249,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301264,23,1264,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1251]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I grant that humans have strange decorating tastes, but would they use a plain iron shield to adorn their fireplace? Perhaps this shield was placed there by the ones who burned the inn.$B$BA warning? A threat?\030An iron shield, blackened by the fire that raged through the inn, is affixed to the crumbling chimney, one of the few remaining parts of the structure that once made up the Shady Rest Inn.$B$BThe shield can be removed from the brick of the chimney.\030Bring the Blackened Iron Shield to Krog in Brackenwall Village.\030What's that you have there, $n? Evidence from the remains of the Shady Rest Inn?\030The Black Shield\0312,1,188,2,257,1,0\0302,193,248,2,257,1,0\0303,1,63,2,384,1,0\0301,1,116,4,272,4,4926\0301,118,185,4,272,4,4926\0301,190,199,4,272,2,4926\0301,201,209,4,276,2,4926\0304,1,31,3,256,2,4926\0304,33,80,3,256,2,4926\0314926,2,3,Krog\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,3,Krog\0302,0,0,3,Brackenwall Village\0311321,23,1321,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,20992,GIVER,?,9,Black Shield",[1252]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It's never good news when a guard's badge is brought to me.$B$BSometimes it's a man or woman who's fallen in battle, and I'm left to bring the news to the grieving family. Other times we never find out what happened to them. And other times it's even worse than that.\030A glint of light on the ground catches your eye from underneath the rubble. Brushing away debris and ash caked onto the object reveals the insignia of a gold anchor on white enameled on the surface: the sign of Theramore.$B$BUnderneath the anchor is embossed the name \"Lieutenant Paval Reethe\".\030Bring Reethe's Badge to Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore.\030Have you found anything of interest at the Shady Rest Inn?\030Lieutenant Paval Reethe\0312,1,75,2,257,1,0\0302,77,221,2,257,1,0\0302,226,294,2,257,1,0\0303,1,58,2,384,1,0\0301,1,59,4,272,1,4944\0301,64,171,4,276,1,4944\0301,173,224,4,272,1,4944\0301,226,267,4,272,1,4944\0304,1,58,3,256,2,4944\0314980,2,3,Paval Reethe\0304944,2,4,Captain Garran Vimes\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,4,Captain Garran Vimes\0302,0,0,4,Theramore\0303,0,0,9,Shady Rest Inn\0311259,23,1259,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,21042,GIVER,?,9,Theramore Guard Badge",[1253]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hm, I'm no expert with the construction of arms and armor. Their use, yes, but not their making.$B$BThis shield seems as ordinary as any, excepting the damage from the fire that engulfed the inn.\030An iron shield, blackened by the fire that raged through the inn, is affixed to the crumbling chimney, one of the few remaining parts of the structure that once made up the Shady Rest Inn.$B$BThe shield can be removed from the brick of the chimney.\030Bring the Blackened Iron Shield to Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore.\030Have you found evidence from the site of the Shady Rest Inn?\030The Black Shield\0312,1,188,2,257,1,0\0302,193,248,2,257,1,0\0303,1,69,2,384,1,0\0301,1,58,4,272,1,4944\0301,60,96,4,272,1,4944\0301,101,195,4,272,4,4944\0304,1,60,3,256,2,4944\0314944,2,3,Captain Garran Vimes\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,3,Captain Garran Vimes\0302,0,0,3,Theramore\0311319,23,1319,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,20992,GIVER,?,9,Black Shield",[1258]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031These are wonderful specimens, $N! The shells are in perfect condition, and the meat is pink and tender. The blood of a chef is in your veins, I'm sure of it!\030Another component of my new recipe is the shelled leg of a giant crab.  And the crabs they have in Dustwallow -- Muckshells they call them -- just won't do!  I'm afraid the only suitable crabs live far away, in the Swamp of Sorrows.$B$BThe shell of the crab leg is a key element of the dish's presentation so I need pristine, unscarred legs.  An adult crab might only have one or two such legs, and I need a lot in order to research my dish.$B$BSo, $N... are you willing to travel?\030Bring 12 Pristine Crawler Legs to Morgan Stern in Theramore.\030My research with the Mudrock tongues is progressing nicely. I trust your crab hunt goes well?\030... and Bugs\0312,1,70,2,257,1,4794\0302,73,156,2,257,1,4794\0302,159,232,2,257,1,4794\0302,237,341,2,259,1,4794\0302,344,441,2,259,4,4794\0302,456,481,2,257,2,4794\0303,1,60,2,384,1,4794\0301,1,34,4,272,1,4794\0301,36,104,4,272,1,4794\0301,106,158,4,272,1,4794\0304,1,59,3,256,1,4794\0304,61,93,3,256,2,4794\0316827,2,1,Crab\0306827,2,4,Crab\0306827,2,5,Crab\0306250,2,7,Crawler\0304794,2,7,Morgan Stern\0306827,3,12,Crab\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,2,Dustwallow\0302,0,0,3,Swamp of Sorrows\0302,0,0,7,Morgan Stern\0302,0,0,7,Theramore\0311204,19,1204,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5938,OBJECTIVE,12,15,",[1259]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hello, $N. You'd like information about a specific member of the Theramore guard? Reethe, was it?$B$BJust give me a moment to find the right book.\030I don't recognize the name of Lieutenant Paval Reethe. Your best bet would be to check with Adjutant Tesoran. He keeps track of all the records for the Theramore guard, from personnel to their equipment.$B$BHe should be able to tell you who this Reethe is with a quick check of his books.\030Find out more about Reethe from Adjutant Tesoran in Theramore.\030\030Lieutenant Paval Reethe\0312,1,54,2,257,1,4944\0302,56,109,2,257,4,4944\0302,111,203,2,257,1,4944\0302,208,288,2,257,1,4944\0303,1,62,2,384,1,4944\0301,1,10,4,272,1,4948\0301,12,81,4,272,2,4948\0301,83,97,4,272,2,4948\0301,102,146,4,272,1,4948\0314980,2,1,Paval Reethe\0304948,2,2,Adjutant Tesoran\0304979,2,3,Theramore Guard\0304948,2,5,Adjutant Tesoran\0304979,4,7,Theramore Guard\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,5,Adjutant Tesoran\0302,0,0,5,Theramore\0311252,19,1252,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301285,23,1285,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[126]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Again, thank you for your help. The Stormwind army is so busy dealing with the orcs, they don't have the troops to protect Redridge from local threats like the gnolls.\030$N, the gnolls are still out there.  I can hear their baying as they hunt in the hills above Lakeshire.  And one cry is louder than the rest - Yowler,  their leader.$B$BKill Yowler and send his pack scattering!  Bring me his paw as proof.$B$BAnd be careful, this gnoll is their leader for a reason.  He is no Mongrel...\030Bring Yowler's Paw to Verner Osgood in Lakeshire.\030Yowler is a dangerous creature, $N. If you're not ready for him, I understand.\030Howling in the Hills\0312,1,35,2,257,1,415\0302,38,103,2,257,1,415\0302,106,165,2,257,1,415\0302,170,210,2,257,1,415\0302,213,238,2,257,1,415\0302,243,298,2,257,1,415\0302,301,319,2,257,1,415\0303,1,49,2,384,1,415\0301,1,31,4,272,1,415\0301,33,167,4,286,1,415\0304,1,35,3,256,1,415\0304,37,78,3,256,4,415\031518,2,3,Yowler\030518,2,4,Yowler\030415,2,8,Verner Osgood\030518,3,11,Yowler\0312,44,1433,0,\0302,0,0,8,Verner Osgood\0302,0,0,8,Lakeshire\031124,19,124,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3614,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1260]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh, my uncle sent you, did he?$B$BWell I've been researching recipes and I have some leads, but I need help.$B$BHelp from someone willing to get his feet wet.\030I'm developing a new menu for the restaurant.  It will be filled with rural dishes with a \"bayou\" theme.  I think my clientele at the Blue Recluse will love them!$B$BI sent my nephew Morgan to Theramore, a city on the edge of the Dustwallow Marsh.  He's there gathering recipes from the locals, and I must know what he found so far.$B$BThe trip to Theramore is long.  Too long for me.  But I bet a young $c like yourself would jump at the chance to travel, yes?\030Speak with Morgan Stern in Theramore.\030\030Morgan Stern\0312,1,45,2,257,1,1141\0302,48,104,2,257,3,1141\0302,107,162,2,257,3,1141\0302,167,247,2,257,1,1141\0302,250,332,2,257,1,1141\0302,337,366,2,257,1,1141\0302,369,384,2,257,1,1141\0302,387,461,2,257,4,1141\0303,1,37,2,384,1,1141\0301,1,30,4,272,2,4794\0301,35,108,4,274,1,4794\0301,113,158,4,272,1,4794\0314794,2,9,Morgan Stern\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,3,Blue Recluse\0302,0,0,4,Theramore\0302,0,0,6,Theramore\0302,0,0,9,Theramore\0311204,23,1204,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301204,24,1204,UNKNOWN\031",[1261]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This pendant was worn by a soldier of Stormwind??$B$BThank you, $N. You have revealed the secret of Marg's death. But this pendant is a new mystery to solve, one that may have dire effects on the Alliance, and the Horde.\030Cursed muckshell!  You can't kill Marg!  Ah, but I am dead.  So it must have slain me...$B$BBut my mission!  My mission!  You, $N, must complete it.$B$BWhile near Theramore, I spied a group of Alliance soldiers camped on the beach.  And one soldier wore a pendant... a pendant laden with more gems than any soldier could afford!$B$BThat night I snuck into their camp and stole the pendant, but on my return to base a muckshell crab-man killed me!$B$B$N, you must find that muckshell and recover the pendant!\030Bring the Jeweled Pendant to Nazeer in Brackenwall Village.\030$N, did you discover Marg's fate?\030Marg Speaks\0312,1,17,2,261,1,0\0302,20,39,2,257,1,0\0302,42,59,2,257,1,0\0302,62,88,2,261,1,0\0302,93,107,2,257,1,0\0302,110,120,2,257,1,0\0302,123,148,2,257,1,0\0302,153,231,2,257,1,0\0302,234,266,2,257,1,0\0302,268,328,2,257,4,0\0302,333,446,2,257,1,0\0302,451,507,2,257,1,0\0303,1,59,2,384,1,0\0301,1,49,4,272,2,4791\0301,54,67,4,272,1,4791\0301,69,113,4,272,1,4791\0301,115,220,4,272,1,4791\0304,1,33,3,256,2,4791\031\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,8,Theramore\0302,0,0,13,Nazeer\0302,0,0,13,Brackenwall Village\0311240,19,1240,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301262,23,1262,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,2076,GIVER,?,9,Bubbling Cauldron\030ITEM,5942,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1262]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This pendant was crafted with great skill and precision, $N. No orc would covet such a jewel...$B$BBut many humans would.$B$BI will have this pendant studied. In time let us hope that its mysteries will be revealed to us.\030It is strange that the pendant Marg stole was in the hands of common soldiers.  Perhaps its owner was in disguise, or perhaps the soldiers themselves stole it!$B$BRegardless of which is true, this is a noble's pendant and we must discover its true owner if we are to unravel its mystery.$B$BTake the pendant to Zor Lonetree in Orgrimmar.  He is well schooled in Alliance politics, and will know if this pendant has a history among the nobles of Stormwind.\030Bring the Jeweled Pendant to Zor Lonetree in Orgrimmar.\030You traveled from Brackenwall Village in Dustwallow? How fares Nazeer, and how fare his efforts in the marsh?\030Report to Zor\0312,1,78,2,257,1,4791\0302,81,159,2,257,4,4791\0302,164,287,2,257,4,4791\0302,292,337,2,257,1,4791\0302,340,455,2,321,4,4791\0303,1,55,2,384,1,4791\0301,1,60,4,272,1,4047\0301,62,95,4,272,4,4047\0301,100,121,4,272,4,4047\0301,126,158,4,272,3,4047\0301,160,221,4,274,3,4047\0304,1,52,3,256,2,4047\0304,54,109,3,256,2,4047\0314047,2,4,Zor Lonetree\0304047,2,6,Zor Lonetree\0307903,4,8,Jewel\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,4,Zor Lonetree\0302,0,0,4,Orgrimmar\0302,0,0,5,Alliance\0302,0,0,6,Zor Lonetree\0302,0,0,6,Orgrimmar\0303,0,0,12,Brackenwall Village\0303,0,0,12,Dustwallow\0311261,19,1261,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0307541,23,7541,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1264]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A pleasure to meet you, $N. I am Commander Samaul. I'm in charge of Miss Proudmoore's forces here in Theramore.$B$BAlthough I'm quite busy, if you have any questions, please feel free to speak up. I might have to keep it short, but there's no reason for me to be rude if you need my help.$B$BIf you plan on traveling out of the city, I'd suggest you be careful. Besides ogres, orcs and murlocs, the southern part of the swamp is filled with black dragons.\030The beginning of every month the Kul Tiras Marines all get paid and usually leave Theramore for somewhere else. A lot of them come here to womanize, carouse, and just have a good time. One of those groups I'd consider regulars here at the tavern, and I believe this Hendel is among them.$B$BCommander Samaul in Theramore would be able to help you find him if Hendel's still stationed there. He's completely loyal to Proudmoore, but if you drop Elling's name, he should help you out... discreetly.\030Find Commander Samaul in Dustwallow Marsh.\030\030The Missing Diplomat\0312,1,111,2,257,1,4963\0302,113,184,2,257,1,4963\0302,186,287,2,257,4,4963\0302,292,390,2,257,4,4963\0302,392,484,2,257,4,4963\0302,486,496,2,257,1,4963\0303,1,42,2,384,1,4963\0301,1,27,4,272,1,4964\0301,29,50,4,272,1,4964\0301,52,111,4,272,1,4964\0301,116,196,4,272,4,4964\0301,198,288,4,274,4,4964\0301,293,361,4,272,4,4964\0301,363,455,4,272,1,4964\0314964,2,4,Commander Samaul\0304964,2,7,Commander Samaul\0304964,4,9,Commander Samaul\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,4,Theramore\0302,0,0,5,Proudmoore\0302,0,0,7,Dustwallow Marsh\0304,0,0,10,Theramore\0311250,19,1250,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301265,23,1265,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1265]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031The man you seek, the one known as Hendel, is not here. Other sources have brought to the Lady Proudmoore information I believe you already know. She has asked me to find you, and give you aid in your venture. If you would allow it, I will tell you where to find Private Hendel so we can bring him to justice.\030Hendel? Yes, I know the man. But why would you need one of my soldiers?$B$BElling sent you to find him? Hmm, I don't like the sound of that. Elling wouldn't have you come to me first if your business wasn't troubling. I understand if you can't tell me what this is about, but know this: I have a duty to protect these lands. If you're going to cause a disturbance, then I suggest you inform me of whatever you can.$B$BI believe Hendel was stationed at the first tower outside of Theramore. Be cautious.\030Search Sentry Point for any sign of Private Hendel.\030Sentry Point explored\030Yes, $N?\030The Missing Diplomat\0312,1,7,2,257,2,4964\0302,9,28,2,257,1,4964\0302,30,71,2,259,4,4964\0302,76,103,2,257,2,4964\0302,105,140,2,257,1,4964\0302,142,217,2,257,4,4964\0302,219,324,2,271,4,4964\0302,326,414,2,257,4,4964\0302,419,489,2,257,4,4964\0302,491,502,2,257,1,4964\0303,1,51,2,384,1,4964\0301,1,55,4,274,1,4967\0301,57,145,4,272,4,4967\0301,147,209,4,272,1,4967\0301,211,309,4,272,4,4967\0305,1,8,3,256,2,4967\0304,1,21,3,384,1,4964\0314966,2,11,Private Hendel\03015065,4,13,Lady\0304966,4,15,Private Hendel\0312,1519,1453,0,\0304,0,0,13,Lady Proudmoore\0311264,19,1264,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301266,23,1266,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1266]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hello, citizen. This is a dangerous place to be wandering about. I wouldn't hang around too long if you value your life.$B$BIf you keep your questions short, I'll see if I can help you. Just keep your eyes open for any of those filthy ogres. Rumor has it there's a Horde base somewhere in the swamps. The infiltrators are doing what they can to find it, but the process has been slow going and we've had little progress.\030Private Hendel is to the west of here. He's currently on guard duty protecting some of Theramore's infiltrators while they rest. They've been keeping tabs on the Horde base, Brackenwall, and looking for anything else that might threaten our borders.$B$BYou should have no problem finding him; just look for the tents along the road.$B$BI have another matter to attend to, but I shall catch up to you soon enough. You can always find me in the Lady Proudmoore's tower if you have any problems.\030Find Private Hendel in Dustwallow Marsh.\030\030The Missing Diplomat\0312,1,38,2,257,1,4967\0302,40,128,2,257,1,4967\0302,130,249,2,261,4,4967\0302,254,332,2,261,1,4967\0302,337,412,2,257,3,4967\0302,414,492,2,257,4,4967\0303,1,40,2,384,1,4967\0301,1,15,4,272,1,4966\0301,17,64,4,272,1,4966\0301,66,120,4,272,4,4966\0301,125,185,4,272,4,4966\0301,187,241,4,272,1,4966\0301,243,300,4,272,1,4966\0301,302,420,4,272,1,4966\0314966,2,1,Private Hendel\03015065,2,6,Lady\0304966,2,7,Private Hendel\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,6,Lady Proudmoore's\0302,0,0,7,Dustwallow Marsh\0311265,19,1265,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301324,23,1324,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1267]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you for your help $N. Please accept this token of my appriciation for your efforts.\030\030Speak to Jaina Proudmore in Dustwallow Swamp.\030\030The Missing Diplomat\0313,1,45,2,384,1,4967\0301,1,27,4,272,1,4968\0301,29,89,4,272,1,4968\031\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,1,Jaina Proudmore\0302,0,0,1,Dustwallow Swamp\0311324,19,1324,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1268]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hoofprints... It could have been the quilboar, I suppose. Or maybe even the centaur. Their presence in the Barrens is not insignificant, and I would not think it a stretch to commit such an act.$B$BDid I tell you? It wasn't just that the inn was burned down... The owner's woman and pup were killed. Bad business, that.$B$BNonetheless, I will send Kagoro to find where the tracks lead.\030Rows of hoofprints lead away from the still-smoking skeleton of the Shady Rest Inn. There are at least a few visible impressions, with more rows of prints almost imperceptible in the soft mud of the marsh.\030Report about the suspicious prints at the Shady Rest Inn to Krog in Brackenwall Village.\030\030Suspicious Hoofprints\0312,1,83,2,257,1,0\0302,85,205,2,257,1,0\0303,1,88,2,384,1,0\0301,1,13,4,272,1,4926\0301,15,57,4,272,4,4926\0301,59,84,4,272,4,4926\0301,86,194,4,272,4,4926\0301,199,213,4,272,2,4926\0301,215,260,4,272,1,4926\0301,262,299,4,272,1,4926\0301,301,319,4,272,1,4926\0301,324,385,4,272,3,4926\0316412,2,1,Skeleton\0304926,2,3,Krog\03093,4,6,Centaur\0304972,4,12,Kagoro\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,3,Shady Rest Inn\0302,0,0,3,Krog\0302,0,0,3,Brackenwall Village\0304,0,0,7,Barrens\031\031OBJECT,187273,GIVER,?,9,Suspicious Hoofprint",[1269]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I know this human, Paval Reethe. Pathetic, even for his kind. He deserted his fellow soldiers and is now hiding out in the woods.$B$BI sent Ogron out to track him down. Some of the others suspect he's been stealing from our supplies. I think I saw Ogron heading off to the southeast.\030A glint of light on the ground catches your eye from underneath the rubble. Brushing debris and ash caked onto the object reveals the insignia of a gold anchor on white, enameled on the surface: the sign of Theramore.$B$BUnderneath the anchor is embossed the name \"Lieutenant Paval Reethe\".\030Bring Reethe's Badge to Krog in Brackenwall Village.\030Have you found any leads on what happened at the Shady Rest Inn?\030Lieutenant Paval Reethe\0312,1,75,2,257,1,0\0302,77,217,2,257,1,0\0302,222,290,2,257,1,0\0303,1,52,2,384,1,0\0301,1,32,4,272,1,4926\0301,34,61,4,272,1,4926\0301,63,129,4,272,1,4926\0301,134,168,4,272,1,4926\0301,170,233,4,272,4,4926\0301,235,283,4,272,1,4926\0304,1,64,3,256,2,4926\0314980,2,3,Paval Reethe\0304926,2,4,Krog\0304980,4,5,Paval Reethe\0304983,4,8,Ogron\0304983,4,10,Ogron\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,4,Krog\0302,0,0,4,Brackenwall Village\0303,0,0,11,Shady Rest Inn\0311273,23,1273,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,21042,GIVER,?,9,Theramore Guard Badge",[127]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Pleasure doin' business with you, matey!\030Lake Everstill is famous for its spotted sunfish.  There's always demand for them...and I'm running low!$B$BBring me a batch of 10 and I'll barter well for them.  If you can't fish yourself, then...maybe you can get them off the murlocs!\030Bring 10 Spotted Sunfish to Dockmaster Baren in Lakeshire.\030You have some sunfish for me, eh?\030Selling Fish\0312,1,49,2,257,1,381\0302,52,104,2,257,1,381\0302,109,161,2,257,1,381\0302,164,237,2,257,4,381\0303,1,58,2,384,1,381\0301,1,40,4,272,1,381\0304,1,33,3,256,2,381\031381,2,5,Dockmaster Baren\0312,44,1433,0,\0302,0,0,5,Dockmaster Baren\0302,0,0,5,Lakeshire\031\031ITEM,1467,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[1270]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Stinky was here with the herbs I ask of him, and he told me you helped him out of a bind. Good work! A friend of Stinky's is a friend of mine!$B$BHe asked me to give you this if I ever saw you, right before he walked back south toward the marsh.\030Great, finally something that doesn't want to eat me!!$B$BI need help handling the critters around here, and you fit the mold, $gbuddy:lady;.$B$BA goblin from Ratchet named Mebok Mizzyrix needs some bogbean leaves for a potion, or something... I honestly don't care why -- his money was good and I know this swamp, so here I am.$B$BToo bad I got myself surrounded before I found the bogbean!  Can you help me out of here, and watch my back as I look for Mebok's plant?\030Escort \"Stinky\" Ignatz, then speak with Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet.\030Help Stinky find Bogbean Leaves\030\030Stinky's Escape\0312,1,54,2,257,1,4880\0302,59,141,2,259,1,4880\0302,146,243,2,259,1,4880\0302,245,328,2,257,1,4880\0302,333,391,2,257,1,4880\0302,394,468,2,257,2,4880\0303,1,66,2,384,1,4880\0301,1,89,4,274,1,3446\0301,91,100,4,272,1,3446\0301,102,142,4,272,1,3446\0301,147,245,4,280,4,3446\0304,1,31,3,384,1,4880\03115065,2,2,Lady\0303446,2,3,Mebok Mizzyrix\0303446,2,7,Mebok Mizzyrix\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,3,Ratchet\0302,0,0,7,Ratchet\031\031",[1271]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031My nephew said you aided him with his research in Dustwallow, and that you helped his associate out of a tight spot. Well, we Sterns stick together and we don't ignore our friends!$B$BSo wash your hands, $N, because we're about to throw a party in your honor!\030\030\030\030Feast at the Blue Recluse\0311,1,116,4,272,1,1141\0301,118,180,4,272,1,1141\0301,185,259,4,274,1,1141\0314950,4,1,Spot\0312,15,1445,0,\0304,0,0,1,Dustwallow\0311222,21,1222,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301258,21,1258,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1273]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Hmph. It is good that Reethe will no longer be lurking around the swamp, but it is a shame that humans are built so frail that he could not recover from a little arrow wound.$B$BIt seems that this thread of the mystery has led nowhere, and we must look elsewhere.\030It took a long time, but I found Reethe. He hide good for a human.$B$BOgron worried that he might be crazy after so much time in swamp. You come with me for we go get answers from him.\030Go with Ogron to speak with Reethe, then return to Krog in Brackenwall Village.\030Question Reethe with Ogron\030Did you find Reethe?\030Questioning Reethe\0312,1,40,2,257,1,4983\0302,42,66,2,257,1,4983\0302,71,135,2,257,4,4983\0302,137,184,2,257,1,4983\0303,1,79,2,384,1,4983\0301,1,5,4,272,1,4926\0301,7,174,4,272,4,4926\0301,179,263,4,272,4,4926\0305,1,20,3,256,2,4926\0304,1,26,3,384,1,4983\0314983,2,3,Ogron\0304983,2,5,Ogron\0304926,2,5,Krog\0304983,3,10,Ogron\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,5,Krog\0302,0,0,5,Brackenwall Village\0311269,19,1269,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1274]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hello, $N. I am Bishop DeLavey.$B$BNo doubt if you're asking me about my business here in the keep then young Thomas has succeeded in requisitioning you to help our kingdom. He has always been adept at following my requests.$B$BI'm afraid I don't have time to elaborate much, so allow me to be blunt... and please, try to keep this from becoming common knowledge.\030Excuse me, $g sir : madam;. Bishop DeLavey asked me to approach adventurers that might be able to help him with a delicate matter.$B$BIf you could quietly head to Stormwind Keep and speak to him at your earliest convenience, I'm sure he would appreciate your help. Again, please be discreet. It is a matter of some importance.\030Find Bishop DeLavey in Stormwind Keep.\030\030The Missing Diplomat\0312,1,27,2,257,1,4982\0302,29,130,2,257,4,4982\0302,135,264,2,257,4,4982\0302,266,291,2,257,1,4982\0302,293,326,2,257,1,4982\0303,1,38,2,384,1,4982\0301,1,10,4,272,1,4960\0301,12,31,4,272,1,4960\0301,36,173,4,272,4,4960\0301,175,224,4,272,1,4960\0301,229,302,4,272,1,4960\0301,304,363,4,272,1,4960\0314960,2,2,Bishop DeLavey\0304960,2,6,Bishop DeLavey\0304960,4,8,Bishop DeLavey\0304982,4,9,Thomas\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,3,Stormwind Keep\0302,0,0,6,Stormwind Keep\0311241,23,1241,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1275]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have traveled far and undoubtedly faced great peril.$B$BYour actions have been selfless. 'Tis for the good of all Azeroth that you help me with my research. I thank you, $N, for all that you have done.$B$BNow if you'll excuse me I have much work to do....\030Foolish blood elves toil with demonic magic. Have they not witnessed what happened with the naga and with the satyrs of Kalimdor?$B$BI fear that the blood elves will meet a similar deformation. Azeroth cannot afford to give birth to another vile race of monsters.$B$BI wish to study the brain stems of the satyr and naga so that I might deduce what fate the elves are headed toward. In Blackfathom Deeps, on the coast of Ashenvale, you will find both satyr and naga.$B$B'Tis a long journey, $n.\030Gershala Nightwhisper in Auberdine wants 8 Corrupt Brain stems.\030Once I have enough samples to study, my true work can begin. With the corrupted brain stems of both the satyr and naga of Blackfathom Deeps I can try to draw a correlation between the mutations.$B$BPerhaps with that gained knowledge we can prevent the blood elves from delving deeper into deformity and evil.\030Researching the Corruption\0312,1,44,2,257,1,8997\0302,46,129,2,257,2,8997\0302,134,193,2,257,3,8997\0302,195,263,2,257,1,8997\0302,268,382,2,259,4,8997\0302,384,466,2,257,3,8997\0302,471,494,2,257,1,8997\0303,1,63,2,390,1,8997\0301,1,56,4,272,1,8997\0301,61,92,4,272,1,8997\0301,94,160,4,274,1,8997\0301,162,205,4,272,1,8997\0301,210,259,4,272,4,8997\0304,1,60,3,256,1,8997\0304,62,194,3,260,1,8997\0304,199,308,3,264,4,8997\0318997,2,8,Gershala Nightwhisper\0312,719,0,0,\0302,0,0,8,Auberdine\031\031ITEM,5952,OBJECTIVE,8,15,",[1276]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes, you are certainly correct. This is a shield that I made.$B$BI'm afraid there's not much more I can tell you though, $n. I craft so many different shields and sets of armor, I can't keep track of them all.\030Ah, I remember now! Mosarn is a well-respected blacksmith in Thunder Bluff. I knew I had heard his name somewhere, before.$B$BIn thanks, the Earthen Ring awarded me with a set of armor crafted by Mosarn. Very good work.$B$BPerhaps he can tell you more about the shield he crafted.$B$BIt's not much of a lead, but since we didn't get anything useful out of Reethe, it's all we have.\030Show the Blackened Iron Shield to Mosarn in Thunder Bluff.\030Hello there, $c. Something I can help you with?\030The Black Shield\0312,1,19,2,257,1,4926\0302,21,75,2,257,1,4926\0302,77,122,2,257,1,4926\0302,127,203,2,257,1,4926\0302,205,219,2,257,1,4926\0302,224,280,2,257,4,4926\0302,285,381,2,257,1,4926\0303,1,58,2,384,1,4926\0301,1,31,4,272,1,4943\0301,33,61,4,272,1,4943\0301,66,124,4,272,1,4943\0301,126,209,4,272,1,4943\0304,1,16,3,256,1,4943\0304,18,47,3,256,2,4943\0314943,2,2,Mosarn\0304943,2,4,Mosarn\0304943,2,8,Mosarn\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,2,Thunder Bluff\0302,0,0,8,Mosarn\0302,0,0,8,Thunder Bluff\0311323,19,1323,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[128]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I see you have fought valiantly against the Blackrock Clan, $C. Your service to our township is great indeed.\030The Blackrock Clan must be destroyed. The Enemy has invaded our lands. These mountains fall under the sovereign right of the King of Stormwind. Our sources tell us that the leaders of each unit within the Clan are known as Champions. You'll find them in their encampment to the north, just west of the road to the Burning Steppes.$B$BMagistrate Solomon wants these foul brutes dead. Slay 15 Blackrock Champions and return to me.\030Kill 15 Blackrock Champions and Guard Howe in Lakeshire will reward you.\030Return once you have slain 15 Blackrock Champions.\030Blackrock Bounty\0312,1,37,2,261,1,903\0302,39,70,2,261,1,903\0302,72,143,2,257,1,903\0302,145,233,2,257,1,903\0302,235,330,2,257,1,903\0302,335,382,2,259,1,903\0302,384,428,2,257,1,903\0303,1,72,2,384,3,903\0301,1,63,4,272,1,903\0301,65,109,4,272,1,903\0304,1,50,3,260,1,903\031344,2,6,Magistrate Solomon\030798,2,6,Solomon\030903,2,8,Guard Howe\0312,44,1433,0,\0302,0,0,4,Clan\0302,0,0,5,Burning Steppes\0302,0,0,8,Lakeshire\031\031NPC,435,OBJECTIVE,15,13,Blackrock Champion",[1282]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031James Hyal's his real name. He opened an inn at the edge of the Barrens. Wanted to make a nice place for travelers to stop over...$B$BMight be he was thinking too big, but the inn did do well for a while. Then we lost control of the roads in the marsh, and the ogres took over.$B$BJames was too stubborn to give up his dream for safety within our walls, and the Shady Rest Inn was burnt to the ground. We're investigating, but haven't had much luck. If you want to help out, see what you can find in the rubble.\030I can't help it if I feel sorry for ol' Jim there. He wasn't always like that. Ran an inn out in the marsh for a while, wonderful place.$B$BLook, I don't really want to talk about it. Bring it up with Captain Vimes if you really have to. He's stationed on the top floor of Foothold Citadel, the large barracks to the east of Lady Jaina's tower.\030Speak with Captain Garran Vimes on the top floor of Foothold Citadel.\030\030They Call Him Smiling Jim\0312,1,50,2,257,4,4921\0302,52,78,2,257,1,4921\0302,80,136,2,257,1,4921\0302,141,183,2,259,1,4921\0302,185,237,2,257,4,4921\0302,239,344,2,257,1,4921\0303,1,69,2,384,1,4921\0301,1,27,4,272,1,4944\0301,29,72,4,272,1,4944\0301,74,130,4,272,1,4944\0301,135,204,4,272,4,4944\0301,206,277,4,276,1,4944\0301,282,401,4,280,1,4944\0301,403,449,4,272,1,4944\0301,451,511,4,274,4,4944\03115065,2,6,Lady\0304944,2,7,Captain Garran Vimes\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,6,Lady Jaina's\0311302,22,1302,UNKNOWN\031",[1284]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hoofprints, eh? It is true that there is an extraordinary amount of centaur activity in the lands near the Dustwallow Marsh. In brief excursions into the Barrens, we found their camps and holdings dotting the area.$B$BI'll send out Falgran Hastil, one of our trackers, to see if he can find where the tracks lead.\030Rows of hoofprints lead away from the still-smoking skeleton of the Shady Rest Inn. There are at least a few visible impressions, with more rows of prints almost imperceptible in the soft mud of the marsh.\030Report about the suspicious prints at the Shady Rest Inn to Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore.\030\030Suspicious Hoofprints\0312,1,83,2,257,1,0\0302,85,205,2,257,1,0\0303,1,94,2,384,1,0\0301,1,15,4,272,2,4944\0301,17,124,4,272,1,4944\0301,126,214,4,272,1,4944\0301,219,313,4,272,4,4944\0316412,2,1,Skeleton\0304944,2,3,Captain Garran Vimes\03093,4,5,Centaur\0305088,4,7,Falgran Hastil\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,3,Shady Rest Inn\0302,0,0,3,Captain Garran Vimes\0302,0,0,3,Theramore\0304,0,0,5,Dustwallow Marsh\031\031OBJECT,187273,GIVER,?,9,Suspicious Hoofprint",[1285]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Missing? That would be Tesoran's kind way of saying traitor.$B$BNo doubt he's one of those fools so blindly loyal to Admiral Daelin that he turned traitor. Isn't that a delicious irony? The deserters accuse us of betraying the Alliance.\030Reddon... Redpath... Ah, here it is! Lieutenant Paval Reethe.$B$BJoined the Theramore guard along with most of the recruits that came across the sea with Lady Proudmoore. Enlisted with the marines of Kul Tiras at the age of sixteen. Distinguished service, promotions...$B$BListed as missing.\030Return the information about Reethe to Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore.\030\030Daelin's Men\0312,1,9,2,257,1,4948\0302,11,20,2,257,1,4948\0302,22,36,2,257,1,4948\0302,38,61,2,257,1,4948\0302,66,170,2,257,1,4948\0302,172,232,2,257,1,4948\0302,234,269,2,257,1,4948\0302,274,291,2,261,1,4948\0303,1,73,2,384,1,4948\0301,1,8,4,276,2,4944\0301,10,60,4,272,4,4944\0301,65,155,4,272,1,4944\0301,157,185,4,272,2,4944\0301,187,236,4,272,1,4944\0314980,2,4,Paval Reethe\0304979,2,5,Theramore Guard\03015065,2,5,Lady\0304944,2,9,Captain Garran Vimes\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,9,Captain Garran Vimes\0302,0,0,9,Theramore\0304,0,0,12,Admiral Daelin\0311259,19,1259,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301286,23,1286,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1286]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Did Vimes send you? Couldn't do his dirty work himself, could he...\030It has been a struggle maintaining a presence in the marsh, but through strength of our resolve, we have been able to maintain several defensive watchtowers throughout the area.$B$BThe latest information and scouting reports I have received indicate that a group of deserters has squatted in our abandoned tower at Lost Point, southeast of the inn.$B$BThe local lieutenant seems to be Balos Jacken. See if you can get some information out of him.$B$BBe warned, $n. He may be a tough nut to crack.\030Get information about Reethe from Balos Jacken and the deserters in Dustwallow Marsh.\030\030The Deserters\0312,1,177,2,257,1,4944\0302,182,348,2,261,1,4944\0302,353,398,2,257,4,4944\0302,400,446,2,257,4,4944\0302,451,464,2,257,1,4944\0302,466,496,2,257,1,4944\0303,1,85,2,384,1,4944\0301,1,19,4,272,2,5089\0301,21,67,4,272,4,5089\0315089,2,3,Balos Jacken\0305089,2,7,Balos Jacken\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,2,Lost Point\0302,0,0,7,Balos Jacken\0302,0,0,7,Dustwallow Marsh\0311285,19,1285,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301287,23,1287,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1287]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I will send Lieutenant Caldwell to deal with the deserters at Lost Point. In addition, I will instruct him to find Reethe. The marsh is not so big and trackless that he should be unable to find him.\030Reethe? That coward?$B$BWe threw him out of camp because he insisted on raiding the supplies of the ogres up at Brackenwall Village. We're not so many in number that we could stand up to those mindless brutes.$B$BHe crossed the line one too many times, so we left him to fend for himself.$B$BNow, I helped you out... So, why don't you help us out and forget you bumped into us?\030Speak with Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore about Reethe.\030\030The Deserters\0312,1,7,2,257,2,5089\0302,9,20,2,257,2,5089\0302,25,132,2,259,1,5089\0302,134,209,2,257,4,5089\0302,214,288,2,257,1,5089\0302,293,316,2,257,1,5089\0302,318,377,2,257,2,5089\0303,1,58,2,384,1,5089\0301,1,73,4,276,3,4944\0301,75,122,4,272,3,4944\0301,124,198,4,272,1,4944\0314944,2,8,Captain Garran Vimes\0305046,4,9,Lieutenant Caldwell\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,3,Brackenwall Village\0302,0,0,8,Theramore\0304,0,0,9,Lost Point\0311286,19,1286,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[129]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thanks, I could really use the meal. Guarding Lakeshire from the orcs and gnolls is tough work!\030Can you do me a favor?  I've prepared a lunch for Guard Parker, but he's out on patrol...he's a big, strong Stormwind guard who can defend himself, but it's much too dangerous out there for a townsperson like me.$B$BSo if you deliver his lunch for me, then come back here and I'll give you a free lunch!  Parker patrols the stretch of road leading to Duskwood.\030Bring Parker's lunch to Guard Parker.  He patrols the road leading to Darkshire.\030Darcy sent me a lunch, did she? Such a kind heart she has. Well...let's have it!\030A Free Lunch\0312,1,22,2,257,2,379\0302,25,212,2,269,1,379\0302,217,303,2,257,4,379\0302,306,360,2,257,1,379\0303,1,37,2,384,1,379\0303,40,80,2,384,1,379\0301,1,36,4,272,4,464\0301,38,95,4,272,1,464\0304,1,31,3,256,2,464\0304,33,58,3,256,1,464\0304,60,80,3,256,1,464\031464,2,2,Guard Parker\0301423,2,2,Stormwind Guard\030464,2,5,Guard Parker\030379,3,9,Darcy\0312,44,1433,0,\0302,0,0,4,Duskwood\0302,0,0,5,Guard Parker\0302,0,0,6,Darkshire\031130,23,130,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[13]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Your worth to The People's Militia has been validated by your brave acts thus far.\030A band of vicious Defias Pillagers has been seen plundering the Gold Coast Quarry, Moonbrook and the Alexston Farmstead.  The People's Militia will not stand for such behavior.  Dispatch immediately, $n, and make the Light's presence known in Westfall.$B$BThe Gold Coast Quarry is near the shore, to the West of the tower.  As the next step of your training, I want you to kill 15 of those foul Defias Pillagers and 15 Defias Looters.\030Gryan Stoutmantle wants you to kill 15 Defias Pillagers and 15 Defias Looters and return to him on Sentinel Hill.\030We have not time to talk, $N. The Defias Pillagers are denying the people of Westfall the peace and prosperity they deserve. Make sure at least 15 Defias Pillagers and 15 Defias Looters have been killed. That will send a clear message that corruption is not welcome here.\030The People's Militia\0312,1,120,2,257,1,234\0302,123,176,2,257,3,234\0302,179,252,2,257,1,234\0302,257,322,2,257,1,234\0302,325,434,2,259,1,234\0303,1,113,2,386,1,234\0301,1,82,4,272,1,234\0304,1,29,3,256,1,234\0304,31,124,3,264,1,234\0304,126,203,3,256,1,234\0304,205,271,3,260,3,234\031234,2,6,Gryan Stoutmantle\0312,40,1436,0,\0302,0,0,3,Westfall\0302,0,0,4,West of the\0304,0,0,7,The People's Militia\03112,19,12,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\03014,23,14,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,589,OBJECTIVE,15,13,Defias Pillager\030NPC,590,OBJECTIVE,15,13,Defias Looter",[130]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You need a bouquet of flowers? You haven't been in town very long...have you already found for yourself a sweetheart here?$B$BI know I shouldn't pry, but it's nice to see that love is in the air... especially in dangerous times like these.\030Before you go back to Darcy, can you bring her some flowers for me?  You can get them at the herbalist shop back in Lakeshire, at the west end of town.$B$BBut when you get the flowers...don't tell the herbalist, Martie, whom they're from, or whom they're for...\030Speak with the Redridge Herbalist, Martie Jainrose.\030\030Visit the Herbalist\0312,1,67,2,257,2,464\0302,70,151,2,257,1,464\0302,156,261,2,257,1,464\0303,1,51,2,384,1,464\0301,1,30,4,274,2,342\0301,32,122,4,272,2,342\0301,127,197,4,272,1,342\0301,199,239,4,272,1,342\031379,2,1,Darcy\030342,2,4,Martie Jainrose\0312,44,1433,0,\0302,0,0,1,Darcy\0302,0,0,2,Lakeshire\031129,19,129,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030131,23,131,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1301]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031James? Oh, he left quite some time ago.$B$BFelt the second wind of patriotism, I suppose. Not hard to see why he would. With all the insanity in Lordaeron, many people joined up with Jaina Proudmoore when she went across the sea.\030Before working here at the Blue Recluse, I was trained by one of the best chefs and innkeepers I'd ever met. His name was James Hyal. Everything I have and everywhere I've gotten in life is thanks to him.$B$BI wonder how he's doing. His brother Vincent and he went to work in a tavern in Menethil Harbor, but I haven't heard from him recently.$B$BIf you ever happen to be headed in that direction, maybe you could say hello to him for me?\030Speak with Vincent Hyal in Menethil Harbor.\030\030James Hyal\0312,1,108,2,257,1,5081\0302,110,133,2,257,1,5081\0302,135,204,2,257,1,5081\0302,209,232,2,257,1,5081\0302,234,343,2,257,1,5081\0302,348,438,2,257,4,5081\0303,1,43,2,384,1,5081\0301,1,6,4,272,2,5082\0301,8,39,4,272,1,5082\0301,44,89,4,272,1,5082\0301,91,119,4,272,4,5082\0301,121,229,4,272,1,5082\0315082,2,7,Vincent Hyal\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,1,Blue Recluse\0302,0,0,5,Menethil Harbor\0302,0,0,7,Menethil Harbor\0304,0,0,12,Lordaeron\0311302,23,1302,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301302,24,1302,UNKNOWN\031",[1302]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031James Hyal, James Hyal... Why does that name sound so familiar?$B$BOf course! The Shady Rest Inn incident. If you have any information about what happened there, I would urge you to speak with Captain Vimes about it. He's handling the investigation.\030My brother James went with Lady Proudmoore across the sea. Last I heard, the fighting had settled down over there, and James was setting up an inn somewhere on the continent. Wherever he is, I'm sure he's doing good business. Damn fine cook he was.$B$BI haven't heard from him for a while now--too busy with his inn, I'd wager--but the clerk in Theramore could probably point you to him. Look for him on the top floor of that keep near the middle of the city. What's it called... Foothold Citadel, that's it.\030Speak with Clerk Lendry at Foothold Citadel in Theramore.\030\030James Hyal\0312,1,58,2,257,1,5082\0302,60,174,2,261,1,5082\0302,176,225,2,257,1,5082\0302,227,248,2,257,1,5082\0302,253,387,2,257,4,5082\0302,389,459,2,257,1,5082\0302,461,479,2,257,1,5082\0302,481,508,2,257,1,5082\0303,1,57,2,384,1,5082\0301,1,25,4,272,1,5083\0301,27,63,4,272,2,5083\0301,68,77,4,272,1,5083\0301,79,106,4,272,1,5083\0301,108,216,4,272,4,5083\0301,218,249,4,272,1,5083\03115065,2,1,Lady\0305083,2,9,Clerk Lendry\0312,11,1437,0,\0302,0,0,5,Theramore\0302,0,0,9,Foothold Citadel\0302,0,0,9,Theramore\0311282,22,1282,UNKNOWN\031",[131]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh, those are lovely! I can't wait to put them in some water!$B$BBut...these are Martie's favorite flowers. Parker didn't have you go to that jealous vixen for this bouquet, did he? You didn't tell her who they were for, did you? If you did, then it wouldn't surprise me if she poisoned them.$B$BOh, but it's not your fault. Thank you, and here's your meal.\030Here is your bouquet.  I chose Daffodils for you.  They're my favorite!\030Give Darcy the Daffodil Bouquet.\030Hello again, $N. Did Parker like the lunch I sent him?\030Delivering Daffodils\0312,1,21,2,257,1,342\0302,24,49,2,257,1,342\0302,52,71,2,257,1,342\0303,1,32,2,384,1,342\0301,1,21,4,272,1,379\0301,23,61,4,272,1,379\0301,66,107,4,272,1,379\0301,109,181,4,272,2,379\0301,183,229,4,272,2,379\0301,231,292,4,276,4,379\0301,297,324,4,272,1,379\0301,326,357,4,272,1,379\0304,1,16,3,256,1,379\0304,18,54,3,256,2,379\031379,2,4,Darcy\0312,44,1433,0,\031130,19,130,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1318]="PARTIAL\031conclusion,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030Now you da king, so maybe you get prized Gordok artifact back from creepy elf who calls himself Prince!  Da king before you failed, just like all da other kings since Tortheldrin - da creepy elf - stole it from old timey Gordok king!$B$BArtifact is called da Gauntlet of Gordok Might.  Old timey stories say only da one true king da Gordok can get it back.  Old timey story also say creepy elf is still around here - you find it and it will become mighty gauntlet you wear forever!  Yar, I show you!\030Find the Gauntlet of Gordok Might and return it to Captain Kromcrush in Dire Maul.$B$BAccording to Kromcrush, the \"old timey story\" says that Tortheldrin - a \"creepy\" elf who called himself a prince - stole it from one of the Gordok kings.\030\030Unfinished Gordok Business\0312,1,103,2,257,4,0\0302,106,233,2,257,1,0\0302,238,284,2,257,4,0\0302,287,356,2,257,1,0\0302,359,481,2,257,3,0\0302,484,499,2,257,1,0\0303,1,82,2,384,4,0\0303,87,239,2,384,1,0\03114325,2,7,Captain Kromcrush\0312,2557,0,0,\0302,0,0,7,Captain Kromcrush\0302,0,0,7,Dire Maul\0302,0,0,8,Kromcrush\031\031ITEM,18336,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1319]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hm... interesting piece of iron you have here. Definitely not made by any of the blacksmiths I know over on this side of the sea, and it's certainly not my work.\030I'm sorry I can't be of much help, $n, but I can refer you to someone who would be. Caz Twosprocket, one of our best blacksmiths, works the forge at the smithy.$B$BTake the shield to him, and see what he can tell you.\030Show the Blackened Iron Shield to Caz Twosprocket in Theramore.\030Something for me to look at?\030The Black Shield\0312,1,83,2,257,4,4944\0302,85,160,2,257,1,4944\0302,165,217,2,257,1,4944\0303,1,63,2,384,1,4944\0301,7,46,4,272,1,4941\0301,48,161,4,272,1,4941\0304,1,28,3,256,2,4941\0314941,2,2,Caz Twosprocket\0304941,2,4,Caz Twosprocket\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,4,Caz Twosprocket\0302,0,0,4,Theramore\0311253,19,1253,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301320,23,1320,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[132]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Bah! I should have let that scoundrel rot when I had the chance. But this information is crucial. Good work.\030What I am about to tell you could cost me my life.  The Defias gang is up to something big.  Last I heard they were working in conjunction with various gnolls, kobolds and even goblins.$B$BTake this note to Stoutmantle.  It explains as much as I know on the subject.\030Take Wiley's Note to Gryan Stoutmantle in Westfall.\030Good to see you back, $N. What did Wiley have to say for himself?\030The Defias Brotherhood\0312,1,50,2,257,4,266\0302,53,91,2,257,1,266\0302,94,185,2,257,1,266\0302,190,219,2,257,1,266\0302,222,266,2,257,1,266\0303,1,51,2,384,1,266\0301,1,4,4,272,1,234\0301,6,64,4,272,1,234\0301,66,97,4,272,1,234\0301,99,108,4,272,1,234\0304,1,25,3,256,1,234\0304,27,65,3,256,2,234\031234,2,6,Gryan Stoutmantle\0312,40,1436,0,\0302,0,0,4,Stoutmantle\0302,0,0,6,Gryan Stoutmantle\0302,0,0,6,Westfall\03165,19,65,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030135,23,135,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1320]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031That's not much information to work on, but we'll have to keep it in mind. Hopefully some of the other pieces of this mystery will fall into place, and paint a more helpful picture of what happened.\030Ah, I almost missed this... The leather strap on the back must have burned off, but it seems like it was made to fit a large person. I'd guess a tauren, actually.$B$BThat's about all I can tell you. Tell Captain Vimes I'm sorry I couldn't be of more help.\030Speak with Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore.\030\030The Black Shield\0312,1,27,2,257,1,4941\0302,29,132,2,257,4,4941\0302,134,162,2,257,1,4941\0302,167,198,2,257,1,4941\0302,200,255,2,257,1,4941\0303,1,45,2,384,1,4941\0301,1,74,4,272,1,4944\0301,76,198,4,280,3,4944\0314944,2,6,Captain Garran Vimes\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,6,Theramore\0311319,19,1319,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1321]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is good shield. Very strong, heavy, good. But Do'gol don't need it. I make shields, not buy them, $n.$B$BYou should know that.\030Hmm... I don't see anything out of the ordinary with this shield. We should have Do'gol, the blacksmith, take a look at it, and see if he can tell us more about it, but I wouldn't hold out hope...\030Show the Blackened Iron Shield to Do'gol in Brackenwall Village.\030Something for me, $c?\030The Black Shield\0312,1,6,2,257,1,4926\0302,8,65,2,257,1,4926\0302,67,196,2,259,4,4926\0303,1,64,2,384,1,4926\0301,1,20,4,272,1,5087\0301,22,46,4,272,1,5087\0301,48,72,4,272,1,5087\0301,74,106,4,272,1,5087\0301,111,131,4,272,1,5087\0304,1,21,3,256,2,5087\0315087,2,3,Do'gol\0305087,2,4,Do'gol\0305087,4,7,Do'gol\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,4,Do'gol\0302,0,0,4,Brackenwall Village\0311251,19,1251,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301322,23,1322,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1322]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I don't like spiders that are so big I can't sit on them and squish them.$B$BThanks for getting them, $n. Now I rip them open and pour them onto the shield...\030Hmmm, there's writing right here on the rim of the shield, but it's hard to read from all the burned stuff.$B$BI need acid to make it clear. Venom from the darkmist spiders would do good. The spiders have taken over an old mine, the Darkmist Cavern, northwest of the village. Get me some of their sacs and I can clean this up.\030Acquire 5 Acidic Venom Sacs for Do'gol in Brackenwall Village.\030Did you get them sacs from the spiders?\030The Black Shield\0312,1,107,2,257,1,5087\0302,112,140,2,259,1,5087\0302,142,187,2,257,4,5087\0302,189,275,2,257,1,5087\0302,277,326,2,257,1,5087\0303,1,62,2,384,1,5087\0301,1,73,4,272,1,5087\0301,78,105,4,272,1,5087\0301,107,158,4,272,1,5087\0304,1,39,3,256,2,5087\0315087,2,6,Do'gol\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,6,Brackenwall Village\0311321,19,1321,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301323,23,1323,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5959,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[1323]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Mosarn? Sounds familiar... I can't put my finger on it. Maybe it'll come to me later.$B$BIt probably isn't important. A shield can come from anywhere and not mean anything...\030Oh, I think I might have dropped too much acid onto the shield. Let me just rub a little...$B$BHm, kind of hard to read, but it looks like the name Mosarn. Never heard of him. Maybe Krog knows. Krog knows many people.\030Talk with Krog in Brackenwall Village.\030\030The Black Shield\0312,1,63,2,257,4,5087\0302,65,91,2,257,1,5087\0302,96,155,2,257,1,5087\0302,157,175,2,257,1,5087\0302,177,193,2,257,4,5087\0302,195,217,2,257,1,5087\0303,1,38,2,384,1,5087\0301,1,7,4,272,2,4926\0301,9,26,4,272,1,4926\0301,28,55,4,272,1,4926\0301,57,85,4,272,4,4926\0301,90,117,4,272,1,4926\0301,119,174,4,272,1,4926\0314943,2,3,Mosarn\0304926,2,5,Krog\0304926,2,6,Krog\0304926,2,7,Krog\0304943,4,8,Mosarn\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,7,Brackenwall Village\0311322,19,1322,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301276,23,1276,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1324]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031I assure you, we're all quite upset about current events, but allow us to take him back to Theramore for some questioning, and we'll see about finding the King.$B$BI'm sure my lady Proudmore would like to thank you for your help. Speak to her when you have a moment.\030What?! You come here accusing me of allying with the Defias, and think I'll just stand here while you insult me?! Something tells me you've had this coming for a long time.\030Defeat Private Hendel in Dustwallow Marsh.\030Subdue Private Hendel\030Hello again, $N. I hope you don't mind the assistance, but we couldn't have Hendel escaping, or worse, wind up dead.\030The Missing Diplomat\0312,1,6,2,257,2,4966\0302,8,113,2,257,2,4966\0302,115,172,2,257,1,4966\0303,1,42,2,384,1,4966\0301,1,160,4,272,1,4967\0301,165,229,4,272,4,4967\0301,231,266,4,272,1,4967\0305,1,16,3,256,1,4967\0305,18,116,3,258,3,4967\0304,1,21,3,384,1,4966\0314966,2,4,Private Hendel\03015065,4,6,Lady\0304966,3,10,Private Hendel\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,4,Dustwallow Marsh\0304,0,0,5,Theramore\0311266,19,1266,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301267,23,1267,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[133]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, thanks. These will do just the trick!\030I live so far from the protection of town, it's a wonder the ghouls and the walking dead haven't eaten me!  In fact, just yesterday a pack of Bone Chewers was pounding on the walls of my house!$B$BI want to make an effigy - a kind of \"scarecrow\" for Ghouls.  To do that I need some Ghoul Ribs.  You can get them from Flesh Eaters, Bone Chewers, Brain Eaters, Rotted Ones and Plague Spreaders.$B$BGet the ribs for me, and I will repay you with some coin.\030Gather 7 Ghoul Ribs and bring them to Abercrombie at his shack.\030I think I hear a pack of Ghouls scurrying around the back of the house - I better put that effigy up quick! Did you get those Ghoul Ribs for me?\030Ghoulish Effigy\0312,1,106,2,257,1,289\0302,109,193,2,257,1,289\0302,198,257,2,259,1,289\0302,260,293,2,259,1,289\0302,296,392,2,261,1,289\0302,397,453,2,257,3,289\0303,1,63,2,384,1,289\0301,1,11,4,272,1,289\0301,13,41,4,272,3,289\0304,1,107,3,256,1,289\0304,109,144,3,256,2,289\031846,2,4,Ghoul\030846,2,7,Ghoul\030289,2,7,Abercrombie\030846,3,11,Ghoul\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,5,Flesh Eaters\0302,0,0,7,Abercrombie\031159,19,159,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030134,23,134,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,884,OBJECTIVE,7,15,",[1338]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, a request from one of the Stormpikes. That's a proud clan, full of quality dwarves. Rich ones, too.$B$BThank you, $N. I'll get to work on Mountaineer Stormpike's shield by the end of the day.\030There is a dwarven armorsmith whose work I admire greatly.  His name is Furen Longbeard, and his skill is unmatched.  I need a new shield, and I must have one of his!$B$BThe problem is... Furen is far to the south, in the dwarven district within Stormwind.  In human lands!  I can't imagine why he would live there, so far from Ironforge.  The humans must pay him a king's ransom to keep him there!$B$BSo, if you want to travel and don't mind making some money, then will you send Furen my request for a shield?\030Bring Stormpike's Request to Furen Longbeard in Stormwind.\030A letter from the dwarven lands? I wonder who would call from so far to the north...$B$BPlease, let me see the order.\030Stormpike's Order\0312,1,58,2,257,1,1343\0302,61,116,2,257,1,1343\0302,119,166,2,259,1,1343\0302,171,187,2,261,1,1343\0302,189,256,2,257,1,1343\0302,259,273,2,257,1,1343\0302,276,338,2,257,4,1343\0302,341,398,2,257,1,1343\0302,403,511,2,259,4,1343\0303,1,58,2,384,1,1343\0301,1,41,4,272,1,5413\0301,43,87,4,272,1,5413\0301,89,103,4,272,1,5413\0301,108,121,4,272,1,5413\0301,123,195,4,272,1,5413\0304,1,32,3,256,2,5413\0304,34,84,3,256,4,5413\0304,89,117,3,256,1,5413\0315413,2,2,Furen Longbeard\0305413,2,10,Furen Longbeard\0301343,4,15,Mountaineer Stormpike\0312,38,1432,0,\0302,0,0,5,Stormwind\0302,0,0,7,Ironforge\0302,0,0,10,Furen Longbeard\0302,0,0,10,Stormwind\031\031",[1339]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031That's right. I have a task that I can't do while I'm guarding. In fact, it'll take you far from Loch Modan.$B$BYour perfect chance for adventure!\030I hear Mountaineer Stormpike is looking for a runner.  Someone to do a little traveling for him.  How about it?  Are you the $r for the job?$B$BIf so, then you'll find Stormpike at the top of the northern guard tower.\030Speak with Mountaineer Stormpike.\030\030Mountaineer Stormpike's Task\0312,1,53,2,257,1,1340\0302,56,96,2,257,1,1340\0302,99,111,2,257,2,1340\0302,114,140,2,257,2,1340\0302,145,217,2,257,4,1340\0303,1,33,2,384,1,1340\0301,1,13,4,272,1,1343\0301,15,63,4,272,1,1343\0301,65,108,4,272,1,1343\0301,113,146,4,272,1,1343\0311343,2,1,Mountaineer Stormpike\0301343,2,6,Mountaineer Stormpike\0312,38,1432,0,\0304,0,0,9,Loch Modan\0311338,23,1338,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301338,24,1338,UNKNOWN\031",[134]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank the Nec-...well, thank YOU, $N! You have more than earned your reward.$B$BAha! Happy! Happy nights ahead!!\030A few weeks ago I was picking herbs far from my house, and a band of ogres attacked me!  I ran, and I was forced to leave behind a crate of precious tools and herbs.$B$BAfter they chased me off, the ogres swaggered back to the ogre mound in southern Duskwood.  I'm sure my crate is somewhere near the mound.$B$BPlease, $N, retrieve this crate for me for I miss it sorely.\030Return Abercrombie's Crate to Abercrombie.\030Do you have my crate? If so, then please...give it to me quickly!\030Ogre Thieves\0312,1,87,2,261,1,289\0302,90,165,2,257,1,289\0302,170,259,2,257,1,289\0302,262,307,2,257,1,289\0302,312,371,2,257,1,289\0303,1,42,2,384,1,289\0301,1,37,4,272,1,289\0301,39,76,4,272,1,289\0301,81,84,4,272,1,289\0301,86,91,4,272,1,289\0301,93,112,4,272,1,289\0304,1,21,3,256,2,289\0304,23,65,3,256,4,289\03114528,2,2,Precious\030211,2,3,Ogre\030289,2,6,Abercrombie\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,6,Abercrombie\031133,19,133,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030160,23,160,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,1349,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[135]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This matter might be more complex than Stoutmantle realizes.\030I wonder what Wiley meant when he mentioned the Stonemasons.  Perhaps that was a slip of tongue.  Could the Defias gang be related to the Stonemasons?  Only one man would know for sure:  Mathias Shaw, head of SI:7. Show him Wiley's Note and see if he has anything to add to this growing mystery. If you have trouble finding Shaw, check the Barracks in Old Town.\030Take Wiley's Note to Mathias Shaw in Stormwind.\030What business do you have with me? I am a very busy man. . .\030The Defias Brotherhood\0312,1,60,2,321,1,234\0302,63,96,2,257,4,234\0302,99,150,2,321,4,234\0302,153,214,2,257,4,234\0302,216,295,2,257,4,234\0302,297,361,2,257,4,234\0303,1,47,2,384,1,234\0301,1,60,4,272,4,332\0304,1,34,3,256,2,332\0304,36,56,3,256,1,332\031\0312,40,1436,0,\0302,0,0,3,Stonemasons\0302,0,0,6,Old Town\0302,0,0,7,Mathias Shaw\0302,0,0,7,Stormwind\031132,19,132,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030141,23,141,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1358]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, very good. If initial reports are true, then the toxicity of these hearts could lead to further advances in our knowledge of poisons.$B$BThis is a welcome delivery, $N. Your reward is well earned.\030A colleague in Kalimdor, Apothecary Helbrim, is researching the effects of Lordaeron toxins on the beasts of Kalimdor.  He would be very interested in a sample of the wolf hearts Renferrel sent me.$B$BHelbrim is stationed in the Barrens, in a village known as the Crossroads.  To reach him, you must travel via zeppelin to the orc capital of Orgrimmar, then travel south, by foot, to Durotar.  Head west into the Barrens, and you will soon reach the Crossroads.\030Bring the Wolf Heart Sample to Apothecary Helbrim in the Barrens.\030You have a package for me?\030Sample for Helbrim\0312,1,118,2,257,1,5204\0302,121,197,2,257,4,5204\0302,202,275,2,257,1,5204\0302,278,392,2,257,1,5204\0302,395,461,2,257,3,5204\0303,1,65,2,384,1,5204\0301,1,14,4,272,1,3390\0301,16,137,4,272,4,3390\0301,142,172,4,272,1,3390\0301,174,200,4,272,1,3390\0304,1,26,3,256,2,3390\0313390,2,1,Apothecary Helbrim\0303390,2,6,Apothecary Helbrim\0312,1497,1458,0,\0302,0,0,1,Kalimdor\0302,0,0,3,Barrens\0302,0,0,4,Durotar\0302,0,0,6,Apothecary Helbrim\0302,0,0,6,Barrens\0311359,19,1359,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1359]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah yes, the heart samples of which Renferrel spoke. I am eager to experiment with these... it is always of interest to the Royal Apothecary Society when new forms of toxins are discovered.\030The wolf hearts you acquired possess a quality unseen in similar specimens.  There is a toxicity to them that should be deadly to the very wolves in which the hearts beat!$B$BIt's quite incredible, and we must study it further.  I kept a few samples of the hearts acquired.  Take them to my colleague, Apothecary Zinge.  You will find her in our headquarters in the Undercity.\030Bring the Wolf Heart Samples to Apothecary Zinge in the Undercity.\030You have something for me?\030Zinge's Delivery\0312,1,75,2,257,1,1937\0302,78,171,2,257,1,1937\0302,176,227,2,257,1,1937\0302,230,273,2,257,1,1937\0302,276,319,2,257,1,1937\0302,322,376,2,257,3,1937\0303,1,66,2,384,1,1937\0301,1,51,4,272,1,5204\0301,53,90,4,272,1,5204\0301,92,188,4,272,1,5204\0304,1,26,3,256,2,5204\0313094,2,1,Unseen\0305204,2,5,Apothecary Zinge\0305204,2,7,Apothecary Zinge\0312,1497,1458,0,\0302,0,0,6,Undercity\0302,0,0,7,Apothecary Zinge\0302,0,0,7,Undercity\0304,0,0,10,Royal Apothecary Society\0313221,19,3221,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301358,23,1358,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[136]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The footlocker slowly creaks open. Sand and water seem to be its only contents. But wait! A small crab scurries out with a clue to the treasure in his claws!\030If ye be readin' this, it means that Ol' Captain Sanders is in a watery grave.  So my treasure is yours now, ye jest need to follow the clues. $B$BFirst ye need to find me footlocker.  It's probably half-buried in sand by now, along the Western Coast of Westfall near the shipwreck.  There be lots of shipwrecks but only one rusty anchor on the coast.  Find that anchor and you'll find me locker!  Look in there for the next clue.\030Find Captain Sanders' footlocker and search it for the next clue.\030\030Captain Sander's Hidden Treasure\0312,1,78,2,257,4,0\0302,81,142,2,259,1,0\0302,148,183,2,259,1,0\0302,186,282,2,257,1,0\0302,285,351,2,257,1,0\0302,354,396,2,257,1,0\0302,399,430,2,257,1,0\0303,1,65,2,384,1,0\0301,1,34,4,272,1,0\0301,36,79,4,272,4,0\0301,81,89,4,272,1,0\0301,91,157,4,272,1,0\0316827,4,12,Crab\0312,40,1436,0,\031138,23,138,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,1357,STARTER,?,10,\030OBJECT,35,FINISHER,?,12,Captain's Footlocker",[1360]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, I feel complete again - thank you kindly.$B$BSome dwarves may treasure the luster of metal, and some may treasure the glint of gems... but a Stoutarm without a treasured stein in hand is hardly a Stoutarm at all!\030I had myself a fine job as a digger at the Uldaman excavation site in the Badlands... that is until those blasted troggs showed up.  I escaped with my hide barely intact, and nothing else.  In the chaos, I left my most treasured possession.  It's safe from the troggs in my chest, sure, but it's right in the thick of 'em.$B$BI'd be in your debt, both in honor and coin, if you could fetch it for me!  A chest with my name on it is at the end of the North Common Hall.  That's the one you need to get in.\030Get Krom Stoutarm's treasured possession from his chest in the North Common Hall of Uldaman, and bring it to him in Ironforge.\030Well now, we're you able to get slap around those troggs long enough to get into my chest and nab my treasure?\030Reclaimed Treasures\0312,1,85,2,257,1,6294\0302,87,131,2,257,1,6294\0302,134,188,2,257,1,6294\0302,191,240,2,257,1,6294\0302,243,322,2,257,1,6294\0302,327,400,2,257,4,6294\0302,403,468,2,257,1,6294\0302,471,504,2,259,1,6294\0303,1,126,2,384,1,6294\0301,1,45,4,272,1,6294\0301,50,138,4,272,1,6294\0301,140,216,4,272,1,6294\0304,1,110,3,256,2,6294\0316294,2,9,Krom Stoutarm\0312,1517,1418,0,\0302,0,0,1,Uldaman\0302,0,0,1,Badlands\0302,0,0,9,North Common Hall of Uldaman\0302,0,0,9,Ironforge\031\031ITEM,8027,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1361]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes, I am recruiting. This mission leads into Desolace, against the centaur there. I will be brief so that you may quickly begin.\030A warrior of the Horde, Regthar Deathgate, is recruiting agents for a mission into the land of Desolace.  Speak with him if you wish to volunteer.  He is stationed in the Barrens, in a series of bunkers west of the Crossroads.$B$BAnd sharpen your weapons.  Desolace is a place torn by war.\030Speak with Regthar Deathgate.\030\030Regthar Deathgate\0312,1,104,2,257,1,2229\0302,107,146,2,259,4,2229\0302,149,226,2,257,1,2229\0302,231,255,2,257,1,2229\0302,258,289,2,261,1,2229\0303,1,29,2,384,1,2229\0301,1,21,4,272,1,3389\0301,23,82,4,272,1,3389\0301,84,129,4,274,3,3389\0313389,2,1,Regthar Deathgate\0302996,2,5,Torn\0303389,2,6,Regthar Deathgate\03093,4,8,Centaur\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,3,Barrens\0302,0,0,3,Crossroads\0311362,23,1362,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1362]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You are here on orders from Regthar? Then you are here to deal with the centaur. Good.$B$BI hope you're rested. I don't know how our campaign against the centaur will end, but I know the struggle will be long.$B$BHave a seat, and listen.\030The Kolkar centaur live in Desolace, and their forces have spread into the Barrens.  This is a known fact and we have Horde agents dealing with them here.$B$BBut as long as the centaur are strong in Desolace, they will always pose a threat.  It is time we rid ourselves of that threat.$B$BSpeak with Felgur Twocuts at Ghost Walker Post in Desolace.  He was sent to gather intelligence on the centaur.  He will know how to best deal with the Kolkar of Desolace.\030Speak with Felgur Twocuts at Ghost Walker Post in Desolace.\030\030The Kolkar of Desolace\0312,1,83,2,257,1,3389\0302,86,154,2,257,1,3389\0302,159,240,2,261,3,3389\0302,243,285,2,261,1,3389\0302,290,348,2,257,1,3389\0302,351,400,2,257,1,3389\0302,403,460,2,257,3,3389\0303,1,59,2,384,1,3389\0301,1,36,4,272,2,5395\0301,38,80,4,272,1,5395\0301,82,86,4,272,1,5395\0301,91,111,4,274,3,5395\0301,113,209,4,272,3,5395\0301,214,237,4,272,1,5395\0314632,2,1,Kolkar Centaur\03093,2,1,Centaur\03093,2,3,Centaur\0305395,2,5,Felgur Twocuts\03093,2,6,Centaur\0305395,2,8,Felgur Twocuts\03093,4,10,Centaur\03093,4,13,Centaur\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,1,Desolace\0302,0,0,3,Desolace\0302,0,0,5,Ghost Walker Post\0302,0,0,5,Desolace\0302,0,0,8,Ghost Walker Post\0302,0,0,8,Desolace\0304,0,0,9,Regthar\031\031",[1363]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It wasn't my fault. Really it wasn't.\030As caretaker of the works here in the library of the Academy of Arcane Arts and Sciences, it is my responsibility to ensure all the magical tomes and scrolls are accounted for at all times. Who knows what folly would unfold if some of these enchanted texts were to fall into the wrong hands?$B$BWhich reminds me... my assistant, Dellis, made a horrible mistake last week. He's quite able in the library but incompetent when he leaves the gates of Stormwind. Be a hero, and help old Dellis out, would you?\030Speak with Acolyte Dellis in Stormwind.\030\030Mazen's Behest\0312,1,189,2,259,1,338\0302,191,291,2,257,4,338\0302,296,314,2,257,1,338\0302,316,371,2,257,1,338\0302,373,457,2,257,1,338\0302,459,504,2,257,4,338\0303,1,39,2,384,1,338\0301,1,19,4,272,1,5386\0301,21,37,4,272,1,5386\0315386,2,7,Acolyte Dellis\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,7,Stormwind\0311364,23,1364,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1364]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, most splendid!$B$BFor some time I had feared my request for Khadgar's Essays on Dimensional Convergence had been overlooked by Master Mazen of the Academy of Arcane Arts and Sciences.$B$BHe must be bogged down with requests considering the many strange happenings going on.$B$BNow, if you'll excuse me, I need to begin my research at once. To finally glimpse the insight of one as great as Khadgar excites me to no end.\030Master Mazen's directions were quite clear: Deliver a very important essay to Watcher Mahar Ba in Nethergarde Keep.$B$BBut I had never been to the Blasted Lands before! The journey was frightening!$B$BWhen I got to the Swamp of Sorrows, I made a wrong turn and ended up surrounded by horrible plant-like swamp creatures. They lurched as if to attack me so I ran. But in my haste I dropped the essay. One of the beasts took it I am sure.$B$BCould you please try to retrieve it and deliver it to Mahar Ba?\030Retrieve Khadgar's Essays on Dimensional Convergence and deliver them to Watcher Mahar Ba in Nethergarde Keep.\030What brings you to Nethergarde Keep, $R?\030Mazen's Behest\0312,1,115,2,257,1,5386\0302,120,168,2,257,1,5386\0302,170,197,2,257,1,5386\0302,202,320,2,257,1,5386\0302,322,362,2,261,4,5386\0302,364,399,2,257,1,5386\0302,401,436,2,257,1,5386\0302,441,503,2,257,4,5386\0303,1,110,2,384,1,5386\0301,1,18,4,272,1,5385\0301,23,187,4,272,1,5385\0301,192,277,4,272,1,5385\0301,282,343,4,274,4,5385\0301,345,423,4,272,1,5385\0304,1,40,3,256,2,5385\0315385,2,1,Watcher Mahar Ba\0305385,2,9,Watcher Mahar Ba\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,1,Watcher Mahar Ba\0302,0,0,1,Nethergarde Keep\0302,0,0,2,Blasted Lands\0302,0,0,4,Swamp of Sorrows\0302,0,0,8,Mahar Ba\0302,0,0,9,Watcher Mahar Ba\0302,0,0,9,Nethergarde Keep\0303,0,0,15,Nethergarde Keep\031\031ITEM,6065,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1365]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done. This swift act against the Kolkar is an effective show of strength, and strength is what the centaur understand best.$B$BThe death of the Kolkar leader will not only disrupt that clan, but give pause to the others.\030The Kolkar are not the only centaur of Desolace.  Many clans wander these dry plains, fighting and dying against each other.  And it is good that they fight among themselves, for they are strong and brutal.  If the centaur united against us, they would be a fierce foe.$B$BWe must deal with them before they unite.$B$BYour first task is to disrupt the Kolkar clan.  Do this by killing its leader, Khan Dez'hepah.$B$BThe Kolkar Village is northeast of here.  Go, and may fortune go with you.\030Bring Khan Dez'hepah's Head to Felgur Twocuts in Desolace.\030$N, have you defeated Khan Dez'hepah?\030Khan Dez'hepah\0312,1,48,2,257,1,5395\0302,51,124,2,261,1,5395\0302,127,206,2,261,1,5395\0302,209,269,2,257,4,5395\0302,274,314,2,265,1,5395\0302,319,364,2,257,1,5395\0302,367,412,2,257,1,5395\0302,417,456,2,257,1,5395\0302,459,490,2,257,1,5395\0303,1,58,2,384,1,5395\0301,1,10,4,272,1,5395\0301,12,128,4,272,1,5395\0301,133,225,4,272,3,5395\0304,1,37,3,256,2,5395\03193,2,1,Centaur\03093,2,4,Centaur\0305600,2,7,Khan Dez'hepah\0305600,2,10,Khan Dez'hepah\0305395,2,10,Felgur Twocuts\03093,4,12,Centaur\0305600,3,14,Khan Dez'hepah\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,10,Felgur Twocuts\0302,0,0,10,Desolace\0311366,23,1366,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6066,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1366]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031By now, the centaur must know your name. I'm sure they know it, and respect it, and fear it. And just as they know you, they know the banner under which you ride.$B$BThe banner of the Horde.\030Now that you scared the centaur clans, it's time to bleed them.  When traveling Desolace, hunt centaur.  I don't care which clan you hunt.  Just gather ears.  A hoard of ears.$B$BBy weakening their numbers you will weaken their resolve, and stamp out any thoughts of expansion.$B$BGood hunting, $N.\030Bring 15 Centaur Ears to Felgur Twocuts in Desolace.\030How is your collection of ears, $N? Large?\030Centaur Bounty\0312,1,63,2,257,1,5395\0302,66,103,2,257,1,5395\0302,106,138,2,257,1,5395\0302,141,157,2,257,1,5395\0302,160,175,2,257,1,5395\0302,180,277,2,257,3,5395\0302,282,298,2,257,1,5395\0303,1,52,2,384,1,5395\0301,1,40,4,272,1,5395\0301,42,92,4,272,1,5395\0301,94,162,4,272,1,5395\0301,167,190,4,272,1,5395\0304,1,35,3,256,2,5395\0304,37,42,3,256,2,5395\03193,2,1,Centaur\03093,2,2,Centaur\03093,2,8,Centaur\0305395,2,8,Felgur Twocuts\03093,4,9,Centaur\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,8,Felgur Twocuts\0302,0,0,8,Desolace\0311365,19,1365,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6067,OBJECTIVE,15,15,",[1367]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The Gelkis cry when they hear your name, $N. They fear you and they hate you. They hate you like they hate the Magram!$B$BMaybe you are strong like the Magram. We will see...\030To beat the centaur, we must use their hatred against them.  We will ally with one of the clans and through them, we will learn how to defeat all the clans.$B$BIf you choose to ally with the Magram then slay their foes, the Gelkis.  This will earn you respect among the Magram.  When you earn enough, then meet with the Magram spokesman Warug, on the outskirts of the Magram Village, in southeast Desolace.\030Gain a Friendly reputation with the Magram, then speak with Warug.\030Leave! The Magram do not speak with the weak. We kill them!$B$BIf you want to speak with me, then show me you are strong. Return after you slay many Gelkis.\030Magram Alliance\0312,1,59,2,257,1,5412\0302,62,156,2,257,3,5412\0302,161,231,2,257,4,5412\0302,234,277,2,257,3,5412\0302,280,406,2,257,1,5412\0303,1,66,2,384,1,5412\0301,1,44,4,272,1,5398\0301,46,77,4,272,1,5398\0301,79,118,4,272,1,5398\0301,123,159,4,272,4,5398\0301,161,174,4,272,3,5398\0304,1,6,3,256,1,5398\0304,8,45,3,256,1,5398\0304,47,59,3,256,1,5398\0304,64,121,3,258,4,5398\0304,123,156,3,256,1,5398\03193,2,1,Centaur\0305398,2,5,Warug\0305398,2,6,Warug\0312,405,1443,0,\0311369,23,1369,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031REPUTATION,93,OBJECTIVE,3000,16,",[1368]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The earth speaks to me. And it says you have killed many Magram. This is good.$B$BIf you are a friend of the Gelkis, then listen. I have more tasks for you.\030To beat the centaur, we must use their hatred against them.  We will ally with one of the clans and through them, we will learn how to defeat all the clans.$B$BIf you choose to ally with the Gelkis then slay their most hated rival, the Magram.  After you earn the respect of the Gelkis, meet with the Gelkis shaman Uthek the Wise, on the outskirts of the Gelkis Village, in southwest Desolace.\030Gain a Friendly reputation with the Gelkis, then speak with Uthek the Wise.\030Your two feet step on Gelkis earth. You are not welcome here!$B$BProve you seek friendship with the Gelkis. Kill Magram centaur. Return when the ground is wet with Magram blood.\030Gelkis Alliance\0312,1,59,2,257,1,5412\0302,62,156,2,257,3,5412\0302,161,243,2,257,4,5412\0302,246,393,2,257,1,5412\0303,1,75,2,384,1,5412\0301,1,23,4,272,1,5397\0301,25,64,4,272,1,5397\0301,66,78,4,272,1,5397\0301,83,129,4,272,4,5397\0301,131,156,4,272,1,5397\0304,1,35,3,256,1,5397\0304,37,61,3,256,1,5397\0304,66,107,3,258,1,5397\0304,109,128,3,256,1,5397\0304,130,177,3,256,1,5397\03193,2,1,Centaur\0305397,2,4,Uthek the Wise\0305397,2,5,Uthek the Wise\03093,3,14,Centaur\0312,405,1443,0,\0311370,23,1370,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031REPUTATION,92,OBJECTIVE,3000,16,",[1369]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030requestItems\030title\031You got the tears! Now the Gelkis will know that Theradras will not help them. She will not cry when we crush them! The Magram will rule!$B$BYou are smart to help us, $N. We are the strongest.\030The Gelkis think our centaur mother, Theradras, protects us.  They are stupid.  No one protects the centaur.  The Magram do not need protection!  We are the strongest!$B$BShow the Gelkis they are stupid.  Go to the cave in their village.  They hoard crystals in that cave, the tears of Theradras.  Destroy the tears and bring me the broken pieces!\030Maintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 3 Broken Tears to Warug in the Magram Village.\030\030Tears Destroyed\030If you are not our enemy, then you will do what I ask!\030Broken Tears\0312,1,60,2,257,1,5398\0302,63,78,2,257,1,5398\0302,81,108,2,257,1,5398\0302,111,144,2,259,1,5398\0302,147,167,2,257,1,5398\0302,172,203,2,257,1,5398\0302,206,237,2,257,1,5398\0302,240,296,2,257,1,5398\0302,299,347,2,261,1,5398\0303,1,98,2,384,1,5398\0301,1,18,4,272,1,5398\0301,20,78,4,272,3,5398\0301,80,115,4,272,3,5398\0301,117,137,4,272,3,5398\0301,142,170,4,272,1,5398\0301,172,192,4,272,1,5398\0306,1,54,3,262,4,5398\0305,1,15,3,388,1,5398\03193,2,1,Centaur\03093,2,3,Centaur\0305398,2,10,Warug\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,10,Warug\0302,0,0,10,Magram Village\0311371,23,1371,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6083,OBJECTIVE,3,15,\030REPUTATION,93,OBJECTIVE,3000,16,",[1370]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Good. I can hear the loud Magram bellies grumble from their village, far away!$B$BI will give this meat to the Gelkis. And we will fight for many days without rest.$B$BWhat you did is good for the Gelkis, $N.\030When we are not at war, we hunt for meat.  Meat gives us strength, and full bellies fight harder than empty ones.$B$BIt is the same with the Magram.  They store extra meat so they may fight longer between hunts.  If you raid their village to the east and take their stores of meat, then their strength will fail.\030Bring 6 bags of Crudely Dried Meat to Uthek the Wise in the Gelkis Village.\030Return after you further prove your worth to the Gelkis!\030Stealing Supplies\0312,1,41,2,261,1,5397\0302,44,113,2,261,1,5397\0302,118,148,2,257,1,5397\0302,151,211,2,261,1,5397\0302,214,312,2,257,4,5397\0303,1,75,2,384,1,5397\0301,1,5,4,272,1,5397\0301,7,78,4,272,1,5397\0301,83,118,4,272,3,5397\0301,120,164,4,276,3,5397\0301,169,208,4,272,1,5397\0304,1,56,3,256,1,5397\0315397,2,6,Uthek the Wise\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,6,Uthek the Wise\0302,0,0,6,Gelkis Village\0304,0,0,9,Gelkis\0303,0,0,12,Gelkis\0311373,23,1373,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6069,OBJECTIVE,6,15,\030REPUTATION,92,OBJECTIVE,3000,16,",[1371]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes, this is what I had! I will make it move again. It makes me laugh!\030Long ago, a little gnome came to Desolace.  He had horses and a cart, and the cart held strange things.  Funny things.  Things that burned different colors.  Things that moved and weren't alive.  I killed the little gnome, but before that... he made me laugh.$B$BI kept my favorite thing from his cart.  It was a human made of wood and it waved at me until I hit it and broke it.$B$BI want a new one.  Get me a new one!\030Maintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring an Advanced Target Dummy to Warug in the Magram Village in Desolace.\030If you are not our enemy, then you will do what I ask!\030Gizmo for Warug\0312,1,42,2,321,1,5398\0302,45,103,2,257,1,5398\0302,106,118,2,257,1,5398\0302,121,156,2,257,1,5398\0302,159,194,2,257,1,5398\0302,197,241,2,257,1,5398\0302,243,259,2,257,1,5398\0302,264,302,2,257,1,5398\0302,305,379,2,257,1,5398\0302,384,400,2,259,1,5398\0302,403,419,2,257,1,5398\0303,1,120,2,384,1,5398\0301,1,24,4,272,1,5398\0301,26,51,4,272,3,5398\0301,53,70,4,272,1,5398\0304,1,54,3,262,4,5398\0312674,2,12,Advanced Target Dummy\0302673,2,12,Target Dummy\0305398,2,12,Warug\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,1,Desolace\0302,0,0,12,Warug\0302,0,0,12,Magram Village\0302,0,0,12,Desolace\0311369,19,1369,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301375,23,1375,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4392,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,93,OBJECTIVE,3000,16,",[1372]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Zraedus was just telling me about the nosey little Infiltrator before you arrived.$B$BQuite a problem, indeed. The last thing we need is a busybody sniffing around Beggar's Haunt.$B$BI am sure the orcs of Stonard would be quite anxious to hear what our friend has to say. Seeing that they are our allies, ahem, we must help them to get any information they can from the human.$B$BWork with me, $N, and we will deliver a truth serum to Stonard.$B$BFor the Horde!$B$B...did I get that right?\030Our expeditionary force was sent at Varimathras's behest to survey lower Azeroth.$B$BWhile out scouting I noticed a human Infiltrator spying on Beggar's Haunt. Before I could apprehend him, some of our orcish... brethren... captured him and took him to Stonard, their stronghold in Swamp of Sorrows.$B$BI want to... help... our orcish allies. They did not see our camp here but nonetheless I want to lend a hand.$B$BWork with Faustin here to develop a... truth serum for our friend in Stonard.\030Speak with Apothecary Faustin at Beggar's Haunt.\030\030Nothing But The Truth\0312,1,81,2,257,1,5418\0302,86,159,2,257,1,5418\0302,161,211,2,257,4,5418\0302,213,223,2,257,1,5418\0302,225,299,2,257,1,5418\0302,304,315,2,259,1,5418\0302,317,323,2,257,1,5418\0302,325,342,2,257,1,5418\0302,344,412,2,259,1,5418\0302,417,454,2,257,1,5418\0302,456,493,2,257,1,5418\0303,1,48,2,384,1,5418\0301,1,82,4,272,1,5414\0301,87,110,4,276,1,5414\0301,112,179,4,274,1,5414\0301,184,271,4,272,4,5414\0301,273,376,4,272,1,5414\0301,381,443,4,272,3,5414\0301,448,461,4,272,1,5414\0301,466,489,4,272,2,5414\0315414,2,12,Apothecary Faustin\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,1,Varimathras's\0302,0,0,5,Stonard\0302,0,0,5,Swamp of Sorrows\0302,0,0,11,Stonard\0302,0,0,12,Beggar's Haunt\0304,0,0,18,Stonard\0311383,23,1383,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1373]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes, this is the shard of which the earth whispered. I can feel strong magic in it! I will use this magic against the enemies of the Gelkis.$B$BYou have done one more task for us, $N. Maybe soon, we will call you friend.\030You have more to prove, and your next task will take you far, so for now the Gelkis will fight the Magram without you.$B$BThe earth whispers many secrets to those who listen.  One secret I hear is of a red crystal.  It is called draenethyst, and it is new to our earth.  It comes from a place where mountains fly, and where demons rule.$B$BBring me a shard of draenethyst, and it will make my magic strong!  The shard is in a place called the Swamp of Sorrows, held by the lost one Ongeku.\030Maintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and bring a Draenethyst Shard to Uthek the Wise in the Gelkis Village in Desolace.\030Show me you are a friend of the Gelkis, $N.\030Ongeku\0312,1,118,2,261,3,5397\0302,123,174,2,257,1,5397\0302,177,214,2,257,1,5397\0302,217,269,2,257,1,5397\0302,272,336,2,257,1,5397\0302,341,406,2,257,3,5397\0302,409,489,2,261,1,5397\0303,1,124,2,384,1,5397\0301,1,52,4,272,1,5397\0301,54,83,4,272,1,5397\0301,85,140,4,276,3,5397\0301,145,183,4,272,1,5397\0301,185,220,4,272,4,5397\0304,1,43,3,256,1,5397\0315622,2,7,Ongeku\0305397,2,8,Uthek the Wise\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,8,Uthek the Wise\0302,0,0,8,Gelkis Village\0302,0,0,8,Desolace\0311370,19,1370,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301374,23,1374,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6190,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,92,OBJECTIVE,3000,16,",[1374]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Khan Jehn was strong, but stupid. He thought his own strength was great. He did not see that earth magic is stronger. The Magram centaur will now fall without their leader, and the Gelkis will one day rule!\030The earth speaks to me, and it says that the Magram grow weak.  Now it is time to kill their Khan!$B$BBring me the head of the Magram Khan, Jehn!\030Bring the Khan Jehn's Head to Uthek the Wise in the Gelkis Village in Desolace.\030Show me you are a friend of the Gelkis, $N.\030Khan Jehn\0312,1,62,2,257,1,5397\0302,65,98,2,257,1,5397\0302,103,145,2,257,1,5397\0303,1,79,2,384,1,5397\0301,1,33,4,272,1,5397\0301,35,72,4,272,1,5397\0301,74,117,4,272,1,5397\0301,119,206,4,272,3,5397\0304,1,43,3,256,1,5397\0315601,2,4,Khan Jehn\0305397,2,4,Uthek the Wise\0305601,4,5,Khan Jehn\03093,4,8,Centaur\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,4,Uthek the Wise\0302,0,0,4,Gelkis Village\0302,0,0,4,Desolace\0311373,19,1373,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301380,23,1380,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6072,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,92,OBJECTIVE,3000,16,",[1375]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Khan Shaka is dead!  I will place his head on a pike, and keep it with me so Shaka can see the strength of the Magram!\030You help the Magram, and I like you.  Now, kill the Khan of the Gelkis!  He is Khan Shaka, and I want his head!  I want to stare at his head and laugh at him!\030Maintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring the Head of Khan Shaka to Warug in the Magram Village in Desolace.\030Do tasks for the Magram, and I will help you.\030Khan Shaka\0312,1,36,2,257,1,5398\0302,39,71,2,257,1,5398\0302,74,111,2,259,1,5398\0302,114,158,2,259,1,5398\0303,1,118,2,384,1,5398\0301,1,19,4,272,1,5398\0301,22,118,4,272,3,5398\0304,1,45,3,256,3,5398\0315602,2,3,Khan Shaka\0305602,2,5,Khan Shaka\0305398,2,5,Warug\0305602,4,6,Khan Shaka\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,5,Warug\0302,0,0,5,Magram Village\0302,0,0,5,Desolace\0311371,19,1371,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301381,23,1381,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6073,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,93,OBJECTIVE,3000,16,",[138]="PARTIAL\031characters,conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Good work, treasure hunter!\030The clue to the treasure reads: Good work, matey!  Now ye need to head due east.  East up the bluffs, east to the road.  Look for the ol' chimney ruins near the side of the road.  There you'll find an old barrel with your next clue.\030Find the old barrel near the ruined chimney and search it for your next clue.\030\030Captain Sander's Hidden Treasure\0312,1,49,2,257,1,0\0302,52,80,2,259,1,0\0302,83,119,2,257,1,0\0302,122,178,2,321,1,0\0302,181,232,2,257,1,0\0303,1,77,2,384,1,0\0301,1,27,4,272,1,0\031\0312,40,1436,0,\031136,19,136,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030139,23,139,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,35,GIVER,?,9,Captain's Footlocker\030OBJECT,36,FINISHER,?,12,Broken Barrel",[1380]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031He is dead! Khan Hratha is dead! And now the Maraudine will fall! When the Gelkis rule this land, $N, we will remember you. And the spirits of the earth will sing your name for all time.\030$N, you helped us against the Magram.  Now, help us beat the Maraudine!  Kill the head of their clan, Khan Hratha!$B$BTo face him, blow the Maraudine War Horn.  It is atop a high bluff in the Valley of Spears.$B$BBut to blow the horn, you must gain a warhorn mouthpiece.  These are rare, carried only by trusted Maraudine centaur.$B$BAfter the horn is blown, centaur will come.  Kill them until Hratha appears.$B$BKhan Hratha holds the piece of... a key.  Bring it to me...\030Maintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and bring the Maraudine Key Fragment to Uthek the Wise in the Gelkis Village.\030Is Khan Hratha dead? Do you have the key fragment?\030Khan Hratha\0312,1,37,2,257,1,5397\0302,40,71,2,257,1,5397\0302,74,114,2,257,1,5397\0302,119,159,2,261,1,5397\0302,162,209,2,257,1,5397\0302,214,270,2,257,1,5397\0302,273,330,2,257,1,5397\0302,335,377,2,257,3,5397\0302,380,410,2,257,1,5397\0302,415,447,2,257,1,5397\0302,449,454,2,257,1,5397\0302,457,473,2,257,1,5397\0303,1,119,2,384,1,5397\0301,1,11,4,272,1,5397\0301,13,32,4,272,1,5397\0301,34,65,4,280,3,5397\0301,67,123,4,272,3,5397\0301,125,186,4,272,3,5397\0304,1,20,3,256,2,5397\0304,22,50,3,256,2,5397\0315402,2,3,Khan Hratha\03093,2,7,Centaur\03093,2,8,Centaur\0305402,2,10,Khan Hratha\0305397,2,13,Uthek the Wise\0305402,4,15,Khan Hratha\0305402,3,19,Khan Hratha\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,5,Valley of Spears\0302,0,0,13,Uthek the Wise\0302,0,0,13,Gelkis Village\0311374,19,1374,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6077,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,92,OBJECTIVE,3000,16,",[1381]="PARTIAL\031conflict,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Khan Hratha is dead!  Now the Magram are the strongest of the centaur!  We will crush the others, and rule Desolace!$B$BWe will remember, you, $N, and you will be spared our hooves when all others are trampled.\030The Gelkis Khan is dead, and now the Maraudine will fall!  Kill the Maraudine Khan, Hratha!$B$BTo face him, blow the horn on the high bluff in the Valley of Spears.  But to blow the horn, you need a mouthpiece.  To get a mouthpiece, kill Maraudine centaur.  Keep killing until you find a mouthpiece.  Then blow the horn.$B$BDo this and Maraudine centaur will come to the tower.  Kill them until Khan Hratha appears.  Hratha holds the piece of a key.  Give this piece to me...\030Maintain your Magram reputation, and bring the Maraudine Key Fragment to Warug in the Magram Village in Desolace.\030Do what I ask.  Prove to me that you are an ally of the Magram!\030Khan Hratha\0312,1,57,2,265,3,5398\0302,60,91,2,257,1,5398\0302,96,164,2,257,1,5398\0302,167,210,2,259,1,5398\0302,213,256,2,257,1,5398\0302,259,299,2,257,1,5398\0302,302,320,2,257,1,5398\0302,325,377,2,257,3,5398\0302,380,415,2,257,1,5398\0302,418,449,2,257,1,5398\0302,452,475,2,257,1,5398\0303,1,113,2,384,1,5398\0301,1,20,4,272,1,5398\0301,23,70,4,304,1,5398\0301,73,116,4,272,3,5398\0301,121,210,4,272,3,5398\0304,1,14,3,258,1,5398\0304,17,63,3,256,1,5398\03193,2,5,Centaur\03093,2,8,Centaur\0305402,2,9,Khan Hratha\0305398,2,12,Warug\0305402,4,13,Khan Hratha\03093,4,14,Centaur\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,3,Valley of Spears\0302,0,0,12,Warug\0302,0,0,12,Magram Village\0302,0,0,12,Desolace\0311375,19,1375,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6077,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,93,OBJECTIVE,3000,16,",[1382]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Your name is whispered among the Gelkis. You have much Magram blood on your hands. This is good.$B$BMaybe it is also good if we speak. Speak of what you can do for the Gelkis, and what we can do for you.\030We are fortunate the centaur clans fight among themselves, for if they joined into a single force then they would be unstoppable.  Yes, we are fortunate, and we should press our advantage.$B$BOne of the centaur clans, the Gelkis clan, is in brutal war with the Magram clan.  If we attack the Magram, then perhaps an alliance may be struck with the Gelkis.$B$BSpeak with Uthek the Wise, in the outskirts of the Gelkis camps in southwestern Desolace.  Through her we might strike an alliance with the Gelkis.\030Gain a Friendly reputation with the Gelkis, then speak with Uthek the Wise.\030Be gone! The Gelkis do not want you here. Leave now!!$B$BReturn after killing many Magram, and then I will speak with you.\030Strange Alliance\0312,1,129,2,261,4,5396\0302,132,188,2,257,1,5396\0302,193,273,2,261,1,5396\0302,276,355,2,261,4,5396\0302,360,448,2,257,1,5396\0302,451,506,2,257,4,5396\0303,1,75,2,384,1,5396\0301,1,40,4,272,1,5397\0301,42,82,4,272,1,5397\0301,84,96,4,272,1,5397\0301,101,134,4,272,4,5397\0301,136,203,4,272,1,5397\0304,1,8,3,256,1,5397\0304,10,41,3,258,1,5397\0304,43,53,3,256,1,5397\0304,58,122,3,256,3,5397\03193,2,1,Centaur\03093,2,3,Centaur\0305397,2,5,Uthek the Wise\0305397,2,7,Uthek the Wise\0312,405,1443,0,\0311384,23,1384,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031REPUTATION,92,OBJECTIVE,3000,16,",[1383]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Splendid, $N! And just in time too. From what Zraedus tells me, the Infiltrator has recovered from his wounds and is ready to be questioned by the orcs.$B$BGive me but a moment to prepare the pois - I mean prepare the truth serum.\030I have just the right serum in mind. It will deal with the truth in precisely the way the truth should be dealt with.$B$BFor this concoction I will need several Shadow Panther hearts from the Swamp. I also require the enchanted fungus off of the Mire Lord who resides there. I am sure one as able as you, $n, can persuade him to part with some.$B$BNow the hard part will be locating a Deepstrider tumor from far-off Desolace. Very rarely the giants there become ill and a tumor forms.$B$BNow, off you go!\030Apothecary Faustin at Beggar's Haunt needs 5 Shadow Panther Hearts, Mire Lord Fungus and a Deep Strider Tumor.\030That Infiltrator in Stonard will surely.... open up... after he drinks my special serum. Haha!$B$BThe ingredients required are by no means easy to procure. Shadow Panthers are common in the Swamp but collecting enough hearts for our purpose can be daunting. And the Mire Lord can be such a fussy beast.$B$BAs for the Deepstrider tumor, they are terribly difficult to find. But the chemical reaction I can draw from it is second to none.\030Nothing But The Truth\0312,1,36,2,257,1,5414\0302,38,117,2,257,3,5414\0302,122,198,2,259,3,5414\0302,200,274,2,257,1,5414\0302,276,344,2,257,1,5414\0302,349,425,2,257,3,5414\0302,427,484,2,257,1,5414\0302,489,504,2,257,1,5414\0303,1,110,2,386,1,5414\0301,1,13,4,272,1,5414\0301,15,35,4,272,1,5414\0301,37,152,4,272,1,5414\0301,157,230,4,272,1,5414\0304,1,43,3,256,3,5414\0304,45,54,3,256,1,5414\0304,56,88,3,256,1,5414\0304,90,94,3,256,1,5414\0304,99,155,3,256,1,5414\0304,157,257,3,256,1,5414\0304,259,302,3,256,1,5414\0304,307,372,3,256,1,5414\0304,374,436,3,256,1,5414\031768,2,3,Shadow Panther\030736,2,3,Panther\0301081,2,4,Mire Lord\0305414,2,9,Apothecary Faustin\030768,2,9,Shadow Panther\030736,2,9,Panther\0301081,2,9,Mire Lord\0305360,2,9,Deep Strider\0304244,3,19,Shadow\0301081,3,20,Mire Lord\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,3,Swamp\0302,0,0,9,Beggar's Haunt\0303,0,0,14,Stonard\0303,0,0,19,Swamp\0311372,19,1372,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301388,23,1388,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6080,OBJECTIVE,5,15,\030ITEM,6081,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,6082,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1384]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You do a good thing for the Gelkis. The Kolkar are weak and will die. Their magic is pathetic and will not save them. You showed them this, and their fear will make them even more feeble!$B$BAnd in our lands, the feeble soon die.\030The Kolkar centaurs think their magic is strong.  They do not know magic!  They would not know magic if it bit them!$B$BYou will show them their magic is weak.  Go to the Kolkar  to the northeast and kill them.  Take their charms.  Bring me the charms and I will throw them in the fire and laugh!\030Maintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and bring 10 Crude Charms to Uthek the Wise in the Gelkis Village in Desolace.\030You have the charms? You showed the Kolkar they are weak?\030Raid on the Kolkar\0312,1,48,2,257,1,5397\0302,51,73,2,257,1,5397\0302,76,116,2,257,4,5397\0302,121,159,2,257,3,5397\0302,162,210,2,257,1,5397\0302,213,230,2,257,1,5397\0302,233,296,2,257,3,5397\0303,1,120,2,384,1,5397\0301,1,35,4,272,1,5397\0301,37,69,4,280,3,5397\0301,71,117,4,280,3,5397\0301,119,187,4,272,3,5397\0301,192,229,4,272,1,5397\0304,1,20,3,256,2,5397\0304,22,57,3,256,2,5397\0315397,2,8,Uthek the Wise\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,5,Kolkar\0302,0,0,8,Uthek the Wise\0302,0,0,8,Gelkis Village\0302,0,0,8,Desolace\0311382,19,1382,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301370,23,1370,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6079,OBJECTIVE,10,15,\030REPUTATION,92,OBJECTIVE,3000,16,",[1385]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Many Gelkis fall to you. I like that. Maybe you can do more things I like. Maybe you and the Magram can be friends.\030Desolace is a land at war.  The centaurs wage war with each other, and we believe the victor among them will spill out and threaten our strongholds.  That, we cannot allow$B$BWe must learn how to beat the centaurs, and to do that... we must ally with one of the clans.  The Magram centaurs war with the Gelkis.  If you fight the Gelkis then the Magram might consider an alliance.$B$BEarn the favor of the Magrams then speak with Warug, in the Magram village in southeastern Desolace.\030Gain a Friendly reputation with the Magram, then speak with Warug.\030You will go now, or the Magram will crush you! To be our friend, you must kill Gelkis.\030Brutal Politics\0312,1,26,2,261,1,5396\0302,29,148,2,261,4,5396\0302,151,171,2,265,1,5396\0302,176,232,2,257,1,5396\0302,234,268,2,257,1,5396\0302,271,310,2,261,1,5396\0302,313,379,2,261,4,5396\0302,384,483,2,257,1,5396\0303,1,66,2,384,1,5396\0301,1,24,4,272,1,5398\0301,26,37,4,272,1,5398\0301,39,74,4,272,4,5398\0301,76,115,4,272,4,5398\0304,1,46,3,256,3,5398\0304,48,86,3,256,1,5398\0315398,2,8,Warug\0305398,2,9,Warug\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,8,Magram\0311386,23,1386,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031REPUTATION,93,OBJECTIVE,3000,16,",[1386]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The Kolkar fear you now! I hope you laughed when you killed them. It is better to laugh when you kill, so the enemy can see he is weak.\030The Kolkar think they are strong, but we laugh at them!  We laugh and we kill them!  You kill them too.  Show me you can kill Kolkar like we do. Head north and slay them all!\030Maintain your reputation with the Magram. Kill 12 Kolkar Centaurs, 12 Kolkar Scouts and 6 Kolkar Maulers, then return to Warug in the Magram Village in Desolace.\030Are you afraid of the Kolkar? Why do you not kill them? Maybe you forgot how to kill. Hurry and kill Kolkar before they are dead!\030Assault on the Kolkar\0312,1,55,2,257,1,5398\0302,58,83,2,257,1,5398\0302,86,103,2,257,1,5398\0302,106,144,2,257,1,5398\0302,146,174,2,257,1,5398\0303,1,41,2,384,1,5398\0303,43,161,2,384,1,5398\0301,1,24,4,272,1,5398\0301,26,65,4,274,3,5398\0301,67,135,4,276,1,5398\0304,1,29,3,256,2,5398\0304,31,55,3,256,2,5398\0304,57,85,3,256,4,5398\0304,87,129,3,264,1,5398\0315398,2,7,Warug\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,7,Warug\0302,0,0,7,Magram Village\0302,0,0,7,Desolace\0311385,19,1385,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301369,23,1369,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,4632,OBJECTIVE,12,13,Kolkar Centaur\030NPC,4633,OBJECTIVE,12,13,Kolkar Scout\030NPC,4634,OBJECTIVE,6,13,Kolkar Mauler\030REPUTATION,93,OBJECTIVE,3000,16,",[1387]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, the ears. Well done.$B$BYour service to the Alliance is unquestioned, $N. The blood you spilled in Desolace will, no doubt, save countless lives.\030Many clans make up the centaur race.  Each has its own leader and agenda, but all the clans have one thing in common.  Cruelty.$B$BIf we are to ever find peace, then the centaurs must be removed.  And so I put you on the task to do just that.$B$BWhile wandering Desolace, hunt centaur and take their ears.  Bring me many, many ears.$B$BDo this in service of the Alliance, $N, and we will be one step closer to war's end.\030Bring 15 Centaur Ears to Corporal Melkins at Nijel's Point in Desolace.\030Do you have a report, $N?\030Centaur Bounty\0312,1,36,2,257,1,5752\0302,39,117,2,257,1,5752\0302,120,127,2,257,1,5752\0302,132,195,2,265,4,5752\0302,198,242,2,257,1,5752\0302,247,305,2,257,1,5752\0302,308,332,2,257,1,5752\0302,337,420,2,261,3,5752\0303,1,71,2,384,1,5752\0301,1,13,4,272,1,5752\0301,15,24,4,272,1,5752\0301,29,77,4,272,1,5752\0301,79,149,4,280,3,5752\0304,1,25,3,256,2,5752\03193,2,1,Centaur\03093,2,6,Centaur\03093,2,9,Centaur\0305752,2,9,Corporal Melkins\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,9,Corporal Melkins\0302,0,0,9,Nijel's Point\0302,0,0,9,Desolace\0304,0,0,12,Alliance\0304,0,0,13,Desolace\031\031ITEM,6067,OBJECTIVE,15,15,",[1388]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I knew old Faustin would come up with something good! You were a tremendous help, no doubt.$B$BNow let's get down to business, shall we?\030Everything is proceeding according to plan, $n. I want you to give this truth serum to Deathstalker Zraedus and he'll show you how to administer it.... properly.$B$BHaha!\030Give Faustin's Truth Serum to Deathstalker Zraedus at Beggar's Haunt.\030I hope you have proven yourself of use to our dear friend, Apothecary Faustin.\030Nothing But The Truth\0312,1,47,2,257,1,5414\0302,49,151,2,259,1,5414\0302,153,161,2,257,1,5414\0302,166,170,2,257,1,5414\0303,1,69,2,384,1,5414\0301,1,53,4,272,4,5418\0301,55,91,4,272,1,5418\0301,96,136,4,272,2,5418\0304,1,78,3,258,3,5418\0315418,2,2,Deathstalker Zraedus\0305418,2,5,Deathstalker Zraedus\0305414,3,9,Apothecary Faustin\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,2,Deathstalker Zraedus\0302,0,0,5,Deathstalker Zraedus\0302,0,0,5,Beggar's Haunt\0311383,19,1383,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301391,23,1391,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1389]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, $N. We, are in your debt.\030The lost ones who live in the Fallow Sanctuary look as we look, but they are monsters... driven mad by the rigors of our journey to Azeroth.  Once our brethren, they now live in the Fallow Sanctuary to the east, catching or killing any who wander near.$B$BAnd they have stolen something sacred to us--draenethyst crystals.$B$BWe lack the force to enter the Fallow Sanctuary and reclaim our stolen draenethyst from among their huts and campfires, but without those crystals... we too may lose our way.\030Bring 6 Draenethyst crystals to Magtoor at The Harborage in the Swamp of Sorrows.\030Do you have the crystals?\030Draenethyst Crystals\0312,1,88,2,261,1,1776\0302,90,140,2,257,1,1776\0302,143,252,2,257,1,1776\0302,257,322,2,261,1,1776\0302,327,475,2,261,1,1776\0302,477,500,2,257,1,1776\0303,1,81,2,384,1,1776\0301,1,14,4,272,1,1776\0301,16,36,4,272,1,1776\0304,1,25,3,256,2,1776\0311776,2,7,Magtoor\0312,8,1435,0,\0302,0,0,1,Fallow Sanctuary\0302,0,0,2,Azeroth\0302,0,0,3,Fallow Sanctuary\0302,0,0,7,Magtoor\0302,0,0,7,The Harborage\0302,0,0,7,Swamp of Sorrows\031\031ITEM,6071,OBJECTIVE,6,15,",[139]="PARTIAL\031characters,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You're on your way to the jackpot, treasure seeker!\030Searching through the barrel you discover another piece of parchment.  This one reads:  Now from this here barrel, face ye North.  Straight as the crow flies, keep ye walkin' till you see the empty jug next to the lone windmill on the sea bluffs.  If ye poke around that jug, ye just might find what you're lookin' for.\030Search the empty jug next to the windmill for the next clue.\030\030Captain Sander's Hidden Treasure\0312,1,69,2,257,1,0\0302,72,129,2,257,1,0\0302,132,246,2,257,1,0\0302,249,319,2,257,4,0\0303,1,60,2,384,1,0\0301,1,51,4,272,1,0\031\0312,40,1436,0,\031138,19,138,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030140,23,140,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,36,GIVER,?,9,Broken Barrel\030OBJECT,34,FINISHER,?,12,Old Jug",[1391]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A drink for me? How kind. It's been days since they've allowed me to drink. Let me drink this down and then I'll tell you what I've learned....\030We need to operate with a certain amount of discretion. After all, it's not like you're going to waltz in there and convince the fool to drink Faustin's concoction here, right?$B$BBut if there's one thing those humans cannot deny it's the booze. I'll take Faustin's serum and mix it into this ale. I guarantee the poor sap will show no reluctance when it comes to chug-a-lugging a brew.$B$BMake haste to Stonard in the Swamp of Sorrows, $n. And keep our little mission nice and quiet...\030Take Zraedus's Brew to Infiltrator Marksen in Stonard.\030Please have mercy on me! I have information that goes beyond alliance boundaries. While I am no sympathizer of the Horde, there is political treachery going on that must be revealed!\030Nothing But The Truth\0312,1,55,2,259,1,5418\0302,57,176,2,257,2,5418\0302,181,245,2,257,4,5418\0302,247,297,2,257,1,5418\0302,299,386,2,257,3,5418\0302,391,440,2,257,1,5418\0302,442,486,2,257,1,5418\0303,1,54,2,384,1,5418\0301,1,15,4,272,2,5416\0301,17,25,4,272,1,5416\0301,27,75,4,272,1,5416\0301,77,143,4,272,1,5416\0304,1,24,3,256,1,5416\0304,26,81,3,256,1,5416\0304,83,182,3,256,1,5416\0315416,2,8,Infiltrator Marksen\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,6,Stonard\0302,0,0,6,Swamp of Sorrows\0302,0,0,8,Infiltrator Marksen\0302,0,0,8,Stonard\0311388,19,1388,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1392]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have gained the weapon of the dreaded Noboru? Is he then dead?$B$BThis is a joyous day for the Harborage. Noboru and his gang were a terror to us, wandering the swamps and killing any Draenei who crossed his path. He was a direct threat to our survival, and we did not have the strength to face him.$B$BWe are fortunate to have a friend in you, $N.\030Noboru has plagued the Draenei of the Harborage for months, and his cudgel is a symbol of the brutality they have suffered at the hands of the lost ones.\030Bring Noboru's Cudgel to the leader of The Harborage in the Swamp of Sorrows.\030Greetings. And welcome to the Harborage.\030Noboru the Cudgel\0312,1,153,2,261,1,0\0303,1,77,2,384,1,0\0301,1,49,4,272,2,1776\0301,51,66,4,272,2,1776\0301,71,109,4,272,1,1776\0301,111,217,4,272,1,1776\0301,219,303,4,284,1,1776\0301,308,352,4,272,1,1776\0304,1,10,3,256,1,1776\0304,12,40,3,256,1,1776\031\0312,8,1435,0,\0302,0,0,2,Swamp of Sorrows\0303,0,0,10,Harborage\031\031ITEM,6196,STARTER,?,10,",[1393]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031The keyhole of this strongbox is filled with black resin. It is impossible to open.$B$BBut Galen told you of a hidden latch on the box's bottom... $B$B...After a quick search the latch is found. The latch is flipped, and the strongbox opens...\030Please help!  These creatures are going to eat me!$B$BHelp me out of here, and I'll give you a great treasure!  It's in my camp in the swamp north of Stonard, but it's locked in a strongbox that can be opened through a trick that only I know.$B$BIf you help me escape, then I'll teach it to you.\030Escort Galen out of danger, then find his camp in the Swamp of Sorrows and open his strongbox.\030Escort Galen out of the Fallow Sanctuary.\030The keyhole of this strongbox is filled with black resin.  It is impossible to open.\030Galen's Escape\0312,1,12,2,257,1,5391\0302,15,50,2,257,3,5391\0302,55,110,2,257,1,5391\0302,113,242,2,257,1,5391\0302,247,295,2,257,4,5391\0303,1,94,2,388,1,5391\0301,1,57,4,272,1,0\0301,59,83,4,272,1,0\0301,88,146,4,272,1,0\0301,152,194,4,272,1,0\0301,196,243,4,272,1,0\0305,1,57,3,256,1,0\0305,60,84,3,256,1,0\0304,1,41,3,384,1,5391\031\0312,8,1435,0,\0302,0,0,4,Stonard\0302,0,0,6,Swamp of Sorrows\031\031OBJECT,32569,FINISHER,?,12,Galen's Strongbox",[1394]="PARTIAL\031conflict,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, $N. It has been a long time since you have last stepped into my home. It seems like many moons have passed since you took your first leap that set you upon your path.$B$BAnd now you return to me stronger than you once were... more enlightened. This pleases me. And you should be justly rewarded for seeing my tests to the end.\030You have done well, $N. You have passed my test, and the tests before mine. Return to Dorn in Thousand Needles. He will sense the change within you, and see that your mind, body and spirit are strong enough that you should be rewarded for your efforts.$B$BStay true to the balance you've shown throughout these trials, $N. Dorn will test you again in the future if you do.\030Speak to Dorn Plainstalker in Thousand Needles.\030\030Final Passage\0312,1,23,2,257,1,4488\0302,25,75,2,257,1,4488\0302,77,111,2,257,1,4488\0302,113,252,2,257,3,4488\0302,257,322,2,265,1,4488\0302,324,372,2,257,4,4488\0303,1,47,2,384,1,4488\0301,9,73,4,272,1,2986\0301,75,170,4,272,4,2986\0301,175,229,4,368,1,2986\0301,231,247,4,272,1,2986\0301,249,264,4,272,1,2986\0301,266,330,4,272,1,2986\0312986,2,7,Dorn Plainstalker\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,3,Dorn\0302,0,0,3,Thousand Needles\0302,0,0,7,Dorn Plainstalker\0302,0,0,7,Thousand Needles\0316628,19,6628,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1395]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, the powerstones! The mages will be happy to see these!$B$BMany thanks, $N. I know your trip from Darkshire was not an easy one.\030This crate of powerstones needs to go to Nethergarde Keep, in the Blasted Lands.  They won't hold their power for long, so we can't ship them with the next caravan.$B$BYou must take them, and you must take them quickly.$B$BBring them to Quartermaster Lungertz in Nethergarde Keep.  To reach the keep, you must travel east through Deadwind Pass, then east through the Swamp of Sorrows, then south through the Blasted Lands.$B$BUse caution, $N.  You will travel through dangerous lands, yet you must not fail.\030Bring the Crate of Powerstones to Quartermaster Lungertz, before the powerstones expire.\030Hello! Don't mind all the commotion, it's just business as usual at Nethergarde Keep.$B$BYou have something for me?\030Supplies for Nethergarde\0312,1,80,2,259,1,5464\0302,83,164,2,257,1,5464\0302,169,219,2,257,1,5464\0302,224,280,2,257,1,5464\0302,283,422,2,257,1,5464\0302,427,442,2,257,1,5464\0302,445,507,2,265,3,5464\0303,1,88,2,384,1,5464\0301,1,20,4,272,1,5393\0301,22,58,4,272,3,5393\0301,63,78,4,272,1,5393\0301,80,131,4,272,1,5393\0304,1,6,3,256,1,5393\0304,8,85,3,256,1,5393\0304,90,115,3,256,2,5393\0315393,2,4,Quartermaster Lungertz\0305393,2,8,Quartermaster Lungertz\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,1,Nethergarde Keep\0302,0,0,1,Blasted Lands\0302,0,0,4,Quartermaster Lungertz\0302,0,0,4,Nethergarde Keep\0302,0,0,8,Quartermaster Lungertz\0304,0,0,12,Darkshire\0303,0,0,14,Nethergarde Keep\031\031",[1396]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The sounds of animals are now faint, more distant. Thank you, $N. Now let's hope they don't return!\030My caravan was destined for the eastern coast, but we did not reach our goal.  Lost Ones attacked us, killing guards and dashing supplies.$B$BI alone survived their assault.  I have sworn to protect what supplies remain, but wild creatures skulk near.  Please, help me defend my camp from the beasts!\030Kill 8 Young Sawtooth Crocolisks, 10 Sorrow Spinners and 10 Swamp Jaguars then return to Watcher Biggs in the Swamp of Sorrows.\030The swamp creatures press close, $N. Please, you must defend the camp!\030Encroaching Wildlife\0312,1,77,2,259,1,5476\0302,80,138,2,261,1,5476\0302,143,173,2,257,1,5476\0302,176,251,2,271,1,5476\0302,254,300,2,269,1,5476\0303,1,127,2,384,1,5476\0301,1,50,4,272,1,5476\0301,52,65,4,272,1,5476\0301,67,99,4,272,3,5476\0304,1,36,3,256,1,5476\0304,38,70,3,268,1,5476\0315476,2,6,Watcher Biggs\0312,8,1435,0,\0302,0,0,6,Watcher Biggs\0302,0,0,6,Swamp of Sorrows\0311421,23,1421,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,1084,OBJECTIVE,8,13,Young Sawtooth Crocolisk\030NPC,858,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Sorrow Spinner\030NPC,767,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Swamp Jaguar",[1398]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This wood is light, but tough. Thank you, $N. It will work nicely.\030I owe you greatly, $N.  An honorable heart beats within you.  And now I have another task for which I humbly ask your aid.$B$BIf I'm ever to reach Nethergarde, then I must fix this wagon.  And for that... I will need wood.  Strong, dry wood--not the spongy, tangled wood of the swamp's trees.$B$B$N, go east to the coast and search for driftwood that has been dried by the sun.  Bring it to me.\030Bring 8 pieces of Sundried Driftwood to Watcher Biggs in the Swamp of Sorrows.\030Did you find any driftwood, $N?\030Driftwood\0312,1,22,2,257,1,5476\0302,25,60,2,257,1,5476\0302,63,122,2,257,1,5476\0302,127,187,2,257,4,5476\0302,190,204,2,257,1,5476\0302,206,222,2,259,3,5476\0302,225,292,2,257,1,5476\0302,297,377,2,257,1,5476\0302,380,394,2,257,1,5476\0303,1,78,2,384,1,5476\0301,1,30,4,272,1,5476\0301,32,45,4,272,1,5476\0301,47,66,4,272,3,5476\0304,1,31,3,256,2,5476\0315476,2,10,Watcher Biggs\0312,8,1435,0,\0302,0,0,10,Watcher Biggs\0302,0,0,10,Swamp of Sorrows\0311421,19,1421,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301425,23,1425,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6146,OBJECTIVE,8,15,",[14]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031When I left the tainted lands of Lordaeron I returned to a grim state of affairs here in my homeland. But there is hope for Westfall yet. As proven by your valor in battle, it is obvious to me that you serve our cause with honor. It is with great pride that I induct thee into The People's Militia. May the Light shine upon you.\030Some Defias have eluded us.  My most trusted scout reports that these Defias have been looting and pillaging the countryside, all the way into Southern Westfall.  We believe they are hiding out in the Dagger Hills, plotting their next move.   Slay the wretches in the name of The People's Militia.\030Gryan Stoutmantle wants you to kill 15 Defias Highwaymen, 5 Defias Pathstalkers and 5 Defias Knuckledusters then return to him on Sentinel Hill.\030$N, now is no time for idle chatter. If you still wish to prove yourself to The People's Militia you need to slay the Defias I notified you about earlier. Return to me when you have completed your duty.\030The People's Militia\0312,1,27,2,257,1,234\0302,30,161,2,257,1,234\0302,164,240,2,257,4,234\0302,244,297,2,257,1,234\0303,1,144,2,386,1,234\0301,1,101,4,272,1,234\0301,103,137,4,274,3,234\0301,139,229,4,276,1,234\0301,231,298,4,272,1,234\0301,300,328,4,272,1,234\0304,1,36,3,256,1,234\0304,38,154,3,258,4,234\0304,156,202,3,256,1,234\031234,2,5,Gryan Stoutmantle\030616,3,11,Chatter\0312,40,1436,0,\0302,0,0,3,Dagger Hills\0303,0,0,12,The People's Militia\03113,19,13,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,122,OBJECTIVE,15,13,Defias Highwayman\030NPC,121,OBJECTIVE,5,13,Defias Pathstalker\030NPC,449,OBJECTIVE,5,13,Defias Knuckleduster",[140]="PARTIAL\031characters,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The hinges on the old chest are rusty but they still work. You force the chest open and take the booty.$B$BCongratulations!\030Sure enough, deep within the Old Jug there is another clue to Sander's treasure.  The ink has run in some places and the paper smells like whiskey but you can make out some of the text:  Now that ye found me ol' whiskey jug, you're almost to the treasure!  Just face West from the bottle and walk down to the shore.  Once ye get to the water, keep going!  Swim straight west till you find the island with me treasure chest!\030Locate Captain Sanders' chest and open it for your reward.\030\030Captain Sander's Hidden Treasure\0312,1,80,2,257,1,0\0302,83,255,2,257,1,0\0302,258,315,2,257,1,0\0302,318,354,2,257,1,0\0302,357,423,2,257,1,0\0303,1,58,2,384,1,0\0301,1,58,4,272,1,0\0301,60,103,4,272,1,0\0301,108,123,4,272,1,0\031\0312,40,1436,0,\0302,0,0,1,Old Jug the\0302,0,0,1,Sander's\031139,19,139,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,34,GIVER,?,9,Old Jug\030OBJECT,33,FINISHER,?,12,Locked Chest",[141]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Edwin VanCleef. . .I know the name well. To think that a man so industrious and talented could turn into such a scoundrel unnerves me. I'll need further proof before I believe this.\030The Stonemasons' Guild was run by a man named Edwin VanCleef.  VanCleef was responsible for rebuilding Stormwind after the orcs razed it in the First War.  Apparently, VanCleef and his men were unhappy with their treatment by the King after the reconstruction was complete.  That just might explain a thing or two.$B$BI have written a more detailed account for your Master in Westfall.  Take this to him at once!\030Take Shaw's report to Gryan Stoutmantle in Westfall.\030Did Master Shaw shed any light on things?\030The Defias Brotherhood\0312,1,61,2,321,1,332\0302,64,154,2,325,1,332\0302,157,273,2,261,4,332\0302,276,314,2,257,4,332\0302,319,385,2,257,1,332\0302,388,412,2,257,1,332\0303,1,52,2,384,1,332\0301,1,15,4,272,1,234\0301,19,40,4,272,1,234\0301,42,134,4,272,4,234\0301,136,181,4,274,4,234\0304,1,41,3,256,2,234\031639,2,1,Edwin VanCleef\030234,2,7,Gryan Stoutmantle\030639,4,8,Edwin VanCleef\0312,40,1436,0,\0302,0,0,2,First War\0302,0,0,5,Westfall\0302,0,0,7,Gryan Stoutmantle\0302,0,0,7,Westfall\031135,19,135,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030142,23,142,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1418]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Helgrum wants a report, eh? I sent an outrunner to Stonard not three days past. Did he fail his mission? If Stonard does not have my report, then it appears he did fail.$B$BLet's hope the next runner I send has more skill, or more luck.\030The Badlands is harsh and lies close to the Alliance-held land of Loch Modan, so communication between Stonard and the Badlands outpost of Kargath is often cut.$B$BProve yourself, $N.  Travel to the Badlands and speak with Neeka Bloodscar, head scout of the Kargath outpost.  Speak with her, and then send her report back to me.\030Speak with Neeka Bloodscar.\030\030Neeka Bloodscar\0312,1,160,2,257,1,1442\0302,165,183,2,257,1,1442\0302,186,274,2,257,1,1442\0302,277,328,2,257,1,1442\0303,1,27,2,384,1,1442\0301,1,27,4,274,2,5394\0301,29,79,4,272,1,5394\0301,81,104,4,272,2,5394\0301,106,169,4,272,4,5394\0301,174,236,4,272,3,5394\0315394,2,3,Neeka Bloodscar\0305394,2,5,Neeka Bloodscar\0312,8,1435,0,\0302,0,0,1,Alliance-held\0302,0,0,3,Badlands\0304,0,0,7,Stonard\0311420,23,1420,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301420,24,1420,UNKNOWN\031",[1419]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031That's a nice collection of jawbones, $N. Now those coyotes won't be tearing through our supplies for scraps.$B$BWell done. The coyotes of the Badlands aren't easy prey. Your deed shows me that you might just survive here.\030Have you spent many days in the Badlands, $c?  Have you felt its heat? Have you faced the beasts that wander its dusty plains?  It's time you did.$B$BCrag coyotes are a tough breed.  Tough, and bold enough to creep into Kargath and steal from our food supplies.  Help rid the outpost of these thieves!$B$BHunt crag coyotes, $N.  Hunt them and bring me their jawbones.  Bring me enough, and maybe I'll believe it when you say you know the Badlands.\030Bring 30 Coyote Jawbones to Neeka Bloodscar in Kargath.\030Do you have the jawbones?\030Coyote Thieves\0312,1,45,2,257,2,5394\0302,48,70,2,257,2,5394\0302,72,126,2,257,2,5394\0302,129,146,2,257,1,5394\0302,151,181,2,257,1,5394\0302,184,261,2,261,1,5394\0302,264,301,2,257,1,5394\0302,306,327,2,257,1,5394\0302,330,367,2,257,1,5394\0302,370,447,2,257,4,5394\0303,1,55,2,384,1,5394\0301,1,41,4,272,1,5394\0301,43,109,4,272,1,5394\0301,114,123,4,272,1,5394\0301,125,169,4,272,1,5394\0301,171,222,4,280,4,5394\0304,1,25,3,256,2,5394\031834,2,11,Coyote\0305394,2,11,Neeka Bloodscar\0312,3,1418,0,\0302,0,0,1,Badlands\0302,0,0,11,Neeka Bloodscar\0302,0,0,11,Kargath\031\031ITEM,6166,OBJECTIVE,30,15,",[142]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is indeed firm proof that VanCleef is in charge. Now all we need to know is where the Defias gang is hiding out.$B$BWe've had a stroke of luck while you were gone. We captured a thief trying to steal Saldean's wagon. He has promised to lead us to the hideout in exchange for his life. I want you to defend the traitor so he can reveal the hideout. Return to me once you have uncovered the location.\030We need to discover the location of the Defias hideout.  $N, my scout reports that a Defias Messenger has been seen on the roads between Moonbrook, the Gold Coast Quarry and the Jangolode Mine.  I want you to capture him.  If he resists, kill him and bring me whatever he is carrying.\030Track down the Defias Messenger in Westfall and bring his message to Stoutmantle.\030$N, were you able to gather any information? Did you locate the messenger?\030The Defias Brotherhood\0312,1,55,2,259,1,234\0302,58,193,2,257,1,234\0302,196,221,2,259,1,234\0302,224,284,2,257,4,234\0303,1,81,2,384,1,234\0301,1,53,4,272,1,234\0301,55,117,4,274,1,234\0301,122,168,4,272,1,234\0301,170,221,4,276,1,234\0301,223,289,4,272,1,234\0301,291,352,4,286,1,234\0301,354,403,4,272,1,234\0304,1,44,3,256,2,234\0304,46,74,3,256,2,234\031550,2,2,Defias Messenger\030550,2,5,Defias Messenger\0312,40,1436,0,\0302,0,0,5,Westfall\0302,0,0,5,Stoutmantle\031141,19,141,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030155,23,155,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,1381,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1420]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, $N. From Neeka's report, I see the Alliance is not without its own problems. And we may find that some enemies are shared between us.\030I wrote a fresh report for Helgrum in Stonard.  Bring it to him.$B$BAnd if you consider yourself an outrunner, then don't lose your way.  Or fall to an enemy.\030Bring Neeka's Report to Helgrum the Swift in Stonard.\030You returned. You have a report?\030Report to Helgrum\0312,1,46,2,257,1,5394\0302,49,64,2,257,1,5394\0302,69,136,2,257,4,5394\0302,139,158,2,261,1,5394\0303,1,53,2,384,1,5394\0301,1,14,4,272,1,1442\0301,16,87,4,272,1,1442\0301,89,144,4,276,1,1442\0304,1,13,3,256,1,1442\0304,15,32,3,256,2,1442\0311442,2,5,Helgrum the Swift\0312,3,1418,0,\0302,0,0,1,Stonard\0302,0,0,5,Helgrum the Swift\0302,0,0,5,Stonard\031\031",[1421]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, you found them! With these, the wizards in Nethergarde may continue their work. I do not know what it is that they do, but it is linked to the Dark Portal in the Blasted Lands, and is vital to the security of the Alliance.\030I was stunned during the attack by the Lost Ones, but before my sight went black I spied one of our wagons being dragged to the Fallow Sanctuary, the lost one village to the north.$B$BA caravan chest with valuable reagents was in that wagon, reagents vital to the studies of the wizards of Nethergarde Keep.  Find the chest and get those reagents, $N.  Get them and bring them to me.\030Find the Caravan Chest in the Fallow Sanctuary, obtain the Wizards' Reagents and bring to Watcher Biggs.\030Do you have the wizard's reagents, $N?\030The Lost Caravan\0312,1,180,2,261,1,5476\0302,185,307,2,257,1,5476\0302,310,351,2,257,1,5476\0302,354,383,2,257,1,5476\0303,1,104,2,384,1,5476\0301,1,19,4,272,1,5476\0301,21,83,4,272,1,5476\0301,85,226,4,280,1,5476\0304,1,38,3,256,2,5476\0315476,2,5,Watcher Biggs\0312,8,1435,0,\0302,0,0,1,Fallow Sanctuary\0302,0,0,5,Fallow Sanctuary\0302,0,0,5,Watcher Biggs\0304,0,0,7,Nethergarde\0304,0,0,8,Dark Portal\0304,0,0,8,Blasted Lands\0311396,19,1396,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301398,23,1398,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6170,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1422]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Be silent a moment, $C. Even over the dull roar of the sea you can still hear those disgusting gurgles from the fish men.\030While I begin work on your weapon, why don't you talk to Katar? He mentioned needing help with patrols along the beach, and I'd rather see you keep your wits and weapons prepared instead of getting drunk with some of the other louses I share this camp with.\030Speak to Katar in the Swamp of Sorrows.\030\030Threat From the Sea\0312,1,63,2,257,2,5592\0302,65,257,2,257,1,5592\0303,1,39,2,384,1,5592\0301,1,23,4,272,1,5593\0301,25,121,4,272,1,5593\0315593,2,1,Katar\0305593,2,3,Katar\0312,8,1435,0,\0302,0,0,1,Katar\0302,0,0,3,Katar\0302,0,0,3,Swamp of Sorrows\031699,19,699,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301426,23,1426,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1423]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, thank you $N! So many supplies are lost from Darkshire to here. It's good to see that some are recovered.\030This barrel is small yet sturdy.  Its seams are sealed with a yellow, pungent wax.  Stamped on the bottom of the barrel are the words:$B$BQUARTERMASTER LUNGERTZ$B$BNETHERGARDE KEEP\030Bring the Lost Supplies to Quartermaster Lungertz.\030You have something for me?\030The Lost Supplies\0312,1,32,2,257,1,0\0302,35,82,2,257,1,0\0302,85,134,2,257,1,0\0302,139,160,2,257,1,0\0302,165,180,2,257,1,0\0303,1,50,2,388,1,0\0301,1,17,4,272,1,5393\0301,19,67,4,276,1,5393\0301,69,109,4,272,1,5393\0304,1,26,3,256,2,5393\0315393,2,4,Quartermaster Lungertz\0305393,2,6,Quartermaster Lungertz\0312,8,1435,0,\0302,0,0,6,Quartermaster Lungertz\0304,0,0,8,Darkshire\031\031ITEM,6172,STARTER,?,10,",[1424]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Your diligence in collecting the Atal'ai artifacts is worthy of praise, $C.\030The Warchief sent us to investigate strange happenings at The Temple of Atal'Hakkar.$B$BThe Atal'ai trolls are a tribe of dark casters, known for practicing forbidden magic. You can imagine how astonished we were when we arrived here to discover the temple had been sunk.$B$BThe green dragons now guard the site, claiming to be protectors of Azeroth.$B$BWe need to discover what happened. Explore around the Pool of Tears and gather Atal'ai artifacts. From those I can begin to piece together this puzzle.\030Fel'zerul in Stonard wants you to gather 10 Atal'ai Artifacts.\030No one knows what dark practices went on inside The Temple of Atal'Hakkar. But we do know that great and powerful forces of magic were used.$B$BWe must learn as much as we can about such magic. Perhaps the spells of the Atal'ai will prove of use to the Horde.$B$BOnce you have gathered enough Atal'ai artifacts from around the Pool of Tears, I can begin to understand what the trolls were hoping to accomplish and what went so horribly wrong.\030Pool of Tears\0312,1,84,2,257,1,1443\0302,89,173,2,257,1,1443\0302,175,271,2,257,1,1443\0302,276,350,2,257,1,1443\0302,355,388,2,259,1,1443\0302,390,451,2,257,1,1443\0302,453,505,2,257,1,1443\0303,1,62,2,386,1,1443\0301,1,75,4,272,1,1443\0304,1,74,3,256,1,1443\0304,76,140,3,256,1,1443\0304,145,193,3,256,1,1443\0304,195,259,3,256,4,1443\0304,264,442,3,256,1,1443\0311443,2,8,Fel'zerul\0312,8,1435,0,\0302,0,0,1,The Temple of Atal'Hakkar\0302,0,0,8,Stonard\0303,0,0,13,Horde\0311429,23,1429,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6175,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[1425]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031What? A package from Biggs' caravan? We thought it, and he, were lost.$B$BThank you, $N. With luck, these supplies will carry the much needed reagent, Azoran Crystals. Our stock is running low...\030While I fix this wagon, $N, I have one last task for you.$B$BI have packed the most vital supplies saved from the ogre attacks.  Take them to Nethergarde Keep.  The keep is nestled in the northern hills of the Blasted Lands, keeping watch over the Dark Portal.$B$BTo reach Nethergard, follow the road east.  When it branches head south into the Blasted Lands, then turn left at the next fork.  Follow the road, $N, and be wary.\030Bring the Shipment to Nethergarde to Quartermaster Lungertz in Nethergarde Keep.\030You have business with me?\030Deliver the Shipment\0312,1,57,2,257,1,5476\0302,62,127,2,261,1,5476\0302,130,159,2,257,1,5476\0302,162,260,2,257,1,5476\0302,265,306,2,257,1,5476\0302,309,392,2,257,1,5476\0302,395,427,2,257,1,5476\0303,1,80,2,384,1,5476\0301,1,5,4,272,2,5393\0301,7,36,4,272,2,5393\0301,38,70,4,276,1,5393\0301,75,88,4,272,1,5393\0301,90,167,4,272,3,5393\0301,169,195,4,272,1,5393\0304,1,26,3,256,2,5393\031211,2,2,Ogre\0305393,2,8,Quartermaster Lungertz\0312,8,1435,0,\0302,0,0,3,Nethergarde Keep\0302,0,0,8,Nethergarde\0302,0,0,8,Quartermaster Lungertz\0302,0,0,8,Nethergarde Keep\0304,0,0,10,Biggs'\0311398,19,1398,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1426]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The sea seems vast and relentless, but you have stained her with the blood of her own spawn. The fish men know pain. Their stupidity will force them to refortify their ranks from the devastation you've caused, and that is good.$B$BLet their gurgling screams overshadow the sea's roar long into the night. I shall smile every time I hear one of them silenced.$B$BReturn to me if you wish to slay more of the fish men. I will gladly reward you again.\030I have no love for the sea, nor any creature I've seen come from its depths. It is a powerful but blind mistress; callous and brutal. It would bring me great pleasure to slay the fish men by the hundreds if it were within my power. But I garner some pleasure from watching their deaths at the hands of any who do the Horde's will.$B$BWhich brings us to you, $c. How many can you slay? Would you test yourself against their most powerful kind?\030Kill 10 Marsh Murlocs, 10 Marsh Inkspewer, and 10 Marsh Flesheater, then return to Katar in the Swamp of Sorrows.\030I am patient. Patient and everlasting like an old kank stone from Draenor. The fish men shall not make it past our borders--not while I still stand. If we had an army at our disposal I would cleanse this world and all others of their presence. I feel my hatred seethe just speaking about them.\030Threat From the Sea\0312,1,76,2,257,1,5593\0302,78,133,2,257,1,5593\0302,135,231,2,257,4,5593\0302,233,330,2,257,3,5593\0302,335,361,2,257,1,5593\0302,363,384,2,257,2,5593\0302,386,442,2,257,4,5593\0303,1,113,2,384,1,5593\0301,1,92,4,272,4,5593\0301,94,116,4,272,1,5593\0301,118,227,4,272,3,5593\0301,232,304,4,272,1,5593\0301,306,358,4,272,3,5593\0301,363,416,4,274,4,5593\0301,418,448,4,272,3,5593\0304,1,13,3,256,1,5593\0304,15,74,3,256,1,5593\0304,76,148,3,256,3,5593\0304,150,243,3,256,4,5593\0304,245,293,3,256,1,5593\031750,2,8,Marsh Inkspewer\030751,2,8,Marsh Flesheater\0305593,2,8,Katar\0312,8,1435,0,\0302,0,0,8,Katar\0302,0,0,8,Swamp of Sorrows\0303,0,0,17,Draenor\0311422,19,1422,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301427,23,1427,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,747,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Marsh Murloc\030NPC,750,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Marsh Inkspewer\030NPC,751,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Marsh Flesheater",[1427]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, $N, you've returned. Good. I've finished crafting more weapons for our fight against the murlocs. For bringing us the fresh sawtooth meat, and for bringing a small smile to Katar's face, I offer one of them to you.\030Before you take rest, speak to Tok'Kar again. While you were gone I believe he finished a few weapons. For your help here, he would offer one of them to you. You would do well to test its strength against the fish men when you are ready... but only to please me further.\030Speak with Tok'Kar in the Swamp of Sorrows.\030\030Threat From the Sea\0312,1,45,2,257,1,5593\0302,47,102,2,257,4,5593\0302,104,157,2,257,4,5593\0302,159,239,2,257,4,5593\0302,241,270,2,257,1,5593\0303,1,43,2,384,1,5593\0301,1,24,4,272,1,5592\0301,26,30,4,272,1,5592\0301,32,101,4,276,1,5592\0301,103,218,4,272,1,5592\0315592,2,1,Tok'Kar\0305592,2,6,Tok'Kar\0312,8,1435,0,\0302,0,0,1,Tok'Kar\0302,0,0,6,Swamp of Sorrows\0304,0,0,10,Katar's\0311426,19,1426,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301428,23,1428,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1428]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $C. I call for more of their blood. Let all the fish men perish.\030It pleases me to see your hatred for the fish men grows with mine.$B$BFind more of their kind along the beach, and when you've had your fill of combat, return to me. We shall speak then of a reward for your diligence.\030Kill 10 Marsh Inkspewers, 10 Marsh Flesheaters, and 10 Marsh Oracles, then return to Katar in the Swamp of Sorrows.\030Not until the sea and all her children are silenced will I be pleased... especially those disgusting fish men.\030Continued Threat\0312,1,66,2,257,1,5593\0302,71,165,2,257,1,5593\0302,167,217,2,257,3,5593\0303,1,115,2,384,1,5593\0301,1,14,4,272,1,5593\0301,16,46,4,272,1,5593\0301,48,75,4,272,1,5593\0304,1,72,3,256,3,5593\0304,74,110,3,256,1,5593\0315593,2,4,Katar\0312,8,1435,0,\0302,0,0,4,Katar\0302,0,0,4,Swamp of Sorrows\0311427,19,1427,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,750,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Marsh Inkspewer\030NPC,751,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Marsh Flesheater\030NPC,752,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Marsh Oracle",[1429]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You bring me the summoning artifacts of the Atail'ai?$B$BI see Jammal'an the Prophet is leading the disciples of the Chamber of Blood towards their chosen fate. Has Hakkar returned to the Temple I wonder? Has their fate been met?\030While you were braving the dangers of the Pool of Tears, one of my scouts returned with a scroll written in blood on dried flesh. It seems to be a judicial sentence against a priest of the Atal'ai tribe.$B$BThis priest was sentenced to a fate worse than death amongst the Atal'ai.$B$BHe was exiled to live far north in the Hinterlands, with the Witherbark trolls.$B$BI will bundle these artifacts. You are to seek out the exile and discover their true use. Return to me once your journey is complete.\030Bring the Bundle of Atal'ai Artifacts to the Atal'ai Exile in the Hinterlands.\030You are brave to come here. Brave or foolish...\030The Atal'ai Exile\0312,1,129,2,257,1,1443\0302,131,203,2,257,4,1443\0302,208,280,2,257,1,1443\0302,285,363,2,257,1,1443\0302,368,397,2,257,3,1443\0302,399,456,2,259,1,1443\0302,458,500,2,257,1,1443\0303,1,78,2,384,1,1443\0301,1,53,4,272,2,5598\0301,58,160,4,272,1,5598\0301,162,204,4,272,2,5598\0301,206,229,4,272,2,5598\0304,1,27,3,256,1,5598\0304,29,47,3,256,1,5598\031111,2,2,Priest\030111,2,3,Priest\0305598,2,8,Atal'ai Exile\0305710,4,10,Jammal'an the Prophet\03014834,4,11,Hakkar\0312,8,1435,0,\0302,0,0,4,Hinterlands\0302,0,0,8,Atal'ai Exile\0302,0,0,8,Hinterlands\0304,0,0,11,Temple\0311424,19,1424,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301444,23,1444,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[143]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Good Messenger, you have served your master well.\030Something odd is afoot with the Stormwind Army.  They should have been here in force by now.  Time is a luxury we don't have, however.  I will not stand by and watch the people of Lakeshire give their lives without trying to enlist more help.  I've heard word of a people's militia forming in Westfall.$B$BTake this plea to their leader, Gryan Stoutmantle.  Perhaps Stoutmantle's men can lend some support here until the King sends reserves.\030Magistrate Solomon wants you to take his written plea to Gryan Stoutmantle in Westfall.\030Hail, $C. What business do you have with The People's Militia?\030Messenger to Westfall\0312,1,47,2,257,1,344\0302,50,92,2,257,1,344\0302,95,134,2,257,1,344\0302,137,242,2,257,3,344\0302,245,302,2,257,1,344\0302,307,356,2,257,1,344\0302,359,441,2,257,4,344\0303,1,87,2,386,1,344\0301,1,49,4,272,1,234\0304,1,9,3,256,1,234\0304,11,62,3,256,2,234\031234,2,6,Gryan Stoutmantle\030344,2,8,Magistrate Solomon\030798,2,8,Solomon\030234,2,8,Gryan Stoutmantle\0312,44,1433,0,\0302,0,0,5,Westfall\0302,0,0,8,Gryan Stoutmantle\0302,0,0,8,Westfall\031121,19,121,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030144,23,144,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1430]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, this should be perfect. I can't wait to taste these after they are prepared perfectly over an open fire. You should take a sample of it with you on your travels. It truly is delicious.\030There's a high demand for the succulent taste of crawler meat among my customers; especially the meat from the monstrous crawlers.$B$BIf you plan on heading to the coast, then I could easily make it worth your while to bring me back some of their legs to have transported back to Orgrimmar.$B$BThe coast is to the east from here, and you should have no problem finding the creatures scurrying along the beaches and under the sea.\030Bring 10 Monstrous Crawler Legs to Dar in the Swamp of Sorrows.\030I have a cask of wine waiting for your success, $N. It's only right I taste the goods before I have it shipped back to my customers.\030Fresh Meat\0312,1,130,2,257,1,5591\0302,135,290,2,257,4,5591\0302,295,429,2,261,1,5591\0303,1,63,2,384,1,5591\0301,1,27,4,272,1,5591\0301,29,108,4,272,1,5591\0301,110,165,4,272,1,5591\0301,167,188,4,272,1,5591\0304,1,51,3,256,1,5591\0304,53,132,3,256,1,5591\0316250,2,1,Crawler\0301088,2,4,Monstrous Crawler\0306250,2,4,Crawler\0312,8,1435,0,\0302,0,0,2,Orgrimmar\0302,0,0,4,Dar\0302,0,0,4,Swamp of Sorrows\031\031ITEM,6184,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[1431]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031$N, noble $C. I am Keldran, student of magic... and other mystical arts.$B$BThe business Craven sent you here to speak to me about requires a touch more subtlety than you've previously needed, but that does not mean you can not still aid our cause.$B$BPlease, make yourself comfortable, and I shall tell you why the Warchief has need of my aid... and yours.$B$BIt starts with appearances, $N. How the Horde sees itself. How our allies see us. And most importantly, how our enemies see us.\030Be still, $c, and allow me to share with you something important to our people, but far from obvious.$B$BWe are a proud race, and the war with the humans tried even Thrall's great patience. You see, our Warchief is wise and prudent, and he continues to put his people first. Ultimately, he is a diplomat, and in his time with the humans he learned much of their ways.$B$BIf the tale I've started piques your interest, then find Keldran near the western exit of the city. His hovel is there.\030Speak to Keldran in Orgrimmar.\030\030Alliance Relations\0312,1,101,2,257,1,5639\0302,106,189,2,261,1,5639\0302,191,274,2,257,1,5639\0302,276,367,2,257,1,5639\0302,372,470,2,257,4,5639\0302,472,490,2,257,1,5639\0303,1,30,2,384,1,5639\0301,1,13,4,272,1,5640\0301,15,47,4,272,1,5640\0301,49,72,4,272,1,5640\0301,77,248,4,272,1,5640\0301,253,346,4,274,3,5640\0301,348,357,4,272,1,5640\0301,362,392,4,272,1,5640\0301,394,419,4,272,1,5640\0301,421,442,4,272,1,5640\0301,444,488,4,276,1,5640\0315640,2,5,Keldran\0305640,2,7,Keldran\0305640,4,9,Keldran\0312,1637,1454,0,\0302,0,0,7,Keldran\0302,0,0,7,Orgrimmar\0311432,23,1432,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1432]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Greetings, $C. You bring news from Orgrimmar; that is good.$B$BThe demon infestation overwhelms this area even more than the smell of centaur dung. The horse-men claim this land as their own, but clearly there are influences out of their control that will crush them if not kept in check.$B$BIt does not please me that we aid the centaur indirectly, but it is for the good of the Horde, so I do my duty for the Warchief, even if it means helping the warlocks within the Horde.\030As the Alliance progresses deeper and deeper into Kalimdor, incorrect conclusions may be drawn about the Horde making pacts with the Burning Legion. The Warchief cannot allow that to happen. And with his blessing, I am taking control of overseeing them removed.$B$BI have agents in the area of Desolace at the Ghost Walker Post north of the great Kodo Graveyard. Head south of the Charred Vale in the Stonetalon Mountains and you shall come across it. When you arrive, seek out Takata Steelblade.\030Speak to Takata Steelblade in Desolace.\030\030Alliance Relations\0312,1,148,2,321,1,5640\0302,150,190,2,265,1,5640\0302,192,261,2,257,1,5640\0302,266,362,2,257,1,5640\0302,364,451,2,257,3,5640\0302,453,496,2,257,1,5640\0303,1,39,2,384,1,5640\0301,1,14,4,272,1,5641\0301,16,59,4,272,1,5641\0301,64,147,4,272,1,5641\0301,149,288,4,272,4,5641\0301,293,476,4,274,4,5641\0315641,2,6,Takata Steelblade\0305641,2,7,Takata Steelblade\03093,4,10,Centaur\03093,4,12,Centaur\0312,1637,1454,0,\0302,0,0,4,Ghost Walker Post\0302,0,0,5,Charred Vale\0302,0,0,5,Stonetalon Mountains\0302,0,0,7,Takata Steelblade\0302,0,0,7,Desolace\0304,0,0,9,Orgrimmar\0304,0,0,12,Horde\0311431,19,1431,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301433,23,1433,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1433]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, yes. Aid from those loyal to the Warchief is always appreciated.$B$BMy name is Maurin. I am here at the behest of Keldran and the Warchief cub Thrall. It is my desire to aid the youngling leader against the evils that threaten his rule.$B$BCome, come closer, $C. I shall explain to you my plan for removing the festering boil that is the Burning Blade.\030The Burning Blade have many agendas, but know that they are evil to their core, their spirits corrupted, and their destruction is the only way to thwart their objectives.$B$BKeldran sent Maurin with me because of his knowledge of the Blade and their warlock ways.$B$BHe has control of our plots against the Blade while I deal with the other demonic threats here in Desolace.$B$BSpeak to him, and he will guide you in his designs.\030Speak to Maurin Bonesplitter in Desolace.\030\030Alliance Relations\0312,1,170,2,261,1,5641\0302,175,263,2,259,1,5641\0302,268,374,2,257,1,5641\0302,379,429,2,257,3,5641\0303,1,41,2,384,1,5641\0301,1,8,4,272,1,4498\0301,10,68,4,272,1,4498\0301,73,90,4,272,1,4498\0301,92,154,4,272,1,4498\0301,156,240,4,278,1,4498\0301,245,266,4,272,1,4498\0301,268,356,4,272,3,4498\0315640,2,2,Keldran\0304498,2,5,Maurin Bonesplitter\0305640,4,9,Keldran\0304949,4,9,Thrall\0312,1637,1454,0,\0302,0,0,3,Desolace\0302,0,0,5,Maurin Bonesplitter\0302,0,0,5,Desolace\0304,0,0,7,Warchief\0311432,19,1432,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301435,23,1435,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1434]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have done well, $c. You have shown honor and dedication.$B$BWhen our campaign in Desolace is done, the Warchief will know that you aided us in our actions here, and that you helped make his will manifest.$B$BI thank you.\030A demon infestation does not occur without other influences--something else allows evil to gain a foothold.$B$BIt may start with a weakened spirit, a needless desire for power; perhaps it's a thirst for revenge, or the appeal for final justice. When we are beset by pain, evil takes advantage of us--evil such as the satyr.$B$BTies have been made between them and the Burning Blade, and Thrall would have them slain. Seek them out to the northeast of here, and return to me when you've driven them back.\030Slay 7 Hatefury Rogues, 7 Hatefury Felsworn, 7 Hatefury Betrayers, and 7 Hatefury Hellcallers, and return to Takata Steelblade in Desolace.\030I was warned by a tauren companion that the satyr are not all they appear to be. He believes there is something more to them, that their evil is a twisting of their true nature. But I have not seen such things.$B$BI see only the ruthless slaughter of the weak and the corruption of those who seek dark power.$B$BI will continue in my duty of annihilating them until the Warchief directs me otherwise. Until then, I take no pity on them.\030Befouled by Satyr\0312,1,107,2,257,1,5641\0302,112,244,2,259,4,5641\0302,246,323,2,257,1,5641\0302,328,416,2,261,4,5641\0302,418,503,2,257,1,5641\0303,1,139,2,384,1,5641\0301,1,23,4,272,1,5641\0301,25,60,4,272,1,5641\0301,65,208,4,272,3,5641\0301,213,224,4,272,1,5641\0304,1,80,3,256,1,5641\0304,82,177,3,256,1,5641\0304,179,210,3,256,1,5641\0304,215,308,3,262,1,5641\0304,313,400,3,264,3,5641\0304,402,436,3,256,1,5641\0314949,2,4,Thrall\0304672,2,6,Hatefury Felsworn\0305641,2,6,Takata Steelblade\0312,1637,1454,0,\0302,0,0,6,Takata Steelblade\0302,0,0,6,Desolace\0304,0,0,9,Desolace\031\031NPC,4670,OBJECTIVE,7,13,Hatefury Rogue\030NPC,4672,OBJECTIVE,7,13,Hatefury Felsworn\030NPC,4673,OBJECTIVE,7,13,Hatefury Betrayer\030NPC,4675,OBJECTIVE,7,13,Hatefury Hellcaller",[1435]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, you've returned successful. That is good. Give me the gems and I shall put them someplace safe....$B$BMy tasks for you are complete, $C. Speak to Takata when you are rested. He may have other tasks for you, or perhaps needs you to return to Orgrimmar to inform Keldran of our progress here in Desolace.\030Death is most desirable for those despicable creatures that turn their back on their liege for such selfish reasons. But death is not enough when dealing with those that have given themselves over to the darkness.$B$BTake this gem. When one of the Burning Blade's near death, activate its magic. The spell shall pull the corrupted spirit out of its victim, leaving an infused gem behind.$B$BBring me these infused gems so I may dispose of them properly.$B$BGo now, and may you elude death.\030Return the Burning Gem and 15 Infused Burning Gems to Maurin Bonesplitter in Desolace.\030I have tried to make the magics as simple as possible. Drawing the spirit of your victim out of its injured form should be child's play. Do not rely on the gem's power to slay your foe completely. You must only activate the gem when they are close to death, or it will be useless.\030The Burning of Spirits\0312,1,116,2,257,1,4498\0302,118,213,2,257,1,4498\0302,218,231,2,257,1,4498\0302,233,295,2,257,1,4498\0302,297,387,2,261,3,4498\0302,392,453,2,257,1,4498\0302,458,489,2,257,1,4498\0303,1,86,2,384,1,4498\0301,1,31,4,272,1,4498\0301,33,45,4,272,1,4498\0301,47,102,4,272,3,4498\0301,107,140,4,272,1,4498\0301,142,177,4,272,1,4498\0301,179,306,4,274,4,4498\0304,1,54,3,256,1,4498\0304,56,136,3,256,1,4498\0304,138,196,3,256,1,4498\0304,198,280,3,256,3,4498\03114512,2,5,Corrupted Spirit\0304498,2,8,Maurin Bonesplitter\0305640,4,14,Keldran\0312,1637,1454,0,\0302,0,0,8,Maurin Bonesplitter\0302,0,0,8,Desolace\0304,0,0,13,Takata\0304,0,0,14,Orgrimmar\0304,0,0,14,Desolace\0311433,19,1433,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301436,23,1436,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6435,OBJECTIVE,15,15,",[1436]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have returned from Desolace more than successful, $N. Thank you.$B$BThank you for your efforts, your time, and your understanding to my plea. Thrall understands and desires peace between the Horde and Alliance, and by taking measures to insure our appearance is acceptable, we will not provoke any further threats of unnecessary violence.$B$BI am indebted to you.\030The fight goes well, $N. Perhaps the Warchief will allow us to return to our homes before the seasons change if we continue to make such great strides in our battle against the demons and their underlings.$B$BReturn to Keldran and let him know what we have done. I am sure he will reward you for your efforts here. His cause is important to him, and he will take pride in knowing that the Warchief respects his concerns.\030Speak to Keldran in Orgrimmar.\030\030Alliance Relations\0312,1,24,2,261,1,5641\0302,26,205,2,261,4,5641\0302,210,262,2,257,1,5641\0302,264,314,2,257,3,5641\0302,316,420,2,257,3,5641\0303,1,30,2,384,1,5641\0301,1,57,4,272,1,5640\0301,59,68,4,272,1,5640\0301,73,145,4,272,1,5640\0301,147,342,4,282,3,5640\0301,347,367,4,272,1,5640\0315640,2,3,Keldran\0305640,2,6,Keldran\0304949,4,10,Thrall\0312,1637,1454,0,\0302,0,0,3,Keldran\0302,0,0,6,Keldran\0302,0,0,6,Orgrimmar\0304,0,0,7,Desolace\0311435,19,1435,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1437]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031As you rummage around the remains of the wagon, it becomes obvious that it was attacked by both spells and weapons. The battle seemed one-sided and quick; there's no blood to be found, and no remains of any bodies.$B$BWhoever attacked the wagon was efficient and swift.\030I am Vahlarriel, $N. I've come here to discover the whereabouts of two missing nobles of a Darnassian merchant family--House Malem. The father of the house fears the worst, and I am to do everything I can to find his missing children. I have yet to start my search for Tyranis or Dalinda, but I am hopeful I shall not be here long.$B$BLast word tells of them passing through the Stonetalon Mountains a few weeks ago.$B$BIf you find their wagon, please, come find me immediately.\030Find and search Tyranis and Dalinda Malem's wagon in Desolace.\030\030Vahlarriel's Search\0312,1,20,2,257,1,5642\0302,22,131,2,261,1,5642\0302,133,234,2,261,1,5642\0302,236,331,2,257,3,5642\0302,336,416,2,257,1,5642\0302,421,478,2,257,4,5642\0303,1,62,2,384,1,5642\0301,1,115,4,276,1,0\0301,117,214,4,276,1,0\0301,219,269,4,276,1,0\0315644,2,7,Dalinda Malem\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,7,Desolace\0311465,23,1465,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,50961,FINISHER,?,12,Malem Chest",[1438]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank Elune someone has finally come to help. Please, $C, I need your help. My brother Tyranis and I were captured and brought here by the Burning Blade. I think they mean to sacrifice me to their demon masters!$B$BI knew coming to Desolace was a mistake, but Tyranis has recently begun craving knowledge of all things arcane--even against the wishes of our people. He decided to make this trek even after hearing tales of this land's demon infestation.$B$BI fear the worst for him.\030Find both Dalinda and Tyranis if you can and come back to me with your findings. Start your search at this fortress. I will contact my superiors in Darnassus immediately and let them know the situation.$B$B$N, there is something else I wish to impress upon you. My superiors have shown some concern over Tyranis' and his motives for coming here. It is more important to them that Dalinda is found and brought back safely. Tyranis is to be... gauged before he is taken home.\030Find Dalinda Malem in Desolace.\030\030Vahlarriel's Search\0312,1,80,2,257,4,5642\0302,82,116,2,257,1,5642\0302,118,202,2,257,3,5642\0302,207,261,2,259,3,5642\0302,263,345,2,257,1,5642\0302,347,421,2,257,1,5642\0302,423,441,2,257,1,5642\0302,443,473,2,265,1,5642\0303,1,31,2,384,1,5642\0301,1,45,4,272,1,5644\0301,47,75,4,274,1,5644\0301,77,153,4,272,1,5644\0301,155,211,4,272,1,5644\0301,216,365,4,274,1,5644\0301,367,453,4,272,1,5644\0301,458,482,4,272,1,5644\0315644,2,9,Dalinda Malem\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,3,Darnassus\0302,0,0,9,Desolace\0304,0,0,14,Desolace\0311465,19,1465,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301439,23,1439,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1439]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is terrible! But I suppose it was necessary. If it wasn't by your hand, it would have surely been by that of my people's. I suppose I should thank you--please forgive me if it doesn't seem sincere. I mean no offense.$B$BWith the knowledge of my brother's fate in hand, it seems the time for my escape has come. If you are still willing, I will accept your aid in escaping this horrible place.$B$BWhen you are ready, we can make our way to safety.\030We were brought here after the orcs slaughtered all our guards and servants. Oh, the terrible things they did to them! I thought surely they would kill us right there and then, but it became obvious they had other plans.$B$BTyranis attempted to speak to them. I think he wanted to impress them with his knowledge of the arcane... I'm not sure why.$B$BPlease, I can't leave here until I know what's happened to my brother. Find him, then come back for me when his fate is known.\030Find Tyranis Malem in Desolace.\030I fear Tyranis will attempt to learn the Burning Blade's secrets and count himself among their kind if they allow it - he has always adored the power magic brings to those who are seduced by it.$B$BI'm not sure I could endure returning home to my family with news of Tyranis' spirit flirting with such dangers. It's a terrible enough crime among my kind to pursue such things, but to become that which we attempt to protect ourselves from, well, that's apprehensible.\030Search for Tyranis\0312,1,76,2,257,1,5644\0302,78,118,2,257,1,5644\0302,120,220,2,257,4,5644\0302,225,259,2,257,1,5644\0302,261,329,2,257,1,5644\0302,331,347,2,257,1,5644\0302,352,421,2,257,1,5644\0302,423,477,2,257,1,5644\0303,1,31,2,384,1,5644\0301,1,17,4,272,1,5644\0301,19,49,4,272,1,5644\0301,51,126,4,272,4,5644\0301,128,202,4,272,4,5644\0301,204,221,4,272,1,5644\0301,226,315,4,272,4,5644\0301,317,397,4,272,4,5644\0301,402,451,4,280,1,5644\0304,1,194,3,256,4,5644\0304,199,310,3,256,4,5644\0304,312,467,3,270,1,5644\0315643,2,9,Tyranis Malem\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,9,Desolace\0311438,19,1438,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301440,23,1440,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6767,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[144]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I do say, this is not good at all. I did not realize that Stoutmantle's situation was not unlike ours here in Lakeshire. What action is so important that it calls the Stormwind Army away from its people? Bah, I should not ponder aloud.$B$BHere, messenger. Accept these coins in exchange for your service to the Township. I might call upon you again.\030Magistrate Solomon's note pains me to read.  But it is obvious he knows not the war which is waged in Westfall or else he would know better than to expect aid from the Militia.  If Stormwind had not deserted us as well, we would not have the need for the Militia.$B$BTake this response to your master in Redridge, $c.  And let him know that my heart is heavy with the loss of good men.\030Return to Magistrate Solomon with Gryan Stoutmantle's response.\030Shall we expect the People's Militia soon? Does Lord Stoutmantle's news bode well?\030Messenger to Westfall\0312,1,43,2,257,1,234\0302,46,176,2,261,4,234\0302,179,263,2,259,4,234\0302,268,317,2,257,1,234\0302,320,385,2,257,1,234\0303,1,63,2,384,1,234\0301,1,34,4,272,1,344\0301,36,120,4,272,1,344\0301,122,203,4,272,2,344\0301,205,235,4,272,1,344\0301,240,255,4,272,1,344\0301,257,320,4,272,1,344\0301,322,349,4,272,4,344\0304,1,42,3,256,2,344\0304,44,82,3,256,2,344\031344,2,1,Magistrate Solomon\030344,2,6,Magistrate Solomon\030798,2,6,Solomon\030234,2,6,Gryan Stoutmantle\0312,44,1433,0,\0302,0,0,2,Westfall\0302,0,0,2,Militia\0302,0,0,4,Redridge\0302,0,0,6,Magistrate Solomon\0304,0,0,8,Lakeshire\0304,0,0,12,Township\031143,19,143,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030145,23,145,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1440]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, $N. Dalinda made it safely back here to Nijel's Point, and in much better condition than I could have asked for. The fact that she arrived here under her own power was a good sign. I hope you're well?$B$BIt pains me to know that both Tyranis and Dalinda didn't return, but the embarrassment of Tyranis' decisions is hers to endure. It is something she will have to deal with when she returns to Darnassus.\030So, the time is now then? I appreciate your efforts, and if the situation does not lend itself, then allow me to thank you now for everything you've done for me and my family. If you're ready, then there is nothing else for me here--we can leave when you feel the time is right.\030Escort Dalinda Malem from Thunder Axe Fortress and then return to Vahlarriel Demonslayer in Desolace.\030Rescue Dalinda Malem\030\030Return to Vahlarriel\0312,1,25,2,257,2,5644\0302,27,175,2,257,4,5644\0302,177,278,2,257,4,5644\0303,1,101,2,384,1,5644\0301,1,14,4,272,1,5642\0301,16,123,4,272,4,5642\0301,125,191,4,272,1,5642\0301,193,211,4,274,2,5642\0301,216,342,4,272,1,5642\0301,344,416,4,272,3,5642\0304,1,20,3,392,1,5644\0315644,2,4,Dalinda Malem\0305642,2,4,Vahlarriel Demonslayer\0305644,3,11,Dalinda Malem\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,4,Thunder Axe Fortress\0302,0,0,4,Vahlarriel Demonslayer\0302,0,0,4,Desolace\0304,0,0,6,Nijel's Point\0304,0,0,10,Darnassus\0311439,19,1439,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1442]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is indeed the gem Stilwell desires, but before I can allow you to bring it to him, it must be purified of corruption--the naga wenches imbue the gems with power, that much is true, but of their own, evil kind.$B$BLet Stilwell know that its power is intact, and it should work well for whatever ritual he wishes it to be part of.$B$BI hope you know what you're doing, $C, this is no simple item you possess.\030Greetings, $N. What can I do for one who follows a holy path?$B$BAh, yes, Stilwell, the blacksmith... from long ago. I remember him well, though, I have not heard his name in some time.$B$BHe never struck me as an impudent man, so I can only assume his desire for a Kor gem is noble.$B$BIf you truly wish for one of the gems, then you must head to the northwest of Ashenvale. You will find Blackfathom Deeps there within some ancient ruins. The naga who still use the gems are down below. Do not go alone, $c.\030Bring a Kor Gem to Thundris Windweaver in Darkshore.\030I would be less trustful of one not on a holy path if they came asking about a Kor gem. But I trust your kind more than some of my kin. I do not judge your entire order based on the actions of just one of your fallen kind.\030Seeking the Kor Gem\0312,1,14,2,257,1,3649\0302,16,61,2,257,2,3649\0302,66,101,2,257,1,3649\0302,103,116,2,321,1,3649\0302,118,185,2,257,1,3649\0302,190,283,2,259,4,3649\0302,288,375,2,259,4,3649\0302,377,440,2,321,3,3649\0302,442,488,2,257,1,3649\0302,490,509,2,257,1,3649\0303,1,52,2,384,1,3649\0301,1,214,4,278,1,3649\0301,219,333,4,274,1,3649\0301,338,411,4,274,3,3649\0304,1,87,3,256,4,3649\0304,89,135,3,256,1,3649\0304,137,222,3,256,1,3649\0313649,2,11,Thundris Windweaver\0312,0,0,11,Thundris Windweaver\0302,0,0,11,Darkshore\0311654,20,1654,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6995,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1444]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It has been quite some time since we spoke, $C. I hope your journey was successful.$B$BWhat knowledge did you gain from the exiled Atal'ai in the Hinterlands?\030Jammal'an the Prophet sentenced me to exile from The Temple of Atal'Hakkar. I once felt the high priest was a worthy leader.$B$BHis unyielding faith in his prophecy will bring about the destruction of the Atal'ai. If it hasn't already.$B$BWhen I expressed my concerns, I was labeled an infidel and ousted from the temple.$B$BThose artifacts you brought to me are harmless. But if Jammal'an has found the proper fetish enchantment for the summoning ritual, the world lies in great peril....\030Return to Fel'Zerul in Stonard.\030\030Return to Fel'Zerul\0312,1,75,2,257,1,5598\0302,77,124,2,257,1,5598\0302,129,213,2,257,3,5598\0302,215,235,2,257,4,5598\0302,240,321,2,257,1,5598\0302,326,372,2,257,1,5598\0302,374,489,2,257,4,5598\0303,1,31,2,384,1,5598\0301,1,47,4,272,1,1443\0301,49,83,4,274,3,1443\0301,88,158,4,272,2,1443\0315710,2,1,Jammal'an the Prophet\030111,2,2,Priest\0301443,2,8,Fel'zerul\0312,47,1425,0,\0302,0,0,1,The Temple of Atal'Hakkar\0302,0,0,8,Fel'Zerul\0302,0,0,8,Stonard\0304,0,0,11,Hinterlands\0311429,19,1429,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301445,23,1445,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1445]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Brave $C, you have proven yourself to be a great champion of the Horde.$B$BNow this collection of fetishes of Hakkar must be dealt with at once!\030So he spoke of Jammal'an's prophecy?$B$BThe Atal'ai spiritual leader believes once Hakkar returns to Azeroth from the Nether, the god will grant the Atal'ai tribe immortality.$B$BFoolish trickery to bring about a premature doomsday if you ask me.$B$BBut you say the exile spoke of enchanted fetishes? This concerns me greatly. If these are in fact the key to the Atal'ai ritual which caused this mess, we must understand their intrinsic powers.$B$BVenture into the Temple, and seize the fetishes!\030Collect 20 Fetishes of Hakkar and bring them to Fel'Zerul in Stonard.\030If the Atal'ai fetishes hold the power to summon Hakkar and fulfill Jammal'an's prophecy they must be seized. Such powers must be understood by the Horde!\030The Temple of Atal'Hakkar\0312,1,36,2,257,2,1443\0302,41,175,2,257,3,1443\0302,180,246,2,257,4,1443\0302,251,300,2,257,2,1443\0302,302,326,2,257,1,1443\0302,328,444,2,257,4,1443\0302,449,496,2,257,1,1443\0303,1,69,2,384,1,1443\0301,1,71,4,272,1,1443\0301,76,144,4,272,1,1443\0304,1,109,3,256,4,1443\0304,111,154,3,256,1,1443\03114834,2,2,Hakkar\03014834,2,8,Hakkar\0301443,2,8,Fel'zerul\03014834,4,10,Hakkar\03014834,3,11,Hakkar\0312,1417,0,0,\0302,0,0,2,Azeroth\0302,0,0,2,Nether\0302,0,0,6,Atal'ai\0302,0,0,8,Fel'Zerul\0302,0,0,8,Stonard\0311444,19,1444,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6181,OBJECTIVE,20,15,",[1446]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Jammal'an's reckless trust of false visions led my people to their eternal doom.$B$BI thank you, $C, for avenging my exile. I mourn for my people. I have no home to return to.\030My Witherbark companions don't take kindly to strangers around their home.$B$BMe? I don't have a home anymore. I was exiled from my people, the great Atal'ai tribe of the Swamp of Sorrows.$B$BOur spiritual leader, Jammal'an, had what he called a prophecy. He believes the summoning of the god, Hakkar will bring the Atal'ai immortality.$B$BBut I urged caution. What if the prophecy was nothing more than manipulation?$B$BI want revenge for my exile. Bring me Jammal'an's head. Maybe then my people will be free.\030The Atal'ai Exile in The Hinterlands wants the Head of Jammal'an.\030Once Jammal'an has been removed, I stand a chance of returning to my people.$B$BWith Jammal'an as their spiritual leader, the Atal'ai face certain destruction.\030Jammal'an the Prophet\0312,1,74,2,257,1,5598\0302,83,110,2,257,1,5598\0302,112,188,2,257,1,5598\0302,193,255,2,257,1,5598\0302,257,336,2,257,3,5598\0302,341,360,2,257,1,5598\0302,362,417,2,257,4,5598\0302,422,449,2,259,1,5598\0302,451,476,2,257,1,5598\0302,478,511,2,257,4,5598\0303,1,65,2,386,1,5598\0301,1,80,4,272,1,5598\0301,85,123,4,272,1,5598\0301,125,146,4,272,1,5598\0301,148,175,4,272,1,5598\0304,1,76,3,256,1,5598\0304,81,159,3,256,1,5598\03114834,2,5,Hakkar\0305598,2,11,Atal'ai Exile\0312,1417,0,0,\0302,0,0,11,The Hinterlands\031\031ITEM,6212,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1447]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031So, you came to me for a reason. What is it you need?\030Yeah, you're obviously not the smartest $c to come into Stormwind, but you're about to be one of the dumbest to never leave.$b$bHave you met me friends?\030Defeat Dashel Stonefist in Stormwind.\030Defeat Dashel Stonefist\030I didn't mean anything by the comment 'bout you being a stupid $C. We're friends, right? No hard feelings?\030The Missing Diplomat\0312,1,124,2,257,1,4961\0302,129,152,2,257,2,4961\0303,1,37,2,384,1,4961\0301,1,32,4,272,1,4961\0301,34,53,4,274,2,4961\0305,1,66,3,256,1,4961\0305,68,88,3,256,2,4961\0305,90,106,3,256,2,4961\0304,1,23,3,384,1,4961\0314961,2,3,Dashel Stonefist\0304961,3,9,Dashel Stonefist\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,3,Stormwind\0311246,19,1246,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301247,23,1247,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1448]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031The Temple of Atal'Hakkar has been sunk beneath the Pool of Tears? And surrounded by the green dragonflight?$B$BAn amazing discovery, $C. But obviously something has gone terribly wrong.\030There was a time when I was young and full of vigor like you, $c.$B$BBut now I'm old and unable to explore the world like I once did. Ah, the things I saw!$B$BBut there was one mystery that eluded me. For my final quest, the Explorers' League sent me in search of The Temple of Atal'Hakkar. It was rumored to be located in the Swamp of Sorrows.$B$BBecause of my frail state, I traveled the skies by gryphon in search of it but never found it.$B$BHelp an old dwarf out? Perhaps you will have better luck on foot.\030Brohann Caskbelly in Stormwind wants you to search for the Temple of Atal'Hakkar.\030Search for the Temple of Atal'Hakkar\030I have traveled the world from the jungles of Azeroth to the snowy peaks of Khaz Modan.$B$BNever before have I asked for help in my adventures. But my old bones are tired.$B$BNothing would leave me feeling more satisfied than knowing that I completed my final quest for the Explorers' League$B$BIf you'd be so kind as to help me search for the Temple of Atal'Hakkar, $C, I'd greatly appreciate it.$B$BScour the Swamp of Sorrows and report back with your findings!\030In Search of The Temple\0312,1,65,2,257,1,5384\0302,70,133,2,257,1,5384\0302,135,155,2,257,1,5384\0302,160,200,2,257,1,5384\0302,202,290,2,257,1,5384\0302,292,344,2,257,1,5384\0302,349,442,2,259,1,5384\0302,447,468,2,257,2,5384\0302,470,511,2,257,4,5384\0303,1,81,2,386,1,5384\0301,1,66,4,272,2,5384\0301,68,108,4,272,2,5384\0301,113,137,4,272,1,5384\0301,139,186,4,272,1,5384\0305,1,87,3,256,1,5384\0305,92,143,3,256,1,5384\0305,145,171,3,256,1,5384\0305,176,291,3,256,4,5384\0305,296,397,3,256,4,5384\0305,402,463,3,256,1,5384\0304,1,36,3,384,1,5384\0315384,2,10,Brohann Caskbelly\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,6,Swamp of Sorrows\0302,0,0,10,Stormwind\0311449,23,1449,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1449]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031What do you want, $gladdy:missy;? Can't you see I've got problems to take care of here? Who has time to stand around yapping with some $R chatterbox?$b$bThere are trolls coming out of the woodwork! Make it snappy.\030As I mentioned earlier, I attempted to scout the temple on my own from the air. Well, I wasn't exactly alone.$B$BI traveled to the renowned gryphon aviary at Aerie Peak in The Hinterlands. There I enlisted the aid of one of their finest pilots. The pilot fell off his mount, down into the swamp...$B$BIn my old age the poor fellow's name eludes me. The master of the aviary would remember, no doubt.$B$BJourney there and seek out Falstad Wildhammer.$B$BWe need to find out what happened to that pilot.\030Speak with High Thane Falstad Wildhammer at Aerie Peak in the Hinterlands.\030\030To The Hinterlands\0312,1,79,2,257,1,5384\0302,81,109,2,257,1,5384\0302,114,188,2,257,1,5384\0302,190,244,2,257,1,5384\0302,246,297,2,257,1,5384\0302,302,348,2,257,1,5384\0302,350,399,2,257,4,5384\0302,404,449,2,259,1,5384\0302,454,501,2,259,1,5384\0303,1,74,2,384,1,5384\0301,1,33,4,274,2,5635\0301,35,87,4,272,2,5635\0301,89,149,4,272,2,5635\0301,154,197,4,272,1,5635\0301,199,213,4,272,1,5635\0315635,2,8,Falstad Wildhammer\0305635,2,10,Falstad Wildhammer\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,3,Aerie Peak\0302,0,0,3,The Hinterlands\0302,0,0,10,Aerie Peak\0302,0,0,10,Hinterlands\0311448,19,1448,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301450,23,1450,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[145]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you for making the long journey here. This is indeed important information.\030I require your assistance once again.  I have written to Lord Ebonlocke, requesting that he sends his trained guards, the Night Watch, to help with Lakeshire's defense.  It is imperative this message makes it to him swiftly.  You must exercise extreme caution.  Ebonlocke is the mayor of Darkshire, in the heart of Duskwood.  Do not stray from the roads.\030Magistrate Solomon wants you to take a letter to Lord Ebonlocke in Darkshire.\030You appear to have traveled from afar, $C. What business do you have here in Darkshire?\030Messenger to Darkshire\0312,1,37,2,257,1,344\0302,40,168,2,257,1,344\0302,171,224,2,257,1,344\0302,227,260,2,257,1,344\0302,263,324,2,257,1,344\0302,327,354,2,257,1,344\0303,1,77,2,386,1,344\0301,1,43,4,272,1,263\0301,45,81,4,272,1,263\0304,1,42,3,256,1,263\0304,44,87,3,256,2,263\031344,2,7,Magistrate Solomon\030798,2,7,Solomon\0312,44,1433,0,\0302,0,0,2,Lord Ebonlocke\0302,0,0,7,Lord Ebonlocke\0302,0,0,7,Darkshire\0303,0,0,11,Darkshire\031144,19,144,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030146,23,146,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1450]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, yes. Of course I remember sending one of my gryphon riders to lend a hand to Brohann Caskbelly.$B$BAlways had a soft spot in my heart for the Explorers' League. My father helped with the initial excavation team that discovered Uldaman as a matter of fact.$B$BI sent who I thought was my best gryphon rider at the time with Brohann. He was a chap by the name of Rhapsody Shindigger.$B$BAnd what a gryphon jockey he was! Well until...\030So you're a glorified errand $g boy:girl; for some old Explorers' League geezer, eh?$B$BWell you listen to me, $c. I don't know who your old buddy was flying around with down in Azeroth. Do I look like Gryphon Master Talonaxe to you? Do I?$B$BIf you're so interested in the flight assignments why don't you ask the gryphon master? If I catch you idling around here for much longer, I'm going to put you to some real work.$B$BNow get a move on.\030Speak with Gryphon Master Talonaxe inside the Aerie Peak Aviary.\030\030Gryphon Master Talonaxe\0312,1,84,2,257,2,5635\0302,89,114,2,257,1,5635\0302,116,186,2,257,1,5635\0302,188,233,2,257,2,5635\0302,244,330,2,257,4,5635\0302,332,421,2,257,4,5635\0302,426,443,2,257,1,5635\0303,1,64,2,384,1,5635\0301,1,8,4,272,1,5636\0301,10,99,4,272,1,5636\0301,104,164,4,272,1,5636\0301,166,259,4,272,1,5636\0301,264,335,4,272,1,5636\0301,337,385,4,272,1,5636\0301,390,422,4,272,1,5636\0301,424,436,4,272,1,5636\031371,2,1,Girl\0305636,2,4,Gryphon Master Talonaxe\0305636,2,8,Gryphon Master Talonaxe\0305384,4,10,Brohann Caskbelly\0304950,4,11,Spot\0305634,4,14,Rhapsody Shindigger\0312,47,1425,0,\0302,0,0,3,Azeroth\0304,0,0,10,Brohann Caskbelly\0311449,19,1449,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301451,23,1451,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1451]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hiccup!$B$BI'm a-lookin' right at you but you keep bobbing up and down. Makin' me dizzy. Hoho!$B$BHiccup!$B$BWhoa! Did ya feel that? Ground is a-shakin', my friend. I need a drink.$B$BHiccup!\030Rhapsody took quite a liking to the booze. Now don't get me wrong -- all of us dwarves up here at the aviary love a good ale when the time is right.$B$BBut ol' Shindigger took to the liquor like a gryphon takes to the skies. And a damned shame it was, too. No one could fly like Rhapsody.$B$BFirst sign of trouble was when he came stumbling back from that mission with your buddy, Brohann. All went down hill quickly after that. Had to let him go.$B$BLast I heard, he's set up a brew camp to the east of here...\030Seek out Rhapsody Shindigger in The Hinterlands.\030\030Rhapsody Shindigger\0312,1,42,2,257,1,5636\0302,44,148,2,257,1,5636\0302,153,224,2,257,1,5636\0302,226,256,2,257,1,5636\0302,258,288,2,257,4,5636\0302,293,389,2,257,1,5636\0302,391,428,2,257,1,5636\0302,430,447,2,257,1,5636\0302,452,511,2,257,1,5636\0303,1,48,2,384,1,5636\0301,1,7,4,272,1,5634\0301,12,71,4,272,1,5634\0301,73,88,4,272,1,5634\0301,90,94,4,272,1,5634\0301,99,105,4,272,1,5634\0301,110,114,4,272,1,5634\0301,116,132,4,272,2,5634\0301,134,164,4,272,1,5634\0301,166,180,4,274,1,5634\0301,185,191,4,272,1,5634\0315634,2,10,Rhapsody Shindigger\0312,47,1425,0,\0302,0,0,10,The Hinterlands\0311450,19,1450,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301452,23,1452,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1452]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I see ya had no trouble at all getting me what I need! Musta been quite a stint you had over there in far-off Kalimdor.$B$BIt won't take but a moment for me to extract what I need from these gizzards and livers. Hiccup!$B$BThen I can distill me a fierce ol' drink and finally tell ya what ya wanna know.$B$BHiccup!$B$BGetting shivers just thinking about that ol' swamp.$B$BHiccup!$B$BLemme whip up a drink real fast.\030Hiccup!$B$BSo that crazy fool Brohann sent ya? My we had quite an adventure...Hiccup!$B$BIf ya want me to tell ya what happened down in the swamp, I'm gonna need me something stiff to drink. It wasn't a pretty scene, ya see. Hiccup!$B$BTell ya what... bring me what I need to whip up a Kalimdor Kocktail and I'll tell ya all about it.$B$BGonna need some Roc gizzards from Tanaris... and let's see... some Groddoc and Ironfur livers from Feralas...$B$BA nice stiff Kalimdor Kocktail... that'll get me talking!\030Rhapsody Shindigger in The Hinterlands wants you to bring him 3 Roc Gizzards, 3 Groddoc Livers and 3 Ironfur Livers.\030Ya ever had a Rhapsody Malt? One of my finest brews, if I do say so myself. Hiccup!$B$BBut if I'm gonna relive the horrors of that fateful flight over... hiccup... the swamp, well I'm gonna need me something a wee bit stronger. Hiccup!$B$BDon't suppose you found me those gizzards and livers I need to add that extra kick to my Kalimdor Kocktail?$B$BHiccup!\030Rhapsody's Kalimdor Kocktail\0312,1,7,2,257,1,5634\0302,12,46,2,259,2,5634\0302,48,85,2,257,1,5634\0302,90,190,2,259,4,5634\0302,192,224,2,257,1,5634\0302,226,232,2,257,1,5634\0302,237,251,2,257,1,5634\0302,253,334,2,259,1,5634\0302,339,382,2,259,1,5634\0302,384,399,2,257,1,5634\0302,401,447,2,257,1,5634\0302,452,484,2,257,1,5634\0302,486,508,2,257,1,5634\0303,1,116,2,386,1,5634\0301,1,54,4,274,1,5634\0301,56,119,4,272,1,5634\0301,124,211,4,274,1,5634\0301,213,219,4,272,1,5634\0301,224,303,4,272,1,5634\0301,308,314,4,272,1,5634\0301,319,369,4,272,1,5634\0301,374,380,4,272,1,5634\0301,385,416,4,272,1,5634\0304,1,28,3,256,2,5634\0304,30,75,3,256,4,5634\0304,77,83,3,256,1,5634\0304,88,153,3,256,4,5634\0304,155,163,3,256,1,5634\0304,165,227,3,258,1,5634\0304,229,235,3,256,1,5634\0304,240,346,3,258,2,5634\0304,351,357,3,256,1,5634\0315634,2,14,Rhapsody Shindigger\0312,47,1425,0,\0302,0,0,9,Tanaris\0302,0,0,11,Feralas\0302,0,0,14,The Hinterlands\0311451,19,1451,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301469,23,1469,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6257,OBJECTIVE,3,15,\030ITEM,6258,OBJECTIVE,3,15,\030ITEM,6259,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[1453]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Glad to see the Reclaimers aren't in short supply of work, or adventurers willing to help out.$B$BI'm Kreldig, $N. You've made a smart move helpin' out the Reclaimers. Everyone needs something these days: they've lost a family heirloom, a magic item, a loved one. You never can tell. But with the Reclaimers around, there's no reason, for the right price, everyone can't find what they've lost.\030There's work to be done in Desolace, $N. It's an atrocious place, befouled by centaur and other nasties. But if you're looking for a good week's honest work, then head there, meet with Kreldig Ungor, and tell him I sentcha.$B$BYou can find him holed up at Nijel's Point--it's a little cozy camp hidden in the mountains of northern Desolace. Just head east if you enter from the Stonetalon Mountains. It's easy to miss, so be on the lookout.\030Speak to Kreldig Ungor in Desolace.\030\030Reclaimers' Business in Desolace\0312,1,40,2,257,1,5637\0302,42,104,2,257,1,5637\0302,106,223,2,257,4,5637\0302,228,340,2,257,1,5637\0302,342,399,2,257,4,5637\0302,401,440,2,257,1,5637\0303,1,35,2,384,1,5637\0301,1,94,4,272,1,5638\0301,99,114,4,272,1,5638\0301,116,167,4,272,1,5638\0301,169,263,4,278,1,5638\0301,265,283,4,272,1,5638\0301,285,394,4,276,1,5638\03193,2,2,Centaur\0305638,2,3,Kreldig Ungor\0305638,2,7,Kreldig Ungor\0312,1537,1455,0,\0302,0,0,1,Desolace\0302,0,0,4,Nijel's Point--it's\0302,0,0,5,Stonetalon Mountains\0302,0,0,7,Kreldig Ungor\0302,0,0,7,Desolace\031\031",[1454]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You notice the chest does not seem to have any water damage.$B$BThe second thing you notice is that the top has been forced open, and whatever magical traps were set to safeguard it have long been triggered--this much is obvious from the burn marks around its edges.\030My first order of business is for the mage Karnitol--a noble of some sort in Stormwind. Seems his ship was attacked by sea giants while off the coast in the northwest of Desolace. He and his servants tried to bring one of his more valuable chests ashore, but when the sea giants attacked in droves, he chose to abandon it and teleport himself and his servants to safety.$B$BHe wants us to find the chest and its contents, and return it to him in Stormwind.\030Find Karnitol's Chest in Desolace.\030\030The Karnitol Shipwreck\0312,1,87,2,257,1,5638\0302,89,179,2,261,4,5638\0302,181,370,2,269,1,5638\0302,375,456,2,259,1,5638\0303,1,34,2,384,1,5638\0301,1,60,4,272,4,0\0301,65,266,4,272,1,0\031\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,1,Stormwind\0302,0,0,4,Stormwind\0302,0,0,5,Desolace\0311453,19,1453,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301455,23,1455,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,35251,FINISHER,?,12,Karnitol's Chest",[1455]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Welcome back to Nijel's Point, $N. So, tell me what you found.$B$BWhat!? Nothing? An empty chest ain't gonna get us paid, I'm afraid.$B$BTell me more about these marks you saw... these slashes.\030You take a few moments to figure out what pried the chest open, and you notice along the sides and top of the chest, long, deep scratches that reveal that something other than a man or giant took interest in it. The marks don't appear as if they were caused by dagger or sword.$B$BAfter going through the chest you find it to be completely empty.$B$BNot having another course of action, you close the chest and prepare to leave. Kreldig will be disappointed.\030Return to Kreldig Ungor in Desolace.\030\030The Karnitol Shipwreck\0312,1,211,2,257,1,0\0302,213,277,2,257,4,0\0302,282,346,2,257,1,0\0302,351,428,2,257,1,0\0302,430,458,2,257,3,0\0303,1,36,2,384,1,0\0301,1,34,4,272,1,5638\0301,36,62,4,272,1,5638\0301,67,72,4,272,2,5638\0301,74,81,4,272,2,5638\0301,83,133,4,272,1,5638\0301,138,178,4,272,1,5638\0301,180,193,4,272,1,5638\0315638,2,6,Kreldig Ungor\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,6,Kreldig Ungor\0302,0,0,6,Desolace\0304,0,0,7,Nijel's Point\0311454,19,1454,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301456,23,1456,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,35251,GIVER,?,9,Karnitol's Chest",[1456]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is great, $N! You found Karnitol's belongings!$B$BThose blasted naga, always causing trouble. I think I'd rather spend my life at war with the Horde than have to go against their kind. You've done a great service to the Reclaimers.\030Intriguing.$B$BWell, we might not be without hope quite yet.$B$BAlong that same coast, but to the north near Ranazjar Isle, there're night elf ruins at the bottom of the ocean. A tribe of naga, the Slitherblade, make that their home. I think that'd be our best bet.$B$BIf a scouting party went that far south, then they must've been pretty powerful. If you're gonna find Karnitol's belongings, I'd start with the more powerful naga: the tidehunters or sea witches.\030Find Karnitol's Satchel and return it to Kreldig Ungor in Desolace.\030No offense to whoever Nijel is, but this camp ain't the most comfortable place I've spent a night, if you know what I mean, $N.\030The Karnitol Shipwreck\0312,1,11,2,257,1,5638\0302,16,60,2,259,4,5638\0302,65,176,2,321,1,5638\0302,178,233,2,257,1,5638\0302,235,265,2,257,1,5638\0302,270,349,2,257,4,5638\0302,351,464,2,257,4,5638\0303,1,67,2,384,1,5638\0301,1,18,4,272,1,5638\0301,20,51,4,272,1,5638\0301,56,98,4,272,1,5638\0301,100,189,4,276,1,5638\0301,191,236,4,272,1,5638\0304,1,127,3,256,4,5638\0315638,2,8,Kreldig Ungor\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,3,Ranazjar Isle\0302,0,0,8,Kreldig Ungor\0302,0,0,8,Desolace\0304,0,0,13,Reclaimers\0311455,19,1455,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301457,23,1457,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6245,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1457]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, the Karnitol business in Desolace. Excellent!$B$BSo, the chest was destroyed, but the items are all here, huh? Well, I'll let him be the judge of that. One good part about this business I got going on here is that if they're not satisfied, I can tell 'em to shove it! They're relyin' on us to find their stuff... not make sure it's all pretty and in good shape when they get it back.$B$BGood work, $N. Let's see about gettin' you paid.\030Take Karnitol's things back to Roetten in Ironforge and he'll pay you for a job well done.$B$BHaha, if you're not careful, he's gonna be so pleased with ya that he'll ask you to join us full time.$B$BAgain, great job, $N.$B$BBe careful on your way back, and don't take too much time--Karnitol's not the most of patient of men, but he's very generous nonetheless.\030Bring Karnitol's Satchel to Roetten Stonehammer in Ironforge.\030Business is booming, $N, and I don't have a lot of time for questions. If you've got business with the Reclaimers, then let's hear it. If not, I'm gonna have to ask you to talk to one of me underlings - they're adept enough at taking care of things 'round here.\030The Karnitol Shipwreck\0312,1,90,2,257,1,5638\0302,95,196,2,257,4,5638\0302,201,221,2,257,1,5638\0302,226,362,2,257,1,5638\0303,1,61,2,384,1,5638\0301,1,38,4,272,1,5637\0301,40,49,4,272,1,5637\0301,54,114,4,276,2,5637\0301,116,155,4,272,1,5637\0301,157,271,4,272,4,5637\0301,273,316,4,272,1,5637\0301,318,387,4,272,1,5637\0301,392,405,4,272,1,5637\0301,407,439,4,272,1,5637\0304,1,70,3,256,1,5637\0304,72,134,3,256,4,5637\0304,136,261,3,256,4,5637\0315637,2,5,Roetten Stonehammer\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,1,Roetten\0302,0,0,1,Ironforge\0302,0,0,5,Roetten Stonehammer\0302,0,0,5,Ironforge\0304,0,0,6,Desolace\0311456,19,1456,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1458]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Good good, $N. Not sure if these are of any good quality, but if Leftwitch wanted a specific type, he should have specified before sending the Reclaimers out here to begin with.$B$BWhat say you to getting on with the next item on his list?\030One of my tasks out here involves picking up some reagents for Leftwitch, a gnome mage in Kharanos . Roetten seems to think it's easy coin in the bank since we're out here already. He doesn't really care that we're short-handed as is.$B$BThe first few items on his list should be easy enough to get, and it'd be a good chunk of coin for anyone helping me out.$B$BI need some horns and claws from the Hatefury satyr to the east of here. Bring 'em back to me and we'll get started on the rest of the list.\030Bring 10 Hatefury Claws, and 10 Hatefury Horns to Kreldig Ungor in Desolace.\030Despicable creatures, the satyr. Story says they're somehow tied to the night elves, but I'm not so sure I believe it.$B$BI think they get that on account of that one elf that brought them into the war few years back. World's never been the same since. Lot more dangerous, and a lot scarier.\030Reagents for Reclaimers Inc.\0312,1,100,2,257,1,5638\0302,102,180,2,257,4,5638\0302,182,234,2,257,1,5638\0302,239,359,2,257,1,5638\0302,364,435,2,259,1,5638\0302,437,503,2,257,1,5638\0303,1,76,2,384,1,5638\0301,1,14,4,272,1,5638\0301,16,177,4,272,4,5638\0301,182,239,4,272,2,5638\0304,1,32,3,256,1,5638\0304,34,118,3,256,4,5638\0304,123,217,3,260,1,5638\0304,219,252,3,256,1,5638\0304,254,291,3,256,1,5638\0315638,2,7,Kreldig Ungor\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,1,Kharanos\0302,0,0,5,Hatefury\0302,0,0,7,Kreldig Ungor\0302,0,0,7,Desolace\0311453,19,1453,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301459,23,1459,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6246,OBJECTIVE,10,15,\030ITEM,6247,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[1459]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Your help here's a boon, $N. You're cutting my time spent here in Desolace by half at least. I'll be back in Ironforge warming my feet in no time with your help.$B$BWhen we get this list taken care of, and I'm back home, look me up, I'll buy you an ale for sure.$B$BBut until then, let's get the rest of these reagents gathered.\030Next on Leftwitch's list is... let's see... hmm. Oh, here it is.$B$BSimple enough, but pretty explicit in his directions. He needs venom from the scorpashi, and hide from some kodo. The fine print says both are from specific creatures: the venom's got to come from any of the scorpashi, and the hide's got to come from an aged kodo, not the dying or ancient ones.$B$BMages, I tell ya, some of the stuff they want... it's just weird.\030Bring 7 vials of Scorpashi Venom and 3 Aged Kodo Hides to Kreldig Ungor in Desolace.\030Sorry I couldn't tell you where to find the kodo or the scorpashi. I'm not terribly familiar with the area, and I haven't had time to explore.\030Reagents for Reclaimers Inc.\0312,1,30,2,257,1,5638\0302,32,43,2,257,1,5638\0302,45,48,2,257,1,5638\0302,50,64,2,257,1,5638\0302,69,121,2,257,1,5638\0302,123,181,2,259,1,5638\0302,183,363,2,321,1,5638\0302,368,415,2,259,1,5638\0302,417,432,2,257,1,5638\0303,1,84,2,384,1,5638\0301,1,28,4,272,1,5638\0301,30,92,4,272,1,5638\0301,94,161,4,272,1,5638\0301,166,262,4,272,1,5638\0301,267,328,4,272,1,5638\0304,1,66,3,256,1,5638\0304,68,142,3,256,1,5638\0314700,2,7,Aged Kodo\0304700,2,10,Aged Kodo\0305638,2,10,Kreldig Ungor\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,10,Kreldig Ungor\0302,0,0,10,Desolace\0304,0,0,12,Desolace\0304,0,0,13,Ironforge\0311458,19,1458,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301466,23,1466,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6248,OBJECTIVE,7,15,\030ITEM,6249,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[146]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031By the Light! The Stormwind Army retreated from Westfall. And the Guard no longer protects Darkshire? There is some treachery abound. How could this be so? $B$BOh I forgot to reward your service, $C. Here are some coins. Now excuse me. Something is amiss in Stormwind and I must get to the bottom of it.\030If I did not know Magistrate Solomon personally, I would say the man has gone mad.  Send the Night Watch to Lakeshire because Stormwind refuses aid?  The Night Watch was formed because Stormwind left us when this foul magic seeped into the land.  If I sent my Night Watch, this town would be overrun by evil before the guards even reached the forest's edge.$B$BTake this letter of response to your Master in Lakeshire.\030Return to Magistrate Solomon with Lord Ebonlocke's letter of response.\030Ah, good to see you back, messenger. Shall I inform the Marshal that the Night Watch is on its way from Darkshire?\030Messenger to Darkshire\0312,1,82,2,257,4,263\0302,85,148,2,259,2,263\0302,151,245,2,259,1,263\0302,248,357,2,257,4,263\0302,362,418,2,257,1,263\0303,1,70,2,384,1,263\0301,1,13,4,272,1,344\0301,15,57,4,272,1,344\0301,59,101,4,272,2,344\0301,103,133,4,272,1,344\0301,135,155,4,272,4,344\0301,161,199,4,272,1,344\0301,201,220,4,272,1,344\0301,222,235,4,272,1,344\0301,237,303,4,272,1,344\0304,1,36,3,256,1,344\0304,38,114,3,256,2,344\031344,2,1,Magistrate Solomon\030798,2,1,Solomon\030344,2,6,Magistrate Solomon\030798,2,6,Solomon\0312,44,1433,0,\0302,0,0,2,Lakeshire\0302,0,0,5,Lakeshire\0302,0,0,6,Magistrate Solomon\0304,0,0,8,Westfall\0304,0,0,15,Stormwind\0303,0,0,17,Darkshire\031145,19,145,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1462]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Take this and remember, it is sacred.\030\030Speak to Seer Ravenfeather for another Earth Sapta.\030\030Earth Sapta\0313,1,51,2,384,1,5888\0301,1,37,4,272,1,5888\0315888,2,1,Seer Ravenfeather\0312,0,0,1,Seer Ravenfeather\0311520,20,1520,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1463]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I give you one in good faith. You already proved yourself once, but me tinkin' you should be more careful in the future.\030\030Speak to Canaga Earthcaller for another Earth Sapta.\030\030Earth Sapta\0313,1,52,2,384,1,5887\0301,1,29,4,272,1,5887\0301,31,120,4,272,1,5887\0315887,2,1,Canaga Earthcaller\0312,0,0,1,Canaga Earthcaller\0311517,20,1517,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1464]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031May fire burn within your heart, $N.$B$BThe elements await you.\030\030Speak to Telf Joolam for another Fire Sapta.\030\030Fire Sapta\0313,1,44,2,384,1,5900\0301,1,36,4,272,1,5900\0301,41,63,4,272,1,5900\0315900,2,1,Telf Joolam\0312,0,0,1,Telf Joolam\0311526,20,1526,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1465]="PARTIAL\031loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Infuriating! This entire fiasco!$B$BThe two of them were warned about how dangerous coming here would be. Now they're both missing... or worse.$B$BYou said you saw tracks heading to a fort nearby? That may be our best bet.$B$BFrom what the locals have said, that fortress is infested with members of the Burning Blade--orcs who have dedicated themselves to demon causes. They may not represent the majority of the Horde's beliefs, but they are evil and will slay you on sight if you're caught spying.\030As you continue your search of the wagon you find not only a pendant, but also footprints leading off towards the south. In the distance you can see smoke rising from a large fort. The smoke is from a kept fire, not the burning of buildings, and your instincts tell you that the Malems, if still alive, were taken that direction.$B$BYou think Vahlarriel at Nijel's Point should not only see the pendant you've found, but also know about the signs of life to the south.\030Return the Malem Pendant to Vahlarriel Demonslayer in Desolace.\030\030Vahlarriel's Search\0312,1,120,2,257,1,0\0302,122,180,2,257,1,0\0302,182,329,2,257,4,0\0302,334,468,2,257,1,0\0303,1,63,2,384,1,0\0301,1,12,4,272,1,5642\0301,14,32,4,272,1,5642\0301,37,105,4,272,4,5642\0301,107,133,4,308,1,5642\0301,135,143,4,272,1,5642\0301,148,196,4,272,2,5642\0301,198,222,4,272,1,5642\0301,227,370,4,272,1,5642\0301,372,500,4,272,4,5642\0315642,2,5,Vahlarriel Demonslayer\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,4,Nijel's Point\0302,0,0,5,Vahlarriel Demonslayer\0302,0,0,5,Desolace\0311437,19,1437,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301438,23,1438,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,50961,GIVER,?,9,Malem Chest",[1466]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Honestly? I wouldn't have thought it. You're amazing, $N. Taking on demons for a mage's experiments, and coming back in one piece to boot. Great job!$B$BI'm personally gonna tell Roetten about you when I get back to Ironforge.\030This is the last of the items, and I won't lie, it ain't pretty. I'm also expecting this to take you a little bit longer than the other items.$B$BSo, enough with the warning, let's get this started. Leftwitch says he needs: ten brains from either mana eaters, mage hunters, or ley hunters. Ten nether wings from a nether maiden, sister or sorceress. And... ten vials of doomwarder blood from a doomwarder captain, or lord.$B$BSimple enough, huh? Sheesh... if you wanna pass on this one, I'd understand.\030Bring 10 Felhound Brains, 10 Nether Wings, and 10 vials of Doomwarder Blood to Kreldig Ungor in Desolace.\030I didn't even realize these demon things were in Desolace. Last I read, centaur pretty much owned the land after the night elves picked up and left years ago.$B$BI wonder why they took up here, and how.\030Reagents for Reclaimers Inc.\0312,1,64,2,257,1,5638\0302,66,142,2,257,1,5638\0302,147,198,2,257,1,5638\0302,200,289,2,259,1,5638\0302,291,349,2,257,1,5638\0302,351,356,2,257,1,5638\0302,358,422,2,257,1,5638\0302,427,445,2,257,2,5638\0302,447,455,2,257,1,5638\0302,457,502,2,257,4,5638\0303,1,105,2,384,1,5638\0301,1,9,4,272,2,5638\0301,11,37,4,272,1,5638\0301,39,57,4,272,1,5638\0301,59,138,4,272,1,5638\0301,140,149,4,272,1,5638\0301,154,226,4,272,1,5638\0304,1,58,3,256,1,5638\0304,60,158,3,320,1,5638\0304,163,202,3,256,1,5638\0314679,2,5,Nether Maiden\0304677,2,7,Doomwarder\0304680,2,7,Doomwarder Captain\0306010,2,11,Felhound\0304677,2,11,Doomwarder\0305638,2,11,Kreldig Ungor\03093,3,19,Centaur\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,11,Kreldig Ungor\0302,0,0,11,Desolace\0304,0,0,17,Ironforge\0303,0,0,18,Desolace\0311459,19,1459,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301467,23,1467,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6250,OBJECTIVE,10,15,\030ITEM,6251,OBJECTIVE,10,15,\030ITEM,6252,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[1467]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, the package for Leftwitch from Desolace. Excellent. I 'preciate the work, and your timeliness, $C. Glad to have you aboard for at least this small bit of work.$B$BI got your payment right here. Let it be known that Reclaimers Inc. always pays well for a hard week's work.\030To get paid, you're gonna have to get back to Ironforge and speak to Roetten himself. He'll love getting Leftwitch's package out of the way anyway. Just give him this and it should be enough to get your booty.$B$BAnd don't worry, I'm still going to put in a good word for you when I get back. I shouldn't be in Desolace much longer.\030Bring Leftwitch's Package back to Roetten Stonehammer in Ironforge.\030Well met, $N. Business is booming, the sounds of anvils being struck rings throughout Ironforge, the bellows blow the fires hot, and me wife's making me a pie for dessert after tonight's dinner. Could life be any grander?\030Reagents for Reclaimers Inc.\0312,1,85,2,257,1,5638\0302,87,147,2,257,1,5638\0302,149,209,2,257,1,5638\0302,214,292,2,257,3,5638\0302,294,332,2,257,1,5638\0303,1,67,2,384,1,5638\0301,1,44,4,272,1,5637\0301,46,55,4,272,1,5637\0301,57,102,4,272,1,5637\0301,104,163,4,272,1,5637\0301,168,197,4,272,1,5637\0301,199,234,4,272,1,5637\0301,236,275,4,272,1,5637\0304,1,13,3,256,1,5637\0304,15,194,3,256,1,5637\0304,196,221,3,256,4,5637\0315637,2,6,Roetten Stonehammer\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,1,Ironforge\0302,0,0,1,Roetten\0302,0,0,5,Desolace\0302,0,0,6,Roetten Stonehammer\0302,0,0,6,Ironforge\0304,0,0,7,Desolace\0311466,19,1466,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1468]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Um... hi. My name is Randis, and I guess you're looking after me? You're an adventurer, like my mom and dad were. I'm happy to meet you.$B$BI hope we'll have a lot of fun together. I have some things I'd like to do, and the matron says you'll be like a big $gbrother:sister; to me during this week. I'd like that a whole bunch, yes $gsir:lady;.\030You're willing to help us here at the orphanage?  Bless you, friend; your aid during Children's Week will be invaluable.$B$BTake this whistle.  You will only be able to use it for a short amount of time - typically not longer than Children's Week itself.  When you use it, you will be able to talk with the child you've agreed to look after.  Using it again will dismiss the child.$B$BBy all means $N - use the whistle and meet your ward!  I'm sure the child will be most eager to meet you.\030Use the Human Orphan Whistle to talk with the child you will be looking after during Children's Week.\030\030Children's Week\0312,1,48,2,257,2,14450\0302,51,120,2,257,3,14450\0302,125,142,2,257,1,14450\0302,145,254,2,257,3,14450\0302,257,341,2,257,3,14450\0302,344,381,2,257,3,14450\0302,386,438,2,257,1,14450\0302,441,490,2,257,3,14450\0303,1,101,2,384,3,14450\0301,11,65,4,272,2,14305\0301,67,113,4,272,1,14305\0301,115,136,4,272,1,14305\0301,141,180,4,274,3,14305\0301,182,298,4,274,1,14305\0301,300,344,4,274,1,14305\03114305,2,9,Human Orphan\03015065,4,15,Lady\031\031\031",[1469]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Rhapsody Shindigger! That's right... how could I forget such a name?$B$BSo he knew about the sinking of the temple all along? Well, that certainly would have saved you some leg work.$B$BBut this Atal'ai artifact! Why, it's quite a find!\030Before the flight, I drank me a whole keg of stout. Hiccup!$B$BAnd what a flight it was. Zipping around with Brohann following me. Didn't see no temple though. Hiccup!$B$BWell, didn't see no temple till I got a little too tipsy and fell off my mount. I plunged right into the water and was sucked down. Found myself surrounded by a bunch of creepy trolls. Sure swam out of there fast! Even made off with this troll souvenir. Here, take it to Brohann and let him know his temple is down there, indeed. Hiccup!\030Bring the Atal'ai Tablet Fragment to Brohann Caskbelly in Stormwind.\030At long last you have returned, $N. It has been quite some time since we last spoke. I thought perhaps you had forgotten about my quest.$B$BDid you locate that wily gryphon rider? Did he have anything to report?\030Rhapsody's Tale\0312,1,51,2,257,1,5634\0302,53,59,2,257,1,5634\0302,64,88,2,257,1,5634\0302,90,130,2,257,1,5634\0302,132,159,2,257,1,5634\0302,161,167,2,257,1,5634\0302,172,250,2,257,1,5634\0302,252,302,2,257,1,5634\0302,304,355,2,257,1,5634\0302,357,384,2,257,1,5634\0302,386,424,2,257,1,5634\0302,426,500,2,257,1,5634\0302,502,508,2,257,1,5634\0303,1,68,2,384,1,5634\0301,1,20,4,272,1,5384\0301,22,36,4,272,1,5384\0301,38,68,4,272,4,5384\0301,73,125,4,272,2,5384\0301,127,182,4,272,4,5384\0301,187,212,4,272,1,5384\0301,214,236,4,272,1,5384\0304,1,35,3,256,1,5384\0304,37,84,3,256,1,5384\0304,86,136,3,256,4,5384\0304,141,179,3,256,2,5384\0304,181,211,3,256,2,5384\0315384,2,14,Brohann Caskbelly\0305634,4,15,Rhapsody Shindigger\0312,47,1425,0,\0302,0,0,12,Brohann\0302,0,0,14,Brohann Caskbelly\0302,0,0,14,Stormwind\0311452,19,1452,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301475,23,1475,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[147]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You found him? Well done, $N. He won't be \"collecting\" from the Elwynn Mines again!$B$BAnd this ring you found is interesting... it's a membership ring for the old Stonemason's Guild in Stormwind. Why would a lowly thief have an artisan guild ring, and why are the Defias Thieves collecting money from our mines?$B$BDifficult questions. I hope one day we'll have answers.\030If the \"Collector\" is taking gold from our mines then he's stealing from the kingdom!  Bring the Collector to justice, and bring me the ring mentioned in the pickup schedule you gave me.  It may tell us whom the Collector is working for...$B$BThat Pickup Schedule says the Collector is hiding out at the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch.  You should search for him there.\030Find and kill \"the Collector\"  then return to Marshal Dughan with The Collector's Ring.\030Did you find the Collector? Did you discover whom he's working for?\030Manhunt\0312,1,85,2,257,4,240\0302,88,186,2,257,1,240\0302,189,239,2,257,1,240\0302,244,328,2,257,1,240\0302,331,362,2,257,1,240\0303,1,87,2,384,1,240\0301,1,14,4,272,2,240\0301,16,29,4,272,1,240\0301,31,83,4,272,1,240\0301,88,128,4,272,1,240\0301,130,196,4,272,1,240\0301,198,312,4,272,4,240\0301,317,336,4,272,1,240\0301,338,371,4,274,3,240\0304,1,27,3,256,2,240\0304,29,67,3,256,2,240\031240,2,6,Marshal Dughan\0312,12,1429,0,\0302,0,0,4,Brackwell Pumpkin Patch\0302,0,0,6,Marshal Dughan\0304,0,0,9,Elwynn Mines\0304,0,0,11,Stormwind\031123,19,123,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,2239,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1470]="PARTIAL\031consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Though you are still untested and young in your learning, you have proven that you possess sufficient ability to master the summoning and binding of an imp. Do not be deceived by an imp's size. Though it lacks physical strength, it possesses powers and a cleverness that will serve you well.$B$BAttend me carefully, $N, for I will not repeat this lesson, and I will leave its mastery to you.\030Greetings, child. I can see that you are still young in the ways of the warlock, power still eluding your grasp. I can sense your eagerness to learn.$B$BAnd you will learn.$B$BThere is no strength in ignorance. Knowledge is our greatest power. Through its application, we can control the chaotic magics and beings of the void, bending them to our will.$B$BI will show you how to bind a servant to your will, but first you must bring me three skulls of the rattlecage skeletons near the abandoned smithy.\030Bring Venya Marthand 3 Rattlecage Skulls.\030Your power is little now, though I suspect already you sense the possibilities.$B$BEven the dead might feel alive, with that power coursing through us.\030Piercing the Veil\0312,1,17,2,257,1,5667\0302,19,112,2,257,1,5667\0302,114,149,2,257,1,5667\0302,154,172,2,257,3,5667\0302,177,210,2,257,1,5667\0302,212,243,2,257,1,5667\0302,245,352,2,257,3,5667\0302,357,503,2,257,3,5667\0303,1,41,2,384,1,5667\0301,1,156,4,276,1,5667\0301,158,193,4,272,1,5667\0301,195,291,4,272,3,5667\0301,296,391,4,272,3,5667\0304,1,79,3,256,4,5667\0304,84,151,3,256,4,5667\0315667,2,9,Venya Marthand\031\031\031ITEM,6281,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[1471]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have done well, $N. Now, I will impart to you the spell used for summoning the voidwalker.$B$BThe power that it unleashed upon you is now yours to command. Use it wisely.\030Surely you have seen the circle of summoning below us? Only there will you be able to draw forth an unbound voidwalker.$B$BUsing these runes, you will be able to draw it forth, and then you must dominate it through strength of arms and magic.$B$BWhen it is subdued, it will be indentured to you. Come to me then, and I will elucidate the spell of summoning, so that it may serve you to whatever end you wish.\030Using the Runes of Summoning, summon and subdue a voidwalker, then return the Runes of Summoning to Carendin Halgar in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity.\030I expect to hear of your success, $N. Not meeting my expectations will be the least of your worries, however, should you fail.\030The Binding\0312,1,54,2,257,2,5675\0302,56,119,2,257,3,5675\0302,124,242,2,257,3,5675\0302,247,295,2,257,3,5675\0302,297,408,2,259,3,5675\0303,1,154,2,384,1,5675\0301,1,23,4,272,1,5675\0301,25,94,4,272,3,5675\0301,99,159,4,272,1,5675\0301,161,174,4,272,1,5675\0304,1,37,3,256,1,5675\0304,39,126,3,256,3,5675\0311860,2,2,Voidwalker\0301860,2,6,Voidwalker\0305675,2,6,Carendin Halgar\0301860,4,8,Voidwalker\0312,0,0,6,Carendin Halgar\0302,0,0,6,Magic Quarter of the Undercity\0311473,19,1473,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,5676,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Summoned Voidwalker",[1472]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You were sent by Carendin? $N, then.$b$bDo not think light of me because my sight is gone. I see things that lie behind now, with clarity I had never known. What I once thought a curse, is now a boon.\030A succubus is a devourer of souls, destroyer of hearts, tempter of men. A creature of profound evil and of singular mind.$B$BIt cannot be brought into our world without a stimulus.$B$BThus we use its own strength against it. With the hearts of good men, pure men, loving men, the succubus will be unable to resist, and will cross into our world. Then you can dominate it, and make it your own.$B$BSpeak with my assistant, Godrick Farsan, within the Temple. He will help you find your bait.\030Speak with Godrick Farsan in the Temple of the Damned.\030\030Devourer of Souls\0312,1,71,2,257,1,5675\0302,73,121,2,257,1,5675\0302,126,180,2,257,1,5675\0302,185,224,2,257,1,5675\0302,226,345,2,257,3,5675\0302,347,393,2,257,1,5675\0302,398,456,2,257,1,5675\0302,458,489,2,257,3,5675\0303,1,54,2,384,1,5675\0301,1,26,4,272,2,5693\0301,28,36,4,272,1,5693\0301,41,90,4,274,1,5693\0301,92,156,4,272,1,5693\0301,158,200,4,276,1,5693\0311863,2,1,Succubus\0301863,2,5,Succubus\0305693,2,7,Godrick Farsan\0305693,2,9,Godrick Farsan\0312,0,0,7,Temple\0302,0,0,9,Temple of the Damned\0311507,22,1507,UNKNOWN\0301476,23,1476,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1473]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, this is excellent. Like as not, Perrine was ignorant to the true power of the musty book he had stolen from us.$B$BIt will not fall out of our hands again. Observe, $N, the structure of the spell, the manner in which your power must be channeled.\030It seems the consensus that you are ready to learn to summon a voidwalker.$B$BA being created of the chaos that lies beyond, if you summon one but cannot control it, you will be torn asunder.$B$BThe first voidwalker was summoned by Egalin, and in his grimoire is the process explained.$B$BUnfortunately, it was stolen from us by an agent of the Scarlet Crusade who has it secreted away in his base at a tower to the west. Bring it to me, and I will impart the knowledge to you.\030Recover Egalin's Grimoire and bring it to Carendin Halgar in the Temple of the Damned.\030Egalin was the teacher that taught me. With hardly a look, he was able to command the voidwalker he had summoned.$B$BWhen it came my turn to try, I was overconfident. Do not trifle with the powers that you wield, $N, they can consume even the vigilant.\030Creature of the Void\0312,1,74,2,257,4,5675\0302,79,191,2,257,4,5675\0302,196,285,2,257,1,5675\0302,290,421,2,261,1,5675\0302,423,477,2,257,3,5675\0303,1,86,2,384,1,5675\0301,1,22,4,272,1,5675\0301,24,115,4,276,1,5675\0301,120,159,4,272,3,5675\0301,161,250,4,272,1,5675\0304,1,38,3,256,1,5675\0304,40,113,3,256,1,5675\0304,118,166,3,256,1,5675\0304,168,252,3,256,1,5675\0311860,2,1,Voidwalker\0302996,2,2,Torn\0301860,2,3,Voidwalker\0305675,2,6,Carendin Halgar\0301860,3,12,Voidwalker\0312,0,0,6,Carendin Halgar\0302,0,0,6,Temple of the Damned\0311471,23,1471,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6285,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1474]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Again, you have done well, $N. It has been quite some time since I have seen a young warlock with as much potential as you. Be assured that I will continue to watch your progress, and prepare and assist you in your future trials.$B$BFor now, let me show you the summoning spell for your newly dominated succubus.\030Using these hearts, cast a spell at the summoning circle to open a doorway for the succubus to come through. Your powers are greater now, and you will need all of them to defeat the succubus. $B$BBeware its charms, $n, many a strong mind has been bound to its will. When overcome, the succubus will be returned to the void, and I will teach you the spell to summon it forth at your command.\030Using the Pure Hearts, summon and subdue a succubus, then return the Pure Hearts to Carendin Halgar in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity.\030Of the powers from beyond the void, the succubus is one of the most dangerous, as the weak are most easily wrapped around its fingers.$B$BRemember that now and in the future.\030The Binding\0312,1,108,2,257,1,5675\0302,110,191,2,259,3,5675\0302,197,265,2,261,3,5675\0302,267,390,2,257,3,5675\0303,1,138,2,384,1,5675\0301,1,30,4,272,1,5675\0301,32,123,4,272,1,5675\0301,125,229,4,272,3,5675\0301,234,312,4,272,1,5675\0304,1,134,3,256,1,5675\0304,139,174,3,256,1,5675\0311863,2,1,Succubus\0301863,2,2,Succubus\0301863,2,4,Succubus\0301863,2,5,Succubus\0305675,2,5,Carendin Halgar\0301863,4,9,Succubus\0301863,3,10,Succubus\0312,0,0,5,Carendin Halgar\0302,0,0,5,Magic Quarter of the Undercity\0311476,19,1476,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,5677,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Summoned Succubus",[1475]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The Atal'ai Tablets! Thank you, $N!$B$BOnce I deliver these to the Explorers' League our names shall go down in history together. You have helped an old dwarf fulfill his final obligation in life. For that I am eternally grateful.\030According to legend, The Temple of Atal'Hakkar is a holy shrine dedicated to the ancient god, Hakkar the Soulflayer. Maintained by a vicious tribe of trolls named the Atal'ai, the temple is rumored to be impenetrable.$B$BNow sunk beneath the Pool of Tears, retrieving artifacts from the temple is even more difficult. But that's what I need you to do, $n.$B$BAid me by gathering the intact Atal'ai Tablets. Bring them to me and I will return to the Explorers' Guild a hero. Together we will share the glory.\030Gather 10 Atal'ai Tablets for Brohann Caskbelly in Stormwind.\030As dusk slowly descends upon my career I turn to you, $N, to help me in my final quest for the Explorers' League. If my old bones could muster the strength to brave the Swamp of Sorrows and the sunken temple I would be fighting right alongside you.$B$BPride makes it hard for me to ask for your help in collecting the Atal'ai Tablets. But old age forces the necessity.$B$BPlease help me, $N. I want to retire from the Explorers' League having completed their final bidding.\030Into The Temple of Atal'Hakkar\0312,1,116,2,321,1,5384\0302,118,217,2,257,1,5384\0302,222,317,2,257,1,5384\0302,319,355,2,259,1,5384\0302,360,406,2,257,1,5384\0302,408,473,2,257,3,5384\0302,475,507,2,257,3,5384\0303,1,61,2,384,1,5384\0301,1,20,4,272,1,5384\0301,22,35,4,272,1,5384\0301,40,129,4,336,3,5384\0301,131,196,4,272,1,5384\0301,198,230,4,272,1,5384\0304,1,113,3,256,1,5384\0304,115,248,3,260,4,5384\0304,253,334,3,256,1,5384\0304,336,368,3,256,1,5384\0304,373,391,3,256,1,5384\0304,393,473,3,258,1,5384\03114834,2,1,Hakkar\03011359,2,1,Soulflayer\0305384,2,8,Brohann Caskbelly\0312,1417,0,0,\0302,0,0,6,Explorers' Guild\0302,0,0,8,Stormwind\0304,0,0,11,Explorers' League\0303,0,0,19,Explorers' League\0311469,19,1469,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6288,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[1476]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The heart of a goodly man seems much the same as any, when you see it like this, don't you think?$B$BPerhaps we possess something of a... different... view on the subject. These will do, though. I have no doubt that a succubus would be attracted by their purity.\030Men of honor and goodness? Does such a man exist?$B$BIt took much research, but through bits of overheard stories, I managed to find two men that should do.$B$BThe first is Dalin Forgewright, who has dedicated himself to the care of the Lordaeron refugees, whom are refused by their kin at the Greymane Wall.$B$BThe other is Comar Villard, a man who remains faithful to his lost love, wandering the Wetlands for a sign of his wife.$B$BDeliver their hearts to Carendin. But first, let me show you your quarry.\030Bring the hearts of Dalin Forgewright and Comar Villard to Carendin Halgar in the Temple of the Damned.\030I have been pleasantly surprised by the speed of your progress so far, $N. Bring me the hearts and you will impress me once again.\030Hearts of the Pure\0312,1,26,2,257,2,5693\0302,28,49,2,257,2,5693\0302,54,156,2,257,1,5693\0302,161,308,2,257,1,5693\0302,313,431,2,261,1,5693\0302,436,468,2,257,1,5693\0302,470,508,2,257,1,5693\0303,1,103,2,384,1,5693\0301,1,97,4,272,4,5675\0301,102,137,4,272,4,5675\0301,139,150,4,272,1,5675\0301,152,171,4,272,1,5675\0301,173,194,4,272,3,5675\0301,196,262,4,272,4,5675\0304,1,74,3,256,1,5675\0304,76,130,3,256,3,5675\0315682,2,4,Dalin Forgewright\0305683,2,5,Comar Villard\0305682,2,8,Dalin Forgewright\0305683,2,8,Comar Villard\0305675,2,8,Carendin Halgar\0301863,4,14,Succubus\0312,0,0,4,Greymane Wall\0302,0,0,6,Carendin\0302,0,0,8,Carendin Halgar\0302,0,0,8,Temple of the Damned\0311472,19,1472,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301474,23,1474,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6312,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,6313,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1477]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Andromath sent you? Very good. I have an important task for you...\030Our mages are conducting research at Nethergarde Keep in the Blasted Lands, research vital to our understanding of the Dark Portals. They require nearly constant supplies, but our supply line to Nethergarde is tenuous.$B$BYou must help ensure the supplies make it to Nethergard.  Report to Watchmaster Sorigal in Darkshire, and do as he asks.  This task will take you into hostile lands, $N.  Prepare yourself.\030Speak with Watchmaster Sorigal.\030\030Vital Supplies\0312,1,132,2,257,1,5694\0302,134,218,2,257,1,5694\0302,223,278,2,257,1,5694\0302,281,342,2,257,1,5694\0302,345,391,2,257,3,5694\0302,394,410,2,257,1,5694\0303,1,31,2,384,1,5694\0301,1,19,4,272,2,5464\0301,21,30,4,272,1,5464\0301,32,66,4,272,1,5464\0315464,2,4,Watchmaster Sorigal\0305464,2,7,Watchmaster Sorigal\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,1,Nethergarde Keep\0302,0,0,1,Blasted Lands\0302,0,0,2,Nethergarde\0302,0,0,3,Nethergard\0302,0,0,4,Watchmaster Sorigal\0302,0,0,4,Darkshire\0311395,23,1395,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301395,24,1395,UNKNOWN\031",[1478]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Good, I see Ageron managed to find you, $N. Let us waste little time with small talk and pleasantries and focus on your training. There is still much you have to learn.\030Ah, $n! I just received word from Carendin Halgar that he would like to see you for further training.$B$BYou should be proud of yourself, $n. It's not every day that Master Halgar personally sees fit to instruct a young warlock.$B$BYou'll be able to find him in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, near the Temple of the Damned.\030Speak with Carendin Halgar in the Undercity.\030\030Halgar's Summons\0312,9,101,2,257,4,5724\0302,106,141,2,257,1,5724\0302,143,228,2,257,1,5724\0302,233,328,2,257,1,5724\0303,1,44,2,384,1,5724\0301,1,43,4,272,1,5675\0301,45,129,4,272,1,5675\0301,131,168,4,272,1,5675\0315675,2,1,Carendin Halgar\0305675,2,5,Carendin Halgar\0312,0,0,1,Carendin Halgar\0302,0,0,4,Magic Quarter of the Undercity\0302,0,0,4,Temple of the Damned\0302,0,0,5,Undercity\0311473,23,1473,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301473,24,1473,UNKNOWN\031",[1479]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Wow, it was cooler than I even imagined - the Bough of the Eternals! I didn't think it'd be so big, but it was! Did you see the bird on top of it too?! I wonder how they got the branches to look like that!$B$BThanks for taking me to Darnassus, $N. You're awesome!\030I've heard stories about how the night elves have their bank in a tree - one that looks like a bear!  That's so cool!  Night elves are neat how they like nature and stuff, but bears are just totally awesome!$B$BWould you take me to see the bear-tree in Darnassus, please?  There's a boat that will take us close to there, and it shouldn't take very long.  Please, please, please!\030Take the orphan to the bank of Darnassus.  The bank itself is hollowed out of a tree known as the Bough of the Eternals.\030Go to the bank in Darnassus, otherwise known as the Bough of the Eternals.\030Are we there yet?\030The Bough of the Eternals\0312,1,100,2,257,1,14305\0302,103,117,2,257,1,14305\0302,120,207,2,257,1,14305\0302,212,271,2,257,4,14305\0302,274,354,2,257,3,14305\0302,357,379,2,257,1,14305\0303,1,41,2,384,1,14305\0303,44,120,2,384,1,14305\0301,1,68,4,272,1,14305\0301,70,111,4,272,1,14305\0301,113,151,4,272,2,14305\0301,153,205,4,272,1,14305\0301,210,247,4,272,1,14305\0301,249,263,4,272,1,14305\0305,1,17,3,256,2,14305\0304,1,74,3,392,1,14305\031\0312,0,0,4,Darnassus\0304,0,0,13,Darnassus\0303,0,0,16,Darnassus\0311468,19,1468,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[148]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, Ghost Hair Thread is what you need, is it? I'm afraid I have none in stock, but I can make some for you...if you can supply the ghost hair.\030Oh, what is a poor old man to do?  I need some supplies from Darkshire, but the village is so far away and I am so old and feeble...I would never make the trip.$B$BCan you go to Darkshire and bring me back some Ghost Hair Thread?  You can get it from Madame Eva at her home on the Darkshire square.\030Speak with Madame Eva.\030\030Supplies from Darkshire\0312,1,33,2,257,2,289\0302,36,160,2,259,4,289\0302,165,229,2,257,2,289\0302,232,298,2,257,1,289\0303,1,22,2,384,1,289\0301,1,46,4,274,2,265\0301,48,143,4,272,4,265\031265,2,4,Madame Eva\030265,2,5,Madame Eva\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,2,Darkshire\0302,0,0,3,Darkshire\0302,0,0,4,Madame Eva\031149,23,149,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1480]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hmm, these runes are indeed a language, $N, an old language. They seem remotely similar to the Eredun language, but the differences are drastic. If I am not mistaken, this is a contract of some kind.... Here, yes, this symbol is the demon's signature: Lord Azrethoc.\030The torn skin smells rotten, and is remarkably pliable for something that appears to be dry and fragile.$B$BAs you unroll it, you can clearly see the red markings of some kind of language on one side. At the bottom of the skin is a very clear symbol that you guess is a signature of some kind.$B$BPerhaps it is something Maurin could tell you more about?\030Bring the Flayed Demon Skin to Maurin Bonesplitter in Desolace.\030The Burning Blade begin to realize how weak they truly are. Their magics are pathetic, their strength feeble.$B$BTheir only power comes from those they serve, and not from any understanding of true power and knowledge.\030The Corrupter\0312,1,104,2,257,1,0\0302,109,200,2,257,1,0\0302,202,293,2,257,1,0\0302,298,354,2,257,4,0\0303,1,63,2,384,1,0\0301,1,60,4,272,1,4498\0301,62,144,4,272,4,4498\0301,146,202,4,272,4,4498\0301,204,266,4,272,1,4498\0304,1,59,3,256,1,4498\0304,61,109,3,256,1,4498\0304,114,218,3,256,1,4498\0312996,2,1,Torn\0304498,2,5,Maurin Bonesplitter\0305760,4,9,Lord Azrethoc\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,5,Maurin Bonesplitter\0302,0,0,5,Desolace\0304,0,0,7,Eredun\0311481,23,1481,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6766,STARTER,?,10,\030ITEM,20310,STARTER,?,10,",[1481]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The shadowstalkers were unable to slay you, $c. Impressive... most impressive.$B$BThis scalp will do nicely for my spell. While you were away, I was able to gather some of the other reagents needed for the spell.$B$BI am almost ready. I only need a focus for the spell--something to project an image of the demon lord and his whereabouts.\030I believe I can find this demon lord given the proper reagents.$B$BIf he is indeed as powerful as I suspect, I will need items gathered from deadly creatures. But you act in the Warchief's name, so I am sure you will accept my task.$B$BFirst, I will have to break any wards he has against scrying. For this, I will need the scalp from a satyr--but not any satyr. The scalp must come from a Hatefury shadowstalker.$B$BSearch for them among the ancient ruins in the northeast of Desolace.\030Bring a Shadowstalker Scalp to Maurin Bonesplitter in Desolace.\030Do not bring me an incorrect scalp, $c. Using the incorrect reagents could cause our deaths. The demon lord may have contingency spells on his person to slay those who would scry upon him.$B$BFate has already dealt me enough pain.\030The Corrupter\0312,1,63,2,257,4,4498\0302,68,158,2,259,4,4498\0302,160,232,2,257,3,4498\0302,237,297,2,257,3,4498\0302,299,362,2,259,3,4498\0302,364,413,2,257,1,4498\0302,418,486,2,321,1,4498\0303,1,63,2,384,1,4498\0301,1,47,4,272,1,4498\0301,49,61,4,272,1,4498\0301,63,78,4,272,1,4498\0301,83,121,4,272,3,4498\0301,123,212,4,272,1,4498\0301,217,234,4,272,1,4498\0301,236,338,4,274,1,4498\0304,1,39,3,256,1,4498\0304,41,92,3,256,4,4498\0304,94,188,3,256,4,4498\0304,193,230,3,256,1,4498\0314674,2,6,Hatefury Shadowstalker\0304498,2,8,Maurin Bonesplitter\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,3,Warchief's\0302,0,0,8,Maurin Bonesplitter\0302,0,0,8,Desolace\0311480,19,1480,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301482,23,1482,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6441,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1482]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A precious oracle crystal... flawless... beautiful. Indeed.$B$BWe shall begin immediately. Finding this demon lord should be our primary concern, and its slaying demands our utmost attention.$B$BTake a step back, $c, and let us see what this demon is, and where he may be found.\030An oracle crystal would do nicely. They are crafted by the naga for their oracles to use.$B$BNorthwest of here, along the coast, is a vast coral reef that the naga have taken as their home when this close to the shore. You can find their oracles there. The Slitherblade are deadly and will not react kindly to your intrusions, so be careful and make haste.$B$BWhen you return, we shall see about finding this demon lord Azrethoc.\030Bring an Oracle Crystal to Maurin Bonesplitter in Desolace.\030I am ready for the oracle crystal, $c. Finding and destroying this Lord Azrethoc would garner a great deal of favor with the Warchief for both of us. We would do well to work together and to do so swiftly so we may further our own ends and curry favor with the Warchief.\030The Corrupter\0312,1,34,2,257,4,4498\0302,36,89,2,257,1,4498\0302,94,218,2,257,1,4498\0302,220,252,2,257,1,4498\0302,254,356,2,257,3,4498\0302,361,429,2,257,3,4498\0303,1,59,2,384,1,4498\0301,1,28,4,272,1,4498\0301,30,40,4,272,1,4498\0301,42,51,4,272,1,4498\0301,53,59,4,272,1,4498\0301,64,90,4,272,3,4498\0301,92,191,4,272,1,4498\0301,196,278,4,272,1,4498\0304,1,38,3,256,1,4498\0304,40,149,3,260,4,4498\0304,151,270,3,256,4,4498\0315760,2,6,Lord Azrethoc\0304498,2,7,Maurin Bonesplitter\03014528,4,8,Precious\0305760,3,16,Lord Azrethoc\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,7,Maurin Bonesplitter\0302,0,0,7,Desolace\0311481,19,1481,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301484,23,1484,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6442,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1483]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I thought those Venture Company higher-ups were slave drivers, but then I met Sputtervalve, the cruelest of them all!$B$BHa! Though it's better than being out of a job, I suppose... Or worse, working with that Gerenzo. If you're here to help, I've got something for you to do.\030The Venture Company stole many of the best goblin minds, but from time to time, we get the opportunity to steal some back.$B$BA while ago, the Venture Company outfit in the Stonetalon Mountains hired Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle--a gnome! Their other engineer, Ziz Fizziks, was so taken aback by this, he pleaded with me to find him new employment with the Tinkers' Union. I set him on a few tasks, but he might need help.$B$BMaybe you could look in on him for me? He's stationed at the western edge of Windshear Crag.\030Speak with Ziz Fizziks in Windshear Crag.\030\030Ziz Fizziks\0312,1,122,2,261,1,3442\0302,127,231,2,257,1,3442\0302,233,365,2,257,1,3442\0302,367,415,2,259,4,3442\0302,420,457,2,257,4,3442\0302,459,511,2,257,1,3442\0303,1,41,2,384,1,3442\0301,1,117,4,272,1,4201\0301,126,181,4,272,1,4201\0301,183,218,4,272,1,4201\0301,220,276,4,272,4,4201\0314202,2,2,Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle\0304201,2,3,Ziz Fizziks\0304201,2,7,Ziz Fizziks\03010116,4,8,Slave\0303442,4,8,Sputtervalve\0312,17,1413,0,\0302,0,0,2,Stonetalon Mountains\0302,0,0,7,Windshear Crag\0311093,23,1093,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1484]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I witnessed what just occurred with Maurin and the demon lord. That creature, even as an apparition, seems to have more power than my warlock companion. I wonder if he's up to the task of defeating the monster? It would serve the Warchief better if I go myself, but with my responsibilities here, I would disgrace my clan if I turned my back on my duties here to battle this evil for my own honor.\030This creature is far more dangerous than I had anticipated.  No doubt Takata questions my abilities to take on such a creature, and it would insult his honor if he were not informed about what just happened.$B$BSpeak to the swordsman, tell him you are willing to slay the demon if he would allow it, but do not press too hard. It is better if he thinks it his own idea.\030Speak to Takata Steelblade in Desolace.\030\030The Corrupter\0312,1,59,2,257,1,4498\0302,62,207,2,257,4,4498\0302,212,326,2,257,4,4498\0302,328,369,2,257,4,4498\0303,1,39,2,384,1,4498\0301,1,62,4,272,1,5641\0301,64,152,4,272,4,5641\0301,154,210,4,272,4,5641\0301,212,397,4,276,4,5641\0315641,2,5,Takata Steelblade\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,5,Takata Steelblade\0302,0,0,5,Desolace\0311482,19,1482,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301488,23,1488,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1485]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Throughout your training as a warlock, you will learn to call forth beings of many sorts. Some may not seem it, but all are useful tools.$B$BDo not be fooled by the imp's small size. As you no doubt noticed, it is still a formidable adversary.\030Those warlocks who came before us have earned the distrust of the Horde, and while we are tolerated, we are not loved.$B$BThis has not brought the warlocks closer together, however, as many choose to live reclusively, dabbling in their magics alone. I will not seek to lead you down one path or the other, but only help you in your maturation.$B$BBefore I teach you the art of summoning, bring me six heads of the vile familiars from the cave to the northeast.\030Bring 6 Vile Familiar Heads to Ruzan.\030It is important that you can control the beings that you summon through your magic. There are few enough interested in learning the ways of the warlock that I would risk throwing your life away by teaching you something before you are ready.\030Vile Familiars\0312,1,118,2,257,1,5765\0302,123,249,2,257,1,5765\0302,251,343,2,259,3,5765\0302,348,460,2,257,1,5765\0303,1,37,2,384,1,5765\0301,1,89,4,272,3,5765\0301,91,137,4,272,4,5765\0301,142,182,4,272,1,5765\0301,184,243,4,272,1,5765\0304,1,83,3,256,1,5765\0304,85,241,3,264,4,5765\0313101,2,5,Vile Familiar\0305765,2,5,Ruzan\0312,0,0,5,Ruzan\0311499,23,1499,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6487,OBJECTIVE,6,15,",[1486]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Your efforts shall not go unnoticed in gathering these hides, $N.$B$BThank you for your dedication.\030As Naralex descended deeper into his nightmare, a strange breed of beasts arose from beneath the Barrens into the Wailing Caverns.$B$BThese deviate creatures have strange, otherworldly properties. While evil in nature, it is my opinion that some good can come from their existence here in Kalimdor. I believe their hides will be of particular use in the ways of leatherworking.$B$BIf you feel up to the task, venture into the caves below and retrieve some deviate hides.\030Nalpak in the Wailing Caverns wants 20 Deviate Hides.\030I am very interested in examining the hides from the deviate creatures who have infested these caves. Have you had any luck in collecting some, $C?\030Deviate Hides\0312,1,130,2,257,1,5767\0302,135,196,2,257,1,5767\0302,198,298,2,257,1,5767\0302,300,377,2,257,4,5767\0302,382,470,2,257,4,5767\0303,1,53,2,386,1,5767\0301,1,65,4,272,3,5767\0301,70,99,4,272,1,5767\0304,1,101,3,256,1,5767\0304,103,147,3,256,2,5767\0313679,2,1,Naralex\0305407,2,1,Nightmare\0305767,2,6,Nalpak\0312,718,0,0,\0302,0,0,3,Kalimdor\0302,0,0,6,Wailing Caverns\031\031ITEM,6443,OBJECTIVE,20,15,",[1487]="PARTIAL\031consequences,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031As a Disciple of Naralex, I commend your bravery, $N.$B$BYour aid in ridding the caverns is the first step in our long plight to see the Barrens restored.$B$BThank you and may you prosper.\030Naralex had a noble goal.$B$BOur great leader aspired to enter the Emerald Dream and help regrow these harsh lands back into the lush forest it once was. But something went terribly wrong.$B$BNaralex's dream turned into a nightmare and corrupt creatures began to inhabit the caverns.$B$BWhile some Disciples of Naralex seek to awake our master, my concern is with ridding these caves of the evil beasts.$B$BBrave the caverns, $n, and eradicate the deviate spawn.\030Ebru in the Wailing Caverns wants you to kill 7 Deviate Ravagers, 7 Deviate Vipers, 7 Deviate Shamblers and 7 Deviate Dreadfangs.\030$N, we, the Disciples of Naralex, need your help. Our numbers are dwindling with our master trapped in his twisted nightmare. We have not the forces necessary to deal with the corrupt creatures which now haunt these caverns.$B$BI beg of you, enter the caves and wage war on the deviate creatures!\030Deviate Eradication\0312,1,25,2,257,1,5768\0302,30,153,2,321,1,5768\0302,155,188,2,257,1,5768\0302,193,283,2,261,1,5768\0302,288,403,2,259,1,5768\0302,408,462,2,257,1,5768\0303,1,129,2,386,1,5768\0301,1,53,4,272,1,5768\0301,58,154,4,272,1,5768\0301,159,188,4,272,1,5768\0304,1,49,3,256,1,5768\0304,51,125,3,256,1,5768\0304,127,224,3,260,1,5768\0304,229,296,3,260,1,5768\0313679,2,1,Naralex\0305407,2,4,Nightmare\0303679,2,5,Naralex\0305768,2,7,Ebru\0303678,4,8,Disciple of Naralex\0303679,4,8,Naralex\0303679,3,11,Naralex\0305407,3,12,Nightmare\0312,718,0,0,\0302,0,0,7,Wailing Caverns\031\031NPC,3636,OBJECTIVE,7,13,Deviate Ravager\030NPC,5755,OBJECTIVE,7,13,Deviate Viper\030NPC,5761,OBJECTIVE,7,13,Deviate Shambler\030NPC,5056,OBJECTIVE,7,13,Deviate Dreadfang",[1488]="PARTIAL\031loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A mighty victory for us all, $N. Let us rejoice in your success. I trust now that our future here is not as bleak as I once thought.$B$BThe demons will be slain, the Burning Blade will fail in their efforts, and we may one day have a place we can safely call home again.\030Although I have no knowledge of this Lord Azrethoc, I agree with Maurin, he must be stopped; especially if he is attempting to gain influence over the Burning Blade to further his goals.$B$BYou have already shown you wish to aid the Warchief, and I would trust you to gather a party to slay the demon lord and his warlock servant.$B$BWhen you are ready, head directly south,  and return to me when the threat has been ended.\030Slay Lord Azrethoc and Jugkar Grim'rod and return to Takata Steelblade in Desolace.\030Glory to the Horde, and death to our enemies, $N!$B$BThe demons in Desolace pose a greater threat than ever before. My hope of returning to the Warchief dwindles as more and more of the foul creatures seem to appear.$B$BI sometimes wish it was only the centaur we had to deal with.\030The Corrupter\0312,1,186,2,257,4,5641\0302,191,330,2,259,4,5641\0302,335,424,2,261,1,5641\0303,1,83,2,384,1,5641\0301,1,32,4,272,1,5641\0301,34,64,4,272,1,5641\0301,66,132,4,304,1,5641\0301,137,270,4,276,3,5641\0304,1,49,3,260,1,5641\0304,54,115,3,260,1,5641\0304,117,216,3,258,4,5641\0304,221,281,3,258,3,5641\0315760,2,1,Lord Azrethoc\0305760,2,4,Lord Azrethoc\0305771,2,4,Jugkar Grim'rod\0305641,2,4,Takata Steelblade\03093,3,12,Centaur\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,4,Takata Steelblade\0302,0,0,4,Desolace\0303,0,0,9,Horde\0303,0,0,10,Desolace\0303,0,0,11,Warchief\0311484,19,1484,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,5760,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Lord Azrethoc\030NPC,5771,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Jugkar Grim'rod",[1489]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I bid you greetings, $N. You are welcome here, and I suggest you gather all your strength. For the task we now set before you ... is a dire one.\030The shells you brought me have a taint, one I have never before seen.  I am certain the water of the Oases is the cause, and I can sense the confusion they cause this land.  It is as if the land dreams and cannot awake.$B$BThe Wailing Caverns must be the source of the taint.  But before you go there, speak with Hamuul Runetotem, the elder druid.  I sent word to him of the happenings in the Barrens.  He is wise, and can offer you counsel.$B$BYou will find him in Thunder Bluff, on the Elder Rise.\030Speak with Hamuul Runetotem.\030\030Hamuul Runetotem\0312,1,69,2,257,1,3448\0302,72,172,2,257,1,3448\0302,175,219,2,257,4,3448\0302,224,275,2,257,1,3448\0302,278,347,2,257,1,3448\0302,350,401,2,257,1,3448\0302,404,441,2,257,1,3448\0302,446,499,2,257,3,3448\0303,1,28,2,384,1,3448\0301,1,24,4,272,1,5769\0301,26,90,4,272,1,5769\0301,92,129,4,272,1,5769\0301,131,144,4,272,1,5769\031\0312,718,0,0,\0302,0,0,6,Barrens\0302,0,0,8,Thunder Bluff\031880,19,880,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301490,23,1490,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[149]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031What is this? A comb? It's lovely! And it glides through my hair as if it weren't the stiff, stringy horror that it is.$B$BOh, if only I had a mirror...\030There is a poor, sad spirit, Blind Mary, who haunts an old farm house in the hills south of Darkshire.$B$BHere, take this Spectral Comb and ask Blind Mary to comb her hair.  Then bring back the comb and I will glean from it the Ghost Hair I'll need for the thread.$B$BAnd take care, for dark things now lurk near that house...\030Bring the Spectral Comb to Blind Mary.\030Oh please, don't look at me! I tore out these eyes with my own hands, but I can still feel your gaze!$B$BI'm hideous! Hideous! Please, look away!!\030Ghost Hair Thread\0312,1,102,2,257,1,265\0302,107,172,2,257,1,265\0302,175,264,2,259,3,265\0302,269,326,2,257,1,265\0303,1,38,2,384,1,265\0301,1,13,4,272,2,302\0301,15,21,4,272,2,302\0301,23,34,4,272,1,302\0301,36,119,4,272,4,302\0301,124,152,4,272,4,302\0304,1,28,3,256,1,302\0304,30,101,3,256,1,302\0304,106,117,3,256,1,302\0304,119,126,3,256,1,302\0304,128,146,3,256,1,302\031302,2,1,Blind Mary\030302,2,2,Blind Mary\030302,2,5,Blind Mary\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,1,Darkshire\0302,0,0,5,Blind Mary\031148,19,148,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030154,23,154,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1490]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes, it is true. I know of the druids in the Wailing Caverns. I have seen their twisted, scaled faces. I know their crimes, and I know their plans.$B$BYou must stop them, $N.\030I entered the land of dreams, and dreamed of a cult of druids who dwell in the Wailing Caverns.  I saw that their goals were once noble, but they have lost their way.  They are now servants of the taint seeping through the Barrens.$B$BI am old and my strength fails.  I could not long dwell in that dreaming place and know little more of the tainted druids.  But Nara is young and her spirit is fierce.  She remained in the dreaming when I fled.$B$BSpeak with Nara.  She is in the tent, over yonder.\030Speak with Nara Wildmane.\030\030Nara Wildmane\0312,1,95,2,257,1,5769\0302,98,166,2,261,1,5769\0302,169,231,2,257,1,5769\0302,236,266,2,257,1,5769\0302,269,357,2,257,4,5769\0302,360,402,2,257,1,5769\0302,405,445,2,257,1,5769\0302,450,465,2,257,1,5769\0302,468,499,2,257,1,5769\0303,1,25,2,384,1,5769\0301,1,16,4,272,1,5770\0301,18,61,4,272,1,5770\0301,63,102,4,272,1,5770\0301,104,147,4,272,1,5770\0301,152,174,4,272,1,5770\0315770,2,10,Nara Wildmane\0312,718,0,0,\0302,0,0,1,Wailing Caverns\0304,0,0,12,Wailing Caverns\0311489,19,1489,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030914,23,914,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1491]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Great, you got it! I can't wait to try it out. This is going to make me a fortune, I just know it!$B$BThank you, $N. Take this, and after I'm rich I'll send you more, I promise!\030Ok, so the raptor horns didn't work so well.  But that's all right -- no one got rich on their first try!  And besides, I think I found something that'll work even better in my smart drinks!$B$BThere is a substance called Wailing Essence, and I think it is the cause of the strange plants and animals in the Barrens.  Get me some and I'll try it in my drink!$B$BI heard the essence gathers in ectoplasmic creatures in the Wailing Caverns to the west.  Hunt those creatures and gather the essence.\030Bring 6 portions of Wailing Essence to Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet.\030Where is my wailing essence?\030Smart Drinks\0312,1,44,2,257,1,3446\0302,47,105,2,257,1,3446\0302,108,190,2,257,1,3446\0302,195,316,2,257,1,3446\0302,319,358,2,257,1,3446\0302,363,450,2,257,1,3446\0302,453,496,2,257,1,3446\0303,1,65,2,384,1,3446\0301,1,18,4,272,1,3446\0301,20,46,4,272,1,3446\0301,48,98,4,272,3,3446\0301,103,116,4,272,1,3446\0301,118,177,4,272,1,3446\0304,1,28,3,256,2,3446\031107,2,1,Raptor\0303446,2,8,Mebok Mizzyrix\0312,718,0,0,\0302,0,0,4,Barrens\0302,0,0,6,Wailing Caverns\0302,0,0,8,Mebok Mizzyrix\0302,0,0,8,Ratchet\031865,19,865,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6464,OBJECTIVE,6,15,",[1492]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A small enough crate. Yes, I should be able to find room for this aboard the ship. It sails with the next tide, I trust this is soon enough? Excellent. Let me just enter it into my ledger.$B$BAll taken care of! Good day to you, $C.\030I have need to send a crate of potions, reagents and other items to my associates in the Old World. Little time I have to actually see them to the dock at Ratchet, and the last caravan has already left.$B$BIf you could, please take this to Wharfmaster Dizzywig. He will ensure that it is placed on the next boat to Blackwater Cove.\030Bring the Secure Crate to Wharfmaster Dizzywig in Ratchet.\030You seek passage on the next ship, or have some item you wish to send aboard it?\030Wharfmaster Dizzywig\0312,1,99,2,259,1,3390\0302,101,202,2,257,1,3390\0302,207,261,2,257,4,3390\0302,263,331,2,257,3,3390\0303,1,58,2,384,1,3390\0301,1,21,4,272,1,3453\0301,23,82,4,272,1,3453\0301,84,140,4,272,2,3453\0301,142,151,4,272,1,3453\0301,153,188,4,272,1,3453\0301,193,210,4,272,1,3453\0301,212,231,4,272,1,3453\0304,1,80,3,258,2,3453\0313453,2,3,Wharfmaster Dizzywig\0303453,2,5,Wharfmaster Dizzywig\0312,17,1413,0,\0302,0,0,1,Old World\0302,0,0,2,Ratchet\0302,0,0,3,Wharfmaster Dizzywig\0302,0,0,4,Blackwater Cove\0302,0,0,5,Wharfmaster Dizzywig\0302,0,0,5,Ratchet\031\031",[1498]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah. I see you have defeated the thunder lizards, which proves you are tough. Now I will show you how tough skin and shrewd movements can combine to form an impenetrable wall of defense.$B$BLearn your lesson well, $N. And be ready for future instruction.\030As a warrior, one of our most crucial tasks is... protection.  We are the shield of the Horde, and we keep our weaker brethren safe.  If you are to join in our ranks, then you must prove your mettle to me.$B$BGo to Thunder Ridge in Durotar, where live the lightning hides and thunder lizards.  Hunt the beasts!  Show me you are tougher than they!  Brave their assaults and bring me a stack of their singed scales as proof.$B$BDo this, and then I will teach you.\030Bring 5 Singed Scales to Uzzek at Far Watch Post in the Barrens.\030Do you have the scales, $N? Unless you can withstand the attacks of the thunder lizards, you will not benefit from my instruction.\030Path of Defense\0312,1,49,2,257,1,5810\0302,51,61,2,257,1,5810\0302,64,132,2,257,1,5810\0302,135,205,2,257,4,5810\0302,210,292,2,257,1,5810\0302,295,310,2,257,1,5810\0302,313,346,2,257,1,5810\0302,349,422,2,257,1,5810\0302,427,461,2,257,3,5810\0303,1,64,2,384,1,5810\0301,5,76,4,272,1,5810\0301,78,185,4,272,3,5810\0301,190,216,4,272,1,5810\0301,218,253,4,272,1,5810\0304,1,27,3,256,2,5810\0304,29,130,3,268,4,5810\0315810,2,10,Uzzek\0312,0,0,5,Thunder Ridge\0302,0,0,5,Durotar\0302,0,0,10,Uzzek\0302,0,0,10,Far Watch Post\0302,0,0,10,Barrens\0311505,19,1505,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301502,23,1502,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6486,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[1499]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have done well, $n.$B$BAlthough the vile familiars were merely pets of the darker powers within the Burning Blade, your success against them foretells greater deeds ahead.\030Zureetha has been sending novices like yourself to help cull the numbers of the creatures in the cave near where you fought the vile familiars.$B$BI think it would be good for you to gain experience by assisting her. Be sure to tell her that you assisted with the imp problem, she'll probably have a reward for you.\030Speak with Zureetha Fargaze.\030\030Vile Familiars\0312,1,143,2,257,1,5765\0302,148,216,2,257,4,5765\0302,218,315,2,261,1,5765\0303,1,28,2,384,1,5765\0301,1,23,4,272,1,3145\0301,28,175,4,272,1,3145\0313145,2,4,Zureetha Fargaze\0314,0,0,6,Burning Blade\0311485,19,1485,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030794,23,794,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[15]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I don't like hearing of all these kobolds in our mine. No good can come of this. Here, take this as payment, and when you're ready, speak to me again. I would like you to go back to the mines one more time...\030$N, my scouts tell me that the kobold infestation is larger than we had thought.  A group of kobold workers has camped near the Echo Ridge Mine to the north.$B$BGo to the mine and remove them.  We know there are at least 10.  Kill them, see if there are more, then report back to me.\030Kill 10 Kobold Workers, then report back to Marshal McBride.\030Have you been to the mines? Are you ready to report?\030Investigate Echo Ridge\0312,1,80,2,257,1,197\0302,83,157,2,257,1,197\0302,162,192,2,257,1,197\0302,195,224,2,257,1,197\0302,227,283,2,257,4,197\0303,1,60,2,384,1,197\0301,1,54,4,272,1,197\0301,56,80,4,272,1,197\0301,82,150,4,272,1,197\0301,152,208,4,274,4,197\0304,1,27,3,256,2,197\0304,29,52,3,256,2,197\031197,2,6,Marshal McBride\0312,9,1429,0,\0302,0,0,2,Echo Ridge Mine\0302,0,0,6,Marshal McBride\0317,19,7,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\03021,23,21,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,257,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Kobold Worker",[150]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $N. I hope you didn't have too much trouble with those murlocs.$B$BIt's strange seeing them so far from the sea. I wonder if they're here because they're running from something...\030Murlocs are becoming a problem.  Larger groups of the fishmen are dropping anchor along the shores of Lake Everstill and fishing up a storm!  We need them gone before they eat all the fish in the lake!$B$BHunt murlocs!  Bring me eight of their fins and I might have something for you...\030Bring 8 Murloc Fins to Dockmaster Baren in Lakeshire.\030Do you have those fins? Hurry, we need those murlocs driven from the lake!\030Murloc Poachers\0312,1,31,2,261,1,381\0302,34,140,2,257,1,381\0302,143,201,2,267,1,381\0302,206,218,2,257,1,381\0302,221,286,2,257,4,381\0303,1,53,2,384,1,381\0301,1,14,4,272,1,381\0301,16,74,4,274,3,381\0301,79,123,4,272,1,381\0301,125,190,4,274,4,381\0304,1,23,3,256,2,381\0304,25,74,3,258,1,381\031285,2,6,Murloc\030381,2,6,Dockmaster Baren\0312,44,1433,0,\0302,0,0,6,Dockmaster Baren\0302,0,0,6,Lakeshire\031\031ITEM,1468,OBJECTIVE,8,15,",[1501]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Good. I hope you inflicted some other losses on the Burning Blade when you went to retrieve this.$B$BThey have been a source of great annoyance for the Warchief, and a great blight upon warlocks as a whole.\030So few warlocks remain... We risk much, but the risks are warranted. You must quickly reach maturity in your ability if you are to be of use to the Horde and to the Warchief.$B$BIt is time that you learned a new summoning spell.$B$BFirst, you must recover the Tablet of Verga, which was stolen by warlocks of the Burning Blade and is now kept at their lair in Skull Rock to the east of the city. With the tablet, I will show you the runes necessary to summoning a voidwalker.\030Retrieve the Tablet of Verga for Gan'rul Bloodeye in Orgrimmar.\030Do you have the Tablet of Verga, $N? If not, I do not wish to speak with you until you do.\030Creature of the Void\0312,1,25,2,257,1,5875\0302,27,68,2,265,1,5875\0302,70,174,2,257,4,5875\0302,179,228,2,257,1,5875\0302,233,395,2,261,1,5875\0302,397,475,2,257,3,5875\0303,1,63,2,384,1,5875\0301,1,5,4,272,1,5875\0301,7,97,4,274,3,5875\0301,102,206,4,272,1,5875\0304,1,36,3,256,2,5875\0304,38,90,3,258,4,5875\0311860,2,6,Voidwalker\0305875,2,7,Gan'rul Bloodeye\0312,0,0,3,Horde\0302,0,0,3,Warchief\0302,0,0,5,Skull Rock\0302,0,0,7,Orgrimmar\0311504,23,1504,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6535,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1502]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031My eyes have long dried out from staring into the forge's flame, but some things I can still see. I can see you want something.$B$BAnd if you found your way here, then I can guess what you desire.\030It is vital that a warrior's weapon is one of quality.  And if there is an orc who can craft quality weapons, then that orc is Thun'grim Firegaze.  He is a hermit who dwells atop the hills east of the Crossroads.$B$BIf you seek a weapon, warrior, then you should seek Thun'grim.  To find him, first travel to the Crossroads to the west, then strike east into the hills.  His camp is high on a hilltop.\030Speak with Thun'grim Firegaze in the Barrens.\030\030Thun'grim Firegaze\0312,1,54,2,257,1,5810\0302,57,146,2,257,4,5810\0302,149,212,2,257,1,5810\0302,217,278,2,259,4,5810\0302,281,369,2,257,1,5810\0302,372,401,2,257,1,5810\0303,1,45,2,384,1,5810\0301,1,97,4,272,1,5878\0301,99,127,4,274,1,5878\0301,132,196,4,274,4,5878\0315878,2,2,Thun'grim Firegaze\0305878,2,7,Thun'grim Firegaze\0312,0,0,3,Crossroads\0302,0,0,5,Crossroads\0302,0,0,7,Barrens\0311498,19,1498,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301503,23,1503,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1503]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You found them! And all the bars are here, which doesn't surprise me. I didn't think the Razormanes would know what to do with fine steel like this.$B$BThank you, $N. Here is your reward. May it serve you well.\030I will give you a weapon, $N, but first you must aid me.  The Razormanes to the northwest came into my camp a few nights past.  They would not meet me in combat, but they know my eyes are bad--a few distracted me with snorts while others stole from me!  The cowards!$B$BThey took an iron chest, and within it were some forged steel bars.  If you can recover them then I will give you the weapon you seek.$B$BSearch for the iron box within the quilboar camps, and return with the forged steel bars.\030Bring the Forged Steel Bars to Thun'grim Firegaze in the Barrens.\030Do you have my steel bars?\030Forged Steel\0312,1,56,2,257,3,5878\0302,59,126,2,257,1,5878\0302,129,252,2,257,4,5878\0302,255,266,2,257,1,5878\0302,271,337,2,257,1,5878\0302,340,404,2,259,4,5878\0302,409,497,2,257,1,5878\0303,1,65,2,384,1,5878\0301,1,15,4,272,1,5878\0301,17,69,4,272,1,5878\0301,71,148,4,272,4,5878\0301,153,166,4,272,1,5878\0301,168,187,4,272,1,5878\0301,189,210,4,272,1,5878\0304,1,26,3,256,2,5878\0315878,2,8,Thun'grim Firegaze\0312,0,0,8,Thun'grim Firegaze\0302,0,0,8,Barrens\0311502,19,1502,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6534,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1504]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have done well, $N. I will show you how to summon the voidwalker similar to the one you just defeated.$B$BYou should know that we have high expectations for you, and you have, so far, matched them.$B$BDo not let it go to your head, however, as the tasks that still lie before you will make this seem as simple as waking in the morning.\030Now, observe the Tablet of Verga, for it contains the glyphs you will need for the summoning. Take them to the circle in Neeru Fireblade's tent on the other side of the cavern. There you will be able to call for the voidwalker.$B$BYou must defeat it using whatever physical and magical means you have at your disposal. When this is completed, return to me with the glyphs of summoning and I will demonstrate how you may bind the creature to your will.\030Using the Glyphs of Summoning, summon and subdue a voidwalker, then return the Glyphs of Summoning to Gan'rul Bloodeye in Orgrimmar.\030The voidwalker is a powerful creature. I remember when it was I that was in your shoes, $N. Over the years, my own voidwalker has grown to fight me less, though I suspect that is only because it hopes I will let my guard down.$B$BRemember that, $N.\030The Binding\0312,1,93,2,259,3,5875\0302,95,176,2,257,1,5875\0302,178,227,2,257,3,5875\0302,232,318,2,257,1,5875\0302,320,451,2,257,3,5875\0303,1,132,2,384,1,5875\0301,1,23,4,272,1,5875\0301,25,106,4,272,3,5875\0301,111,201,4,272,1,5875\0301,206,339,4,272,4,5875\0304,1,38,3,256,1,5875\0304,40,91,3,256,1,5875\0304,93,226,3,262,4,5875\0304,231,248,3,256,1,5875\0313216,2,2,Neeru Fireblade\0301860,2,3,Voidwalker\0301860,2,6,Voidwalker\0305875,2,6,Gan'rul Bloodeye\0301860,4,8,Voidwalker\0301860,3,11,Voidwalker\0301860,3,13,Voidwalker\0312,0,0,2,Neeru Fireblade's\0302,0,0,6,Gan'rul Bloodeye\0302,0,0,6,Orgrimmar\0311501,19,1501,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,5676,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Summoned Voidwalker",[1505]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hello, young one. Here for some instruction, are you?\030The Horde honors its warriors because their strength is unquestioned.  But the truly great warriors are great students as well.$B$BSeek out Uzzek.  He is a veteran of many battles and now instructs young warriors in the ways of combat.  You will find him south of Far Watch Post, the orc garrison on the border of the Barrens and Durotar.\030Speak with Uzzek at Far Watch Post.\030\030Veteran Uzzek\0312,1,69,2,259,1,0\0302,72,127,2,257,1,0\0302,132,146,2,257,1,0\0302,149,235,2,257,1,0\0302,238,338,2,257,3,0\0303,1,35,2,384,1,0\0301,1,17,4,272,1,5810\0301,19,53,4,272,2,5810\0315810,2,3,Uzzek\0305810,2,6,Uzzek\0312,0,0,5,Far Watch Post\0302,0,0,6,Far Watch Post\0311818,22,1818,UNKNOWN\0301498,23,1498,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1506]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Good. I was afraid Ophek wouldn't reach you.$B$BIt is time that I further your warlock training. Any business you have currently will have to wait.$B$BI trust there will not be a problem with this?\030You there. $n, right?$B$BI hope your schedule isn't busy, because Gan'rul wants to see you right away. You'll find him with the senior warlocks in the Cleft of Shadow.$B$BBased on my past dealings with Gan'rul, your summons is either a very good thing or a very bad thing.\030Speak with Gan'rul Bloodeye in Orgrimmar.\030\030Gan'rul's Summons\0312,1,10,2,257,1,3294\0302,12,21,2,257,2,3294\0302,26,102,2,259,3,3294\0302,104,167,2,257,1,3294\0302,172,272,2,257,1,3294\0303,1,41,2,384,1,3294\0301,1,5,4,272,1,5875\0301,7,44,4,272,1,5875\0301,49,96,4,272,1,5875\0301,98,147,4,272,3,5875\0301,152,197,4,276,2,5875\0314244,2,4,Shadow\0305875,2,6,Gan'rul Bloodeye\0303294,4,8,Ophek\0312,0,0,4,Cleft of Shadow\0302,0,0,6,Orgrimmar\0311501,23,1501,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301501,24,1501,UNKNOWN\031",[1507]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hm... $n. You are still new to your path, but I sense the possibility for greatness in you.$B$BYou were born with gifts, $n. See that they do not go to waste.\030The time has come for you to learn more of the summoning magics. You will learn to summon a succubus, a creature of incredible mental powers. It can lull those of weak minds into its servitude--but have no fear! I feel certain that you will be equal to the challenge.$B$BA succubus can only be summoned when baited with an item that represents great devotion and love. I leave it to you to find such an object.$B$BA suggestion? Speak with Cazul... There seems to be little the ancient warlock does not know.\030Speak with Cazul in the Cleft of Shadow.\030\030Devourer of Souls\0312,1,64,2,257,1,5875\0302,66,141,2,257,3,5875\0302,143,211,2,257,1,5875\0302,213,267,2,257,3,5875\0302,272,368,2,257,1,5875\0302,370,410,2,257,1,5875\0302,415,427,2,257,2,5875\0302,429,447,2,257,1,5875\0302,449,507,2,321,4,5875\0303,1,40,2,384,1,5875\0301,11,91,4,272,1,5909\0301,96,124,4,272,1,5909\0301,126,158,4,272,1,5909\0311863,2,2,Succubus\0301863,2,5,Succubus\0305909,2,8,Cazul\0305909,2,10,Cazul\0304244,2,10,Shadow\0312,0,0,10,Cleft of Shadow\0311472,22,1472,UNKNOWN\0301508,23,1508,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1508]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Have you come with news of Dogran? He was to have returned days ago, and I have heard nothing...\030Hmm... But, of course, that is not why you have come to speak with me.$B$BIf Gan'rul has sent you to me, it must be that you are to summon a succubus, and need an object to use for enticement.$B$BHmm... If you trust a blind man to lead you, $n, then listen. In the bluffs of Orgrimmar, west of the wind rider tower, lives Zankaja. She waits for the return of her mate.$B$BGo to her.\030Speak with Zankaja in Orgrimmar.\030\030Blind Cazul\0312,1,6,2,257,1,5909\0302,8,70,2,257,1,5909\0302,75,192,2,259,4,5909\0302,197,202,2,257,1,5909\0302,204,257,2,257,4,5909\0302,259,330,2,257,1,5909\0302,332,368,2,257,1,5909\0302,373,382,2,257,1,5909\0303,1,32,2,384,1,5909\0301,1,34,4,272,2,5910\0301,36,96,4,272,1,5910\0311863,2,3,Succubus\0302224,2,6,Wind Rider\0305910,2,6,Zankaja\0305910,2,9,Zankaja\0312,0,0,9,Orgrimmar\0311507,19,1507,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301509,23,1509,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1509]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Zankaja? That's Dogran's mate, right?$B$BYeah, I've heard from him, but it's not the sort of news we should let get back to her...$B$BNo, he's not dead. But he is injured and a prisoner of the quilboar.\030My mate, Dogran, was recently sent to the Crossroads for duty. It was a promotion, and he was very proud.$B$BI was sad, of course, but I didn't let him know that. And worried, too. The Barrens is a more dangerous place than Orgrimmar, and I feared the worst.$B$BNow it's been a week after he should have returned, and I have received no word from him...$B$BPerhaps you could go to the Crossroads and see if they have any news? He worked with Gazrog, who should still be stationed there.\030Speak with Gazrog at the Crossroads.\030\030News of Dogran\0312,1,62,2,257,1,5910\0302,64,105,2,257,1,5910\0302,110,162,2,257,1,5910\0302,164,180,2,257,1,5910\0302,182,258,2,257,1,5910\0302,263,353,2,257,1,5910\0302,358,426,2,257,4,5910\0302,428,486,2,257,1,5910\0303,1,36,2,384,1,5910\0301,1,8,4,272,2,3464\0301,10,37,4,272,2,3464\0301,42,130,4,272,1,3464\0301,135,152,4,272,1,3464\0301,154,202,4,272,1,3464\0313464,2,8,Gazrog\0303464,2,9,Gazrog\0305910,4,10,Zankaja\0312,0,0,1,Crossroads\0302,0,0,7,Crossroads\0302,0,0,9,Crossroads\0311508,19,1508,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301510,23,1510,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[151]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you so much, $N! Poor Old Blanchy will be so happy!\030Poor Old Blanchy!  Such a tired beast after all the work we put her through. I fed her before we left the farm, but we weren't expecting the wagon to break on us. If you could bring her a few handfuls of oats from the fields, I'd be grateful.$B$BI bet you could find some around all of the farms in Westfall, if you can steer clear of those horrific machines that have taken over. There are several farms southwest of here.\030Verna Furlbrow in Westfall wants you to bring her 8 Handfuls of Oats.\030Old Blanchy is on her last leg. Did you happen to find any oats for her?\030Poor Old Blanchy\0312,1,17,2,257,1,238\0302,20,76,2,257,1,238\0302,78,162,2,265,1,238\0302,164,242,2,257,4,238\0302,247,380,2,257,4,238\0302,382,423,2,257,1,238\0303,1,69,2,386,1,238\0301,1,22,4,272,1,238\0301,24,57,4,272,3,238\0304,1,31,3,256,1,238\0304,33,72,3,256,2,238\031582,2,1,Old Blanchy\030238,2,7,Verna Furlbrow\030582,4,9,Old Blanchy\030582,3,10,Old Blanchy\0312,40,1436,0,\0302,0,0,5,Westfall\0302,0,0,7,Westfall\031\031ITEM,1528,OBJECTIVE,8,15,",[1510]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Another $R, eh? I hope you haven't come for the other. He didn't make it. Those goblins did him in good.$B$BHe said he needed a healing draught, but not much else.\030He was stationed at Camp Taurajo, where we've been trying to weed out the quilboar. He led a few grunts to one of their camps, where he was hurt bad. The others made it back and tried to rescue him. He was in bad shape, his wounds festered, so they were afraid to move him without patching him up first.$B$BThey sent a message here, requesting a healing draught from the trolls at the Malaka'jin at the base of the Stonetalon Mountains. We sent someone to get it, but they haven't returned yet.\030Speak with Ken'zigla at the Malaka'jin.\030\030News of Dogran\0312,1,83,2,257,1,3464\0302,85,149,2,257,1,3464\0302,151,198,2,267,1,3464\0302,200,303,2,257,1,3464\0302,308,436,2,257,1,3464\0302,438,494,2,257,1,3464\0303,1,39,2,384,1,3464\0301,1,15,4,272,2,4197\0301,17,54,4,274,3,4197\0301,56,73,4,272,1,4197\0301,75,104,4,272,1,4197\0301,109,163,4,272,1,4197\0314197,2,7,Ken'zigla\0312,0,0,1,Camp Taurajo\0302,0,0,5,Malaka'jin\0302,0,0,7,Malaka'jin\0311509,19,1509,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301511,23,1511,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1511]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well, it's about time! Dogran has been dying out there, waiting for this.$B$BWe need to get this out to him right away, but most of the grunts stationed here are out on a foraging mission.\030I figured there might be another coming to get the draught, so I prepared it anyways.$B$BHere you go, $n. Mind you, you should only give half of it to him! That will give him enough strength to move without bleeding himself dry. Wait a night, then give him the other half.$B$BAnyways, you'll want to bring this to Logmar at Camp Taurajo. From what the first one told me, he should have an idea where this Dogran is.\030Bring Ken'zigla's Draught to Grunt Logmar at Camp Taurajo.\030Yes, what is it?\030Ken'zigla's Draught\0312,1,85,2,257,4,4197\0302,90,105,2,257,1,4197\0302,107,155,2,257,1,4197\0302,157,228,2,257,3,4197\0302,230,272,2,257,1,4197\0302,277,337,2,259,1,4197\0302,339,415,2,257,1,4197\0303,1,58,2,384,1,4197\0301,1,22,4,272,1,5911\0301,24,73,4,272,1,5911\0301,78,188,4,274,1,5911\0304,1,16,3,256,2,5911\0315911,2,8,Grunt Logmar\0312,0,0,6,Logmar\0302,0,0,6,Camp Taurajo\0302,0,0,8,Grunt Logmar\0302,0,0,8,Camp Taurajo\0311510,19,1510,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301515,23,1515,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1512]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031If you tell me that this will suffice, then I trust you, $N. Allow me to clean it though... Pristine and shining, it may be even more enticing to a succubus.\030Zankaja is young and beautiful. To be chained to an invalid... I will not allow her to suffer that injustice.$B$BLeave me, $n. And thank you. I may end my life in glorious battle, instead of a lifeless husk.$B$BAnd please, I would ask you not to tell my mate of this... I do not want guilt on her conscience.\030Bring the Dirt-caked Pendant to Gan'rul Bloodeye in Orgrimmar.\030You have returned. Are you ready to battle a succubus?\030Love's Gift\0312,1,31,2,257,1,5908\0302,33,62,2,257,1,5908\0302,64,109,2,261,3,5908\0302,114,126,2,257,1,5908\0302,128,141,2,257,1,5908\0302,143,207,2,261,1,5908\0302,212,269,2,257,4,5908\0302,271,308,2,259,1,5908\0303,1,62,2,384,1,5908\0301,1,60,4,272,4,5875\0301,62,91,4,272,1,5875\0301,93,157,4,272,1,5875\0304,1,18,3,256,1,5875\0304,20,54,3,260,2,5875\0315910,2,1,Zankaja\0305875,2,9,Gan'rul Bloodeye\0301863,4,12,Succubus\0301863,3,14,Succubus\0312,0,0,9,Gan'rul Bloodeye\0302,0,0,9,Orgrimmar\0311515,19,1515,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301513,23,1513,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1513]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Success! Be sure I expected nothing less from my star pupil.$B$BYou have proven your worth, and gladly will I show you the method of summoning your subdued succubus. Go now, you have much to learn, and when next I see you, I will expect you to have found true mastery over your succubus.$B$BLeave the sorrow of Dogran and Zankaja to those of us who are longer in years, but remember it, and hold it as protection against the wiles of the dark power you have learned to summon today.\030Take this to the summoning circle in Neeru's tent, $n. Summon forth a foul succubus, then show it your mastery. I believe in the strength of your magic. As always, though, be wary, for pride and overconfidence has overcome many a promising warlock.$B$BWhen you have defeated it, return the pendant to me so that I might deliver the news to Zankaja.\030Using Dogran's Pendant, summon and subdue a succubus, then return Dogran's Pendant to Gan'rul Bloodeye in Orgrimmar.\030When I look upon a succubus, my heart begins to soar... But at the same time, I can almost sense my soul's ebb, drifting away like the tides.$B$BBe wary, my friend.\030The Binding\0312,1,54,2,257,1,5875\0302,56,111,2,257,1,5875\0302,113,152,2,257,4,5875\0302,154,248,2,257,1,5875\0302,253,348,2,259,4,5875\0303,1,116,2,384,1,5875\0301,1,8,4,272,1,5875\0301,10,60,4,272,1,5875\0301,65,165,4,272,3,5875\0301,167,287,4,272,3,5875\0301,292,482,4,272,1,5875\0304,1,55,3,256,1,5875\0304,57,141,3,256,1,5875\0304,146,164,3,256,1,5875\0311863,2,2,Succubus\0305910,2,5,Zankaja\0301863,2,6,Succubus\0305875,2,6,Gan'rul Bloodeye\0301863,4,9,Succubus\0301863,4,10,Succubus\0305910,4,11,Zankaja\0301863,3,12,Succubus\0312,0,0,1,Neeru's\0302,0,0,5,Zankaja\0302,0,0,6,Gan'rul Bloodeye\0302,0,0,6,Orgrimmar\0311512,19,1512,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,5677,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Summoned Succubus",[1514]="PARTIAL\031characters,consequences,loreConnections,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You apply two Cenarion plant salves to the windblossom. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.\030\030\030You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a windblossom plant. The berries that hang from the plant appear rotten and poisonous. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.\030Corrupted Windblossom\0311,1,55,4,272,1,0\0301,57,150,4,276,1,0\0304,1,85,3,260,1,0\0304,87,151,3,256,1,0\0304,153,233,3,258,4,0\031\0312,361,1448,0,\031\031OBJECT,173327,GIVER,?,9,Corrupted Windblossom\030OBJECT,173327,FINISHER,?,12,Corrupted Windblossom\030ITEM,11516,OBJECTIVE,2,15,",[1515]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Foul tasting brew...$B$BI can feel the strength in me now, enough to hobble away... But my leg, I will have lost it for the rest of my life. My arm, too.\030You've made it this far, so if you want to see this through to the end, I won't stop you. I can't spare you any additional manpower though, you'll be on your own.$B$BDogran is being held in a quilboar camp to the north of here. Look for a group of two huts. He'll be heavily guarded--that is, if they haven't killed him yet, or he hasn't succumbed to his wounds.$B$BGood luck.\030Bring Ken'zigla's Draught to Dogran in the Barrens.\030Urrrghhhh...\030Dogran's Captivity\0312,1,89,2,259,4,5911\0302,91,162,2,257,1,5911\0302,167,227,2,257,1,5911\0302,229,257,2,257,1,5911\0302,259,362,2,257,4,5911\0302,367,376,2,257,1,5911\0303,1,51,2,384,1,5911\0301,1,20,4,272,1,5908\0301,25,83,4,272,1,5908\0301,85,140,4,276,3,5908\0301,142,153,4,272,1,5908\0304,1,12,3,256,1,5908\031\0312,0,0,7,Dogran\0302,0,0,7,Barrens\0311511,19,1511,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301512,23,1512,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1516]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Excellent. Your success shows that you are prepared.$B$BOf all the elements, earth represents the foundation of all things. It is your strength, your stamina, and your patience. Earth will protect you, but only if shown the proper respect. Like the other elements, even earth can be fickle. Earth is the basis for life, and by observing its laws, you will gain greater wisdom. Never forget the secrets earth shares with you.$B$BI shall make a sapta for you now, and by accepting it, you will realize your path.\030The time is now, young $c. You've grown strong and your spirit endures like the earth. Following the shaman's path shows you have wisdom before even proving yourself.$B$BThe element of earth will guide your destiny, becoming part of you if you are ready. But you must stand before the earth itself. If you are ready, then you will see things only shaman know of.$B$BSeek out the Felstalkers to the north, and take from them two of their hooves. Return to me then, and we shall speak more of your future.$B\030Bring 2 Felstalker Hooves to Canaga Earthcaller in the Valley of Trials.\030Patience is earth's greatest virtue. The earth witnesses the cycle of all things: the mountains becoming deserts; rivers becoming canyons. The earth is the most stubborn and wise of all the elements and it does not tolerate impatience.$B$BThe earth beckons you now because a time of conflict draws near. When you return to me successful, then you shall be that much closer to being made whole.$B$BOthers will be envious of your wisdom and hate you for their ignorance.\030Call of Earth\0312,1,26,2,257,1,5887\0302,28,86,2,257,1,5887\0302,88,166,2,257,1,5887\0302,171,254,2,257,4,5887\0302,256,298,2,257,1,5887\0302,300,362,2,257,4,5887\0302,367,444,2,257,1,5887\0302,446,503,2,257,3,5887\0303,1,72,2,384,1,5887\0301,1,10,4,272,1,5887\0301,12,52,4,272,1,5887\0301,57,123,4,272,1,5887\0301,125,177,4,272,1,5887\0301,179,239,4,284,4,5887\0301,241,290,4,272,1,5887\0301,292,376,4,272,3,5887\0301,378,424,4,272,1,5887\0301,429,510,4,272,3,5887\0304,1,36,3,256,1,5887\0304,38,138,3,256,1,5887\0304,140,235,3,256,1,5887\0304,240,303,3,258,1,5887\0304,305,393,3,256,3,5887\0304,398,468,3,256,3,5887\0313102,2,9,Felstalker\0305887,2,9,Canaga Earthcaller\0312,0,0,9,Canaga Earthcaller\0302,0,0,9,Valley of Trials\0311517,23,1517,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6640,OBJECTIVE,2,15,",[1517]="PARTIAL\031consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah... $N... pleased is the earth to have you here.$B$BBound together in body and spirit, you will go forward knowing that the mountains are your strength; the plains, your patience; and the world itself your essence.$B$BStanding before the earth humbly is all that is required of you for you to pass this rite. But the others are not as passive. They may be chaotic and often violent, but such is the nature of the elements. Dual natures opposing one another, you must come to learn these things intricately.\030A sapta is a drink created to bind our spirits to the elements. Fused with magic, the potion will allow the strong willed to see the elements as no one else can. Your spirit will be connected to the element the sapta was created for, and only a select few shaman know the recipe.$B$BThe sapta is always drunk in a holy place, and never anywhere else--remember that.$B$BSeek out Spirit Rock southwest of here--it is found at the end of the Hidden Path. Drink your sapta there, and... well, you shall see.\030Find Spirit Rock and drink the Earth Sapta.\030\030Call of Earth\0312,1,63,2,257,1,5887\0302,65,161,2,257,3,5887\0302,163,279,2,257,3,5887\0302,284,365,2,257,1,5887\0302,370,451,2,257,1,5887\0302,453,482,2,257,1,5887\0302,484,503,2,257,3,5887\0303,1,43,2,384,1,5887\0301,13,50,4,272,1,5891\0301,55,216,4,276,3,5891\0301,221,310,4,272,1,5891\0301,312,345,4,272,1,5891\0301,347,424,4,272,1,5891\0301,426,508,4,272,1,5891\031\031\0311516,19,1516,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301518,23,1518,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1518]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Excellent!$B$BThe totem I will craft for you is more than a symbol of your status among $C--it has abilities beyond that. One use of the totem is as a focus for spells. Those spells are tied to the earth, and as you earn greater and greater wisdom, more of the earth's abilities will be made accessible to you.$B$BThe trainers will know when you are ready for greater knowledge.$B$BBut for now, take this earth totem, and a scroll to teach you your first ability.\030Take this rough quartz from me and bring it to Canaga Earthcaller as proof of our meeting. He will craft a totem for you, and this pebble will be the heart of it. As small as it may seem, you will come to find that size does not matter, and that even the smallest of things can outlast many others.$B$BBe patient, $N. Remain strong. And seek wisdom. This is what earth asks of you. In the end, you shall become one with the earth--respect it as it shall respect you.\030Bring the Rough Quartz to Canaga Earthcaller in the Valley of Trials.\030I wish to be the first to welcome you fully to the first of four paths that will forever lead you in your destiny.$B$BIf you have the stone the earth gave to you, I will give you the totem it promised.$B$BIf not, then be gone with you until you have found your way.\030Call of Earth\0312,1,90,2,257,1,5891\0302,92,162,2,257,3,5891\0302,164,298,2,257,4,5891\0302,303,317,2,257,1,5891\0302,319,332,2,257,1,5891\0302,334,349,2,259,1,5891\0302,351,381,2,257,1,5891\0302,383,466,2,257,3,5891\0303,1,69,2,384,1,5891\0301,1,10,4,272,1,5887\0301,15,121,4,272,3,5887\0301,123,168,4,272,1,5887\0301,170,310,4,272,3,5887\0301,315,378,4,272,3,5887\0301,383,463,4,272,1,5887\0304,1,114,3,258,3,5887\0304,119,201,3,256,4,5887\0304,206,265,3,256,4,5887\0315887,2,1,Canaga Earthcaller\0305887,2,9,Canaga Earthcaller\0312,0,0,1,Canaga Earthcaller\0302,0,0,9,Canaga Earthcaller\0302,0,0,9,Valley of Trials\0311517,19,1517,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1519]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Good, $N. Your return here signifies that you are indeed prepared for the next step.$B$BOf all the elements, earth represents the foundation of all things. It is your strength, your stamina, and your patience. The Earth Mother will protect you, but only if you show her proper respect. She is the basis for life, and by observing her laws, you will gain a greater wisdom. Never forget the secrets she shares with you.$B$BI shall make your sapta for you now, and by accepting it, a new path will open before you.\030The time has come, young $c. Your body ages and grows strong, and your spirit endures like the earth. I see it within you-you have wisdom already.$B$BThe earth guides our people, and it speaks to us, as it will to you in time. But you must be tested. If you are ready, then you shall see things only our kind know of.$B$BSeek out the Bristleback shamans in their ravine to the east, and take from them a salve they use in their rituals. Return to me only when you have enough for your own potion.\030Bring 2 applications of Ritual Salve to Seer Ravenfeather in Camp Narache.\030The earth is patient, and will wait for you until you are ready because she knows in time all things erode and are reborn. It is the cycle of things. Mountains become deserts. Rivers become canyons. The earth is the most stubborn and wise of all the elements.$B$BYou must learn patience and stamina above all things. The earth calls for you now because she feels you are ready. Consider this your rebirth if you succeed. You will never be able to go back to ignorance afterwards.\030Call of Earth\0312,1,28,2,257,1,5888\0302,30,101,2,257,1,5888\0302,103,146,2,257,1,5888\0302,151,226,2,257,3,5888\0302,228,250,2,257,1,5888\0302,252,317,2,257,4,5888\0302,322,436,2,257,1,5888\0302,438,496,2,257,1,5888\0303,1,74,2,384,1,5888\0301,1,9,4,272,1,5888\0301,11,84,4,272,1,5888\0301,89,155,4,272,1,5888\0301,157,209,4,272,1,5888\0301,211,285,4,284,4,5888\0301,287,371,4,272,3,5888\0301,373,417,4,272,1,5888\0301,422,511,4,272,3,5888\0304,1,122,3,258,3,5888\0304,124,149,3,256,1,5888\0304,151,175,3,256,1,5888\0304,177,198,3,256,1,5888\0304,200,259,3,256,1,5888\0304,264,316,3,256,1,5888\0304,318,377,3,258,1,5888\0304,379,420,3,256,4,5888\0304,422,479,3,256,3,5888\0315888,2,9,Seer Ravenfeather\0312,0,0,9,Seer Ravenfeather\0302,0,0,9,Camp Narache\0311520,23,1520,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6634,OBJECTIVE,2,15,",[152]="PARTIAL\031conflict,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $N. You have quite a knack for combat. Thanks to you the Coast of Westfall is a safer place.\030You probably noticed all of the shipwrecks along the coast.  The Great Sea is treacherous indeed.  The coast of Westfall needs to be kept clear, so that if sailors find their way to our beaches, they are safe.  The Murlocs are trouble though.$B$BKill 7 Tidehunters, 7 Warriors, 7 Oracles and 7 Coastrunners and I will see to it that you are rewarded.\030Kill 7 Tidehunters, 7 Warriors, 7 Oracles and 7 Coastrunners and return to Captain Grayson at the Westfall Lighthouse.\030Kill 7 Tidehunters, 7 Warriors, 7 Oracles and 7 Coastrunners and I will see to it that you are rewarded.\030The Coast Isn't Clear\0312,1,59,2,257,1,392\0302,62,97,2,257,1,392\0302,100,209,2,259,4,392\0302,212,242,2,257,1,392\0302,247,350,2,257,3,392\0303,1,118,2,384,1,392\0301,1,14,4,272,1,392\0301,16,49,4,272,1,392\0301,51,103,4,304,1,392\0304,1,104,3,256,3,392\031392,2,6,Captain Grayson\0312,40,1436,0,\0302,0,0,6,Captain Grayson\0302,0,0,6,Westfall Lighthouse\031\031NPC,126,OBJECTIVE,7,13,Murloc Coastrunner\030NPC,171,OBJECTIVE,7,13,Murloc Warrior\030NPC,127,OBJECTIVE,7,13,Murloc Tidehunter\030NPC,517,OBJECTIVE,7,13,Murloc Oracle",[1520]="PARTIAL\031consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah... $N... pleased is the earth to have you here.$B$BBound together in body and spirit, you will go forward knowing that the mountains are your strength; the plains, your patience; and the world itself your essence.$B$BStanding before the earth humbly is all that is required of you for you to pass this rite. But the others are not as passive. They may be chaotic and often violent, but such is the nature of the elements. Dual natures opposing one another, you must come to learn these things intricately.\030A sapta is a drink created to bind our spirits to the elements. Fused with magic, the potion will allow the open minded to see the elements as no one has seen them before. Your spirit will forever be tied to the element the sapta was created for, and only a select few of our kind know the secrets of its creation.$B$BThe sapta is always imbibed in a holy place, and never anywhere else.$B$BSeek out the shaman shrine to the east of here and drink of the sapta.\030Find Kodo Rock and drink the Earth Sapta.\030\030Call of Earth\0312,1,63,2,257,1,5888\0302,65,171,2,257,3,5888\0302,173,314,2,257,3,5888\0302,319,387,2,257,1,5888\0302,392,461,2,257,1,5888\0303,1,41,2,384,1,5888\0301,13,50,4,272,1,5891\0301,55,216,4,276,3,5891\0301,221,310,4,272,1,5891\0301,312,345,4,272,1,5891\0301,347,424,4,272,1,5891\0301,426,508,4,272,1,5891\031\031\0311519,19,1519,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301521,23,1521,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1521]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Splendid.$B$BThe totem I will craft for you is more than a symbol--it has abilities beyond that. One use of the totem is a focus for spells. Those spells are tied to the earth, and as you earn greater and greater wisdom, more of the earth's abilities will be made accessible to you. Trainers found throughout Kalimdor will know when you are ready for greater knowledge and will let you know as much when you visit them.$B$BBut for now, take this earth totem, and a scroll to teach you your first ability.\030Take this rough quartz from me and bring it to Seer Ravenfeather as proof of our meeting. She will craft a totem for you, and this pebble will be the heart of it. As small as it may seem, you will come to find that size does not matter, and that even the smallest of things can outlast mountains.$B$BBe patient, $N. Remain strong. And seek wisdom. This is what earth asks of you. In the end, you shall become one with the earth--respect it as it shall respect you.\030Bring the Rough Quartz to Seer Ravenfeather in Camp Narache.\030Greetings, $N. You would not return to me if you had not accomplished your task. May I be the first to welcome you fully to the first path of four that will forever rule your travels.$B$BIf you have the stone the earth gave to you, I will give you the totem it promised. If not, then I pity you. There is much pride to be had when you've fully dedicated yourself to the elements.\030Call of Earth\0312,1,89,2,257,1,5891\0302,91,162,2,257,3,5891\0302,164,296,2,257,4,5891\0302,301,315,2,257,1,5891\0302,317,330,2,257,1,5891\0302,332,347,2,259,1,5891\0302,349,379,2,257,1,5891\0302,381,464,2,257,3,5891\0303,1,60,2,384,1,5891\0301,1,9,4,272,1,5888\0301,14,96,4,272,3,5888\0301,98,140,4,272,1,5888\0301,142,282,4,272,3,5888\0301,284,419,4,272,3,5888\0301,424,504,4,272,1,5888\0304,1,14,3,256,1,5888\0304,16,80,3,256,4,5888\0304,82,183,3,256,3,5888\0304,188,270,3,256,4,5888\0304,272,295,3,256,4,5888\0304,297,379,3,256,1,5888\0315888,2,1,Seer Ravenfeather\0305888,2,9,Seer Ravenfeather\0312,0,0,1,Seer Ravenfeather\0302,0,0,9,Seer Ravenfeather\0302,0,0,9,Camp Narache\0311520,19,1520,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1522]="PARTIAL\031conflict,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hmmm, Searn sent you to me, did he?$B$BWell then, Searn could always be trusted, so that must mean you're ready to take part of the next sapta--the sapta of fire.$B$BI see it in your eyes already, the burning, the desire. You've tasted power, and now you're ready for more of it. Patience, $N. Remember what earth taught you. Power and destruction will come easily, but you must still know when to stay your hand.\030Fire be witcha, mon. I see you be strong in da ways of earth already, an' me tinkin' you be ready to talk to Kranal.$B$BKranal live north of da Crossroads in da Barrens. He be strong in da ways of da elements and can teach ya da ways of fire... if you tink you be ready.$B$BHe be easy ta find, just don' go too far--ya go too far an' ya find yerself in da elves' lands.\030Find Kranal Fiss in the Barrens.\030\030Call of Fire\0312,1,20,2,257,1,5892\0302,22,116,2,257,1,5892\0302,121,169,2,257,1,5892\0302,171,244,2,257,1,5892\0302,246,270,2,257,4,5892\0302,275,369,2,257,1,5892\0303,1,32,2,384,1,5892\0301,1,35,4,272,2,5907\0301,40,162,4,274,4,5907\0301,167,221,4,274,1,5907\0301,223,279,4,304,1,5907\0301,281,293,4,272,1,5907\0301,295,325,4,272,1,5907\0301,327,413,4,272,3,5907\0315907,2,7,Kranal Fiss\0312,0,0,2,Kranal\0302,0,0,7,Barrens\0311523,22,1523,UNKNOWN\0302983,22,2983,UNKNOWN\0302984,22,2984,UNKNOWN\0301524,23,1524,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301524,24,1524,UNKNOWN\031",[1523]="PARTIAL\031conflict,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hmmm, Narm sent you to me, did he?$B$BWell then, Narm could always be trusted, so that must mean you're ready to take part of the next sapta--the sapta of fire.$B$BI see it in your eyes already, the burning, the desire. You've tasted power, and now you're ready for more of it. Patience, $N. Remember what earth taught you. Power and destruction will come easily, but you must still know when to stay your hand.\030Long has it been since you were last tested, $N. You have shown patience thus far in your studies, but the time has come for you to learn more. The time has come for you to learn about destruction... and chaos. The element of fire is yours for the understanding, if you're prepared to pay for it.$B$BSeek out Kranal Fiss in the Barrens. He lives in a small dwelling north of the Crossroads, but be mindful, if you've reached the night elf lands, you've gone too far.\030Find Kranal Fiss in the Barrens.\030\030Call of Fire\0312,1,48,2,257,1,3032\0302,50,143,2,257,1,3032\0302,145,199,2,257,1,3032\0302,201,210,2,257,1,3032\0302,212,296,2,257,4,3032\0302,301,336,2,257,1,3032\0302,338,466,2,257,4,3032\0303,1,32,2,384,1,3032\0301,1,34,4,272,2,5907\0301,39,160,4,274,4,5907\0301,165,219,4,274,1,5907\0301,221,277,4,304,1,5907\0301,279,291,4,272,1,5907\0301,293,323,4,272,1,5907\0301,325,411,4,272,3,5907\0315907,2,6,Kranal Fiss\0305907,2,8,Kranal Fiss\0312,0,0,6,Barrens\0302,0,0,7,Crossroads\0302,0,0,8,Barrens\0311522,22,1522,UNKNOWN\0302983,22,2983,UNKNOWN\0302984,22,2984,UNKNOWN\0301524,23,1524,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301524,24,1524,UNKNOWN\031",[1524]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, my mistake, $N. I apologize. I did not realize you possessed the Torch. I am pleased to make your acquaintance.$B$BMany adventurers find their way here while looking for lost treasure or the promise of mystical creatures to slay, only to be turned away from a seemingly empty shrine. But we know the truth, do we not, $N?$B$BThis shrine holds a greater secret from the mundane members of the Horde. To us, it is sacred.\030You are powerful enough to wield the totem of fire, but that does not mean you are ready.$B$BAlong the Southfury River in Durotar, before the Great Sea, lies a hidden trail to one of the highest peaks in the land. Find your way to the top and you shall find one of our holy shrines watched over by Telf Joolam--the Shrine of the Dormant Flame.$B$BTake this torch to him--it marks that you attempt to tame fire. Return it to me aflame by the brazier at the shrine and I will see you are given the totem of fire.\030Bring the Torch of the Dormant Flame to Telf Joolam in Durotar.\030Greetin's, $N. You've found yerself at the Shrine of the Dormant Flame. Only those knowledgeable enough in the shamanistic arts will ever learn the secrets of this place and the power it holds. I'm sorry you made the trip all this way, only to be turned back now--the journey up here is far from safe after all--but I am the keeper of the shrine, and I cannot allow just anyone to wander around here.\030Call of Fire\0312,1,89,2,257,1,5907\0302,94,213,2,257,1,5907\0302,215,343,2,257,3,5907\0302,348,410,2,257,1,5907\0302,412,510,2,257,3,5907\0303,1,63,2,384,1,5907\0301,1,19,4,272,1,5900\0301,21,32,4,272,1,5900\0301,34,75,4,272,1,5900\0301,77,115,4,272,1,5900\0301,120,287,4,276,1,5900\0301,289,325,4,272,2,5900\0301,330,402,4,272,1,5900\0301,404,423,4,272,1,5900\0304,1,14,3,256,1,5900\0304,16,71,3,256,1,5900\0304,73,193,3,256,3,5900\0304,195,400,3,264,1,5900\0315900,2,3,Telf Joolam\0305900,2,6,Telf Joolam\0312,0,0,2,Durotar\0302,0,0,6,Telf Joolam\0302,0,0,6,Durotar\0303,0,0,16,Shrine of the Dormant Flame\0311525,23,1525,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1525]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031These will do nicely, $N.$B$BFire is more than chaos and destruction--do well to remember that. It is also about life, and creation. All things are tied together in such a way. Forces oppose one another, but at the same time, one cannot exist without the other. Both extinguish one another, but also give one another meaning. Always remember this.$B$BUsing different types of magic in conjunction with one another will show not only true skill, but great wisdom.\030But you did not come here for a history lesson, did you? You came for the Eternal Flame and fire totem.$B$BThe first step is to create a sapta and bind you to the flame.$B$BI can create the fire sapta for you if you bring me two items. The first is fire tar, a simple item usually carried by Razormane spellcasters in eastern Barrens.$B$BThe second item will be more dangerous: a reagent pouch from one of the cultists of the Burning Blade. You can find them in a cave above the ravines northeast of Razor Hill.\030Bring 1 Fire Tar and 1 Reagent Pouch to Telf Joolam in Durotar.\030I have enough ingredients for a sapta of fire if you can find the reagent pouch and some fire tar. The Burning Blade fanatics carry the proper components for most of their spells in those pouches, and usually have enough of the items I need that we will not have to search much farther for anything else.$B$BThe saptas are always made from ingredients that are closely tied to their respective elements. It makes our work easier because of the warlocks' ties to fire.\030Call of Fire\0312,1,56,2,321,2,5900\0302,58,103,2,257,1,5900\0302,108,169,2,257,1,5900\0302,174,235,2,257,4,5900\0302,237,334,2,257,1,5900\0302,339,440,2,257,3,5900\0302,442,511,2,257,1,5900\0303,1,63,2,384,1,5900\0301,1,25,4,272,3,5900\0301,30,95,4,272,1,5900\0301,97,132,4,272,1,5900\0301,134,176,4,272,1,5900\0301,178,261,4,272,1,5900\0301,263,325,4,272,1,5900\0301,327,347,4,272,1,5900\0301,352,462,4,272,3,5900\0304,1,98,3,256,4,5900\0304,100,304,3,258,3,5900\0304,309,403,3,256,1,5900\0304,405,467,3,258,1,5900\0315900,2,8,Telf Joolam\0312,0,0,8,Telf Joolam\0302,0,0,8,Durotar\0311524,19,1524,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301526,23,1526,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5026,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,6652,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1526]="PARTIAL\031consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A white hot flame ignites within the bowl as you place the ember within. You can feel the magical effects of the sapta coursing through your body and the fire dances rhythmically before you.$B$BYou place the top of the torch within the basin, and it immediately catches on fire.\030The fire sapta is finished. The time has come for you to face the flame. Use the sapta at the shrine and head to the top of the mountain to face the manifestation there. He will not attack until you are ready, but he will realize you are able to see him.$B$BStrike him down swiftly, $N, for he shall only grow in power the longer you take to slay him. Once he is defeated, place his glowing embers within the brazier and light the torch.\030Defeat the Minor Manifestation of Fire, and place the Glowing Ember in the brazier atop the Shrine of Eternal Flame.\030The brazier stands about a third your height, and looks normal, save for the inscriptions along its smooth metal rails. The metal shows no signs of wear from the weather, and the bowl seated at the top of it feels cool to the touch.\030Call of Fire\0312,1,27,2,257,1,5900\0302,29,72,2,257,1,5900\0302,74,169,2,257,1,5900\0302,171,254,2,261,3,5900\0302,259,351,2,257,3,5900\0302,353,437,2,257,1,5900\0303,1,116,2,384,1,5900\0301,1,72,4,272,1,0\0301,74,190,4,272,1,0\0301,195,278,4,272,1,0\0304,1,119,3,264,1,0\0304,121,232,3,256,1,0\0315893,2,7,Minor Manifestation of Fire\0307266,2,7,Ember\0307266,4,8,Ember\031\0311525,19,1525,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301527,23,1527,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,61934,FINISHER,?,12,Brazier of the Dormant Flame\030ITEM,6655,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1527]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Your spirit burns brighter than any torch I've ever seen, $N, and for that, you should be proud.$B$BIf you continue down this path, the elements will be yours to command, and our brethren will look to you for guidance and wisdom. Let me be the first to congratulate you and present to you your newest totem.\030Torch firmly in hand, you turn away from the brazier and look out over Durotar. You feel an excitement tugging at your spirit as the wind picks up and forces the flame to dance violently.$B$BYou start off down the path back to the Barrens in search of Kranal Fiss.\030Bring the Torch of Eternal Flame to Kranal Fiss in the Barrens.\030Yes, $N? What do you have there?\030Call of Fire\0312,1,79,2,257,1,0\0302,81,187,2,257,1,0\0302,192,264,2,257,1,0\0303,1,63,2,384,1,0\0301,1,96,4,272,1,5907\0301,101,229,4,272,4,5907\0301,231,307,4,272,1,5907\0304,1,8,3,256,2,5907\0304,10,32,3,256,2,5907\0315907,2,3,Kranal Fiss\0305907,2,4,Kranal Fiss\03011045,4,5,Burns\0312,0,0,3,Barrens\0302,0,0,4,Kranal Fiss\0302,0,0,4,Barrens\0311526,19,1526,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,61934,GIVER,?,9,Brazier of the Dormant Flame",[1528]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The wind approaches you quickly from the horizon; the earth is steady beneath your feet; and your spirit is already warmed by fire--I would say it is time for you to learn about the purity of water.$B$BYour path has led you this far, and your spirit will give you the strength to carry on even further. But the first step is yours to take.\030Water be in ya future, mon. I see you be strong in da ways of fire already, an' me tinkin' you be ready to talk to Islen.$B$BIslen live along the coast of da Barrens. If ya head south along the Southfury River, ya canna miss her--look fer da big shark! She be strong in da ways of da elements and can teach ya da ways of water... if you tink you be ready.$B$BShe be easy ta find, just don' go too far south--she be jus' beyond Ratchet.\030Find Islen Waterseer in the Barrens.\030\030Call of Water\0312,1,27,2,257,1,5892\0302,29,121,2,257,1,5892\0302,126,166,2,257,1,5892\0302,168,252,2,257,4,5892\0302,254,329,2,257,1,5892\0302,331,355,2,257,4,5892\0302,360,435,2,257,1,5892\0303,1,36,2,384,1,5892\0301,1,198,4,272,4,5901\0301,203,302,4,272,3,5901\0301,304,339,4,272,1,5901\0315901,2,8,Islen Waterseer\0312,0,0,2,Islen\0302,0,0,8,Barrens\0311529,22,1529,UNKNOWN\0302985,22,2985,UNKNOWN\0302986,22,2986,UNKNOWN\0301530,23,1530,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301530,24,1530,UNKNOWN\031",[1529]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The wind approaches you quickly from the horizon; the earth is steady beneath your feet; and your spirit is already warmed by fire--I would say it is time for you to learn about the purity of water.$B$BYour path has led you this far, and your spirit will give you the strength to carry on even further. But the first step is yours to take.\030Long has it been since you were last tested, $N. You have shown patience thus far in your studies, but the time has come for you to learn more. The time has come for you to learn about the purity of water.$B$BSeek out Islen Waterseer in the Barrens. She is along the eastern coast, south of the Southfury River and Ratchet. You will find her there at her fishing hut. Good luck to you, $N.\030Find Islen Waterseer in the Barrens.\030\030Call of Water\0312,1,48,2,257,1,5906\0302,50,143,2,257,1,5906\0302,145,205,2,257,1,5906\0302,210,249,2,257,1,5906\0302,251,323,2,257,1,5906\0302,325,367,2,257,3,5906\0302,369,389,2,257,1,5906\0303,1,36,2,384,1,5906\0301,1,198,4,272,4,5901\0301,203,302,4,272,3,5901\0301,304,339,4,272,1,5901\0315901,2,4,Islen Waterseer\0305901,2,8,Islen Waterseer\0312,0,0,4,Barrens\0302,0,0,5,Southfury River\0302,0,0,8,Barrens\0311528,22,1528,UNKNOWN\0302985,22,2985,UNKNOWN\0302986,22,2986,UNKNOWN\0301530,23,1530,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301530,24,1530,UNKNOWN\031",[153]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Nice work, $R. Please accept one of these items as payment for all your hard work.\030The Defias Front is constantly shifting.  I've been following their movements for quite some time now.  On a side note, I've ascertained that many members of the gang can be tracked by the Red Leather Bandanas they wear.$B$BBring me 15 of these Bandanas and I'll see to it you are rewarded.\030Bring 15 Red Leather Bandanas to Scout Galiaan at Sentinel Hill.\030Bring me 15 red leather bandanas and I'll pay you well.\030Red Leather Bandanas\0312,1,40,2,257,1,878\0302,43,102,2,257,1,878\0302,105,220,2,257,1,878\0302,225,290,2,257,1,878\0303,1,64,2,384,1,878\0301,1,14,4,272,1,878\0301,16,82,4,272,1,878\0304,1,55,3,256,1,878\031878,2,5,Scout Galiaan\0312,40,1436,0,\0302,0,0,5,Scout Galiaan\0302,0,0,5,Sentinel Hill\031\031ITEM,829,OBJECTIVE,15,15,",[1530]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes?$B$BMmm. I have a feeling I know what you're going to ask me: what would possess someone to live out here in the deepest part of the Barrens, the threat of quilboar all around, and no protection? Well, we all have our reasons to justify why we act the way we do. The real question is, what brings a lowly $R to the deepest reaches of the Barrens to speak to a woman who obviously has no concern for her own well-being?$B$BI'm willing to bet we both know the answer to that.\030If there is one lesson you must learn of water, it is this: water means rebirth.$B$BIts power flows, erodes, and makes clean all manner of things. You will find its ability to heal and replenish incomparable, but only when it is pure.$B$BWhen you understand that water, when polluted, can devastate all that it touches, you will appreciate how vital a resource it is.$B$BIf you wish the water sapta, find Brine deep in Southern Barrens. Her home is continually molested by the quilboar there.\030Find Brine in Southern Barrens.\030\030Call of Water\0312,1,80,2,257,4,5901\0302,85,146,2,257,1,5901\0302,148,234,2,257,3,5901\0302,239,367,2,257,3,5901\0302,372,436,2,259,4,5901\0302,438,492,2,257,1,5901\0303,1,31,2,384,1,5901\0301,1,4,4,272,2,5899\0301,9,12,4,272,1,5899\0301,14,199,4,276,4,5899\0301,201,266,4,272,1,5899\0301,268,422,4,272,2,5899\0301,427,477,4,272,1,5899\0315899,2,5,Brine\0305899,2,7,Brine\0312,0,0,5,Southern Barrens\0302,0,0,7,Southern Barrens\0311535,23,1535,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1531]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031For the time being. I shall give you what you need to focus your spells and to call upon the spirits of air. Take this totem, and when you are ready, train with me some more.\030You be makin' headway now, mon. Your be ready to prove yerself worthy of the air totem, but first, ya must fin' Prate Cloudseer in Thousand Needles. She be willin' ta tell ya how to get yer air totem if ya treat her wit enough respect.$B$BHead south through the Barrens, and after ya reach Thousand Needles, head east. You'll find her hiddin' in a hole wit' her boyfriend--haha, don' tell her I be dissin' her none--she not take it too kindly.\030Find Prate Cloudseer in Thousand Needles.\030\030Call of Air\0312,1,31,2,257,1,5892\0302,33,148,2,257,1,5892\0302,150,235,2,257,4,5892\0302,240,318,2,257,1,5892\0302,320,443,2,257,1,5892\0303,1,41,2,384,1,5892\0301,1,19,4,272,1,5905\0301,21,108,4,274,3,5905\0301,110,174,4,272,1,5905\0315905,2,2,Prate Cloudseer\0305905,2,6,Prate Cloudseer\0312,0,0,2,Thousand Needles\0302,0,0,6,Thousand Needles\0311532,22,1532,UNKNOWN\031",[1532]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031For the time being. I shall give you what you need to focus your spells and to call upon the spirits of air. Take this totem, and when you are ready, train with me some more.\030The winds of Kalimdor rush to meet you and you shall be counted among some of our most powerful $g brothers:sisters;. I am proud to see you have come this far and have such a promising future.$B$BThe element of air is a difficult one to control, but I have faith that your skills will overcome any obstacles that are placed in front of you.$B$BHead to the very south of the Barrens, and enter Thousand Needles. It is there, far to the east, that you will find Prate Cloudseer. She will teach you more.\030Find Prate Cloudseer in Thousand Needles.\030\030Call of Air\0312,1,117,2,257,3,5906\0302,119,192,2,257,1,5906\0302,197,340,2,257,3,5906\0302,345,410,2,257,1,5906\0302,412,476,2,257,3,5906\0302,478,501,2,257,3,5906\0303,1,41,2,384,1,5906\0301,1,19,4,272,1,5905\0301,21,108,4,274,3,5905\0301,110,174,4,272,1,5905\0315905,2,5,Prate Cloudseer\0305905,2,7,Prate Cloudseer\0312,0,0,4,Barrens\0302,0,0,7,Thousand Needles\0311531,22,1531,UNKNOWN\031",[1534]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Wonderful, $N. With all three samples gathered, I can create for you a vial of the purest water any living creature will find. It will be used in the next steps of your rite of passage.$B$BI am pleased to count you among our kind, $N. You do all $C proud, and I look forward to hearing about your exploits in the future.\030Take this waterskin and head deep into the lush forest the night elves call Ashenvale. It is to the far north of the Barrens.$B$BOnce you've entered the forest, travel west. Along the mountains that separate Stonetalon and Ashenvale, and beyond Lake Mystral, you will find a holy place: the Ruins of Stardust. At the center of the lake you will find a small fountain.$B$BBring me a sample of the fountain's water. It will be the final component you'll need before I send you back to Islen.\030Fill the Empty Blue Waterskin at the Ruins of Stardust in Ashenvale and return to Brine in the Barrens.\030Do you have the water yet, $N? Tales say the ruins were protected by large creatures of nature that do not care for visitors, but those could be myths to scare off the enemies of the night elves.$B$BRegardless, be careful.\030Call of Water\0312,1,86,2,257,1,5899\0302,88,125,2,257,1,5899\0302,130,173,2,257,1,5899\0302,175,309,2,321,3,5899\0302,311,367,2,257,3,5899\0302,372,413,2,257,1,5899\0302,415,489,2,259,3,5899\0303,1,103,2,448,1,5899\0301,1,14,4,272,1,5899\0301,16,126,4,272,3,5899\0301,128,185,4,272,3,5899\0301,190,234,4,272,1,5899\0301,236,320,4,272,1,5899\0304,1,30,3,256,2,5899\0304,32,195,3,324,4,5899\0304,200,222,3,256,1,5899\0315899,2,8,Brine\0312,0,0,2,Barrens\0302,0,0,7,Islen\0302,0,0,8,Ruins of Stardust\0302,0,0,8,Ashenvale\0302,0,0,8,Brine\0302,0,0,8,Barrens\0311536,19,1536,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030220,23,220,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7770,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1535]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I thought some bloodshed might ensue if you tried to take water from the pool. It is a pity the quilboar do not realize that all living things are tied together; that their greed only perpetuates the pain and suffering of their people. How much could they accomplish if they were to put their differences aside and their clans came together.$B$BAgain, a pity, but more than likely a boon for the other races of the Barrens.\030To find understanding and gain the sapta from me, you must seek out only the purest forms of water. As you fetch the samples for me, take note of your surroundings. Be aware of the creatures that rely on the water, that protect it. See how it affects forests and deserts. Witness how the very substance that sustains life will force creatures to take lives.$B$BWe shall start with a simple task: down below my hut there is a pond of the precious liquid. Fill this skin with it and return to me.\030Fill the Empty Brown Waterskin at the watering hole below Brine's hut and return it to her in the Barrens.\030I am just about prepared to send you on your other tasks. Have you filled the skin yet?$B$BI know how protective the quilboar can be. Even such a small water source is a vast hoard of wealth to them. They have great feasts when even the slightest rain comes to the Barrens. Water is sacred to their kind because it is so scarce. Do you understand?\030Call of Water\0312,1,99,2,259,1,5899\0302,101,164,2,257,1,5899\0302,166,231,2,269,1,5899\0302,233,271,2,257,1,5899\0302,273,357,2,257,3,5899\0302,362,453,2,257,3,5899\0302,455,494,2,257,1,5899\0303,1,106,2,384,1,5899\0301,1,78,4,272,4,5899\0301,80,235,4,276,1,5899\0301,237,341,4,272,4,5899\0301,346,423,4,272,1,5899\0304,1,57,3,256,1,5899\0304,59,87,3,256,2,5899\0304,92,133,3,256,1,5899\0304,135,199,3,256,1,5899\0304,201,273,3,256,1,5899\0304,275,328,3,258,1,5899\0304,330,347,3,256,2,5899\03114528,2,6,Precious\0312,0,0,8,Barrens\0303,0,0,17,Barrens\0311530,19,1530,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301536,23,1536,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7769,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1536]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is good, $N. You're dedicated to the task at hand and have the ability to seek out that which is needed.$B$BOne more sample is all I need to create the reagent needed for your sapta. Islen will be pleased as well.\030Long ago I followed some companions into the Hillsbrad Foothills. We defended ourselves from some tenacious humans who make their home there and we found ourselves in a small town the Forsaken had taken over: Tarren Mill.$B$BIt was there I found a most peculiar thing: in the center of town was a small well of fresh spring water. I'm not sure the plagued citizens of the town even realize its value--it's a small holy vestige in an unhallowed sea.$B$BBring me a sample of that water in this waterskin.\030Fill the Empty Red Waterskin at the well in Tarren Mill and return to Brine in the Barrens.\030The well remaining pure within the town reminds me of stories told to me when I was younger, $N. Even in times of great pain and sorrow one can find a sliver of hope, a small symbol to rally around. The orc people see Thrall this way. He survived against great odds and rose up to lead our people through his strength and example.$B$BI'm not sure any orc has suffered as much as he has, but at the same time, I'm not sure any orc is as strong as he is either.\030Call of Water\0312,1,65,2,321,1,5899\0302,67,221,2,257,1,5899\0302,226,330,2,257,1,5899\0302,332,448,2,257,1,5899\0302,453,502,2,257,1,5899\0303,1,91,2,384,1,5899\0301,1,17,4,272,1,5899\0301,19,109,4,274,1,5899\0301,114,187,4,274,1,5899\0301,189,218,4,272,3,5899\0304,1,96,3,256,1,5899\0304,98,198,3,258,3,5899\0304,200,234,3,256,1,5899\0304,236,330,3,256,1,5899\0304,335,459,3,256,1,5899\0315899,2,6,Brine\0304949,3,13,Thrall\0312,0,0,6,Tarren Mill\0302,0,0,6,Brine\0302,0,0,6,Barrens\0311535,19,1535,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301534,23,1534,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7771,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[154]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I can make a spool of Ghost Hair Thread with this, and have a few strands to spare. Here are some coins for those extra strands.\030NO!!!!!$B$BTake it, take this comb away from me!$B$BI'm a monster, and no one will ever think me lovely again!\030Return the Ghost Hair Comb to Madame Eva in Darkshire.\030I sense that you have seen Blind Mary. You have my Comb...?\030Return the Comb\0312,12,48,2,257,1,302\0302,53,110,2,257,3,302\0303,1,54,2,384,1,302\0301,1,83,4,272,1,265\0301,85,128,4,272,1,265\0304,1,38,3,256,1,265\0304,40,59,3,256,2,265\031265,2,3,Madame Eva\030302,3,6,Blind Mary\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,3,Madame Eva\0302,0,0,3,Darkshire\031149,19,149,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030157,23,157,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[155]="PARTIAL\031loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Most excellent, $N! VanCleef is as good as ours now that we know where he is hiding.\030So Stoutmantle sends a scrawny $r like you to protect me?  Guess you'll have to do.  Better bring some friends too. $B$BYou know the deal, right?  You watch my back and I'll take you to the Defias hideout.  But you better be close by my side.  The Defias gang wants my head now.  If they see me with you, they'll try to kill me.$B$BLet me know when you and any friends you can round up are ready to go.\030Escort the Defias Traitor to the secret hideout of the Defias Brotherhood.  Once the Defias Traitor shows you where VanCleef and his men are hiding out, return to Gryan Stoutmantle with the information.\030Escort The Defias Traitor to discover where VanCleef is hiding\030What business do you have with me? I am a very busy man...\030The Defias Brotherhood\0312,1,57,2,271,2,467\0302,60,83,2,257,1,467\0302,86,115,2,257,1,467\0302,121,145,2,257,2,467\0302,148,205,2,257,1,467\0302,208,242,2,257,1,467\0302,245,278,2,259,1,467\0302,281,328,2,257,4,467\0302,333,402,2,257,1,467\0303,1,74,2,384,1,467\0303,77,202,2,384,1,467\0301,1,19,4,272,1,234\0301,21,84,4,304,1,234\0305,1,34,3,256,2,234\0305,36,58,3,256,1,234\0304,1,62,3,384,1,467\031467,2,10,The Defias Traitor\030467,2,11,The Defias Traitor\030234,2,11,Gryan Stoutmantle\030467,3,16,The Defias Traitor\0312,40,1436,0,\0302,0,0,5,Defias\0302,0,0,11,Gryan Stoutmantle\031142,19,142,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030166,23,166,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1558]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031WOW - the dam was WAY bigger than I thought! I could barely hear myself talk from the sound of all the rushing water! Hey, do you think it would ever run out of water? Man, what would happen if that damn ever broke! WOW, that would be scary!$B$BThanks for taking me to see the dam. That was very kind of you. I told you I wouldn't lean over too far!\030Ironforge is where all the dwarves and gnomes live.  Near there is a place called Loch Modan, and the dwarves built a HUGE dam there.  They say it's one of the biggest things anyone's ever made.  Wow!$B$BCould you take me to Loch Modan and see the dam there, please?  I think it is the Stone... um... Stonewrench Dam?  Stonewrought?  It's big - that's for sure.  I'd like to look out over the big waterfall.  I promise I won't lean over too far!\030Take the orphan to the Stonewrought Dam in Loch Modan.  You should take him to the middle of the dam so he can see out over the giant waterfall.\030Go to the top of the Stonewrought Dam in Loch Modan.\030Are we there yet?\030The Stonewrought Dam\0312,1,51,2,257,1,14305\0302,54,133,2,257,1,14305\0302,136,194,2,257,1,14305\0302,197,200,2,257,1,14305\0302,205,266,2,257,4,14305\0302,269,294,2,257,1,14305\0302,302,317,2,257,2,14305\0302,320,332,2,257,2,14305\0302,335,361,2,257,1,14305\0302,364,407,2,259,1,14305\0302,410,445,2,257,1,14305\0303,1,54,2,384,1,14305\0303,57,144,2,384,1,14305\0301,1,44,4,272,1,14305\0301,46,117,4,272,4,14305\0301,119,167,4,272,4,14305\0301,169,215,4,272,4,14305\0301,217,241,4,272,4,14305\0301,246,281,4,272,1,14305\0301,283,308,4,272,1,14305\0301,310,349,4,272,1,14305\0305,1,17,3,256,2,14305\0304,1,52,3,384,1,14305\031\0312,0,0,5,Loch Modan\0302,0,0,12,Stonewrought Dam\0302,0,0,12,Loch Modan\0303,0,0,23,Loch Modan\0311468,19,1468,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1559]="UNRESOLVED\031conclusion,conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes,storytellingContext\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030\030\030\030Flash Bomb Recipe\031\031\031\031705,19,705,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[156]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Good, you got the rot blossoms. And I'll tell Althea Ebonlocke of the Night Watch that you were killing skeletons.$B$BKeeping the people of Darkshire safe is a grim burden for the Night Watch, and news that others are helping stem the tide of fiends in Duskwood is welcome news indeed.\030If you bring me some rot blossoms then I can brew you up a batch of zombie juice.$B$BRot blossoms grow in strange places.  In particular, I hear you can find them inside the skulls of Skeletal Horrors and Skeletal Fiends... not that I've gotten close enough to look!$B$BThe Raven Hill Cemetery is lousy with those skeletons.  You may as well get rid of them while you're looking for rot blossoms.  The town of Darkshire would be grateful.\030Gather 8 Rot Blossoms and bring them to Tavernkeep Smitts in Darkshire.\030Hi, $N. You have that rot blossoms for me yet?\030Gather Rot Blossoms\0312,1,81,2,257,4,273\0302,86,121,2,257,1,273\0302,124,223,2,257,1,273\0302,225,266,2,257,1,273\0302,271,324,2,257,1,273\0302,327,396,2,257,1,273\0302,399,438,2,257,4,273\0303,1,71,2,384,1,273\0301,1,31,4,272,1,273\0301,33,114,4,272,1,273\0301,119,285,4,272,1,273\0304,9,46,3,256,2,273\0317605,2,5,Raven\030273,2,8,Tavernkeep Smitts\03014235,4,9,The Rot\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,8,Tavernkeep Smitts\0302,0,0,8,Darkshire\0304,0,0,11,Duskwood\031158,19,158,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030159,23,159,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,1598,OBJECTIVE,8,15,",[1560]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031So he couldn't find his way back on his own? Figures.$B$BWell, I guess you deserve something for your troubles....\030I am so lost!$B$BMy wife, Torta, sent me out to fetch dinner and I must have taken a wrong turn somewhere.$B$BWould you be so kind as to lead me back to Torta? She's waiting for me just south of Steamwheedle Port.\030Show Tooga the way back to his wife, Torta.\030Lead Tooga to Torta\030Where is Tooga?\030Tooga's Quest\0312,1,13,2,261,1,5955\0302,18,106,2,257,1,5955\0302,111,159,2,257,4,5955\0302,161,213,2,257,1,5955\0303,1,43,2,384,1,5955\0301,1,44,4,272,2,6015\0301,46,53,4,272,1,6015\0301,58,114,4,272,1,6015\0305,1,15,3,256,2,6015\0304,1,19,3,384,1,5955\0316015,2,2,Torta\0306015,2,3,Torta\0305955,2,5,Tooga\0306015,2,5,Torta\0305955,3,9,Tooga\0305955,3,10,Tooga\0306015,3,10,Torta\0312,440,1446,0,\0302,0,0,3,Torta\0302,0,0,4,Steamwheedle Port\0303,0,0,10,Torta\031\031",[157]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Delightful! This will do splendidly...$B$BHere, good $N, take this as payment for your honorable deed.\030Here is your thread, $N.  It has a thousand uses, from binding evil spirits to sewing life into inanimate objects.\030Bring the Ghost Hair Thread to Abercrombie, in his shack north of the Raven Hill Cemetery.\030I need to string the Ghost Hair Thread along my door and my windows to keep out unwanted spirits. Did you get it for me?\030Deliver the Thread\0312,1,24,2,257,1,265\0302,27,114,2,261,1,265\0303,1,90,2,384,1,265\0301,1,11,4,272,1,289\0301,13,38,4,272,3,289\0301,43,102,4,272,1,289\0304,1,97,3,258,1,289\0304,99,120,3,256,2,289\031289,2,3,Abercrombie\0307605,2,3,Raven\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,3,Abercrombie\0302,0,0,3,Raven Hill Cemetery\031154,19,154,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030158,23,158,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1578]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, apologies! I didn't realize you were here to help resupply our troops. The stuff you made will be a big help!$B$BHere are plans for some armor. I hope you find them useful.\030The mountaineers of Loch Modan are fighting troggs, and having a busy time of it!  They need constant supplies of new armor and weapons if we're ever to get a handle on those troggs.$B$BThat's why my colleague Thorvald is there, trying to keep the mountaineers in good gear.  So if you were to make some copper axes and copper chain belts and bring them to Thorvald, he would be obliged.  He might even share his knowledge with you.$B$BThorvald is in Loch Modan's southern guard tower.\030Bring 6 Copper Axes and 6 Copper Chain Belts to Thorvald in the southern guard tower of Loch Modan.\030I have no time to chat. Do you have business with me?\030Supplying the Front\0312,1,81,2,261,1,6031\0302,84,182,2,259,4,6031\0302,187,274,2,257,1,6031\0302,277,387,2,257,4,6031\0302,390,432,2,257,4,6031\0302,437,485,2,257,1,6031\0303,1,99,2,384,1,6031\0301,1,14,4,272,1,6030\0301,16,74,4,272,1,6030\0301,76,113,4,272,3,6030\0301,118,147,4,272,1,6030\0301,149,176,4,274,3,6030\0304,1,23,3,256,1,6030\0304,25,53,3,256,2,6030\031\0312,0,0,4,Thorvald\0302,0,0,6,Loch Modan's\0302,0,0,7,Thorvald\031\031ITEM,2845,OBJECTIVE,6,15,\030ITEM,2851,OBJECTIVE,6,15,",[1579]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I can't believe you found them! You must be the luckiest $R in Kalimdor!\030I came to Auberdine because of the quiet.  I want to invent my inventions where it's quiet, because after a night of drinking I don't like all the noise of Ironforge!$B$BSo I took a ship to Auberdine and had a little too much to drink on the way.  I dropped my box of gaffer jacks overboard!  I need my gaffer jacks!$B$BI don't know exactly where I dropped them, but if you fish for them in the ocean you might get lucky...\030Bring 8 Gaffer Jacks to Wizbang Cranktoggle in Auberdine.\030Did you find my gaffer jacks, $N? Without my gaffer jacks I can't tune my stintle pegs!\030Gaffer Jacks\0312,1,41,2,259,1,3666\0302,44,166,2,259,1,3666\0302,171,246,2,257,1,3666\0302,249,291,2,257,1,3666\0302,294,316,2,259,1,3666\0302,321,423,2,257,4,3666\0303,1,57,2,384,1,3666\0301,1,31,4,272,4,3666\0301,33,72,4,272,1,3666\0304,1,33,3,256,2,3666\0304,35,87,3,256,1,3666\0313666,2,7,Wizbang Cranktoggle\0312,0,0,1,Auberdine\0302,0,0,3,Auberdine\0302,0,0,7,Wizbang Cranktoggle\0302,0,0,7,Auberdine\0304,0,0,9,Kalimdor\0311580,23,1580,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6717,OBJECTIVE,8,15,",[158]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You need some Zombie Juice, do you? Hmm...that's some strong stuff - I don't usually get requests for it.\030I need a bottle of a certain liquor - Zombie Juice.  Tavernkeep Smitts at the Scarlet Raven Tavern in Darkshire should have some.$B$BAnd please hurry, $N.  These nights get cold, and I need that drink to put fire in my veins again!\030Speak with Tavernkeep Smitts.\030\030Zombie Juice\0312,1,51,2,259,1,289\0302,54,129,2,257,1,289\0302,134,154,2,257,1,289\0302,157,231,2,259,1,289\0303,1,29,2,384,1,289\0301,1,35,4,274,2,273\0301,37,105,4,272,1,273\031273,2,2,Tavernkeep Smitts\0307605,2,2,Raven\030273,2,5,Tavernkeep Smitts\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,2,Scarlet Raven Tavern\0302,0,0,2,Darkshire\031157,19,157,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030156,23,156,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1580]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I can't believe it! You found them! You are the best fisherman I've ever seen!$B$BThank you, $N. And here, take these. Although you're so good and you probably don't need them, they will help you with your fishing.\030We know you're lucky, but... just how lucky are you, $N?$B$BOne night I was wandering the roads of Darkshore.  I was looking for a good river or lake to try my new self-propelled, exploding duck decoy and I think I was a little tipsy... because I passed out and awoke hours later in Auberdine.  My hair was singed and my bag of electropellers was gone!  I must have dropped them in the water!$B$BI need those electropellers!  Maybe you can fish them out of some lake or stream in Darkshore...\030Bring 12 Electropellers to Wizbang Cranktoggle in Auberdine.\030Did you find any electropellers? I'll need them if I'm to continue my research on duck decoys...\030Electropellers\0312,1,28,2,257,1,3666\0302,30,56,2,257,2,3666\0302,61,109,2,257,1,3666\0302,112,236,2,257,1,3666\0302,238,293,2,259,1,3666\0302,296,352,2,257,1,3666\0302,355,392,2,257,1,3666\0302,397,424,2,259,1,3666\0302,427,492,2,257,4,3666\0303,1,60,2,384,1,3666\0301,1,19,4,272,4,3666\0301,21,35,4,272,1,3666\0301,37,78,4,272,1,3666\0301,83,96,4,272,1,3666\0301,98,118,4,272,1,3666\0301,120,214,4,272,3,3666\0304,1,32,3,256,2,3666\0304,34,96,3,258,4,3666\0313666,2,10,Wizbang Cranktoggle\0312,0,0,5,Auberdine\0302,0,0,9,Darkshore\0302,0,0,10,Wizbang Cranktoggle\0302,0,0,10,Auberdine\0311579,19,1579,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6718,OBJECTIVE,12,15,",[1581]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031These are nicely mixed. You take great care in your trade, $N, and that is important for an alchemist.$B$BHere are your herbs, freshly gathered. May you use them well.\030Our herb and alchemy shop is booming, but my husband spends so much time mixing potions that we never have time for each other.$B$BCan you help us?$B$BIf you can bring me a supply of pre-made elixirs, then I would be happy to trade with you.  I have some rare herbs that you might find useful.\030Bring 6 Elixirs of Lion's Strength and 2 Elixirs of Minor Defense to Syral Bladeleaf in Dolanaar.\030Hello, $N. Do you have the elixirs to trade?\030Elixirs for the Bladeleafs\0312,1,127,2,257,1,2083\0302,132,147,2,257,2,2083\0302,152,241,2,257,4,2083\0302,244,293,2,257,4,2083\0303,1,97,2,384,1,2083\0301,1,23,4,272,1,2083\0301,25,102,4,272,1,2083\0301,107,144,4,272,1,2083\0301,146,167,4,272,1,2083\0304,1,10,3,256,1,2083\0304,12,44,3,256,2,2083\0312083,2,5,Syral Bladeleaf\0312,0,0,5,Syral Bladeleaf\0302,0,0,5,Dolanaar\031\031ITEM,2454,OBJECTIVE,6,15,\030ITEM,5997,OBJECTIVE,2,15,",[1582]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes, these are good pieces. You have a skilled hand and an eye for detail. Your future as a leatherworker is promising.$B$BHere, $N. Let me show you the pattern to make the Moonglow Vest.\030We in Darnassus, especially we craftsman, are quite busy.  Young adventurers are eager to test themselves in the wilderness, and are in constant need of supplies.$B$BIf you can help me fill my orders of leather goods, then perhaps I can teach you an advanced leatherworking technique.\030Bring 1 Embossed Leather Gloves, 5 Embossed Leather Boots and 5 Embossed Leather Cloaks to Lotherias in Darnassus.\030Greetings, $N.\030Moonglow Vest\0312,1,57,2,257,1,6034\0302,60,162,2,259,1,6034\0302,167,284,2,257,4,6034\0303,1,114,2,384,1,6034\0301,1,27,4,272,1,6034\0301,29,74,4,272,1,6034\0301,76,119,4,272,1,6034\0301,124,132,4,272,1,6034\0301,134,187,4,272,1,6034\0304,1,14,3,256,1,6034\0316034,2,4,Lotherias\0312,0,0,1,Darnassus\0302,0,0,4,Lotherias\0302,0,0,4,Darnassus\031\031ITEM,4239,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,2309,OBJECTIVE,5,15,\030ITEM,2310,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[159]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A thousand thanks, $N. You warm an old man's heart with your foolish-...I mean...with your kindness!$B$BHere you are, friend. Take this as a token of my gratitude.\030Here's your Zombie Juice...$B$B...and be careful with this stuff.  It's strong enough to raise the dead!\030Bring the Zombie Juice to Abercrombie at his shack.\030I need that Zombie Juice to keep me warm on these cold, dark nights. Did you get it for me?\030Juice Delivery\0312,1,27,2,257,1,273\0302,32,65,2,257,1,273\0302,68,104,2,257,1,273\0303,1,51,2,384,1,273\0301,1,22,4,272,1,289\0301,24,100,4,272,1,289\0301,105,125,4,272,1,289\0301,127,163,4,272,1,289\0304,1,68,3,258,1,289\0304,70,91,3,256,2,289\031289,2,4,Abercrombie\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,4,Abercrombie\031156,19,156,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030133,23,133,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1598]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Excellent... I was never able to gain access to this text, it was held in a protected wing of the library that would have looked suspicious for me to be loitering around.$B$BWell, you did a good job in getting this, and I'm convinced that you can probably handle your own imp, so there's no reason for me not to show you how to summon one.\030You there! $n, right?$B$BI hope you're sure about becoming a warlock, because if you can't hold your own, you're likely to get pulled under.$B$BI'm to teach you, but I need to make sure you're strong enough first.$B$BThere was a novice studying at the Abbey who ran off to join the Defias Brotherhood. Why do I care? Well, he stole some important books.$B$BOne of those happens to be a book I've wanted for myself, the Powers of the Void. Steal it for me, they have it hidden at their tent in the Vineyards.\030Retrieve the Powers of the Void for Drusilla La Salle.\030It was too conspicuous for me to steal the book myself. What luck one of their own patsies did the dirty work for me.\030The Stolen Tome\0312,1,10,2,257,1,459\0302,12,21,2,257,2,459\0302,26,140,2,259,4,459\0302,145,213,2,259,1,459\0302,218,301,2,257,1,459\0302,303,316,2,257,2,459\0302,318,353,2,257,1,459\0302,358,438,2,257,1,459\0302,440,507,2,261,1,459\0303,1,54,2,384,1,459\0301,1,12,4,272,1,459\0301,14,170,4,272,4,459\0301,175,339,4,272,1,459\0304,1,55,3,260,1,459\0304,57,117,3,256,1,459\031459,2,10,Drusilla La Salle\0312,0,0,5,Abbey\0302,0,0,9,Vineyards\031\031ITEM,6785,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1599]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very good, very good! You've done well, $n. Perhaps the interest that is being shown in you is deserved, after all.$B$BThat'll be for the others to decide--assuming your imp doesn't overpower you and nip your career in the bud. For now, I'm satisfied that you'll probably survive your first few months as a warlock.$B$BA word about the imp, $n. As a gnome knows, don't let its size fool you, its magic can be very dangerous.\030You must be the new warlock everyone's been whispering about. Must be someone's taken a liking to you if they've asked me to take time away from my research to start your training.$B$BDon't worry, I won't hold it against you.$B$BThe simplest of the summoning spells you will learn is that of the imp. Before I impart this to you, however, you must prove that you have the necessary magical and physical ability.$B$BBring me three feather charms from the frostmane novices from the cave to the southwest.\030Bring 3 Feather Charms to Alamar Grimm in Anvilmar.\030Those feather charms the novices carry have some sort of magical power to them. It will be interesting to research them. I wouldn't have expected it from the trolls.\030Beginnings\0312,1,61,2,257,1,460\0302,63,180,2,257,4,460\0302,185,225,2,257,1,460\0302,230,300,2,257,3,460\0302,302,411,2,257,1,460\0302,416,503,2,257,1,460\0303,1,51,2,384,1,460\0301,1,21,4,272,1,460\0301,23,43,4,272,1,460\0301,45,115,4,272,4,460\0301,120,227,4,272,1,460\0301,229,315,4,280,1,460\0301,320,344,4,272,1,460\0301,346,424,4,272,1,460\0304,1,79,3,256,1,460\0304,81,120,3,256,3,460\0304,122,165,3,256,1,460\031460,2,7,Alamar Grimm\0312,0,0,7,Alamar Grimm\0302,0,0,7,Anvilmar\031\031ITEM,6753,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[16]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thanks, $N! And come back if you want to trade again.\030\030\030Farming is thirsty work, and I'm always looking for refreshing spring water.$B$BIf you have any, then I'm willing to make a trade.\030Give Gerard a Drink\0311,1,11,4,272,1,255\0301,13,53,4,274,4,255\0304,1,76,3,256,1,255\0304,81,130,3,256,4,255\031\0312,12,1429,0,\031\031ITEM,159,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[160]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Ello looks at the letter...>$B$BWhat language is this? It looks ancient...I can't read it.\030Take this note to Ello Ebonlocke, the Mayor of Darkshire.$B$BHe and I are old friends...and when he reads it and discovers what you did for me...I'm sure he'll be just as happy as I am!  Hahahaha!\030Bring Abercrombie's Letter to Ello Ebonlocke, Mayor of Darkshire.\030Abercrombie...? I don't know a person of that name. You say you have a letter for me from this Abercrombie fellow?$B$BWell let's have it then...\030Note to the Mayor\0312,1,57,2,257,1,289\0302,62,185,2,257,1,289\0302,188,196,2,257,1,289\0303,1,65,2,384,1,289\0301,1,29,4,272,1,263\0301,34,55,4,272,2,263\0301,57,91,4,336,1,263\0304,1,15,3,256,2,263\0304,17,51,3,256,1,263\0304,53,114,3,256,2,263\0304,119,144,3,256,1,263\031289,3,8,Abercrombie\030289,3,10,Abercrombie\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,1,Ello Ebonlocke\0302,0,0,4,Ello Ebonlocke\031134,19,134,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030251,23,251,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[161]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, well Ol' Hinderweir is wise to be worried.\030If my suspicions are correct, this is some type of explosive powder.  This must be analyzed by an explosives expert so we know just what we're dealing with here.  Ashlan Stonesmirk was assigned to the regiment guarding Dun Modr and the Thandol Span.  I need you to make a grave and perilous journey, $N.$B$BTravel through the Algaz Gate, follow the road through the Wetlands and seek out Stonesmirk in Dun Modr.  Heed my advice: stick to the roads and stop for nothing!\030Chief Engineer Hinderweir wants you to take the strange smelling powder to Ashlan Stonesmirk, the explosives expert in Dun Modr.\030You say somethin', sonny? Can't hear a bloody thing besides the ringin' in me ears. Say, what's that you got there?\030A Dark Threat Looms\0312,1,68,2,257,4,1093\0302,71,161,2,257,1,1093\0302,164,249,2,257,1,1093\0302,252,303,2,259,1,1093\0302,308,411,2,259,1,1093\0302,414,469,2,257,1,1093\0303,1,128,2,386,1,1093\0301,1,46,4,272,1,1073\0304,1,25,3,256,2,1073\0304,27,83,3,256,1,1073\0304,85,115,3,256,2,1073\0311073,2,3,Ashlan Stonesmirk\0301073,2,7,Ashlan Stonesmirk\0312,38,1432,0,\0302,0,0,5,Dun Modr\0302,0,0,7,Ashlan Stonesmirk\0302,0,0,7,Dun Modr\031199,19,199,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030274,23,274,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1618]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, $N. This will help me out tremendously. With the Blackrock orcs attacking from Stonewatch Keep and the Redridge gnolls lurking in the foothills to the north, I'm always fixing armor and making new weapons for our troops.$B$BThe supplies you brought will give me a moment's peace. I will have enough time to teach you something...\030We dwarves aren't the only ones fighting.  Our human allies have their hands full too!$B$BRedridge is under periodic attack from blackrock orcs, and their supply of equipment is always low.  If you were to help them out, I'm sure their resident blacksmith, Verner Osgood, would teach you a trick or two.\030Tormus Deepforge  wants you to bring 4 Runed Copper Belts and 4 Heavy Copper Mauls to Verner Osgood in Redridge.\030I hope you're here with good news from Ironforge. Because I'm at my wit's end!\030Gearing Redridge\0312,1,41,2,261,1,6031\0302,44,86,2,257,1,6031\0302,91,189,2,261,1,6031\0302,192,303,2,257,4,6031\0303,1,112,2,384,1,6031\0301,1,14,4,272,1,415\0301,16,50,4,272,3,415\0301,52,231,4,276,1,415\0301,236,290,4,280,3,415\0301,292,340,4,272,3,415\0304,1,49,3,258,3,415\0304,51,78,3,258,1,415\031415,2,4,Verner Osgood\0306031,2,5,Tormus Deepforge\030415,2,5,Verner Osgood\0312,0,0,5,Verner Osgood\0302,0,0,5,Redridge\0304,0,0,8,Stonewatch Keep\0303,0,0,11,Ironforge\031\031ITEM,2857,OBJECTIVE,4,15,\030ITEM,6214,OBJECTIVE,4,15,",[162]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This report... we night elves know of the terror mentioned here.  Fizzledowser was wise to send this, and you, to me.$B$BThese creatures will consume the Tanaris desert rapidly; they are nothing short of one of the greatest menaces we all will ever face.  Familiarize yourself with this name, $n: silithid.  The insects mentioned here are the silithid, and they are the tools of one of the greatest threats that both the Horde and Alliance face.$B$BIf only we were smart enough to see that before.\030I urge you to take this report to someone who has working knowledge in this kind of thing.$B$BI know this night elf scholar named Gracina Spiritmight.  She's spent a lot of time studying life forms that are unique to the ecology of Azeroth; she's a historian to boot!  If you want someone to help figure out what exactly this threat is, and more importantly how to stop it, give her the report.  We'll need the help.$B$BLast I heard, she was residing in the Temple of the Moon, located in Darnassus.\030Take the Insect Analysis Report to Gracina Spiritmight in Darnassus.\030Peace and tranquility be upon you, stranger.  Why have you sought me out this day?\030Rise of the Silithid\0312,1,90,2,257,1,7724\0302,95,150,2,257,1,7724\0302,153,267,2,257,1,7724\0302,270,394,2,263,4,7724\0302,397,416,2,259,1,7724\0302,421,499,2,257,1,7724\0303,1,68,2,384,1,7724\0301,1,14,4,272,1,7740\0301,16,64,4,272,1,7740\0301,67,117,4,272,1,7740\0301,122,254,4,272,3,7740\0301,257,306,4,272,1,7740\0301,309,445,4,272,1,7740\0301,450,497,4,272,4,7740\0304,1,44,3,264,1,7740\0304,47,82,3,256,2,7740\0317740,2,2,Gracina Spiritmight\0307740,2,7,Gracina Spiritmight\0312,440,1446,0,\0302,0,0,6,Temple of the Moon\0302,0,0,6,Darnassus\0302,0,0,7,Gracina Spiritmight\0302,0,0,7,Darnassus\031113,19,113,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[163]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031No! Please don't kill me! It's just me... Jitters!! They're everywhere... I can't escape them! Monsters in Raven Hill? N-n-n-o... couldn't be. Only harmless Jitters.\030Something's amiss at Raven Hill, $n. Calor swears that someone--or something--is haunting the buildings there. Two nights running he's noticed the shadows moving, and the third before that he says he saw light in one of the windows.$B$BIf, as you say, you care about the safety of Duskwood, find out what monster haunts in Raven Hill.\030Find out what is haunting Raven Hill.\030\030Raven Hill\0312,1,36,2,257,1,633\0302,38,110,2,257,1,633\0302,112,232,2,257,1,633\0302,237,334,2,265,4,633\0303,1,37,2,384,1,633\0301,5,25,4,272,1,288\0301,27,41,4,272,1,288\0301,43,51,4,272,1,288\0301,53,73,4,272,1,288\0301,75,94,4,272,1,288\0301,96,118,4,272,2,288\0301,131,142,4,272,1,288\0301,144,165,4,272,1,288\0317605,2,1,Raven\030663,2,2,Calor\0307605,2,4,Raven\0307605,2,5,Raven\030288,4,8,Jitters\0307605,4,11,Raven\030288,4,13,Jitters\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,1,Raven Hill\0302,0,0,4,Raven Hill\0304,0,0,11,Raven Hill\0315,24,5,UNKNOWN\031",[1638]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh ho! Have a drink with me, $N. You look tough on the outside, but let's see if your gut can handle a few mugs of the Pig and Whistle's strongest!!$B$BOr... were you here for a lesson?\030You've shown yourself to be a competent warrior, $N.  But you're still young and have a lot to learn.$B$BSpeak with Harry Burlguard--he's usually in the Pig and Whistle tavern, in the Old Town of Stormwind.  Harry is an old veteran and a good teacher.  He can show you a few moves that'll keep you breathing longer.\030Speak with Harry Burlguard.\030\030A Warrior's Training\0312,1,52,2,257,1,0\0302,55,101,2,257,1,0\0302,106,206,2,257,1,0\0302,209,251,2,257,1,0\0302,254,315,2,257,1,0\0303,1,27,2,384,1,0\0301,8,32,4,272,1,6089\0301,34,148,4,272,4,6089\0301,159,185,4,272,2,6089\0316089,2,3,Harry Burlguard\0306089,2,6,Harry Burlguard\0312,0,0,3,Pig\0302,0,0,3,Old Town of Stormwind\0311679,22,1679,UNKNOWN\0301684,22,1684,UNKNOWN\0301639,23,1639,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1639]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hello, fancy $gboy:girl;! What's a prissy thing like you doing in the Pig and Whistle? Be careful, or you might break a nail...\030Yeah, I can teach you.  But first I wanna see what moves you have already.$B$BSee that drunk over there at the end of the bar?  Bartleby?  I want you to get his mug.$B$BHah, and if you know Bartleby then you know he won't just give it to you.\030Speak with Bartleby.\030\030Bartleby the Drunk\0312,1,22,2,257,1,6089\0302,25,74,2,257,1,6089\0302,79,126,2,257,2,6089\0302,129,137,2,257,2,6089\0302,140,165,2,259,1,6089\0302,170,242,2,257,4,6089\0303,1,20,2,384,1,6089\0301,1,25,4,272,1,6090\0301,27,86,4,272,2,6090\0301,88,127,4,272,4,6090\0316090,2,4,Bartleby\0306090,2,6,Bartleby\0306090,2,7,Bartleby\030371,4,8,Girl\0314,0,0,9,Pig\0311638,19,1638,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301640,23,1640,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[164]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031These supplies will be most useful. The aid of the Carevin family is always appreciated. Here is a little something for your trouble.\030Do you know Sven? Now, there is a man who does the work of the Light! He and his followers keep a camp at the northwestern edge of Duskwood.$B$BUnfortunately, because they are so few, they cannot even spare a man to fetch supplies from town. Will you deliver these supplies to him?\030Deliver the supplies to Sven.\030You look a sturdy type, $C. Have you come to join our fight?\030Deliveries to Sven\0312,1,17,2,257,2,633\0302,19,69,2,257,1,633\0302,71,140,2,257,1,633\0302,145,241,2,259,1,633\0302,243,281,2,257,2,633\0303,1,29,2,384,1,633\0301,1,35,4,272,3,311\0301,37,88,4,272,1,311\0301,90,133,4,272,1,311\0304,1,27,3,256,1,311\0304,29,60,3,260,2,311\031\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,6,Sven\03195,24,95,UNKNOWN\031",[1640]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031You're a lot tougher than you look!\030You want what??  You're crazy!$B$BThe only way you'll get this mug is if you pry it from my cold, dead fingers...\030Beat Bartleby, then talk to him.\030Beat Bartleby\030The only way you'll get this mug is if you pry it from my cold, dead fingers...\030Beat Bartleby\0312,1,15,2,259,2,6090\0302,18,30,2,257,1,6090\0302,35,113,2,257,4,6090\0303,1,32,2,384,1,6090\0301,1,35,4,272,1,6090\0305,1,79,3,256,4,6090\0304,1,13,3,384,1,6090\0316090,2,4,Bartleby\0306090,3,7,Bartleby\031\0311639,19,1639,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301665,23,1665,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1641]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Here in Stormwind, I am responsible for putting paladins on the path to greater virtue as they devote themselves to the Light and defend Azeroth from the Scourge and other threats.$B$BThe time has come for you to take your first step towards being truly virtuous. If you accept it, I will give you a Book of Divinity. In studying it, you shall learn some about the Light, and what is expected of you. If you understand it, and are capable, then you will succeed in attaining greater abilities.\030\030\030\030The Tome of Divinity\0311,1,180,4,348,1,6171\0301,185,263,4,272,1,6171\0301,265,317,4,272,4,6171\0301,319,400,4,272,3,6171\0301,402,493,4,272,4,6171\031\0314,0,0,1,Stormwind\0304,0,0,1,Light\0304,0,0,1,Scourge\031\031",[1642]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hello again, $N. How goes your studies of the Tome of Divinity?$B$BThen you should be prepared to have yourself tested. There are always tasks to be done throughout the city and our lands; acts of compassion and understanding; people who need help; creatures to slay.$B$BBy proving you have the patience to help others, especially those who are less fortunate, you prove that you are a servant of the Light and of sound mind.\030In all things, a paladin must reflect the Light which supplements our strength. To strive to be divine for one of our kind does not mean we strive for godhood--we strive to be good in all actions.$B$BAlthough called upon to smite evil in these harsh times, you must always remember that it's aiding others that will truly set you apart from the citizens of Azeroth. Compassion, patience, bravery--these things mean as much to a paladin as strength in battle.$B$BKnow this well, and never forget it.\030Speak to Duthorian Rall in Stormwind.\030\030The Tome of Divinity\0312,1,79,2,257,1,0\0302,81,196,2,257,1,0\0302,201,365,2,257,3,0\0302,367,458,2,261,1,0\0302,463,498,2,257,1,0\0303,1,37,2,384,1,0\0301,1,16,4,272,1,6171\0301,18,63,4,272,2,6171\0301,68,119,4,272,1,6171\0301,121,267,4,274,1,6171\0301,272,425,4,272,1,6171\0316171,2,6,Duthorian Rall\0312,0,0,6,Duthorian Rall\0302,0,0,6,Stormwind\0311643,23,1643,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6775,STARTER,?,10,",[1643]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh, hello, luv. How go your adventures? Oh, I'm so glad to hear you're doing well.$B$BOh, me? Thank you for asking--I'm doing well, all things considered.$B$BThe increase in tradesmen has kind of put a damper on the amount of leather and cloth people are willing to part with these days, so it's been tougher to make clothing for the children at the orphanage, but we'll manage. By \"we\" I mean my husband and I. He's up in Ironforge trying to seek help from the citizens there.\030Your task then, $N, is to find someone here in Stormwind that is in need of aid. Someone who is pure of heart and motive. Perhaps someone helping others. Perhaps someone in need of a guide. Regardless, the person must have noble intent and be relying on your kindness.$B$BDo this, and return to me when you are finished. Then, we shall discuss more of your path and what it means to be a paladin of the Light.\030Search the Trade District of Stormwind for Stephanie Turner.\030\030The Tome of Divinity\0312,1,80,2,259,1,6171\0302,82,121,2,257,1,6171\0302,123,153,2,257,4,6171\0302,155,189,2,259,4,6171\0302,191,268,2,257,1,6171\0302,273,320,2,257,1,6171\0302,322,409,2,257,3,6171\0303,1,60,2,384,1,6171\0301,1,15,4,272,1,6174\0301,17,39,4,272,2,6174\0301,41,82,4,272,1,6174\0301,95,154,4,272,1,6174\0301,159,378,4,272,1,6174\0301,380,411,4,272,1,6174\0301,413,477,4,274,1,6174\0316174,2,8,Stephanie Turner\0312,0,0,1,Stormwind\0304,0,0,15,Ironforge\0311642,19,1642,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301644,23,1644,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1644]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, $N, thank you so much!$B$BThe children will be so pleased, and you've saved me so much time. I'll now be able to focus on the children's other needs, and hopefully my John will be able to return home sooner than we thought.$B$BThank you again, $N. I knew I could rely on the charity of others. The Light be with you.\030Bless their hearts, most of them have no families because of the Scourge attacks in the last decade.$B$BMy husband John collects the materials for me to make the shirts and pants for the children, but I haven't even had time to do that. I've been too focused on keeping food on their plates, and a roof over their heads.$B$BWhat's that? You'd be willing to help? Oh, thank the Light, and thank you, $N.$B$BIf you could bring me some linen cloth so I can sew clothes for the kids, that would help me out so much.\030Bring 10 Linen Cloth to Stephanie Turner in Stormwind.\030I hope my John is having better luck in Ironforge. He so dislikes his trips there because it leaves the kids and me alone, but he knows it must be done. He's so kind-hearted.$B$BSome years have been easier than others, but this one's been rougher by far. It's almost as though something in the air is signaling a huge change. Who knows though?\030The Tome of Divinity\0312,1,100,2,327,1,6174\0302,105,236,2,257,1,6174\0302,238,320,2,257,1,6174\0302,325,336,2,257,2,6174\0302,338,362,2,257,2,6174\0302,364,402,2,257,1,6174\0302,407,511,2,257,4,6174\0303,1,54,2,384,1,6174\0301,1,33,4,272,1,6174\0301,38,103,4,272,3,6174\0301,105,234,4,274,3,6174\0301,239,258,4,272,1,6174\0301,260,304,4,272,4,6174\0301,306,327,4,272,1,6174\0304,1,50,3,258,3,6174\0304,52,152,3,258,1,6174\0304,154,174,3,256,1,6174\0304,179,254,3,256,1,6174\0304,256,325,3,256,1,6174\0304,327,343,3,256,2,6174\031806,2,2,John\0306174,2,8,Stephanie Turner\030806,4,11,John\030806,3,15,John\0312,0,0,8,Stephanie Turner\0302,0,0,8,Stormwind\0303,0,0,15,Ironforge\0311643,19,1643,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301780,23,1780,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,2589,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[1645]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Here in Ironforge, I am responsible for putting paladins on the path to greater virtue as they devote themselves to the Light and defend Azeroth from the Scourge and other threats.$B$BThe time has come for you to take your first step towards being truly virtuous. If you accept it, I will give you a Book of Divinity. In studying it, you shall learn some about the Light, and what is expected of you. If you understand it, and are capable, then you will succeed in attaining greater abilities.\030\030\030\030The Tome of Divinity\0311,1,180,4,348,1,6179\0301,185,263,4,272,1,6179\0301,265,317,4,272,4,6179\0301,319,400,4,272,3,6179\0301,402,493,4,272,4,6179\031\0314,0,0,1,Ironforge\0304,0,0,1,Light\0304,0,0,1,Scourge\031\031",[1646]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Welcome back, $N. You've spent time reading the book, I hope?$B$BThen you should be prepared to have yourself tested. There are always tasks to be done throughout the city and our lands; acts of compassion and understanding; people who need help; creatures to slay.$B$BBy proving you have the patience to help others, especially those who are less fortunate, you prove that you are a servant of the Light and of sound mind.\030In all things, a paladin must reflect the Light which supplements our strength. To strive to be divine for one of our kind does not mean we strive for godhood--we strive to be good in all actions.$B$BAlthough called upon to smite evil in these harsh times, you must always remember that it's aiding others that will truly set you apart from the citizens of Azeroth. Compassion, patience, bravery--these things mean as much to a paladin as strength in battle.$B$BKnow this well, and never forget it.\030Speak to Tiza Battleforge in Ironforge.\030\030The Tome of Divinity\0312,1,79,2,257,1,0\0302,81,196,2,257,1,0\0302,201,365,2,257,3,0\0302,367,458,2,261,1,0\0302,463,498,2,257,1,0\0303,1,39,2,384,1,0\0301,1,17,4,272,1,6179\0301,19,61,4,274,2,6179\0301,66,117,4,272,1,6179\0301,119,265,4,274,1,6179\0301,270,423,4,272,1,6179\0316179,2,6,Tiza Battleforge\0312,0,0,6,Tiza Battleforge\0302,0,0,6,Ironforge\0311647,23,1647,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6916,STARTER,?,10,",[1647]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031THE ORPHANAGE OF STOR... oh, sorry, didn't mean to shout at you, sir.$B$BMy name is John Turner. How are you?$B$BGood, good, glad to hear things go well for you. I've had a long day of work already, and I miss my wife terribly, but that's the price you have to pay when there are mouths to feed and backs to clothe.\030Your task then, $N, is to find someone here in Ironforge that is in need of aid. Someone who is pure of heart and motive. Perhaps someone helping others. Perhaps someone in need of a guide. Regardless, the person must have noble intent and be relying on your kindness.$B$BDo this, and return to me when you are finished. Then, we shall discuss more of your path and what it means to be a paladin of the Light. I will remain here in the temple for your return. Other paladins will need my guidance also.\030Search the outer ring of Ironforge for John Turner.\030\030The Tome of Divinity\0312,1,80,2,259,1,6179\0302,82,121,2,257,1,6179\0302,123,153,2,257,4,6179\0302,155,189,2,259,4,6179\0302,191,268,2,257,1,6179\0302,273,320,2,257,1,6179\0302,322,409,2,257,3,6179\0302,411,459,2,257,3,6179\0302,461,502,2,259,3,6179\0303,1,51,2,384,1,6179\0301,1,24,4,272,1,6175\0301,26,69,4,272,1,6175\0301,74,96,4,272,1,6175\0301,98,109,4,272,2,6175\0301,114,161,4,272,1,6175\0301,163,315,4,272,1,6175\0316175,2,10,John Turner\0306175,4,13,John Turner\0312,0,0,1,Ironforge\0311646,19,1646,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301648,23,1648,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1648]="PARTIAL\031consequences\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is so wonderful of you, $N. Thank you again.$B$BYou're a noble man for doing this for me. It's no wonder you've chosen to follow the Light. I wish there was some way I could repay you for all you've done... what's that? It's the least you could do? See? That's what I'm talking about, $N, noble to the end.$B$BBe safe, and may the Light protect you in your travels.\030My wife and I run an orphanage in Stormwind, mostly for children who have lost parents due to the attacks by the Scourge in the last decade. I come to Ironforge every month or so to see about collecting more supplies from the citizens here, and talk to the various groups to see if they can do anything to help.$B$BThis trip's been agonizingly slow, and not very productive.$B$BIf I could just get some more linen for my wife to make some clothes, I could finally send a shipment home.\030Bring 10 Linen Cloth to John Turner in Ironforge.\030What with the influx of tradesmen here and throughout Azeroth, there's a smaller supply of items we use to make clothes for the children of our orphanage. Helping me collect linen so my wife can make new clothes for them is very noble of you, $N. Thank you.$B$BHopefully, I'll be able to return home to my wife soon.\030The Tome of Divinity\0312,1,140,2,325,1,6175\0302,142,311,2,257,4,6175\0302,316,374,2,257,1,6175\0302,379,485,2,257,4,6175\0303,1,49,2,384,1,6175\0301,1,32,4,272,1,6175\0301,34,49,4,272,1,6175\0301,54,94,4,272,1,6175\0301,96,144,4,272,1,6175\0301,146,211,4,274,4,6175\0301,213,224,4,272,2,6175\0301,226,253,4,272,4,6175\0301,255,258,4,272,2,6175\0301,260,311,4,272,1,6175\0301,316,370,4,284,1,6175\0304,1,154,3,256,1,6175\0304,156,246,3,256,1,6175\0304,248,257,3,256,1,6175\0304,262,316,3,256,3,6175\0316175,2,5,John Turner\0312,0,0,1,Stormwind\0302,0,0,2,Ironforge\0302,0,0,5,John Turner\0302,0,0,5,Ironforge\0311647,19,1647,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301778,23,1778,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,2589,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[1649]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, you wish to petition me for a test of valor. Splendid.$B$BThere are many tasks throughout the city and surrounding lands that hold much challenge, and they could use a $G man:woman; with your skills.$B$BThis test should not be taken lightly, $N. This, like many things along our path, could take our lives. The Church always wishes to bolster its ranks, but it understands the sacrifices needed to ensure the paladins serving it are worthy.$B$BAre you prepared?\030Valor, and all the virtues that go along with it, are like rare minerals: you must cherish them when you find them because of their value, but you must also take time to harvest them... refine them. When mixed together properly, a strong alloy is formed, sometimes unbreakable by even the most powerful blows.$B$BThis strength, your faith, your bravery, must be tested. You must learn to never lose faith and realize that with the power of the Light, you can overcome things that most others cannot.\030Speak to Duthorian Rall in Stormwind.\030\030The Tome of Valor\0312,1,185,2,259,1,0\0302,187,198,2,257,1,0\0302,200,309,2,257,1,0\0302,314,369,2,257,1,0\0302,371,499,2,257,1,0\0303,1,37,2,384,1,0\0301,1,48,4,274,3,6171\0301,50,58,4,272,1,6171\0301,63,203,4,272,4,6171\0301,208,249,4,272,1,6171\0301,251,310,4,272,4,6171\0301,312,444,4,274,1,6171\0301,449,465,4,272,2,6171\0316171,2,6,Duthorian Rall\0312,0,0,6,Duthorian Rall\0302,0,0,6,Stormwind\0311650,23,1650,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6776,STARTER,?,10,",[165]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hehe, oh yes... of course, the Carevins.$B$BNo, nothing's wrong but it is hard for me to go into town now. The roads are dangerous and I'm not getting any younger. Maybe you can do an old man some favors?\030There was an old man who used to come into town to buy supplies rather frequently, but I haven't seen him for quite some time now. He lives out in a shack overlooking Raven Hill cemetery, if I remember correctly. Perhaps you should go see if something is amiss.\030Check on the old man in the shack near Raven Hill cemetery.\030\030The Hermit\0312,1,130,2,257,1,633\0302,132,212,2,257,4,633\0302,214,261,2,257,4,633\0303,1,59,2,384,1,633\0301,1,15,4,272,1,289\0301,17,40,4,272,1,289\0301,45,106,4,272,1,289\0301,108,163,4,272,1,289\0301,165,204,4,272,4,289\0317605,2,2,Raven\0307605,2,4,Raven\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,4,Raven Hill\031148,24,148,UNKNOWN\031",[1650]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hello, $N. I'm assuming by all that armor and weapon of yours, you're either here to try and take my land, or the Church finally sent someone to help protect me while my Jordan's gone.$B$B Well, let me introduce myself: I'm Daphne Stilwell. It's a pleasure.$B$BNow, you're not too late... I've only killed a half dozen of the scum since last sun up. They've been a little slow getting 'round the bend up there, but they probably saw you coming, which means they'll probably be here any minute.\030Good! Your lack of hesitation is a sure sign that you are prepared and eager to test yourself. So be it.$B$BAt the very ends of Westfall's Longshore, a small house overlooks the ocean. There, a couple lives, the Stilwells. Jordan is an incredible smith, and he's gone to Ironforge to meet with the dwarves for a while. But this has left Daphne, his wife, alone and unprotected.$B$BReports suggest that the Defias have all but taken over the area, Daphne may need some protection from the villains. Go there.\030Find Daphne Stilwell in Westfall.\030\030The Tome of Valor\0312,1,5,2,257,1,6171\0302,7,94,2,257,1,6171\0302,109,184,2,257,1,6171\0302,186,222,2,257,1,6171\0302,224,318,2,257,1,6171\0302,320,377,2,257,1,6171\0302,382,497,2,259,1,6171\0302,499,507,2,257,1,6171\0303,1,33,2,384,1,6171\0301,1,10,4,272,1,6182\0301,12,184,4,284,1,6182\0301,189,240,4,272,1,6182\0301,242,257,4,272,1,6182\0301,262,288,4,272,1,6182\0301,290,349,4,272,1,6182\0301,351,493,4,272,1,6182\03111905,2,5,Jordan\0306182,2,9,Daphne Stilwell\0306182,4,12,Daphne Stilwell\0312,0,0,5,Ironforge\0302,0,0,9,Westfall\0311649,19,1649,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301651,23,1651,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1651]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031We've done it, $N! Thank you for your help. You were truly amazing out there. I never thought a $C could handle so many enemies at once.$B$BYou've truly shown bravery in the face of overwhelming odds.\030Now, they'll be coming again soon, I'd wager, so get yourself ready.$B$BI've got myself a gun in the house. I'll grab it and be ready to help you out, but for the most part, you're on your own.$B$BI've no idea how many they'll send, but I'm sure it'll be more than the few they sent earlier.$B$BAsk the Light for whatever blessings you can because... did you hear that? I think they're coming.$B$BWe make our stand near the house!\030Defend Daphne Stilwell from the Defias attack.$B$BNeither of your spirits must be released from their mortal coils if you wish to succeed.$B$BAfter you are successful, speak to Daphne Stilwell again.\030Protect Daphne Stilwell\030We'll make our stand at the house!\030The Tome of Valor\0312,1,68,2,257,1,6182\0302,73,107,2,257,1,6182\0302,109,193,2,257,1,6182\0302,198,291,2,257,1,6182\0302,296,350,2,259,1,6182\0302,352,369,2,257,2,6182\0302,371,393,2,257,1,6182\0302,398,430,2,257,1,6182\0303,1,46,2,396,1,6182\0303,51,138,2,386,4,6182\0303,143,199,2,384,1,6182\0301,1,18,4,272,1,6182\0301,20,43,4,272,1,6182\0301,45,77,4,272,1,6182\0301,79,136,4,276,4,6182\0301,141,200,4,272,1,6182\0305,1,34,3,256,1,6182\0304,1,23,3,396,1,6182\0316182,2,9,Daphne Stilwell\0306182,2,11,Daphne Stilwell\0306182,3,18,Daphne Stilwell\0312,0,0,9,Defias\0302,0,0,11,Daphne Stilwell\0311650,19,1650,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301652,23,1652,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1652]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031So, we meet again, $N, and you are in high spirits, I see.$B$BThe Stilwell home will be safe for another day, and from your story I see that there was no shortage of danger to be found. Well done.$B$BDaphne and Jordan have helped the Church greatly, and having you protect their property--and their very lives--was the least we could do for them.$B$BFor your valor, you will be rewarded.\030Please, return to Duthorian and let him know that I'm safe for now. I have you and the Church to thank for that.$B$BHe'll send word to Ironforge to let my Jordan know that he has nothing to fear.$B$BOh, how I miss my husband. I can't wait till he returns.\030Speak to Duthorian Rall in Stormwind.\030\030The Tome of Valor\0312,1,67,2,257,1,6182\0302,69,112,2,257,1,6182\0302,117,195,2,257,1,6182\0302,200,225,2,257,1,6182\0302,227,255,2,257,1,6182\0303,1,37,2,384,1,6182\0301,1,58,4,272,1,6171\0301,63,185,4,276,3,6171\0301,187,196,4,272,1,6171\0301,201,346,4,284,4,6171\0301,351,387,4,272,3,6171\03111905,2,3,Jordan\0306171,2,6,Duthorian Rall\03011905,4,10,Jordan\0312,0,0,1,Duthorian\0302,0,0,3,Ironforge\0302,0,0,6,Duthorian Rall\0302,0,0,6,Stormwind\0311651,19,1651,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301653,23,1653,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1653]="PARTIAL\031loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Good day, $N. The Light is with you, I trust?$B$BWhat's that? You were sent by Duthorian!? My wife, how is she? I knew there was going to be trouble if I left.$B$BPlease tell me she's... oh, thank goodness. I'm so glad that she's safe. The Defias were a threat long before these attacks, but now the King's advisors cannot deny it.$B$BWhat else did Duthorian have to say? You're the one that was sent to protect my wife? Then I thank you again, $N. I couldn't think of a better test of valor than that.\030Actually, I have no doubt that Jordan himself would like to thank you, and seeing as I need a messenger to send word that his wife is safe, I think you'd be a perfect choice.$B$BJordan was to be a paladin of the Light before his dedication to his father's craft took him on another path--he's intimately familiar with our way of life and is considered among our most faithful.$B$BHe should still be in Ironforge--he likes to work outside the gates during the day, something about the cool mountain air.\030Speak to Jordan Stilwell in Ironforge\030\030The Test of Righteousness\0312,1,174,2,259,4,6171\0302,179,376,2,257,1,6171\0302,381,502,2,257,1,6171\0303,1,37,2,384,1,6171\0301,1,13,4,272,1,6181\0301,15,45,4,272,2,6181\0301,50,61,4,272,2,6181\0301,63,90,4,272,2,6181\0301,92,111,4,272,2,6181\0301,113,159,4,272,4,6181\0301,164,186,4,272,1,6181\0301,188,206,4,272,1,6181\0301,208,235,4,272,1,6181\0301,237,331,4,308,1,6181\0301,336,371,4,272,2,6181\0301,373,420,4,286,2,6181\0301,422,448,4,272,1,6181\0301,450,502,4,272,1,6181\03111905,2,1,Jordan\03011905,2,2,Jordan\0306181,2,4,Jordan Stilwell\0312,0,0,3,Ironforge--he\0302,0,0,4,Jordan Stilwell\0302,0,0,4,Ironforge\0311652,19,1652,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301654,23,1654,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1654]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is wonderful! You've gotten all the items.$B$BI should have no problem forging you a grand weapon with these. I've actually had the plans for doing this for some time. I just never had the opportunity to gather the goods. Thank you, $N.$B$BIt feels good to have my father's hammer again...and a Kor gem. I never thought I'd see one of these myself.\030I'd like to reward you if you'd be willing to accept such a thing? Don't misunderstand me, my generosity is dependent on how much help you can be, but I see us both benefiting greatly from such an alliance.$B$BI will craft for you a weapon worthy of what you've accomplished, a symbol of paladinhood and the Light, but you must gather the items I need to craft it. I've already started taking notes on the items, it just requires someone brave and skilled enough to recover them. What do you say, $c?\030Using Jordan's Weapon Notes, find some Whitestone Oak Lumber, Bailor's Refined Ore Shipment, Jordan's Smithing Hammer, and a Kor Gem, and return them to Jordan Stilwell in Ironforge.\030The items you're seeking will be difficult to acquire, but I can assure you, the weapon I will craft for you will be worth the effort.$B$BIt will be my finest work to date, and only a small payment for the service you've done me.\030The Test of Righteousness\0312,1,66,2,259,4,6181\0302,68,206,2,257,1,6181\0302,211,364,2,259,3,6181\0302,366,479,2,257,1,6181\0302,481,500,2,257,2,6181\0303,1,182,2,384,1,6181\0301,1,18,4,272,1,6181\0301,20,47,4,272,1,6181\0301,52,114,4,276,1,6181\0301,116,172,4,272,1,6181\0301,174,226,4,272,1,6181\0301,228,241,4,272,1,6181\0301,246,308,4,272,1,6181\0301,310,353,4,272,1,6181\0304,1,134,3,256,3,6181\0304,139,229,3,256,3,6181\0316181,2,6,Jordan Stilwell\0312,0,0,6,Jordan Stilwell\0302,0,0,6,Ironforge\0311653,19,1653,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301806,23,1806,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6994,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,6993,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,6895,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,7083,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1655]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yup yup, this is it. Ha! If I'd known you were really gonna head out there and fight some o' them ogres, I woulda given you a list of things to get instead of just this one thing. But, you're not here doin' business for me, are ya?.$B$BA deal's a deal; Jordan wanted a shipment of me alloy, that's what he's gonna get.$B$BTell 'em hello fer me, and be safe, $C.\030Ach, ya startled me, $G man:woman;! Can't ya see I was lost in thought?$B$BWhat's that? Jordan's shipment... fer Ironforge. Ahhh, yeah, I know whatcha speak of. Mo'grosh ogres... dat's who took me ol' friend's ore shipment. Caravan was headin' here from the Wetlands and was ambushed. The guard who survived their attack just passed away a few days ago--healer couldn't get to 'em fast enough.$B$BIf you want the shipment, you'll have to head northeast across the Loch. It's got to be there somewhere.\030Bring Jordan's Ore Shipment to Bailor Stonehand in Loch Modan.\030So, any luck yet? Haha, those ogres didn't get the best of ya yet, did they?\030Bailor's Ore Shipment\0312,1,35,2,257,1,6241\0302,37,71,2,261,2,6241\0302,76,87,2,257,2,6241\0302,89,108,2,257,1,6241\0302,110,123,2,257,1,6241\0302,125,160,2,257,1,6241\0302,162,178,2,257,1,6241\0302,180,223,2,257,1,6241\0302,225,284,2,257,1,6241\0302,286,393,2,261,1,6241\0302,398,469,2,259,4,6241\0302,471,501,2,257,1,6241\0303,1,62,2,384,1,6241\0301,1,20,4,272,1,6241\0301,26,179,4,276,4,6241\0301,181,232,4,272,2,6241\0301,237,318,4,272,1,6241\0301,323,361,4,272,1,6241\0304,1,17,3,256,2,6241\0304,19,76,3,256,2,6241\0316241,2,13,Bailor Stonehand\03011905,4,17,Jordan\0312,0,0,9,Wetlands\0302,0,0,13,Bailor Stonehand\0302,0,0,13,Loch Modan\0311654,20,1654,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6992,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1656]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, the furs I was expecting. Thank you.$B$BThese came faster than I had expected. They will make good blankets for anyone who wishes to stay here.$B$BPlease feel free to stay as long as you like. My inn is always open and all of our people are welcome here. And don't underestimate a good night's rest, it can make a great difference while you're out traveling.\030$N, please, I beg of you, can you help me? I have not finished my tasks here on the Mesa--I'm in the middle of my Rite of Strength--and my father asked me to deliver these furs to the inn in Bloodhoof.$B$BI'm far from rested enough to complete both my rite and this task for my father. Would you mind going on for me?$B$BThe inn is pleasant and a perfect place to rest during your long travels. I'm sure you'll agree once you see it.\030Bring the Bundle of Furs to Innkeeper Kauth in Bloodhoof Village.\030Yes, young one? What can Kauth do for you?$B$BThe journey here from the Mesa can be a tremendous burden for some, but a welcome sight for others. Which is it for you, I wonder?\030A Task Unfinished\0312,1,42,2,257,2,6775\0302,44,201,2,257,1,6775\0302,206,285,2,257,1,6775\0302,287,317,2,257,4,6775\0302,322,394,2,257,1,6775\0302,396,433,2,257,1,6775\0303,1,65,2,384,1,6775\0301,1,29,4,272,1,6747\0301,31,40,4,272,1,6747\0301,45,82,4,272,1,6747\0301,84,147,4,274,3,6747\0301,152,196,4,272,1,6747\0301,198,258,4,272,1,6747\0301,260,362,4,272,1,6747\0304,1,15,3,256,2,6747\0304,17,42,3,256,2,6747\0304,47,145,3,256,1,6747\0304,147,176,3,256,2,6747\0316747,2,7,Innkeeper Kauth\0312,220,1412,0,\0302,0,0,2,Bloodhoof\0302,0,0,7,Innkeeper Kauth\0302,0,0,7,Bloodhoof Village\0303,0,0,17,Mesa\031\031",[1657]="PARTIAL\031consequences,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, well done! I hope the Alliance chokes on the foul gift we've given them, much like we were forced to choke on the yoke of enslavement to the Scourge!$B$BYou've kept the ideas of Hallow's End true, $N, and for that I salute you. As an extra bonus, let me share some of these Hallow's End treats I have with you. I think you might find them to be quite the enjoyable diversion!\030Celebrate Hallow's End in style... by bringing grief to our enemies in Southshore!$B$BTake one of these specially crafted stink bombs.  It is filled with an odiferous funk that no human - or any weak-willed beast for that matter - can stand to smell.  You'll need to throw it right in the heart of Southshore for it to do its job, so be prepared for a fight against the Alliance!$B$BWhen you've completed this task... this tribute to our liberation, return to me!\030Toss three Forsaken Stink Bombs into the heart of Southshore in Hillsbrad, and return to Darkcaller Yanka at the Wickerman Festival in Tirisfal Glade.\030\030Toss Stink Bomb into Southshore\030Have you delivered our \"gift\" to the people of Southshore?$B$B<Darkcaller Yanka laughs wickedly.>\030Stinking Up Southshore\0312,1,34,2,257,1,15197\0302,36,82,2,261,1,15197\0302,87,134,2,257,1,15197\0302,137,250,2,257,1,15197\0302,253,379,2,263,1,15197\0302,384,417,2,257,1,15197\0302,419,463,2,257,1,15197\0303,1,150,2,384,1,15197\0301,1,14,4,272,1,15197\0301,16,153,4,338,3,15197\0301,158,231,4,272,1,15197\0301,233,314,4,272,1,15197\0301,316,379,4,272,4,15197\0306,1,58,3,256,2,15197\0306,63,97,3,256,1,15197\0305,1,31,3,384,1,15197\03115197,2,8,Darkcaller Yanka\03015197,3,15,Darkcaller Yanka\0312,0,0,2,Southshore\0302,0,0,8,Hillsbrad\0302,0,0,8,Darkcaller Yanka\0302,0,0,8,Wickerman Festival\0302,0,0,8,Tirisfal Glade\0304,0,0,10,Scourge\031\031NPC,15415,OBJECTIVE,3,13,Southshore Stink Bomb Counter",[1658]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $N. The Wickerman Festival will continue to be trouble so long as the abominable Forsaken are allowed to haunt the remnants of Lordaeron. It is NOT a fitting tribute to that once proud kingdom, let me tell you...$B$BHere's some coin for any repairs you might need, and in the spirit of the season I've also included some treats you might like. Happy Hallow's End - let's keep it as safe as possible here in Southshore.\030I need brave individuals to head up to Tirisfal Glade and check out the Wickerman Festival.  I'm not going to lie - heading up there will be dangerous.  The guards at the festival will be exceptionally vicious.  Still, we need to know how big the festival is this year, and how much trouble the Forsaken are going to cause us during Hallow's End.$B$BIf you're up for it, head to Tirisfal and scout out the festival.  Return to me with the information, and I'll make sure you're well compensated.\030Locate the Forsaken's Wickerman Festival in Tirisfal Glade.  Return to Sergeant Hartman in Southshore once you've done so.\030Scout out the Forsaken's Wickerman Festival.\030\030Crashing the Wickerman Festival (PvP)\0312,1,91,2,259,1,15199\0302,94,151,2,257,3,15199\0302,154,210,2,257,3,15199\0302,213,346,2,259,3,15199\0302,351,415,2,257,4,15199\0302,418,495,2,257,1,15199\0303,1,59,2,384,1,15199\0303,62,122,2,384,1,15199\0301,1,14,4,272,1,15199\0301,16,148,4,272,3,15199\0301,150,223,4,272,1,15199\0301,228,354,4,274,4,15199\0301,356,429,4,272,1,15199\0304,1,44,3,384,1,15199\03115199,2,8,Sergeant Hartman\0312,0,0,1,Tirisfal Glade\0302,0,0,5,Tirisfal\0302,0,0,7,Tirisfal Glade\0302,0,0,8,Sergeant Hartman\0302,0,0,8,Southshore\0304,0,0,13,Southshore\031\031",[166]="PARTIAL\031conflict,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031$N, your bravery is remarkable. The People's Militia thanks you for your service to the people of Westfall. With VanCleef dead, this marks the beginning of the end for the Defias Brotherhood. Hopefully some day soon peace will once again grace the plains of this fair land.$B$BI salute you, $gLord:Lady;!\030There is but one task left for you to complete.  Edwin VanCleef must be assassinated.  While it saddens me to condemn any man to a death sentence, it is for the greater good of the people of Westfall that VanCleef is laid to rest once and for all.  Bring me the villain's head once the deed is done.\030Kill Edwin VanCleef and bring his head to Gryan Stoutmantle.\030How goes the hunt for Edwin VanCleef?\030The Defias Brotherhood\0312,1,47,2,257,1,234\0302,50,85,2,257,1,234\0302,88,247,2,265,1,234\0302,250,299,2,257,1,234\0303,1,60,2,384,1,234\0301,1,31,4,272,1,234\0301,33,107,4,272,1,234\0301,109,191,4,304,1,234\0301,193,273,4,280,3,234\0301,278,304,4,272,1,234\0304,1,37,3,256,2,234\031639,2,2,Edwin VanCleef\030639,2,5,Edwin VanCleef\030234,2,5,Gryan Stoutmantle\03015065,4,10,Lady\030639,3,11,Edwin VanCleef\0312,1581,0,0,\0302,0,0,5,Gryan Stoutmantle\031155,19,155,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3637,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1661]="PARTIAL\031conclusion,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030I greet you once again, $N. I am more proud to call you $g brother:sister; than ever before--your dedication is a tribute to us all.$B$BThe time has come for me to bestow a great gift upon you. But know this, for now I give you this freely, but later, when time permits, this will be a much greater challenge to all paladins who choose to undertake my quest.$B$BSpeak to me again and I shall grant you a great boon.\030Speak to Duthorian Rall in Stormwind.\030\030The Tome of Nobility\0312,1,27,2,257,1,6171\0302,29,132,2,257,1,6171\0302,137,193,2,257,1,6171\0302,195,358,2,257,3,6171\0302,363,415,2,257,3,6171\0303,1,37,2,384,1,6171\0316171,2,6,Duthorian Rall\0312,0,0,6,Duthorian Rall\0302,0,0,6,Stormwind\031\031",[1665]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031There it is! He sure didn't want to part with it, but you were persuasive. Well done.$B$BNow for your lesson...\030Ok, here's my mug.  Wait!  Let me finish what's in it first... there we go.\030Bring Bartleby's Mug to Burlguard\030I saw your fight with Bartleby. Nicely done! Did you get his mug?\030Bartleby's Mug\0312,1,18,2,257,1,6090\0302,21,25,2,257,1,6090\0302,28,62,2,257,1,6090\0302,64,75,2,257,1,6090\0303,1,33,2,384,1,6090\0301,1,12,4,272,1,6089\0301,14,74,4,272,1,6089\0301,76,85,4,272,1,6089\0301,90,111,4,272,1,6089\0304,1,31,3,260,1,6089\0304,33,44,3,256,1,6089\0304,46,65,3,256,2,6089\0316090,3,10,Bartleby\0312,0,0,5,Burlguard\0311640,19,1640,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301666,23,1666,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1666]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Who's that?$B$BBurlguard, is that you?$B$BYou'll have to step a little closer. My eyes aren't what they used to be.$B$BWalking up like that, I thought you were a gnoll!\030You've learned a few moves, but you could still use a decent weapon.  I bet if you spoke with Marshal Haggard he could help you.$B$BMarshal Haggard lives in a manor in Elwynn Forest, at the Eastvale Lumber Camp.  He's retired now but he collected a lot of gear during his career.$B$BLet him know I sent you, and with luck he'll have a spare weapon to offer.\030Speak with Marshal Haggard.\030\030Marshal Haggard\0312,1,68,2,257,4,6089\0302,71,128,2,257,4,6089\0302,133,211,2,257,1,6089\0302,214,279,2,257,1,6089\0302,284,357,2,257,1,6089\0303,1,27,2,384,1,6089\0301,1,11,4,272,2,294\0301,16,38,4,272,2,294\0301,43,78,4,272,1,294\0301,80,115,4,336,1,294\0301,120,168,4,272,1,294\031294,2,2,Marshal Haggard\030294,2,3,Marshal Haggard\030294,2,6,Marshal Haggard\0312,0,0,3,Elwynn Forest\0302,0,0,3,Eastvale Lumber Camp\0311665,19,1665,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301667,23,1667,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1667]="PARTIAL\031conflict,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Great, you found it! I feared it was gone forever, used by the Defias to impersonate a Stormwind official. Well that won't happen now, thanks to you.$B$BHere are some weapons I used when I was a Marshal. I kept them in great shape--take your pick!\030Burlguard sent you, did he?  Yes, I have spare weapons around here, but first I have a task for you...$B$BA while ago a Defias villain Dead-tooth Jack tricked me.  It was dark and he was wearing a Stormwind tabard and I thought he was Marshal Dughan.  He said he needed my old Stormwind Marshal's badge and I gave it to him... and then he laughed and ran off before I could catch him!$B$BGet back my badge!  Dead-tooth Jack probably has it stowed in his camp to the south.\030Retrieve Haggard's Badge from Dead-tooth Jack's camp, and return to Marshal Haggard.\030Do you have my badge? I don't want to think of the mischief Dead-tooth Jack could cause with it.\030Dead-tooth Jack\0312,1,27,2,257,2,294\0302,30,102,2,257,1,294\0302,107,162,2,257,1,294\0302,165,250,2,257,1,294\0302,253,326,2,257,1,294\0302,328,384,2,257,4,294\0302,389,406,2,257,1,294\0302,409,472,2,257,1,294\0303,1,84,2,384,1,294\0301,1,20,4,272,1,294\0301,22,106,4,272,1,294\0301,108,149,4,304,1,294\0301,154,203,4,272,1,294\0301,205,247,4,272,1,294\0304,1,21,3,256,2,294\0304,23,96,3,256,4,294\0316093,2,3,Dead-Tooth Jack\030240,2,4,Marshal Dughan\0306093,2,8,Dead-Tooth Jack\0306093,2,9,Dead-Tooth Jack\030294,2,9,Marshal Haggard\0306093,3,16,Dead-Tooth Jack\0312,0,0,9,Dead-tooth Jack's\0302,0,0,9,Marshal Haggard\0311666,19,1666,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6782,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[167]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031My suspicions were correct. My poor brother.... Well, thank you for bringing some conclusion to this mystery, even if the conclusion was grim.\030We were deep in a vast mine in Westfall, hidden beneath a barn in Moonbrook. No clue where these stinkin' thieving types came from. Anyway, the mine tunnel collapsed on us. I got out but the others... well... the others haven't been heard from.$B$BYou look like you might have better luck in there. If you could look for my brother, I'd be thankful.  He always carried his Explorers' League Badge. If you can't find him, that badge would at least give me some peace of mind.\030Bring Foreman Thistlenettle's Explorers' League Badge to Wilder Thistlenettle in Stormwind.\030Did you find any sign of my brother? Is there any hope after all this time?\030Oh Brother. . .\0312,1,76,2,257,1,656\0302,78,131,2,257,1,656\0302,133,172,2,257,1,656\0302,174,200,2,257,1,656\0302,202,208,2,257,1,656\0302,210,244,2,257,1,656\0302,249,298,2,257,4,656\0302,300,349,2,257,4,656\0302,352,397,2,257,1,656\0302,399,474,2,265,4,656\0303,1,91,2,384,1,656\0301,1,27,4,272,1,656\0301,29,47,4,272,1,656\0301,49,142,4,272,4,656\0304,1,36,3,256,2,656\0304,38,75,3,258,2,656\031626,2,11,Foreman Thistlenettle\030656,2,11,Wilder Thistlenettle\0312,1581,0,0,\0302,0,0,1,Westfall\0302,0,0,1,Moonbrook\0302,0,0,11,Wilder Thistlenettle\0302,0,0,11,Stormwind\031\031ITEM,1875,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1678]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Vejrek sure was an ugly one, eh?  Nicely done, $n!  You have what it takes, now let's start your lesson...$B$BYou may not know it, but a strong defense is very important to a warrior.  It keeps him standing against foes that'd fell others, and that's what your allies need.\030If you want to rise in the ranks of the warriors, then you better be tough.  I can teach you new moves but before that, prove to me you can handle yourself against real foes.$B$BVejrek is the toughest troll you'll find in these parts, and he's who you have to beat.  He has a hut in the foothills just south of Frostmane Hold$B$BBring me Vejrek's head and I'll know you have mettle.\030Bring Vejrek's Head to Muren Stormpike in Ironforge.\030Have you been to Vejrek's hut, $n?  Is that troll stink I smell on you?\030Vejrek\0312,1,75,2,259,4,6114\0302,78,174,2,257,1,6114\0302,179,265,2,257,1,6114\0302,268,325,2,257,1,6114\0302,330,382,2,257,1,6114\0303,1,52,2,384,1,6114\0301,1,32,4,272,2,6114\0301,35,50,4,272,1,6114\0301,53,106,4,272,1,6114\0301,111,183,4,272,1,6114\0301,186,273,4,274,1,6114\0304,1,34,3,256,2,6114\0304,37,71,3,256,2,6114\0316113,2,3,Vejrek\0306114,2,6,Muren Stormpike\0306113,4,7,Vejrek\0312,0,0,4,Frostmane Hold\0302,0,0,6,Muren Stormpike\0302,0,0,6,Ironforge\0303,0,0,12,Vejrek's\0311679,19,1679,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301680,23,1680,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6799,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1679]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, $N. I heard the warriors of Dun Morogh bouncing your name around. I hope you haven't spent all your time in the breweries!\030Hello, warrior!  You show a lot of promise, but you still need to learn some tricks and Muren Stormpike is just the dwarf to teach you.$B$BYou can find Muren at the Hall of Arms in the Military Ward of Ironforge.  Talk to him when you're ready to learn what it is to be a warrior.\030Speak with Muren Stormpike.\030\030Muren Stormpike\0312,1,15,2,257,1,1229\0302,18,135,2,259,1,1229\0302,140,212,2,257,1,1229\0302,215,280,2,257,1,1229\0303,1,27,2,384,1,1229\0301,9,69,4,272,1,6114\0301,71,126,4,274,3,6114\0316114,2,2,Muren Stormpike\0306114,2,5,Muren Stormpike\0312,0,0,3,Hall of Arms\0302,0,0,3,Military Ward of Ironforge\0311638,22,1638,UNKNOWN\0301684,22,1684,UNKNOWN\0301678,23,1678,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[168]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you for collecting these, $N. Your efforts will help bring peace to the dead in the wake of this tragedy. I will see to it that the families are notified.\030Many of my friends perished that horrible day when the mine tunnel caved in.  If your adventures happen to bring you into that wing of the mine in Moonbrook, please keep an eye out for any sign which might identify them.  If you come across any of their Miners' Union Cards, bring them back to me and I'll make sure their families get some resolution from this horrible accident.\030Retrieve 4 Miners' Union Cards and return them to Wilder Thistlenettle in Stormwind.\030Were you able to retrieve any of my old co-worker's Miners' Union Cards?\030Collecting Memories\0312,1,76,2,257,1,656\0302,79,220,2,257,4,656\0302,223,379,2,257,4,656\0303,1,84,2,384,1,656\0301,1,35,4,272,1,656\0301,37,111,4,280,3,656\0301,113,160,4,272,3,656\0304,1,72,3,256,2,656\031656,2,4,Wilder Thistlenettle\0312,1581,0,0,\0302,0,0,2,Moonbrook\0302,0,0,4,Wilder Thistlenettle\0302,0,0,4,Stormwind\031\031ITEM,1894,OBJECTIVE,4,15,",[1680]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Muren sent you, did he?  Yes, I can make you a nice weapon... but before I do that, I have a favor to ask of you.$B$BDon't worry.  It's plenty dangerous and could mean your death; it's exactly the sort of job a warrior wants.\030Now that you've learned some moves, it's time to get you a decent weapon.  Speak with Tormus Deepforge.  He can make you a weapon I'm sure you'll like.$B$BYou'll find Tormus here in Ironforge, at the Great Forge.\030Speak with Tormus Deepforge.\030\030Tormus Deepforge\0312,1,73,2,257,1,6114\0302,76,103,2,257,1,6114\0302,106,151,2,257,1,6114\0302,156,212,2,257,1,6114\0303,1,28,2,384,1,6114\0301,1,23,4,272,2,6031\0301,26,61,4,272,1,6031\0301,63,113,4,272,1,6031\0301,118,129,4,272,1,6031\0301,132,225,4,274,4,6031\0316031,2,2,Tormus Deepforge\0306031,2,5,Tormus Deepforge\0312,0,0,4,Ironforge\0302,0,0,4,Great Forge\0311678,19,1678,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301681,23,1681,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1681]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You found it! Well done!$B$BI hope you killed a host of Dark Iron dwarves while searching. I fear that Ironband's compound won't be the last place we see them.$B$BBut thank you for the ore, $N. I'm eager to work it and find its properties.\030My mentor, Sturgy Ironband, had a compound south of Helm's Bed Lake in eastern Dun Morogh.  There he taught blacksmithing and he was the best.$B$BBut one day, one of his students brought him a load of strange ore.  Master Ironband called it umbral ore and was eager to work with it, but soon after it arrived... a band of Dark Iron dwarves attacked his compound.  They killed everyone!$B$BEnter Ironband's compound, $N, and avenge my master's death.  And bring me the load of umbral ore that caused it.\030Bring a load of Umbral Ore to Tormus Deepforge in Ironforge.\030Have you entered Ironband's Compound? Did you find the umbral ore?\030Ironband's Compound\0312,1,90,2,257,1,6031\0302,93,142,2,257,1,6031\0302,147,213,2,257,1,6031\0302,216,311,2,257,1,6031\0302,313,362,2,261,1,6031\0302,365,385,2,257,1,6031\0302,390,449,2,257,1,6031\0302,452,502,2,257,1,6031\0303,1,60,2,384,1,6031\0301,1,13,4,272,1,6031\0301,15,24,4,272,1,6031\0301,29,90,4,274,3,6031\0301,92,159,4,272,1,6031\0301,164,193,4,272,1,6031\0301,195,239,4,272,1,6031\0304,1,37,3,256,2,6031\0304,39,66,3,256,2,6031\0316031,2,9,Tormus Deepforge\0312,0,0,1,Helm's Bed Lake\0302,0,0,9,Tormus Deepforge\0302,0,0,9,Ironforge\0311680,19,1680,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301682,23,1682,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6800,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1682]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Here are some weapons, hot off the anvil and made with the new umbral ore you brought me!$B$BPlease, $N, take your pick!\030\030\030\030Grey Iron Weapons\0311,1,89,4,272,1,6031\0301,94,120,4,272,1,6031\031\031\0311681,19,1681,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1683]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $N. It is good to know Vorlus is defeated and our moonwell cleansed, and it is good to see young warriors eager to keep our beloved Teldrassil free of corruption.$B$BNow let us begin your training...\030Before I can teach you, you must show me your resolve.$B$BThe satyr Vorlus Vilehoof has found one of our remote moonwells, southeast of the Ban'ethil Barrow Den.  He now splashes within it, defiling its pure waters with his filth.$B$BFind Vorlus at the moonwell and destroy him.  Bring me his horn as proof and I will begin your advanced training as a warrior.$B$BThe path to the moonwell is hidden well, $N, but stay focused and alert and you will find it.\030Bring the Horn of Vorlus to Elanaria in Darnassus.\030Do you have the horn, $N? Is our moonwell free of the fiend Vorlus?\030Vorlus Vilehoof\0312,1,54,2,257,1,4088\0302,59,161,2,257,1,4088\0302,164,230,2,257,1,4088\0302,235,278,2,261,1,4088\0302,281,360,2,257,3,4088\0302,365,457,2,257,3,4088\0303,1,50,2,384,1,4088\0301,1,14,4,272,1,4088\0301,16,173,4,276,1,4088\0301,178,210,4,272,1,4088\0304,1,25,3,256,2,4088\0304,27,67,3,256,2,4088\0316128,2,2,Vorlus Vilehoof\0304088,2,7,Elanaria\0312,0,0,7,Elanaria\0302,0,0,7,Darnassus\0311684,19,1684,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301686,23,1686,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6805,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1684]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I bid you greetings, $n.  Your name rings loudly in Darnassus, for you show promise.  But we shall soon see if you possess the strength of will to follow the path of the warrior.\030Greetings, warrior.  Your skill grows, but there is more to your profession than you may believe.  To further progress, you must soon find a teacher.$B$BThe warrior Elanaria dwells in Darnassus, at the Warrior's Terrace.  She can instruct you.\030Speak with Elanaria.\030\030Elanaria\0312,1,19,2,257,1,0\0302,22,97,2,257,4,0\0302,100,149,2,257,1,0\0302,154,220,2,257,1,0\0302,223,243,2,257,1,0\0303,1,20,2,384,1,0\0301,1,24,4,272,1,4088\0301,27,84,4,272,1,4088\0301,87,178,4,272,4,4088\0314088,2,4,Elanaria\0304088,2,6,Elanaria\0312,0,0,4,Darnassus\0302,0,0,4,Warrior's Terrace\0304,0,0,8,Darnassus\0311638,22,1638,UNKNOWN\0301679,22,1679,UNKNOWN\0301683,23,1683,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1685]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I'm glad someone was able to get a hold of you, $n. I was beginning to fear the worst. It would be a shame to lose you, after the time we've invested in you. We can talk later, though. Your training is the only important thing now.\030Isn't that how it always works? Was looking for you all day and couldn't find you, now when I'm not expecting it, you come and walk right up to me.$B$BI've wasted enough time trying to find you, so I won't delay you any longer. Master Gakin's summoned you for additional training. Seems to me you should seek him out as soon as possible.$B$BYou'll find him in the basement of the Slaughtered Lamb tavern. By the way, you might want to keep that particular location quiet. Don't want word spreading about it.\030Report to Gakin the Darkbinder in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind.\030\030Gakin's Summons\0312,1,31,2,257,2,6121\0302,33,147,2,257,1,6121\0302,152,227,2,257,1,6121\0302,229,280,2,257,1,6121\0302,282,337,2,259,4,6121\0302,342,404,2,257,1,6121\0302,406,471,2,259,4,6121\0302,473,507,2,257,1,6121\0303,1,64,2,384,1,6121\0301,1,51,4,272,1,6122\0301,53,86,4,272,1,6122\0301,88,157,4,272,4,6122\0301,159,184,4,272,1,6122\0301,186,231,4,272,1,6122\0316122,2,9,Gakin the Darkbinder\0312,0,0,9,Gakin the Darkbinder\0302,0,0,9,Mage Quarter of Stormwind\0311715,22,1715,UNKNOWN\0301688,23,1688,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301688,24,1688,UNKNOWN\031",[1686]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Bravely done, $N.$B$BYou have given the Shade of Elura much deserved peace, and we will use the gathered elunite to make a fine weapon for you.\030You have learned much, $N.  Now we will craft you a weapon.  A warrior's weapon.$B$BTo do this, you must travel to Darkshore.$B$BLong ago a ship crashed upon the rocks near the Auberdine lighthouse, scattering many crates of elunite ore along the ocean floor.$B$BFirst, you must defeat the elunite's guardian, the Shade of Elura.  Once the ship's captain, she cursed herself to roam the deeps and protect her shipment for all time.  Defeat her, gain her medallion, and gather the crates of lost Elunite.\030Bring 8 loads of Elunite Ore and the Medallion of Elura to Elanaria in Darnassus.\030Have you defeated the Shade of Elura, $N? And do you have the lost elunite ore?\030The Shade of Elura\0312,1,26,2,257,1,4088\0302,29,59,2,257,3,4088\0302,62,80,2,257,1,4088\0302,85,125,2,257,1,4088\0302,130,259,2,321,1,4088\0302,264,329,2,257,1,4088\0302,332,431,2,269,1,4088\0302,434,503,2,261,1,4088\0303,1,81,2,384,1,4088\0301,1,17,4,272,1,4088\0301,22,143,4,280,3,4088\0304,1,41,3,256,2,4088\0304,43,79,3,260,2,4088\0316133,2,6,Shade of Elura\0304088,2,9,Elanaria\0306133,4,11,Shade of Elura\0306133,3,12,Shade of Elura\0312,0,0,4,Darkshore\0302,0,0,5,Auberdine\0302,0,0,9,Elanaria\0302,0,0,9,Darnassus\0311683,19,1683,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301692,23,1692,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6808,OBJECTIVE,8,15,\030ITEM,6809,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1687]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031WOW, that was a real life ghost! That was so awesome - I can't wait to tell everyone back at the orphanage. Captain Grayson... he even looked like a pirate! When I grow up I wanna be a ghost pirate too!$B$BThanks for taking me to Westfall, $N. I know there are scary things out there in the wilds of Westfall, and I hope I wasn't too much of a pain. You're awesome!\030Sometimes late at night, our matrons at the orphanage will tell us spooky stories.  Those RULE!  There's one about a ghost that haunts a lighthouse in Westfall.  They say he was a pirate captain who had his ship taken from him by other pirates.  Wow!$B$BCould you please take me to the lighthouse in Westfall?  I wanna see if the ghost of that captain is there!  I promise to stay close to you; I won't run off or anything!\030Take the orphan to see the lighthouse off the coast of Westfall.$B\030Go to the Westfall Lighthouse.\030Are we there yet?\030Spooky Lighthouse\0312,1,82,2,257,3,14305\0302,85,95,2,257,1,14305\0302,98,160,2,257,1,14305\0302,163,244,2,257,1,14305\0302,247,250,2,257,1,14305\0302,255,309,2,257,4,14305\0302,312,361,2,257,4,14305\0302,364,423,2,257,1,14305\0303,1,64,2,384,1,14305\0301,1,32,4,272,1,14305\0301,34,107,4,272,1,14305\0301,109,126,4,272,1,14305\0301,128,156,4,272,1,14305\0301,158,202,4,272,1,14305\0301,207,243,4,272,1,14305\0301,245,349,4,274,3,14305\0301,351,365,4,272,1,14305\0305,1,17,3,256,2,14305\0304,1,30,3,384,1,14305\031392,4,12,Captain Grayson\0312,0,0,3,Westfall\0302,0,0,6,Westfall\0304,0,0,15,Westfall\0303,0,0,19,Westfall Lighthouse\0311468,19,1468,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1688]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Surena was talented, but not enough so to gain mastery of warlock magic on her own. It's a shame to see talent wasted, but sometimes it is necessary.$B$BI hope my investment in you will bear different results.\030I had a student named Surena Caledon. She stood where you stand now, eager to learn of warlock magic, and possessing no small bit of talent. More than that she was young and pleasing to the eye. Had I seen it then, the traitorous trollop!$B$BThe thieving wench ran off with one of the Defias, Erlan Drudgemoor. While her loss is of little importance, I gifted her a bloodstone choker that I must have.$B$BHer life means nothing to me now. You will find her at the Brackwell Pumpkin Patch. Retrieve what is mine.\030Retrieve Surena's Choker for Gakin the Darkbinder in Stormwind.\030Even the older and wiser can be unmanned by the wiles of youth and beauty, $N. A piece of advice you would do well to remember throughout your life.\030Surena Caledon\0312,1,37,2,257,1,6122\0302,39,140,2,257,1,6122\0302,142,194,2,257,1,6122\0302,196,238,2,257,1,6122\0302,243,310,2,257,1,6122\0302,312,401,2,257,1,6122\0302,406,438,2,257,1,6122\0302,440,488,2,257,3,6122\0302,490,511,2,257,1,6122\0303,1,63,2,384,1,6122\0301,1,83,4,272,1,6122\0301,85,149,4,272,1,6122\0301,154,209,4,274,3,6122\0304,1,78,3,256,1,6122\0304,80,148,3,256,4,6122\031881,2,1,Surena Caledon\030880,2,5,Erlan Drudgemoor\0306122,2,10,Gakin the Darkbinder\0312,0,0,8,Brackwell Pumpkin Patch\0302,0,0,10,Stormwind\0311689,23,1689,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6810,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1689]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You did better than I expected, $N, but as well as I'd hoped. Now, you can learn to command your subjugated voidwalker, an ally you will find valuable in the trials that are sure to stand before you.$B$BI have nothing more to teach you at the present, but I am far from done with you, $N.\030By retrieving my choker and besting Surena, you've proven that you're at least as capable as she was.$B$BWith that said, I can tell you're direly in need of training. You can manage the flows of magic, yes, but being a warlock is much more than that.$B$BI will show you how to command a voidwalker, but before I can, you must call one forth at a summoning circle and subdue it using whatever weapons--physical and magical--you have at your disposal. Use the magic of this choker at the summoning circle below.\030Using the Bloodstone Choker, summon and subdue a voidwalker, then return the Bloodstone Choker to Gakin the Darkbinder in Stormwind.\030I cannot show you how to control a voidwalker until you have overtaken one.\030The Binding\0312,1,101,2,257,1,6122\0302,106,166,2,259,1,6122\0302,168,250,2,257,1,6122\0302,255,449,2,257,3,6122\0302,451,509,2,257,1,6122\0303,1,132,2,384,1,6122\0301,1,61,4,272,1,6122\0301,63,199,4,272,3,6122\0301,204,288,4,272,1,6122\0304,1,75,3,256,1,6122\0311860,2,4,Voidwalker\0301860,2,6,Voidwalker\0306122,2,6,Gakin the Darkbinder\0301860,4,8,Voidwalker\0301860,3,10,Voidwalker\0312,0,0,6,Gakin the Darkbinder\0302,0,0,6,Stormwind\0311688,19,1688,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,5676,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Summoned Voidwalker",[169]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Fantastic work, $N! Gath'Ilzogg led those brutes into battle, killing many innocent humans. Vindication is ours. This is the first step in reclaiming the keep for the kingdom of Stormwind!\030Wanted! Gath'Ilzogg, Leader of the Blackrock attacks on Stonewatch Keep and raids against the township of Lakeshire. $B$BGath'Ilzogg is extremely dangerous.  He is reportedly holed up in the recently conquered keep plotting the Blackrock clan's further crimes against humanity.  The orc infestation must be quelled at all costs.  A gracious reward will be given to whatever brave soul can deliver the head of Gath'Ilzogg to Magistrate Solomon.\030Kill Gath'Ilzogg and bring his head to Magistrate Solomon in Lakeshire for the reward.\030What do you have there, $R?\030Wanted: Gath'Ilzogg\0312,1,7,2,257,1,0\0302,9,116,2,261,1,0\0302,122,156,2,257,1,0\0302,159,277,2,257,1,0\0302,280,328,2,257,1,0\0302,331,443,2,257,3,0\0303,1,86,2,384,1,0\0301,1,19,4,272,1,344\0301,21,91,4,276,1,344\0301,93,112,4,272,1,344\0301,114,188,4,272,1,344\0304,1,27,3,256,2,344\031334,2,2,Gath'Ilzogg\030334,2,3,Gath'Ilzogg\030334,2,6,Gath'Ilzogg\030344,2,6,Magistrate Solomon\030798,2,6,Solomon\030334,2,7,Gath'Ilzogg\030344,2,7,Magistrate Solomon\030798,2,7,Solomon\030334,4,9,Gath'Ilzogg\0312,44,1433,0,\0302,0,0,6,Magistrate Solomon\0302,0,0,7,Magistrate Solomon\0302,0,0,7,Lakeshire\031\031OBJECT,60,GIVER,?,9,Wanted: Gath'Ilzogg\030ITEM,3633,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1690]="PARTIAL\031conflict,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Now that's what I call efficiency! You've helped thin out the nomad's numbers enough now that we can start to think about how we can win back those water wells.$B$BThe Gadgetzan Water Company thanks you for your help, but we're far from done in dealing with those foul nomads. Listen close - here's what we need next...\030You there!  It's time for you to be a big helper to the Gadgetzan Water Company.$B$BThe Wastewander nomads out in the Tanaris desert have seized almost all the water wells!  Without access to them, our water supply will dry up in no time.  If you want to get in our good graces, then you'll help us bring justice to those nomads!$B$BHead east of here and bring down ten Wastewander Bandits and Thieves, then report back to me on the double.  Justice waits for no man... goblin... bah, just get on it!\030Take down 10 Wastewander Bandits and Thieves east of Gadgetzan, then report back to Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle.\030Back so soon? I hope you were able to bring some goblin-style justice to those Wastewander Bandits and Thieves like I asked you to!\030Wastewander Justice\0312,1,10,2,257,1,7407\0302,13,80,2,257,1,7407\0302,85,172,2,257,1,7407\0302,175,238,2,257,3,7407\0302,241,329,2,259,4,7407\0302,334,440,2,257,1,7407\0302,443,469,2,257,1,7407\0302,471,479,2,257,1,7407\0302,481,500,2,257,1,7407\0303,1,112,2,384,1,7407\0301,1,34,4,304,1,7407\0301,36,160,4,304,1,7407\0301,165,276,4,272,1,7407\0301,278,319,4,274,1,7407\0304,1,13,3,256,2,7407\0304,15,131,3,258,3,7407\0317407,2,10,Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle\0312,440,1446,0,\0302,0,0,2,Gadgetzan Water Company\0302,0,0,3,Tanaris\0302,0,0,10,Gadgetzan\0302,0,0,10,Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle\0311691,23,1691,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,5618,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Wastewander Bandit\030NPC,5616,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Wastewander Thief",[1691]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Top notch work, $N... top notch! You've thinned down the nomad population to a point where we can actually take the fight to them!$B$BIf you haven't already, talk to Spigot Operator Luglunket here; he gives a bounty on any of the Wastewander water pouches you may have run across while bringing those nomads to justice!\030We need you to take on the stronger ranks of the Wastewander nomads now.  You've done a good job thus far, but if we are to take back those water wells, then it only makes sense to do it against as few nomads as possible!$B$BThis time around we need you to take down their rogues, assassins, and shadow mages.  You'll find them east and southeast of here.$B$BI'm not going to lie to you - they're a nasty lot.  Do this for us though, and we'll be on our way to taking back what is rightfully ours!\030Take down 10 Wastewander Shadow Mages, 8 Wastewander Rogues, and 6 Wastewander Assassins for Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle in Gadgetzan.$B\030Well, were you able to take out those nomads like I asked? The Gadgetzan Water Company is developing plans based on your success here! Don't let us down, now...\030More Wastewander Justice\0312,1,72,2,259,1,7407\0302,75,221,2,257,4,7407\0302,226,309,2,259,1,7407\0302,312,355,2,257,1,7407\0302,360,409,2,257,3,7407\0302,412,497,2,257,1,7407\0303,1,134,2,384,1,7407\0301,1,21,4,272,1,7407\0301,23,32,4,272,1,7407\0301,34,130,4,276,1,7407\0301,135,319,4,272,4,7407\0304,1,58,3,256,2,7407\0304,60,134,3,256,1,7407\0304,136,160,3,256,1,7407\0314244,2,3,Shadow\0304244,2,7,Shadow\0307407,2,7,Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle\0307408,4,11,Spigot Operator Luglunket\0312,440,1446,0,\0302,0,0,7,Gadgetzan\0304,0,0,11,Spigot Operator Luglunket\0311690,19,1690,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,5615,OBJECTIVE,8,13,Wastewander Rogue\030NPC,5623,OBJECTIVE,6,13,Wastewander Assassin\030NPC,5617,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Wastewander Shadow Mage",[1692]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, elunite ore. This is a fine metal to work with, for it is blessed by the goddess Elune herself. It would be an honor to craft weapons with it.$B$BPlease wait while I work...\030I have placed the elunite you gathered into a case.  Take it to the blacksmith Mathiel, and he will craft for you an elunite weapon.$B$BMathiel is to the south, on the other side of this building.\030Bring the Case of Elunite to Smith Mathiel.\030Greetings, young warrior.  How might my skills serve you?\030Smith Mathiel\0312,1,51,2,257,1,4088\0302,54,132,2,257,3,4088\0302,137,196,2,257,1,4088\0303,1,43,2,384,1,4088\0301,1,16,4,272,1,6142\0301,18,99,4,272,1,6142\0301,101,146,4,272,4,6142\0301,151,177,4,272,1,6142\0304,1,25,3,256,1,6142\0304,28,57,3,256,4,6142\0316142,2,2,Mathiel\0306142,2,3,Mathiel\0306142,2,4,Mathiel\0312,0,0,4,Smith Mathiel\0311686,19,1686,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301693,23,1693,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1693]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031$N, I have crafted these weapons with the elunite you brought to me. Please, take whichever most suits you.$B$BAnd I must thank you. Working with elunite is both an honor and a pleasure.\030\030\030\030Weapons of Elunite\0311,1,68,4,272,1,6142\0301,70,107,4,272,1,6142\0301,112,132,4,272,1,6142\0301,134,186,4,272,1,6142\031\031\0311692,19,1692,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1698]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hah! So you heard of my challenge, did you?$B$BWell sit down and listen. Have a drink, and savor it... because it might be your last.\030Yorus Barleybrew has issued a challenge to all able warriors of the Alliance.  He waits at the Lakeshire Inn, in Redridge, and pledges a grand reward to anyone able to pass his trial.\030Speak with Yorus Barleybrew.\030\030Yorus Barleybrew\0312,1,77,2,257,1,0\0302,80,183,2,257,1,0\0303,1,28,2,384,1,0\0301,1,4,4,272,1,6166\0301,6,43,4,272,2,6166\0301,48,72,4,272,1,6166\0301,74,102,4,272,1,6166\0301,104,133,4,274,4,6166\0316166,2,1,Yorus Barleybrew\0306166,2,3,Yorus Barleybrew\0312,0,0,2,Lakeshire Inn\0302,0,0,2,Redridge\0311699,23,1699,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301699,24,1699,UNKNOWN\031",[1699]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031You made it! Well done! Three cheers for $N!\030I call my challenge the Rethban Gauntlet.  To pass the trial, all you must do is enter the Rethban Caverns, to the first fork, then return here.  Easy!  Except there are a few wrinkles...$B$BYou have to return within an hour.$B$BThere are whole heaps of Redridge Gnolls in the way.$B$BBefore you start, you have to take a swig of my family's signature drink: Barleybrew Scalder!$B$BSo what do you say?  The Rethban Caverns are in the foothills north of Lakeshire.  Are you ready to run the Rethban Gauntlet?\030Enter the Rethban Caverns, reach the first fork, and return to Yorus Barleybrew within the time allowed.$B$BYou must not die and release your spirit.\030Enter the Rethban Caverns\030Time is wasting, $N.  If I were you, I'd get going...\030The Rethban Gauntlet\0312,1,41,2,257,1,6166\0302,44,144,2,257,1,6166\0302,147,151,2,257,1,6166\0302,154,187,2,257,1,6166\0302,192,225,2,257,1,6166\0302,230,281,2,257,1,6166\0302,286,378,2,257,1,6166\0302,383,401,2,257,2,6166\0302,404,463,2,257,1,6166\0302,466,507,2,257,2,6166\0303,1,104,2,384,1,6166\0303,109,149,2,392,1,6166\0301,1,12,4,272,1,6166\0301,14,23,4,272,1,6166\0301,25,44,4,272,1,6166\0305,1,20,3,256,1,6166\0305,23,53,3,256,4,6166\0304,1,25,3,384,1,6166\0316166,2,11,Yorus Barleybrew\0312,0,0,9,Lakeshire\0302,0,0,11,Yorus Barleybrew\0311702,23,1702,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[17]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done $N, you've proven your worth once again! The caps will be an interesting study, yon verily!$B$BAnd now, as promised, enjoy a taste of one of my more potent restorative brews from my personal stock...$B$BIf you are a skilled alchemist, then perhaps we might have some additional business to conduct. Regardless, I thank you for your assistance!\030I've heard about a newly discovered plant called the magenta fungus caps.  They grow in clusters at the Uldaman dig site and can be found in the early tunnels and deep within the less-explored areas.  I want to study their potential use in alchemy, and that's where you come in.$B$BFind the magenta cap clusters and bring me a dozen caps.  Be warned, the clusters may spew out poison spores if jostled.$B$BDo this for me, and I'll whip up a batch of one of my famous restorative elixirs for you!\030Bring 12 Magenta Fungus Caps to Ghak Healtouch in Thelsamar.\030Have you obtained the magenta fungus caps I need for my alchemical work? No caps - no reward!\030Uldaman Reagent Run\0312,1,73,2,257,1,1470\0302,76,199,2,257,1,1470\0302,202,278,2,259,1,1470\0302,283,338,2,257,1,1470\0302,341,402,2,261,4,1470\0302,407,495,2,257,1,1470\0303,1,60,2,384,1,1470\0301,1,50,4,272,1,1470\0301,52,101,4,272,3,1470\0301,106,209,4,272,1,1470\0301,214,308,4,272,4,1470\0301,310,353,4,272,1,1470\0304,1,72,3,258,2,1470\0304,74,93,3,256,1,1470\0311470,2,7,Ghak Healtouch\0312,1517,1418,0,\0302,0,0,2,Uldaman\0302,0,0,7,Ghak Healtouch\0302,0,0,7,Thelsamar\0312500,19,2500,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,8047,OBJECTIVE,12,15,",[170]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031If the problems we've had here are indicative of what is happening elsewhere in our lands, by Magni's beard, we have some troubles ahead of us! I can only hope that the king and Senate are taking steps to deal with the threat the troggs pose.\030I hope you're here to lend us a hand, $c. After the last trogg attack, we could use all the help we can get.$B$BI hear the buggers have been popping up all across the lands, and it seems Coldridge Valley is no exception. They've been spotted all over the hills to the southeast and near the frozen lake.$B$BAnd that's not all, just a few nights ago, they attacked and overran our camp to the west! $B$BWe're a bit shorthanded here, $g lad : lass;, and we need strong arms to help drive the troggs back.\030Balir Frosthammer wants you to kill 6 Rockjaw Troggs and 6 Burly Rockjaw Troggs.\030Tenacious little buggers, aren't they?\030A New Threat\0312,1,41,2,259,3,713\0302,43,108,2,261,4,713\0302,113,220,2,257,4,713\0302,222,303,2,257,1,713\0302,308,397,2,261,1,713\0302,403,502,2,259,1,713\0303,1,80,2,386,1,713\0301,1,143,4,272,4,713\0301,145,242,4,278,3,713\0304,1,38,3,256,2,713\031713,2,7,Balir Frosthammer\0312,132,1426,0,\031179,19,179,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,707,OBJECTIVE,6,13,Rockjaw Trogg\030NPC,724,OBJECTIVE,6,13,Burly Rockjaw Trogg",[1700]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Furen wrote this? How dare he! Why, I taught him everything he knows! To think he could teach me something is outrageous! Outrageous!$B$BHm... but there is something in his notes that I'd like to try...\030I made a copy of my notes on the techniques I learned while making your armor, and I need them sent to Grimand Elmore.  He's here in the Dwarven District, in the weapon shop.$B$BAnd duck when you give these to him.  He's fiercely proud of his skills, and won't like the idea of learning something from me...\030Bring Furen's Notes to Grimand Elmore.\030Hello, and well met. How might I be of service to you?\030Grimand Elmore\0312,1,118,2,259,1,5413\0302,121,174,2,257,1,5413\0302,179,214,2,257,1,5413\0302,217,307,2,257,1,5413\0303,1,38,2,384,1,5413\0301,1,17,4,272,2,1416\0301,19,30,4,272,1,1416\0301,32,69,4,272,1,1416\0301,71,121,4,272,4,1416\0301,123,133,4,272,1,1416\0301,144,202,4,274,1,1416\0304,1,20,3,256,1,1416\0304,22,54,3,256,4,1416\0311416,2,1,Grimand Elmore\0301416,2,5,Grimand Elmore\0312,0,0,1,Grimand Elmore\0302,0,0,2,Dwarven District\0302,0,0,5,Grimand Elmore\0311701,19,1701,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301705,23,1705,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301705,24,1705,UNKNOWN\031",[1701]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You got it all? Amazing! I was afraid those chimaeras would eat you up for sure!$B$BWell let's get started on that armor...\030So I gave you a nice shield, but we don't have to stop there.  I know the secrets to make extremely hard mail armor.  It's not easy and it takes very rare materials, but if you're willing to do the legwork then I'll make a piece for you.$B$BWhat do you say, $N?  If you're up for the challenge, then I'll give you a list of what to get and where to get them.\030Gather the materials Furen Longbeard requires, and bring them to him in Stormwind.\030How goes the scavenger hunt, $N? Do you have the materials?\030Fire Hardened Mail\0312,1,61,2,257,1,5413\0302,64,116,2,257,1,5413\0302,119,237,2,257,4,5413\0302,242,261,2,257,2,5413\0302,264,358,2,257,4,5413\0303,1,82,2,384,1,5413\0301,1,15,4,272,2,5413\0301,17,24,4,272,1,5413\0301,26,80,4,272,4,5413\0301,85,123,4,272,1,5413\0304,1,32,3,256,2,5413\0304,34,59,3,256,2,5413\0315413,2,6,Furen Longbeard\0312,0,0,6,Stormwind\0311702,19,1702,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6838,OBJECTIVE,50,15,\030ITEM,6839,OBJECTIVE,12,15,\030ITEM,6840,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,6841,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1702]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, Barleybrew Scalder.  Great stuff!  So you've been to see Yorus, eh?$B$BI can get you a shield, yes $gsir:ma'am;!  You won't find a better one, and that's no lying!\030You really showed what you were made of when you ran the Rethban Gauntlet, $N.  And I'm true to my word.  I'll get you the reward I promised...$B$BExcept it's in Stormwind.$B$BTalk to my friend, Furen Longbeard, in the Dwarven District of Stormwind.  He's the best shieldsmith you'll ever meet, and he owes me a big favor.$B$BHere, take Furen this cask of Barleybrew Scalder and ask him for a shield.  He'll give you a nice one.\030Bring the Cask of Scalder to Furen Longbeard.\030Hello! Dry times, don't you think?\030The Shieldsmith\0312,1,78,2,257,1,6166\0302,81,104,2,257,1,6166\0302,107,143,2,257,1,6166\0302,148,172,2,257,1,6166\0302,177,249,2,257,1,6166\0302,252,322,2,257,1,6166\0302,327,400,2,257,1,6166\0302,403,428,2,257,1,6166\0303,1,45,2,384,1,6166\0301,1,23,4,272,1,5413\0301,26,37,4,272,1,5413\0301,40,71,4,272,2,5413\0301,76,116,4,272,1,5413\0301,119,167,4,272,1,5413\0304,1,6,3,256,1,5413\0304,8,34,3,256,2,5413\0315413,2,5,Furen Longbeard\0305413,2,9,Furen Longbeard\0312,0,0,4,Stormwind\0302,0,0,5,Dwarven District of Stormwind\0302,0,0,9,Furen Longbeard\0311699,19,1699,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301701,23,1701,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1703]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I bid you greetings, warrior.\030I made a copy of my notes on the techniques I learned while making your armor, and need them sent to the blacksmith Mathiel.  He lives in Darnassus which is quite a long way off, but I'm sure he'll be very grateful to learn what I've learned.\030Bring Furen's Notes to Mathiel.\030I bid you greetings, $C.\030Mathiel\0312,1,124,2,259,1,5413\0302,127,242,2,257,1,5413\0303,1,31,2,384,1,5413\0301,1,29,4,272,1,6142\0304,1,24,3,256,1,6142\0316142,2,1,Mathiel\0306142,2,3,Mathiel\0312,0,0,2,Darnassus\0302,0,0,3,Mathiel\0311701,19,1701,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301710,23,1710,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301710,24,1710,UNKNOWN\031",[1704]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh my! These notes are amazing! And what's more... they're incredible and they're stupendous and they make my knees go all a-wobbly!$B$BFuren had a breakthrough! A real breakthrough! I can't wait to try out his new technique!\030I made a copy of my notes on the techniques I learned while making your armor, and need someone to take them to Klockmort Spannerspan.  He's a gnomish blacksmith in Ironforge and when he learns what I've learned... I bet he'll pull off his own beard in excitement.\030Bring Furen's Notes to Klockmort Spannerspan.\030Good day, or morning or evening. I can't tell from way down here. So do you have business for me?\030Klockmort Spannerspan\0312,1,134,2,259,1,5413\0302,137,214,2,257,1,5413\0302,216,264,2,257,1,5413\0303,1,45,2,384,1,5413\0301,8,31,4,272,1,6169\0301,33,50,4,272,1,6169\0301,52,132,4,272,1,6169\0301,137,161,4,272,1,6169\0301,163,182,4,272,1,6169\0301,184,225,4,272,1,6169\0304,1,32,3,256,1,6169\0304,34,65,3,256,1,6169\0304,67,97,3,256,2,6169\0316169,2,1,Klockmort Spannerspan\0306169,2,4,Klockmort Spannerspan\0312,0,0,1,Klockmort Spannerspan\0302,0,0,2,Ironforge\0302,0,0,4,Klockmort Spannerspan\0311701,19,1701,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301708,23,1708,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301708,24,1708,UNKNOWN\031",[1705]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Nice work! Now if you'll excuse me, I have some work to do myself...\030I hate to admit that Furen might have really found something.  But to be sure I'll need to try his techniques on a new piece of armor.  If you help me with the materials, $N, then you can have the armor.$B$BTo make this armor, I need samples of burning blood and a burning rock.$B$BThe only place I know to get them is Duskwood.  The Nightbane worgen based in the Roland's Doom mine have burning blood, and their leader Gutspill will have the rock.$B$BMay fortune grant you speed, $N.\030Bring 20 vials of Burning Blood and 1 Burning Rock to Grimand Elmore in Stormwind.\030$N, do you have the burning blood and rock? I'll need them to complete the armor.\030Burning Blood\0312,1,61,2,257,4,1416\0302,64,134,2,259,1,1416\0302,137,203,2,257,4,1416\0302,208,278,2,259,1,1416\0302,283,328,2,257,1,1416\0302,331,448,2,257,3,1416\0302,453,484,2,257,1,1416\0303,1,82,2,384,1,1416\0301,1,10,4,272,1,1416\0301,12,68,4,272,4,1416\0304,1,43,3,256,2,1416\0304,45,81,3,258,1,1416\031898,2,6,Nightbane Worgen\0306170,2,6,Gutspill\0301416,2,8,Grimand Elmore\0312,0,0,6,Roland's Doom\0302,0,0,8,Grimand Elmore\0302,0,0,8,Stormwind\0311706,23,1706,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6844,OBJECTIVE,20,15,\030ITEM,6845,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1706]="UNRESOLVED\031conclusion,conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes,storytellingContext\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030\030\030\030Grimand's Armor\031\031\031\0311705,19,1705,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1707]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Excellent - the more water pouches we are able to reclaim, the further away from disaster we'll all be! Keep 'em coming, and I will be sure to reward you for every five water pouches you bring me.\030Greetings $n - the name's Luglunket, and we've got an important job for you if you're up for it!  Huzzah!$B$BNothing would please me more as a seasoned spigot operator to take any Wastewander water pouches you might find out in the desert.  That's our water anyway - the nomads have just stolen it is all!  The Gadgetzan Water Company will offer you an official care package for every five you turn in.  Most importantly though, you're helping Gadgetzan help itself!\030Bring 5 Wastewander Water Pouches to Spigot Operator Luglunket in Gadgetzan.\030Got the five Wastewander Water Pouches we need? If you do, then the Gadgetzan Water Company Care Package, Model 103-XB, will be yours!\030Water Pouch Bounty\0312,1,96,2,257,4,7408\0302,99,105,2,257,1,7408\0302,110,239,2,257,4,7408\0302,242,305,2,261,1,7408\0302,308,402,2,257,3,7408\0302,405,466,2,257,1,7408\0303,1,76,2,384,1,7408\0301,1,103,4,272,1,7408\0301,105,196,4,272,3,7408\0304,1,47,3,258,2,7408\0304,49,134,3,256,4,7408\0317408,2,7,Spigot Operator Luglunket\0312,440,1446,0,\0302,0,0,7,Spigot Operator Luglunket\0302,0,0,7,Gadgetzan\0311878,23,1878,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,8483,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[1708]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031That's the stuff! Well done! Now let me get this smelted and hammered so I can apply Furen's technique with my own and then we can see what happens!$B$BOh my, oh my! I just know the armor will be very very very tough!\030I want to try Furen Longbeard's new techniques on my own piece of armor.  And because you helped Furen and he helped me, you're welcome to the armor after I make it!$B$BTo finish the piece, I need a special coral, searing coral.  It grows in only one place--along the coast south of Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands.$B$BBring me enough searing coral and I'll get right to work on the armor.  And hurry, $N.  I'm so eager to get started it's making my toes twist!\030Bring 20 loads of Searing Coral to Klockmort Spannerspan in Ironforge.\030Hello hello, $N! Do you have the searing coral? I can't wait to get to work!\030Iron Coral\0312,1,72,2,259,1,6169\0302,75,165,2,259,1,6169\0302,170,228,2,259,1,6169\0302,231,315,2,257,1,6169\0302,320,389,2,257,1,6169\0302,392,405,2,257,1,6169\0302,408,461,2,257,1,6169\0303,1,70,2,384,1,6169\0301,1,17,4,272,1,6169\0301,19,28,4,272,1,6169\0301,30,148,4,272,1,6169\0301,167,217,4,272,3,6169\0304,1,16,3,256,1,6169\0304,18,47,3,256,2,6169\0304,49,76,3,256,1,6169\0315413,2,1,Furen Longbeard\0306169,2,8,Klockmort Spannerspan\0312,0,0,4,Menethil Harbor\0302,0,0,4,Wetlands\0302,0,0,8,Klockmort Spannerspan\0302,0,0,8,Ironforge\0311709,23,1709,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6848,OBJECTIVE,20,15,",[1709]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Here's your armor, $N. Furen's process worked brilliantly! Perfectly! Marvelously, truly!$B$BYou could run this armor over with a siege engine and it would spring right back into shape!\030\030\030\030Klockmort's Creation\0311,1,22,4,272,1,6169\0301,24,58,4,272,1,6169\0301,60,69,4,272,1,6169\0301,71,89,4,272,1,6169\0301,94,185,4,272,4,6169\031\031\0311708,19,1708,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[171]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031May the heavens bless you, $N. You've done more for Randis than most would ever think of doing for him. Thank you - you're a shining star in the skies of the Alliance.$B$BPlease - if you can spare the time, come back and visit us. I know that Randis would like that, as would I.\030You have been so very kind to me, $N.  I never dreamed that I'd have so much fun during Children's Week.  Thank you.  I don't wanna be sad about what's happened to me and all - my folks always told me to rise above anything bad that happens.  You know, when I grow up I wanna be a hero... just like you.$B$BI'm sad to say this, but it's time for me to go home.  Let's go back and I'll tell the matron what an awesome person you are!\030Return your ward to the Stormwind orphanage by handing in the Human Orphan Whistle to Orphan Matron Nightingale in the Cathedral District.\030It is a pleasure to see you again, $N. Have you attended to the duties you've volunteered for during Children's Week?\030A Warden of the Alliance\0312,1,37,2,257,1,14305\0302,40,104,2,257,1,14305\0302,107,116,2,257,1,14305\0302,119,241,2,257,1,14305\0302,244,288,2,257,1,14305\0302,290,303,2,257,1,14305\0302,308,360,2,257,1,14305\0302,363,432,2,257,1,14305\0303,1,138,2,384,1,14305\0301,1,30,4,272,1,14450\0301,32,103,4,272,4,14450\0301,105,167,4,272,1,14450\0301,172,230,4,272,4,14450\0301,232,278,4,272,4,14450\0304,1,38,3,256,1,14450\0304,40,117,3,256,2,14450\03114305,2,9,Human Orphan\03014450,2,9,Orphan Matron Nightingale\0312,0,0,9,Stormwind\0302,0,0,9,Human Orphan Whistle\0302,0,0,9,Orphan Matron Nightingale\0302,0,0,9,Cathedral District\031558,21,558,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304822,21,4822,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,18598,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1710]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, thank you. These will work splendidly!$B$BI will begin fashioning the armor immediately...\030My colleague, Furen Longbeard, made a discovery which I am eager to test.  I wish to try it on a new armor that I am researching, for I believe Furen's techniques will produce superior results.$B$BWill you help me?  If you gather what I need to make the armor, then I will make an extra piece for you.$B$BI need the sunscorched egg shells of the Highperch Wyverns who dwell at Highperch, in Thousand Needles.  Search for the shells below their nests, and return to me when you have a sufficient amount.\030Bring 20 Sunscorched Shells to Mathiel in Darnassus.\030Do you have the shells, $N? They are quite strong, and can be rendered into a lacquer I will use to coat the links of my new mail armor.\030Sunscorched Shells\0312,1,73,2,257,1,6142\0302,76,193,2,259,4,6142\0302,198,214,2,257,2,6142\0302,217,301,2,259,4,6142\0302,306,408,2,259,1,6142\0302,411,502,2,257,1,6142\0303,1,52,2,384,1,6142\0301,1,14,4,272,1,6142\0301,16,42,4,272,3,6142\0301,47,94,4,272,3,6142\0304,1,27,3,256,2,6142\0304,29,136,3,256,3,6142\0315413,2,1,Furen Longbeard\0306142,2,7,Mathiel\0312,0,0,5,Highperch\0302,0,0,5,Thousand Needles\0302,0,0,7,Mathiel\0302,0,0,7,Darnassus\0311711,23,1711,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6849,OBJECTIVE,20,15,",[1711]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I have finished with your piece of armor, and I am quite pleased. Furen's new techniques meshed perfectly with my own and I am sure this armor will prove to be quite resilient.$B$BThank you, $N. And may this serve you well in future battles.\030\030\030\030Mathiel's Armor\0311,1,65,4,272,1,6142\0301,67,176,4,272,3,6142\0301,181,194,4,272,1,6142\0301,196,241,4,272,1,6142\031\031\0311710,19,1710,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1712]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have gathered the items for my spell, and have shown me your strength and cunning. But the next stage of our quest is even more perilous.$B$BLet us hope your strength does not falter.\030I have spent ages watching this site.  I watch, so that one day I might see the great Cyclonian fall.  But I have not yet found a champion to defeat the wind lord.$B$BPerhaps you are that champion.$B$BProve it to me.  Gather the items I need to summon Cyclonian, and I will know you are a great warrior.  Perhaps then you can defeat him and gain his whirlwind heart.$B$BIf so, then I will infuse the heart's power in a weapon, and I will give that weapon to you.$B$BHere is a parchment with the items I need.\030Bring the items on Bath'rah's Parchment to Bath'rah the Windwatcher in Alterac.\030Do you have the items, $N? Gathering them is the proof I need that you have the strength to face Cyclonian.\030Cyclonian\0312,1,37,2,257,1,6176\0302,40,101,2,259,4,6176\0302,104,163,2,257,1,6176\0302,168,197,2,257,4,6176\0302,202,216,2,257,1,6176\0302,219,303,2,259,3,6176\0302,306,366,2,257,4,6176\0302,371,462,2,257,4,6176\0302,467,508,2,259,1,6176\0303,1,79,2,384,1,6176\0301,1,86,4,272,1,6176\0301,88,141,4,272,1,6176\0301,146,187,4,274,3,6176\0304,1,26,3,256,2,6176\0304,28,107,3,258,1,6176\0316239,2,2,Cyclonian\0306239,2,6,Cyclonian\0306176,2,10,Bath'rah the Windwatcher\0306239,3,15,Cyclonian\0312,0,0,10,Bath'rah the Windwatcher\0302,0,0,10,Alterac\0311791,19,1791,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301713,23,1713,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3357,OBJECTIVE,8,15,\030ITEM,3901,OBJECTIVE,30,15,\030ITEM,6851,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1713]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You did it! You defeated Cyclonian and gained the Whirlwind Heart!\030I am ready to perform the ritual to summon Cyclonian.  When he is summoned, you must defeat him and take his whirlwind heart.  This I will use to instill a weapon with Cyclonian's power.$B$B$N, are you ready to face the wind lord?\030Bring the Whirlwind Heart to Bath'rah Windwatcher.\030$N, I must have the whirlwind heart!\030The Summoning\0312,1,53,2,257,1,6176\0302,56,125,2,257,1,6176\0302,128,186,2,257,3,6176\0302,191,230,2,257,2,6176\0303,1,50,2,384,1,6176\0301,1,11,4,272,1,6176\0301,13,66,4,272,1,6176\0304,1,36,3,256,1,6176\0316239,2,1,Cyclonian\0306239,4,7,Cyclonian\0312,0,0,5,Bath'rah Windwatcher\0311712,19,1712,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301792,23,1792,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6894,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1714]="PARTIAL\031characters,conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The charms sink slowly into the cauldron's depths...$B$BA large bubble rises to the surface of the liquid and breaks...$B$B...And a churning lump of molten rock is revealed.\030\030\030The cauldron bubbles. Its vapors beckon...\030Essence of the Exile\0311,1,52,4,272,1,0\0301,57,119,4,272,1,0\0301,124,173,4,272,1,0\0304,1,21,3,256,1,0\0304,23,42,3,256,1,0\031\031\0311712,20,1712,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,89931,GIVER,?,9,Bath'rah's Cauldron\030OBJECT,89931,FINISHER,?,12,Bath'rah's Cauldron\030ITEM,4480,OBJECTIVE,8,15,\030ITEM,4479,OBJECTIVE,8,15,\030ITEM,4481,OBJECTIVE,8,15,",[1715]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Sent by Blackwrench, were you? Damn warlocks in Ironforge need to get things sorted out. There's only so much room and so many teachers in Stormwind. With all the increased traffic, we're sure to attract attention sooner or later.\030Hmph. Times past, all warlocks in Khaz Modan were trained under the auspices of the masters of Gnomeregan, but now that we've all been forced to relocate into this rat's hole in Ironforge, and Magni's decided to keep a careful watch on us, we're forced to send our novices to Stormwind for training.$B$BLuckily, Gakin's no slouch, so you'll still learn what you need to know, but it burns my blood!$B$BAnyways, you'll find Gakin in the basement of the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind.\030Report to Gakin the Darkbinder in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind.\030\030The Slaughtered Lamb\0312,1,5,2,257,1,6120\0302,7,299,2,257,1,6120\0302,304,398,2,259,1,6120\0302,403,482,2,257,1,6120\0303,1,64,2,384,1,6120\0301,1,30,4,272,2,6122\0301,32,88,4,274,1,6122\0301,90,149,4,272,1,6122\0301,151,230,4,272,1,6122\03111045,2,3,Burns\0306122,2,5,Gakin the Darkbinder\0312,0,0,2,Khaz Modan\0302,0,0,2,Ironforge\0302,0,0,2,Stormwind\0302,0,0,4,Stormwind\0302,0,0,5,Gakin the Darkbinder\0302,0,0,5,Mage Quarter of Stormwind\0304,0,0,7,Ironforge\0304,0,0,8,Stormwind\0311685,22,1685,UNKNOWN\0301688,24,1688,UNKNOWN\031",[1716]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Was your crossing difficult, $N? You have come a long way to speak with me. But fear not, I know why Gakin has sent you, and he was wise to, for I can help you in your search.\030A succubus is a devourer of souls, destroyer of hearts, and dominator of minds. It knows nothing but evil.$B$BThis will be the creature you will learn to summon and control, but it cannot be brought into our world without a stimulus.$B$BWith a symbol of love as bait, it will surely answer your call. Then you can defeat it, and make it your tool.$B$BIt will be hard to find something of this nature, though. You should speak with Takar the Seer. You will find him in the Barrens of Kalimdor near Camp Taurajo.\030Speak with Takar the Seer in the Barrens.\030\030Devourer of Souls\0312,1,79,2,257,1,6122\0302,81,106,2,257,1,6122\0302,111,233,2,257,3,6122\0302,238,300,2,257,3,6122\0302,302,347,2,257,1,6122\0302,352,408,2,257,3,6122\0302,410,446,2,257,1,6122\0302,448,510,2,257,3,6122\0303,1,41,2,384,1,6122\0301,1,32,4,272,2,6244\0301,34,75,4,272,1,6244\0301,77,175,4,272,1,6244\0311863,2,1,Succubus\0306244,2,7,Takar the Seer\0306244,2,9,Takar the Seer\0312,0,0,8,Barrens of Kalimdor\0302,0,0,8,Camp Taurajo\0302,0,0,9,Barrens\0311738,23,1738,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1717]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I'm glad someone was able to get a hold of you, $n. I was beginning to fear the worst. It would be a shame to lose you, after the time we've invested in you. We can talk later, though. Your training is the only important thing now.\030$n! Didn't expect to see you around these parts, but I was instructed to keep an eye out for you.$B$BIt's past time you got some more training, so you should stop in to see Gakin the next time you're in Stormwind. He'll be waiting for you.\030Report to Gakin the Darkbinder in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind.\030\030Gakin's Summons\0312,5,97,2,257,1,6120\0302,102,213,2,257,1,6120\0302,215,239,2,257,1,6120\0303,1,64,2,384,1,6120\0301,1,51,4,272,1,6122\0301,53,86,4,272,1,6122\0301,88,157,4,272,4,6122\0301,159,184,4,272,1,6122\0301,186,231,4,272,1,6122\0316122,2,4,Gakin the Darkbinder\0312,0,0,2,Stormwind\0302,0,0,4,Gakin the Darkbinder\0302,0,0,4,Mage Quarter of Stormwind\0311716,23,1716,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301716,24,1716,UNKNOWN\031",[1718]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hello, $N. It's good to see you made it to Fray Island. I hope you find it to your liking...\030Your renown as a warrior grows, $N.  Now it is time to pit yourself against your peers and see where you stand.$B$BThere is an island off the coast of the Barrens, south of Ratchet.  It is called Fray Island and it is a place where warriors meet.$B$BMeet, and fight.$B$BSpeak with the chief warrior of Fray Island, Klannoc Macleod.  If he finds you worthy, then Klannoc will lead you further down the warrior's path.$B$BTo reach Fray Island, search for the sand bar shallows along the Merchant Coast.\030Speak with Klannoc Macleod.\030\030The Islander\0312,1,35,2,257,1,0\0302,38,111,2,257,1,0\0302,116,181,2,257,1,0\0302,184,246,2,257,1,0\0302,251,266,2,261,1,0\0302,271,331,2,257,1,0\0302,334,416,2,257,4,0\0302,421,500,2,257,1,0\0303,1,27,2,384,1,0\0301,1,10,4,272,1,6236\0301,12,55,4,272,1,6236\0301,57,92,4,274,3,6236\0316236,2,6,Klannoc Macleod\0306236,2,9,Klannoc Macleod\0312,0,0,3,Ratchet\0304,0,0,11,Fray Island\0311719,23,1719,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1719]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $N. You have passed The Affray!$B$BYou are a worthy warrior, and I am honored to teach you...\030If you want to learn from me, then you must first pass The Affray.  It is a challenge we on Fray Island like to offer rising warriors who think they're tough, and if you can pass this test then I'll know you are.$B$BTo begin, walk into the middle of that crowd yonder and step on the grate.  That'll tell Twiggy Flathead you're ready, and he'll send challengers against you.$B$BBeat all the challengers and he'll call out Big Will.  Kill Big Will, and return to me in the time we allow.\030Kill Big Will, then speak to Klannoc Macleod on Fray Island.\030Step on the grate to begin the Affray\030Have you completed your challenge?\030The Affray\0312,1,66,2,259,4,6236\0302,69,212,2,257,4,6236\0302,217,290,2,257,1,6236\0302,293,374,2,257,1,6236\0302,379,431,2,257,3,6236\0302,434,486,2,257,3,6236\0303,1,60,2,384,3,6236\0301,1,14,4,272,1,6236\0301,16,42,4,272,1,6236\0301,47,104,4,272,1,6236\0305,1,34,3,256,2,6236\0304,1,37,3,384,1,6236\0316248,2,4,Twiggy Flathead\0306238,2,5,Big Will\0306238,2,6,Big Will\0306238,2,7,Big Will\0306236,2,7,Klannoc Macleod\0312,0,0,7,Klannoc Macleod\0311718,19,1718,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301791,23,1791,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,6238,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Big Will",[172]="PARTIAL\031consequences,locations,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Zug zug! My name is Grunth, and I guess you're looking after me? You're an adventurer, like my mom and dad were. My matron says that they died with honor in battle. I'm happy to meet you.$B$BI hope we'll do plenty of things together. I have some things I'd like to do, and the matron says you'll be like a big $gbrother:sister; to me during this week. I'd like that a whole bunch.\030You're willing to help us here at the orphanage?  Bless you, friend; your aid during Children's Week will be invaluable.$B$BTake this whistle.  You will only be able to use it for a short amount of time - typically not longer than Children's Week itself.  When you use it, you will be able to talk with the child you've agreed to look after.  Using it again will dismiss the child.$B$BBy all means $N - use the whistle and meet your ward!  I'm sure the child will be most eager to meet you.\030Use the Orcish Orphan Whistle to talk with the child you will be looking after during Children's Week.\030\030Children's Week\0312,1,48,2,257,2,14451\0302,51,120,2,257,3,14451\0302,125,142,2,257,1,14451\0302,145,254,2,257,3,14451\0302,257,341,2,257,3,14451\0302,344,381,2,257,3,14451\0302,386,438,2,257,1,14451\0302,441,490,2,257,3,14451\0303,1,102,2,384,3,14451\0301,1,8,4,272,1,14444\0301,10,64,4,272,2,14444\0301,66,112,4,272,1,14444\0301,114,164,4,276,1,14444\0301,166,187,4,272,1,14444\0301,192,233,4,274,3,14444\0301,235,351,4,274,1,14444\0301,353,380,4,274,1,14444\03114444,2,9,Orcish Orphan\031\031\031",[173]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Impressive, $N. It would seem that you are capable enough to handle yourself. Perhaps a more suitable challenge could be found for one of your abilities.$B$BIt is curious though... The worgen seemed to just appear out of thin air. But then, with all the other strange creatures that have moved across our borders, I suppose it's only one of many concerns.\030Darkness seems drawn inexorably to Duskwood. Master Carevin's quest is the expulsion of evil and heresy. Through our efforts are the people of Darkshire kept safe.$B$BYou believe yourself worthy to join us?$B$BI once thought as you. Disillusioned by the complacency of the Watch, I joined Master Carevin. If you wish to prove yourself, it will not be through words.$B$BTest your skills against the Nightbane Shadow Weaver worgen in Brightwood Grove--bright, hah!--and the Rotting Orchard.\030Kill 6 Nightbane Shadow Weaver worgen for Calor in Darkshire.\030$N, how fares the hunt?\030Worgen in the Woods\0312,1,44,2,257,4,663\0302,46,104,2,257,1,663\0302,106,163,2,257,1,663\0302,168,206,2,257,4,663\0302,211,232,2,257,1,663\0302,234,304,2,257,1,663\0302,306,365,2,259,4,663\0302,370,488,2,257,1,663\0303,1,61,2,384,1,663\0301,1,15,4,272,1,663\0301,17,77,4,272,4,663\0301,79,153,4,272,4,663\0301,158,180,4,272,1,663\0301,182,230,4,272,1,663\0301,232,355,4,272,1,663\0304,1,23,3,256,2,663\031533,2,8,Nightbane Shadow Weaver\0304244,2,8,Shadow\0305720,2,8,Weaver\030533,2,9,Nightbane Shadow Weaver\0304244,2,9,Shadow\0305720,2,9,Weaver\030663,2,9,Calor\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,1,Duskwood\0302,0,0,8,Brightwood Grove--bright\0302,0,0,9,Darkshire\031221,23,221,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,533,OBJECTIVE,6,13,Nightbane Shadow Weaver",[1738]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes, I can tell this will do nicely, let me just work with it for a moment...$B$BTakar is a resourceful fellow to have around, isn't he? If only I could persuade him to move back to civilization.\030In preparation for your coming, I used my sight to look over the world and through the mists of time. I have found what it is you seek.$B$BIn the War of the Ancients, two lovers fell together in battle. Where they took their last breaths, a tree known as the heartswood grew, a symbol of their undying love.$B$BThat should be enough to tempt a succubus. You will find it in the ruins of Ordil'Aran in the northwestern part of the forest of Ashenvale.\030Retrieve the Heartswood from Ashenvale and bring it to Gakin the Darkbinder in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind.\030Was your search a success, $N?\030Heartswood\0312,1,101,2,257,1,6244\0302,103,135,2,259,1,6244\0302,140,202,2,325,1,6244\0302,204,307,2,257,1,6244\0302,312,353,2,257,1,6244\0302,355,450,2,321,3,6244\0303,1,109,2,384,1,6244\0301,1,77,4,272,3,6122\0301,82,136,4,272,2,6122\0301,138,195,4,272,4,6122\0304,1,30,3,256,2,6122\0311863,2,5,Succubus\0306122,2,7,Gakin the Darkbinder\0312,0,0,7,Ashenvale\0302,0,0,7,Gakin the Darkbinder\0302,0,0,7,Mage Quarter of Stormwind\0311716,19,1716,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301739,23,1739,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6912,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1739]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, well done, $N. I see we've done right in deciding to train you. Your performance certainly does not disappoint.$B$BI've no qualms in showing you the way to control your newly bound succubus. Observe carefully.\030Using the heartswood core, you will be able to cast a spell at the summoning circle in the crypt below to open a portal for the succubus to pass through.$B$BBe careful, $n, succubi have overrun even the strongest of minds.$B$BOnce you have bested and returned it to the void, return to me and I will show you how to call and control it.\030Using the Heartswood Core, summon and subdue a succubus, then return the Heartswood Core to Gakin the Darkbinder in the Slaughtered Lamb.\030Sometimes I wonder if Surena was not a succubus in disguise, sent to warp and twist my mind... Ha! I give her too much credit, I think.\030The Binding\0312,1,153,2,257,3,6122\0302,158,222,2,257,1,6122\0302,227,336,2,257,3,6122\0303,1,137,2,384,1,6122\0301,1,25,4,272,1,6122\0301,27,74,4,272,1,6122\0301,76,122,4,272,1,6122\0301,127,201,4,276,1,6122\0301,203,220,4,272,1,6122\0304,1,94,3,256,4,6122\0304,100,135,3,256,1,6122\0311863,2,1,Succubus\0301863,2,4,Succubus\0306122,2,4,Gakin the Darkbinder\0301863,4,8,Succubus\0301863,3,10,Succubus\0312,0,0,4,Gakin the Darkbinder\0302,0,0,4,Slaughtered Lamb\0311738,19,1738,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,5677,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Summoned Succubus",[174]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is perfect, $N. The first step is complete!\030My Gnomish friend, Cog, has promised to help me build a device which will let me peer towards the stars.  A truth exists, beyond magic, that can explain the strange transformation in the forest.$B$BBring to me a bronze tube made by a skilled engineer.  That is the first step, according to Cog's blueprint.\030Viktori Prism'Antras of Darkshire wants you to bring him a bronze tube.\030Have you found a skilled engineer to create a bronze tube yet?\030Look To The Stars\0312,1,104,2,257,3,276\0302,107,194,2,257,1,276\0302,199,251,2,257,1,276\0302,254,306,2,257,1,276\0303,1,71,2,386,1,276\0301,1,20,4,272,1,276\0301,22,48,4,272,1,276\0304,1,62,3,256,2,276\031276,2,5,Viktori Prism'Antras\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,4,Cog's\031175,23,175,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4371,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1740]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes... The orb was not greatly fragmented, and almost all of the pieces are here. It is a simple thing to recreate them, to make Soran'ruk whole again.$B$BI have dedicated my life to the study of the Burning Legion's orbs and their recreation. You have done me a favor collecting these pieces to study, and I will give you them back - fully reconstructed - in a form of your choosing.\030When demons of the Legion fall out of favor, their spirits are imprisoned within orbs and distributed to their mages and warlocks.$B$BMany were carried by their servants in Azeroth. Even fragmented, they still possess the powers of the demons trapped inside.$B$BThe orb of Soran'ruk was broken into two pieces, one was further broken to be used by the acolytes of the Twilight's Hammer in Blackfathom Deeps. The other, larger piece, was possessed by a wizard in Shadowfang Keep. Find them and I can reform it.\030Find 3 Soran'ruk Fragments and 1 Large Soran'ruk Fragment and return them to Doan Karhan in the Barrens.\030It took me many years to collect the pieces of the orb of Zargain, but it has served me well, as I am sure the orb of Soran'ruk will serve you.\030The Orb of Soran'ruk\0312,1,130,2,261,1,6247\0302,135,181,2,257,1,6247\0302,183,258,2,257,1,6247\0302,263,407,2,257,1,6247\0302,409,478,2,257,1,6247\0302,480,509,2,257,1,6247\0303,1,104,2,384,1,6247\0301,1,6,4,272,1,6247\0301,8,81,4,272,1,6247\0301,83,151,4,272,1,6247\0301,156,243,4,336,1,6247\0301,245,384,4,272,3,6247\0304,1,143,3,256,3,6247\0316247,2,7,Doan Karhan\0312,0,0,2,Azeroth\0302,0,0,4,Blackfathom Deeps\0302,0,0,5,Shadowfang Keep\0302,0,0,7,Doan Karhan\0302,0,0,7,Barrens\031\031ITEM,6914,OBJECTIVE,3,15,\030ITEM,6915,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[175]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Why yes, I used to own a looking glass.\030According to Cog's blueprint, what I need now is a way to reflect light.  I remember a woman by the name of Mary who became well known around these parts for always carrying a looking glass.  Perhaps you can track Mary down and see if she might lend us a reflective surface for this project?  I believe she once resided in southern Duskwood. . .\030Locate Mary and persuade her to give up a reflective surface for Viktori's project.\030\030Look To The Stars\0312,1,72,2,259,1,276\0302,75,190,2,257,1,276\0302,193,291,2,257,4,276\0302,294,341,2,257,4,276\0303,1,83,2,384,1,276\0301,1,39,4,272,1,302\031\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,1,Cog's\031174,19,174,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030177,23,177,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1758]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Tome of Cabal? Hmm...sounds familiar. I have never seen it here before, though--and believe me, I remember every book I read. $B$BHmm... Ah, yes!$B$BI have seen reference to it in library cataloging books.\030It will take more than a simple summoning circle to bring forth a felhunter for you to challenge.$B$BMy three acolytes and I will assist in creating the magic circles. You require a copy of the Tome of the Cabal, which has been lost to us for some time. It was written by the first group of warlocks to summon a felhunter unaided.$B$BPerhaps Krom Stoutarm can help you with this. An itinerant warlock these days, he spends his days hoarding ancient texts and skulking about the library in Ironforge.\030Speak with Krom Stoutarm in Ironforge.\030\030Tome of the Cabal\0312,1,97,2,257,3,6251\0302,102,167,2,257,3,6251\0302,169,253,2,261,1,6251\0302,255,330,2,257,1,6251\0302,335,379,2,257,4,6251\0302,381,499,2,321,1,6251\0303,1,38,2,384,1,6251\0301,1,14,4,272,2,6294\0301,16,37,4,272,1,6294\0301,39,125,4,272,4,6294\0301,131,136,4,272,1,6294\0301,138,145,4,272,1,6294\0301,150,205,4,272,1,6294\031417,2,1,Felhunter\030417,2,4,Felhunter\0306294,2,5,Krom Stoutarm\0306294,2,7,Krom Stoutarm\0312,0,0,6,Ironforge\0302,0,0,7,Ironforge\0311802,23,1802,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[176]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hah! Well done! I was starting to think no one would take down that monster!$B$BHere you are, $N. And thanks - that Gnoll was giving me a headache the size of Blackrock Spire!\030Wanted: Hogger$B$BA huge gnoll, Hogger, is prowling the woods in southwestern Elwynn.  He has overpowered all attempts at his capture.$B$BThe Stormwind Army has placed a generous bounty on the Gnoll.  To earn the reward, bounty hunters should bring proof of Hogger's demise to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire.\030Slay the gnoll Hogger and bring his Huge Gnoll Claw to Marshal Dughan.\030Yes, Hogger has been a real pain for me and my men. You have something to report about the beast?\030Wanted:  \"Hogger\"\0312,1,14,2,257,1,0\0302,19,85,2,257,1,0\0302,88,134,2,257,1,0\0302,139,199,2,257,1,0\0302,202,305,2,257,1,0\0303,1,70,2,384,1,0\0301,1,4,4,272,1,240\0301,6,15,4,272,1,240\0301,17,76,4,272,4,240\0301,81,97,4,272,1,240\0301,99,175,4,272,1,240\0304,1,51,3,256,1,240\0304,53,97,3,256,2,240\031448,2,1,Hogger\030448,2,2,Hogger\030240,2,5,Marshal Dughan\030448,2,6,Hogger\030240,2,6,Marshal Dughan\030448,3,12,Hogger\03010430,3,13,The Beast\0312,12,1429,0,\0302,0,0,5,Marshal Dughan\0302,0,0,5,Goldshire\0302,0,0,6,Marshal Dughan\031\031OBJECT,68,GIVER,?,9,Wanted Poster\030OBJECT,156561,GIVER,?,9,Wanted Poster\030ITEM,1931,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[177]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Most superb! This will work perfectly. Many thanks!\030The looking glass was one of my finest treasures until. . .the incident.  After that happened, I discarded it behind the barn.  There was an Insane Ghoul who used to roam back there.  Perhaps he picked it up.  Rumor has it the devilish beast resides in the Tranquil Gardens Cemetery.\030Retrieve Blind Mary's Looking Glass from the Insane Ghoul and give it to Viktori in Darkshire.\030I showed Cog the beginnings of our star-viewing machine. He was impressed. Did you happen to find a reflective device?\030Look To The Stars\0312,1,55,2,257,1,302\0302,59,72,2,257,1,302\0302,75,126,2,257,1,302\0302,129,182,2,257,1,302\0302,185,208,2,257,4,302\0302,211,283,2,257,1,302\0303,1,94,2,384,1,302\0301,1,12,4,272,1,276\0301,14,38,4,272,3,276\0301,40,51,4,272,1,276\0304,1,56,3,256,1,276\0304,58,74,3,256,1,276\0304,76,118,3,256,2,276\031511,2,4,Insane Ghoul\030846,2,4,Ghoul\030302,2,7,Blind Mary\030511,2,7,Insane Ghoul\030846,2,7,Ghoul\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,6,Tranquil Gardens Cemetery\0302,0,0,7,Insane Ghoul\0302,0,0,7,Viktori\0302,0,0,7,Darkshire\031175,19,175,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030181,23,181,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,1946,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1778]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031So, you've returned so quickly, huh? And what pray tell have you accomplished in your time away from here?$B$BWere you able to help a noble cause? Perhaps you've learned the value of charity or some more about your obligations to the citizens of Azeroth. Tell me, who have you helped and how.... Impressive, $N, those are surely the actions of one who follows the Light.$B$BSuch sacrifice will always be rewarded in time.\030I'm going to see about making plans to return home soon. Hopefully, Stephanie is doing well back in Stormwind. I can't wait to see her again. Till next we meet, $c.\030Speak to Tiza Battleforge in Ironforge.\030\030The Tome of Divinity\0312,1,56,2,257,3,6175\0302,58,110,2,257,3,6175\0302,112,141,2,257,1,6175\0302,143,164,2,257,1,6175\0303,1,39,2,384,1,6175\0301,1,36,4,272,2,6179\0301,38,106,4,272,2,6179\0301,111,146,4,272,2,6179\0301,148,254,4,272,4,6179\0301,256,295,4,272,1,6179\0301,297,370,4,272,1,6179\0301,375,421,4,272,3,6179\0316179,2,5,Tiza Battleforge\0312,0,0,2,Stormwind\0302,0,0,5,Tiza Battleforge\0302,0,0,5,Ironforge\0311648,19,1648,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301779,23,1779,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1779]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031*cough*$B$BGood day to ya, $C. Don't mind me wounds, the good priest 'ere'll take care of ol' Muiredon in time. Not needin' the power of that Symbol of Life ya got there quite yet.$B$BSo, me wife sent ya o'er to speak to me, huh? Fair 'nough. I'll take the time to talk to ya-I'll tell ya exactly wut happened to Muiredon and his best friend Narm, a $C jus' like yerself.\030I want you to take this, $N. It is called the Symbol of Life.$B$BYou've proven charitable and patient, and now I want you to prove just how adept you've become in both combat, and power.$B$BMy husband Muiredon returned recently from an encounter with some Dark Iron dwarves, and he barely escaped with his life--he's over there having his wounds healed by one of our priests.$B$BTake the Symbol and speak to him. If you can help him, then we will speak again soon. May the Light shine upon you.\030Take the Symbol of Life and speak to Muiredon Battleforge in Ironforge.\030\030The Tome of Divinity\0312,1,28,2,259,1,6179\0302,30,61,2,257,1,6179\0302,66,186,2,259,1,6179\0302,191,375,2,257,1,6179\0302,380,412,2,257,1,6179\0302,414,464,2,257,4,6179\0302,466,494,2,257,1,6179\0303,1,71,2,384,1,6179\0301,1,7,4,272,1,6178\0301,12,30,4,272,1,6178\0301,32,111,4,272,1,6178\0301,113,180,4,272,1,6178\0301,185,229,4,272,2,6178\0301,231,242,4,272,1,6178\0301,244,371,4,272,1,6178\0316178,2,8,Muiredon Battleforge\030111,4,11,Priest\0312,0,0,8,Muiredon Battleforge\0302,0,0,8,Ironforge\0304,0,0,15,Muiredon\0311778,19,1778,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301783,23,1783,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[178]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have my gratitude, $N. I sent that message to the Shadowhide Pendants weeks ago and had believed it a failure. But it seems the spell did reach at least some pendants, after a significant delay.$B$BIn time I hope to learn how to send an attack through the pendants, to immobilize any Shadowhide Gnolls who wear them.$B$BBut before that is possible, I'm afraid that much more research is required.\030<You hear a disembodied voice...>$B$BDo not be alarmed.  I am Theocritus, High Mage of Tower Azora in Elwynn Forest.  The pendant you are holding is a method of communication between the Shadowhide Gnolls and their master, Morganth.$B$BThrough months of research, I believe I too can communicate through these pendants.  If you can hear this message, then my spell was a success.$B$BBring me this pendant and I will reward you for the service.\030Bring the Faded Shadowhide Pendant to Theocritus the Mage.\030I spoke to you through a pendant, you say? Hmm...give it to me, so that I might study it.\030Theocritus' Retrieval\0312,1,33,2,257,1,0\0302,38,55,2,257,1,0\0302,58,116,2,257,1,0\0302,119,232,2,257,1,0\0302,237,319,2,257,4,0\0302,322,379,2,257,4,0\0302,384,443,2,257,3,0\0303,1,58,2,384,1,0\0301,1,26,4,272,1,313\0301,28,114,4,272,1,313\0301,116,198,4,272,4,313\0301,203,320,4,278,3,313\0301,325,400,4,272,1,313\0304,1,42,3,256,2,313\0304,44,89,3,258,4,313\031313,2,3,Theocritus\030397,2,4,Morganth\030313,2,8,Theocritus\0312,44,1433,0,\0302,0,0,3,Elwynn Forest\0302,0,0,8,Theocritus the Mage\0304,0,0,10,Shadowhide Pendants\031\031ITEM,1962,STARTER,?,10,",[1780]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You've returned so quickly, $N. And what have you accomplished in your time away from the Cathedral?$B$BHave you helped a noble cause? Perhaps you've learned the value of charity or some more about your obligations to the citizens of Azeroth. Tell me, who have you helped and how... Well, I'm impressed, $N, those are surely the actions of one who follows the Light and values others above oneself.$B$BSuch sacrifice will always be rewarded in time.\030I'll take these to the children this very day. Please be safe, good $c. It is not often $G men:women; of your character show their faces in the city, but you've proven that the paladins here in Stormwind shall never turn their backs on those in need.$B$BFarewell.\030Speak to Duthorian Rall in Stormwind.\030\030The Tome of Divinity\0312,1,46,2,257,1,6174\0302,48,71,2,257,1,6174\0302,73,250,2,259,3,6174\0302,255,263,2,257,1,6174\0303,1,37,2,384,1,6174\0301,1,31,4,272,1,6171\0301,33,100,4,272,2,6171\0301,105,134,4,272,2,6171\0301,136,242,4,272,4,6171\0301,244,282,4,272,1,6171\0301,284,398,4,272,1,6171\0301,403,449,4,272,3,6171\0316171,2,5,Duthorian Rall\0312,0,0,3,Stormwind\0302,0,0,5,Duthorian Rall\0302,0,0,5,Stormwind\0304,0,0,7,Cathedral\0311644,19,1644,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301781,23,1781,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1781]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031*cough*$B$BPleasure to meet you, $R. Don't mind my wounds, the good priest here can take care of ol' Gazin this time. I won't be needing the power of that Symbol of Life you've got there... not yet anyway.$B$BSo, Duthorian sent you to speak to me, huh? Fair enough. I'll tell you exactly what befell me and my friend Henze. And with any luck, and some skill on your part, perhaps you can still help us all.\030Take this, $N. It is called the Symbol of Life.$B$BYou've proven charitable and patient, and now the time has come to see if you're powerful enough to focus one of the Light's greatest gifts.$B$BMy friend Gazin returned recently from an encounter with some Defias in Elwynn near Heroes' Vigil--he barely escaped with his life. He's near the altar having his wounds healed by our priests.$B$BTake the Symbol and speak to him. If you can help him, then we will speak again soon. May you bask in the Light's glory.\030Take the Symbol of Life to Gazin Tenorm in Stormwind.\030\030The Tome of Divinity\0312,1,14,2,257,1,6171\0302,16,47,2,257,1,6171\0302,52,191,2,257,4,6171\0302,196,326,2,257,1,6171\0302,328,387,2,257,1,6171\0302,392,424,2,257,1,6171\0302,426,476,2,257,4,6171\0302,478,511,2,257,1,6171\0303,1,53,2,384,1,6171\0301,1,7,4,272,1,6173\0301,12,36,4,272,1,6173\0301,38,117,4,272,1,6173\0301,119,189,4,272,1,6173\0301,191,205,4,272,1,6173\0301,210,252,4,272,2,6173\0301,254,265,4,272,1,6173\0301,267,323,4,272,1,6173\0301,325,406,4,272,4,6173\0316173,2,9,Gazin Tenorm\030111,4,12,Priest\0312,0,0,4,Elwynn\0302,0,0,4,Heroes' Vigil--he\0302,0,0,8,Light's\0302,0,0,9,Gazin Tenorm\0302,0,0,9,Stormwind\0311780,19,1780,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301786,23,1786,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1782]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Here's your armor, $N. This will stand up to the strongest assaults or my name isn't Furen Longbeard!$B$BAnd I have to thank you. I learned a lot while working with the materials$Byou brought me. I think I'll have another breakthrough one day!$B$BI'm going to send what I learned to other$Bblacksmiths of the Alliance.$B$BI'll tell them you were a big help, and maybe they'll want to return the favor.\030\030\030\030Furen's Armor\0311,1,22,4,272,1,5413\0301,24,101,4,272,3,5413\0301,106,129,4,272,1,5413\0301,131,178,4,272,1,5413\0301,181,195,4,272,1,5413\0301,197,243,4,272,1,5413\0301,248,288,4,272,3,5413\0301,291,318,4,272,1,5413\0301,323,401,4,274,4,5413\0315413,4,2,Furen Longbeard\031\0311701,19,1701,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1783]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I can't thank you enough, $gbrother:sister;.$B$BI can only assume that Tiza and Muiredon sent you here to aid me if you carry the Symbol of Life.$B$BIt's true, I fell to the Dark Iron while trying to attain one of the scripts: I was able to hold on long enough to allow Muiredon to escape, but the Light had almost embraced me fully when you came along. The fact that you were powerful enough to use the Symbol means great things for you, but there's time to speak of that later.\030We was spyin' on some of the Dark Iron dwarves that've bunkered down south of Helm's Bed Lake. We knew they was up to no good, so Narm an' me thought we'd take a closer look--got ta see their leader given orders to some o' his men.$B$BNarm an' me took the chance to kill a few of 'em, but they proved tougher than we thought, an' more of 'em got the jump on us. Narm tol' me to run an' get support, so 'ere I am.$B$BNarm needs help, an' I'll not rest till he gets it.$B$BC'n ya help, $N?\030Take the Symbol of Life and resurrect Narm Faulk in Dun Morogh.\030\030The Tome of Divinity\0312,1,94,2,257,1,6178\0302,96,231,2,257,1,6178\0302,236,361,2,257,1,6178\0302,363,412,2,257,1,6178\0302,417,467,2,259,1,6178\0302,472,487,2,257,2,6178\0303,1,63,2,384,1,6178\0301,1,44,4,272,1,6177\0301,49,145,4,272,4,6177\0301,150,353,4,272,1,6177\0301,355,479,4,272,1,6177\0316177,2,7,Narm Faulk\0312,0,0,1,Helm's Bed Lake\0302,0,0,7,Dun Morogh\0304,0,0,10,Dark Iron\0311779,19,1779,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301784,23,1784,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,6177,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Narm Faulk\030SPELL,8593,OBJECTIVE,?,17,",[1784]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Haha! You've done it! Ya saved Narm, and ya found the proof me wife needs to take to the council. Yer a blessin' o' the Light if I ever saw one... not includin' me wife o' course.$B$BThank ya again, $N.\030Before I fell in battle, Muiredon and I had almost defeated one of the Dark Iron spies near that small house. We witnessed their captain passing orders to them, and sought to kill him and take the orders.$B$BSome of the council in Ironforge do not yet believe the presence of Dark Iron dwarves exists in Dun Morogh. By attaining one of those scripts, we'll not only have proof of their movements, but possibly an idea of what they're planning.$B$BGet one of those scripts and take it back to Muiredon, $N.\030Retrieve a Dark Iron Script from the Dark Iron dwarves near Helm's Bed, and return to Muiredon Battleforge in Ironforge.\030Yer back! I'm glad to see it, $N. My wounds are healed and I'm about ready to return to Helm's Bed lake as soon as I c'n convince me wife that I'll be fine.\030The Tome of Divinity\0312,1,109,2,261,1,6177\0302,111,204,2,257,1,6177\0302,209,315,2,257,4,6177\0302,317,443,2,257,1,6177\0302,448,505,2,257,1,6177\0303,1,120,2,384,1,6177\0301,1,5,4,272,1,6178\0301,7,21,4,272,1,6178\0301,23,97,4,274,1,6178\0301,99,146,4,272,4,6178\0301,148,179,4,272,1,6178\0301,184,202,4,272,1,6178\0304,1,9,3,256,1,6178\0304,11,33,3,256,1,6178\0304,35,156,3,256,1,6178\0316178,2,6,Muiredon Battleforge\0312,0,0,3,Ironforge\0302,0,0,3,Dun Morogh\0302,0,0,5,Muiredon\0302,0,0,6,Dark Iron\0302,0,0,6,Helm's Bed\0302,0,0,6,Muiredon Battleforge\0302,0,0,6,Ironforge\0303,0,0,15,Helm's Bed\0311783,19,1783,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301785,23,1785,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6847,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1785]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You've done all of Ironforge a great favor today, $N. I'm proud to count you among us, and if you feel you're ready, I would like to bless you with this scroll. The Symbol of Life would only have worked when used by a $C who was ready for one of the Light's greatest blessings-the power to restore the dead back to life.$B$BI will teach you the ability to resurrect your companions. Use it wisely, $N, and thank you, on behalf of myself, my husband, and Ironforge.\030I c'n see me wife's o'er there beamin' wit pride already. Ya better get yer tuchus o'er there pronto. I be thinkin' she'd have some words wit ya.$B$BLight be witcha, mighty $c. I'll be lookin' fer ya on the battlefield against the Scourge and dem Dark Irons when the time comes.\030Speak to Tiza Battleforge in Ironforge.\030\030The Tome of Divinity\0312,1,57,2,257,1,6178\0302,59,101,2,257,1,6178\0302,103,145,2,257,1,6178\0302,150,176,2,257,1,6178\0302,178,278,2,321,1,6178\0303,1,39,2,384,1,6178\0301,1,53,4,272,1,6179\0301,55,160,4,274,4,6179\0301,162,320,4,274,4,6179\0301,325,382,4,272,3,6179\0301,384,464,4,272,1,6179\0316179,2,6,Tiza Battleforge\0312,0,0,6,Tiza Battleforge\0302,0,0,6,Ironforge\0311784,19,1784,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1786]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, $Gbrother:sister;.$B$BSeeing you wield the Symbol of Life, may I assume Duthorian or Gazin sent you?$B$BI fell to the Defias spell casters while Gazin and I tried to get their plans from them: I was able to hold on long enough to allow Gazin to escape, but in the end, their magics overwhelmed me.$B$BBut you were able to bring me back: the ability to use the Symbol doesn't come to just anyone, $N. It bodes well for you that you were able to empower it with your own faith.\030Henze and I had made it to Heroes' Vigil, an island in the middle of Stone Cairn Lake in northeastern Elwynn. We'd heard the Defias had infiltrated our borders and we wanted proof to take to the king's advisors.$B$BWe caught sight of a couple of the scum going over some documents, and we attacked. Unfortunately, we were quickly overwhelmed by more of the mages.$B$BHenze held them off for me while I escaped... the daft fool, going and being brave.$B$BHe's out there now, Henze is. Can you help us, $N?\030Take the Symbol of Life and resurrect Henze Faulk in Elwynn.\030\030The Tome of Divinity\0312,1,109,2,257,1,6173\0302,111,211,2,257,1,6173\0302,216,298,2,261,1,6173\0302,300,363,2,257,1,6173\0302,368,412,2,257,1,6173\0302,414,450,2,257,1,6173\0302,455,483,2,257,1,6173\0302,485,504,2,257,2,6173\0303,1,60,2,384,1,6173\0301,1,29,4,272,1,6172\0301,34,111,4,272,4,6172\0301,116,308,4,272,1,6172\0301,313,410,4,272,1,6172\0301,412,486,4,272,1,6172\0316172,2,9,Henze Faulk\0312,0,0,1,Heroes' Vigil\0302,0,0,9,Elwynn\0304,0,0,12,Defias\0311781,19,1781,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301787,23,1787,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,6172,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Henze Faulk\030SPELL,8593,OBJECTIVE,?,17,",[1787]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Wonderful! You made it, and saved Henze. The Light is with you for sure, $N!\030We'll have time to talk more about the Symbol at a later time. What's important now is to get those papers we saw the Defias going over. If we can get our hands on them, we'll be able to prove the Defias have infiltrated Elwynn and hopefully gain some insight into what their plans are.$B$BI'm in no shape for battle as of now, $N. Do you think you're strong enough to get those papers from the Defias here on the island?$B$BIf you're able to get them, bring them back to Gazin and let him know I'm all right.\030Retrieve a Defias Script from the Defias Rogue Wizards in Elwynn, and return to Gazin Tenorm in Stormwind.\030Is Henze safe, $N? Were you successful?$B$BBetween your skill with a weapon, and the power of the Light, I'd imagine Heroes' Vigil is safe from any Defias threat, but that's for the King and his advisors to say.\030The Tome of Divinity\0312,1,62,2,257,1,6172\0302,64,136,2,257,1,6172\0302,138,286,2,257,4,6172\0302,291,331,2,261,1,6172\0302,333,421,2,257,2,6172\0302,426,509,2,257,4,6172\0303,1,106,2,384,1,6172\0301,1,10,4,272,1,6173\0301,12,40,4,272,1,6173\0301,42,76,4,272,1,6173\0304,1,18,3,256,2,6173\0304,20,39,3,256,2,6173\0304,44,211,3,260,1,6173\0316173,2,7,Gazin Tenorm\0312,0,0,5,Defias\0302,0,0,6,Gazin\0302,0,0,7,Defias Rogue Wizards\0302,0,0,7,Elwynn\0302,0,0,7,Gazin Tenorm\0302,0,0,7,Stormwind\0311786,19,1786,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301788,23,1788,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6846,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1788]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You've done well this day, $N. You should take some pride in what you've accomplished.$B$BEven more so, you should be proud of your abilities. Not everyone can use the power of the Symbol of Life. Calling upon the Light to bring back the dead means you're prepared for one of the $C's greatest honors: the power of resurrection.$B$BYou shall have the power to bring back fallen companions much like you did for Henze.$B$BBe well, $N. The Light shines upon you and you should welcome it wholly.\030I'll take the script to the King's advisors after Duthorian's taken a look at them, but in the meantime, you should go speak to Duthorian now. He'll be wanting to pat you on the back for sure!$B$BThank you again, $N. I hope we meet again. You're surely an ally I'm proud to call friend.\030Speak to Duthorian Rall in Stormwind.\030\030The Tome of Divinity\0312,1,142,2,257,1,6173\0302,144,192,2,257,1,6173\0302,197,216,2,257,1,6173\0302,218,238,2,259,3,6173\0302,240,286,2,257,1,6173\0303,1,37,2,384,1,6173\0301,1,30,4,272,1,6171\0301,32,86,4,272,1,6171\0301,91,142,4,272,1,6171\0301,144,196,4,272,1,6171\0301,198,328,4,272,1,6171\0301,333,417,4,272,3,6171\0301,422,433,4,272,1,6171\0301,435,493,4,272,1,6171\0316171,2,6,Duthorian Rall\0312,0,0,1,King's\0302,0,0,1,Duthorian\0302,0,0,6,Duthorian Rall\0302,0,0,6,Stormwind\0311787,19,1787,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1789]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Make haste, $N, more than one life hangs in the balance if you fail.$B$BIf for some reason you fail to help Muiredon and Narm, then return to me and I will give you another Symbol of Life for your travels.$B$BDon't mistake my aid as simple charity, you must prove yourself worthy like any other $C and continual failure may reflect upon you later.\030\030\030\030The Symbol of Life\0311,1,68,4,280,4,6179\0301,73,205,4,272,4,6179\0301,210,347,4,272,1,6179\031\031\031\031",[179]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah! Wonderful. The wolf meat should do nicely. Oh, don't worry, $N, I wouldn't forget my part of the bargain. Here, one of these should fit you.\030What do we have here? You look as though you might need something to keep your hands warm, hm?$B$BI'll tell you what would help: a pair of nice, warm gloves. And, being the kind soul that I am, I'd be more than happy to provide you with a suitable pair. I've one condition, however.$B$BI need you to go get me some wolf meat. Nice arrangement, hm? You bring me some wolf meat, and I'll make sure you don't lose any digits to frostbite. Well, what do you say?\030Sten Stoutarm would like 8 pieces of Tough Wolf Meat.\030Wolves giving you a bit of trouble? You'd do well to avoid the fangs and claws and other sharp bits, yes?\030Dwarven Outfitters\0312,1,21,2,257,2,658\0302,23,94,2,259,4,658\0302,99,157,2,257,4,658\0302,159,253,2,257,1,658\0302,255,282,2,257,1,658\0302,287,325,2,259,1,658\0302,327,347,2,257,2,658\0302,349,435,2,257,1,658\0302,437,458,2,257,2,658\0303,1,53,2,384,4,658\0301,5,14,4,272,1,658\0301,16,46,4,272,1,658\0301,48,109,4,272,1,658\0301,111,144,4,272,1,658\0304,1,35,3,256,2,658\0304,37,105,3,256,2,658\031658,2,10,Sten Stoutarm\0312,132,1426,0,\031\031ITEM,750,OBJECTIVE,8,15,",[1790]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Make haste, $N, more than one life hangs in the balance if you fail.$B$BIf for some reason you fail to help Gazin and Henze, then return to me and I will give you another Symbol of Life for your travels.$B$BDon't mistake my aid as simple charity, you must prove yourself worthy like any other $C and continual failure may reflect upon you later.\030\030\030\030The Symbol of Life\0311,1,68,4,280,4,6171\0301,73,203,4,272,4,6171\0301,208,345,4,272,1,6171\031\031\031\031",[1791]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have traveled far, young warrior.  I see fire in your eyes.  You seek a weapon of great power, yes?$B$BI can help you with your quest.  And you can help me with mine.\030Now that you've learned your berserker's stance, you'll want a nice weapon to use it with.$B$BTalk to Bath'rah the Windwatcher, a troll hermit who lives between the Alterac Mountains and the Western Plaguelands.  He is a skilled weapon maker and a powerful shaman.$B$BTo find Bath'rah, go to the river that flows along Tarren Mill's eastern flank.  Follow it north--Bath'rah is camped near ruins that rest along the river's eastern bank.\030Speak with Bath'rah the Windwatcher.\030\030The Windwatcher\0312,1,90,2,259,1,6236\0302,95,211,2,257,1,6236\0302,214,264,2,257,1,6236\0302,269,347,2,257,1,6236\0302,350,437,2,321,1,6236\0303,1,36,2,384,1,6236\0301,1,37,4,272,1,6176\0301,40,63,4,272,1,6176\0301,66,103,4,274,2,6176\0301,108,138,4,272,1,6176\0301,141,170,4,272,1,6176\0316176,2,2,Bath'rah the Windwatcher\0306176,2,6,Bath'rah the Windwatcher\0312,0,0,2,Bath'rah the Windwatcher\0311719,19,1719,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301712,23,1712,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1792]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I have the whirlwind heart, and am ready to place it within your vessel of choice.$B$BChoose your weapon, $N, and know that its power is the power of Cyclonian.\030\030\030\030Whirlwind Weapon\0311,1,82,4,272,1,6176\0301,87,160,4,272,1,6176\0316239,4,2,Cyclonian\031\0311713,19,1713,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1793]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It has been proven that the Light is with you, $N, but as times grow more dangerous, it becomes important to know what strength lies beneath the flesh. When demons, dragons, or any other evil set foot in your lands, your mettle will be tested. Will you be strong enough?$B$BBravery, regardless of the situation, is as much a part of paladinhood as the Light, your armor, and your weapon. Protecting the weak, and not losing faith are two more lessons you must master while you study in the Cathedral of Light.\030\030\030\030The Tome of Valor\0311,1,151,4,272,1,6171\0301,153,243,4,272,3,6171\0301,245,270,4,272,2,6171\0301,275,387,4,272,1,6171\0301,389,509,4,272,1,6171\031\0314,0,0,5,Cathedral of Light\0311794,22,1794,UNKNOWN\031",[1794]="UNRESOLVED\031conclusion,conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes,storytellingContext\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030\030\030\030The Tome of Valor\031\031\031\0311793,22,1793,UNKNOWN\031",[1795]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I must say I'm impressed, $N. When I faced down my felhunter, I barely escaped with my life. I sense that you have the potential to become one of the most powerful warlocks of this era.\030If you are sufficiently prepared, then we should begin. Let me explain the process to you.$B$BI will begin by creating the basic summoning circle. When that is finished, my acolytes will use the rods of channeling to create the greater circle.$B$BOnce that is done, read the incantation from the Tome of the Cabal, and the felhunter will be pulled forth. Be careful, $n. A felhunter is a powerful foe, and I'd like to see you keep your head on your shoulders.\030Using the Tome of the Cabal, summon and subdue a felhunter, then return the Tome of the Cabal to Strahad Farsan in Ratchet.\030Every warlock should have a felhunter at his command. Though it be difficult to tame, the powers it brings to its master far outweigh the cost.\030The Binding\0312,1,55,2,257,4,6251\0302,57,90,2,257,1,6251\0302,95,146,2,257,3,6251\0302,148,243,2,257,3,6251\0302,248,354,2,257,3,6251\0302,356,370,2,257,1,6251\0302,372,459,2,259,1,6251\0303,1,123,2,384,1,6251\0301,1,29,4,272,1,6251\0301,31,92,4,272,1,6251\0301,94,185,4,272,1,6251\0304,1,53,3,256,1,6251\0304,55,143,3,256,1,6251\031417,2,5,Felhunter\030417,2,7,Felhunter\030417,2,8,Felhunter\0306251,2,8,Strahad Farsan\030417,4,10,Felhunter\030417,3,12,Felhunter\0312,0,0,5,Tome of the Cabal\0302,0,0,8,Strahad Farsan\0302,0,0,8,Ratchet\0311805,19,1805,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,6268,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Summoned Felhunter",[1796]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This will do nicely, $N.$B$BAll magical items must begin with an item of high quality. The more effort and skill put into an item, the greater the magics it can hold. Rare and more expensive components hold the magic better. You will not regret having the robes fashioned into the ones we will make for you later on.\030The first item I will aid you in creating is a robe. You will gather the items for me, and we will put them together. Afterwards, assuming you succeed, you will have the first of many items that will make you more powerful and aid you in your struggles.$B$BTo start, you must have crafted Robes of Arcana. A tailor can make this for you, or perhaps you can purchase one from someone else--I'd be most impressed if you could make it yourself--but regardless, bring me the robes, and we shall go from there.\030Bring Robes of the Arcana to Menara Voidrender in the Barrens.\030How goes your search for the robes, $N? Have you created them yourself? Such personal touches I find make the imbuing of magic that much sweeter. It gives you a greater sense of accomplishment. But I understand if you choose the quicker path and have it made for you - there's something to be said for such... ambition.\030Components for the Enchanted Gold Bloodrobe\0312,1,52,2,257,3,6266\0302,54,117,2,257,3,6266\0302,119,253,2,257,3,6266\0302,258,305,2,257,1,6266\0302,307,505,2,257,4,6266\0303,1,62,2,384,1,6266\0301,1,24,4,272,3,6266\0301,29,86,4,272,1,6266\0301,88,166,4,272,1,6266\0301,168,224,4,272,1,6266\0301,226,316,4,272,3,6266\0304,1,39,3,256,2,6266\0304,41,71,3,256,2,6266\0304,73,145,3,256,1,6266\0304,147,193,3,256,1,6266\0304,195,309,3,256,4,6266\0304,311,319,3,256,1,6266\0316266,2,6,Menara Voidrender\0312,0,0,6,Menara Voidrender\0302,0,0,6,Barrens\0314781,23,4781,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5770,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1798]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031$N? Ah, of course. Our latest prodigy. The real thing can not live up to the legend, I am afraid. $B$BNo matter, you have come here to learn, not to hear me make jokes to myself.\030It is time you learned the felhunter summoning, $n. I do not have the reagents and items necessary to teach you here, so you will have to seek out another, Strahad Farsan, another of our inner circle.$B$BHe makes his residence in the goblin port of Ratchet. I will send word ahead of you to inform him of your coming.\030Speak with Strahad Farsan in the Barrens.\030\030Seeking Strahad\0312,1,51,2,257,1,6122\0302,53,200,2,259,3,6122\0302,205,257,2,257,1,6122\0302,259,317,2,257,3,6122\0303,1,41,2,384,1,6122\0301,5,18,4,272,1,6251\0301,20,38,4,272,1,6251\0301,40,97,4,272,1,6251\0301,103,178,4,272,1,6251\031417,2,1,Felhunter\0306251,2,2,Strahad Farsan\0306251,2,5,Strahad Farsan\0312,0,0,5,Barrens\0311758,23,1758,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301758,24,1758,UNKNOWN\031",[1799]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh, so Menara sent you. Fair enough... I suppose you may stay as my guest for the time being. But you must be on some pressing business - perhaps you're here seeking lost power? Maybe I'm mistaken. Maybe corruption isn't too far away from you after all.\030Good, then we shall begin.$B$BThe first thing you must do is speak to my acolytes inside. Choose one of their paths to follow--they will explain more.$B$BSecond, you must travel to Desolace and find an Infernal Orb from one of the warlocks of Mannoroc Coven. It is that orb that you will cleanse with the help of a mage named Tabetha deep in southern Dustwallow Marsh. She will aid you because of our history together.$B$BAgain, do not come back until you have done both things I've asked.\030Speak to Menara's acolytes inside the tower above Ratchet and choose one of their paths to follow.$B$BAfterwards, bring an Infernal Orb to Tabetha in Dustwallow Marsh.\030And obviously not being a mage, I wonder if I can trust you at all. I can smell the power of the arcane on you, but you seem to have eluded the stank of corruption that comes so willingly with your kind.$B$BYes, a warlock... a warlock has come to ask for my help.$B$BWell, what is it I can do for you, $n?\030Fragments of the Orb of Orahil\0312,1,26,2,257,3,6266\0302,31,89,2,257,1,6266\0302,91,150,2,257,3,6266\0302,155,258,2,257,1,6266\0302,260,368,2,257,3,6266\0302,370,418,2,323,3,6266\0302,423,489,2,257,1,6266\0303,1,98,2,384,1,6266\0303,103,167,2,384,1,6266\0301,1,23,4,272,1,6546\0301,25,38,4,272,1,6546\0301,40,93,4,272,1,6546\0301,95,177,4,276,4,6546\0301,179,197,4,272,4,6546\0301,199,253,4,276,4,6546\0304,1,67,3,256,4,6546\0304,69,203,3,260,4,6546\0304,208,224,3,256,1,6546\0304,226,263,3,256,1,6546\0304,268,305,3,256,2,6546\03189,2,4,Infernal\0306546,2,5,Tabetha\03089,2,9,Infernal\0306546,2,9,Tabetha\0312,0,0,4,Desolace\0302,0,0,8,Menara's\0302,0,0,9,Tabetha\0302,0,0,9,Dustwallow Marsh\0314961,23,4961,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7291,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[18]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Back with some bandanas, I see. The Stormwind Army appreciates your help.\030Recently, a new group of thieves has been hanging around Northshire.  They call themselves the Defias Brotherhood, and have been seen across the river to the east.$B$BI don't know what they're up to, but I'm sure it's not good!  Bring me the bandanas they wear, and I'll reward you with a weapon.\030Bring 12 Red Burlap Bandanas to Deputy Willem outside the Northshire Abbey.\030Have you gathered those bandanas for me yet?\030Brotherhood of Thieves\0312,1,68,2,257,1,823\0302,71,163,2,257,1,823\0302,168,227,2,257,1,823\0302,230,296,2,257,1,823\0303,1,75,2,384,1,823\0301,1,31,4,272,1,823\0301,33,73,4,272,1,823\0304,1,44,3,256,2,823\031823,2,5,Deputy Willem\0312,9,1429,0,\0302,0,0,5,Deputy Willem\0302,0,0,5,Northshire Abbey\031783,19,783,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306,23,6,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,752,OBJECTIVE,12,15,",[180]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031So the evil Lieutenant Fangore is dead? Good riddance to that foul creature. You are very brave, $C. The Township of Lakeshire thanks you for your aid.\030Wanted: Lieutenant Fangore$B$BKnown leader of the Shadowhide Gnoll Clan, working under the enemy of the Township and Kingdom, Morganth.  By mandate of Magistrate Solomon, this vile betrayer of Stormwind is wanted dead.  Show his paw to the Magistrate as proof of his death.\030Kill Lieutenant Fangore and return to Magistrate Solomon in Lakeshire with his paw.\030What news do you bring before the Court?\030Wanted: Lieutenant Fangore\0312,1,26,2,257,1,0\0302,31,135,2,261,1,0\0302,138,218,2,257,1,0\0302,221,273,2,257,1,0\0303,1,83,2,384,1,0\0301,1,39,4,272,2,344\0301,41,76,4,272,1,344\0301,78,100,4,272,1,344\0301,102,151,4,272,1,344\0304,1,40,3,256,2,344\031703,2,1,Lieutenant Fangore\030433,2,2,Shadowhide Gnoll\030397,2,2,Morganth\030344,2,3,Magistrate Solomon\030798,2,3,Solomon\030703,2,5,Lieutenant Fangore\030344,2,5,Magistrate Solomon\030798,2,5,Solomon\030703,4,6,Lieutenant Fangore\0312,44,1433,0,\0302,0,0,4,Magistrate\0302,0,0,5,Magistrate Solomon\0302,0,0,5,Lakeshire\031\031OBJECT,47,GIVER,?,9,Wanted: Lieutenant Fangore\030ITEM,3632,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1800]="PARTIAL\031consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031That throne room was scary, $N! Even though it was empty, it felt like a great evil had happened there. I felt mad... but I also felt sad too. I understand why the matrons tell us such stories; I will never betray my people like that!$B$BThank you for taking me to the throne room, $N. I learned a lot.\030The orphan matrons at my home tell mighty stories of battle and lore at night if we are good and do our chores.  One story was about how Lordaeron fell, and about how the evil Arthas took his own father's life to become ruler.$B$BHe had no honor, $N!  When I grow up and become a mighty Horde warrior, my blade will be guided by honor - never evil!$B$BWould you take me to see the throne room, please?  It is just before where you would go down into the Undercity.\030Take your ward to the old Lordaeron Throne Room that lies just before descending into the Undercity.$B\030Go to the old Lordaeron Throne Room that lies just before descending into the Undercity.\030Are we there yet?\030Lordaeron Throne Room\0312,1,111,2,261,4,14444\0302,114,226,2,257,1,14444\0302,231,250,2,257,1,14444\0302,253,348,2,257,3,14444\0302,353,401,2,257,4,14444\0302,404,464,2,257,4,14444\0303,1,100,2,384,1,14444\0301,1,31,4,272,1,14444\0301,33,103,4,272,1,14444\0301,105,117,4,272,1,14444\0301,119,142,4,272,1,14444\0301,144,234,4,272,3,14444\0301,239,285,4,272,1,14444\0301,287,302,4,272,1,14444\0305,1,17,3,256,2,14444\0304,1,88,3,384,1,14444\031\031\031172,19,172,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1801]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Map making! Pictures, estimations of reality. I have no use for such things.$B$BIn books, narrative, description! That is where truth lies. I would trade all the maps in this store for one book on the rise of necromancy, or a tale of the Dark Lady's triumph.\030It will take more than a simple summoning circle to bring forth a felhunter for you to challenge.$B$BMy three acolytes and I will assist in creating the magic circles. You require a copy of the Tome of the Cabal, which has been lost to us for some time. It was written by the first group of warlocks to summon a felhunter unaided.$B$BPerhaps Jorah Annison can help you with this. He's employed as a cartographer in the Undercity these days, but still knows more of ancient texts than any I know.\030Speak with Jorah Annison in the Undercity.\030\030Tome of the Cabal\0312,1,97,2,257,3,6251\0302,102,167,2,257,3,6251\0302,169,253,2,261,1,6251\0302,255,330,2,257,1,6251\0302,335,379,2,257,4,6251\0302,381,495,2,321,1,6251\0303,1,42,2,384,1,6251\0301,1,11,4,272,1,6293\0301,13,45,4,272,1,6293\0301,47,76,4,272,1,6293\0301,81,113,4,272,1,6293\0301,115,139,4,272,1,6293\0301,141,258,4,272,4,6293\031417,2,1,Felhunter\030417,2,4,Felhunter\0306293,2,5,Jorah Annison\0306293,2,7,Jorah Annison\0312,0,0,6,Undercity the\0302,0,0,7,Undercity\0311803,23,1803,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1802]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Fantastic! Now I may join the ranks of the few that have spied its contents.$B$BI can't wait to further peruse this text. This is a great day, $N! If you will just allow me to glance at it before you leave. I'm sure that Strahad will be willing to send me a copy.\030It was lost, but there's some idea as to where it might be found.$B$BThere was only one copy ever made and it was vandalized at some point, a large portion of it ripped from the binding. Rumor has it that it somehow passed into the hands of the centaur of Thousand Needles.$B$BThe rest was lost off the coast west of Southshore, where it was to be transported to Menethil Harbor by boat. It never arrived.$B$BIn exchange for this knowledge, all I ask is that if you find it, bring it to me to see.\030Retrieve the Moldy Tome and Tattered Manuscript for Krom Stoutarm in Ironforge.\030Did the rumors prove true, $N?\030Tome of the Cabal\0312,1,65,2,261,4,6294\0302,70,186,2,261,1,6294\0302,188,273,2,257,1,6294\0302,278,387,2,261,1,6294\0302,389,405,2,257,1,6294\0302,410,497,2,259,4,6294\0303,1,79,2,384,1,6294\0301,1,10,4,272,1,6294\0301,12,76,4,272,1,6294\0301,81,121,4,272,1,6294\0301,123,146,4,272,1,6294\0301,148,206,4,272,4,6294\0301,208,263,4,272,3,6294\0304,1,30,3,256,2,6294\03193,2,3,Centaur\0306294,2,7,Krom Stoutarm\0312,0,0,4,Southshore\0302,0,0,4,Menethil Harbor\0302,0,0,7,Ironforge\0311758,19,1758,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301804,23,1804,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6931,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,6997,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1803]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well well well! What do we have here?$B$BThis is impressive, $N. I wouldn't have thought it possible, but here it is in my very hands, the complete Tome of the Cabal.$B$BAllow me to leaf through its pages for just a moment before you are off again.\030Ah! I see that you are a warlock of similar tastes to mine. Indeed, acquiring the Tome of the Cabal is a worthy aspiration. Did you know that it was once held within the walls of Lordaeron? It was vandalized though, almost half its pages removed. Who would commit such a heinous act?$B$BThat half is lost, though rumor says that it fell into the hands of the centaur of the Thousand Needles.$B$BThe rest of the text was to be transferred to Ironforge, but was lost in transit on the coast west of Southshore.\030Retrieve the Moldy Tome and Tattered Manuscript for Jorah Annison in the Undercity.\030It may be that you are chasing after fairy tales, $N, but truth can be found at the center of even the wildest rumors.\030Tome of the Cabal\0312,5,59,2,257,1,6293\0302,61,123,2,257,1,6293\0302,125,189,2,257,2,6293\0302,191,246,2,257,1,6293\0302,248,283,2,257,4,6293\0302,288,391,2,261,1,6293\0302,396,508,2,261,1,6293\0303,1,83,2,384,1,6293\0301,1,15,4,272,1,6293\0301,17,37,4,272,2,6293\0301,42,64,4,272,1,6293\0301,66,166,4,272,1,6293\0301,171,248,4,272,1,6293\0304,1,118,3,256,1,6293\03193,2,6,Centaur\0306293,2,8,Jorah Annison\0312,0,0,7,Ironforge\0302,0,0,7,Southshore\0302,0,0,8,Undercity\0311801,19,1801,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301805,23,1805,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6931,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,6997,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1804]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done! The Tome of the Cabal and three pristine--slightly scratched, I suppose--rods of channeling.$B$BThis will be interesting. It's been some time since a young warlock took on a felhunter to make his own.\030Well, ah, it's hard to let it go. But you found it, and you have more important things to do with it, of course. Just, please, be sure to mention to Strahad that I wanted a copy.$B$BWhile you were out, he sent a message for you. He wanted me to tell you that for his acolytes to assist with the summoning, you'll have to acquire three rods of channeling.$B$BHe might not know where to find them, but I do! They were last used by the orcs of the Dragonmaw clan in the Wetlands. I'd check their spellcasters!\030Bring the Reconstructed Tome and 3 Rods of Channeling to Strahad Farsan in Ratchet.\030Haven't seen you around these parts for a while. Have you found the tome and the rods?\030Tome of the Cabal\0312,1,33,2,257,1,6294\0302,35,112,2,257,1,6294\0302,114,178,2,257,1,6294\0302,183,228,2,257,1,6294\0302,230,354,2,257,1,6294\0302,359,405,2,257,4,6294\0302,407,476,2,257,1,6294\0302,478,506,2,257,1,6294\0303,1,83,2,384,1,6294\0301,1,10,4,272,1,6251\0301,12,103,4,272,1,6251\0301,108,132,4,272,3,6251\0301,134,211,4,272,1,6251\0304,1,48,3,256,1,6251\0304,50,86,3,256,2,6251\0316251,2,9,Strahad Farsan\030417,4,13,Felhunter\0312,0,0,3,Strahad\0302,0,0,7,Wetlands\0302,0,0,9,Strahad Farsan\0302,0,0,9,Ratchet\0311802,19,1802,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301795,23,1795,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6930,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[1805]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done! The Tome of the Cabal and three pristine--slightly scratched, I suppose--rods of channeling.$B$BThis will be interesting. It's been some time since a young warlock took on a felhunter to make his own.\030This is one of the most interesting texts I have perused in the last few years. The selection here is sparse--mostly books on geography--and I have already read them all. I should hope that Strahad would send me a copy of this tome when he has the chance.$B$BSpeaking of him, he sent word to me while you were away. For your task, you must obtain three rods of channeling.$B$BFor allowing me to look at this text, I will share a secret: You can find the rods on orcs of the Dragonmaw Clan in the Wetlands.\030Bring the Reconstructed Tome and 3 Rods of Channeling to Strahad Farsan in Ratchet.\030Yes, $N? Of what service can I be to you?\030Tome of the Cabal\0312,1,79,2,257,1,6293\0302,81,170,2,257,1,6293\0302,172,255,2,259,4,6293\0302,260,315,2,257,1,6293\0302,317,372,2,257,1,6293\0302,377,505,2,257,3,6293\0303,1,83,2,384,1,6293\0301,1,10,4,272,1,6251\0301,12,103,4,272,1,6251\0301,108,132,4,272,3,6251\0301,134,211,4,272,1,6251\0304,1,8,3,256,2,6251\0304,10,41,3,256,2,6251\0316251,2,7,Strahad Farsan\030417,4,11,Felhunter\0312,0,0,6,Wetlands\0302,0,0,7,Strahad Farsan\0302,0,0,7,Ratchet\0311803,19,1803,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301795,23,1795,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6930,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[1806]="PARTIAL\031consequences,locations,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Here it is, $N. A weapon worthy of a champion of the Light such as yourself. I've named it after a great dwarven paladin who was a friend of mine. His name was Verigan... Bosch Verigan.$B$BPlease take it on behalf of myself and my wife. We owe you a great debt, and the world will be a safer place with one of your skill traveling the land.\030Why don't we go over to the forge and get started on this? I've been preparing for your arrival for some time, so it shouldn't take long at all.$B$BWhen we're done, you'll be far more prepared to defend the Light than you have been, this much I swear.$B$BI'll be somewhat honest, $N, seeing the results of your exploits makes me somewhat envious. But knowing that I can contribute to your adventures in my own significant way does bring me some joy.\030Wait for Jordan Stilwell to finish forging a weapon for you.\030\030The Test of Righteousness\0312,1,58,2,257,2,6181\0302,60,144,2,257,1,6181\0302,149,251,2,271,1,6181\0302,256,346,2,257,1,6181\0302,348,449,2,257,1,6181\0303,1,60,2,384,1,6181\0301,1,15,4,272,1,6181\0301,17,76,4,272,1,6181\0301,78,146,4,272,1,6181\0301,148,170,4,272,1,6181\0301,172,185,4,272,1,6181\0301,190,236,4,272,1,6181\0301,238,340,4,272,3,6181\0316181,2,6,Jordan Stilwell\031\0311654,19,1654,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[181]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031At last! The stargazing device is complete! Thank you, $N. Now I can continue my research. . .\030Now there is just one more item needed to complete this device.  Cog's blueprint calls for a lens of some sort.  The only lens I know of that would be large enough will be very difficult to acquire.$B$BThere is an ogre by the name of Zzarc'Vul who resides in the mound in southern Duskwood.  If you can, bring to me his monocle and I will use that as our lens!\030Locate Zzarc'Vul in the southern ogre mound in Duskwood and return his monocle to Viktori in Darkshire.\030Were you able to convince Zzarc'Vul to lend us his monocle for our experiment?\030Look To The Stars\0312,1,63,2,257,1,276\0302,66,111,2,257,1,276\0302,114,198,2,257,4,276\0302,203,290,2,257,1,276\0302,293,360,2,257,4,276\0303,1,103,2,384,1,276\0301,1,8,4,272,1,276\0301,10,43,4,272,1,276\0301,45,58,4,272,1,276\0301,60,90,4,272,1,276\0304,1,78,3,256,2,276\031211,2,4,Ogre\030211,2,6,Ogre\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,6,Duskwood\0302,0,0,6,Viktori\0302,0,0,6,Darkshire\031177,19,177,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,1968,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1818]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You're here for a mission? Good. I have an important one, and one that will test your skill in combat... and your resolve in the defense of the Forsaken.\030I was told Deathguard Dillinger has a job for someone like you.  If you're willing to show your value to the Dark Lady's forces, then report to Dillinger immediately.$B$BDeathguard Dillinger's post is on the west end of Brill, near the graveyard.\030Speak with Deathguard Dillinger in Brill.\030\030Speak with Dillinger\0312,1,63,2,257,1,0\0302,66,166,2,257,4,0\0302,171,246,2,257,1,0\0303,1,41,2,384,1,0\0301,1,26,4,272,2,1496\0301,28,32,4,272,1,1496\0301,34,104,4,272,3,1496\0301,106,153,4,272,1,1496\0311496,2,1,Deathguard Dillinger\0301496,2,3,Deathguard Dillinger\0301496,2,4,Deathguard Dillinger\0312,0,0,2,Dark Lady's\0302,0,0,2,Dillinger\0302,0,0,4,Brill\0311505,22,1505,UNKNOWN\0301819,23,1819,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1819]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $n.  Ulag was no minor agent of the Scourge.  You have shown the Deathguards, and hence the Dark Lady, that you are a warrior of skill and resolve, and are worthy of further instruction.\030When the Scourge swept through Tirisfal Glades, we captured one to study.  He had a free mind, and called himself Ulag the Cleaver.  But, although his will was free, he was still enthralled by the Lich King.$B$BWe hoped to find a way to break the king's control over Ulag, but we failed.  Now, finally, it is time to free him.  $B$BFree him, and kill him.$B$BActivate the skull stone trigger near the mausoleum to the north.  This will lift the magical seal that binds him.$B$BThen... be ready, $N.\030Kill Ulag the Cleaver, then speak with Deathguard Dillinger.\030Your task is yet undone, $n.  It is not wise for a warrior to show fear...\030Ulag the Cleaver\0312,1,73,2,321,1,1496\0302,76,131,2,257,1,1496\0302,134,207,2,321,3,1496\0302,212,287,2,257,1,1496\0302,290,326,2,257,1,1496\0302,333,355,2,257,1,1496\0302,360,424,2,257,1,1496\0302,427,473,2,257,3,1496\0302,478,484,2,257,1,1496\0302,486,498,2,257,1,1496\0303,1,60,2,384,1,1496\0301,1,14,4,272,1,1496\0301,17,55,4,336,1,1496\0301,58,197,4,272,1,1496\0304,1,28,3,256,1,1496\0304,31,74,3,256,1,1496\0316390,2,2,Ulag the Cleaver\03016980,2,3,The Lich King\0306390,2,11,Ulag the Cleaver\0301496,2,11,Deathguard Dillinger\03015065,4,14,Lady\031\0311818,19,1818,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301820,23,1820,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,6390,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Ulag the Cleaver",[182]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Argh! Those Light-blasted trolls!$B<He takes a few breaths and seems to settle down... a bit.>$BA group of them came in the night and stole my journal! I knew better than to trust that good-for-nothing appr...\030My brother Senir and I were sent to different parts of Dun Morogh to investigate the threat posed by the trolls. The Senate has its hands full with the troggs, so they've no need for further annoyances.$B$BFrom what I've seen, the trolls aren't well situated here in Coldridge Valley--mostly the southern cave. I'd say that the army will not be necessary. A few strong arms should be more than enough.$B$BPerhaps you'd like to assist in this endeavor? I have the authority to offer compensation for your help.\030Grelin Whitebeard would like you to kill 14 Frostmane Troll Whelps.\030From what I've learned, these trolls hail from the Frostmane clan. I'm afraid I don't know much else about them that would be of any use to you, $N.\030The Troll Cave\0312,1,112,2,261,1,786\0302,114,202,2,259,1,786\0302,207,310,2,257,1,786\0302,312,355,2,257,3,786\0302,357,401,2,257,1,786\0302,406,451,2,257,4,786\0302,453,509,2,257,1,786\0303,1,67,2,384,4,786\0301,1,5,4,272,1,786\0301,7,33,4,272,1,786\0301,36,86,4,272,4,786\0301,88,94,4,272,1,786\0301,97,151,4,272,1,786\0301,153,209,4,272,1,786\0304,1,66,3,256,1,786\0304,68,148,3,256,4,786\031786,2,8,Grelin Whitebeard\0301120,2,8,Frostmane Troll\0312,132,1426,0,\0302,0,0,3,Coldridge Valley--mostly the\0303,0,0,15,Frostmane\031218,23,218,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,706,OBJECTIVE,14,13,Frostmane Troll Whelp",[1820]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes, it is true. I have need for your skills in combat. My means are small, but my task aids both me and the Forsaken's cause. Do it, and your reward will be twofold.\030You have proven your value to the Dark Lady, now perhaps you can prove yourself to one of her subjects.$B$BColeman Farthing awaits a warrior who is willing to be his instrument of revenge against the Forsaken's enemies.$B$BYou will find him in the Gallow's End Tavern in eastern Brill.\030Speak with Coleman Farthing.\030\030Speak with Coleman\0312,1,103,2,257,4,1496\0302,108,219,2,263,1,1496\0302,224,285,2,257,3,1496\0303,1,28,2,384,1,1496\0301,1,16,4,272,1,1500\0301,18,55,4,274,1,1500\0301,57,126,4,272,1,1500\0301,128,166,4,272,3,1500\03115065,2,1,Lady\0301500,2,2,Coleman Farthing\0301500,2,4,Coleman Farthing\0312,0,0,1,Dark Lady\0302,0,0,3,Gallow's End Tavern\0311819,19,1819,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301821,23,1821,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1821]="PARTIAL\031locations,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah! You retrieved them! Now the last semblance of honor and memory is stripped from the cursed Agamand lands. The family truly is no more!\030The Agamand family were my employers in life, and they were the cause of my death!  It is fitting that the Agamands are now mindless minions of the Lich King.$B$BNow I would have their last vestiges of honor.  Go into their family crypt and rob them of their family heirlooms: a sword, an axe, a dagger and a mace.  Bring them to me!$B$BThe Agamand family crypt is at the north end of the Agamand mills, protected by lurking scourge and dead Agamands.\030Bring Coleman Farthing the Agamand Family Axe, the Agamand Family Sword, the Agamand Family Mace and the Agamand Family dagger.\030Do you have the heirlooms, $N?\030Agamand Heirlooms\0312,1,82,2,257,1,1500\0302,85,158,2,321,1,1500\0302,163,208,2,257,4,1500\0302,211,314,2,257,1,1500\0302,317,333,2,257,1,1500\0302,338,451,2,321,1,1500\0303,1,127,2,384,1,1500\0301,5,23,4,272,1,1500\0301,25,109,4,308,1,1500\0301,111,138,4,272,1,1500\0304,1,30,3,256,2,1500\03116980,2,2,The Lich King\0301500,2,7,Coleman Farthing\031\0311820,19,1820,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301822,23,1822,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7567,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,7568,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,7569,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,7566,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1822]="PARTIAL\031consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I will keep three of the weapons you returned to me, as mementos of my pain and loss. But please, $N, choose your favorite of the heirlooms and keep it for yourself.$B$BMay it serve you greater than it served its cursed, former owners.\030\030\030\030Heirloom Weapon\0311,1,85,4,272,3,1500\0301,87,165,4,272,1,1500\0301,170,235,4,276,1,1500\031\031\0311821,19,1821,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1823]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You are here for my trial, $N?\030You are a warrior of skill and growing renown.  Perhaps you are ready for Ruga Ragetotem's trial?  If so, then find Ruga in Camp Taurajo in the Barrens.$B$BHe awaits those warriors who answer his call.\030Speak with Ruga Ragetotem.\030\030Speak with Ruga\0312,1,46,2,257,1,3354\0302,49,97,2,257,4,3354\0302,100,152,2,257,4,3354\0302,157,201,2,257,1,3354\0303,1,26,2,384,1,3354\0301,1,30,4,272,2,6394\0316394,2,2,Ruga Ragetotem\0306394,2,5,Ruga Ragetotem\0312,0,0,3,Camp Taurajo\0302,0,0,3,Barrens\0311824,23,1824,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301824,24,1824,UNKNOWN\031",[1824]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Nicely done, $N! In passing the trial at the Field of Giants, you take one more step down the warrior's path.\030To pass this trial, you must travel south to the Field of Giants.  There you will find a host of crawling, insect creatures.  They are new to the Barrens and I do not like what they herald.$B$BBring me their still-twitching antennae, and waste no time, $N, for harvested antennae will not twitch for long.  Bring me the antennae in the time allowed, and you will pass the trial.\030Bring 5 twitching antennae to Ruga Ragetotem at Camp Taurajo\030Do you have the antennae? If so then give them to me quickly, for twitching antennae do not twitch forever...\030Trial at the Field of Giants\0312,1,65,2,257,1,6394\0302,68,124,2,257,3,6394\0302,127,189,2,257,1,6394\0302,194,305,2,257,3,6394\0302,308,378,2,257,3,6394\0303,1,60,2,384,1,6394\0301,1,16,4,272,1,6394\0301,18,109,4,272,1,6394\0304,1,25,3,256,2,6394\0304,27,109,3,256,4,6394\03114848,2,3,Herald\0306394,2,6,Ruga Ragetotem\0312,0,0,1,Field of Giants\0302,0,0,3,Barrens\0302,0,0,6,Ruga Ragetotem\0302,0,0,6,Camp Taurajo\0304,0,0,8,Field of Giants\0311825,23,1825,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7119,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[1825]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes, you have come. This is good, for we have much to discuss, you and I.\030Thun'grim Firegaze, an orc blacksmith of renown, has heard of your continued deeds of valor in service of the Horde.  He would like to fashion for you a suit of armor, and bids you speak with him immediately.$B$BThun'grim is camped east of the Crossroads in the Barrens.\030Speak with Thun'grim Firegaze in the Barrens.\030\030Speak with Thun'grim\0312,1,116,2,257,1,6394\0302,119,208,2,257,4,6394\0302,213,270,2,257,1,6394\0303,1,45,2,384,1,6394\0301,1,19,4,272,1,5878\0301,21,73,4,272,1,5878\0315878,2,1,Thun'grim Firegaze\0305878,2,4,Thun'grim Firegaze\0312,0,0,3,Crossroads\0302,0,0,3,Barrens\0302,0,0,4,Barrens\0311824,19,1824,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301838,23,1838,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[183]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Excellent! I can go back to my... leisurely... hunting now. Thank you, $N.\030Nothing like a day of boar hunting, eh?$B$BThough, here in Coldridge Valley, there are so many boars it almost takes the fun out of it. No need to get them charging. They're all angry and ready without any help. In fact, recently, there've been so many boars in the area, it's become dangerous for me to do my daily hunting.$B$BLong story short, if you could help me kill some of the boars, I would appreciate it.\030Talin Keeneye would like you to kill 12 Small Crag Boars.\030How goes the hunt?\030The Boar Hunter\0312,1,39,2,257,2,714\0302,44,135,2,257,1,714\0302,137,165,2,259,1,714\0302,167,211,2,257,1,714\0302,213,324,2,257,1,714\0302,329,413,2,257,4,714\0303,1,57,2,384,4,714\0301,1,10,4,272,1,714\0301,12,33,4,272,1,714\0301,35,46,4,272,1,714\0301,48,59,4,272,1,714\0301,61,74,4,272,1,714\0304,1,18,3,256,2,714\0312809,2,1,Boar\030714,2,7,Talin Keeneye\0312,132,1426,0,\0302,0,0,2,Coldridge Valley\031\031NPC,708,OBJECTIVE,12,13,Small Crag Boar",[1838]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You brought all that I asked. Now, I will do my part...\030I have heard tales of your strength and valor, and wish to make for you a suit of armor, a companion to aid you as tales of your great deeds grow.$B$BBut the fashioning of this armor will be a quest unto itself, $N.  I will need your help, and the help of other smiths of the Horde.$B$BHere, take this scroll.  I spent many nights, struggling with near-blind eyes, writing that which I need for the armor.  Bring me the items on this scroll and I will create for you the first piece of the suit.\030Bring to Thun'grim Firegaze 15 Smoky Iron Ingots, 10 Powdered Azurite, 10 Iron Bars and a Vial of Phlogiston.\030Do you have the items on my scroll, $N?\030Brutal Armor\0312,1,146,2,259,3,5878\0302,151,215,2,257,3,5878\0302,218,282,2,259,3,5878\0302,287,309,2,257,1,5878\0302,312,405,2,259,1,5878\0302,408,495,2,257,3,5878\0303,1,109,2,384,1,5878\0301,1,29,4,272,1,5878\0301,31,55,4,272,3,5878\0304,1,39,3,256,2,5878\0315878,2,7,Thun'grim Firegaze\0312,0,0,7,Thun'grim Firegaze\0311825,19,1825,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7126,OBJECTIVE,15,15,\030ITEM,7127,OBJECTIVE,10,15,\030ITEM,3575,OBJECTIVE,10,15,\030ITEM,6841,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1839]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Greetings, $n.  Old Thun'grim sent word to me of your coming, but had he kept silent your presence here would not have surprised me.$B$BThe spirits follow your progress, young warrior, and they tell me that many foes have fallen before you.\030The troll smith Ula'elek will craft for you the brutal gauntlets.  He dwells in Durotar, in Sen'jin Village with his Darkspear brethren, and he awaits your coming.\030Speak with Ula'elek in Durotar.\030\030Ula'elek and the Brutal Gauntlets\0312,1,65,2,257,3,5878\0302,68,163,2,257,1,5878\0303,1,31,2,384,1,5878\0301,1,14,4,272,1,6408\0301,17,132,4,272,4,6408\0301,137,240,4,272,1,6408\0316408,2,1,Ula'elek\0306408,2,3,Ula'elek\0312,0,0,2,Durotar\0302,0,0,2,Sen'jin Village\0302,0,0,3,Durotar\0311838,19,1838,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301842,23,1842,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301842,24,1842,UNKNOWN\031",[184]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Loads of thanks, $N! As I was saying, these parts aren't fit for honest folk anymore, but if things get better, then this deed will let us reclaim our land.$B$BI don't have much to offer you, but here -- take this.\030This is the deed to an expanse of farmlands within Westfall.  It is signed by a Theodore Furlbrow and cosigned by his wife, Verna.  And on the back of the deed are hastily scrawled words:$B$B\"We leaned on Furlbrow and got his deed.  Thought it might be handy if you wanted to forge one of these for your own place.$B$BThe Furlbrows won't give us trouble.  Last I saw them they were on their way out of Westfall, stuck with a broken wagon.\"$B$BYou think the Furlbrows might want their deed back...\030Bring Furlbrow's Deed to Farmer Furlbrow.\030You have the deed to my farm?? That's good news! Some ruffians stole it days ago... I thought it was gone for good!$B$BPlease, let me have it. We're on our way out of Westfall and ain't coming back any time soon, but if we do then we'll need those papers...\030Furlbrow's Deed\0312,1,60,2,257,1,0\0302,63,130,2,257,1,0\0302,133,187,2,257,1,0\0302,192,231,2,257,1,0\0302,234,314,2,257,4,0\0302,319,354,2,257,1,0\0302,357,439,2,257,1,0\0302,444,496,2,259,4,0\0303,1,41,2,384,1,0\0301,1,20,4,272,1,237\0301,22,156,4,272,4,237\0301,161,214,4,272,1,237\0304,1,30,3,256,2,237\0304,32,48,3,256,1,237\0304,50,83,3,256,1,237\0304,85,115,3,256,1,237\0304,120,142,3,256,1,237\0304,144,257,3,258,4,237\031237,2,9,Farmer Furlbrow\0312,40,1436,0,\0302,0,0,1,Westfall\0302,0,0,9,Farmer Furlbrow\031\031ITEM,1972,STARTER,?,10,",[1840]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Greetings, warrior.  I am Orm, and Thun'grim tells me you wish a helm made?\030Orm Stonehoof is respected greatly for his skill.  He will make for you the brutal helm.$B$BSeek him out in Thunder Bluff, near the pool by the city's great, central totem.\030Speak with Orm Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff.\030\030Orm Stonehoof and the Brutal Helm\0312,1,49,2,257,1,5878\0302,52,88,2,257,3,5878\0302,93,172,2,257,1,5878\0303,1,42,2,384,1,5878\0301,1,19,4,272,1,6410\0301,22,75,4,274,2,6410\0316410,2,1,Orm Stonehoof\0306410,2,4,Orm Stonehoof\0312,0,0,3,Thunder Bluff\0302,0,0,4,Thunder Bluff\0311838,19,1838,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301844,23,1844,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301844,24,1844,UNKNOWN\031",[1841]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You are here for leg armor? Great!$B$BUm... am I making the armor for you, or are you making it for me?$B$BThat was joke. Was it funny? I can't tell... I lost my sense of humor the same time I lost my sense of smell. Which was about the same time I stopped breathing.\030It is said that, before her death, Velora Nitely was one of the finest armorsmiths in Lordaeron.  Death, it seems, has not decreased her talents.  Speak with Velora--she will make your brutal legguards.$B$BVelora plies her trade in the Undercity of Lordaeron, in the trade quarter.\030Speak with Velora Nitely in the Undercity.\030\030Velora Nitely and the Brutal Legguards\0312,1,96,2,257,1,5878\0302,99,145,2,257,4,5878\0302,148,202,2,257,3,5878\0302,207,281,2,257,1,5878\0303,1,42,2,384,1,5878\0301,1,27,4,272,2,6411\0301,29,34,4,272,1,6411\0301,45,103,4,272,2,6411\0301,108,121,4,272,1,6411\0301,123,135,4,272,2,6411\0301,137,151,4,272,1,6411\0301,153,216,4,276,1,6411\0301,218,267,4,272,1,6411\0316411,2,1,Velora Nitely\0306411,2,5,Velora Nitely\0312,0,0,1,Lordaeron\0302,0,0,4,Undercity of Lordaeron\0302,0,0,5,Undercity\0311838,19,1838,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301846,23,1846,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301846,24,1846,UNKNOWN\031",[1842]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, you have them! Now, just as the Satyrs leeched the strength of Ashenvale, I will leech the power held within these hooves and harness it into my crafting...\030I can make you a pair of brutal gauntlets, and great magic will they hold.  But first, you must collect this magic and bring it to me.$B$BThe satyrs dwell in northeastern Ashenvale because of the forest's power.  They feed off its purity, leeching and corrupting.  You can tell which satyrs have drawn the most of Ashenvale's magic by their swollen, uncloven hooves.$B$BThese hooves hold great power.  I will need them for your gauntlets' crafting.\030Bring 7 Uncloven Satyr Hooves to Ula'elek at Sen'jin Village in Durotar.\030Do you have the hooves, $N? The magic within them is strong.\030Satyr Hooves\0312,1,74,2,257,3,6408\0302,77,134,2,257,1,6408\0302,139,211,2,259,1,6408\0302,214,263,2,261,1,6408\0302,266,366,2,257,1,6408\0302,371,400,2,257,1,6408\0302,403,448,2,259,3,6408\0303,1,72,2,384,1,6408\0301,1,18,4,272,1,6408\0301,20,160,4,272,3,6408\0304,1,27,3,256,2,6408\0304,29,60,3,256,1,6408\0316408,2,8,Ula'elek\0312,0,0,8,Ula'elek\0302,0,0,8,Sen'jin Village\0302,0,0,8,Durotar\0311843,23,1843,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7128,OBJECTIVE,7,15,",[1843]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, $N. These gauntlets are my best work. Take them. In wearing them, you bring honor to me and my ancestors.\030\030\030\030Brutal Gauntlets\0311,1,14,4,272,1,6408\0301,16,48,4,272,1,6408\0301,50,59,4,272,1,6408\0301,61,116,4,272,1,6408\031\031\0311842,19,1842,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1844]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have completed your task, $N, and shown me your worth and resolve. The helm will be yours...\030I will make you the helm, but you must show me you are worthy of it.$B$BNestled in the northwestern reaches of the Stonetalon Mountains there lies the Charred Vale.  It was once a verdant place, but is now defiled and ashen, and what creatures remain there are mad with pain and despair.$B$BThat place is where I send you, $N.$B$BYou must go to the Charred Vale and find a chimaera matriarch.  Slay her, free her of her misery.  Bring me her galvanized horn as proof, and I shall make for you the helm.\030Bring a Galvanized Horn to Orm Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff.\030Do you have the horn? Is the matriarch free of pain?\030Chimaeric Horn\0312,1,68,2,257,3,6410\0302,73,164,2,257,1,6410\0302,167,287,2,257,1,6410\0302,292,326,2,257,1,6410\0302,331,392,2,257,1,6410\0302,395,427,2,257,1,6410\0302,430,502,2,257,3,6410\0303,1,58,2,384,1,6410\0301,1,70,4,272,1,6410\0301,72,96,4,272,3,6410\0304,1,21,3,256,2,6410\0304,23,52,3,256,2,6410\0316167,2,5,Chimaera Matriarch\0306410,2,8,Orm Stonehoof\0312,0,0,5,Charred Vale\0302,0,0,8,Orm Stonehoof\0302,0,0,8,Thunder Bluff\0311845,23,1845,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6840,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1845]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I give this helm to you.$B$BGreat deeds brought you to me, $N, and Earthmother willing... even greater deeds lie before you.\030\030\030\030Brutal Helm\0311,1,24,4,272,1,6410\0301,29,89,4,272,1,6410\0301,91,124,4,272,1,6410\031\031\0311844,19,1844,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1846]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done! These all look strong. I think they'll do quite nicely. How did those orcs mind you taking their shins, $N? Complain much?$B$BThat was another joke. You're not laughing.$B$BI'm not very funny these days, am I...\030To make the brutal leg guards, I need a brace of sturdy shinbones.  The Dragonmaw orcs of the Wetlands have nice, thick shinbones.  I'll need theirs.$B$BBut they must be sturdy.  Be sure to test the shinbones as you collect them.  If you can break them with your bare hands, then they won't be sturdy enough to work with.\030Bring 8 Sturdy Dragonmaw Shinbones to Velora Nitely in the Undercity.\030I'm waiting for those shinbones, $N. They'll make a nice frame for your leg guards.\030Dragonmaw Shinbones\0312,1,66,2,259,1,6411\0302,69,130,2,257,1,6411\0302,133,149,2,259,1,6411\0302,154,177,2,257,1,6411\0302,180,229,2,257,1,6411\0302,232,321,2,257,4,6411\0303,1,69,2,384,1,6411\0301,1,10,4,272,1,6411\0301,12,33,4,272,1,6411\0301,35,66,4,272,1,6411\0301,68,118,4,272,2,6411\0301,120,133,4,272,2,6411\0301,138,159,4,272,1,6411\0301,161,180,4,272,1,6411\0301,185,222,4,272,1,6411\0304,1,36,3,256,1,6411\0304,38,83,3,256,1,6411\0316411,2,7,Velora Nitely\0312,0,0,7,Velora Nitely\0302,0,0,7,Undercity\0311847,23,1847,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7134,OBJECTIVE,8,15,",[1847]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Here are your legguards, $N. Let me know how they fit or if you need any modifications. I aim to please! At least I used to.$B$BThese days I don't care much for my craft. But it beats being a mindless minion of the Scourge!$B$BI guess.\030\030\030\030Brutal Legguards\0311,1,28,4,272,1,6411\0301,30,87,4,274,4,6411\0301,89,104,4,272,1,6411\0301,106,124,4,272,1,6411\0301,129,170,4,272,1,6411\0301,172,223,4,336,1,6411\0301,228,235,4,272,1,6411\031\031\0311846,19,1846,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1848]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I am sure you endured much hardship and shed much blood on my task, $N. Here is the product of your toil.$B$BMay you wear it well, and may you one day return here with stories of its service to you.\030\030\030\030Brutal Hauberk\0311,1,71,4,272,1,5878\0301,73,105,4,272,1,5878\0301,110,198,4,272,1,5878\031\031\0311838,19,1838,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[185]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Nicely done, $n.  You are ready to move on.\030When I was but a young girl, my father trained me in the art of tiger hunting.$B$BYou'll find the young felines much easier to track and slay.  For this reason, we'll start you out easy.  One can often find young tigers near the expedition camp.$B$BTest your tracking skills and see if you can hunt some of the beasts down.\030Ajeck Rouack of Nesingwary's Expedition wants you to kill 10 Young Stranglethorn Tigers.\030I don't feel confident in training you further, $n, until you have proven yourself skilled in slaying the youngest of the tigers first.\030Tiger Mastery\0312,1,78,2,257,1,717\0302,83,142,2,257,1,717\0302,145,186,2,257,1,717\0302,189,245,2,257,1,717\0302,250,323,2,257,4,717\0303,1,88,2,386,1,717\0301,1,16,4,272,1,717\0301,19,43,4,272,1,717\0304,1,135,3,256,1,717\031371,2,1,Girl\030717,2,6,Ajeck Rouack\0312,33,1434,0,\031583,19,583,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030186,23,186,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,681,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Young Stranglethorn Tiger",[1858]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hmmm, now this is interesting. You've more than proved your worth with this, $N. I am quite impressed. Consider yourself the newest member of the Shattered Hand. And take this, it will be a great help to you in the future, I think.\030I'll leave it to you to get Tazan's satchel open, and return to me with its contents. The locking mechanism is complex, so it would probably be easiest if you obtained the key.$B$BAs you didn't find it on Tazan's body, I can only assume that he left the key in the care of another... Ah, yes, that's right. He had an assistant named Gamon. A drunkard, you'll most likely find him at the tavern. Perhaps you could quietly relieve him of the key.\030Steal Tazan's key, then use it to open his Satchel and deliver its contents to Therzok in the Cleft of Shadow in Orgrimmar.\030Is it not vexing to have the subject of your desire within your grasp, but to have no way of getting to it?\030The Shattered Hand\0312,1,85,2,257,1,6446\0302,87,176,2,257,4,6446\0302,181,283,2,257,4,6446\0302,285,306,2,257,1,6446\0302,308,339,2,257,1,6446\0302,341,394,2,257,1,6446\0302,396,444,2,257,4,6446\0303,1,123,2,388,1,6446\0301,1,30,4,272,1,6446\0301,32,80,4,272,1,6446\0301,82,102,4,272,1,6446\0301,104,161,4,272,1,6446\0301,163,231,4,272,3,6446\0304,1,107,3,258,2,6446\0316466,2,5,Gamon\0306446,2,8,Therzok\0304244,2,8,Shadow\0312,0,0,8,Therzok\0302,0,0,8,Cleft of Shadow\0302,0,0,8,Orgrimmar\0311963,19,1963,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7295,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1859]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very good, I'm glad Kaplak was able to get a hold of you.$B$BWe have some things to speak of, not the least of which is your future with the Hand.\030Lower your voice, $n. Yeah, I know your name. Was told to keep an eye out for an orc by your description.$B$BFrom what we've heard about you, you can handle yourself in combat, and aren't opposed to a little sneakery from time to time.$B$BAm I right?$B$BAnyways, you should go see Therzok in Orgrimmar. He's got an offer for you to hear.\030Speak with Therzok in the Cleft of Shadow in Orgrimmar.\030\030Therzok\0312,1,21,2,257,1,3170\0302,23,45,2,257,1,3170\0302,47,105,2,257,1,3170\0302,110,235,2,257,1,3170\0302,240,250,2,257,2,3170\0302,255,302,2,257,1,3170\0302,304,337,2,257,1,3170\0303,1,55,2,384,1,3170\0301,1,57,4,272,1,6446\0301,62,146,4,272,1,6446\0316446,2,6,Therzok\0306446,2,8,Therzok\0304244,2,8,Shadow\0303170,4,9,Kaplak\0312,0,0,6,Orgrimmar\0302,0,0,8,Cleft of Shadow\0302,0,0,8,Orgrimmar\0311885,22,1885,UNKNOWN\0301963,23,1963,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[186]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I am impressed, $c.  You are progressing quite well.\030You are learning, $c.  Let us test your skills with the mature cats now. Kill 10 Stranglethorn Tigers this time out.\030Ajeck Rouack of Nesingwary's Expedition wants you to kill 10 Stranglethorn Tigers.\030If you strive for greater challenges you must first prove yourself with the task at hand. Return to me after you've killed 10 Stranglethorn Tigers.\030Tiger Mastery\0312,1,21,2,257,1,717\0302,24,72,2,257,1,717\0302,74,116,2,257,1,717\0303,1,82,2,386,1,717\0301,1,19,4,272,1,717\0301,22,52,4,272,1,717\0304,1,89,3,256,4,717\0304,91,147,3,256,1,717\031717,2,4,Ajeck Rouack\0312,33,1434,0,\031185,19,185,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030187,23,187,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,682,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Stranglethorn Tiger",[1860]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have been sent to aid me in my task, $N? Good. It is heartening to see young mages eager to help in our cause...$B$BWhat cause, you ask? In time, young one. You shall know... in time.\030We mages have a task that needs doing.  One that is vital to the safety of Stormwind and Elwynn forest.$B$BJennea Cannon has the details.  She studies in the wizard's sanctum, in the mage district of Stormwind.  You should make your way to her with haste.\030Speak with Jennea Cannon in Stormwind.\030\030Speak with Jennea\0312,1,38,2,259,1,328\0302,41,103,2,265,1,328\0302,108,137,2,257,1,328\0302,140,210,2,257,1,328\0302,213,255,2,257,1,328\0303,1,38,2,384,1,328\0301,1,44,4,272,2,5497\0301,46,50,4,272,1,5497\0301,52,116,4,272,1,5497\0301,121,140,4,272,2,5497\0301,142,160,4,272,1,5497\0301,162,178,4,272,3,5497\0301,180,187,4,272,1,5497\0315497,2,3,Jennea Cannon\0305497,2,6,Jennea Cannon\0312,0,0,6,Stormwind\0311879,22,1879,UNKNOWN\0301861,23,1861,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1861]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, $N. I will test this water for magical properties. Let us hope that it contains none, or we may find that those who drink from Mirror Lake for too long will be adversely affected.$B$BHere, $N. Take this orb or staff as a token of your service. May it serve you well.\030This world has been victim to massive mystic struggles, which tore magic currents from once stable channels.  We struggle to determine the effects these changes have caused, and some of us fear the worst!$B$BBut I will reveal more of this later.  Right now, we need you to gather information.$B$BHere, take this flask.  Go to the base of the waterfall at Mirror Lake, southwest of the Stormwind gates, and retrieve a sample of the water there.  Return it to me so that I might test it for magical taints.\030Bring a Mirror Lake sample to Jennea Cannon in Stormwind.\030Do you have the sample, $N? The flow of magic in Stormwind and Elwynn has been altered, and I must know if it is seeping into the water.\030Mirror Lake\0312,1,108,2,257,1,5497\0302,111,204,2,257,1,5497\0302,209,245,2,257,3,5497\0302,248,292,2,259,1,5497\0302,297,318,2,257,1,5497\0302,321,443,2,257,1,5497\0302,446,504,2,259,4,5497\0303,1,57,2,384,1,5497\0301,1,14,4,272,1,5497\0301,16,61,4,272,3,5497\0301,63,190,4,274,3,5497\0301,195,203,4,272,1,5497\0301,205,254,4,272,1,5497\0301,256,277,4,272,1,5497\0304,1,27,3,256,2,5497\0304,29,136,3,256,4,5497\0315497,2,8,Jennea Cannon\0312,0,0,6,Mirror Lake\0302,0,0,8,Jennea Cannon\0302,0,0,8,Stormwind\0304,0,0,11,Mirror Lake\0303,0,0,16,Stormwind\0311860,19,1860,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7206,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[187]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Most impressive.  I believe you are almost ready.\030Now I'm going to up the stakes on you and truly test your skill.  Prove to me you can kill 10 Elder Stranglethorn Tigers.  If you can do that, you will be ready for your final challenge before I declare you a master tiger hunter in Master Nesingwary's presence.$B$BElder Stranglethorn Tigers are not only the most difficult to find, they are also the fiercest to defeat.\030Ajeck Rouack of Nesingwary's Expedition wants you to kill 10 Elder Stranglethorn Tigers.\030You must kill 10 Elder Stranglethorn Tigers before I give you the final challenge that will determine if you are a true tiger hunting master.\030Tiger Mastery\0312,1,64,2,257,3,717\0302,67,121,2,257,1,717\0302,124,261,2,257,4,717\0302,266,370,2,257,1,717\0303,1,88,2,386,1,717\0301,1,16,4,272,1,717\0301,19,49,4,272,4,717\0304,1,141,3,256,4,717\031717,2,5,Ajeck Rouack\0312,33,1434,0,\0302,0,0,3,Master Nesingwary's\031186,19,186,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030188,23,188,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,1085,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Elder Stranglethorn Tiger",[1878]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Excellent - the more water pouches we are able to reclaim, the further away from disaster we'll all be! Keep 'em coming, and I will be sure to reward you for every five water pouches you bring me.\030\030\030Back again, $n?  If you have five more Wastewander water pouches, then I have a care package with your name on it!\030Water Pouch Bounty\0311,1,103,4,272,1,7408\0301,105,196,4,272,3,7408\0304,1,15,3,256,2,7408\0304,18,114,3,256,4,7408\031\0312,440,1446,0,\0311707,19,1707,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,8483,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[1879]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh, I can see you have promise, yes you do! But it takes more than promise to be a good mage.  And if you're not a good mage, then you're a bad mage.  And bad mages are part of the problem, yes they are!$B$BOops, I'm getting ahead of things.  Let's begin at the start!\030$N!  Bink, my gnome colleague in Ironforge, sends word.  She has a task that needs doing and won't rely on anyone but a mage to do it!  Are you that mage, $N?$B$BIf so, then speak with Bink.  She spends her time in the Hall of Mysteries in the Mystic Ward of Ironforge.\030Speak with Bink in Ironforge.\030\030Speak with Bink\0312,6,55,2,257,1,1228\0302,58,134,2,259,1,1228\0302,137,158,2,257,2,1228\0302,163,190,2,257,4,1228\0302,193,269,2,257,1,1228\0303,1,29,2,384,1,1228\0301,1,43,4,272,1,5144\0301,45,93,4,272,1,5144\0301,96,149,4,272,4,5144\0301,152,203,4,276,1,5144\0301,208,241,4,272,1,5144\0301,244,268,4,272,1,5144\0315144,2,1,Bink\0305144,2,4,Bink\0305144,2,6,Bink\0312,0,0,1,Ironforge\0302,0,0,5,Hall of Mysteries\0302,0,0,5,Mystic Ward of Ironforge\0302,0,0,6,Ironforge\0311860,22,1860,UNKNOWN\0301880,23,1880,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[188]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Most impressive, I do say!  You are a true Master Tiger Hunter, $N!\030Here is the final challenge that I will put forth.  We've been tracking an elusive tiger for weeks.  We call the beast Sin'Dall.  See if you can do what no $r has done before: hunt down and kill Sin'Dall.  Bring me her paw as proof of your accomplishment.$B$BTracking her down will be no easy task.\030Ajeck Rouack of Nesingwary's Expedition wants you to kill Sin'Dall and return with her paw.\030How goes the hunt for Sin'Dall?\030Tiger Mastery\0312,1,50,2,257,3,717\0302,53,99,2,257,1,717\0302,102,128,2,257,1,717\0302,131,204,2,257,4,717\0302,207,255,2,257,1,717\0302,260,298,2,257,3,717\0303,1,91,2,386,1,717\0301,1,26,4,272,1,717\0301,29,67,4,272,1,717\0304,1,31,3,256,2,717\03110430,2,3,The Beast\030729,2,3,Sin'Dall\030729,2,4,Sin'Dall\030717,2,7,Ajeck Rouack\030729,2,7,Sin'Dall\030729,3,10,Sin'Dall\0312,33,1434,0,\031187,19,187,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3879,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1880]="PARTIAL\031consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh, splendid day!  When I made the gizmonitor I never realized how dependent on it I would become.  Now I can begin my studies anew!$B$BThank you, $n!  And here--these were my first tools as a mage.  They're a little scratched but they're well tested.  Take your pick--I'm sure you'll find either of them useful.\030We mages do more than just waggle our fingers and make pretty sparks!  We control magic, the base fabric of our world!  And that takes great care, and resolve.  And knowledge... so much knowledge!$B$BOne of my devices, the mage-tastic gizmonitor, collects and stores that knowledge in huge amounts!  But it's lost!  When we fled our home of Gnomeregan, I left it in a chest in one of our huts outside the city, and now the place is crawling with leper gnomes!$B$BPlease, $N, retrieve my gizmonitor!\030Bring Bink her Mage-tastic Gizmonitor.\030Did you find the gizmonitor? I must have it before its energy supply runs out!\030Mage-tastic Gizmonitor\0312,1,69,2,257,1,5144\0302,72,118,2,257,1,5144\0302,121,159,2,257,1,5144\0302,162,177,2,257,1,5144\0302,179,196,2,257,1,5144\0302,201,298,2,257,1,5144\0302,301,314,2,261,1,5144\0302,317,459,2,257,1,5144\0302,464,498,2,257,1,5144\0303,1,38,2,384,1,5144\0301,1,17,4,272,1,5144\0301,20,98,4,272,4,5144\0301,101,132,4,272,1,5144\0301,137,150,4,272,1,5144\0301,153,198,4,272,1,5144\0301,201,251,4,272,1,5144\0301,254,312,4,272,1,5144\0304,1,28,3,256,2,5144\0304,30,78,3,256,1,5144\0315144,2,10,Bink\031\0311879,19,1879,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7226,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1881]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Greetings, $N. You were wise to answer my call, and wiser still if you heed what I next say...\030$N, Anastasia Hartwell has a task for someone of your talents.  Speak with her in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, and prepare yourself for your first task for the mages of the Forsaken.\030Speak with Anastasia Hartwell.\030\030Speak with Anastasia\0312,1,62,2,257,1,2128\0302,65,189,2,257,1,2128\0303,1,30,2,384,1,2128\0301,1,14,4,272,1,4568\0301,16,94,4,272,4,4568\0314568,2,1,Anastasia Hartwell\0304568,2,3,Anastasia Hartwell\0312,0,0,2,Magic Quarter of the Undercity\0311883,22,1883,UNKNOWN\0301882,23,1882,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301882,24,1882,UNKNOWN\031",[1882]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, a fine specimen this is. I will send it to be studied by our apothecaries to determine the extent of the Plagueland's taint.$B$BWell done, $N. For your services, I present to you this choice: an orb or staff. Whichever you choose, you will find it quite useful.\030The Plaguelands to the east are an aberration.  Devised by the Lich King, they spread their magic into the soil, corrupting and killing all that live.  Although there is a certain charm to the destructive forces of the plague, we, the mages of the Forsaken, believe it is unruly and must be curtailed.$B$BBut first, we must measure how far it has spread into Tirisfal.  Go to the Balnir Farmstead in eastern Tirisfal.  In the garden are flowers--snapdragons.  Gather these and return.\030Bring Balnir Snapdragons to Anastasia Hartwell in the Mage Quarter of the Undercity.\030Do you have the snapdragons? That breed of flower is highly receptive to magic energies, and studying the snapdragons so close to the Plaguelands can tell us if the plague has entered Tirisfal Glades.\030The Balnir Farmstead\0312,1,46,2,257,1,4568\0302,49,150,2,325,1,4568\0302,153,301,2,261,4,4568\0302,306,368,2,257,1,4568\0302,371,417,2,257,1,4568\0302,420,458,2,257,1,4568\0302,461,484,2,257,1,4568\0303,1,84,2,384,1,4568\0301,1,28,4,272,1,4568\0301,30,128,4,272,3,4568\0301,133,146,4,272,1,4568\0301,148,212,4,272,1,4568\0301,214,265,4,272,3,4568\0304,1,28,3,256,2,4568\0304,30,200,3,260,4,4568\03116980,2,2,The Lich King\0304568,2,8,Anastasia Hartwell\0312,0,0,5,Balnir Farmstead\0302,0,0,8,Anastasia Hartwell\0302,0,0,8,Mage Quarter of the Undercity\0303,0,0,15,Plaguelands\031\031ITEM,7227,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1883]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hail, $N. Praise to you, for my call for aid is now answered. Let us hope you are up to the task...\030Un'thuwa, tribal mage of Sen'jin Village, detects a disturbance in the magic currents of Durotar and asks for aid.  Speak with Un'thuwa and do what you can to help him.$B$BDo this, and in time further secrets will be revealed to you.\030Speak with Un'thuwa.\030\030Speak with Un'thuwa\0312,1,114,2,257,1,7311\0302,117,168,2,257,1,7311\0302,173,233,2,257,3,7311\0303,1,20,2,384,1,7311\0301,1,9,4,272,1,5880\0301,11,61,4,272,1,5880\0301,63,99,4,274,3,5880\0315880,2,1,Un'Thuwa\0305880,2,2,Un'Thuwa\0305880,2,4,Un'Thuwa\031\0311881,22,1881,UNKNOWN\0301884,23,1884,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301884,24,1884,UNKNOWN\031",[1884]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030requestItems\030title\031I sense that Zalazane's ju-ju heaps were destroyed, and with time, and luck, the flow of magic in Durotar will return to normal.$B$BA great deed you have done for your people, $N. And you have shown your worth to us, the mages of the Horde.\030The warlock Zalazane of the Echo Isles has disrupted the normal flow of magic in Durotar.  He does this through tainted fetishes, ju-ju heaps, which he has placed among his huts on the main Echo Isle.$B$BThese heaps corrupt our wildlife and give power to the warlocks and infernal creatures that lurk in the land's dark corners.$B$BYou must destroy the ju-ju heaps, $N, before the flow of magic is forever altered.\030Destroy 4 Ju-Ju Heaps, then return to Un'thuwa in Sen'jin Village.\030\030Ju-Ju Heaps Destroyed\030You must hurry, $N. Destroy the ju-ju heaps!\030Ju-Ju Heaps\0312,1,89,2,257,1,5880\0302,92,200,2,257,1,5880\0302,205,328,2,261,1,5880\0302,333,414,2,261,1,5880\0303,1,66,2,388,1,5880\0301,1,128,4,276,3,5880\0301,133,179,4,272,1,5880\0301,181,240,4,272,1,5880\0306,1,19,3,256,1,5880\0306,21,44,3,260,1,5880\0305,1,21,3,388,1,5880\0313205,2,1,Zalazane\03089,2,3,Infernal\0305880,2,5,Un'Thuwa\0312,0,0,1,Durotar\0302,0,0,5,Un'thuwa\0302,0,0,5,Sen'jin Village\0304,0,0,6,Durotar\031\031OBJECT,102986,OBJECTIVE,4,14,Ju-Ju Heap",[1885]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hm. No doubt you made your way here at first mention of my summons, yes? Of course. I would expect no less from a prospective Deathstalker.\030$n? Not quite what I was expecting, considering Carkad himself has taken an interest to you. Looks can be deceiving though, right?$B$BEither way, you should go see him as soon as possible. You wouldn't want to know what happened to the last few that chose to ignore his summons.\030Speak with Mennet Carkad in the Rogues' Quarter of the Undercity.\030\030Mennet Carkad\0312,5,92,2,257,1,2130\0302,94,130,2,257,2,2130\0302,135,188,2,257,1,2130\0302,190,278,2,257,1,2130\0303,1,65,2,384,1,2130\0301,5,72,4,272,2,6467\0301,74,83,4,272,1,6467\0301,85,139,4,272,4,6467\0316467,2,5,Mennet Carkad\0312,0,0,5,Rogues' Quarter of the Undercity\0311859,22,1859,UNKNOWN\0301886,23,1886,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1886]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $N. You've passed the first part of this test. Hopefully Andron will not have caught wind of your activities, and we will be able to convince him that you are, in fact, the messenger he is expecting.\030If you wish to join the Deathstalkers, Lord Varimathras' elite guard, you will have to prove your worth.$B$BI will not lie to you, $n, this task could mean your death.$B$BI have some things that need attending to. I require the personal effects of Astor Hadren, a messenger who travels between Silverpine and the Undercity. I will leave the method of procurement to your discretion.$B$BIt will be better for you if you know less of the nature of this business. Succeed and I shall tell you more.\030Get Astor's Letter of Introduction and return it to Mennet Carkad in the Rogues' Quarter.\030Success to report?\030The Deathstalkers\0312,1,104,2,259,4,6467\0302,109,167,2,257,4,6467\0302,172,213,2,259,1,6467\0302,215,323,2,257,1,6467\0302,325,382,2,257,3,6467\0302,387,460,2,257,4,6467\0302,462,495,2,257,3,6467\0303,1,89,2,384,1,6467\0301,1,14,4,272,1,6467\0301,16,57,4,272,1,6467\0301,59,210,4,272,3,6467\0304,1,18,3,256,2,6467\0316497,2,4,Astor Hadren\0306467,2,8,Mennet Carkad\0312,0,0,8,Mennet Carkad\0302,0,0,8,Rogues' Quarter\0311885,19,1885,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301898,23,1898,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7231,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[189]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh excellent, excellent. That'll help a little, for the present...$B$B<He trails off, grumbling about profit margins and costs...>$B$BWhat? You're still here? Reward? Oh, right... of course, here, take this... it should be more than enough.\030Damn trolls! They've been killing off our agents in the jungle! I've already lost a good number of my best guards to skirmishes with them. The costs are piling up! How will I explain this to Baron Revilgaz?$B$BDecisive action... Think, Kebok... you weren't assigned to the post you have today for sitting around... I've got it! You... $n, is it? You'll help me, won't you? There's money to be had!$B$BHere's the deal... you bring me the ears of fifteen Bloodscalp Trolls, and I'll compensate you well.\030Acquire 15 Bloodscalp Ears and return them to Kebok in Booty Bay.\030You've had success I hope? All over the place, those trolls. Filthy devils.$B$BOh yes, that reminds me! Be sure to tell your friends, yes? We could use much assistance!\030Bloodscalp Ears\0312,1,12,2,257,1,737\0302,14,63,2,257,1,737\0302,65,138,2,261,1,737\0302,140,163,2,257,1,737\0302,165,206,2,257,2,737\0302,211,228,2,257,1,737\0302,230,244,2,257,1,737\0302,246,314,2,257,1,737\0302,316,327,2,257,1,737\0302,329,334,2,257,1,737\0302,347,372,2,257,2,737\0302,374,397,2,257,1,737\0302,402,419,2,257,1,737\0302,421,501,2,257,1,737\0303,1,65,2,384,1,737\0301,1,24,4,272,1,737\0301,26,66,4,272,1,737\0301,71,130,4,272,1,737\0301,135,139,4,272,2,737\0301,141,158,4,272,2,737\0301,160,166,4,272,2,737\0301,168,179,4,272,1,737\0301,181,209,4,272,1,737\0301,211,240,4,272,1,737\0304,1,26,3,258,2,737\0304,28,60,3,256,1,737\0304,62,75,3,256,1,737\0304,80,103,3,256,1,737\0304,105,138,3,256,2,737\0304,140,168,3,256,4,737\0312496,2,5,Baron Revilgaz\030737,2,7,Kebok\030737,2,15,Kebok\0312,33,1434,0,\0302,0,0,5,Baron Revilgaz\0302,0,0,15,Kebok\0302,0,0,15,Booty Bay\031209,23,209,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,1519,OBJECTIVE,15,15,",[1898]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, yes, I've been expecting you. I have no doubt our mutual acquaintances are pleased with the information that I have provided so far?$B$BI suppose there's no point in asking you, I doubt they would burden you with this knowledge. Why place so much trust in the messenger, hm?\030The letter of introduction should be enough to convince Andron that you are the messenger he's been waiting for. I've met Andron before, he doesn't quite have the mental capacity to be that suspicious.$B$BLord Varimathras suspects that Andron has been providing aid to some other group. He wishes to know what organization this is and requires proof of it.$B$BI want you to speak with Andron, and obtain this information. You'll find him at his shop near the Apothecarium.\030Speak with Andron Gant in the Undercity.\030Hello. Something I can do for you?\030The Deathstalkers\0312,1,112,2,257,1,6467\0302,114,201,2,257,1,6467\0302,206,286,2,257,1,6467\0302,288,356,2,259,1,6467\0302,361,421,2,259,1,6467\0302,423,472,2,257,1,6467\0303,1,40,2,384,1,6467\0301,1,33,4,272,1,6522\0301,35,136,4,272,2,6522\0301,141,232,4,272,4,6522\0301,234,278,4,272,2,6522\0304,1,6,3,256,1,6522\0304,8,34,3,256,2,6522\0312425,2,3,Varimathras\0306522,2,7,Andron Gant\0312,0,0,6,Apothecarium\0302,0,0,7,Undercity\0311886,19,1886,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301899,23,1899,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1899]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well, this is certainly more information than I suspected to get out of Andron. Give me a moment to peruse it, before I set you to your next task.\030You'll find the ledger with the information your employers seek on the bookshelf behind me. Deliver it with my regards, and tell them that I would prefer it if they sent you, if they find enough value that they should wish to continue our arrangement.\030Bring Andron's Ledger to Mennet Carkad in the Rogues' Quarter of Undercity.\030Success, $N?\030The Deathstalkers\0312,1,91,2,259,1,6522\0302,93,251,2,259,4,6522\0303,1,75,2,384,1,6522\0301,1,79,4,272,1,6467\0301,81,146,4,272,1,6467\0304,1,12,3,256,2,6467\0316467,2,3,Mennet Carkad\0312,0,0,3,Mennet Carkad\0302,0,0,3,Rogues' Quarter of Undercity\0311898,19,1898,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301978,23,1978,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7294,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[19]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Tharil'zun was a vicious, crafty orc. Well done - I'm sure he didn't go down easy. Here is your reward, $N.\030Blackrock Outrunners and Renegades are running ambushes between here and Stonewatch Keep.  The leader of the Outrunners is an orc named Tharil'zun--we want this orc.  Bring me the head of Tharil'zun!\030Bring Tharil'zun's Head to Marshal Marris in Redridge.\030Orc pressure from Blackrock is still tense. But have you at least rid us of Tharil'zun?\030Tharil'zun\0312,1,89,2,257,1,382\0302,92,165,2,259,1,382\0302,168,199,2,257,1,382\0303,1,54,2,384,1,382\0301,1,37,4,272,1,382\0301,39,82,4,272,1,382\0301,84,107,4,272,1,382\0304,1,43,3,256,1,382\0304,45,87,3,256,2,382\031486,2,3,Tharil'zun\030382,2,4,Marshal Marris\030486,4,5,Tharil'zun\030486,3,9,Tharil'zun\0312,44,1433,0,\0302,0,0,4,Marshal Marris\0302,0,0,4,Redridge\0303,0,0,8,Blackrock\03120,19,20,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,1260,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[190]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Off to a good start, $N!\030If you want to be a part of the hunt with this crack group under Hemet's leadership, you're going to need to prove yourself an able panther hunter.  We'll start you out easy -- don't you worry.  Let's see you kill 10 young panthers to start.$B$BTracking them down is only half the challenge...\030Sir S. J. Erlgadin of Nesingwary's Expedition wants you to kill 10 Young Panthers.\030A true panther hunter would be out in the fields, trying to stalk his prey. Show some commitment to your goal, $c, and get back out there.\030Panther Mastery\0312,1,147,2,259,4,718\0302,150,193,2,257,1,718\0302,196,241,2,257,1,718\0302,246,293,2,257,1,718\0303,1,6,2,384,1,718\0303,11,82,2,386,1,718\0301,1,24,4,272,1,718\0304,1,75,3,256,4,718\0304,77,138,3,256,1,718\031736,2,1,Panther\030736,3,8,Panther\0312,33,1434,0,\031583,19,583,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030191,23,191,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,683,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Young Panther",[191]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Perfectly executed, $N!\030Now you're ready to turn it up a notch.  If you want to prove yourself worthy of socializing with the likes of these big game hunters, you'll need to prove that you can kill 10 panthers.$B$BThose big boys are tougher.  They're not as easy as the young ones you were killing earlier.\030Sir S. J. Erlgadin of Nesingwary's Expedition wants you to kill 10 Panthers.\030\030Panther Mastery\0312,1,39,2,257,1,718\0302,42,186,2,259,4,718\0302,191,217,2,257,1,718\0302,220,282,2,257,1,718\0303,1,6,2,384,1,718\0303,11,76,2,386,1,718\0301,1,23,4,272,1,718\031\0312,33,1434,0,\031190,19,190,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030192,23,192,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,736,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Panther",[1918]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You find a nasty ball of water and decide to bring it to me? Who am I, the Earthen Ring or something?$B$BActually, that does give me an idea... perhaps you do need the Earthen Ring for this. I mean, if it helps clear up the situation at the lake for good, then I'm all for it.$B$BYou know who the Earthen Ring are, $N?\030The slain elemental has produced an intensely glowing globe of water.  The contents of the globe are, at best, disgusting.  It would be safe to assume that whatever has befouled the water of Mystral Lake is most likely present in the water of the globe.$B$BIt's not exactly common knowledge who might be interested in such a find; perhaps the person who originally sent you out to the lake, Mastok Wrilehiss at Splintertree Post, might have an idea.\030Bring the Befouled Water Globe to Mastok Wrilehiss at Splintertree Post, Ashenvale.\030Yeah, what do you need?\030The Befouled Element\0312,1,69,2,261,1,0\0302,72,122,2,257,1,0\0302,125,253,2,257,4,0\0302,258,449,2,257,4,0\0303,1,83,2,384,1,0\0301,1,60,4,272,2,12737\0301,62,101,4,272,2,12737\0301,106,143,4,272,1,12737\0301,145,190,4,274,4,12737\0301,192,276,4,272,4,12737\0301,281,318,4,272,2,12737\0304,1,23,3,258,2,12737\03112737,2,4,Mastok Wrilehiss\03012737,2,5,Mastok Wrilehiss\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,4,Splintertree Post\0302,0,0,5,Mastok Wrilehiss\0302,0,0,5,Splintertree Post\031824,23,824,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,16408,STARTER,?,10,",[1919]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031$N, I have a mission for you, here in the mage district. Listen closely, for there is no time to waste.\030Your knowledge of the craft grows, young $N.  Are you now ready to begin your true lessons?  Are you ready to take your place in the secret war we wage?$B$BIf so, then speak with Jennea Cannon, in the wizard's sanctum in the mage district of Stormwind.  She has a task for you which will open your first window into the invisible world.\030Speak with Jennea Cannon in Stormwind.\030\030Report to Jennea\0312,1,44,2,257,1,0\0302,47,91,2,257,2,0\0302,94,152,2,261,2,0\0302,157,252,2,257,4,0\0302,255,336,2,257,3,0\0303,1,38,2,384,1,0\0301,1,56,4,272,1,5497\0301,58,103,4,272,1,5497\0315497,2,4,Jennea Cannon\0305497,2,6,Jennea Cannon\0312,0,0,6,Stormwind\0311920,23,1920,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301920,24,1920,UNKNOWN\031",[192]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You've done well, $N!\030Now the hard part.  A true panther hunter can show skill by dropping Shadowmaw Panthers, the deadliest in Stranglethorn.  Prove to us that you can slay 10 of these beasts.$B$BIf you think they are hard to track, wait until you attempt to slay one....\030Sir S. J. Erlgadin of Nesingwary's Expedition wants you to kill 10 Shadowmaw Panthers.\030What are you doing here, $N! You should be crawling through the brush, trying to kill 10 Shadowmaw Panthers. I thought you fancied yourself a big game hunter?\030Panther Mastery\0312,1,18,2,257,1,718\0302,21,120,2,257,1,718\0302,123,171,2,257,1,718\0302,176,250,2,257,4,718\0303,1,6,2,384,1,718\0303,11,86,2,386,1,718\0301,1,21,4,272,1,718\0304,1,28,3,256,1,718\0304,30,108,3,256,1,718\0304,110,158,3,256,2,718\031736,2,2,Panther\0312,33,1434,0,\0302,0,0,2,Stranglethorn\031191,19,191,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030193,23,193,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,684,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Shadowmaw Panther",[1920]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very well done!  I will study these creatures and, with diligence and luck, determine how they slipped into our world.$B$BYour value to the society of mages grows, $N.\030A disturbance has been reported at the Blue Recluse tavern in the Mage Quarter.  Strange, invisible creatures now wander the tavern, and I fear a mana rift has formed there.$B$BI want you to investigate the tavern and capture those creatures.  Use the cantation of manifestation in the tavern to make the creatures visible, subdue them then use a containment coffer to capture them.  When you have enough, return to me with your filled coffers, your empty coffers and the cantation.\030Obtain a Cantation of Manifestation and a Chest of Containment coffers from behind Jennea Cannon.  Bring 3 Filled Containment Coffers to Jennea at the Wizard's Sanctum.\030Have you captured the creatures, $n?  They must be studied in order to determine the reason behind their arrival.\030Investigate the Blue Recluse\0312,1,79,2,257,1,5497\0302,82,173,2,257,1,5497\0302,178,242,2,259,1,5497\0302,245,382,2,257,1,5497\0302,385,482,2,257,1,5497\0303,1,97,2,384,1,5497\0303,100,168,2,384,1,5497\0301,1,15,4,272,1,5497\0301,18,118,4,272,3,5497\0301,123,167,4,272,1,5497\0304,1,36,3,256,2,5497\0304,39,113,3,258,1,5497\0315497,2,6,Jennea Cannon\0312,0,0,1,Blue Recluse\0302,0,0,1,Mage Quarter\0302,0,0,7,Jennea\0302,0,0,7,Wizard's Sanctum\0311921,23,1921,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7292,OBJECTIVE,3,15,\030ITEM,7247,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,7308,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1921]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes, these are great pieces of linen.  I can make a fine robe with them.  And after I weave the rift gems into it, we'll have a garment fit for a mage!\030You have served your fellow mages well, and now it is time to don your wizard's robe.  Wynne Larson can make your robe, but you must bring her the needed materials  $B$BThe robe will be made of linen which is easy to find, but you must also gain charged rift gems, and the only known location of the gems is in the Silver Stream Mine of Loch Modan, left in crates by the dwarven miners' league.$B$BGather the linen and the gems and bring them to Wynne Larson at the Larson Clothiers in the Mage District.\030Bring 10 Linen Cloth and the 6 Charged Rift Gems to Wynne Larson in Stormwind.\030Hello, $N.  Jennea told me you would come.  Do you have something for me?\030Gathering Materials\0312,1,85,2,257,1,5497\0302,88,165,2,257,1,5497\0302,170,394,2,257,3,5497\0302,399,504,2,257,1,5497\0303,1,78,2,384,1,5497\0301,1,37,4,272,1,1309\0301,40,72,4,272,1,1309\0301,75,151,4,272,1,1309\0304,1,10,3,256,1,1309\0304,13,42,3,256,4,1309\0304,45,73,3,256,2,1309\0311309,2,2,Wynne Larson\0301309,2,4,Wynne Larson\0301309,2,5,Wynne Larson\0312,0,0,3,Silver Stream Mine of Loch Modan\0302,0,0,4,Wynne Larson\0302,0,0,4,Larson Clothiers\0302,0,0,4,Mage District\0302,0,0,5,Wynne Larson\0302,0,0,5,Stormwind\0311920,19,1920,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301941,23,1941,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,2589,OBJECTIVE,10,15,\030ITEM,7249,OBJECTIVE,6,15,",[193]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031So the great Bhag'thera is dead! Cheers to you, $N. You are a mighty $C indeed!\030You've almost proven yourself to be a master hunter of panthers.  A panther by the name of Bhag'thera has been prowling the jungle.  So far he's eluded our party.  See if you can use your skills to kill the great Bhag'thera.$B$BBring me the Fang of Bhag'thera and you'll have earned my respect!\030Sir S. J. Erlgadin of Nesingwary's Expedition wants you to bring him the Fang of Bhag'thera.\030Bhag'thera can prove to be an elusive beast. How fares the hunt?\030Panther Mastery\0312,1,64,2,257,1,718\0302,67,131,2,257,1,718\0302,134,162,2,257,1,718\0302,165,224,2,257,4,718\0302,229,294,2,257,1,718\0303,1,6,2,384,1,718\0303,11,92,2,386,1,718\0301,1,32,4,272,1,718\0301,34,51,4,272,1,718\0301,53,79,4,272,1,718\0304,1,44,3,256,1,718\0304,46,64,3,256,2,718\031736,2,2,Panther\030728,2,2,Bhag'thera\030728,2,4,Bhag'thera\03014892,2,5,Fang\030728,2,5,Bhag'thera\03014892,2,7,Fang\030728,2,7,Bhag'thera\030728,4,8,Bhag'thera\030728,3,11,Bhag'thera\0312,33,1434,0,\031192,19,192,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3876,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1938]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I feared that Morganth had hidden the book elsewhere, or that he had found a way to open it and read its contents.$B$BIt is good to see that he did not, and that the seals we placed on Ur's Treatise on Shadow Magic still hold.\030Long ago, three mages studied in this tower until one fell to the dark arts.  He was urged to turn away from that evil magic, but he could not resist.  And so he was banished.$B$BThe fallen mage's new domain is the tower of Ilgalar in Redridge, and he took with him a powerful book--Ur's Treatise on Shadow Magic.$B$BWe, the mages of Stormwind, would have that book returned.  Enter the tower of Ilgalar, find the tome in his library, and bring it to me.\030Bring Ur's Treatise on Shadow Magic to High Sorcerer Andromath in Stormwind.\030Do you have the book, $N? Its secrets are not meant for the untrained, and plumbing its depths can lead to doom and ruin.\030Ur's Treatise on Shadow Magic\0312,1,76,2,321,1,5694\0302,79,150,2,257,4,5694\0302,153,175,2,257,1,5694\0302,180,313,2,257,1,5694\0302,318,375,2,257,4,5694\0302,378,454,2,257,1,5694\0303,1,76,2,384,1,5694\0301,1,114,4,272,1,5694\0301,119,226,4,272,1,5694\0304,1,25,3,256,2,5694\0304,27,121,3,256,1,5694\0314244,2,4,Shadow\0304244,2,7,Shadow\0305694,2,7,High Sorcerer Andromath\030397,4,8,Morganth\0304244,4,9,Shadow\0312,0,0,4,Redridge\0302,0,0,7,High Sorcerer Andromath\0302,0,0,7,Stormwind\0311940,23,1940,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7266,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1939]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Greetings, $N. I am pleased to see you, and hope you have time to listen to an old man's words...\030High Sorcerer Andromath wishes to speak with you, $N.  He is at the top of the wizard's sanctum, in the mage's district of Stormwind.$B$BIt would be wise to speak with him, for Andromath is one of the most powerful mages not locked away in Dalaran.  Council with him is high council indeed.\030Speak with High Sorcerer Andromath.\030\030High Sorcerer Andromath\0312,1,53,2,259,1,5497\0302,56,133,2,257,1,5497\0302,138,248,2,257,4,5497\0302,251,290,2,257,1,5497\0303,1,35,2,384,1,5497\0301,1,14,4,272,1,5694\0301,16,97,4,274,3,5694\0315694,2,1,High Sorcerer Andromath\0305694,2,5,High Sorcerer Andromath\0312,0,0,3,Dalaran\0311938,23,1938,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301938,24,1938,UNKNOWN\031",[194]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Nicely done, old chap!\030So you think your hunting skills are in tip-top shape?  I can put them to the test in a jiffy.  Head out into that jungle and kill 10 Stranglethorn Raptors.  We'll see just how much of a big game hunter you are.$B$BAnd no, I won't tell you where you can find them!  Locating the beasts is half the challenge.\030Hemet Nesingwary wants you to kill 10 Stranglethorn Raptors.\030I never met a hunter who got any kills by standing around the campfire. Were you planning on killing those Stranglethorn Raptors or were you hoping they would die of old age?\030Raptor Mastery\0312,1,54,2,257,2,715\0302,57,94,2,257,1,715\0302,97,156,2,257,1,715\0302,159,211,2,257,1,715\0302,216,264,2,257,1,715\0302,267,308,2,257,1,715\0303,1,60,2,386,1,715\0301,1,22,4,272,1,715\0304,1,71,3,256,1,715\0304,73,174,3,256,4,715\031715,2,7,Hemet Nesingwary\0312,33,1434,0,\031583,19,583,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030195,23,195,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,685,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Stranglethorn Raptor",[1940]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Nice specimens, these. I'll get right to work!\030Your service has been unwavering, $N.  I think, perhaps, it is time you had a finer garment, one more suiting your station as an adept mage.  If you gather the needed materials, then we will arrange the robe made.$B$BYou must enter Duskwood and hunt carrion recluse spiders.  Extract their silk, but only the finest, most pristine silk will do.  When you have enough, take it to Wynne Larson, here in the mage district at the Larson Clothiers.  She will craft your robe.\030Bring 8 Pristine Spider Silk to Wynne Larson in Stormwind.\030Ah, yes. The mages of the Wizard's Sanctum said you'd speak with me. Do you have the required silk?\030Pristine Spider Silk\0312,1,37,2,257,1,5694\0302,40,140,2,257,4,5694\0302,143,213,2,257,4,5694\0302,218,274,2,257,1,5694\0302,277,344,2,257,3,5694\0302,347,443,2,257,1,5694\0302,446,470,2,257,3,5694\0303,1,58,2,384,1,5694\0301,1,22,4,272,1,1309\0301,24,46,4,272,1,1309\0304,1,8,3,256,1,1309\0304,10,68,3,256,1,1309\0304,70,99,3,256,2,1309\031949,2,4,Carrion Recluse\0301309,2,6,Wynne Larson\03014881,2,8,Spider\0301309,2,8,Wynne Larson\0312,0,0,6,Wynne Larson\0302,0,0,6,Larson Clothiers\0302,0,0,8,Wynne Larson\0302,0,0,8,Stormwind\0311938,19,1938,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301942,23,1942,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7267,OBJECTIVE,8,15,",[1941]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Here is your robe.  It's one of my best made yet!  Wear it with pride, and when people ask... tell them you got it at the Larson Clothiers!\030\030\030\030Manaweave Robe\0311,1,18,4,272,1,1309\0301,21,49,4,272,1,1309\0301,52,93,4,272,1,1309\0301,95,139,4,272,1,1309\031\0314,0,0,4,Larson Clothiers\0311921,19,1921,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1942]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Your garment is ready!  And that silk you gathered was so nice... you don't mind if I made it a little short so that I'd have some silk left over for me, do you?$B$BI'm only joking.  It'll fit you great, and will be perfect for both adventure and formal dining.  Enjoy!\030\030\030\030Astral Knot Garment\0311,1,22,4,272,1,1309\0301,25,65,4,272,1,1309\0301,67,161,4,274,4,1309\0301,166,181,4,272,1,1309\0301,184,261,4,272,3,1309\0301,264,269,4,272,1,1309\031\031\0311940,19,1940,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1943]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Good, you have come.  My task is not an easy one, but vital to the society of mages.  If you aid me, I am sure you will find it worthwhile.\030The troll mage Deino has need of your assistance, $N.  She resides in Orgrimmar, in the Darkbriar Lodge.\030Speak with Deino.\030\030Speak with Deino\0312,1,53,2,259,1,4568\0302,56,104,2,257,1,4568\0303,1,17,2,384,1,4568\0301,1,20,4,272,1,5885\0301,23,84,4,272,1,5885\0301,87,139,4,272,4,5885\0315885,2,1,Deino\0305885,2,3,Deino\0312,0,0,2,Orgrimmar\0302,0,0,2,Darkbriar Lodge\0311944,23,1944,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301944,24,1944,UNKNOWN\031",[1944]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, very good. I trust the satyrs of Xavian gave you little trouble?$B$BThank you, $N. I will study this sample of Xavian water immediately.\030The fabled city of Xavian lies nestled deep within eastern Ashenvale, and tales of its ancient knowledge are well known among the learned.  It is said that the waters of Xavian hold vast magical powers.$B$BI would have a sample of those waters, from their source.$B$BTake this flask and go to Xavian.  Gather water from the bottom of its highest waterfall, and return to me.  And use care as you move through that ancient city--satyrs now hold the ruins and do not like mages prying into their affairs.\030Bring the Xavian Water Sample to Deino in Orgrimmar.\030I am pleased you have returned with your skin intact, $N. Do you have the water sample? I am eager to study its properties.\030Waters of Xavian\0312,1,138,2,321,1,5885\0302,141,202,2,257,1,5885\0302,207,263,2,257,4,5885\0302,268,300,2,257,1,5885\0302,303,374,2,257,1,5885\0302,377,502,2,321,1,5885\0303,1,52,2,384,1,5885\0301,1,14,4,272,1,5885\0301,16,68,4,272,2,5885\0301,73,86,4,272,1,5885\0301,88,140,4,272,3,5885\0304,1,57,3,256,1,5885\0304,59,87,3,256,2,5885\0304,89,123,3,256,1,5885\0315885,2,7,Deino\0312,0,0,4,Xavian\0302,0,0,7,Deino\0302,0,0,7,Orgrimmar\0311945,23,1945,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7268,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1945]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, this hair will weave into a fine robe, $N. It is a pity the laughing sisters had to die to part with it, though I do doubt they would ever give it willingly.$B$BA pity, but only a small one.\030For your services, I have arranged for the creation of your new robes, provided you can gather the needed materials...$B$BFor these robes, you must return to Ashenvale for the locks of hair from laughing sisters--dryads who gather near the Raynewood Retreat.$B$BWhen you have their hair, bring it to Kil'hala, a troll tailor at the Crossroads in the Barrens.  He will be expecting you, and will fashion your robes.\030Bring 12 Laughing Sister's Hairs to Kil'hala at the Crossroads.\030Greetings, $N. Deino said you would come, and would bring the laughing sisters' hair. Do you have it?\030Laughing Sisters\0312,1,118,2,257,1,5885\0302,123,258,2,257,1,5885\0302,263,358,2,257,1,5885\0302,361,414,2,257,3,5885\0303,1,63,2,384,1,5885\0301,1,46,4,272,3,3484\0301,48,161,4,272,4,3484\0301,166,194,4,272,1,3484\0304,1,14,3,256,1,3484\0304,16,85,3,256,4,3484\0304,87,101,3,256,2,3484\0313484,2,3,Kil'hala\0304054,2,5,Laughing Sister\0303484,2,5,Kil'hala\0305885,3,10,Deino\0312,0,0,2,Ashenvale\0302,0,0,2,Raynewood Retreat\0302,0,0,3,Kil'hala\0302,0,0,3,Crossroads\0302,0,0,3,Barrens\0302,0,0,5,Kil'hala\0302,0,0,5,Crossroads\0311944,19,1944,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301946,23,1946,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7270,OBJECTIVE,12,15,",[1946]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Here is your nether-lace, $n.  It is both comfortable and durable, and holds the magic of the laughing sisters' hair.$B$BEnjoy, and if you find it amenable, please mention so to Deino.  She is a mage on whose good side I wish to stay...\030\030\030\030Nether-lace Garment\0311,1,29,4,272,1,3484\0301,32,117,4,272,1,3484\0301,122,184,4,272,4,3484\0301,187,236,4,274,3,3484\0315885,4,3,Deino\0314,0,0,3,Deino\0311945,19,1945,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1947]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Quiet! I'm in a delicate juncture and mustn't be disturbed!$B$BOne moment...\030Now it is time for you to earn your mage's wand.  To begin this quest, speak with the human hermit Tabetha in Dustwallow Marsh.  You will find her shack deep in the marsh, west of Theramore.$B$BSpeak with her, for her knowledge is vast.  You will find Tabetha's cottage west of Theramore, and just north of the Stonemaul Ruins.\030Speak with Tabetha.\030\030Journey to the Marsh\0312,1,48,2,257,1,0\0302,51,127,2,257,1,0\0302,130,190,2,257,3,0\0302,195,236,2,257,1,0\0302,239,327,2,321,3,0\0303,1,19,2,384,1,0\0301,1,6,4,272,1,6546\0301,8,59,4,272,1,6546\0301,64,76,4,272,1,6546\0316546,2,2,Tabetha\0306546,2,6,Tabetha\0312,0,0,2,Dustwallow Marsh\0302,0,0,3,Theramore\0302,0,0,5,Theramore\0302,0,0,5,Stonemaul Ruins\0311949,23,1949,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1948]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Aha! You got the jade and made the bramble! Well done!$B$BIs that smoke I see rising from your ears? You might have gotten too close when the lightning struck the totem sticks, but don't worry. Being hit by lightning is good luck!\030The building of a mage's wand is not easy.  Rare substances are required, and a vessel must be made that can store great quantities of magical energy.  You must gather these things and bring them to me.$B$BI have written onto this parchment that which you need, and instructions on how to get it.  Bring me exactly what is on this list, and follow my written directions to the letter, for if you do not then when we make your wand things might go... badly.\030Bring 1 Jade and the Bolt Charged Bramble to Tabetha in Dustwallow Marsh.\030Hello, $N. Do you have the items I require?\030Items of Power\0312,1,42,2,257,1,6546\0302,45,150,2,257,1,6546\0302,153,202,2,257,1,6546\0302,207,296,2,259,1,6546\0302,299,449,2,257,4,6546\0302,451,456,2,257,1,6546\0303,1,73,2,384,1,6546\0301,1,4,4,272,1,6546\0301,6,43,4,272,1,6546\0301,45,54,4,272,1,6546\0301,59,100,4,272,2,6546\0301,102,193,4,272,4,6546\0301,195,230,4,272,1,6546\0304,1,10,3,256,1,6546\0304,12,43,3,256,2,6546\0311063,2,7,Jade\0306546,2,7,Tabetha\0301063,4,9,Jade\0312,0,0,7,Tabetha\0302,0,0,7,Dustwallow Marsh\031\031ITEM,1529,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,7272,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1949]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031What?  Speak up!  These old ears aren't as sharp as they used to be.$B$BWell, I hope you're here with a fresh mug of ale or some hot tips on the next race!  If not, then you best keep walking... because I have a polymorph wand with your name on it!\030To make your wand, there are key passages in a certain book that I must read.  The book is called Rituals of Power, written by the Magus Tirth.$B$BI do not have a copy of his book, and none of the world's great libraries possess it.  So you must speak with Tirth and gain it from him.$B$BGood luck.  Tirth used to be a great mage and scholar, but now he spends his time at the gnome and goblin races in the Shimmering Flats, drinking and gambling.\030Speak with Magus Tirth in the Shimmering Flats.\030\030Hidden Secrets\0312,1,77,2,257,1,6546\0302,80,143,2,257,1,6546\0302,148,232,2,257,1,6546\0302,235,284,2,257,1,6546\0302,289,298,2,257,1,6546\0302,301,447,2,321,1,6546\0303,1,47,2,384,1,6546\0301,1,5,4,272,2,6548\0301,8,16,4,272,1,6548\0301,19,68,4,336,1,6548\0301,73,155,4,274,3,6548\0301,158,194,4,272,4,6548\0301,196,248,4,274,1,6548\0316548,2,2,Magus Tirth\0306548,2,7,Magus Tirth\0312,0,0,6,Shimmering Flats\0302,0,0,7,Shimmering Flats\0311947,19,1947,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301950,23,1950,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[195]="PARTIAL\031conflict,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Now that's how you get a trophy or two over the ol' hearth!  Nice killing, $N!\030Now let's step up the challenge and see if you're up to it.  Venture into the jungle and bag yourself 10 of those bloody Lashtail Raptors.  Let's see what you've got!\030Hemet Nesingwary wants you to kill 10 Lashtail Raptors.\030A true hunter sets his focus on his prey. You, my friend, seem more concerned with chit-chatting around the campfire. Now get out there and kill 10 Lashtails before I go and rid the entire bloody jungle of them in one hunt.\030Raptor Mastery\0312,1,59,2,257,4,715\0302,62,138,2,257,1,715\0302,141,166,2,257,1,715\0303,1,55,2,386,1,715\0301,1,59,4,304,1,715\0301,62,78,4,272,1,715\0304,1,41,3,256,1,715\0304,43,117,3,256,4,715\0304,119,223,3,256,1,715\031715,2,4,Hemet Nesingwary\0312,33,1434,0,\031194,19,194,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030196,23,196,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,686,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Lashtail Raptor",[1950]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, now I remember...$B$BI had forgotten about that little curse I put on Johnson.  I can't remember why I did it but I'm sure it served him right, the little ingrate!\030I can help you with the book, but first you have to help me!$B$BThe tome you seek is in my magically locked strongbox.  To open it a special phrase must be uttered, and I can't remember the phrase!  Normally my assistant helps me remember these things but he's nowhere to be found.$B$BIf you want my book, then find my apprentice!  Ask around the race track--if you're lucky then someone has seen him.  Either drag him back here, or at least get my magic phrase from him so we can open my box!\030Find the phrase to Tirth's strongbox, then return to Tirth.\030Secret phrase found\030What are you waiting for? I need my magic phrase!\030Get the Scoop\0312,1,60,2,257,1,6548\0302,65,118,2,259,1,6548\0302,121,197,2,257,1,6548\0302,200,281,2,257,1,6548\0302,286,330,2,259,4,6548\0302,333,401,2,257,4,6548\0302,404,493,2,257,1,6548\0303,1,59,2,384,1,6548\0301,1,21,4,272,1,6548\0301,26,82,4,276,1,6548\0301,85,167,4,272,1,6548\0305,1,25,3,256,2,6548\0305,27,49,3,258,1,6548\0304,1,19,3,384,1,6548\031\0312,0,0,8,Tirth's\0302,0,0,8,Tirth\0311949,19,1949,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301951,23,1951,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1951]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031That's it!  It's just what I need to prepare for the ritual to create your wand!  I hope it wasn't too much trouble to find...\030Hm... now that I think about it, I don't have my book!  You see, I had some gambling debts and to pay them off I sold the last copy of Rituals of Power to a member of the clergy....$B$BA member of the Scarlet Brotherhood.  He must have taken it to their library in the Scarlet Monastery in Tirisfal Glades!$B$BIf you want that book, then you'll have to go to the monastery to find it.  And sorry about all the trouble.  I'm not myself these days...\030Bring the book Rituals of Power to Tabetha in Dustwallow Marsh.\030Greetings, $N.  Did you find the book, Rituals of Power?\030Rituals of Power\0312,7,54,2,257,1,6548\0302,57,181,2,257,1,6548\0302,186,221,2,257,1,6548\0302,224,306,2,257,1,6548\0302,311,384,2,259,4,6548\0302,387,418,2,257,1,6548\0302,421,448,2,257,1,6548\0303,1,63,2,384,1,6548\0301,1,10,4,272,1,6546\0301,13,80,4,274,1,6546\0301,83,126,4,274,3,6546\0304,1,14,3,256,1,6546\0304,17,56,3,256,2,6546\0316546,2,8,Tabetha\0312,0,0,4,Scarlet Monastery\0302,0,0,4,Tirisfal Glades\0302,0,0,8,Tabetha\0302,0,0,8,Dustwallow Marsh\0311950,19,1950,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301952,23,1952,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7274,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1952]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Here are the wands I made.  Take your pick!\030I'll go make the wands now.\030Speak with Tabetha after her ritual.\030\030Mage's Wand\0312,1,27,2,257,1,6546\0303,1,36,2,384,1,6546\0301,1,26,4,272,1,6546\0301,29,43,4,272,1,6546\0316546,2,2,Tabetha\031\0311951,19,1951,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1953]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, yes.  You are here for an orb or a staff, $N?  Very well.  I will aid you in its construction.$B$BBut be forewarned--the process is a perilous one and could mean your death.$B$BOr my death.  Definitely someone's death... $B$BBut let's hope it's someone else's death, eh?\030It is time, $N, for you to speak with Tabetha... the hermit of Dustwallow Marsh.  She will instruct you on the creation of a powerful mage's implement.$B$BTabetha's shack lies deep in Dustwallow Marsh, west of Theramore.\030Speak with Tabetha.\030\030Return to the Marsh\0312,1,48,2,257,1,0\0302,50,80,2,257,1,0\0302,83,151,2,257,3,0\0302,156,220,2,257,1,0\0303,1,19,2,384,1,0\0301,1,8,4,272,1,6546\0301,11,49,4,272,2,6546\0301,52,61,4,272,1,6546\0301,64,98,4,272,3,6546\0301,103,177,4,272,4,6546\0301,182,193,4,272,1,6546\0301,196,224,4,272,1,6546\0301,230,274,4,272,2,6546\0316546,2,1,Tabetha\0306546,2,5,Tabetha\0312,0,0,4,Dustwallow Marsh\0302,0,0,4,Theramore\0311954,23,1954,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1954]="PARTIAL\031loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh, that's a nice one!  No, I don't mean it's \"nice\" like cool juice is nice on a hot day.$B$BIn fact, it's very NOT nice now that I think about it.  Not the juice.  The orb!$B$BFocus, $N!  We'll need you focused if we're ever to finish our task!\030The first step is to acquire an orb with power.  The warlocks of the Burning Blade have nice, high quality orbs... it's too bad they've bound demons into them!  But we can fix that, yes we can.$B$BGo to Desolace and snatch an infernal orb from a Burning Blade summoner.  You'll find summoners at the Mannoroc Coven.$B$BWhen you have the orb, return to me.\030Bring an Infernal Orb to Tabetha in Dustwallow Marsh.\030Do you have an infernal orb, $N?\030The Infernal Orb\0312,1,47,2,257,1,6546\0302,50,114,2,257,1,6546\0302,116,159,2,261,1,6546\0302,162,193,2,257,1,6546\0302,198,269,2,257,1,6546\0302,272,315,2,257,1,6546\0302,320,355,2,257,1,6546\0303,1,53,2,384,1,6546\0301,1,22,4,272,1,6546\0301,25,90,4,272,1,6546\0301,95,148,4,304,1,6546\0301,151,164,4,272,1,6546\0301,167,174,4,272,1,6546\0301,179,188,4,272,1,6546\0301,191,246,4,274,4,6546\0304,1,32,3,256,2,6546\03189,2,5,Infernal\0304668,2,5,Burning Blade Summoner\03089,2,8,Infernal\0306546,2,8,Tabetha\03089,3,16,Infernal\0312,0,0,5,Desolace\0302,0,0,6,Mannoroc Coven\0302,0,0,8,Tabetha\0302,0,0,8,Dustwallow Marsh\0311953,19,1953,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301955,23,1955,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7291,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1955]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Nicely done, $N! You gave that demon a lesson he won't soon forget.$B$BHe'll think twice before he sticks his ugly head back in this world, looking for the stupid mortal who beat him. Probably with friends this time. Big, scaly friends who'd want nothing more than to tear you into little $R pieces.$B$BI didn't scare you, did I...$N?\030Now that we have a summoner's orb, we must exorcise the demon within it.  I can do that.  That's the easy part.$B$BYou're the one who has the hard job.  You're the one who has to kill the demon once it's out.$B$BAnd you'll have to be quick.  If you take too long then he'll jump back in the orb and we'll have to start over!$B$BSo get yourself ready.  Prepare your strongest spells and keep your potions handy, and go get a friend if you have one.  Because this isn't going to be pretty.\030Kill the Demon of the Orb, then speak with Tabetha.\030You'll have to kill that demon to remove its taint from the orb, $N.\030The Exorcism\0312,1,72,2,257,1,6546\0302,75,88,2,257,1,6546\0302,91,111,2,257,1,6546\0302,116,151,2,257,1,6546\0302,154,208,2,257,1,6546\0302,213,240,2,257,1,6546\0302,243,324,2,257,4,6546\0302,329,350,2,257,1,6546\0302,353,447,2,257,4,6546\0302,450,487,2,259,3,6546\0303,1,51,2,384,1,6546\0301,1,16,4,272,1,6546\0301,18,67,4,272,1,6546\0301,72,183,4,280,1,6546\0301,185,216,4,272,1,6546\0301,218,299,4,272,1,6546\0301,304,334,4,272,2,6546\0304,1,68,3,256,1,6546\0316549,2,11,Demon of the Orb\0306546,2,11,Tabetha\031\0311954,19,1954,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301956,23,1956,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,6549,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Demon of the Orb",[1956]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You did it?  Well done!$B$BI was chatting with some of my colleagues and when your name came up they said, \"You know that $N sure works well under stress!\"$B$BBut when I told them I sent you to Uldaman against the obsidian sentinel, they said I was crazy!  They said, \"Tabetha, you're crazy!  There's no way $N could take on that sentinel!\"$B$BAnd I said, \"We'll see\", and then they said \"Yeah, we'll see...\"$B$BWell we sure showed them, didn't we!\030Now that the demon has been removed, we must gain a power source.  Unfortunately, the best power sources are usually the oldest and the hardest to get.  It's neat how fate likes to take a bite out of you sometimes, isn't it?$B$BSo you're going to need to go to Uldaman and defeat the obsidian sentinel there.  He's big, he's tough, and his power source packs a punch!$B$BI wish you the best of luck, $N.  And if you don't get lucky then, well... it was nice knowing you.\030Retrieve an Obsidian Power Source and bring it to Tabetha in Dustwallow Marsh.\030Have you been to Uldaman, $N?  Did you defeat the obsidian sentinel?\030Power in Uldaman\0312,1,65,2,257,1,6546\0302,68,151,2,257,1,6546\0302,154,224,2,257,2,6546\0302,229,308,2,259,3,6546\0302,311,367,2,257,1,6546\0302,372,403,2,259,3,6546\0302,406,445,2,257,4,6546\0302,447,470,2,257,1,6546\0303,1,78,2,384,1,6546\0301,1,11,4,272,2,6546\0301,14,23,4,272,1,6546\0301,28,155,4,272,1,6546\0301,160,255,4,272,1,6546\0301,258,291,4,272,1,6546\0301,294,340,4,272,4,6546\0301,345,408,4,272,1,6546\0301,413,448,4,272,1,6546\0304,1,29,3,256,2,6546\0304,32,68,3,256,2,6546\0317023,2,4,Obsidian Sentinel\0306546,2,9,Tabetha\0307023,4,13,Obsidian Sentinel\0306546,4,14,Tabetha\0307023,3,19,Obsidian Sentinel\0312,0,0,4,Uldaman\0302,0,0,9,Tabetha\0302,0,0,9,Dustwallow Marsh\0304,0,0,13,Uldaman\0303,0,0,18,Uldaman\0311955,19,1955,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301957,23,1957,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,8053,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1957]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You did it!  I never doubted you for a second!  Ok, maybe for just a second, or two... but basically I didn't have much doubt.$B$BHonest.\030We are almost finished, but this last step is the most perilous, $N.$B$BI have the empty summoner's orb and am ready to empower it.  We will do this by harnessing the energy of a mana rift.  I'll cast a spell that will temporarily open a rift, from which creatures, mana surges, will pour out.  You must defeat the mana surges and their power will be released, which I will then collect.$B$BKill enough mana surges before the rift closes and I will place all their collected energy in your orb.\030Kill 12 Mana Surges in the allowed time limit.\030You have not killed the required amount of mana surges, $N.\030Mana Surges\0312,1,68,2,257,1,6546\0302,73,131,2,257,1,6546\0302,134,189,2,257,3,6546\0302,192,293,2,257,3,6546\0302,296,387,2,257,3,6546\0302,392,494,2,257,3,6546\0303,1,46,2,384,1,6546\0301,1,11,4,272,1,6546\0301,14,46,4,272,1,6546\0301,49,86,4,272,4,6546\0301,88,126,4,272,1,6546\0301,131,137,4,272,1,6546\0304,1,59,3,256,1,6546\031\031\0311956,19,1956,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301958,23,1958,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,6550,OBJECTIVE,12,13,Mana Surge",[1958]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You should be proud of yourself, $N.  Many mages have fallen to the creatures you faced.$B$BThe Celestial Orb is ready.  Or if you'd like I can mount it atop a staff.  It's up to you.  I'd prefer the orb, but who am I to judge?\030\030\030\030Celestial Power\0311,1,36,4,272,1,6546\0301,39,88,4,272,1,6546\0301,93,119,4,272,1,6546\0301,122,166,4,272,4,6546\0301,169,183,4,272,1,6546\0301,186,227,4,272,2,6546\031\031\0311957,19,1957,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1959]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It is true.  A magical disturbance has been detected in our city.  We are not yet sure of its origin, or whether it is malign or benign.  We must first gather more information...$B$BAnd that, $N, brings us to your task.\030The mages of the Undercity have noted a magical disturbance within the city, and have sent word for mages of the Horde to investigate.$B$BAnastasia Hartwell can tell you more.  Speak with her in the Magic Quarter in the Undercity.\030Speak with Anastasia Hartwell.\030\030Report to Anastasia\0312,1,134,2,257,1,7311\0302,139,175,2,257,1,7311\0302,178,230,2,257,1,7311\0303,1,30,2,384,1,7311\0301,1,11,4,272,1,4568\0301,14,65,4,272,1,4568\0301,68,136,4,272,1,4568\0301,139,178,4,272,1,4568\0301,183,219,4,272,1,4568\0314568,2,2,Anastasia Hartwell\0304568,2,4,Anastasia Hartwell\0312,0,0,3,Magic Quarter\0302,0,0,3,Undercity\0311960,23,1960,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301960,24,1960,UNKNOWN\031",[196]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ho ho!! We have ourselves a true raptor slayer! Nicely done, old chap!\030Let's see how you handle this next challenge.  There is a cagey breed of raptor out there.  We call them Jungle Stalkers.  They are far more difficult to track down and kill than the other breeds you've been trying your luck at.  Kill 10 Jungle Stalkers and I'll tip you off to the best hunting yet.\030Hemet Nesingwary wants you to kill 10 Jungle Stalkers.\030Bah! What are you doing standing around, $N! A true big game hunter never gives up once his prey is in his sights. Those Jungle Stalkers aren't going to come running up to this campfire and throw themselves in it. Silly bloke.\030Raptor Mastery\0312,1,45,2,257,1,715\0302,48,90,2,257,1,715\0302,93,121,2,257,1,715\0302,124,228,2,257,1,715\0302,231,299,2,257,1,715\0303,1,54,2,386,1,715\0301,9,47,4,272,1,715\0301,49,70,4,272,1,715\0304,1,4,3,256,1,715\0304,6,44,3,256,1,715\0304,46,114,3,256,1,715\0304,116,213,3,256,3,715\0304,215,226,3,256,1,715\031107,2,2,Raptor\030715,2,6,Hemet Nesingwary\030107,4,7,Raptor\0312,33,1434,0,\031195,19,195,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030197,23,197,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,687,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Jungle Stalker",[1960]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very good, $N.  The creatures within these containment coffers will be studied by our finest minds, and the reason behind their presence in the Undercity will be determined.$B$BIf their appearance is caused by a rift in the natural flow of magic, then we must determine if the rift was random.  If it was not random, but instead an attack by some magical force, then we must prepare for future, more serious disturbances.\030Algernon's alchemist shop in the Apothecarium is the locus of a strange disturbance.  Invisible creatures, made solely of magic, wander the shop--there must be a reason, and we must find it!$B$BInvestigate the disturbance and capture those creatures.  Take a chest of coffers and a scroll from behind me.  Use the scroll at the shop to make the creatures visible, subdue them with your spells, then throw down a coffer to capture them.  Return with the filled coffers, the empty coffers and the cantation.\030Obtain a Cantation of Manifestation and a Chest of Containment Coffers from behind Anastasia Hartwell.  Bring 3 Filled Containment Coffers, the Chest of Containment Coffers and the Cantation of Manifestation to Anastasia in the Undercity.\030Have you investigated the disturbance, $N?  Have you captured the creatures?\030Investigate the Alchemist Shop\0312,1,84,2,257,1,4568\0302,87,190,2,257,1,4568\0302,195,250,2,257,1,4568\0302,253,304,2,257,1,4568\0302,307,435,2,257,1,4568\0302,438,505,2,257,1,4568\0303,1,102,2,384,1,4568\0303,105,238,2,384,1,4568\0301,1,14,4,272,1,4568\0301,17,173,4,272,3,4568\0301,178,293,4,272,4,4568\0301,296,421,4,276,4,4568\0304,1,42,3,256,2,4568\0304,45,76,3,256,2,4568\0314568,2,7,Anastasia Hartwell\0312,0,0,1,Apothecarium\0302,0,0,8,Anastasia\0302,0,0,8,Undercity\0304,0,0,10,Undercity\0311961,23,1961,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7292,OBJECTIVE,3,15,\030ITEM,7247,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,7308,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1961]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is very good material, and although I lack the talent to gauge the quality of these mana gems, we'll soon know if they possess the power needed to create spellfire robes...\030It is time for you to don your first mage's robes, $N.  They are a sign of your station, and a testament to your worth.$B$BTo gain the robes, you must gather the mana gems from the Dalaran mages of Silverpine.  Their beliefs are similar to ours and so killing them is somewhat distasteful, but if they lack the strength to resist us, then they do not deserve their lives.$B$BBring the gems and a supply of linen to Josef Gregorian at the Magic Quarter's tailor shop.\030Bring 10 Linen Cloth and 6 Dalaran Mana Gems to Josef Gregorian.\030Anastasia said you would come to me, and I am prepared to fashion your robes.  Do you have the gems and the linen?\030Gathering Materials\0312,1,54,2,257,1,4568\0302,57,119,2,257,1,4568\0302,124,209,2,257,1,4568\0302,212,371,2,257,4,4568\0302,376,466,2,257,1,4568\0303,1,64,2,384,1,4568\0301,1,177,4,272,4,4576\0304,1,77,3,256,4,4576\0304,80,114,3,256,2,4576\0314576,2,5,Josef Gregorian\0304576,2,6,Josef Gregorian\0312,0,0,3,Dalaran\0302,0,0,5,Josef Gregorian\0302,0,0,5,Magic Quarter's\0302,0,0,6,Josef Gregorian\0311960,19,1960,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301962,23,1962,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,2589,OBJECTIVE,10,15,\030ITEM,7293,OBJECTIVE,6,15,",[1962]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Here are your robes, $N.  Wear them well.\030\030\030\030Spellfire Robes\0311,1,24,4,272,1,4576\0301,27,41,4,272,1,4576\031\031\0311961,19,1961,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[1963]="PARTIAL\031loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hm, while I am glad to hear that Tazan is no longer with us, a locked satchel does us no good. We need the information kept within.$B$BThis should prove a worthy second challenge for one who wishes to join the Shattered Hand.\030The Warchief is too subtle in his methods. He is cautious to unleash the might of the Horde. Once we were stronger, mighty conquerors all. That pride we must regain, and the Shattered Hand will do so.$B$BWe build strength from the shadows and strike at the exposed, secretly laying our enemies low. A task you must complete for me, to prove your worth.$B$BThe troll Tazan trades with the pirates near Ratchet. He has information I must have. Kill him and bring me his satchel.\030Kill Tazan and bring his Satchel to Therzok in the Cleft of Shadow in Orgrimmar.\030It is a fool who believes a charge with axe drawn is more dangerous than a knife in the dark.\030The Shattered Hand\0312,1,42,2,257,1,6446\0302,44,92,2,257,4,6446\0302,94,138,2,257,1,6446\0302,140,200,2,257,3,6446\0302,205,298,2,261,1,6446\0302,300,352,2,257,1,6446\0302,357,409,2,257,1,6446\0302,411,441,2,257,1,6446\0302,443,476,2,257,1,6446\0303,1,80,2,384,1,6446\0301,1,94,4,304,1,6446\0301,96,131,4,274,1,6446\0301,136,225,4,274,1,6446\0304,1,93,3,256,1,6446\0316494,2,7,Tazan\0306494,2,10,Tazan\0306446,2,10,Therzok\0304244,2,10,Shadow\0306494,4,11,Tazan\0312,0,0,7,Ratchet\0302,0,0,10,Therzok\0302,0,0,10,Cleft of Shadow\0302,0,0,10,Orgrimmar\0311859,19,1859,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301858,23,1858,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7209,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[197]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Master $N, the raptor slayer!$B$BHas a nice ring to it, eh?\030Because you proved yourself to be such a go-getter in the jungle, let me tell you about a ferocious raptor that even I have failed to kill.  Ajeck here calls this wily raptor Tethis.$B$BIf you want to prove yourself a true master, kill Tethis and bring me his talon.  It would be a feat that no other big game hunter has accomplished.\030Hemet Nesingwary wants you to kill Tethis, an elusive, dangerous raptor in Stranglethorn.\030How goes the hunt for Tethis? Tracked her all the way back to camp, did you?\030Raptor Mastery\0312,1,139,2,259,1,715\0302,142,182,2,257,1,715\0302,187,266,2,259,4,715\0302,269,334,2,257,4,715\0303,1,89,2,386,1,715\0301,1,29,4,272,1,715\0301,34,59,4,272,2,715\0304,1,29,3,256,2,715\0304,31,76,3,256,2,715\031107,2,1,Raptor\030107,2,2,Raptor\030730,2,2,Tethis\030730,2,3,Tethis\030715,2,5,Hemet Nesingwary\030730,2,5,Tethis\030107,2,5,Raptor\030107,4,6,Raptor\030730,3,8,Tethis\0312,33,1434,0,\0302,0,0,5,Stranglethorn\031196,19,196,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3877,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1978]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hmm, this is interesting. The Deathstalkers have performed their duties admirably in ferreting this out.$B$BFrom what I understand, you also deserve commendation for your performance. I hope that this will become routine for you, $N, my Deathstalkers always have use of a good man.\030The Syndicate? I would never have suspected. It seems the lords of Alterac have fallen far in the years since their betrayal.$B$BLord Varimathras will be pleased to learn of this, and as you were so instrumental in this discovery, it would be fitting if you were the one to deliver it to him.$B$BAh, and how could I forget?$B$BWelcome to the Deathstalkers.\030Deliver Andron's Ledger to Varimathras in the Hall of the Dark Lady in the Undercity.\030Yes?\030The Deathstalkers\0312,1,14,2,257,2,6467\0302,16,44,2,257,4,6467\0302,46,125,2,257,4,6467\0302,130,292,2,257,4,6467\0302,297,323,2,257,4,6467\0302,328,356,2,257,1,6467\0303,1,85,2,384,1,6467\0301,1,25,4,272,1,2425\0301,27,104,4,272,1,2425\0301,109,183,4,272,1,2425\0301,185,281,4,274,3,2425\0304,1,4,3,256,2,2425\0312425,2,4,Varimathras\0302425,2,7,Varimathras\03015065,2,7,Lady\0312,0,0,6,Deathstalkers\0302,0,0,7,Varimathras\0302,0,0,7,Hall of the Dark Lady\0302,0,0,7,Undercity\0311899,19,1899,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[198]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031These land mines will help us defend ourselves from that animal Kurzen and his men. Thank you for bringing them. If you need further work, I can probably find something for you to do. And you won't have to deal with those goblins, hm?\030Hmm. Yes, I do have something you could do, actually. Lieutenant Doren and his followers up in the north need their regular supplies from us.$B$BThey haven't been delivered, and with the trolls attacking, I'll need someone to do it. Doren's camp lies northwest of the road at the entrance to Stranglethorn from Duskwood. Give the supplies to Private Thorsen, if he's not in the camp, then he'll be patrolling south of it. He'll take care of them.$B$BMind you, if you fail, you'll owe me restitution.\030Deliver the Miscellaneous Goblin Supplies to Private Thorsen.\030Yes? What do you want? Oh, supplies from the goblins. Strange seeing a $R delivering them, usually they send their own. No matter... you didn't touch them did you? Good good... we wouldn't want anything to happen to our mines, oh no.\030Supplies to Private Thorsen\0312,1,4,2,257,1,773\0302,6,53,2,257,4,773\0302,55,141,2,259,1,773\0302,146,232,2,263,1,773\0302,234,320,2,257,1,773\0302,322,421,2,257,4,773\0302,423,446,2,257,1,773\0302,451,499,2,257,4,773\0303,1,61,2,384,1,773\0301,1,83,4,284,3,738\0301,85,112,4,272,1,738\0301,114,183,4,274,4,738\0301,185,234,4,272,2,738\0304,1,4,3,256,2,738\0304,6,22,3,258,2,738\0304,24,53,3,256,1,738\0304,55,119,3,256,1,738\0304,121,132,3,256,1,738\0304,134,163,3,256,2,738\0304,165,176,3,256,1,738\0304,178,233,3,256,1,738\031469,2,3,Lieutenant Doren\030738,2,6,Private Thorsen\030738,2,9,Private Thorsen\0312,33,1434,0,\0302,0,0,5,Stranglethorn\0302,0,0,5,Duskwood\0302,0,0,6,Private Thorsen\0302,0,0,9,Private Thorsen\031\031",[199]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is an alarming discovery, to say the least!\030You take a sample of the strange smelling powder.\030Return to Chief Engineer Hinderweir and show him the clue that you discovered.\030Did you happen to discover any clues, $N?\030A Dark Threat Looms\0312,1,49,2,257,1,0\0303,1,78,2,384,1,0\0301,1,48,4,272,1,1093\0304,1,41,3,256,2,1093\031\0312,38,1432,0,\0302,0,0,2,Chief Engineer Hinderweir\031250,19,250,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030161,23,161,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,257,GIVER,?,9,Suspicious Barrel",[1998]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You've done well, $N. It occurs to me that you have performed many services for the Deathstalkers, proving your worth, and that perhaps it is time that we furthered your training in the shadow arts.\030Lord Varimathras has just sent me a missive about a threat to the Forsaken that must be immediately removed. His name is Fenwick Thatros, one whom Lord Varimathras believes is a leader of the undead that have taken root in Silverpine Forest.$B$BYour name came to mind immediately, $n. I have faith enough in your abilities that you will carry out this mission flawlessly.$B$BThe latest reports from the Deathstalkers in Silverpine indicate that Thatros can be found near the decrepit dock on Lordamere.\030Kill Fenwick Thatros and bring his head back to Mennet Carkad in the Rogues' Quarter of the Undercity.\030I have placed the utmost faith in you to perform this service for Lord Varimathras.\030Fenwick Thatros\0312,1,108,2,261,1,6467\0302,110,241,2,257,1,6467\0302,246,284,2,257,1,6467\0302,286,371,2,257,3,6467\0302,376,502,2,257,1,6467\0303,1,102,2,384,1,6467\0301,1,21,4,272,1,6467\0301,23,198,4,272,4,6467\0304,1,83,3,256,1,6467\0312425,2,1,Varimathras\0306570,2,2,Fenwick Thatros\0302425,2,2,Varimathras\0306570,2,6,Fenwick Thatros\0306467,2,6,Mennet Carkad\0304244,4,8,Shadow\0302425,3,9,Varimathras\0312,0,0,1,Forsaken\0302,0,0,2,Silverpine Forest\0302,0,0,5,Deathstalkers\0302,0,0,5,Silverpine\0302,0,0,6,Mennet Carkad\0302,0,0,6,Rogues' Quarter of the Undercity\0311999,23,1999,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7306,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[1999]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very good, $N! You have learned the fine art of lockpicking well, and faster than I could have possibly expected.$B$BI see that I was right to place my trust in you. Believe me, boy, I foresee that you will go far in this line of work.\030The wizards of the Kirin Tor at Ambermill have stored away important documents pertaining to the current state of Dalaran. This we know from the admissions of one of our prisoners. Lord Varimathras has placed the duty of recovering them in the hands of the Deathstalkers.$B$BThis task falls to you, $n. You will need some equipment, however, and the knowledge of lockpicking. Speak with Estelle Gendry, our outfitter, and ask her for a set of tools before you set out.\030Find the Dalaran Status Report and return it to Mennet Carkad in the Rogues' Quarter of the Undercity.\030Have you located the documents, $N?\030Tools of the Trade\0312,1,122,2,257,1,6467\0302,124,180,2,257,1,6467\0302,182,271,2,257,1,6467\0302,276,302,2,257,1,6467\0302,304,375,2,259,3,6467\0302,377,468,2,257,1,6467\0303,1,102,2,384,1,6467\0301,1,14,4,272,1,6467\0301,16,113,4,272,4,6467\0301,118,165,4,272,1,6467\0301,167,235,4,272,4,6467\0304,1,35,3,256,2,6467\0312425,2,3,Varimathras\0306566,2,6,Estelle Gendry\0306467,2,7,Mennet Carkad\0312,0,0,1,Ambermill\0302,0,0,7,Mennet Carkad\0302,0,0,7,Rogues' Quarter of the Undercity\0311998,19,1998,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7309,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[2]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Most impressive, $N... the claw of Sharptalon could not have been easy to get! The Ashenvale Hunt goes well for you!$B$BSharptalon had long terrorized the peons from the lumber camps near its path as they tried to travel here to Splintertree Post. No doubt once the word gets out that it was you who put down the beast, many rousing songs of your bravery will be heard at campfires and lumber mills across Ashenvale!\030The mighty hippogryph Sharptalon has been slain, with the claw of the felled beast serving as a testament to your victory.  Senani Thunderheart at the Splintertree Post will no doubt be interested in seeing this trophy as proof of your deeds.\030Bring Sharptalon's Claw to Senani Thunderheart at Splintertree Post, Ashenvale.\030Yes, mighty $C, I sensed your arrival. I trust you have more news to report to me about your hunt?\030Sharptalon's Claw\0312,1,122,2,261,1,0\0302,125,242,2,257,3,0\0303,1,79,2,384,1,0\0301,1,22,4,272,1,12696\0301,24,78,4,272,4,12696\0301,80,116,4,272,1,12696\0301,121,247,4,276,1,12696\0301,249,416,4,272,3,12696\0304,1,38,3,256,1,12696\0304,40,98,3,256,2,12696\03112676,2,1,Sharptalon\03012696,2,2,Senani Thunderheart\0309084,2,2,Thunderheart\03012696,2,3,Senani Thunderheart\0309084,2,3,Thunderheart\03012676,4,5,Sharptalon\03012676,4,7,Sharptalon\03010430,4,8,The Beast\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,2,Splintertree Post\0302,0,0,3,Senani Thunderheart\0302,0,0,3,Splintertree Post\0304,0,0,7,Splintertree Post\0316383,19,6383,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,16305,STARTER,?,10,",[20]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031That makes for a lot fewer orcs to worry about, thanks.\030The Blackrock orcs have travelled from the Burning Steppes and claimed Stonewatch Keep to the north.  From there they maraud the areas north of Lakeshire and keep its citizens in town, penned like cattle.$B$BHelp rid Lakeshire of this menace.  Kill these Blackrock orcs and bring me ten of their Battleworn Axes as proof.$B$BAnd although Blackrocks threaten us from the north, we've received reports of more in the southeastern pocket of Redridge.  If you find any there, then they too should be hunted.\030Bring 10 Battleworn Axes to Marshal Marris in Lakeshire.\030Have you been slaying orcs, $N? If so, then show me...\030Blackrock Menace\0312,1,100,2,257,1,382\0302,103,204,2,257,1,382\0302,209,242,2,257,1,382\0302,245,321,2,257,1,382\0302,326,447,2,261,1,382\0302,450,503,2,257,4,382\0303,1,56,2,384,1,382\0301,1,55,4,272,1,382\0304,1,31,3,256,2,382\0304,33,54,3,256,4,382\031382,2,7,Marshal Marris\0312,44,1433,0,\0302,0,0,1,Burning Steppes\0302,0,0,2,Lakeshire\0302,0,0,7,Marshal Marris\0302,0,0,7,Lakeshire\03119,23,19,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3014,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[200]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031These are Bookie Herod's notes and records.$B$BAmong them are: a list of supplies within the camp, material requests from Colonel Kurzen, and various letters and correspondences.\030If Kurzen knows Thorsen's secret, then we have a spy in our midst.  We must determine how the secret was leaked!$B$BThorsen's contact within Kurzen's camp was Bookie Herod.  Herod is Kurzen's logistics officer and knows everything about the running of Kurzen's Compound.  If you can get Herod's notes or records, maybe we can find out how Thorsen was discovered.$B$BWhen we were still with Kurzen, Bookie's office was on the top floor of the camp's only two-story house.  His records are probably still there.\030Find Bookie Herod's Records.\030\030Bookie Herod\0312,1,66,2,257,4,469\0302,69,112,2,257,1,469\0302,117,172,2,257,1,469\0302,175,270,2,257,1,469\0302,273,362,2,257,4,469\0302,367,470,2,257,1,469\0302,473,509,2,257,1,469\0303,1,28,2,384,1,469\0301,1,43,4,272,1,0\0301,48,178,4,272,1,0\031815,2,3,Bookie Herod\0303975,2,3,Herod\0303975,2,4,Herod\030815,2,8,Bookie Herod\030815,4,9,Bookie Herod\030813,4,10,Colonel Kurzen\0312,33,1434,0,\0302,0,0,3,Kurzen's\0304,0,0,10,Colonel Kurzen\031215,19,215,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030328,23,328,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,287,FINISHER,?,12,Bookie Herod's Records",[201]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Hmmm, so my information was correct, as usual. Interesting. Well, I don't suppose they pose any sort of threat of interference with our operation, but perhaps they have a need for some of our excellent manufactured products. Hmmm...\030I've gotten reports of a group of hunters that have set up camp upriver of the Venture Company mining camp on Lake Nazferiti.  Now, normally I wouldn't care, but improbably, I heard that Hemet Nesingwary was one of the hunters there.  He's certainly well-connected, if you catch my meaning, and you never can be too safe.$B$BWhy don't you go check out the camp, $n, see what they're about?\030Find the hunters' camp and report its location to Krazek in Booty Bay.\030Locate the hunters' camp\030Well?  Did you have any luck in locating the camp?\030Investigate the Camp\0312,1,125,2,257,1,773\0302,128,233,2,257,1,773\0302,236,321,2,257,4,773\0302,326,389,2,257,2,773\0303,1,70,2,384,1,773\0301,1,46,4,272,1,773\0301,48,59,4,272,1,773\0301,61,224,4,276,4,773\0301,226,232,4,272,1,773\0305,1,5,3,256,2,773\0305,8,50,3,256,2,773\0304,1,24,3,384,1,773\031715,2,2,Hemet Nesingwary\030773,2,5,Krazek\0312,33,1434,0,\0302,0,0,5,Krazek\0302,0,0,5,Booty Bay\031\031",[202]="PARTIAL\031conflict,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I dared not believe the reports, but you bring us proof that... Kurzen and his leaders are defeated. You have saved us!$B$BThese jungles are filled with menaces of all types, but none had the cruel intellect of Kurzen. We may all breathe easier now that he is gone.\030You have proven yourself time and again, and your resourcefulness seems to rival even that of Kurzen himself.  You may be the salvation of our band of rebels...if you can pit yourself against Kurzen and prevail!$B$BHe commands his men from deep within the Stockpile.  You must enter that cave, brave through his defenders, and face Kurzen and his leaders.$B$BFarewell, $N.  My hope, and the fate of my men, go with you.\030Kill 6 Kurzen Elite, 4 Kurzen Subchiefs, and bring Kurzen's Head to Lieutenant Doren at the Rebel Camp.\030Dare I hope that Kurzen and his defenders are dead, $N?\030Colonel Kurzen\0312,1,109,2,257,4,469\0302,112,211,2,257,4,469\0302,216,266,2,257,1,469\0302,269,355,2,257,1,469\0302,360,372,2,257,1,469\0302,375,419,2,259,3,469\0303,1,103,2,384,1,469\0301,1,63,4,272,4,469\0301,65,100,4,272,1,469\0301,102,119,4,304,1,469\0301,124,218,4,272,1,469\0301,220,265,4,304,1,469\0304,1,55,3,258,2,469\031939,2,7,Kurzen Elite\030469,2,7,Lieutenant Doren\0312,33,1434,0,\0302,0,0,3,Stockpile\0302,0,0,7,Lieutenant Doren\0302,0,0,7,Rebel Camp\031574,19,574,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,939,OBJECTIVE,6,13,Kurzen Elite\030NPC,978,OBJECTIVE,4,13,Kurzen Subchief\030ITEM,3615,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[203]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done. The loss of those Jungle Fighters will relieve some of the pressure on our camp.$B$BBut now that you've had a taste of the forces we're up against, do you still want to throw your lot in with us??\030We're fighting a losing battle with Colonel Kurzen.  Not only is he a brilliant tactician, he outnumbers us at least 10 to 1!  To survive, we need to use his own, covert tactics against him.$B$BEnter his camp to the east and kill his men.  Lots of them.  And get out before reinforcements can close on you.\030Kill 15 Kurzen Jungle Fighters.$B$BReturn to Sergeant Yohwa at the Rebel Camp.\030I hope you've been successful in your hunting, $N. We won't last long against him without your help.\030The Second Rebellion\0312,1,51,2,261,1,733\0302,54,125,2,257,1,733\0302,128,190,2,267,1,733\0302,195,238,2,257,1,733\0302,241,253,2,257,1,733\0302,256,306,2,257,1,733\0303,1,31,2,384,1,733\0303,36,78,2,384,1,733\0301,1,10,4,272,1,733\0301,12,91,4,272,3,733\0301,96,207,4,274,2,733\0304,1,50,3,258,3,733\0304,52,100,3,256,1,733\031813,2,1,Colonel Kurzen\030733,2,8,Sergeant Yohwa\0312,33,1434,0,\0302,0,0,8,Sergeant Yohwa\0302,0,0,8,Rebel Camp\031\031NPC,937,OBJECTIVE,15,13,Kurzen Jungle Fighter",[2038]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You've done the movement a great service, $N. The troggs and leper gnomes infesting Gnomeregan will soon feel the brunt of a gnomish air assault!\030As if crashing into the Loch wasn't bad enough, troggs from the nearby island attacked me and stole my tools and special Blastenheimer Blastencapper explosives. With no gyrocopter and no explosives, the movement has no chance!$B$BGet my tools back and find my Blastencapper explosives, $N. For Gnomeregan!\030Find and return Bingles' supplies:$B$BBingles' Wrench, Bingles' Screwdriver, Bingles' Hammer, and Bingles' Blastencapper.\030$N! Where are my things?!\030Bingles' Missing Supplies\0312,1,160,2,261,4,6577\0302,162,226,2,257,1,6577\0302,231,289,2,257,1,6577\0302,291,305,2,257,1,6577\0303,1,34,2,384,1,6577\0303,39,121,2,384,1,6577\0301,1,45,4,272,1,6577\0301,47,145,4,272,3,6577\0304,5,25,3,256,2,6577\031\0312,38,1432,0,\031\031ITEM,7343,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,7345,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,7346,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,7376,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[2039]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031So Gnoarn doesn't trust my reconnaissance abilities? I wonder why...$B$BNevermind that, I need your assistance! Nay! The movement needs your assistance!\030We've lost contact with Bingles! He was sent on a reconnaissance mission over Gnomeregan and hasn't reported back in over a week. I just know he's gone and blown himself up.$B$BHe was last seen flying over the Loch. Perhaps you can investigate, $N.\030Find Bingles Blastenheimer in Loch Modan.\030\030Find Bingles\0312,1,32,2,261,1,6569\0302,34,129,2,257,1,6569\0302,131,173,2,257,1,6569\0302,178,215,2,257,1,6569\0302,217,248,2,257,4,6569\0303,1,41,2,384,1,6569\0301,1,52,4,272,2,6577\0301,54,68,4,272,1,6577\0301,73,111,4,274,1,6577\0301,113,116,4,272,1,6577\0301,118,152,4,274,1,6577\0316577,2,6,Bingles Blastenheimer\0306569,4,7,Gnoarn\0312,1537,1455,0,\0302,0,0,6,Loch Modan\0312038,23,2038,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302038,24,2038,UNKNOWN\031",[204]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $N. These remedies will keep more of us alive and in fighting shape. And the extracts will help us create our own remedies.\030To have a chance against Kurzen, we need his healing support neutralized.  He has gathered a large number of Medicine Men who heal his forces with Jungle Remedies and poison our fighters with Venom Fern Extracts.$B$BWe need those remedies and extracts for our own.  Search the Kurzen Compound - his Medicine Men and Jungle fighers will have the remedies, and the extracts are probably stowed in some of the camp's supply boxes.\030Bring 7 Jungle Remedies and 1 Venom Fern Extract to Sergeant Yohwa at the Rebel Camp.\030I'm waiting on those remedies and that extract, $N.\030Bad Medicine\0312,1,73,2,259,1,733\0302,76,212,2,261,1,733\0302,217,264,2,259,1,733\0302,267,427,2,257,3,733\0303,1,85,2,384,1,733\0301,1,14,4,272,1,733\0301,16,79,4,276,3,733\0301,81,134,4,272,3,733\0304,1,51,3,256,1,733\031733,2,5,Sergeant Yohwa\0312,33,1434,0,\0302,0,0,5,Sergeant Yohwa\0302,0,0,5,Rebel Camp\031\031ITEM,2633,OBJECTIVE,7,15,\030ITEM,2634,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[2040]="PARTIAL\031conflict,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $N. Thanks to you, Gnomeregan is one step closer to its day of liberation!\030Gnomeregan has fallen under the control of those dastardly troggs! The situation is grave but perhaps you can help, $N.$B$BDeep in the Deadmines is a functional goblin shredder. Find that shredder and bring back the intact power supply. With the shredder's power supply, we can give our gyrodrillmatic excavationators the power they need to break through the rocky underground borders of Gnomeregan, opening the way for a gnomish assault!\030Retrieve the Gnoam Sprecklesprocket from the Deadmines and return it to Shoni the Shilent in Stormwind.\030Have you found the Gnoam Sprecklesprocket, $N?\030Underground Assault\0312,1,66,2,257,1,6579\0302,68,119,2,257,4,6579\0302,124,177,2,257,1,6579\0302,179,236,2,257,1,6579\0302,238,438,2,259,1,6579\0303,1,103,2,384,1,6579\0301,1,14,4,272,1,6579\0301,16,85,4,304,1,6579\0304,1,46,3,256,2,6579\0316579,2,6,Shoni the Shilent\0312,1581,0,0,\0302,0,0,3,Deadmines\0302,0,0,6,Deadmines\0302,0,0,6,Shoni the Shilent\0302,0,0,6,Stormwind\031\031ITEM,7365,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[2041]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Do you bring word from central command?\030Perhaps... Perhaps you can help us in the battle for Gnomeregan.$B$BIn Stormwind you will find the commander of our underground assault crew, Shoni the Shilent. Shoni needs assistance with her gyrodrillmatic excavationators.$B$BYou will probably find her amongst the dwarves in Stormwind.$B$BGood luck, $N.\030Speak with Shoni the Shilent in Stormwind.\030\030Speak with Shoni\0312,1,10,2,257,4,6569\0302,12,64,2,261,4,6569\0302,69,160,2,257,3,6569\0302,162,224,2,259,1,6569\0302,229,288,2,257,3,6569\0302,293,306,2,257,1,6569\0303,1,42,2,384,1,6569\0301,1,39,4,272,2,6579\0316579,2,3,Shoni the Shilent\0306579,2,7,Shoni the Shilent\0312,1537,1455,0,\0302,0,0,5,Stormwind\0302,0,0,7,Stormwind\0312040,23,2040,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302040,24,2040,UNKNOWN\031",[205]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you.  I will study these fetishes and see if they hold the secret of Kurzen's fall into evil.\030While I study those legends you acquired, gather for me implements of evil troll magic.  Enter the territory of the Skullsplitter trolls, a second tribe to the distant south, and acquire Skullsplitter Fetishes from their Witchdoctors and Mystics.\030Bring 4 Skullsplitter Fetishes to Brother Nimetz at the Rebel Camp.\030Do you have those fetishes, $N? They might hold the secret to Kurzen's degradation...I must know!\030Troll Witchery\0312,1,87,2,257,1,739\0302,90,246,2,257,1,739\0303,1,67,2,384,1,739\0301,1,10,4,272,1,739\0301,13,99,4,272,4,739\0304,1,31,3,256,2,739\0304,33,97,3,256,4,739\031739,2,3,Brother Nimetz\0312,33,1434,0,\0302,0,0,3,Brother Nimetz\0302,0,0,3,Rebel Camp\0303,0,0,7,Kurzen's\031207,19,207,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,2466,OBJECTIVE,4,15,",[206]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Aha! You've done it! You are a great force for good, $N, and may your strength never fade!$B$BI will study this Mind's Eye and determine if it may be used for good. If not... then it must be destroyed.\030Kurzen may be dead, but...that which drove him to evil still lives!  Through my studies I have discovered this: An Ogre Mage - Mai'Zoth - dwells in an Ogre Mound within the eastern mountains of Stranglethorn.  He is rumored to employ mind-controlling magic, and I am positive that he corrupted Kurzen.$B$BIf Mai'Zoth is allowed to live, then his evil may influence others, and may even cause another Kurzen to surface.$B$BKill him, and bring me his Mind's Eye, the artifact he uses to corrupt others.\030Bring the Mind's Eye to Brother Nimetz at the Rebel Camp.\030I give you my blessing. Mai'Zoth's strength is matched only by his evil.\030Mai'Zoth\0312,1,67,2,257,1,739\0302,70,208,2,257,1,739\0302,211,301,2,261,1,739\0302,306,418,2,257,4,739\0302,423,500,2,261,1,739\0303,1,57,2,384,1,739\0301,1,4,4,272,1,739\0301,6,20,4,272,1,739\0301,22,90,4,272,1,739\0301,95,164,4,272,4,739\0301,166,174,4,272,4,739\0301,176,201,4,276,1,739\0304,1,23,3,256,1,739\0304,25,72,3,256,1,739\031211,2,2,Ogre\030818,2,2,Mai'Zoth\030818,2,4,Mai'Zoth\030739,2,6,Brother Nimetz\0312,33,1434,0,\0302,0,0,6,Brother Nimetz\0302,0,0,6,Rebel Camp\031202,21,202,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030205,21,205,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3616,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[207]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, $N. I will study these legends to see if there is some link between the trolls and the evil that has possessed Colonel Kurzen.\030Colonel Kurzen was once a great, noble man - I must find what caused his fall into depravity!  He may be under the sway of troll magic.  To confirm this, I must study some of their legends.$B$BThere are 4 tablets hidden within the troll ruins of Stranglethorn.  I must see what is written on these tablets!  Transcribe their markings and bring the transcriptions back to me.$B$BThe first tablet is in the Bal'lal Ruins, the second is in the Vile Reef, and the third and fourth are in the Ruins of Zul'Kunda.\030Find the 4 tablets and bring their legends back to Brother Nimetz.\030$N! Do you have the troll legends? I must know their secrets!\030Kurzen's Mystery\0312,1,93,2,257,1,739\0302,96,135,2,257,1,739\0302,138,189,2,257,1,739\0302,194,260,2,321,1,739\0302,263,306,2,257,1,739\0302,309,374,2,257,1,739\0302,379,507,2,321,1,739\0303,1,66,2,384,1,739\0301,1,14,4,272,1,739\0301,16,137,4,272,4,739\0304,5,34,3,256,2,739\0304,36,61,3,256,1,739\031813,2,1,Colonel Kurzen\030739,2,8,Brother Nimetz\030813,4,10,Colonel Kurzen\0312,33,1434,0,\0302,0,0,7,Bal'lal Ruins\0302,0,0,7,Vile Reef\0302,0,0,7,Ruins of Zul'Kunda\0302,0,0,8,Brother Nimetz\031204,21,204,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030205,23,205,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,2005,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,2006,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,2007,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,2008,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[2078]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030requestItems\030title\031Yarrr... Ye be provin' yerself to be more than a yella sea dog, landlubber.$B$BThe Cap'n may promote ye to poop deck swabby if ye be keepin' this up...\030Landlubber, ye needs to find me first mate.$B$BTake this'n key, puts it in his gulliver an' bring him back here to serve the Cap'n.$B$BThem murlocs an' their chief ain't gonna be too happy once me first mate gets a hold of em!\030Find Gelkak's First Mate, the Threshwackonator 4100, and lead it back to Gelkak.\030\030Gelkak's First Mate\030Where be me first mate, $N? Shackles n' sharks fer ye soon if ye don't hurry!\030Gyromast's Revenge\0312,1,43,2,259,1,6667\0302,48,131,2,257,1,6667\0302,136,226,2,257,1,6667\0303,1,80,2,384,1,6667\0301,1,8,4,272,1,6667\0301,10,75,4,272,1,6667\0301,80,151,4,272,4,6667\0306,1,27,3,256,2,6667\0306,29,77,3,256,4,6667\0305,1,19,3,384,1,6667\0316669,2,4,The Threshwackonator 4100\0312,148,1439,0,\0302,0,0,4,Gelkak\0312098,19,2098,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,6669,OBJECTIVE,1,13,The Threshwackonator 4100",[208]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Bloody well done! Right-o! Congratulations, $N, for succeeding where others have failed.$B$BI am honored to count you as a comrade of our great hunting party here. No one will ever doubt your expertise in hunting and tracking!$B$BCheers to you, I say! Cheers!\030$N, you are a hunter worthy of our company.  From the battlefields of Lordaeron to the deepest jungle, I have rarely witnessed such prowess with weaponry as you have demonstrated.$B$BYou have killed the ferocious Sin'Dall, the elusive Bag'thera and the treacherous Tethis.  But the true prize is the head of King Bangalash.  That white tiger is the reason I am here.  I've had my sights on him for quite some time now.  Kill King Bangalash and your hunting prowess is proven to be second to none.\030Hemet Nesingwary wants you to bring him the head of King Bangalash, the great white tiger.\030I see you're back, old bloke. King Bangalash has caused me to come crawling back to camp many times. Hang in there.\030Big Game Hunter\0312,1,43,2,257,1,715\0302,46,179,2,257,1,715\0302,184,272,2,257,1,715\0302,275,323,2,257,1,715\0302,326,366,2,257,1,715\0302,369,418,2,257,1,715\0302,421,496,2,257,1,715\0303,1,90,2,386,1,715\0301,1,17,4,272,1,715\0301,19,26,4,272,1,715\0301,28,88,4,272,1,715\0301,93,163,4,272,1,715\0301,165,226,4,272,3,715\0301,231,251,4,272,1,715\0301,253,259,4,272,1,715\0304,1,29,3,256,1,715\0304,31,100,3,256,1,715\0304,102,115,3,256,1,715\031729,2,3,Sin'Dall\030730,2,3,Tethis\030731,2,4,King Bangalash\030731,2,7,King Bangalash\030715,2,8,Hemet Nesingwary\030731,2,8,King Bangalash\030731,3,17,King Bangalash\0312,33,1434,0,\031188,21,188,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030193,21,193,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030197,21,197,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3880,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[209]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, good work, good work! Ugh, though you could have done a better job cleaning off the-- Well, no matter, no matter! My thanks to you, $N, our operation will no doubt see increased output and productivity thanks to your help! Good good, now, onto other matters...\030It's expensive and hard to kill enough tigers to support the export of tiger fangs to the islands in the South Seas. Luckily, we've developed a technique that allows us to take mundane horn-like objects and turn them into undetectable forgeries.$B$BThe closest match we've found, amazingly, are the tusks of the Skullsplitter trolls.$B$BHey, before you say anything, what the buyer doesn't know doesn't hurt them, am I right? Bring me a large number of them so we can get to work on the monthly shipment!\030Acquire 18 Skullsplitter Tusks and return them to Kebok.\030Tough buggers, aren't they? Well, have you had any luck? Sorry to seem impatient, but this has been a huge thorn in my side! Well?\030Skullsplitter Tusks\0312,1,116,2,257,1,737\0302,118,245,2,257,1,737\0302,250,333,2,257,1,737\0302,338,425,2,257,2,737\0302,427,504,2,257,1,737\0303,1,56,2,384,1,737\0301,1,25,4,272,1,737\0301,27,117,4,272,4,737\0301,119,226,4,272,3,737\0301,228,264,4,272,1,737\0304,1,27,3,256,2,737\0304,29,56,3,256,2,737\0304,58,124,3,256,4,737\0304,126,130,3,256,2,737\031737,2,6,Kebok\0312,33,1434,0,\0302,0,0,1,South Seas\0302,0,0,6,Kebok\031189,19,189,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,1524,OBJECTIVE,18,15,",[2098]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Avast ye scurvy sea dog! Ye did it! Soon me first mate be back in workin' order and them beasties won't know what hit em!$B$BHrm, have ye seen me first mate?\030A pirate's life ain't an easy one, landlubber. It ain't all about plunderin' and booze! Alas, me ship be sunk just off shore thanks to them pesky Threshadons.$B$BWhat I be needin' is me first mate back in workin' order!$B$BWhen I washed up'n shore, the key for me first mate broke on the rocks and was pilfered by the beasties of Darkshore. Out of the corner of me eyes I saw some of them Ragin' Crawlers, Ferocious Foreststrider, and murloc rummaging through the wreckage....\030Find and return the three pieces of Gelkak's Key to Gelkak Gyromast.\030Have ye found me broke down key, landlubber?\030Gyromast's Retrieval\0312,1,46,2,257,1,6667\0302,48,87,2,257,1,6667\0302,89,158,2,257,1,6667\0302,163,219,2,257,1,6667\0302,224,340,2,257,1,6667\0302,342,476,2,257,1,6667\0303,1,68,2,384,1,6667\0301,1,24,4,272,1,6667\0301,26,35,4,272,1,6667\0301,37,121,4,272,1,6667\0301,126,157,4,272,2,6667\0304,1,44,3,256,2,6667\0312322,2,6,Foreststrider\030285,2,6,Murloc\0306667,2,7,Gelkak Gyromast\0312,148,1439,0,\0302,0,0,7,Gelkak Gyromast\0312078,23,2078,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7498,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,7499,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,7500,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[21]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Once again, you have earned my respect, and the gratitude of the Stormwind Army. There may yet be kobolds in the mine, but I will marshal others against them. We have further tasks for you.\030Your previous investigations are proof that the Echo Ridge Mine needs purging.  Return to the mine and help clear it of kobolds.$B$BWaste no time, $N.  The longer the kobolds are left unmolested in the mine, the deeper a foothold they gain in Northshire.\030Kill 12 Kobold Laborers, then return to Marshal McBride at Northshire Abbey.\030I know it's bloody work, $N, but it's vital to the safety of Northshire. Are you ready to report?\030Skirmish at Echo Ridge\0312,1,78,2,259,1,197\0302,81,128,2,257,1,197\0302,133,150,2,257,1,197\0302,153,254,2,257,1,197\0303,1,76,2,384,1,197\0301,1,80,4,272,1,197\0301,82,158,4,272,3,197\0301,160,189,4,272,1,197\0304,1,72,3,264,1,197\0304,74,97,3,256,2,197\031197,2,5,Marshal McBride\0312,9,1429,0,\0302,0,0,4,Northshire\0302,0,0,5,Marshal McBride\0302,0,0,5,Northshire Abbey\03115,19,15,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\03054,23,54,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,80,OBJECTIVE,12,13,Kobold Laborer",[210]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh I see, it's a Krazek's Crock Pot! An ingenious piece of work, but it can break a spring or throw a gear now and then. Let me see what's wrong with this one...$B$BAha! Its steam charger is rusted out, it has a cracked knuckle-gasket and its fobulator is missing teeth. I'm surprised the pot could even boil a turnip in this state!$B$BCan I fix it? Of course I can fix it!$B$BBut there's a price. Oh yes, there is always a price...\030I do most of the cooking at the camp.  And it used to be a lot of work, until I bought a mechanical cooking pot from a goblin merchant in Booty Bay.  The pot is a wonder!  It saved me countless hours...until it broke!$B$BCan you take the pot back to the goblin for me so he can fix it?  His name is Krazek.\030Bring Krazek's Crock Pot to Krazek the goblin.\030Hello! You brought me something?\030Krazek's Cookery\0312,1,37,2,257,1,770\0302,40,148,2,321,1,770\0302,151,170,2,257,1,770\0302,173,217,2,257,1,770\0302,222,285,2,257,2,770\0302,288,306,2,257,1,770\0303,1,46,2,384,1,770\0301,1,36,4,272,1,773\0301,38,120,4,272,1,773\0301,122,161,4,272,1,773\0301,166,169,4,272,1,773\0301,171,270,4,276,1,773\0301,272,332,4,272,4,773\0301,337,349,4,272,2,773\0301,351,373,4,272,1,773\0301,378,397,4,272,1,773\0301,399,432,4,272,1,773\0304,1,6,3,256,1,773\0304,8,32,3,256,2,773\031773,2,6,Krazek\030773,2,7,Krazek\0312,33,1434,0,\0302,0,0,2,Booty Bay\0302,0,0,7,Krazek the\031627,23,627,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[211]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You've done it! Araj... the lich is finally defeated!$B$BYou've done a tremendous service to the Alliance on this day, $N. Your bravery and perseverance are a testament to what it means to be a true hero. Please - accept this as a token for all to see and know that you have delivered the Alliance a victory for the ages!\030Alas, the time to attack Andorhal and drive out the lich that controls it is upon us!$B$BInside the ruins of the city is where the lich - Araj the Summoner - holds dominion.  He is guarded by numerous Scourge surrounding the remains of city's center, and his personal retinue of guardians attached to him directly is formidable.  You will need numerous allies to even stand a chance of facing him successfully.$B$BDestroy Araj, $N, and bring me a shard from his phylactery as proof!\030Bring Araj's Phylactery Shard to Commander Ashlam Valorfist at Chillwind Camp, Western Plaguelands.\030Your task has been given to you, $N. Do you have a shard from the lich's phylactery as proof of the task being accomplished?\030Alas, Andorhal\0312,1,85,2,261,1,10838\0302,90,173,2,321,1,10838\0302,176,328,2,321,1,10838\0302,331,410,2,259,3,10838\0302,415,482,2,261,1,10838\0303,1,99,2,384,1,10838\0301,1,15,4,272,1,10838\0301,17,23,4,272,1,10838\0301,25,53,4,272,1,10838\0301,58,122,4,272,1,10838\0301,124,204,4,272,1,10838\0301,206,321,4,272,1,10838\0304,1,36,3,256,1,10838\0304,38,124,3,256,2,10838\0311852,2,2,Araj the Summoner\03010838,2,6,Commander Ashlam Valorfist\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,6,Commander Ashlam Valorfist\0302,0,0,6,Chillwind Camp\0304,0,0,10,Alliance\0315097,19,5097,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,17114,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[2118]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030requestItems\030title\031Our work has only just begun, $N. Are you prepared for your next task?\030A sickness spreads across the Darkshore, gripping the minds and bodies of all it touches.$B$BThe Thistle Bears have been hit the hardest by this plague. The once noble beasts are now an instrument of destruction - rabid and frenzied. I may have a cure for this ailment.$B$BTake this trap to the forest and lay it on the ground. Any Rabid Thistle Bear that crosses the light shall become docile for a short time. Once the bear is docile, it shall follow you. Lead it back here, $N.\030Capture a living Rabid Thistle Bear and bring it back to Tharnariun.$B$BShould you fail to capture a Rabid Thistle Bear and lose your trap, return to Tharnariun Treetender and request another trap.\030\030Rabid Thistle Bear Captured\030Have you brought me the sick animal, $N?$B$BShould you fail to spring the trap, do not fret - Tharnariun's Hope is eternal. If you require another trap, abandon your task and report back to me.\030Plagued Lands\0312,1,89,2,257,1,3701\0302,94,152,2,261,1,3701\0302,154,233,2,257,1,3701\0302,235,269,2,257,1,3701\0302,274,327,2,257,1,3701\0302,329,411,2,257,3,3701\0302,413,457,2,257,3,3701\0302,459,480,2,257,1,3701\0303,1,68,2,384,1,3701\0303,73,197,2,384,1,3701\0301,1,33,4,272,1,3701\0301,35,70,4,272,2,3701\0306,1,40,3,256,2,3701\0306,45,123,3,256,3,3701\0306,125,193,3,256,4,3701\0305,1,27,3,384,1,3701\0312164,2,6,Rabid Thistle Bear\0302163,2,6,Thistle Bear\0302164,2,9,Rabid Thistle Bear\0302163,2,9,Thistle Bear\0302164,2,10,Rabid Thistle Bear\0302163,2,10,Thistle Bear\0303701,2,10,Tharnariun Treetender\0302164,3,16,Rabid Thistle Bear\0302163,3,16,Thistle Bear\0312,148,1439,0,\0302,0,0,9,Tharnariun\0302,0,0,10,Tharnariun Treetender\0312138,23,2138,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,11836,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Captured Rabid Thistle Bear",[212]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, this will do nicely! Many, many thanks!$B$BNow if you'll excuse me, I must get the haunch chopped, marinated and garnished for the banquet.\030One of my most famous dishes is Chilled Basilisk in Lime Vinaigrette.  But the problem is... the meat is impossible to keep fresh, and I must serve the dish tonight for a noble's birthday!$B$BSo if you can bring me a Chilled Basilisk Haunch from a freshly-killed Cold Eye Basilisk, quickly, then I will owe you a king's feast!$B$BCold Eye Basilisks are known to roam along the beach dunes of northwestern Stranglethorn, so you have much traveling to do.  And be swift!\030Kill a Cold Eye Basilisk, get a Chilled Basilisk Haunch, and return it to Angus Stern in the Blue Recluse.\030$N! Do you have that haunch? I must begin preparing it soon, or the banquet will be ruined!\030A Meal Served Cold\0312,1,69,2,257,1,1141\0302,72,92,2,261,1,1141\0302,94,188,2,257,1,1141\0302,193,326,2,257,4,1141\0302,331,453,2,257,1,1141\0302,456,468,2,257,1,1141\0303,1,106,2,384,1,1141\0301,1,24,4,272,3,1141\0301,26,43,4,272,1,1141\0301,48,143,4,272,4,1141\0304,5,28,3,256,2,1141\0304,30,91,3,256,3,1141\031690,2,4,Cold Eye Basilisk\030690,2,7,Cold Eye Basilisk\0301141,2,7,Angus Stern\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,1,Lime Vinaigrette\0302,0,0,7,Angus Stern\0302,0,0,7,Blue Recluse\031\031ITEM,2476,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[213]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Fascinating. That the crystals have been tumbled using this process can only indicate that they are planning to use them as some sort of fuel or other catalyst. I don't know much more than that. Samples will have to be dispatched to Head Chemist Gigglefont.\030He's done it this time! Bad enough that Gelriz's muscling out the moguls who were appointed by the trade princes, now he tries to cut in on the most notorious pirate!$B$BRevilgaz won't have it, and he's told me to take care of the problem in my own way.$B$BMy way? Theft. The Venture Co. geologists near Lake Nazferiti are deeply interested in those strange blue crystals they have been finding in the mines. Bring me samples of the stone from their geologists, I don't care what you have to do to get them.\030Retrieve 8 Tumbled Crystals and return them to Kebok in Booty Bay.\030I need those stones, $n. By whatever means necessary! Just do it, don't give me the details!$B$BIt's about results, $n, nothing more, nothing less.\030Hostile Takeover\0312,1,23,2,257,1,737\0302,25,166,2,257,1,737\0302,171,253,2,261,1,737\0302,258,264,2,257,2,737\0302,266,271,2,257,1,737\0302,273,287,2,257,1,737\0302,289,408,2,257,1,737\0302,410,507,2,257,1,737\0303,1,66,2,384,1,737\0301,1,12,4,272,1,737\0301,14,160,4,272,1,737\0301,162,194,4,272,1,737\0301,196,257,4,272,3,737\0304,1,24,3,258,1,737\0304,26,53,3,256,1,737\0304,55,92,3,256,1,737\0304,97,147,3,256,1,737\031737,2,9,Kebok\0312,33,1434,0,\0302,0,0,7,Lake Nazferiti\0302,0,0,9,Kebok\0302,0,0,9,Booty Bay\0304,0,0,13,Head Chemist Gigglefont\031\031ITEM,4106,OBJECTIVE,8,15,",[2138]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have done Auberdine a great service, $N, but your task is not yet complete.\030As I had feared, the cure does not work.$B$BIt saddens me greatly to order the death of any of nature's beasts, but the sick and tainted thistle bears must be put down.$B$BReturn to the forest and destroy 20 rabid thistle bears, $N. It will most certainly not put a stop to the plague but it will slow down the damage the animals are doing to our forest and its inhabitants for a short time.\030Cleanse the forest of 20 Rabid Thistle Bears and return to Tharnariun Treetender in Darkshore.\030Is your task complete?\030Cleansing of the Infected\0312,1,40,2,257,1,3701\0302,45,168,2,257,1,3701\0302,173,232,2,261,1,3701\0302,234,391,2,261,3,3701\0303,1,94,2,384,1,3701\0301,1,79,4,272,1,3701\0304,1,22,3,256,2,3701\0313701,2,5,Tharnariun Treetender\0312,148,1439,0,\0302,0,0,5,Tharnariun Treetender\0302,0,0,5,Darkshore\0312118,19,2118,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302139,23,2139,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,2164,OBJECTIVE,20,13,Rabid Thistle Bear",[2139]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have fought for Auberdine with bravery and honor, $N. In our war torn lands, death and despair are common. Many will not rise to meet the challenge of life in our new home, choosing instead to hide in their homes or escape to the more fortified lands of the Alliance.$B$BThank you, $N. Perhaps someday soon we shall fight along side as comrades versus another foe.\030The survival of our people and lands comes at unfortunate costs, $N.$B$BYou have spilled the blood of nature's servants; many sick animals you have felled. The people of Auberdine are indebted to you, for the forest's pain is eased - even if only for a moment.$B$BI have one final task for you, but be warned, you will have to kill again. It is my hope that this will be the last time I call upon you, $N.$B$BIn a cave to the northeast, near Bashal'Aran, resides the Den Mother. Slay her.\030Find and kill the Den Mother.\030With the infected Den Mother slain, the population of Rabid Thistle Bears entering our land is lessened. Waste no time, $N.\030Tharnariun's Hope\0312,1,68,2,265,1,3701\0302,73,155,2,257,1,3701\0302,157,260,2,257,4,3701\0302,265,338,2,257,3,3701\0302,340,405,2,259,3,3701\0302,410,478,2,257,1,3701\0302,480,488,2,257,1,3701\0303,1,29,2,384,1,3701\0301,1,57,4,272,1,3701\0301,59,110,4,276,1,3701\0301,112,271,4,272,3,3701\0301,276,289,4,272,1,3701\0301,291,368,4,276,4,3701\0304,1,104,3,260,1,3701\0304,106,123,3,256,1,3701\0316788,2,6,Den Mother\0306788,2,8,Den Mother\0302996,4,10,Torn\0306788,3,14,Den Mother\0312,148,1439,0,\0302,0,0,6,Bashal'Aran\0312138,19,2138,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,6788,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Den Mother",[214]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $N! On behalf of The People's Militia I salute you for your efforts. Soon we will return this land to the people with help from brave souls like you.\030It's no secret that the trademark of the Defias Gang is their Red Bandanas.  But we've learned that the material from which these bandanas are made signifies the member's rank.$B$BThat being said, I want you to eliminate as many high ranking Defias members as you can.  The highest ranking members will undoubtedly be found in VanCleef's secret hideout.  When you're done bring me 10 Red Silk Bandanas as proof of their deaths and I will reward you.  Good luck, $N.\030Scout Riell at the Sentinel Hill Tower wants you to bring her 10 Red Silk Bandanas.\030Have you been reclaiming our land from the Defias gang? If so show me 10 Red Silk Bandanas as proof.\030Red Silk Bandanas\0312,1,75,2,257,1,820\0302,78,176,2,257,1,820\0302,181,268,2,259,1,820\0302,271,353,2,257,3,820\0302,356,449,2,257,3,820\0302,452,465,2,257,1,820\0303,1,83,2,386,1,820\0301,1,14,4,272,1,820\0301,16,79,4,272,1,820\0301,81,160,4,272,3,820\0304,1,55,3,256,2,820\0304,57,100,3,256,4,820\031820,2,7,Scout Riell\0312,1581,0,0,\0302,0,0,4,VanCleef's\0302,0,0,7,Sentinel Hill Tower\0303,0,0,11,Defias\031155,19,155,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,915,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[215]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes, what Thorsen told you is true. You must be discrete with this. At one time, we rebels were fiercely loyal to Colonel Kurzen. But such was Kurzen's corruption, our passion twisted into rage.  If it was made known that Private Thorsen has had recent dealings with Kurzen's men, then one night he would find himself with a slit throat.$B$BTo my knowledge, only Sergeant Yohwa, Thorsen and I were privy to Thorsen's mission. But there must be another. A traitor.\030Thank you for saving me, $N.  I know how this looks, but...allow me to explain.$B$BI was charged by Lieutenant Doren to re-enlist with Kurzen's men, so that I might spy on them and bring sorely needed intelligence to the rebels.  You saw here what I had thought would be my chance to infiltrate Kurzen's Compound.  I was wrong, and again, thanks for saving me.$B$BThis was a top secret mission, so you must tell no one.  But if you speak with Doren he will explain.\030Speak with Lieutenant Doren at the Rebel Camp.\030\030Jungle Secrets\0312,1,28,2,257,1,738\0302,31,79,2,257,1,738\0302,84,228,2,259,4,738\0302,231,313,2,257,4,738\0302,316,360,2,257,1,738\0302,365,419,2,257,1,738\0302,422,465,2,257,4,738\0303,1,46,2,384,1,738\0301,1,35,4,272,1,469\0301,37,67,4,272,1,469\0301,69,129,4,272,1,469\0301,131,194,4,276,1,469\0301,197,337,4,272,4,469\0301,342,425,4,272,1,469\0301,427,452,4,272,1,469\0301,454,463,4,272,1,469\031469,2,3,Lieutenant Doren\030469,2,8,Lieutenant Doren\030813,4,11,Colonel Kurzen\030738,4,13,Private Thorsen\030733,4,14,Sergeant Yohwa\0312,33,1434,0,\0302,0,0,8,Rebel Camp\0304,0,0,11,Colonel Kurzen\0304,0,0,14,Thorsen's\031200,23,200,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2158]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Rest and relaxation for the tired and cold -- that's our motto! Please, take a seat by the fire and rest your weary bones.$B$BWould you like to try a sampling of some of our fine food and drink?\030Every adventurer should rest when exhaustion sets in - and there is no finer place to get rest and relaxation than at the Lion's Pride Inn!$B$BMy best friend, Innkeeper Farley, runs the Lion's Pride. If you tell him I sent you, he may give you the special discounted rates on food and drink.$B$BTo find the Lion's Pride Inn, travel south along the road from here -- you can't miss it!\030Speak with Innkeeper Farley at the Lion's Pride Inn.\030\030Rest and Relaxation\0312,1,139,2,257,1,6774\0302,144,199,2,257,1,6774\0302,201,291,2,257,4,6774\0302,296,384,2,257,1,6774\0303,1,52,2,384,1,6774\0301,1,63,4,272,1,295\0301,65,122,4,272,1,295\0301,127,194,4,272,4,295\031295,2,2,Innkeeper Farley\030295,2,5,Innkeeper Farley\0312,12,1429,0,\0302,0,0,1,Lion's Pride Inn\0302,0,0,5,Lion's Pride Inn\031\031",[2159]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah yes, the delivery of herbs from Shadowglen. It is a shame Porthannius could not bring it himself, for we have much to discuss, he and I. But I am glad to get the herbs nonetheless, and I am glad you came.$B$BWhile you are here, please, rest yourself. Heroes must keep their strength and spirits high, and must find rest and solace whenever they may. For to neglect one's peace of body and mind is a sure path to failure.$B$BSo... rest.\030Greetings, young $c.  Can you offer me aid?  I have a package of herbs that I must deliver to the town of Dolanaar.  But I still have business with the druids of Shadowglen and cannot yet leave.$B$BCan you deliver this package for me?  It must be sent to Innkeeper Keldamyr, at the Dolanaar inn.  It lies along the road, to the south.\030Bring the Dolanaar Delivery to Innkeeper Keldamyr.\030How might I be of service to you, young one? Are you here to rest in the inn? Do you require a hearthstone?\030Dolanaar Delivery\0312,1,20,2,257,1,6780\0302,23,43,2,257,2,6780\0302,46,115,2,257,1,6780\0302,118,194,2,257,1,6780\0302,199,234,2,257,2,6780\0302,237,295,2,257,1,6780\0302,298,334,2,257,1,6780\0303,1,50,2,384,1,6780\0301,1,46,4,272,1,6736\0301,48,139,4,272,4,6736\0301,141,207,4,272,1,6736\0301,212,253,4,272,1,6736\0301,255,352,4,272,1,6736\0301,354,423,4,280,1,6736\0301,434,438,4,272,1,6736\0304,1,44,3,256,4,6736\0304,46,77,3,256,2,6736\0304,79,107,3,256,2,6736\0316736,2,6,Innkeeper Keldamyr\0306736,2,8,Innkeeper Keldamyr\0306780,4,10,Porthannius\0312,141,1438,0,\0302,0,0,6,Innkeeper Keldamyr\0302,0,0,6,Dolanaar\0302,0,0,8,Innkeeper Keldamyr\0304,0,0,9,Shadowglen\031\031",[216]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done $C, well done! I will continue to send forces to thin out the furbolg, but I can at least count on a different path that will be free of Alliance entanglements. The Horde conquest of Ashenvale is now in full swing!$B$BYou've earned your pay this day, hero. I salute you!\030The Thistlefur furbolgs are threatening our expansion!  Thistlefur Village to our east blocks the way between us here and the Splintertree Post.  It's a path that would circumvent the village of Astranaar; without it, we give the Alliance an extra expansion path.$B$B$N, we must not allow... an expansion path gap!$B$BProceed to Thistlefur Village and thin out the furbolgs.  You will be given compensation for this task, but more importantly you will be doing your duty for the Horde!\030Take down 8 Thistlefur Avengers and 8 Thistlefur Shaman; most are located east of Zoram Strand in Thistlefur Village.  Once completed, return to Karang Amakkar at Zoram'gar Outpost, Ashenvale.\030Have you taken the fight to the Thistlefur?  With a clear path between our bases, our chances of claiming the whole of Ashenvale increase dramatically.\030Between a Rock and a Thistlefur\0312,1,54,2,261,1,12757\0302,57,144,2,257,1,12757\0302,147,263,2,257,4,12757\0302,268,291,2,265,1,12757\0302,293,314,2,257,1,12757\0302,319,374,2,257,1,12757\0302,377,485,2,257,3,12757\0303,1,117,2,384,1,12757\0303,120,192,2,384,1,12757\0301,1,24,4,272,1,12757\0301,26,170,4,272,3,12757\0301,172,224,4,272,1,12757\0301,229,266,4,272,1,12757\0301,268,280,4,272,1,12757\0304,1,43,3,260,2,12757\0304,46,151,3,256,1,12757\0313924,2,8,Thistlefur Shaman\03012757,2,9,Karang Amakkar\03031,4,11,Furbolg\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,6,Thistlefur Village\0302,0,0,8,Zoram Strand\0302,0,0,8,Thistlefur Village\0302,0,0,9,Karang Amakkar\0302,0,0,9,Zoram'gar Outpost\0303,0,0,15,Thistlefur\0316621,23,6621,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,3925,OBJECTIVE,8,13,Thistlefur Avenger\030NPC,3924,OBJECTIVE,8,13,Thistlefur Shaman",[2160]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, at last, the supplies from Hands! I was beginning to worry, we've had scarce word from Anvilmar ever since the troggs overran the pass.$B$BThanks for bring this to me, $N. And please, make yourself comfortable. You must be tired after your journey.\030Hey! You look like a hearty adventurer. If you're planning on braving the pass, do you suppose you could bring a package to the inn in Kharanos?$B$BYou were planning on stopping at the inn, right? If you make it through the pass, you'll definitely want to take a breather there.$B$BAnyways, bring this to Tannok Frosthammer, the innkeeper's assistant. I can't get through the pass myself, and it'll be days until a Mountaineer escort comes through!\030Deliver the Crate of Inn Supplies to Tannok Frosthammer in Kharanos.\030Hi there! Come in, take a seat by the fire and warm yourself with a flagon of ale.\030Supplies to Tannok\0312,1,4,2,257,1,6782\0302,6,39,2,257,1,6782\0302,41,144,2,257,4,6782\0302,149,196,2,257,2,6782\0302,198,278,2,259,4,6782\0302,283,351,2,257,1,6782\0302,353,448,2,257,1,6782\0303,1,68,2,384,1,6782\0301,1,37,4,272,1,6806\0301,39,139,4,272,1,6806\0301,144,175,4,272,1,6806\0301,177,214,4,272,1,6806\0301,216,252,4,272,1,6806\0304,1,9,3,256,1,6806\0304,11,82,3,256,1,6806\0316806,2,6,Tannok Frosthammer\0306806,2,8,Tannok Frosthammer\0312,1,1426,0,\0302,0,0,3,Kharanos\0302,0,0,6,Tannok Frosthammer\0302,0,0,8,Tannok Frosthammer\0302,0,0,8,Kharanos\0304,0,0,9,Hands\0304,0,0,10,Anvilmar\031\031",[2161]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, this is the food Ukor brought to the Valley of Trials. Did they not need it? Well, I guess they like to starve you heroes in training. Builds spirit, they say!$B$BThank you for returning the food. I'll stick it back on the shelves... but here, let me offer you some refreshment first!$B$BAnd don't forget to rest here in the inn. You may be a brave $C ready to take on the world, but if your energy is sapped you won't be doing yourself, or the Horde, much good.\030Excuse me?  Can you help me?$B$BI have a load of food here.  I walked along the road and braved scorpids and spiders and worse!  I brought the food to the Valley of Trials because I thought they needed it and I like to help out.  But they don't need any food!  Now I have to take it back to Razor Hill and I'm afraid of all the beasts along the way...$B$BCan you take it for me?  I'm just a peon, but you're a hero.  You fear nothing!$B$BTake it to Innkeeper Grosk at the Razor Hill inn.  Thank you!\030Bring Ukor's Burden to Innkeeper Grosk in Razor Hill.\030Welcome to Razor Hill!\030A Peon's Burden\0312,1,10,2,257,2,6786\0302,13,28,2,257,2,6786\0302,33,59,2,257,1,6786\0302,62,127,2,257,1,6786\0302,130,228,2,259,1,6786\0302,231,259,2,257,1,6786\0302,262,351,2,257,1,6786\0302,356,378,2,257,2,6786\0302,381,415,2,257,1,6786\0302,418,434,2,257,1,6786\0302,439,487,2,257,1,6786\0302,490,499,2,257,1,6786\0303,1,53,2,384,1,6786\0301,1,58,4,272,1,6928\0301,60,80,4,274,2,6928\0301,82,138,4,284,1,6928\0301,140,163,4,272,1,6928\0301,168,200,4,272,1,6928\0301,202,237,4,272,1,6928\0301,239,288,4,272,1,6928\0301,293,333,4,272,1,6928\0301,335,466,4,272,4,6928\0304,1,22,3,256,1,6928\03114901,2,9,Peon\0306928,2,11,Innkeeper Grosk\0306928,2,13,Innkeeper Grosk\0306786,4,14,Ukor\0312,14,1411,0,\0302,0,0,5,Valley of Trials\0302,0,0,7,Razor Hill\0302,0,0,11,Innkeeper Grosk\0302,0,0,11,Razor Hill\0302,0,0,13,Innkeeper Grosk\0302,0,0,13,Razor Hill\0304,0,0,14,Valley of Trials\0303,0,0,23,Razor Hill\031\031",[217]="PARTIAL\031conflict,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Most excellent, $N! You have brought hope to Loch Modan. With Grawmug dead, we stand a better chance of seeing the Troggs eliminated from the land.\030$N, our scouts have identified the leader of this recent Trogg incursion.  It appears that these beasts in Loch Modan are following the lead of a chieftain named Grawmug.  Grawmug is heavily guarded, however.  Two of his most elite guards, Gnasher and Brawler, never leave his side.$B$BIf you feel yourself worthy, $N, I want you to lead the assassination mission on Grawmug and his two thugs.  With the Trogg leadership dead, we just might stand a chance at pushing these beasts back into the ground.\030Kill the Trogg leader, Grawmug, and his two guards, Gnasher and Brawler then report back to Captain Rugelfuss in the southern guard tower.\030Grawmug and his two guards, Gnasher and Brawler, are still alive. Your mission is not complete until all 3 have been brought to death. The Dwarven empire is counting on you, $N.\030In Defense of the King's Lands\0312,1,73,2,257,1,1092\0302,76,170,2,257,1,1092\0302,173,208,2,257,1,1092\0302,211,282,2,257,1,1092\0302,287,393,2,259,4,1092\0302,396,501,2,257,4,1092\0303,1,138,2,384,1,1092\0301,1,19,4,272,1,1092\0301,21,56,4,274,3,1092\0301,58,147,4,304,1,1092\0304,1,65,3,256,1,1092\0304,67,134,3,256,1,1092\0304,136,177,3,256,1,1092\0311205,2,2,Grawmug\0301205,2,3,Grawmug\0301206,2,4,Gnasher\0301207,2,4,Brawler\0301205,2,5,Grawmug\0301205,2,7,Grawmug\0301206,2,7,Gnasher\0301207,2,7,Brawler\0301092,2,7,Captain Rugelfuss\0301205,4,10,Grawmug\0301205,3,11,Grawmug\0301206,3,11,Gnasher\0301207,3,11,Brawler\0312,38,1432,0,\0302,0,0,2,Loch Modan\0302,0,0,7,Captain Rugelfuss\0304,0,0,9,Loch Modan\031263,19,263,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,1205,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Grawmug\030NPC,1206,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Gnasher\030NPC,1207,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Brawler",[2178]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Fantastic! Try it and tell me what you think, $N!\030Do you smell that delicious aroma? It's my secret recipe, $N--fresh strider stew. Delicious!$B$BPerhaps you would be interested in learning the recipe?$B$BBefore I teach you the recipe, you will need to prove that you can handle the beasts.$B$BNow, I don't expect you to go out and tame one and ride it back to me, but if you can kill a few and bring back some of their succulent meat, I may be persuaded to show you the ways of strider stew.\030Bring back 5 Strider Meat to Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine.\030The pot is empty and I'm hungry! What's taking you so long?\030Easy Strider Living\0312,1,34,2,257,2,3702\0302,36,81,2,257,1,3702\0302,83,92,2,257,1,3702\0302,97,151,2,257,4,3702\0302,156,240,2,259,3,3702\0302,245,442,2,257,4,3702\0303,1,64,2,384,1,3702\0301,1,10,4,272,1,3702\0301,12,49,4,272,1,3702\0304,1,32,3,256,1,3702\0304,34,59,3,256,2,3702\0313702,2,7,Alanndarian Nightsong\0312,0,0,7,Alanndarian Nightsong\0302,0,0,7,Auberdine\031\031ITEM,5469,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[218]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Wonderful, $N! Many thanks for retrieving my notebook. Well, it would seem that the troll situation here in Coldridge Valley is under control and not much cause for worry.$B$BAfter I put the finishing touches on my report, I'll need someone to courier it to my brother Senir.\030My journal! They took it away to the cave. The one that had it... It was a big brute with some odd markings on his skin and face. I didn't get a much better look than that.$B$BYou've had some luck with the trolls, maybe you could go get it back for me?\030Grelin Whitebeard wants you to kill Grik'nir the Cold, and retrieve his journal.\030$N! Any luck?\030The Stolen Journal\0312,1,11,2,257,1,786\0302,13,42,2,257,1,786\0302,44,65,2,257,1,786\0302,67,129,2,257,1,786\0302,131,172,2,257,1,786\0302,177,252,2,257,4,786\0303,1,80,2,386,1,786\0301,1,14,4,272,1,786\0301,16,54,4,272,1,786\0301,56,171,4,272,4,786\0301,176,275,4,274,1,786\0304,5,13,3,256,2,786\031786,2,7,Grelin Whitebeard\030808,2,7,Grik'nir the Cold\0312,132,1426,0,\0304,0,0,10,Coldridge Valley\031182,19,182,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030282,23,282,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,2004,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[219]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031You have served the Kingdom well, $C. Thank you for assisting Corporal Keeshan with his escape from those dreaded Blackrock Orcs. You shall be rewarded for your brave acts this day.\030At last, friends of the Alliance!$B$BHelp... please... $B$BThe last thing I remember these foul Orcs overpowered our regiment.  Most the men were killed. I took a strong blow to the head and everything went black. Now I am held captive in this cave.  Help me, I am hurt badly.$B$BI'll need help getting back to town... please... you're my last hope...\030Protect Corporal Keeshan on the journey back to Redridge.\030Escort Corporal Keeshan back to Redridge\030Yes?\030Missing In Action\0312,1,33,2,257,1,349\0302,38,44,2,257,1,349\0302,46,54,2,257,1,349\0302,60,126,2,257,1,349\0302,129,153,2,257,1,349\0302,155,213,2,257,1,349\0302,215,249,2,261,1,349\0302,252,276,2,257,1,349\0302,281,318,2,259,1,349\0302,320,328,2,257,1,349\0302,330,351,2,259,3,349\0303,1,57,2,396,1,349\0301,1,37,4,272,1,382\0301,39,129,4,272,1,382\0301,131,181,4,272,3,382\0305,1,4,3,256,2,382\0304,1,40,3,384,1,349\031349,2,12,Corporal Keeshan\030349,4,14,Corporal Keeshan\030349,3,17,Corporal Keeshan\0312,44,1433,0,\0302,0,0,12,Redridge\0303,0,0,17,Redridge\031\031",[2198]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes... I am the jeweler who made this necklace. I also am not in the business of handing out information as though it were free. Information is never free, friend. If I am going to help you out, you need to help ME out first.\030You have found a tarnished necklace, though the tarnish belies intricate and magical craftsmanship.  The necklace has been shattered, as its setting appears to be missing three gems.  On the underside of the necklace is the faint imprint of the city seal for Ironforge.  Below the seal are three tiny, engraved letters: \"TdK\".$B$BIf there is anything to be gleaned from the necklace, you will need to learn about its origins.  Perhaps the seal and the initials are a start...\030Search for the original creator of the shattered necklace to learn of its potential value.\030You've got the wrong gnome, pal! I was never there! You can't prove anything!$B$BWait a second... who are you? What the... where did you find this necklace at?\030The Shattered Necklace\0312,1,99,2,257,1,0\0302,102,182,2,261,1,0\0302,185,269,2,257,1,0\0302,272,326,2,257,1,0\0302,331,425,2,259,4,0\0302,428,475,2,257,4,0\0303,1,90,2,384,1,0\0301,1,6,4,272,1,6826\0301,8,47,4,272,1,6826\0301,49,128,4,272,1,6826\0301,130,163,4,272,1,6826\0301,165,225,4,274,4,6826\0304,1,32,3,256,1,6826\0304,34,51,3,256,1,6826\0304,53,77,3,256,1,6826\0304,82,97,3,256,1,6826\0304,99,110,3,256,2,6826\0304,112,122,3,256,1,6826\0304,124,159,3,256,2,6826\031\0312,1517,1418,0,\0312199,23,2199,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7666,STARTER,?,10,",[2199]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You're all right in my book; I don't care what everyone else has been saying... I kid, I kid!  Seriously, thank you my friend.$B$BNow, the necklace you have is one of my finest creations, but it is missing three gems that help bind magic power to it.  I crafted it for a paladin some time ago.  He was on a self-appointed quest to clear out the \"evil taint\" present at an excavation site in the Badlands called Uldaman.$B$BWell... that paladin died in Uldaman, and that was just the beginning of my woes.\030I am a jeweler of great renown here in Ironforge!  Well, former renown anyway... I have fallen onto hard times due to the chicanery of a competitor!  A bad reputation in this business spells financial disaster.  As a result, I find myself without a copper to my good-though-currently-sullied name.$B$BI want you to get me five silver bars to finish an order I received - the first in what seems like an eternity.$B$BYou get me those five silver bars, and I'll answer your questions on the necklace.\030Bring five silver bars to Talvash del Kissel in Ironforge.\030Have you got the five silver bars I asked for?  I will share my sad tale of woe with you concerning the necklace you now possess... but only after I get those bars!  Please, help a gnome out, won't ya?\030Lore for a Price\0312,1,49,2,257,1,6826\0302,52,80,2,257,1,6826\0302,82,148,2,257,1,6826\0302,151,210,2,257,1,6826\0302,213,297,2,257,1,6826\0302,302,412,2,259,4,6826\0302,417,498,2,257,1,6826\0303,1,58,2,384,1,6826\0301,1,79,4,272,1,6826\0301,81,93,4,272,1,6826\0301,96,126,4,272,1,6826\0301,131,250,4,276,1,6826\0301,253,293,4,272,1,6826\0301,296,419,4,272,1,6826\0301,424,430,4,272,1,6826\0301,432,504,4,272,1,6826\0304,1,46,3,256,2,6826\0304,49,131,3,256,3,6826\0304,133,164,3,256,1,6826\0304,167,201,3,256,2,6826\0316826,2,8,Talvash del Kissel\0312,1517,1418,0,\0302,0,0,1,Ironforge\0302,0,0,8,Talvash\0302,0,0,8,Ironforge\0304,0,0,14,Badlands\0304,0,0,16,Uldaman\0312198,19,2198,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302200,23,2200,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,2842,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[22]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031These are just perfect, $N! Thank you so much. Farmer Saldean and I are going to feast tonight. And here is a little something for you, for the hard work. You didn't think I was going to let a $C like you go hungry, did you?\030The onions are peeled.  The garlic is minced.  The rosemary is crushed.  The crust has been baked.  The dill weed is chopped.  The gravy is simmering.  Now all I need for my famous meat pie are 8 Goretusk Livers!\030Salma Saldean needs 8 Goretusk livers to make a Goretusk Liver Pie.\030All I need for my famous meat pie are 8 Goretusk Livers!\030Goretusk Liver Pie\0312,1,22,2,257,1,235\0302,25,45,2,257,1,235\0302,48,71,2,257,1,235\0302,74,98,2,257,1,235\0302,101,125,2,257,1,235\0302,128,150,2,257,1,235\0302,153,212,2,259,1,235\0303,1,67,2,386,1,235\0301,1,27,4,272,1,235\0301,29,46,4,272,1,235\0301,48,95,4,272,3,235\0301,97,154,4,272,1,235\0301,156,224,4,272,2,235\0304,1,56,3,258,1,235\031157,2,7,Goretusk\030235,2,8,Salma Saldean\030157,2,8,Goretusk\030233,4,11,Farmer Saldean\030157,3,14,Goretusk\0312,40,1436,0,\031\031ITEM,723,OBJECTIVE,8,15,",[220]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, a vial of water created and blessed by Brine, and gathered by you, no less.$B$BThe liquid in this vial will be key in creating a sapta for you, but also used in one other task.$B$BThe sapta I create for you should be used to see the water spirits at the shrine in Silverpine Forest, south of the Undercity. The remaining drops, well, the remaining drops I will tell you about if you feel you are ready.$B$BAre you prepared for one more journey, $N?\030Islen will have one more task for you before rewarding you with your next totem. The vial of water I've given you is necessary for whatever that task is.$B$BGo now and find her. We shall meet again some day.\030Bring the Vial of Purest Water to Islen Waterseer in the Barrens.\030Hello again, $N. You're looking well.$B$BWhat brings you back to me so soon?\030Call of Water\0312,1,80,2,257,3,5899\0302,82,153,2,257,1,5899\0302,158,177,2,257,1,5899\0302,179,207,2,257,3,5899\0303,1,65,2,384,1,5899\0301,1,79,4,272,1,5901\0301,84,180,4,272,3,5901\0301,185,310,4,272,1,5901\0301,312,406,4,272,4,5901\0301,411,452,4,272,2,5901\0304,1,16,3,256,1,5901\0304,18,37,3,256,1,5901\0304,42,76,3,256,2,5901\0315901,2,5,Islen Waterseer\0305899,4,6,Brine\0312,0,0,5,Islen Waterseer\0302,0,0,5,Barrens\0304,0,0,8,Silverpine Forest\0304,0,0,8,Undercity\0311534,19,1534,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\03063,23,63,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2200]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Remains of a paladin: Reading the journal reveals that after much effort, the paladin had identified the location of all three missing gems:$B$BThe Shadowforge dwarves hid the ruby in their barricaded area as they battled the Troggs for control of Uldaman.$B$BThe troggs stashed the topaz in an urn located near some unusual inhabitants of Uldaman - Alliance dwarves!$B$BFinally, the trogg elder himself took the sapphire as his own.\030A competitor of mine started a rumor that my necklace cursed the paladin.  Needless to say, no one wants to buy cursed items from a jeweler.$B$B$N, I'll make you a deal - find the gems and I'll reassemble the necklace, so long as you'll advertise that I do NOT make cursed items!$B$BTry looking for clues in Uldaman; maybe see if the paladin's body is down there, since he's the one who we know had it last!  When you find the gems you should use this; it'll allow you to contact me here in Ironforge.\030Search for clues as to the current disposition of Talvash's necklace within Uldaman.  The slain paladin he mentioned was the person who had it last.\030\030Back to Uldaman\0312,1,73,2,261,1,6826\0302,76,140,2,263,1,6826\0302,145,279,2,261,1,6826\0302,284,407,2,257,4,6826\0302,410,501,2,257,1,6826\0303,1,84,2,384,1,6826\0303,87,148,2,388,1,6826\0301,1,140,4,276,1,6912\0301,145,256,4,272,1,6912\0301,261,367,4,272,1,6912\0301,372,433,4,272,1,6912\0316912,4,8,Remains of a Paladin\0312,1517,1418,0,\0302,0,0,4,Uldaman\0302,0,0,5,Ironforge\0302,0,0,6,Uldaman\0312199,19,2199,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302201,23,2201,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2201]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yep, those indeed are the three gems.  Good job!  Unfortunately, your work isn't quite over just yet.$B$BNo, I'm not trying to pull a fast one here, silly $C.  This is about making magic jewelry - Talvash del Kissel quality-level jewelry!  You need a strong power source to give it some oomph.  Well, that necklace has no more oomph to give.\030The paladin's journal has provided perhaps the only clues that Uldaman will yield as to the location of the necklace's gems.  If the paladin's scribing remains accurate, then the Shadowforge dwarves and the troggs that vie for control of the dig site will need to be dealt with.$B$BArmed with this knowledge, the search for the gems begins in earnest.  When all the gems have been acquired, Talvash in Ironforge should be notified via the Phial of Scrying as per his instructions.\030Find the ruby, sapphire, and topaz that are scattered throughout Uldaman.  Once acquired, contact Talvash del Kissel remotely by using the Phial of Scrying he previously gave you.$B$BFrom the journal, you know...$B* The ruby has been stashed in a barricaded Shadowforge area.$B* The topaz has been hidden in an urn in one of the Trogg areas, near some Alliance dwarves.$B$B* The sapphire has been claimed by Grimlok, the trogg leader.\030Talvash's image comes into focus from the waters of the scrying bowl.$B$B\"Wow, you're still alive! Did you manage to find the gems? Are you truly the savior of my reputation I have hoped for? Please tell me you didn't waste a charge on the phial just to chat; those things are NOT cheap, and I'm already in dire financial straits.\"\030Find the Gems\0312,1,124,2,257,4,6912\0302,127,278,2,259,4,6912\0302,283,351,2,257,1,6912\0302,354,480,2,257,1,6912\0303,1,73,2,384,1,6912\0303,76,179,2,384,1,6912\0303,184,212,2,384,1,6912\0303,215,275,2,384,1,6912\0303,278,369,2,384,1,6912\0303,374,434,2,384,1,6912\0301,1,37,4,272,1,0\0301,40,48,4,272,1,0\0301,51,101,4,272,1,0\0301,106,158,4,272,1,0\0301,161,238,4,272,1,0\0301,241,293,4,274,1,0\0301,296,341,4,272,1,0\0304,1,69,3,256,1,0\0304,74,98,3,256,1,0\0304,100,131,3,256,2,0\0304,133,191,3,256,2,0\0304,193,331,3,256,1,0\0316826,2,6,Talvash del Kissel\0304854,2,10,Grimlok\0306826,4,15,Talvash del Kissel\0312,1517,1418,0,\0302,0,0,4,Ironforge\0312200,19,2200,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302204,23,2204,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,112877,FINISHER,?,12,Talvash's Scrying Bowl\030ITEM,7669,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,7670,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,7671,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[2202]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done $N, you've proven your worth once again! The caps will be an interesting study, you betcha.$B$BAnd now, as promised, enjoy a taste of one of my more potent restorative brews from my personal stock...$B$BIf you are a skilled alchemist, then perhaps we might have some additional business to conduct. Regardless, I thank you for your assistance!\030I've heard about a newly discovered plant called the magenta fungus caps.  They grow in clusters at the Uldaman dig site and can be found in the early tunnels and deep within the less-explored areas.  I want to study their potential use in alchemy, and that's where you come in.$B$BFind the magenta cap clusters and bring me a dozen caps.  Be warned, the clusters may spew out poison spores if jostled.$B$BDo this for me, and I'll whip up a batch of one of my famous restorative elixirs for you!\030Bring 12 Magenta Fungus Caps to Jarkal Mossmeld in Kargath.\030Have you obtained the magenta fungus caps I need for my alchemical work? No caps - no reward!\030Uldaman Reagent Run\0312,1,73,2,257,1,6868\0302,76,199,2,257,1,6868\0302,202,278,2,259,1,6868\0302,283,338,2,257,1,6868\0302,341,402,2,261,4,6868\0302,407,495,2,257,1,6868\0303,1,59,2,384,1,6868\0301,1,50,4,272,1,6868\0301,52,101,4,272,3,6868\0301,106,209,4,272,1,6868\0301,214,308,4,272,4,6868\0301,310,353,4,272,1,6868\0304,1,72,3,258,2,6868\0304,74,93,3,256,1,6868\0316868,2,7,Jarkal Mossmeld\0312,1517,1418,0,\0302,0,0,2,Uldaman\0302,0,0,7,Jarkal Mossmeld\0302,0,0,7,Kargath\0312258,19,2258,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302203,23,2203,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,8047,OBJECTIVE,12,15,",[2203]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031From one alchemist to another, I salute you.  Here, take this recipe and commit it to your knowledge.  May it bring you the success and rewards that it has brought me over the years.\030You have been most helpful to me, $c.  I would reward you with the very recipe for the brew I gave you earlier... but I would ask of you a task that is quite dangerous.  Hear my request.$B$BThis lockbox contains three empty thaumaturgy vessels; they are imbued with an attunement aura that will drain the blood of a scorched guardian dragon.  Using one on the beast will anger it greatly, so be warned.  Once you have all three filled, bring them to me.$B$BDo this, and the recipe will be yours.\030Use the empty thaumaturgy vessels on scorched guardian dragons found in the Badlands.  Once you have them filled, bring them to Jarkal Mossmeld in Kargath.\030Have you used the vessels to get me the scorched guardian dragon blood I need?  Yes, I know it is a dangerous task... but the recipe for my restorative brew awaits your success.  Risk and reward, my friend... risk and reward...\030Badlands Reagent Run II\0312,1,37,2,257,1,6868\0302,40,113,2,257,4,6868\0302,115,168,2,257,4,6868\0302,171,186,2,257,1,6868\0302,191,341,2,257,3,6868\0302,344,402,2,257,3,6868\0302,405,453,2,257,1,6868\0302,458,495,2,257,3,6868\0303,1,85,2,384,1,6868\0303,88,155,2,384,1,6868\0301,1,44,4,272,1,6868\0301,47,101,4,272,1,6868\0301,104,182,4,272,1,6868\0304,1,78,3,258,2,6868\0304,81,117,3,256,1,6868\0304,119,177,3,256,1,6868\0304,180,208,3,264,1,6868\0304,210,227,3,264,1,6868\0312726,2,5,Scorched Guardian\03010430,2,6,The Beast\0302726,2,9,Scorched Guardian\0306868,2,10,Jarkal Mossmeld\0302726,3,14,Scorched Guardian\0312,3,1418,0,\0302,0,0,9,Badlands\0302,0,0,10,Jarkal Mossmeld\0302,0,0,10,Kargath\0312202,19,2202,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7867,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[2204]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well I'll be - I sure am glad to see you and this power source in one piece.  It will take me a moment to magically fuse the power source with the necklace now that the gems have been reunited with it.  Once it is done, however, the necklace will be yours!$B$BYou're excited, aren't you?  All tingly with anticipation?  Now where did I put that spell focus at...\030You are going to need to find some \"oomph\" for the necklace, and Uldaman is probably the best place for it, actually.  I guess there are a lot of constructs running around in there, yeah?  Well, take out the biggest, baddest construct in that place and grab its power source!  I am pretty sure I can fuse that source into the necklace.$B$BWithout that power source, fixing the necklace will be impossible.  Come back to me here to Ironforge when you have it, and we'll get it all fixed up for you!\030Obtain a power source from the most powerful construct you can find in Uldaman, and deliver it to Talvash del Kissel in Ironforge.\030You didn't even stop to tidy yourself up after leaving Uldaman, did you.  You just came straight here, lingering dungeon odors be damned.  Well, let's hope this visit is merely an odiferous one, and not a useless one to boot.$B$BDo you have the power source for the necklace?\030Restoring the Necklace\0312,1,117,2,259,3,0\0302,120,187,2,257,2,0\0302,190,275,2,257,1,0\0302,278,335,2,257,1,0\0302,340,405,2,257,3,0\0302,408,497,2,257,1,0\0303,1,130,2,384,1,0\0301,1,76,4,272,1,6826\0301,79,201,4,272,3,6826\0301,204,256,4,272,3,6826\0301,261,287,4,272,2,6826\0301,290,318,4,272,2,6826\0301,321,362,4,272,1,6826\0304,1,72,3,256,1,6826\0304,75,137,3,256,1,6826\0304,140,225,3,256,3,6826\0304,230,275,3,256,2,6826\0316826,2,7,Talvash del Kissel\0312,1517,1418,0,\0302,0,0,6,Ironforge\0302,0,0,7,Uldaman\0302,0,0,7,Talvash\0302,0,0,7,Ironforge\0312201,19,2201,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302361,23,2361,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,112877,GIVER,?,9,Talvash's Scrying Bowl\030ITEM,7672,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[2205]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You found me - and by looking at you, I'd say the run and subsequent search may have been a great strain on your system, both mentally and physically.$B$BWould you like Renzik to show you the way to an inn or are you ready for some work?\030The badge? Oh, it's nothing, fish - nothing you could handle anyhow. By the looks of you, I'd say Mathias is likely to mistake you for the cheese delivery $g boy:girl; instead of a proper rogue. Regardless, I've been assigned a job and I've made a promise to deliver on that job.$B$BSpeaking of which, deliver this package to Mathias and he may give you a small task or two.$B$BGet cracking. $B\030Deliver Keryn Sylvius's package to Master Mathias Shaw at the Stormwind Barracks.\030Can I help you, $C?\030Seek out SI: 7\0312,1,10,2,257,2,917\0302,12,68,2,257,4,917\0302,70,194,2,257,1,917\0302,196,279,2,257,1,917\0302,284,374,2,257,1,917\0302,379,391,2,257,1,917\0303,1,81,2,384,1,917\0301,1,150,4,272,1,332\0301,155,237,4,272,4,332\0304,1,19,3,256,2,332\031371,2,3,Girl\030917,2,7,Keryn Sylvius\030332,2,7,Master Mathias Shaw\0312,0,0,5,Mathias\0302,0,0,7,Master Mathias Shaw\0302,0,0,7,Stormwind Barracks\0312218,22,2218,UNKNOWN\0302241,22,2241,UNKNOWN\0302206,24,2206,UNKNOWN\031",[2206]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I am astonished... Astonished that Keryn finally found a recruit that could possibly have the makings of a proper $C. Take this blade, $N. A day will come when you will be called upon again to serve the SI:7. Hone your skills, keep your eyes open and that blade sharp.$B$BYou won't see us coming but you'll feel it when we get there...\030Our operatives in the field are reporting heavy Defias activity south of Goldshire. The reports indicate that the Defias have taken over Jerod's Landing and are now using it as a way to smuggle large quantities of contraband from Redridge to Westfall.$B$BI need you to infiltrate the dock house and get me that shipping schedule, $N. You will probably find it buried deep in the pockets of the Dockmaster.$B$B...and $N, should you be discovered, SI:7 will disavow all knowledge of your existence.\030Find the Defias Dockmaster and recover the Shipping Schedule for Master Mathias Shaw.$B\030Your mortality wanes with every moment you waste loitering in the barracks, $C.\030Snatch and Grab\0312,1,83,2,257,1,332\0302,85,251,2,257,1,332\0302,256,333,2,259,1,332\0302,335,405,2,257,3,332\0302,410,496,2,257,3,332\0303,1,85,2,384,1,332\0301,1,18,4,272,1,332\0301,20,117,4,272,4,332\0301,119,138,4,272,1,332\0301,140,208,4,272,3,332\0301,210,268,4,272,1,332\0301,273,335,4,272,1,332\0304,1,79,3,256,1,332\0316846,2,6,Defias Dockmaster\030332,2,6,Master Mathias Shaw\0312,0,0,1,Goldshire\0302,0,0,2,Redridge\0302,0,0,2,Westfall\031\031ITEM,7675,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[221]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You performed well against the Dark Runners, $N. But it seems as though their numbers are inexhaustible. Every time we make progress, more spring up to refill their ranks.$B$BWhat is the evil power that draws them here? Why have they come to disturb our unhappy realm...$B$BI will put my faith in Master Carevin. No doubt he will get to the bottom of the problem.\030You might have noticed some larger worgen wandering around with the Shadow Weavers in the woods? From what we can tell, these Dark Runners make up the bulk of the worgen numbers.$B$BOn my rangings, I've also noticed that they have overrun the Rotting Orchard southwest of town. These worgen are a bit tougher than the last you faced.$B$BBe on your guard.\030Kill 12 Nightbane Dark Runner worgen for Calor in Darkshire.\030Back so soon, $N? I hope you haven't come to tell me you've given up.\030Worgen in the Woods\0312,1,96,2,257,4,663\0302,98,178,2,257,1,663\0302,183,277,2,257,1,663\0302,279,333,2,257,1,663\0302,338,354,2,257,1,663\0303,1,60,2,384,1,663\0301,1,48,4,272,1,663\0301,50,104,4,272,4,663\0301,106,171,4,272,1,663\0301,176,219,4,272,2,663\0301,221,270,4,276,1,663\0301,275,312,4,272,3,663\0301,314,363,4,276,3,663\0304,1,17,3,256,2,663\0304,19,69,3,258,3,663\0314244,2,1,Shadow\030205,2,6,Nightbane Dark Runner\030663,2,6,Calor\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,6,Darkshire\0304,0,0,12,Master Carevin\031173,19,173,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030222,23,222,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,205,OBJECTIVE,12,13,Nightbane Dark Runner",[2218]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031So ye think yer a right scoundrel? Destined to be one o' Blackbeard's chosen few - an officer o' the Hidden Circle?$B$BOnly a good fer nothin' scallywag would think so highly o' hisself.$B$BThat's exactly what we be lookin' fer! Welcome aboard, $N!\030Another lost soul looking for guidance, eh? I suppose you want to find a purpose - your purpose. I've seen it a thousand times, another hero looking for work.$B$BWell, today's your lucky day, friend. Hogral's got the cure for your ailment.$B$BHere's what you do: Take this road here up to Ironforge and make your way to the Forlorn Cavern. Once there, locate the thieves' guild and speak with Hulfdan Blackbeard. He'll put you on the road to salvation.$B\030Speak with Hulfdan Blackbeard in Ironforge.\030\030Road to Salvation\0312,1,43,2,261,2,1234\0302,45,96,2,259,1,1234\0302,98,158,2,257,1,1234\0302,163,199,2,257,1,1234\0302,201,239,2,257,1,1234\0302,244,339,2,257,1,1234\0302,341,412,2,257,1,1234\0302,414,452,2,257,1,1234\0303,1,43,2,384,1,1234\0301,1,34,4,272,2,5165\0301,36,115,4,272,2,5165\0301,120,186,4,272,4,5165\0301,191,228,4,272,1,5165\0301,230,248,4,272,1,5165\0311531,2,1,Lost Soul\0305165,2,7,Hulfdan Blackbeard\0305165,2,9,Hulfdan Blackbeard\0312,0,0,6,Ironforge\0302,0,0,6,Forlorn Cavern\0302,0,0,9,Ironforge\0312205,22,2205,UNKNOWN\0302241,22,2241,UNKNOWN\0302238,23,2238,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302238,24,2238,UNKNOWN\031",[222]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031$N, to be honest with you, I did not believe that you would get this far, but you are clearly a $C to be reckoned with. In fact, if you wish to formally join Master Carevin's struggle, I will gladly write for you a letter of recommendation.\030Your previous accomplishments have convinced me that you are ready to take on the toughest worgen infesting the woods.$B$BOf the worgen that have made their new home here, the Vile Fangs and the Tainted Ones have proven the most dangerous. They've settled down near some of the caves and in the mine to the south.$B$BFrom far away you can even see the light from their bonfires...\030Kill 8 Nightbane Vile Fang and 8 Nightbane Tainted One worgen for Calor in Darkshire.\030Intimidating beasts aren't they? But have no fear, $N, those who stand for the Light will never fall!\030Worgen in the Woods\0312,1,118,2,257,1,663\0302,123,239,2,257,1,663\0302,241,313,2,257,1,663\0302,318,380,2,257,1,663\0303,1,85,2,384,1,663\0301,1,119,4,272,4,663\0301,121,240,4,274,4,663\0304,1,32,3,256,2,663\0304,34,101,3,256,3,663\031206,2,5,Nightbane Vile Fang\03014892,2,5,Fang\030920,2,5,Nightbane Tainted One\030663,2,5,Calor\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,5,Darkshire\031221,19,221,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030223,23,223,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,206,OBJECTIVE,8,13,Nightbane Vile Fang\030NPC,920,OBJECTIVE,8,13,Nightbane Tainted One",[223]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Excuse me for my cold reception, $N, but as I'm sure you can tell, I am an extremely busy man. I see that you have impressed Calor--and I assure you, that is no small feat--and that he has given his recommendation.$B$BThere are unsavory types afoot, $N, and we can use the help of all who have proven themselves. We battle against demons, the undead, and those who would provide them aid. Be vigilant, be wary, and trust none who would not give aid to our cause.$B$BGlory under the Light.\030Here you go, $n. Bring this message to Master Carevin.$B$B<He quickly removes a piece of faded parchment and offers it to you.>$B$BA few more like you, and we will outnumber the Night Watch! Perhaps then we could complete the work that we few carry on today.\030Bring Calor's note to Jonathan Carevin.\030Yes, what is it? Make it quick, I've pressing matters to attend to.\030Worgen in the Woods\0312,1,16,2,257,1,663\0302,18,54,2,257,1,663\0302,59,127,2,257,1,663\0302,132,190,2,257,3,663\0302,192,258,2,257,4,663\0303,1,39,2,384,1,663\0301,1,94,4,272,1,661\0301,96,214,4,272,1,661\0301,219,312,4,272,1,661\0301,314,388,4,276,4,661\0301,390,462,4,272,4,661\0301,467,488,4,272,1,661\0304,1,16,3,256,2,661\0304,18,67,3,256,1,661\031661,2,6,Jonathan Carevin\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,2,Master Carevin\0302,0,0,6,Jonathan Carevin\031222,19,222,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2238]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Shhhh! Keep it down you daft fool. They'll hear us.\030Ye see, the King be strip mining the quarry fer ore and gems. More riches than any one dwarf should see in ten lifetimes.$B$BThe Hidden Circle has values, $N. We value valuables. Can ye understand?$B$BNow we feels the King should be sharing some of that booty, but we don't want ol' 'Stinkbeard' to know he's sharin' - if ye catch me drift.$B$BWe needs ye to speak with Onin MacHammar over by Gnomeregan and bring back a report. The crafty dwarf has hidden hisself amongst the lepers. Be careful.\030Find Onin MacHammar by Gnomeregan.\030\030Simple Subterfugin'\0312,1,61,2,257,1,5165\0302,63,121,2,257,1,5165\0302,126,158,2,257,1,5165\0302,160,178,2,257,1,5165\0302,180,197,2,257,2,5165\0302,202,340,2,257,4,5165\0302,345,428,2,259,1,5165\0302,430,484,2,257,1,5165\0302,486,496,2,257,1,5165\0303,1,34,2,384,1,5165\0301,1,6,4,272,1,6886\0301,8,34,4,272,1,6886\0301,36,51,4,272,1,6886\0316886,2,7,Onin MacHammar\0306886,2,10,Onin MacHammar\031\0312239,23,2239,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2239]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Long route? In the name o' me own beard!$B$BYe done good, $N. Take this dagger and be gone with ye. The Circle will call upon ye again when step three be ready to be set into motion.$B$BWhat's step three? It comes right after step two - me putting me boot up yer backside.$B$BInterested?\030The Quarry? Yap, I see those monstrous armored steam tanks come by this post near every day.$B$BMy contacts to the east tell me that the tank starts off at Ironforge, makes a pickup at the Gol'Bolar Quarry, stops over at Kharanos to refuel and then for some blasted reason, it takes the long way around past Gnomeregan, before reaching Ironforge to drop off the shipment.$B$BIt's all in the report, $r. Take it back to Hulfdan so he can plan the next step.$B\030Take Onin's Report back to Hulfdan in Ironforge.\030Did ye enjoy the stench of leper gnome? I only ask because ye got a crazy smile on yer face.$B$BWhat news do ye bring from Onin?\030Onin's Report\0312,1,11,2,257,2,6886\0302,13,92,2,257,1,6886\0302,97,371,2,257,1,6886\0302,376,402,2,257,1,6886\0302,404,456,2,257,1,6886\0303,1,48,2,384,1,6886\0301,1,11,4,272,2,5165\0301,13,40,4,272,1,5165\0301,45,61,4,272,1,5165\0301,63,99,4,272,1,5165\0301,101,182,4,272,3,5165\0301,187,204,4,272,2,5165\0301,206,272,4,272,1,5165\0301,277,287,4,272,2,5165\0304,1,39,3,256,2,5165\0304,41,92,3,258,1,5165\0304,97,128,3,256,2,5165\0311211,3,15,Leper Gnome\0312,0,0,3,Ironforge\0302,0,0,3,Gol'Bolar Quarry\0302,0,0,3,Kharanos\0302,0,0,5,Hulfdan\0302,0,0,6,Hulfdan\0302,0,0,6,Ironforge\0303,0,0,17,Onin\0312238,19,2238,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[224]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $N! You demonstrated uncanny courage on the battlefield. Our war against the Troggs will be won with efforts such as yours. You have served King Magni well.$B$BIf you fancy yourself well-suited for this kind of adventuring, I suggest you speak with Mountaineer Gravelgaw. The Captain has him assigned to a rough patrol that I am sure he can use some help with. Check with Gravelgaw just inside the tower.\030We need to protect the Loch, $N!  With so many of the King's soldiers fighting valiantly on remote battlefields, we've become overwhelmed on the home front.  Troggs are tunneling up from every crevice!  The Trogg infestation poses the largest threat to Ironforge.  These disgusting mutants must be destroyed.$B$BWe need you, brave adventurer, to venture forth and lay waste to the Trogg threat.  Slay 10 Stonesplinter Troggs and 10 Stonesplinter Scouts and report back.\030Mountaineer Cobbleflint of the southern guard tower wants you to kill 10 Stonesplinter Troggs and 10 Stonesplinter Scouts.\030Loch Modan is under siege, $N! We need every able-bodied member of the Alliance to aid our cause. Have you killed 10 Stonesplinter Troggs and 10 Stonesplinter Scouts yet?\030In Defense of the King's Lands\0312,1,32,2,271,1,1089\0302,35,156,2,261,1,1089\0302,159,201,2,257,1,1089\0302,204,263,2,261,1,1089\0302,266,308,2,261,1,1089\0302,313,394,2,263,1,1089\0302,397,469,2,257,1,1089\0303,1,122,2,386,1,1089\0301,1,14,4,272,1,1089\0301,16,67,4,272,1,1089\0301,69,134,4,276,3,1089\0301,136,167,4,272,1,1089\0301,172,282,4,272,4,1089\0301,284,371,4,272,1,1089\0301,373,415,4,272,1,1089\0304,1,30,3,256,1,1089\0304,32,97,3,258,1,1089\0304,99,170,3,256,2,1089\0311089,2,8,Mountaineer Cobbleflint\0301091,4,13,Mountaineer Gravelgaw\0312,38,1432,0,\0302,0,0,4,Ironforge\0302,0,0,6,Trogg\031237,23,237,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,1161,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Stonesplinter Trogg\030NPC,1162,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Stonesplinter Scout",[2240]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031You have seen the Chamber of Khaz'mul? Amazing! Baelog was sure it existed, but I must admit that I had my doubts.$B$BThank you, $N. With luck your finding will incite our leaders to renew their efforts to retake Uldaman. And if it is ever again under Ironforge control, then the secrets of the Chamber of Khaz'mul will be ours!\030Now for the task at hand.$B$BThere is a secret chamber, the Chamber of Khaz'mul, that must be explored.  The problem is that the chamber's behind a huge, locked door!  It's a lucky thing I know how to open it.$B$BI've described everything in my journal, here on the table.  My band and I are stuck here for now... so you, $N, must find the chamber of Khaz'mul for us!$B$BRead my journal, explore the chamber, then report to Prospector Stormpike at the Explorers' League in Ironforge.\030Read Baelog's Journal, explore the hidden chamber, then report to Prospector Stormpike.\030Explore the Hidden Chamber\030Do you have something to report?\030The Hidden Chamber\0312,1,25,2,257,1,6906\0302,30,103,2,257,1,6906\0302,106,166,2,261,1,6906\0302,169,209,2,257,1,6906\0302,214,272,2,257,1,6906\0302,275,313,2,257,1,6906\0302,315,367,2,257,1,6906\0302,372,483,2,257,1,6906\0303,1,87,2,384,1,6906\0301,1,38,4,272,2,1356\0301,40,47,4,272,1,1356\0301,49,114,4,272,1,1356\0301,119,132,4,272,1,1356\0301,134,221,4,272,3,1356\0301,223,328,4,272,4,1356\0305,1,32,3,256,2,1356\0304,1,26,3,384,1,6906\0311356,2,8,Prospector Stormpike\0301356,2,9,Prospector Stormpike\0306906,4,12,Baelog\0312,1517,1418,0,\0302,0,0,8,Prospector Stormpike\0302,0,0,8,Explorers' League\0302,0,0,8,Ironforge\0302,0,0,9,Prospector Stormpike\0312398,19,2398,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2241]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Had I saved every flower that dolt, Jannok, had sent me, I would have had the means to open a shop. Regardless, it seems as if Jannok's latest courier may prove to be useful.Interested in some work, $C?\030They say I'm 'lovestruck,' whatever that means.$B$BSure, I spend my every waking moment thinking about Syurna. Sure, my home is full of paintings and drawings of Syurna. Sure, I often go days without eating, sleeping, or drinking, while I lament about the love we could have had. Is that so wrong?$B$BNow she won't see me! ME! I've tried sending her messages but she won't even talk to another person unless they are a rogue.$B$BCould you deliver this flower to her? Don't forget to tell her it's from Jannok.\030Take Jannok's Rose to Syurna in Darnassus.\030Oh, isn't this wonderful. You've brought flowers for your own funeral.\030The Apple Falls\0312,1,47,2,257,1,3599\0302,52,110,2,257,1,3599\0302,112,169,2,257,1,3599\0302,171,279,2,257,4,3599\0302,281,297,2,257,2,3599\0302,302,322,2,257,1,3599\0302,328,425,2,265,4,3599\0302,430,466,2,257,4,3599\0302,468,509,2,257,1,3599\0303,1,42,2,384,1,3599\0301,1,99,4,272,4,4163\0301,101,202,4,272,4,4163\0304,1,25,3,256,1,4163\0304,27,70,3,256,1,4163\0314163,2,2,Syurna\0304163,2,3,Syurna\0304163,2,10,Syurna\0312,0,0,9,Jannok\0302,0,0,10,Syurna\0302,0,0,10,Darnassus\0312205,22,2205,UNKNOWN\0302218,22,2218,UNKNOWN\0302242,24,2242,UNKNOWN\031",[2242]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is grim news, $N. It would seem that the sickness which has gripped the forests and rivers of Darkshore has begun to taint our home.$B$BYou have served us well, but there is nothing more you can do here. Take this blade as a reward for your service to Teldrassil.\030We believe there is one being that may be able to help us understand what is happening to the forests of Teldrassil. Unfortunately, getting the creature to cooperate has proven disastrous.$B$BHe hides on a branch at the outskirts of the Oracle Glade. All who have so far approached the satyr, whether through force or diplomacy, have met with doom. Perhaps stealth is the answer, $N.$B$BFind what Sethir the Ancient carries in his packs and report back to me.$B\030Find Sethir the Ancient and bring back any clues that you may discover to Syurna.$B\030Have you anything to report from Sethir the Ancient, $N?\030Destiny Calls\0312,1,116,2,257,4,4163\0302,118,188,2,257,1,4163\0302,193,250,2,257,1,4163\0302,252,348,2,257,1,4163\0302,350,383,2,257,4,4163\0302,388,459,2,321,1,4163\0303,1,81,2,448,1,4163\0301,1,22,4,272,1,4163\0301,24,137,4,272,4,4163\0301,142,208,4,272,1,4163\0301,210,268,4,272,1,4163\0304,1,56,3,320,2,4163\0316909,2,6,Sethir the Ancient\0306909,2,7,Sethir the Ancient\0304163,2,7,Syurna\0306909,3,12,Sethir the Ancient\0312,0,0,7,Syurna\0304,0,0,11,Teldrassil\0303,0,0,12,Sethir the Ancient\031\031ITEM,7737,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[225]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Morgan Ladimore?$B$BAhh, yes, of course. His was a long and sorrowful tale. I knew him, well, before he left for the war, but that was the last time I saw him. A noble and good man, he was, but he suffered a bad end.$B$BHere, I should have something here that can tell the tale better than my own recollections...\030The weathered grave marker reads simply:$B$BMORGAN LADIMORE$B$B<Upon further examination, you notice that dirt over the grave has been recently disturbed, and that a good amount of the dirt seems to have been displaced...>\030Speak with Sirra Von'Indi in Darkshire.\030\030The Weathered Grave\0312,1,40,2,257,1,0\0302,45,59,2,257,1,0\0302,64,222,2,257,4,0\0303,1,39,2,384,1,0\0301,1,16,4,272,2,268\0301,21,40,4,272,1,268\0301,42,75,4,272,1,268\0301,77,159,4,284,1,268\0301,161,216,4,272,1,268\0301,221,313,4,272,1,268\0313301,2,2,Morgan Ladimore\030268,2,4,Sirra Von'Indi\0303301,4,5,Morgan Ladimore\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,4,Darkshire\031227,23,227,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,61,GIVER,?,9,A Weathered Grave",[2258]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, well done! These should last me for a little while, at least. Here is your pay as promised.$B$BIf you're interested, I have some more reagents I could use. These, however, are only found in the depths of the Uldaman excavation. They will not be easy to get, but I will make it worth your while if you are interested in helping me again.$B$BPerhaps something more than some shiny coins, yes?\030$N, I could use your aid if you're up for it.  I am an alchemist of some note, and I seek your aid in acquiring some reagents found out in the Badlands.$B$BI need the following items to replenish my stocks: five buzzard gizzards, ten crag coyote fangs, and five rock elemental shards.  Obviously, you can get them off of the beasties themselves; if you're not the fighting type, then find friends who are.$B$BAcquire these items for me, you'll get some coin out of the deal.  Watcha wanna do?\030Bring 5 Buzzard Gizzards, 10 Crag Coyote Fangs, and  5 Rock Elemental Shards to Jarkal Mossmeld in Kargath, Badlands.\030Have you gotten the things I need yet? You won't get paid unless you bring me those reagents.\030Badlands Reagent Run\0312,1,45,2,257,4,6868\0302,48,152,2,259,1,6868\0302,157,284,2,259,1,6868\0302,287,405,2,261,4,6868\0302,410,474,2,257,1,6868\0302,477,492,2,257,2,6868\0303,1,117,2,384,1,6868\0301,1,14,4,272,1,6868\0301,16,65,4,272,1,6868\0301,67,95,4,272,1,6868\0301,100,159,4,272,4,6868\0301,161,231,4,272,1,6868\0301,233,340,4,272,4,6868\0301,345,394,4,272,4,6868\0304,1,38,3,258,2,6868\0304,40,93,3,264,4,6868\0312830,2,3,Buzzard\0302727,2,3,Crag Coyote\030834,2,3,Coyote\03092,2,3,Rock Elemental\0302830,2,7,Buzzard\0302727,2,7,Crag Coyote\030834,2,7,Coyote\03092,2,7,Rock Elemental\0306868,2,7,Jarkal Mossmeld\0312,3,1418,0,\0302,0,0,2,Badlands\0302,0,0,7,Jarkal Mossmeld\0302,0,0,7,Kargath\0312202,23,2202,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7847,OBJECTIVE,5,15,\030ITEM,7846,OBJECTIVE,10,15,\030ITEM,7848,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[2259]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It is time to branch out, $R - the world awaits.\030Do not worry, $N, I am not sending you to see Syurna. Erion requires your presence at the Cenarion Enclave. Make haste!\030Contact Erion Shadewhisper in Darnassus.$B\030\030Erion Shadewhisper\0312,1,53,2,257,1,3599\0302,55,107,2,257,1,3599\0302,109,119,2,257,1,3599\0303,1,40,2,384,1,3599\0301,1,48,4,272,1,4214\0314163,2,1,Syurna\0304214,2,4,Erion Shadewhisper\0312,0,0,2,Cenarion Enclave\0302,0,0,4,Darnassus\0312260,23,2260,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302260,24,2260,UNKNOWN\031",[226]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh good. You thinned out that pack quite a bit, and without those wolves nipping out our heels, we can bind our minds to dealing with Morbent Fel.$B$BHere, take some of these Flash Bundles. They make them in town, and a lot have been donated to Sven to help with his cause.\030Sven and I have dangerous days ahead of us, what with the Necromancer to the east and all.  And out here alone as we are, we have to hunt for our own food.  It seems every time I'm heading back to camp with some meat on me, starving or rabid dire wolves come out of the forest wanting a bite.  It goes without saying, living out here is dangerous work!$B$BBut if you can rid us of some of those wolves, we'd have an easier time of it.  They mostly prowl north and east of here, near the river.\030Kill 12 Starving Dire Wolves and 8 Rabid Dire Wolves, then return to Lars at Sven's Camp on the western border of Duskwood.\030You still hunting wolves...?\030Wolves at Our Heels\0312,1,90,2,257,1,893\0302,93,155,2,257,1,893\0302,158,292,2,269,4,893\0302,295,352,2,257,1,893\0302,357,434,2,257,4,893\0302,437,493,2,257,1,893\0303,1,123,2,396,1,893\0301,1,8,4,272,1,893\0301,10,146,4,272,1,893\0301,151,189,4,272,1,893\0301,191,273,4,272,1,893\0304,1,28,3,256,2,893\0318553,2,1,Necromancer\030893,2,7,Lars\0301200,4,9,Morbent Fel\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,7,Lars\0302,0,0,7,Sven's Camp\0304,0,0,11,Sven\031\031NPC,213,OBJECTIVE,12,13,Starving Dire Wolf\030NPC,565,OBJECTIVE,8,13,Rabid Dire Wolf",[2260]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have answered SI:7's calling, $N and journeyed from distant shores to join our ranks, however, there is much for you to learn.\030Word of your deeds has spread far and wide, $N. So far, in fact, that Stormwind Intelligence has asked for you by name.$B$BThe journey is taxing and not without peril, but an opportunity to train under SI:7 should not be taken lightly.$B$BA new world awaits you, $N. Make your way to Old Town in Stormwind and speak with Renzik \"The Shiv\" at SI:7 headquarters.$B\030Travel to Stormwind City and seek council with Renzik \"The Shiv.\"$B\030\030Erion's Behest\0312,1,47,2,257,1,4214\0302,49,119,2,257,1,4214\0302,124,235,2,257,1,4214\0302,240,266,2,257,1,4214\0302,268,360,2,257,1,4214\0303,1,65,2,386,1,4214\0301,1,130,4,272,1,6946\0316946,2,5,Renzik \"The Shiv\"\0312,0,0,5,Old Town\0302,0,0,5,Stormwind\0302,0,0,5,SI\0302,0,0,6,Stormwind City\0312281,24,2281,UNKNOWN\031",[227]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Morgan Ladimore? Never heard of...$B$BOh, you mean Mor'Ladim! I guess you haven't heard the story?$B$BWell, I'll give you the short version. A wandering undead calling itself Mor'Ladim has been wandering Duskwood. From what we've gathered, it appears to be the undead body of Morgan Ladimore, of whom you apparently know. He's been causing us all sorts of problems, attacking Watchmen on patrol and killing people.$B$B<She sizes you up.>$B$BYou seem to be capable enough, maybe you could lay him to rest.\030<He searches through the shelves and comes up with a leatherbound book.>$B$BIf you would like to know more, you might ask Althea, she's been the one to handle the... trouble... with him of late.\030Speak with Commander Althea Ebonlocke in Darkshire.\030\030Morgan Ladimore\0312,1,72,2,257,1,268\0302,77,165,2,257,4,268\0302,167,176,2,257,1,268\0302,178,194,2,257,1,268\0303,1,51,2,384,1,268\0301,1,16,4,272,2,264\0301,18,34,4,272,1,264\0301,39,61,4,272,1,264\0301,63,98,4,272,2,264\0301,103,140,4,272,1,264\0301,142,213,4,272,1,264\0301,215,321,4,272,4,264\0301,323,414,4,276,1,264\0301,419,437,4,272,1,264\0301,442,504,4,272,4,264\031264,2,5,Commander Althea Ebonlocke\0303301,4,6,Morgan Ladimore\030522,4,8,Mor'Ladim\030522,4,11,Mor'Ladim\0303301,4,12,Morgan Ladimore\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,5,Darkshire\031225,19,225,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030228,23,228,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2278]="PARTIAL\031characters,conflict,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Following the instructions of the stone watcher, you once again access the Discs of Norgannon now that you have learned about the history of the Earthen, the troggs, and the dwarves. A faint, brief hum is heard from within the discs. The stone watcher then speaks:$B$B\"The discs have now been synthesized. Access the Discs of Norgannon once more to receive your personal copy.\"\030The centerpieces of this treasure chamber are four huge platinum discs, each adorned with numerous sigils of an unknown origin.  Touching them makes your hand tingle.  Just after touching the discs, the visage of a large stone watcher springs forth.$B$B\"Salutations.  I am a keeper of knowledge.  The Creators' synthesis of the Earthen has been chronicled and stored here for this world in the Discs of Norgannon.\"$B$BYou have uncovered a wealth of previously undiscovered worldly lore!\030Speak with stone watcher and learn what ancient lore it keeps.  Once you have learned what lore it has to offer, activate the Discs of Norgannon.\030Learn what lore that the stone watcher has to offer\030The voice of the stone watcher seems to resonate within your very inner being:$B$B\"You must first satisfy the data assimilation prerequisite of Discs of Norgannon; once you fulfill this requirement, you will then be permitted to obtain a portable version of the stored data. Please be sure you have fully explored the information within this repository first.\"\030The Platinum Discs\0312,1,127,2,257,1,0\0302,130,166,2,257,1,0\0302,169,249,2,257,1,0\0302,254,266,2,257,1,0\0302,269,295,2,257,1,0\0302,298,414,2,257,1,0\0302,419,486,2,257,1,0\0303,1,62,2,448,1,0\0303,65,145,2,384,1,0\0301,1,182,4,368,1,0\0301,184,233,4,272,1,0\0301,235,264,4,272,1,0\0301,269,305,4,272,1,0\0301,307,377,4,272,1,0\0305,1,78,3,256,4,0\0305,83,274,3,256,3,0\0305,276,360,3,256,1,0\0304,1,51,3,384,1,0\031\0312,1517,1418,0,\0302,0,0,6,Discs of Norgannon\031\031OBJECT,131474,GIVER,?,9,The Discs of Norgannon\030OBJECT,131474,FINISHER,?,12,The Discs of Norgannon",[2279]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031What do you have there... oh my.  You found this where?$B$BNo, really?$B$BYou spoke to whom about what?$B$BNO, REALLY?!$B$BMy fine $C, you may have just made the archaeological find of the year!  By the Gods who am I kidding, the find of the century!  If these discs are what I think them to be, then this could be the very key we have been looking for!  This may well prove outright once and for all the legitimacy of the Dwarves' enchanted creation!\030Touching the Discs of Norgannon once again makes your hand tingle.  This time, however, a strange grinding noise is heard from inside the discs.$B$BYour backpack suddenly becomes heavier than it was before.  Inside, you discover a miniature version of the discs!$B$BNo doubt, an item of this sort would be invaluable for someone interested in the ancient history of Azeroth.  The Explorers' League in Ironforge is such a group, known throughout the Alliance; perhaps they can make good use of it.\030Take the miniature version of the Discs of Norgannon to the Explorers' League in Ironforge.\030Yes, may I help you with something?  I assure you I am a very busy right now.  If it is grave importance to the Explorers' League, however, then I am all ears!\030The Platinum Discs\0312,1,66,2,257,1,0\0302,69,144,2,257,1,0\0302,149,206,2,257,1,0\0302,209,262,2,257,1,0\0302,267,374,2,321,4,0\0302,377,496,2,257,4,0\0303,1,91,2,384,1,0\0301,1,25,4,272,1,5387\0301,35,55,4,272,2,5387\0301,60,70,4,272,2,5387\0301,75,103,4,272,2,5387\0301,108,119,4,272,2,5387\0301,124,194,4,272,1,5387\0301,197,250,4,272,1,5387\0301,253,353,4,272,4,5387\0301,356,451,4,272,1,5387\0304,1,35,3,256,2,5387\0304,38,77,3,256,1,5387\0304,80,159,3,256,4,5387\031\0312,1517,1418,0,\0302,0,0,6,Ironforge\0302,0,0,7,Explorers' League\0302,0,0,7,Ironforge\0303,0,0,19,Explorers' League\0312278,19,2278,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302439,23,2439,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,131474,GIVER,?,9,The Discs of Norgannon",[228]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You killed him? That's no small accomplishment, $N! On behalf of the people of Darkshire and the Night Watch, I thank you.$B$BAh... there is one small matter, however...\030From what my scouts tell me, Mor'Ladim wanders throughout Duskwood, following a strange and meandering path through the cemetery. We buried him out past the house on the hill, you know where that is?$B$BThere isn't anything I can do to help you, but I wish you good luck.\030Kill Mor'Ladim, then return his skull to Commander Althea Ebonlocke in Darkshire.\030I don't blame you if you're having trouble with him, $N. Some of our strongest Watchers have been lost to Mor'Ladim.\030Mor'Ladim\0312,1,129,2,257,1,264\0302,131,199,2,257,2,264\0302,204,271,2,259,3,264\0303,1,81,2,384,1,264\0301,1,15,4,272,2,264\0301,17,51,4,272,1,264\0301,53,122,4,272,1,264\0301,133,169,4,272,1,264\0304,1,56,3,256,4,264\0304,58,116,3,260,1,264\031522,2,1,Mor'Ladim\030522,2,4,Mor'Ladim\030264,2,4,Commander Althea Ebonlocke\030522,3,10,Mor'Ladim\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,4,Commander Althea Ebonlocke\0302,0,0,4,Darkshire\0303,0,0,10,Mor'Ladim\031227,19,227,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030229,23,229,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3514,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[2280]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031What are these here then?$B$BImpressive, young one! These discs, in them I sense secrets that the earth has held on to tightly for many years. You were very wise to bring them here to me.\030Touching the Discs of Norgannon once again makes your hand tingle.  This time, however, a strange grinding noise is heard from inside the discs.$B$BYour backpack suddenly becomes heavier than it was before.  Inside, you discover a miniature version of the discs!$B$BNo doubt, an item of this sort would be invaluable for someone interested in the ancient history of Azeroth.  The sages of Thunder Bluff are such historians, known throughout the Horde; perhaps they can make good use of it.\030Take the miniature version of the Discs of Norgannon to the one of the sages in Thunder Bluff.\030Yes young one, I see you marching into my tent with intensity in your stride... with determination in your purpose. You seek my counsel is some matter of grave importance to the Horde? Perhaps you wish a mystery of the universe revealed to you?\030The Platinum Discs\0312,1,66,2,257,1,0\0302,69,144,2,257,1,0\0302,149,206,2,257,1,0\0302,209,262,2,257,1,0\0302,267,374,2,321,4,0\0302,377,489,2,257,4,0\0303,1,94,2,384,1,0\0301,1,25,4,272,2,3978\0301,30,51,4,272,1,3978\0301,53,142,4,272,1,3978\0301,144,187,4,272,1,3978\0304,1,79,3,256,1,3978\0304,81,115,3,256,1,3978\0304,117,184,3,258,2,3978\0304,186,244,3,258,4,3978\031\0312,1517,1418,0,\0302,0,0,7,Thunder Bluff\0303,0,0,14,Horde\0312278,19,2278,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302440,23,2440,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,131474,GIVER,?,9,The Discs of Norgannon",[2281]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, so your fingers are a little fat, eh? Don't worry, $N, I've turned more useless thieves than you into accomplished rogues.\030Sending you out in the field now would be suicide. Renzik doesn't need another dead rogue on his hands. Don't fret, though, $N - Renzik is going to get you up to speed.$B$BMake your way to the Redridge Mountains and speak with an associate of SI:7 named Lucius. You will find him hanging around the docks of Lakeshire with the other shady good-for-nothings.\030Venture forth to Lakeshire in the Redridge Mountains and speak with Lucius.$B\030\030Redridge Rendezvous\0312,1,50,2,257,4,6946\0302,52,103,2,257,1,6946\0302,105,168,2,257,3,6946\0302,173,261,2,257,1,6946\0302,263,357,2,257,3,6946\0303,1,75,2,384,1,6946\0301,1,41,4,272,2,6966\0301,43,126,4,272,1,6966\0316966,2,4,Lucius\0306966,2,6,Lucius\0312,0,0,4,Redridge Mountains\0302,0,0,6,Lakeshire\0302,0,0,6,Redridge Mountains\0312282,23,2282,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2282]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Cracked it open, did you? Nice work, $N.$B$BIf you die now, we can rest easy knowing it was due to your own stupidity and not inexperience.\030We've been training thieves here for years! After all, not every rapscallion is born with the grace and finesse of old Lucius.$B$BUp off the road here you'll find Alther's Mill. I got a chest up there with something important inside. Go get it for me! Bring back that token and you'll receive your Certificate of Thievery!\030Open Lucius's Lockbox, recover the Token of Thievery and return it to Lucius in Lakeshire.\030Did I forget to mention the orcs?$B$BI hear they have been nosing around up by the mill.\030Alther's Mill\0312,1,43,2,257,1,6966\0302,45,126,2,257,1,6966\0302,131,177,2,257,1,6966\0302,179,233,2,257,1,6966\0302,235,251,2,257,1,6966\0302,253,322,2,257,1,6966\0303,1,90,2,384,1,6966\0301,1,25,4,272,2,6966\0301,27,40,4,272,1,6966\0301,45,139,4,272,4,6966\0304,1,33,3,256,2,6966\0304,38,88,3,256,1,6966\0316966,2,2,Lucius\0306966,2,7,Lucius\0312,0,0,7,Lucius\0302,0,0,7,Lakeshire\0312281,19,2281,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7871,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[2283]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Mmmm salvage!  I can smell the necklace from here.  Now let's look at that beauty...$B$BHey, what do you think you're trying to do here?  This necklace is missing the gems!  You think we wouldn't notice?  Even Malton could see that the gems are gone.$B$BWell, maybe you didn't steal them... but this necklace is worthless without those gems!  Your job isn't done here yet, not by a long shot!\030We've got work for you, that is if you've got the guts to do it!$B$BDeep in the Badlands is the Uldaman dig site.  We've heard a tale about some idiot paladin who died there recently.  Why we even care is that he had a very valuable necklace on him.  It's supposedly got three large gems: a ruby, a sapphire, and a topaz.$B$BThe shot: we want it, and we're payin' TOP SILVER to get it.  It may be damaged, but that's neither here nor there; we'll fix whatever scratches are on it.\030Look for a valuable necklace within the Uldaman dig site and bring it back to Dran Droffers in Orgrimmar.  The necklace may be damaged.\030Well, do you have the necklace?  You won't see a copper from us if you don't have that necklace!\030Necklace Recovery\0312,1,64,2,257,4,6986\0302,69,113,2,257,1,6986\0302,116,183,2,257,1,6986\0302,186,249,2,257,1,6986\0302,252,321,2,257,1,6986\0302,326,385,2,259,1,6986\0302,388,480,2,257,1,6986\0303,1,105,2,384,1,6986\0303,108,135,2,384,1,6986\0301,1,13,4,272,1,6986\0301,16,50,4,272,1,6986\0301,53,84,4,272,1,6986\0301,89,136,4,272,2,6986\0301,139,172,4,276,1,6986\0301,175,203,4,272,2,6986\0301,206,250,4,272,4,6986\0301,255,290,4,276,4,6986\0301,292,341,4,272,1,6986\0301,344,392,4,272,1,6986\0304,1,31,3,256,2,6986\0304,34,96,3,256,4,6986\0316986,2,8,Dran Droffers\0312,1517,1418,0,\0302,0,0,2,Badlands\0302,0,0,8,Uldaman\0302,0,0,8,Dran Droffers\0302,0,0,8,Orgrimmar\0312284,23,2284,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7666,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[2284]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You seem to have found the remains of the paladin that Dran had mentioned from before. Searching the remains uncovers what would appear to be his journal. The book is in poor condition, as dried blood has stained most of the text in the book. What you can read, however, is gibberish; it is written in the native tongue of the humans, to the best of your knowledge.$B$BYou will need the book translated if you are to glean any knowledge from it.\030As sure as Malton is a dummy, those gems are still in Uldaman somewhere.  You're going to have to go back there and look for them.$B$BLike I said before, if the information we have is correct then there's a ruby, a sapphire, and a topaz that go with the necklace.  Find them and put them in the necklace.$B$BAs to where the gems are, who knows?  Maybe you'll get lucky and find the corpse of the Paladin.  If he's not been stripped clean already, then maybe he's got them on him still.\030Find a clue as to the gems' whereabouts in the depths of Uldaman.\030\030Necklace Recovery, Take 2\0312,1,72,2,257,1,6986\0302,75,130,2,257,3,6986\0302,135,263,2,257,4,6986\0302,266,304,2,257,1,6986\0302,309,344,2,257,2,6986\0302,347,404,2,257,4,6986\0302,407,485,2,257,4,6986\0303,1,65,2,384,1,6986\0301,1,86,4,272,4,6912\0301,88,154,4,272,4,6912\0301,156,242,4,272,1,6912\0301,244,365,4,272,1,6912\0301,370,445,4,274,4,6912\031\0312,1517,1418,0,\0302,0,0,1,Uldaman\0312283,19,2283,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302318,23,2318,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[229]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes? My father...$B$B<Her eyes become downcast.>$B$BI wish... there was something I could have done for him... If only I had talked to him before he...\030I should have told you this earlier...$B$BHow do I put this...$B$BMorgan may have believed that his family was all dead, but, in fact, his daughter Sarah Ladimore is now a Watcher. She's always been troubled by the... circumstances... surrounding her father's death. Perhaps you could go to bring the news to her.\030Speak with Watcher Sarah Ladimore in Darkshire.\030\030The Daughter Who Lived\0312,1,38,2,257,1,264\0302,43,62,2,257,1,264\0302,67,180,2,257,1,264\0302,182,217,2,257,1,264\0302,219,234,2,257,1,264\0302,236,266,2,257,1,264\0302,268,313,2,257,4,264\0303,1,47,2,384,1,264\0301,1,4,4,272,2,576\0301,6,17,4,272,1,576\0301,22,48,4,272,1,576\0301,53,61,4,274,3,576\0301,63,110,4,272,4,576\0301,112,151,4,280,4,576\031\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,8,Darkshire\031228,19,228,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030231,23,231,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2298]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It's always good to have one of Hulfdan's rogues among our ranks!\030So there we were, about to start plottin' out phase III when a couple o' Magni's blockheads come bargin' in here talkin' bout some kind o' heist and arresting some o' the Hidden Circle.$B$BWell nobody puts the iron on old Blackbeard! The argumentations got heavy and thick and somehow yer name weres blurted out!$B$BMe advice? Take the first Gryphon out o' Ironforge and get to Stormwind. Get yerself to Old Town and once there, talk to an old friend o' mine named Renzik \"The Shiv.\"\030Travel to Stormwind and seek out Renzik \"The Shiv.\"\030\030Kingly Shakedown\0312,1,185,2,257,1,5165\0302,190,233,2,257,1,5165\0302,235,312,2,257,1,5165\0302,317,326,2,257,2,5165\0302,328,388,2,257,1,5165\0302,390,483,2,257,1,5165\0303,1,51,2,386,1,5165\0301,1,65,4,272,1,6946\031\0312,0,0,5,Stormwind\0302,0,0,6,Old Town\0302,0,0,7,Stormwind\0312281,24,2281,UNKNOWN\031",[2299]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Keep yer voice down, $N, the guards may hear ye.\030Where have you been, $N? Hulfdan's been looking all over the place for you. We thought the king may have put you in irons.$B$BGet to Ironforge as soon as possible and speak with Hulfdan!\030Travel to Ironforge and speak with Hulfdan Blackbeard.\030\030To Hulfdan!\0312,1,24,2,257,2,1234\0302,26,75,2,257,1,1234\0302,77,122,2,257,1,1234\0302,127,186,2,257,1,1234\0303,1,54,2,384,1,1234\0301,1,48,4,272,1,5165\0315165,2,5,Hulfdan Blackbeard\0312,0,0,4,Ironforge\0302,0,0,5,Ironforge\0312298,23,2298,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302298,24,2298,UNKNOWN\031",[23]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, the paw of Ursangous! Your skill is impressive, $C; he is credited with numerous kills. The crescent on his paw is no doubt a sign that he was trained by the night elves that skulk about Ashenvale. Ursangous is... was one of the mightiest bears you'd find in these parts. To have bested such a creature is a testament to your will and resolve.$B$BYour ancestors would be proud!\030The paw of the mighty bear Ursangous is your trophy for this part of the Ashenvale Hunt.  On the paw is a small quarter-crescent emblem; the significance of the emblem remains a mystery.$B$BThe paw should be brought to Senani Thunderheart in Splintertree Post to prove that you have bested the mighty creature and completed this portion of the hunt.\030Bring Ursangous's Paw to Senani Thunderheart at Splintertree Post, Ashenvale.\030Ah - $N - I was just thinking about you! How goes your hunting?\030Ursangous's Paw\0312,1,88,2,257,1,0\0302,91,186,2,257,1,0\0302,191,349,2,257,1,0\0303,1,77,2,384,1,0\0301,1,25,4,272,1,12696\0301,27,91,4,272,1,12696\0301,93,201,4,272,1,12696\0301,203,217,4,272,1,12696\0301,219,275,4,272,1,12696\0301,277,347,4,272,3,12696\0301,352,381,4,272,4,12696\0304,1,40,3,256,1,12696\0304,42,63,3,256,2,12696\03112678,2,1,Ursangous\03012696,2,3,Senani Thunderheart\0309084,2,3,Thunderheart\03012696,2,4,Senani Thunderheart\0309084,2,4,Thunderheart\03012678,4,5,Ursangous\03012678,4,8,Ursangous\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,3,Senani Thunderheart\0302,0,0,3,Splintertree Post\0302,0,0,4,Senani Thunderheart\0302,0,0,4,Splintertree Post\0316383,19,6383,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,16303,STARTER,?,10,",[230]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Sven reads the book's pages, then slams it shut.>$B$BThat shadowy figure I saw was a witness to my family's death! There are questions I'd like to ask that man...if only I knew who he was!\030Digging through the mound, you find a small, dirt-stained book.$B$BThe book has no title, but...it has information Sven would like to know.\030Bring the Book from Sven's Farm to Sven.\030You found what?? Please, let me see it...\030Sven's Camp\0312,1,63,2,257,1,0\0302,68,139,2,257,4,0\0303,1,40,2,384,1,0\0301,1,50,4,272,1,311\0301,55,115,4,272,1,311\0301,117,189,4,274,4,311\0304,1,16,3,256,2,311\0304,18,41,3,256,1,311\031\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,3,Sven's Farm\0302,0,0,3,Sven\03195,19,95,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030262,23,262,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,59,GIVER,?,9,Mound of loose dirt",[2300]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Are you ready to get to work or do you need to take a nap before we get started?\030Renzik was looking for you, fish.$B$BI wouldn't keep Mathias's second in command waiting if I were you.$B\030Travel to Stormwind and seek out Renzik \"The Shiv.\"$B\030\030SI:7\0312,1,33,2,257,1,917\0302,38,103,2,257,4,917\0303,1,51,2,386,1,917\0301,1,80,4,282,2,6946\031\0312,0,0,3,Stormwind\0312281,23,2281,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302281,24,2281,UNKNOWN\031",[231]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<A ghostly voice sounds on the wind...>$B$BThis is...? Sarah? Could it be she's still alive? The weight is removed from my shoulders...$B$B$N. Take my sword, Archeus. As my soul is put to rest, I have no more need for it. It was forged to do good, and though I have proved myself unworthy to hold it, perhaps you will carry on the Light through it.$B$BLys, my love...\030Here, take this and lay it on his grave. Maybe... somehow, he'll know that I'm okay, and that none of us hold him responsible for what happened.$B$B<There are tears in her eyes now, as she slides a ring from her right hand, and presses it into your hands.>$B$BAnd... thank you, $n.\030Take Sarah Ladimore's ring to Morgan Ladimore's grave.\030Leave me be...\030A Daughter's Love\0312,1,40,2,257,1,576\0302,42,49,2,257,4,576\0302,51,144,2,257,1,576\0302,149,256,2,257,1,576\0302,261,266,2,257,1,576\0302,268,281,2,257,1,576\0303,1,54,2,384,1,576\0301,1,39,4,272,1,0\0301,44,54,4,272,2,0\0301,56,61,4,272,2,0\0301,63,92,4,272,4,0\0301,94,135,4,272,1,0\0301,144,166,4,272,1,0\0301,168,221,4,274,1,0\0301,223,348,4,272,4,0\0301,353,367,4,272,1,0\0304,1,14,3,256,1,0\0313301,2,7,Morgan Ladimore\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,7,Morgan Ladimore's\031229,19,229,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,61,FINISHER,?,12,A Weathered Grave",[2318]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Mighty $C, I know what you are doing out here in the Badlands. I know you seek my gift of tongues. You're after the parts to that necklace you found in Uldaman.$B$BSurprised? Don't be - it's my job to know such things. Instead, let's discuss what you're going to do for a translated journal. Trust me - I'm the only one you'll find that can translate it.$B$BBetter still, let me make you a better offer than Dran Droffers is, and it'll let you still complete your deal with them. Interested now, yes?\030At an impasse of sorts, you know that you will need the book translated into a language you can understand.  There certainly are a number of people in the world who could do it; the closest location that might have someone who could, however, is the Kargath outpost in the Badlands.  Perhaps that is a good place to start.$B\030Find someone who can translate the paladin's journal.  The closest location that might have someone is Kargath, in the Badlands.\030\030Translating the Journal\0312,1,107,2,259,3,6912\0302,110,282,2,257,4,6912\0302,285,322,2,257,4,6912\0303,1,53,2,384,1,6912\0303,56,128,2,384,4,6912\0301,1,62,4,272,1,6868\0301,64,98,4,274,1,6868\0301,100,160,4,272,1,6868\0301,165,174,4,272,2,6868\0301,176,218,4,272,1,6868\0301,220,291,4,272,3,6868\0301,293,354,4,272,1,6868\0301,359,479,4,272,1,6868\0301,481,500,4,272,2,6868\0316986,4,13,Dran Droffers\0312,1517,1418,0,\0302,0,0,2,Badlands\0302,0,0,5,Badlands\0304,0,0,6,Badlands\0304,0,0,8,Uldaman\0312284,19,2284,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302338,23,2338,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[232]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, Zinge needs a kit, does she?  It saddens me that Zinge does not choose to grace myself with her sweet presence.$B$BVery well, let me procure a kit for you.\030The Royal Apothecary Society needs your assistance.  Listen closely, and both of us may profit from my plan.$B$BApothecary Keever in the next room may be... touched... but his research does potentially bear fruit if it were pursued by a clever researcher.  Fortunately, I am such a researcher.  I want you to take this purchase order to Alessandro Luca, the proprietor of Blue Moon Odds and Ends; he'll give you a testing kit.  When you have it, bring it back to me and I'll outline your task in detail.\030Take the purchase order to Alessandro Luca in the Undercity.\030Yes, and what may I assist you with?  Are you here on business for the Royal Apothecary Society, or have you arrived here merely to brighten my day?\030Errand for Apothecary Zinge\0312,1,51,2,259,1,5204\0302,54,108,2,257,1,5204\0302,113,156,2,257,1,5204\0302,158,167,2,257,1,5204\0302,169,255,2,257,4,5204\0302,258,293,2,257,1,5204\0302,296,426,2,259,1,5204\0302,429,503,2,257,1,5204\0303,1,60,2,384,1,5204\0301,1,32,4,274,2,7683\0301,35,115,4,272,1,7683\0301,120,159,4,272,1,7683\0304,1,36,3,256,2,7683\0304,39,148,3,256,2,7683\0315734,2,3,Apothecary Keever\0307683,2,7,Alessandro Luca\0307683,2,9,Alessandro Luca\0312,1497,1458,0,\0302,0,0,7,Alessandro Luca\0302,0,0,9,Alessandro Luca\0302,0,0,9,Undercity\031238,23,238,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[233]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, I've been waiting for these letters for quite some time...$B$BUnfortunately, these letters aren't all for me. This one is addressed to Grelin Whitebeard. He's not too far away if you'd like to deliver it to him.\030Hm, I don't suppose you'd be willing to do a favor for me, $g lad : lass;? A stack of letters came through the pass today, but I don't have the time to send them along.$B$BThey're all addressed to Talin Keeneye. You can find him to the west down the road. He's set up camp next to the frozen lake.$B$BWhat do you say?\030Deliver the stack of letters to Talin Keeneye.\030Yes? Do you have something for me?\030Coldridge Valley Mail Delivery\0312,1,74,2,257,2,658\0302,76,168,2,257,1,658\0302,173,211,2,257,1,658\0302,213,255,2,257,1,658\0302,257,297,2,257,1,658\0302,302,317,2,257,2,658\0303,1,46,2,384,1,658\0301,1,69,4,272,1,714\0301,74,120,4,272,1,714\0301,122,164,4,272,1,714\0301,166,222,4,272,4,714\0304,1,4,3,256,2,714\0304,6,34,3,256,2,714\031714,2,3,Talin Keeneye\030714,2,7,Talin Keeneye\030786,4,10,Grelin Whitebeard\0312,132,1426,0,\0302,0,0,3,Talin Keeneye\0302,0,0,7,Talin Keeneye\0304,0,0,10,Grelin Whitebeard\031179,19,179,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030234,23,234,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2338]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You know a good deal when you see one - I knew I could count on you.$B$BIt will be just a moment while I cast a spell to quickly translate the human tongue into a form you will understand. I am a troll of my word; ask anyone in the Horde about Jarkal Mossmeld. Now, let's get this started...\030Droffers and Son Salvage aren't smart enough to restore the magic in the necklace, but I am.  All I want to do is study the necklace so I can learn to make them myself.  To do that, I will need your necklace.  Let me borrow it, and in exchange for the time I get to study it I will translate the journal for you.  While you are searching for the gems, I should have enough time to learn what I need to.$B$BIt's a simple deal, and no one else will be the wiser.  Whatcha wanna do?\030Let Jarkal borrow the necklace.  In exchange, he will translate the journal for you.\030You've thought about it, yes? You're a smart $C if you take this deal - you and I will get what we both want, and Droffers and Son Salvage will think they're getting what they want.\030Translating the Journal\0312,1,92,2,259,1,6868\0302,95,168,2,259,1,6868\0302,171,208,2,259,3,6868\0302,211,312,2,257,3,6868\0302,315,402,2,259,1,6868\0302,407,460,2,257,3,6868\0302,463,479,2,257,2,6868\0303,1,31,2,384,1,6868\0303,34,84,2,384,3,6868\0301,1,68,4,272,4,6868\0301,73,188,4,272,3,6868\0301,190,260,4,272,1,6868\0301,262,291,4,272,1,6868\0304,1,29,3,256,2,6868\0304,31,181,3,258,4,6868\0316868,4,12,Jarkal Mossmeld\0312,1517,1418,0,\0304,0,0,12,Horde\0312318,19,2318,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302339,23,2339,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2339]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very well done, $C.  Now the fruits of our redirection will pay themselves out handsomely.  I'm finished with the necklace itself, and I am confident I can duplicate the construction process consistently.$B$BBut first, I will use a specially prepared incantation to quickly analyze those gems before you take them and the necklace back to Orgrimmar.  This will take just a brief moment to do.\030Here is the journal, translated for you to read on your own.  The crux of it says dwarves hid the ruby, the troggs hid the topaz, and a trogg named Grimlok has the sapphire.$B$BLook - you're going to need a power source to make the necklace work again.  Dran Droffers doesn't know this.  To find one, here's what I'd do: go as deep as you can in Uldaman and kill whatever construct there is the strongest.  No doubt whatever that is would have it.$B$BWhen you have everything collected, come back here!\030Recover all three gems and a power source for the necklace from Uldaman, and then bring them to Jarkal Mossmeld in Kargath.  Jarkal believes a power source might be found on the strongest construct present in Uldaman.$B$BFrom the journal, you know...$B* The ruby has been stashed in a barricaded Shadowforge area.$B* The topaz has been hidden in an urn in one of the Trogg areas, near some Alliance dwarves.$B* The sapphire has been claimed by Grimlok, the trogg leader.\030You've got another trip into the depths of Uldaman in store for yourself if you don't have the gems and a power source capable of channeling magical power back into the necklace.$B$BYou'll be getting the gems back to deliver to the goons in Orgrimmar; I will be keeping the power source, since it will be the thing that will make the necklace work in the first place...\030Find the Gems and Power Source\0312,1,60,2,257,1,6868\0302,63,173,2,257,1,6868\0302,178,252,2,259,3,6868\0302,255,286,2,257,1,6868\0302,289,405,2,257,1,6868\0302,408,447,2,257,4,6868\0302,452,502,2,257,1,6868\0303,1,123,2,384,1,6868\0303,126,217,2,384,4,6868\0303,222,250,2,384,1,6868\0303,253,313,2,384,1,6868\0303,316,407,2,384,1,6868\0303,410,470,2,384,1,6868\0301,1,19,4,272,1,6868\0301,22,90,4,272,3,6868\0301,93,204,4,272,1,6868\0301,209,349,4,272,3,6868\0301,352,392,4,272,3,6868\0304,1,178,3,256,4,6868\0304,183,369,3,256,3,6868\0314854,2,2,Grimlok\0306986,2,4,Dran Droffers\0306868,2,8,Jarkal Mossmeld\0304854,2,13,Grimlok\0312,1517,1418,0,\0302,0,0,5,Uldaman\0302,0,0,8,Uldaman\0302,0,0,8,Jarkal Mossmeld\0302,0,0,8,Kargath\0302,0,0,9,Uldaman\0304,0,0,17,Orgrimmar\0303,0,0,20,Orgrimmar\0312338,19,2338,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302340,23,2340,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7669,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,7670,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,7671,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,7672,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[234]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ahh, excellent. It's been a while since I received word from Ironforge.\030If I remember correctly, Grelin's camp is down the road to the southeast. No doubt he'll be eager to get his mail.\030Deliver the letter to Grelin Whitebeard.\030Is there something I can help you with?\030Coldridge Valley Mail Delivery\0312,1,73,2,257,4,714\0302,75,114,2,257,1,714\0303,1,40,2,384,1,714\0301,1,15,4,272,1,786\0301,17,71,4,272,1,786\0304,1,39,3,256,2,786\031786,2,3,Grelin Whitebeard\0312,132,1426,0,\0302,0,0,3,Grelin Whitebeard\0304,0,0,5,Ironforge\031233,19,233,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2340]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yep, it's all here. Say, mind if we keep the bag too? No? Thanks, appreciate it! Har!$B$BThis necklace will be our greatest haul yet! Don't feel too bad though; I'm sure the necklace wouldn't fit you anyway. Har again!$B$BA deal is a deal, so here's your fee for the salvage. Our business is done here for now; check back later to see if we have more work. Until then, beat it!\030Any necklace setting and gem will work, so long as they are the same material.  This power source, however, is what will bring the magic back to the necklace... I hope.$B$BI'll gladly supply the gems needed for your version of the necklace, so long as the power source actually works.$B$BHead to Orgrimmar and keep your end of the bargain with Droffers and Son Salvage.  Just keep your mouth shut about our deal, and when you get back I might have a wonderful surprise for you.\030Deliver the Necklace and Gem Salvage to Dran Droffers in Orgrimmar.\030Well, look who it is! Took your sweet time getting here, I see. Let's hope this isn't a waste of my time! You'll not get paid unless you have everything I asked for. And trust me on this - we'll be double and triple checking everything!\030Deliver the Gems\0312,1,78,2,257,3,6868\0302,81,160,2,257,3,6868\0302,162,168,2,259,3,6868\0302,173,284,2,257,1,6868\0302,289,369,2,257,1,6868\0302,372,477,2,257,4,6868\0303,1,67,2,384,1,6868\0301,1,19,4,272,1,6986\0301,21,53,4,272,4,6986\0301,59,80,4,272,1,6986\0301,82,85,4,272,1,6986\0301,90,133,4,272,3,6986\0301,135,207,4,272,1,6986\0301,209,218,4,272,1,6986\0301,223,275,4,272,1,6986\0301,277,356,4,272,4,6986\0301,358,377,4,272,1,6986\0304,1,21,3,256,1,6986\0304,23,63,3,256,1,6986\0304,65,105,3,256,3,6986\0304,107,165,3,264,4,6986\0304,167,236,3,256,1,6986\0316986,2,7,Dran Droffers\0312,1517,1418,0,\0302,0,0,5,Orgrimmar\0302,0,0,7,Dran Droffers\0302,0,0,7,Orgrimmar\0312339,19,2339,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302341,23,2341,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2341]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The power source you gave me exceeded every expectation I had for it. I was able to make both you and me a necklace, and I have enough left over to make at least three more. They will fetch quite the fee, with Droffers and Son Salvage none the wiser.$B$BHere you go, my friend. I give you my thanks on a splendid job... and something quite special for your trouble.\030As Dran and Malton Droffers begin to squabble over their new salvage, half of the deal is now complete.  A trip to the Badlands is now in order to finish things up, as Jarkal Mossmeld in Kargath might have a special reward waiting for you there.\030Visit Jarkal Mossmeld in Kargath to see if he was successful.\030\030Necklace Recovery, Take 3\0312,1,103,2,257,1,6986\0302,106,245,2,259,4,6986\0303,1,61,2,384,4,6986\0301,1,69,4,272,1,6868\0301,71,173,4,272,1,6868\0301,175,250,4,272,3,6868\0301,255,277,4,272,1,6868\0301,279,319,4,272,1,6868\0301,321,365,4,272,1,6868\0316987,2,1,Malton Droffers\0306868,2,2,Jarkal Mossmeld\0306868,2,3,Jarkal Mossmeld\0312,1517,1418,0,\0302,0,0,2,Badlands\0302,0,0,2,Kargath\0302,0,0,3,Kargath\0312340,19,2340,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2342]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031At last - a broom worthy of a Garrett.  You're bloody well worth every silver I spent on you, I say!$B$BDo you hear me, foul bats?  I now wield the Garrett family weapon of choice!  Tremble, bats, tremble!!\030Sweeping the bat pens with this broom is not befitting a Garrett!  I've earned a little coin from this accursed job, and I'm willing to spend it on you to better my station.$B$BThe Garrett family weapon of choice is locked away in our chest in the South Common Hall of Uldaman from when we Garretts toiled there as diggers.  Without it, I will be stuck here forever - literally - sweeping up after these infernal bats.$B$BReclaim my family's treasure and bring it to me!  Help me restore my birthright!\030Get Patrick Garrett's family treasure from their family chest in the South Common Hall of Uldaman, and bring it to him in the Undercity.\030The sweeping never ends... these bats are prolific in their mockery of me and my broom.  Please tell me you've reclaimed my family's treasure!  I've offered you my silver - is that not enough?!\030Reclaimed Treasures\0312,1,65,2,257,1,5651\0302,68,173,2,257,1,5651\0302,178,323,2,257,1,5651\0302,326,418,2,257,3,5651\0302,423,470,2,257,1,5651\0302,473,502,2,257,1,5651\0303,1,136,2,384,1,5651\0301,1,38,4,272,1,5651\0301,41,100,4,272,1,5651\0301,105,130,4,272,2,5651\0301,133,180,4,272,1,5651\0301,183,206,4,272,1,5651\0304,1,26,3,256,1,5651\0304,28,87,3,256,1,5651\0304,90,142,3,256,1,5651\0304,145,193,3,256,2,5651\03189,2,4,Infernal\0305651,2,7,Patrick Garrett\0312,1517,1418,0,\0302,0,0,3,South Common Hall of Uldaman\0302,0,0,7,South Common Hall of Uldaman\0302,0,0,7,Undercity\031\031ITEM,8026,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[235]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Welcome to the new frontier, $N. Ashenvale is a land of opportunity, one where a young $C like yourself is able to find boundless chances to prove their mettle. Look around the outpost here, and be sure to travel out to the Zoram Strand, as the Horde has another outpost there as well.$B$BYour presence here tells me that you've come to learn more about the hunt. Listen close, and I will gladly share with you what you need to know.\030Attention, young adventurers!  The wilds of Ashenvale await you!$B$BThe Horde has established a strong presence in the lands north of the Barrens.  Our two outposts - Splintertree Post and the Zoram Strand Outpost - strive to bring glory to the Horde!  Those who would prove themselves should seek out guidance there.  Of note: Senani Thunderheart in Splintertree Post, directly north of the Barrens, seeks adventurers willing to take part in a great hunt of Ashenvale!\030Speak with Senani Thunderheart at Splintertree Post, Ashenvale.\030\030The Ashenvale Hunt\0312,1,29,2,257,1,10880\0302,32,64,2,257,1,10880\0302,69,146,2,257,1,10880\0302,149,251,2,257,1,10880\0302,254,317,2,259,4,10880\0302,320,469,2,257,1,10880\0303,1,63,2,384,1,10880\0301,1,32,4,272,1,12696\0301,34,160,4,272,1,12696\0301,162,285,4,272,1,12696\0301,290,363,4,272,1,12696\0301,365,433,4,274,3,12696\03112696,2,6,Senani Thunderheart\0309084,2,6,Thunderheart\03012696,2,7,Senani Thunderheart\0309084,2,7,Thunderheart\0312,1637,1454,0,\0302,0,0,3,Barrens\0302,0,0,4,Horde\0302,0,0,6,Splintertree Post\0302,0,0,6,Barrens\0302,0,0,7,Splintertree Post\0304,0,0,10,Zoram Strand\031742,22,742,UNKNOWN\0306382,22,6382,UNKNOWN\0306383,24,6383,UNKNOWN\031",[2358]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031To deny Ravenholdt the artifact, would be to deny one's own existence. Well done, $C. You may yet walk among the assassins of Ravenholdt.$B$BAs a young rogue adventuring in Darkshore, I discovered a tea that replenishes energy in combat. It has served me well throughout the years and now I pass on a taste of the thistle tea to you. Drink of it when you tire, $N, and fight with vigor once more!$B$B\030Many years ago, the Horns of Nez'ra were stolen from Ravenholdt manor. Across continents and oceans I have searched, only to discover that these insignificant beasts have had it in their possession all along.$B$BSlay every Blackrock orc you cross until the Horns of Nez'ra are recovered. Should you recover the horns, find me in Lakeshire.$B$BDo this for me and your name shall be known to Ravenholdt, $N.\030Return the Horns of Nez'ra to Arantir's Shadow in Lakeshire.\030Do you have the demon prince's horns?\030Horns of Nez'ra\0312,1,70,2,325,1,7009\0302,72,208,2,257,1,7009\0302,213,287,2,257,1,7009\0302,289,339,2,257,1,7009\0302,344,405,2,257,3,7009\0303,1,60,2,384,1,7009\0301,1,70,4,272,4,7009\0301,72,85,4,272,1,7009\0301,87,137,4,272,1,7009\0301,142,237,4,272,1,7009\0301,239,333,4,272,1,7009\0301,335,396,4,276,1,7009\0304,1,37,3,256,2,7009\03113936,2,1,Ravenholdt\03013936,2,5,Ravenholdt\0307229,2,6,Arantir's Shadow\0304244,2,6,Shadow\03013936,4,7,Ravenholdt\03013936,4,9,Ravenholdt\0312,0,0,1,Ravenholdt\0302,0,0,4,Lakeshire\0302,0,0,5,Ravenholdt\0302,0,0,6,Arantir's Shadow\0302,0,0,6,Lakeshire\0304,0,0,10,Darkshore\031\031ITEM,7906,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[2359]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This would explain the Defias drones you and Kearnen saw outside of the tower, $N. It would also explain the Venture Company's involvement with the Defias and the strange shipments out of Duskwood.$B$BAccording to this book, the Zanzil trolls in Stranglethorn have discovered a way to raise the dead through potions... or to be more specific: poison.$B$BYou'll be of no use to SI:7 without a firm understanding of poisons, $N -- especially with the recipe to create undeath at our fingertips.\030I've been staking out this tower for weeks, $N. Recently a major shipment came through from Duskwood, and along with it came those guards.$B$BWhat are they? Your guess is as good as mine. I can tell you one thing - they aren't human.$B$BAnyhow, the shipment had a chest - which is what I assume those abominations are guarding. The zombie with the spikes holds a key we'll need.$B$BGet that key, get in the tower, and uncover whatever is in that chest. Take your findings back to Mathias.\030Steal the Defias Tower Key, break into the Defias Tower and uncover the contents of the Duskwood Chest. Take whatever information you find back to Mathias Shaw in Stormwind. Read Kearnen's Journal to gain insight about the tower.$B\030Any news from Agent Kearnen?\030Klaven's Tower\0312,1,47,2,257,1,7024\0302,49,138,2,257,1,7024\0302,143,156,2,257,2,7024\0302,158,187,2,257,1,7024\0302,189,233,2,257,1,7024\0302,238,327,2,257,4,7024\0302,329,378,2,259,1,7024\0302,383,452,2,257,1,7024\0302,454,488,2,257,1,7024\0303,1,103,2,388,1,7024\0303,105,173,2,384,1,7024\0303,175,229,2,384,1,7024\0301,1,82,4,272,4,332\0301,84,197,4,272,4,332\0301,202,318,4,272,1,332\0301,320,350,4,276,1,332\0301,355,492,4,272,1,332\0304,1,28,3,256,2,332\0317024,3,18,Agent Kearnen\0312,0,0,2,Duskwood\0302,0,0,9,Mathias\0302,0,0,11,Mathias Shaw\0302,0,0,11,Stormwind\0304,0,0,15,Stranglethorn\0304,0,0,17,SI\0303,0,0,18,Agent Kearnen\0312360,19,2360,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302607,23,2607,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7908,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,7923,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[2360]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Mathias finally sent another agent to back me up, eh? Well I hope he's ready to hear some bad news.\030Not a moment too soon, $N. SI:7 reconnaissance is reporting unusually heavy Defias activity in Westfall.$B$BIt would seem that the Defias have taken over an abandoned Alliance watch tower southeast of Sentinel Hill and are using it as a base of operations to smuggle in goods from the Redridge supply route.$B$BGet to Westfall and contact Agent Kearnen for your debriefing. You will find her hidden near the tower.$B$B...and $N, should you be discovered, SI:7 will disavow all knowledge of your existence.\030Travel to Westfall and find Agent Kearnen for your debriefing.\030\030Mathias and the Defias\0312,1,26,2,257,1,332\0302,28,104,2,257,1,332\0302,109,307,2,257,4,332\0302,312,373,2,257,1,332\0302,375,414,2,257,3,332\0302,419,505,2,257,3,332\0303,1,62,2,384,1,332\0301,1,53,4,272,2,7024\0301,55,99,4,274,3,7024\0317024,2,4,Agent Kearnen\0307024,2,7,Agent Kearnen\0312,0,0,2,Westfall\0302,0,0,3,Redridge\0302,0,0,4,Westfall\0302,0,0,7,Westfall\0312359,23,2359,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2361]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I gladly give you this necklace, mighty $C.  You have done me an invaluable service, and for that I thank you.  Wear it with pride, and make sure you mention loudly and repeatedly who made it for you!$B$BAlso, if you could toss in the fact that it really isn't cursed, that would be great.\030\030\030\030Restoring the Necklace\0311,1,43,4,272,1,6826\0301,46,110,4,272,1,6826\0301,113,200,4,272,1,6826\0301,205,289,4,276,4,6826\031\0312,1517,1418,0,\0312204,19,2204,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[237]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You accomplished your mission well, $R. The King himself would be proud.$B$BThe reinforcements promised to us never showed, however. Apparently the Alliance front is a sea of crimson from the blood of our fallen brethren. The news of the losses leaves a bitter taste in one's mouth. But we must not let their deaths go for naught. We must rally in these grim times and bring glory back to the Alliance.$B$BSpeak with Mountaineer Wallbang for reassignment. You're needed now more than ever.\030Mountaineer Cobbleflint had nothing but good things to say about you, $r.  For that reason I am going to entrust upon you a mission of utmost importance.  We need to keep pressure on the invading Trogg forces until our Dwarven brethren return from the Alliance front.$B$BSet forth into the southern hills and kill 10 Stonesplinter Skullthumpers and 10 Stonesplinter Seers.  Your attacks will buy us some time.  Report back when your mission is complete.\030Mountaineer Gravelgaw in the southern guard tower wants you to kill 10 Stonesplinter Skullthumpers and 10 Stonesplinter Seers and report back to him.\030We need more time, $r. Your orders are to kill 10 Stonesplinter Skullthumpers and 10 Stonesplinter Seers. Keep the enemy under pressure until we are granted reinforcements. This is no time for idle behavior.\030In Defense of the King's Lands\0312,1,73,2,257,1,1091\0302,76,153,2,257,3,1091\0302,156,267,2,263,1,1091\0302,272,372,2,257,1,1091\0302,375,409,2,261,3,1091\0302,412,453,2,257,1,1091\0303,1,149,2,386,1,1091\0301,1,39,4,272,1,1091\0301,41,72,4,272,4,1091\0301,77,132,4,272,1,1091\0301,134,221,4,272,4,1091\0301,223,282,4,272,1,1091\0301,284,330,4,280,1,1091\0301,332,402,4,272,1,1091\0301,407,455,4,272,1,1091\0301,457,489,4,272,1,1091\0304,1,22,3,258,1,1091\0304,24,105,3,256,1,1091\0304,107,172,3,260,1,1091\0304,174,207,3,256,1,1091\0311089,2,1,Mountaineer Cobbleflint\0301091,2,7,Mountaineer Gravelgaw\0301090,4,15,Mountaineer Wallbang\0312,38,1432,0,\0302,0,0,3,Alliance\0304,0,0,14,Alliance\031224,19,224,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030263,23,263,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,1163,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Stonesplinter Skullthumper\030NPC,1166,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Stonesplinter Seer",[2378]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031So, you are what our mighty allies have sent Shenthul? How uninspiring....\030You have served the Deathstalkers well, $N, but perhaps it is time for you to venture outward. While you have shown aptitude in the ways of stealth and deception, you still require much training.$B$BThe Deathstalkers have allies within the Shattered Hand. Seek out those that would assist us - find Shenthul in Orgrimmar.$B\030Journey to Orgrimmar and speak with Shenthul at the Cleft of Shadow.\030\030Find the Shattered Hand\0312,1,94,2,257,4,6467\0302,96,195,2,257,1,6467\0302,200,255,2,257,1,6467\0302,257,321,2,257,4,6467\0303,1,68,2,384,1,6467\0301,1,54,4,272,2,3401\0301,56,74,4,272,1,3401\0313401,2,4,Shenthul\0303401,2,5,Shenthul\0304244,2,5,Shadow\0303401,4,6,Shenthul\0312,0,0,3,Shattered Hand\0302,0,0,4,Orgrimmar\0302,0,0,5,Orgrimmar\0302,0,0,5,Cleft of Shadow\0312380,22,2380,UNKNOWN\0302379,23,2379,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2379]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Perhaps Zando'zan was wrong. Zando'zan apologizes.\030Your determination alone is not enough to overcome the obstacles that lay ahead of us.$B$BSpeak with Zando'zan to begin your training as an operative of the Shattered Hand.$B$BIt is only when you have mastered the practices of stealth and thievery that you may take the next step towards your destiny.$B\030Speak with Zando'zan at the Cleft of Shadow.\030\030Zando'zan\0312,1,86,2,257,1,3401\0302,91,172,2,257,1,3401\0302,177,301,2,257,1,3401\0303,1,44,2,384,1,3401\0301,1,28,4,272,4,3402\0301,30,50,4,272,1,3402\0313402,2,2,Zando'zan\0303402,2,4,Zando'zan\0304244,2,4,Shadow\0303402,4,5,Zando'zan\0303402,4,6,Zando'zan\0312,0,0,4,Cleft of Shadow\0312382,23,2382,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[238]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Good - it pleases me to be working with someone who takes pride in not wasting my time.$B$BAfter I make some adjustments to this kit, you'll be ready to head out into the field. You'll be using it to collect some vital data to the task at hand.$B$BIt will take just a moment for me to finish the modifications. While you are waiting, you should probably start thinking about what you'd like to bring to the desert with you.$B$BYes, I said the desert.\030The kit is ready, $n.  No doubt that Apothecary Zinge will want this as soon as possible.  Take it to her without delay, and let her know that I will add the cost of the kit to the Society's tab.  Also, please extend to her my warmest salutations.$B$BWell, don't just stand there.  Such is the life of a simple courier, yes?\030Bring the Field Sampling Kit to Apothecary Zinge in the Undercity.\030Yes, I think Luca is as disturbing as you do. It matters not - hand me the field sampling kit. I will need to make some adjustments to it in order to survey for the proper base materials.$B$BYou have the kit, don't you?\030Errand for Apothecary Zinge\0312,1,21,2,257,1,7683\0302,24,89,2,259,3,7683\0302,92,195,2,257,3,7683\0302,198,247,2,257,1,7683\0302,252,280,2,257,1,7683\0302,283,324,2,257,2,7683\0303,1,66,2,384,1,7683\0301,1,87,4,272,1,5204\0301,92,177,4,272,1,5204\0301,179,244,4,272,1,5204\0301,249,310,4,272,3,5204\0301,312,423,4,272,1,5204\0301,428,450,4,272,1,5204\0304,1,45,3,256,1,5204\0304,47,94,3,256,1,5204\0304,96,187,3,258,3,5204\0304,192,219,3,256,2,5204\0315204,2,2,Apothecary Zinge\0305204,2,7,Apothecary Zinge\0312,1497,1458,0,\0302,0,0,3,Society's\0302,0,0,7,Apothecary Zinge\0302,0,0,7,Undercity\031232,19,232,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030243,23,243,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2380]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It is important that the Shattered Hand remains vigilant in the face of the changes Thrall wishes to bring about to the Horde. Our numbers alone will not be enough to overcome his rule - stealth and deception must be mastered.\030A master of stealth and deception you are not, however, all of that can and will change. You've obviously impressed those in charge with your meager skills, as the great Shenthul has asked for you by name.$B$BTake the road north of here to Orgrimmar and speak with Shenthul in the Cleft of Shadow.$B\030Speak with Shenthul at the Cleft of Shadow in Orgrimmar.\030\030To Orgrimmar!\0312,1,88,2,257,3,3170\0302,90,205,2,257,1,3170\0302,210,297,2,257,1,3170\0303,1,56,2,384,1,3170\0301,1,126,4,274,1,3401\0301,128,226,4,272,3,3401\0313401,2,2,Shenthul\0303401,2,3,Shenthul\0304244,2,3,Shadow\0303401,2,4,Shenthul\0304244,2,4,Shadow\0304949,4,5,Thrall\0312,0,0,3,Orgrimmar\0302,0,0,3,Cleft of Shadow\0302,0,0,4,Cleft of Shadow\0302,0,0,4,Orgrimmar\0304,0,0,5,Horde\0312378,22,2378,UNKNOWN\0302379,23,2379,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2381]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Incredible! Improbable! Simply amazing! You've got talent, $N. Either that or you're the luckiest $gman:woman; alive!$b$bHere's your cut of the action. I'm sure you would make better use of this stuff than I could.$b$b\030I don't mean to scare you, $N, but the last five thieves I sent to steal the southsea treasure came back to me in pieces.$B$BSouth along the coast you'll find Tide Razor, the southsea freebooter's ship. Nestled in the hold is the payoff - the southsea treasure. On the second level of that ship is the pirate's den, a place where they train all of their thieves.$B$BBoard that ship, steal the treasure, and bring it back to me. Use the pirate's den if you need to practice your thievery, but be careful!$B\030Bring the Southsea Treasure back to Wrenix the Wretched in Ratchet. Do not forget to get an E.C.A.C. and Thieves' Tools from Wrenix's Gizmotronic Apparatus. You will need both of these items to complete your mission.$B$BShould you be attacked by any unusually hostile parrots, use your E.C.A.C.!$B$B\030Well, at least you still have all of your body parts. Did you find the treasure?$B$B\030Plundering the Plunderers\0312,1,121,2,261,1,7161\0302,126,202,2,257,1,7161\0302,204,261,2,257,1,7161\0302,263,362,2,257,1,7161\0302,367,427,2,261,1,7161\0302,429,503,2,259,4,7161\0303,1,67,2,384,1,7161\0303,69,100,2,384,1,7161\0303,102,156,2,384,1,7161\0303,158,216,2,386,3,7161\0303,221,295,2,388,1,7161\0301,1,11,4,272,1,7161\0301,13,23,4,272,1,7161\0301,25,39,4,272,1,7161\0301,41,62,4,272,1,7161\0301,64,117,4,272,1,7161\0301,122,151,4,272,1,7161\0301,153,214,4,272,4,7161\0304,1,53,3,256,1,7161\0304,55,80,3,256,2,7161\0317856,2,2,Southsea Freebooter\0307161,2,7,Wrenix the Wretched\0307166,2,9,Wrenix's Gizmotronic Apparatus\0312,0,0,7,Wrenix the Wretched\0302,0,0,7,Ratchet\0302,0,0,9,Wrenix's Gizmotronic Apparatus\0312382,19,2382,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7968,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[2382]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Another one? The last five that crazy troll sent me ended up as shark food. Let's hope you fare a little better, eh?$B$B\030Zando'zan has seen it! Yes, the day comes! Thrall's death... the dagger in his back, poison seeping through to his every vein... Zando'zan has said too much.$B$B$N! Zando'zan has a task for $N! $N must travel to Ratchet, east of the Crossroads, and speak with Wrenix the Wretched. Go!$B\030Travel to Ratchet and speak with Wrenix the Wretched.\030\030Wrenix of Ratchet\0312,1,22,2,257,1,3402\0302,24,42,2,257,1,3402\0302,44,60,2,257,1,3402\0302,62,128,2,261,1,3402\0302,130,157,2,257,1,3402\0302,166,193,2,257,1,3402\0302,195,280,2,257,1,3402\0303,1,53,2,384,1,3402\0301,1,12,4,272,2,7161\0301,14,75,4,272,1,7161\0301,77,116,4,272,2,7161\0313402,2,1,Zando'zan\0303402,2,5,Zando'zan\0303402,2,6,Zando'zan\0307161,2,7,Wrenix the Wretched\0307161,2,8,Wrenix the Wretched\0312,0,0,7,Ratchet\0302,0,0,7,Crossroads\0302,0,0,8,Ratchet\0312379,19,2379,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302381,23,2381,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2383]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, that's my parchment.  I heard you'd be coming to the Valley, $n.  I'm glad to see you made it--let's hope you survive the trials ahead. Like I said, as you gain in power, come to me--I will do what I can to train you in the ways of the warrior.$B$BGood luck, $n, and return to me whenever you feel ready.\030Ah, while you were gone a parchment came for you, $N.$B$BRead it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from the warrior trainer Frang. He would have words with you when you're ready. You'll find him outside the Den, taking cover in the shade.\030Read the Simple Parchment and speak to Frang in the Valley of Trials.\030What's that you have there? A parchment? You're not a scholar, I hope...\030Simple Parchment\0312,1,53,2,257,1,3143\0302,58,84,2,257,1,3143\0302,86,145,2,257,4,3143\0302,147,193,2,257,4,3143\0302,195,253,2,257,1,3143\0303,1,69,2,384,1,3143\0301,1,24,4,272,1,3153\0301,27,68,4,272,1,3153\0301,71,139,4,280,3,3153\0301,141,248,4,272,3,3153\0301,253,308,4,272,1,3153\0304,1,27,3,256,2,3153\0304,29,40,3,256,2,3153\0304,42,72,3,258,3,3153\0313153,2,3,Frang\0305954,2,5,Shade\0303153,2,6,Frang\0312,0,0,5,Den\0302,0,0,6,Frang\0302,0,0,6,Valley of Trials\0304,0,0,8,Valley\031788,19,788,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[239]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Marshall Dughan sent you, eh? Well you're not from the army, but if Dughan sent you then that's good enough for me!$B$BOur situation is, to say the least, a stressed one. I hope you can give us a hand.\030The Garrison on our western border sends word of increasing gnoll and thief activity.  They're requesting we send more Stormwind soldiers... but we just don't have any to spare!$B$BIf you can help, we could use it.  Go and speak with Deputy Rainer at the Westbrook Garrison and see what he needs done.$B$BThe Garrison is down the road to the west.  After you cross the bridge over the small brook it will be to the right.\030Go to the Westbrook Garrison and speak with Deputy Rainer.\030\030Westbrook Garrison Needs Help!\0312,1,85,2,257,1,240\0302,88,140,2,257,1,240\0302,142,177,2,257,1,240\0302,182,214,2,257,4,240\0302,217,301,2,259,1,240\0302,306,347,2,257,1,240\0302,350,421,2,257,3,240\0303,1,58,2,384,1,240\0301,1,29,4,272,2,963\0301,31,115,4,272,4,963\0301,120,170,4,272,1,963\0301,172,201,4,274,3,963\031963,2,5,Deputy Rainer\030963,2,8,Deputy Rainer\0312,12,1429,0,\0302,0,0,5,Westbrook Garrison\0302,0,0,8,Westbrook Garrison\03176,19,76,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\03011,23,11,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\03011,24,11,UNKNOWN\031",[2398]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It's about time you showed up! I was in danger of losing a bet with Olaf!$B$BHe wagered that his beard would grow to his knees before he saw another living $R. Well here you are, and as you can see Olaf's beard has a few more inches to go.$B$BThanks, $N. I'll split the winnings with you.\030The dig site at Uldaman wasn't always overrun.  We Ironforge dwarves used to control the area, but... that was before the troggs came.  They came so fast and in such numbers that not even dwarven might could stop them!$B$BIn fact, their attack was so sudden that I fear some of our people may be trapped behind enemy lines.$B$BMy friend Baelog led a small band of dwarves deep within the site just before the troggs showed up.  If he and his company live, then I want you to find them.\030Find Baelog in Uldaman.\030\030The Lost Dwarves\0312,1,46,2,257,1,1356\0302,49,101,2,257,1,1356\0302,103,134,2,257,1,1356\0302,137,218,2,257,4,1356\0302,223,323,2,261,1,1356\0302,328,426,2,257,1,1356\0302,429,485,2,259,4,1356\0303,1,23,2,384,1,1356\0301,1,30,4,272,1,6906\0301,32,73,4,276,1,6906\0301,78,159,4,280,4,6906\0301,161,239,4,272,1,6906\0301,244,254,4,272,1,6906\0301,256,288,4,272,1,6906\0316906,2,6,Baelog\0306906,2,8,Baelog\0306908,4,10,Olaf\0312,1517,1418,0,\0302,0,0,1,Uldaman\0302,0,0,8,Uldaman\0312240,23,2240,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2399]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The fronds Denalan planted within his garden have sprouted and grown.  They tremble, eager to be picked....\030\030\030\030The Sprouted Fronds\0311,1,69,4,272,1,0\0301,72,107,4,272,1,0\0312080,4,1,Denalan\0312,141,1438,0,\031931,19,931,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,7510,GIVER,?,9,Sprouted Frond\030OBJECT,7510,FINISHER,?,12,Sprouted Frond",[24]="PARTIAL\031loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A victory for $N in the Ashenvale Hunt! Well done - the head of Shadumbra is a fitting trophy to claim for such an impressive fight, no doubt.$B$BShadumbra's savagery was well known throughout the post here. Any trip to the west, especially on foot trying to get out to the Zoram Strand, was wrought with danger because of this tiger. Thanks to you, this danger has abated.\030The once swift Shadumbra now lies still as you claim victory over it.  The head of the slain nightsaber is a fitting trophy for this fight of the Ashenvale Hunt.  Senani Thunderheart at Splintertree Post will want to see such a trophy to award you credit for this part of the Ashenvale Hunt.\030Bring Shadumbra's Head to Senani Thunderheart at Splintertree Post, Ashenvale.\030Greetings once again, $N! Have you come to show me proof of your hunt?\030Shadumbra's Head\0312,1,69,2,257,1,0\0302,72,161,2,261,1,0\0302,164,291,2,259,3,0\0303,1,78,2,384,1,0\0301,1,39,4,272,1,12696\0301,41,142,4,276,1,12696\0301,147,207,4,272,1,12696\0301,209,334,4,310,1,12696\0301,336,373,4,308,1,12696\0304,1,25,3,256,1,12696\0304,27,70,3,256,2,12696\03112677,2,1,Shadumbra\0302042,2,2,Nightsaber\03012696,2,3,Senani Thunderheart\0309084,2,3,Thunderheart\03012696,2,4,Senani Thunderheart\0309084,2,4,Thunderheart\03012677,4,6,Shadumbra\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,3,Splintertree Post\0302,0,0,4,Senani Thunderheart\0302,0,0,4,Splintertree Post\0304,0,0,5,Ashenvale Hunt\0304,0,0,8,Zoram Strand\0316383,19,6383,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,16304,STARTER,?,10,",[240]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Aha! Thank you, $N. Those really hit the spot!$B$BAnd here, please let me pay you for these!\030And here we are - \"Crab\" Cakes ala Grual!\030Return to Jitters with the Dusky Crab Cakes.\030$N, you're here! Do you have my food?!?\030Return to Jitters\0312,1,41,2,257,1,272\0303,1,44,2,384,1,272\0301,1,4,4,272,1,288\0301,6,19,4,272,1,288\0301,21,46,4,272,1,288\0301,51,92,4,272,1,288\0304,1,16,3,256,1,288\0304,18,39,3,256,2,288\0316827,2,1,Crab\030288,2,2,Jitters\0306827,2,2,Crab\0304950,4,5,Spot\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,2,Jitters\03193,19,93,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2418]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031That's great, you found some!  Thanks a lot, $N.  You're the most dependable $r I've met!$B$BI can't wait to try these on some devices I've been tinkering with.  I bet that, under the right circumstances, devices powered with these stones will keep going, and going, and going...\030A while ago, I had an incident with the Shadowforge Dwarves.  They brought me to Angor Fortress to study two types of strange stones from Uldaman.  I discovered that the stones were sustained, stable power sources if treated correctly.  It's amazing the things one can find in that old dig site!$B$BAnyway, after I told them the secret of the stones they kicked me out of Angor Fortress and began digging for more in Uldaman.$B$BI want those stones for myself!  Bring me both types and I'll pay you plenty!\030Bring 8 Dentrium Power Stones and 8 An'Alleum Power Stones to Rigglefuzz in the Badlands.\030Do you have the power stones, $N?  I have a robotic rodent that needs a power supply...\030Power Stones\0312,1,60,2,257,1,2817\0302,63,146,2,257,1,2817\0302,149,235,2,257,4,2817\0302,238,295,2,257,1,2817\0302,300,425,2,257,1,2817\0302,430,460,2,259,1,2817\0302,463,506,2,257,1,2817\0303,1,89,2,384,1,2817\0301,1,29,4,272,1,2817\0301,32,48,4,272,1,2817\0301,51,89,4,272,1,2817\0301,94,160,4,272,1,2817\0301,163,279,4,272,3,2817\0304,1,33,3,256,2,2817\0304,36,87,3,258,1,2817\0312817,2,8,Rigglefuzz\0312,1517,1418,0,\0302,0,0,2,Angor Fortress\0302,0,0,2,Uldaman\0302,0,0,5,Uldaman\0302,0,0,8,Rigglefuzz\0302,0,0,8,Badlands\031\031ITEM,8009,OBJECTIVE,8,15,\030ITEM,8052,OBJECTIVE,8,15,",[243]="PARTIAL\031conflict,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, our model 4711-FTZ power sources! We normally use them to power the water wells, but THANKS TO THE VILE NOMADS, we have an over abundance of power sources right now.$B$BSure, I can get you a power source for whatever nefarious science experiment you think you're trying to hide from me. It ain't gonna be free though, $R. Nothing's free in Gadgetzan.\030You will be headed to the Tanaris desert, testing the tissue consistency of the basilisks, scorpids, and hyena native there.  Obtain tissue samples and use them with the testing kit in tow; expect a chunk of the samples to fail.  I need eight acceptable samples of each creature type.$B$BIn addition, the goblins of Gadgetzan have a power source that must be used with this kind of modified kit.  Speak to Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle and acquire one for the kit.$B$BReturn to me only when you are successful.\030Speak to Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle in Gadgetzan about getting a power source for the testing kit.\030\030Into the Field\0312,1,124,2,257,3,5204\0302,127,228,2,257,1,5204\0302,231,284,2,259,1,5204\0302,289,395,2,257,1,5204\0302,398,462,2,257,1,5204\0302,467,508,2,257,1,5204\0303,1,99,2,384,1,5204\0301,1,37,4,272,1,7407\0301,39,169,4,304,1,7407\0301,174,290,4,272,1,7407\0301,292,325,4,272,1,7407\0301,327,354,4,272,1,7407\0317407,2,5,Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle\0307407,2,7,Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle\0312,440,1446,0,\0302,0,0,1,Tanaris\0302,0,0,5,Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle\0302,0,0,7,Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle\0302,0,0,7,Gadgetzan\0304,0,0,12,Gadgetzan\031238,19,238,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030379,23,379,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2438]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031My emerald dreamcatcher is of great importance to me. It is a gift only given to few. Thank you for returning it, $N.\030I was once given an emerald dreamcatcher from Gaerolas Talvethen, the warden of the druids in the Ban'ethil Barrow Den. This powerful amulet is able to siphon energy from the Emerald Dream, bestowing luck upon those who carry it.$B$BSadly, I have not been able to retrieve it from my dresser in Starbreeze Village... Although Starbreeze was once a tranquil place, it has now succumbed to the corruption of the furbolg that reside there.$B$BPerhaps you would be willing to recover my dreamcatcher, $c?\030Bring the Emerald Dreamcatcher to Tallonkai Swiftroot in Dolanaar.\030Please move swiftly. I can only hope that my emerald dreamcatcher has been unharmed by the furbolg.$B$BHave you recovered it yet, $N?\030The Emerald Dreamcatcher\0312,1,119,2,257,1,3567\0302,121,229,2,257,1,3567\0302,234,316,2,257,1,3567\0302,318,436,2,261,1,3567\0302,441,500,2,257,4,3567\0303,1,66,2,384,1,3567\0301,1,53,4,272,1,3567\0301,55,85,4,272,1,3567\0301,87,117,4,272,1,3567\0304,1,20,3,256,1,3567\0304,22,99,3,258,3,3567\0304,104,133,3,256,2,3567\03131,2,4,Furbolg\0303567,2,6,Tallonkai Swiftroot\03031,3,11,Furbolg\0312,141,1438,0,\0302,0,0,1,Gaerolas Talvethen\0302,0,0,1,Ban'ethil Barrow Den\0302,0,0,2,Emerald Dream\0302,0,0,3,Starbreeze Village\0302,0,0,6,Tallonkai Swiftroot\0302,0,0,6,Dolanaar\0312459,23,2459,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,8048,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[2439]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031As yes, a voucher from the Explorers' League... and quite the valuable one, might I add.$B$BThe Explorers' League lends me the authority to offer you a choice in your compensation directly from their vault.  You are to receive this item, and you may choose between five superior healing potions or five greater mana potions as your reward.\030This object is an incredible find.  The ancient Titans, or the Creators as these discs refer to them as, are the link to our enchanted creation, if the lore stored in here is correct!  We'll need to invest as much research time into this as possible.$B$BAs for you, heroic $c, take this voucher to Dinita Stonemantle at the vault.  It grants you what I think is a fitting for such a tremendous find!$B$BReturn to me directly when you are ready; there is much more to do for the Explorers' League!\030Take your reward voucher to Dinita Stonemantle in the Vault of Ironforge.\030Welcome to the Vault of Ironforge, $N.  What may I do for you today?\030The Platinum Discs\0312,1,34,2,257,1,5387\0302,37,183,2,321,4,5387\0302,186,250,2,259,1,5387\0302,255,330,2,257,1,5387\0302,333,399,2,257,1,5387\0302,404,496,2,257,1,5387\0303,1,73,2,384,1,5387\0301,1,47,4,272,1,7292\0301,49,88,4,272,4,7292\0301,93,206,4,272,1,7292\0301,209,339,4,272,1,7292\0304,1,38,3,256,1,7292\0304,41,68,3,256,2,7292\0317292,2,4,Dinita Stonemantle\0307292,2,7,Dinita Stonemantle\0312,1537,1455,0,\0302,0,0,4,Dinita Stonemantle\0302,0,0,7,Dinita Stonemantle\0302,0,0,7,Vault of Ironforge\0304,0,0,8,Explorers' League\0303,0,0,12,Vault of Ironforge\0312279,19,2279,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302963,23,2963,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[244]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031There are Redridge gnolls that close to Elwynn?? They may be poised to advance into our homeland. Soon the people of Lakeshire may not be the only humans under siege!$B$BHere is your pay, though you bring us dire news. And it comes at a bad time, for we are ill equipped to deal with it.\030Hail, $c.  I am charged to patrol this stretch of road.  Although the road is safe for now, I've seen gnoll encampments to the north and east of here.$B$BLakeshire must know of the gathering gnoll force!  Report to Deputy Feldon in Lakeshire and tell him of the gnolls.  Do this, and I'm sure Feldon will offer you a scout's wage.$B$BFeldon's usually inspecting the area south of the bridge to Lakeshire.\030Report to Deputy Feldon.\030\030Encroaching Gnolls\0312,1,9,2,257,1,464\0302,12,55,2,257,1,464\0302,58,150,2,257,1,464\0302,155,203,2,257,1,464\0302,206,269,2,257,1,464\0302,272,330,2,257,3,464\0302,335,404,2,257,1,464\0303,1,24,2,384,1,464\0301,1,48,4,272,2,1070\0301,50,97,4,272,1,1070\0301,99,166,4,272,1,1070\0301,171,218,4,272,1,1070\0301,220,287,4,272,1,1070\0311070,2,5,Deputy Feldon\0301070,2,8,Deputy Feldon\0312,44,1433,0,\0302,0,0,5,Deputy Feldon\0302,0,0,5,Lakeshire\0302,0,0,7,Lakeshire\0302,0,0,8,Deputy Feldon\0304,0,0,9,Elwynn\031246,23,246,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2440]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well $N, you must have pleased Sage Truthseeker greatly for him to give you this item. You are also to be granted a gift from his cache of potions; you may choose between 5 superior healing potions or 5 greater mana potions as your reward.\030I shall focus my energies on these discs; they will reveal their true workings to me in due time.$B$BAs for you $N, I will now reward you for your diligence in bringing this to my attention.  Take this voucher to Bena Winterhoof, the alchemy trainer for Thunder Bluff.  She will give you a special item I believe you will find appealing, and she will supply you with a choice of potions from my personal stock.$B$BReturn to me soon, as I sense there is much more at hand for us to do regarding this find.\030Take the reward voucher to Bena Winterhoof in Thunder Bluff.\030Greetings, $C! Are you here for alchemy training, or perhaps something else?\030The Platinum Discs\0312,1,97,2,257,3,3978\0302,102,190,2,257,3,3978\0302,193,268,2,257,1,3978\0302,271,410,2,257,4,3978\0302,415,504,2,257,1,3978\0303,1,60,2,384,1,3978\0301,1,86,4,272,1,3009\0301,88,239,4,272,1,3009\0304,1,14,3,256,1,3009\0304,16,76,3,256,4,3009\0313009,2,3,Bena Winterhoof\0303009,2,6,Bena Winterhoof\0303978,4,7,Sage Truthseeker\0312,1638,1456,0,\0302,0,0,3,Bena Winterhoof\0302,0,0,6,Bena Winterhoof\0302,0,0,6,Thunder Bluff\0312280,19,2280,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302965,23,2965,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[245]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah! You're back. And not too much worse for wear, it'd seem. Of course, $N, the Night Watch is grateful for your work, and I did promise you a reward, so here.\030Hail, $c. Perhaps you've seen those spiders that have taken over the western border? The eight-legged menaces are too much for us to handle, and the Commander hasn't enough manpower to spare so far from Darkshire.$B$BI hate to ask this of you, but you seem like you might be able to handle them. I can't promise you anything of great value, but I can reward you if you can help root out the filthy bugs.$B$BOh, and a word of advice, you'll want to avoid their venom if you can.\030Kill 15 Pygmy Venom Web Spiders, and then report back to Watcher Dodds in Duskwood.\030You'd best be careful when dealing with the spiders, I've lost a few of my men to them, and trust me, it isn't a pleasant sight to see a man hanging upside down in their webs after the venom has started to soften them up.$B$BI wouldn't want to see one of the bugs having you for lunch.\030Eight-Legged Menaces\0312,1,9,2,257,1,888\0302,11,84,2,257,4,888\0302,86,213,2,257,1,888\0302,218,295,2,257,4,888\0302,297,403,2,257,4,888\0302,408,477,2,259,4,888\0303,1,83,2,384,1,888\0301,5,16,4,272,1,888\0301,18,60,4,272,4,888\0301,62,159,4,272,1,888\0304,1,221,3,260,1,888\0304,226,285,3,256,1,888\031888,2,7,Watcher Dodds\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,3,Darkshire\0302,0,0,7,Watcher Dodds\0302,0,0,7,Duskwood\031\031NPC,539,OBJECTIVE,15,13,Pygmy Venom Web Spider",[2458]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It's good to see another agent of the Shattered Hand in these parts, however, the flare may have been a little too much!$B$BNext time you need to speak with me, blow into this whistle twice and I'll know you are an ally.\030The Venture Company... Perhaps you have heard of them?$B$BFor one year we have worked on planting an agent deep within their ranks. Through much hard work and careful planning, we succeeded.$B$BRecently we received word that the Venture Co. are planning something on a grand scale. Go north of the Sludge Fen to the Venture Co. tower and contact our undercover agent, Taskmaster Fizzule.$B$BWhen you find the tower, use this flare gun, then approach Fizzule and show him the salute of the Shattered Hand.$B\030Travel to the Venture Co. Tower, north of the Sludge Fen and contact the Shattered Hand's covert operative, Taskmaster Fizzule.$B$BWhen the tower is in sight, use the Flare Gun to signal your arrival to Taskmaster Fizzule. Fire off TWO flares, then approach Taskmaster Fizzule and perform the Shattered /Salute.$B$BThese actions must be performed in the correct order, as Fizzule will attack and terminate any person he does not recognize.\030\030Deep Cover\0312,1,22,2,257,1,3401\0302,24,54,2,257,4,3401\0302,59,131,2,257,1,3401\0302,133,190,2,257,1,3401\0302,195,240,2,257,1,3401\0302,242,281,2,257,1,3401\0302,283,327,2,257,1,3401\0302,329,387,2,257,1,3401\0302,392,504,2,257,1,3401\0303,1,25,2,384,1,3401\0303,27,127,2,384,1,3401\0303,132,222,2,384,1,3401\0303,224,311,2,384,1,3401\0303,316,439,2,388,3,3401\0301,1,120,4,272,1,7233\0301,125,220,4,274,1,7233\0312479,2,7,Sludge\0307233,2,8,Taskmaster Fizzule\0302479,2,11,Sludge\0307233,2,11,Taskmaster Fizzule\0307233,2,12,Taskmaster Fizzule\0307233,2,13,Taskmaster Fizzule\0312,0,0,7,Sludge Fen\0302,0,0,7,Venture Co\0302,0,0,10,Venture Co\0302,0,0,11,Sludge Fen\0302,0,0,12,Taskmaster Fizzule\0312460,19,2460,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302478,23,2478,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2459]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Now I can repair my dreamcatcher. Thank you, $N.\030The emerald... It is missing! My dreamcatcher has been damaged!$B$BThere is a band of Gnarlpine mystics located to the north of Starbreeze. I have heard reports that their leader, Ferocitas the Dream Eater has been wearing a necklace that glows green in the night. Now seeing my dreamcatcher, I am sure that he has stolen my emerald... He would never realize that its power is useless to him.$B$BFind this missing jewel, $N. And, while you're there, clear out some of the corrupted mystics as well.\030Tallonkai Swiftroot in Dolanaar wants you to kill 7 Gnarlpine Mystics and find the Missing Jewel.\030Ferocitas and the Gnarlpine Mystics must return what is mine. Please retrieve the emerald so that I may repair my emerald dreamcatcher.\030Ferocitas the Dream Eater\0312,1,14,2,257,1,3567\0302,16,29,2,261,1,3567\0302,31,63,2,257,1,3567\0302,68,139,2,257,1,3567\0302,141,264,2,257,1,3567\0302,266,335,2,261,1,3567\0302,337,392,2,257,4,3567\0302,397,424,2,261,1,3567\0302,426,498,2,261,1,3567\0303,1,97,2,390,1,3567\0301,1,33,4,272,1,3567\0301,35,48,4,272,1,3567\0304,1,61,3,256,1,3567\0304,63,135,3,258,1,3567\0317234,2,5,Ferocitas the Dream Eater\0307903,2,8,Jewel\0303567,2,10,Tallonkai Swiftroot\0307903,2,10,Jewel\0312,141,1438,0,\0302,0,0,4,Starbreeze\0302,0,0,10,Dolanaar\0312438,19,2438,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,7235,OBJECTIVE,7,13,Gnarlpine Mystic\030ITEM,8050,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[246]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Deputy Feldon listens to your report...>$B$BThere's a sizable force of gnolls encamped there, and from what you tell me they are tough ones. It must not have been easy for you to gather this intelligence.$B$BHere you are, $N. We are grateful for your aid.$B$BAnd if you haven't already done so, speak with Marshal Marris and Magistrate Solomon within Lakeshire. Our situation grows ever more desperate - those two will have need of you I'm sure.\030We don't have men to spare, but something must be done about those gnolls you reported to me.$B$BScout southern Redridge for gnolls.  Harry them, kill those you can and report back to me with a count of their numbers and an assessment of the threat they present.  You may find those gnolls camped all along the southern road of Redridge.$B$BDo this for the Stormwind Army, $N, and you will be rewarded.\030Kill 10 Redridge Mongrels and 6 Redridge Poachers, then report back to Deputy Feldon in Lakeshire.\030Excuse me, $N, but we have a lot to keep our hands tied here. If you have nothing to report, then I must put my mind to other matters.\030Assessing the Threat\0312,1,93,2,257,1,1070\0302,98,132,2,257,1,1070\0302,135,262,2,261,1,1070\0302,265,337,2,257,1,1070\0302,342,402,2,257,3,1070\0303,1,98,2,384,1,1070\0301,1,41,4,272,1,1070\0301,46,141,4,272,1,1070\0301,143,205,4,280,1,1070\0301,210,226,4,272,1,1070\0301,228,256,4,272,1,1070\0301,261,362,4,272,4,1070\0301,364,446,4,274,3,1070\0304,1,61,3,256,1,1070\0304,63,134,3,256,4,1070\0311070,2,6,Deputy Feldon\0301070,4,7,Deputy Feldon\030382,4,12,Marshal Marris\030344,4,12,Magistrate Solomon\030798,4,12,Solomon\0312,44,1433,0,\0302,0,0,6,Deputy Feldon\0302,0,0,6,Lakeshire\0304,0,0,12,Lakeshire\031244,19,244,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,423,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Redridge Mongrel\030NPC,424,OBJECTIVE,6,13,Redridge Poacher",[2460]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $N. You are now ready to proceed.\030As a rogue of the Shattered Hand, it is imperative that you learn the Shattered Salute. It is the only way to truly identify another member of the Hand.$B$BWatch, learn, repeat.\030Perform the Shattered Salute on Shenthul.\030Shattered Salute Performed\030\030The Shattered Salute\0312,1,87,2,257,1,3401\0302,89,152,2,257,1,3401\0302,157,177,2,257,1,3401\0303,1,41,2,384,1,3401\0301,1,14,4,272,1,3401\0301,16,44,4,272,1,3401\0304,1,26,3,384,1,3401\0313401,2,4,Shenthul\031\0312458,23,2458,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[247]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031$N, you have slain all three beasts that comprise the Ashenvale Hunt. You have brought me adequate proof of their demise; there is no question of your strength and tenacity. The blood of a hunter streaks through your veins, and you should be commended!$B$BPlease, accept this bauble as a sign of congratulations on your mighty deeds done in Ashenvale for the Horde today. May your ancestors watch over you!\030\030\030\030The Hunt Completed\0311,1,69,4,276,1,12696\0301,71,173,4,272,1,12696\0301,175,252,4,272,1,12696\0301,257,371,4,272,1,12696\0301,373,406,4,272,1,12696\031\0312,331,1440,0,\0304,0,0,4,Ashenvale\0312,21,2,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\03023,21,23,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\03024,21,24,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2478]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Poor Fizzule, he was a good agent -- one of our best. Alas, it is the price we pay, $N. Being a field agent of the Shattered Hand is dangerous work.$B$BYou have performed your duty well, $C. It would be a shame if you did not live to serve us again.\030You will need to steal the tower key from Foreman Silixiz, $N. Once you've got the key in your possession, hold on to it - I may need it later.$B$BRemember, the poison has weakened everything in this tower. Use your abilities to bring chaos and destruction to its inhabitants. Slay them all -- show no mercy!$B$BOnce everything inside lays in a bloodied heap, pick Gallywix's lockbox and steal the cache of Zanzil's mixture held inside. Take both the head of Gallywix and the mixture to Shenthul in Orgrimmar.\030Steal Silixiz's Tower Key from Foreman Silixiz, then kill two Mutated Venture Co. Drones, two Venture Co. Patrollers, and two Venture Co. Lookouts.$B$BAssassinate Grand Foreman Gallywix and take his head, then pick the lock on Gallywix's lockbox and steal the Cache of Zanzil's Altered Mixture. Take the Cache and Gallywix's Head back to Shenthul in Orgrimmar for further instruction.$B\030What have you to report, $N?\030Mission: Possible But Not Probable\0312,1,62,2,263,3,7233\0302,64,143,2,259,1,7233\0302,148,206,2,261,1,7233\0302,208,276,2,257,1,7233\0302,278,308,2,257,1,7233\0302,313,436,2,261,1,7233\0302,438,509,2,257,1,7233\0303,1,81,2,388,1,7233\0303,83,105,2,384,1,7233\0303,107,137,2,384,1,7233\0303,139,147,2,384,1,7233\0303,152,294,2,388,1,7233\0303,296,384,2,384,1,7233\0301,1,53,4,272,1,3401\0301,55,87,4,272,1,3401\0301,89,148,4,272,1,3401\0301,153,190,4,272,1,3401\0301,192,249,4,272,4,3401\0304,1,28,3,256,2,3401\0317287,2,1,Foreman Silixiz\0303401,2,7,Shenthul\0307287,2,8,Foreman Silixiz\0303401,2,13,Shenthul\0312,0,0,1,Foreman Silixiz\0302,0,0,7,Shenthul\0302,0,0,7,Orgrimmar\0302,0,0,8,Foreman Silixiz\0302,0,0,13,Shenthul\0302,0,0,13,Orgrimmar\0312458,19,2458,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302479,23,2479,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,7310,OBJECTIVE,2,13,Mutated Venture Co. Drone\030NPC,7307,OBJECTIVE,2,13,Venture Co. Lookout\030NPC,7308,OBJECTIVE,2,13,Venture Co. Patroller\030ITEM,8074,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,8072,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,8073,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[2479]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You look deliciously pale, $C. And what is that foul aroma you are giving off? I must know!\030Take a sample of the mixture to Serge Hinott in Tarren Mill.$B$BIf anyone can cure you, it's Serge. Live long enough and Serge will show you the ways of poison creation and use.\030Travel to Tarren Mill in Hillsbrad Foothills and deliver the Sample of Zanzil's Mixture to Serge Hinott.$B$BTo get to Tarren Mill, take the Zeppelin to the Undercity and follow the road south through Silverpine and towards Hillsbrad. Follow the signs!$B$B\030What's this???\030Hinott's Assistance\0312,1,60,2,257,1,3401\0302,65,99,2,257,4,3401\0302,101,177,2,261,3,3401\0303,1,104,2,384,1,3401\0303,109,233,2,384,1,3401\0303,235,251,2,384,1,3401\0301,1,30,4,272,1,2391\0301,32,78,4,272,2,2391\0301,80,91,4,272,1,2391\0304,1,14,3,256,2,2391\0312391,2,1,Serge Hinott\0302391,2,4,Serge Hinott\0312,0,0,1,Serge Hinott\0302,0,0,1,Tarren Mill\0302,0,0,4,Tarren Mill\0302,0,0,4,Hillsbrad Foothills\0302,0,0,4,Serge Hinott\0302,0,0,5,Tarren Mill\0302,0,0,5,Undercity\0312478,19,2478,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302480,23,2480,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[248]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It is a suitable vessel for the Glyph of Azora, allowing Theocritus to delve into the minds within Stonewatch Keep.\030I have been watching the Tower of Ilgalar, and can detect that Morganth is in conflict with the Orcs in Stonewatch Keep.  I do not know the reason behind their contention, but you may aid me in unraveling this mystery.$B$BTake another Glyph of Azora, then go to the top of the intact watch tower beside Stonewatch Keep.$B$BFind a suitable object on which to place the Glyph.  A chest or a jar -- some place where the glyph will not be noticed -- will suit my purpose.\030Climb the intact watch tower beside Stonewatch Keep.$B$BFind a suitable container to place the Glyph of Azora.\030This jar once held a foul-smelling liquor, but now lies empty and forgotten on a pair of barrels.\030Looking Further\0312,1,120,2,257,1,0\0302,123,218,2,257,1,0\0302,223,319,2,257,1,0\0302,324,374,2,257,1,0\0302,377,467,2,257,3,0\0303,1,52,2,384,1,0\0303,57,110,2,384,1,0\0301,1,115,4,272,1,0\0304,1,97,3,256,1,0\031397,2,1,Morganth\030313,4,8,Theocritus\0312,44,1433,0,\0302,0,0,1,Stonewatch Keep\0304,0,0,8,Stonewatch Keep\03194,19,94,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030249,23,249,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,31,GIVER,?,9,Old Lion Statue\030OBJECT,76,FINISHER,?,12,An Empty Jar",[2480]="PARTIAL\031consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031The cure is ready! Drink this anti-toxin and the creeping madness will stop, however, I will not be able to do anything about the smell.\030I have never seen such wondrous results from a poison! Zanzil you say? Never heard of him, however, I must commend him on the creation of this concoction.$B$BSo, I am to cure you of this and then teach you how to make use of the poison?$B$BGive me a few moments to examine the toxin, $N.\030Wait for Serge Hinott to complete the cure.\030Cure Completed\030\030Hinott's Assistance\0312,1,54,2,261,1,2391\0302,56,70,2,257,2,2391\0302,72,154,2,257,1,2391\0302,159,236,2,261,2,2391\0302,241,287,2,257,1,2391\0303,1,43,2,384,1,2391\0301,1,18,4,272,1,2391\0301,20,136,4,272,3,2391\0304,1,14,3,384,1,2391\0312391,2,6,Serge Hinott\031\0312479,19,2479,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[249]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have done well, $N. In defeating the warlock Morganth, Stormwind is saved from a grave peril.$B$BI offer you this reward most humbly. And I would bid you peace, if these were peaceful times.$B$BBut instead, I will bid you luck with your trials, and victory in the conflicts ahead.\030After much observation, I have discovered Morganth's plans.$B$BHe searches for the Scythe of Elune...and he may have found it!  If he has, then the Redridge Mountains, and the kingdom of Stormwind, will soon feel his dark might.$B$BI am not prepared to pit myself against Morganth, but I fear he must be dealt with now.  So you must enter the Tower of Ilgalar and face Morganth.$B$BDefeat him, and bring me his Pendant of Shadow.  Do this, and the kingdom will owe you much.\030Defeat Morganth.$B$BBring his Pendant of Shadow to Theocritus at the Tower of Azora in Elwynn Forest.\030Hurry, $N, before my fears of Morganth spreading his power are made real!\030Morganth\0312,1,59,2,257,1,313\0302,64,126,2,257,1,313\0302,129,228,2,257,4,313\0302,233,319,2,257,1,313\0302,322,378,2,257,1,313\0302,383,429,2,257,1,313\0302,432,474,2,257,3,313\0303,1,16,2,384,1,313\0303,21,101,2,384,1,313\0301,1,23,4,272,1,313\0301,25,97,4,272,1,313\0301,102,137,4,272,1,313\0301,139,194,4,280,4,313\0301,199,284,4,272,3,313\0304,1,73,3,256,1,313\031397,2,4,Morganth\030397,2,5,Morganth\0304244,2,6,Shadow\030397,2,8,Morganth\0304244,2,9,Shadow\030313,2,9,Theocritus\030397,4,11,Morganth\030397,3,15,Morganth\0312,44,1433,0,\0302,0,0,9,Theocritus\0302,0,0,9,Tower of Azora\0302,0,0,9,Elwynn Forest\031248,19,248,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,31,GIVER,?,9,Old Lion Statue\030ITEM,3617,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[2498]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, so Rellian sent you to aid me. I am glad you arrived here so soon.$B$BI have discovered something quite disturbing!\030I have just received word that  Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth has discovered what may be the cause of the tumors that plague the timberlings. Please speak with him, and tell him I sent you.$B$BMake haste, $N; he needs our help.\030Rellian Greenspyre wants you to speak with Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth.\030\030Return to Denalan\0312,1,136,2,261,1,3517\0302,138,184,2,257,1,3517\0302,189,222,2,259,1,3517\0303,1,68,2,386,1,3517\0301,1,34,4,272,1,2080\0301,36,70,4,272,1,2080\0301,75,119,4,272,1,2080\0312080,2,1,Denalan\0303517,2,4,Rellian Greenspyre\0302080,2,4,Denalan\0312,141,1438,0,\0302,0,0,1,Lake Al'Ameth\0302,0,0,4,Lake Al'Ameth\031923,19,923,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302499,23,2499,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2499]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I knew you were more than capable of ridding the lake of that horrible beast.$B$BIt is a distressing situation; Oakenscowl was once a grand leader amongst his kind... but corruption does not discriminate between the lowly and the noble.$B$BThe size of this tumor is quite disturbing, but I must study it to learn more about the disease that upsets the timberling population.$B$BThank you, $N.\030In a cave along the southern bank of the lake, a timberling named Oakenscowl is spreading corruption to all the creatures that make Lake Al'Ameth their home.$B$BI dared not get too close, but even from a distance, it is obvious: Oakenscowl is being poisoned by the largest tumor I have ever seen...  I would call it gargantuan, even.$B$B$N, you have already done much to aid my efforts, but I ask of you one more task. Hunt down Oakenscowl and collect the tumor; remove this source of corruption from my home.\030Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth wants you to collect the Gargantuan Tumor from Oakenscowl.\030Have you located Oakenscowl yet, $R?\030Oakenscowl\0312,1,157,2,261,1,2080\0302,162,298,2,261,1,2080\0302,301,333,2,257,4,2080\0302,338,418,2,259,1,2080\0302,420,509,2,261,1,2080\0303,1,83,2,386,1,2080\0301,1,77,4,272,1,2080\0301,82,166,4,272,1,2080\0301,168,236,4,276,1,2080\0301,241,374,4,272,1,2080\0301,379,392,4,272,1,2080\0304,1,36,3,256,2,2080\0312022,2,1,Timberling\0302166,2,1,Oakenscowl\0302166,2,2,Oakenscowl\0302166,2,5,Oakenscowl\0302080,2,6,Denalan\0302166,2,6,Oakenscowl\0302166,4,8,Oakenscowl\0302022,4,10,Timberling\0302166,3,12,Oakenscowl\0312,141,1438,0,\0302,0,0,6,Lake Al'Ameth\0302,0,0,6,Oakenscowl\0312498,19,2498,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,8136,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[25]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Yeah, I heard that someone tore up the lake out there like a dust devil through the Barrens. From the sound of it too, we might be able to set up a possible observation area out there to keep an eye on our Alliance friends. Well, that is if we can keep it on the down low...$B$BLooks like you ended up being quite useful after all; the transports between here and Stonetalon should have an easier time of it. Take this - you've earned it.\030If you want to be useful, then why don't you do something about the situation near Talondeep Path?$B$BThe transports between Ashenvale and Stonetalon are at a standstill because of the lake coming alive and attacking anything that gets close... which means anyone on the path.  What'd be even more useful than just putting the hammer down on the water elementals there is someone scouting the gazebo on Mystral Lake - the one that has a solid view of the Alliance outpost there.$B$BYou up for being useful?\030Dispatch 12 Befouled Water Elementals at Mystral Lake, due east of the Talondeep Path and southwest of Splintertree Post.$B$BScout the gazebo on Mystral Lake that overlooks the nearby Alliance outpost.$B$BReturn to Mastok Wrilehiss at Splintertree Post, Ashenvale.\030Scout the gazebo on Mystral Lake that overlooks the nearby Alliance outpost.\030You back already? What's the situation out there - all cleared up now, thanks to you?\030Stonetalon Standstill\0312,1,98,2,259,4,12737\0302,103,244,2,263,1,12737\0302,246,276,2,257,1,12737\0302,279,478,2,257,1,12737\0302,483,506,2,257,2,12737\0303,1,121,2,384,1,12737\0303,126,201,2,384,1,12737\0303,206,264,2,384,1,12737\0301,1,92,4,272,1,12737\0301,94,223,4,272,4,12737\0301,225,274,4,272,4,12737\0301,279,408,4,272,1,12737\0301,410,438,4,272,1,12737\0305,1,17,3,256,2,12737\0305,19,85,3,256,2,12737\0304,1,76,3,384,1,12737\03112737,2,8,Mastok Wrilehiss\030832,4,9,Dust Devil\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,1,Talondeep Path\0302,0,0,6,Mystral Lake\0302,0,0,6,Talondeep Path\0302,0,0,8,Mastok Wrilehiss\0302,0,0,8,Splintertree Post\031\031NPC,3917,OBJECTIVE,12,13,Befouled Water Elemental",[250]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The suspicious looking barrel contains a strange smelling powder.\030Thank the stars someone is concerned about the well-being of the Dam.  First the destruction of the Thandol Span and then the pillaging of Dun Modr!  I have no doubt that the Dam will be the target of the next Dark Iron threat.  Most of the security detail here was reassigned to the Alliance Front, including my top inspector.$B$BThat's why I need you, $N.  I spotted some Dark Iron Sappers milling about the eastern ramp of the Dam.   Investigate the area and bring back a clue.\030Investigate the area near the eastern ramp of the Dam and bring Chief Engineer Hinderweir a clue that might reveal what the Dark Iron Dwarves are up to.\030\030A Dark Threat Looms\0312,1,69,2,257,1,1093\0302,72,148,2,257,1,1093\0302,151,227,2,261,3,1093\0302,230,327,2,265,1,1093\0302,332,357,2,259,1,1093\0302,360,434,2,257,1,1093\0302,438,480,2,257,1,1093\0303,1,152,2,384,4,1093\0301,1,65,4,272,1,0\031\0312,38,1432,0,\0302,0,0,4,Alliance Front\031199,23,199,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,257,FINISHER,?,12,Suspicious Barrel",[2500]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, well done $N.  These should last me for a little while at least.  Here is your pay, as promised.$B$BIf you're interested, I have some more reagents I could use.  These, however, are only found in the depths of the Uldaman excavation.  They will not be easy to get, but I will make it worth your while if you are interested in helping me again.$B$BPerhaps something more than some shiny coins, yes?\030$C, I would make use of your services.  I am an alchemist of some note, and I seek your aid in acquiring some reagents found out in the Badlands.$B$BI need the following items to replenish my stocks: five buzzard gizzards, ten crag coyote fangs, and five rock elemental shards.  Obviously, you can get them off of the beasties themselves; if you're not the fighting type, then find friends who are.$B$BAcquire these items for me, you'll get some coin out of the deal.$B$BWell, what say ye?\030Acquire the reagents Ghak Healtouch needs from the Badlands, then return to him in Thelsamar.\030Have you gotten the things I need yet?  You won't get paid unless you bring me those reagents.\030Badlands Reagent Run\0312,1,38,2,257,4,1470\0302,41,145,2,259,1,1470\0302,150,277,2,259,1,1470\0302,280,398,2,261,4,1470\0302,403,467,2,257,1,1470\0302,472,489,2,257,2,1470\0303,1,93,2,386,1,1470\0301,1,17,4,272,1,1470\0301,20,68,4,272,1,1470\0301,71,100,4,272,1,1470\0301,105,164,4,272,4,1470\0301,167,237,4,272,1,1470\0301,240,347,4,272,4,1470\0301,352,401,4,272,4,1470\0304,1,38,3,258,2,1470\0304,41,94,3,264,4,1470\0312830,2,3,Buzzard\0302727,2,3,Crag Coyote\030834,2,3,Coyote\03092,2,3,Rock Elemental\0301470,2,7,Ghak Healtouch\0312,38,1432,0,\0302,0,0,2,Badlands\0302,0,0,7,Badlands\0302,0,0,7,Thelsamar\031\031ITEM,7847,OBJECTIVE,5,15,\030ITEM,7846,OBJECTIVE,10,15,\030ITEM,7848,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[2501]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031From one alchemist to another, I salute you.  Here, take this recipe and commit it to your knowledge.  May it bring you the success and rewards that it has brought me over the years!\030You have been most helpful to me, $N.  I would like to reward you with the very recipe for the brew I gave you earlier, but I must ask of you a favor that is quite dangerous.$B$BThis lockbox contains three empty thaumaturgy vessels; they are imbued with an attunement aura that will drain the blood of a scorched guardian dragon.  Using one on the beast will anger it greatly, so be careful.  Once you have all three filled, bring them to me.$B$BDo this, and the recipe will be yours.\030Use the empty thaumaturgy vessels on scorched guardian dragons found in the Badlands.  Once you have them filled, bring them to Ghak Healtouch in Thelsamar.\030Have you used the vessels to get me the scorched guardian dragon blood I need?  Yes, I know it is a dangerous task... but the recipe for my restorative brew awaits your success.  Risk and reward, my friend... risk and reward...\030Badlands Reagent Run II\0312,1,37,2,257,1,1470\0302,40,174,2,259,4,1470\0302,179,329,2,257,3,1470\0302,332,391,2,257,3,1470\0302,394,442,2,257,1,1470\0302,447,484,2,257,3,1470\0303,1,85,2,384,1,1470\0303,88,156,2,384,1,1470\0301,1,44,4,272,1,1470\0301,47,101,4,272,1,1470\0301,104,182,4,272,1,1470\0304,1,78,3,258,2,1470\0304,81,117,3,256,1,1470\0304,119,177,3,256,1,1470\0304,180,208,3,264,1,1470\0304,210,227,3,264,1,1470\0312726,2,3,Scorched Guardian\03010430,2,4,The Beast\0302726,2,7,Scorched Guardian\0301470,2,8,Ghak Healtouch\0302726,3,12,Scorched Guardian\0312,38,1432,0,\0302,0,0,7,Badlands\0302,0,0,8,Ghak Healtouch\0302,0,0,8,Thelsamar\0312500,19,2500,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,7867,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[251]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Sirra begins translating the note...>\030Take the note you gave me to Sirra Von'Indi.  He's very learned in languages and ancient arts - if anyone here can translate this message, it's he.\030Bring the Letter to Ello to Sirra Von'Indi.\030A note from Abercrombie the hermit, eh? I don't know him, though if he lives out at the graveyard then I do know his brains have rotted out!\030Translate Abercrombie's Note\0312,1,44,2,257,1,263\0302,47,147,2,321,4,263\0303,1,43,2,384,1,263\0301,1,38,4,272,1,268\0304,1,39,3,256,2,268\0304,41,140,3,256,4,268\031268,2,1,Sirra Von'Indi\030268,2,3,Sirra Von'Indi\030289,3,5,Abercrombie\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,1,Sirra Von'Indi\0302,0,0,3,Ello\0302,0,0,3,Sirra Von'Indi\0303,0,0,5,Abercrombie the\031160,19,160,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030401,23,401,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2518]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The forest mourns for Lady Sathrah, but it was something that had to be done.$B$BThank you, $N.\030Lady Sathrah was once beloved of Elune. Graceful and pure, the spider spun her silver threads through the moonlight, catching the evening mist. The silvery dew had strong healing powers and was kept here in the temple.$B$BBut of late, Sathrah has descended into madness. Her future generations are now threatened as well.$B$BFind Lady Sathrah, $N, and end her suffering. She dwells along the northern borders of Teldrassil, near Wellspring Lake. Gather her silvery spinnerets and bring them back to me.\030Priestess A'moora in the Temple of the Moon at Darnassus wants you to bring her Lady Sathrah's Silvery Spinnerets.\030I regret the task that I have asked you to carry out; but Lady Sathrah is beyond hope.$B$BIt is our hope to offer the sacrifice of the spinnerets to Elune. With this sacrifice, Elune will bless Sathrah so that she might be reborn, and at peace.\030Tears of the Moon\0312,1,39,2,257,1,7313\0302,41,143,2,257,1,7313\0302,145,218,2,257,1,7313\0302,223,270,2,257,1,7313\0302,272,321,2,261,1,7313\0302,326,370,2,261,1,7313\0302,372,445,2,257,1,7313\0302,447,502,2,257,1,7313\0303,1,114,2,386,1,7313\0301,1,77,4,272,1,7313\0301,82,95,4,272,1,7313\0304,1,86,3,258,3,7313\0304,91,155,3,258,3,7313\0304,157,244,3,266,4,7313\0317319,2,1,Lady Sathrah\03014881,2,2,Spider\0303568,2,2,Mist\0307319,2,6,Lady Sathrah\0307313,2,9,Priestess A'moora\0307319,2,9,Lady Sathrah\0307319,4,10,Lady Sathrah\0307319,3,12,Lady Sathrah\0312,1657,1457,0,\0302,0,0,7,Wellspring Lake\0302,0,0,9,Temple of the Moon\0302,0,0,9,Darnassus\0303,0,0,13,Elune\0312520,23,2520,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,8344,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[2519]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031So, Sister Aquinne sent you?\030A once great creature of the forest is in need of help, $r.$B$BThere is a difficult task that must be done.$B$BPlease seek out Priestess A'moora; she will explain things to you. Find her to the southeast of here, inside the Temple of the Moon.\030Sister Aquinne wants you to speak with Priestess A'moora in the Temple of the Moon.\030\030The Temple of the Moon\0312,1,59,2,259,1,7316\0302,64,107,2,257,1,7316\0302,112,177,2,259,3,7316\0302,179,243,2,257,1,7316\0303,1,83,2,386,1,7316\0301,1,28,4,272,2,7313\0317313,2,3,Priestess A'moora\0307316,2,5,Sister Aquinne\0307313,2,5,Priestess A'moora\0307316,4,6,Sister Aquinne\0312,1657,1457,0,\0302,0,0,5,Temple of the Moon\0312518,23,2518,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[252]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Ello reads the letter...and his face goes white. He then looks at you...>$B$BAlthough the aid you gave Abercrombie may have been motivated from kindness, your actions have doomed our town.$B$B<Ello becomes lost in his thoughts...>\030Oh my!  If what is written on this note is true, then Abercrombie's done something...unspeakable.$B$BYou better bring the translated note back to Ello.$B$BAnd do so quickly, for I fear a doom already lumbers toward our town...\030Bring the Translated Letter to Lord Ello Ebonlocke\030Ah, is the note translated? Please, let me see it...\030Translation to Ello\0312,9,97,2,257,4,268\0302,102,151,2,257,1,268\0302,156,226,2,257,1,268\0303,1,50,2,384,1,268\0301,1,49,4,272,1,263\0301,51,74,4,272,1,263\0301,79,189,4,272,1,263\0301,194,231,4,276,1,263\0304,1,27,3,256,2,263\0304,29,52,3,256,1,263\031263,2,4,Lord Ello Ebonlocke\030289,4,7,Abercrombie\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,2,Ello\0302,0,0,4,Lord Ello Ebonlocke\031401,19,401,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030253,23,253,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2520]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031The loss of Lady Sathrah is distressing, but in this way only may she be reborn with a renewed spirit.$B$BMay Elune willingly accept the sacrifice that you have offered her.\030Now you must finish the task to which you have been appointed. Take the spinnerets and offer Lady Sathrah's sacrifice to Elune; lay the great spider to rest.$B$BInside this temple, find the central fountain. There is where you may leave the sacrifice.  The holy waters will purify and cleanse the corruption that drove Sathrah mad.$B$BWhen you have completed this, return to me.\030Priestess A'moora wants you to place Lady Sathrah's silvery spinnerets at the fountain inside the temple, and then return to her.\030Offer the sacrifice at the fountain\030Have you placed the sacrifice at the fountain, $n?\030Sathrah's Sacrifice\0312,1,62,2,257,1,7313\0302,64,157,2,257,1,7313\0302,162,207,2,257,1,7313\0302,209,251,2,257,1,7313\0302,254,331,2,261,3,7313\0302,336,378,2,257,1,7313\0303,1,129,2,386,1,7313\0301,1,102,4,272,1,7313\0301,107,173,4,272,1,7313\0305,1,50,3,256,2,7313\0304,1,35,3,384,1,7313\0317319,2,2,Lady Sathrah\03014881,2,2,Spider\0307313,2,7,Priestess A'moora\0307319,2,7,Lady Sathrah\0307319,4,8,Lady Sathrah\0312,1657,1457,0,\0302,0,0,2,Elune\0312518,19,2518,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2521]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Do my eyes deceive me? Impossible! Where did you... How...$B$BPerhaps now a rift can be opened, returning us to our homeland.\030$R, can your miniscule brain comprehend the rarity of a flawless sphere of draenethyst? Draenei have spent lifetimes in search of just one of these crystals, only to meet horrible fates, their purpose unfulfilled.$B$BSo you stand before Kum'isha, knowing what Kum'isha has requested and still wish to assist? Very well, $r... At any time during your travels across these lands, should you find a flawless sphere of draenethyst, return it to me and I shall reward you with riches beyond your wildest dreams.\030In your journeys throughout the Blasted Lands, should you ever come across a Flawless Draenethyst Sphere, take the item back to Kum'isha the Collector.$B$BBe warned, this gem is one of the most rare crystals in all of Azeroth. Any creature in these lands could be holding a Flawless Draenethyst Sphere.$B$BYou will be rewarded for each Flawless Draenethyst Sphere you have collected.\030I have dedicated my life to the search of flawless draenethyst spheres. A lifetime, $r!\030To Serve Kum'isha\0312,1,87,2,257,2,7363\0302,89,213,2,257,1,7363\0302,218,308,2,259,2,7363\0302,310,325,2,257,1,7363\0302,327,506,2,257,3,7363\0303,1,151,2,384,1,7363\0303,156,226,2,384,1,7363\0303,228,302,2,384,4,7363\0303,307,383,2,384,3,7363\0301,1,22,4,272,2,7363\0301,24,34,4,272,1,7363\0301,36,51,4,272,1,7363\0301,53,58,4,272,1,7363\0301,63,125,4,272,4,7363\0304,1,71,3,256,1,7363\0304,73,87,3,256,1,7363\0317364,2,6,Flawless Draenethyst Sphere\0307363,2,6,Kum'isha the Collector\0307364,2,8,Flawless Draenethyst Sphere\0307364,2,9,Flawless Draenethyst Sphere\0312,4,1419,0,\0302,0,0,6,Kum'isha the Collector\0312522,23,2522,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,8244,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[2522]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Simply amazing. I had doubted that you could find another sphere, yet here it is, pulsating in my hands.$B$BWell done, $N!$B$BShould you find anymore--and I believe this to be an impossibility--return them to me and I shall reward you again.\030Even though the portal conjuration was a failure, I remain hopeful that my next attempt will be successful.$B$BThe hope of the Draenei is as fervent as your greed for trinkets, $r. Go back out into these cursed lands and recover another flawless draenethyst sphere.$B$BOf course, the choice to take on this task is completely left to you *grin*.\030Find and return a Flawless Draenethyst Sphere to Kum'isha the Collector.\030Have you found another flawless draenethyst sphere?\030Kum'isha's Endeavors\0312,1,107,2,257,3,7363\0302,112,180,2,259,3,7363\0302,182,265,2,261,1,7363\0302,270,345,2,257,1,7363\0303,1,72,2,384,1,7363\0301,1,15,4,272,1,7363\0301,17,104,4,272,4,7363\0301,109,122,4,272,1,7363\0301,127,241,4,272,4,7363\0304,1,51,3,256,2,7363\0317364,2,3,Flawless Draenethyst Sphere\0307364,2,5,Flawless Draenethyst Sphere\0307363,2,5,Kum'isha the Collector\0307364,3,10,Flawless Draenethyst Sphere\0312,4,1419,0,\0302,0,0,5,Kum'isha the Collector\0312521,19,2521,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,8244,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[2523]="PARTIAL\031characters,consequences,loreConnections,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You apply some Cenarion plant salve to the songflower. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.\030\030\030You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a songflower plant. A pungent, unhealthy odor emanates from the plant. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.\030Corrupted Songflower\0311,1,54,4,272,1,0\0301,56,149,4,276,1,0\0304,1,84,3,260,1,0\0304,86,135,3,256,1,0\0304,137,217,3,258,4,0\031\0312,361,1448,0,\031\031OBJECT,164886,GIVER,?,9,Corrupted Songflower\030OBJECT,164886,FINISHER,?,12,Corrupted Songflower\030ITEM,11516,OBJECTIVE,2,15,",[253]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You've done it! The magic within his heart will be proof against the Embalmer's evil, and a powerful aegis over the town of Darkshire.$B$BYou have done a great thing for our people, $N. Your name will remain in our annals forever.\030The Embalmer is a name told in one of our children's stories.  He was a kindly alchemist, driven mad by the death of his wife, Eliza.  To restore her, he used dark magic to place his own heart within the bosom of his dead spouse.$B$BThis revived Eliza...but it cursed her with a hunger for human flesh, forcing the Embalmer to keep her buried.$B$BHis heart is his power.  Find his wife's grave, retrieve his heart, and bring it to me while it still beats.  Do this and his power will be broken.\030Find Eliza's grave.  Retrieve the Embalmer's Heart from her, then return to Ello Ebonlocke.\030Have you yet found Eliza's grave? Do you have the Embalmer's heart?\030Bride of the Embalmer\0312,1,61,2,257,1,263\0302,64,133,2,257,1,263\0302,136,229,2,259,1,263\0302,234,343,2,261,1,263\0302,348,370,2,257,1,263\0302,373,455,2,257,1,263\0302,458,494,2,257,3,263\0303,1,19,2,384,1,263\0303,22,91,2,384,1,263\0301,1,15,4,272,1,263\0301,17,134,4,272,3,263\0301,139,185,4,272,1,263\0301,187,230,4,272,3,263\0304,1,33,3,256,2,263\0304,35,67,3,256,2,263\031314,2,2,Eliza\030314,2,4,Eliza\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,9,Ello Ebonlocke\031252,19,252,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,2382,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[254]="PARTIAL\031characters,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You dig through the semi-loose dirt over the grave...and find the remains of a coffin.$B$BWithin the coffin you can feel the vibrating scrapes of clawed fingers and the gnashing of rotted teeth...$B$BWill you open the coffin and retrieve the Embalmer's heart?\030\030\030\030Digging Through the Dirt\0311,1,86,4,272,1,0\0301,91,196,4,272,1,0\0301,201,259,4,272,2,0\031\0312,10,1431,0,\031253,20,253,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,51708,GIVER,?,9,Eliza's Grave Dirt\030OBJECT,51708,FINISHER,?,12,Eliza's Grave Dirt",[2541]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, $N.$B$BWhat an odd trinket this is... I can sense the vile aura emanating from it; this is a very powerful enchantment.\030The Gnarlpine shaman that inhabit this place have discovered a way of separating a sleeping druid's spirit from the physical body. The furbolg have animated my physical form and are using it to attack anyone that attempts to explore the Ban'ethil Barrow Den. I am now trapped in the Emerald Dream, powerless to stop this.$B$BYou must help me. The Gnarlpine shaman carry a strange charm which is used to perform this ritual, and I'd like to examine it. Please, $N, bring one to me.\030Bring a Shaman Voodoo Charm to Oben Rageclaw in the Ban'ethil Barrow Den.\030If I can examine the charm, I may be able to figure out how to break the enchantment. Have you found one?\030The Sleeping Druid\0312,1,130,2,257,1,7317\0302,132,258,2,261,1,7317\0302,260,321,2,257,1,7317\0302,326,342,2,257,1,7317\0302,344,451,2,259,1,7317\0302,453,480,2,257,1,7317\0303,1,73,2,384,1,7317\0301,1,14,4,272,1,7317\0301,19,48,4,272,1,7317\0301,50,130,4,272,1,7317\0304,1,85,3,256,4,7317\0304,87,105,3,256,2,7317\0312009,2,1,Gnarlpine Shaman\03031,2,2,Furbolg\0302009,2,5,Gnarlpine Shaman\0307317,2,7,Oben Rageclaw\0307318,2,7,Rageclaw\0312,141,1438,0,\0302,0,0,3,Emerald Dream\0302,0,0,7,Oben Rageclaw\0302,0,0,7,Ban'ethil Barrow Den\0312561,23,2561,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,8363,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[255]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, this is excellent news! Your efforts are greatly appreciated by myself and the people of Thelsamar. Better yet, if we can solve the ogre problem, we'll be able to shift our focus to those Light-burning troggs.\030Two months just to hear from Ironforge that we'll be spared a handful of soldiers for our own defense, and another two months until they arrive! Bad enough that our town goes unprotected, but the excavation and the dam--the dam!--are open to attacks as well.$B$BI've no choice then, it seems. I'll need hired arms.$B$BHow about you? You seem a likely sort, $c. A group of ogres has set up camp on the northeast of the lake. Perhaps you will be the one to remove the threat to our town?\030Magistrate Bluntnose of Thelsamar has hired you to kill 4 Mo'grosh Ogres, 4 Mo'grosh Brutes and 4 Mo'grosh Enforcers.\030Have you had any luck?\030Mercenaries\0312,1,144,2,257,1,1139\0302,146,258,2,261,1,1139\0302,263,292,2,257,4,1139\0302,294,314,2,259,1,1139\0302,319,332,2,257,2,1139\0302,334,360,2,257,4,1139\0302,362,423,2,257,1,1139\0302,425,485,2,261,4,1139\0303,1,117,2,384,1,1139\0301,1,27,4,272,1,1139\0301,29,103,4,272,1,1139\0301,105,213,4,276,4,1139\0304,1,22,3,256,2,1139\0311139,2,9,Magistrate Bluntnose\030211,4,12,Ogre\0312,38,1432,0,\0302,0,0,1,Ironforge\031\031NPC,1178,OBJECTIVE,4,13,Mo'grosh Ogre\030NPC,1180,OBJECTIVE,4,13,Mo'grosh Brute\030NPC,1179,OBJECTIVE,4,13,Mo'grosh Enforcer",[256]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yech! What is that thing? And why would you bring it...$B$BBloody--! Is it? Well, Light burn me, is that the head of that bloody ogre? This certainly is a catch then! Here, your reward and the thanks of myself and the people of Thelsamar.\030By order of the Magistrate of Thelsamar:$B$BChok'sul, the ogre presumed to be the leader and coordinator of attacks against the town of Thelsamar, Stonewrought Dam, and the excavation site, is wanted dead through any means necessary.$B$BMonetary compensation will be provided when proof is brought to the Magistrate of Chok'sul's death.$B$BChok'sul was last seen at the ogre encampment in the northeastern part of Loch Modan.\030Kill Chok'sul and bring his head to Magistrate Bluntnose of Thelsamar.\030Yes? Is there something I can do for you?\030WANTED: Chok'sul\0312,1,40,2,257,1,0\0302,45,233,2,261,1,0\0302,238,336,2,257,3,0\0302,341,425,2,257,1,0\0303,1,70,2,384,1,0\0301,1,5,4,272,1,1139\0301,7,25,4,272,2,1139\0301,27,55,4,272,4,1139\0301,60,68,4,272,1,1139\0301,77,134,4,272,2,1139\0301,136,166,4,272,1,1139\0301,168,238,4,272,1,1139\0304,1,4,3,256,2,1139\0304,6,41,3,256,2,1139\0311210,2,2,Chok'sul\030211,2,2,Ogre\0301210,2,4,Chok'sul\030211,2,4,Ogre\0301210,2,5,Chok'sul\0301139,2,5,Magistrate Bluntnose\030211,4,10,Ogre\0312,38,1432,0,\0302,0,0,3,Magistrate of Chok'sul's\0302,0,0,5,Magistrate Bluntnose of Thelsamar\031\031OBJECT,256,GIVER,?,9,WANTED\030ITEM,2561,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[2561]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031I am finally free of the control of the Gnarlpine. Thank you, $N.$B$BMy spirit may now rest peacefully forever in the Emerald Dream.$B$BPerhaps one day we may meet again, young $C. But, for now, please accept this reward as a symbol of my gratitude.\030After examining this charm, $N, I see now what must be done. Please take it, and do as I ask.$B$BYou are to explore the deepest areas of the Ban'ethil Barrow Den. There, you will find my soulless body... Although I regret what I am about to tell you, I see no other way to free myself from the control of the Gnarlpine.$B$BIn order for me to escape them, you must kill my physical form.  Once that is done, use the voodoo charm on my fallen body. After you have completed this task, please return to me.\030Oben Rageclaw wants you to kill his soulless body, and then use the Voodoo Charm.\030Release Oben Rageclaw's spirit\030$N, be wary when approaching my physical form; the enchantment it is under is quite powerful.\030Druid of the Claw\0312,1,60,2,257,1,7317\0302,62,93,2,259,1,7317\0302,98,162,2,257,1,7317\0302,164,203,2,257,3,7317\0302,205,319,2,257,1,7317\0302,324,386,2,257,1,7317\0302,389,446,2,257,1,7317\0302,448,503,2,257,1,7317\0303,1,81,2,386,1,7317\0301,1,50,4,272,1,7317\0301,52,65,4,272,1,7317\0301,70,132,4,272,1,7317\0301,137,180,4,272,4,7317\0301,182,249,4,272,1,7317\0305,1,93,3,256,1,7317\0304,1,30,3,384,1,7317\03114687,2,4,Soulless\0307317,2,9,Oben Rageclaw\0307318,2,9,Rageclaw\03014687,2,9,Soulless\0307317,3,16,Oben Rageclaw\0312,141,1438,0,\0304,0,0,12,Emerald Dream\0312541,19,2541,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,7318,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Rageclaw\030SPELL,10617,OBJECTIVE,?,17,",[257]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031What? Success?$B$BTake it from me, $Nama, you don't let it get to your head. I mean, any unshaven boy with a bow could have killed such... small specimens. And I hope you don't enjoy killing the buzzards so much, yes? We wouldn't want them to become extinct.$B$BWell, err... Never let it be said that Daryl the Bold would not hold to his word.\030Think you can match wits with Daryl the Bold, huh? I should think not! Of course, you're more than welcome to try. Here's a challenge that should prove to be above your abilities, so don't feel too bad if you can't face up to it.$B$BA flock of buzzards has nested here in Loch Modan. Why don't you try to take down some of the beasts? Tell you what, if you meet my challenge in fifteen minutes, I'll give you my bow or gun.$B$B<He looks you over dismissively.>$B$BIt seems you haven't much to lose, anyways.\030Kill 6 Mountain Buzzards and return to Daryl the Youngling in the Farstrider Lodge within 15 minutes.\030No luck? Don't feel too bad, $N...$B$BNot everyone can be me.\030A Hunter's Boast\0312,1,50,2,257,2,1187\0302,52,70,2,257,1,1187\0302,72,114,2,257,1,1187\0302,116,229,2,257,4,1187\0302,234,283,2,257,1,1187\0302,285,334,2,257,2,1187\0302,336,423,2,257,4,1187\0302,428,460,2,257,1,1187\0302,465,507,2,257,4,1187\0303,1,101,2,384,1,1187\0301,1,5,4,272,2,1187\0301,7,14,4,272,2,1187\0301,19,76,4,272,1,1187\0301,78,138,4,272,4,1187\0301,140,155,4,272,1,1187\0301,157,217,4,274,2,1187\0301,219,258,4,272,1,1187\0301,263,274,4,272,1,1187\0301,276,343,4,272,4,1187\0304,1,8,3,256,2,1187\0304,10,34,3,256,1,1187\0304,39,61,3,256,1,1187\0311187,2,10,Daryl the Youngling\0312,38,1432,0,\0302,0,0,5,Loch Modan\0302,0,0,10,Daryl the Youngling\0302,0,0,10,Farstrider Lodge\031258,23,258,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,1194,OBJECTIVE,6,13,Mountain Buzzard",[258]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You seem a bit worse for wear. No doubt the boars gave you some trouble, hm? No worries, I will be discreet about your struggle, I can imagine how hard it must be for you without the accusations of wagging tongues.$B$BOh! You managed to kill the boars? I... well, that is... that is to say, I'm not surprised! Any child could have--bet?$B$BWhat bet?\030$nath, is it? I can tell you're bursting with pride over completing the first test, hm? As I told you before, it's no large feat.$B$BYou should try your hand at boar hunting. Trust me, this is no Coldridge Valley boar hunt, so you'd best have a care with them. I'll give you just twelve minutes this time.$B$BDon't feel bad if you fail. I'd give you the shirt off my back if you succeeded!$B$BHave I ever related to you the story of how I received my famous scar? No? It was two years ago...\030Kill 5 Elder Mountain Boars and return to Daryl the Youngling in the Farstrider Lodge within 12 minutes.\030It's only natural to feel sorry for yourself when shown up by someone so new to this world. You shouldn't feel bad, $N.$B$BHm? Did I get your name wrong?\030A Hunter's Challenge\0312,1,13,2,257,2,1187\0302,15,87,2,257,2,1187\0302,89,129,2,257,1,1187\0302,134,174,2,257,1,1187\0302,176,260,2,257,1,1187\0302,262,305,2,257,1,1187\0302,310,336,2,257,4,1187\0302,338,389,2,257,4,1187\0302,394,463,2,257,2,1187\0302,469,491,2,321,1,1187\0303,1,104,2,384,1,1187\0301,1,30,4,272,4,1187\0301,32,76,4,272,2,1187\0301,78,214,4,272,3,1187\0301,223,252,4,272,2,1187\0301,259,274,4,272,1,1187\0301,276,309,4,272,1,1187\0301,311,336,4,272,4,1187\0301,341,349,4,272,2,1187\0304,1,91,3,256,1,1187\0304,93,119,3,256,1,1187\0304,128,153,3,256,2,1187\0312809,2,4,Boar\0302809,2,5,Boar\0301187,2,11,Daryl the Youngling\0312,38,1432,0,\0302,0,0,11,Daryl the Youngling\0302,0,0,11,Farstrider Lodge\031257,19,257,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030271,23,271,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,1192,OBJECTIVE,5,13,Elder Mountain Boar",[2581]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031How do you feel, $N? You radiate with the aura of the snickerfang--your strength, unmatched by mortals!$B$BUnfortunately, with the components you brought to me, I could only make enough of the assay for one tablet. I will require more components, should you require another tablet.\030It is a well known fact that hyenas possess tremendous strength in their jowls, but the strength to snap through three inches of thorium steel? Impossible, improbable, and yet I have seen this demonstrated with my own eyes.$B$BVenture forth, into the Blasted Lands, and bring me three snickerfang jowls. As you search for the snickerfang, be on the lookout for boars and scorpoks: The initial assay also requires two blasted boar lungs and one scorpok pincer to complete.\030Bring three Snickerfang Jowls, two Blasted Boar Lungs, and one Scorpok Pincer to Bloodmage Drazial.\030You smell foul, $N. Have you been traipsing in sulfur fields? And where are my components?!\030Snickerfang Jowls\0312,1,143,2,257,2,7505\0302,145,223,2,257,1,7505\0302,228,303,2,257,1,7505\0302,305,471,2,257,1,7505\0303,1,99,2,384,1,7505\0301,1,20,4,272,2,7505\0301,22,103,4,272,1,7505\0301,108,214,4,272,4,7505\0301,216,281,4,272,3,7505\0304,1,19,3,256,1,7505\0304,21,61,3,256,2,7505\0304,63,91,3,256,2,7505\0312809,2,4,Boar\0302809,2,5,Boar\0307505,2,5,Bloodmage Drazial\0312,4,1419,0,\0302,0,0,5,Bloodmage Drazial\0312582,23,2582,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,8391,OBJECTIVE,3,15,\030ITEM,8392,OBJECTIVE,2,15,\030ITEM,8393,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[2582]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031There you go! Remember, use it sparingly. If you require another, come see me after you finish the one you currently have in your possession.\030Ah, $N, welcome back. It seems you enjoyed the effect of the robust, operational imbue, derived from snickerfang. Be warned, while the immediate effect is a titanic burst of strength, the long term effects on your spirit and intelligence could be hazardous.$B$BWith that said, do you require more? If so, bring me another three snickerfang jowls, two blasted boar lungs, and one scorpok pincer.\030Bring three Snickerfang Jowls, two Blasted Boar Lungs, and one Scorpok Pincer to Bloodmage Drazial.\030Do you have the beast organs?\030Rage of Ages\0312,1,21,2,257,1,7505\0302,23,113,2,257,4,7505\0302,115,257,2,257,4,7505\0302,262,297,2,257,2,7505\0302,299,394,2,257,4,7505\0303,1,99,2,384,1,7505\0301,1,13,4,272,1,7505\0301,15,41,4,272,1,7505\0301,43,141,4,272,4,7505\0304,1,29,3,256,2,7505\0312809,2,5,Boar\0302809,2,6,Boar\0307505,2,6,Bloodmage Drazial\03010430,3,10,The Beast\0312,4,1419,0,\0302,0,0,6,Bloodmage Drazial\0312581,19,2581,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,8391,OBJECTIVE,3,15,\030ITEM,8392,OBJECTIVE,2,15,\030ITEM,8393,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[2583]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The spirit of the boar illuminates your being, $N! I wonder, do you believe yourself to be as invulnerable as these beasts?\030Within these blasted lands exists two species of boar: the ash-mane boar and the helboar.$B$BIt would appear that the stamina of these beasts renders them nearly immune to harm, as the other animals find them too difficult to kill and consequently, not worth the effort.$B$BWe need to perform further analysis, $N. Should you bring me three blasted boar lungs, two scorpok pincers, and one basilisk brain, I shall create a divine elixir from the residue of the assay. You will be my first test subject!\030Bring three Blasted Boar Lungs, two Scorpok Pincers, and one Basilisk Brain to Bloodmage Drazial.$B\030Where are the organs, $N!?\030A Boar's Vitality\0312,1,89,2,257,1,7505\0302,94,270,2,257,4,7505\0302,275,314,2,259,1,7505\0302,316,467,2,257,3,7505\0302,469,502,2,257,3,7505\0303,1,97,2,384,1,7505\0301,1,50,4,272,1,7505\0301,52,123,4,272,4,7505\0304,1,26,3,256,2,7505\0312809,2,1,Boar\0305993,2,1,Helboar\0302809,2,4,Boar\0302809,2,6,Boar\0307505,2,6,Bloodmage Drazial\0302809,4,7,Boar\0312,4,1419,0,\0302,0,0,6,Bloodmage Drazial\0312584,23,2584,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,8392,OBJECTIVE,3,15,\030ITEM,8393,OBJECTIVE,2,15,\030ITEM,8394,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[2584]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I must warn you, $N, do not attempt to mix the formulas I have created. The chemical properties of the formula you most recently ingested will always take precedence over former enchantments; thus, rendering the other formulation null.\030When I first administered the elixir, $N, I could tell that one or two applications would not satiate your appetite. Even now, I can see the hunger in your eyes. The concoction has addictive properties of which, seemingly, the most strong of will cannot resist.$B$BSo be it! Should you require more of the lung juice cocktail, venture back into the wasteland and find for me three blasted boar lungs, two scorpok pincers, and one basilisk brain.\030Bring three Blasted Boar Lungs, two Scorpok Pincers, and one Basilisk Brain to Bloodmage Drazial.$B\030Where are the organs, $N!?\030Spirit of the Boar\0312,1,116,2,257,4,7505\0302,118,161,2,257,1,7505\0302,163,261,2,257,3,7505\0302,276,445,2,257,1,7505\0303,1,97,2,384,1,7505\0301,1,71,4,272,1,7505\0301,73,235,4,272,3,7505\0304,1,26,3,256,2,7505\0312809,2,4,Boar\0302809,2,5,Boar\0307505,2,5,Bloodmage Drazial\0312,4,1419,0,\0302,0,0,5,Bloodmage Drazial\0312583,19,2583,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,8392,OBJECTIVE,3,15,\030ITEM,8393,OBJECTIVE,2,15,\030ITEM,8394,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[2585]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Fascinating. This has been the most difficult of all assays to analyze.$B$BTake a pinch of this residual salt and place it under your tongue. You should experience a slight feeling of euphoria followed by a state of unprecedented agility and quickness.\030Have you ever watched them in battle, $N? The scorpoks, I mean. Have you ever seen the grace and agility with which they move? The decisiveness of their strikes?$B$BIf only we could somehow isolate that agility and encapsulate it, we would be wealthy beyond our... I mean... it would be a boon for the scientific community.$B$BAssist me, $N, and I shall allow you a sampling of the assay.$B$BIn order to create a stable sample, I will need three scorpok pincers, two vulture gizzards, and one blasted boar lung.\030Bring three Scorpok Pincers, two Vulture Gizzards, and one Blasted Boar Lung to Bloodmage Drazial.$B\030Where are the organs, $N!?$B$B\030The Decisive Striker\0312,1,41,2,261,2,7505\0302,43,63,2,257,1,7505\0302,65,126,2,257,2,7505\0302,128,161,2,257,2,7505\0302,166,264,2,257,4,7505\0302,266,274,2,257,1,7505\0302,276,323,2,257,4,7505\0302,328,388,2,257,3,7505\0302,393,511,2,259,3,7505\0303,1,98,2,384,1,7505\0301,1,12,4,272,1,7505\0301,14,71,4,272,1,7505\0301,76,141,4,272,1,7505\0301,143,252,4,272,1,7505\0304,1,26,3,256,2,7505\0312809,2,9,Boar\0302809,2,10,Boar\0307505,2,10,Bloodmage Drazial\0312,4,1419,0,\0302,0,0,10,Bloodmage Drazial\0312586,23,2586,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,8393,OBJECTIVE,3,15,\030ITEM,8396,OBJECTIVE,2,15,\030ITEM,8392,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[2586]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Fine work, $N. Here is one sample of the assay for you and the remaining nine will be used in my research.$B$BAnytime you require more of the ground scorpok assay, return to me and we shall work out a deal.\030You live! This is good news, indeed. I assume you are back for more of the scorpok assay?$B$BVery well, $N, back to the wasteland with you and do not return until you have collected three scorpok pincers, two vulture gizzards, and one blasted boar lung.\030Bring three Scorpok Pincers, two Vulture Gizzards, and one Blasted Boar Lung to Bloodmage Drazial.\030Where are the organs, $N!?\030Salt of the Scorpok\0312,1,9,2,257,1,7505\0302,11,36,2,257,1,7505\0302,38,89,2,257,4,7505\0302,94,253,2,257,1,7505\0303,1,98,2,384,1,7505\0301,1,14,4,272,1,7505\0301,16,106,4,272,3,7505\0301,111,206,4,272,3,7505\0304,1,26,3,256,2,7505\0312809,2,4,Boar\0302809,2,5,Boar\0307505,2,5,Bloodmage Drazial\0312,4,1419,0,\0302,0,0,5,Bloodmage Drazial\0312585,19,2585,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,8393,OBJECTIVE,3,15,\030ITEM,8396,OBJECTIVE,2,15,\030ITEM,8392,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[26]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Salutations, young $C; the time has come for you to know our aquatic form. It is one that lets you move freely and indefinitely through water. You will find this aspect a useful tool and a blessing... but it is one that must be earned before it is mastered.$B$BYou will face two trials to overcome. The first will test your ability to work in water under pressure. The second will test your resolve to understand the aspects of the form itself.$B$BStand ready, as the time of testing is now upon us.\030$N, I have been following your progress with much delight.  You are most assuredly developing yourself into a valued protector of nature.$B$BThe time has come for you to learn more about one of the various animal aspects that Cenarius has blessed us with the ability to change into - one that affords you command and mastery of the water.  For this, you must travel to the village of Nighthaven in Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze of the Cenarion Circle there.  He will guide you further.\030Speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade.\030\030A Lesson to Learn\0312,1,58,2,257,1,4217\0302,61,137,2,257,1,4217\0302,142,338,2,257,1,4217\0302,341,471,2,321,1,4217\0302,474,499,2,257,3,4217\0303,1,70,2,384,1,4217\0301,1,74,4,272,1,11802\0301,76,142,4,272,1,11802\0301,144,200,4,272,3,11802\0301,202,257,4,280,1,11802\0301,262,298,4,272,3,11802\0301,300,364,4,272,3,11802\0301,366,444,4,272,3,11802\0301,449,499,4,272,1,11802\03111802,2,4,Dendrite Starblaze\03011802,2,6,Dendrite Starblaze\0312,0,0,4,Moonglade\03128,23,28,SOURCE_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2601]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is wondrous, $N! My offering to you is a taste of the inner workings of the redstone basilisk.$B$BShould the compound be to your liking, more can always be made... for a price.\030These wastelands are riddled with redstone basilisk, $N. These basilisk have adapted and flourished, more so than any of the other wildlife within the region.$B$BI have watched from afar as they hunt and go about their daily activities - the beasts exhibit a thought process more complex than even some humanoids.$B$BI must study their brains!$B$BRetrieve ten of their brains for me, $N. The compound cannot be complete, however, without two vulture gizzards to form the base of the solution.\030Bring ten Basilisk Brains and two Vulture Gizzards to Bloodmage Lynnore.$B\030Have you returned with the requested organs?\030The Basilisk's Bite\0312,1,56,2,257,1,7506\0302,58,158,2,257,1,7506\0302,163,313,2,257,1,7506\0302,318,343,2,257,1,7506\0302,348,387,2,257,1,7506\0302,389,492,2,257,1,7506\0303,1,72,2,384,1,7506\0301,1,21,4,272,1,7506\0301,23,99,4,272,1,7506\0301,104,168,4,272,1,7506\0301,170,181,4,272,1,7506\0304,1,44,3,256,2,7506\0315990,2,1,Redstone Basilisk\0307506,2,7,Bloodmage Lynnore\0305990,4,9,Redstone Basilisk\0312,4,1419,0,\0302,0,0,7,Bloodmage Lynnore\0312602,23,2602,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,8394,OBJECTIVE,10,15,\030ITEM,8396,OBJECTIVE,2,15,",[2602]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes, yes, give me a moment and more of the compound will be ready for your consumption, $N.$B$BTake it... and $N, do not attempt to consume these experimental concoctions in rapid succession. The results could be disastrous.\030Your focused concentration has dwindled so soon? More research must be done!$B$BOh yes, the price remains the same, $N. Venture forth into the blasted lands and return to me with ten brains from the redstone and two vulture gizzards.$B\030Bring ten Basilisk Brains and two Vulture Gizzards to Bloodmage Lynnore.\030Have you returned with the requested organs?\030Infallible Mind\0312,1,48,2,257,2,7506\0302,50,76,2,257,1,7506\0302,81,119,2,257,1,7506\0302,121,233,2,257,1,7506\0303,1,72,2,384,1,7506\0301,1,91,4,272,3,7506\0301,96,105,4,272,1,7506\0301,107,191,4,272,1,7506\0301,193,224,4,272,4,7506\0304,1,44,3,256,2,7506\0317506,2,5,Bloodmage Lynnore\0312,4,1419,0,\0302,0,0,5,Bloodmage Lynnore\0312601,19,2601,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,8394,OBJECTIVE,10,15,\030ITEM,8396,OBJECTIVE,2,15,",[2603]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Most excellent! I shall get to work immediately. Perhaps a cure for many of the ailments of the world is to be found!$B$BAh yes, your reward - of course, should you require more of the gum, return to me and another task you shall be given.\030Death does indeed have wings in these blasted lands, $r. I have witnessed the black slayers and bonepickers feasting upon the corpse of many a fallen explorer - sometimes feeding upon the most vile and disease ridden of carcasses. It is a wonder, then, how their internal systems overcome the pestilence that claims these lands.$B$BAssist me in my studies, $N! Gizzards I need! Two snickerfang jowls will also be required for the base of the concoction.$B$BYou shall be rewarded two-fold for your efforts.\030Bring ten Vulture Gizzards and two Snickerfang Jowls to Bloodmage Lynnore.$B\030Do not waste my time, $N. We have nothing to discuss, unless you have recovered the items I have requested.\030Vulture's Vigor\0312,1,56,2,257,1,7506\0302,58,230,2,257,1,7506\0302,232,328,2,257,1,7506\0302,333,360,2,257,1,7506\0302,362,377,2,259,1,7506\0302,379,453,2,257,3,7506\0302,458,505,2,257,3,7506\0303,1,74,2,384,1,7506\0301,1,15,4,272,1,7506\0301,17,48,4,272,3,7506\0301,50,117,4,272,4,7506\0301,122,239,4,272,3,7506\0304,1,25,3,256,1,7506\0304,27,107,3,264,4,7506\0317506,2,8,Bloodmage Lynnore\0312,4,1419,0,\0302,0,0,8,Bloodmage Lynnore\0312604,23,2604,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,8396,OBJECTIVE,10,15,\030ITEM,8391,OBJECTIVE,2,15,",[2604]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Perhaps one day I shall be able to isolate the active enzymes of this assay and produce a much more efficient resultant. Unfortunately, you will have to settle for what I am currently able to produce. Return to me should you require more gizzard gum.\030I see that the inner fire has dwindled. Would you say the spiritual euphoria lasted an hour?$B$BIf it's more of the gizzard gum you desire, then more of the gizzards I require. Back to the wastelands, $N. Do not return until you have recovered ten gizzards and two jowls.\030Bring ten Vulture Gizzards and two Snickerfang Jowls to Bloodmage Lynnore.$B\030Do not waste my time, $N. We have nothing to discuss, unless you have recovered the items I have requested.\030Spiritual Domination\0312,1,39,2,257,1,7506\0302,41,92,2,257,4,7506\0302,97,176,2,259,4,7506\0302,178,204,2,257,1,7506\0302,206,271,2,257,1,7506\0303,1,74,2,384,1,7506\0301,1,120,4,272,4,7506\0301,122,200,4,272,3,7506\0301,202,250,4,272,1,7506\0304,1,25,3,256,1,7506\0304,27,107,3,264,4,7506\0317506,2,6,Bloodmage Lynnore\0312,4,1419,0,\0302,0,0,6,Bloodmage Lynnore\0312603,19,2603,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,8396,OBJECTIVE,10,15,\030ITEM,8391,OBJECTIVE,2,15,",[2605]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh, wonderful! Give it here -- let me drink it!\030I've got an idea, see. I've heard of some strange creatures called dew collectors that live to the southwest... and that they are able to store water in special glands.$B$BI think that if I could get one of these glands, I could create a drink that would quench my terrible thirst! Do you think you could help me, $N?$B$BLook for the cactus garden, $N; that's where you'll find the dew collectors.\030Collect a Laden Dew Gland and bring it to Marin Noggenfogger in Gadgetzan.\030Please, tell me you found the dew collectors?\030The Thirsty Goblin\0312,1,22,2,257,1,7564\0302,24,111,2,257,1,7564\0302,113,168,2,257,1,7564\0302,173,281,2,257,4,7564\0302,283,317,2,257,4,7564\0302,322,397,2,257,1,7564\0303,1,74,2,384,1,7564\0301,1,14,4,272,1,7564\0301,16,47,4,272,1,7564\0304,1,45,3,256,2,7564\0317564,2,7,Marin Noggenfogger\0312,440,1446,0,\0302,0,0,7,Marin Noggenfogger\0302,0,0,7,Gadgetzan\0312606,23,2606,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,8428,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[2606]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Marin's a good guy, don't get me wrong -- just a little... eccentric, I'd say.$B$BAnd of course he needs my help, yet again.\030Blech! This stuff tastes terrible! So much for that idea...$B$BWait, what's that? Oh, I know, I know, you think I shouldn't give up on this stuff. Well, okay then.$B$BUhhhh, I have an idea! Brilliant! Take this dew to my friend Sprinkle -- she's an excellent chef. Tell her what we're up to here and that we want to make it go down a little easier.$B$BI mean, if it's going to taste that bad, it at least should have some kick to it... And I'm just not feeling it...\030Marin Noggenfogger wants you to speak with Sprinkle in Gadgetzan.\030So old Marin's up to it again, eh? What's this concoction made from?\030In Good Taste\0312,1,6,2,257,1,7564\0302,8,34,2,257,1,7564\0302,36,59,2,257,1,7564\0302,64,81,2,257,2,7564\0302,83,146,2,257,1,7564\0302,148,163,2,257,1,7564\0302,168,189,2,257,1,7564\0302,191,200,2,257,1,7564\0302,202,264,2,257,1,7564\0302,266,348,2,259,1,7564\0302,353,435,2,257,4,7564\0302,437,466,2,257,1,7564\0303,1,65,2,386,1,7564\0301,1,58,4,272,1,7583\0301,60,78,4,272,1,7583\0301,83,124,4,274,1,7583\0304,1,34,3,256,2,7583\0304,36,68,3,256,2,7583\0317583,2,9,Sprinkle\0307564,2,13,Marin Noggenfogger\0307583,2,13,Sprinkle\0312,440,1446,0,\0302,0,0,13,Gadgetzan\0312605,19,2605,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302641,23,2641,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2607]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It's about time! Just put the cheese on the table and skedaddle. Osborne will pay you on the way out.\030It appears as if you've brought back more information than even I expected. This certainly is a strange turn of events, $N.$B$BA cure? Hrm... Go down to the cellar and speak with Doc Mixilpixil - he may be able to help.\030Speak with Doc Mixilpixil in the cellar of the Barracks.\030\030The Touch of Zanzil\0312,1,75,2,257,4,332\0302,77,123,2,257,1,332\0302,128,134,2,257,2,332\0302,136,141,2,257,1,332\0302,143,219,2,257,1,332\0303,1,56,2,384,1,332\0301,1,16,4,272,1,7207\0301,18,64,4,272,1,7207\0301,66,101,4,272,3,7207\0317207,2,5,Doc Mixilpixil\0307207,2,6,Doc Mixilpixil\031\0312359,19,2359,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302608,23,2608,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2608]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Give me a moment to confer with my colleagues, $N. Dr. Montgomery, Mr. Noarm, let us conference!\030Oh my, you look like death. Correction - I've seen death, you look worse than death. You, $g sir:miss;, would be what death coughed up at his last physical.$B$BHah! You hear that Noarm? Write that one down!$B$B*Cough* Hrm yes, in order for me to help you, I'll need to draw some blood. Don't worry, it only hurts the first few... fifty times or so... /lay down when you're ready for the treatment, $N.\030/Lay down to be examined by Doc Mixilpixil. How can he find the cure if he can't find the cause?$B\030Diagnosis Complete\030When you're ready for the examination, /lay down on the ground and I'll begin the phlebotomy.\030The Touch of Zanzil\0312,1,27,2,257,1,7207\0302,29,84,2,257,1,7207\0302,86,156,2,257,4,7207\0302,161,164,2,257,1,7207\0302,166,185,2,257,2,7207\0302,187,206,2,257,1,7207\0302,211,285,2,259,1,7207\0302,287,329,2,257,1,7207\0302,331,350,2,257,1,7207\0302,352,401,2,257,1,7207\0303,1,43,2,384,1,7207\0303,45,96,2,384,4,7207\0301,1,50,4,272,1,7207\0301,56,70,4,272,1,7207\0301,72,96,4,272,1,7207\0305,1,93,3,256,1,7207\0304,1,18,3,384,1,7207\0317208,2,5,Noarm\0307207,2,11,Doc Mixilpixil\0307208,4,15,Noarm\031\0312607,19,2607,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302609,23,2609,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2609]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031What am I doing? What does it look like I'm doing? I'm devising a cure for your 'itis!' Don't get indignant with me now, $n!$B$BJust a few more seconds. There! Just spray this, um, fantastic smelling medicine on yourself and you'll be as good as new.\030It's unanimous, $N. You've got the 'itis.'$B$BLuckily, I have a cure for the 'itis.'$B$BHere's what I need: One bundle of simple wildflowers, one leaded vial, one bronze tube, and last but certainly not least, one spool of light chartreuse silk thread. Ol' Emma left a spool of it for me at 'The Finest Thread.' You can find the shop along the canals.$B$BHurry along now, $N, and try not to touch anyone until you're cured. Oh, and Dr. Montgomery says you need a shower -- his words, not mine.\030Bring Doc Mixilpixil one bundle of Simple Wildflowers, one Leaded Vial, one Bronze Tube, and one Spool of Light Chartreuse Silk Thread. The 'itis' doesn't cure itself, young $g fella:lady;.\030If you want the 'itis' cured, you're going to have to try harder than that, $n. Where are the reagents for the cure?\030The Touch of Zanzil\0312,1,19,2,257,1,7207\0302,21,42,2,257,1,7207\0302,47,84,2,257,1,7207\0302,89,252,2,259,1,7207\0302,254,351,2,257,1,7207\0302,356,423,2,257,1,7207\0302,425,435,2,257,1,7207\0302,437,493,2,259,1,7207\0303,1,135,2,384,1,7207\0303,137,189,2,384,1,7207\0301,1,16,4,272,2,7207\0301,18,50,4,272,2,7207\0301,52,124,4,272,1,7207\0301,129,152,4,272,1,7207\0301,154,159,4,272,1,7207\0301,161,250,4,272,1,7207\0304,1,79,3,258,4,7207\0304,81,116,3,256,2,7207\0313520,2,5,Ol' Emma\0307207,2,9,Doc Mixilpixil\03015065,2,10,Lady\031\0312608,19,2608,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3421,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,3372,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,4371,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,8431,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[261]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have proven your resolve, and the Scarlet Crusade commends you.$B$BIf you do not shy from righteous slaughter, then perhaps your path lies with us...\030I will be frank.  We are at war with the Scourge.  It is an evil that corrupts our people and infects our land.  It must be stopped before it overwhelms us and drags our world into shadow.  We of the Scarlet Crusade have sworn to fight the Scourge with body and soul.$B$BIf you are with us, then gather your courage and prove your allegiance--destroy the undead ravagers of Desolace, in the Valley of Bones to the south.$B$BDo this, and the Crusade will embrace you.\030Destroy 30 Undead Ravagers, then return to Brother Anton at Nijel's Point.\030The Scourge grows in power with the passing of each day. If you truly wish to halt its advances, then show me.\030Down the Scarlet Path\0312,1,16,2,257,3,1182\0302,19,49,2,325,1,1182\0302,52,111,2,257,1,1182\0302,114,188,2,257,1,1182\0302,191,267,2,325,1,1182\0302,272,420,2,261,4,1182\0302,425,466,2,257,3,1182\0303,1,74,2,388,1,1182\0301,1,67,4,272,1,1182\0301,72,153,4,272,4,1182\0304,1,56,3,320,1,1182\0304,58,110,3,258,4,1182\0314244,2,4,Shadow\0301182,2,8,Brother Anton\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,6,Valley of Bones\0302,0,0,8,Brother Anton\0302,0,0,8,Nijel's Point\0311052,23,1052,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,11561,OBJECTIVE,30,13,Undead Ravager",[262]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hmm... Someone handled this book recently, someone who is driven by revenge. But the impressions left on it, at least the impressions from the original owner, are faint.$B$BI can tell, however, that the original owner of this book is not a native of Darkshire.\030I must know who was that skulker in the shadows I saw the night my family was killed!$B$BPlease, $N, you have shown your resourcefulness.  Please find that shadowy figure.  I must learn what secrets he holds!$B$BI do not have clues that you do not already know, but here - take the book you found at my farm.  Perhaps some of the townsfolk can link this book with its owner.\030Take the book you found at Sven's farm and show it to townsfolk in Darkshire.\030If you have something that belongs to the shadowy figure for whom you seek, then let me see it. I may be able to divine something of its owner.\030The Shadowy Figure\0312,1,85,2,257,1,311\0302,90,137,2,257,1,311\0302,140,171,2,257,1,311\0302,174,208,2,257,1,311\0302,213,308,2,257,1,311\0302,311,374,2,257,4,311\0303,1,77,2,384,1,311\0301,1,6,4,272,1,265\0301,8,76,4,274,1,265\0301,78,169,4,272,1,265\0301,174,260,4,272,1,265\0304,1,95,3,258,4,265\0304,97,143,3,256,1,265\031\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,7,Sven's\0302,0,0,7,Darkshire\031230,19,230,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030265,23,265,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2621]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thrall's Grasp... The story is still fresh in my mind.$B$B<Commander Ruag shakes his head>$B$BTerrible thing that happened to that regiment. The horde lost some of its best soldiers when that battalion was destroyed.\030Regret. It is all I have now. One bad decision resulting in several horrible outcomes. If only I had waited for those orders. Maybe they would have detailed the horrors that awaited us in those cursed lands! Maybe they were to redirect us to another detail? Ultimately, it was my fault. All of it was my fault.$B$BSo here I stand, awaiting orders. I must know. I must have those orders.$B$BDispatch Commander Ruag resides in Stonard. Find him and find out what became of the orders.$B\030Speak to Dispatch Commander Ruag in Stonard.\030\030The Disgraced One\0312,1,7,2,257,1,7572\0302,9,29,2,257,1,7572\0302,31,86,2,257,1,7572\0302,88,125,2,257,4,7572\0302,127,207,2,261,4,7572\0302,209,257,2,257,4,7572\0302,259,286,2,257,1,7572\0302,288,310,2,257,1,7572\0302,315,347,2,257,1,7572\0302,349,360,2,257,1,7572\0302,362,386,2,257,1,7572\0302,391,433,2,257,1,7572\0302,435,482,2,257,1,7572\0303,1,44,2,384,1,7572\0301,1,17,4,272,1,7623\0301,19,54,4,272,1,7623\0301,59,90,4,272,1,7623\0301,95,140,4,272,1,7623\0301,142,216,4,276,1,7623\0317623,2,12,Dispatch Commander Ruag\0307623,2,14,Dispatch Commander Ruag\0312,4,1419,0,\0302,0,0,12,Stonard\0302,0,0,14,Dispatch Commander Ruag\0302,0,0,14,Stonard\0312784,19,2784,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302622,23,2622,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2622]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Swamp tal... talk.. talker...$B$B\030The orders? What could you possibly want with the orders?$B$BWhat are you implying, $N? Of course I relayed those orders! The soldiers I sent the orders with were ambushed and brutally beaten by murlocs. Only one survived, if you can call that surviving. He can hardly speak, cannot walk, and must be fed through a tube. If you want to know what happened to those orders, speak with Bengor. I'm sure he is around here somewhere... and, $N, be mindful of what you stick your nose into - it may get bitten off.\030Speak to Bengor.\030\030The Missing Orders\0312,1,11,2,257,2,7623\0302,13,57,2,259,4,7623\0302,62,87,2,257,2,7623\0302,89,121,2,257,1,7623\0302,123,203,2,257,1,7623\0302,205,254,2,265,4,7623\0302,256,320,2,257,1,7623\0302,322,390,2,259,4,7623\0302,392,430,2,257,1,7623\0302,432,508,2,257,1,7623\0303,1,16,2,384,1,7623\0301,1,12,4,272,1,7643\0301,14,19,4,272,1,7643\0301,21,29,4,272,1,7643\0317643,2,8,Bengor\0307643,2,11,Bengor\0312,8,1435,0,\0302,0,0,11,Bengor\0312621,19,2621,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302623,23,2623,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2623]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It is worse than I imagined. Nineteen of my men could have been spared from the agony which they faced. If only I had not acted so irrationally.$B$BYou must help them, $N! I am powerless to act.\030Orders were given by the dispatch commander. We took... took orders. On way to Blasted Lands, ambushed.$B$BMurlocs... Many murlocs... One named Swamp Talker. Took orders from my hands as spear thrust into my skull. East... cave....$B$B<Bengor passes out.>$B\030Retrieve the Warchief's Orders and return them to the Fallen Hero of the Horde.\030Awaiting orders.\030The Swamp Talker\0312,1,44,2,257,1,7643\0302,46,55,2,257,1,7643\0302,57,68,2,257,1,7643\0302,70,103,2,257,1,7643\0302,108,117,2,257,1,7643\0302,119,133,2,257,1,7643\0302,135,157,2,257,1,7643\0302,159,214,2,257,1,7643\0302,216,222,2,257,1,7643\0302,224,231,2,257,1,7643\0302,236,255,2,257,1,7643\0303,1,79,2,384,1,7643\0301,1,28,4,272,1,7572\0301,30,103,4,272,4,7572\0301,105,144,4,272,4,7572\0301,149,171,4,272,1,7572\0301,173,194,4,272,1,7572\0304,1,16,3,256,1,7572\031950,2,7,Swamp Talker\0307643,2,11,Bengor\0307572,2,12,Fallen Hero of the Horde\03015394,2,12,Hero of the Horde\0312,8,1435,0,\0302,0,0,4,Blasted Lands\0302,0,0,12,Fallen Hero of the Horde\0312622,19,2622,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,8463,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[263]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I knew the second I laid eyes on you, $N, that you would make Ironforge proud. You have served King Magni well. Now that you've proven yourself to be such a loyal aid to the Kingdom, perhaps you should talk with the Captain to see if he'll entrust you with a higher detail.$B$BI salute you, $N.\030The Mountaineers tell me you are quite brave and capable, $N.  We need a $r like you around here.  The Trogg problem isn't getting any better.  The reserves have been called to the front and we're all alone out here.  But now that we have a seasoned $c here, let's see what you can do.$B$BGo out and kill 10 Stonesplinter Shaman and 10 Stonesplinter Bonesnappers.  Let's see if you live up to your reputation, Trogg-Slayer.\030Mountaineer Wallbang in the southern guard tower wants you to kill 10 Stonesplinter Shaman and 10 Stonesplinter Bonesnappers.\030Back so soon? In case I didn't make myself clear we need you to kill 10 Stonesplinter Shaman and 10 Stonesplinter Bonesnappers, $N. Now go get 'em, Trogg-Slayer!\030In Defense of the King's Lands\0312,1,61,2,257,1,1090\0302,64,97,2,259,1,1090\0302,100,142,2,261,1,1090\0302,145,216,2,257,1,1090\0302,219,285,2,257,1,1090\0302,290,363,2,257,1,1090\0302,366,423,2,257,4,1090\0303,1,125,2,386,1,1090\0301,1,78,4,272,4,1090\0301,80,111,4,272,1,1090\0301,113,273,4,272,4,1090\0301,278,294,4,272,1,1090\0304,1,13,3,256,2,1090\0304,15,131,3,258,1,1090\0304,133,161,3,256,1,1090\0311197,2,6,Stonesplinter Shaman\0301090,2,8,Mountaineer Wallbang\0301197,2,8,Stonesplinter Shaman\0301197,3,14,Stonesplinter Shaman\0312,38,1432,0,\0304,0,0,11,Kingdom\031237,19,237,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030217,23,217,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,1197,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Stonesplinter Shaman\030NPC,1164,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Stonesplinter Bonesnapper",[264]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You place the worthless pendant on the grave, and the gemstone within the setting seems to dull noticeably.$B$BAs you stand to leave, you look down at the pendant; it lies lifelessly over the hands of the relief sculpted into the top of the coffin. Your thoughts are interrupted by a stiff, cool breeze passing over the Sepulcher. For a moment everything around you is silent.\030Filthy scum! Leaves me for his damn crusade. Because \"the Light is the most important thing we have against the threats the undead pose.\"$B$BWell, what about his children?! What about ME?! Night after night I sat patiently waiting for him... always second to his blasted duty!$B$BWell, witness what \"justice\" brings you, $N! He's dead and I'm bearing the very thing he was trying to stop!$B$BTake this piece of junk and put it on his tomb at the Sepulcher. I want nothing to do with it anymore... or him!\030Place Clarice's Pendant on Yuriv's Tomb in Silverpine.\030The stone is cold to the touch, but has obviously been abused. Trash litters the area; nicks and gashes decorate the relief atop the coffin; and the foliage around the grave has started to grow over the site.$B$BNo one cares for whoever is buried here, especially not any victims of the plague.\030Until Death Do Us Part\0312,1,12,2,257,1,5543\0302,14,44,2,257,1,5543\0302,46,137,2,259,1,5543\0302,142,172,2,257,2,5543\0302,174,188,2,257,2,5543\0302,190,241,2,257,1,5543\0302,243,276,2,257,1,5543\0302,281,324,2,257,1,5543\0302,326,388,2,257,1,5543\0302,393,456,2,257,1,5543\0302,458,496,2,259,1,5543\0302,498,504,2,257,1,5543\0303,1,54,2,384,1,5543\0301,1,107,4,272,4,0\0301,112,248,4,272,1,0\0301,250,330,4,272,1,0\0301,332,376,4,272,1,0\0304,1,62,3,256,1,0\0304,64,208,3,256,1,0\0304,213,294,3,260,1,0\031\0312,1638,1456,0,\0302,0,0,10,Sepulcher\0302,0,0,13,Silverpine\031\031OBJECT,24776,FINISHER,?,12,Yuriv's Tombstone",[2641]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031That's the stuff, $N!$B$BIt looks so good, I might just...  Haha, gotcha!\030When I was a kid, my sister used to do all the cooking. It was horrible! I could barely stomach some of her concoctions -- until I found what I like to call my \"secret\" ingredient! Add it to anything, and... WOW! It tastes great!$B$BWhat is it, you ask? It's a mushroom called the Violet Tragan. If you want me to help you turn this horrid-tasting brew into something edible, head to the Hinterlands, and look for a small lake there.$B$BOh, and remember, the Violet Tragan can only be found underwater.\030Sprinkle in Gadgetzan wants you to collect a Violet Tragan and return it to her.\030Under the waters of that lake -- it's the only place where the Violet Tragan can be found.  Hope you're good at holding your breath!\030Sprinkle's Secret Ingredient\0312,1,55,2,257,1,7583\0302,57,72,2,257,1,7583\0302,74,180,2,257,4,7583\0302,182,207,2,257,1,7583\0302,209,212,2,257,1,7583\0302,214,229,2,257,1,7583\0302,234,253,2,257,2,7583\0302,255,295,2,257,1,7583\0302,297,433,2,259,4,7583\0302,438,502,2,257,1,7583\0303,1,80,2,386,1,7583\0301,1,21,4,272,1,7583\0301,26,58,4,272,4,7583\0301,61,73,4,272,1,7583\0304,1,90,3,256,1,7583\0304,93,132,3,256,3,7583\0317583,2,11,Sprinkle\0312,440,1446,0,\0302,0,0,9,Hinterlands\0302,0,0,11,Gadgetzan\0312606,19,2606,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302661,23,2661,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,8526,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[265]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, yes. I sold this book a month ago to a shady person. He didn't tell me his name, but he was a nervous, jittery chap, always looking over his shoulder.$B$BI hope that helps you...\030Here is your book back, $N, and I bid you fortune with your search.  If you ask others in town, perhaps they can offer you more clues.$B$BAnd here is one more for you - although the author of this book is a stranger to Darkshire, the book itself was purchased here.\030See if other townsfolk have clues about the shadowy figure.\030Sometimes I'll sell blank books to scholars and mages, or to anyone who wants to keep a journal.$B$BI remember well everyone to whom I sold a book within the last few months...\030The Shadowy Search Continues\0312,1,67,2,257,1,265\0302,70,134,2,257,4,265\0302,139,265,2,257,1,265\0303,1,59,2,384,4,265\0301,1,8,4,272,1,267\0301,10,56,4,272,1,267\0301,58,154,4,272,1,267\0301,159,182,4,274,3,267\0304,1,96,3,258,1,267\0304,101,176,3,256,1,267\031\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,3,Darkshire\031262,19,262,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030266,23,266,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[266]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh yeah, I remember this book. Its owner rented a room for a few days, and spent his nights at the bar, writing.$B$BHe left town in a hurry, muttering about being hunted by...something. Last I saw him he was heading west out of town, looking for a new spot to hide.$B$BThe first place he'd find to the west is Raven Hill...\030Here is your book, and good luck with your inquiries.$B$BYou might want to expand your search to the inn.  If the person whom you seek spent time in town, then chances are someone saw him there.\030Search the inn for clues about the shadowy figure.\030The Scarlet Raven doesn't see the business it used to, but we still do get travelers passing through.$B$BIf you can describe the person you're looking for, maybe I'll remember him.\030Inquire at the Inn\0312,1,53,2,257,1,267\0302,58,105,2,259,4,267\0302,108,194,2,259,4,267\0303,1,50,2,384,1,267\0301,1,30,4,272,1,273\0301,32,112,4,272,1,273\0301,117,185,4,272,1,273\0301,187,265,4,272,1,273\0301,270,323,4,272,1,273\0304,1,101,3,256,1,273\0304,106,180,3,256,4,273\0314950,4,8,Spot\0307605,4,9,Raven\0307605,3,10,Raven\0312,10,1431,0,\031265,19,265,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030453,23,453,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2661]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Violet Powder, eh? Let's give it a try -- it sure couldn't make it any worse, that's for sure!\030Here's the Violet Powder, $N. Take it to Marin and tell him he owes me a favor!\030Sprinkle wants to you take the Violet Powder to Marin Noggenfogger in Gadgetzan.\030Oh, $N, you're finally back.  What have you brought?\030Delivery for Marin\0312,1,29,2,257,1,7583\0302,31,79,2,257,1,7583\0303,1,80,2,386,1,7583\0301,1,18,4,272,2,7564\0301,20,94,4,272,1,7564\0304,1,28,3,256,1,7564\0304,31,52,3,256,2,7564\0317583,2,3,Sprinkle\0307564,2,3,Marin Noggenfogger\0312,440,1446,0,\0302,0,0,2,Marin\0302,0,0,3,Marin Noggenfogger\0302,0,0,3,Gadgetzan\0312641,19,2641,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302662,23,2662,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2662]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Drink this! It's absolutely wonderful!!!$B$BI knew I had it in me... Oh thanks again, $N for your help, but please, stand a little to the side, will you? You're blocking my business! I'm going to make millions on the fabulous Noggenfogger Elixir, millions!$B$BWhat's that? Sprinkle says I owe her a favor? Oh, that Sprinkle, such a kidder!\030Now, to mix this powder in with the dew.$B$BCome back and talk to me in a minute... after I have perfected the fabulous Noggenfogger Elixir!\030Marin Noggenfogger wants you to speak to him again after he creates his elixir.\030\030Noggenfogger Elixir\0312,1,40,2,257,1,7564\0302,45,83,2,257,1,7564\0302,85,140,2,257,1,7564\0303,1,79,2,386,1,7564\0301,1,11,4,272,1,7564\0301,13,40,4,272,1,7564\0301,45,68,4,272,1,7564\0301,70,153,4,272,2,7564\0301,155,182,4,272,1,7564\0301,184,256,4,272,3,7564\0301,261,272,4,272,2,7564\0301,274,305,4,272,2,7564\0301,307,339,4,272,1,7564\0317564,2,4,Marin Noggenfogger\0307583,4,12,Sprinkle\0307583,4,13,Sprinkle\0312,440,1446,0,\0312661,19,2661,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[267]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I am quite impressed, $N. You have done the Dwarven race a great favor by defending our lands. King Magni Bronzebeard himself would be proud!\030$C, you may or may not be aware of the Trogg threat looming over Dwarven lands.  With the Ironforge Reserve called up to the Alliance Front, we are left with a fraction of the defense forces needed to keep these lands safe.  My regiment is assigned to watch over the Gate here and we cannot leave our post for fear of invasion.$B$BBut we need some pressure put on those damned Troggs lurking in the hills.  If you're up to the task, wage an assault on the Troggs.  Bring me back 8 Trogg Stone Teeth as proof.\030Bring 8 Trogg Stone Teeth to Captain Rugelfuss in the southern guard tower.\030Do you have 8 Trogg Stone Teeth to show me? If not, there is still work to be done, $N.\030The Trogg Threat\0312,1,79,2,261,1,1092\0302,82,223,2,257,1,1092\0302,226,327,2,261,1,1092\0302,332,405,2,259,1,1092\0302,408,463,2,257,4,1092\0302,466,508,2,257,1,1092\0303,1,75,2,384,1,1092\0301,1,25,4,272,1,1092\0301,27,94,4,272,1,1092\0301,96,141,4,272,4,1092\0304,1,43,3,256,2,1092\0304,45,87,3,256,4,1092\0311092,2,7,Captain Rugelfuss\0302784,4,10,King Magni Bronzebeard\0312,38,1432,0,\0302,0,0,2,Alliance Front\0302,0,0,7,Captain Rugelfuss\031\031ITEM,2536,OBJECTIVE,8,15,",[268]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This journal explains much to me, and sets me on the path against the dark riders! I have seen these riders in Duskwood, and have seen them speak with the wizard Morbent Fel, at the Forlorn Rowe.\030The book you found was only half finished.  I had to leave it at Sven's farm when I fled there...$B$BHere.  Take my completed journal to Sven.  It describes more fully what happened at his farm.$B$BAlthough this journal has been my only company these past weeks, if giving it up keeps me from having to face Sven and his wrath, then I do it willingly!\030Return to Sven with Jitters' completed journal.\030Did you find who the Shadowy Figure was?\030Return to Sven\0312,1,42,2,257,1,288\0302,45,97,2,257,1,288\0302,102,106,2,257,1,288\0302,109,142,2,257,1,288\0302,145,194,2,257,1,288\0302,199,351,2,257,4,288\0303,1,47,2,384,1,288\0301,1,82,4,272,1,311\0301,84,195,4,272,1,311\0304,1,40,3,256,2,311\0311200,4,9,Morbent Fel\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,2,Sven's\0302,0,0,4,Sven\0302,0,0,7,Sven\0304,0,0,9,Duskwood\0304,0,0,9,Forlorn Rowe\031453,19,453,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030323,23,323,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2681]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030objectiveLabel3\030objectiveLabel4\030objectiveLabel5\030requestItems\030title\031You have done it, $N! The poor, tortured souls can finally rest.$B$BOur work is not yet over, $N. We have much to discuss and much more to accomplish.\030It will take more than you alone to overcome the forces of Razelikh and his subordinates.$B$BGather a suitable group of adventurers and free my men of their eternal torture! Eighteen stones you must shatter.$B$BFight hard and die with honor, $N.\030Free nine Servants of Razelikh, three Servants of Sevine, three Servants of Allistarj, and three Servants of Grol. Return to the Fallen Hero when your task is complete. You must remain within close proximity of the stones or the process will fail.\030\030Servants of Razelikh Freed\030Servants of Grol Freed\030Servants of Allistarj Freed\030Servants of Sevine Freed\030It is no easy task, $N. Do not give up!\030The Stones That Bind Us\0312,1,89,2,257,3,7572\0302,94,173,2,257,1,7572\0302,175,207,2,257,1,7572\0302,212,245,2,261,1,7572\0303,1,114,2,384,1,7572\0303,116,168,2,384,1,7572\0303,170,247,2,384,3,7572\0301,1,21,4,272,1,7572\0301,23,64,4,272,1,7572\0301,69,97,4,272,1,7572\0301,99,150,4,272,1,7572\0309,1,23,3,256,1,7572\0309,25,39,3,256,1,7572\0305,1,26,3,384,1,7572\0306,1,22,3,384,1,7572\0307,1,27,3,384,1,7572\0308,1,24,3,384,1,7572\03110996,2,6,Fallen Hero\0312,4,1419,0,\0302,0,0,6,Fallen Hero\0312801,19,2801,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302702,23,2702,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,7668,OBJECTIVE,9,13,Servant of Razelikh\030NPC,7669,OBJECTIVE,3,13,Servant of Grol\030NPC,7670,OBJECTIVE,3,13,Servant of Allistarj\030NPC,7671,OBJECTIVE,3,13,Servant of Sevine",[269]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<After reading the journal and hearing your intent...>$B$BAn evil taint has gained a foothold within the already beleaguered Duskwood. I thank the Light we have a hero such as you to face it.$B$BBut you must first prepare yourself for the coming trial...for the Necromancer Morbent Fel is immensely powerful, and has cast dark enchantments about himself to protect him from physical assaults. If you are to defeat him, you will need a weapon that is proof against these protections.\030Go to the city of Stormwind and speak with Bishop Farthing in the Cathedral of Light.  Give him Jitters' journal and tell him you mean to face Morbent Fel.$B$BAlthough Stormwind has forsaken Darkshire, Farthing is a kind soul and very wise.  He may help you on your quest to save us.$B$BYour mission is perilous, but hurry, $N.  With each passing hour, the shadows of Duskwood grow ever darker.\030Give Jitters' Completed Journal to Bishop Farthing in Stormwind.\030Rest, $gbrother:sister;. I can tell you have traveled far, and you bear a heavy burden. Can you tell me what casts that dark shadow over you?\030Seeking Wisdom\0312,1,85,2,257,1,311\0302,88,155,2,257,1,311\0302,160,240,2,257,1,311\0302,243,283,2,267,1,311\0302,288,327,2,257,1,311\0302,330,394,2,257,1,311\0303,1,64,2,384,1,311\0301,1,54,4,272,1,1212\0301,59,134,4,272,1,1212\0301,136,191,4,272,1,1212\0301,196,392,4,286,1,1212\0301,394,482,4,274,4,1212\0304,1,24,3,256,1,1212\0304,26,87,3,256,1,1212\0304,89,141,3,256,2,1212\0311212,2,1,Bishop Farthing\0301200,2,2,Morbent Fel\0301212,2,7,Bishop Farthing\0308553,4,11,Necromancer\0301200,4,11,Morbent Fel\0304244,3,15,Shadow\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,1,Cathedral of Light\0302,0,0,7,Bishop Farthing\0302,0,0,7,Stormwind\031323,19,323,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030270,23,270,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[27]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Salutations, young $C; the time has come for you to know our aquatic form. It is one that lets you move freely and indefinitely through water. You will find this aspect a useful tool and a blessing... but it is one that must be earned before it is mastered.$B$BYou will face two trials to overcome. The first will test your ability to work in water under pressure. The second will test your resolve to understand the aspects of the form itself.$B$BStand ready, as the time of testing is now upon us.\030$N, I have been following your progress with much delight.  You are most assuredly developing yourself into a valued protector of nature.$B$BThe time has come for you to learn more about one of the various animal aspects that Cenarius has blessed us with the ability to change into - one that affords you command and mastery of the water.  For this, you must travel to the village of Nighthaven in Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze of the Cenarion Circle there.  He will guide you further.\030Speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade.\030\030A Lesson to Learn\0312,1,58,2,257,1,3033\0302,61,137,2,257,1,3033\0302,142,338,2,257,1,3033\0302,341,471,2,321,1,3033\0302,474,499,2,257,3,3033\0303,1,70,2,384,1,3033\0301,1,74,4,272,1,11802\0301,76,142,4,272,1,11802\0301,144,200,4,272,3,11802\0301,202,257,4,280,1,11802\0301,262,298,4,272,3,11802\0301,300,364,4,272,3,11802\0301,366,444,4,272,3,11802\0301,449,499,4,272,1,11802\03111802,2,4,Dendrite Starblaze\03011802,2,6,Dendrite Starblaze\0312,0,0,4,Moonglade\03129,23,29,SOURCE_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[270]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Lightforge Iron is a precious metal, but it sounds like your quest is a dire one. You've come a long way, $gBrother:Sister;. With luck, you might just find what you seek!$B$BAnd if you do get the iron, I know who can fashion it into a weapon against this Necromancer you speak of in Duskwood.\030Years ago, the Third Fleet of Kul'Tiras sunk along the coasts of The Wetlands, an expanse of marsh north of the Dwarven kingdom of Ironforge.  Aboard one ship was a load of Lightforge Iron.$B$BThis metal is precious to us, for items crafted from it strike with holy truth.  If you are to face Morbent Fel, then you will need such a weapon.$B$BGo to Menethil Harbor and speak with my dwarven colleague Glorin Steelbrow.  If that lost metal can be found, he'll know where to look.\030Go to Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands, and speak with Glorin Steelbrow.\030\030The Doomed Fleet\0312,1,141,2,321,1,1212\0302,144,189,2,257,1,1212\0302,194,272,2,257,1,1212\0302,275,339,2,259,4,1212\0302,344,418,2,257,1,1212\0302,421,478,2,261,4,1212\0303,1,71,2,384,1,1212\0301,1,81,4,272,1,1217\0301,83,124,4,272,1,1217\0301,126,170,4,274,4,1217\0301,175,292,4,272,4,1217\03114528,2,3,Precious\0301200,2,4,Morbent Fel\0301217,2,5,Glorin Steelbrow\0301217,2,7,Glorin Steelbrow\03014528,4,8,Precious\0308553,4,11,Necromancer\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,1,Dwarven\0302,0,0,5,Menethil Harbor\0302,0,0,7,Menethil Harbor\0302,0,0,7,Wetlands\0304,0,0,11,Duskwood\031269,19,269,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030321,23,321,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[2701]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You are temporarily blinded by the sparkle and gleam.\030Please, take from this a relic of old. We no longer have a use for the item.$B$BMay it serve you well in your fight against the legion.$B\030Open the chest and claim your reward.\030\030Heroes of Old\0312,1,38,2,257,1,7750\0302,40,76,2,257,1,7750\0302,81,135,2,261,1,7750\0303,1,37,2,384,1,7750\0301,1,53,4,272,1,0\031\0312,4,1419,0,\0312702,19,2702,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302721,23,2721,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,141980,FINISHER,?,12,Spectral Lockbox",[2702]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Indeed, you have honored us all. Our thanks alone are not sufficient.\030You have honored me with your nobility and heroism, $N.$B$BYou have also honored them...\030Speak to Corporal Thund Splithoof.\030\030Heroes of Old\0312,1,55,2,257,1,7572\0302,60,88,2,257,1,7572\0303,1,34,2,384,1,7572\0301,1,32,4,272,1,7750\0301,34,69,4,272,1,7750\0317750,2,3,Corporal Thund Splithoof\0302857,2,3,Thund\0312,4,1419,0,\0302,0,0,3,Corporal Thund Splithoof\0312681,19,2681,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302701,23,2701,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[271]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Er... what's this? A bear's head, by the looks at it.$B$B<He runs a finger along his scar unconsciously.>$B$BWell, that's quite an interesting kill you have yourself there. Couldn't be that bear from back then...$B$B<He trails off then starts to visibly shake.>$B$BOh, take that away take it away! Get that grisly thing out of here!\030I don't suppose you'd be interested in a little payback for His Boldness? Daryl does have some skill, it pains me to say.$B$BA year ago, a large bear had been the target of the Farstrider Lodge, but none of the hunters had any luck with him. So, Daryl thought he'd try his hand against him. All he had to show for his effort was that ugly scar over his eye.$B$BKill the bear, and I'm sure even Daryl would be speechless for once.$B$BThe bear, Ol' Sooty, can be found around his lair in the hills over Thelsamar.\030Kill Ol' Sooty then show your handiwork to Daryl the Youngling at the Farstrider Lodge.\030Ah, $N! Back so soon? No doubt you've been at the hunt again? Don't worry if you've had some setbacks, in the long run it will make you better!$B$B... You couldn't get much worse, anyway...\030Vyrin's Revenge\0312,1,73,2,257,2,1156\0302,75,121,2,257,1,1156\0302,126,241,2,321,1,1156\0302,243,290,2,257,1,1156\0302,292,357,2,257,1,1156\0302,362,429,2,257,4,1156\0302,434,511,2,257,1,1156\0303,1,87,2,384,1,1156\0301,7,18,4,272,2,1187\0301,20,53,4,272,1,1187\0301,58,105,4,272,1,1187\0301,110,172,4,272,1,1187\0301,174,212,4,272,1,1187\0301,217,261,4,272,1,1187\0301,266,297,4,272,1,1187\0301,299,332,4,272,1,1187\0304,9,21,3,256,2,1187\0304,23,61,3,256,2,1187\0304,63,143,3,256,4,1187\0304,152,189,3,256,1,1187\0311225,2,7,Ol' Sooty\0301225,2,8,Ol' Sooty\0301187,2,8,Daryl the Youngling\0312,38,1432,0,\0302,0,0,8,Daryl the Youngling\0302,0,0,8,Farstrider Lodge\031258,19,258,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030531,23,531,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,2713,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[272]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You've completed the Trial of the Sea Lion, $N - congratulations.$B$BEach task in acquiring the pendant shows that both agility and endurance are necessary to act in harmony with what you desire to do underwater. Neither can exist without the other, and both cannot be done without your willingness to embrace the aspect of the sea lion.$B$BRemember these lessons well, and count on them once you have gained your aquatic form.\030For the second trial, you'll need the two halves that make the Pendant of the Sea Lion.  One half draws power from the agility of the sea lion aspect, gliding through water; the other draws power from the incredible endurance of the sea lion aspect.  Druids draw on both these traits equally to embody the aspect of their aquatic form.$B$BSpeak with the locals of Moonglade to learn where the parts may lie, and bring both here to join them together.  Once formed, take the pendant to Dendrite Starblaze.\030Find the Half Pendant of Aquatic Agility and the Half Pendant of Aquatic Endurance.  Speak with the residents of Moonglade to learn clues as to where these items may be located.$B$BForm the Pendant of the Sea Lion from the two pendant halves.  You need to be in proximity of the Shrine of Remulos to do this.$B$BBring the joined pendant to Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade.\030Have you formed your pendant for me to inspect, $N? If you need help in locating the parts, try asking the local populace for information. Not only will you find what you seek, but it will give you a reason to explore this wondrous and sacred glade.\030Trial of the Sea Lion\0312,1,87,2,259,1,11799\0302,90,249,2,257,1,11799\0302,252,335,2,257,1,11799\0302,340,450,2,257,1,11799\0302,453,504,2,257,1,11799\0303,1,83,2,384,1,11799\0303,86,177,2,384,1,11799\0303,182,242,2,384,1,11799\0303,245,308,2,386,1,11799\0303,313,399,2,384,1,11799\0301,1,65,4,272,1,11802\0301,70,212,4,274,1,11802\0301,214,337,4,272,1,11802\0301,342,427,4,272,1,11802\0304,1,51,3,256,2,11802\0304,53,138,3,258,4,11802\0304,140,249,3,258,3,11802\03111802,2,5,Dendrite Starblaze\03011802,2,10,Dendrite Starblaze\0312,0,0,5,Dendrite Starblaze\0302,0,0,10,Dendrite Starblaze\03129,19,29,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305061,23,5061,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,15885,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[2721]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Trebor? Trebor sent you?\030As one chapter of your adventure closes, another one begins, $N.$B$BOne of my men is still unaccounted for, lost somewhere in the Blasted Lands. I am talking about Lieutenant Kirith, of course.$B$BAs I had mentioned earlier, we were both imprisoned and tortured by Allistarj, but poor Kirith, his strength of will faltered. I could hear the experiments from my cage; the tortured screams rang through the halls of the cave. That was the last I saw or heard of Kirith.\030Find out what became of Lieutenant Kirith.\030\030Kirith\0312,1,64,2,257,1,7572\0302,69,144,2,261,1,7572\0302,146,193,2,257,1,7572\0302,198,323,2,261,3,7572\0302,325,423,2,257,4,7572\0302,425,467,2,257,1,7572\0303,1,42,2,384,1,7572\0301,1,7,4,272,2,7729\0301,9,24,4,272,2,7729\031\0312,4,1419,0,\0302,0,0,2,Blasted Lands\0312701,19,2701,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0302743,23,2743,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[273]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Hmph, it'll take more than a Dark Iron ambush to stop the deliveries!$B$BBut Saean... I would never have suspected him to be one of their sympathizers. We've been working with him for almost a year now... maybe I missed the signs.$B$BWell, I'll consider that later.\030It's not too late though, you're welcome to go look for Huldar. He can't have made it very far, strong as they are, Miran and Saean can only move so fast laden down with those barrels.$B$BThey're taking the normal route to the site, leaving south out of town and following the curve of the Loch.$B$BShouldn't have a problem finding them unless they've already gotten there.\030Speak with Huldar.\030Find Huldar, Miran, and Saean\030\030Resupplying the Excavation\0312,1,63,2,257,1,1105\0302,65,184,2,257,1,1105\0302,189,295,2,257,1,1105\0302,300,373,2,269,4,1105\0303,1,18,2,384,1,1105\0301,1,69,4,276,1,2057\0301,74,85,4,272,1,2057\0301,87,151,4,272,4,2057\0301,153,204,4,272,1,2057\0301,206,230,4,272,4,2057\0301,235,265,4,272,1,2057\0304,1,29,3,384,1,1105\0312057,2,1,Huldar\0301379,2,2,Miran\0301380,2,2,Saean\0302057,2,5,Huldar\0301380,4,7,Saean\0302057,3,12,Huldar\0301379,3,12,Miran\0301380,3,12,Saean\0312,38,1432,0,\031302,19,302,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030454,23,454,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[274]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A disarming colloid? For Seaforium? Oh heavens!\030This ain't no ordinary blast powder.  Look at the tiny silver crystals.  And the distinct smell!  Why it's clear as daylight that this is Seaforium Powder.  Seaforium is harmless enough.  But once it's wet it could blow Ironforge out of the mountain.$B$BThe chemical reaction can be defused by mixing four components:  lurker venom, crushed Mo'Grosh crystal, a crocolisk tear and this disarming colloid.  Now tell Hinderweir before it's too late!\030Ashlan Stonesmirk wants you to return to Chief Engineer Hinderweir and inform him of the new discovery.\030What is that you bring from Ashlan?\030A Dark Threat Looms\0312,1,36,2,257,1,1073\0302,39,71,2,257,1,1073\0302,74,96,2,257,1,1073\0302,99,155,2,257,1,1073\0302,158,186,2,257,1,1073\0302,189,250,2,257,4,1073\0302,255,403,2,257,1,1073\0302,406,446,2,265,1,1073\0303,1,103,2,386,1,1073\0301,1,20,4,272,2,1093\0301,22,35,4,272,2,1093\0301,37,47,4,272,1,1093\0304,1,35,3,256,2,1093\0311073,2,9,Ashlan Stonesmirk\0312,38,1432,0,\0302,0,0,9,Chief Engineer Hinderweir\0303,0,0,13,Ashlan\031161,19,16