il-doing leper gnomes.$B$BOzzie and I plan to reverse the horrible leper effect with our latest invention: The Recombobulator.  The machine is almost complete but we are in dire need of some Restabilization Cogs and Gyromechanic Gears.  Retrieve some from the leper gnomes out front of Gnomeregan for us.\030Bring Razzle Sprysprocket in Kharanos 8 Restabilization Cogs and 8 Gyromechanic Gears.\030The Recombobulator will be up and running as soon as we have sufficient Restabilization Cogs and Gyromechanic Gears.\030Operation Recombobulation\0312,1,223,2,257,4,1269\0302,228,327,2,257,3,1269\0302,330,436,2,259,1,1269\0302,439,505,2,257,1,1269\0303,1,86,2,384,1,1269\0301,1,131,4,272,1,1269\0301,133,316,4,272,3,1269\0304,1,116,3,256,3,1269\0318613,2,2,Ozzie\0301269,2,5,Razzle Sprysprocket\0312,1,1426,0,\0302,0,0,5,Kharanos\031\031ITEM,3083,OBJECTIVE,8,15,\030ITEM,3084,OBJECTIVE,8,15,",[4120]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It sounds from your descriptions as if the creatures show a mindless ferocity...$B$BStay alert, $N. It would be in your best interest to learn more of the corruption. Always know your enemy.\030Being a hunter, I strive to emulate the strengths I see in my opponents. It is possible to turn the battle in your favor by simply knowing your enemy well, $N.$B$BIn a place called Felwood, north of Ashenvale, the creatures have been tainted by a substance called fel. The bears and wolves have been driven mad by it, but I believe that they have also grown even stronger as well.$B$BGo, $N. Travel to Felwood and face these beasts. Learn for yourself if they are truly as strong as I believe.\030Talo Thornhoof at Camp Mojache in Feralas wants you to kill 12 Angerclaw Grizzlies and 12 Felpaw Ravagers in Felwood.\030Everything touched by the fel emanates a strange green glow... I sense it is evil, but at the same time, very powerful.\030The Strength of Corruption\0312,1,72,2,257,1,7776\0302,74,159,2,261,1,7776\0302,164,268,2,257,1,7776\0302,270,380,2,257,4,7776\0302,393,432,2,257,1,7776\0302,434,493,2,257,4,7776\0303,1,117,2,386,1,7776\0301,1,80,4,272,4,7776\0301,85,99,4,272,1,7776\0301,101,166,4,276,4,7776\0301,168,190,4,276,1,7776\0304,1,62,3,256,1,7776\0304,64,119,3,256,1,7776\0317776,2,7,Talo Thornhoof\0312,357,1444,0,\0302,0,0,3,Ashenvale\0302,0,0,5,Felwood\0302,0,0,7,Camp Mojache\0302,0,0,7,Feralas\0302,0,0,7,Felwood\031\031NPC,8957,OBJECTIVE,12,13,Angerclaw Grizzly\030NPC,8961,OBJECTIVE,12,13,Felpaw Ravager",[4121]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Your heroics will not go unrecognized, $N. You have earned this tribute. The Warlord will speak with you now in regards to the final mission.\030Do you truly believe that you will make it to your rendezvous point with me in custody? You actually expected to break into a heavily fortified Blackrock fortress to capture a prized asset of theirs without alerting anyone or anything to your presence?$B$BYou will be destroyed!$B\030Escort your prisoner, Grark Lorkrub, through Burning Steppes and through Blackrock Mountain to the Searing Gorge.$B$BYou recall Lexlort mentioning that he would have his men waiting on the other side to take Grark into custody.$B$BYou will also be required to hand over your Thorium Shackles to Lexlort.\030Prisoner Transport\030I will take this traitorous filth, $N.\030Precarious Predicament\0312,1,87,2,257,4,9520\0302,89,252,2,257,2,9520\0302,257,278,2,261,3,9520\0303,1,113,2,384,1,9520\0303,118,227,2,384,4,9520\0303,232,303,2,384,3,9520\0301,1,42,4,272,3,9080\0301,44,72,4,272,1,9080\0301,74,141,4,272,3,9080\0305,1,38,3,256,3,9080\0304,1,18,3,384,1,9520\0319520,2,4,Grark Lorkrub\0309080,2,5,Lexlort\0309080,2,6,Lexlort\0312,1584,0,0,\0302,0,0,4,Searing Gorge\0302,0,0,6,Lexlort\0314122,19,4122,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304132,23,4132,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,11286,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[4122]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Can you not see the power we gain by joining the legion of Blackrock?\030I tracked him across the Searing Gorge, through the mountain, and into the Burning Steppes. That traitor was caught red-handed giving the Blackrock orcs vital information about our day to day operations. I'm speaking of Grark Lorkrub.$B$BHe now sits in the Burning Steppes, safely under their protection - or so he thinks.$B$BTake these shackles, $N. Find Grark, place the shackles on him and lead him through Blackrock Mountain. Do this and a tribute is yours.$B\030Travel to the Burning Steppes and find Grark Lorkrub. You recall Lexlort mentioning that he was last seen in a massive Blackrock fortress.$B$BWhen you find Grark Lorkrub, use the Thorium Shackles to bind him and then lead him back through Blackrock Mountain to the Searing Gorge. Lexlort will have his men waiting on the other side to take Grark into custody.$B\030\030Grark Lorkrub\0312,1,91,2,257,1,9080\0302,93,203,2,257,1,9080\0302,205,234,2,257,1,9080\0302,239,322,2,257,1,9080\0302,327,350,2,257,1,9080\0302,352,429,2,257,1,9080\0302,431,461,2,257,1,9080\0303,1,53,2,384,1,9080\0303,55,138,2,384,1,9080\0303,143,279,2,384,1,9080\0303,281,359,2,384,3,9080\0301,1,69,4,272,2,9520\0319520,2,3,Grark Lorkrub\0309520,2,8,Grark Lorkrub\0309080,2,9,Lexlort\0309520,2,10,Grark Lorkrub\0309080,2,11,Lexlort\0312,1584,0,0,\0302,0,0,4,Burning Steppes\0302,0,0,8,Burning Steppes\0302,0,0,10,Searing Gorge\0314121,23,4121,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4123]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have the heart! Amazing! It is even more beautiful than I imagined!$B$BPlease, $N, take this as payment!\030For years I have sought a certain gem.  It is called the Heart of the Mountain and it's the size of your fist!  The Dark Iron dwarves have it locked in their vault and, try as I may, they won't let me purchase it.$B$BSo I must resort to force.$B$BFight your way to the Lower Vault of Blackrock Depths, breach its secret safe and gain the Heart.  To do that, you must defeat Watchman Doomgrip, and he won't appear until you've opened every relic coffer in the vault!$B$BGood luck.\030Bring the Heart of the Mountain to Maxwort Uberglint in the Burning Steppes.\030Do you have the Heart of the Mountain?  To me, its value is without limit.\030The Heart of the Mountain\0312,1,38,2,257,1,9536\0302,41,110,2,257,1,9536\0302,113,213,2,257,1,9536\0302,218,243,2,257,1,9536\0302,248,344,2,261,1,9536\0302,347,465,2,257,1,9536\0302,470,479,2,257,1,9536\0303,1,76,2,384,1,9536\0301,1,19,4,272,1,9536\0301,21,28,4,272,1,9536\0301,30,71,4,272,1,9536\0301,76,108,4,272,1,9536\0304,1,38,3,256,2,9536\0304,41,74,3,256,1,9536\0319476,2,6,Watchman Doomgrip\0309536,2,8,Maxwort Uberglint\0312,1584,0,0,\0302,0,0,5,Lower Vault of Blackrock Depths\0302,0,0,8,Maxwort Uberglint\0302,0,0,8,Burning Steppes\031\031ITEM,11309,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[4124]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Latro sent you to me, I presume.  While I think it is a lost cause at this point, I'll take whatever assistance you can offer.  I must admit... I'll be glad once I can put my mind to rest on this matter.  Every day I set out into the wilds of Feralas looking for signs of Raschal, and every night I have come back with nothing to show for my work save gnoll teeth and disappointment.\030An associate of mine, Ginro Hearthkindle, is looking for assistance concerning the location of a courier and the parcels he was carrying.  It has been a week or so since the courier went missing; our own searches have proved fruitless, and we're at an impasse.  Unfortunately, I have had to declare the courier as missing in action.$B$BIf you have the time and resources to spare, please speak with Ginro.  He should be here in the Stronghold - perhaps in his quarters.\030Speak with Ginro Hearthkindle in Feathermoon Stronghold.\030\030The Missing Courier\0312,1,137,2,257,1,7877\0302,140,260,2,261,1,7877\0302,263,332,2,261,1,7877\0302,337,405,2,257,4,7877\0302,408,469,2,257,4,7877\0303,1,56,2,384,1,7877\0301,1,32,4,272,1,7880\0301,35,126,4,276,1,7880\0301,129,143,4,272,1,7880\0301,145,203,4,272,1,7880\0301,206,383,4,280,1,7880\0317880,2,1,Ginro Hearthkindle\0307880,2,6,Ginro Hearthkindle\0312,357,1444,0,\0302,0,0,5,Stronghold\0302,0,0,6,Feathermoon Stronghold\0314125,23,4125,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4125]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have found what appears to be a wrecked row boat.  Through the slightly muddy water you see gaping holes riddling the port side; the boat is nearly shredded down to its simple wooden frame.  Whatever broke this boat most likely tried to snap it in two.  A small crest of the Feathermoon Stronghold is painted on the starboard side.$B$BIn the mud at the base of the boat, a glint of something metallic catches your eye...\030It's been about a week since Raschal, the courier, set out for Thalanaar.  He knows Feralas well; he's been with us since General Feathermoon led the expeditionary forces here.  I know his plan was to take a row boat down the coast and try and traverse across southern Feralas to avoid the Horde camp.$B$BI couldn't find his boat, but maybe you can.  Maybe it is hidden, or maybe it was sunk.  Regardless, it might hold a clue as to where he is.  If you uncover something, please let me know.\030Locate the courier's boat somewhere along the coast of Feralas.\030\030The Missing Courier\0312,1,73,2,257,1,7880\0302,76,176,2,257,1,7880\0302,179,301,2,257,1,7880\0302,306,349,2,257,4,7880\0302,352,392,2,257,4,7880\0302,395,445,2,257,4,7880\0302,448,492,2,257,4,7880\0303,1,63,2,384,1,7880\0301,1,53,4,272,1,0\0301,56,193,4,272,1,0\0301,196,256,4,272,1,0\0301,259,335,4,272,1,0\0301,340,424,4,272,1,0\031\0312,357,1444,0,\0314124,19,4124,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304127,23,4127,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,164909,FINISHER,?,12,Wrecked Row Boat",[4126]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You found it! Well done! And I hope you gave those Dark Irons, and Hurley Blackbreath, a good thumping!$B$BThe Thunderbrews are at your service, $N. You are a hero of heroes!\030The Dark Iron dwarves, led by the villain Hurley Blackbreath, stole one of the Thunderbrew's best recipes, Thunderbrew Lager.  The villains!  They don't deserve such a fine brew!$B$B$N, I have a tough task for you.  Go to the Blackrock Depths in the Burning Steppes, destroy any kegs of Thunderbrew Lager you find, and bring back our recipe for Thunderbrew Lager!$B$BPlease, get that recipe back, even if you have to turn Blackrock Depths upside down to do it!\030Bring the Lost Thunderbrew Recipe to Ragnar Thunderbrew in Kharanos.\030Do you have the recipe, $N? I can't stand the idea of those Dark Iron dwarves drinking my family's drink!\030Hurley Blackbreath\0312,1,125,2,257,1,1267\0302,128,140,2,257,1,1267\0302,143,178,2,257,1,1267\0302,183,214,2,257,1,1267\0302,217,363,2,261,1,1267\0302,368,460,2,257,4,1267\0303,1,68,2,388,1,1267\0301,1,13,4,272,1,1267\0301,15,24,4,272,1,1267\0301,26,103,4,274,3,1267\0301,108,148,4,272,1,1267\0301,150,174,4,272,1,1267\0304,1,27,3,256,2,1267\0304,29,105,3,256,1,1267\0319537,2,1,Hurley Blackbreath\0301267,2,7,Ragnar Thunderbrew\0309537,4,10,Hurley Blackbreath\0312,1584,0,0,\0302,0,0,5,Blackrock Depths\0302,0,0,5,Burning Steppes\0302,0,0,7,Ragnar Thunderbrew\0302,0,0,7,Kharanos\031\031ITEM,11312,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[4127]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Interesting... I believe that this is Raschal's knife.  You say you found it at the bottom of the water, along with his boat?  Well, just the knife's discovery might not be enough to connect this to Raschal's disappearance; we do, however, have an unconventional option available to us to try and learn more.$B$BHave you ever heard of psychometry?\030Running your hand along the mud, your fingers graze the handle of a knife.  It looks well cared for, and it might be safe to assume that whoever was on the boat might have lost it.  Perhaps the large chunk of the missing boat might have something to do with the loss.$B$BYou grab the knife, remembering that Ginro Hearthkindle in the Feathermoon Stronghold instructed you to return to him with any found clues.  You get the feeling, however, that you are not quite alone in the water...\030Return to Feathermoon Stronghold and show Ginro Hearthkindle the Discarded Knife you have found.\030Ah, welcome back $N.  I hope that you were able to uncover some clue as to Raschal's ultimate fate, as tragic as that may be.\030Boat Wreckage\0312,1,74,2,257,1,0\0302,77,180,2,261,4,0\0302,183,267,2,261,4,0\0302,272,410,2,257,1,0\0302,413,486,2,257,1,0\0303,1,96,2,384,1,0\0301,1,14,4,272,1,7880\0301,16,54,4,272,4,7880\0301,57,125,4,272,2,7880\0301,128,308,4,272,4,7880\0301,313,347,4,272,2,7880\0304,1,20,3,256,1,7880\0304,23,125,3,258,3,7880\0317880,2,4,Ginro Hearthkindle\0307880,2,6,Ginro Hearthkindle\0312,357,1444,0,\0302,0,0,4,Feathermoon Stronghold\0302,0,0,6,Feathermoon Stronghold\0304,0,0,10,Raschal's\0303,0,0,13,Raschal's\0314125,19,4125,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304129,23,4129,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,164909,GIVER,?,9,Wrecked Row Boat",[4128]="PARTIAL\031conflict,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You're right I'm mad!  I've been robbed!  Robbed of one of our family recipes!  How dare they!  As if I didn't have enough cause to hate the Dark Iron dwarves!  Now, oh... now they're in for it!\030Ho, $n.  I heard that Ragnar Thunderbrew is steaming mad about someone stealing his ale.  He's looking for stalwart adventurers, and willing to pay plenty.$B$BTalk to Ragnar if you're interested.  He's at the Thunderbrew Distillery in Kharanos, in Dun Morogh.\030Speak with Ragnar Thunderbrew.\030\030Ragnar Thunderbrew\0312,10,88,2,257,1,9540\0302,91,155,2,257,1,9540\0302,160,195,2,257,4,9540\0302,198,259,2,257,1,9540\0303,1,30,2,384,1,9540\0301,1,21,4,272,1,1267\0301,24,40,4,272,1,1267\0301,43,78,4,272,1,1267\0301,81,94,4,272,1,1267\0301,97,159,4,272,4,1267\0301,162,171,4,272,1,1267\0301,173,194,4,304,1,1267\0311267,2,1,Ragnar Thunderbrew\0301267,2,5,Ragnar Thunderbrew\0312,1584,0,0,\0302,0,0,3,Ragnar\0302,0,0,4,Thunderbrew Distillery\0302,0,0,4,Kharanos\0302,0,0,4,Dun Morogh\0314126,23,4126,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304126,24,4126,UNKNOWN\031",[4129]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, $N.$B$BWhile psychometry isn't an exact art by any stretch of the imagination, I've used it in times past to give insight into situations that others have chalked up to lost causes.  I think using it on the knife you've uncovered will give us a glimpse into what happened to Raschal.$B$BIt will only take a moment to do, but it isn't what I'd call a caster-friendly task.  Bear with me on this.\030The Stronghold's resident druid, Quintis Jonespyre, has some... unusual skills.  One of them involves psychometry - the ability to reveal an item's history by touch.  Don't ask me how he does it; I chalk it up to magic I do not and choose not to understand.  I do know, however, two things: one, I've seen it work and two, the bum owes me.$B$BTake the knife up to Quint in his little tree-house here, and tell him for me that his Kalimdor Hold 'Em debt will be paid if he works his mojo on that knife.\030Take the Discarded Knife to Quintis Jonespyre in Feathermoon Stronghold.\030Ginro sent you, eh?$B$BMy psychometric readings are fairly draining on the psyche... but so are my losses at Kalimdor Hold 'Em.  They call me \"King of the Bad Beats\" here in the Stronghold.  Unlucky at cards... lucky at mastering the secrets of nature, I guess.$B$BAnyway, of course I'll do it.  This may be just the breakthrough we need to uncover Raschal's fate.  If you would hand me the knife, we can get started.\030The Knife Revealed\0312,1,63,2,257,1,7880\0302,65,79,2,257,1,7880\0302,82,165,2,321,1,7880\0302,168,257,2,257,1,7880\0302,260,339,2,257,1,7880\0302,344,501,2,257,4,7880\0303,1,72,2,384,1,7880\0301,1,14,4,272,1,7879\0301,19,192,4,276,1,7879\0301,195,294,4,272,3,7879\0301,299,382,4,272,3,7879\0301,385,405,4,272,1,7879\0304,1,19,3,256,2,7879\0304,24,84,3,256,1,7879\0304,86,127,3,256,1,7879\0304,130,189,3,256,1,7879\0304,192,210,3,256,1,7879\0304,212,261,3,256,1,7879\0304,266,294,3,256,1,7879\0304,297,364,3,258,1,7879\0304,367,417,3,256,4,7879\0317879,2,1,Quintis Jonespyre\0307879,2,7,Quintis Jonespyre\0312,357,1444,0,\0302,0,0,6,Quint\0302,0,0,7,Quintis Jonespyre\0302,0,0,7,Feathermoon Stronghold\0304,0,0,10,Raschal\0303,0,0,15,Kalimdor Hold\0303,0,0,16,Stronghold\0314127,19,4127,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304130,23,4130,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[413]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Mountaineer Barleybrew tastes the Shimmer Stout...>$B$BOh. Whoa! This stuff really puts a shine in your eyes. I feel like I can see in the dark!\030I'd like my brother Wellart to try my new Shimmer Stout.  He's a Mountaineer stationed in the southern guard tower, one of two towers on the border to Loch Modan.$B$BHe may not be a brewer like the rest of us Barleybrews, but he loves his drinks and I know he'll like this one.$B$BCan you bring him this Barrel of Shimmer Stout for me?\030Take the Barrel of Shimmer Stout to Mountaineer Barleybrew.\030Hello, $C! And what business takes you all the way out here?$B$BSomething exciting, I hope. I haven't been in a good fight in days, and this barrel of ale is almost dry...\030Shimmer Stout\0312,1,56,2,259,1,1374\0302,59,162,2,257,1,1374\0302,167,277,2,257,1,1374\0302,282,335,2,257,2,1374\0303,1,59,2,384,1,1374\0301,1,52,4,272,1,1959\0301,61,65,4,272,1,1959\0301,67,110,4,272,1,1959\0301,112,145,4,272,1,1959\0304,1,10,3,256,1,1959\0304,12,60,3,256,2,1959\0304,65,91,3,258,3,1959\0304,93,171,3,260,1,1959\0311959,2,5,Mountaineer Barleybrew\0301959,4,6,Mountaineer Barleybrew\0312,1,1426,0,\0302,0,0,2,Loch Modan\0302,0,0,5,Mountaineer Barleybrew\031315,19,315,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030414,23,414,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4130]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thanks for passing along Quint's visions to me, $N.  I'll try to remember to be a little easier on him the next time we play cards.$B$BRaschal can hold his own in a fight, and gnolls aren't anything that would get him worried - nay, terrified.  Still, maybe you and yours can act on this new information and make the breakthrough we desperately need.\030I'm a little wobbly still, sorry.  Anyway, I received some useful visions.$B$BRaschal takes two large leather backpacks from his boat and goes inland; he returns to the boat, however.  I see gnoll scalps... he ran into some gnolls - Woodpaw I think they're called.  He's very worried - almost terrified - about something.  So much so, that he is not paying attention to water elementals forming behind him.  The images... stop there.$B$BI need to rest, sorry $N.  Tell Gin what I've seen.  He needs to know.\030Speak with Ginro Hearthkindle in Feathermoon Stronghold.\030\030Psychometric Reading\0312,1,33,2,257,1,7879\0302,36,74,2,257,1,7879\0302,79,183,2,257,1,7879\0302,186,206,2,257,1,7879\0302,208,264,2,257,1,7879\0302,267,321,2,257,1,7879\0302,324,406,2,257,1,7879\0302,409,421,2,257,1,7879\0302,423,433,2,257,1,7879\0302,438,462,2,259,1,7879\0302,465,488,2,257,1,7879\0302,491,507,2,259,1,7879\0303,1,56,2,384,1,7879\0301,1,51,4,272,1,7880\0301,54,131,4,272,1,7880\0301,136,243,4,276,4,7880\0301,246,350,4,274,4,7880\0317880,2,13,Ginro Hearthkindle\0312,357,1444,0,\0302,0,0,13,Feathermoon Stronghold\0314129,19,4129,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304131,23,4131,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4131]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Tacked up on a nearby tree are two large leather backpacks.  Each bears a small insignia of the Feathermoon Stronghold on the front of the pack...\030Our \"friends\" the Woodpaw might have gotten Raschal in the end, but something tells me that's not what occurred.  Still, they're the best place to start looking.$B$BI wish I had clearer insight as to what to do, but all I have right now is 'Search the Woodpaw camps - go.'  I do know that gnolls will keep items they scavenge and fight over them; maybe they ran across the backpacks Quint mentioned.  I hadn't risked a head-on fight in past searches, but with Quint's vision on this I say rip into them.\030Search the Woodpaw Gnoll camps of southern Feralas for evidence of the courier's belongings or the courier himself.\030\030The Woodpaw Gnolls\0312,1,112,2,257,4,7880\0302,115,161,2,257,1,7880\0302,166,399,2,263,4,7880\0302,402,503,2,261,1,7880\0303,1,115,2,384,1,7880\0301,1,59,4,272,1,0\0301,62,146,4,272,1,0\031\0312,357,1444,0,\0314130,19,4130,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304135,23,4135,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,164953,FINISHER,?,12,Large Leather Backpacks",[4132]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Finally! The villain been brought to justice! You are a remarkable individual, $N. Wear this medallion as a symbol of your stalwart dedication to the Horde and the K.E.F.\030You have done an exemplary job, $N. It is now time to send you on your last mission.$B$BGeneral Angerforge, the Dark Iron responsible for coordinating the attacks on the 109th division of the K.E.F. and the mass slaughter of our forces must be brought to justice.$B$BThis will undoubtedly be your most grueling mission, but should you succeed, you will be richly rewarded.$B\030Travel to Blackrock Depths and slay General Angerforge! Return to Warlord Goretooth when the task is complete.\030Has the Butcher of Blackrock been disposed of?\030Operation: Death to Angerforge\0312,1,35,2,257,1,9077\0302,37,84,2,257,1,9077\0302,89,198,2,261,1,9077\0302,200,263,2,257,1,9077\0302,268,372,2,257,3,9077\0303,1,55,2,384,1,9077\0303,57,110,2,384,1,9077\0301,1,8,4,272,1,9077\0301,10,45,4,272,1,9077\0301,47,82,4,272,1,9077\0301,84,170,4,272,1,9077\0304,1,46,3,256,2,9077\0319033,2,3,General Angerforge\0309033,2,6,General Angerforge\0309077,2,7,Warlord Goretooth\0312,1584,0,0,\0302,0,0,6,Blackrock Depths\0302,0,0,7,Warlord Goretooth\0304,0,0,11,Horde\0314121,19,4121,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,9033,OBJECTIVE,1,13,General Angerforge",[4133]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you for coming, $N. This place is not without a stark charm, but is lacks the amenities of the Apothecarium.$B$BEnough with the pleasantries. To business, yes?\030Shadowmaster Vivian Lagrave is in need of your services.  She is in the Badlands, in the orcish outpost of Kargath, pursuing rumors of a certain brew made by the Dark Iron dwarves of Blackrock Depths.$B$BSpeak with Vivian.  She awaits you.\030Speak with Shadowmaster Vivian Lagrave in Kargath.\030\030Vivian Lagrave\0312,1,56,2,259,1,5204\0302,59,200,2,257,1,5204\0302,205,222,2,257,1,5204\0302,225,239,2,257,1,5204\0303,1,50,2,384,1,5204\0301,1,25,4,272,1,9078\0301,27,114,4,272,1,9078\0301,119,147,4,272,1,9078\0301,149,165,4,272,2,9078\031\0312,1584,0,0,\0302,0,0,2,Badlands\0302,0,0,5,Kargath\0314134,23,4134,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304134,24,4134,UNKNOWN\031",[4134]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very good. I will send this recipe to the Apothecarium to be studied, and in time we will unlock its secrets. One day, the dwarves of the Alliance may find the virtues of this drink used against them!$B$BI find that terribly amusing. Perhaps death has an affect on one's sense of humor... do you think?\030It is rumored that the Dark Iron Hurley Blackbreath has stolen a recipe for ale.  This ale, Thunderbrew Lager, is said to infuse its imbiber with great strength and courage.  We wish to study the drink.  Perhaps, we will find other applications for its virtues... applications more in line with Forsaken objectives.$B$BDelve into Blackrock Depths, find Hurley, take from him the recipe for Thunderbrew lager and bring it to me.$B$BAnd to find him, you may have to entice him by threatening his precious ale.\030Bring the Lost Thunderbrew Recipe to Vivian Lagrave in Kargath.\030Do you have the recipe for the Thunderbrew Lager, $N?\030Lost Thunderbrew Recipe\0312,1,80,2,261,1,9078\0302,83,173,2,257,1,9078\0302,176,202,2,259,3,9078\0302,205,263,2,257,4,9078\0302,265,315,2,257,1,9078\0302,320,427,2,257,1,9078\0302,432,507,2,261,1,9078\0303,1,63,2,388,1,9078\0301,1,10,4,272,1,9078\0301,12,109,4,272,3,9078\0301,111,200,4,272,1,9078\0301,205,233,4,272,1,9078\0301,235,288,4,272,4,9078\0301,290,302,4,272,2,9078\0304,1,53,3,256,2,9078\0319537,2,1,Hurley Blackbreath\03014528,2,7,Precious\0312,1584,0,0,\0302,0,0,8,Vivian Lagrave\0302,0,0,8,Kargath\0304,0,0,10,Apothecarium\031\031ITEM,11312,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[4135]="PARTIAL\031characters,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have discovered a large pod of an alien nature.  The texture of the pod appears mucous, though hardened protrusions stick out from random parts of it.  The pod itself has the height and width to easily encompass a humanoid inside of it... and from the faint humanoid shape visible through the skin of the pod, you surmise that this is what it indeed encapsulates.\030Inside the backpacks are two items: the first is a parcel of goods that was bound for Thalanaar, and the second is a note hastily penned to an unknown reader.$B$BThe note tells of discovering insidious bug-like creatures south of the gnoll camps in a place called the Writhing Deep.  The author felt the need to investigate it personally, as though it was a serious threat to all of Feralas.  The note is signed, \"Raschal of Feathermoon\".$B$BIt would seem that you have located where Raschal ultimately went.\030Now that Raschal's last known whereabouts have been discovered, continue your search for him or his remains in the Writhing Deep.  According to the note, it is located to the south of the Woodpaw gnoll camps.\030\030The Writhing Deep\0312,1,158,2,261,1,0\0302,163,282,2,257,1,0\0302,285,391,2,263,1,0\0302,394,438,2,257,1,0\0302,443,508,2,257,4,0\0303,1,129,2,384,1,0\0303,132,208,2,384,1,0\0301,1,51,4,272,1,0\0301,54,154,4,272,1,0\0301,157,242,4,272,1,0\0301,244,367,4,272,1,0\031\0312,357,1444,0,\0302,0,0,6,Writhing Deep\0302,0,0,7,Woodpaw\0314131,19,4131,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304265,23,4265,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,164953,GIVER,?,9,Large Leather Backpacks\030OBJECT,164954,FINISHER,?,12,Zukk'ash Pod",[4136]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Aha! You found him! And... it appears that my little brother didn't want to come quiety. It's a pity. I would have liked to see the look on his face when I told him our plans to turn him in to Revilgaz.$B$BThank you, $N. You've made my family very happy. And Ribbly's never looked as peaceful as he does now.\030My brother Ribbly has always been a drain to his family, taking our money and wasting it on one scheme after another.$B$BWell, his last scheme must have been his worst, because Baron Revilgaz of Booty Bay just put a price on poor Ribbly's head.  I can't tell you how happy this makes the Screwspigots!  Our little Ribbly's finally worth something!$B$BBut now he's hiding out, deep in Blackrock Depths.  Please, find him and bring him to me!$B$BOr, if he won't come, then that's ok... just bring me his head.\030Bring Ribbly's Head to Yuka Screwspigot in the Burning Steppes.\030Do you have Ribbly?  Or, at least a part of him?\030Ribbly Screwspigot\0312,1,117,2,257,1,9544\0302,122,244,2,259,1,9544\0302,247,301,2,257,1,9544\0302,304,347,2,257,1,9544\0302,352,401,2,257,1,9544\0302,404,440,2,257,1,9544\0302,445,483,2,257,4,9544\0302,485,507,2,257,1,9544\0303,1,63,2,384,1,9544\0301,1,4,4,272,1,9544\0301,6,19,4,272,1,9544\0301,21,26,4,272,1,9544\0301,28,88,4,272,1,9544\0301,90,101,4,272,1,9544\0301,103,202,4,272,4,9544\0301,207,220,4,272,1,9544\0301,222,254,4,272,1,9544\0301,256,308,4,272,1,9544\0304,1,19,3,256,2,9544\0304,22,48,3,256,2,9544\0312496,2,2,Baron Revilgaz\0309544,2,9,Yuka Screwspigot\0312,1584,0,0,\0302,0,0,5,Blackrock Depths\0302,0,0,9,Yuka Screwspigot\0302,0,0,9,Burning Steppes\0304,0,0,15,Revilgaz\031\031ITEM,11313,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[414]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Now, let me have a taste...$B$BMagni's Beard! This stuff gets your head turning! And it lightens the limbs, too.$B$BI feel like I can fly!\030I've been drinking more of that Shimmer Stout my brother made - it's great stuff!  I want a fellow Mountaineer to try it.  His name's Kadrell, and he's usually patrolling the road through Thelsamar in Loch Modan.$B$BTo get to Thelsamar, go southeast through the tunnel, then turn northeast when the path forks into a road.  Follow that road straight into Thelsamar.$B$BGive Mountaineer Kadrell this cask of Shimmer Stout and see what he thinks!\030Take the Cask of Shimmer Stout to Mountaineer Kadrell.\030Greetings, $C, and welcome to Thelsamar!\030Stout to Kadrell\0312,1,81,2,257,1,1959\0302,84,121,2,259,1,1959\0302,124,212,2,257,1,1959\0302,217,322,2,257,1,1959\0302,325,365,2,257,1,1959\0302,370,444,2,257,1,1959\0303,1,54,2,384,1,1959\0301,1,27,4,272,1,1340\0301,32,45,4,272,1,1340\0301,47,80,4,272,1,1340\0301,82,112,4,272,1,1340\0301,117,138,4,272,1,1340\0304,1,40,3,256,1,1340\0311340,2,6,Mountaineer Kadrell\0301340,2,7,Mountaineer Kadrell\0312,1,1426,0,\0302,0,0,3,Loch Modan\0302,0,0,4,Thelsamar\0302,0,0,7,Mountaineer Kadrell\0303,0,0,13,Thelsamar\031413,19,413,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4141]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I hope they didn't give you too much trouble, $N. I try to steer clear of them -- they're wild!$B$BI tried jumping over one... I was attacked! Plants just shouldn't be acting that way!\030See Larion over there? It's HIS fault we're here!$B$BI told him we were going the wrong way, but would he listen? And would you believe that he's the one that won't speak to me? Well, until he changes his mind, let's have a bit of fun with him.$B$BHave you noticed the strange plant-like creatures around here? They're nothing but trouble, really, but I think if trained properly, I could get them to obey commands.$B$BFirst thing though, I'll need some samples to study. Do you think you could collect some?\030Collect 15 Bloodpetals and return to Muigin.\030Larion's got something coming, that's for sure!\030Muigin and Larion\0312,1,22,2,257,2,9119\0302,24,49,2,257,1,9119\0302,54,113,2,257,4,9119\0302,115,177,2,257,4,9119\0302,179,244,2,257,1,9119\0302,249,310,2,257,2,9119\0302,312,415,2,257,4,9119\0302,420,471,2,259,1,9119\0302,473,508,2,257,4,9119\0303,1,44,2,384,1,9119\0301,1,49,4,274,3,9119\0301,51,95,4,272,1,9119\0301,100,126,4,272,1,9119\0301,128,142,4,276,1,9119\0301,144,184,4,272,1,9119\0304,1,47,3,256,1,9119\0319118,2,1,Larion\0309119,2,10,Muigin\0312,490,1449,0,\0302,0,0,10,Muigin\0314142,23,4142,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,11316,OBJECTIVE,15,15,",[4142]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Bloodpetal, eh? Hmmm... Well, you better explain the plan, and then I'll tell you whether or not I can help you.\030I'm not quite sure what to make of this, $N. The plants... they seem to have some minimal intelligence.$B$BI'm no expert, though. But, I do know someone that is!$B$BHead to northern Feralas, and look for a buddy of mine named Gregan Brewspewer. He's an expert on this sort of thing.$B$BI'm sure Gregan can help us out here. You'll find him out in the wilderness; he's not the type to live in a big city.\030Take a Bloodpetal to Gregan Brewspewer in Feralas.\030I live out here in the forest... Peaceful.$B$BWell, at least I thought it would be. I get more visitors out here than I ever did when I lived in Ironforge!\030A Visit to Gregan\0312,1,44,2,257,1,9119\0302,46,58,2,257,1,9119\0302,60,103,2,257,4,9119\0302,108,129,2,257,1,9119\0302,131,161,2,257,1,9119\0302,166,244,2,257,1,9119\0302,246,282,2,257,1,9119\0302,287,323,2,257,1,9119\0302,325,403,2,257,1,9119\0303,1,50,2,384,1,9119\0301,1,15,4,272,2,7775\0301,17,23,4,272,1,7775\0301,25,112,4,272,1,7775\0304,1,32,3,256,1,7775\0304,34,42,3,256,1,7775\0304,47,83,3,256,4,7775\0304,85,155,3,256,1,7775\0317775,2,6,Gregan Brewspewer\0307775,2,10,Gregan Brewspewer\0312,490,1449,0,\0302,0,0,10,Gregan Brewspewer\0302,0,0,10,Feralas\0303,0,0,17,Ironforge\0314141,19,4141,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304143,23,4143,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4143]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I admit, I'm a bit hesitant to touch that stuff, $N! But if Gregan says it'll work, then I'm willing to give it a try!\030To tell you the truth, $N, I've never seen any plants like this in my travels. Perhaps I should take a trip to this crater...$B$BAt any rate, I think I know just the thing Muigin's looking for -- Atal'ai haze. It's horrid stuff, hard to collect, but it's just what he needs to control the little monsters.$B$BYou'll need to visit the temple of Atal'Hakkar in the Swamp of Sorrows. The Atal'ai Haze can be collected from the deep lurkers, murk worms, or oozes found there. Good luck, $N!\030Collect 5 samples of Atal'ai Haze, then return to Muigin in Un'Goro Crater.\030Larion's still not speaking to me! He sure knows how to hold a grudge.\030Haze of Evil\0312,1,78,2,257,1,7775\0302,80,125,2,257,4,7775\0302,130,209,2,257,1,7775\0302,211,305,2,259,1,7775\0302,310,380,2,259,1,7775\0302,382,471,2,257,1,7775\0302,473,486,2,257,1,7775\0303,1,75,2,384,1,7775\0301,1,52,4,272,1,9119\0301,54,118,4,272,4,9119\0304,1,34,3,256,1,9119\0304,36,70,3,256,1,9119\0319119,2,8,Muigin\0312,490,1449,0,\0302,0,0,5,Swamp of Sorrows\0302,0,0,8,Muigin\0302,0,0,8,Un'Goro Crater\0314142,19,4142,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304144,23,4144,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,11318,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[4144]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Here goes nothing, $N! This will get Larion's attention!\030\030\030Here's the plan, $N: Go out and collect some bloodpetal sprouts -- you know, the plants that haven't fully sprouted yet, and bring them here. Then I'll see what the Atal'ai haze can do.$B$BYou may think I'm vengeful... Actually, you'd be right about that!$B$BTruth is, I know the way out of here, but until Larion will admit that I'm right, I'm staying right here!$B$BSo off with you, find those bloodpetal sprouts and let's have some fun!\030Bloodpetal Sprouts\0311,1,22,4,272,1,9119\0301,24,56,4,272,3,9119\0304,1,141,3,256,1,9119\0304,143,185,3,256,1,9119\0304,190,218,3,256,1,9119\0304,220,255,3,256,1,9119\0304,260,364,3,256,3,9119\0304,369,439,3,256,1,9119\0319118,3,7,Larion\0312,490,1449,0,\0314143,19,4143,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,11315,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[4145]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thanks for your help, $N, but I'm afraid I have some bad news...\030See Muigin over there? It's HIS fault we're lost!$B$BI'm the one that knew the way, but he insisted he knew a shortcut, and we ended up here!$B$BTo make matters worse, now he keeps sending his crazy plant pests to annoy me. I'm so angry that I'm not planning on talking to him any time soon, but these pests are too much to handle.$B$BWhy don't we try to limit his supply, first thing. Go out and hunt some Bloodpetals, then return to me.\030Hunt 5 Bloodpetal Lashers, 5 Bloodpetal Threshers, 5 Bloodpetal Flayers and 5 Bloodpetal Trappers for Larion at Marshal's Refuge.\030Muigin needs to apologize first before I'll talk to him again!\030Larion and Muigin\0312,1,22,2,257,2,9118\0302,24,49,2,261,1,9118\0302,54,141,2,257,1,9118\0302,146,223,2,257,1,9118\0302,225,331,2,257,1,9118\0302,336,385,2,257,1,9118\0302,387,438,2,257,1,9118\0303,1,129,2,384,1,9118\0301,1,64,4,272,1,9118\0304,1,62,3,258,1,9118\0319119,2,1,Muigin\0309118,2,8,Larion\0309119,3,10,Muigin\0312,490,1449,0,\0302,0,0,8,Marshal's Refuge\0314147,23,4147,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,6509,OBJECTIVE,5,13,Bloodpetal Lasher\030NPC,6512,OBJECTIVE,5,13,Bloodpetal Trapper\030NPC,6510,OBJECTIVE,5,13,Bloodpetal Flayer\030NPC,6511,OBJECTIVE,5,13,Bloodpetal Thresher",[4146]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031So, Marvon wasn't around? Well, show me what you got, anyway.\030You're in luck, $n! I've been working on some of my own experiments while Marvon's been gone, and one of them is a short range bug zapper. With just a few adjustments, it should be great for ridding yourself of those Bloodpetal pests.$B$BI can let you have one of my zapper prototypes, but you'll still need to collect the fuel. You can get the necessary Atal'ai haze that the zapper needs in the temple of Atal'Hakkar. The deep lurkers, murk worms, or oozes are the ones you'll need to get it from.\030Deliver the Unloaded Zapper and 5 samples of Atal'ai Haze to Larion in Marshal's Refuge.\030This is exhausting, $N. Those things just won't leave me alone!\030Zapper Fuel\0312,1,19,2,257,1,8496\0302,21,138,2,257,1,8496\0302,140,234,2,257,1,8496\0302,239,328,2,259,1,8496\0302,330,419,2,259,1,8496\0302,421,499,2,259,1,8496\0303,1,88,2,384,1,8496\0301,1,25,4,272,2,9118\0301,27,61,4,272,1,9118\0304,1,23,3,256,1,9118\0304,25,63,3,256,1,9118\0319118,2,7,Larion\0312,1417,0,0,\0302,0,0,7,Larion\0302,0,0,7,Marshal's Refuge\0314147,19,4147,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304148,23,4148,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,11318,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[4147]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Marvon's been gone quite a long time now, $N. He went off to Tanaris to study some of the ancient troll ruins.$B$BNow, what was it that you said you needed?\030I managed to spy on what Muigin was doing, and he's actually growing the darn things over there!$B$BI think the only solution here is to... no, not go talk to him... What are you thinking? The solution is to fight back!$B$BWe'll need the help of my friend, Marvon, who has a workshop in Ratchet.  I'm sure he'll be able to create some sort of gadget that will help us.\030Travel to Marvon Rivetseeker's workshop in Ratchet.\030\030Marvon's Workshop\0312,1,96,2,257,1,9118\0302,101,139,2,257,1,9118\0302,141,165,2,257,1,9118\0302,167,188,2,257,2,9118\0302,190,219,2,261,1,9118\0302,224,295,2,259,1,9118\0302,298,368,2,257,3,9118\0303,1,51,2,384,1,9118\0301,1,45,4,272,1,8496\0301,47,110,4,336,1,8496\0301,115,156,4,272,2,8496\0319119,2,1,Muigin\0307771,2,8,Marvon Rivetseeker\0312,490,1449,0,\0302,0,0,6,Ratchet\0302,0,0,8,Marvon Rivetseeker's\0302,0,0,8,Ratchet\0304,0,0,10,Tanaris\0314145,19,4145,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304146,23,4146,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4148]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Looks like this is going to work perfectly, $N. Now remember, if you see any of those pests around, don't hesitate to use that zapper!\030\030\030For the zapper to work, it needs a sample of the target creature. Head out into the crater and collect a Bloodpetal sprout. Then I can calibrate it to work on Muigin's little friends...$B$BIf he weren't so stubborn, we could be on our way home, already... But until then, I'll just have to show him that his little prank doesn't bother me at all!\030Bloodpetal Zapper\0311,1,47,4,272,3,9118\0301,49,134,4,272,4,9118\0304,1,65,3,258,1,9118\0304,67,123,3,256,1,9118\0304,125,185,3,256,1,9118\0304,190,255,3,256,4,9118\0304,257,346,3,256,1,9118\031\0312,490,1449,0,\0314146,19,4146,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,11315,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[415]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031$N! You know that Shimmerweed you brought me? Well I used it in a few recipes I've been working on, and one of them turned out great!$B$BHere, try it out and tell me what you think...\030Rejold Barleybrew at Brewnall Village has been asking for you.$B$BHe wants to talk to you about a new drink he's been brewing...said something about you helping him with it.  You might want to head back to Brewnall Village and see what he has to say.$B$BThere could be some free booze in it for you...\030Speak with Rejold Barleybrew.\030\030Rejold's New Brew\0312,1,62,2,257,1,1872\0302,67,173,2,259,1,1872\0302,176,250,2,259,4,1872\0302,255,301,2,257,4,1872\0303,1,29,2,384,1,1872\0301,5,45,4,272,2,1374\0301,47,133,4,272,1,1374\0301,138,183,4,272,1,1374\0311374,2,1,Rejold Barleybrew\0301374,2,5,Rejold Barleybrew\0312,1,1426,0,\0302,0,0,1,Brewnall Village\0302,0,0,3,Brewnall Village\031413,23,413,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030413,24,413,UNKNOWN\031",[416]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ugh! When I asked for those ears I didn't realize they'd smell so bad!$B$BHere's your reward, $N. Well done.\030We have a real infestation problem to the west.  Tunnel rat kobolds have moved into the foothills, setting up dens and fouling our land with their filth!$B$BWe want them eliminated.  Hunt them, bring me their ears and earn their bounty.$B$BYou can find tunnel rat kobolds and their dens west of Thelsamar, littered along the mountainside.\030Bring 12 Tunnel Rat Ears to Mountaineer Kadrell in Thelsamar.\030Hail, $N. How goes the rat catching?\030Rat Catching\0312,1,47,2,261,1,1340\0302,50,153,2,257,1,1340\0302,158,181,2,259,1,1340\0302,184,236,2,257,1,1340\0302,241,338,2,257,1,1340\0303,1,61,2,384,1,1340\0301,1,4,4,272,1,1340\0301,6,70,4,272,1,1340\0301,75,97,4,272,1,1340\0301,99,108,4,272,1,1340\0304,1,9,3,256,1,1340\0304,11,36,3,256,2,1340\0311340,2,6,Mountaineer Kadrell\0312,38,1432,0,\0302,0,0,5,Thelsamar\0302,0,0,6,Mountaineer Kadrell\0302,0,0,6,Thelsamar\031\031ITEM,3110,OBJECTIVE,12,15,",[4161]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Always remember what I have shown you today, $N. You are part of the balance that the night elves strive to keep intact, even during troublesome times.\030Long ago, the night elves were called the kaldorei, a name that means \"children of the stars.\" Learning of the past is an important step in your path as a $c, $N, so listen well to what I have to tell you.$B$BThe kaldorei have always taken much pride in their harmonious relationship with nature. This means that we only take from nature what is necessary, and that we return in kind. This balance has afforded us much, $N.$B$BGo out and collect seven small spider legs -- no more than that, and return to me.\030Collect 7 Small Spider Legs for Zarrin in Dolanaar.\030Remember the balance, $N. I wish you to develop an understanding and a strong empathy for the living forests.\030Recipe of the Kaldorei\0312,1,205,2,321,1,6286\0302,210,296,2,257,1,6286\0302,298,384,2,257,1,6286\0302,386,423,2,265,1,6286\0302,428,509,2,257,1,6286\0303,1,51,2,384,1,6286\0301,1,48,4,272,1,6286\0301,50,151,4,280,1,6286\0304,1,25,3,264,1,6286\0304,27,109,3,258,3,6286\03114881,2,5,Spider\03014881,2,6,Spider\0306286,2,6,Zarrin\0312,0,0,6,Dolanaar\031\031ITEM,5465,OBJECTIVE,7,15,",[417]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is grim news, for Hildelve was a good friend. And I wish I could have been there with you when you found the beast, Mangeclaw!$B$BThank you, $N. Your deed will be remembered by the pilots of the Ironforge Siege Brigade.\030Hildelve wrote in his journal that he was attacked by Mangeclaw, a \"huge Ice Claw Bear.\"  He drove off the beast, but not before it mauled him savagely.$B$BJudging from the state of Hildelve's body, Mangeclaw must have later returned and killed him.$B$BHowever, Hildelve wrote in his journal his one, final wish:$B$BRevenge against Mangeclaw.\030Kill Mangeclaw.$B$BBring his Mangy Claw and Hildelve's Journal to Pilot Hammerfoot.\030Hello, $N. Do you have word of my friend Hildelve?\030A Pilot's Revenge\0312,1,152,2,261,1,0\0302,157,249,2,257,1,0\0302,254,312,2,259,3,0\0302,317,342,2,259,1,0\0303,1,15,2,384,1,0\0303,20,83,2,384,1,0\0301,1,50,4,272,1,1960\0301,52,131,4,274,4,1960\0301,136,149,4,272,1,1960\0301,151,224,4,272,3,1960\0304,1,10,3,256,1,1960\0304,12,50,3,256,2,1960\0311961,2,1,Mangeclaw\0301196,2,1,Ice Claw Bear\03010430,2,1,The Beast\0301961,2,2,Mangeclaw\0301961,2,4,Mangeclaw\0301961,2,5,Mangeclaw\0301960,2,6,Pilot Hammerfoot\03010430,4,8,The Beast\0301961,4,8,Mangeclaw\0312,1,1426,0,\0302,0,0,6,Pilot Hammerfoot\031419,19,419,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,2059,GIVER,?,9,A Dwarven Corpse\030ITEM,3183,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[418]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Trust me, it seems a lot harder than it looks, but...$B$BOh, I've never known someone to take much interest in the making of sausages, but I'll give you the recipe just in case. Here you go, mind you eat them fresh!\030There's never a shortage of empty bellies here in Thelsamar, kids running in and out, workers from the excavation coming in after  a hard day's work. We're famous for our blood sausages, I don't suppose you've ever tried them?$B$BNo? Well, around here you've got to work for your meals, and don't think just because you're a fancy $c, you'll be any exception.$B$BI'll need bear meat, boar intestines for the casings, and spider ichor for spice. You get me some of those, and leave the cooking to Vidra!\030Bring 3 pieces of Bear Meat, 3 Boar Intestines, and 3 Spider Ichor to Vidra Hearthstove in Thelsamar.\030I'm all ready to start cooking, do you have the ingredients for me?\030Thelsamar Blood Sausages\0312,1,149,2,257,1,1963\0302,151,226,2,257,2,1963\0302,235,359,2,259,1,1963\0302,364,444,2,259,1,1963\0302,446,502,2,257,1,1963\0303,1,101,2,384,1,1963\0301,1,53,4,272,4,1963\0301,58,177,4,272,1,1963\0301,179,215,4,272,1,1963\0304,1,67,3,256,2,1963\0312809,2,4,Boar\03014881,2,4,Spider\0302809,2,6,Boar\03014881,2,6,Spider\0301963,2,6,Vidra Hearthstove\0312,38,1432,0,\0302,0,0,1,Thelsamar\0302,0,0,5,Vidra\0302,0,0,6,Vidra Hearthstove\0302,0,0,6,Thelsamar\031\031ITEM,3172,OBJECTIVE,3,15,\030ITEM,3173,OBJECTIVE,3,15,\030ITEM,3174,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[4181]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well $N, you were wise to seek my tutelage! Any schlep can become an expert at the basics of engineering - the gnomes and their irradiated home of Gnomeregan are proof of that. It takes a strong mind and a steady hand (emphasis on STEADY) though to master the discipline of Goblin Engineering.$B$BKeep your ears perked $N, and you might learn something.\030Expert engineering yields two distinct disciplines: gnome and goblin.  I only bother to mention goblin engineering because I'm a fair trainer.  They like to make things that blow up, and they rarely care what is in the way - even themselves.$B$B$N, read this manual.  If you want to learn how to blow yourself up, then take it to Nixx Sprocketspring in Gadgetzan.   Remember - membership is permanent and prevents joining the other discipline, so make sure this is what you want before finishing his task.\030If you wish to learn more about Goblin Engineering, take the Manual of Engineering Disciplines to Nixx Sprocketspring in Gadgetzan.\030I can smell fresh recruits much like I can an excellent blasting powder - from a mile away. Have you come seeking to learn about the mastery of the explosion?\030Goblin Engineering\0312,1,69,2,257,1,5518\0302,72,142,2,259,1,5518\0302,145,241,2,257,1,5518\0302,246,266,2,257,1,5518\0302,269,363,2,259,4,5518\0302,367,505,2,259,1,5518\0303,1,131,2,386,4,5518\0301,1,43,4,274,1,8126\0301,45,176,4,272,1,8126\0301,178,293,4,272,1,8126\0301,298,353,4,272,4,8126\0304,1,91,3,256,1,8126\0304,93,158,3,256,2,8126\0318126,2,5,Nixx Sprocketspring\0308126,2,7,Nixx Sprocketspring\0312,0,0,5,Nixx Sprocketspring\0302,0,0,5,Gadgetzan\0302,0,0,7,Nixx Sprocketspring\0302,0,0,7,Gadgetzan\0313526,22,3526,UNKNOWN\0303629,22,3629,UNKNOWN\0303630,22,3630,UNKNOWN\0303632,22,3632,UNKNOWN\0303633,22,3633,UNKNOWN\0303634,22,3634,UNKNOWN\0303635,22,3635,UNKNOWN\0303637,22,3637,UNKNOWN\031",[4182]="PARTIAL\031loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Superb slaying, $N. Now that we know you can handle yourself around dragonkin, we can talk of more pressing matters.\030Life in the Burning Steppes is rife with conflict.$B$BJust look at this place! We know very little of what happened to these buildings, but we do know that at one time, before the great explosion, this was all part of the Redridge mountain range.$B$BEnough lamenting! We have a problem, $N. You may have noticed the dragonkin below this ridge. We need assistance in pushing them back. Kill as many as you can and return to me. Succeed and perhaps we can talk of other things.$B\030Slay 15 Black Broodlings, 10 Black Dragonspawn, 4 Black Wyrmkin and 1 Black Drake. Return to Helendis Riverhorn when the task is complete.\030How goes the dragon hunt?\030Dragonkin Menace\0312,1,50,2,257,1,9562\0302,55,78,2,257,1,9562\0302,80,246,2,257,1,9562\0302,251,267,2,257,1,9562\0302,269,290,2,261,1,9562\0302,292,343,2,257,1,9562\0302,345,384,2,259,1,9562\0302,386,426,2,257,1,9562\0302,428,475,2,257,4,9562\0303,1,82,2,384,1,9562\0303,84,138,2,384,1,9562\0301,1,19,4,272,1,9562\0301,21,116,4,304,1,9562\0304,1,25,3,256,2,9562\0317040,2,10,Black Dragonspawn\0307041,2,10,Black Wyrmkin\0307044,2,10,Black Drake\0309562,2,11,Helendis Riverhorn\0312,46,1428,0,\0302,0,0,1,Burning Steppes\0302,0,0,11,Helendis Riverhorn\0314183,23,4183,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,7047,OBJECTIVE,15,13,Black Broodling\030NPC,7040,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Black Dragonspawn\030NPC,7044,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Black Drake\030NPC,7041,OBJECTIVE,4,13,Black Wyrmkin",[4183]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Magistrate Solomon opens the sealed letter from Helendis and begins reading.>\030We had always assumed that the Blackrock orcs were a product of their savage upbringing. What we have found here, in their homeland, tells us another story.$B$BIndeed, it is bloodlust and thirst for conflict that empowers them, but the black dragonflight are the beings whom control the orcs of Blackrock. We suspect that it is the black dragonflight that fuels them with rage and hostility.$B$BTake this letter to Magistrate Solomon. He will know what must be done.$B$B<Helendis hands you a sealed letter.>\030Travel to Lakeshire and deliver Helendis Riverhorn's Letter to Magistrate Solomon.\030Greetings, $N. Have we met before? You look vaguely familiar.\030The True Masters\0312,1,88,2,257,1,9562\0302,90,156,2,257,1,9562\0302,161,305,2,257,1,9562\0302,307,391,2,257,4,9562\0302,396,434,2,257,1,9562\0302,436,466,2,257,3,9562\0302,471,507,2,257,1,9562\0303,1,82,2,384,1,9562\0301,1,78,4,272,1,344\0304,1,14,3,256,1,344\0304,16,34,3,256,2,344\0304,36,61,3,256,1,344\031344,2,5,Magistrate Solomon\030798,2,5,Solomon\0309562,2,8,Helendis Riverhorn\030344,2,8,Magistrate Solomon\030798,2,8,Solomon\030344,4,9,Magistrate Solomon\030798,4,9,Solomon\0312,46,1428,0,\0302,0,0,5,Magistrate Solomon\0302,0,0,8,Lakeshire\0302,0,0,8,Magistrate Solomon\0304,0,0,9,Helendis\0314182,19,4182,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304184,23,4184,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4184]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Dragons? Impossible!\030This is grim news, $N. To discover that our mortal enemies are merely pawns of a much greater threat is disheartening. There is no possible way that Lakeshire could survive an attack from both the Blackrock orcs and the black dragonflight. Should Lakeshire fall to this menace, Darkshire would fall next, and then what? Goldshire? Stormwind itself?$B$BYou must take this information to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon in Stormwind at once! If this does not merit the aid of Stormwind, nothing will and all is lost.$B\030Travel to Stormwind and deliver Solomon's Plea to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon.$B$BBolvar resides in Stormwind Keep.\030What brings you to Stormwind Keep?\030The True Masters\0312,1,22,2,257,1,344\0302,24,118,2,261,1,344\0302,120,239,2,269,4,344\0302,241,319,2,257,4,344\0302,321,330,2,257,2,344\0302,332,348,2,257,2,344\0302,353,433,2,257,1,344\0302,435,508,2,261,4,344\0303,1,76,2,384,1,344\0303,81,113,2,384,1,344\0301,1,8,4,272,2,1748\0301,10,20,4,272,1,1748\0304,1,34,3,256,2,1748\0311748,2,7,Highlord Bolvar Fordragon\0301748,2,9,Highlord Bolvar Fordragon\0312,46,1428,0,\0302,0,0,7,Highlord Bolvar Fordragon\0302,0,0,7,Stormwind\0302,0,0,9,Stormwind\0302,0,0,9,Highlord Bolvar Fordragon\0302,0,0,10,Stormwind Keep\0303,0,0,13,Stormwind Keep\0314183,19,4183,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304185,23,4185,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4185]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031<Bolvar cups his chin as if in deep thought.>$B$BWhile I respect Lady Prestor's stance, I believe that there is a solution to this dilemma that may put all of our concerns to rest.\030Solomon paints a dreary picture. Still, we cannot afford to send our thinly spread troops to the aid of Lakeshire on speculation. I will need proof of these claims before I can act.$B$BSpeak with Lady Prestor, $N. She is a learned woman and knows much of dragons and dragonkin. She may be able to shed some light on this situation.$B\030Speak with Highlord Bolvar Fordragon after speaking with Lady Katrana Prestor.\030Advice from Lady Prestor\030<Bolvar watches you intently.>\030The True Masters\0312,1,32,2,257,1,1748\0302,34,129,2,257,1,1748\0302,131,181,2,259,3,1748\0302,186,213,2,257,1,1748\0302,215,277,2,257,1,1748\0302,279,331,2,257,1,1748\0303,1,78,2,384,1,1748\0301,1,45,4,272,4,1748\0301,50,180,4,272,4,1748\0305,1,30,3,256,1,1748\0304,1,24,3,384,1,1748\031798,2,1,Solomon\03015065,2,4,Lady\0301748,2,7,Highlord Bolvar Fordragon\0301749,2,7,Lady Katrana Prestor\03015065,4,9,Lady\03015065,3,11,Lady\0312,46,1428,0,\0303,0,0,11,Lady Prestor\0314184,19,4184,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304186,23,4186,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4186]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It could have been worse, I suppose...$B$B<Magistrate Solomon looks you over.>$B$BIt appears as if the fate of Lakeshire rests squarely on your shoulders.$B$B<You notice Magistrate Solomon blinking rapidly. He appears to be crying.>\030I am going to empower you as an acting deputy of Stormwind, $N.$B$BReturn to Magistrate Solomon in Lakeshire and deliver this decree.\030Take Bolvar's Decree to Magistrate Solomon in Lakeshire.$B\030Any news from Bolvar?\030The True Masters\0312,1,63,2,257,3,1748\0302,68,133,2,257,1,1748\0303,1,56,2,384,1,1748\0301,1,38,4,272,4,344\0301,43,78,4,272,1,344\0301,83,154,4,272,4,344\0301,159,206,4,272,1,344\0301,208,232,4,272,1,344\0304,1,21,3,256,2,344\031344,2,2,Magistrate Solomon\030798,2,2,Solomon\030344,2,3,Magistrate Solomon\030798,2,3,Solomon\030344,4,5,Magistrate Solomon\030798,4,5,Solomon\030344,4,7,Magistrate Solomon\030798,4,7,Solomon\0312,46,1428,0,\0302,0,0,2,Magistrate Solomon\0302,0,0,2,Lakeshire\0302,0,0,3,Magistrate Solomon\0302,0,0,3,Lakeshire\0303,0,0,9,Bolvar\0314185,19,4185,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304223,23,4223,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[419]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Here is the corpse of a dwarf -- mauled, frozen, and picked clean by mountain scavengers. Clutched in its hand is a book containing the roughly scribbled notes of Mori Hildelve. And around its frame, still in superior condition, is a Brigadier's Vest.$B$BThis grisly scene must have been where the Siege Engine pilot met his end.\030My friend and fellow Siege Engine pilot, Mori Hildelve, is lost in the hills.  We were looking for a rare ore that's needed for a high-grade blastpowder, and during our search he drove his engine up a steep hill and busted it!$B$BStill convinced that ore was in these mountains, Hildelve charged me to guard our engines while he continued on foot, searching.$B$BIt's been days, and I've heard some beastly growls in the hills at night.  Mori's tough as nails, but I'm worried.$B$BPlease, $N.  Find him.\030Find Pilot Hildelve.\030\030The Lost Pilot\0312,1,77,2,261,1,1960\0302,80,226,2,257,1,1960\0302,231,358,2,257,1,1960\0302,363,435,2,257,1,1960\0302,438,476,2,257,1,1960\0302,481,491,2,257,1,1960\0302,494,502,2,257,1,1960\0303,1,20,2,384,1,1960\0301,1,89,4,272,1,0\0301,91,177,4,272,1,0\0301,179,251,4,272,1,0\0301,256,329,4,272,1,0\031\0312,1,1426,0,\031417,23,417,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,2059,FINISHER,?,12,A Dwarven Corpse",[420]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031What's this? Ah, my brother's report. Hmm...$B$BI told him to be sparing with the use of the King's name, but he didn't listen. No harm, I suppose, though it's sure to ruffle some feathers in the Senate. Not that those weren't some feathers that needed ruffling! Hah!$B$BNonetheless, I guess that means that I should send my report on to Ironforge as well, but I must admit I'm a bit behind. Bloody cold.$B$BI should have some work for you later, if you're interested.\030The troggs in the tunnel are extremely hostile, and haven't shown any hesitation in attacking travelers through the tunnel. You seem tough enough, though, so you should probably be safe.$B$BDirections? If you're going to speak with Senir, you'll find him in Kharanos.$B$BMake your way through the tunnel, and after you come out on the other side, just keep following the road, it'll run right into Kharanos.\030Deliver Grelin's report to Senir Whitebeard in Kharanos.\030How are you? Like to share a drink with me, perhaps? Not much else to do in the cold.\030Senir's Observations\0312,1,123,2,261,1,1965\0302,125,186,2,257,4,1965\0302,191,201,2,257,2,1965\0302,203,267,2,257,4,1965\0302,272,407,2,257,1,1965\0303,1,56,2,384,1,1965\0301,1,12,4,272,2,1252\0301,14,37,4,272,1,1252\0301,39,44,4,272,1,1252\0301,49,127,4,272,1,1252\0301,129,203,4,272,1,1252\0301,205,262,4,272,1,1252\0301,264,267,4,272,1,1252\0301,272,391,4,272,1,1252\0301,393,404,4,272,1,1252\0301,409,468,4,272,4,1252\0304,1,12,3,256,2,1252\0304,14,52,3,256,4,1252\0304,54,85,3,256,1,1252\0311252,2,6,Senir Whitebeard\0312,132,1426,0,\0302,0,0,4,Kharanos\0302,0,0,6,Senir Whitebeard\0302,0,0,6,Kharanos\0304,0,0,11,Senate\0304,0,0,14,Ironforge\031282,19,282,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030287,23,287,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4201]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh, you've done it!  I can now make my potion and use it on Rocknot.  Finally, he will fall victim to my charms!$B$BThank you, $N.  You are a champion of love!\030Oh, the pains of love!  My dear Private Rocknot is immune to my charms.  I am spurned!  It's maddening!$B$BYou must help me!  We succubi know much of love, and I can make a potion to beat down the iron walls around Rocknot's heart.  To make it, I need these items: the herb gromsblood, giant silver veins from the cliff giants of Azshara, and water from the Golakka Springs Crater in Un'Goro.  You can place the water in this vial.$B$BPlease, $N, help a poor soul in her quest for happiness!\030Bring 4 Gromsblood, 10 Giant Silver Veins and Nagmara's Filled Vial to Mistress Nagmara in Blackrock Depths.\030Do you have the ingredients?  The hole in my heart threatens to consume me!\030The Love Potion\0312,1,22,2,257,1,9500\0302,25,71,2,257,1,9500\0302,74,86,2,257,1,9500\0302,89,103,2,257,1,9500\0302,108,124,2,257,1,9500\0302,127,231,2,257,1,9500\0302,234,392,2,259,1,9500\0302,395,431,2,257,1,9500\0302,436,491,2,257,1,9500\0303,1,108,2,384,1,9500\0301,1,19,4,272,1,9500\0301,22,68,4,272,1,9500\0301,71,112,4,280,3,9500\0301,117,130,4,272,1,9500\0301,133,159,4,272,1,9500\0304,1,28,3,256,2,9500\0304,31,75,3,260,1,9500\0319503,2,2,Private Rocknot\0309500,2,10,Mistress Nagmara\0312,1584,0,0,\0302,0,0,7,Golakka Springs Crater\0302,0,0,7,Un'Goro\0302,0,0,10,Mistress Nagmara\0302,0,0,10,Blackrock Depths\031\031ITEM,8846,OBJECTIVE,4,15,\030ITEM,11405,OBJECTIVE,10,15,\030ITEM,11413,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[421]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have served me well, $C. It is obvious to me that you will be a worthy aide to me as I prepare to rid Silverpine Forest of Arugal's curse.\030Lady Sylvanas has charged Varimathras with the conquering of the human and dwarven lands to the south.$B$BBut that fool, Arugal -- charlatan of Dalaran and now cursed beast of Shadowfang Keep -- let his reckless magic wreak havoc with the strategic stronghold of Silverpine Forest.$B$BI need someone skilled in the ways of combat to help clean up Arugal's mess.  Prove yourself to me by killing 5 Moonrage Whitescalps.  The wretched beasts can often be found just off the road, down the hill below.\030Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher wants you to kill 5 Moonrage Whitescalps.\030If you wish to prove yourself to me, you must kill 5 Moonrage Whitescalps.  Accomplish that task, and I will see to it your skill is put to more worthy assignments.\030Prove Your Worth\0312,1,102,2,257,1,1938\0302,107,281,2,261,1,1938\0302,286,361,2,259,1,1938\0302,364,418,2,257,1,1938\0302,421,498,2,257,1,1938\0303,1,75,2,386,1,1938\0301,1,28,4,272,1,1938\0301,30,142,4,276,3,1938\0304,1,74,3,258,4,1938\0304,77,164,3,256,3,1938\03115065,2,1,Lady\0302425,2,1,Varimathras\03010000,2,2,Arugal\0301938,2,6,Dalar Dawnweaver\0312,130,1421,0,\0302,0,0,6,Sepulcher\031422,23,422,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,1769,OBJECTIVE,5,13,Moonrage Whitescalp",[422]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is precisely the spell I was in search of, $C. If your dedication to The Dark Lady's cause remains infallible you will find you have quite a future amongst The Forsaken.\030How Arugal gained acceptance within the Kirin Tor is beyond me.  His spell-casting knowledge seemed as transparent as a blown glass bauble.$B$BWhat's important now is learning exactly what magic Arugal used so that I can turn it against him and secure Silverpine Forest for the Dark Lady.$B$BArugal first stayed at the wheat farm just north of the bridge.  One of the Deathstalkers reported seeing some spellbooks but could not secure them.  Retrieve for me the spell labeled Remedy of Arugal from those books.\030Retrieve the Remedy of Arugal for Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher.\030Before I know what we are dealing with here, $C, I need to study the spell known as Remedy of Arugal. Bring it to me now or I shall be forced to find myself a worthy servant.\030Arugal's Folly\0312,1,63,2,257,1,1938\0302,66,139,2,257,1,1938\0302,144,288,2,259,1,1938\0302,293,355,2,257,1,1938\0302,358,440,2,257,4,1938\0302,443,510,2,257,1,1938\0303,1,68,2,384,1,1938\0301,1,51,4,272,1,1938\0301,53,174,4,272,4,1938\0304,1,101,3,258,1,1938\0304,103,174,3,256,3,1938\03110000,2,1,Arugal\03010000,2,3,Arugal\03015065,2,3,Lady\03010000,2,4,Arugal\03010000,2,6,Arugal\03010000,2,7,Arugal\0301938,2,7,Dalar Dawnweaver\03010000,3,10,Arugal\0312,130,1421,0,\0302,0,0,1,Kirin Tor\0302,0,0,7,Sepulcher\0304,0,0,9,The Dark Lady's\031421,19,421,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030423,23,423,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3155,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[4221]="PARTIAL\031characters,consequences,loreConnections,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You apply two Cenarion plant salves to the windblossom. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.\030\030\030You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a windblossom plant. The berries that hang from the plant appear rotten and poisonous. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.\030Corrupted Windblossom\0311,1,55,4,272,1,0\0301,57,150,4,276,1,0\0304,1,85,3,260,1,0\0304,87,151,3,256,1,0\0304,153,233,3,258,4,0\031\0312,361,1448,0,\031\031OBJECT,174604,GIVER,?,9,Corrupted Windblossom\030OBJECT,174604,FINISHER,?,12,Corrupted Windblossom\030ITEM,11516,OBJECTIVE,2,15,",[4222]="PARTIAL\031characters,consequences,loreConnections,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You apply two Cenarion plant salves to the windblossom. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.\030\030\030You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a windblossom plant. The berries that hang from the plant appear rotten and poisonous. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.\030Corrupted Windblossom\0311,1,55,4,272,1,0\0301,57,150,4,276,1,0\0304,1,85,3,260,1,0\0304,87,151,3,256,1,0\0304,153,233,3,258,4,0\031\0312,361,1448,0,\031\031OBJECT,174603,GIVER,?,9,Corrupted Windblossom\030OBJECT,174603,FINISHER,?,12,Corrupted Windblossom\030ITEM,11516,OBJECTIVE,2,15,",[4223]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Marshal Maxwell laughs.>\030<Magistrate Solomon sighs.>$B$BYou must return to the Burning Steppes, $N. As a deputy of Stormwind, you will be required to report to Marshal Maxwell. Good luck.\030Speak with Marshal Maxwell in the Burning Steppes.\030\030The True Masters\0312,1,27,2,257,1,344\0302,32,74,2,257,1,344\0302,76,151,2,257,3,344\0302,153,162,2,257,1,344\0303,1,50,2,384,1,344\0301,1,25,4,272,1,9560\031344,2,1,Magistrate Solomon\030798,2,1,Solomon\0309560,2,3,Marshal Maxwell\0309560,2,5,Marshal Maxwell\0309560,4,6,Marshal Maxwell\0312,46,1428,0,\0302,0,0,2,Burning Steppes\0302,0,0,3,Marshal Maxwell\0302,0,0,5,Burning Steppes\0314186,19,4186,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304224,23,4224,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4224]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031I could have warned you, but what fun is that?\030What? You thought you were the first? How many soldiers must we lose before Stormwind acts?$B$BWe had accumulated enormous amounts of intelligence pertaining to the Blackrock menace before we lost our commanding officer, Marshal Windsor. With Marshal Windsor went all of our precious information.$B$BWhat we need is that documentation. Speak with Ragged John, $N. He was with Windsor when they were attacked by a Blackrock raiding party.  He was last seen in a cave to the north.\030Speak with Ragged John to learn of Marshal Windsor's fate and return to Marshal Maxwell when you have completed this task.$B$BYou recall Marshal Maxwell telling you to search for him in a cave to the north.\030Ragged John's Story\030Have you spoken with John yet?\030The True Masters\0312,1,5,2,257,2,9560\0302,7,37,2,257,2,9560\0302,39,91,2,257,2,9560\0302,96,237,2,269,1,9560\0302,239,296,2,257,1,9560\0302,301,335,2,259,1,9560\0302,337,363,2,257,1,9560\0302,365,437,2,261,1,9560\0302,440,479,2,257,1,9560\0303,1,122,2,384,1,9560\0303,127,206,2,384,1,9560\0301,1,46,4,272,4,9560\0305,1,30,3,256,2,9560\0304,1,19,3,384,1,9560\0319023,2,4,Marshal Windsor\0309023,2,5,Marshal Windsor\03014528,2,5,Precious\0309563,2,7,Ragged John\030806,2,7,John\0309563,2,10,Ragged John\030806,2,10,John\0309023,2,10,Marshal Windsor\0309560,2,10,Marshal Maxwell\0309560,2,11,Marshal Maxwell\030806,3,13,John\0309563,3,14,Ragged John\0312,46,1428,0,\0302,0,0,4,Blackrock\0302,0,0,10,Marshal Maxwell\0314223,19,4223,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304241,23,4241,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[423]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I hope I can acquire enough energy from such a limited sample. Perhaps I should have had you get more shackles.$B$BNonetheless, you showed great skill in collecting these, $C.\030After examining Arugal's work my worst suspicions were confirmed.  The old hack was not qualified to clean chamber pots in Dalaran let alone represent the Kirin Tor in its most dire hour.  Fools!$B$BArugal used enchanted items to reinforce his weak magic.  I need to examine these items first hand.  Travel forth and slay Moonrage Gluttons and Moonrage Darksouls until you have collected enough of their enchanted shackles for my research.  The foul creatures have been seen to the north and east.\030Bring 6 Glutton Shackles and 3 Darksoul Shackles to Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher.\030I will need 6 Glutton Shackles and 3 Darksoul Shackles before I can assess the situation and devise a final solution for Arugal. Now heed your bidding and slay Moonrage Gluttons and Moonrage Darksouls until you have what I need.\030Arugal's Folly\0312,1,65,2,257,1,1938\0302,68,187,2,257,1,1938\0302,190,195,2,257,1,1938\0302,200,255,2,257,1,1938\0302,258,298,2,259,1,1938\0302,301,439,2,257,1,1938\0302,442,497,2,257,1,1938\0303,1,86,2,384,1,1938\0301,1,62,4,274,3,1938\0301,64,111,4,272,4,1938\0301,116,175,4,272,1,1938\0304,1,128,3,258,3,1938\0304,130,228,3,258,1,1938\03110000,2,4,Arugal\0308567,2,8,Glutton\0301938,2,8,Dalar Dawnweaver\0308567,3,12,Glutton\03010000,3,12,Arugal\0312,130,1421,0,\0302,0,0,2,Dalaran\0302,0,0,8,Dalar Dawnweaver\0302,0,0,8,Sepulcher\031422,19,422,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030424,23,424,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3156,OBJECTIVE,6,15,\030ITEM,3157,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[424]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Most excellent. The mine will provide superb resources for our forces as we spread throughout Silverpine and into Azeroth.\030It will indeed take me longer than I had thought to uncover the dark secrets behind the enchantments Arugal was using.$B$BBut in the meantime I need you to take care of a slight problem our Darkstalkers have discovered.  It seems that Arugal let his magic spread to the Deep Elem Mine in the hills to the southeast.$B$BThe mine would prove to be quite a resource for Varimathras's advance.$B$BI want you to behead the tainted foreman of the mine, Grimson the Pale.  With his death, the mine shall be ours.\030Kill Grimson the Pale and bring his head to Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher.\030Has Grimson the Pale been slain? Varimathras will not be pleased if we ignore his bidding.\030Arugal's Folly\0312,1,118,2,257,3,1938\0302,123,219,2,263,1,1938\0302,222,315,2,257,4,1938\0302,320,389,2,257,4,1938\0302,394,464,2,259,1,1938\0302,467,505,2,257,3,1938\0303,1,78,2,384,1,1938\0301,1,15,4,272,1,1938\0301,17,122,4,272,3,1938\0304,1,32,3,260,2,1938\0304,34,90,3,256,4,1938\03110000,2,1,Arugal\03010000,2,3,Arugal\0301972,2,5,Grimson the Pale\0301972,2,7,Grimson the Pale\0301938,2,7,Dalar Dawnweaver\0301972,3,10,Grimson the Pale\0302425,3,11,Varimathras\0312,130,1421,0,\0302,0,0,3,Deep Elem Mine\0302,0,0,7,Dalar Dawnweaver\0302,0,0,7,Sepulcher\031423,19,423,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\03099,23,99,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3634,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[4241]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Where is he! I'll murder him!\030So that good for nothing coward says that Windsor is alive, eh?$B$BSuit up, deputy, you are going in to find him. If Windsor is alive, you are to bring him back. If he's dead, I want proof.$B$B<Maxwell laughs.>$B$BI bet you are getting tired of hearing that, aren't you?\030Travel to Blackrock Mountain in the northwest and enter Blackrock Depths. Find out what became of Marshal Windsor.$B$BYou recall Ragged John talking about Windsor being dragged off to a prison.\030\030Marshal Windsor\0312,1,63,2,259,2,9560\0302,68,113,2,257,1,9560\0302,115,161,2,257,4,9560\0302,163,189,2,259,4,9560\0302,194,210,2,257,1,9560\0302,215,270,2,257,2,9560\0303,1,73,2,384,1,9560\0303,75,114,2,384,1,9560\0303,119,193,2,384,1,9560\0301,1,12,4,272,1,9023\0301,14,29,4,276,1,9023\0319023,2,8,Marshal Windsor\0309563,2,9,Ragged John\030806,2,9,John\0312,1584,0,0,\0302,0,0,7,Blackrock Mountain\0314224,19,4224,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304242,23,4242,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4242]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031He's gone mad, apparently.$B$B<Maxwell lowers his head in mourning.>$B$BIt is unfortunate that a once proud and noble warrior would be turned into a blithering head case. I GUESS we've reached a dead end...$B$BI must reward you for your efforts thus far, $N.\030Bolvar is a fool. I was gathering his precious 'proof' so that I could shove it down his throat.$B$BHe is a blind buffoon. Proof stands two feet away from him and he does not see.$B$BAs for my data, it's lost. Gone. Unrecoverable.$B$BShould I ever find Ironfoe and make it out of this labyrinth, my first stop will be Stormwind, to place my hammer in between that reptile's eyes.$B$BLeave me, $N.\030Give Marshal Maxwell the bad news.\030\030Abandoned Hope\0312,1,17,2,257,1,9023\0302,19,96,2,259,4,9023\0302,101,122,2,257,1,9023\0302,124,179,2,257,1,9023\0302,184,209,2,261,1,9023\0302,211,215,2,257,1,9023\0302,217,230,2,257,1,9023\0302,235,379,2,257,3,9023\0302,384,396,2,257,1,9023\0303,1,34,2,384,1,9023\0301,1,26,4,272,4,9560\0301,31,68,4,272,1,9560\0301,73,170,4,272,4,9560\0301,172,206,4,272,1,9560\0301,211,258,4,272,1,9560\03114528,2,2,Precious\0309560,2,10,Marshal Maxwell\0312,1584,0,0,\0314241,19,4241,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304264,23,4264,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4243]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031As you look A-Me 01 over, you see two huge dents tarnishing what Karna obviously feels is a well-crafted piece of engineering. One dent decorates A-Me 01's shoulder, the other is on her head.$B$BNo power seems to be running through her components as you investigate further.\030Unfortunately, something's happened to one of my greatest inventions. You've seen mechanical squirrels, yes? Well, to get closer to the apes of Un'Goro Crater, I created a mechanical ape to blend in with their kind--I call her A-Me 01.$B$BShe has scrying gems for eyes so I could see everything she saw. She made it to Fungal Rock--the apes' lair--just east of here, and that's when I lost contact. The last thing I saw was one of their alpha males rushing up to say hello to her!$B$BCan you help me find her?\030Find A-Me 01 in Un'Goro Crater.\030\030Chasing A-Me 01\0312,1,69,2,257,1,9618\0302,71,108,2,257,2,9618\0302,110,235,2,257,1,9618\0302,240,303,2,257,4,9618\0302,305,398,2,261,1,9618\0302,400,480,2,257,1,9618\0302,485,509,2,257,2,9618\0303,1,31,2,384,1,9618\0301,1,126,4,272,1,9623\0301,128,191,4,272,1,9623\0301,196,274,4,272,4,9623\0319623,2,3,A-Me 01\0309623,2,8,A-Me 01\0309623,4,9,A-Me 01\0309623,4,10,A-Me 01\0312,490,1449,0,\0302,0,0,5,Fungal Rock--the\0302,0,0,8,Un'Goro Crater\0314244,23,4244,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4244]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You remove the panel from A-Me 01's back yet again and carefully remove the old mithril casing that seems to have burnt out. The new one slides into place easily. The only thing left to do, assuming the mithril casing was the problem, is to flip the switch to the \"Off\" position, and then back to the \"On\" position.\030A little further investigation shows a panel that slides open. Clearly written above some wiring is the statement, \"Replace Mithril Casing And Turn Power Off Then On.\"$B$BTaking a moment to replace the panel, you wonder if it'll be that simple to fix A-Me 01 and get her back to Karna Remtravel near Marshall's Refuge.$B$BOnly trying it will tell.\030Find a Mithril Casing and return to A-Me 01 in Un'Goro Crater.\030The panel in which the mithril casing goes is still closed shut. The rest of A-Me 01 remains inert.\030Chasing A-Me 01\0312,1,62,2,257,1,9623\0302,64,167,2,257,1,9623\0302,172,318,2,257,4,9623\0302,323,347,2,257,3,9623\0303,1,62,2,384,1,9623\0301,1,124,4,272,4,9623\0301,126,162,4,272,1,9623\0301,164,315,4,276,1,9623\0304,1,64,3,256,1,9623\0304,66,99,3,256,1,9623\0319623,2,3,A-Me 01\0309618,2,3,Karna Remtravel\0309623,2,5,A-Me 01\0309623,4,6,A-Me 01\0309623,3,10,A-Me 01\0312,490,1449,0,\0302,0,0,3,Karna Remtravel\0302,0,0,3,Marshall's Refuge\0302,0,0,5,A-Me\0302,0,0,5,Un'Goro Crater\0304,0,0,6,A-Me\0314243,19,4243,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304245,23,4245,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,10561,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[4245]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Oh, you've done it! Wonderful! Thank you, $N.$B$BOh, my poor, A-Me. Look at all those dents. We'll get her up and running perfectly with just a little work.$B$BThank you again, $N. I really appreciate it.\030Checking to see if you're prepared to lead A-Me 01 back to Karna Remtravel, you flip the switch to the \"Off\" position. Glancing around once again to make sure none of the gorillas are coming, you prepare to see what happens when you flip the switch back to the \"On\" position.$B$BThis is your last chance... are you sure this is what you want to do?\030Escort A-Me 01 back to Karna Remtravel in Un'Goro Crater.\030Protect A-Me 01 until you reach Karna Remtravel\030Have you been able to help A-Me? That mithril casing you mentioned being destroyed was a good guess at what was wrong. I'm sure if you replace that, she'll reactivate and be able to come home.\030Chasing A-Me 01\0312,1,118,2,257,4,9623\0302,120,275,2,257,1,9623\0302,280,306,2,257,1,9623\0302,308,348,2,259,2,9623\0303,1,57,2,384,1,9623\0301,1,19,4,272,1,9618\0301,21,30,4,272,1,9618\0301,32,45,4,272,1,9618\0301,50,67,4,272,1,9618\0301,69,92,4,272,1,9618\0301,94,156,4,272,1,9618\0301,161,180,4,272,1,9618\0301,182,204,4,272,1,9618\0305,1,32,3,256,2,9618\0305,34,118,3,260,1,9618\0305,120,192,3,256,4,9618\0304,1,47,3,396,1,9623\0319623,2,1,A-Me 01\0309618,2,1,Karna Remtravel\0309623,2,5,A-Me 01\0309618,2,5,Karna Remtravel\0309623,3,17,A-Me 01\0309618,3,17,Karna Remtravel\0312,490,1449,0,\0302,0,0,1,Karna Remtravel\0302,0,0,5,Karna Remtravel\0302,0,0,5,Un'Goro Crater\0314244,19,4244,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[425]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, thank you. You have my gratitude, $N.$B$BAnd I will include you in the report I make to my superiors.\030My brother Quinn and I were tasked to recon Silverpine Forest and report to High Executor Hadrec.  But we didn't get far -- when moving through this farm we were attacked by the ghoul Ivar the Foul.$B$BWe escaped from Ivar, but he seriously mauled Quinn.  He's healing from the potion you gave him, but Ivar may return before Quinn recovers.$B$BKill Ivar so Quinn will have time to heal.  Ivar is usually in the barn yonder, waiting for my guard to drop.\030Kill Ivar the Foul, and bring Ivar's Head to Rane Yorick at the Ivar Patch.\030Have you killed Ivar the Foul? If you won't do it for me and my brother, then do it for the Forsaken.\030Ivar the Foul\0312,1,97,2,257,1,1950\0302,100,198,2,261,1,1950\0302,203,254,2,257,1,1950\0302,257,341,2,257,1,1950\0302,346,387,2,257,3,1950\0302,390,454,2,257,1,1950\0303,1,75,2,384,1,1950\0301,1,14,4,272,1,1950\0301,16,41,4,272,1,1950\0301,46,105,4,272,3,1950\0304,1,30,3,256,2,1950\0304,32,101,3,256,4,1950\03111756,2,1,Quinn\0301952,2,1,High Executor Hadrec\030846,2,2,Ghoul\0301971,2,2,Ivar the Foul\03011756,2,3,Quinn\03011756,2,4,Quinn\03011756,2,5,Quinn\0301971,2,7,Ivar the Foul\0301950,2,7,Rane Yorick\0301971,3,11,Ivar the Foul\0312,130,1421,0,\0302,0,0,1,High Executor Hadrec\0302,0,0,3,Ivar\0302,0,0,7,Rane Yorick\0302,0,0,7,Ivar Patch\031430,19,430,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3621,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[426]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Your efforts in the war are felt among us, $N. I will not thank you for doing what is necessary, but the Deathguards of Tirisfal will remember your name.\030The Scourge are trying to form a base at the Agamand Mills.  If they do, then they can stage further attacks within Tirisfal.$B$BThe orders have been given.  The Scourge in the Mills must be destroyed.$B$BGo to the Mills.  Collect Notched Ribs from Rattlecage and Cracked Skull Soldiers, and Blackened Skulls from Darkeye Bonecasters.$B$BTo get to the Mills, follow the road west.  After crossing the bridge, take the next fork north then keep going north.  When you see windmills, the battle will begin.\030Gather 5 Notched Ribs and 3 Blackened Skulls, then return to Deathguard Dillinger in Brill.\030Our battles with the Scourge wage on, $N. Do your part and throw those cursed, mindless undead back into the Plaguelands!\030The Mills Overrun\0312,1,59,2,321,1,1496\0302,62,125,2,261,4,1496\0302,130,156,2,257,1,1496\0302,159,201,2,325,1,1496\0302,206,221,2,257,1,1496\0302,224,334,2,257,1,1496\0302,339,380,2,257,1,1496\0302,383,456,2,257,1,1496\0302,459,504,2,261,3,1496\0303,1,91,2,384,1,1496\0301,1,46,4,276,1,1496\0301,48,153,4,272,3,1496\0304,1,41,3,320,1,1496\0304,43,121,3,260,1,1496\0311496,2,10,Deathguard Dillinger\03011030,3,14,Mindless Undead\0312,85,1420,0,\0302,0,0,1,Agamand Mills\0302,0,0,2,Tirisfal\0302,0,0,4,Mills\0302,0,0,5,Mills\0302,0,0,6,Rattlecage\0302,0,0,6,Darkeye Bonecasters\0302,0,0,7,Mills\0302,0,0,10,Deathguard Dillinger\0302,0,0,10,Brill\031404,19,404,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3162,OBJECTIVE,5,15,\030ITEM,3163,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[4261]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Yes, $N. Felwood has been through much hardship. Thank you for what you have done.$B$BOne day, we may be able to reclaim Felwood from the corruption; every kind deed helps.\030Felwood was once a peaceful and serene land... Until the legion took hold. The infernals, destruction, chaos...$B$BThe skull of Gul'dan ensured that none were spared here. All fell to the corruption.$B$BEven now, as a spirit, I still find myself trapped, bearing the suffering of this land. Help me find my way home. Please, $N, tell me you will lead an ancient spirit away from here, where I may finally rest.$B$BOnce I am free, seek out Kayneth Stillwind, a druid that resides in Forest Song, to the east.\030Escort Arei to safety, then speak with Kayneth Stillwind in Forest Song, in eastern Ashenvale.\030Help Arei get to Safety\030\030Ancient Spirit\0312,1,46,2,257,1,9598\0302,48,74,2,257,1,9598\0302,76,111,2,257,1,9598\0302,116,171,2,257,1,9598\0302,173,199,2,261,1,9598\0302,204,290,2,261,1,9598\0302,292,316,2,257,1,9598\0302,318,410,2,321,3,9598\0302,415,507,2,257,1,9598\0303,1,94,2,392,1,9598\0301,1,8,4,272,1,3848\0301,10,48,4,272,1,3848\0301,50,82,4,272,1,3848\0301,87,172,4,276,1,3848\0304,1,23,3,392,1,9598\0313848,2,9,Kayneth Stillwind\0309598,2,10,Arei\0303848,2,10,Kayneth Stillwind\0309598,3,15,Arei\0312,361,1448,0,\0302,0,0,9,Forest Song\0302,0,0,10,Forest Song\0303,0,0,15,Safety\0314442,19,4442,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4262]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Incendius? Oh dear...\030The last five of my mages that went snooping around in Blackrock Mountain came back extra crispy with a permanent orange gnomefro - or worse.$B$B<Jalinda picks up some ashes from the ground and releases them into the air.>$B$BOne nasty bugger in particular, Overmaster Pyron, seems to be causing quite a bit of trouble. We need that elemental terminated so that our expedition crew can make its way into Blackrock Depths!$B$BHe guards the entrance at the Blackrock Quarry.\030Slay Overmaster Pyron and return to Jalinda Sprig.$B$BYou recall Jalinda talking about Pyron guarding the quarry. Perhaps you should search there?\030<Jalinda appears to be staring at your head.>\030Overmaster Pyron\0312,1,141,2,257,1,9561\0302,146,222,2,257,1,9561\0302,227,319,2,257,4,9561\0302,321,421,2,259,1,9561\0302,426,472,2,257,1,9561\0303,1,50,2,384,1,9561\0303,55,113,2,384,1,9561\0303,115,146,2,384,4,9561\0301,1,10,4,272,2,9561\0301,12,21,4,272,1,9561\0304,1,45,3,256,1,9561\0319026,2,3,Overmaster Pyron\0309026,2,6,Overmaster Pyron\0309561,2,6,Jalinda Sprig\0312,25,0,0,\0302,0,0,1,Blackrock Mountain\0302,0,0,5,Blackrock Quarry\0302,0,0,6,Jalinda Sprig\0314263,23,4263,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,9026,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Overmaster Pyron",[4263]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh dear! Are you sure Incendius said 'Ragnaros?'$B$B<Jalinda hands you something and pats you on the wrist as she fades deep into thought.>\030Are you sure Pyron said 'Incendius' when he died?$B$B<Jalinda swallows hard.>$B$BLord Incendius is purported to be a minion of Ragnaros! Oh dear, oh dear... whatever will we do?$B$BDo you think you can handle another mission? I don't have anybody else to send, $N!$B$BWe will never get a team in if Incendius continues to raise Pyron from the ashes.$B$BYou'll have to find and destroy Lord Incendius!$B\030Find Lord Incendius in Blackrock Depths and destroy him!\030Is the fiend dead??\030Incendius!\0312,1,49,2,257,2,9561\0302,54,77,2,257,1,9561\0302,82,136,2,257,1,9561\0302,138,156,2,257,1,9561\0302,158,177,2,257,2,9561\0302,182,225,2,257,2,9561\0302,227,264,2,257,1,9561\0302,269,349,2,257,4,9561\0302,354,400,2,261,1,9561\0303,1,56,2,388,1,9561\0301,1,8,4,272,1,9561\0301,10,48,4,272,2,9561\0301,53,139,4,272,1,9561\0304,1,19,3,256,2,9561\0319017,2,3,Lord Incendius\03011502,2,3,Ragnaros\0309017,2,9,Lord Incendius\0309017,2,10,Lord Incendius\0312,1584,0,0,\0302,0,0,10,Blackrock Depths\0314262,19,4262,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,9017,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Lord Incendius",[4264]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Marshal Windsor takes the note and begins reading.>\030The note has stains covering its surface. The text is barely legible, but you make out the following:$B$B...sweet irony...$B$B...the fall of the broken Alliance...$B$B...if it were not for General Angerforge's diligence, we may have never discovered the pattern to the encryption...$B$B...Argelmach is almost done with the decryption of Windsor's notes.$B$BOur lord will rise from the depths and crush any that remain...$B$B-Emperor Dagran Thaurissan.$B\030You may have just stumbled on to something that Marshal Windsor would be interested in seeing. There may be hope, after all.\030<Marshal Windsor eyes the note in your hand.>$B$BWhat do you have there, $N?\030A Crumpled Up Note\0312,1,41,2,257,1,0\0302,43,101,2,257,1,0\0302,106,122,2,257,1,0\0302,127,163,2,257,1,0\0302,168,282,2,257,4,0\0302,287,353,2,257,1,0\0302,358,420,2,257,3,0\0302,425,451,2,257,1,0\0303,1,94,2,384,4,0\0303,96,124,2,386,3,0\0301,1,52,4,272,1,9023\0304,1,45,3,256,1,9023\0304,50,76,3,256,2,9023\0319033,2,5,General Angerforge\0309023,2,9,Marshal Windsor\0309023,4,11,Marshal Windsor\0309023,3,12,Marshal Windsor\0312,1584,0,0,\0314242,19,4242,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304282,23,4282,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,11446,STARTER,?,10,",[4265]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Welcome home, $N.  Raschal checked in just a little while ago and told me what happened.$B$BI... no, the entire Stronghold can't even begin to thank you for your great deed; Raschal would have been dead without your timely aid, and your assistance came to us without even so much as the whisper of a mercenary's fee.  You bear the mark of a true hero.  Know that you will always have a friend in Ginro Hearthkindle.\030The pod splits opens some when you touch it, revealing a night elven male who is surprisingly still alive.  He seems to be in good health, though deeply stunned.  As you help him down from the pod, he stirs to life.$B$B\"Thank Elune - you've saved me, friend!  I... I'm Raschal, and I awoke paralyzed inside this pod after these bugs overwhelmed me.  Were you sent by the Stronghold?\"$B$BIt would seem that you've found the missing courier!\030Free Raschal from the Zukk'ash hive.$B$BReturn to Ginro Hearthkindle in Feathermoon Stronghold and let him know that Raschal is alive and well.\030Free Raschal.\030You have something to report, $n?\030Freed from the Hive\0312,1,106,2,257,1,0\0302,109,161,2,257,4,0\0302,164,215,2,257,1,0\0302,220,258,2,257,1,0\0302,266,348,2,257,1,0\0302,351,383,2,257,2,0\0302,388,439,2,261,4,0\0303,1,36,2,384,1,0\0303,41,143,2,384,1,0\0301,1,17,4,272,1,7880\0301,20,88,4,272,1,7880\0301,98,316,4,272,4,7880\0301,319,351,4,272,1,7880\0301,354,415,4,272,3,7880\0305,1,33,3,256,2,7880\0304,1,13,3,384,1,0\0317880,2,9,Ginro Hearthkindle\030795,4,13,Mark\0307880,4,14,Ginro Hearthkindle\0312,357,1444,0,\0302,0,0,8,Zukk'ash\0302,0,0,9,Ginro Hearthkindle\0302,0,0,9,Feathermoon Stronghold\0304,0,0,14,Ginro Hearthkindle\0314135,19,4135,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304266,23,4266,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,164954,GIVER,?,9,Zukk'ash Pod",[4266]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031$N, I give you my warmest thanks for the aid you've given us.  Your bravery in the face of overwhelming odds has warranted a reward worth a thousand times greater.  Nevertheless, I hope you accept this on behalf of the entire Stronghold.$B$BNow, if I may... I'd like to ask for your aid one more time.  In light of the discovery of the Zukk'ash hive here in Feralas, I think you're the best choice for this mission.\030$N, General Shandris Feathermoon would like to speak with you personally.  No doubt she wants to thank you for your service to the Stronghold, but I do know that she also wants to talk to you about the insect creatures that you and Raschal faced in southern Feralas.  The reports of those Zukk'ash insects are... frightening, to say the least.$B$BGeneral Feathermoon is waiting for you in the main compound.\030Speak with Shandris Feathermoon in Feathermoon Stronghold.\030\030A Hero's Welcome\0312,1,73,2,257,4,7880\0302,76,266,2,259,1,7880\0302,269,312,2,257,1,7880\0302,314,343,2,257,1,7880\0302,348,407,2,257,1,7880\0303,1,58,2,384,1,7880\0301,1,61,4,272,1,3936\0301,64,163,4,272,1,3936\0301,166,237,4,274,3,3936\0301,242,257,4,272,4,3936\0301,259,301,4,274,1,3936\0301,304,415,4,272,1,3936\0313936,2,1,Shandris Feathermoon\0303936,2,6,Shandris Feathermoon\0312,357,1444,0,\0302,0,0,2,Stronghold\0302,0,0,6,Feathermoon Stronghold\0304,0,0,12,Feralas\0314265,19,4265,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304267,23,4267,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4267]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031We night elves know of the terror outlined in this report.  Shandris was wise to send this, and you, to me.$B$BThese creatures will consume Feralas rapidly; they are nothing short of one of the greatest menaces we all will ever face.  The insects you and the courier encountered are known as the silithid.  They are mere tools of one of the greatest threats that both the Horde and Alliance will ever face.$B$BI pray we will have the resolve to defeat them before they destroy us.\030I am entrusting you with a copy of the report Raschal made on the infestation of southeastern Feralas.  While the main report is being filed in Darnassus, I want you to give this copy to an associate of the Protectorate.  Her name is Gracina Spiritmight; she is a priestess who dwells in the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.  She has broad knowledge on these kinds of creatures, and her receiving this report would benefit us all.$B$BYou're dismissed - good luck, $N; may Elune watch over us all.\030Bring Raschal's Report to Gracina Spiritmight in Darnassus.\030Welcome to this blessed temple, friend.  Your arrival here from Feathermoon Stronghold has been foretold to me.  Do you have the report Shandris Feathermoon asked you to bring?\030Rise of the Silithid\0312,1,102,2,257,1,3936\0302,105,220,2,259,1,3936\0302,223,324,2,257,1,3936\0302,327,430,2,257,4,3936\0302,435,496,2,257,1,3936\0303,1,59,2,384,1,3936\0301,1,58,4,272,1,7740\0301,61,107,4,272,1,7740\0301,112,233,4,272,3,7740\0301,236,305,4,272,1,7740\0301,308,406,4,272,3,7740\0301,411,480,4,284,3,7740\0304,1,39,3,256,1,7740\0304,42,111,3,256,1,7740\0304,114,176,3,256,2,7740\0317740,2,3,Gracina Spiritmight\030112,2,3,Priestess\0307740,2,6,Gracina Spiritmight\0303936,3,15,Shandris Feathermoon\0312,357,1444,0,\0302,0,0,2,Darnassus\0302,0,0,3,Temple of the Moon\0302,0,0,3,Darnassus\0302,0,0,6,Gracina Spiritmight\0302,0,0,6,Darnassus\0303,0,0,14,Feathermoon Stronghold\0314266,19,4266,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[427]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Most excellent, $C. Your skill in the art of combat is undeniable.\030The documents Executor Arren provided are just the break we needed in our battle with the wretched Scarlet Crusade.  We now know their exact locations throughout Tirisfal Glades.$B$BBut the Deathguard has larger concerns.  The Lich King's army grows in number each night.  We need someone with \"initiative\" like yourself to drive the Scarlet Crusade to the grave.$B$BProve to me you are capable of serving The Dark Lady by travelling west to the tower past the Solliden Farmstead and slay 10 Scarlet Warriors.\030Executor Zygand of Brill wants you to kill 10 Scarlet Warriors.\030If you wish to prove your worth to The Dark Lady, slay 10 Scarlet Warriors, $C.\030At War With The Scarlet Crusade\0312,1,115,2,261,1,1515\0302,118,178,2,257,1,1515\0302,183,221,2,257,1,1515\0302,224,271,2,321,1,1515\0302,274,363,2,259,1,1515\0302,368,509,2,257,1,1515\0303,1,63,2,386,1,1515\0301,1,19,4,272,1,1515\0301,21,66,4,272,1,1515\0304,1,79,3,258,4,1515\0311570,2,1,Executor Arren\03016980,2,4,The Lich King\03015065,2,6,Lady\0301515,2,7,Executor Zygand\03015065,3,10,Lady\0312,85,1420,0,\0303,0,0,10,The Dark Lady\031383,19,383,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030370,23,370,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,1535,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Scarlet Warrior",[428]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You found us! And not a moment too soon...\030A couple weeks ago two of our Deathstalkers, Rane and Quinn Yorick, were sent on a reconnaissance mission through northern Silverpine.  We have not heard from them.$B$BThey may have become victim to the Scourge, though if that is true then I want it confirmed.  Find these Deathstalkers.$B$BTheir first objective was to scout the farms in northern Silverpine.  You should begin your search there.\030Find the Deathstalkers Quinn and Rane Yorick.\030\030Lost Deathstalkers\0312,1,134,2,257,1,1952\0302,137,164,2,257,1,1952\0302,169,260,2,323,4,1952\0302,263,287,2,257,1,1952\0302,292,359,2,257,1,1952\0302,362,396,2,257,1,1952\0303,1,45,2,384,1,1952\0301,1,13,4,272,1,1950\0301,15,42,4,272,1,1950\0311951,2,1,Quinn Yorick\03011756,2,7,Quinn\0301950,2,7,Rane Yorick\0312,130,1421,0,\0302,0,0,3,Scourge\031429,23,429,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030429,24,429,UNKNOWN\031",[4281]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Elune be praised, the delivery from Feathermoon Stronghold has finally arrived!$B$BYour presence here indicates to me that perhaps some ill fate may have befallen Raschal, our usual courier. I hope that everything works out. I know that recently, the Woodpaw have become highly agitated from some source to their south. Maybe he fell to the wilds there; I would be careful, friend.$B$BRegardless, thank you again. Here is payment for this parcel's delivery.\030This parcel of goods you found in the Woodpaw gnoll camps was supposed to be delivered to the small way-station of Thalanaar in southeastern Feralas.  Regardless of the missing courier's fate, the task of delivering the parcel remains unfinished.$B$BExamining the parcel in detail reveals a hand written name of \"Falfindel Waywarder\" on the outside of the packaging.  Perhaps this is the parcel's ultimate recipient.\030Bring the Undelivered Parcel to Falfindel Waywarder in Thalanaar.\030Welcome to Thalanaar, $C. Do you need assistance of some sort?\030Thalanaar Delivery\0312,1,149,2,257,1,0\0302,152,246,2,261,1,0\0302,251,366,2,257,1,0\0302,369,416,2,257,4,0\0303,1,65,2,384,1,0\0301,1,79,4,272,1,4048\0301,84,190,4,272,4,4048\0301,192,224,4,274,3,4048\0301,226,319,4,272,1,4048\0301,321,381,4,272,4,4048\0301,386,413,4,272,1,4048\0301,415,457,4,272,1,4048\0304,1,25,3,256,1,4048\0304,27,62,3,258,2,4048\0314048,2,3,Falfindel Waywarder\0304048,2,5,Falfindel Waywarder\0312,357,1444,0,\0302,0,0,1,Woodpaw\0302,0,0,5,Falfindel Waywarder\0302,0,0,5,Thalanaar\0304,0,0,6,Feathermoon Stronghold\0303,0,0,13,Thalanaar\031\031ITEM,11463,STARTER,?,10,",[4282]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Marshal Windsor snatches the two tablets from your hands.>$B$BWe need to get out of here!\030<Marshal Windsor shakes the note excitedly.>$B$BDo you realize what this means, $N?$B$BPerhaps all is not lost! From what I can ascertain, the information is being held by two Dark Iron dwarves: General Angerforge and the golem lord, Argelmach. I have a feeling that they won't just hand over the information if we ask nicely.$B$BI hope you are ready to battle.$B$BVenture forth and find these two villains! Destroy them and return my lost information.\030Return Marshal Windsor's Lost Information.$B$BMarshal Windsor believes that the information is being held by Golem Lord Argelmach and General Angerforge.\030Soon this grand subterfuge will be over.\030A Shred of Hope\0312,1,44,2,257,1,9023\0302,49,83,2,257,2,9023\0302,88,111,2,261,4,9023\0302,113,244,2,257,1,9023\0302,246,326,2,259,4,9023\0302,331,361,2,263,3,9023\0302,366,407,2,257,1,9023\0302,409,452,2,261,1,9023\0303,1,42,2,388,1,9023\0303,47,153,2,384,1,9023\0301,1,59,4,272,1,9023\0301,64,90,4,274,1,9023\0304,1,40,3,256,3,9023\0319023,2,1,Marshal Windsor\0309033,2,4,General Angerforge\0309023,2,9,Marshal Windsor\0309023,2,10,Marshal Windsor\0308983,2,10,Golem Lord Argelmach\0309033,2,10,General Angerforge\0309023,4,11,Marshal Windsor\0312,1584,0,0,\0314264,19,4264,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304322,23,4322,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,11464,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,11465,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[4283]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You've done it! Your reward is: RUB MY BELLY! GO ON! RUB IT!\030I'm going to let you in on a little secret, soldier. Come a little closer.$B$BI'M THE ONLY SANE ONE HERE!$B$BLook at these people! Would you believe that they're all insane!? Well they are! NUTS! CRAZY!$B$B<Oralius lowers his voice.>$B$BLet's just keep that between me, you, and my pal Captain Winky.$B$B<Oralius grabs at the air and squeezes.>$B$BAnyhooooo... I'm collecting badges to go along with my ogre ear collection. Orc is the flavor of the day. Fifty. GO!$B$B<Oralius blows into a horn.>$B$BSHIP IT!\030Oralius wants 50 Blackrock Medallions. Chances are high that these medallions can be found on the orcs in the Burning Steppes.\030<Oralius is talking into a rather large, severed ogre ear.>$B$BBurning Steppes to control, come in control.\030FIFTY! YEP!\0312,1,52,2,257,3,9177\0302,54,74,2,257,1,9177\0302,79,105,2,257,1,9177\0302,110,130,2,257,1,9177\0302,132,174,2,257,4,9177\0302,176,189,2,257,1,9177\0302,191,195,2,257,1,9177\0302,197,202,2,257,1,9177\0302,207,233,2,257,1,9177\0302,238,300,2,257,1,9177\0302,305,344,2,257,1,9177\0302,349,360,2,257,1,9177\0302,362,423,2,257,1,9177\0302,425,453,2,257,1,9177\0302,455,460,2,257,1,9177\0302,469,496,2,257,1,9177\0302,501,508,2,257,1,9177\0303,1,38,2,386,1,9177\0303,40,126,2,384,1,9177\0301,1,15,4,272,1,9177\0301,17,45,4,272,1,9177\0301,54,60,4,272,1,9177\0304,1,59,3,256,1,9177\0304,64,107,3,256,1,9177\0319177,2,9,Oralius\0309177,2,11,Oralius\030211,2,13,Ogre\0309177,2,16,Oralius\0309177,2,18,Oralius\0309177,3,23,Oralius\030211,3,23,Ogre\0312,46,1428,0,\0302,0,0,19,Burning Steppes\031\031ITEM,11467,OBJECTIVE,50,15,",[4284]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Now I will continue my experiments! Thank you, $N.\030I'm sure you've noticed 'em, $N. They're everywhere!$B$BWhat am I talking about? Why, the crystals, of course!$B$BThe crystals... They're all over the crater. Most people ignore them, but I have a strange feeling that they hold power within them. I've been doing experiments here with them for a while, but I can't seem to find anything. Well, I haven't yet, anyway.$B$BSay, I'm running a little low on the crystals I have here -- think you might be able to collect some more for me?\030Collect 7 Power Crystals of each color: red, blue, yellow, and green. Bring them to J.D. Collie at Marshal's Refuge.\030I just know I'm onto something here, $N!\030Crystals of Power\0312,1,32,2,257,1,9117\0302,34,52,2,257,1,9117\0302,57,80,2,257,2,9117\0302,82,110,2,257,1,9117\0302,115,129,2,257,1,9117\0302,131,158,2,257,1,9117\0302,160,246,2,257,1,9117\0302,248,337,2,257,4,9117\0302,339,366,2,257,1,9117\0302,371,483,2,257,4,9117\0303,1,69,2,384,1,9117\0303,71,88,2,384,1,9117\0303,90,116,2,384,1,9117\0301,1,35,4,272,3,9117\0301,37,50,4,272,1,9117\0304,1,40,3,256,1,9117\031\0312,490,1449,0,\0302,0,0,13,Marshal's Refuge\031\031ITEM,11186,OBJECTIVE,7,15,\030ITEM,11188,OBJECTIVE,7,15,\030ITEM,11185,OBJECTIVE,7,15,\030ITEM,11184,OBJECTIVE,7,15,",[4285]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031I know the stories are true, $N.\030What could they be for? I can't get the thought out of my head!$B$BIt's driving me crazy --  that the rumors I have heard about the crystal pylons are all true. Call me gullible, but I'll usually believe anything people tell me.$B$BAnyway, I have heard that there is one of the crystal pylons fairly close. Somewhere in the north... Please locate it, $N. I just know they exist.\030Discover the location of the Northern Crystal Pylon in Un'Goro Crater.\030Discover and examine the Northern Crystal Pylon\030Have you visited the pylon, $N?\030The Northern Pylon\0312,1,23,2,257,4,9117\0302,25,63,2,257,1,9117\0302,68,160,2,257,1,9117\0302,162,228,2,257,4,9117\0302,233,306,2,257,1,9117\0302,308,332,2,257,1,9117\0302,334,354,2,257,1,9117\0302,356,378,2,257,1,9117\0303,1,70,2,384,1,9117\0301,1,32,4,272,1,9117\0305,1,31,3,256,2,9117\0304,1,47,3,384,1,9117\031\0312,490,1449,0,\0302,0,0,9,Un'Goro Crater\0314284,19,4284,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4286]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Oralius starts rummaging through the mountainous pile of fanny packs.>$B$BOH WONDERFUL!$B$B<Oralius sticks his large nose into the pile and takes a whiff.>$B$BDELICIOUS! Look at all these goodies!$B$BTake one for yourself, $N. There's plenty to go around.\030Captain Winky tells me that the Dark Irons in the Depths got all the good stuff. Ain't that right, Winky?$B$B<Oralius does his best impersonation of a pirate.>$B$BARRR MATEY! IT BE RIGHT!$B$BSee what I'm saying? You need to get in there and bring me back some samples of the good stuff.$B$BGet in there and shake your moneymaker!$B\030Travel to Blackrock Depths and recover 20 Dark Iron Fanny Packs. Return to Oralius when you have completed this task. You assume that the Dark Iron dwarves inside Blackrock Depths carry these 'fanny pack' contraptions.$B\030I can't be bothered right now, $N. Me and Winky got a meeting to attend.\030The Good Stuff\0312,1,80,2,257,1,9177\0302,82,105,2,257,2,9177\0302,110,159,2,257,1,9177\0302,164,174,2,257,1,9177\0302,176,187,2,257,1,9177\0302,192,211,2,257,2,9177\0302,213,286,2,259,1,9177\0302,291,329,2,257,1,9177\0303,1,64,2,384,1,9177\0303,66,117,2,384,1,9177\0303,119,218,2,384,4,9177\0301,1,71,4,272,1,9177\0301,76,88,4,272,1,9177\0301,93,156,4,272,1,9177\0301,161,170,4,272,1,9177\0301,172,197,4,272,1,9177\0301,202,227,4,272,1,9177\0301,229,256,4,272,1,9177\0304,1,34,3,256,1,9177\0304,36,72,3,256,1,9177\0319177,2,3,Oralius\0309177,2,10,Oralius\0309177,4,12,Oralius\0309177,4,14,Oralius\0312,1584,0,0,\0302,0,0,1,Depths\0302,0,0,9,Blackrock Depths\0302,0,0,10,Oralius\031\031ITEM,11468,OBJECTIVE,20,15,",[4287]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Un'Goro is such a strange place, $N. When you enter the crater, it's as if you are in a completely different world...\030During my stay here, I have heard strange rumors about mysterious pylons existing out in the wilderness of the crater, $N. I guess that they are quite large, with crystals lining their interiors.$B$BAlthough I've never seen one, I can't help but think that the rumors are true -- and that the pylons have something to do with all the crystals we found$B$BSo why don't you help me put my curiosity to rest? Supposedly, there is one in the eastern area of the crater. Do you think you can find it?\030Discover the location of the Eastern Crystal Pylon in Un'Goro Crater.\030Discover and examine the Eastern Crystal Pylon\030Have you visited the pylon, $N?\030The Eastern Pylon\0312,1,122,2,257,1,9117\0302,124,195,2,257,1,9117\0302,200,351,2,257,1,9117\0302,356,405,2,257,2,9117\0302,407,465,2,257,1,9117\0302,467,495,2,257,2,9117\0303,1,69,2,384,1,9117\0301,1,36,4,272,1,9117\0301,38,117,4,272,4,9117\0305,1,31,3,256,2,9117\0304,1,46,3,384,1,9117\031\0312,490,1449,0,\0302,0,0,7,Un'Goro Crater\0314284,19,4284,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4288]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031There are many hidden areas of the crater along the sides. Try exploring the winding paths if you can't think of anywhere else to look, $N.\030My experiments so far have not yielded any positive results, $N. I can't help but hope that you can find a solution by searching for one of the pylons that I have heard exist.$B$BPerhaps if we combine certain colors at them... but I get ahead of myself. Let's find them first!$B$B$N, search the western area of the crater; a pylon is said to be somewhere in that area.\030Discover the location of the Western Crystal Pylon.\030Discover and examine the Western Crystal Pylon\030Have you visited the pylon, $N?\030The Western Pylon\0312,1,64,2,257,1,9117\0302,66,175,2,259,3,9117\0302,180,226,2,257,4,9117\0302,228,253,2,257,1,9117\0302,255,276,2,257,1,9117\0302,281,368,2,257,1,9117\0303,1,51,2,384,1,9117\0301,1,58,4,272,1,9117\0301,60,139,4,272,4,9117\0305,1,31,3,256,2,9117\0304,1,46,3,384,1,9117\031\0312,490,1449,0,\0314284,19,4284,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4289]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031So, you have proven strong, strong enough to best the great apes of Un'Goro--that is good. The challenge was small compared to Lar'korwi, but I will not take such a great victory away from you.$B$BThese pelts will make wonderful clothing for my tribe. You have helped me and proven worthy.$B$BBefore you set off on another task, let us give praise to the Earth Mother and thank the spirits of those apes you killed--they must know their deaths will not be wasted.\030This crater has many strange creatures--they seem to be nobler versions of the creatures found throughout my homeland and beyond. I cannot explain it, but this place cries of the Earth Mother. I pay homage to her every time I track one of her beautiful creatures across its basin.$B$BIf you too wish to feel the enlightenment that accompanies such a great feat, then head to the north. There you'll find great apes who are a test for any mortal's strength. Bring me their pelts... prove your strength.\030Bring 2 Un'Goro Gorilla Pelts, 2 Un'Goro Stomper Pelts, and 2 Un'Goro Thunderer Pelts to Torwa Pathfinder at the entrance of Un'Goro Crater.\030Have the creatures here bested you already, $N?$B$BDo not be dissuaded so easily. Tracking and defeating the apes of Un'Goro is no simple task, even for a great hunter.\030The Apes of Un'Goro\0312,1,129,2,257,4,9619\0302,131,192,2,257,1,9619\0302,194,280,2,257,1,9619\0302,285,385,2,259,4,9619\0302,387,456,2,257,1,9619\0302,458,480,2,257,1,9619\0302,482,501,2,257,1,9619\0303,1,140,2,384,1,9619\0301,1,90,4,272,1,9619\0301,92,193,4,272,3,9619\0301,198,251,4,272,3,9619\0301,253,289,4,272,1,9619\0301,294,463,4,272,3,9619\0304,1,47,3,256,2,9619\0304,52,81,3,256,1,9619\0304,83,168,3,256,1,9619\0316514,2,8,Un'Goro Gorilla\0306513,2,8,Un'Goro Stomper\0306516,2,8,Un'Goro Thunderer\0309619,2,8,Torwa Pathfinder\0309684,4,10,Lar'korwi\0312,490,1449,0,\0302,0,0,8,Torwa Pathfinder\0304,0,0,10,Lar'korwi\0304,0,0,13,Earth Mother\0314301,23,4301,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,11478,OBJECTIVE,2,15,\030ITEM,11479,OBJECTIVE,2,15,\030ITEM,11480,OBJECTIVE,2,15,",[429]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Renferrel takes the hearts>$B$BIt is troubling to hear our Deathstalkers have failed their mission.$B$BLet us hope that these failures are rare.$B$BI'll give you the potion in a moment, but here is its recipe - if those Deathstalkers find themselves in need of future aid, then perhaps you can give it yourself.\030My brother Quinn was badly hurt by the ghoul, Ivar the Foul, and I don't know if he will heal properly without magical aid.  Although I am not an apothecary, I do know that our apothecaries can make healing potions from the discolored hearts of worgs.$B$BGather such hearts and take them to Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher to the south.  Then return here with the potion.$B$BYou can find plenty of worgs between here and Malden's Orchard to the east.\030Gather 6 discolored worg hearts and bring them to Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher.\030My time is short, $c, for the Dark Lady has charged me with a grave task.\030Wild Hearts\0312,1,123,2,257,4,1950\0302,126,251,2,257,1,1950\0302,256,342,2,257,1,1950\0302,345,377,2,257,1,1950\0302,382,456,2,257,1,1950\0303,1,88,2,384,1,1950\0301,1,28,4,272,1,1937\0301,33,100,4,272,1,1937\0301,105,145,4,274,3,1937\0301,150,312,4,274,4,1937\0304,1,73,3,256,1,1937\03111756,2,1,Quinn\030846,2,1,Ghoul\0301971,2,1,Ivar the Foul\0301937,2,3,Apothecary Renferrel\0301765,2,6,Worg\0301937,2,6,Apothecary Renferrel\03015065,3,11,Lady\0312,130,1421,0,\0302,0,0,3,Apothecary Renferrel\0302,0,0,3,Sepulcher\0302,0,0,6,Apothecary Renferrel\0302,0,0,6,Sepulcher\031430,23,430,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3164,OBJECTIVE,6,15,",[4290]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This will do nicely, $N. It seems Lar'korwi eats well these days. Although, I wonder where he found a threshadon in this area. Odd.$B$BRegardless, I will hold onto this until you are ready for your confrontation with the beast. Do not worry for my safety--I am sure you've angered Lar'korwi enough that he will not kill me until after he's tasted your flesh.\030Once, a long time ago, a brother of mine took some meat from one of Lar'korwi's kills. He didn't know it at the time, but Lar'korwi saw him from the forest. Lar'korwi followed my brother for days, destroying everything he touched. My brother, scared, finally decided to run from the Crater and leave Lar'korwi behind.$B$BLar'korwi killed him not far from this spot.$B$BIf you want to provoke Lar'korwi, find a fresh kill of his and take some of the meat from it.$B$BReturn to me afterwards.\030Find the carcass of Lar'korwi's freshest kill and steal a Piece of Threshadon Carcass before returning to Torwa Pathfinder in Un'Goro Crater.\030Do not take my words lightly, $N. If you truly wish to face this creature, then you must be careful... and smart. It will take a great deal of strength and insight to draw out Lar'korwi and defeat him.\030The Fare of Lar'korwi\0312,1,86,2,257,1,9619\0302,88,156,2,257,1,9619\0302,158,230,2,261,1,9619\0302,232,317,2,257,1,9619\0302,322,365,2,257,1,9619\0302,370,462,2,259,4,9619\0302,467,490,2,257,1,9619\0303,1,141,2,388,1,9619\0301,1,24,4,272,3,9619\0301,26,65,4,272,4,9619\0301,67,126,4,272,1,9619\0301,128,131,4,272,1,9619\0301,136,227,4,272,3,9619\0301,229,358,4,280,3,9619\0304,1,33,3,256,1,9619\0304,35,102,3,258,4,9619\0304,104,113,3,256,1,9619\0304,115,201,3,256,3,9619\0319684,2,2,Lar'korwi\0309684,2,3,Lar'korwi\0309684,2,4,Lar'korwi\0309684,2,5,Lar'korwi\0304950,2,5,Spot\0309684,2,6,Lar'korwi\0309619,2,8,Torwa Pathfinder\0309684,4,10,Lar'korwi\03010430,4,13,The Beast\0309684,4,14,Lar'korwi\0309684,3,18,Lar'korwi\0312,490,1449,0,\0302,0,0,4,Crater\0302,0,0,8,Torwa Pathfinder\0302,0,0,8,Un'Goro Crater\0314291,23,4291,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,11504,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[4291]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, fine specimens, $N. The two pieces you've found should be perfect for baiting Lar'korwi into the open. I cannot wait to see the outcome of your fight with the monster. He is a massive thing with claws as sharp as the finest blades. You will look into his eyes and you will know death.\030I'm actually surprised he has not come for you yet, $N. But all is well, for I have a final plan that will bring the monster to us.$B$BBeing the dominant male gives Lar'korwi rights to breed with any female he chooses--and he chooses many of them. You'll find many ravasaur eggs to the west of here. Get close to them and you should provoke an attack by his mates. The females produce an awful smell from a gland in their heads that allow males to know they are ready to breed. Bring me two of those glands.\030Bring 2 Ravasaur Pheromone Glands to Torwa Pathfinder near the entrance to Un'Goro Crater.\030Be careful, $N. Getting close to any of nest of eggs surely will provoke the mothers... even if you've already secured a gland from one. The mothers can be just as deadly as Lar'korwi himself when they fight to protect their young. But, if you are successful, then we shall have a definitive way of bringing Lar'korwi out from hiding.\030The Scent of Lar'korwi\0312,1,55,2,257,1,9619\0302,57,131,2,257,3,9619\0302,136,247,2,257,1,9619\0302,249,299,2,257,1,9619\0302,301,364,2,261,1,9619\0302,366,477,2,257,1,9619\0302,479,507,2,257,1,9619\0303,1,90,2,384,1,9619\0301,1,23,4,272,1,9619\0301,25,106,4,272,1,9619\0301,108,171,4,276,1,9619\0301,173,235,4,272,1,9619\0301,237,288,4,272,3,9619\0304,1,15,3,256,1,9619\0304,17,87,3,256,3,9619\0304,89,136,3,256,4,9619\0304,138,231,3,270,1,9619\0304,233,334,3,256,4,9619\0319684,2,3,Lar'korwi\0306505,2,4,Ravasaur\0306505,2,8,Ravasaur\0309619,2,8,Torwa Pathfinder\0309684,4,10,Lar'korwi\0309684,3,17,Lar'korwi\0309684,3,18,Lar'korwi\0312,490,1449,0,\0302,0,0,8,Torwa Pathfinder\0302,0,0,8,Un'Goro Crater\0314290,19,4290,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304292,23,4292,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,11509,OBJECTIVE,2,15,",[4292]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The Earth Mother be praised! You've done it! Fair play to you, $N. You have proven to be a great $C in your own right. Your spirit is strong. Your bravery unmatched. And your strength has been fortified. I bow down to your skills.$B$BOnly the greatest of my ancestors could have accomplished something so incredible. Congratulations.\030This will be the most difficult part because there is some complexity to the plan. To the north of here, you will find a small trail into the mountains. It was here I saw Lar'korwi last. You will know you are in the right area because of all the bones from massive creatures that once wandered nearby. Take the meat you recovered and place it there. Then, rub this mixture I created on the meat. If both lures mingled together do not bring Lar'korwi to you, then I know nothing else that will.\030Using the contents of Torwa's Pouch, summon Lar'korwi and defeat him. Then bring Lar'korwi's Head to Torwa Pathfinder near the entrance to Un'Goro Crater.\030Do not let fear overpower you, $N. Fear is the great betrayer... you must remain strong!$B$BTake the meat, place it in the small valley, and then use the gland on it. Only then will death come for you.\030The Bait for Lar'korwi\0312,1,82,2,259,3,9619\0302,84,152,2,257,3,9619\0302,154,186,2,257,1,9619\0302,188,301,2,259,3,9619\0302,303,349,2,257,1,9619\0302,351,395,2,257,1,9619\0302,397,493,2,257,4,9619\0303,1,69,2,384,1,9619\0303,71,154,2,384,1,9619\0301,1,28,4,272,1,9619\0301,30,44,4,272,1,9619\0301,46,66,4,272,1,9619\0301,68,118,4,272,1,9619\0301,120,141,4,272,1,9619\0301,143,165,4,272,1,9619\0301,167,203,4,272,1,9619\0301,205,230,4,272,1,9619\0301,235,316,4,272,4,9619\0301,318,333,4,272,1,9619\0304,1,34,3,256,1,9619\0304,36,64,3,256,1,9619\0304,66,88,3,256,1,9619\0304,93,166,3,256,1,9619\0304,168,201,3,256,3,9619\0319684,2,3,Lar'korwi\0309684,2,7,Lar'korwi\0309684,2,8,Lar'korwi\0309619,2,9,Torwa Pathfinder\0312,490,1449,0,\0302,0,0,9,Torwa Pathfinder\0302,0,0,9,Un'Goro Crater\0314291,19,4291,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,11510,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[4293]="PARTIAL\031consequences,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, excellent. These samples will do nicely. I thank you for your help.$B$BOnce we've gathered all the samples of slimes, we'll be able to determine more. I am beginning to suspect that Lady Sylvanas' hunch was not only correct, but more insightful than even she could have predicted. These samples are very interesting. Just seeing how they've reacted with my compounds... hmm, yes, we'll definitely need to investigate further.\030Felwood is a forest far north of the Barrens, even farther than Ashenvale. There, slimes are found all around pools of water blessed by the touch of Fel. The Scourge decimated the area with attacks of Infernals and other demonic magics--the slimes supposedly crept up through the earth during these attacks.$B$BGather samples of Felwood slimes and we will use the testing equipment next to me to create a control group for our tests against other samples you gather.\030Gather Felwood Slime Samples from any of the slimes in Felwood. Then, using the Testing Equipment next to Chemist Fuely in Undercity, see which of your samples are the most corrupt. Bring 5 of the Corrupted Felwood Samples you find to Chemist Fuely.\030I will need at least five corrupted samples for our control group, $N. Continue to gather Felwood slime samples until you're able to give me that which we'll need. The Lady Sylvanas decrees it...\030A Sample of Slime...\0312,1,74,2,257,1,10136\0302,76,153,2,257,1,10136\0302,155,307,2,325,1,10136\0302,312,466,2,257,3,10136\0303,1,63,2,384,1,10136\0303,65,181,2,388,1,10136\0303,183,249,2,388,1,10136\0301,1,14,4,272,1,10136\0301,16,44,4,272,3,10136\0301,46,71,4,272,1,10136\0301,76,154,4,272,1,10136\0301,156,284,4,272,4,10136\0301,286,320,4,272,1,10136\0301,322,373,4,272,1,10136\0301,375,429,4,274,1,10136\0304,1,70,3,262,3,10136\0304,72,163,3,258,1,10136\0304,165,195,3,256,1,10136\031364,2,5,Slime\03010136,2,6,Chemist Fuely\03010136,2,7,Chemist Fuely\03015065,4,12,Lady\030364,3,17,Slime\03015065,3,18,Lady\0312,1497,1458,0,\0302,0,0,1,Barrens\0302,0,0,5,Felwood\0302,0,0,6,Chemist Fuely\0302,0,0,6,Undercity\0302,0,0,7,Chemist Fuely\031\031ITEM,12234,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[4294]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Truly amazing, $N. This Un'Goro Crater is holding many more secrets than I expected. I wonder what else we will discover as we test further.$B$BSimply amazing... look at the purity of these samples. Hmm, I wonder what it could mean. They seem to be elemental in nature, but... something more. They remind me of... of the Old Gods. We've found traces of them throughout Azeroth, and now I wonder if these creatures aren't related to them somehow.$B$BWe shall have to test further.\030Have you heard of the Un'Goro Crater, $N? It is near the Tanaris desert, and it is a magnificent place: lush, vibrant, full of creatures and plant life.$B$BIt is there you must go. Word has reached me that the place seems completely untainted by outside hands. Explorers are just now discovering its secrets.$B$BI would like to test the slimes or oozes there. If it is true--that they are uncorrupt--then I would like to see how such creatures have evolved.\030Gather Un'Goro Slime Samples from any of the slimes in Un'Goro Crater. Then, using the Testing Equipment next to Chemist Fuely in Undercity, see which of your samples are the most pure. Bring 5 of the Pure Un'Goro Samples you find to Chemist Fuely.\030Yes, $N? How goes your search?\030... and a Batch of Ooze\0312,1,41,2,257,2,10136\0302,43,152,2,257,1,10136\0302,157,180,2,257,1,10136\0302,182,260,2,257,4,10136\0302,262,308,2,257,1,10136\0302,313,359,2,259,4,10136\0302,361,457,2,259,4,10136\0303,1,70,2,384,1,10136\0303,72,185,2,384,1,10136\0303,187,248,2,384,1,10136\0301,1,18,4,272,1,10136\0301,20,84,4,272,1,10136\0301,86,140,4,272,3,10136\0301,145,161,4,272,1,10136\0301,163,198,4,272,1,10136\0301,200,232,4,272,4,10136\0301,234,276,4,272,4,10136\0301,278,292,4,272,1,10136\0301,294,313,4,272,1,10136\0301,315,330,4,336,1,10136\0301,332,445,4,272,4,10136\0301,450,479,4,272,3,10136\0304,1,8,3,256,2,10136\0304,10,30,3,256,2,10136\031364,2,8,Slime\03010136,2,9,Chemist Fuely\03010136,2,10,Chemist Fuely\0312,1497,1458,0,\0302,0,0,2,Tanaris\0302,0,0,8,Un'Goro Crater\0302,0,0,9,Chemist Fuely\0302,0,0,9,Undercity\0302,0,0,10,Chemist Fuely\031\031ITEM,12236,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[4295]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031What's this?  Ah!  It smells like Dark Iron Ale!  Drink has blurred my sight, but I can tell that you, sir, are a real friend!\030\030\030Oh, ale! I would kill for some Dark Iron ale!! Quick, I'm getting sober! I know this because sobriety blurs my vision... and it's making you look like the $R I slew last week!\030Rocknot's Ale\0311,1,12,4,272,2,9503\0301,20,48,4,272,1,9503\0301,51,126,4,272,1,9503\0304,1,8,3,256,1,9503\0304,10,46,3,256,4,9503\0304,48,72,3,256,1,9503\0304,74,120,3,258,1,9503\0304,122,175,3,256,1,9503\031\0312,1584,0,0,\031\031ITEM,11325,OBJECTIVE,2,15,",[4296]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, you found the tablet! And your transcription is superb! Are you sure you're a $C and not a scribe?$B$BHere you are, $N. Here is the payment I promised.\030I came to the Burning Steppes, following the legends of the Seven.  They were dwarves of great knowledge and power, and if you have knowledge and power, then wealth is sure to follow.$B$BThat's what I want.  Wealth!$B$BIf we can learn more of the Seven, then maybe we can get rich together.  The ruins of Thaurissan is rumored to keep the Tablet of the Seven, which holds knowledge of the ancient dwarves.  Find this tablet, copy its text and bring it to me.  Let's discover its secrets together!\030Bring the Tablet Transcript to Maxwort Uberglint in the Burning Steppes.\030Do you have the writings of the Seven, $N? Have you learned the secrets from their tablet?\030Tablet of the Seven\0312,1,66,2,257,1,9536\0302,69,183,2,257,4,9536\0302,188,206,2,259,1,9536\0302,209,215,2,257,1,9536\0302,220,290,2,257,4,9536\0302,293,405,2,321,1,9536\0302,408,458,2,257,1,9536\0302,461,496,2,257,1,9536\0303,1,72,2,384,1,9536\0301,1,25,4,272,1,9536\0301,27,59,4,272,1,9536\0301,61,102,4,272,2,9536\0301,107,123,4,272,1,9536\0301,125,155,4,272,1,9536\0304,1,42,3,256,2,9536\0304,44,90,3,256,2,9536\0319536,2,9,Maxwort Uberglint\0312,46,1428,0,\0302,0,0,1,Burning Steppes\0302,0,0,9,Maxwort Uberglint\0302,0,0,9,Burning Steppes\031\031ITEM,11470,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[4297]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031These'll do nicely, and if I'm not mistaken, your little egg's just about ready to hatch. How does it feel? You know, you about to be a $gfather:mother;? Haha, didn't think ya'd have to deal with such responsibility, now did ya?\030Sprite darters are omnivores--that means they eat both meat and vegetation. If your egg here's gonna hatch, we best be prepared. Some good eats for these little guys are flanks of meat, raw and juicy, believe it or not. I was never able to find out why, but it has somethin' to do with Elune's plan for the elves... maybe they were to be protectors or somethin', I don't know.$B$BI'll take care of the egg for now, why don't you get me some good Silvermane stalker flanks for 'em to eat when he's hatched.\030Bring 5 Silvermane Stalker Flanks to Agnar Beastamer in Hinterlands.\030Find that meat yet, $N? Your little egg here's just about ready to hatch. If he don't have a good enough first meal, then he might not make it past his first week, and I'd hate for that to happen.$B$BCan't much lie to ya, $N. I'm jealous of you gettin' this egg to begin with. Don't make me regret helpin' ya out like this.\030Food for Baby\0312,1,75,2,257,1,9660\0302,77,128,2,257,4,9660\0302,130,219,2,257,4,9660\0302,221,315,2,257,1,9660\0302,317,376,2,257,4,9660\0302,381,505,2,257,1,9660\0303,1,68,2,384,1,9660\0301,1,89,4,272,4,9660\0301,91,107,4,272,2,9660\0301,109,153,4,272,2,9660\0301,155,228,4,272,2,9660\0304,1,23,3,256,2,9660\0304,25,73,3,256,1,9660\0304,75,196,3,256,4,9660\0304,201,225,3,256,1,9660\0304,227,276,3,256,1,9660\0304,278,323,3,256,1,9660\0312926,2,6,Silvermane Stalker\0302926,2,7,Silvermane Stalker\0309660,2,7,Agnar Beastamer\0312,357,1444,0,\0302,0,0,7,Agnar Beastamer\0302,0,0,7,Hinterlands\0313843,19,3843,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304298,23,4298,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,11472,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[4298]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Here, take the egg... better you have it so it bonds to you and looks to you to be its $gdadda:momma;.$B$BCongrats, $N. You're a parent... kinda.\030Whoa, it was a lot more ready than I thought...\030Speak to Agnar Beastamer in the Hinterlands.\030\030Becoming a Parent\0312,1,47,2,257,1,9660\0303,1,44,2,384,1,9660\0301,1,21,4,272,1,9660\0301,23,102,4,272,1,9660\0301,107,119,4,272,1,9660\0301,121,138,4,272,1,9660\0301,140,145,4,272,1,9660\0319660,2,2,Agnar Beastamer\0312,357,1444,0,\0302,0,0,2,Agnar Beastamer\0302,0,0,2,Hinterlands\0314297,19,4297,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[430]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Quinn takes the potion and drinks it>$B$BYes, I can feel it working. I will soon be able to travel.$B$BYou have done me a great favor, $N.\030Here is the potion to aid in Quinn Yorick's recovery.$B$BNow if you will excuse me, I have very important work to continue...\030Bring Quinn's potion to Quinn Yorick at the Ivar Patch, north of the Sepulcher.\030My sister told me you were here to aid us. Is that true?\030Return to Quinn\0312,1,53,2,257,1,1937\0302,58,125,2,257,4,1937\0303,1,79,2,384,1,1937\0301,1,38,4,272,1,1951\0301,43,69,4,272,1,1951\0301,71,100,4,272,3,1951\0301,105,139,4,272,1,1951\0304,1,42,3,256,1,1951\0304,44,56,3,256,2,1951\0311951,2,1,Quinn Yorick\0301951,2,3,Quinn Yorick\03011756,4,4,Quinn\0312,130,1421,0,\0302,0,0,1,Quinn Yorick's\0302,0,0,3,Quinn Yorick\0302,0,0,3,Ivar Patch\0302,0,0,3,Sepulcher\031429,19,429,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030425,23,425,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4300]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, these do nicely. Thank you, $N. An' you be here long before they needed... that be good.$B$BMaybe we have a weapon fashioned for you from the claws. What do you say?\030Hmm, maybe there be somethin' you can do for the Hand now that me think 'bout it. Yes, Jes'rimon could use your help for sure.$B$BIn Un'Goro Crater there be raptors with deadly claws. Some of those raptors sometimes have white claws instead of ones black like death. The Hand have... clients... that like weapons crafted from these claws. Bring me many of those white claws, and me pay you good coin. Do it fast enough, and maybe me help you in other ways.\030Bring 8 White Ravasaur Claws to Jes'rimon in Orgrimmar.\030Me clients are not so patient, $N. Have you gotten any of the claws yet?\030Bone-Bladed Weapons\0312,1,81,2,257,4,8659\0302,83,126,2,257,4,8659\0302,131,183,2,257,1,8659\0302,185,266,2,257,1,8659\0302,268,283,2,257,1,8659\0302,285,294,2,257,1,8659\0302,296,338,2,257,1,8659\0302,340,400,2,257,1,8659\0302,402,456,2,257,4,8659\0303,1,55,2,384,1,8659\0301,1,20,4,272,1,8659\0301,22,35,4,272,1,8659\0301,37,78,4,280,1,8659\0301,80,92,4,272,1,8659\0301,97,152,4,272,4,8659\0301,154,169,4,272,2,8659\0304,1,34,3,256,1,8659\0304,36,72,3,256,2,8659\0318659,2,2,Jes'rimon\0306505,2,10,Ravasaur\0308659,2,10,Jes'rimon\0312,1637,1454,0,\0302,0,0,10,Jes'rimon\0302,0,0,10,Orgrimmar\031\031ITEM,11477,OBJECTIVE,8,15,",[4301]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $N. I am pleased. You have done a great thing here today.$B$BU'cha was one of the greatest apes I had ever seen. The fact that you have bested his strength speaks well of your own strength... and courage.$B$BIt is only fitting that I give you this as a sign of respect. You have earned it.\030While you have been exploring Un'Goro, I have seen other things that a mighty hunter such as yourself would relish in. One such sight was a huge ape among the other gorillas to the north. You have been to that cave before, but this time, I wonder if you'll survive the encounter if you accept my task.$B$BI call him U'cha, and he is one of the Earth Mother's greatest sons, of that you can be sure. Defeat U'cha and bring me his pelt. Do this, and I will defend your right to call yourself a great hunter.\030Bring U'cha's Pelt to Torwa Pathfinder at the entrance of Un'Goro Crater.\030U'cha... the beast was magnificent. Huge and red, with teeth the size of daggers. His arms as thick as tree trunks, and as fast as any mountain lion I have ever laid eyes upon. You should consider yourself lucky to find such a test of bravery--my people would go generations without seeing such a creature.\030The Mighty U'cha\0312,1,118,2,257,4,9619\0302,120,187,2,257,1,9619\0302,189,301,2,265,4,9619\0302,306,398,2,257,1,9619\0302,400,434,2,257,1,9619\0302,436,505,2,269,3,9619\0303,1,73,2,384,1,9619\0301,1,14,4,272,1,9619\0301,16,28,4,272,1,9619\0301,30,68,4,272,1,9619\0301,73,123,4,272,1,9619\0301,125,202,4,272,1,9619\0301,204,215,4,272,1,9619\0301,220,280,4,272,1,9619\0301,282,300,4,272,1,9619\0304,1,8,3,256,1,9619\0304,10,35,3,256,1,9619\0304,37,81,3,256,1,9619\0304,83,176,3,256,1,9619\0304,178,306,3,256,4,9619\0319622,2,4,U'cha\0309622,2,5,U'cha\0309619,2,7,Torwa Pathfinder\0309622,4,11,U'cha\0309622,3,16,U'cha\03010430,3,17,The Beast\0302406,3,19,Mountain Lion\0312,490,1449,0,\0302,0,0,7,Torwa Pathfinder\0314289,19,4289,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,11476,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[431]="PARTIAL\031characters,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You grab one of the candles and place it in your pack.\030\030\030\030Candles of Beckoning\0311,1,54,4,272,1,0\031\0312,85,1420,0,\031409,20,409,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,1586,GIVER,?,9,Crate of Candles\030OBJECT,1586,FINISHER,?,12,Crate of Candles",[432]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well, that makes me feel a little better...$B$BBut I won't be happy until they're all dead! All of them!\030Those Light-blasted troggs, turning my work site into a wreck! Look at that, there goes another barrel of powder!$B$BOhhh, I wish I could go down there and wring every one of their scrawny little necks! I want to kill them all!$B$BThis can't be good for my health, all this stress and anger... What have they left me with? Nothing!$B$BI'd kill them myself, but my aim's no good anymore! You go into the quarry and kill some of the filthy buggers! I'll pay you! Just hurt them, kill them!\030Kill 6 Rockjaw Skullthumpers for Foreman Stonebrow at the Gol'Bolar quarry.\030It makes me so mad! Grrr...\030Those Blasted Troggs!\0312,1,62,2,257,1,1254\0302,64,113,2,257,1,1254\0302,118,202,2,259,4,1254\0302,204,227,2,259,1,1254\0302,232,293,2,257,1,1254\0302,295,322,2,257,2,1254\0302,324,331,2,257,1,1254\0302,336,386,2,257,1,1254\0302,388,446,2,257,1,1254\0302,448,460,2,257,1,1254\0302,462,487,2,257,1,1254\0303,1,75,2,384,1,1254\0301,1,43,4,272,1,1254\0301,48,91,4,272,1,1254\0301,93,104,4,272,1,1254\0304,1,19,3,256,1,1254\0304,21,27,3,256,1,1254\0311254,2,12,Foreman Stonebrow\0312,1,1426,0,\0302,0,0,12,Gol'Bolar\031\031NPC,1115,OBJECTIVE,6,13,Rockjaw Skullthumper",[4321]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Alright, $N. This is fascinating... I can only hope that my diagrams are correct! I compiled everything into this manual, which you can have.$B$BI believe I can answer any questions you have about the crystals now, $N.\030The information you have given me about the pylons is very interesting...$B$BGive me a moment to do some calculations, $N. Speak to me again in a moment and I should be able to give you the answer we have been looking for.\030Speak with J.D. Collie in a moment.\030\030Making Sense of It\0312,1,73,2,257,1,9117\0302,78,122,2,257,1,9117\0302,124,222,2,257,1,9117\0303,1,15,2,384,1,9117\0303,17,35,2,384,1,9117\0301,1,12,4,272,1,9117\0301,14,35,4,272,1,9117\0301,37,81,4,274,3,9117\0301,83,141,4,272,1,9117\0301,146,218,4,272,4,9117\031\0312,490,1449,0,\0314285,21,4285,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304287,21,4287,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304288,21,4288,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4322]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Amazing, $N. Simply amazing. Windsor stormed through here not five minutes ago. He makes some grand claims but purports that they are supported by his evidence. He is on his way to Stormwind now to confront Bolvar and ... Lady Prestor.\030We need to get out of here, $N. Help me get my gear back from the supply area and free my friends. If we make it out of here, you are to proceed to Morgan's Vigil and speak with Marshal Maxwell. He will give you further instruction.\030Help Marshal Windsor get his gear back and free his friends. Return to Marshal Maxwell if you succeed.\030Jail Break!\030You look exhausted, $n. Perhaps you should have a seat by the fire and relax.\030Jail Break!\0312,1,31,2,259,1,9023\0302,33,98,2,257,1,9023\0302,100,194,2,257,4,9023\0302,196,232,2,257,3,9023\0303,1,60,2,384,1,9023\0303,62,102,2,384,4,9023\0301,1,12,4,272,1,9560\0301,14,28,4,272,1,9560\0301,30,79,4,272,1,9560\0301,81,160,4,272,1,9560\0301,162,221,4,272,1,9560\0301,223,235,4,272,1,9560\0305,1,23,3,256,1,9560\0305,25,77,3,256,4,9560\0304,1,11,3,384,1,9023\0319560,2,3,Marshal Maxwell\0309023,2,5,Marshal Windsor\0309560,2,6,Marshal Maxwell\03015065,4,12,Lady\0312,1584,0,0,\0302,0,0,3,Morgan's Vigil\0302,0,0,6,Marshal Maxwell\0304,0,0,11,Stormwind\0314282,19,4282,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306402,23,6402,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4324]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes, I'm looking for my brother.  We must find him and retrieve him, bless his heart.$B$BBut if we can't bring all of him... then his head will suffice.\030Although my little brother Ribbly has been worthless his whole life, I think, finally, he has some value!  But... we might need your help to capitalize on Ribbly's newfound worth.$B$BMy sister Yuka has been looking for him for weeks, and tracked him to the Burning Steppes.  She sent word to me, asking for some hired hands.$B$BSo, what do you say?  Want to help?  If so, then speak with my sister.  You'll find her holed up in Flame Crest, a cave northwest of Dreadmaul Rock.\030Speak with Yuka Screwspigot in the Burning Steppes.\030\030Yuka Screwspigot\0312,1,105,2,257,1,9706\0302,108,113,2,257,1,9706\0302,115,179,2,259,4,9706\0302,184,273,2,257,1,9706\0302,276,324,2,257,1,9706\0302,329,348,2,257,2,9706\0302,351,363,2,257,2,9706\0302,366,398,2,257,4,9706\0302,401,476,2,257,1,9706\0303,1,51,2,384,1,9706\0301,1,32,4,272,1,9544\0301,35,85,4,272,1,9544\0301,90,124,4,272,4,9544\0301,126,152,4,272,3,9544\0319544,2,10,Yuka Screwspigot\0312,1584,0,0,\0302,0,0,4,Burning Steppes\0302,0,0,9,Flame Crest\0302,0,0,10,Burning Steppes\0314136,23,4136,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304136,24,4136,UNKNOWN\031",[433]="PARTIAL\031consequences,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It is a start. Hopefully we can take advantage of it, and move some Mountaineers in to secure the area. Then we can begin to restore our infrastructure and get the miners back to work.$B$BThank you for your assistance, $N.\030As a member of the Senate and the Explorers' League, I've taken it upon myself to take care of this part of the trogg infestation that has gripped our lands.$B$BThey've certainly made a mess of Gol'Bolar quarry, and for no reason. As we dug deep into the earth, they poured out, destroying our equipment and driving the miners out. There's not much for us to do but to exterminate the lot of them, rebuild, then get back to work.$B$BIf you help me with the troggs, I'll gladly recompense you for your time.\030Kill 10 Rockjaw Bonesnappers for Senator Mehr Stonehallow at the Gol'Bolar quarry.\030If we can remove the troggs from Gol'Bolar quarry, it will be the first step of many that we will have to undertake to rid ourselves of this menace.\030The Public Servant\0312,1,157,2,257,1,1977\0302,162,230,2,257,1,1977\0302,232,331,2,261,1,1977\0302,333,429,2,321,1,1977\0302,434,506,2,257,4,1977\0303,1,82,2,384,1,1977\0301,1,14,4,272,1,1977\0301,16,103,4,272,3,1977\0301,105,184,4,274,1,1977\0301,189,222,4,272,1,1977\0304,1,148,3,256,4,1977\0311977,2,6,Senator Mehr Stonehallow\0312,1,1426,0,\0302,0,0,6,Gol'Bolar\0303,0,0,11,Gol'Bolar\031\031NPC,1117,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Rockjaw Bonesnapper",[434]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031So it is done? Good. Thank you greatly for your discretion, $N. You've proven worthy on more than one count. I'll be sure to keep my eyes on you and your progress within the Alliance.$B$BBe sure to keep your nose clean.\030After I put on Spybot's disguise, he'll head in to talk to Lescovar. The guards should let him pass no problem.$B$BWhile you were getting materials for me, I took care of informing Marzon that it was time for him and Lescovar to meet again. I even dropped some false information.$B$BLescovar will dismiss his guards and wait for Marzon out here in the garden. After you catch wind of talk about the Defias, make your move. You need to kill them both before the guards return! When you're done, speak to Trias.\030Remain in the garden until Lord Gregor Lescovar and Marzon the Silent Blade have had their conversation. Afterwards, kill them both before returning to Elling Trias in Stormwind.\030Overhear Lescovar and Marzon's Conversation\030Yes, $N? Are things going well with Tyrion? He apprised me of the situation and I've helped him trick Marzon into going to the castle.$B$BMarzon has been a thorn in the side of many people in Stormwind; many of which are close friends of mine. No one messes with my friends... not if they know what's healthy for them.$B$BIt's just a shame I'm indirectly doing a favor for Shaw and SI:7 in the meantime. Oh well, not every plan is perfect.\030The Attack!\0312,1,68,2,257,1,7766\0302,70,111,2,261,1,7766\0302,116,240,2,257,1,7766\0302,242,279,2,257,1,7766\0302,284,359,2,257,3,7766\0302,361,422,2,257,1,7766\0302,424,475,2,259,1,7766\0302,477,509,2,257,1,7766\0303,1,104,2,384,1,7766\0303,106,178,2,384,1,7766\0301,1,14,4,272,2,482\0301,16,20,4,272,1,482\0301,22,63,4,272,1,482\0301,65,108,4,272,1,482\0301,110,183,4,272,1,482\0301,188,219,4,272,1,482\0305,1,8,3,256,2,482\0305,10,43,3,256,2,482\0305,45,134,3,256,3,482\0305,139,243,3,256,1,482\0305,245,276,3,256,1,482\0305,278,318,3,256,4,482\0305,323,403,3,256,1,482\0305,405,439,3,256,1,482\0304,1,43,3,384,1,7766\0311754,2,9,Lord Gregor Lescovar\0301755,2,9,Marzon the Silent Blade\030482,2,10,Elling Trias\0307766,3,18,Tyrion\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,1,Lescovar\0302,0,0,8,Trias\0302,0,0,10,Elling Trias\0302,0,0,10,Stormwind\0304,0,0,15,Alliance\0303,0,0,20,Stormwind\0312746,19,2746,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030394,23,394,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,1754,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Lord Gregor Lescovar\030NPC,1755,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Marzon the Silent Blade",[4341]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Please, let me explain.\030You have been to the smoldering ruins of Thaurissan? Did you happen to run into a pitiful lout named Kharan Mighthammer? The dwarf that was supposedly watching over my baby girl!$B$B<The King sobs.>$B$BAnd now she's gone, $N!$B$BI have had my men turn the Steppes upside down. The only clue they have as to the whereabouts of my daughter is that she may be inside the Depths. For all I know, she could be dead!$B$BKharan is supposedly being held prisoner there... find him! I want answers!\030Travel to Blackrock Depths and find Kharan Mighthammer.$B$BThe King mentioned that Kharan was being held prisoner there - perhaps you should try looking for a prison.\030\030Kharan Mighthammer\0312,1,52,2,321,2,2784\0302,54,120,2,257,2,2784\0302,122,178,2,257,1,2784\0302,183,198,2,257,1,2784\0302,203,225,2,257,1,2784\0302,230,276,2,257,1,2784\0302,278,375,2,257,1,2784\0302,377,410,2,257,4,2784\0302,415,463,2,257,1,2784\0302,465,473,2,257,1,2784\0302,475,489,2,259,1,2784\0303,1,55,2,384,1,2784\0303,60,166,2,384,4,2784\0301,1,23,4,272,1,9021\0319021,2,2,Kharan Mighthammer\030371,2,3,Girl\0309021,2,12,Kharan Mighthammer\0312,1584,0,0,\0302,0,0,12,Blackrock Depths\0313701,19,3701,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304361,23,4361,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4342]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031As you can see, there was nothing I could have done.\030Please, hear me out before passing judgement!$B\030Listen as Kharan Mighthammer tells his story.\030Kharan's Tale\030Allow me to finish telling my story.\030Kharan's Tale\0312,1,45,2,257,1,9021\0303,1,45,2,384,1,9021\0301,1,52,4,272,4,9021\0305,1,36,3,256,1,9021\0304,1,13,3,384,1,9021\0319021,2,2,Kharan Mighthammer\0312,1584,0,0,\0314361,23,4361,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4343]="PARTIAL\031characters,consequences,loreConnections,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You apply two Cenarion plant salves to the windblossom. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.\030\030\030You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a windblossom plant. The berries that hang from the plant appear rotten and poisonous. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.\030Corrupted Windblossom\0311,1,55,4,272,1,0\0301,57,150,4,276,1,0\0304,1,85,3,260,1,0\0304,87,151,3,256,1,0\0304,153,233,3,258,4,0\031\0312,361,1448,0,\031\031OBJECT,174602,GIVER,?,9,Corrupted Windblossom\030OBJECT,174602,FINISHER,?,12,Corrupted Windblossom\030ITEM,11516,OBJECTIVE,2,15,",[435]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you for the aid, $N. I had feared Erland was overcome by the dangers of Silverpine. With your help, I see that he has not.\030The wolves outside won't leave, and they eye me evilly every time I step foot out that door.  They must be incredibly hungry to think I'm worth eating.$B$BI have to report to my teammate, the Deathstalker Rane Yorick.  And to get to Rane, I'll need help against those wolves.$B$BPlease escort me!  And there are a lot of wolves out there, so we'll have a better chance if you have friends who can help...\030Escort Erland through the wolves, to Rane Yorick.\030Erland must reach Rane Yorick\030Please be brief.  There is much danger about and we cannot stand idle in conversation.\030Escorting Erland\0312,1,92,2,257,1,1978\0302,95,151,2,257,1,1978\0302,156,217,2,257,1,1978\0302,220,275,2,259,1,1978\0302,280,296,2,257,1,1978\0302,299,404,2,257,4,1978\0303,1,49,2,384,1,1978\0301,1,26,4,272,1,1950\0301,28,89,4,272,