021\0301,1,42,4,272,1,2784\0312784,2,3,King Magni Bronzebeard\0312,1584,0,0,\0302,0,0,1,King Magni\0302,0,0,3,Ironforge\0302,0,0,3,King Magni Bronzebeard\0314341,19,4341,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304362,23,4362,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4362]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Princess Bronzebeard weeps over the loss of Emperor Dagran Thaurissan.>$B$BWhy???\030It would seem as if my old adversary, Dagran Thaurissan, has me and the kingdom of Ironforge at his mercy.$B$BYou may be my last hope, $N. You must rescue my dear daughter, Moira!$B$BThere is only one way to make sure that the spell Thaurissan has cast on Moira is broken: Kill him.$B$BAnd $N, do not harm her! Remember, she is being controlled by Thaurissan! The things she may do or say are a result of Thaurissan's evil spell!\030Return to Blackrock Depths and rescue Princess Moira Bronzebeard from the evil clutches of Emperor Dagran Thaurissan.$B\030\030The Fate of the Kingdom\0312,1,106,2,257,4,2784\0302,111,138,2,259,3,2784\0302,140,179,2,265,1,2784\0302,184,282,2,257,1,2784\0302,287,310,2,257,1,2784\0302,312,359,2,257,1,2784\0302,361,429,2,257,1,2784\0303,1,117,2,392,1,2784\0301,1,72,4,272,1,8929\0301,77,82,4,272,2,8929\0318929,2,8,Princess Moira Bronzebeard\0309019,2,8,Emperor Dagran Thaurissan\030330,4,9,Princess\0309019,4,9,Emperor Dagran Thaurissan\0312,1584,0,0,\0302,0,0,8,Blackrock Depths\0314361,19,4361,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304363,23,4363,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,9019,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Emperor Dagran Thaurissan",[4363]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<King Magni Bronzebeard is visibly upset.>$B$BIt seems that even in death, Thaurissan has won.$B$BYou are dismissed, $N. Before you leave, you may choose your reward from the royal vault.$B$B<King Bronzebeard slumps into his throne to mull over this bizarre change of events.>\030Thaurissan was a great and honorable dwarf. You ruined my life and the life of my unborn child!$B$B<You think that Princess Bronzebeard may still be suffering from the residual effect of the Emperor's spell.>$B$BReturn to Ironforge and tell my father that the heir to the Kingdom of Ironforge will be a Dark Iron dwarf.$B$BWhether he approves or not, it shall be.\030Return to Ironforge and speak with King Magni Bronzebeard.\030\030The Princess's Surprise\0312,1,43,2,257,1,8929\0302,45,95,2,257,1,8929\0302,100,208,2,261,1,8929\0302,213,319,2,257,3,8929\0302,324,363,2,257,3,8929\0303,1,58,2,384,1,8929\0301,1,42,4,272,1,2784\0301,47,94,4,272,4,2784\0301,99,120,4,272,1,2784\0301,122,187,4,272,1,2784\0301,192,276,4,272,1,2784\031330,2,3,Princess\0301051,2,4,Dark Iron Dwarf\0302784,2,6,King Magni Bronzebeard\0302784,4,7,King Magni Bronzebeard\0312,1584,0,0,\0302,0,0,4,Ironforge\0302,0,0,4,Kingdom of Ironforge\0302,0,0,6,Ironforge\0314362,19,4362,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[437]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031I heard of your successful raid against the rot hides, $N, and this essence is proof of Nightlash's death.$B$BThe Scourge have lost ground this day. Your value to the Forsaken grows.\030Our initial scouting reports of Silverpine show the rot hides have a base at an old farm to the north, the Dead Fields.  We have sent small assaults against them, but each time they are reinforced by the banshee Nightlash, who uses her magic to rout our forces.$B$BWe want Nightlash destroyed.$B$BGo to the Dead Fields and assault the rot hides.  If you don't see Nightlash then kill the rot hides until she appears, then defeat her.$B$BHer essence will turn to dust.  Bring me that dust as proof.\030Kill rot hide gnolls at the Dead Fields.$B$BWhen Nightlash appears, kill her.$B$BBring the Essence of Nightlash to High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher.\030Enter the Dead Fields\030Have you defeated Nightlash, $N?  Our success against the rot hides depends on her destruction!\030The Dead Fields\0312,1,119,2,257,1,1952\0302,122,261,2,257,1,1952\0302,266,293,2,263,1,1952\0302,298,345,2,257,1,1952\0302,348,433,2,257,4,1952\0302,438,467,2,257,3,1952\0302,470,497,2,257,1,1952\0303,1,40,2,384,1,1952\0303,45,77,2,384,1,1952\0303,82,153,2,384,1,1952\0301,1,106,4,272,1,1952\0301,111,148,4,340,1,1952\0301,150,182,4,272,1,1952\0305,1,32,3,256,2,1952\0305,35,95,3,256,1,1952\0304,1,21,3,384,1,1952\03114235,2,1,The Rot\0301983,2,2,Nightlash\0301983,2,3,Nightlash\03014235,2,4,The Rot\0301983,2,5,Nightlash\03014235,2,5,The Rot\0301983,2,9,Nightlash\0301983,2,10,Nightlash\0301952,2,10,High Executor Hadrec\03014235,4,11,The Rot\0301983,3,14,Nightlash\03014235,3,15,The Rot\0312,130,1421,0,\0302,0,0,4,Dead Fields\0302,0,0,8,Dead Fields\0302,0,0,10,High Executor Hadrec\0302,0,0,10,Sepulcher\0304,0,0,13,Forsaken\031438,23,438,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3622,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[438]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Heaped within this boat is a pile of wrapped corpses. And looking east across Lordamere Lake, an opposing dock on Fenris Isle can be seen.$B$BThe fate of the corpses must lie on Fenris Isle.\030$N, we've discovered a new hive for the Scourge: the Decrepit Ferry.  The ferry lies east of the Sepulcher, and is heavily patrolled by rot hides and other undead.$B$BThere must be a reason for the Scourge's occupation of the area.  Go to the Decrepit Ferry and find out why the Scourge are there.\030Go to the Decrepit Ferry.$B$BSearch for the reason the Scourge are there.\030\030The Decrepit Ferry\0312,1,68,2,321,1,1952\0302,71,163,2,257,1,1952\0302,168,231,2,321,1,1952\0302,234,297,2,321,1,1952\0303,1,25,2,384,1,1952\0303,30,73,2,448,1,1952\0301,1,53,4,272,1,0\0301,55,138,4,272,1,0\0301,143,190,4,272,1,0\031\0312,130,1421,0,\0302,0,0,2,Sepulcher\0302,0,0,4,Decrepit Ferry\03