ves,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031As quickly as it started, the Sparklematic 5200 comes to an abrupt halt. A simple \"ding\" is heard from the machine, and the mouth of the machine spirals upward. Inside the Sparklematic 5200 is a small box wrapped in a little bow. The machine would appear to wrap an object up after eliminating its grime-encrusted status. Even if the machine didn't work, at least the item is now wrapped in a pretty box.$B$BWell, there is one way to find out if it cleaned the item or not...\030\030\030\030The Sparklematic 5200!\0311,1,72,4,272,1,0\0301,74,160,4,272,1,0\0301,162,229,4,272,1,0\0301,231,321,4,272,4,0\0301,323,404,4,272,4,0\0301,409,475,4,272,4,0\031\0312,133,1426,0,\0314601,19,4601,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304603,23,4603,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,175084,GIVER,?,9,The Sparklematic 5200\030OBJECT,175084,FINISHER,?,12,The Sparklematic 5200",[4606]="PARTIAL\031characters,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031As quickly as it started, the Sparklematic 5200 comes to an abrupt halt. A simple \"ding\" is heard from the machine, and the mouth of the machine spirals upward. Inside the Sparklematic 5200 is a small box wrapped in a little bow. The machine would appear to wrap an object up after eliminating its grime-encrusted status. Even if the machine didn't work, at least the item is now wrapped in a pretty box.$B$BWell, there is one way to find out if it cleaned the item or not...\030\030\030\030The Sparklematic 5200!\0311,1,72,4,272,1,0\0301,74,160,4,272,1,0\0301,162,229,4,272,1,0\0301,231,321,4,272,4,0\0301,323,404,4,272,4,0\0301,409,475,4,272,4,0\031\0312,133,1426,0,\0314602,19,4602,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304604,23,4604,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,175085,GIVER,?,9,The Sparklematic 5200\030OBJECT,175085,FINISHER,?,12,The Sparklematic 5200",[461]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031There we are, it's open. Leave me here. I spent the best days of my life in this keep, and the thought of resting within its walls gives me comfort.$B$BBe sure to close the alcove tight - I don't want those Rot Hides to find me.$B$BOh, and take this. You've earned it.\030I know of a hidden niche within the keep that holds an item dear to Thule, and his old colleagues.  It also holds something you might find useful.  Take me there!$B$BThe alcove is in the southwestern tower of the keep, behind a dusty shelf.$B$BTake my body, but leave my boots.  They never fit me anyway...\030Take Alaric to the hidden alcove.\030This is the spot! Bring me closer...\030The Hidden Niche\0312,1,98,2,257,1,0\0302,101,146,2,257,4,0\0302,149,162,2,257,1,0\0302,167,240,2,257,1,0\0302,245,277,2,257,1,0\0302,280,306,2,257,1,0\0303,1,33,2,384,1,0\0301,1,24,4,272,1,0\0301,26,39,4,272,1,0\0301,41,148,4,272,1,0\0301,153,228,4,272,1,0\0301,233,250,4,272,1,0\0301,252,268,4,272,1,0\0304,1,17,3,256,1,0\0304,19,36,3,256,1,0\0314950,3,14,Spot\0312,130,1421,0,\0302,0,0,1,Thule\031460,19,460,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030491,23,491,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,1599,GIVER,?,9,Shallow Grave\030OBJECT,112888,FINISHER,?,12,Dusty Shelf",[4621]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Avast ye... Admiral $N!  Yer a pirate of pirates, lass!$B$BIt warms the cackles of me heart to give ye this hat.  Ye will ne'er find one like it anywheres, and all that gazes upon ye will see that yer an Admiral of the Bloodsail Navy!\030Listen close, sea dawg... the powers of Booty Bay is what keeps us Bloodsail from sailing wheres we like and taking whats we want as rights o' plunder.  Were ye to put a knife to Fleet Master Seahorn, we'd ne'er run afoul of a Booty Bay's vessel.  Were ye to put a knife to Baron Revilgaz, we'd ne'er face the law on their terms.$B$BIf ye are to be an honorary admiral amongst us - yes, ADMIRAL, you'll puts a knife to both of 'em as I've says.  Go now $g lad : lass;, and return to me once ye does the deeds.\030Slay Fleet Master Seahorn and Baron Revilgaz of Booty Bay, and then return to Fleet Master Firallon aboard the Crimson Veil off the coast of Stranglethorn Vale.\030Yer back already, ya blasted tar! Haves ye done as I've ordered? Fail us, and ye will be walkin' the plank.$B$BArrrrr...\030Avast Ye, Admiral!\0312,1,25,2,257,1,2546\0302,27,151,2,259,1,2546\0302,154,246,2,257,1,2546\0302,249,329,2,257,1,2546\0302,334,444,2,257,4,2546\0302,447,509,2,257,1,2546\0303,1,160,2,384,1,2546\0301,1,11,4,272,1,2546\0301,13,23,4,272,1,2546\0301,26,55,4,272,1,2546\0301,60,112,4,272,1,2546\0301,115,234,4,272,3,2546\0304,1,33,3,256,1,2546\0304,35,64,3,256,2,2546\0304,66,107,3,256,3,2546\0304,112,120,3,256,1,2546\0312487,2,3,Fleet Master Seahorn\0302496,2,4,Baron Revilgaz\0302487,2,7,Fleet Master Seahorn\0302496,2,7,Baron Revilgaz\0302546,2,7,Fleet Master Firallon\0312,33,1434,0,\0302,0,0,3,Fleet Master Seahorn\0302,0,0,4,Baron Revilgaz\0302,0,0,7,Fleet Master Firallon\031\031NPC,2496,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Baron Revilgaz\030NPC,2487,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Fleet Master Seahorn\030REPUTATION,87,OBJECTIVE,3000,16,",[463]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The roots and ferns speak well of you, small one. Although I have many names, I answer to only a few. But you may call me Rethiel.$B$BAnd you must harken...for these lands weep from festered wounds, and I would charge you to heal them.\030You've heard of the Greenwarden?  You're not looking for him, are you?  Well I say you're crazy if you are, but who am I to keep a fool from $ghis:her; death?$B$BIf you are seeking that beast, then I hear he is in the marsh, east of the road where it forks to Dun Modr.  He's lurking there among the crocs...and worse!$B$BAnd leave your money here.  You won't need it where you're going...and you don't want to chip ol' Greenie's tooth on your gold when he bites you in half, do you?\030Find the Greenwarden.\030\030The Greenwarden\0312,1,32,2,257,2,1239\0302,35,70,2,257,2,1239\0302,73,158,2,257,4,1239\0302,163,269,2,257,4,1239\0302,272,318,2,257,1,1239\0302,323,348,2,257,1,1239\0302,351,483,2,257,2,1239\0303,1,21,2,384,1,1239\0301,1,49,4,272,1,1244\0301,51,101,4,272,1,1244\0301,103,130,4,272,1,1244\0301,135,235,4,272,4,1244\031\0312,11,1437,0,\0302,0,0,4,Dun Modr\031276,23,276,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030276,24,276,UNKNOWN\031",[464]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well fought, $N. The Dragonmaws are not the same threat they were when they had dragons, but they're still fierce opponents.$B$BThe Dragonmaws are led by Nek'rosh, son of Nekros, who was the former head of the Dragonmaws years ago. Nekros used powerful magic to tame the Red Dragons, but when that magic failed him...the dragons were not happy.$B$BNekros was killed, and his son has vowed revenge against the dragons who slew his father.\030The Dragonmaw orc clan was all but destroyed by the end of the Second War, after they lost control of their red dragon pets.  The dragons were not very happy with their old masters, and fiercely hunted the Dragonmaws.  What few remained fled from Grim Batol and into the Mountains east of Whelgar's Excavation.$B$BNow they've gained strength, and have an encampment northeast of Menethil.$B$BWe want you to attack that encampment.  Gather and bring me their war banners as proof.\030Bring 8 Dragonmaw War Banners to Captain Stoutfist.\030Have you attacked the Dragonmaw encampment?\030War Banners\0312,1,124,2,325,1,2104\0302,127,217,2,257,1,2104\0302,220,310,2,257,1,2104\0302,315,388,2,257,1,2104\0302,393,430,2,263,1,2104\0302,433,479,2,261,1,2104\0303,1,51,2,388,1,2104\0301,1,16,4,272,1,2104\0301,18,124,4,276,1,2104\0301,129,231,4,336,1,2104\0301,233,344,4,272,1,2104\0301,349,437,4,274,1,2104\0304,1,43,3,260,2,2104\0312104,2,7,Captain Stoutfist\0312,11,1437,0,\0302,0,0,3,Grim Batol\0302,0,0,3,Whelgar's Excavation\0302,0,0,7,Captain Stoutfist\031473,19,473,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030465,23,465,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3337,OBJECTIVE,8,15,",[4641]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Another one of Kaltunk's recruits, hm?$B$BA sorry state of affairs we find ourselves in if this is the best the Horde can produce. No matter. By the time we think you're ready to leave the Valley, you'll be a proud $C of the Horde.\030Finally, you are of age, $N... of age to battle in the name of the Horde. To conquer for the glory of the Warchief.$B$BYes...$B$B<Kaltunk looks you over.>$B$BYou will do nicely.$B$BNo doubt you wish to find a great dragon or demon and strangle it with your bare hands, but perhaps it would be wise to start on something less... dangerous.$B$B<Kaltunk laughs.>$B$BReport to Gornek, he should be able to assign a task better suited to a young $c. You will find Gornek in the Den, to the west.\030Speak with Gornek. You recall Kaltunk marking your map with his location and mentioning that Gornek resided in the Den, a building to the west.\030The carapace of a scorpid isn't so thick that the strength of a determined $C will be deterred. Strike strongly and without doubt, and the scorpids should prove easy prey.\030Your Place In The World\0312,1,30,2,257,1,10176\0302,32,73,2,261,1,10176\0302,75,115,2,257,1,10176\0302,120,125,2,257,1,10176\0302,130,154,2,257,1,10176\0302,159,177,2,257,3,10176\0302,182,327,2,259,4,10176\0302,329,338,2,257,1,10176\0302,343,359,2,257,1,10176\0302,364,444,2,257,1,10176\0302,446,490,2,257,3,10176\0303,1,18,2,384,1,10176\0303,20,143,2,384,1,10176\0301,1,38,4,272,2,3143\0301,43,130,4,272,4,3143\0301,132,141,4,272,1,3143\0301,143,231,4,272,1,3143\0304,1,95,3,256,3,3143\0304,97,171,3,256,1,3143\03110176,2,5,Kaltunk\03010176,2,9,Kaltunk\0303143,2,10,Gornek\0303143,2,11,Gornek\0303143,2,12,Gornek\03010176,2,13,Kaltunk\0303143,2,13,Gornek\0312,363,1411,0,\0302,0,0,10,Gornek\0302,0,0,11,Den\0302,0,0,13,Den\031788,23,788,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030788,24,788,UNKNOWN\031",[4642]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh, most excellent, $N. This is most excellent.$B$BSuch a tale. Who would have thought the two would interact with one another in such a way... I will have to spend more time looking at the environmental issues that cause changes in these creatures.$B$BI will continue my research for now. Perhaps we will speak again soon. Until then, I wish you well.\030Here is some encased ooze created from the Felwood samples you recovered. Take the case to Un'Goro Crater and find a pure ooze... the primal variety will do nicely. When you get close enough, release the ooze in the case, and let us see what the two think of one another.$B$BAfter the experiment concludes, bring me a sample of whatever is left over. I will await you here in the Apothecarium.\030Bring a Merged Ooze Sample to Chemist Fuely in Undercity.\030How goes the experiment, $N? I will continue to study the samples you've recovered for me--I am starting to see why Lady Sylvanas is so interested in these creatures. If they are truly part of the Old Gods, then who knows how it can be used to our benefit.\030Melding of Influences\0312,1,73,2,257,1,10136\0302,75,129,2,257,1,10136\0302,131,164,2,257,3,10136\0302,166,271,2,257,1,10136\0302,276,350,2,257,1,10136\0302,352,393,2,257,3,10136\0303,1,57,2,384,1,10136\0301,1,23,4,272,1,10136\0301,25,47,4,272,1,10136\0301,52,63,4,272,1,10136\0301,65,143,4,272,4,10136\0301,145,249,4,272,3,10136\0301,254,289,4,272,3,10136\0301,291,323,4,272,4,10136\0301,325,352,4,274,3,10136\0304,1,28,3,256,2,10136\0304,30,166,3,256,3,10136\0304,168,256,3,320,4,10136\03110136,2,7,Chemist Fuely\03015065,3,17,Lady\0312,1497,1458,0,\0302,0,0,1,Felwood\0302,0,0,2,Un'Goro Crater\0302,0,0,6,Apothecarium\0302,0,0,7,Chemist Fuely\0302,0,0,7,Undercity\0314293,21,4293,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304294,21,4294,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12291,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[465]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You place some of the tinder on the catapult then strike a spark onto it.$B$BFlame erupts and quickly spreads!\030While you were fighting the Dragonmaws, we discovered more of their plans.$B$BNek'rosh has built catapults and aims to lay siege to Menethil!  And with the fighting in Dun Algaz, we're effectively blocked from reinforcements!$B$BYou need to take out those catapults.  They're in the Dragonmaw encampment.$B$BHere, take this tinder.  Fight your way to the catapults and light them with the tinder.$B$BAnd after you've done that, find and kill Nek'rosh.  We need to cut this Dragonmaw beast down...at its neck.\030Destroy the Dragonmaw catapults.\030The first catapult is before you. Will you set it aflame?\030Nek'rosh's Gambit\0312,1,74,2,261,1,2104\0302,79,141,2,257,1,2104\0302,144,225,2,261,1,2104\0302,230,266,2,259,1,2104\0302,269,304,2,257,1,2104\0302,309,331,2,257,1,2104\0302,334,396,2,261,1,2104\0302,401,451,2,257,1,2104\0302,454,508,2,259,1,2104\0303,1,32,2,388,1,2104\0301,1,73,4,272,1,0\0301,78,110,4,272,1,0\0304,1,33,3,256,1,0\0304,35,57,3,256,2,0\031\0312,11,1437,0,\0302,0,0,2,Menethil\0302,0,0,3,Dun Algaz\0302,0,0,5,Dragonmaw\031464,19,464,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030474,23,474,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,1609,FINISHER,?,12,Dragonmaw Catapult",[466]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You got the ore! Well done, $N! I'll get someone to work with this right away. Let's hope he doesn't blow himself up!\030I heard that a rare ore, incendicite, was found in the Wetlands, in a cave northwest of Algaz Gate.  Incendicite is volatile stuff and hard to use without blowing yourself up, but I'm sure if it's smelted the right way it could make cannon shells that pack a mighty punch!$B$BGet me incendicite ore and I'll find someone brave enough to experiment with it.$B$BOh, and to extract that ore from a vein you'll need skill in mining.  If you don't have it, then ... bring a friend who does to that cave!\030Bring 6 loads of Incendicite Ore to Pilot Stonegear in Dun Morogh.\030Where is that ore, $N?!\030Search for Incendicite\0312,1,99,2,257,1,1377\0302,102,272,2,257,4,1377\0302,277,356,2,257,1,1377\0302,361,428,2,259,1,1377\0302,431,460,2,257,4,1377\0302,462,498,2,257,1,1377\0303,1,66,2,384,1,1377\0301,1,16,4,272,1,1377\0301,18,31,4,272,1,1377\0301,33,78,4,272,1,1377\0301,80,117,4,272,3,1377\0304,1,23,3,256,2,1377\0311377,2,7,Pilot Stonegear\0312,1,1426,0,\0302,0,0,1,Wetlands\0302,0,0,7,Pilot Stonegear\0302,0,0,7,Dun Morogh\031\031ITEM,3340,OBJECTIVE,6,15,",[4661]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You pick up the petri dish with the slime sample in it. The only way to discern if the samples is pure enough is to open it and examine the contents yourself. Ideally you'll find a sample that fits Chemist Fuely's criteria.\030\030\030You take a sample of slime from Felwood and place some of it into the various tubes and beakers on the table. As things begin to boil and spurt, the slime changes colors. When the process slows down and the liquids calm, you see a small petri dish with your altered Felwood slime samples in it along with some other remnants.\030Testing for Corruption - Felwood\0311,1,55,4,272,1,0\0301,57,158,4,272,4,0\0301,160,223,4,272,1,0\0304,1,109,3,256,1,0\0304,111,170,3,256,1,0\0304,172,325,3,256,1,0\031364,4,1,Slime\03010136,4,3,Chemist Fuely\030364,3,4,Slime\030364,3,5,Slime\030364,3,6,Slime\0312,1497,1458,0,\0303,0,0,4,Felwood\0314293,20,4293,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,174848,GIVER,?,9,Testing Equipment\030OBJECT,174848,FINISHER,?,12,Testing Equipment\030ITEM,12230,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[467]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hello $N. You're here about the task I have, eh? It's good to see a young $R like yourself whose blood burns at the prospect of adventure!\030Pilot Stonegear loves his siege engine, as every pilot should!  And he's always eager to find new ways to improve his tank's firepower!$B$BHe heard rumors of a rare ore and is looking for someone to hunt it down for him.  If your boots are starting to itch, then find Stonegear at Steelgrill's Depot in Dun Morogh and see what he wants.\030Speak with Pilot Stonegear.\030\030Stonegear's Search\0312,1,62,2,257,1,0\0302,65,135,2,257,1,0\0302,140,220,2,257,1,0\0302,223,336,2,259,4,0\0303,1,27,2,384,1,0\0301,1,9,4,272,1,1377\0301,11,48,4,272,2,1377\0301,50,138,4,272,1,1377\0311377,2,1,Pilot Stonegear\0301377,2,5,Pilot Stonegear\03011045,4,8,Burns\0312,1,1426,0,\0302,0,0,4,Steelgrill's Depot\0302,0,0,4,Dun Morogh\031466,23,466,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030466,24,466,UNKNOWN\031",[468]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hello, $C! You're here for the scouting mission, are you? Very good!$B$BI hope your gear is in good condition, because this \"scouting\" mission has changed into something more messy...\030Mountaineer Rockgar is looking for volunteers for a mission through Dun Algaz and into the Wetlands.  $B$BIf you want to get your boots wet in that soggy county to the north, then speak with Rockgar at Dun Algaz.  Dun Algaz is north up the road, beyond the guard tower.\030Speak with Mountaineer Rockgar.\030\030Report to Mountaineer Rockgar\0312,1,100,2,257,1,1340\0302,107,212,2,259,4,1340\0302,215,269,2,257,1,1340\0303,1,31,2,384,1,1340\0301,1,10,4,272,1,1342\0301,12,57,4,272,2,1342\0301,59,68,4,272,1,1342\0301,73,183,4,274,3,1342\0311342,2,1,Mountaineer Rockgar\0301342,2,4,Mountaineer Rockgar\0312,11,1437,0,\0302,0,0,2,Dun Algaz\031455,23,455,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030455,24,455,UNKNOWN\031",[4681]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You've been a tremendous help here today; we now have a solid chance at unlocking the mystery of why these creatures choose to beach themselves on the cost of Darkshore. The idea that they might be fleeing the area around Teldrassil is disturbing. Should you come across others in your travels, please let me know. Our research here is but in its infancy.$B$BOn behalf of the Temple of the Moon, please accept this as thanks for the effort you have given. Thank you, $N!\030That beached creature is not an isolated incident here in Darkshore.  There are more along the coastline and even in the water.  I would like for you to investigate another one that we know of; this one was reported to be in the water due west of Auberdine, close to a sunken vessel.  Return to me with anything that you may recover that would aid our research.$B$BAlso, in your travels you may find other creatures.  By all means, if you should discover anything then please bring it to our attention!\030Recover the Sea Turtle Remains from the Skeletal Sea Turtle in the waters west of Auberdine, and then speak with Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde back in Auberdine.\030Once you have investigated the creature's remains in the water to the west of here, I should be able to file a proper report with the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus. Perhaps then we will be closer to discovering the reason why these unfortunate creatures choose to end their lives beached on the coast of Darkshore.\030Washed Ashore\0312,1,68,2,257,1,10219\0302,71,127,2,257,1,10219\0302,130,283,2,259,4,10219\0302,286,361,2,257,4,10219\0302,366,416,2,257,1,10219\0302,419,502,2,257,4,10219\0303,1,153,2,384,1,10219\0301,1,169,4,272,1,10219\0301,171,247,4,272,4,10219\0301,249,314,4,272,1,10219\0301,316,355,4,272,1,10219\0301,360,455,4,272,1,10219\0301,457,470,4,272,1,10219\0304,1,166,3,256,1,10219\0304,168,316,3,256,4,10219\03110219,2,7,Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde\0312,148,1439,0,\0302,0,0,1,Darkshore\0302,0,0,3,Auberdine\0302,0,0,7,Skeletal Sea Turtle\0302,0,0,7,Auberdine\0302,0,0,7,Auberdine\0303,0,0,14,Darnassus\0313524,19,3524,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12289,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[469]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hmm, this is from Einar, right? Hasn't delivered his skins to me in person for almost a week now. No doubt it's some differences with the wife!$B$BMaybe I'll have my wife go speak with Sida sometime...\030Greetings, traveler!$B$BDon't suppose you might be heading in the direction of Menethil, would you? If you're not, I'd suggest you stop there, it's a good place to purchase goods and even have a pint and relax.$B$BNow, if it just so happens that you're heading in that direction, I don't suppose you'd mind taking this bundle of crocolisk skins to James Halloran, the tanner?$B$BI'd do it myself, but my wife's been in quite a mood lately, and I'd like to put off facing her as long as possible.\030Deliver the Bundle of Crocolisk Skins to James Halloran, the tanner, in Menethil Harbor.\030Hello there, $C. Could I interest you in a pair of boots? Perhaps some newly cured skins?\030Daily Delivery\0312,1,20,2,257,1,2093\0302,25,99,2,257,4,2093\0302,101,210,2,257,4,2093\0302,215,375,2,257,4,2093\0302,380,495,2,259,1,2093\0303,1,88,2,384,1,2093\0301,1,31,4,272,2,2094\0301,33,97,4,272,1,2094\0301,99,143,4,272,1,2094\0301,148,201,4,272,4,2094\0304,1,16,3,256,1,2094\0304,18,57,3,256,4,2094\0304,59,89,3,256,4,2094\0312094,2,4,James Halloran\0302094,2,6,James Halloran\0302111,4,10,Sida\0312,11,1437,0,\0302,0,0,4,James Halloran\0302,0,0,6,James Halloran\0302,0,0,6,Menethil Harbor\0304,0,0,7,Einar\031\031",[47]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thanks for the dust, $N. Here's your cash, and...here is a token from associates of mine. You might find it useful...useful.\030The Kobolds in these parts sometimes carry Gold Dust on them.  I could really use the stuff - bring me a load of it and I'll give you the best price in town...best price in town!$B$BYou can find kobolds in the Fargodeep Mine to the south, and around the Jasperlode Mine to the northeast.\030Bring 10 Gold Dust to Remy \"Two Times\" in Goldshire.  Gold Dust is gathered from Kobolds in Elwynn Forest.\030Psst! You have that Gold Dust for me...for me?\030Gold Dust Exchange\0312,1,61,2,257,1,241\0302,64,178,2,257,4,241\0302,183,287,2,257,1,241\0303,1,52,2,384,1,241\0303,55,106,2,384,1,241\0301,1,24,4,272,1,241\0301,26,89,4,272,1,241\0301,91,124,4,272,4,241\0304,1,5,3,256,1,241\0304,7,46,3,256,2,241\031241,2,4,Remy \"Two Times\"\0312,12,1429,0,\0302,0,0,3,Fargodeep Mine\0302,0,0,4,Remy\0302,0,0,4,Goldshire\0302,0,0,5,Kobolds\0302,0,0,5,Elwynn Forest\031\031ITEM,773,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[470]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh, thank you, $N! I was afraid that it was lost for good!$B$B<She quickly empties the contents of the ooze-covered bag onto the ground, before scooping them up.>$B$BHm, I don't have much use for this anymore, but wash it off and I'm sure you could make use of it.\030On my weekly visit to Ironbeard's Tomb I was attacked by dreadful, dripping oozes! Naturally, I panicked.$B$BI threw my bag at one, but it didn't do anything! The ooze just sucked it right up... Luckily, it did give me enough time to get away.$B$BThe bad news is that I really need to get the contents of my bag!$B$BI don't know which ooze I threw my bag at; they all looked the same! Ironbeard's Tomb is northeast of here, near Dun Modr. Thank you so much!\030One of the oozes at Ironbeard's Tomb has Sida's bag, retrieve it and bring it back to her in Menethil Harbor.\030Did you find my bag?\030Digging Through the Ooze\0312,1,82,2,261,1,2111\0302,84,105,2,257,1,2111\0302,110,158,2,257,1,2111\0302,160,194,2,257,1,2111\0302,196,243,2,257,1,2111\0302,248,312,2,259,1,2111\0302,317,384,2,257,1,2111\0302,386,438,2,257,1,2111\0302,440,457,2,257,1,2111\0303,1,109,2,384,1,2111\0301,1,18,4,272,1,2111\0301,20,58,4,276,1,2111\0301,63,162,4,272,1,2111\0301,167,264,4,272,4,2111\0304,1,20,3,256,2,2111\031\0312,11,1437,0,\0302,0,0,1,Ironbeard's Tomb\0302,0,0,8,Dun Modr\0302,0,0,10,Ironbeard's Tomb\0302,0,0,10,Menethil Harbor\031\031ITEM,3349,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[4701]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Do not dwell upon her suffering, $N. The beast was corrupt - a product of dark magic. You have done the Alliance a great service and you shall be rewarded.\030You have no doubt seen the worgs which the Blackrock orcs command.$B$BIt is curious - no matter how many we destroy, their numbers never dwindle. My scouts have reported that the worgs are bred, trained, and ultimately exported from Blackrock Spire: capital city of the Blackrock orcs. You must travel to Blackrock Spire and discover the source of this menace. Discover... and destroy.$B$BGood luck, $N. May Cenarius protect you...$B\030Travel to Blackrock Spire and destroy the source of the worg menace. As you left Helendis, he shouted a name: Halycon. It is what the orcs refer to in regards to the worg.\030Have you discovered and dealt with the source of the worg menace?\030Put Her Down\0312,1,66,2,257,1,9562\0302,71,145,2,261,1,9562\0302,147,285,2,257,1,9562\0302,287,360,2,257,1,9562\0302,362,372,2,257,1,9562\0302,374,385,2,261,1,9562\0302,390,403,2,257,1,9562\0302,405,431,2,269,1,9562\0303,1,68,2,388,1,9562\0303,70,118,2,384,1,9562\0303,120,171,2,384,1,9562\0301,1,36,4,276,1,9562\0301,38,85,4,276,1,9562\0301,87,155,4,272,3,9562\0304,1,65,3,256,2,9562\0311765,2,9,Worg\03010220,2,10,Halycon\0301765,2,11,Worg\03010430,4,13,The Beast\0301765,3,15,Worg\0312,1583,0,0,\0302,0,0,3,Blackrock Spire\0302,0,0,4,Blackrock Spire\0302,0,0,9,Blackrock Spire\031\031NPC,10220,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Halycon",[471]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hmm... Don't suppose you'd be interested in becoming my apprentice, would you?$B$BHah! No, I'm just kidding. You're much too old, for one thing. Besides - from the looks of you, it would seem that you have other ambitions in life. Nonetheless, these are some fine skins you've procured, and I'll be able to put them to good use.\030I sent my apprentice out into the marshes to skin some of our famous giant Wetlands crocolisks. When he didn't return, I went out to look for him... Let's just say it wasn't a pretty sight.$B$BMidwife says he might pull through, but in the meantime I still need my skins!$B$B...If you'd like to kill a few more of the brutes, I wouldn't be opposed, after what they did. You'll find the crocs north up the coast, beyond the murloc hovels.\030Collect 6 Giant Crocolisk Skins and bring them to James Halloran in Menethil Harbor.\030My apprentice is like a son to me. It's going to be hard for him to live his life with only one leg.$B$BAh, $N, how goes it? Do you have my skins?\030Apprentice's Duties\0312,1,95,2,257,1,2094\0302,97,148,2,257,1,2094\0302,150,189,2,257,1,2094\0302,194,271,2,259,4,2094\0302,276,369,2,257,4,2094\0302,371,437,2,257,1,2094\0303,1,84,2,384,1,2094\0301,1,6,4,272,1,2094\0301,8,78,4,272,4,2094\0301,83,86,4,272,1,2094\0301,88,108,4,272,1,2094\0301,110,144,4,272,1,2094\0301,146,230,4,272,4,2094\0301,232,328,4,272,1,2094\0304,1,34,3,256,1,2094\0304,36,100,3,256,3,2094\0304,105,124,3,256,2,2094\0304,126,146,3,256,2,2094\031285,2,6,Murloc\0302094,2,7,James Halloran\0312,11,1437,0,\0302,0,0,7,James Halloran\0302,0,0,7,Menethil Harbor\031484,19,484,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3348,OBJECTIVE,6,15,",[472]="PARTIAL\031questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031What brave $C sends word from Menethil? Ah $N, they call you.$B$BYou bring hope to a hopeless situation. 'Tis good news indeed that young Harlo survived. While fleeing he received a grievous wound. We had but little time to send him on his way on the back of the only surviving steed with the regiment.$B$BBut now we face a perilous situation. Dun Modr has fallen and we are but a shadow of the great regiment we once were.\030Dun Modr has fallen to the Dark Iron Dwarves!$B$BMy wounds are grave, $c.  Most of the regiment was killed!  The Dark Iron thugs attacked us before we could regroup from the Thandol Span ambush.$B$BOur leader, Longbraid, sounded the retreat horn.  As we left the town I was hit by a stray axe in the back.  All went black.$B$BI awoke here in Menethil but I fear for my fellow soldiers.  Hope still burns within me.  Perhaps Longbraid is still alive!  See if you can find him near Dun Modr, $r!\030Search for Longbraid near the town of Dun Modr.\030\030Fall of Dun Modr\0312,1,45,2,257,1,2097\0302,50,73,2,257,1,2097\0302,76,107,2,257,1,2097\0302,110,194,2,269,4,2097\0302,199,246,2,257,1,2097\0302,249,305,2,257,1,2097\0302,308,322,2,257,1,2097\0302,327,385,2,257,1,2097\0302,388,414,2,257,3,2097\0302,417,449,2,257,4,2097\0302,452,493,2,257,4,2097\0303,1,47,2,384,1,2097\0301,1,39,4,272,2,1071\0301,41,61,4,272,1,1071\0301,66,104,4,274,3,1071\0301,106,153,4,272,1,1071\0301,155,197,4,272,1,1071\0301,199,302,4,280,1,1071\0301,307,343,4,304,1,1071\0301,345,423,4,336,1,1071\03111045,2,9,Burns\0305689,4,18,Steed\0304244,4,20,Shadow\0312,11,1437,0,\0302,0,0,1,Dark Iron Dwarves\0302,0,0,4,Thandol Span\0302,0,0,8,Menethil\0302,0,0,11,Dun Modr\0304,0,0,13,Menethil\031\031",[4721]="PARTIAL\031loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hard work is something I have great respect for, $N. Now we can move forward with our plans for Winterspring.\030Runners have returned from Winterspring with reports that there is a series of small caves in the southern area of Winterspring. It seems that there are wildkin situated in the area around these caves. If there is something valuable that they are guarding, I believe that this is the place we will find it.$B$BYou will find these to be more of a challenge than the previous types, $N. The creatures seem to have gone mad from exposure to the very thing that they strive to protect.\030Trull Failbane in Felwood wants you to hunt 10 Berserk Owlbeasts in Winterspring.\030You know your orders, $N.\030Wild Guardians\0312,1,128,2,257,1,10306\0302,130,201,2,257,4,10306\0302,203,306,2,257,4,10306\0302,311,384,2,257,3,10306\0302,386,481,2,271,4,10306\0303,1,81,2,386,1,10306\0301,1,52,4,272,1,10306\0301,54,109,4,304,1,10306\0304,1,25,3,256,1,10306\03110306,2,6,Trull Failbane\0312,361,1448,0,\0302,0,0,1,Winterspring\0302,0,0,6,Felwood\0302,0,0,6,Winterspring\0314741,19,4741,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,7454,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Berserk Owlbeast",[4722]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Another discovery for us to research - well done $N!  These remains will be properly studied once they get to Darnassus.  Please accept this small honorarium in exchange for the remains you have provided for our study.\030You find a corpse of a sea turtle that had beached itself on the coast of Darkshore some time ago.  It has been scavenged by the murlocs who have encamped themselves around the creature's remains.  Still, there appear to be some suitable samples left on the creature's remains that Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine might be able to make use of.\030Take the Sea Turtle Remains to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine.\030Hello $N - do you have any discoveries of creatures that have washed ashore to report on?\030Beached Sea Turtle\0312,1,98,2,257,1,0\0302,101,196,2,257,1,0\0302,199,346,2,257,4,0\0303,1,66,2,384,1,0\0301,1,52,4,272,1,10219\0301,55,120,4,272,3,10219\0301,123,218,4,272,1,10219\0304,1,89,3,256,2,10219\03110219,2,3,Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde\03010219,2,4,Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde\0312,148,1439,0,\0302,0,0,3,Auberdine\0302,0,0,4,Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde\0302,0,0,4,Auberdine\0304,0,0,6,Darnassus\0314681,19,4681,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,176190,GIVER,?,9,Beached Sea Turtle",[4723]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The bones you have are from gentle sea mammals that are known to inhabit the waters surrounding the base of Teldrassil. They had never been known to violently beach themselves like the threshers had been known to. Why would these creatures do this, I wonder? Well, perhaps the study of their remains will bear the fruits of knowledge that we seek.$B$BAgain, thank you for your aid. Please accept this honorarium from the Temple of the Moon.\030The remains of a giant thresher - much larger than one you'd expect to find in Darkshore - lie beached on the coast of the Mist's Edge.  How this creature came to be here is unknown; the group of murlocs that now feast off the carcass of it seem to be much too weak, even in large numbers, to have brought down the beast. $B$BWhile some of it has been picked clean, enough of it remains to take a sample for Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine to study.\030Take the Sea Creature Bones to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine.\030Hello again, $N! Are you here to report on another discovery?\030Beached Sea Creature\0312,1,135,2,257,1,0\0302,138,321,2,257,4,0\0302,327,452,2,257,1,0\0303,1,66,2,384,1,0\0301,1,119,4,272,1,10219\0301,121,213,4,272,1,10219\0301,215,258,4,272,4,10219\0301,260,347,4,274,4,10219\0301,352,381,4,272,1,10219\0301,383,440,4,272,1,10219\0304,1,16,3,256,1,10219\0304,18,61,3,256,2,10219\03110430,2,2,The Beast\03010219,2,3,Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde\03010219,2,4,Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde\0312,148,1439,0,\0302,0,0,1,Darkshore\0302,0,0,3,Auberdine\0302,0,0,4,Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde\0302,0,0,4,Auberdine\0304,0,0,10,Temple of the Moon\0314681,19,4681,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,175233,GIVER,?,9,Beached Sea Creature",[4724]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Rabid pups? Gizrul the Slavener? And you live to tell the tale?! Incredible! A tribute well earned!\030Some say the worg controlled by the Blackrock orcs are the creation of a supernatural force. Others say they are not true worg but instead a breed of demon dog, granted to the orcs by a fallen pit lord.$B$BThe truth is far less contrived but every bit as frightening. The worg of Blackrock come from Halycon and her mate. Halycon is the gigantic den mother of the worg. Her mate? Nobody has ever lived to tell the tale of that one.$B$BStrike at the heart of the worg. Destroy Halycon... and $N, watch your back.\030Slay Halycon, pack mistress of the Bloodaxe worg.\030With the pack mistress slain, we can begin to thin out the worg sentries of the Spire and eventually make some headway into the city.\030The Pack Mistress\0312,1,92,2,257,1,9081\0302,94,202,2,257,1,9081\0302,207,267,2,257,1,9081\0302,269,321,2,257,1,9081\0302,323,369,2,257,1,9081\0302,371,379,2,257,2,9081\0302,381,431,2,257,1,9081\0302,436,467,2,257,1,9081\0302,469,486,2,261,1,9081\0302,488,511,2,257,1,9081\0303,1,49,2,384,1,9081\0301,1,11,4,272,2,9081\0301,13,32,4,272,2,9081\0301,34,64,4,272,2,9081\0301,66,76,4,272,1,9081\0301,78,99,4,272,1,9081\0304,1,133,3,260,1,9081\0311765,2,1,Worg\0301765,2,2,Worg\0301765,2,4,Worg\03010220,2,4,Halycon\03010220,2,5,Halycon\0306788,2,5,Den Mother\0301765,2,5,Worg\0301765,2,8,Worg\03010220,2,9,Halycon\03010220,2,11,Halycon\0309696,2,11,Bloodaxe Worg\0301765,2,11,Worg\03010268,4,13,Gizrul the Slavener\0301765,3,17,Worg\0312,1583,0,0,\0302,0,0,4,Halycon\031\031NPC,10220,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Halycon",[4725]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I have heard of the kinds of carriages found on the back of the turtle you found. Those I do believe are naga carriages, used both in battle and in transportation of their supplies on to land. The markings on the box you found are of the naga; this would explain their invasive presence in far-northern Darkshore.$B$BI will send this box to Darnassus along with the rest of your discoveries. This is for you - thank you again for your assistance.\030More sea turtle remains lie beached along the coastline.  This particular set has an abandoned carriage attached to the turtle's shell.  Perhaps this creature was driven to the shoreline by unknown beings rather than beaching itself as some of the other remains suggested.  Greymist murlocs now make the remains of this creature their home, feasting off the carrion.$B$BIn the carriage, you find a box with strange markings on it; perhaps Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine can make sense of it.\030Take the Strangely Marked Box to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine.\030It is a pleasure to see you again, $N. We are making great strives in uncovering the mystery of why majestic sea creatures beach themselves on the Darkshore coastline, but with every question answered, two more are raised it seems.$B$BAre you here to offer us more aid in our research?\030Beached Sea Turtle\0312,1,56,2,257,1,0\0302,59,135,2,257,1,0\0302,138,272,2,257,4,0\0302,275,366,2,257,1,0\0302,371,495,2,257,4,0\0303,1,68,2,384,1,0\0301,1,81,4,272,1,10219\0301,83,192,4,276,4,10219\0301,194,313,4,272,4,10219\0301,318,391,4,272,3,10219\0301,393,446,4,272,1,10219\0304,1,38,3,256,1,1