\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Mau'ari can derive da juju for $N... Use da Cache of Mau'ari to cast dis upon yourself or your allies.\030\030\030In Winterspring, you will find large bears wit extremely thick hides. These Shardtooth bears gain much protection from what dey can withstand. If you wish ta gain the resistance against fire, bring me da E'ko you find from da Shardtooth.$B$BRememba, you must have the Cache of Mau'ari in your inventory if you want ta hunt for E'ko.$B$B\030Shardtooth E'ko\0311,1,36,4,272,1,10307\0301,38,102,4,272,1,10307\0304,1,69,3,256,3,10307\0304,71,142,3,256,1,10307\0304,144,237,3,258,4,10307\0304,242,332,3,258,4,10307\031\0312,618,1452,0,\031975,19,975,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12432,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[4804]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Mau'ari can derive da juju for $N... Use da Cache of Mau'ari to cast dis upon yourself or your allies.\030\030\030In Winterspring, you will fight great flying creatures called da Chillwind. These beasts possess da power ta wield frost magics. If you wish ta gain resistance ta frost, bring me da E'ko you find from da Chillwind.$B$BRememba, you must have the Cache of Mau'ari in your inventory if you want ta hunt for E'ko.$B$B\030Chillwind E'ko\0311,1,36,4,272,1,10307\0301,38,102,4,272,1,10307\0304,1,75,3,260,3,10307\0304,77,128,3,256,1,10307\0304,130,214,3,258,4,10307\0304,219,309,3,258,4,10307\031\0312,618,1452,0,\031975,19,975,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12434,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[4805]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Mau'ari can derive da juju for $N... Use da Cache of Mau'ari to cast dis upon yourself or your allies.\030\030\030In Winterspring, you will fight great creatures called da ice thistle yeti. These beasts move slowly, but dey are able to evade many blows from da protection their thick fur provides dem. If you wish ta gain da ability to dodge attacks, bring me da E'ko you find from dem.$B$BRememba, you must have the Cache of Mau'ari in your inventory if you want ta hunt for E'ko.$B$B\030Ice Thistle E'ko\0311,1,36,4,272,1,10307\0301,38,102,4,272,1,10307\0304,1,75,3,260,3,10307\0304,77,187,3,256,1,10307\0304,189,272,3,262,4,10307\0304,277,367,3,258,4,10307\0317458,3,3,Ice Thistle Yeti\0312,618,1452,0,\031975,19,975,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12435,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[4806]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Mau'ari can derive da juju for $N... Use da Cache of Mau'ari to cast dis upon yourself or your allies.\030\030\030In Winterspring, you have fought da large ice giants called frostmaul. Sheer power and force is at their disposal. If you wish ta gain da force of da frostmaul, bring me da E'ko you find from dem.$B$BRememba, you must have the Cache of Mau'ari in your inventory if you want ta hunt for E'ko.\030Frostmaul E'ko\0311,1,36,4,272,1,10307\0301,38,102,4,272,1,10307\0304,1,70,3,256,1,10307\0304,72,114,3,256,1,10307\0304,116,196,3,258,4,10307\0304,201,291,3,258,4,10307\031\0312,618,1452,0,\031975,19,975,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12436,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[4807]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Mau'ari can derive da juju for $N... Use da Cache of Mau'ari to cast dis upon yourself or your allies.\030\030\030In Winterspring, you will fight creatures of might dat seem to possess an innate magic ability. These wildkin can use strong magics. If you wish ta gain an increase in your intellect bring me da E'ko you find from any a' da owlbeasts you find der.$B$BRememba, you must have the Cache of Mau'ari in your inventory if you want ta hunt for E'ko.$B$B\030Wildkin E'ko\0311,1,36,4,272,1,10307\0301,38,102,4,272,1,10307\0304,1,95,3,260,4,10307\0304,97,132,3,256,1,10307\0304,134,247,3,258,4,10307\0304,252,342,3,258,4,10307\031\0312,618,1452,0,\031975,19,975,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12433,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[4808]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031That's no blanket! But what have we here? I letter from Tinkee? I wonder what she has to say...$B$BAh, she's studying in the Burning Steppes. That makes sense--that's a good source for dragonkin. Oh, but look! It says here that she needs some parts for a device she wants to build. I guess that's where I come in, eh?\030I have another favor to ask of you.$B$BMy initial study of the essence you collected shows that it might be possible to freeze dragon whelp eggs and preserve them!  I want to test this theory, but first I need specially made engineering components.  My colleague, Felnok Steelspring, can make them.$B$BHere, take this letter to Felnok.  It tells him what I need.  You'll find Felnok in Winterspring, in the town of Everlook.\030Give Tinkee's Letter to Felnok Steelspring.\030It's cold up here! I hope you brought me a blanket!\030Felnok Steelspring\0312,1,35,2,257,1,10267\0302,40,163,2,257,4,10267\0302,166,248,2,259,1,10267\0302,251,298,2,257,1,10267\0302,303,335,2,257,1,10267\0302,338,362,2,259,1,10267\0302,365,424,2,257,1,10267\0303,1,43,2,384,1,10267\0301,1,18,4,272,1,10468\0301,20,41,4,272,2,10468\0301,43,63,4,272,2,10468\0301,65,95,4,272,1,10468\0301,100,141,4,272,1,10468\0301,143,195,4,272,1,10468\0301,197,209,4,272,1,10468\0301,211,281,4,274,1,10468\0301,283,317,4,272,2,10468\0304,1,18,3,256,1,10468\0304,20,51,3,258,3,10468\03110468,2,4,Felnok Steelspring\03010468,2,8,Felnok Steelspring\0312,46,1428,0,\0302,0,0,5,Felnok\0302,0,0,7,Winterspring\0302,0,0,8,Felnok Steelspring\0304,0,0,11,Tinkee\0304,0,0,13,Burning Steppes\0314726,19,4726,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304809,23,4809,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4809]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031These are good specimens. They're packed with cold! Let me get some gloves on, then pack them along with the other things Tinkee needs...\030I have most of what Tinkee needs, but I'm missing one important component, and that's chillwind horns.  The horns of the chillwind chimaera in Winterspring are a concentrated source of cold, but only pristine, uncracked horns will do!  I'll need a supply of those to complete Tinkee's order.$B$BBring me the uncracked chillwind horns, and I'll prepare a package for Tinkee.\030Bring 8 Uncracked Chillwind Horns to Felnok Steelspring.\030Do you have the chillwind horns, $N?\030Chillwind Horns\0312,1,102,2,263,1,10468\0302,105,234,2,257,3,10468\0302,237,291,2,259,1,10468\0302,296,373,2,257,1,10468\0303,1,56,2,384,1,10468\0301,1,25,4,272,1,10468\0301,27,51,4,272,1,10468\0301,53,137,4,274,1,10468\0304,1,36,3,256,2,10468\0317448,2,2,Chillwind Chimaera\03010468,2,5,Felnok Steelspring\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,2,Winterspring\0302,0,0,5,Felnok Steelspring\0314808,19,4808,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304810,23,4810,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12444,OBJECTIVE,8,15,",[481]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Interesting, more machinations of the Kirin Tor, it would seem. This is a powerful artifact. It was used frequently by powerful wizards of the Kirin Tor to channel magical energies.$B$BThat they are delivering so many to Ambermill indicates that they must be undergoing a project of some magnitude.$B$BI will see if I can pierce their shields and ascertain their intent.\030Take the pendant to Dalar Dawnweaver, perhaps he can shed some light on the wizards' plans.\030Take the rune-inscribed pendant to Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher.\030Yes, $C? What is it?\030Dalar's Analysis\0312,1,91,2,257,4,2121\0303,1,69,2,384,1,2121\0301,1,63,4,272,4,1938\0301,65,92,4,272,1,1938\0301,94,181,4,272,1,1938\0301,186,298,4,272,1,1938\0301,303,370,4,272,4,1938\0304,1,8,3,256,2,1938\0304,10,20,3,256,2,1938\0311938,2,1,Dalar Dawnweaver\0301938,2,2,Dalar Dawnweaver\0312,130,1421,0,\0302,0,0,1,Dalar Dawnweaver\0302,0,0,2,Dalar Dawnweaver\0302,0,0,2,Sepulcher\0304,0,0,6,Ambermill\031478,19,478,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030482,23,482,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4810]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You brought them! Great! I'll get to work right away! Thanks a ton, $N!$B$BYou've been so helpful to me, I might need you for even more important tasks later...\030Ok, everything is prepared and packed and ready for transport!  Good luck in your journey, and make sure you tell Tinkee that she owes me!\030Bring Felnok's Package to Tinkee Steamboil in the Burning Steppes.\030$N! Did you talk to Felnok? Did you bring the components I need?\030Return to Tinkee\0312,1,62,2,257,1,10468\0302,65,138,2,257,1,10468\0303,1,66,2,384,1,10468\0301,1,17,4,272,1,10267\0301,19,24,4,272,1,10267\0301,26,53,4,272,1,10267\0301,55,71,4,272,1,10267\0301,76,160,4,274,4,10267\0304,5,27,3,256,2,10267\0304,29,64,3,258,2,10267\03110267,2,3,Tinkee Steamboil\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,3,Tinkee Steamboil\0302,0,0,3,Burning Steppes\0303,0,0,9,Felnok\0314809,19,4809,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304907,23,4907,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4811]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031So the crystal exists, $N? Fascinating... anyway, your task has been well executed; good work!$B$BWhat exactly is this crystal? This is but a single question in a sea of questions. Another question that comes to mind is why the moonkin would be drawn to this object? Is the crystal benign in nature, or does it hold a more sinister purpose?$B$BI have many more questions, but we're going to need to examine that crystal closely to get some answers.\030Hostile moonkin roam in ever increasing numbers to our east.  They once were thought to be gentle, almost mystical creatures.  While some continue to hold reverence for them, the safety of Auberdine forces me to keep a more realistic view.$B$BI've received reports that moonkin are being drawn to a large red crystal along Darkshore's eastern mountain range.  No one has any idea what that crystal is, or even if it really exists.  I want you to locate it over there and report back to me what you find.\030Travel east of Auberdine and look for a large, red crystal along Darkshore's eastern mountain range.  Report back what you find to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine.\030Locate the large, red crystal on Darkshore's eastern mountain range\030What do you have to report on that red crystal? Does it even really exist?\030The Red Crystal\0312,1,60,2,257,1,2930\0302,63,125,2,321,1,2930\0302,128,239,2,265,1,2930\0302,244,358,2,257,1,2930\0302,361,430,2,257,4,2930\0302,433,503,2,259,1,2930\0303,1,100,2,384,1,2930\0303,103,169,2,384,1,2930\0301,1,26,4,272,2,2930\0301,28,41,4,272,1,2930\0301,43,94,4,272,1,2930\0301,99,127,4,272,2,2930\0301,129,180,4,272,1,2930\0301,182,266,4,272,4,2930\0301,268,340,4,272,2,2930\0301,345,448,4,274,3,2930\0305,1,47,3,256,2,2930\0305,49,74,3,256,2,2930\0304,1,67,3,384,1,2930\03110158,2,1,Moonkin\03010158,2,4,Moonkin\0302930,2,8,Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea\03010158,4,14,Moonkin\0312,148,1439,0,\0302,0,0,7,Auberdine\0302,0,0,8,Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea\0302,0,0,8,Auberdine\0314812,23,4812,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4812]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have made it once more to the mysterious crystal. Removing the stopper on the tube of moonwell water, you gingerly pour the contents out over the top of the crystal. As the water cascades down its lattices, you see the opaque surface turn transparent...\030Use this empty vial and fill up on some moonwell water here in Auberdine.  Such potent magic should provide a clue as to the composition of the crystal.  To do that, you'll pour the liquid over the crystal; it should take care of the rest.$B$BWhile I don't anticipate anything bad happening to you, I still want you to be careful.  Above us to the east is Felwood; if that crystal is tied to that place as I suspect it is, then it could prove to be very dangerous.\030Fill the Empty Water Tube at the Auberdine moonwell, and then investigate the red crystal along Darkshore's eastern mountain wall.\030The crystal looks very alien against the wooded scenery of Darkshore. You think you hear a very slight humming coming from deep within it.\030As Water Cascades\0312,1,73,2,257,1,2930\0302,76,152,2,257,1,2930\0302,155,239,2,257,1,2930\0302,244,330,2,259,1,2930\0302,333,464,2,257,4,2930\0303,1,130,2,384,1,2930\0301,1,53,4,272,1,0\0301,55,169,4,272,1,0\0301,171,257,4,272,1,0\0304,1,69,3,256,1,0\0304,71,138,3,256,1,0\031\0312,148,1439,0,\0302,0,0,1,Auberdine\0302,0,0,6,Auberdine\0314811,19,4811,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304813,23,4813,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,175524,FINISHER,?,12,Mysterious Red Crystal\030ITEM,14339,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[4813]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well, it would seem that even though we know more about this crystal, more unanswered questions are the result!$B$BI'll take the information you've uncovered to the council here in Auberdine. Perhaps they'll know a course of action to follow on this crystal. Well, that is if there is one to be taken; for now, the threat remains far enough to our east to be out of harm's way.$B$BAs for you, please have this. Consider it a reward for a job well done, $N.\030The moonwell water has revealed that embedded inside the crystal are a few small fragments of bone, as well as half of a jawbone.  The jawbone appears to be from a humanoid, but it is unclear without breaking open the crystal - a feat that even the strongest of magic would find near impossible.$B$BWith the task at hand complete, all that remains is to report back to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine.\030Report back what you have found to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine.\030\030The Fragments Within\0312,1,129,2,257,1,0\0302,132,295,2,257,4,0\0302,300,407,2,257,1,0\0303,1,73,2,384,1,0\0301,1,111,4,272,4,2930\0301,116,191,4,272,1,2930\0301,193,258,4,272,4,2930\0301,260,377,4,276,4,2930\0301,382,410,4,272,1,2930\0301,412,456,4,272,1,2930\0312930,2,3,Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea\0302930,2,4,Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea\0312,148,1439,0,\0302,0,0,3,Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea\0302,0,0,3,Auberdine\0302,0,0,4,Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea\0302,0,0,4,Auberdine\0304,0,0,6,Auberdine\0314812,19,4812,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,175524,GIVER,?,9,Mysterious Red Crystal",[482]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ill news you bring, $N. If Dalar is correct--and I've no reason to believe he isn't--we must move quickly.$B$BI must confer with him on our plan of attack. But in the meanwhile we will have to delay their progress.\030Of course! How could I have forgotten?$B$BAmbermill was one of the sites earmarked by the Kirin Tor, noted because it houses a dormant ley energy node. The wizards must be planning to reactivate the node and use its energies for some greater purpose.$B$BWe cannot allow this to happen...$B$BIt will take a great amount of power to activate the area's ley energies, we can stall them by taking the pendants away from the wizards.$B$BRelay this information to Allister, he will decide a course of action.\030Speak with Shadow Priest Allister at the Sepulcher.\030\030Dalaran's Intentions\0312,1,10,2,257,1,1938\0302,12,38,2,257,4,1938\0302,43,151,2,259,1,1938\0302,153,250,2,257,1,1938\0302,255,287,2,265,1,1938\0302,292,428,2,257,3,1938\0302,433,502,2,257,3,1938\0303,1,51,2,384,1,1938\0301,1,23,4,272,1,2121\0301,25,106,4,272,4,2121\0301,111,155,4,276,1,2121\0301,157,214,4,272,3,2121\0312121,2,8,Shadow Priest Allister\030111,2,8,Priest\0312,130,1421,0,\0302,0,0,7,Allister\0302,0,0,8,Sepulcher\031481,19,481,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030479,23,479,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4821]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes, finally... the mysterious egg has finally been delivered to me. Now, let me take a closer look at this... What..! What is this..?$B\030A rumor has surfaced about an alien egg here in Thousand Needles. Those that report seeing this egg have failed to even get close enough to examine it in detail. Serpents guard the egg as if it's one of their own.$B$BI want you to seek out this alien egg and bring it to me so that I may examine it. Reports say the egg is located within a serpent den, but there are several serpent dens along the base of the cliff walls south and northeast of Freewind Post.\030Return the Alien Egg to Hagar Lightninghoof in Freewind Post.\030I must know more about this mysterious egg, who knows what will hatch from it.\030Alien Egg\0312,1,65,2,257,1,10539\0302,67,161,2,257,1,10539\0302,163,213,2,257,4,10539\0302,218,299,2,259,1,10539\0302,301,459,2,257,1,10539\0303,1,61,2,384,1,10539\0301,1,15,4,272,1,10539\0301,17,68,4,272,1,10539\0301,70,110,4,272,1,10539\0301,112,118,4,272,1,10539\0301,120,134,4,272,2,10539\0304,1,78,3,256,3,10539\03110539,2,6,Hagar Lightninghoof\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,1,Thousand Needles\0302,0,0,6,Hagar Lightninghoof\0302,0,0,6,Freewind Post\0314865,23,4865,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12467,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[4822]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Mmmmmmmmm! I love their strawberry ice cream! If there's one thing Tigule and Foror know to do, it's make ice cream!$B$BThank you very much $N - this is the best treat ever!\030ICE CREAM!  Oh please please please could you get me some ice cream?!  Strawberry is my favorite flavor, and there's no better strawberry ice cream in the world than Tigule and Foror's Strawberry Ice Cream!  It's my favorite ice cream in the whole wide world!$B$BI had it once a long time ago when I was at the Shimmering Flats race track, but I heard that they might be selling them in town now!  Please?  Pretty please?  With Tigule and Foror's Strawberry Ice Cream on top??!?!\030Get some Strawberry Ice Cream for your ward.  The lad seems to prefer Tigule and Foror's brand ice cream.\030I wish they'd make more flavors of ice cream other than strawberry, but I guess I'm lucky that strawberry is my favorite!\030You Scream, I Scream...\0312,1,10,2,257,1,14305\0302,13,69,2,257,4,14305\0302,72,206,2,257,1,14305\0302,209,259,2,257,1,14305\0302,264,396,2,257,4,14305\0302,399,405,2,257,2,14305\0302,408,421,2,257,2,14305\0302,424,479,2,257,2,14305\0303,1,44,2,384,1,14305\0303,47,105,2,384,4,14305\0301,1,10,4,272,1,14305\0301,12,45,4,272,1,14305\0301,47,116,4,272,4,14305\0301,121,173,4,272,1,14305\0304,1,121,3,258,3,14305\031\0312,0,0,5,Shimmering Flats\031\031ITEM,7228,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[483]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have succeeded, young $C! Well done. And just in time I might add.\030Gnarlpine invaders were seen ravaging the Ban'ethil Barrow Den to the west.$B$BThe slumbering druids will be trapped in the Emerald Dream for eternity, unaware of their fate, unless we help. The delicate hibernation ritual cannot be broken without the Relics of Wakening.$B$BJourney to the Den and retrieve the Raven Claw Talisman, Black Feather Quill, Sapphire of Sky, and Rune of Nesting. The druids store them in sacred chests.  Return them to me and I will prepare the awakening ritual.\030Retrieve the Relics of Wakening and bring them to Athridas Bearmantle in Dolanaar.\030$N, the kidnapped Druids of the Talon will be forever trapped in the Emerald Dream if we cannot retrieve the Relics of Wakening from the Ban'ethil Barrow Den to the west.$B$BFor every minute we delay their fate comes one step closer to eternal doom.\030The Relics of Wakening\0312,1,75,2,261,1,2078\0302,80,190,2,265,4,2078\0302,192,271,2,257,1,2078\0302,276,390,2,257,1,2078\0302,392,430,2,257,1,2078\0302,433,490,2,257,3,2078\0303,1,82,2,384,1,2078\0301,1,29,4,272,1,2078\0301,31,40,4,272,1,2078\0301,42,70,4,272,4,2078\0304,1,170,3,260,4,2078\0304,175,249,3,256,1,2078\0317605,2,4,Raven\0302078,2,7,Athridas Bearmantle\0312,141,1438,0,\0302,0,0,2,Emerald Dream\0302,0,0,4,Den\0302,0,0,7,Athridas Bearmantle\0302,0,0,7,Dolanaar\0303,0,0,11,Emerald Dream\0303,0,0,11,Ban'ethil Barrow Den\031476,19,476,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030486,23,486,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3405,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,3406,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,3407,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,3408,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[484]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Nice work you've done here, $N. The quality of these skins is superb. I'll have to get them into the curing process as soon as possible. Oh, but before I get to that, there's some other work I need done that I think you might be able to take care of.\030I'm James Halloran, the tanner. My cured crocolisk skins are sought after all over, shipments leaving by boat to ports around the world.$B$BMet Einar? He's one of the hunters that brings crocolisk skins in for me.$B$BI'm a bit short on the softer skins that come off crocolisk young.$B$BBeing that I'm running low, I'll pay you top coin for a stack of the skins. You can find the young crocs in the marshes right outside of town.\030Obtain 4 Young Crocolisk Skins for James Halloran in Menethil Harbor.\030$N, right? Do you have my skins?\030Young Crocolisk Skins\0312,1,31,2,257,1,2094\0302,33,136,2,257,1,2094\0302,141,150,2,257,2,2094\0302,152,213,2,257,1,2094\0302,218,283,2,257,1,2094\0302,288,362,2,257,1,2094\0302,364,429,2,257,1,2094\0303,1,69,2,384,1,2094\0301,1,31,4,272,1,2094\0301,33,69,4,272,1,2094\0301,71,136,4,272,1,2094\0301,138,250,4,274,4,2094\0304,1,10,3,256,2,2094\0304,12,32,3,256,2,2094\0312094,2,1,James Halloran\0302094,2,8,James Halloran\0312,11,1437,0,\0302,0,0,8,Menethil Harbor\031471,23,471,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3397,OBJECTIVE,4,15,",[4841]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031For my gratitude, this is for you, $N.\030$N, I entreat you to hunt these centaur down. They shall feel the wrath of our revenge. Attack the centaur camp to the north of Freewind Post!  Let wrath guide your hand!$B\030Kill 12 Galak Scouts, 10 Galak Wranglers, and 6 Galak Windchasers, and then return to Cliffwatcher Longhorn in Freewind Post.\030Come now $N, I know you haven't killed your share yet. Hunt them down, and I shall give you a reward for my gratitude.\030Pacify the Centaur\0312,1,45,2,257,1,10537\0302,47,87,2,259,3,10537\0302,89,142,2,261,1,10537\0302,145,170,2,257,1,10537\0303,1,125,2,384,1,10537\0301,1,38,4,272,1,10537\0304,1,54,3,256,1,10537\0304,56,118,3,256,3,10537\03193,2,1,Centaur\03093,2,3,Centaur\03010537,2,5,Cliffwatcher Longhorn\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,3,Freewind Post\0302,0,0,5,Cliffwatcher Longhorn\0302,0,0,5,Freewind Post\0314542,19,4542,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305064,23,5064,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,4094,OBJECTIVE,12,13,Galak Scout\030NPC,4093,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Galak Wrangler\030NPC,4096,OBJECTIVE,6,13,Galak Windchaser",[4842]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Yes, the demons there in Darkwhisper Gorge; I believe it is their presence that is affecting the land in this way. I am going to continue observing the hot springs here and see if I learn anything more.$B$BI'd wait until you are a bit stronger if you have plans of heading farther into Darkwhisper Gorge.\030To tell you the truth, although there are no volcanoes here in Winterspring, I believe that there are far more threatening reasons for these hot springs...$B$BWell, I think you'll want to see it for yourself. You'll need to travel the length of Winterspring, and head to the very south. When the air becomes thick and muggy, and the sky turns dark, you'll have found what I believe to be the source of the hot springs.$B$BHave a look. I'm sure you'll have many questions when you return.\030Follow Donova Snowden's instructions, then report back.\030Discover Darkwhisper Gorge\030The water in the springs seems to have some very odd properties... I am still unsure of what it means...\030Strange Sources\0312,1,155,2,261,4,9298\0302,160,208,2,259,1,9298\0302,210,286,2,259,1,9298\0302,288,418,2,257,4,9298\0302,423,434,2,257,1,9298\0302,436,487,2,257,1,9298\0303,1,55,2,384,1,9298\0301,1,114,4,272,4,9298\0301,116,202,4,272,4,9298\0301,207,304,4,272,4,9298\0305,1,66,3,256,4,9298\0305,68,104,3,256,1,9298\0304,1,26,3,384,1,9298\0319298,2,7,Donova Snowden\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,1,Winterspring\0304,0,0,8,Darkwhisper Gorge\031980,19,980,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[485]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You place the egg... distress beacon... inside the chicken... homing robot.$B$BHums and whirs are heard from inside the robot as it struggles to stand up. After the robot comes to life, Oglethorpe's voice is heard once more, but now from inside the robot:$B$B\"OOX-09/HL is working at least, but it needs major repairs! It is much too heavy for you to carry it... but I think I have an idea. Are you up for watching over it some more?\"\030You have uncovered some sort of strange, egg-shaped device made from metal.  Fiddling with one of its knobs springs the egg to life, as it opens up into some sort of gnomish robotic contraption!  A voice from inside the robotic egg crackles to life.$B$B\"My name's Oglethorpe Obnoticus, and my homing robot has crashed!  I will reward you for its recovery; please take this beacon to the robot!\"$B$B\"I now have computed the coordinates of the robot for you; it crashed at the head of the river near Skulk Rock!\"\030Take the distress beacon to Oglethorpe's homing robot at the head of the river in the Hinterlands, near Skulk Rock.\030You appear to have uncovered the wreckage of... a robotic chicken? The voice from within the egg crackles to life again:$B$B\"Yes, excellent work! This is indeed my homing robot, though my sensors indicate that it needs a jump start before it can fly back to Booty Bay for repairs. Go ahead and place the beacon inside the rover - the beacon will take care of the rest!\"\030Find OOX-09/HL!\0312,1,75,2,257,1,0\0302,78,194,2,257,1,0\0302,197,249,2,257,1,0\0302,254,318,2,257,1,0\0302,321,394,2,257,3,0\0302,399,510,2,257,1,0\0303,1,115,2,384,1,0\0301,1,20,4,272,1,7806\0301,22,39,4,272,1,7806\0301,41,61,4,272,1,7806\0301,63,75,4,272,1,7806\0301,80,154,4,272,1,7806\0301,156,255,4,272,1,7806\0301,260,318,4,274,1,7806\0301,320,362,4,272,1,7806\0301,364,390,4,272,1,7806\0301,392,434,4,272,2,7806\0304,1,47,3,256,1,7806\0304,49,66,3,256,2,7806\0304,68,120,3,256,1,7806\0304,125,145,3,256,1,7806\0304,147,280,3,258,1,7806\0304,282,369,3,256,3,7806\0317406,2,4,Oglethorpe Obnoticus\030620,4,10,Chicken\030620,3,19,Chicken\0312,47,1425,0,\0302,0,0,6,Skulk Rock\0302,0,0,7,Oglethorpe's\0302,0,0,7,Hinterlands\0302,0,0,7,Skulk Rock\0303,0,0,22,Booty Bay\031836,23,836,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,8704,STARTER,?,10,",[486]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031$N you have proven yourself a most worthy and able $C. A night elf who follows the path of honor as sure as you do is certain to find great glory in this world.$B$BMay the forest spirits protect you wherever your travels may take you.\030Now the time has come to save the Druids of the Talon. If we fail now, $N, they will be forever lost in sleep.$B$BI shall prepare the Relics of Wakening and perform the ritual. For my work to take effect, the cursed beast responsible for this horrible situation must be slain.  Only then will the ritual be complete.$B$BIt was Ursal the Mauler who meddled with our brethren's calling and it is Ursal the Mauler who must now pay so they can be freed.  Travel to Gnarlpine Hold in the southwest and slay him.\030Kill Ursal the Mauler and return to Athridas Bearmantle in Dolanaar.\030Our brethren cannot be awakened until Ursal the Mauler has been slain, $N.\030Ursal the Mauler\0312,1,54,2,267,1,2078\0302,56,110,2,261,4,2078\0302,115,176,2,257,3,2078\0302,178,276,2,261,1,2078\0302,279,316,2,257,3,2078\0302,321,449,2,257,1,2078\0302,452,506,2,257,1,2078\0303,1,68,2,384,1,2078\0301,1,54,4,272,1,2078\0301,56,160,4,272,1,2078\0301,165,234,4,284,1,2078\0304,1,74,3,260,1,2078\0312039,2,6,Ursal the Mauler\0302039,2,8,Ursal the Mauler\0302078,2,8,Athridas Bearmantle\0302039,3,12,Ursal the Mauler\0312,141,1438,0,\0302,0,0,7,Gnarlpine Hold\0302,0,0,8,Athridas Bearmantle\0302,0,0,8,Dolanaar\031483,19,483,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,2039,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Ursal the Mauler",[4861]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A severely damaged crate stands out among the rest of the destroyed belongings at the camp...\030Hey there, $Glad:lass;! I was chased from my camp in southern Winterspring by some bloodthirsty wildkin! Well, I suppose I got too close to something the wildkin were guarding.$B$BI barely managed to get away safely; I fear a buddy of mine wasn't as lucky. Would you mind braving the wildkin and heading to the camp? I really need my supplies, and I'd also like to get back the amulet I unearthed yesterday at the dig site.\030Locate Jaron Stoneshaper's wrecked camp and supplies in southern Winterspring.\030\030Enraged Wildkin\0312,1,23,2,257,1,10301\0302,25,104,2,257,1,10301\0302,106,176,2,257,1,10301\0302,181,256,2,257,1,10301\0302,258,316,2,257,4,10301\0302,318,423,2,259,1,10301\0303,1,78,2,384,1,10301\0301,1,93,4,276,1,0\03110301,2,7,Jaron Stoneshaper\0312,618,1452,0,\0314863,23,4863,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,175587,FINISHER,?,12,Damaged Crate",[4862]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031What a load! I mean, look at all those eggs! These should bring in a right few gold.$B$BAs promised, here's your own little critter. Don't get bitten!\030Believe it or not, there are people out there willing to pay for the most vile of domesticated beast!$B$BI'd sent Bijou into the Spire to try and collect some of those spire spider eggs but I haven't heard from her in weeks. Maybe you can help me out?$B$BI'll tell you what, $N. Go to Blackrock Spire and collect some spire spider eggs for me. Bring them back here and not only will I give you a little cash, but I'll even domesticate one for you!\030Travel to Blackrock Spire and collect 15 Spire Spider Eggs for Kibler.$B$BBy the sound of it, these eggs could be found near spiders.$B\030Are those spider eggs in your pack or are you just happy to see me?\030En-Ay-Es-Tee-Why\0312,1,101,2,257,4,10260\0302,106,224,2,257,1,10260\0302,226,251,2,257,4,10260\0302,256,278,2,257,1,10260\0302,280,343,2,257,1,10260\0302,345,447,2,257,3,10260\0303,1,70,2,384,1,10260\0303,75,133,2,384,4,10260\0301,1,12,4,272,1,10260\0301,14,44,4,272,1,10260\0301,46,84,4,272,1,10260\0301,89,132,4,272,1,10260\0301,134,150,4,272,1,10260\0304,1,67,3,256,2,10260\03110257,2,2,Bijou\03010374,2,2,Spire Spider\03014881,2,2,Spider\03010374,2,5,Spire Spider\03014881,2,5,Spider\03010374,2,7,Spire Spider\03014881,2,7,Spider\03010260,2,7,Kibler\03014881,3,14,Spider\0312,1583,0,0,\0302,0,0,5,Blackrock Spire\0302,0,0,7,Blackrock Spire\031\031ITEM,12530,OBJECTIVE,15,15,",[4863]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Approaching the wagon, it doesn't appear that there is much more here for Jaron. But, looking on the ground, you notice some crates that look undamaged, despite being half-buried in the snow.\030Looking around, you don't see much that Jaron could want here. However, you do notice that the crate you found has been smashed open, almost as if this was what the wildkin were after...$B$BLooking to the east, you can barely make out an abandoned wagon. Perhaps you might find Jaron's things there. It's worth a look.\030Find Jaron Stoneshaper's wrecked wagon.\030\030Enraged Wildkin\0312,1,62,2,259,4,0\0302,64,186,2,257,4,0\0302,191,254,2,257,1,0\0302,256,299,2,257,4,0\0302,301,318,2,257,1,0\0303,1,39,2,384,1,0\0301,1,80,4,272,1,0\0301,82,191,4,272,1,0\03110301,2,6,Jaron Stoneshaper\0312,618,1452,0,\0314861,19,4861,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304864,23,4864,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,175587,GIVER,?,9,Damaged Crate\030OBJECT,175586,FINISHER,?,12,Jaron's Wagon",[4864]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well, I expected to hear as much, lad. I figured that the crazed beasts destroyed all of my belongings...$B$BBut you did find my tools, and most importantly, the amulet! I wonder why the wildkin so fiercely defended this item... In any case, I'll think twice before heading their way again!\030After inspecting the contents of the box, you decide that Jaron could make use of the tools and other items inside. However, there is no sign of the amulet.$B$BIt appears that the wildkin inhabit the lands to the north and east of here, so you decide that the next step is to face the creatures and reclaim the amulet from them.\030Pick up Jaron's Supplies from the snow, then find the wildkin that stole the amulet Jaron spoke of.$B$BBring Jaron's Supplies and the Blue-feathered Amulet to Jaron Stoneshaper at the lodge in Winterspring.\030Aye... Tell me the news.\030Enraged Wildkin\0312,1,115,2,257,4,0\0302,117,156,2,257,1,0\0302,161,328,2,257,1,0\0303,1,99,2,384,1,0\0303,104,206,2,384,1,0\0301,1,38,4,272,1,10301\0301,40,105,4,276,1,10301\0301,110,169,4,272,1,10301\0301,171,228,4,272,1,10301\0301,230,290,4,272,1,10301\0304,1,6,3,256,1,10301\0304,8,24,3,256,1,10301\03110301,2,5,Jaron Stoneshaper\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,5,Jaron Stoneshaper\0302,0,0,5,Winterspring\0314863,19,4863,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,175586,GIVER,?,9,Jaron's Wagon\030ITEM,12525,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,12524,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[4865]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Vengeance! So, the legend of Arikara is true. Indeed, this is a problem that must be resolved immediately.\030If I did not see that with my own eyes I would never have believed it to be true. Vengeance has come to Thousand Needles!$B$B<Hagar wipes his brow.>$B$B$N, you must act quickly! Go now and seek out Motega Firemane; he is located at Whitereach Post just northwest of Freewind Post along the road. He will know what to do!\030Report your findings to Motega Firemane.\030\030Serpent Wild\0312,1,81,2,257,4,10539\0302,83,121,2,259,1,10539\0302,126,148,2,257,1,10539\0302,153,177,2,257,1,10539\0302,179,295,2,259,1,10539\0302,297,320,2,257,3,10539\0303,1,40,2,384,1,10539\0301,1,10,4,274,1,10428\0301,12,45,4,272,1,10428\0301,47,106,4,276,1,10428\03110428,2,5,Motega Firemane\03010428,2,7,Motega Firemane\03010882,4,9,Arikara\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,2,Thousand Needles\0302,0,0,5,Whitereach Post\0302,0,0,7,Motega Firemane\0314821,19,4821,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305062,23,5062,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[4866]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031This is gonna make the best ale yet!$B$BEh, what did you think I was gonna use this for? Poison or something??$B$BCrazy kids...\030It's probably one of the most potent poisons in the world, $r!$B$BI've overheard the Blackrock speaking about its lethality in my jaunts into the Spire. They call it 'Mother's Milk', named after Mother Smolderweb, the big nasty spider in the Skitterweb cave.$B$BNow here's what I need from you: A live sample of the Milk, flowing through YOUR veins. Just bringing me the gland won't be enough! Get her to poison you and come back to me!$B$BThen... I get to milk ya!$B$B<Rubs his hands together in anticipation.>\030In the heart of Blackrock Spire you will find Mother Smolderweb. Engage her and get her to poison you. Chances are good that you will have to kill her as well. Return to Ragged John when you are poisoned so that he can 'milk' you.\030Milked\030<Ragged John pinches you.>\030Mother's Milk\0312,1,62,2,257,1,9563\0302,67,152,2,257,1,9563\0302,154,258,2,257,1,9563\0302,263,349,2,259,1,9563\0302,351,393,2,257,1,9563\0302,395,436,2,261,1,9563\0302,441,447,2,257,1,9563\0302,449,465,2,257,1,9563\0302,470,511,2,257,1,9563\0303,1,64,2,384,3,9563\0303,66,102,2,388,1,9563\0303,104,159,2,384,3,9563\0303,161,230,2,390,1,9563\0301,1,36,4,272,1,9563\0301,41,88,4,272,2,9563\0301,90,110,4,276,2,9563\0301,115,127,4,272,1,9563\0305,1,26,3,256,1,9563\0304,1,6,3,384,1,9563\03110596,2,3,Mother Smolderweb\03014881,2,3,Spider\03010596,2,10,Mother Smolderweb\0309563,2,13,Ragged John\030806,2,13,John\0309563,3,18,Ragged John\030806,3,18,John\0312,1583,0,0,\0302,0,0,3,Skitterweb\0302,0,0,13,Ragged John\031\031",[4867]="PARTIAL\031loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Aha! I can already feel my powers returning to me. And my mind is no longer wracked by Urok's curse.$B$BThank you, $N! Humility is below me, but I must acknowledge your aid.$B$BAnd I bid you fortune in your journeys through Blackrock Spire. You are a fool to think you could make your way to the top, but your bravery is without question.\030Argh!  So hard to speak!$B$BTake this note!  Get me my mojo!\030Read Warosh's Scroll.  Bring Warosh's Mojo to Warosh.\030Ah! Do you have my mojo?\030Urok Doomhowl\0312,1,5,2,257,1,10799\0302,8,24,2,257,1,10799\0302,29,43,2,257,1,10799\0302,46,60,2,257,1,10799\0303,1,21,2,384,1,10799\0303,24,53,2,384,1,10799\0301,1,4,4,272,1,10799\0301,6,50,4,272,1,10799\0301,52,100,4,308,1,10799\0301,105,118,4,272,1,10799\0301,120,173,4,272,1,10799\0301,178,240,4,272,1,10799\0301,242,338,4,272,4,10799\0304,5,24,3,256,2,10799\03110799,2,6,Warosh\0312,1583,0,0,\0302,0,0,6,Warosh\031\031ITEM,12712,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[487]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have served the good people of Dolanaar and Darnassus well, brave $C. As a member of the Sentinel force of Teldrassil I salute your efforts.\030The road to Darnassus must be kept safe.  Travelers heading from Dolanaar to Darnassus have been reporting ruthless attacks by corrupted furbolgs from the Gnarlpine tribe.$B$BImportant news and commerce travels to and from Darnassus by way of this road daily.  We cannot afford to have a rogue band of heathens terrorizing people.$B$BTake up arms in the name of the sacred forest, $c.  Their den lies somewhere below this vantage point.  Slay 6 of these Gnarlpine ambushers and report back to me.\030Slay 6 Gnarlpine Ambushers and return to Sentinel Amara Nightwalker outside of Dolanaar.\030The road is still not safe, $c. Travel forth and slay 6 Gnarlpine Ambushers and return to me.\030The Road to Darnassus\0312,1,40,2,257,1,2151\0302,43,171,2,261,1,2151\0302,176,259,2,257,1,2151\0302,262,330,2,257,1,2151\0302,335,384,2,257,1,2151\0302,387,436,2,257,1,2151\0302,439,496,2,257,1,2151\0303,1,88,2,384,1,2151\0301,1,73,4,272,1,2151\0301,75,144,4,272,1,2151\0304,1,31,3,256,1,2151\0304,33,93,3,256,1,2151\031\0312,141,1438,0,\0302,0,0,1,Darnassus\0302,0,0,2,Dolanaar\0302,0,0,2,Darnassus\0302,0,0,2,Gnarlpine\0302,0,0,3,Darnassus\0302,0,0,8,Sentinel Amara Nightwalker\031\031NPC,2152,OBJECTIVE,6,13,Gnarlpine Ambusher",[488]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ha ha! Well, done indeed.$B$BWho would have ever guessed that I, Zenn Foulhoof, would have a $R to do my bidding? Certainly not me! But so it goes... this beloved world of ours is full of surprises.$B$BThree cheers for the naive and gullible!\030Eager for work, I see.  Lucky for you a day never goes by that I don't wish I had a fledgling $c to perform my bidding.$B$BYou see, $N, I can make you very happy and provide you with things you never dreamed of having.  But in order for that to happen you must bring me certain items.$B$BMy business in the forest often requires certain. . .reagents.  Fetch for me 3 Nightsaber Fangs, 3 Strigid Owl Feathers and 3 swatches of Webwood Spider Silk.$B$BLet's keep this our little secret, $r.\030Bring Zenn Foulhoof outside of Dolanaar 3 Nightsaber Fangs, 3 Strigid Owl Feathers and 3 swatches of Webwood Spider Silk.\030Have you been a busy little bee, $N? I've been waiting for you to bring me what I need.\030Zenn's Bidding\0312,1,22,2,257,1,2150\0302,25,119,2,257,3,2150\0302,124,218,2,257,1,2150\0302,221,284,2,257,1,2150\0302,289,337,2,257,1,2150\0302,341,350,2,257,1,2150\0302,353,446,2,257,1,2150\0302,451,488,2,257,1,2150\0303,1,121,2,384,1,2150\0301,8,25,4,272,1,2150\0301,30,113,4,272,4,2150\0301,115,131,4,272,1,2150\0301,133,149,4,272,1,2150\0301,151,198,4,272,1,2150\0301,203,242,4,272,1,2150\0304,1,36,3,256,2,2150\0304,38,87,3,258,1,2150\0312042,2,7,Nightsaber\0301995,2,7,Strigid Owl\0301986,2,7,Webwood Spider\03014881,2,7,Spider\0302150,2,9,Zenn Foulhoof\0302042,2,9,Nightsaber\0301995,2,9,Strigid Owl\0301986,2,9,Webwood Spider\03014881,2,9,Spider\0302150,4,11,Zenn Foulhoof\0312,141,1438,0,\031489,23,489,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3409,OBJECTIVE,3,15,\030ITEM,3411,OBJECTIVE,3,15,\030ITEM,3412,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[4881]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031They come to kill me? I will show them how a Tauren fights!\030The Tauren, Kanati Greycloud is bold to set up a hunting camp in Thousand Needles. We must kill him to rid this hunting camp and all who may follow him. We will converge at the small post Southwest of the Great Lift.$B\030Warn Kanati Greycloud at Whitereach Post of the plot to kill him.\030\030Assassination Plot\0312,1,82,2,257,1,0\0302,84,152,2,257,1,0\0302,154,216,2,257,3,0\0303,1,65,2,384,1,0\0301,1,21,4,272,2,10638\0301,23,59,4,272,3,10638\03110638,2,1,Kanati Greycloud\03010638,2,4,Kanati Greycloud\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,1,Thousand Needles\0302,0,0,4,Whitereach Post of the\0314966,23,4966,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12564,STARTER,?,10,",[4882]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031An important discovery?\030You are unsure of the significance of the necklace that fell from the neck of the recently-slain wildkin. It glows brightly, slowly fading in and out.$B$BTrull Failbane might be able to tell you more, since his knowledge of the wildkin seems extensive. Perhaps you should ask him about it.\030Take the Blue-feathered Necklace to Trull Failbane at Bloodvenom Post.\030Reporting for another assignment?\030Guarding Secrets\0312,1,105,2,261,1,0\0302,107,150,2,257,1,0\0302,155,252,2,257,4,0\0302,254,289,2,257,4,0\0303,1,70,2,384,1,0\0301,1,23,4,272,2,10306\0304,1,33,3,256,2,10306\03110306,2,3,Trull Failbane\03010306,2,5,Trull Failbane\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,5,Trull Failbane\0302,0,0,5,Bloodvenom Post\0314883,23,4883,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12558,STARTER,?,10,",[4883]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The energy of this necklace, $N. I believe that it has only one source.$B$B<Nara closes her eyes and is quiet for a moment.>$B$BThe wildkin, now misguided and confused, were once not so. They once had a purpose, and were guided to serve. The night elf goddess Elune created these creatures to guard her most sacred areas.$B$BWhile this fact may seem like it holds little value; I urge you to look deeper.$B$BYou will learn, in time. Thank you for bringing this to me, $N.\030While I do possess much knowledge about the owlbeasts you defeated in Winterspring, I am not very learned on the subject of the magics they wield. But I do believe I know of one that would be able to examine the necklace and most likely tell you what it is.$B$BNara Wildmane in Thunder Bluff is an expert in this field; see her. Good luck, $N.\030Take the Blue-feathered Necklace to Nara Wildmane.\030How may I help you, $N?\030Guarding Secrets\0312,1,146,2,257,1,10306\0302,148,257,2,257,4,10306\0302,262,328,2,257,1,10306\0302,330,343,2,257,1,10306\0303,1,50,2,384,1,10306\0301,1,32,4,272,1,5770\0301,34,71,4,272,4,5770\0301,76,124,4,272,1,5770\0301,129,186,4,272,1,5770\0301,188,237,4,272,1,5770\0301,239,321,4,272,1,5770\0301,326,404,4,272,4,5770\0301,409,432,4,272,3,5770\0301,434,471,4,272,1,5770\0304,1,23,3,256,2,5770\0315770,2,3,Nara Wildmane\0305770,2,5,Nara Wildmane\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,1,Winterspring\0302,0,0,3,Thunder Bluff\0302,0,0,5,Nara Wildmane\0314882,19,4882,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[489]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, what a sweet $R! I knew you would come in handy!\030The Council of the Forest has news that you aided Zenn Foulhoof. The satyr is an enemy of the forest. As a $r, you should know better than to defile the forest by killing Nature's creatures.$B$BYou must redeem yourself in the eyes of the Council if you wish to remain a friend of Teldrassil.$B$BTeach Foulhoof a lesson and you shall be redeemed. Fel Cones are corrupted seeds that fall from the trees. They billow with green smoke.$B$BGive some to Foulhoof. He'll think you have brought him a harmless snack.\030Collect 3 Fel Cones and give them to Zenn Foulhoof outside of Dolanaar.\030What do you have for me, $N? A lovely snack I presume?\030Seek Redemption!\0312,1,64,2,257,1,2083\0302,66,101,2,261,1,2083\0302,103,190,2,257,1,2083\0302,195,291,2,259,4,2083\0302,296,345,2,257,3,2083\0302,347,401,2,261,1,2083\0302,403,431,2,257,1,2083\0302,436,457,2,257,1,2083\0302,459,508,2,257,1,2083\0303,1,71,2,384,1,2083\0301,1,20,4,272,1,2150\0301,22,52,4,272,4,2150\0304,1,28,3,256,2,2150\0304,30,54,3,256,2,2150\0312150,2,1,Zenn Foulhoof\0302150,2,10,Zenn Foulhoof\0312,141,1438,0,\0302,0,0,8,Foulhoof\0302,0,0,10,Zenn Foulhoof\031488,19,488,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3418,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[49]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hiccup! Ho ho!\030Amber is the hue of my life's longest love$BLike the last embers of dusk in the sky above$BRetrieve for me so that my love shall be born$BOne sack of each: barley, rye and corn.\030Grimbooze Thunderbrew wants a Sack of Barley, a Sack of Rye and a Sack of Corn.\030Encore? Well, sure!$B$BAmber is the hue of my life's longest love$BLike the last embers of dusk in the sky above$BRetrieve for me so that my love shall be born$BOne sack of each: barley, rye and corn.\030Sweet Amber\0312,1,42,2,257,1,239\0302,45,89,2,257,1,239\0302,92,136,2,259,3,239\0302,139,177,2,257,1,239\0303,1,79,2,386,1,239\0301,1,7,4,272,1,239\0304,1,7,3,256,2,239\0304,9,19,3,256,1,239\0304,24,65,3,256,1,239\0304,68,112,3,256,1,239\0304,115,159,3,258,3,239\0304,162,200,3,256,1,239\031239,2,5,Grimbooze Thunderbrew\0312,40,1436,0,\03148,19,48,NO_