0302,171,215,2,257,1,288\0302,220,314,2,257,1,288\0303,1,22,2,384,1,288\0301,1,33,4,274,2,272\0301,35,81,4,272,4,272\031272,2,4,Chef Grual\0307605,2,4,Raven\0306827,2,4,Crab\030272,2,5,Chef Grual\0306827,4,6,Crab\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,4,Scarlet Raven Tavern\0302,0,0,4,Darkshire\03193,23,93,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[50]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hiccup! Ho ho!\030I'll mix and mix till we have a mash$BFor this will be our own private stash$BA still must be fashioned of metal strong$BBring me some Truesilver so I can finish this song.\030Grimbooze Thunderbrew wants Truesilver.\030An encore for you? Well sure friend!$B$BI'll mix and mix till we have a mash$BFor this will be our own private stash$BA still must be fashioned of metal strong$BBring me some Truesilver so I can finish this song.\030Sweet Amber\0312,1,36,2,257,1,239\0302,39,76,2,257,3,239\0302,79,119,2,257,1,239\0302,122,172,2,257,1,239\0303,1,39,2,386,1,239\0301,1,7,4,272,1,239\0304,1,18,3,256,2,239\0304,20,36,3,256,1,239\0304,41,76,3,256,1,239\0304,79,116,3,256,3,239\0304,119,159,3,256,1,239\0304,162,212,3,256,1,239\031239,2,5,Grimbooze Thunderbrew\0312,40,1436,0,\03149,19,49,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\03051,23,51,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6037,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[500]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very good, $N You must have hacked through a whole mess of ogres to get all these knucklebones.$B$BThat should keep them out of our hair. At least, for a while.\030Crushridge ogres have dug an ogre mound up in the Alterac Mountains near the ruined city of Alterac.  And my scouts tell me they've taken over those ruins as well.$B$BWe can't let them get cozy up there; if they think they're safe where they are, then their next step will be to move down into the foothills, which will put them right at our front door!$B$BGo north to the Alterac Mountains and hunt ogres.  Bring me the Dirty Knucklebones they carry and you will earn a nice bounty.\030Gather 9 Dirty Knucklebones from Crushridge ogres in the Alterac Mountains.  Bring them to Marshal Redpath in Southshore.\030$N, are you still hunting ogres? Do you have the knucklebones I had you gather?\030Crushridge Bounty\0312,1,100,2,257,1,2263\0302,103,163,2,321,1,2263\0302,168,353,2,257,4,2263\0302,358,406,2,257,1,2263\0302,409,483,2,257,3,2263\0303,1,75,2,384,1,2263\0303,78,121,2,384,1,2263\0301,1,95,4,272,1,2263\0301,100,137,4,272,1,2263\0301,139,160,4,272,1,2263\0304,1,32,3,256,2,2263\0304,34,79,3,256,2,2263\031211,2,1,Ogre\0302263,2,7,Marshal Redpath\0312,36,1416,0,\0302,0,0,1,Alterac Mountains\0302,0,0,4,Alterac Mountains\0302,0,0,6,Crushridge\0302,0,0,6,Alterac Mountains\0302,0,0,7,Marshal Redpath\0302,0,0,7,Southshore\031504,23,504,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,2843,OBJECTIVE,9,15,",[5001]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well I'll be! Where were they??\030Ordinarily I don't deal with $rs but it seems that I'm stuck between a troll and a hard place. You see, my mission here is one of utmost importance to the Horde. The information I've discovered, however, applies to the well being of the Alliance as well. Now believe me, I'm no Alliance sympathizer, but the Blackrock threat is bigger than just a bunch of orcs.$B$BYou help me out by finding my belongings and I'll help you out with some information that could prove useful to your kind.$B$BDeal?\030Find Bijou's Belongings and return them to her. Good luck!$B\030Any luck?\030Bijou's Belongings\0312,1,94,2,257,4,10257\0302,96,161,2,257,1,10257\0302,163,254,2,257,1,10257\0302,256,361,2,261,4,10257\0302,366,487,2,257,4,10257\0302,492,496,2,257,2,10257\0303,1,47,2,384,1,10257\0303,49,58,2,384,1,10257\0301,1,13,4,272,1,10257\0301,15,31,4,272,2,10257\0304,1,9,3,256,2,10257\031\0312,1583,0,0,\0302,0,0,2,Horde\0315002,23,5002,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12345,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5002]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This coincides with much of what we already knew. Regardless, it is interesting and rather unfortunate information.$B$BThe markings on this map will prove valuable in thinning the Blackrock menace.\030I'm a goblin of my word, $r. Now listen closely:$B$BThese orcs are used primarily as beasts of burden and cannon fodder for the black dragonflight!$B$BTheir true leader is none other than Nefarian, brood of Deathwing. I've also discovered the location of Nefarian's subordinates in this part of the citadel.$B$BTake this map to Marshal Maxwell in the Burning Steppes. It has the location of these fiends marked for easy identification.\030Travel to the Burning Steppes and give Bijou's Information to Marshal Maxwell.\030Ah, $N. It has been a long time.\030Message to Maxwell\0312,1,28,2,257,1,10257\0302,30,48,2,257,1,10257\0302,53,147,2,257,1,10257\0302,152,217,2,257,1,10257\0302,219,307,2,257,1,10257\0302,312,367,2,257,1,10257\0302,369,435,2,257,1,10257\0303,1,78,2,384,1,10257\0301,1,49,4,272,1,9560\0301,51,115,4,272,1,9560\0301,120,197,4,272,3,9560\0304,9,32,3,256,1,9560\03111583,2,4,Nefarian\0309560,2,6,Marshal Maxwell\0309560,2,8,Marshal Maxwell\0312,1583,0,0,\0302,0,0,6,Marshal Maxwell\0302,0,0,6,Burning Steppes\0302,0,0,8,Burning Steppes\0302,0,0,8,Marshal Maxwell\0315001,19,5001,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305081,23,5081,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[501]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Superb collecting, $N.\030Oh, $N. . .the flowers are blooming in Hillsbrad and the air is so fresh and brisk.  I can't help but to wallow in the misery of it all.  I look out my grimy window and long for the day when our New Plague brings this world the death it deserves.$B$BAs much as I would love to sit and brood all day, my duty to the Dark Lady calls.  Help me, would you?  My research leads me to believe I can make the most splendid death-brew with the blood of a Mountain Lion.  Bring some to me and we'll have a little fun.\030Bring 10 vials of Mountain Lion Blood to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill.\030I remember you, $N. You were going to help me out in concocting my latest elixir. I'll need that blood before I can bring my own special brand of misery to the inhabitants of Hillsbrad.\030Elixir of Pain\0312,11,83,2,257,1,2216\0302,86,136,2,257,1,2216\0302,139,246,2,261,1,2216\0302,251,331,2,257,4,2216\0302,334,352,2,257,4,2216\0302,355,460,2,257,4,2216\0302,463,507,2,257,1,2216\0303,1,73,2,384,1,2216\0301,1,22,4,272,1,2216\0304,1,19,3,256,1,2216\0304,21,81,3,256,3,2216\0304,83,185,3,258,1,2216\03115065,2,4,Lady\0302406,2,6,Mountain Lion\0302406,2,8,Mountain Lion\0302216,2,8,Apothecary Lydon\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,1,Hillsbrad\0302,0,0,4,Dark Lady\0302,0,0,8,Apothecary Lydon\0302,0,0,8,Tarren Mill\031502,23,502,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3496,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[502]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You pour some of the elixir into your hand and hold it before Stanley's mouth.\030Ah, nothing like the smell of fresh blood in the foothills!$B$BNow we'll mix in a touch of this and a little of that and let the real fun begin!  What I have created with this blood, I like to call an Elixir of Pain.  If my calculations are correct this concoction could be the start of something very beautiful for Lady Sylvanas.  But what we need is a test.$B$BTake this elixir out to the northern farm in Hillsbrad Fields to the southwest.  Let's see how Farmer Ray's little dog Stanley likes this \"treat.\"\030Feed the Elixir of Pain to Stanley.\030Woof?\030Elixir of Pain\0312,1,59,2,257,1,2216\0302,64,144,2,257,1,2216\0302,147,216,2,257,1,2216\0302,219,330,2,257,4,2216\0302,333,359,2,259,1,2216\0302,364,442,2,257,1,2216\0302,445,509,2,257,1,2216\0303,1,35,2,384,1,2216\0301,1,78,4,272,1,2274\0304,1,5,3,256,2,2274\03115065,2,4,Lady\030232,2,7,Farmer Ray\0302274,2,7,Stanley\0302274,2,8,Stanley\0304491,3,10,Woof\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,6,Hillsbrad Fields\0302,0,0,8,Stanley\031501,19,501,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5021]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A package in the barn that you might have otherwise overlooked now stands out amongst the decay and ruin. Perhaps this is the one that the ghost of Janice Felstone was clamoring about...\030\"The package must be delivered... delivered before I'm trapped here!\"$B$BThe cries of a panicked woman feel almost like a whisper floating through the house.  Cowered in the upstairs corner is the apparition of a woman.  She does not seem to be fully cognizant of her surroundings, and she is only vaguely aware of you.$B$B\"Are you here to deliver my package?  Please, before it gets much worse!  I was going to ride out of here.  It should still be by my horse... or am I too late?\"\030The ramblings of the ghostly woman indicated that she needed a package delivered.  She claimed that it was where her horse was.  As to where the horse is or where the package was to be delivered - the ghost remains incomprehensible.\030\030Better Late Than Never\0312,1,33,2,257,1,10778\0302,35,69,2,257,1,10778\0302,74,157,2,257,1,10778\0302,160,219,2,257,1,10778\0302,222,319,2,257,4,10778\0302,324,359,2,257,2,10778\0302,362,395,2,257,1,10778\0302,398,429,2,257,3,10778\0302,432,464,2,257,1,10778\0302,466,483,2,257,2,10778\0303,1,81,2,384,1,10778\0303,84,127,2,384,1,10778\0303,130,232,2,384,1,10778\0301,1,105,4,280,4,0\0301,107,186,4,272,4,0\031385,2,9,Horse\030385,2,12,Horse\030385,2,13,Horse\03010778,4,15,Janice Felstone\0312,28,1422,0,\031\031OBJECT,175894,FINISHER,?,12,Janice's Parcel",[5022]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A package for an Emma Felstone, you say? Last known address was Stormwind, four years ago? Well let me see here...$B$BAccording to what we know, there was an Emma Felstone in the city about four years ago. Well, I should say possibly - this census I refer to is from five years ago, and I don't have a report of her vacating the city. This doesn't mean that she is still here though.$B$BWait a second... this package couldn't be for Ol' Emma, could it?\030You pick up the package, wiping off a small layer of dust and grime that had settled on it.  It is addressed in a hurried hand to an Emma Felstone of Stormwind; the delivery of the package is dated for well over four years ago.$B$BThough it is unclear if Emma Felstone is even alive, it is widely known that the Stormwind City Hall keep records on the populace of the city.  This is handled through the Royal Factors of the Stormwind Census.\030Check with the Royal Factors of Stormwind to learn the whereabouts of an Emma Felstone.  There is usually a census officer located in City Hall.\030Welcome to the office of the Stormwind census. If you are in need of information on our populace, then I can assist you.\030Better Late Than Never\0312,1,91,2,257,1,0\0302,94,227,2,321,1,0\0302,232,373,2,257,4,0\0302,376,441,2,257,1,0\0303,1,87,2,384,1,0\0303,90,144,2,384,1,0\0301,1,40,4,272,2,10782\0301,42,90,4,336,2,10782\0301,92,114,4,272,1,10782\0301,119,205,4,336,1,10782\0301,207,334,4,336,1,10782\0301,336,383,4,272,1,10782\0301,388,403,4,272,1,10782\0301,405,452,4,272,4,10782\0304,1,46,3,256,1,10782\0304,48,120,3,258,4,10782\0313520,4,14,Ol' Emma\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,6,City Hall\0315021,19,5021,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305048,23,5048,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,175894,GIVER,?,9,Janice's Parcel",[5023]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A package for a Jeremiah Felstone, with his last known address as Lordaeron... I should be able to assist you.$B$BJeremiah Felstone was in the city before the plague. Well, I should say the former Jeremiah Felstone - some of the Forsaken have changed their last names to rid themselves of their former countenance. This case is no exception; the former Jeremiah Felstone is now known as Jeremiah Payson.$B$BWait a minute... isn't he the cockroach vendor?\030You pick up the package, wiping off a small layer of dust and grime that had settled on it.  It is addressed in a hurried hand to a Jeremiah Felstone of Lordaeron; the delivery of the package is dated for well over four years ago.$B$BThough it is unclear if Jeremiah Felstone is even alive, it is widely known that the Undercity, formerly known as Lordaeron, keeps records on the populace of the city.  This is handled through the Royal Overseers of the Undercity Census.\030Check with the Royal Overseers of the Undercity to learn the whereabouts of a Jeremiah Felstone.  There is usually a census officer located near guild and tabard registration.\030Are you here to seek the assistance of the Undercity census, or just to ask me if someone you knew is dead? I get asked that a lot.\030Better Late Than Never\0312,1,91,2,257,1,0\0302,94,230,2,321,1,0\0302,235,401,2,321,4,0\0302,404,471,2,257,1,0\0303,1,96,2,384,1,0\0303,99,175,2,384,1,0\0301,1,78,4,272,1,10781\0301,80,110,4,272,1,10781\0301,115,166,4,276,1,10781\0301,168,314,4,272,1,10781\0301,316,403,4,272,1,10781\0301,408,423,4,272,1,10781\0301,425,454,4,272,2,10781\0304,1,107,3,258,4,10781\0304,109,131,3,256,1,10781\0318403,4,11,Jeremiah Payson\0307395,4,13,Cockroach\0312,28,1422,0,\0315021,19,5021,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305049,23,5049,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,175894,GIVER,?,9,Janice's Parcel",[503]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, $N. I led the expedition from Durotar under the Warchief's orders, but as you can see, our plans went somewhat awry. They have held me captive here in this town, forcing me to work, hauling burdens, digging...$B$BWhat I have suffered is unimportant, however. There is important information you must deliver to whomever is leading our group now.\030From what I can tell of the documents you procured, Gol'dir is being held in a large Syndicate base to the north, most likely in the Alterac Mountains. He has been held captive far too long and must be freed.\030Free Gol'dir then return to Krusk in Tarren Mill.\030Find where Gol'dir is being held\030Give me the key, $C, I will undo the lock myself.\030Gol'dir\0312,1,151,2,257,1,2229\0302,153,208,2,261,1,2229\0303,1,49,2,384,1,2229\0301,1,14,4,272,1,2316\0301,16,127,4,272,1,2316\0301,129,220,4,276,1,2316\0301,225,269,4,272,1,2316\0301,271,355,4,272,1,2316\0305,1,49,3,256,3,2316\0304,1,32,3,384,1,2229\0312316,2,1,Gol'dir\0302316,2,3,Gol'dir\0302229,2,3,Krusk\0302316,3,10,Gol'dir\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,1,Alterac Mountains\0302,0,0,3,Krusk\0302,0,0,3,Tarren Mill\0304,0,0,5,Durotar\031533,19,533,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030506,23,506,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3704,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[504]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very good. Here is your reward.$B$BAnd when you were hunting those Warmongers, how did Alterac city look? It's in bad shape I would guess. Ogres are not known for their cleanliness.$B$BThankfully, your efforts will help keep them away from Southshore.\030Now that you've had a taste of the Crushridge ogres, I want you to really bloody their noses...$B$BGo into the Ruins of Alterac and seek out the Crushridge Warmongers.  I want you to cut down a good number of them - that's the only way those brutes will learn to keep their distance from Alliance territory.\030Slay 10 Crushridge Warmongers, then return to Marshal Redpath in Southshore.\030You have more Warmongers to slay, $N. You should be up on the mountains on your task, not down here with your weapon stowed.\030Crushridge Warmongers\0312,1,95,2,259,1,2263\0302,100,167,2,323,1,2263\0302,170,307,2,259,3,2263\0303,1,76,2,384,1,2263\0301,1,10,4,272,1,2263\0301,12,31,4,272,1,2263\0301,36,105,4,272,2,2263\0301,107,138,4,272,4,2263\0301,140,181,4,272,1,2263\0301,186,251,4,272,3,2263\0304,1,37,3,256,1,2263\0304,39,124,3,256,1,2263\0312263,2,4,Marshal Redpath\0312,36,1416,0,\0302,0,0,3,Alliance\0302,0,0,4,Marshal Redpath\0302,0,0,4,Southshore\0304,0,0,10,Southshore\031500,19,500,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,2287,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Crushridge Warmonger",[5041]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Haha! Thank you, $N! This will help us greatly. You're a boon to the Crossroads and to the Horde. If there is anything I can do for you, please, let me know.\030That attack on the caravan contained supplies we desperately needed.$B$BYou've been brave enough to take on the Razormane tribe so far, and I will ask you to do so again, but this time, I wonder if I could ask you to keep your eyes open for some of our lost supplies. You can probably find them throughout their camps, the quilboar getting fat off their dishonorable acts.$B$BThe people of the Crossroads would be in your debt.\030Find and return Crossroads' Supply Crates to Thork in the Barrens.\030How goes your search for the supplies, $N? I trust the quilboar fall under your strength easily.\030Supplies for the Crossroads\0312,1,68,2,261,1,3429\0302,73,267,2,261,4,3429\0302,269,372,2,257,1,3429\0302,377,427,2,257,4,3429\0303,1,66,2,384,1,3429\0301,1,5,4,272,1,3429\0301,7,20,4,272,1,3429\0301,22,47,4,272,3,3429\0301,49,97,4,272,1,3429\0301,99,157,4,272,4,3429\0304,1,42,3,256,2,3429\0304,44,96,3,256,1,3429\0313429,2,5,Thork\0312,17,1413,0,\0302,0,0,5,Thork\0302,0,0,5,Barrens\0304,0,0,9,Crossroads\0304,0,0,9,Horde\031\031ITEM,12708,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5042]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031If only Mangletooth were free to see you decimate those who betrayed him! <snort>$B$BI thank you for destroying more of the Bristleback by gathering these shards. Please, continue to do so, and I will continue to aid you. <snort>\030\030\030I will need 4 blood shards if you wish Agamaggan's strength, $r.$B$BYour foes will cower before your strength were you to be given this blessing. <snort>$B$BThe Razormane's greatest warriors are infused with such power!\030Agamaggan's Strength\0311,1,73,4,272,4,3430\0301,75,81,4,272,1,3430\0301,86,162,4,276,1,3430\0301,164,221,4,272,3,3430\0301,223,229,4,272,1,3430\0304,1,64,3,258,4,3430\0304,69,145,3,256,3,3430\0304,147,153,3,256,1,3430\0304,158,219,3,256,1,3430\0313430,4,1,Mangletooth\0312,17,1413,0,\0315052,19,5052,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5075,OBJECTIVE,4,15,",[5043]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031May your aim be unerring, and the mark of your weapon be true, $R.$B$BAgamaggan's spirit is with you. Return <snort> to me if you wish. Mangletooth will bless you again if the great boar god deems me worthy. <snort>\030\030\030My tribes greatest scouts are said to be unrivaled in their accuracy, and no rogue <snort> could measure up to their quickness in battle.$B$BBring me 4 blood shards and I will make you even more agile than any quilboar born.\030Agamaggan's Agility\0311,1,66,4,272,1,3430\0301,71,101,4,272,1,3430\0301,103,135,4,274,4,3430\0301,137,207,4,272,4,3430\0301,209,215,4,272,1,3430\0304,1,137,3,260,4,3430\0304,142,224,3,256,3,3430\031795,4,1,Mark\0303430,4,4,Mangletooth\0302809,4,4,Boar\0312,17,1413,0,\0315052,19,5052,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5075,OBJECTIVE,4,15,",[5044]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Your enemies should fear you even more, $R. <snort>$B$BTell Mangletooth tales of your cunning in battle when next we meet--be it in this life, or the next. <snort>\030\030\030The shaman and geomancers of the quilboar tribes <snort> call upon the strength of Agamaggan to help them in battle and in their rituals, $r.$B$BIf you too wish the added power of Agamaggan's blessing with your spells, then bring me 4 blood shards and Mangletooth will aid you. <snort>\030Wisdom of Agamaggan\0311,1,43,4,276,1,3430\0301,45,51,4,272,1,3430\0301,56,155,4,276,1,3430\0301,157,163,4,272,1,3430\0304,1,141,3,260,1,3430\0304,146,277,3,258,4,3430\0304,279,285,3,256,1,3430\0313430,4,3,Mangletooth\0303430,3,6,Mangletooth\0312,17,1413,0,\0315052,19,5052,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5075,OBJECTIVE,4,15,",[5045]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Our greatest warriors, and our greatest <snort> shamans would envy your will, $R.$B$BDefeat more of the Bristlebacks knowing that they cannot stop you! <snort>\030\030\030Warriors of all types <snort> have need of a strong spirit. It drives you to greater feats when all hope has been lost. This is not unknown to the <snort> Razormane. We are a spiritual tribe--we are more proud of our connection to Agamaggan than our prowess <snort> in battle.$B$BBring me 4 blood shards and I will bless your spirit for battle. <snort>\030Rising Spirit\0311,1,81,4,272,4,3430\0301,86,151,4,272,1,3430\0301,153,159,4,272,1,3430\0304,1,59,3,258,1,3430\0304,61,119,3,262,3,3430\0304,121,165,3,256,1,3430\0304,167,276,3,260,1,3430\0304,281,344,3,260,3,3430\0304,346,352,3,256,1,3430\031\0312,17,1413,0,\0303,0,0,7,Agamaggan\0315052,19,5052,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5075,OBJECTIVE,4,15,",[5046]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,objectives,setup\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Go to war, $R.\030\030\030All those who <snort> enter battle have need of protection. Their bones must be strong. Their skin tough. <snort> My tribe knows this as well, and to add to the natural protection our quills and hide give us, <snort> we often call upon Agamaggan to protect us from harm before we go to war.$B$BBring me 4 blood shards <snort> and I will grant you the same protection.\030Razorhide\0311,1,14,4,276,1,3430\0304,1,59,3,262,1,3430\0304,61,87,3,256,1,3430\0304,89,105,3,256,1,3430\0304,107,290,3,270,1,3430\0304,295,367,3,256,3,3430\031\0312,17,1413,0,\0315052,19,5052,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5075,OBJECTIVE,4,15,",[5047]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Alive? Suit worked? And what do we have here?\030You'll find Malyfous Darkhammer in Everlook, $c. Tell him that 'Finkle is A-OK' and that the suit works perfectly.$B$BThen hand him this:$B$B<Finkle hands you a glowing piece of flesh.>$B$BI snatched it from the beast's innards during my 'vacation.'$B$BI bet Malyfous could give you a fairly accurate assessment of what he can do with parts from a monster like this!$B$BOh, I suppose you don't know where Everlook is, do you? To Winterspring, $g fella:lady;!\030Talk to Malyfous Darkhammer in Everlook.\030Yea?\030Finkle Einhorn, At Your Service!\0312,1,48,2,257,1,10776\0302,50,114,2,257,1,10776\0302,119,137,2,257,1,10776\0302,142,185,2,257,1,10776\0302,190,249,2,257,1,10776\0302,254,366,2,257,4,10776\0302,371,425,2,257,2,10776\0302,427,458,2,257,1,10776\0303,1,40,2,384,1,10776\0301,1,6,4,272,2,10637\0301,8,19,4,272,2,10637\0301,21,45,4,272,2,10637\0304,1,4,3,256,2,10637\03110637,2,1,Malyfous Darkhammer\03010430,2,5,The Beast\03015065,2,8,Lady\03010637,2,9,Malyfous Darkhammer\0312,1583,0,0,\0302,0,0,1,Everlook\0302,0,0,9,Malyfous Darkhammer\0302,0,0,9,Everlook\031\031",[5048]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031My name is indeed Emma Felstone - you're the first person in years to call me that. Who... who are you?$B$BYou say you knew... my sister?! Is she still alive? Who am I kidding, of course she isn't. When the plague broke out in Lordaeron, I had come to expect the worst. So many of my family died... or worse. Here I am now, crazy Ol' Emma, all alone. What are you, a grave-robber or something? Looking for your next target?$B$BWhat... you have a package for me from my sister?\030She's a tad ornery, and quite possibly out of her gourd... but the records indicate that Ol' Emma does fit the framework of who Emma Felstone might be.$B$BPerhaps you've seen Ol' Emma wander the city - she talks to herself, most often in nonsensical jibber-jabber.  Still, she doesn't hurt anything or anyone, so folks pretty much leave her be.$B$BAll things considered, I would say that Ol' Emma is in fact Emma Felstone.  You might try asking if her last name is indeed Felstone.\030Find Ol' Emma in Stormwind and see if she is in fact Emma Felstone.  If she is, then perhaps she'd like the package Janice Felstone made for her.\030I would tell you to get off my lawn, but as you can see I don't have one.\030Good Natured Emma\0312,1,58,2,257,1,10782\0302,60,151,2,257,4,10782\0302,156,264,2,257,4,10782\0302,267,344,2,257,1,10782\0302,349,422,2,257,4,10782\0302,425,481,2,257,4,10782\0303,1,67,2,384,4,10782\0303,70,145,2,384,4,10782\0301,1,83,4,272,1,3520\0301,85,90,4,272,1,3520\0301,92,103,4,272,2,3520\0301,108,126,4,272,1,3520\0301,128,138,4,272,2,3520\0301,140,158,4,272,2,3520\0301,160,197,4,272,1,3520\0301,199,269,4,276,1,3520\0301,271,298,4,272,1,3520\0301,300,308,4,272,1,3520\0301,310,350,4,272,1,3520\0301,352,393,4,272,2,3520\0301,395,423,4,272,2,3520\0301,428,434,4,272,1,3520\0301,436,476,4,272,2,3520\0304,1,73,3,256,4,3520\0313520,2,2,Ol' Emma\0303520,2,3,Ol' Emma\0303520,2,5,Ol' Emma\0303520,2,7,Ol' Emma\03010778,2,8,Janice Felstone\0303520,4,19,Ol' Emma\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,7,Stormwind\0304,0,0,16,Lordaeron\0315022,19,5022,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305050,23,5050,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5049]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I haven't used that name in years... but yes, at one point in my life - before this glorious unlife - that was my last name.$B$BYou claim to have known my sister... or rather, have recently spoken to my sister.$B$BWho's been dead.$B$BFor four years.$B$BYou know, if my bones weren't already brittle enough, I'd be tempted to break my foot off on your posterior. You're quite the vulture, aren't you?$B$B What... you have a package for me from my sister?\030From the evidence I am able to muster, the person you seek - and the intended recipient of the parcel - is Jeremiah Payson, the Undercity cockroach vendor.$B$BI've always been of the opinion that it takes a special gift to sell... cockroaches.  No doubt you are on quite the epic sojourn now, mighty $c.  I will leave you to your world-shaping endeavors.  Allow me, however, to be a part of your magnum opus and reveal that he is located near the bank, suitably groveling under one of the walkways.\030Find Jeremiah Payson in the Undercity and see if he is in fact Jeremiah Felstone.  If he is, then perhaps he'd like the package Janice Felstone made for him.\030Every time someone steps on a cockroach, I cry. Please don't make me cry.\030The Jeremiah Blues\0312,1,155,2,259,1,10781\0302,160,230,2,257,1,10781\0302,232,243,2,257,1,10781\0302,246,303,2,257,1,10781\0302,306,354,2,257,3,10781\0302,357,498,2,257,1,10781\0303,1,81,2,384,4,10781\0303,84,157,2,384,4,10781\0301,1,36,4,272,1,8403\0301,38,124,4,272,1,8403\0301,129,164,4,272,1,8403\0301,166,210,4,272,1,8403\0301,215,230,4,272,1,8403\0301,235,249,4,272,1,8403\0301,254,361,4,272,4,8403\0301,363,399,4,272,2,8403\0301,404,411,4,272,1,8403\0301,413,453,4,272,2,8403\0304,1,47,3,256,1,8403\0304,49,73,3,256,1,8403\0318403,2,1,Jeremiah Payson\0307395,2,1,Cockroach\03010262,2,6,Opus\0308403,2,7,Jeremiah Payson\03010778,2,8,Janice Felstone\0307395,3,19,Cockroach\0312,1497,1458,0,\0302,0,0,7,Undercity\0315023,19,5023,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305050,23,5050,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[505]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, $N. Although they may still be lurking about, we hope that some of the thieves and footpads you slew were responsible for the last magistrate's death. But even if they weren't, the Syndicate is a taint on this land and a stain on the human race.$B$BTheir deaths are welcome to Southshore.\030I am the new magistrate of Southshore, recently assigned after the assassination of the previous magistrate.  The assassins were never found, but through our investigations we're almost certain they were hired by the Syndicate - a group of thieves led by villainous nobles of the now fallen kingdom of Alterac.$B$BThe Syndicate has a camps in Sofera's Naze and Corahn's Dagger, north and west of the Horde-occupied Tarren Mill.  Slay the Syndicate members you find in these camps.\030Kill 12 Syndicate Footpads and 8 Syndicate Thieves, then return to Magistrate Henry Maleb in Southshore.\030You have slain those Syndicate thugs, I trust?\030Syndicate Assassins\0312,1,108,2,257,1,2276\0302,111,310,2,257,1,2276\0302,315,427,2,257,1,2276\0302,430,480,2,257,1,2276\0303,1,104,2,384,1,2276\0301,1,14,4,272,1,2276\0301,16,161,4,274,3,2276\0301,163,256,4,272,4,2276\0301,261,299,4,272,1,2276\0304,1,46,3,260,2,2276\0312276,2,5,Magistrate Henry Maleb\0312,36,1416,0,\0302,0,0,3,Sofera's Naze\0302,0,0,3,Horde-occupied Tarren Mill\0302,0,0,5,Magistrate Henry Maleb\0302,0,0,5,Southshore\0304,0,0,9,Southshore\031\031NPC,2240,OBJECTIVE,12,13,Syndicate Footpad\030NPC,2241,OBJECTIVE,8,13,Syndicate Thief",[5050]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You give the half-charm back to the apparition. She looks at it, then at you expectantly.$B$B\"Honey, where did you put your half of the charm? We can't be together unless we have both halves. Honey... can you see me?\"\030It would seem that I was wrong about you $N, and for that I owe you an apology.  My sister sent me a number of personal effects, including humorously enough the deed to the Felstone farm.  I think I'll pass on reclaiming it right now.$B$BIf my sister's spirit remains tethered to the farm and cannot rest, please... could you return this to her?  It is half of a good luck charm she had, with her husband having the other half.$B$BMaybe her knowing I have these things will now put her soul to rest.\030Return to Janice Felstone in Western Plaguelands her Good Luck Half-Charm.\030John, sweetheart... is that you? I'm so cold all the sudden...\030Good Luck Charm\0312,1,79,2,257,4,0\0302,82,187,2,257,1,0\0302,190,234,2,257,1,0\0302,239,315,2,257,4,0\0302,317,345,2,257,4,0\0302,348,427,2,257,1,0\0302,432,499,2,257,4,0\0303,1,74,2,384,1,0\0301,1,47,4,272,1,10778\0301,49,89,4,272,1,10778\0301,94,142,4,272,2,10778\0301,144,191,4,280,4,10778\0301,193,200,4,272,1,10778\0301,202,217,4,272,2,10778\0304,1,19,3,256,1,10778\0304,21,32,3,256,2,10778\0304,34,62,3,256,1,10778\03110778,2,8,Janice Felstone\030806,3,15,John\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,2,Felstone\0302,0,0,8,Janice Felstone\0302,0,0,8,Western Plaguelands\0315051,23,5051,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5051]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You hand the reassembled good luck charm to Janice Felstone's ghost. As soon as she grasps it, you observe an almost immediate change in her. Her ethereal form shimmers, and she looks upon you with clear yet sad eyes.$B$B\"You've freed me... I no longer will need this charm. Please, take it and perhaps it will give you the solace it has given me.\"\030The ramblings of the poor ghost continue:$B$B\"I'm so cold, John.  Bring me your charm, and we'll be together!  Quickly John, before the plague comes to change us into hideous beasts!  I can't see you John... but I know you're near.  I feel you near me.\"$B$BPerhaps if the second half of the charm was found and reassembled, this would constitute what the spirit of Janice Felstone is seeking.\030Locate the other half of the Good Luck Charm somewhere on the Felstone Farm in Western Plaguelands and reassemble it.$B$BGive the Good Luck Charm to Janice Felstone on the Felstone Farm, Western Plaguelands.\030John, don't let the ghouls get you... don't let the ghouls get me... nasty ghouls... our charm will keep us safe.\030Two Halves Become One\0312,1,41,2,257,1,10778\0302,46,64,2,257,1,10778\0302,67,109,2,257,1,10778\0302,112,182,2,261,1,10778\0302,185,207,2,257,1,10778\0302,209,231,2,257,1,10778\0302,234,253,2,257,1,10778\0302,258,392,2,257,4,10778\0303,1,117,2,384,1,10778\0303,122,207,2,384,1,10778\0301,1,68,4,272,1,10778\0301,70,141,4,272,1,10778\0301,143,217,4,272,1,10778\0301,222,240,4,272,1,10778\0301,242,274,4,272,3,10778\0301,276,348,4,272,4,10778\0304,1,37,3,256,1,10778\0304,39,68,3,256,1,10778\0304,70,84,3,256,1,10778\0304,86,113,3,256,3,10778\031806,2,2,John\030806,2,4,John\030806,2,5,John\03010778,2,8,Janice Felstone\03010778,2,10,Janice Felstone\03010778,4,11,Janice Felstone\030806,3,17,John\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,9,Western Plaguelands\0302,0,0,10,Janice Felstone\0304,0,0,11,Janice Felstone's\0315050,19,5050,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12723,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5052]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, you do understand. <snort> My words were not lost on your ears, $R. Mangletooth may be caged, but no cage can stop Agamaggan's power! <snort>$B$BThe touch of the shard, the feel of it... it has been a long time, $R.$B$BDo you know what it is like? To have your power severed from you?$B$BBut, that is a tale for another time. I promised you information. I promised you Agamaggan's power. My people turned their backs on Mangletooth. Now, I lose you upon them. <snort>\030Along with the thorns, the blood affected <snort> other aspects of the earth: blood red stones mixed in with other minerals. The Bristleback dig up these shards and carry them as totems <snort> for strength in battle and as totems for their magics. <snort>$B$BI know the secrets of that magic.$B$BBring Mangletooth one of these blood shards to show you understand. Bring Mangletooth many of the shards, and he will bless you with quilboar magic--the magic of Agamaggan! <snort>\030Bring a Blood Shard to Mangletooth in Camp Taurajo in the Barrens.$B$BCollect more Blood Shards if you want him to bless you with Agamaggan's power.\030Our tribes flock to the thorny areas throughout the Barrens <snort> because they are holy places, but none as holy as Razorfen. Agamaggan's body makes up the entirety of the Razorfen, <snort> but the Downs are especially protected because the entrance is made from his great maw! <snort> It will swallow whole those not loyal to him, and spit out their bodies after he's chewed them up! <snort>$B$BAgamaggan has left his body behind to protect us, and he gives of his spirit so we may protect him. <snort>\030Blood Shards of Agamaggan\0312,1,124,2,257,1,3430\0302,126,248,2,261,1,3430\0302,250,256,2,257,1,3430\0302,261,293,2,257,1,3430\0302,298,364,2,257,1,3430\0302,366,469,2,257,3,3430\0302,471,477,2,257,1,3430\0303,1,66,2,384,1,3430\0303,71,148,2,386,4,3430\0301,1,22,4,272,1,3430\0301,24,71,4,276,1,3430\0301,73,137,4,272,1,3430\0301,139,145,4,272,1,3430\0301,150,190,4,272,1,3430\0301,192,219,4,272,1,3430\0301,224,251,4,272,2,3430\0301,253,288,4,272,2,3430\0301,293,329,4,272,1,3430\0301,331,357,4,272,1,3430\0301,359,391,4,272,1,3430\0301,393,436,4,272,1,3430\0301,438,463,4,272,1,3430\0301,465,471,4,272,1,3430\0304,1,127,3,258,1,3430\0304,129,279,3,258,1,3430\0304,281,386,3,256,3,3430\0304,388,394,3,256,1,3430\0304,399,497,3,270,1,3430\0304,499,505,3,256,1,3430\0313430,2,5,Mangletooth\0303430,2,6,Mangletooth\0303430,2,8,Mangletooth\0303430,4,12,Mangletooth\0303430,4,21,Mangletooth\0312,17,1413,0,\0302,0,0,8,Mangletooth\0302,0,0,8,Camp Taurajo\0302,0,0,8,Barrens\031878,19,878,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5075,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5054]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This was no easy task, yet you have excelled. But do not be too quick to think you have impressed me, $N.\030In the snowy mountains of Winterspring, to the northwest, a skilled hunter stalks his prey... I speak of Ursius of the shardtooth bears, an agile and clever beast.$B$BI send you now against him. He roams the sloping hills to the northwest of Everlook. Find and hunt him, before he discovers your intent.$B$BAll that have gone up against Ursius have quickly found themselves to be the prey, and he, the hunter. Stay on your guard.\030Storm Shadowhoof at Everlook in Winterspring wants you to kill Ursius.\030Go now, $c. Seek out Ursius.\030Ursius of the Shardtooth\0312,1,93,2,257,1,10303\0302,95,163,2,257,1,10303\0302,168,194,2,257,1,10303\0302,196,251,2,257,1,10303\0302,253,303,2,265,1,10303\0302,308,409,2,257,1,10303\0302,411,429,2,257,1,10303\0303,1,70,2,386,1,10303\0301,1,45,4,272,1,10303\0301,47,105,4,272,1,10303\0304,1,11,3,256,1,10303\0304,13,28,3,256,1,10303\03110806,2,2,Ursius\03010806,2,6,Ursius\03010303,2,8,Storm Shadowhoof\03010806,2,8,Ursius\03010806,3,12,Ursius\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,8,Everlook\0302,0,0,8,Winterspring\0315055,23,5055,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,10806,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Ursius",[5055]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes. You have returned. I believe now that you are a true $C by nature. You have faced the most ferocious of creatures and have returned, surpassing my expectations.$B$BYou are now ready for my final request.\030Swift, and clever, Brumeran glides silently across the snowy landscape of southern Winterspring. But do not let her graceful appearance convince you that she is harmless. All that cross her pay considerably, and often with their own lives.$B$BSeek out Brumeran of the chillwind among the chimera. Defeat her, then return again to me.\030Storm Shadowhoof at Everlook in Winterspring wants you to kill Brumeran.\030Brumeran calls out to you, $N.\030Brumeran of the Chillwind\0312,1,96,2,257,1,10303\0302,98,170,2,257,1,10303\0302,172,239,2,257,1,10303\0302,244,296,2,257,1,10303\0302,298,333,2,257,1,10303\0303,1,72,2,386,1,10303\0301,1,4,4,272,1,10303\0301,6,23,4,272,1,10303\0301,25,71,4,272,4,10303\0301,73,165,4,272,1,10303\0301,170,208,4,272,1,10303\0304,1,30,3,256,1,10303\03110807,2,1,Brumeran\03010807,2,4,Brumeran\03010303,2,6,Storm Shadowhoof\03010807,2,6,Brumeran\03010807,3,12,Brumeran\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,6,Everlook\0302,0,0,6,Winterspring\0315054,19,5054,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305056,23,5056,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,10807,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Brumeran",[5056]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have proven both your strength and your determination. Many more challenges await you, but I have already shown you as much as I am able.$B$BGood luck, $N.\030In northern Winterspring, great cats assemble around a large landmark called Frostsaber Rock. The leader of these cats is known by the name Shy-Rotam. Defeating the matriarch of the frostsabers would grant you much respect in the eyes of your fellow $r.$B$BGo again to the harsh wilds, and once there, gather sacred meat from the frostsabers. Find the stone of Shy-Rotam, and place it there. Placing the meat of her kin before her will summon Shy-Rotam, in anger.$B$BBe ready for her fury, and defeat her.\030Storm Shadowhoof at Everlook in Winterspring wants you to defeat Shy-Rotam.\030Shy-Rotam is bold and unforgiving; she will defend her kind with fervent enthusiasm.\030Shy-Rotam\0312,1,93,2,257,1,10303\0302,95,150,2,257,1,10303\0302,152,253,2,257,4,10303\0302,258,342,2,257,1,10303\0302,344,391,2,257,1,10303\0302,393,463,2,257,3,10303\0302,468,505,2,257,1,10303\0303,1,75,2,386,1,10303\0301,1,58,4,272,1,10303\0301,60,141,4,272,1,10303\0301,146,159,4,272,1,10303\0304,1,84,3,268,3,10303\0317431,2,1,Frostsaber\03010737,2,2,Shy-Rotam\03010737,2,5,Shy-Rotam\03010737,2,6,Shy-Rotam\03010303,2,8,Storm Shadowhoof\03010737,2,8,Shy-Rotam\03010737,3,12,Shy-Rotam\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,8,Everlook\0302,0,0,8,Winterspring\0315055,19,5055,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305057,23,5057,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,10737,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Shy-Rotam",[5057]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031We learn from our life experiences, $N. From what this marker says, I am sure that you have only become stronger and wiser as a result of yours. You have grown much since we last spoke.$B$BTake this in remembrance of the difficult tasks you have accomplished as a $R $C, and know that you will always have my respect and admiration.\030Before you spoke to me, $N, I had heard of your endeavors... that you had an unyielding desire to prove yourself, that you had an exceptional ability as a $c, and I now know these things to be the truth.$B$BThose that excel as you do are worthy of recognition. Take this marker to a friend of mine in Thunder Bluff named Melor Stonehoof. I'm sure he will remember you, and what you accomplished so long ago. Speak to him of you recent victories, and do not ever forget what you have accomplished today.\030Bring Storm Shadowhoof's Marker to Melor Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff.\030\030Past Endeavors\0312,1,60,2,257,1,10303\0302,62,203,2,259,1,10303\0302,208,260,2,257,1,10303\0302,262,337,2,257,1,10303\0302,339,407,2,321,3,10303\0302,409,502,2,257,1,10303\0303,1,68,2,384,1,10303\0301,1,39,4,272,1,10303\0301,41,144,4,272,1,10303\0301,146,185,4,272,1,10303\0301,190,332,4,272,3,10303\0313441,2,4,Melor Stonehoof\03010303,2,7,Storm Shadowhoof\0303441,2,7,Melor Stonehoof\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,4,Thunder Bluff\0302,0,0,7,Melor Stonehoof\0302,0,0,7,Thunder Bluff\0315056,19,5056,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5058]="PARTIAL\031characters,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A diary with yellowing pages lies open to the last entry:$B$B\"I don't know what's going to happen now that Harold's turned.  It took everything out of me to drag him into the only place I could find that'd lock him up tight and hold him.  I hid the key on me, and I pray it works...$B$BI hope I can get out of here, but I need money to do that.  Our stuff's all in the cabinet I think... and now that I think about it, doesn't Harold keep the key on him?$B$BI'll rest on it, I'm dead tired now.\"\030\030\030\030Mrs. Dalson's Diary\0311,1,57,4,272,1,0\0301,62,123,4,272,3,0\0301,126,237,4,272,4,0\0301,240,282,4,272,1,0\0301,287,344,4,274,3,0\0301,347,387,4,272,1,0\0301,389,454,4,272,2,0\0301,459,495,4,272,1,0\031\0312,28,1422,0,\031\031OBJECT,175926,GIVER,?,9,Mrs. Dalson's Diary\030OBJECT,175926,FINISHER,?,12,Mrs. Dalson's Diary",[5059]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Using the key found on the skeleton of the former Mrs. Dalson, you unlock the door to the outhouse. A bloodthirsty ghoul leaps from the outhouse, having been trapped inside for who knows how long.$B$BIt is clear by the bloodcurdling scream of the ghoul at your presence that the former Farmer Dalson is now beyond saving.\030\030\030The door to the outhouse has begun to splinter at the edges of the frame as though it has been repeatedly and incessantly tried to be forced open. It is currently locked up tight from the outside of the outhouse.$B$BAs you rattle the door, you hear a guttural moaning come from inside! Whatever is inside there, it certainly does not sound friendly.\030Locked Away\0311,1,54,4,272,1,0\0301,56,99,4,272,1,0\0301,101,196,4,272,1,0\0301,201,321,4,272,1,0\0304,1,146,3,256,1,0\0304,148,212,3,256,1,0\0304,217,285,3,256,1,0\0304,287,349,3,256,1,0\0316412,4,1,Skeleton\030846,4,3,Ghoul\030846,4,4,Ghoul\03010836,4,4,Farmer Dalson\0312,28,1422,0,\031\031OBJECT,175925,GIVER,?,9,Outhouse\030OBJECT,175925,FINISHER,?,12,Outhouse\030ITEM,12738,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[506]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The nerve of those overbearing humans! We'll show them that the orcs shall never submit to their will!$B$BThis will now be our mission, in addition to recovering the trinket the Warchief desires. It would seem that by accomplishing one, we will also accomplish the other.\030A day or two ago, I was visited by the leader of this Syndicate. His name was Aliden Perenolde, and styled himself lord of this land. He confided in me his plans to take the orcs that stood against him as slaves, just as his father and his mentor, the despised Blackmoore, had planned.$B$BMore important was that he brought his mistress, a wisp of a girl named Elysa. Around her neck was the pendant the Warchief desires.$B$BNow go, I will make my own way, after I have settled my business here.\030Return the information gathered by Gol'dir to Krusk in Tarren Mill.\030\030Blackmoore's Legacy\0312,1,64,2,257,1,2316\0302,66,133,2,257,1,2316\0302,135,285,2,257,1,2316\0302,290,367,2,257,1,2316\0302,369,421,2,259,1,2316\0302,426,495,2,257,3,2316\0303,1,67,2,384,1,2316\0301,1,38,4,272,1,2229\0301,40,102,4,272,3,2229\0301,107,195,4,274,3,2229\0301,197,271,4,272,4,2229\0313681,2,4,Wisp\030371,2,4,Girl\0302317,2,4,Elysa\0302316,2,7,Gol'dir\0302229,2,7,Krusk\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,7,Krusk\0302,0,0,7,Tarren Mill\031503,19,503,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030507,23,507,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5060]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The key taken from Farmer Dalson's ghoulish remains fits the lock perfectly. The doors of the cabinet swing open, revealing several items that remain intact and appear quite valuable.\030\030\030An extremely sturdy cabinet stands before you, securely fastened shut by a built-in lock. The front of the cabinet is deeply scratched and marked. This could be surmised as being from numerous and violent failed attempts to reveal whatever secrets the cabinet currently obfuscates from view.$B$BIf you are going to open this cabinet, you will need to find the key.\030Locked Away\0311,1,76,4,272,1,0\0301,78,183,4,272,1,0\0304,1,89,3,256,1,0\0304,91,146,3,256,1,0\0304,148,291,3,256,4,0\0304,296,364,3,258,4,0\03110836,4,1,Farmer Dalson\0312,28,1422,0,\0304,0,0,1,Farmer Dalson's\031\031OBJECT,175924,GIVER,?,9,Locked Cabinet\030OBJECT,175924,FINISHER,?,12,Locked Cabinet\030ITEM,12739,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5061]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very impressive, $N. You are ready to learn your aquatic form, and it is my pleasure to teach it to you.$B$BAlso, in recognition of your achievement during the two trials, I give you this item. I hope you'll find it to be a welcome addition to your gear as a protector of nature and a keeper of the balance.\030You have completed the necessary lessons all young druids are taught before they can adopt an aquatic aspect.  Go now back to your trainer, Mathrengyl Bearwalker, in Darnassus.  Show him your pendant and prove to him you are ready to learn what he has to teach you.  He will complete your training, allowing you to become one with the water.$B$BGoodbye, young druid.  We shall speak again.\030Return to Darnassus and show Mathrengyl Bearwalker the Pendant of the Sea Lion.\030Your return to Darnassus is not without heralding, though I will need proof of your lessons learned in Moonglade before I will teach you your aquatic form.$B$BDo you have the Pendant of the Sea Lion?\030Aquatic Form\0312,1,109,2,265,1,11802\0302,112,176,2,257,1,11802\0302,179,265,2,257,1,11802\0302,268,341,2,257,3,11802\0302,346,366,2,257,1,11802\0302,369,389,2,257,3,11802\0303,1,79,2,384,1,11802\0301,1,20,4,272,1,4217\0301,22,104,4,272,1,4217\0301,109,193,4,272,1,4217\0301,195,307,4,282,3,4217\0304,1,155,3,258,3,4217\0304,160,199,3,256,2,4217\0314217,2,2,Mathrengyl Bearwalker\0304217,2,7,Mathrengyl Bearwalker\0312,0,0,2,Darnassus\0302,0,0,7,Darnassus\0303,0,0,12,Darnassus\0303,0,0,12,Moonglade\031272,19,272,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5062]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Good, you have gathered the essential amount of Incendia agave. This rare herb found only in Thousand Needles will help light the dormant sacred fire of life.$B$B<Magatha begins to enchant the Incendia agave.>\030Arikara is a deadly creature that must be dealt with swiftly. In order to hunt her down you will need to light the sacred fire of life - this will summon Arikara.$B$BGo now and harvest the rare Incendia agave plant. Once you have harvested enough agave, seek council with Magatha Grimtotem on Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. She is a powerful shaman that can enchant the agave plant to create a powder that will light the fire.$B$BTravel northeast to the Boiling Pool and gather Incendia Agave.\030Gather 10 bushels of Incendia Agave, and then consult Magatha Grimtotem on Elder Rise in Thunderbluff.\030So, Motega Firemain sends word of Arikara...well now that is grave news.$B$B$B$BArikara is a deadly creature born only to seek vengeance against those who have committed heinous acts.$B$B\030Sacred Fire\0312,1,61,2,257,1,10428\0302,63,162,2,259,3,10428\0302,167,215,2,257,1,10428\0302,217,321,2,257,1,10428\0302,323,424,2,257,3,10428\0302,429,491,2,257,1,10428\0303,1,102,2,384,1,10428\0301,1,63,4,272,1,4046\0301,65,158,4,272,3,4046\0301,163,209,4,272,1,4046\0304,1,72,3,256,1,4046\0304,81,183,3,258,1,4046\03110882,2,1,Arikara\03010882,2,2,Arikara\0304046,2,4,Magatha Grimtotem\0304046,2,7,Magatha Grimtotem\03010882,3,11,Arikara\03010882,3,12,Arikara\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,4,Thunder Bluff\0302,0,0,6,Boiling Pool\0302,0,0,7,Thunderbluff\0304,0,0,9,Thousand Needles\0314865,19,4865,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305088,23,5088,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12732,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[5063]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Astounding! It must have taken weeks to gather those components... and how did you find a pristine hide?!?$B$BEnjoy the cap, $n!\030A finer cap you may never see. From the pristine hide of the beast, our expert crafters will create the most phenomenal hat a prestidigitator could ever hope to don!$B$BFifty gold pieces along with the listed items and your head shall be graced with the Cap of the Scarlet Savant:$B$B*The pristine hide of the Beast.$B$B*Frayed abomination stitchings.$B$B*Arcane crystals.$B$B*Enchanted scarlet thread.$B$BBEHOLD!\030In order to create the Cap of the Scarlet Savant, you will be required to bring the following items back to Malyfous Darkhammer: 1 Pristine Hide of the Beast; 5 Frayed Abomination Stitchings; 8 Arcane Crystals; 5 Enchanted Scarlet Thread. $B$BYou will also be required to pay 50 gold pieces for the crafting of the item.\030Unless you've got everything I need, you're wasting my time.\030Cap of the Scarlet Savant\0312,1,30,2,257,1,0\0302,32,165,2,259,4,0\0302,170,280,2,257,3,0\0302,285,316,2,257,1,0\0302,321,351,2,257,1,0\0302,356,372,2,257,1,0\0302,377,402,2,257,1,0\0302,407,413,2,257,1,0\0303,1,238,2,386,3,0\0303,244,320,2,384,3,0\0301,1,11,4,272,1,10637\0301,13,66,4,272,1,10637\0301,68,106,4,272,2,10637\0301,111,128,4,272,1,10637\0304,1,60,3,266,4,10637\03110430,2,2,The Beast\03010430,2,4,The Beast\0308545,2,5,Abomination\03010637,2,9,Malyfous Darkhammer\03010430,2,9,The Beast\0308545,2,9,Abomination\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,9,Malyfous Darkhammer\0315047,19,5047,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,175927,GIVER,?,9,Malyfous's Catalogue\030ITEM,12731,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,12735,OBJECTIVE,5,15,\030ITEM,12363,OBJECTIVE,8,15,\030ITEM,12734,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[5064]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Great Spirit Totem! This is dire news indeed. I must begin to plan for whatever may come.$B$B$N, as promised, here is your reward for your brave service.$B$B\030$N, you have served us well in the past, so I now entrust to you an important mission. The Grimtotem Clan is up to something secretive. Three agents of unknown origin were seen visiting the Grimtotem over the recent weeks. We discovered that separate chests in Darkcloud Pinnacle hold these guarded messages.$B$B$N, if you succeed in this dangerous mission, I will reward you in kind.$B\030Locate and retrieve the three Secret Notes in Darkcloud Pinnacle.\030Have you discovered what the Grimtotem are up to?\030Grimtotem Spying\0312,1,86,2,257,1,10537\0302,88,135,2,257,1,10537\0302,137,222,2,257,1,10537\0302,224,308,2,257,1,10537\0302,313,384,2,257,4,10537\0303,1,65,2,384,1,10537\0301,1,19,4,272,1,10537\0301,21,45,4,272,1,10537\0301,47,89,4,272,1,10537\0301,94,153,4,272,1,10537\0304,1,49,3,256,2,10537\03115363,4,7,Spirit Totem\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,4,Darkcloud Pinnacle\0302,0,0,6,Darkcloud Pinnacle\0314841,19,4841,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12765,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,12766,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,12768,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5065]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You found them!  Great!$B$BThank you, $N.  I will pour over these texts and decipher their meaning.$B$BYou, however, have another task...\030The troll with whom you spoke did not tell the truth.  The two tablets you gained for him spoke of containing the essence of Hakkar, but there is more to that legend.  I have studied long, and found that there are six Tablets of Mosh'aru, not two!  Six!$B$BAnd I fear that we will not like what secrets the others hold..$B$BFind the third and fourth tablets of Mosh'aru.  They're in the Eastern Plaguelands, held by the mossflayer trolls. Find them, and bring them to me.\030Bring the Third and Fourth Mosh'aru Tablets to Prospector Ironboot in Tanaris.\030Do you have the tablets?  I fear their texts will reveal a great threat to our world.\030The Lost Tablets of Mosh'aru\0312,1,53,2,257,1,10460\0302,56,166,2,257,1,10460\0302,169,247,2,257,1,10460\0302,250,253,2,257,1,10460\0302,258,320,2,257,3,10460\0302,325,370,2,257,1,10460\0302,373,438,2,257,1,10460\0302,440,471,2,257,1,10460\0303,1,78,2,384,1,10460\0301,1,15,4,272,1,10460\0301,18,23,4,272,1,10460\0301,28,41,4,272,1,10460\0301,44,99,4,272,3,10460\0301,104,137,4,272,1,10460\0304,1,24,3,256,2,10460\0304,27,85,3,260,3,10460\03114834,2,2,Hakkar\03010460,2,9,Prospector Ironboot\0312,139,1423,0,\0302,0,0,7,Eastern Plaguelands\0302,0,0,9,Prospector Ironboot\0302,0,0,9,Tanaris\0313528,19,3528,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304788,23,4788,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12411,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,12412,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5066]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Welcome to the Plaguelands, hero. This is one of most dangerous frontiers in Azeroth, especially with the looming threat of the Scourge to our north and northeast. I am glad to hear that the clarion call of duty and service to the greater good did not fall on deaf ears with you!$B$BIf you are ready to get your hands dirty, then there is plenty for willing and able heroes to do here on the edge of the Plaguelands.\030Hear ye, hear ye!  All heroes are called upon to heed these words!$B$BA call to arms has been issued by the Kingdom of Stormwind!  All able bodied individuals are entreated to take up arms against the dark threat of the Scourge in the northern lands of the Eastern Kingdoms!  Rumors fly of new threats rising from the ruins of the Plaguelands!$B$BHeroes of the realm - seek out Commander Ashlam Valorfist who has set up his base camp in Chillwind Camp, north of the Alterac Mountains!\030Seek out Commander Ashlam Valorfist.  His base camp is located at Chillwind Camp, north of the Alterac Mountains.\030\030A Call to Arms: The Plaguelands!\0312,1,17,2,257,1,2198\0302,20,66,2,257,1,2198\0302,71,129,2,257,1,2198\0302,132,274,2,325,1,2198\0302,277,343,2,321,1,2198\0302,348,484,2,257,1,2198\0303,1,36,2,384,1,2198\0303,39,113,2,384,1,2198\0301,1,33,4,272,1,10838\0301,35,163,4,340,1,10838\0301,165,279,4,272,1,10838\0301,284,416,4,272,4,10838\03110838,2,6,Commander Ashlam Valorfist\03010838,2,7,Commander Ashlam Valorfist\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,6,Chillwind Camp\0302,0,0,6,Alterac Mountains\0302,0,0,8,Chillwind Camp\0302,0,0,8,Alterac Mountains\0304,0,0,9,Plaguelands\0304,0,0,10,Azeroth\0315090,22,5090,UNKNOWN\0305091,22,5091,UNKNOWN\0305092,23,5092,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305092,24,5092,UNKNOWN\031",[5067]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Few more improbable tasks I have seen completed by mortals. Bask in the glory of my handiwork! Reap its rewards!\030While the crafting of such an item has never successfully been accomplished, it is thought to be possible - under the right circumstance.$B$BShould the seeker of arcanum desire to imbue leggings with immense power, the following they must find:$B$B* The pristine hide of the Beast.$B$B* Frayed abomination stitchings.$B$B*Arcanite Bars.$B$B*Frostwhisper's embalming fluid.$B$BBEHOLD!\030In order to create the Leggings of Arcana, you will be required to bring the following items back to Malyfous Darkhammer: 1 Pristine Hide of the Beast; 5 Frayed Abomination Stitchings; 5 Arcanite Bars; 5 Frostwhisper's Embalming Fluid.$B$BYou will also be required to pay 50 gold pieces for the crafting of the item.\030Unless you've got everything I need, you're wasting my time.\030Leggings of Arcana\0312,1,137,2,257,1,0\0302,142,244,2,259,1,0\0302,249,281,2,257,1,0\0302,286,317,2,257,1,0\0302,322,336,2,257,1,0\0302,341,372,2,257,1,0\0302,377,383,2,257,1,0\0303,1,235,2,386,3,0\0303,240,316,2,384,3,0\0301,1,59,4,272,1,10637\0301,61,94,4,272,1,10637\0301,96,112,4,272,1,10637\0304,1,60,3,266,4,10637\03110430,2,3,The Beast\0308545,2,4,Abomination\03010637,2,8,Malyfous Darkhammer\03010430,2,8,The Beast\0308545,2,8,Abomination\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,8,Malyfous Darkhammer\0315047,19,5047,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,175927,GIVER,?,9,Malyfous's Catalogue\030ITEM,12731,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,12735,OBJECTIVE,5,15,\030ITEM,12360,OBJECTIVE,5,15,\030ITEM,12736,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[5068]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I thought I would be dead and buried before I ever saw this day.$B$BAn accomplishment of this magnitude can only be overshadowed by the reward.\030It is said that only one Breastplate of Bloodthirst has ever been created and that it was made for the legendary assassin, Garona. Whether this world will ever see another is doubtful.$B$BRegardless! Our master crafters can reproduce the item given the necessary components:$B$B*The pristine hide of the Beast.$B$B*Frayed abomination stitchings.$B$B*Arcanite bars.$B$B*The skin of shadow.$B$BBEHOLD!\030In order to create the Breastplate of Bloodthirst, you will be required to bring the following items back to Malyfous Darkhammer: 1 Pristine Hide of the Beast; 10 Frayed Abomination Stitchings; 5 Arcanite Bars; 5 Skin of Shadow.$B$BYou will also be required to pay 50 gold pieces for the crafting of the item.\030Unless you've got everything I need, you're wasting my time.\030Breastplate of Bloodthirst\0312,1,130,2,257,1,0\0302,132,184,2,257,3,0\0302,189,199,2,257,1,0\0302,201,274,2,257,1,0\0302,279,310,2,257,1,0\0302,315,345,2,257,1,0\0302,350,364,2,257,1,0\0302,369,388,2,257,1,0\0302,393,399,2,257,1,0\0303,1,228,2,386,3,0\0303,233,309,2,384,3,0\0301,1,64,4,272,4,10637\0301,69,143,4,272,1,10637\0304,1,60,3,266,4,10637\0316767,2,1,Garona\03010430,2,5,The Beast\0308545,2,6,Abomination\0304244,2,8,Shadow\03010637,2,10,Malyfous Darkhammer\03010430,2,10,The Beast\0308545,2,10,Abomination\0304244,2,10,Shadow\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,10,Malyfous Darkhammer\0315047,19,5047,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,175927,GIVER,?,9,Malyfous's Catalogue\030ITEM,12731,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,12735,OBJECTIVE,10,15,\030ITEM,12360,OBJECTIVE,5,15,\030ITEM,12753,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[507]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031No, no please don't hurt me! I never meant your people any harm, he's had me against my will! Please... spare me!\030It is clear that Perenolde must be killed, his foulness removed from the world. His manor lies a ways to the north of here, on the shores of Lordamere Lake. Do your duty, $n, then retrieve the pendant that the Warchief desires, and return here.\030Kill Lord Aliden Perenolde and ask his mistress, Elysa, about Taretha's pendant.\030W-what do you want?\030Lord Aliden Perenolde\0312,1,79,2,257,1,2229\0302,81,156,2,257,1,2229\0302,158,244,2,259,1,2229\0303,1,80,2,384,1,2229\0301,1,28,4,272,1,2317\0301,30,93,4,272,3,2317\0301,95,103,4,272,1,2317\0301,105,113,4,272,1,2317\0304,1,19,3,258,2,2317\0312423,2,4,Lord Aliden Perenolde\0302317,2,4,Elysa\0312,267,1424,0,\031506,19,506,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030508,23,508,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,2423,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Lord Aliden Perenolde",[508]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It is strange that the Warchief would expend so much over such a small thing. I do not claim to understand him, but I will follow him, whatever his commands. You did well, $N, no doubt the Warchief will be glad to hear of your success.\030The pendant? Of course you can have it... Take it! I want no memory of him... just please, please leave in peace...\030Return Taretha's pendant to Krusk in Tarren Mill.\030You've returned, $N. Success to report?\030Taretha's Gift\0312,1,12,2,257,2,2317\0302,14,41,2,257,1,2317\0302,43,50,2,257,1,2317\0302,52,77,2,259,1,2317\0302,79,115,2,265,1,2317\0303,1,49,2,384,1,2317\0301,1,77,4,272,4,2229\0301,79,157,4,272,3,2229\0301,159,235,4,272,3,2229\0304,1,20,3,256,1,2229\0304,22,39,3,256,2,2229\0312229,2,6,Krusk\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,6,Krusk\0302,0,0,6,Tarren Mill\031507,19,507,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5081]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Excellent work, $N. At the very least, you have bought us more time - precious, precious time.\030This information fills in the gaps to our otherwise impeccable intelligence of Blackrock Spire.$B$BThe attack must be decisive, $N.$B$BFirst their war master, the troll Voone, must be destroyed. Without his battle plans, the Blackrock orcs will be thrown into chaos.$B$BYou must then take out the ogre Highlord, Omokk. The cowardly ogres of Blackrock are powerless without his leadership.$B$BLastly, the overlord of the citadel: Wyrmthalak. With Wyrmthalak dead, their central command unit is without a conduit.\030Travel to Blackrock Spire and destroy War Master Voone, Highlord Omokk, and Overlord Wyrmthalak. Return to Marshal Maxwell when the job is done.\030Status?\030Maxwell's Mission\0312,1,95,2,265,1,9560\0302,100,131,2,261,1,9560\0302,136,194,2,261,1,9560\0302,196,266,2,261,3,9560\0302,271,318,2,257,1,9560\0302,320,388,2,257,1,9560\0302,393,440,2,257,1,9560\0302,442,511,2,257,1,9560\0303,1,96,2,388,1,9560\0303,98,144,2,384,1,9560\0301,1,19,4,272,1,9560\0301,21,94,4,272,1,9560\0304,1,7,3,256,2,9560\031211,2,5,Ogre\0309237,2,9,War Master Voone\0309196,2,9,Highlord Omokk\0309568,2,9,Overlord Wyrmthalak\0309560,2,10,Marshal Maxwell\03014528,4,12,Precious\0312,1583,0,0,\0302,0,0,9,Blackrock Spire\0302,0,0,10,Marshal Maxwell\0315002,19,5002,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,9237,OBJECTIVE,1,13,War Master Voone\030NPC,9196,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Highlord Omokk\030NPC,9568,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Overlord Wyrmthalak",[5082]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thanks so much, $N! Now I can get back to work here.$B$BDid you find anything of interest at the Winterfall camp?\030I came to Winterspring to investigate the Frostfire Hot Springs. I've noticed that the water seems to have ...strange qualities. I haven't yet been able to discover the source, and to tell you the truth, I've had some difficulty lately, due to the Winterfall furbolg.$B$BThey seem to be drawn to the springs, just as I am. They have become extremely protective of the water, and won't let me come near the two larger springs to the north of here.$B$BI'd like to continue my studies, so won't you help me?\030Donova Snowden in Winterspring wants you to kill 8 Winterfall Pathfinders, 8 Winterfall Den Watchers, and 8 Winterfall Totemics.\030I appreciate your help!\030Threat of the Winterfall\0312,1,64,2,257,1,9298\0302,66,128,2,257,4,9298\0302,130,267,2,257,1,9298\0302,272,322,2,257,4,9298\0302,324,446,2,257,1,9298\0302,451,504,2,259,2,9298\0303,1,128,2,386,1,9298\0301,1,19,4,272,1,9298\0301,21,52,4,272,1,9298\0301,57,113,4,272,2,9298\0304,1,23,3,256,1,9298\03131,2,3,Furbolg\0309298,2,7,Donova Snowden\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,1,Winterspring\0302,0,0,3,Winterfall\0302,0,0,7,Winterspring\0304,0,0,10,Winterfall\031\031NPC,7442,OBJECTIVE,8,13,Winterfall Pathfinder\030NPC,7440,OBJECTIVE,8,13,Winterfall Den Watcher\030NPC,7441,OBJECTIVE,8,13,Winterfall Totemic",[5083]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You got this from the Winterfall?\030This vial that you picked up from the Winterfall furbolg is empty, but you can detect a few drops of a strange green liquid inside; it almost glows.$B$BIs it something important?$B$BDonova Snowden would probably be able to tell you more, since she has been camped by the hot springs in Winterspring for some time now.\030Bring the Empty Firewater Flask to Donova Snowden in Winterspring.\030What is that you have found?\030Winterfall Firewater\0312,1,148,2,257,1,0\0302,153,178,2,257,2,0\0302,183,317,2,257,4,0\0303,1,66,2,384,1,0\0301,1,33,4,272,2,9298\0304,1,28,3,256,2,9298\03131,2,1,Furbolg\0309298,2,3,Donova Snowden\0309298,2,4,Donova Snowden\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,1,Winterfall\0302,0,0,3,Winterspring\0302,0,0,4,Donova Snowden\0302,0,0,4,Winterspring\0304,0,0,5,Winterfall\0315084,23,5084,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12771,STARTER,?,10,",[5084]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Inside the cauldron bubbles a rotting, repulsive-smelling substance...\030This greenish liquid... it reminds me a bit of the sludge I saw when traveling through Felwood. And I have seen some Winterfall Runners passing into Timbermaw... Perhaps these things have something to do with the flask you found, $N.$B$BThere is a large group of furbolg just past Timbermaw Hold, in Felwood. Called the Deadwood tribe, they have been corrupted and driven mad by the fel. Why don't you look around there and see if you can find any evidence of dealings between the Winterfall and the Deadwood?\030Search the Deadwood furbolg camp in northern Felwood for a clue.\030\030Falling to Corruption\0312,1,23,2,257,1,9298\0302,25,95,2,257,1,9298\0302,97,161,2,257,1,9298\0302,163,233,2,257,4,9298\0302,238,308,2,257,1,9298\0302,310,387,2,261,1,9298\0302,389,509,2,257,4,9298\0303,1,64,2,384,1,9298\0301,1,70,4,272,1,0\0312479,2,2,Sludge\03031,2,5,Furbolg\03031,2,8,Furbolg\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,5,Felwood\0315083,19,5083,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305085,23,5085,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,176091,FINISHER,?,12,Deadwood Cauldron",[5085]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You are very resourceful, $N. Do you think that the Winterfall furbolgs have been to the Deadwood camp?\030The greenish substance inside the cauldron appears to be similar to what you found in the flask. This strange gooey stuff could be as corrupted as the furbolg that created it...$B$BIf the Winterfall furbolg are using it, does this mean that they will soon be as corrupted as the Deadwood tribe?$B$BIt would be best to report back to Donova with your findings, along with a sample of the liquid in the cauldron.\030Report back to Donova Snowden with your findings.\030I hope you found something, $N. The Winterfall are becoming increasingly aggressive!\030Mystery Goo\0312,1,96,2,257,1,0\0302,98,177,2,261,4,0\0302,182,294,2,261,4,0\0302,299,410,2,257,4,0\0303,1,49,2,384,1,0\0301,1,29,4,272,1,9298\0301,31,103,4,272,2,9298\0304,1,31,3,258,3,9298\0304,33,84,3,256,1,9298\03131,2,2,Furbolg\03031,2,3,Furbolg\0309298,2,5,Donova Snowden\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,4,Donova\0302,0,0,5,Donova Snowden\0304,0,0,7,Deadwood\0315084,19,5084,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305086,23,5086,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,176091,GIVER,?,9,Deadwood Cauldron",[5086]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I have to compare this to the substance you found in the cauldron, and then I'm sure we'll know more.\030I've studied the sample you returned with, and while I can't say for sure, I believe it contains traces of toxic elements. However, the only way to know for sure is to gather some as a comparison.$B$BI believe that the Deadwood furbolg may be gathering these elements from other corrupted creatures in Felwood; in particular, the elementals living in the Irontree Woods, called toxic horrors.$B$BCollect a few samples for me to compare, but be careful -- it's very dangerous there!\030Collect 3 Toxic Horror Droplets for Donova Snowden in Winterspring.\030I think we are beginning to uncover what is happening here, $N.\030Toxic Horrors\0312,1,122,2,257,4,9298\0302,124,196,2,257,1,9298\0302,201,392,2,261,4,9298\0302,397,481,2,257,1,9298\0303,1,67,2,384,1,9298\0301,1,101,4,272,1,9298\0304,1,63,3,256,1,9298\03131,2,3,Furbolg\0307132,2,5,Toxic Horror\0309298,2,5,Donova Snowden\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,3,Felwood\0302,0,0,3,Irontree Woods\0302,0,0,5,Winterspring\0315085,19,5085,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305087,23,5087,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12822,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[5087]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Donova examines the contents of the crate>$B$BI wonder if consuming this substance makes the furbolg more aggressive. They do seem much larger...\030Very interesting, $N...$B$BWhen this toxic substance is mixed with the water from the hot springs, it loses its toxicity, only retaining the ability to temporarily affect those that ingest it. This must be why the Winterfall protect the hot springs so fervently -- they need them to purify their firewater.$B$BWe need to stop this -- cut off contact between the Winterfall and the Deadwood. A group of runners walks the distance between their village and Felwood. Find and defeat them, and steal their shipment.\030Find the Winterfall Runners and stop them from delivering their shipment to Winterfall Village.\030We'll see what happens when the Winterfall don't get their firewater!\030Winterfall Runners\0312,1,23,2,257,1,9298\0302,28,192,2,257,1,9298\0302,194,306,2,271,1,9298\0302,311,390,2,259,1,9298\0302,392,463,2,257,1,9298\0302,465,511,2,261,1,9298\0303,1,95,2,384,1,9298\0301,1,43,4,272,1,9298\0301,48,118,4,272,4,9298\0301,120,146,4,272,4,9298\0304,1,69,3,256,1,9298\03131,4,9,Furbolg\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,7,Winterfall Village\0315086,19,5086,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305121,23,5121,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12829,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5088]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031This does not make sense. Why would Arikara be after Cairne Bloodhoof? Magatha could not be wrong, she is our most powerful shaman.$B$B<Motega shakes his head.>$B$BRegardless, your great deed to the Horde shall not go unnoticed - please, choose one of these as a reward for your aid.\030Take this refined and purified Incendia powder to Thousand Needles and toss it on the sacred fire of life. It is located in the Darkcloud Pinnacle on an isolated needle where they bury their dead.$B$BThe enchantment that I have weaved into the Incendia powder will summon Arikara to you, $N.$B$BI fear she may be stalking Cairne Bloodhoof; too much Tauren lore has changed, and I fear this has angered Arikara. Move quickly before all is lost, $c!\030Slay Arikara. Bring her remains and the Incendia powder to Motega Firemane in Whitereach Post as proof of your deed.\030Light the Sacred Fire of Life\030Have you slain the vicious serpent Arikara, $N?\030Arikara\0312,1,106,2,257,1,4046\0302,108,196,2,257,1,4046\0302,201,291,2,257,3,4046\0302,296,410,2,257,1,4046\0302,412,447,2,261,1,4046\0303,1,13,2,384,1,4046\0303,15,116,2,384,1,4046\0301,1,25,4,272,1,10428\0301,27,70,4,272,4,10428\0301,72,131,4,272,4,10428\0301,136,160,4,272,1,10428\0301,165,283,4,272,3,10428\0305,1,47,3,260,2,10428\0304,1,29,3,384,1,4046\03110882,2,3,Arikara\0303057,2,4,Cairne Bloodhoof\03010882,2,4,Arikara\03010882,2,6,Arikara\03010428,2,7,Motega Firemane\03010882,4,9,Arikara\0303057,4,9,Cairne Bloodhoof\03010882,3,13,Arikara\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,1,Thousand Needles\0302,0,0,2,Darkcloud Pinnacle\0302,0,0,7,Motega Firemane\0302,0,0,7,Whitereach Post\0304,0,0,12,Horde\0315062,19,5062,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12925,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5089]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The plot thickens...\030From the corpse of the defeated serpent you uncover what appears to be a note of some importance: A letter from his superior, General Drakkisath, concerning protocol.$B$BYour instinct tells you that you should take it to Marshal Maxwell.\030Take General Drakkisath's Command to Marshal Maxwell in Burning Steppes.\030What have you got there, $N?\030General Drakkisath's Command\0312,1,166,2,257,1,0\0302,171,237,2,257,1,0\0303,1,72,2,384,1,0\0301,1,20,4,272,1,9560\0304,1,28,3,256,2,9560\03110363,2,1,General Drakkisath\0309560,2,2,Marshal Maxwell\03010363,2,3,General Drakkisath\0309560,2,3,Marshal Maxwell\0312,1583,0,0,\0302,0,0,2,Marshal Maxwell\0302,0,0,3,Marshal Maxwell\0302,0,0,3,Burning Steppes\0315102,23,5102,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12780,STARTER,?,10,",[509]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, the horrible reek of Mudsnout Blossoms. At least those filthy Gnolls are good for something.\030Another day, another elixir to be made. If it were up to me, I'd just let the pathetic humans and Scourge fight it out.  They seem bent on killing each other as is.$B$BAlas, our Dark Lady wants to help speed up the process a tad so why not pass these morbid days by spreading a little death and disease across the land?$B$BHere's the plan, $N: you go out to Nethander Stead, south of Tarren Mill and east of the river and Southshore. Collect for me 6 Mudsnout Blossoms from the field for my next elixir.\030Bring 6 Mudsnout Blossoms to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill.\030Any luck at Nethander Stead?\030Elixir of Agony\0312,1,39,2,257,1,2216\0302,41,119,2,325,4,2216\0302,122,164,2,257,4,2216\0302,169,319,2,259,2,2216\0302,324,433,2,257,1,2216\0302,435,503,2,257,1,2216\0303,1,61,2,384,1,2216\0301,1,43,4,272,1,2216\0301,45,96,4,272,1,2216\0304,1,28,3,256,2,2216\03115065,2,4,Lady\0302216,2,7,Apothecary Lydon\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,5,Nethander Stead\0302,0,0,5,Tarren Mill\0302,0,0,7,Apothecary Lydon\0302,0,0,7,Tarren Mill\0303,0,0,10,Nethander Stead\031513,23,513,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3502,OBJECTIVE,6,15,",[5090]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Welcome to the Plaguelands, hero. This is one of most dangerous frontiers in Azeroth, especially with the looming threat of the Scourge to our north and northeast. I am glad to hear that the clarion call of duty and service to the greater good did not fall on deaf ears with you!$B$BIf you are ready to get your hands dirty, then there is plenty for willing and able heroes to do here on the edge of the Plaguelands.\030Hear ye, hear ye!  All heroes are called upon to heed these words!$B$BA call to arms has been issued by the Kingdom of Stormwind!  All able bodied individuals are entreated to take up arms against the dark threat of the Scourge in the northern lands of the Eastern Kingdoms!  Rumors fly of new threats rising from the ruins of the Plaguelands!$B$BHeroes of the realm - seek out Commander Ashlam Valorfist who has set up his base camp in Chillwind Camp, north of the Alterac Mountains!\030Seek out Commander Ashlam Valorfist.  His base camp is located at Chillwind Camp, north of the Alterac Mountains.\030\030A Call to Arms: The Plaguelands!\0312,1,17,2,257,1,10877\0302,20,66,2,257,1,10877\0302,71,129,2,257,1,10877\0302,132,274,2,325,1,10877\0302,277,343,2,321,1,10877\0302,348,484,2,257,1,10877\0303,1,36,2,384,1,10877\0303,39,113,2,384,1,10877\0301,1,33,4,272,1,10838\0301,35,163,4,340,1,10838\0301,165,279,4,272,1,10838\0301,284,416,4,272,4,10838\03110838,2,6,Commander Ashlam Valorfist\03010838,2,7,Commander Ashlam Valorfist\0312,1537,1455,0,\0302,0,0,6,Chillwind Camp\0302,0,0,6,Alterac Mountains\0302,0,0,8,Chillwind Camp\0302,0,0,8,Alterac Mountains\0304,0,0,9,Plaguelands\0304,0,0,10,Azeroth\0315066,22,5066,UNKNOWN\0305091,22,5091,UNKNOWN\0305092,23,5092,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305092,24,5092,UNKNOWN\031",[5091]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Welcome to the Plaguelands, hero.  This is one of the most dangerous frontiers in Azeroth, especially with the looming threat of the Scourge to our north and northeast.  I am glad to hear that the clarion call of duty and service to the greater good did not fall on deaf ears with you!$B$BIf you are ready to get your hands dirty, then there is plenty for willing and able heroes to do here on the edge of the Plaguelands.\030Hear ye, hear ye!  All heroes are called upon to heed these words!$B$BA call to arms has been issued by the Kingdom of Stormwind!  All able bodied individuals are entreated to take up arms against the dark threat of the Scourge in the northern lands of the Eastern Kingdoms!  Rumors fly of new threats rising from the ruins of the Plaguelands!$B$BHeroes of the realm - seek out Commander Ashlam Valorfist who has set up his base camp in Chillwind Camp, north of the Alterac Mountains!\030Seek out Commander Ashlam Valorfist.  His base camp is located at Chillwind Camp, north of the Alterac Mountains.\030\030A Call to Arms: The Plaguelands!\0312,1,17,2,257,1,10878\0302,20,66,2,257,1,10878\0302,71,129,2,257,1,10878\0302,132,274,2,325,1,10878\0302,277,343,2,321,1,10878\0302,348,484,2,257,1,10878\0303,1,36,2,384,1,10878\0303,39,113,2,384,1,10878\0301,1,33,4,272,1,10838\0301,36,168,4,340,1,10838\0301,171,285,4,272,1,10838\0301,290,422,4,272,4,10838\03110838,2,6,Commander Ashlam Valorfist\03010838,2,7,Commander Ashlam Valorfist\0312,1657,1457,0,\0302,0,0,6,Chillwind Camp\0302,0,0,6,Alterac Mountains\0302,0,0,8,Chillwind Camp\0302,0,0,8,Alterac Mountains\0304,0,0,9,Plaguelands\0304,0,0,10,Azeroth\0315066,22,5066,UNKNOWN\0305090,22,5090,UNKNOWN\0305092,23,5092,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305092,24,5092,UNKNOWN\031",[5092]="PARTIAL\031consequences,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Mission accomplished, $N!  Well played, well played.$B$BAllow me to reward your work thus far with some coin from the Stormwind coffers.  I'd recommend spending it on materiel that will aid you in your next mission... one that will take you into the ruins of Andorhal itself.$B$BBe ready!  Be vigilant!\030With Andorhal's western and northern roads into the city well fortified, I'm looking to strike at it from the less defended eastern road.  The Scourge relies on the buffer of undead that infests Sorrow Hill as a first line of defense.  If we are to advance on Andorhal, we will need to do it through Sorrow Hill.$B$BYour first assignment will be to clear the way through Sorrow Hill.  Thin out the skeletons and ghouls that haunt the area; report back to me when this is done!\030Kill 10 Skeletal Flayers and 10 Slavering Ghouls in Sorrow Hill.$B$BReturn to Commander Ashlam Valorfist at Chillwind Camp, Western Plaguelands.\030I want you to prepare for the worst, $N - dig deep.  The task in front of us will not be easy.  As we rally our forces here to eventually strike out against the Scourge, you will be part of our advance effort that takes the fight to them!  Your assigned mission in Sorrow Hill will begin our path to victory!\030Clear the Way\0312,1,137,2,257,1,10838\0302,140,234,2,321,1,10838\0302,237,312,2,259,4,10838\0302,317,383,2,257,3,10838\0302,386,476,2,257,1,10838\0303,1,64,2,384,1,10838\0303,69,144,2