 you are, $N... and thanks. News of Anrak's foul deeds boiled my blood!\030Wanted: Arnak Grimtotem$B$BArnak the outcast is wanted for the heinous crimes of murder and kidnapping. Handsome rewards will be given to those brave enough to bring this criminal to justice.$B$BArnak was last seen on the cliffs near the Darkcloud Pinnacle. Show the proof of your deed to Cliffwatcher Longhorn in Freewind Post in order to claim the reward.\030Slay Arnak Grimtotem and bring proof of your deed to Cliffwatcher Longhorn in Freewind Post.\030Have you any news of that murderous Arnak Grimtotem?\030Wanted - Arnak Grimtotem\0312,1,23,2,257,1,0\0302,28,103,2,261,1,0\0302,105,191,2,257,3,0\0302,196,257,2,257,1,0\0302,259,357,2,259,1,0\0303,1,92,2,384,1,0\0301,1,4,4,272,1,10537\0301,6,34,4,272,1,10537\0301,36,101,4,272,4,10537\0301,106,124,4,272,1,10537\0301,126,136,4,272,1,10537\0301,138,180,4,272,1,10537\0304,1,52,3,256,2,10537\03110896,2,1,Arnak Grimtotem\03010537,2,5,Cliffwatcher Longhorn\03010896,2,6,Arnak Grimtotem\03010537,2,6,Cliffwatcher Longhorn\03010896,3,13,Arnak Grimtotem\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,4,Darkcloud Pinnacle\0302,0,0,5,Cliffwatcher Longhorn\0302,0,0,5,Freewind Post\0302,0,0,6,Cliffwatcher Longhorn\0302,0,0,6,Freewind Post\031\031OBJECT,176115,GIVER,?,9,Wanted Poster - Arnak Grimtotem\030ITEM,12884,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5148]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You've given your finest offerings, and nature will soon permit you to bend her to your will. Once I have finished my tutelage, your work will be a force of nature unto itself.$B$BTo train in the art for the future, simply speak to me and I will make available any knowledge that you have yet to commit as yours.\030To learn tribal leatherworking demands an understanding of how primal nature truly is; I know that you have already mastered the art of making wild leather armor, and I am willing to complete your training.$B$BKnow this, $c: by choosing this path you agree never to learn dragonscale or elemental leatherworking; there is only room for practice of one of the three arts.  Furthermore, bring to me the finest samples of your wild leather armor.  From there, we will begin your mastery.\030Bring a Wild Leather Vest and a Wild Leather Helmet to Se'Jib in Stranglethorn Vale.$B$BCompleting this quest will give you access to the Tribal Leatherworking arts.$B$BThe completion of this quest will prevent you from learning Dragonscale Leatherworking and Elemental Leatherworking; be sure this is the path you wish to follow before doing so.\030Nature is a force that must be appeased before you hope to learn how to bend its will into your leather garments. Bring me your offering to this force, and I will make sure you are heard.\030Tribal Leatherworking\0312,1,206,2,257,1,7871\0302,211,370,2,257,1,7871\0302,373,443,2,257,1,7871\0302,446,484,2,257,3,7871\0303,1,84,2,384,1,7871\0303,89,165,2,384,3,7871\0303,170,346,2,394,3,7871\0301,1,93,4,272,3,7871\0301,95,176,4,272,3,7871\0301,181,312,4,272,3,7871\0304,1,113,3,258,3,7871\0304,115,187,3,256,3,7871\0317871,2,5,Se'Jib\0304795,4,9,Force of Nature\0312,0,0,5,Se'Jib\0302,0,0,5,Stranglethorn Vale\0302,0,0,6,Tribal Leatherworking\0315145,22,5145,UNKNOWN\0305146,22,5146,UNKNOWN\031ITEM,8211,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,8214,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5149]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You found it! You found my doll! Oh, thank you!\030My auntie Marlene told me to stay here in our house because my father had to go and fight.  My father's the bravest man in the whole world!$B$BBut I've been here for a long time, and he hasn't come for me.  Sometimes bad people come and whisper to me and I want my dad to make them go away, but he's not here!$B$BAnd sometimes when it gets dark I want to play with my doll but I can't because I left it in town.$B$BWill you find my doll for me?\030Find Pamela's doll.\030Did you find my doll?\030Pamela's Doll\0312,1,90,2,263,1,10926\0302,93,139,2,257,1,10926\0302,144,205,2,257,1,10926\0302,208,309,2,259,1,10926\0302,314,411,2,259,1,10926\0302,416,444,2,257,2,10926\0303,1,19,2,384,1,10926\0301,1,13,4,272,1,10926\0301,15,32,4,272,1,10926\0301,34,47,4,272,1,10926\0304,1,21,3,256,2,10926\031\0312,139,1423,0,\031\031ITEM,12885,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[515]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The excitement of this experiment has me feeling giddy! You have been such a great help, $N. Together we will spread death and disease to this land!\030A mudsnout composite?  Absolutely brilliant!  Why didn't I think of that?$B$BLet me contribute my colloid of decay to this devilish brew.$B$BIn order to activate the contaminating agents in this mudsnout mixture, Lydon is going to need a strong troll's blood potion, as well as some daggerspine scales and torn fin eyes from the southern coast of Hillsbrad.  He'll know what to do once you've gathered him all the reagents.  And my, how anxious I am to hear how his experiment goes!\030Bring the Mudsnout Mixture, a Strong Troll's Blood Potion, 5 Daggerspine Scales and 5 Torn Fin Eyes to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill.\030So glad to see you back, $N. I was growing so terribly bored here. Not a single entertaining thing to do besides poison and disease Umpi and reanimate her. . .over and over and over again.$B$BHow went the trip to the Undercity? Were you fortunate enough to slaughter any humans along the way?\030Elixir of Agony\0312,1,21,2,257,2,2055\0302,24,44,2,257,1,2055\0302,47,73,2,257,2,2055\0302,78,137,2,257,1,2055\0302,142,357,2,259,3,2055\0302,360,423,2,257,1,2055\0302,426,482,2,257,1,2055\0303,1,135,2,384,1,2055\0301,1,55,4,272,1,2216\0301,57,92,4,272,1,2216\0301,94,148,4,272,3,2216\0304,1,28,3,256,1,2216\0304,30,66,3,256,1,2216\0304,68,155,3,260,1,2216\0304,159,188,3,256,1,2216\0304,193,227,3,256,2,2216\0304,229,292,3,256,2,2216\0312996,2,5,Torn\0302996,2,8,Torn\0302216,2,8,Apothecary Lydon\0302230,3,14,Umpi\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,8,Apothecary Lydon\0302,0,0,8,Tarren Mill\0303,0,0,16,Undercity\031513,19,513,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030517,23,517,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3388,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,3509,OBJECTIVE,5,15,\030ITEM,3510,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[5150]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Placing the sprouts in front of her, Dadanga seems pleased.$B$BShe nudges a small brown-wrapped package towards you, in exchange for the treat!\030\030\030Dadanga looks up at you as you approach her. She seems to be hoping for something...$B$BShe's probably hungry!$B$BThere's got to be something growing in the crater that would be just the perfect snack for a large herbivore. Dadanga's a big girl; whatever you bring her, there would need to be a lot of it!\030Dadanga is Hungry!\0311,1,59,4,272,4,9274\0301,64,143,4,272,1,9274\0304,1,44,3,256,1,9274\0304,46,84,3,256,4,9274\0304,89,110,3,256,1,9274\0304,115,223,3,256,4,9274\0304,225,305,3,258,4,9274\0319274,4,1,Dadanga\0309274,3,3,Dadanga\030371,3,7,Girl\0312,490,1449,0,\031\031ITEM,11315,OBJECTIVE,15,15,",[5151]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031My hypercapacitor! This will keep me busy for a while until I can figure out what it does...\030I am the only survivor from our caravan attack by the centaur! A rare yet mighty panther is guarding my best gizmo, which is around his neck. Hah! Even the centaur tremble in the presence of this ferocious beast!$B$BHere is the key to the cage. They took everything there, but left him alone. Slay this beast and bring back my hypercapacitor, and I shall reward you.$B$BThe wrecked caravan is just north of here.$B\030Slay the beast and bring back the Hypercapacitor Gizmo and Panther Cage Key to Wizlo Bearingshiner.\030Do you have my hypercapacitor?\030Hypercapacitor Gizmo\0312,1,62,2,261,1,10941\0302,64,141,2,257,1,10941\0302,143,146,2,257,1,10941\0302,148,212,2,257,1,10941\0302,217,244,2,257,1,10941\0302,246,292,2,257,1,10941\0302,294,366,2,257,3,10941\0302,371,412,2,257,1,10941\0303,1,99,2,384,1,10941\0301,1,18,4,272,1,10941\0301,20,92,4,272,3,10941\0304,1,30,3,256,2,10941\03193,2,1,Centaur\030736,2,2,Panther\03093,2,4,Centaur\03010430,2,9,The Beast\030736,2,9,Panther\03010941,2,9,Wizlo Bearingshiner\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,9,Wizlo Bearingshiner\031\031ITEM,12946,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5152]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You saw Pamela? How is she? Is she alive?? Oh, no! Poor Pamela! She was so young, and such a happy child...$B$BShe doesn't know what happened to her father, does she? My brother, Joseph?$B$BNo... she couldn't understand what happened to Joseph. And even if she could, I don't have the heart to tell her...\030Oh, I'm so lonely!  Where is my family?  Auntie Marlene told me to stay here, but then she left and never came back!  And my dad... have you seen him?$B$BMaybe Auntie Marlene knows where he is.  She lives near Andorhal, in a house to the south.  I think it was on a hill... she said it was on a hill.$B$BPlease, $N.  You're my new friend!  Will you talk to my Auntie for me?\030Speak with Marlene, south of the Ruins of Andorhal.\030\030Auntie Marlene\0312,1,18,2,257,1,10926\0302,21,39,2,257,2,10926\0302,42,116,2,257,1,10926\0302,119,131,2,257,1,10926\0302,133,150,2,257,2,10926\0302,155,193,2,257,4,10926\0302,196,244,2,257,1,10926\0302,247,273,2,257,1,10926\0302,275,300,2,257,1,10926\0302,305,315,2,257,1,10926\0302,318,338,2,257,1,10926\0302,341,374,2,257,2,10926\0303,1,51,2,448,1,10926\0301,1,15,4,272,2,10927\0301,17,27,4,272,2,10927\0301,29,42,4,272,2,10927\0301,52,63,4,272,1,10927\0301,65,107,4,272,1,10927\0301,112,166,4,272,2,10927\0301,168,186,4,272,2,10927\0301,197,244,4,272,1,10927\0301,246,305,4,272,4,10927\031\0312,139,1423,0,\0302,0,0,7,Andorhal\0302,0,0,13,Ruins of Andorhal\0304,0,0,21,Joseph\0315149,19,5149,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305153,23,5153,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5153]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031What is this? A wedding ring? Let me see...$B$BAh! This ring was once on the hand of a great man, but there is much tragedy in that man's past.$B$BAre you here to help him? It's far too late for him now... but perhaps we can help him in the past!\030I wish Joseph could again be with his daughter, but it cannot be so.  His soul was twisted by the Scourge, and he became a monster.  Oh, he is doomed!$B$BBut perhaps we can change his fate.$B$BSearch the graves outside for Joseph's monument.  His body's not there, for it was trampled and destroyed years ago, but under the monument is his wedding ring.  Take that ring to Chromie... a strange gnome with very strange powers.$B$BChromie is staying in the ruined inn at the northwest corner of Andorhal.\030Bring Joseph's Wedding Ring to Chromie.\030There is something timely about your visit. You're not from the future, are you?\030A Strange Historian\0312,1,68,2,259,4,10927\0302,71,131,2,321,1,10927\0302,134,150,2,257,1,10927\0302,155,189,2,257,4,10927\0302,194,241,2,257,1,10927\0302,244,353,2,325,1,10927\0302,356,383,2,257,1,10927\0302,385,425,2,257,1,10927\0302,430,502,2,257,1,10927\0303,1,39,2,384,1,10927\0301,1,13,4,272,2,10667\0301,15,29,4,272,2,10667\0301,31,43,4,272,1,10667\0301,52,143,4,272,1,10667\0301,148,172,4,272,2,10667\0301,174,205,4,272,1,10667\0301,207,246,4,272,4,10667\0304,1,43,3,256,1,10667\0304,45,80,3,256,2,10667\03110667,2,7,Chromie\03010667,2,9,Chromie\03010667,2,10,Chromie\0312,139,1423,0,\0302,0,0,7,Chromie\0302,0,0,10,Chromie\0315152,19,5152,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305154,23,5154,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12894,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5154]="PARTIAL\031consequences\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, you found it!$B$BDid you read it? Is Joseph Redpath mentioned? If he is, then perhaps we can save him!$B$BAh. The Annals of Darrowshire tell a very unsettling tale. It says that during the battle, Joseph Redpath was corrupted and joined the ranks of the Scourge! He then betrayed the defenders of Darrowshire.$B$BThat is an ill fate. If we can, we should try to change that fate, don't you think?\030To save Joseph Redpath, we must first discover his past.  We can learn this in the Annals of Darrowshire, a book held in the city hall of Andorhal.$B$BBring me that book.  We can then learn Joseph's fate, and with luck... change it!\030Bring the Annals of Darrowshire to Chromie in Andorhal.\030Did you find the book, $N?\030The Annals of Darrowshire\0312,1,56,2,267,1,10667\0302,59,147,2,257,1,10667\0302,152,170,2,257,1,10667\0302,173,221,2,257,1,10667\0302,223,232,2,257,1,10667\0303,1,55,2,384,1,10667\0301,1,24,4,272,1,10667\0301,29,44,4,272,2,10667\0301,46,73,4,272,2,10667\0301,75,113,4,280,4,10667\0301,122,175,4,272,1,10667\0301,177,273,4,340,1,10667\0301,275,320,4,272,1,10667\0301,325,344,4,272,1,10667\0301,346,407,4,272,4,10667\0304,1,26,3,256,2,10667\03110936,2,1,Joseph Redpath\03010667,2,6,Chromie\03010936,4,9,Joseph Redpath\03010936,4,12,Joseph Redpath\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,2,Annals of Darrowshire\0302,0,0,6,Chromie\0302,0,0,6,Andorhal\0315153,19,5153,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305210,23,5210,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12900,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5155]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Good, $N! With their numbers weakening, we can further press them.$B$BHow was your first taste of their power? Were they as strong as you thought they would be? Stronger? Or perhaps they were no challenge for you at all. Wouldn't that be something?$B$BWe can discuss the details of your exploits later. There are other things we must focus on now.\030If I am to trust you in this matter, you will first have to prove yourself.$B$BI must know that you are an enemy of the Shadow Council--the ones responsible for many evils here and abroad.$B$BTravel deeper into Felwood. To the west you will see a path leading to Jaedenar. It is there that the Council plots with the Burning Legion.$B$BEnter the depths of one of the corrupted Barrow Dens they inhabit and slay their kind. Return to me after you've done this. Then I will know you truly seek to help us.\030Enter Jaedenar and slay 4 Jaedenar Hounds, 4 Jaedenar Guardsmen, 6 Jaedenar Adepts, and 6 Jaedenar Cultists before returning to Greta Mosshoof in Felwood.\030How goes your fight, $N? I know the shedding of blood as proof of honor can be disgusting to some, but you must understand that it serves two goals: you make my task easier by hurting their numbers, and we gain a respect for each other that will only make us stronger in times to come.$B$BI hope you understand.\030Forces of Jaedenar\0312,1,75,2,257,4,10922\0302,80,188,2,261,1,10922\0302,193,219,2,257,1,10922\0302,221,272,2,257,3,10922\0302,274,332,2,321,1,10922\0302,337,422,2,261,1,10922\0302,424,459,2,257,1,10922\0302,461,503,2,259,3,10922\0303,1,154,2,384,1,10922\0301,1,9,4,272,1,10922\0301,11,66,4,272,1,10922\0301,71,110,4,272,2,10922\0301,112,160,4,272,4,10922\0301,162,170,4,272,2,10922\0301,172,220,4,272,4,10922\0301,222,248,4,272,2,10922\0301,253,302,4,272,1,10922\0301,304,347,4,272,1,10922\0304,1,24,3,260,2,10922\0304,26,285,3,256,3,10922\0304,290,311,3,258,3,10922\0314244,2,2,Shadow\03010922,2,9,Greta Mosshoof\0312,361,1448,0,\0302,0,0,4,Jaedenar\0302,0,0,9,Greta Mosshoof\0302,0,0,9,Felwood\0315157,23,5157,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,7125,OBJECTIVE,4,13,Jaedenar Hound\030NPC,7113,OBJECTIVE,4,13,Jaedenar Guardian\030NPC,7115,OBJECTIVE,6,13,Jaedenar Adept\030NPC,7112,OBJECTIVE,6,13,Jaedenar Cultist",[5156]="PARTIAL\031consequences,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Good that you're alive, $N. Bad that the water still exists. I was hoping to find at least one pure source of water here in Felwood. It looks like my search has failed. The process of healing the land could have been made much easier with its existence.$B$BI will have to concern myself with saving what forest creatures I can while destroying those that have become so corrupt that they endanger themselves as much as travelers through this once-mighty forest.\030To the north, along the east of the road in what's called Shatter Scar Vale, is an area where infernals were called down during the last great war--the craters still scar the land, as do the infernals themselves.$B$BI am curious about two things. First, are there still entropic elementals roaming the area? And second, are the craters still filled with the corrupt, fetid water that gathered there years ago? Will you help me and check, $N? Be careful though, the infernals destroy anything in their path.\030Seek out and destroy 2 Entropic Beasts and 2 Entropic Horrors while exploring Shatter Scar Vale. After checking to see if the craters there are still filled with corrupt fel water, return to Taronn Redfeather in Felwood.\030Explore the craters in Shatter Scar Vale\030I hope your search goes well, $N. I haven't started heading that far north, but I will admit, the thought of crossing the path of an infernal at any point scares me just a little. The creatures are brainless, but still quite intimidating.\030Verifying the Corruption\0312,1,212,2,261,1,10921\0302,217,246,2,257,1,10921\0302,248,307,2,257,2,10921\0302,309,409,2,325,2,10921\0302,411,441,2,257,2,10921\0302,443,506,2,261,1,10921\0303,1,96,2,388,1,10921\0303,98,220,2,388,4,10921\0301,1,27,4,272,1,10921\0301,29,60,4,272,1,10921\0301,62,132,4,272,1,10921\0301,134,168,4,272,1,10921\0301,170,253,4,272,4,10921\0301,258,461,4,276,3,10921\0305,1,33,3,258,3,10921\0305,35,179,3,256,3,10921\0305,181,238,3,256,1,10921\0304,1,40,3,384,1,10921\03110921,2,8,Taronn Redfeather\03089,3,16,Infernal\0312,361,1448,0,\0302,0,0,8,Taronn Redfeather\0302,0,0,8,Felwood\0304,0,0,11,Felwood\0303,0,0,18,Shatter Scar Vale\031\031NPC,9878,OBJECTIVE,2,13,Entropic Beast\030NPC,9879,OBJECTIVE,2,13,Entropic Horror",[5157]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This will do nicely, $N.$B$BNow all we have to do besides apply the waters to the braziers is to have it purified. That should not be difficult--it should only require a little travel.$B$BHopefully we can do this quickly.\030Deep within Jaedenar lies Shadow Hold--the main fortress of their corruption and evil.$B$BThe Shadow Council has protective spells surrounding their lair in the form of braziers. If I am to find out any more information about our enemy through scrying, then those braziers must be extinguished. By doing so, I should be able to spy on the Council and find out who leads them.$B$BIf you can, take this canteen and fill it at the Moon Well in the center of Jaedenar. Return to me afterwards.\030Take the Empty Canteen to the Moon Well in the center of Jaedenar and fill it before returning to Greta Mosshoof in Felwood.\030Once we have the waters from the Moon Well, we will purify it and use it to extinguish the braziers of protection within Shadow Hold. That should allow me ample time to see into the chambers even deeper and discern who actually leads this... cult.$B$BI pray the Earthmother is with us.\030Collection of the Corrupt Water\0312,1,86,2,261,1,10922\0302,91,178,2,257,1,10922\0302,180,294,2,261,4,10922\0302,296,375,2,257,1,10922\0302,380,464,2,257,4,10922\0302,466,489,2,257,1,10922\0303,1,124,2,384,1,10922\0301,1,24,4,272,3,10922\0301,29,114,4,272,1,10922\0301,116,184,4,272,1,10922\0301,189,221,4,272,3,10922\0304,1,133,3,256,3,10922\0304,135,241,3,256,1,10922\0304,243,247,3,256,1,10922\0304,252,285,3,256,1,10922\0314244,2,1,Shadow\0304244,2,2,Shadow\03010922,2,7,Greta Mosshoof\0304244,3,12,Shadow\0312,361,1448,0,\0302,0,0,1,Jaedenar\0302,0,0,5,Moon Well\0302,0,0,7,Moon Well\0302,0,0,7,Greta Mosshoof\0302,0,0,7,Felwood\0303,0,0,12,Moon Well\0303,0,0,12,Shadow Hold\0315155,19,5155,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305158,23,5158,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12907,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5158]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, you need the water from this Moon Well cleansed. Stopping this force of malice in Felwood seems noble enough, but it is not for me to decide if the water will be purified. I will ask the spirits of water--it will be up to them to decide if the cause is just.$B$BGive me a moment and I will tell them of your plea. I hope they are as sympathetic as I am to your cause.\030Take the corrupt water to the Barrens, $N. South of Ratchet, hidden along the shore, is an old friend of mine, a shaman named Islen Waterseer. She is a powerful shaman who will help us. Her relationship with the spirits of water has always been strong. Our task being a noble one should be enough to persuade her and the spirits of water to aid us in this task.$B$BYou should find her at a small camp right along the water's edge. And, $N, ignore the pirates... they are but a nuisance and no threat to you.\030Take the Corrupt Moon Well Water to Islen Waterseer in the Barrens.\030I sense you are not just a simple traveler looking for the path to Ratchet. Come, sit and rest at our camp. Speak to me when you're ready.\030Seeking Spiritual Aid\0312,1,42,2,261,1,10922\0302,44,142,2,257,1,10922\0302,144,185,2,257,3,10922\0302,187,252,2,257,1,10922\0302,254,361,2,257,1,10922\0302,366,430,2,257,1,10922\0302,432,461,2,257,1,10922\0302,463,507,2,261,1,10922\0303,1,67,2,388,1,10922\0301,1,52,4,274,1,5901\0301,54,175,4,272,4,5901\0301,177,262,4,272,4,5901\0301,267,317,4,272,3,5901\0301,319,371,4,274,3,5901\0304,1,75,3,256,1,5901\0304,77,107,3,256,1,5901\0304,109,138,3,256,1,5901\0315901,2,2,Islen Waterseer\0305901,2,9,Islen Waterseer\0312,361,1448,0,\0302,0,0,1,Barrens\0302,0,0,9,Islen Waterseer\0302,0,0,9,Barrens\0304,0,0,11,Felwood\0303,0,0,15,Ratchet\0315157,19,5157,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305159,23,5159,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5159]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This should be more than enough water for our purposes.$B$BI'm glad to hear that Islen was able to help us. Her strength with the water spirits has always been a strong one. She is also wise, and rare is it that the spirits do not agree with her purpose. The fact that both of them have blessed our task gives me hope that we are on the right path.\030Thank the spirits, $N. They are the ones that have come to your aid, not me.$B$BI give this purified water to you now. Please give my regards to Greta and my best wishes. She is tackling something greater than many of us... as I'm sure she will soon find out.$B$BThe Shadow Council is not a force to be trifled with, $N. Remember that.$B$BGo now. Take the water and return to Greta.\030Take the Purified Moon Well Water to Greta Mosshoof in Felwood.\030Ah, I see you've returned, $N. Good. Did you find Islen in the Barrens? Or do we have to find another way to accomplish our goals?\030Cleansed Water Returns to Felwood\0312,1,22,2,257,1,5901\0302,24,76,2,257,1,5901\0302,81,118,2,257,1,5901\0302,120,170,2,259,1,5901\0302,172,223,2,257,1,5901\0302,225,259,2,257,3,5901\0302,264,320,2,257,1,5901\0302,322,335,2,257,1,5901\0302,340,346,2,257,1,5901\0302,348,382,2,257,1,5901\0303,1,63,2,384,1,5901\0301,1,55,4,272,1,10922\0301,60,107,4,272,1,10922\0301,109,173,4,272,1,10922\0301,175,254,4,272,1,10922\0301,256,348,4,274,3,10922\0304,1,30,3,256,1,10922\0304,32,36,3,256,1,10922\0304,38,71,3,256,2,10922\0304,73,130,3,256,2,10922\0314244,2,7,Shadow\03010922,2,11,Greta Mosshoof\0312,361,1448,0,\0302,0,0,4,Greta\0302,0,0,10,Greta\0302,0,0,11,Greta Mosshoof\0302,0,0,11,Felwood\0303,0,0,19,Barrens\0315158,19,5158,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305165,23,5165,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[516]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031If our scouts and agents continue to procure valuable information such as this, we shall have the Lich King's Scourge removed from our lands in no time.\030I have received reports that a group of undead are holing up to prepare for an attack against us. Armed with this information, we can turn the tables and attack them first, nipping their little plan in the bud.$B$BUnfortunately, my information is spotty, at best. They are reported to be hiding in a location known as Beren's Peril. The exact location is unknown, but it appears to be a cave in the hills, near a pocket of Dalaran wizards.$B$BI trust your resourcefulness. Find them, and put them down.\030Locate Beren's Peril, then kill 6 Ravenclaw Drudgers and 6 Ravenclaw Guardians, then return to Shadow Priest Allister at the Sepulcher.\030Have you located their base yet, $n? Time is of the essence!\030Beren's Peril\0312,1,97,2,261,1,2121\0302,99,210,2,261,1,2121\0302,215,263,2,257,1,2121\0302,265,332,2,257,1,2121\0302,334,439,2,257,1,2121\0302,444,472,2,257,1,2121\0302,474,502,2,257,1,2121\0303,1,135,2,384,1,2121\0301,1,152,4,336,4,2121\0304,1,36,3,256,2,2121\0304,38,60,3,256,1,2121\0312121,2,8,Shadow Priest Allister\030111,2,8,Priest\03016980,4,9,The Lich King\0312,130,1421,0,\0302,0,0,8,Shadow Priest Allister\0302,0,0,8,Sepulcher\031\031NPC,1974,OBJECTIVE,6,13,Ravenclaw Drudger\030NPC,1973,OBJECTIVE,6,13,Ravenclaw Guardian",[5160]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The Aspects insist that we stay out of the affairs of mortals. In this world, however, such a thing is not always possible - especially when one of our own contemptuously disregards such edicts.\030Travel to Kalimdor, $r. Our flight makes its home in the frigid landscape of Winterspring. Once you reach Winterspring, find the caves of Mazthoril.$B$BUpon the icy floors of Mazthoril you will find cobalt runes. Hold one of my scales and stand upon a rune and you shall be transported to Haleh, our matron protectorate.$B$BGive her the scale so that she may scry what it is I have seen and felt, here in this doomed place.\030Travel to Winterspring and find Haleh. Give her Awbee's scale.\030It is good to see you, $N.\030The Matron Protectorate\0312,1,23,2,257,1,10740\0302,25,90,2,257,1,10740\0302,92,148,2,257,1,10740\0302,153,212,2,257,3,10740\0302,214,320,2,257,3,10740\0302,325,423,2,259,1,10740\0303,1,38,2,384,1,10740\0303,40,62,2,384,1,10740\0301,1,62,4,272,1,10929\0301,64,194,4,272,1,10929\0304,1,26,3,256,1,10929\03110929,2,5,Haleh\03010929,2,7,Haleh\0312,1583,0,0,\0302,0,0,1,Kalimdor\0302,0,0,5,Haleh\0302,0,0,7,Winterspring\0315161,23,5161,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5161]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031So it shall be...\030We understand what the cursed brood of Deathwing attempts to do and we know that it cannot be allowed.$B$BBecause of the protection Blackrock mountain affords Nefarian, it has become increasingly difficult for us to intercede.$B$BWe can, however, empower you, mortal - should you so choose.$B$BThe path before you is one full of peril. You must decide whether to accept our help. Ponder this and speak with me again when a decision has been made.\030Speak with Haleh if you wish to continue.\030\030Wrath of the Blue Flight\0312,1,102,2,261,1,10929\0302,107,226,2,259,1,10929\0302,231,290,2,257,1,10929\0302,295,335,2,257,1,10929\0302,337,379,2,257,1,10929\0302,381,446,2,257,1,10929\0303,1,41,2,386,4,10929\0301,1,17,4,272,3,10929\03111583,2,2,Nefarian\03010929,2,7,Haleh\0312,618,1452,0,\0315160,19,5160,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305162,23,5162,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5162]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I am Jeziba, known to many as the Sculptor. What I sculpt, however, are not statues, but heroes.$B$B\030It is the arcane that I control and the arcane which will send you to your next destination.$B$BWhen you are ready, the journey will begin. To the Plaguelands you will go and to Jeziba you will speak.$B$BHe is a mortal as wise as the ancients and as patient as the immovable earth. Find him in Andorhal.$B\030Speak with Jeziba in the Plaguelands. He resides in Andorhal.\030\030Wrath of the Blue Flight\0312,1,92,2,257,3,10929\0302,97,139,2,257,3,10929\0302,141,200,2,257,3,10929\0302,205,281,2,257,1,10929\0302,283,303,2,257,1,10929\0303,1,37,2,384,1,10929\0303,39,61,2,384,1,10929\0301,1,43,4,272,1,10976\0301,45,96,4,272,1,10976\03110976,2,3,Jeziba\03010976,2,6,Jeziba\03010976,4,8,Jeziba\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,3,Jeziba\0302,0,0,5,Andorhal\0302,0,0,6,Plaguelands\0302,0,0,7,Andorhal\0315161,19,5161,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305164,23,5164,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5163]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030objectiveLabel3\030objectiveLabel4\030requestItems\030title\031Hah! They'll think twice before making fun of my ideas again!$B$BThanks for your help, $N. I couldn't have had so much fun without you!\030It's all ready, $N!$B$BNow, I sent some mail to my friends already, telling them that I have a surprise for them. This is where you come in!$B$BI'm going to give you my mechanical yeti, and you need to surprise them by paying each of my friends a visit, turning the yeti on and sending it towards them.$B$B Once you have shown Legacki in Everlook, Sprinkle in Gadgetzan, and Quixxil in Marshal's Refuge, come back and tell me what happened!$B$BPlease bring my yeti back to me then, too.\030Take Umi's Mechanical Yeti and scare her friends with it:$B$BLegacki in Everlook (Winterspring)$BSprinkle in Gadgetzan (Tanaris)$BQuixxil in Marshal's Refuge (Un'Goro Crater)$B$BWhen you are done, bring the Mechanical Yeti back to Umi.\030\030Scare Legacki\030Scare Sprinkle\030Scare Quixxil\030I can't wait to hear how my friends react!$B$BThey'll never expect it!\030Are We There, Yeti?\0312,1,19,2,257,1,10305\0302,24,113,2,257,1,10305\0302,115,140,2,257,1,10305\0302,145,302,2,259,3,10305\0302,307,440,2,257,1,10305\0302,445,486,2,257,1,10305\0303,1,57,2,384,1,10305\0303,62,95,2,384,1,10305\0303,98,128,2,384,1,10305\0303,131,174,2,384,1,10305\0303,179,235,2,384,1,10305\0301,1,4,4,272,1,10305\0301,6,61,4,272,1,10305\0301,66,90,4,272,1,10305\0301,92,135,4,272,1,10305\0308,1,42,3,256,1,10305\0308,47,70,3,256,1,10305\0305,1,13,3,384,1,10305\0306,1,14,3,384,1,10305\0307,1,13,3,384,1,10305\03112257,2,4,Mechanical Yeti\03010978,2,5,Legacki\0307583,2,5,Sprinkle\03010977,2,5,Quixxil\03010980,2,7,Umi's Mechanical Yeti\03012257,2,7,Mechanical Yeti\03010978,2,8,Legacki\0307583,2,9,Sprinkle\03010977,2,10,Quixxil\03012257,2,11,Mechanical Yeti\03010978,3,18,Legacki\0307583,3,19,Sprinkle\03010977,3,20,Quixxil\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,5,Everlook\0302,0,0,5,Gadgetzan\0302,0,0,5,Marshal's Refuge\0302,0,0,8,Everlook\0302,0,0,9,Gadgetzan\0302,0,0,10,Marshal's Refuge\0302,0,0,11,Umi\031977,19,977,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0308798,23,8798,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,10978,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Legacki\030NPC,7583,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Sprinkle\030NPC,10977,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Quixxil\030SPELL,17166,OBJECTIVE,?,17,\030SPELL,17166,OBJECTIVE,?,17,\030SPELL,17166,OBJECTIVE,?,17,",[5164]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hundreds upon hundreds of pages filled with garbled text and symbols make up the brunt of this book.\030A finer instrument of justice, Haleh could not have chosen. Read from the catalogue of the wayward and be enlightened.$B$BShould you persist... should you do what is asked of you... should you survive... a hero you will make.\030Read from the Catalogue of the Wayward.$B\030\030Catalogue of the Wayward\0312,1,59,2,257,4,10976\0302,61,118,2,257,1,10976\0302,123,143,2,257,1,10976\0302,145,181,2,257,1,10976\0302,183,203,2,265,1,10976\0302,205,225,2,257,3,10976\0303,1,39,2,384,1,10976\0301,1,100,4,272,1,0\03110929,2,1,Haleh\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,7,Catalogue of the Wayward\0315162,19,5162,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,176192,FINISHER,?,12,Catalogue of the Wayward",[5165]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030objectiveLabel3\030objectiveLabel4\030objectiveLabel5\030requestItems\030title\031I was able to see you with my spells as soon as the last brazier's flames died. Well done, $N.$B$BI learned a few things before the Shadow Council's warlocks were able to recast their spells. Hopefully it will be enough.$B$BFor now, rest. I will tell you what I've learned in a moment.\030Now, you must return to Jaedenar. The braziers are more than likely spread throughout Shadow Hold. Douse each of their flames and the protections the Council has set up will fall for at least a short period of time. I will be waiting for that to happen. When it does, I will look deep within the Hold and try to find out who the head of this beast is. Then, and only then, will we see about attacking them directly.\030Using the Purified Moon Well Water, douse the flames of the four braziers of protection within Shadow Hold in Felwood, then return to Greta Mosshoof in the Emerald Sanctuary.\030\030Extinguish the Brazier of Pain\030Extinguish the Brazier of Malice\030Extinguish the Brazier of Suffering\030Extinguish the Brazier of Hatred\030The braziers must be extinguished if we are to have any hope of being prepared for a much greater battle. Going in to the dragon's lair without any knowledge is a fool's errand. And this is much worse than a dragon. The Shadow Council are solely responsible for a great number of crimes and atrocities. We'll have to work quickly if we're to stop them.\030Dousing the Flames of Protection\0312,1,33,2,257,1,10922\0302,35,98,2,257,1,10922\0302,100,215,2,265,3,10922\0302,217,253,2,257,3,10922\0302,255,351,2,257,3,10922\0302,353,415,2,261,3,10922\0303,1,174,2,384,1,10922\0301,1,79,4,272,1,10922\0301,81,94,4,272,1,10922\0301,99,191,4,272,1,10922\0301,193,220,4,272,3,10922\0301,225,238,4,272,1,10922\0301,240,285,4,272,3,10922\0309,1,105,3,262,4,10922\0309,107,177,3,256,1,10922\0309,179,215,3,256,1,10922\0309,217,302,3,256,1,10922\0309,304,352,3,256,4,10922\0305,1,30,3,384,1,10922\0306,1,32,3,384,1,10922\0307,1,35,3,388,1,10922\0308,1,32,3,384,1,10922\0314244,2,2,Shadow\0304244,2,7,Shadow\03010922,2,7,Greta Mosshoof\0304244,4,10,Shadow\0304244,3,17,Shadow\0312,361,1448,0,\0302,0,0,1,Jaedenar\0302,0,0,5,Hold\0302,0,0,7,Shadow Hold\0302,0,0,7,Felwood\0302,0,0,7,Greta Mosshoof\0302,0,0,7,Emerald Sanctuary\0315159,19,5159,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305242,23,5242,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,176158,OBJECTIVE,1,14,Brazier of Pain\030OBJECT,176159,OBJECTIVE,1,14,Brazier of Malice\030OBJECT,176160,OBJECTIVE,1,14,Brazier of Suffering\030OBJECT,176161,OBJECTIVE,1,14,Brazier of Hatred\030SPELL,17155,OBJECTIVE,?,17,\030SPELL,17155,OBJECTIVE,?,17,\030SPELL,17155,OBJECTIVE,?,17,\030SPELL,17155,OBJECTIVE,?,17,",[5166]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Do you not yet understand? The journey was the destination. Can you not feel the battle scars? The pain you underwent?$B$BHaving survived the ordeal, you are a more powerful being. Much more powerful. This breastplate is merely a reflection of your own innate abilities.\030The forging of a powerful breastplate to protect against the unrelenting attacks of the chromatic flight is one built upon irony.$B$BThe scales of the very beasts we battle must be sewn to the pristine carapace of an elder chromatic drake or dragon. None are known to exist at this time and we should hope that none will ever exist.$B$BLastly, perhaps the most difficult of all components: the blood of heroes.$B$BThe Sculptor must ultimately forge this creation.\030To forge the Breastplate of the Chromatic Flight, you will be required to bring the following items to Jeziba the 'Sculptor':$B$B1 Chromatic Carapace.$B$B10 Brilliant Chromatic Scales.$B$B10 Blood of Heroes.$B$B10 Frayed Abomination Stitchings.\030You have chosen wisely, $R.\030Breastplate of the Chromatic Flight\0312,1,129,2,271,1,0\0302,134,249,2,261,1,0\0302,251,332,2,259,3,0\0302,337,410,2,257,4,0\0302,415,463,2,257,1,0\0303,1,125,2,384,3,0\0303,130,150,2,384,1,0\0303,155,184,2,384,1,0\0303,189,207,2,384,1,0\0303,212,244,2,384,1,0\0301,1,26,4,272,2,10976\0301,28,59,4,272,1,10976\0301,61,94,4,276,2,10976\0301,96,118,4,272,2,10976\0301,123,180,4,272,1,10976\0301,182,200,4,272,1,10976\0301,202,270,4,272,1,10976\0304,1,27,3,256,1,10976\03110976,2,6,Jeziba\0308545,2,10,Abomination\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,6,Jeziba the\0315164,19,5164,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,176192,GIVER,?,9,Catalogue of the Wayward\030ITEM,12871,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,12607,OBJECTIVE,10,15,\030ITEM,12938,OBJECTIVE,10,15,\030ITEM,12735,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[5167]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031They will smell their kin as you enter their halls, $N. Crush them with their own fear!\030The carapace of a mature chromatic drake is needed to form the foundation of the leggings. Brilliant chromatic scales are then layered upon the wire frame and enchanted in the blood of heroes. Finally, the supple skin of shadow must be applied to the inner greaves.\030To forge the Legplates of the Chromatic Defier, you will be required to bring the following items to Jeziba the 'Sculptor':$B$B1 Chromatic Carapace.$B$B10 Brilliant Chromatic Scales.$B$B10 Blood of Heroes.$B$B5 Skin of Shadow.\030Such an item has never been crafted!\030Legplates of the Chromatic Defier\0312,1,90,2,257,1,0\0302,92,192,2,257,1,0\0302,194,265,2,257,1,0\0303,1,123,2,384,3,0\0303,128,148,2,384,1,0\0303,153,182,2,384,1,0\0303,187,205,2,384,1,0\0303,210,226,2,384,1,0\0301,1,55,4,272,3,10976\0301,57,87,4,272,1,10976\0304,1,36,3,256,1,10976\0314244,2,3,Shadow\03010976,2,4,Jeziba\0304244,2,8,Shadow\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,4,Jeziba the\0315164,19,5164,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,176192,GIVER,?,9,Catalogue of the Wayward\030ITEM,12871,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,12607,OBJECTIVE,10,15,\030ITEM,12938,OBJECTIVE,10,15,\030ITEM,12753,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[5168]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have the libram and the shield!$B$BTheir history is entwined with the history of Darrowshire, and somehow, I know that fate will bring them together again.\030The heroes of Darrowshire hold a place in my heart, and the book you brought me, the Annals of Darrowshire, tells their tales.$B$BIt tells of the paladin Davil Lightfire and how the Crusade took his libram to the town hall of Hearthglen.$B$BIts passages also speak of my brother, Captain Redpath.  After his betrayal, his shield was cracked and discarded and now lies in the most unlikely of places -- near the barn of Gahrron's Withering.$B$BGather these relics, $N.  For fate and tragedy surrounds them.\030Bring Davil's Libram and Redpath's Shield to Carlin Redpath.\030Do you have the relics, $N?\030Heroes of Darrowshire\0312,1,126,2,257,1,11063\0302,131,237,2,257,1,11063\0302,242,296,2,257,1,11063\0302,299,439,2,257,1,11063\0302,444,467,2,257,1,11063\0302,470,505,2,257,1,11063\0303,1,60,2,384,1,11063\0301,1,35,4,272,1,11063\0301,40,159,4,336,3,11063\0304,1,27,3,256,2,11063\03110944,2,2,Davil Lightfire\03010937,2,3,Captain Redpath\03011063,2,7,Carlin Redpath\0312,139,1423,0,\0302,0,0,7,Carlin Redpath\0315210,19,5210,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12954,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,12955,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[517]="PARTIAL\031loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Finally! Now we are ready for action!\030This new elixir is finally ready to be tested.  But why let a perfectly good, highly contagious plague go to waste on a mere frog or dog?  Let's have us some true fun in the name of Lady Sylvanas.$B$BHead down to Dun Garok.  You know the barracks where those filthy little dwarves skitter about.  Steal me a keg of their Shindigger Stout.  Once I have that keg, you and I will have quite the party, $N.\030Bring a keg of Shindigger Stout to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill.\030Sometimes I get so bored out here in Tarren Mill I like to open up the formaldehyde jar and let the lovely aroma waft through the air. Makes Umpi a little nervous though.$B$BSo were you able to get a keg from the Dwarves? I swear if I have to stare at this deadly elixir without using on it someone for another day I am going to scream.\030Elixir of Agony\0312,1,46,2,257,1,2216\0302,49,137,2,261,2,2216\0302,140,196,2,257,1,2216\0302,201,223,2,257,1,2216\0302,226,295,2,257,1,2216\0302,298,338,2,261,1,2216\0302,341,402,2,257,3,2216\0303,1,67,2,384,1,2216\0301,1,8,4,272,1,2216\0301,10,37,4,304,1,2216\0304,1,134,3,256,1,2216\0304,136,170,3,256,1,2216\0304,175,221,3,256,2,2216\0304,223,336,3,256,4,2216\03113321,2,2,Frog\03015065,2,3,Lady\0302216,2,8,Apothecary Lydon\0302230,3,12,Umpi\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,4,Dun Garok\0302,0,0,8,Apothecary Lydon\0302,0,0,8,Tarren Mill\0303,0,0,11,Tarren Mill\0303,0,0,13,Dwarves\031515,19,515,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030524,23,524,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3517,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[518]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The snow blooms red with the blood of the ogres, but we cannot cease our efforts until the spirit and numbers of the Crushridge have been crushed and ground into the dirt and snow.\030Mug'Thol and his Crushridge ogres have overrun the ruins of Alterac. It will be hard to inflict any serious punishment upon him without thinning out the ogres' numbers.$B$BAfter softening them up, we'll proceed.$B$BUnderstood? Good. Now go.\030Kill 10 Crushridge Maulers for Melisara in Tarren Mill.\030I note that your task is unfinished, $N. Shall I inform Sharlindra of your ineptitude?\030The Crown of Will\0312,1,68,2,321,1,2278\0302,70,168,2,257,3,2278\0302,173,211,2,257,1,2278\0302,216,226,2,257,2,2278\0302,228,232,2,257,1,2278\0302,234,240,2,257,1,2278\0303,1,55,2,384,1,2278\0301,1,180,4,272,1,2278\0304,1,40,3,256,1,2278\0304,42,86,3,256,2,2278\0312257,2,1,Mug'thol\0302278,2,7,Melisara\0302227,3,10,Sharlindra\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,7,Tarren Mill\031519,23,519,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,2254,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Crushridge Mauler",[5181]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You found them! Well done, $N! These relics hold a power I do not fully understand, a power you will one day harness.$B$BThey also bring dark memories to my mind, memories death and treachery, and of the last night of Darrowshire...\030The Annals of Darrowshire tells of the villains of that battle.  It tells how the ghoul lord Horgus the Ravager was destroyed by Alliance forces during the battle.  His body was cast into a lake, northwest of Corin's Crossing, and his skull remains there.$B$BMarduk the Black was never defeated, but his fabled sword was shattered and lost.  It lies at the bottom of the gorge west of Corin's Crossing.$B$BRetrieve these items, $N.  I know not why, but I am certain their fate lies with you.\030Bring the Skull of Horgus and the Shattered Sword of Marduk to Carlin Redpath at Light's Hope Chapel.\030Did you find the skull and the sword, $N?\030Villains of Darrowshire\0312,1,63,2,261,1,11063\0302,66,163,2,261,1,11063\0302,166,255,2,257,1,11063\0302,260,340,2,261,1,11063\0302,343,402,2,257,1,11063\0302,407,431,2,257,1,11063\0302,434,491,2,257,1,11063\0303,1,101,2,384,3,11063\0301,1,15,4,272,1,11063\0301,17,30,4,272,1,11063\0301,32,117,4,272,3,11063\0301,122,232,4,272,1,11063\0304,1,41,3,256,2,11063\031846,2,2,Ghoul\03010946,2,2,Horgus the Ravager\03010939,2,4,Marduk the Black\03011063,2,8,Carlin Redpath\0312,139,1423,0,\0302,0,0,5,Corin's Crossing\0302,0,0,8,Carlin Redpath\0302,0,0,8,Light's Hope Chapel\0315210,19,5210,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12956,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,12957,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[519]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031...and I thought ogres smelled foul enough to begin with.$B$BWhen you bring me Mug'Thol's head, I will have the four of them mounted on pikes above Alterac. A fitting monument to those who go against the Dark Lady's wishes.\030Targ, Muckrake, and Glommus are Mug'Thol's lieutenants. They are loyal to him, though who can say what drives an ogre to loyalty.$B$BBring me their heads, $n, and then all that will remain is to remove Mug'Thol's head, crown and all.\030Kill Targ, Muckrake, and Glommus and bring their heads to Melisara in Tarren Mill.\030I want their heads, $N, not excuses.\030The Crown of Will\0312,1,55,2,257,1,2278\0302,57,129,2,257,1,2278\0302,134,233,2,257,3,2278\0303,1,82,2,384,1,2278\0301,1,57,4,272,1,2278\0301,62,156,4,272,3,2278\0301,158,223,4,272,1,2278\0304,1,36,3,258,1,2278\0312420,2,1,Targ\0302421,2,1,Muckrake\0302422,2,1,Glommus\030211,2,2,Ogre\0302420,2,4,Targ\0302421,2,4,Muckrake\0302422,2,4,Glommus\0302278,2,4,Melisara\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,4,Melisara\0302,0,0,4,Tarren Mill\031518,19,518,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030520,23,520,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3550,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,3551,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,3552,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[52]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thanks a lot for the help, $N. Something in the forest must be making these animals so bold.$B$BWhatever it is, I hope it stays there.\030Hail, $N.  Wild animals are growing more and more aggressive the farther we get from Goldshire, and the Eastvale Logging Camp suffers nearly constant attacks from wolves and bears!$B$BWe could use your help out here.\030Kill 8 Prowlers and 5 Young Forest Bears, and then return to Guard Thomas at the east Elwynn bridge.\030Have you killed those wolves and bears?\030Protect the Frontier\0312,1,9,2,257,1,261\0302,12,180,2,261,1,261\0302,185,216,2,257,4,261\0303,1,100,2,384,1,261\0301,1,30,4,272,1,261\0301,32,92,4,272,1,261\0301,97,134,4,274,3,261\0304,1,39,3,256,2,261\031261,2,4,Guard Thomas\0304982,2,4,Thomas\0312,12,1429,0,\0302,0,0,2,Goldshire\0302,0,0,4,Guard Thomas\031\031NPC,118,OBJECTIVE,8,13,Prowler\030NPC,822,OBJECTIVE,5,13,Young Forest Bear",[520]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have done your duty well, $N. Mug'Thol's head shall adorn the highest peak of the ruins of Alterac, and the Deathguard will sweep the remnants of the Crushridge into the ground.\030With Mug'Thol's lieutenants dead, all that remains is to kill Mug'Thol and retrieve the Crown of Will. I have no doubt he'll be reluctant to part with it. Most likely expecting you, too, given the... departure... of his fellows.$B$BFind Mug'Thol, and deliver his head and the Crown to me. The Crushridge resistance will be at an end.\030Kill Mug'Thol, and return his head with the Crown of Will to Melisara in Tarren Mill.\030Three heads I have, a fourth I need. It will be Mug'Thol's, or it will be yours, $N. That I promise.\030The Crown of Will\0312,1,102,2,257,3,2278\0302,104,154,2,257,1,2278\0302,156,199,2,257,1,2278\0302,201,212,2,257,1,2278\0302,214,228,2,257,1,2278\0302,233,288,2,257,1,2278\0302,290,333,2,257,3,2278\0303,1,85,2,384,3,2278\0301,1,33,4,272,1,2278\0301,35,181,4,336,3,2278\0304,1,36,3,258,1,2278\0304,38,84,3,256,3,2278\0304,86,100,3,256,1,2278\0312257,2,1,Mug'thol\0302257,2,6,Mug'thol\0302257,2,8,Mug'thol\0302278,2,8,Melisara\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,8,Melisara\0302,0,0,8,Tarren Mill\031519,19,519,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030521,23,521,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3553,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,3554,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5201]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I am relieved to hear that for a short moment, we will not have to worry about the Winterfall intrusion.$B$BYou are beginning to show your perseverance, $N.\030My presence goes unnoticed by most, $N. However, there is an annoyance that seems firmly rooted here in Winterspring: the Winterfall furbolg.$B$BAlthough I have never directly attacked the furbolg, they seem crazed, fearful of anything in their path. I have watched them slay countless creatures that had the misfortune to simply be in the wrong place at the wrong time.$B$BI am weary of their meddling -- please, help me by fighting back. Slay the furbolg and keep them away from Frostsaber Rock.\030Rivern Frostwind wants you to slay 5 Winterfall Shaman and 5 Winterfall Ursa.\030The furbolgs seem to suffer from such paranoia...\030Winterfall Intrusion\0312,1,39,2,257,1,10618\0302,41,141,2,257,4,10618\0302,146,250,2,261,4,10618\0302,252,370,2,257,1,10618\0302,375,439,2,261,1,10618\0302,441,497,2,257,1,10618\0303,1,77,2,386,1,10618\0301,1,104,4,272,3,10618\0301,109,156,4,272,1,10618\0304,1,49,3,260,4,10618\03131,2,2,Furbolg\03031,2,3,Furbolg\03031,2,6,Furbolg\0307431,2,6,Frostsaber\03010618,2,7,Rivern Frostwind\0307439,2,7,Winterfall Shaman\0307438,2,7,Winterfall Ursa\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,2,Winterspring\0302,0,0,6,Frostsaber Rock\031\031NPC,7439,OBJECTIVE,5,13,Winterfall Shaman\030NPC,7438,OBJECTIVE,5,13,Winterfall Ursa",[5202]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The key, you've found it! Please, give it to me and I can finally escape!\030The small red key seems to be made of some kind of bone material. It is heavy in your hand, but appears very fragile. Why would a member of the Shadow Council have such a thing? Perhaps there is something within Jaedenar that this strange key unlocks.\030Search through Jaedenar to discover what the Blood Red Key is used for.\030I begin to wonder if I'll ever escape this cage.$B$BIt's only a matter of time before they sacrifice me to whatever demons they worship. The monsters!\030A Strange Red Key\0312,1,65,2,257,4,0\0302,67,117,2,257,1,0\0302,119,177,2,257,4,0\0302,179,251,2,257,4,0\0303,1,71,2,384,1,0\0301,1,25,4,272,1,11016\0301,27,73,4,272,1,11016\0304,1,48,3,256,4,11016\0304,53,136,3,264,1,11016\0304,138,150,3,256,1,11016\0314244,2,3,Shadow\0312,361,1448,0,\0302,0,0,4,Jaedenar\0315203,23,5203,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,13140,STARTER,?,10,",[5203]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031You were the one who helped Arko escape? I'm so glad you found me. She passed by here not too long ago on her way to Darnassus. She had Lightforge in tow and wouldn't even take time to speak to the druids to be healed. She said it was far too urgent.$B$BBut she did tell me about your encounter with Trey's spirit. What a terrible fate for a Knight of the Silver Hand. She didn't show it, but I know it's tearing her up inside, the thought of losing one of her closest friends.\030But, as much as it pains me, there is one thing that must be done first: I have to find Trey's sword Lightforge and escape Shadow Hold to tell my superiors what's happening here. Can you help me, $N?$B$BOur equipment isn't far from here, and you've already proven you can survive the path to the top.$B$BAfter we escape, I'll head to Darnassus if you can find my friend Jessir near the Ashenvale border. She was to meet us at the Emerald Circle's camp near there.$B$BWhat do you say, $N? Can you help me again?\030Escort Arko'narin to where Lightforge and her equipment are being held, and then protect her as you escape Shadow Hold. Afterwards, seek out Jessir Moonbow in Felwood to let her know what's happened to her friends.\030Protect Arko'narin out of Shadow Hold\030You look winded, $n. Are you all right, or is something wrong?\030Rescue From Jaedenar\0312,1,178,2,257,1,11016\0302,180,199,2,257,2,11016\0302,204,300,2,265,1,11016\0302,305,403,2,257,4,11016\0302,405,463,2,257,1,11016\0302,468,487,2,257,2,11016\0302,489,510,2,257,2,11016\0303,1,119,2,396,1,11016\0303,121,214,2,384,1,11016\0301,1,40,4,272,2,11019\0301,42,66,4,272,1,11019\0301,68,127,4,336,1,11019\0301,129,218,4,272,1,11019\0301,220,250,4,272,1,11019\0301,255,314,4,272,1,11019\0301,316,368,4,272,1,11019\0301,370,477,4,272,1,11019\0305,1,20,3,256,1,11019\0305,22,62,3,256,2,11019\0304,1,37,3,396,1,11016\0314244,2,1,Shadow\03011018,2,8,Arko'narin\0304244,2,8,Shadow\03011019,2,9,Jessir Moonbow\03011018,3,20,Arko'narin\0304244,3,20,Shadow\0312,361,1448,0,\0302,0,0,4,Darnassus\0302,0,0,4,Ashenvale\0302,0,0,5,Emerald Circle's\0302,0,0,9,Felwood\0304,0,0,12,Darnassus\0315202,19,5202,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305204,23,5204,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5204]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You gather the paladin's remains as carefully as you can, recalling that at least his spirit has been released from any pain or suffering that might have been forced upon him.\030She would like to pretend that she's fine. She'd love for me to think that she's strong enough to deal with all of this on her own, but I know better than that. Trey's death and hearing the torture he was put through is going to haunt her for a long time, and there's nothing we can do to stop that. But we can give her some peace!$B$B$N, return to Shadow Hold, kill Trey's torturer and find his remains. There is no reason we can't tie off all these loose ends while Arko'narin mourns in her own private way.\030Return to Jaedenar and kill the succubus Rakaiah before finding the Remains of Trey Lightforge.\030You inspect the body, and there is no doubt that these are the remains of the Knight of the Silver Hand, Trey Lightforge. For a moment you think of Arko'narin and question if anyone in your life meant as much to you as this man meant to the Night elf captive you recently helped escape Shadow Hold.$B$BAfter taking another moment to gather your thoughts, you know that you cannot take the paladin's remains back to Jessir without killing his torturer first.\030Retribution of the Light\0312,1,42,2,257,4,11019\0302,44,160,2,257,1,11019\0302,162,299,2,257,3,11019\0302,301,331,2,265,1,11019\0302,336,404,2,257,1,11019\0302,406,509,2,257,1,11019\0303,1,95,2,384,1,11019\0301,1,175,4,276,4,11020\0304,1,121,3,256,1,11020\0304,123,298,3,260,4,11020\0304,303,457,3,256,1,11020\0314244,2,5,Shadow\03011018,2,6,Arko'narin\0301863,2,7,Succubus\0309518,2,7,Rakaiah\03011020,2,7,Remains of Trey Lightforge\03011018,3,10,Arko'narin\0304244,3,10,Shadow\0312,361,1448,0,\0302,0,0,5,Shadow Hold\0302,0,0,7,Jaedenar\0303,0,0,10,Night\0303,0,0,11,Jessir\0315203,19,5203,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305385,23,5385,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,9518,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Rakaiah",[5206]="PARTIAL\031consequences\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You found them! Wonderful!$B$BAlthough I don't fully understand how they can help us, I feel their power and I know in my bones that they are linked to my home village of Darrowshire.\030Chromie said the relics you gathered are reagents to a powerful spell, and one more is required: skulls from the scourge who took part in the battle of Darrowshire.$B$BTake this crystal and hunt scourge champions for their skulls.  The crystal is enchanted; if a champion took part in the battle, then when you pass the crystal over its skull it will resonate.  Bring me those resonating skulls.$B$BGo, $N.  You'll find scourge champions in the Noxious Glade to the north and the Fungal Vale to the west.\030Bring 5 Resonating Skulls and the Mystic Crystal to Carlin Redpath in Eastern Plaguelands.\030Do you have the skulls? Chromie said they will be critical for her spell, and that spell will give us the chance to save Darrowshire.\030Marauders of Darrowshire\0312,1,164,2,325,1,11063\0302,169,230,2,321,1,11063\0302,233,360,2,261,4,11063\0302,363,395,2,257,1,11063\0302,409,504,2,321,1,11063\0303,1,90,2,384,1,11063\0301,1,15,4,272,1,11063\0301,17,26,4,272,1,11063\0301,31,183,4,272,1,11063\0304,1,23,3,256,2,11063\0304,25,133,3,266,3,11063\03110667,2,1,Chromie\03011063,2,6,Carlin Redpath\03010667,3,11,Chromie\0312,139,1423,0,\0302,0,0,5,Noxious Glade\0302,0,0,6,Carlin Redpath\0302,0,0,6,Eastern Plaguelands\0315168,21,5168,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305181,21,5181,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305941,23,5941,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,13155,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[521]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031So this is the relic the ogre used to duck the will of the Dark Lady...$B$BStrange that something so simple could wield so great a power. And to fall into as clumsy hands as those. Well done, $N, I will deliver the crown to Lady Sylvanas, and see that she hears of your accomplishment.\030All that remains is to deliver the Crown of Will to Sharlindra in the Undercity. She will see that it is delivered to Lady Sylvanas. I would warn you against thinking to use it for your own purposes, $n, Mug'Thol's fate should be illustration enough.\030Deliver the Crown of Will to Sharlindra in the Undercity.\030I note that your task is unfinished, $N. Shall I inform Sharlindra of your ineptitude?\030The Crown of Will\0312,1,80,2,257,3,2278\0302,82,132,2,257,3,2278\0302,134,250,2,257,4,2278\0303,1,57,2,384,3,2278\0301,1,71,4,272,3,2227\0301,76,137,4,272,4,2227\0301,139,180,4,272,1,2227\0301,182,285,4,272,3,2227\0304,1,40,3,256,1,2227\0304,42,86,3,256,2,2227\0312227,2,1,Sharlindra\03015065,2,2,Lady\0302227,2,4,Sharlindra\030211,4,5,Ogre\03015065,4,5,Lady\03015065,4,8,Lady\0302227,3,10,Sharlindra\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,1,Sharlindra\0302,0,0,1,Undercity\0302,0,0,2,Lady Sylvanas\0302,0,0,4,Sharlindra\0302,0,0,4,Undercity\0304,0,0,8,Lady Sylvanas\031520,19,520,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5210]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031What is this book? The Annals of Darrowshire? That was my home before the war... my home before the battle that destroyed it! Why did you bring me this book?$B$BBut look here! At the end there are pages that tell tales of the days beyond the battle! Here is a passage about me! And one about my brother Joseph! Is this book true?$B$BWe must discover the truth!\030The Annals of Darrowshire, through my magic, has gained pages at its end, and now it extends its history beyond the battle.  One of the extra passages tells of another Redpath, Carlin, who survived Joseph's betrayal.  Carlin's now in the Plaguelands to the east, at the Light's Hope Chapel.$B$BTake the book and speak with him.\030Bring the Extended Annals of Darrowshire to Carlin Redpath in Eastern Plaguelands.\030You've come from the west? How fare the rest of Lordaeron? I know that Andorhal is lost, but has the Scourge yet reached fair Tirisfal?\030Brother Carlin\0312,1,123,2,325,1,10667\0302,126,216,2,257,1,10667\0302,219,290,2,257,3,10667\0302,295,327,2,257,1,10667\0303,1,82,2,384,1,10667\0301,1,18,4,272,2,11063\0301,20,45,4,272,2,11063\0301,47,80,4,276,1,11063\0301,82,125,4,276,1,11063\0301,127,157,4,272,2,11063\0301,162,175,4,272,1,11063\0301,177,249,4,276,1,11063\0301,251,277,4,272,1,11063\0301,279,310,4,272,1,11063\0301,312,329,4,272,2,11063\0301,334,360,4,272,1,11063\0304,1,26,3,256,2,11063\0304,28,58,3,256,2,11063\0304,60,135,3,324,2,11063\03111063,2,5,Carlin Redpath\0312,139,1423,0,\0302,0,0,3,Plaguelands\0302,0,0,3,Light's Hope Chapel\0302,0,0,5,Carlin Redpath\0302,0,0,5,Eastern Plaguelands\0315154,19,5154,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305181,23,5181,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5211]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030requestItems\030title\031It is good to hear you found the tortured souls of my brethren and freed them. My heart will weep less, knowing at least some of the defenders of Darrowshire no longer wallow in the vile subservience of the Scourge.\030Many of the defenders fell at the battle of Darrowshire.  And many roam again as the ghastly servants of the Scourge!  Find these poor souls and end their misery!$B$BHunt cannibal ghouls, gibbering ghouls and diseased flayers.  Many of these fiends were once the good folk of Darrowshire and destroying their forms now will set their souls free.$B$BYou will find them in Plaguewood and Corin's Crossing, and in other Scourge strongholds of Eastern Plaguelands.\030Free 15 Darrowshire Spirits and return to Carlin Redpath.\030\030Darrowshire Spirits Freed\030The poor defenders of Darrowshire cry out to me in my dreams, $N. You must free them!\030Defenders of Darrowshire\0312,1,56,2,261,1,11063\0302,59,117,2,321,1,11063\0302,120,162,2,257,1,11063\0302,167,226,2,257,1,11063\0302,229,345,2,261,3,11063\0302,350,460,2,321,3,11063\0303,1,57,2,384,1,11063\0301,1,78,4,272,1,11063\0301,80,215,4,336,3,11063\0306,1,65,3,256,1,11063\0306,67,85,3,256,1,11063\0305,1,25,3,384,1,11063\03111063,2,7,Carlin Redpath\0312,139,1423,0,\0302,0,0,6,Plaguewood\0302,0,0,7,Carlin Redpath\0315241,19,5241,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,11064,OBJECTIVE,15,13,Darrowshire Spirit",[5212]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031There is something that has changed in the chemical structure of the plague's active agents. More data is required.\030The Forsaken apothecaries are not the only beings in this world schooled in the sciences.$B$BI have been studying the plague for years, $r. We had previously thought that the potency of the plague was dwindling, but what I have discovered here in the Plaguelands is startling. The plague seems to be growing in strength!$B$BI need to run more tests! The most potent source of the plague is from the tainted flesh of the most recently infected. Travel to Stratholme and bring me samples, $N.$B\030Recover 10 Plagued Flesh Samples from Stratholme and return them to Betina Bigglezink. You suspect that any creature in Stratholme would have said flesh sample.\030Some say I worry too much - to them I say, 'You don't worry enough!'\030The Flesh Does Not Lie\0312,1,89,2,257,1,11035\0302,94,139,2,261,1,11035\0302,141,276,2,261,1,11035\0302,278,320,2,261,4,11035\0302,325,349,2,259,1,11035\0302,351,443,2,261,1,11035\0302,445,490,2,257,1,11035\0303,1,86,2,384,1,11035\0303,88,160,2,384,4,11035\0301,1,92,4,276,1,11035\0301,94,115,4,272,1,11035\0304,1,68,3,256,1,11035\03111035,2,8,Betina Bigglezink\0312,2017,0,0,\0302,0,0,3,Plaguelands\0302,0,0,7,Stratholme\0302,0,0,8,Stratholme\0302,0,0,8,Betina Bigglezink\0302,0,0,9,Stratholme\0315213,23,5213,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,13174,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[5213]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Astonishing! This will take months to dissect and analyze. The Argent Dawn thanks you for your efforts, $N.$B$BWith our blessing, take your pick between either this Seal of the Dawn or this Rune of the Dawn. You can use either of them instead of a standard Argent Dawn Commission to collect scourgestones on our behalf. Should you lose yours, speak with me and I'll get you a replacement.\030You will have to delve deeper into Stratholme, $N.$B$BBeyond the first gates you will find the ziggurats. We know that the Scourge draws great power from these structures. Search the Ziggurats and return with any information that you may discover.$B\030Travel to Stratholme and search the ziggurats. Find and return new Scourge Data to Betina Bigglezink.$B\030We are on the verge of discovering what this new active plague agent may be!\030The Active Agent\0312,1,50,2,257,3,11035\0302,55,105,2,257,3,11035\0302,107,171,2,321,1,11035\0302,173,247,2,257,1,11035\0303,1,46,2,384,1,11035\0303,48,101,2,448,1,11035\0301,1,12,4,272,1,11035\0301,14,58,4,272,3,11035\0301,60,107,4,272,1,11035\0301,112,207,4,272,1,11035\0301,209,319,4,272,1,11035\0301,321,388,4,272,1,11035\0304,1,76,3,260,1,11035\03111035,2,6,Betina Bigglezink\0312,2017,0,0,\0302,0,0,5,Stratholme\0302,0,0,6,Betina Bigglezink\0315212,19,5212,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,13176,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5214]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh sweet, sweet stogie, how I have missed you...\030Terrible thing... what happened to Fras. You see, the town was sacked and Fras didn't want to leave his precious goods behind. The last thing I remember him saying was, 'I'll burn every last leaf before they get their damned, dirty hands on them!'$B$BI may love a good stogie but I'm no fool. I left Fras and his delightful store that day. I assume he went down in flames but if there's a chance that even one box of his famous tobacco is still intact...$B$BWhat do you say, $N? Find a box for ol' Smokey?\030Find Fras Siabi's smoke shop in Stratholme and recover a box of Siabi's Premium Tobacco. Return to Smokey LaRue when the job is done.$B\030I can't take it, $N! You gotta help me! I'm dying!\030The Great Fras Siabi\0312,1,17,2,257,1,11033\0302,19,40,2,257,1,11033\0302,42,126,2,257,1,11033\0302,128,247,2,265,1,11033\0302,252,292,2,257,1,11033\0302,294,339,2,257,1,11033\0302,341,454,2,257,4,11033\0302,459,478,2,257,2,11033\0302,480,505,2,257,2,11033\0303,1,88,2,384,1,11033\0303,90,133,2,384,1,11033\0301,1,48,4,272,1,11033\0304,1,20,3,256,1,11033\0304,22,39,3,256,1,11033\0304,41,50,3,256,1,11033\03114528,2,3,Precious\03011058,2,10,Fras Siabi\03011033,2,11,Smokey LaRue\0312,2017,0,0,\0302,0,0,2,Fras\0302,0,0,10,Stratholme\0302,0,0,11,Smokey LaRue\031\031ITEM,13172,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5215]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031May the power of the Light shine upon you in these dark times, $c.  I am pleased to serve as your coordinator for our plan to sabotage the Scourge's cauldrons.$B$BOur goal will be to change the composition of the plague that the cauldrons create into something that negatively affects the Scourge.  In order to affect this change, you will need to secure access to each of the four cauldrons present in the Western Plaguelands.$B$BStand ready hero, for a glorious battle against the vile Scourge awaits you!\030Within the lands of former Lordaeron are eight cauldrons - four here in the west, and four more ensconced in the east.  These cauldrons spew poisons into the air, propagating the plague throughout the land for the Scourge.$B$BThe necromantic might of Kel'Thuzad is too strong to outright shut down these cauldrons, but we think we might have a way to subvert them to our advantage.  My second, High Priestess MacDonnell, will be your point on this assignment; she'll continue the briefing from here.\030Speak with High Priestess MacDonnell at Chillwind Point, Western Plaguelands.\030\030The Scourge Cauldrons\0312,1,118,2,257,1,10838\0302,121,222,2,325,1,10838\0302,227,381,2,257,4,10838\0302,384,499,2,257,3,10838\0303,1,77,2,384,1,10838\0301,1,66,4,272,1,11053\0301,69,159,4,336,3,11053\0301,164,297,4,342,3,11053\0301,300,427,4,274,3,11053\0301,432,507,4,340,1,11053\03115990,2,3,Kel'Thuzad\03011053,2,4,High Priestess MacDonnell\030112,2,4,Priestess\03011053,2,5,High Priestess MacDonnell\030112,2,5,Priestess\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,5,Chillwind Point\0304,0,0,9,Western Plaguelands\0315092,19,5092,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305216,23,5216,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5216]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The key taken from Cauldron Lord Bilemaw is a perfect fit in unlocking the access panel.  A foul stench emanates from the opened panel as an unknown mix of concentrated substances swirl inside the cauldron.$B$BThere is a small spigot that the bottle fits well enough under, allowing you to draw a sample for High Priestess MacDonnell back at Chillwind Point.\030Of the four cauldrons here in the west, the one located at Felstone Field may be the easiest one in obtaining access to.  The Scourge have greener troops positioned here, though they should not be underestimated.$B$BGo to Felstone Field, northwest of Andorhal, and engage the cauldron lord there.  We think it has a key that will unlock access to the cauldron.  When unlocked, use this bottle to obtain a sample of the poisons inside the cauldron; we'll need it for study in developing a counter agent.\030Go to Felstone Field in Western Plaguelands to locate and defeat the Cauldron Lord present there.  It may have a key that will allow access to the cauldron.  You must have the Empty Felstone Field Bottle with you to secure a sample of the poisons used inside the cauldron.\030An access panel to the cauldron remains securely fastened.  In order to open it, you will need to find the key.\030Target: Felstone Field\0312,1,120,2,257,1,11053\0302,123,212,2,321,1,11053\0302,217,296,2,257,1,11053\0302,299,360,2,257,3,11053\0302,363,502,2,259,1,11053\0303,1,97,2,384,1,11053\0303,100,156,2,384,3,11053\0303,159,272,2,384,1,11053\0301,1,88,4,272,1,0\0301,91,206,4,272,1,0\0301,211,358,4,272,1,0\0304,1,58,3,256,1,0\0304,61,111,3,258,3,0\03111075,4,9,Cauldron Lord Bilemaw\03011053,4,11,High Priestess MacDonnell\030112,4,11,Priestess\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,1,Felstone Field\0302,0,0,3,Felstone Field\0302,0,0,6,Felstone Field\0302,0,0,6,Western Plaguelands\0304,0,0,9,Cauldron Lord Bilemaw\0304,0,0,11,Chillwind Point\0315215,19,5215,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305217,23,5217,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,176361,FINISHER,?,12,Scourge Cauldron\030ITEM,13194,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5217]="PARTIAL\031consequences\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done $N - it should take Alchemist Arbington no time at all to analyze this and devise a counter agent to introduce into the cauldron.  If we are able to pump out enough of it into the air, we might be able to weaken all the Scourge present here.$B$BThis will no doubt be an ongoing ordeal; we will need to continually hit these cauldrons and introduce our reagents into their mix.  Still, if we can keep it up, we will have a huge advantage over Scourge when the time comes for battle!\030You fill the bottle with enough of the cauldron's poisonous concoction for a suitable sample to be studied.$B$BWith the poison in hand, it is time to return to High Priestess MacDonnell at Chillwind Camp to complete the mission.\030Bring the Filled Felstone Field Bottle to High Priestess MacDonnell at Chillwind Camp, Western Plaguelands.\030Welcome back to the relative safety of Chillwind Camp, $N.  What progress on the cauldrons do you have to report?\030Return to Chillwind Camp\0312,1,107,2,257,1,0\0302,112,228,2,261,1,0\0303,1,107,2,384,1,0\0301,1,139,4,272,1,11053\0301,142,251,4,336,4,11053\0301,256,386,4,274,3,11053\0301,389,491,4,340,4,11053\0304,1,58,3,264,1,11053\0304,61,113,3,256,2,11053\03111053,2,2,High Priestess MacDonnell\030112,2,2,Priestess\03011053,2,3,High Priestess MacDonnell\030112,2,3,Priestess\03011056,4,4,Alchemist Arbington\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,2,High Priestess MacDonnell\0302,0,0,2,Chillwind Camp\0302,0,0,3,High Priestess MacDonnell\0302,0,0,3,Chillwind Camp\0315216,19,5216,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305219,23,5219,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,176361,GIVER,?,9,Scourge Cauldron",[5218]="PARTIAL\031characters,consequences,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Adding the reagents to the cauldron's mix begins to change the color and texture of the cloud it spews forth.  Scourge that are even remotely near the cauldron appear to recoil at the introduction of the new components into the environment.\030\030\030The Scourge's plague cauldron stands before you, spewing vast amounts of toxins into the air.  A small, non-descript access panel lies in the base of the cauldron's vast platform.$B$BHaving already defeated the cauldron lord and acquired its key, you are free to add the appropriate reagents to the cauldron to make a counter agent to the plague.\030Felstone Field Cauldron\0311,1,109,4,272,1,0\0301,112,240,4,336,1,0\0304,1,93,3,324,1,0\0304,96,179,3,256,1,0\0304,184,346,3,260,1,0\031\0312,28,1422,0,\0315237,19,5237,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,176361,GIVER,?,9,Scourge Cauldron\030OBJECT,176361,FINISHER,?,12,Scourge Cauldron\030ITEM,13320,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,13357,OBJECTIVE,6,15,\030ITEM,14047,OBJECTIVE,4,15,",[5219]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The macabre key found on the cauldron lord easily slides into a keyhole and then disappears, allowing you permanent access to it.  Crude, viscous ichors pulsate through twisted tubes within the cauldrons underpinnings.$B$BThere is a small spigot that the bottle fits well enough under, allowing you to draw a sample for High Priestess MacDonnell back at Chillwind Point.\030One of the plague cauldrons is located in the field of a former farmhouse now referred to as Dalson's Tears.  Well, we shall shed no tears this day as we thwart the Scourge and have them choke on their own fumes!$B$BGo to Dalson's Tears, almost due north of Andorhal, and eliminate the cauldron lord there.  It should have a key like the last one did, allowing you into the cauldron.  Use this bottle to obtain a sample from inside the cauldron; each cauldron has its own distinct brew of toxins it uses.\030Go to Dalson's Tears in Western Plaguelands to locate and defeat the Cauldron Lord present there, and use its key to gain access to the cauldron.  You must have the Empty Dalson's Tears Bottle with you to secure a sample of the poisons used inside the cauldron.\030An access panel to the cauldron remains securely fastened. In order to open it, you will need to find the key.\030Target: Dalson's Tears\0312,1,108,2,261,1,11053\0302,111,212,2,321,3,11053\0302,217,306,2,257,1,11053\0302,309,383,2,257,1,11053\0302,386,504,2,257,1,11053\0303,1,145,2,384,1,11053\0303,148,261,2,384,1,11053\0301,1,129,4,272,1,0\0301,132,218,4,272,1,0\0301,223,370,4,272,1,0\0304,1,58,3,256,1,0\0304,60,110,3,258,3,0\03111053,4,10,High Priestess MacDonnell\030112,4,10,Priestess\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,3,Dalson's Tears\0302,0,0,3,Andorhal\0302,0,0,6,Dalson's Tears\0302,0,0,6,Western Plaguelands\0304,0,0,10,Chillwind Point\0315217,19,5217,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305220,23,5220,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,177289,FINISHER,?,12,Scourge Cauldron\030ITEM,13195,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[522]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Maleb inspects the contract.>$B$BThat explains the latest attack on Southshore. The Syndicate must be after me, just as they were the last magistrate!\030This is a contract for the assassination of Magistrate Henry Maleb.  It was sealed and stamped in red wax, using a distinctive signet ring.\030Bring the Assassin's Contract to Magistrate Maleb in Southshore.\030You look out of breath! Do you have something to report?\030Assassin's Contract\0312,1,67,2,257,1,0\0302,70,139,2,257,1,0\0303,1,64,2,384,1,0\0301,1,30,4,272,1,2276\0301,35,80,4,276,1,2276\0301,82,151,4,272,1,2276\0304,1,23,3,256,1,2276\0304,25,56,3,256,2,2276\0312276,2,1,Magistrate Henry Maleb\0312,36,1416,0,\0302,0,0,3,Magistrate Maleb\0302,0,0,3,Southshore\031523,23,523,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3668,STARTER,?,10,",[5220]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, there is plenty in here for study. Well done, $N!$B$BFor now, the next step is in our hands. We'll need to produce a list of reagents that, when combined with what is already in the cauldron, will act as its counter.$B$BThe only way we will be able to introduce this is by placing the reagents into the cauldron directly. Alchemist Arbington will have more information on that, so be sure to speak with him at your earliest convenience.\030You carefully fill the bottle with enough of the cauldron's ichors for what you consider to be suitably sized sample.$B$BWith the poison in hand, it is time to return to High Priestess MacDonnell at Chillwind Camp to complete the mission.\030Bring the Filled Dalson's Tears Bottle to High Priestess MacDonnell at Chillwind Camp, Western Plaguelands.\030We know that each cauldron employs a different mix of reagents to generate its plague-inducing toxin; likewise, we know that we will need to develop a counter agent that is unique for each cauldron. Your sample from Dalson's Tears will be the key to figure out that cauldron's distinct reagent requirement.\030Return to Chillwind Camp\0312,1,117,2,257,1,0\0302,122,238,2,261,1,0\0303,1,107,2,384,1,0\0301,1,38,4,272,1,11053\0301,40,53,4,272,1,11053\0301,58,96,4,272,1,11053\0301,98,220,4,274,3,11053\0301,225,325,4,272,3,11053\0301,327,440,4,272,3,11053\0304,1,198,3,262,3,11053\0304,200,306,3,256,3,11053\03111053,2,2,High Priestess MacDonnell\030112,2,2,Priestess\03011053,2,3,High Priestess MacDonnell\030112,2,3,Priestess\03011056,4,9,Alchemist Arbington\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,2,High Priestess MacDonnell\0302,0,0,2,Chillwind Camp\0302,0,0,3,High Priestess MacDonnell\0302,0,0,3,Chillwind Camp\0303,0,0,11,Dalson's Tears\0315219,19,5219,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305222,23,5222,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,177289,GIVER,?,9,Scourge Cauldron",[5221]="PARTIAL\031characters,consequences,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Adding the reagents to the cauldron's mix begins to change the color and texture of the cloud it spews forth. Scourge that are even remotely near the cauldron appear to recoil at the introduction of the new components into the environment.\030\030\030The Scourge's plague cauldron stands before you, spewing vast amounts of toxins into the air.  A small, non-descript access panel lies in the base of the cauldron's vast platform.$B$BHaving already defeated the cauldron lord and acquired its key, you are free to add the appropriate reagents to the cauldron to make a counter agent to the plague.\030Dalson's Tears Cauldron\0311,1,109,4,272,1,0\0301,111,239,4,336,1,0\0304,1,93,3,324,1,0\0304,96,179,3,256,1,0\0304,184,346,3,260,1,0\031\0312,28,1422,0,\0315237,19,5237,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,177289,GIVER,?,9,Scourge Cauldron\030OBJECT,177289,FINISHER,?,12,Scourge Cauldron\030ITEM,13320,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,13356,OBJECTIVE,5,15,\030ITEM,14047,OBJECTIVE,4,15,",[5222]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The cauldron lord's key unlocks the access panel to this cauldron and then disappears, much like the other keys have for the previous two cauldrons you've dealt of.  A putrid smelling substance churns violently beneath the platform of the cauldron.$B$BThere is a small spigot that the bottle fits well enough under, allowing you to draw a sample for High Priestess MacDonnell back at Chillwind Point.\030Two cauldrons have been successfully opened; while you will be able to access them indefinitely, we still want to open up the other two that remain.  This will provide all of us with more options to introduce the counter agent!$B$BThis time, you'll be hitting the Writhing Haunt's cauldron.  It is almost due east of Andorhal, relatively close to the ruined city walls; again, eliminate the cauldron lord present there for its key.  Use this bottle to obtain the sample from the cauldron.$B$BGood hunting, $N!\030Go to the Writhing Haunt in Western Plaguelands to locate and defeat the Cauldron Lord present there, and use its key to gain access to the cauldron.  You must have the Empty Writhing Haunt Bottle with you to secure a sample of the poisons used inside the cauldron.\030An access panel to the cauldron remains securely fastened. In order to open it, you will need to find the key.\030Target: Writhing Haunt\0312,1,148,2,259,3,11053\0302,151,227,2,257,3,11053\0302,232,290,2,257,1,11053\0302,293,431,2,257,1,11053\0302,434,488,2,257,1,11053\0302,493,509,2,257,1,11053\0303,1,149,2,384,1,11053\0303,152,265,2,384,1,11053\0301,1,164,4,272,1,0\0301,167,248,4,272,1,0\0301,253,400,4,272,1,0\0304,1,58,3,256,1,0\0304,60,110,3,258,3,0\03111053,4,11,High Priestess MacDonnell\030112,4,11,Priestess\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,4,Andorhal\0302,0,0,7,Writhing Haunt\0302,0,0,7,Western Plaguelands\0304,0,0,11,Chillwind Point\0315220,19,5220,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305223,23,5223,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,176393,FINISHER,?,12,Scourge Cauldron\030ITEM,13197,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5223]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Another finely executed mission, $N! This makes three cauldrons available to us to turn against the Scourge. If Kel'Thuzad's necromantic dominance over these lands wasn't as strong as it currently is, I'd dare say you'd shut them down completely!$B$BAlchemist Arbington will have a report on what this cauldron - as well as the other cauldrons subverted - will require to deliver our counter agent to the plague. With that, the time has come to bring the last cauldron of the west under our influence!\030You delicately top off the empty bottle; a sample of the foul substance that churns under the platform of the cauldron now oozes back and forth inside the fragile glass container.$B$BWith the poison in hand, it is time to return to High Priestess MacDonnell at Chillwind Camp to complete the mission.\030Bring the Filled Writhing Haunt Bottle to High Priestess MacDonnell at Chillwind Camp, Western Plaguelands.\030Once we successfully analyze the sample drawn from the Writhing Haunt's cauldron, it will provide us with a third avenue to deliver a devastating counter agent onto the Scourge!\030Return to Chillwind Camp\0312,1,179,2,257,1,0\0302,184,300,2,261,1,0\0303,1,107,2,384,1,0\0301,1,36,4,272,1,11053\0301,38,108,4,336,1,11053\0301,110,246,4,272,4,11053\0301,251,412,4,276,3,11053\0301,414,501,4,272,1,11053\0304,1,177,3,320,3,11053\03111053,2,2,High Priestess MacDonnell\030112,2,2,Priestess\03011053,2,3,High Priestess MacDonnell\030112,2,3,Priestess\03011056,4,7,Alchemist Arbington\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,2,High Priestess MacDonnell\0302,0,0,2,Chillwind Camp\0302,0,0,3,High Priestess MacDonnell\0302,0,0,3,Chillwind Camp\0303,0,0,9,Writhing Haunt's\0315222,19,5222,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305225,23,5225,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,176393,GIVER,?,9,Scourge Cauldron",[5224]="PARTIAL\031characters,consequences,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Adding the reagents to the cauldron's mix begins to change the color and texture of the cloud it spews forth. Scourge that are even remotely near the cauldron appear to recoil at the introduction of the new components into the environment.\030\030\030The Scourge's plague cauldron stands before you, spewing vast amounts of toxins into the air.  A small, non-descript access panel lies in the base of the cauldron's vast platform.$B$BHaving already defeated the cauldron lord and acquired its key, you are free to add the appropriate reagents to the cauldron to make a counter agent to the plague.\030Writhing Haunt Cauldron\0311,1,109,4,272,1,0\0301,111,239,4,336,1,0\0304,1,93,3,324,1,0\0304,96,179,3,256,1,0\0304,184,346,3,260,1,0\031\0312,28,1422,0,\0315237,19,5237,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,176393,GIVER,?,9,Scourge Cauldron\030OBJECT,176393,FINISHER,?,12,Scourge Cauldron\030ITEM,13320,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,13356,OBJECTIVE,5,15,\030ITEM,14047,OBJECTIVE,4,15,",[5225]="PARTIAL\031consequences\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Cauldron Lord Soulwrath's key disintegrates as it touches the lock on the access panel at the base of the cauldron's platform.  A slight clanking noise is heard within, and the access panel swings open to reveal more viscous toxins within the cauldron's framework.$B$BThere is a small spigot that the bottle fits well enough under, allowing you to draw a sample for High Priestess MacDonnell back at Chillwind Point.\030The last cauldron that remains is located on a farm now called Gahrron's Withering.  It is guarded by some of the Scourge's tougher minions - specifically, wraiths and ghosts.  They are not to be trifled with, $N.$B$BGahrron's Withering is due northeast of our position here, close to where the Eastern Plaguelands begin; again, eliminate the cauldron lord present there for its key.  Here is your empty sample bottle; bring it to me filled.  May the Light protect you in this dangerous mission, $c.\030Go to Gahrron's Withering in Western Plaguelands to locate and defeat the Cauldron Lord present there, and use its key to gain access to the cauldron.  You must have the Empty Gahrron's Withering Bottle with you to secure a sample of the poisons used inside the cauldron.\030An access panel to the cauldron remains securely fastened.  In order to open it, you will need to find the key.\030Target: Gahrron's Withering\0312,1,83,2,257,1,11053\0302,86,175,2,321,1,11053\0302,178,213,2,257,1,11053\0302,218,383,2,257,1,11053\0302,386,441,2,257,1,11053\0302,444,499,2,269,1,11053\0303,1,150,2,384,1,11053\0303,153,271,2,384,1,11053\0301,1,126,4,272,1,0\0301,129,264,4,272,1,0\0301,269,416,4,272,1,0\0304,1,58,3,256,1,0\0304,61,111,3,258,3,0\03111078,4,9,Cauldron Lord Soulwrath\03011053,4,11,High Priestess MacDonnell\030112,4,11,Priestess\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,7,Gahrron's Withering\0302,0,0,7,Western Plaguelands\0304,0,0,11,Chillwind Point\0315223,19,5223,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305226,23,5226,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,176392,FINISHER,?,12,Scourge Cauldron\030ITEM,13196,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5226]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Congratulations $N, you've unlocked the last cauldron for us! Alchemist Arbington will soon know what this cauldron requires as far as reagents needed for the mix.$B$BAs for you, I am sure that Commander Valorfist will want to thank you personally for the assistance you've given us. Without you, our struggle against the Scourge would have been nearly insurmountable. Thank you, hero!\030You carefully close the spigot in the control panel, watching the cauldron's putrid ichors drip into the empty bottle.$B$BWith the poison in hand, it is time to return to High Priestess MacDonnell at Chillwind Camp to complete the mission.\030Bring the Filled Gahrron's Withering Bottle to High Priestess MacDonnell at Chillwind Camp, Western Plaguelands.\030Gahrron's Withering houses the last cauldron here in the west that we need access to. Once we have a sample of the plague it spews forth, we will be able to introduce our reagents into the environment through four separate vessels! The Scourge will be hard pressed to keep us out of all four, even with the power of Kel'Thuzad behind them.\030Return to Chillwind Point\0312,1,118,2,257,1,0\0302,123,239,2,261,1,0\0303,1,112,2,384,1,0\0301,1,61,4,272,1,11053\0301,63,163,4,272,3,11053\0301,168,283,4,274,3,11053\0301,285,368,4,336,4,11053\0301,370,385,4,272,1,11053\0304,1,85,3,258,1,11053\0304,87,231,3,260,3,11053\0304,233,339,3,320,3,11053\03111053,2,2,High Priestess MacDonnell\030112,2,2,Priestess\03011053,2,3,High Priestess MacDonnell\030112,2,3,Priestess\03011056,4,5,Alchemist Arbington\03015990,3,11,Kel'Thuzad\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,2,High Priestess MacDonnell\0302,0,0,2,Chillwind Camp\0302,0,0,3,High Priestess MacDonnell\0302,0,0,3,Chillwind Camp\0315225,19,5225,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305237,23,5237,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,176392,GIVER,?,9,Scourge Cauldron",[5227]="PARTIAL\031characters,consequences,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Adding the reagents to the cauldron's mix begins to change the color and texture of the cloud it spews forth. Scourge that are even remotely near the cauldron appear to recoil at the introduction of the new components into the environment.\030\030\030The Scourge's plague cauldron stands before you, spewing vast amounts of toxins into the air.  A small, non-descript access panel lies in the base of the cauldron's vast platform.$B$BHaving already defeated the cauldron lord and acquired its key, you are free to add the appropriate reagents to the cauldron to make a counter agent to the plague.\030Gahrron's Withering Cauldron\0311,1,109,4,272,1,0\0301,111,239,4,336,1,0\0304,1,93,3,324,1,0\0304,96,179,3,256,1,0\0304,184,346,3,260,1,0\031\0312,28,1422,0,\0315237,19,5237,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,176392,GIVER,?,9,Scourge Cauldron\030OBJECT,176392,FINISHER,?,12,Scourge Cauldron\030ITEM,13320,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,13354,OBJECTIVE,4,15,\030ITEM,14047,OBJECTIVE,4,15,",[5228]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031From the shadows, brother $R, I bid you greetings. I am to serve as your coordinator for our plan to sabotage the Scourge's cauldrons.$B$BOur goal will be to change the composition of the plague that the cauldrons create into something that negatively affects the Scourge. In order to affect this change, you will need to secure access to each of the four cauldrons here in the Western Plaguelands.$B$BThe time has come for you to lead the charge against the Scourge, hero.\030Within the lands of former Lordaeron are eight cauldrons - four in the west, and four more entrenched in the east.  These cauldrons spew poisons into the air, propagating the plague throughout the land for the Scourge.$B$BThe necromantic might of Kel'Thuzad is too strong to outright shut down these cauldrons, but we think we might have a way to subvert them to our advantage.  My second, Shadow Priestess Vandis, will be your point on this assignment; she'll continue the briefing from here.\030Speak with Shadow Priestess Vandis at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands.\030\030The Scourge Cauldrons\0312,1,114,2,257,1,10837\0302,117,218,2,325,1,10837\0302,223,377,2,257,4,10837\0302,380,493,2,257,3,10837\0303,1,71,2,384,1,10837\0301,1,50,4,272,1,11055\0301,52,134,4,336,3,11055\0301,139,272,4,342,3,11055\0301,274,398,4,274,3,11055\0301,403,473,4,336,1,11055\03115990,2,3,Kel'Thuzad\03011055,2,4,Shadow Priestess Vandis\030112,2,4,Priestess\03011055,2,5,Shadow Priestess Vandis\030112,2,5,Priestess\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,5,Bulwark\0304,0,0,9,Western Plaguelands\0315096,19,5096,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305229,23,5229,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5229]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The key taken from Cauldron Lord Bilemaw is a perfect fit in unlocking the access panel, though it disappears after you use it.  Still, you think you can open the panel now without a key.  A foul stench emanates from the opened panel as an unknown mix of concentrated substances swirl inside the cauldron.$B$BThere is a small spigot that the bottle fits well enough under, allowing you to draw a sample for Shadow Priestess Vandis back at the Bulwark.\030Of the four cauldrons in the Western Plaguelands, the one at Felstone Field may be the easiest one to gain access to.  The Scourge have greener troops positioned here, though they should not be underestimated.$B$BGo to Felstone Field, due east of here and northwest of Andorhal, and engage the cauldron lord there.  On it is a key that will unlock access to the cauldron.  When unlocked, use this bottle to get a sample of the cauldron's toxins; we'll need it for study in developing a counter agent.\030Go to Felstone Field in Western Plaguelands to locate and defeat the Cauldron Lord present there.  It may have a key that will allow access to the cauldron.  You must have the Empty Felstone Field Bottle with you to secure a sample of the poisons used inside the cauldron.\030An access panel to the cauldron remains securely fastened.  In order to open it, you will need to find the key.\030Target: Felstone Field\0312,1,117,2,257,1,11055\0302,120,209,2,321,1,11055\0302,214,314,2,257,1,11055\0302,317,371,2,257,3,11055\0302,374,500,2,259,1,11055\0303,1,97,2,384,1,11055\0303,100,156,2,384,3,11055\0303,159,272,2,384,1,11055\0301,1,127,4,272,1,0\0301,130,187,4,272,1,0\0301,190,305,4,272,1,0\0301,310,451,4,272,1,0\0304,1,58,3,256,1,0\0304,61,111,3,258,3,0\03111075,4,9,Cauldron Lord Bilemaw\03011055,4,12,Shadow Priestess Vandis\030112,4,12,Priestess\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,1,Western Plaguelands\0302,0,0,1,Felstone Field\0302,0,0,3,Felstone Field\0302,0,0,6,Felstone Field\0302,0,0,6,Western Plaguelands\0304,0,0,9,Cauldron Lord Bilemaw\0304,0,0,12,Bulwark\0315228,19,5228,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305230,23,5230,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,176361,FINISHER,?,12,Scourge Cauldron\030ITEM,13194,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[523]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, $N. My head rests a little easier, knowing that villain lost his.\030The contract you recovered was signed by Baron Vardus, a noble of the former kingdom of Alterac, and one known for a cold heart and brutal practices.  I'm not surprised someone like the Baron was behind this.$B$BFind this man.  Find him, and bring him to justice.  He must be among the Syndicate haunts - perhaps at the ruins of Strahnbrad, or perhaps within the valley north of them.\030Bring the Head of Baron Vardus to Magistrate Maleb in Southshore.\030Baron Vardus cannot think Southshore will allow him to send his thugs against us with impunity. I want his head!\030Baron's Demise\0312,1,149,2,257,1,2276\0302,152,208,2,257,1,2276\0302,213,226,2,257,1,2276\0302,229,263,2,257,1,2276\0302,266,384,2,321,4,2276\0303,1,65,2,384,1,2276\0301,1,14,4,272,1,2276\0301,16,76,4,276,1,2276\0304,1,95,3,256,3,2276\0304,97,112,3,258,1,2276\0312306,2,1,Baron Vardus\0302306,2,6,Baron Vardus\0302306,3,9,Baron Vardus\0312,36,1416,0,\0302,0,0,6,Magistrate Maleb\0302,0,0,6,Southshore\031522,19,522,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3626,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5230]="PARTIAL\031consequences\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done $N - it should take Apothecary Dithers no time at all to analyze this and devise a counter agent to introduce into the cauldron. If we are able to pump out enough of it into the air, we might be able to weaken all the Scourge present here.$B$BThis will no doubt be an ongoing ordeal; we will need to continually hit these cauldrons and introduce our reagents into their mix. Still, if we can keep it up, we will have a huge advantage over Scourge when the time comes for battle!\030You fill the bottle with enough of the cauldron's poisonous concoction for a suitable sample to be studied.$B$BWith the poison in hand, it is time to return to Shadow Priestess Vandis at the Bulwark to complete the mission.\030Bring the Filled Felstone Field Bottle to Shadow Priestess Vandis at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands.\030Welcome back to the relative safety of the Bulwark, $N. What progress on the cauldrons do you have to report?\030Return to the Bulwark\0312,1,107,2,257,1,0\0302,112,223,2,261,1,0\0303,1,102,2,384,1,0\0301,1,138,4,272,1,11055\0301,140,249,4,336,4,11055\0301,254,384,4,274,3,11055\0301,386,488,4,340,4,11055\0304,1,55,3,264,1,11055\0304,57,109,3,256,2,11055\03111055,2,2,Shadow Priestess Vandis\030112,2,2,Priestess\03011055,2,3,Shadow Priestess Vandis\030112,2,3,Priestess\03011057,4,4,Apothecary Dithers\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,2,Shadow Priestess Vandis\0302,0,0,2,Bulwark\0302,0,0,3,Shadow Priestess Vandis\0302,0,0,3,Bulwark\0315229,19,5229,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305231,23,5231,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,176361,GIVER,?,9,Scourge Cauldron",[5231]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The skeletal key found on the cauldron lord easily slides into a keyhole and then disappears, allowing you permanent access to it. Crude, viscous ichors pulsate through twisted tubes within the cauldrons underpinnings.$B$BThere is a small spigot that the bottle fits well enough under, allowing you to draw a sample for Shadow Priestess Vandis back at the Bulwark.\030One of the plague cauldrons is located in the field of a former farmhouse now referred to as Dalson's Tears.  No tears will be shed this day, $c; we must strike at this cauldron and gain access to it!$B$BGo to Dalson's Tears, almost due north of Andorhal, and eliminate the cauldron lord there.  It should have a key like the last one did, allowing you inside the cauldron's innards.  Use this bottle to obtain a sample from inside the cauldron; each cauldron has its own distinct brew of toxins it uses.\030Go to Dalson's Tears in Western Plaguelands to locate and defeat the Cauldron Lord present there, and use its key to gain access to the cauldron.  You must have the Empty Dalson's Tears Bottle with you to secure a sample of the poisons used inside the cauldron.\030An access panel to the cauldron remains securely fastened. In order to open it, you will need to find the key.\030Target: Dalson's Tears\0312,1,108,2,261,1,11055\0302,111,200,2,257,3,11055\0302,205,294,2,257,1,11055\0302,297,383,2,257,1,11055\0302,386,504,2,257,1,11055\0303,1,145,2,384,1,11055\0303,148,261,2,384,1,11055\0301,1,130,4,272,1,0\0301,132,218,4,272,1,0\0301,223,364,4,272,1,0\0304,1,58,3,256,1,0\0304,60,110,3,258,3,0\03111055,4,10,Shadow Priestess Vandis\030112,4,10,Priestess\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,3,Dalson's Tears\0302,0,0,3,Andorhal\0302,0,0,6,Dalson's Tears\0302,0,0,6,Western Plaguelands\0304,0,0,10,Bulwark\0315230,19,5230,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305232,23,5232,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,177289,FINISHER,?,12,Scourge Cauldron\030ITEM,13195,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5232]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, there is plenty in here for study. Well done, $N!$B$BFor now, the next step is in our hands. We'll need to produce a list of reagents that, when combined with what is already in the cauldron, will act as its counter.$B$BThe only way we will be able to introduce this is by placing the reagents into the cauldron directly. Apothecary Dithers will have more information on that, so be sure to speak with him as soon as possible.\030You carefully fill the bottle with enough of the cauldron's ichors for what you consider to be suitably sized sample.$B$BWith the poison in hand, it is time to return to Shadow Priestess Vandis at the Bulwark to complete the mission.\030Bring the Filled Dalson's Tears Bottle to Shadow Priestess Vandis at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands.\030We know that each cauldron employs a different mix of reagents to generate its plague-inducing toxin; likewise, we know that we will need to develop a counter agent that is unique for each cauldron. Your sample from Dalson's Tears will be the key to figure out that cauldron's distinct reagent requirement.\030Return to the Bulwark\0312,1,117,2,257,1,0\0302,122,233,2,261,1,0\0303,1,102,2,384,1,0\0301,1,38,4,272,1,11055\0301,40,53,4,272,1,11055\0301,58,96,4,272,1,11055\0301,98,220,4,274,3,11055\0301,225,325,4,272,3,11055\0301,327,430,4,272,3,11055\0304,1,198,3,262,3,11055\0304,200,306,3,256,3,11055\03111055,2,2,Shadow Priestess Vandis\030112,2,2,Priestess\03011055,2,3,Shadow Priestess Vandis\030112,2,3,Priestess\03011057,4,9,Apothecary Dithers\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,2,Shadow Priestess Vandis\0302,0,0,2,Bulwark\0302,0,0,3,Shadow Priestess Vandis\0302,0,0,3,Bulwark\0303,0,0,11,Dalson's Tears\0315231,19,5231,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305233,23,5233,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,177289,GIVER,?,9,Scourge Cauldron",[5233]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The cauldron lord's key unlocks the access panel to this cauldron and then disappears, much like the other keys have for the previous ones you've dealt of.  A putrid smelling substance churns violently beneath the platform of the cauldron.$B$BThere is a small spigot that the bottle fits well enough under, allowing you to draw a sample for Shadow Priestess Vandis back at the Bulwark.\030Two cauldrons have been successfully opened; while you'll be able to access them indefinitely, we still want to open up the other two that remain.  This will provide all of us with more options to introduce the counter agent!$B$BThis time, you'll be hitting the Writhing Haunt's cauldron.  It is almost due east of Andorhal, relatively close to the ruined city walls; again, eliminate the cauldron lord present there for its key.  Use this bottle to obtain the sample from the cauldron.$B$BGood hunting, $N!\030Go to the Writhing Haunt in Western Plaguelands to locate and defeat the Cauldron Lord present there, and use its key to gain access to the cauldron.  You must have the Empty Writhing Haunt Bottle with you to secure a sample of the poisons used inside the cauldron.\030An access panel to the cauldron remains securely fastened.  In order to open it, you will need to find the key.\030Target: Writhing Haunt\0312,1,146,2,259,1,11055\0302,149,225,2,257,3,11055\0302,230,288,2,257,1,11055\0302,291,429,2,257,1,11055\0302,432,486,2,257,1,11055\0302,491,507,2,257,1,11055\0303,1,149,2,384,1,11055\0303,152,265,2,384,1,11055\0301,1,155,4,272,1,0\0301,158,239,4,272,1,0\0301,244,385,4,272,1,0\0304,1,58,3,256,1,0\0304,61,111,3,258,3,0\03111055,4,11,Shadow Priestess Vandis\030112,4,11,Priestess\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,4,Andorhal\0302,0,0,7,Writhing Haunt\0302,0,0,7,Western Plaguelands\0304,0,0,11,Bulwark\0315232,19,5232,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305234,23,5234,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,176393,FINISHER,?,12,Scourge Cauldron\030ITEM,13197,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5234]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Another finely executed mission, $N! This makes three cauldrons available to us to turn against the Scourge. If Kel'Thuzad's necromantic dominance over these lands wasn't as strong as it currently is, I'd dare say you'd shut them down completely!$B$BApothecary Dithers will have a report on what this cauldron - as well as the other cauldrons subverted - will require to deliver our counter agent to the plague. With that, the time has come to bring the last cauldron of the west under our influence!\030You delicately top off the empty bottle; a sample of the foul substance that churns under the platform of the cauldron now oozes back and forth inside the fragile glass container.$B$BWith the poison in hand, it is time to return to Shadow Priestess Vandis at the Bulwark to complete the mission.\030Bring the Filled Writhing Haunt Bottle to Shadow Priestess Vandis at The Bulwark, Western Plaguelands.\030Once we successfully analysis the sample drawn from the Writhing Haunt's cauldron, it will provide us with a third avenue to deliver a devastating counter agent against the Scourge!\030Return to the Bulwark\0312,1,179,2,257,1,0\0302,184,295,2,261,1,0\0303,1,102,2,384,1,0\0301,1,36,4,272,1,11055\0301,38,108,4,336,1,11055\0301,110,246,4,272,4,11055\0301,251,411,4,276,3,11055\0301,413,500,4,272,1,11055\0304,1,181,3,320,3,11055\03111055,2,2,Shadow Priestess Vandis\030112,2,2,Priestess\03011055,2,3,Shadow Priestess Vandis\030112,2,3,Priestess\03011057,4,7,Apothecary Dithers\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,2,Shadow Priestess Vandis\0302,0,0,2,Bulwark\0302,0,0,3,Shadow Priestess Vandis\0302,0,0,3,The Bulwark\0303,0,0,9,Writhing Haunt's\0315233,19,5233,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305235,23,5235,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,176393,GIVER,?,9,Scourge Cauldron",[5235]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Cauldron Lord Soulwrath's key disintegrates as it touches the lock on the access panel at the base of the cauldron's platform. A slight clanking noise is heard within, and the access panel swings open to reveal more viscous toxins within the cauldron's framework.$B$BThere is a small spigot that the bottle fits well enough under, allowing you to draw a sample for Shadow Priestess Vandis back at the Bulwark.\030The last cauldron that remains is located on a farm now called Gahrron's Withering.  It is guarded by some of the Scourge's tougher minions - specifically, wraiths and ghosts.  They are not to be trifled with, $N.$B$BGahrron's Withering is far to the east of the Bulwark, close to where the Eastern Plaguelands begin; again, eliminate the cauldron lord present there for its key.  Here is your empty sample bottle; bring it to me filled.  May the shadows cloak you in safety for this dangerous mission, $c.\030Go to Gahrron's Withering in Western Plaguelands to locate and defeat the Cauldron Lord present there, and use its key to gain access to the cauldron.  You must have the Empty Gahrron's Withering Bottle with you to secure a sample of the poisons used inside the cauldron.\030An access panel to the cauldron remains securely fastened. In order to open it, you will need to find the key.\030Target: Gahrron's Withering\0312,1,83,2,257,1,11055\0302,86,175,2,321,1,11055\0302,178,213,2,257,1,11055\0302,218,379,2,257,1,11055\0302,382,437,2,257,1,11055\0302,440,506,2,265,1,11055\0303,1,150,2,384,1,11055\0303,153,271,2,384,1,11055\0301,1,126,4,272,1,0\0301,128,263,4,272,1,0\0301,268,409,4,272,1,0\0304,1,58,3,256,1,0\0304,60,110,3,258,3,0\03111078,4,9,Cauldron Lord Soulwrath\03011055,4,11,Shadow Priestess Vandis\030112,4,11,Priestess\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,4,Bulwark\0302,0,0,7,Gahrron's Withering\0302,0,0,7,Western Plaguelands\0304,0,0,11,Bulwark\0315234,19,5234,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305236,23,5236,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,176392,FINISHER,?,12,Scourge Cauldron\030ITEM,13196,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5236]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Congratulations $N, you've unlocked the last cauldron for us! Apothecary Dithers will soon know what this cauldron requires as far as reagents needed for the mix.$B$BAs for you, I am sure that High Executor Derrington will want to thank you personally for the assistance you've given us. Without you, our struggle against the Scourge would have been nearly insurmountable. I thank you, mighty $C.\030You carefully close the spigot in the control panel, watching the cauldron's putrid ichors drip into the empty bottle.$B$BWith the poison in hand, it is time to return to Shadow Priestess Vandis at the Bulwark to complete the mission.\030Bring the Filled Gahrron's Withering Bottle to Shadow Priestess Vandis at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands.\030Gahrron's Withering houses the last cauldron that we need to acquire access to here in the west. Once we have a sample of the plague from that cauldron, we will be able to introduce our reagents into the environment through four separate vessels! The Scourge will be hard pressed to keep us out of all four, even with the power of Kel'Thuzad behind them.\030Return to the Bulwark\0312,1,118,2,257,1,0\0302,123,234,2,261,1,0\0303,1,107,2,384,1,0\0301,1,61,4,272,1,11055\0301,63,162,4,272,3,11055\0301,167,287,4,274,3,11055\0301,289,372,4,336,4,11055\0301,374,396,4,272,1,11055\0304,1,96,3,258,1,11055\0304,98,246,3,260,3,11055\0304,248,354,3,320,3,11055\03111055,2,2,Shadow Priestess Vandis\030112,2,2,Priestess\03011055,2,3,Shadow Priestess Vandis\030112,2,3,Priestess\03011057,4,5,Apothecary Dithers\03010837,4,6,High Executor Derrington\03015990,3,11,Kel'Thuzad\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,2,Shadow Priestess Vandis\0302,0,0,2,Bulwark\0302,0,0,3,Shadow Priestess Vandis\0302,0,0,3,Bulwark\0315235,19,5235,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305238,23,5238,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,176392,GIVER,?,9,Scourge Cauldron",[5237]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031$N, your successful re-engineering of the cauldrons is a tremendous victory for us!$B$B<The high executor clears his throat and begins to bellow loudly.>$B$BLet all within my presence hear: for service to the Forsaken and to the Horde as a whole above and beyond what was expected - in the face of overwhelming odds and incredible danger, might I add - I give $N this, and I extend upon $Ghis:her; our undying gratitude as a true hero of the Horde. Huzzah!\030\030\030\030Mission Accomplished!\0311,1,83,4,272,1,10838\0301,88,153,4,272,1,10838\0301,158,448,4,276,4,10838\0301,450,456,4,272,1,10838\03115394,4,3,Hero of the Horde\0312,28,1422,0,\0304,0,0,3,Forsaken\0304,0,0,3,Horde\0315226,19,5226,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305238,22,5238,UNKNOWN\031",[5238]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031$N, your successful re-engineering of the cauldrons is a tremendous victory for us!$B$B<The commander clears his throat and begins to bellow loudly.>$B$BLet all within my presence hear: for service to the Kingdom of Stormwind and to the Alliance above and beyond the call of duty - in the face of overwhelming odds and incredible danger, might I add - I give $N this, and I extend upon $Ghis:her; our undying gratitude as a true hero of the Alliance. Cheers, I say!\030\030\030\030Mission Accomplished!\0311,1,83,4,272,1,10837\0301,88,149,4,272,1,10837\0301,154,450,4,276,4,10837\0301,452,465,4,272,1,10837\031\0312,28,1422,0,\0304,0,0,3,Kingdom of Stormwind\0304,0,0,3,Alliance\0315236,19,5236,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305237,22,5237,UNKNOWN\031",[524]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You rest the tainted deg on the dusty rug.\030Next door the Deathguards are holding a few captured farmers hostage.  High Executor Darthalia suspected one of the military strategists from Stormwind to be hiding out amongst them.  Apparently the military chap was found dead in the Plaguelands last night.  Darthalia, always looking out for me, decided the prisoners would be left to my disposal.$B$BI think it's time we threw those farmers a party.  Sounds like a grand ol' time!$B$BPlace this tainted keg on the rug in their room.  Plagued brew for all!\030Place the Tainted Keg on the rug for the captured farmers.\030A musty smell emanates from the rug.\030Elixir of Agony\0312,1,69,2,257,1,2216\0302,72,182,2,257,1,2216\0302,185,258,2,257,4,2216\0302,261,349,2,257,4,2216\0302,354,402,2,257,1,2216\0302,405,433,2,257,1,2216\0302,438,485,2,257,1,2216\0302,488,508,2,257,1,2216\0303,1,58,2,384,1,2216\0301,1,42,4,272,1,0\0304,1,36,3,256,1,0\0312215,2,2,High Executor Darthalia\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,2,Stormwind\0302,0,0,3,Plaguelands\031517,19,517,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,1728,FINISHER,?,12,Dusty Rug",[5241]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You've seen Pamela? She's alive?$B$BShe's dead? No! Oh, Pamela! Why does your spirit still suffer in this world. Why are you perished, while fortune keeps me alive? In an instant I would switch places with you and wander dead Darrowshire, a ghost and alone!$B$BAh, but this news cannot change fate. Thank you, $N. Now my duty, my duty to revenge, burns hot as ever.\030Sometimes, when it's nighttime, I can hear my Uncle Carlin crying.  It sounds like he's far away, to the east.$B$BI hope he's not crying for me!  $N, will you find my uncle and tell him I'm alright?$B$BIf you find him say I'm waiting for him, and I want to hear the story he used to tell... the one about the rabbits and the berry jam!  That story's so funny!\030Find Carlin Redpath.\030\030Uncle Carlin\0312,1,66,2,257,1,10926\0302,69,110,2,257,1,10926\0302,115,144,2,259,3,10926\0302,147,198,2,257,2,10926\0302,203,290,2,323,4,10926\0302,292,335,2,257,1,10926\0302,338,359,2,257,1,10926\0303,1,20,2,384,1,10926\0301,1,19,4,272,2,11063\0301,21,32,4,272,2,11063\0301,37,47,4,272,2,11063\0301,53,63,4,272,1,11063\0301,65,112,4,276,1,11063\0301,114,164,4,272,2,11063\0301,166,257,4,272,4,11063\0301,262,298,4,272,1,11063\0301,300,313,4,272,1,11063\0301,315,365,4,274,1,11063\03111063,2,8,Carlin Redpath\03011045,4,18,Burns\0312,139,1423,0,\0315149,19,5149,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305211,23,5211,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5242]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Earthmother be praised, $N! Thank you! This is a great day, indeed!$B$BThe Shadow Council will be hard pressed to scale to the same levels of power they once held with this blow to their hierarchy. You have done a great thing this day!\030Unfortunately, I see the only way to stop this threat to Felwood is a frontal attack. There are no other ways into Shadow Hold, and I have no means to teleport you inside. The straight path down to the bottom is the only way... and I also know who you should seek out. His name is Fel'dan... Shadow Lord Fel'dan. He is the mortal in power down below... he is the head of the serpent. Kill him and his two succubus servants and return to me. Fel'dan is the one making pacts with the Legion. He must be stopped.\030Kill Moora and Salia, and bring Shadow Lord Fel'dan's Head to Greta Mosshoof in Felwood.\030Without Fel'dan, the Shadow Council will hopefully lose focus and start infighting. They will struggle with one another for control and hoard assets for future plans. That will be an opportune time to devastate them and their demon slaves.\030A Final Blow\0312,1,85,2,261,1,10922\0302,87,171,2,257,1,10922\0302,173,227,2,257,1,10922\0302,229,268,2,259,1,10922\0302,270,291,2,257,1,10922\0302,293,312,2,257,1,10922\0302,314,352,2,257,1,10922\0302,354,383,2,257,1,10922\0302,385,440,2,257,1,10922\0302,442,489,2,257,1,10922\0302,491,509,2,257,1,10922\0303,1,88,2,384,1,10922\0301,1,27,4,272,1,10922\0301,29,38,4,272,1,10922\0301,40,67,4,272,1,10922\0301,72,197,4,272,3,10922\0301,199,235,4,272,1,10922\0304,1,83,3,256,3,10922\0304,85,166,3,256,3,10922\0304,168,239,3,256,3,10922\0314244,2,2,Shadow\0309517,2,6,Shadow Lord Fel'dan\0301863,2,9,Succubus\0309861,2,12,Moora\0309860,2,12,Salia\0309517,2,12,Shadow Lord Fel'dan\03010922,2,12,Greta Mosshoof\0304244,4,16,Shadow\0304244,3,18,Shadow\0312,361,1448,0,\0302,0,0,1,Felwood\0302,0,0,12,Greta Mosshoof\0302,0,0,12,Felwood\0315165,19,5165,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,9861,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Moora\030NPC,9860,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Salia\030ITEM,13207,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5243]="PARTIAL\031consequences,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $R. You have proven that while you are tolerant of others, you will stop at nothing to destroy the minions of Kel'Thuzad.$B$B\030I look at my undeath as a malady, $r. An illness that merely requires treatment; however, it is also a great blessing for the Argent Dawn. What better vessel to smite the heathens of the Scourge than through the undead?$B$BI am revered by my colleagues because of the sacrifices I have made, but the accolades mean nothing to me.$B$BIf you are interested in assisting the Argent Dawn, then a job I can offer.$B$BVenture to Stratholme and recover our surplus of holy water. Search the supply crates.$B\030Travel to Stratholme, in the north. Search the supply crates that litter the city and recover 5 Stratholme Holy Water. Return to Leonid Barthalomew the Revered when you have collected enough of the blessed fluid.\030Be wary, not all supply crates will have survived the destruction of the city. The Scourge dare not touch the water but surely the holy water will not prevent vermin infestations.$B$B\030Houses of the Holy\0312,1,37,2,257,1,11036\0302,39,138,2,257,1,11036\0302,140,219,2,321,2,11036\0302,224,329,2,259,1,11036\0302,334,408,2,257,4,11036\0302,413,472,2,257,1,11036\0302,474,498,2,257,1,11036\0303,1,35,2,384,1,11036\0303,37,118,2,384,1,11036\0303,120,212,2,384,1,11036\0301,1,14,4,272,1,11036\0301,16,132,4,276,3,11036\0304,1,78,3,256,3,11036\0304,80,179,3,328,3,11036\03111036,2,10,Leonid Barthalomew the Revered\03015990,4,12,Kel'Thuzad\0312,2017,0,0,\0302,0,0,6,Stratholme\0302,0,0,8,Stratholme\0302,0,0,10,Leonid Barthalomew the Revered\031\031ITEM,13180,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[5244]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well, sure, I can tell you more about Kel'Theril. Mind you now, I'm no historian, but I can tell ya about what I saw there...\030The story behind Kel'Theril is one of a cursed race, bound to the place where they attempted an unfortunate ritual...$B$BThe highborne that you will find there once stole a sacred artifact, believing that they could siphon its power for themselves, becoming even more powerful. In their efforts, the relic shattered in a huge explosion, driving the pieces below the ice of the lake...$B$BSpeak with Jaron Stoneshaper if you'd like to learn more; he has recently visited the area and can tell you more.\030Speak with Jaron Stoneshaper in Starfall Village.\030\030The Ruins of Kel'Theril\0312,1,117,2,261,1,11079\0302,122,277,2,321,4,11079\0302,279,384,2,257,1,11079\0302,389,501,2,257,4,11079\0303,1,49,2,384,1,11079\0301,1,49,4,272,1,10301\0301,51,125,4,272,1,10301\03110301,2,4,Jaron Stoneshaper\03010301,2,5,Jaron Stoneshaper\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,5,Starfall Village\0315245,23,5245,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5245]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The past of the high elves is something that I do not wish to discuss, $N. Please, it pains me to think of all that has happened... And that there is no way to make things right.\030The highborne spirits are miserable creatures, that's for sure. They are still searching for pieces of the very thing that has cursed them to Kel'Theril forever -- the stolen relic.$B$BIf you are that interested, take my pick and go south to the lake, see if you can gather the pieces of it from within the ice.$B$BNow, I can't tell you a thing about what you find, but I do know of someone who might... Aurora Skycaller; she dwells near the Northpass Tower in the northern part of Eastern Plaguelands.\030Use Jaron's Pick to find the four Highborne Relic Fragments. Bring them to Aurora Skycaller in Eastern Plaguelands.\030Why have you come here?\030Troubled Spirits of Kel'Theril\0312,1,63,2,321,1,10301\0302,65,181,2,261,1,10301\0302,186,311,2,257,4,10301\0302,316,403,2,257,4,10301\0302,405,502,2,257,1,10301\0303,1,60,2,448,1,10301\0303,62,115,2,384,1,10301\0301,1,74,4,274,3,10304\0301,76,131,4,272,1,10304\0301,133,178,4,272,1,10304\0304,1,23,3,256,2,10304\03110304,2,5,Aurora Skycaller\03010304,2,7,Aurora Skycaller\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,2,Kel'Theril\0302,0,0,5,Northpass Tower\0302,0,0,7,Aurora Skycaller\0302,0,0,7,Eastern Plaguelands\0315244,19,5244,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305246,23,5246,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12896,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,12897,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,12898,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,12899,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5246]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The pages have gone untouched for many many years...\030I did not realize... Forgive my callous words, $c.$B$BThe mistakes of my ancestors are not what I wish to dwell on, but if your request is truly genuine, then I will help you.$B$B<Aurora examines the fragments.>$B$BI believe this is the Crystal of Zin-Malor, an artifact that can contain and control strong arcane forces. It could have been used for good, but the evil intentions of those that stole it caused it to shatter.$B$BGo to the Temple of Zin-Malor in Azshara - I can only hope the book is still there.\030Find the Sacred Highborne Writings in the Temple of Zin-Malor in Azshara, and bring them to Aurora Skycaller near the Northpass Tower in Eastern Plaguelands.\030It is only in the pages of the sacred writings that I will be able to discern whether or not I can help you...\030Fragments of the Past\0312,1,20,2,257,1,10304\0302,22,50,2,257,1,10304\0302,55,175,2,259,4,10304\0302,180,211,2,257,1,10304\0302,216,321,2,257,4,10304\0302,323,424,2,257,4,10304\0302,429,511,2,259,3,10304\0303,1,157,2,448,1,10304\0301,1,52,4,272,1,10304\0304,1,110,3,256,3,10304\03110304,2,8,Aurora Skycaller\0312,139,1423,0,\0302,0,0,7,Temple of Zin-Malor\0302,0,0,7,Azshara\0302,0,0,8,Temple of Zin-Malor\0302,0,0,8,Azshara\0302,0,0,8,Aurora Skycaller\0302,0,0,8,Northpass Tower\0302,0,0,8,Eastern Plaguelands\0315245,19,5245,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305247,23,5247,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,13313,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5247]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Using these elements, I can fuse the fragments together... to hopefully what they once were.\030I will be able to help you, if recreating the artifact is truly what you wish to do.$B$BTo seal the pieces back together, I will need items with strong magical qualities. An enchanted thorium bar and five crystal restore... You'll also need to collect some water from what might seem an unlikely place... Find the dire pool along Eldreth Row at Dire Maul in Feralas, and fill this vial.$B$BWhile you are gone, I will attempt to glean from these pages the knowledge I need to repair the damage done to the relic.\030Bring an Enchanted Thorium Bar, 5 Crystal Restore, and a Vial of Dire Water to Aurora Skycaller near the Northpass Tower in Eastern Plaguelands.\030The relic must be placed in the hands of only the most trustworthy. It can not be stolen again...\030Fragments of the Past\0312,1,84,2,259,4,10304\0302,89,170,2,259,3,10304\0302,172,223,2,257,1,10304\0302,225,304,2,259,4,10304\0302,306,386,2,257,1,10304\0302,391,511,2,259,3,10304\0303,1,144,2,384,1,10304\0301,1,58,4,272,1,10304\0301,60,92,4,336,3,10304\0304,1,67,3,256,1,10304\0304,69,97,3,260,1,10304\03110304,2,7,Aurora Skycaller\0312,139,1423,0,\0302,0,0,5,Dire Maul\0302,0,0,5,Feralas\0302,0,0,7,Aurora Skycaller\0302,0,0,7,Northpass Tower\0302,0,0,7,Eastern Plaguelands\0315246,19,5246,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305248,23,5248,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12655,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,11562,OBJECTIVE,5,15,\030ITEM,16973,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5248]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Pleeease, leeeave meeeeee...\030$N, I weep for what has happened in the past. Like this crystal, the elves, as a race, have been shattered. I do not know if the pieces will ever again be reunited into one, but my sorrow has been eased by being able to help you with this one small task. $B$BWe must not forget the past, $N...$B$BPlease take the Crystal of Zin-Malor back to Lake Kel'Theril. You must find a highborne spirit that realizes the error of what was done so long ago. Show the spirit that we have made things right again.\030Take the Crystal of Zin-Malor to Lake Kel'Theril in Winterspring and find a highborne spirit that will speak to you.\030Currrrrsed... Forevvvverrrr...\030Tormented By the Past\0312,1,45,2,257,1,10304\0302,47,107,2,257,1,10304\0302,109,254,2,257,4,10304\0302,260,293,2,265,1,10304\0302,298,358,2,257,1,10304\0302,360,445,2,321,1,10304\0302,447,499,2,257,1,10304\0303,1,116,2,448,3,10304\0301,1,28,4,272,1,10684\0304,1,13,3,256,1,10684\0304,15,30,3,256,1,10684\031\0312,139,1423,0,\0302,0,0,5,Lake Kel'Theril\0302,0,0,8,Lake Kel'Theril\0302,0,0,8,Winterspring\0315247,19,5247,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305252,23,5252,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5249]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A friend of Ivy Leafrunner? Nice to meet you, $N.\030In Winterspring, to the north of here, there are many ancient elven ruins. It's a harsh land, but it holds many secrets and places to explore.$B$BWith all my work to do here in Felwood, I have not had the opportunity to travel to Winterspring. But there's no reason why you shouldn't!$B$BWhile you're there, look for Wynd Nightchaser. He spends most of his time in Starfall Village and he knows a lot about the area.\030Find Starfall Village in Winterspring and speak with Wynd Nightchaser.\030\030To Winterspring!\0312,1,74,2,321,1,10924\0302,76,142,2,257,1,10924\0302,147,243,2,257,1,10924\0302,245,284,2,257,1,10924\0302,289,334,2,257,1,10924\0302,336,416,2,257,1,10924\0303,1,70,2,384,1,10924\0301,1,27,4,272,2,11079\0301,29,49,4,272,1,11079\03111079,2,5,Wynd Nightchaser\03011079,2,7,Wynd Nightchaser\03010924,4,8,Ivy Leafrunner\0312,361,1448,0,\0302,0,0,3,Felwood\0302,0,0,3,Winterspring\0302,0,0,6,Starfall Village\0302,0,0,7,Winterspring\0315250,22,5250,UNKNOWN\0305244,23,5244,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305244,24,5244,UNKNOWN\031",[525]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Maleb reads the letter.>$B$BThis is translated from a letter you found in a Syndicate encampment? This was not written by a thief, or even a noble of Alterac.$B$BIt appears The Syndicate has ties to another power, and I shudder to think what that might be.\030I decrypted the letter, but I don't know what to make of it.  You found this among thieves in the Alterac foothills?  Very strange...$B$BYou should take this to the magistrate of Southshore.  Although this letter is cryptic, his is the closest town to Alterac; if a threat is brewing, then he should know.\030Bring the Decrypted Letter to Magistrate Maleb in Southshore.\030$N. Have you been traveling through the foothills and mountains again? What news do you bring?\030Further Mysteries\0312,1,60,2,257,1,1356\0302,63,116,2,257,2,1356\0302,119,133,2,257,1,1356\0302,138,190,2,257,1,1356\0302,193,305,2,261,4,1356\0303,1,61,2,384,1,1356\0301,1,25,4,272,1,2276\0301,30,98,4,272,2,2276\0301,100,159,4,272,1,2276\0301,164,257,4,272,4,2276\0304,5,70,3,256,2,2276\0304,72,94,3,256,2,2276\031\0312,36,1416,0,\0302,0,0,2,Alterac\0302,0,0,5,Alterac\0302,0,0,6,Magistrate Maleb\0302,0,0,6,Southshore\031514,19,514,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030537,23,537,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5250]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A student of Daryn Lightwind? Nice to meet you, $N.\030In Winterspring, to the north of Felwood, there are many ancient elven ruins. It's a harsh land, but it holds many secrets and places to explore.$B$BMy studies here keep me so busy that I have not had the opportunity to travel to Winterspring for some time. But there's no reason why you shouldn't travel there and study the ruins.$B$BWhile you're there, look for Wynd Nightchaser. He spends most of his time in Starfall and he knows a lot about the area.$B$BTell him that you are a student of mine...\030Find Starfall in Winterspring and speak with Wynd Nightchaser.\030\030Starfall\0312,1,77,2,321,1,7907\0302,79,145,2,257,1,7907\0302,150,257,2,257,1,7907\0302,259,331,2,321,1,7907\0302,336,381,2,257,1,7907\0302,383,455,2,257,1,7907\0302,460,501,2,257,1,7907\0303,1,62,2,384,1,7907\0301,1,29,4,272,2,11079\0301,31,51,4,272,1,11079\03111079,2,5,Wynd Nightchaser\03011079,2,8,Wynd Nightchaser\0307907,4,9,Daryn Lightwind\0312,702,1438,0,\0302,0,0,1,Felwood\0302,0,0,3,Winterspring\0302,0,0,6,Starfall\0302,0,0,8,Winterspring\0315249,22,5249,UNKNOWN\0305244,23,5244,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305244,24,5244,UNKNOWN\031",[5251]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030objectiveLabel3\030requestItems\030title\031Outstanding, $N! Years of intelligence, lost! The Scarlet Crusade will surely feel this blow in the coming weeks.\030Anything taken to an extreme is hazardous to our world, $N. Take for example, the Scarlet Crusade. Do you believe that their blind zealotry serves a greater good? How many innocents have they destroyed in the name of the Light?$B$BBlasphemers, one and all!$B$BOne in particular interests me, though; the Archivist Galford of Stratholme: A man that watches over the Crusade's most valued documents. Destroy him and burn down his archives! Should you succeed, return to me and be rewarded.\030Travel to Stratholme and find Archivist Galford of the Scarlet Crusade. Destroy him and burn down the Scarlet Archive.\030\030\030Archive Burned\030Remember, $N - we must be tolerant yet rigid in our beliefs!\030The Archivist\0312,1,59,2,257,1,11039\0302,61,98,2,257,1,11039\0302,100,162,2,257,4,11039\0302,164,227,2,261,2,11039\0302,232,256,2,257,1,11039\0302,261,397,2,257,1,11039\0302,399,437,2,261,1,11039\0302,439,487,2,257,1,11039\0303,1,71,2,384,1,11039\0303,73,118,2,388,1,11039\0301,1,16,4,272,1,11039\0301,18,45,4,276,1,11039\0301,47,113,4,272,3,11039\0307,1,60,3,256,1,11039\0306,1,14,3,384,1,11039\03110811,2,6,Archivist Galford\03010811,2,9,Archivist Galford\0312,2017,0,0,\0302,0,0,9,Stratholme\0315262,23,5262,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,10811,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Archivist Galford\030OBJECT,176245,OBJECTIVE,1,14,Scarlet Archive",[5252]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Is that... what I think it is?\030The... the crystal...$B$BThe highborne here are clouded by their own misssery...$B$BI am sorrrrrowful, but I realize the errorrrr of what happened so long ago. Even though there is no waaaay to change the past, I am now at peacccce knowing that you have recovered the crystal of Zin-Malor...$B$BYouuu must return it...$B$BIt muuuussst be returrrned.\030Speak with Wynd Nightchaser in Starfall Village, and ask about the proper place for the Crystal of Zin-Malor.\030It has been some time since you left, $N. How have you fared?\030Remorseful Highborne\0312,1,6,2,257,1,10684\0302,8,21,2,257,1,10684\0302,26,80,2,321,1,10684\0302,85,159,2,321,1,10684\0302,161,291,2,257,1,10684\0302,296,318,2,257,1,10684\0302,323,349,2,257,1,10684\0303,1,109,2,384,1,10684\0301,1,10,4,272,1,11079\0301,12,30,4,272,2,11079\0304,1,41,3,256,1,11079\0304,43,61,3,256,2,11079\03111079,2,8,Wynd Nightchaser\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,8,Starfall Village\0315248,19,5248,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305253,23,5253,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5253]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I have heard of the Crystal of Zin-Malor; the user of the crystal becomes capable of incredible arcane power, but only if truly worthy. I am impressed that you not only recovered the crystal, but you also realize your own limits, and did not attempt to use the crystal yourself.$B$BThank you for bringing it to me, $N. We will keep it safe, and may the cursed sprits that once guarded the shattered crystal finally be at peace.\030Quite impressive, $N.$B$BThe crystal of Zin-Malor can never be returned to the temple which, as you know, lies in ruin. But I believe that your effort to undo the evil of the past should not go unrewarded.$B$BSeek out Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus, and bring the crystal to him, $N. It should be in the hands of those that will not abuse its power. From the looks of it, only a handful of the strongest magic users would be able to control such a power.\030Deliver the Crystal of Zin-Malor to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus.\030Yes, $R?\030The Crystal of Zin-Malor\0312,1,21,2,257,1,11079\0302,26,119,2,257,1,11079\0302,121,205,2,257,4,11079\0302,210,293,2,257,1,11079\0302,295,359,2,257,3,11079\0302,361,464,2,257,4,11079\0303,1,77,2,384,1,11079\0301,1,135,4,272,4,3516\0301,137,278,4,272,1,3516\0301,283,318,4,272,1,3516\0301,320,427,4,284,3,3516\0304,1,8,3,256,2,3516\0313516,2,4,Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm\03015382,2,4,Fandral Staghelm\0303516,2,7,Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm\03015382,2,7,Fandral Staghelm\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,4,Darnassus\0302,0,0,7,Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm\0302,0,0,7,Darnassus\0315252,19,5252,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[526]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, you found them! Now let's get this lightforge iron hammered into something useful, eh?\030You might have found one lightforge ingot in that chest, but that's not enough to craft anything decent!$B$BYou should go back there and look for more.  Maybe the murlocs around that wrecked ship have lightforge ingots on them.\030Gather 5 lightforge ingots, then return to Glorin Steelbrow in the Wetlands.\030Did you find the lightforge iron you need?\030Lightforge Ingots\0312,1,104,2,257,4,1217\0302,109,151,2,257,1,1217\0302,154,227,2,257,4,1217\0303,1,76,2,384,1,1217\0301,1,19,4,272,1,1217\0301,21,90,4,272,2,1217\0304,1,42,3,258,2,1217\0311217,2,4,Glorin Steelbrow\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,4,Glorin Steelbrow\0302,0,0,4,Wetlands\031324,19,324,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030322,23,322,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,2702,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[5261]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031That's true.  I'm looking for someone to hunt me some wolves!  Are you that person?\030Eagan Peltskinner is looking for someone to hunt wolves for him.  That's good news, because we're seeing a lot more wolves in Northshire Valley lately.$B$BIf you're interested then speak with Eagan.  He's around the side of the abbey, to the left.\030Speak with Eagan Peltskinner.\030\030Eagan Peltskinner\0312,1,64,2,257,1,823\0302,67,151,2,259,1,823\0302,156,198,2,257,4,823\0302,201,247,2,257,1,823\0303,1,29,2,384,1,823\0301,1,12,4,272,1,196\0301,15,61,4,272,1,196\0301,64,83,4,272,2,196\031196,2,1,Eagan Peltskinner\030196,2,5,Eagan Peltskinner\0312,9,1429,0,\0302,0,0,2,Northshire Valley\031783,19,783,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\03033,23,33,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\03033,24,33,UNKNOWN\031",[5262]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031What will this mean to the Crusade? Could it be possible that they have been under the control of this demon? Unwittingly serving as the pawns to a greater evil?\030You try and gather your thoughts as the dust settles across the chamber. You go over the events that just transpired and still cannot comprehend the gravity of the situation.$B$BThe Grand Crusader of the Scarlet Crusade a demon? And not just any demon but brother to Varimathras, arch lord of the Undercity?$B$BYou carefully stow the severed head of the dreadlord into your pack. Surely, none would believe the tale you would tell without proof.$B$BDuke Nicholas Zverenhoff must be told at once!\030Take the Head of Balnazzar to Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff in the Eastern Plaguelands.\030What have you got there, $N?\030The Truth Comes Crashing Down\0312,1,72,2,257,1,0\0302,74,174,2,257,1,0\0302,179,228,2,257,2,0\0302,230,307,2,257,2,0\0302,312,379,2,257,1,0\0302,381,445,2,257,4,0\0302,450,495,2,257,1,0\0303,1,82,2,384,1,0\0301,1,35,4,272,2,11039\0301,37,109,4,272,4,11039\0301,111,161,4,272,2,11039\0304,1,28,3,256,2,11039\0312425,2,4,Varimathras\0308716,2,5,Dreadlord\03011039,2,7,Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff\03010813,2,8,Balnazzar\03011039,2,8,Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff\0312,2017,0,0,\0302,0,0,4,Varimathras\0302,0,0,8,Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff\0302,0,0,8,Eastern Plaguelands\0304,0,0,9,Crusade\0315251,19,5251,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305263,23,5263,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,13250,STARTER,?,10,",[5263]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It has been many years since I have ushered a champion into our ranks. You are the first to be granted audience with Lord Maxwell in years.\030You display a natural aptitude for destruction and you follow orders. It is rare to see the two coexist. I am beginning to think that you may make an excellent vehicle of divine justice.$B$B<Zverenhoff clasps his hands together in front of his face.>$B$BKel'Thuzad's errand boy rules over Stratholme. Prove to me that you are a champion - my champion. Destroy Baron Rivendare and return to me with his head. $B\030Venture to Stratholme and destroy Baron Rivendare. Take his head and return to Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff.$B\030The Baron has slain more people than you have most likely seen in your lifetime.\030Above and Beyond\0312,1,69,2,257,1,11039\0302,71,104,2,257,1,11039\0302,106,186,2,257,1,11039\0302,191,250,2,257,1,11039\0302,255,300,2,257,1,11039\0302,302,351,2,257,1,11039\0302,353,407,2,261,1,11039\0303,1,50,2,388,1,11039\0303,52,104,2,384,1,11039\0301,1,70,4,272,1,11039\0301,72,139,4,272,1,11039\0304,1,80,3,260,1,11039\03110440,2,7,Baron Rivendare\03010440,2,8,Baron Rivendare\03011039,2,9,Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff\0312,2017,0,0,\0302,0,0,8,Stratholme\0302,0,0,9,Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff\0315262,19,5262,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305264,23,5264,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,13251,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5264]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You are a worthy ally, $N. You shall reap the rewards of your stalwart dedication.\030I am about to bestow a great honor upon you, $N.$B$BLord Maxwell wishes to reward you for your service to the Argent Dawn!$B$BIt has been years since Maxwell has granted audience to outsiders.$B\030Speak with Lord Maxwell Tyrosus. He is inside the church.\030\030Lord Maxwell Tyrosus\0312,1,48,2,257,1,11039\0302,53,122,2,259,1,11039\0302,127,192,2,257,1,11039\0303,1,32,2,384,1,11039\0303,34,57,2,384,1,11039\0301,1,26,4,272,1,11034\0301,28,82,4,272,3,11034\03111034,2,4,Lord Maxwell Tyrosus\0312,139,1423,0,\0302,0,0,2,Argent Dawn\0315263,19,5263,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305265,23,5265,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5265]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Whoa...\030Through the years the Argent Hold has remained locked. None have been worthy to reach inside and take from it the power of the Argent Dawn - until today.$B$BThe Argent Hold is now open to you, $N.\030Open the Argent Hold and claim your reward.\030\030The Argent Hold\0312,1,54,2,257,1,11034\0302,56,153,2,257,1,11034\0302,158,196,2,257,1,11034\0303,1,43,2,384,1,11034\0301,1,7,4,272,1,0\031\0312,139,1423,0,\0315264,19,5264,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,176317,FINISHER,?,12,The Argent Hold",[527]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031At ease, $C. I see you have returned from battle. My sources tell me you performed well on the Hillsbrad front.\030Stand at attention while addressing me, $c.$B$BI am under direct command of Varimathras.  We are to quell the human infestation until our apothecaries can develop the new plague.$B$BOur information leads us to believe that the town of Hillsbrad is vulnerable to attack.  Your first assignment is aimed at disrupting their food supply and infrastructure.$B$BTravel west.  Raid the northernmost farms of Hillsbrad Fields.  Make sure that the landowners, Farmer Ray and Farmer Getz, are executed as well.\030Kill 6 Hillsbrad Farmhands, 6 Hillsbrad Farmers, Farmer Ray and Farmer Getz and report back to Darthalia in Tarren Mill.\030As High Executor of Tarren Mill, under the direct command of Varimathras and the Dark Lady, you are subject to follow my command.$B$BPerhaps you take this war with the Alliance lightly? If such is the case I should behead you right here and now. Otherwise, travel west to the town of Hillsbrad and wage battle against the humans, as ordered.$B$BDismissed.\030Battle of Hillsbrad\0312,1,43,2,257,1,2215\0302,48,88,2,257,1,2215\0302,91,178,2,261,1,2215\0302,183,269,2,261,4,2215\0302,272,353,2,257,1,2215\0302,358,369,2,257,1,2215\0302,372,419,2,257,1,2215\0302,422,501,2,257,1,2215\0303,1,120,2,384,1,2215\0301,1,12,4,272,1,2215\0301,14,49,4,276,1,2215\0301,51,111,4,272,1,2215\0304,1,129,3,256,1,2215\0304,134,185,3,260,4,2215\0304,187,245,3,256,4,2215\0304,247,341,3,268,1,2215\0304,346,355,3,256,1,2215\0312425,2,2,Varimathras\030232,2,8,Farmer Ray\0302403,2,8,Farmer Getz\030232,2,9,Farmer Ray\0302403,2,9,Farmer Getz\0302425,3,13,Varimathras\03015065,3,13,Lady\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,9,Darthalia\0302,0,0,9,Tarren Mill\031528,23,528,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,2266,OBJECTIVE,6,13,Hillsbrad Farmer\030NPC,2360,OBJECTIVE,6,13,Hillsbrad Farmhand\030NPC,232,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Farmer Ray\030NPC,2403,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Farmer Getz",[528]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The grip of death is tightening around the town of Hillsbrad. The battle goes well.\030Word of the attack on the northern farms has the townsfolk panicked.  Most excellent.$B$BOur Deathstalkers report peasants fleeing to the fields in southern Hillsbrad.  The fools think they can hide in the orchards and escape their doom.$B$BProve them wrong, $N.  Return to Hillsbrad Fields and seek out the cowering peasants.  Lay waste to them in the name of our Dark Lady.$B$BDismissed!\030Kill 15 Hillsbrad Peasants and report back to Darthalia in Tarren Mill.\030You have your orders, $c. Quit dawdling here in Tarren Mill when there is work to be done elsewhere.\030Battle of Hillsbrad\0312,1,68,2,261,1,2215\0302,71,85,2,257,1,2215\0302,90,167,2,257,1,2215\0302,170,237,2,257,1,2215\0302,242,262,2,257,1,2215\0302,265,326,2,259,1,2215\0302,329,375,2,257,1,2215\0302,380,389,2,257,1,2215\0303,1,71,2,384,1,2215\0301,1,61,4,272,1,2215\0301,63,83,4,276,1,2215\0304,1,25,3,256,1,2215\0304,27,100,3,256,1,2215\03115065,2,7,Lady\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,6,Hillsbrad Fields\0302,0,0,9,Darthalia\0302,0,0,9,Tarren Mill\0303,0,0,13,Tarren Mill\031527,19,527,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030529,23,529,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,2267,OBJECTIVE,15,13,Hillsbrad Peasant",[5281]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Alen has finally found someone brave enough, eh?\030There are those that died tragically in the fall of Stratholme. Many took their own lives, opting to hurl themselves into the myriad flames of the smoldering city rather than become one of the Scourge.$B$BThey now walk the streets of Stratholme as restless spirits.$B$BWe must aid them, $N!$B$BI have an associate named Egan who has been doing miraculous work with ghosts and souls. Seek him out. He walks the eastern Plaguelands, near Stratholme, testing his innovations.\030Find Egan. You only know that he was last seen around Stratholme.\030\030The Restless Souls\0312,1,63,2,257,1,11038\0302,65,201,2,321,1,11038\0302,206,265,2,257,1,11038\0302,270,290,2,257,1,11038\0302,295,382,2,257,1,11038\0302,384,396,2,257,1,11038\0302,398,472,2,257,1,11038\0303,1,10,2,384,1,11038\0303,12,65,2,384,1,11038\0301,1,48,4,272,2,11140\03111140,2,5,Egan\03011140,2,8,Egan\0312,139,1423,0,\0302,0,0,7,Stratholme\0315282,23,5282,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5282]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030requestItems\030title\031<Egan wipes a tear from his eye.>$B$BDid you see my mother, $N? Did you free her?$B$BYou are a shining example of decency. For your troubles...\030I draw my power - my will to continue living and breathing - from the unmitigated hatred I have for the Scourge and all that they have done. I am, however, no zealot. There are those, like the Scarlet Crusade, who would sooner destroy the innocent undead than lend them even an ounce of compassion.$B$BWhich brings me to this: My blaster. It will unchain the tortured souls from Stratholme.$B$BUse it on the ghosts that haunt the ransacked streets. Free their souls.\030Use Egan's Blaster on the ghostly and spectral citizens of Stratholme. When the restless souls break free from their ghostly shells, use the blaster again - freedom will be theirs!$B$BFree 15 Restless Souls and return to Egan.\030\030Souls Freed\030Compassion is what separates us from the animals, $N. Remember that...\030The Restless Souls\0312,1,140,2,321,3,11140\0302,142,166,2,257,1,11140\0302,168,298,2,261,4,11140\0302,303,338,2,257,1,11140\0302,340,390,2,257,3,11140\0302,395,448,2,257,1,11140\0302,450,466,2,257,1,11140\0303,1,70,2,384,1,11140\0303,72,180,2,392,3,11140\0303,185,226,2,384,1,11140\0301,1,33,4,272,1,11140\0301,38,63,4,272,2,11140\0301,65,81,4,272,2,11140\0301,86,122,4,272,1,11140\0301,124,143,4,272,1,11140\0306,1,53,3,256,1,11140\0306,55,70,3,256,1,11140\0305,1,11,3,384,1,11140\03111140,2,10,Egan\03011140,4,11,Egan\0312,2017,0,0,\0302,0,0,5,Stratholme\0302,0,0,10,Egan\0315281,19,5281,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,11122,OBJECTIVE,15,13,Restless Soul",[5283]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This be it, $N. After this, there ain't no way to turn back. It's not too late to become a toy maker, er, weaponsmith.$B$BI trust ye'll make the right decision.\030So ye made the smart decision.$B$BThere ain't no love lost betwixt me an old Ironus here. That good for nothing toy maker knows who the true craftsmen round here be.$B$BThe truly great wars are won with a good defense. When it be go time, no offense is gonna be helping ye out.$B$BRight, so let's get to work. All ye need to do is show me that ye've got some raw talent. After that, I'll yank whatever impurities be left in ye and mold ye into an armorsmith. Ye do know how to make ornate mithril, don't ye?\030To become an Armorsmith, you must make the following items and return them to Grumnus: 4 Ornate Mithril Helms, 2 Ornate Mithril Boots, 1 Ornate Mithril Breastplate.\030Ah, ain't nothing like a good forge tan. Ye can tell who's got the really good tans by their apron lines.\030The Art of the Armorsmith\0312,1,30,2,257,1,5164\0302,35,89,2,261,1,5164\0302,91,165,2,257,1,5164\0302,170,218,2,257,1,5164\0302,220,277,2,257,1,5164\0302,282,309,2,257,1,5164\0302,311,370,2,259,1,5164\0302,372,458,2,257,1,5164\0302,460,507,2,257,2,5164\0303,1,164,2,384,1,5164\0301,1,15,4,272,1,5164\0301,17,60,4,272,1,5164\0301,62,118,4,272,1,5164\0301,123,160,4,272,1,5164\0304,1,40,3,256,1,5164\0304,42,105,3,256,1,5164\031\0312,0,0,10,Grumnus\0315284,22,5284,UNKNOWN\031ITEM,7937,OBJECTIVE,4,15,\030ITEM,7936,OBJECTIVE,2,15,\030ITEM,7935,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5284]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031About time! I've got customers waiting.$B$BGive those here and pay attention. You're going to take the first step in your career as a weaponsmith.\030As a weaponsmith you'll find that more often than not, heroes and adventurers will be coming to you for gear. While the workload can be unbearable at times, the riches more than make up for the back strain and ash lung.$B$BOh yes, $N, weaponsmiths are the ones with all the gold!$B$BIf you wish to join our ranks, you'll need to show me that you can make me a silver or two - I mean, show me that you've got what it takes to be the go to $g guy:girl; when people need superior quality weapons. Get to work!\030To become a Weaponsmith, you must make the following items and return them to Ironus: 4 Moonsteel Broadswords, 4 Massive Iron Axes, 2 Heavy Mithril Axes, and 2 Big Black Maces.$B\030<Ironus is busy stacking gold coins into neat little piles.>\030The Way of the Weaponsmith\0312,1,109,2,257,3,11146\0302,111,219,2,257,1,11146\0302,224,279,2,257,1,11146\0302,284,493,2,259,4,11146\0302,495,506,2,257,1,11146\0303,1,176,2,384,1,11146\0301,1,11,4,272,1,11146\0301,13,39,4,272,1,11146\0301,44,77,4,272,1,11146\0301,79,146,4,272,3,11146\0304,1,60,3,256,1,11146\031371,2,4,Girl\0312,0,0,6,Ironus\0315283,22,5283,UNKNOWN\031ITEM,3853,OBJECTIVE,4,15,\030ITEM,3855,OBJECTIVE,4,15,\030ITEM,7941,OBJECTIVE,2,15,\030ITEM,7945,OBJECTIVE,2,15,",[529]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Mission accomplished, $C. And carried out quite skillfully, I might add.\030The humans of Hillsbrad have been putting up unexpected resistance.  The problem appears to be that the townsfolk are being armed by the local blacksmith.  We need to shut down all supply lines.$B$BYour mission will be to execute Blacksmith Verringtan.  Slay his apprentices as well.  While there, bring back a shipment of iron from their stockpile.  The supplies will come in handy when we are done with the conquering of Hillsbrad and begin razing Southshore.\030Kill Blacksmith Verringtan and 4 Hillsbrad Apprentice Blacksmiths.$B$BRetrieve a shipment of iron and report back to Darthalia in Tarren Mill.\030Were you able to carry out your orders, $C? Did you dispose of Verringtan and his assistants? And where is that iron shipment?\030Battle of Hillsbrad\0312,1,67,2,257,1,2215\0302,70,154,2,261,1,2215\0302,157,194,2,259,1,2215\0302,199,252,2,257,3,2215\0302,255,283,2,257,1,2215\0302,286,349,2,257,1,2215\0302,352,461,2,257,3,2215\0303,1,66,2,384,1,2215\0303,71,142,2,384,1,2215\0301,1,25,4,272,1,2215\0301,27,72,4,272,4,2215\0304,1,43,3,256,2,2215\0304,45,93,3,256,2,2215\0304,95,126,3,256,2,2215\0312404,2,4,Blacksmith Verringtan\0302404,2,8,Blacksmith Verringtan\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,9,Darthalia\0302,0,0,9,Tarren Mill\031528,19,528,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030532,23,532,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,2404,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Blacksmith Verringtan\030NPC,2265,OBJECTIVE,4,13,Hillsbrad Apprentice Blacksmith\030ITEM,3564,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[53]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Aged in the barrel, filtered through coal$BIt passes your lips and right through your soul.$BSo lets us drink now, a toast to you$BAnd me while we're at it, Grimbooze Thunderbrew!\030Mellifluous liquid clear as a baby's tears$BTurns a lovely deep amber over the years$BBut before we proceed to get lit to the hilt$BA barrel of charred oak must be built.\030Bring Grimbooze Thunderbrew a bundle of Charred Oak.\030Sure, I'll sing it again for you, friend!$B$BMellifluous liquid clear as a baby's tears$BTurns a lovely deep amber over the years$BBut before we proceed to get lit to the hilt$BA barrel of charred oak must be built.\030Sweet Amber\0312,1,42,2,257,1,239\0302,45,84,2,257,1,239\0302,87,130,2,265,1,239\0302,133,170,2,257,1,239\0303,1,52,2,384,1,239\0301,1,41,4,272,1,239\0301,44,91,4,272,1,239\0301,94,129,4,272,1,239\0301,132,179,4,272,1,239\0304,1,41,3,256,1,239\0304,46,87,3,256,1,239\0304,90,129,3,256,1,239\0304,132,175,3,264,1,239\0304,178,215,3,256,1,239\031239,2,5,Grimbooze Thunderbrew\030239,4,9,Grimbooze Thunderbrew\0312,40,1436,0,\03151,19,51,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,743,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[530]="PARTIAL\031loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, good. These hands killed my wife, Deliah. Revenge for her murder was my only care, and you were the instrument of that revenge.$B$BHere, take the ring you returned earlier. Deliah has been dead to me for so long, her ring is a bauble I no longer care to keep. Instead, I will keep these hands as a remembrance of my friend's betrayal.\030Valdred, once my good friend, was my wife's murderer.  Although I am incapable of grieving, I do yearn for revenge.  If you kill Valdred and bring me his cursed hands, then I will reward you.$B$BI last heard he was at the Greymane Wall in southern Silverpine, trying to flee into the kingdom of Gilneas.\030Kill Valdred Moray.$B$BBring his hands to Raleigh Andrean in the Undercity.\030Do you have those hands, $N?\030A Husband's Revenge\0312,1,53,2,257,1,2050\0302,56,115,2,259,1,2050\0302,118,191,2,261,4,2050\0302,196,303,2,257,1,2050\0303,1,19,2,384,1,2050\0303,24,75,2,384,1,2050\0301,1,9,4,272,1,2050\0301,11,45,4,272,1,2050\0301,47,131,4,278,1,2050\0301,136,176,4,272,1,2050\0301,178,263,4,304,1,2050\0301,265,338,4,272,3,2050\0304,1,28,3,256,2,2050\0312332,2,5,Valdred Moray\0302050,2,6,Raleigh Andrean\0312,130,1421,0,\0302,0,0,4,Greymane Wall\0302,0,0,6,Raleigh Andrean\0302,0,0,6,Undercity\031441,19,441,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3613,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5301]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is the final step before you begin your new career as an armorsmith, $N. Should you choose to back out, now would be your last chance. Otherwise, prepare yourself for a lifetime of glory.\030Satisfaction. It is what I draw from the hammer and the anvil. To see a proud Horde warrior protected under my steel reminds me of what it is to be alive. It is an addiction that I dare never give up, $N.$B$BI can not grant you this satisfaction, merely set you upon the path. As with all of life's endeavors, the path of the armorsmith is a journey.$B$BIf you wish to be one of the select few, you need only to ask and I shall train, but, a task you must first complete.\030To become an armorsmith, you must make the following items and return them to Okothos: 4 Ornate Mithril Helms, 2 Ornate Mithril Boots, 1 Ornate Mithril Breastplate.\030I will pound the steel until the breath itself has been taken from me.\030The Art of the Armorsmith\0312,1,13,2,257,1,11177\0302,15,62,2,257,1,11177\0302,64,154,2,257,1,11177\0302,156,204,2,257,1,11177\0302,209,276,2,257,1,11177\0302,278,350,2,257,1,11177\0302,355,471,2,259,4,11177\0303,1,164,2,384,1,11177\0301,1,77,4,272,1,11177\0301,79,139,4,272,4,11177\0301,141,192,4,280,1,11177\0304,1,70,3,256,3,11177\031\0312,0,0,8,Okothos\0315302,22,5302,UNKNOWN\031ITEM,7937,OBJECTIVE,4,15,\030ITEM,7936,OBJECTIVE,2,15,\030ITEM,7935,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5302]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is the final step before you begin your new career as a weaponsmith, $N. Should you choose to back out, now would be your last chance. Otherwise, prepare to be consumed by knowledge!\030One day, I will create a legendary hammer. A hammer fit for a Warchief!$B$BIt is my life's work, $N. My passion. I recognize that you have the potential to be among us, one of us - a weaponsmith. I am the one that can help you harness that potential.$B$BA simple task is all that you must complete. Simple for one of your exceptional skill.\030To become a Weaponsmith, you must make the following items and return them to Borgosh: 4 Moonsteel Broadswords, 4 Massive Iron Axes, 2 Heavy Mithril Axes, and 2 Big Black Maces.$B\030For the glory of the Horde!\030The Way of the Weaponsmith\0312,1,42,2,257,3,11178\0302,44,71,2,257,1,11178\0302,76,100,2,257,1,11178\0302,102,112,2,257,1,11178\0302,114,195,2,257,1,11178\0302,197,250,2,257,1,11178\0302,255,298,2,257,1,11178\0302,300,340,2,257,1,11178\0303,1,177,2,384,1,11178\0301,1,77,4,272,1,11178\0301,79,139,4,272,4,11178\0301,141,187,4,280,1,11178\0304,1,27,3,256,1,11178\031\0312,0,0,9,Borgosh\0315301,22,5301,UNKNOWN\031ITEM,3853,OBJECTIVE,4,15,\030ITEM,3855,OBJECTIVE,4,15,\030ITEM,7941,OBJECTIVE,2,15,\030ITEM,7945,OBJECTIVE,2,15,",[5305]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031May you bash in many a brain, $N!\030Within the confines of the Scarlet Bastion lies sweet Serenity. The Crimson Hammersmith guards the recipe with his life. Defeat him and bring me his apron. For that, I shall reward you with the knowledge required to create an enchanted battlehammer!\030Travel to Stratholme and kill the Crimson Hammersmith. Recover the Crimson Hammersmith's Apron and return to Lilith.$B\030His apron! Where is it?\030Sweet Serenity\0312,1,63,2,257,1,11191\0302,65,120,2,257,1,11191\0302,122,155,2,257,1,11191\0302,157,249,2,257,3,11191\0303,1,54,2,384,1,11191\0303,56,116,2,384,1,11191\0301,1,33,4,272,1,11191\0304,1,10,3,256,1,11191\0304,12,23,3,256,2,11191\03111120,2,2,Crimson Hammersmith\03011120,2,5,Crimson Hammersmith\03011120,2,6,Crimson Hammersmith\0312,0,0,5,Stratholme\0302,0,0,6,Lilith\031\031ITEM,13351,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5306]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Knowledge is power!\030Don't let her beauty fool you, $c. The shadow huntress, Vosh'gajin is deadly and deranged.$B$B<Kilram points to the scar on his face.>$B$BAye, she gave me that - a love tap, she called it.$B$BThe time for vengeance has finally come.$B$BYou can find Vosh'gajin in Blackrock Spire. Slay her and return to me with her snakestone. Do this and I will teach you the secret to crafting Dawn's Edge!\030Travel to Blackrock Spire and slay Shadow Hunter Vosh'gajin. Recover Vosh'gajin's Snakestone and return to Kilram.\030Legend states that one use of Vosh'gajin's snakestone will keep an axe razor sharp for a 1000 years!\030Snakestone of the Shadow Huntress\0312,1,34,2,257,1,11192\0302,36,90,2,257,1,11192\0302,95,134,2,257,1,11192\0302,139,188,2,257,1,11192\0302,193,232,2,259,1,11192\0302,237,279,2,257,1,11192\0302,281,326,2,257,1,11192\0302,328,391,2,257,3,11192\0303,1,60,2,384,1,11192\0303,62,114,2,384,1,11192\0301,1,19,4,272,1,11192\0304,1,100,3,256,3,11192\0314244,2,2,Shadow\03011192,2,3,Kilram\0309236,2,9,Shadow Hunter Vosh'gajin\03011192,2,10,Kilram\0312,0,0,6,Blackrock Spire\0302,0,0,9,Blackrock Spire\0302,0,0,10,Kilram\031\031ITEM,13352,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5307]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It should be obvious that a sword is always the best choice.\030If I am short with you, it is for a reason. The plans for the creation of the great blade, Corruption, have been stolen by the Black Guard: Elite skeletal units of Baron Rivendare.$B$BYes, Baron Rivendare of Stratholme.$B$BThe Black Guard swordsmith now guards those plans with his... undeath.$B$BSlay him and return proof of this deed and I shall grant you the knowledge required to create a blazing rapier!\030Find the Black Guard Swordsmith in Stratholme and destroy him. Recover the Insignia of the Black Guard and return to Seril Scourgebane.\030Have you forgotten what it is that you were tasked with, $N?\030Corruption\0312,1,43,2,257,4,11193\0302,45,180,2,261,1,11193\0302,185,219,2,257,1,11193\0302,224,284,2,257,1,11193\0302,286,293,2,257,1,11193\0302,298,408,2,257,3,11193\0303,1,62,2,388,1,11193\0303,64,135,2,384,1,11193\0301,1,60,4,272,1,11193\0304,1,60,3,256,2,11193\03110440,2,2,Baron Rivendare\03010440,2,3,Baron Rivendare\03011121,2,4,Black Guard Swordsmith\03011121,2,7,Black Guard Swordsmith\03011193,2,8,Seril Scourgebane\0312,0,0,7,Stratholme\0302,0,0,8,Seril Scourgebane\031\031ITEM,13350,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[531]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thanks for helping me out with my little plan, $N. I've been itching for months to get back at that snooty, stuck-up boy, and I'd say we did a pretty good job! Here, have this, you've earned it.\030Light! Don't bring things like that into the Lodge... it's unsanitary, unspeakable, un... un... unsanitary!$B$BJust get it out of here, will you? No one wants to see your bloody little trophy, really!\030Bring Ol' Sooty's head to Vyrin Swiftwind at the Farstrider Lodge.\030Great job, $N! We really showed him! Here, give me the head and I'll take care of it.\030Vyrin's Revenge\0312,1,6,2,257,1,1187\0302,8,53,2,257,1,1187\0302,55,89,2,257,1,1187\0302,97,107,2,257,1,1187\0302,112,145,2,257,2,1187\0302,147,200,2,259,1,1187\0303,1,66,2,384,1,1187\0301,1,50,4,272,1,1156\0301,52,159,4,272,1,1156\0301,161,194,4,272,1,1156\0304,1,14,3,256,1,1156\0304,16,36,3,256,1,1156\0304,38,85,3,256,1,1156\0311225,2,7,Ol' Sooty\0301156,2,7,Vyrin Swiftwind\0312,38,1432,0,\0302,0,0,7,Vyrin Swiftwind\0302,0,0,7,Farstrider Lodge\031271,19,271,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[532]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030objectiveLabel3\030objectiveLabel4\030requestItems\030title\031News of your glories in Hillsbrad traveled fast. You have done well, $C.\030The town of Hillsbrad is in disarray and we believe it will soon fall.  We must, however, persist in our ruthlessness until the human scum are wiped from the foothills for eternity.$B$BDespite their overwhelming losses, the humans rally around their leadership and keep fighting.  We must eliminate their leader, Magistrate Burnside, as well as the town council.  Destroy their revered political document as well, the Hillsbrad Proclamation.  And while you're at it, steal the town registry.\030Kill Magistrate Burnside and 4 Hillsbrad Councilmen.  Destroy the Hillsbrad Proclamation.  Steal the Hillsbrad Town Registry.  Report back to Darthalia in Tarren Mill afterwards.\030\030\030\030Hillsbrad Proclamation destroyed\030What news have you?\030Battle of Hillsbrad\0312,1,70,2,257,4,2215\0302,73,181,2,257,1,2215\0302,186,279,2,261,1,2215\0302,282,362,2,257,1,2215\0302,365,441,2,261,1,2215\0302,444,491,2,261,1,2215\0303,1,52,2,384,1,2215\0303,55,89,2,388,1,2215\0303,92,125,2,388,1,2215\0303,128,178,2,384,1,2215\0301,1,48,4,272,1,2215\0301,50,72,4,272,1,2215\0308,1,19,3,256,2,2215\0307,1,32,3,388,1,2215\0312335,2,4,Magistrate Burnside\0302335,2,7,Magistrate Burnside\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,10,Darthalia\0302,0,0,10,Tarren Mill\0304,0,0,11,Hillsbrad\031529,19,529,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030539,23,539,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,2335,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Magistrate Burnside\030NPC,2387,OBJECTIVE,4,13,Hillsbrad Councilman\030OBJECT,1761,OBJECTIVE,1,14,Hillsbrad Proclamation\030ITEM,3657,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5321]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Oh, I am so happy Kerlonian made it! And I'm sure I'll find him sleeping somewhere around here, won't I?$B$BThank you for showing him the way, $N.\030I was on my way to Maestra's Post to meet Liladris Moonriver, but I decided to stop here and take a short nap. Ever since I awoke from the emerald dream, I have been so sleepy...$B$B<yawn>$B$BWould you mind showing me the way? I understand that Maestra's Post is south of here, along the road in Ashenvale. It can be dangerous, so I hope you have some friends that will join us.$B$BLastly, I may fall asleep so if you ever need to wake me, please use my horn. You'll find it in the chest here.\030Escort Kerlonian Evershade to Liladris Moonriver at Maestra's Post in Ashenvale.\030Escort Kerlonian Evershade to Maestra's Post\030Has Kerlonian arrived?\030The Sleeper Has Awakened\0312,1,110,2,257,1,11218\0302,112,178,2,257,1,11218\0302,183,188,2,257,1,11218\0302,193,226,2,257,4,11218\0302,228,306,2,257,1,11218\0302,308,378,2,259,3,11218\0302,383,459,2,259,4,11218\0302,461,493,2,257,1,11218\0303,1,80,2,384,1,11218\0301,1,36,4,272,1,11219\0301,38,104,4,272,2,11219\0301,109,146,4,272,1,11219\0305,1,22,3,256,2,11219\0304,1,44,3,384,1,11218\03111219,2,1,Liladris Moonriver\03011218,2,9,Kerlonian Evershade\03011219,2,9,Liladris Moonriver\03011218,3,14,Kerlonian Evershade\0312,148,1439,0,\0302,0,0,1,Maestra's Post\0302,0,0,5,Ashenvale\0302,0,0,9,Liladris Moonriver\0302,0,0,9,Maestra's Post\0302,0,0,9,Ashenvale\0303,0,0,14,Maestra's Post\031\031ITEM,13536,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[533]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Finally, we know where Gol'dir is being held. The camp in question is not too far from here, and hopefully they will not be as well prepared as they were when they captured us the first time.\030At last we begin to hear word and rumor, find evidence of Gol'dir's whereabouts. The humans have been moving him around, but we are narrowing down our search and focusing on the large Syndicate camp just north of here.$B$BGo there, $n, and bring back whatever information you can get your hands on.\030Retrieve information about Gol'dir's whereabouts for Krusk in Tarren Mill.\030Have you found anything? I fear Gol'dir's prospects grow worse by the day...\030Infiltration\0312,1,80,2,257,1,2229\0302,82,218,2,257,1,2229\0302,223,298,2,257,1,2229\0303,1,74,2,384,1,2229\0301,1,45,4,272,1,2229\0301,47,191,4,272,3,2229\0304,1,24,3,256,2,2229\0304,26,76,3,256,1,2229\0312229,2,4,Krusk\0302316,4,5,Gol'dir\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,4,Tarren Mill\031498,19,498,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030503,23,503,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3601,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5341]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Excellent work, $R. Now to secure my inheritance...\030Within the Scholomance lays the Barov family fortune. I, Alexi Barov, am one of the last two remaining heirs of the house Barov. My brother, Weldon, is the other.$B$BWeldon, the miserable coward, fled during the war and thus retained his worthless existence as a human.$B$BHe now searches for the deeds so that he may claim the fortune for his own. Recover the deeds before my brother does and I shall make you wealthy beyond your wildest dreams!\030Venture to the Scholomance and recover the Barov family fortune. Four deeds make up this fortune: The Deed to Caer Darrow; The Deed to Brill; The Deed to Tarren Mill; and The Deed to Southshore. Return to Alexi Barov when you have completed this task.\030Bow your head in my presence, $r. I am a noble, after all, and you are a copperless peasant.\030Barov Family Fortune\0312,1,53,2,257,1,11022\0302,55,128,2,257,1,11022\0302,130,162,2,257,1,11022\0302,167,269,2,261,1,11022\0302,274,348,2,259,1,11022\0302,350,446,2,257,3,11022\0303,1,64,2,384,1,11022\0303,66,194,2,384,1,11022\0303,196,251,2,384,1,11022\0301,1,19,4,272,1,11022\0301,21,51,4,272,1,11022\0304,1,33,3,256,1,11022\0304,35,92,3,256,1,11022\03111022,2,2,Alexi Barov\03011022,2,9,Alexi Barov\030351,3,13,Peasant\0312,2057,0,0,\0302,0,0,7,Scholomance\0302,0,0,8,Caer Darrow\0302,0,0,8,Brill\0302,0,0,8,Tarren Mill\0302,0,0,8,Southshore\0302,0,0,9,Alexi Barov\0315342,23,5342,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,13471,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,13448,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,13450,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,13451,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5342]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Wonderful! Now only I hold the power and fortune of house Barov!$B$B<Alexi throws a large bag at you.>$B$BAnd keep the change, you filthy animal.\030Naturally, with my brother still alive, there may be some contention as to the primary beneficiary of the family's fortune. This cannot be.$B$BA low down guttersnipe like you isn't above a little cold-blooded murder, I hope.$B$BIt's a simple task and one that I expect you will complete; that is, if you wish to claim your reward.$B$BWeldon sits under Alliance protection at Chillwind Camp, to the east. Slay him, return his head.$B$B<Alexi yawns.>$B$BHurry along now.\030Travel to Chillwind Camp - Alliance territory - and assassinate Weldon Barov. Take his head and return to Alexi Barov.$B$BBe warned, Weldon will probably be well protected by Alliance scum.\030Secure my fortune and share in the spoils.\030The Last Barov\0312,1,123,2,257,1,11022\0302,125,139,2,257,1,11022\0302,144,224,2,263,3,11022\0302,229,330,2,259,4,11022\0302,335,403,2,257,1,11022\0302,405,430,2,257,1,11022\0302,435,448,2,257,1,11022\0302,453,468,2,257,1,11022\0303,1,77,2,384,1,11022\0303,79,118,2,384,1,11022\0303,123,189,2,384,3,11022\0301,1,10,4,272,1,11022\0301,12,64,4,272,1,11022\0301,69,102,4,272,1,11022\0301,107,145,4,272,1,11022\0304,1,42,3,256,1,11022\03111023,2,9,Weldon Barov\03011022,2,10,Alexi Barov\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,5,Chillwind Camp\0302,0,0,9,Chillwind Camp\0302,0,0,10,Alexi Barov\0315341,19,5341,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,13469,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5343]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Excellent work, $R. Now to secure my inheritance...\030My dear brother Alexi. What a fool I was to spare his life. I looked into the face of the enemy, one of the undead, and let him live.$B$B<Weldon spits.>$B$BHe now searches for MY inheritance. This simply cannot happen.$B$BFind my family's deeds before that vile retch gets his boney hands upon them and I shall reward you with vast riches. They lay in the ruins of the Scholomance. Make haste!\030Venture to the Scholomance and recover the Barov family fortune. Four deeds make up this fortune: The Deed to Caer Darrow; The Deed to Brill; The Deed to Tarren Mill; and The Deed to Southshore. Return to Weldon Barov when you have completed this task.\030Bow your head in my presence, $R. I am a noble, after all, and you are a copperless peasant.\030Barov Family Fortune\0312,1,22,2,257,1,11023\0302,24,59,2,257,1,11023\0302,61,133,2,261,1,11023\0302,138,152,2,257,1,11023\0302,157,191,2,257,1,11023\0302,193,218,2,257,1,11023\0302,223,339,2,257,3,11023\0302,341,381,2,321,1,11023\0302,383,393,2,257,1,11023\0303,1,64,2,384,1,11023\0303,66,194,2,384,1,11023\0303,196,252,2,384,1,11023\0301,1,19,4,272,1,11023\0301,21,51,4,272,1,11023\0304,1,33,3,256,1,11023\0304,35,92,3,256,1,11023\03111023,2,12,Weldon Barov\030351,3,16,Peasant\0312,2057,0,0,\0302,0,0,10,Scholomance\0302,0,0,11,Caer Darrow\0302,0,0,11,Brill\0302,0,0,11,Tarren Mill\0302,0,0,11,Southshore\0302,0,0,12,Weldon Barov\0315344,23,5344,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,13471,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,13448,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,13450,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,13451,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5344]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A glorious day it is! Finally, the pockmark of house Barov eliminated and my fortune secure!$B$BTake this and leave my sight, peasant.\030With the deeds recovered, there is but one thing left to do. Alexi must be killed. With him dead, I need not ever worry about an unscrupulous gang of mercenaries seeking my head.$B$BIt's a simple task. Alexi hides under the protection of the Horde - at the Bulwark.$B$BNo, I do not expect you to just walk up and kill him, I want his head! How you get it... well, that part is up to you. That type of behavior is below one of my noble upbringing.\030Travel to the Bulwark - Horde territory - and assassinate Alexi Barov. Take his head and return to Weldon Barov.$B$BBe warned, Alexi will probably be well protected by Horde filth.\030You do want payment, do you not?\030The Last Barov\0312,1,60,2,257,1,11023\0302,62,82,2,257,1,11023\0302,84,178,2,259,1,11023\0302,183,201,2,257,1,11023\0302,203,265,2,257,1,11023\0302,270,339,2,259,1,11023\0302,341,357,2,257,1,11023\0302,359,387,2,257,1,11023\0302,389,446,2,257,1,11023\0303,1,70,2,384,1,11023\0303,72,112,2,384,1,11023\0303,117,180,2,384,3,11023\0301,1,21,4,272,1,11023\0301,23,92,4,272,1,11023\0301,97,134,4,272,1,11023\0304,1,32,3,258,2,11023\03111022,2,10,Alexi Barov\03011023,2,11,Weldon Barov\030351,4,15,Peasant\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,5,Bulwark\0302,0,0,10,Bulwark\0302,0,0,11,Weldon Barov\0315343,19,5343,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,13470,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[535]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Given my impending death, I think I can safely say that this is the sweetest tasting thing ever... Here, take this, won't do me any good when I'm dead.$B$BWell, get on with it!\030Urrgh... Injured and dying and confronted with the enemy.$B$BNo doubt you'll kill me anyway, but if you bring me some Southshore stout--your kind does drink, don't they?--I'll tell you what you want to know.\030Bring a mug of Southshore Stout to Valik in the Syndicate camp.\030Did you bring me something to drink or did you just come back to finish the job?\030Valik\0312,1,8,2,257,1,2333\0302,10,57,2,261,1,2333\0302,62,207,2,259,4,2333\0303,1,63,2,384,1,2333\0301,1,98,4,272,1,2333\0301,100,151,4,272,1,2333\0301,156,176,4,272,1,2333\0304,1,80,3,256,2,2333\031\0312,36,1416,0,\0302,0,0,4,Valik\0302,0,0,4,Syndicate\031\031ITEM,3703,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[536]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I hope this will be enough to convince Redpath that I've--ha!--been carrying out his orders and ridding Southshore of the terrible and horrible menace of the dreaded murlocs! For there could be no greater evil than the ravages of overgrown fish!\030Transferred from the Stormwind city guard to Southshore, a town that should be abandoned by the looks of it... Smell of the harbor day and night.$B$BNot to mention ol' Redpath... Wants me to take care of the murlocs. Ha! $B$BI can barely rouse myself to go out to some of the pockets of the overgrown fish down the Western Strand. If you would go in my place and take care of them, I'd appreciate it.\030Kill 10 Torn Fin Tidehunters and 10 Torn Fin Oracles for Lieutenant Farren Orinelle in Southshore.\030Another ale, please, the last one just seemed to have disappeared!$B$BLight, how much longer am I going to be stuck out here?$B$BOh, it's you, $N. Have you killed those murlocs yet?\030Down the Coast\0312,1,110,2,257,1,2228\0302,112,145,2,257,1,2228\0302,150,178,2,257,1,2228\0302,180,216,2,257,1,2228\0302,226,330,2,257,1,2228\0302,332,400,2,257,4,2228\0303,1,98,2,384,1,2228\0301,1,174,4,274,3,2228\0301,176,245,4,272,4,2228\0304,1,66,3,256,1,2228\0304,71,125,3,256,2,2228\0304,130,146,3,256,1,2228\0304,148,181,3,256,2,2228\03168,2,1,Stormwind City Guard\0302996,2,7,Torn\0302228,2,7,Lieutenant Farren Orinelle\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,1,Stormwind\0302,0,0,1,Southshore\0302,0,0,7,Southshore\031559,23,559,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,2377,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Torn Fin Tidehunter\030NPC,2376,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Torn Fin Oracle",[5361]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I know not what connection you have with my brother but it would seem he has trust with you, $C.$B$BI am Nataka Longhorn and would like to welcome you to Ghost Walker Post, we have many needs of a $C! Talk with others, perhaps there is need of you here.\030My brother Nataka is stationed at Ghost Walker Post over in Desolace. I'd like to ask you... could you give this report to him for me? A year has passed since the last time I wrote, there has been unusual centaur activity since then and he should be informed.$B$BJourney to Stonetalon Mountain north of the Crossroads, and then head west into Charred Vale. From there, head south into Desolace; there you will find a road going south to Ghost Walker Post.\030Deliver Cliffwatcher Longhorn Report to Nataka Longhorn at Ghost Walker Post in Desolace.\030What news have you, $C! Ah - a message from my brother you say? Well then, hand over the report!\030Family Tree\0312,1,69,2,257,1,10537\0302,71,92,2,259,1,10537\0302,94,134,2,257,4,10537\0302,136,259,2,257,1,10537\0302,264,356,2,257,1,10537\0302,358,455,2,257,3,10537\0303,1,89,2,384,1,10537\0301,1,96,4,272,4,11259\0301,101,200,4,274,4,11259\0301,202,253,4,274,4,11259\0304,1,23,3,256,1,11259\0304,25,63,3,256,2,11259\0304,65,96,3,256,1,11259\03193,2,4,Centaur\03010537,2,7,Cliffwatcher Longhorn\03011259,2,7,Nataka Longhorn\03011259,4,9,Nataka Longhorn\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,1,Ghost Walker Post\0302,0,0,1,Desolace\0302,0,0,5,Stonetalon Mountain\0302,0,0,5,Crossroads\0302,0,0,6,Ghost Walker Post\0302,0,0,7,Nataka Longhorn\0302,0,0,7,Ghost Walker Post\0302,0,0,7,Desolace\0304,0,0,9,Ghost Walker Post\031\031",[537]="PARTIAL\031loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $N. The Argus Wake does not sound like a group we want running the Syndicate.$B$BAnd although you may have destroyed their leader here, Nagaz was merely the servant of another. The Argus Wake might run deep through the continent of Azeroth.$B$BOr even the world.\030The letter you brought me was written by a being who calls himself Nagaz, a member of the Argus Wake.  I don't know what this Argus Wake is, but if they're in alliance with the Syndicate then they must be a threat.$B$BI want you to find Nagaz and the Argus Shadow Mages mentioned in that letter.  I want you to find them, and kill them.$B$BSearch in the Uplands, where the Syndicate is strongest.  It is north of Strahnbrad.$B$BWith luck, you'll find these envoys of the Argus Wake there.\030Kill 4 Argus Shadow Mages.$B$BBring the Head of Nagaz to Magistrate Maleb in Southshore.\030Did you find the envoys of The Argus Wake?\030Dark Council\0312,1,101,2,257,1,2276\0302,104,214,2,261,4,2276\0302,219,295,2,259,1,2276\0302,298,336,2,259,1,2276\0302,341,396,2,257,1,2276\0302,399,424,2,257,1,2276\0302,429,488,2,257,1,2276\0303,1,26,2,384,1,2276\0303,31,88,2,384,1,2276\0301,1,14,4,272,1,2276\0301,16,88,4,274,1,2276\0301,93,187,4,308,1,2276\0301,189,251,4,272,4,2276\0301,256,273,4,272,1,2276\0304,1,42,3,256,2,2276\0312320,2,1,Nagaz\0302320,2,3,Nagaz\0304244,2,3,Shadow\0304244,2,8,Shadow\0302320,2,9,Nagaz\0302320,4,12,Nagaz\0312,36,1416,0,\0302,0,0,5,Uplands\0302,0,0,6,Strahnbrad\0302,0,0,9,Magistrate Maleb\0302,0,0,9,Southshore\031525,19,525,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,2318,OBJECTIVE,4,13,Argus Shadow Mage\030ITEM,3672,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[538]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah yes, I remember Milton. A bookworm, no doubt. Bless him.$B$BAnd he's right. The Ruins of Alterac still hold stores of knowledge in danger of being lost!$B$BOgres now dwell in Alterac, and they don't care much for higher learning.\030$N.  If you don't mind a long journey then I have a task for you, to again help Stormwind fill its library.$B$BThe old kingdom of Alterac fell after the great war, and it had a large collection of books.  It's a tragedy that the city is ruined, but even more tragic is all of their knowledge lost!  We must recover what we can.$B$BSouthshore is the closest town to the Ruins of Alterac.  Go there and speak with Loremaster Dibbs.  He can direct you to the ruins, and to what books may be found there.\030Speak with Loremaster Dibbs in Southshore.\030\030Southshore\0312,6,107,2,257,4,1440\0302,112,203,2,261,1,1440\0302,206,297,2,261,1,1440\0302,300,327,2,257,1,1440\0302,332,386,2,321,1,1440\0302,389,429,2,257,1,1440\0302,432,500,2,321,1,1440\0303,1,42,2,384,1,1440\0301,1,26,4,272,1,2277\0301,28,48,4,272,1,2277\0301,50,59,4,272,1,2277\0301,6