ished, justice must be meted out.$B$BFind him and exact upon him the agony he has inflicted upon countless innocents. Once he is destroyed, burn our remains. Turn them to ashes, $N.\030Find Doctor Theolen Krastinov inside the Scholomance. Destroy him, then burn the Remains of Eva Sarkhoff and the Remains of Lucien Sarkhoff. Return to Eva Sarkhoff when the task is complete.$B\030\030\030Remains of Eva Sarkhoff Burned\030Remains of Lucien Sarkhoff Burned\030The Butcher must be stopped!\030Doctor Theolen Krastinov, the Butcher\0312,1,53,2,257,1,11216\0302,55,101,2,257,1,11216\0302,106,185,2,257,1,11216\0302,187,225,2,261,1,11216\0302,227,249,2,257,1,11216\0303,1,53,2,384,1,11216\0303,55,140,2,388,1,11216\0303,142,190,2,384,1,11216\0301,1,33,4,272,1,11216\0301,35,124,4,272,1,11216\0308,1,28,3,256,1,11216\0306,1,30,3,384,1,11216\0307,1,33,3,384,1,11216\03111261,2,6,Doctor Theolen Krastinov\03011216,2,7,Eva Sarkhoff\03011217,2,7,Lucien Sarkhoff\03011216,2,8,Eva Sarkhoff\03011216,3,12,Eva Sarkhoff\03011217,3,13,Lucien Sarkhoff\0312,2057,0,0,\0302,0,0,8,Eva Sarkhoff\0315515,23,5515,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,11261,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Doctor Theolen Krastinov\030OBJECT,176544,OBJECTIVE,1,14,Remains of Eva Sarkhoff\030OBJECT,176545,OBJECTIVE,1,14,Remains of Lucien Sarkhoff",[5384]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031With the death of Kirtonos, a chapter in the horrible tale of Scholomance comes to a close. There is, however, more to be done. Others here are now aware of your brave acts. Take this, $N. It is a piece of our own essence. It will allow you to communicate with the other lost souls of Caer Darrow.\030This is it, $N.$B$B<Eva points to the vial inside the bag.>$B$BThe blood of innocents. The purest blood, used to appease Krastinov's master.$B$BIt is with this blood that Kirtonos may be summoned. It is with this blood, then, that Kirtonos must be destroyed.$B$BTake the blood to the porch. Place it upon the brazier. Kirtonos will come - he cannot resist. When he appears, unleash the fury and wrath of a thousand innocent deaths upon him.$B$BShould you succeed, you will earn more than just our gratitude.\030Return to the Scholomance with the Blood of Innocents. Find the porch and place the Blood of Innocents in the brazier. Kirtonos will come to feast upon your soul.$B$BFight valiantly, do not give an inch! Destroy Kirtonos and return to Eva Sarkhoff.$B\030Be wary, Kirtonos is a seasoned fighter.\030Kirtonos the Herald\0312,1,15,2,257,1,11216\0302,20,59,2,257,1,11216\0302,64,86,2,257,1,11216\0302,88,140,2,257,1,11216\0302,145,196,2,257,1,11216\0302,198,258,2,261,1,11216\0302,263,290,2,257,1,11216\0302,292,317,2,257,1,11216\0302,319,356,2,257,3,11216\0302,358,440,2,257,1,11216\0302,445,507,2,257,3,11216\0303,1,54,2,384,1,11216\0303,56,118,2,384,1,11216\0303,120,162,2,384,3,11216\0303,167,203,2,388,1,11216\0303,205,248,2,388,1,11216\0301,1,91,4,272,1,11216\0301,93,127,4,272,1,11216\0301,129,173,4,272,1,11216\0301,175,188,4,272,1,11216\0301,190,222,4,272,1,11216\0301,224,297,4,276,3,11216\0304,1,40,3,256,1,11216\03111216,2,16,Eva Sarkhoff\0312,2057,0,0,\0302,0,0,12,Scholomance\0302,0,0,16,Eva Sarkhoff\0315515,19,5515,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305461,23,5461,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,10506,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Kirtonos the Herald",[5385]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You've done it! Praise be to Elune and whichever powers you worshihp, $N. You have done an honorable and noble thing this day. I am certain Arko'narin will be pleased that you not only took the time to save her, but to also slay the creature who tortured one of her best friends.$B$BI wish I could do more for you, but please, take this.\030You pick up the sack carefully and prepare to make your way back to Jessir Moonbow on the border of Felwood and Ashenvale. Hopefully the paladin will be given the proper respects once you've passed his remains on to his friends.\030Return the Remains of Trey Lightforge to Jessir Moonbow in Felwood.\030How did things go in Jaedenar, $N?\030The Remains of Trey Lightforge\0312,1,122,2,257,1,11020\0302,124,228,2,257,3,11020\0303,1,67,2,384,1,11020\0301,1,15,4,272,1,11019\0301,17,73,4,272,1,11019\0301,75,126,4,272,1,11019\0301,128,279,4,282,3,11019\0301,284,337,4,274,4,11019\0304,1,34,3,256,2,11019\03111019,2,1,Jessir Moonbow\03011020,2,3,Remains of Trey Lightforge\03011019,2,3,Jessir Moonbow\03011018,4,7,Arko'narin\0312,361,1448,0,\0302,0,0,1,Jessir Moonbow\0302,0,0,3,Jessir Moonbow\0302,0,0,3,Felwood\0304,0,0,5,Elune\0303,0,0,9,Jaedenar\0315204,19,5204,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5386]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You are a savior, $N! These Bloodbelly fish look almost good enough to eat raw.$B$B<Nataka starts salivating.>$B$BHere you go - choose one of these items as a payment for these fish.\030The smell of cooked fish has long been missing here at Ghost Walker Post. The trolls at Shadowprey Village are the best at catching fish... but alas, with all the centaur activities I have little time to make a journey to the trolls. Hrm...$B$BDo me a favor and journey to Shadowprey Village. Talk to the local fisherman Jinar'Zillen and bring me back my favorite, Bloodbelly fish. The road south of here will take you west to the troll village.\030Talk to Jinar'Zillen at Shadowprey Village, and then bring Nataka Longhorn 2 Bloodbelly fish.\030My hoof tingles and my mouth starts to water when I think of fried Bloodbelly fish... You have any on you?\030Catch of the Day\0312,1,73,2,261,1,11259\0302,75,139,2,257,1,11259\0302,141,233,2,257,1,11259\0302,235,240,2,257,1,11259\0302,245,292,2,257,1,11259\0302,294,381,2,257,1,11259\0302,383,445,2,257,3,11259\0303,1,93,2,384,1,11259\0301,1,21,4,272,1,11259\0301,23,79,4,272,1,11259\0301,84,110,4,272,1,11259\0301,115,182,4,272,1,11259\0304,1,85,3,256,1,11259\0304,87,106,3,256,2,11259\03193,2,3,Centaur\03011317,2,6,Jinar'Zillen\03011317,2,8,Jinar'Zillen\03011259,2,8,Nataka Longhorn\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,1,Ghost Walker Post\0302,0,0,2,Shadowprey Village\0302,0,0,5,Shadowprey Village\0302,0,0,8,Jinar'Zillen\0302,0,0,8,Shadowprey Village\031\031ITEM,13546,OBJECTIVE,2,15,",[539]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The Dark Lady will be pleased when she learns that she has a new mine from which she can arm her soldiers.\030The Hillsbrad Town Registry indicates that the Azureload Mine is under Alliance control.  Furthermore, the mine is a prime source of iron ore for the Alliance armories.$B$BEven though we've struck a decisive blow to the town of Hillsbrad, the Alliance still supports and protects the Azureload Mine fervently.$B$BThe mine lies due south of Hillsbrad.  Go there and slay the foreman, a human by the name of Bonds.  Kill his miners as well.  That should send a clear message to the Alliance.\030Kill Foreman Bonds and 10 Hillsbrad Miners and report back to Darthalia in Tarren Mill.\030You were given direct orders to attack the Azureload Mine. Your reasons for loafing about Tarren Mill better be good or I will behead you for treason.\030Battle of Hillsbrad\0312,1,88,2,257,1,2215\0302,91,168,2,257,1,2215\0302,173,309,2,257,1,2215\0302,314,350,2,257,1,2215\0302,353,412,2,257,1,2215\0302,415,438,2,257,1,2215\0302,441,489,2,257,1,2215\0303,1,87,2,384,1,2215\0301,1,106,4,272,3,2215\0304,1,58,3,260,1,2215\0304,60,150,3,256,3,2215\0312305,2,8,Foreman Bonds\03015065,4,9,Lady\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,4,Hillsbrad\0302,0,0,7,Alliance\0302,0,0,8,Darthalia\0302,0,0,8,Tarren Mill\031532,19,532,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030541,23,541,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,2305,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Foreman Bonds\030NPC,2269,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Hillsbrad Miner",[54]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well, it says here that you've been awarded Acting Deputy Status with the Stormwind Marshals. Congratulations.$B$BAnd good luck - keeping Elwynn safe is no picnic... what with most the army busy doing who knows what for who knows which noble!$B$BIt's hard to keep track of politics in these dark days...\030$N, you are a $c with proven interest in the security of Northshire.  You are now tasked with the protection of the surrounding Elwynn Forest.$B$BIf you accept this duty, then I have prepared papers that must be delivered to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire.  Goldshire lies along the southern road, past the border gates.\030Take Marshal McBride's Documents to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire.\030You have word from McBride? Northshire is a garden compared to Elwynn Forest, but I wonder what Marshal McBride has to report.$B$BHere, let me have his papers...\030Report to Goldshire\0312,1,68,2,265,1,197\0302,71,142,2,257,1,197\0302,147,253,2,257,4,197\0302,256,317,2,257,1,197\0303,1,64,2,384,1,197\0301,1,93,4,272,1,240\0301,95,110,4,272,1,240\0301,115,165,4,272,1,240\0301,167,242,4,272,1,240\0301,247,303,4,272,1,240\0304,1,27,3,256,2,240\0304,29,126,3,256,1,240\0304,131,161,3,256,1,240\031240,2,3,Marshal Dughan\030197,2,5,Marshal McBride\030240,2,5,Marshal Dughan\030197,3,12,Marshal McBride\0312,9,1429,0,\0302,0,0,3,Marshal Dughan\0302,0,0,3,Goldshire\0302,0,0,5,Marshal Dughan\0302,0,0,5,Goldshire\0303,0,0,11,McBride\0303,0,0,12,Elwynn Forest\03121,19,21,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[540]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh, you got them! Splendid! I must begin studying the Arm of Gri'lek immediately!\030Those beastly ogres now reside within Alterac's ruins, and I shudder to think what they're doing with the precious books still there.  You must recover what you can!$B$BEnter the Ruins of Alterac and search for tomes looted by the ogres.  Get whatever you can find and bring them to me, but also seek out one book in particular: The Arm of Gri'lek.  It contains ancient troll lore that I must learn, and the Ruins of Alterac was the last known location of an intact copy of this book.\030Bring 5 Recovered Tomes and the Worn Leather Book containing The Arm of Gri'lek to Loremaster Dibbs in Southshore.\030I wish I could search the ruins too, but I fear these bones wouldn't hold me during my climb up the mountains. However, how does your hunt for knowledge progress, $N?\030Preserving Knowledge\0312,1,133,2,321,1,2277\0302,136,165,2,257,1,2277\0302,170,237,2,321,1,2277\0302,240,348,2,259,1,2277\0302,351,484,2,321,1,2277\0303,1,114,2,384,1,2277\0301,1,17,4,272,1,2277\0301,19,27,4,272,1,2277\0301,29,81,4,272,1,2277\0304,1,110,3,322,4,2277\0304,112,166,3,256,2,2277\03114528,2,1,Precious\0300,2,4,Gri'lek\0300,2,6,Gri'lek\0302277,2,6,Loremaster Dibbs\0300,4,9,Gri'lek\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,1,Alterac's\0302,0,0,6,Loremaster Dibbs\0302,0,0,6,Southshore\031538,19,538,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030542,23,542,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3658,OBJECTIVE,5,15,\030ITEM,3659,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5401]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031All who fight evil on behalf of the Argent Dawn must don our commission.  Wearing such will earn your right to claim rewards our quartermasters have to offer.$B$BWhile under commission, you'll be able to acquire Scourgestones from slain Scourge; these are marks of insignia that they sometimes possess.  Procure these insignia and bring them to me.  For each set you turn in, you will receive our marker of heroism - the Argent Dawn Valor Token.$B$BAchieve your destiny, $c - join the fight today!\030\030\030\030Argent Dawn Commission\0311,1,72,4,276,1,10840\0301,75,158,4,272,3,10840\0301,163,302,4,340,1,10840\0301,305,348,4,272,1,10840\0301,351,445,4,272,3,10840\0301,450,497,4,276,1,10840\031\0312,28,1422,0,\0315405,22,5405,UNKNOWN\0305503,22,5503,UNKNOWN\031",[5402]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Congratulations, $N - I am pleased to award you with an Argent Dawn valor token!$B$BThe tokens serve two purposes. One - they can be used to further your standing within the Argent Dawn; to do so may avail you options and rewards that are reserved for our honored and revered allies. Two - they can be given to our quartermasters, along with coin, as payment for some of the Dawn's more prized items.$B$BWhatever you decide, know that you are earning your commission. Well done!\030\030\030A Minion's Scourgestone is the insignia of the Scourge rank and file.  These are sometimes found on the weaker of their troops positioned in the Plaguelands, though the term \"weaker\" is certainly to be considered in context.  The Scourge, no matter where they are, should never be underestimated.$B$BThe Argent Dawn currently offers a valor token in exchange for twenty of these insignia - an exchange I'm happy to do, provided you have earned enough scourgestones!\030Minion's Scourgestones\0311,1,80,4,272,1,10840\0301,85,114,4,272,1,10840\0301,116,283,4,272,1,10840\0301,285,400,4,272,1,10840\0301,405,467,4,272,1,10840\0301,469,478,4,272,1,10840\0304,1,69,3,320,1,10840\0304,72,224,3,256,1,10840\0304,227,296,3,320,1,10840\0304,301,465,3,256,1,10840\031\0312,28,1422,0,\0304,0,0,3,Argent Dawn\0303,0,0,8,Plaguelands\031\031ITEM,12840,OBJECTIVE,20,15,",[5403]="PARTIAL\031consequences,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Congratulations, $N - I am pleased to award you with an Argent Dawn valor token!$B$BEach valor token handed out to worthy recipients is a sign of the tide turning against the Scourge. With more and more heroes fighting the Scourge in their own lands, the Argent Dawn will assuredly be at the forefront when the time comes to wage war on the ultimate evil of the Scourge. I hope that the valor you've shown what it took to acquiring your token will carry the day then as well!\030\030\030An Invader's Scourgestone is the insignia of the Scourge's elite troops.  These are sometimes found on the stronger of the troops positioned in the Plaguelands.  Slaying such a creature is indeed a challenge, but one that should be relished with a commission to vanquish evil.$B$BThe Argent Dawn currently offers a valor token in exchange for ten of these insignia.  Bring them to me here, and I will make sure you receive your just reward.\030Invader's Scourgestones\0311,1,80,4,272,1,10840\0301,85,183,4,336,1,10840\0301,185,370,4,340,3,10840\0301,372,475,4,274,3,10840\0304,1,72,3,320,1,10840\0304,75,160,3,256,1,10840\0304,163,276,3,256,1,10840\0304,281,365,3,256,1,10840\0304,368,440,3,256,3,10840\031\0312,28,1422,0,\0303,0,0,6,Plaguelands\031\031ITEM,12841,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[5404]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Congratulations, $N - I am pleased to award you with an Argent Dawn valor token!$B$BTo acquire a valor token in such a manner indicates that you are a true hero in the cause of good. We value all effort brought to bear against the Scourge, but to take down one of their leaders is to truly deliver onto them a crushing defeat!$B$BFor the Dawn, my $Gbrother:sister;!\030\030\030A Corruptor's Scourgestone is the insignia of the Scourge's overlords.  A powerful being that holds a position of authority over the Scourge will always possess one.  To slay such a malevolent creature would surely advance the cause of the Argent Dawn, and all good causes!$B$BOn behalf of the Argent Dawn, I will give you a valor token in exchange for just a single one these insignia.  Use caution in acquiring one, $N - such powerful beings are not to be trifled with.\030Corruptor's Scourgestones\0311,1,80,4,272,1,10840\0301,85,182,4,272,1,10840\0301,184,326,4,336,1,10840\0301,331,365,4,272,1,10840\0304,1,70,3,320,1,10840\0304,73,165,3,320,3,10840\0304,168,273,3,256,4,10840\0304,278,386,3,256,3,10840\0304,389,471,3,256,1,10840\031\0312,28,1422,0,\031\031ITEM,12843,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5405]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031All who fight evil on behalf of the Argent Dawn must don our commission. Wearing such will earn your right to claim rewards our quartermasters have to offer.$B$BWhile under commission, you'll be able to acquire Scourgestones from slain Scourge; these are marks of insignia that they sometimes possess. Procure these insignia and bring them to me. For each set you turn in, you will receive our marker of heroism - the Argent Dawn Valor Token.$B$BAchieve your destiny, $C join the fight today!\030\030\030\030Argent Dawn Commission\0311,1,72,4,276,1,10839\0301,74,157,4,272,3,10839\0301,162,301,4,340,1,10839\0301,303,346,4,272,1,10839\0301,348,442,4,272,3,10839\0301,447,492,4,276,1,10839\031\0312,28,1422,0,\0315401,22,5401,UNKNOWN\0305503,22,5503,UNKNOWN\031",[5406]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Congratulations, $N - I am pleased to award you with an Argent Dawn valor token!$B$BTo acquire a valor token in such a manner indicates that you are a true hero in the cause of good. We value all effort brought to bear against the Scourge, but to take down one of their leaders is to truly deliver onto them a crushing defeat!$B$BFor the Dawn, my $Gbrother:sister;!\030\030\030A Corruptor's Scourgestone is the insignia of the Scourge's overlords.  A powerful being that holds a position of authority over the Scourge will always possess one.  To slay such a malevolent creature would surely advance the cause of the Argent Dawn, and all good causes!$B$BOn behalf of the Argent Dawn, I will give you a valor token in exchange for just a single one these insignia.  Use caution in acquiring one, $N - such powerful beings are not to be trifled with.\030Corruptor's Scourgestones\0311,1,80,4,272,1,10839\0301,85,182,4,272,1,10839\0301,184,326,4,336,1,10839\0301,331,365,4,272,1,10839\0304,1,70,3,320,1,10839\0304,73,165,3,320,3,10839\0304,168,273,3,256,4,10839\0304,278,386,3,256,3,10839\0304,389,471,3,256,1,10839\031\0312,28,1422,0,\031\031ITEM,12843,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5407]="PARTIAL\031consequences,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Congratulations, $N - I am pleased to award you with an Argent Dawn valor token!$B$BEach valor token handed out to worthy recipients is a sign of the tide turning against the Scourge. With more and more heroes fighting the Scourge in their own lands, the Argent Dawn will assuredly be at the forefront when the time comes to wage war on the ultimate evil of the Scourge. I hope that the valor you've shown what it took to acquiring your token will carry the day then as well!\030\030\030An Invader's Scourgestone is the insignia of the Scourge's elite troops.  These are sometimes found on the stronger of the troops positioned in the Plaguelands.  Slaying such a creature is indeed a challenge, but one that should be relished with a commission to vanquish evil.$B$BThe Argent Dawn currently offers a valor token in exchange for ten of these insignia.  Bring them to me here, and I will make sure you receive your just reward.\030Invader's Scourgestones\0311,1,80,4,272,1,10839\0301,85,183,4,336,1,10839\0301,185,370,4,340,3,10839\0301,372,475,4,274,3,10839\0304,1,72,3,320,1,10839\0304,75,160,3,256,1,10839\0304,163,276,3,256,1,10839\0304,281,365,3,256,1,10839\0304,368,440,3,256,3,10839\031\0312,28,1422,0,\0303,0,0,6,Plaguelands\031\031ITEM,12841,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[5408]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Congratulations, $N - I am pleased to award you with an Argent Dawn valor token!$B$BThe tokens serve two purposes. One - they can be used to further your standing within the Argent Dawn; to do so may avail you options and rewards that are reserved for our honored and revered allies. Two - they can be given to our quartermasters, along with coin, as payment for some of the Dawn's more prized items.$B$BWhatever you decide, know that you are earning your commission. Well done!\030\030\030A Minion's Scourgestone is the insignia of the Scourge rank and file.  These are sometimes found on the weaker of their troops positioned in the Plaguelands, though the term \"weaker\" is certainly to be considered in context.  The Scourge, no matter where they are, should never be underestimated.$B$BThe Argent Dawn currently offers a valor token in exchange for twenty of these insignia - an exchange I'm happy to do, provided you have earned enough scourgestones!\030Minion's Scourgestones\0311,1,80,4,272,1,10839\0301,85,114,4,272,1,10839\0301,116,283,4,272,1,10839\0301,285,400,4,272,1,10839\0301,405,467,4,272,1,10839\0301,469,478,4,272,1,10839\0304,1,69,3,320,1,10839\0304,72,224,3,256,1,10839\0304,227,296,3,320,1,10839\0304,301,465,3,256,1,10839\031\0312,28,1422,0,\0304,0,0,3,Argent Dawn\0303,0,0,8,Plaguelands\031\031ITEM,12840,OBJECTIVE,20,15,",[541]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Your actions on the battlefield are worthy of the highest praise.\030Dwarves aiding the humans?  Damn those filthy little beasts.$B$BWe shall test the strength of the so-called Alliance.  We'll see how anxious those little ankle-bashers are to help the humans once they feel our wrath.  We know exactly where their stronghold is in this territory.$B$BThey have established a barracks in southeastern Hillsbrad along Thoradin's Wall called Dun Garok.  The final mission of this battle is to lay siege on Dun Garok, $c.  Captain Ironhill, their leader, must die.\030Travel to Dun Garok and kill 8 Mountaineers, 4 Riflemen, 2 Priests and Captain Ironhill and report back to Darthalia in Tarren Mill.\030Dun Garok proves to be too much of an obstacle for you, $C? And here I thought you had established yourself valiantly in Hillsbrad.$B$BIf you're not up to handle the mission assigned to you, I will find another who can produce better results. As for you, well, I am sure the Dark Lady could always use more grave diggers back in Tirisfal Glades.\030Battle of Hillsbrad\0312,1,26,2,257,2,2215\0302,29,60,2,257,1,2215\0302,65,117,2,257,3,2215\0302,120,216,2,257,1,2215\0302,219,278,2,257,1,2215\0302,283,380,2,257,1,2215\0302,383,448,2,261,1,2215\0302,451,491,2,257,1,2215\0303,1,132,2,384,1,2215\0301,1,65,4,272,1,2215\0304,1,59,3,256,2,2215\0304,61,131,3,256,1,2215\0304,136,242,3,256,4,2215\0304,244,345,3,256,4,2215\0312304,2,8,Captain Ironhill\0302304,2,9,Captain Ironhill\03015065,3,14,Lady\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,9,Dun Garok\0302,0,0,9,Darthalia\0302,0,0,9,Tarren Mill\0303,0,0,12,Hillsbrad\0303,0,0,14,Tirisfal Glades\031539,19,539,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030550,23,550,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,2344,OBJECTIVE,8,13,Dun Garok Mountaineer\030NPC,2345,OBJECTIVE,4,13,Dun Garok Rifleman\030NPC,2346,OBJECTIVE,2,13,Dun Garok Priest\030NPC,2304,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Captain Ironhill",[542]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031My oh my! Look at these! I can't believe they survived the ruination of Alterac. And all those ogres too!$B$BThank you, $N. Thank you so much! You have helped preserve human knowledge, and you add to the grandeur of the Royal Library of Stormwind.\030I need to spend some time studying the Arm of Gri'lek book you brought me, though I'm sure Milton is eager to get the other recovered books into Stormwind's collection.$B$BHere are the books you gathered from the Ruins of Alterac, packed and catalogued.  Take them back to Milton Sheaf in Stormwind and I'm sure he'll be grateful.\030Bring the Tomes of Alterac to Milton Sheaf in Stormwind.\030$N, you've returned! How did your foray into Alterac go? Did you bring anything back with you?\030Return to Milton\0312,1,168,2,259,1,2277\0302,173,253,2,321,1,2277\0302,256,330,2,257,1,2277\0303,1,56,2,384,1,2277\0301,11,24,4,272,1,1440\0301,26,80,4,272,4,1440\0301,82,105,4,272,1,1440\0301,110,123,4,272,1,1440\0301,125,142,4,272,1,1440\0301,144,247,4,272,1,1440\0304,1,20,3,256,1,1440\0304,22,56,3,256,2,1440\0304,58,94,3,256,2,1440\0310,2,1,Gri'lek\0301440,2,3,Milton Sheaf\0301440,2,4,Milton Sheaf\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,2,Ruins of Alterac\0302,0,0,3,Milton Sheaf\0302,0,0,3,Stormwind\0302,0,0,4,Milton Sheaf\0302,0,0,4,Stormwind\031540,19,540,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5421]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Sweet mon, nothing beats work being done, especially if it's someone else doing the work... eh?\030\030\030I'll reward anyone who makes my life a bit easier... I enjoy doing as little as possible, mon!$B$BBelow the docks here in Shadowprey Village, I've many shellfish traps.  If you're kind enough to do my work and collect me my shellfish, then I'll reward you with something you want... get my drift mon?  For every five shellfish you bring me I will give you a fine Bloodbelly fish!\030Fish in a Bucket\0311,1,91,4,272,4,11317\0304,1,52,3,256,1,11317\0304,54,94,3,256,1,11317\0304,99,168,3,256,1,11317\0304,171,282,3,258,4,11317\0304,284,300,3,256,2,11317\0304,303,379,3,256,3,11317\031\0312,405,1443,0,\0303,0,0,4,Shadowprey Village\0315386,20,5386,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,13545,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[543]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, this is splendid. This will have to be cleaned of course, but you really outdid yourself, $N. I will have someone prepare the tiara and place it within our collection posthaste.\030The Perenolde Tiara is an old heirloom of the Perenolde \"nobles\" - the ruling family of Alterac before that kingdom fell to ruin.  It is said to have been crafted by master jewelers in Ironforge, and fitted with the finest of emeralds.$B$BWhen Alterac was destroyed the Tiara was lost, but there are rumors that an Ogre Mage, Grel'borg the Miser, found the tiara and now wanders the Ruins of Alterac searching for more treasures.$B$BWe would have you acquire the tiara for us.\030Bring the Perenolde Tiara to Remington Ridgewell in Stormwind.\030Salutations, $N. Do try to avoid stepping on my pant cuffs. This outfit is newly tailored.\030The Perenolde Tiara\0312,1,129,2,257,1,2285\0302,132,235,2,257,1,2285\0302,240,429,2,325,1,2285\0302,434,476,2,257,4,2285\0303,1,62,2,384,1,2285\0301,1,21,4,272,1,2285\0301,23,97,4,272,3,2285\0301,99,181,4,272,3,2285\0304,1,16,3,256,1,2285\0304,18,59,3,256,1,2285\0304,61,90,3,256,1,2285\031211,2,3,Ogre\0302417,2,3,Grel'borg the Miser\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,2,Ironforge\0302,0,0,5,Remington Ridgewell\0302,0,0,5,Stormwind\031\031ITEM,3684,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[544]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have done a great service for the Forsaken, $N. These artifacts have been sorely missed.$B$BAnd it is good to hear that Kegan and the other betrayers have found justice.\030I came to Tarren Mill to research, but now must resolve a crisis.  You see, four Forsaken fled the Undercity a few months ago.  They turned their backs on their brethren, but what's worse...they stole from the Dark Lady.$B$BThese thieves broke into a secure vault and stole four artifacts, items our apothecaries required in certain studies.  Sylvanas would have these artifacts returned.$B$BThe thieves fled the Undercity to Dalaran, and those wizards quarantined them in the Lordamere Internment Camp.\030Find the traitors and recover their artifacts, then return to Magus Voidglare in Tarren Mill.\030Did you find the thieves?  And more importantly, did you find what they stole?\030Prison Break In\0312,1,65,2,257,1,2410\0302,68,126,2,257,1,2410\0302,129,220,2,257,1,2410\0302,225,341,2,257,1,2410\0302,344,388,2,257,4,2410\0302,393,503,2,257,1,2410\0303,1,93,2,384,1,2410\0301,1,51,4,272,1,2410\0301,53,92,4,272,1,2410\0301,97,173,4,272,1,2410\0304,1,25,3,256,2,2410\0304,28,78,3,256,2,2410\03115065,2,3,Lady\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,1,Tarren Mill\0302,0,0,3,Dark Lady\0302,0,0,6,Dalaran\0302,0,0,6,Lordamere Internment Camp\0302,0,0,7,Magus Voidglare\0302,0,0,7,Tarren Mill\031545,23,545,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3691,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,3689,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,3690,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,3688,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5441]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030requestItems\030title\031Good, good. Maybe they'll think twice before slacking next time! Thanks for the help!\030Cursed peons!  They work hard gathering lumber from the trees of the valley, but they're always taking naps!  I need someone to help keep the peons in line.$B$BYou look like the right $r for my task.  Here, you take this blackjack and use it on any lazy peons you find sleeping on the job.  A good smack will get them right back to work!  Return the blackjack when you're done.$B$BLousy slacking peons...\030Use the Foreman's Blackjack on Lazy Peons when they're sleeping.  Wake up 5 peons, then return the Foreman's Blackjack to Foreman Thazz'ril in the Valley of Trials.\030\030Peons Awoken\030No good lazy...$B$B Eh? Do you have my blackjack? Did you catch any peons sleeping on the job?!\030Lazy Peons\0312,1,13,2,261,1,11378\0302,16,108,2,257,1,11378\0302,111,156,2,259,1,11378\0302,161,199,2,257,1,11378\0302,202,289,2,257,1,11378\0302,292,337,2,257,3,11378\0302,340,377,2,257,1,11378\0302,382,404,2,257,1,11378\0303,1,64,2,384,1,11378\0303,67,164,2,384,1,11378\0301,1,11,4,272,1,11378\0301,13,64,4,272,4,11378\0301,66,85,4,272,1,11378\0306,1,15,3,256,1,11378\0306,25,49,3,256,2,11378\0306,51,95,3,256,2,11378\0305,1,12,3,384,1,11378\03111378,2,10,Foreman Thazz'ril\0312,363,1411,0,\0302,0,0,10,Foreman Thazz'ril\0302,0,0,10,Valley of Trials\0316394,23,6394,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,10556,OBJECTIVE,5,13,Lazy Peon",[545]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very good. Those ruins should now be safe enough to search, if one is careful.$B$BThank you, $N.\030The wizards of Dalaran constructed a vast, magical dome around the heart of their city.  Some believe it was for protection from the violence of these times, while others say they merely wanted solitude, to study and plot.$B$BI don't care what the reason was.  I do care that the ruined outskirts of their city, outside the dome, may hide valuable magical treasures.$B$BBut the area is patrolled by the wizards and their elemental slaves.$B$BSo hunt them, and return when their numbers are sufficiently reduced.\030Kill 6 Dalaran Summoners and 12 Elemental Slaves, then return to Magus Voidglare in Tarren Mill.\030Have you yet thinned the Dalaran patrols around their ruins?\030Dalaran Patrols\0312,1,87,2,257,1,2410\0302,90,222,2,257,4,2410\0302,227,259,2,257,1,2410\0302,262,366,2,257,1,2410\0302,371,438,2,257,1,2410\0302,443,511,2,257,1,2410\0303,1,96,2,384,1,2410\0301,1,10,4,272,1,2410\0301,12,78,4,336,4,2410\0301,83,96,4,272,1,2410\0304,1,60,3,320,2,2410\031\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,7,Magus Voidglare\0302,0,0,7,Tarren Mill\031544,19,544,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,2358,OBJECTIVE,6,13,Dalaran Summoner\030NPC,2359,OBJECTIVE,12,13,Elemental Slave",[546]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Precious skulls! So beautiful! I owe you as promised, $N!\030I hear you were enlisted by Darthalia to wage war on the humans of Hillsbrad.  So jealous I am. . .$B$BWhile you're off having all the fun -- slaying humans, pillaging the town, terrorizing innocent people -- I am stuck standing guard here in Tarren Mill.$B$BPerhaps you'll take pity on an old Deathguard like myself?  You see I am collecting human skulls.  And you will be fighting humans for quite some time.  Over the course of your long battle, bring me 30 skulls and I will make it worth your while.\030Deathguard Samsa of Tarren Mill wants 30 Hillsbrad Human Skulls.\030So the lucky $N returns? How many humans have you slaughtered today? Hundreds I do hope!$B$BHave you any skulls for me?\030Souvenirs of Death\0312,1,77,2,261,1,2418\0302,80,95,2,257,1,2418\0302,104,255,2,257,1,2418\0302,260,317,2,257,4,2418\0302,320,356,2,257,1,2418\0302,359,410,2,261,3,2418\0302,413,504,2,261,3,2418\0303,1,64,2,386,1,2418\0301,1,16,4,272,1,2418\0301,18,30,4,272,1,2418\0301,32,57,4,272,1,2418\0304,1,24,3,256,2,2418\0304,26,68,3,256,2,2418\0304,70,88,3,258,3,2418\0304,93,119,3,256,2,2418\0312418,2,8,Deathguard Samsa\03014528,4,9,Precious\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,3,Tarren Mill\031527,19,527,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3692,OBJECTIVE,30,15,",[5461]="PARTIAL\031consequences\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I had doubted the possibility of such an item existing. This certainly opens up an incredible opportunity - one we must not squander.$B$BPrepare yourself, $N, for what I am about to ask of you will take you into the depths of hell.\030The undead fear life just as the living fear death. It is not unusual for a sentient undead being to completely destroy all remnants of his or her previous life after having turned.$B$BUnfortunately, in order to create an artifact capable of reverting Ras Frostwhisper to a mortal, we must have a keepsake from his years among the living.$B$BYou must venture to the ruined city of Stromgarde, Frostwhisper's home, and search for such an item. May luck be with you, $N.\030Travel to the Arathi Highlands, to the ruins of Stromgarde. Search Stromgarde for a Keepsake of Remembrance. If you find such an item, return with it to Magistrate Marduke.\030A keepsake of remembrance is a rare find, $N.\030The Human, Ras Frostwhisper\0312,1,51,2,257,1,11286\0302,53,181,2,261,1,11286\0302,186,338,2,259,1,11286\0302,343,442,2,257,1,11286\0302,444,468,2,257,1,11286\0303,1,59,2,448,1,11286\0303,61,108,2,384,1,11286\0303,110,172,2,384,4,11286\0301,1,55,4,272,1,11286\0301,57,133,4,280,1,11286\0301,138,231,4,272,3,11286\0304,1,45,3,256,1,11286\03110508,2,3,Ras Frostwhisper\03011286,2,8,Magistrate Marduke\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,6,Arathi Highlands\0302,0,0,8,Magistrate Marduke\0315384,19,5384,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305462,23,5462,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,13585,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5462]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Leonid looks over the keepsake.>$B$BYour quandary stirs up memories that I had hoped would never resurface.\030Upon tainted soil, the keepsake must be attuned.$B$BIt is rumored that Stratholme is where Frostwhisper succumbed to the Lich King. Upon those bloodied grounds he gave his life - freely and with motive - to become one of the undying.$B$BIt is those grounds that must be found.$B$BThere is one, an undead dissenter of the Scourge, freed by the Banshee Queen but loyal to the cause of the Argent Dawn. Find him: Leonid Barthalomew the Revered. He may know more. Seek out Light's Hope, $N.\030Travel to Light's Hope in Eastern Plaguelands and seek out Leonid Barthalomew the Revered. Show him the Keepsake of Remembrance and tell him all that you have discovered.\030Do not ask questions of which you do not want answers.\030The Dying, Ras Frostwhisper\0312,1,48,2,257,1,11286\0302,53,131,2,321,1,11286\0302,133,233,2,257,1,11286\0302,238,276,2,257,1,11286\0302,281,399,2,321,1,11286\0302,401,441,2,257,1,11286\0302,443,459,2,257,1,11286\0302,461,486,2,257,3,11286\0303,1,90,2,386,3,11286\0303,92,170,2,384,1,11286\0301,1,33,4,272,1,11036\0301,38,108,4,272,4,11036\0304,1,54,3,258,1,11036\03116980,2,2,The Lich King\03015193,2,5,The Banshee Queen\03011036,2,6,Leonid Barthalomew the Revered\03011036,2,9,Leonid Barthalomew the Revered\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,2,Lich King\0302,0,0,9,Light's Hope\0302,0,0,9,Eastern Plaguelands\0315461,19,5461,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305463,23,5463,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5463]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You place the keepsake on the tainted soil.\030I watched as the human, Ras Frostwhisper, pledged his undying soul to the Lich King. He drew the dagger to his own throat and with a smile, cut from ear to ear. His body collapsed inside the borders of the pentagram. The Lich King stood over the fallen mage and with a single motion, Ras Frostwhisper the lich, was born.$B$B<Leonid gazes at the ground and then looks up at you.>$B$BYes, $r, I remember. What you seek has a name - Menethil's Gift: The ground blessed by the Lich King - holy ground to Scourge.$B\030Travel to Stratholme and find Menethil's Gift. Place the Keepsake of Remembrance upon the unholy ground.\030The area around Menethil's Gift is exceptionally cold.\030Menethil's Gift\0312,1,84,2,321,1,11036\0302,86,160,2,257,1,11036\0302,162,216,2,257,1,11036\0302,218,320,2,321,1,11036\0302,325,378,2,257,1,11036\0302,383,402,2,257,1,11036\0302,404,508,2,323,1,11036\0303,1,46,2,384,1,11036\0303,48,104,2,384,1,11036\0301,1,43,4,272,1,0\0304,1,54,3,256,1,0\03110508,2,1,Ras Frostwhisper\03016980,2,1,The Lich King\03016980,2,4,The Lich King\03010508,2,4,Ras Frostwhisper\03016980,2,7,The Lich King\0312,2017,0,0,\0302,0,0,1,Lich King\0302,0,0,7,Scourge\0302,0,0,8,Stratholme\0315462,19,5462,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305464,23,5464,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,176631,FINISHER,?,12,Menethil's Gift",[5464]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031As the soul clung to the keepsake, so shall it cling to the physical form of Ras Frostwhisper.\030The soul of the fallen clings to that which represents its former life and transforms the item into a soulbound keepsake. You pick the item up and place it in your pack.\030Take the Soulbound Keepsake to Leonid Barthalomew in Eastern Plaguelands.\030<Leonid shudders.>\030Menethil's Gift\0312,1,121,2,257,1,0\0302,123,169,2,257,1,0\0303,1,73,2,384,1,0\0301,1,94,4,272,3,11036\0304,1,18,3,256,1,11036\03110508,4,4,Ras Frostwhisper\0312,139,1423,0,\0302,0,0,3,Leonid Barthalomew\0302,0,0,3,Eastern Plaguelands\0315463,19,5463,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305465,23,5465,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,176631,GIVER,?,9,Menethil's Gift",[5465]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I was certain that you would be joining me as another hapless spirit.\030Return to Marduke with the keepsake, $N. He will instruct you in its use.\030Return to Magistrate Marduke in Caer Darrow. Show him the Soulbound Keepsake.\030Have you done the impossible?\030Soulbound Keepsake\0312,1,40,2,257,1,11036\0302,42,73,2,257,3,11036\0303,1,44,2,384,1,11036\0303,46,77,2,384,1,11036\0301,1,69,4,272,4,11286\0304,1,29,3,256,2,11286\03111286,2,3,Magistrate Marduke\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,1,Marduke\0302,0,0,3,Magistrate Marduke\0302,0,0,3,Caer Darrow\0315464,19,5464,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305466,23,5466,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5466]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ten thousand souls cry out in unison, $N! You have struck a mortal blow to the Scourge and their masters.\030There is but one task remaining, $N. Confront the lich, Ras Frostwhisper, in his lair.$B$BUse the power of the keepsake against the beast -  be unrelenting in your actions!  Weather the blows that the flailing beast will surely bring down upon you. Do not give in to the pain!$B$BWhen the ritual is complete, Ras will be mortal once more. It is at that point that he must be slain. Strike him down and take his human head.\030Find Ras Frostwhisper in the Scholomance. When you have found him, use the Soulbound Keepsake on his undead visage. Should you succeed in reverting him to a mortal, strike him down and recover the Human Head of Ras Frostwhisper. Take the head back to Magistrate Marduke.\030You carry the burden of ten thousand restless souls, $N.\030The Lich, Ras Frostwhisper\0312,1,36,2,257,1,11286\0302,38,86,2,257,1,11286\0302,91,172,2,257,1,11286\0302,175,248,2,257,3,11286\0302,250,276,2,257,1,11286\0302,281,338,2,257,3,11286\0302,340,381,2,261,1,11286\0302,383,422,2,257,1,11286\0303,1,41,2,384,1,11286\0303,43,115,2,384,1,11286\0303,117,228,2,384,1,11286\0303,230,270,2,384,1,11286\0301,1,41,4,272,1,11286\0301,43,105,4,336,1,11286\0304,1,56,3,256,1,11286\03110508,2,2,Ras Frostwhisper\03010430,2,3,The Beast\03010508,2,9,Ras Frostwhisper\03010508,2,11,Ras Frostwhisper\03011286,2,12,Magistrate Marduke\0312,2057,0,0,\0302,0,0,9,Scholomance\0302,0,0,12,Magistrate Marduke\0304,0,0,14,Scourge\0315465,19,5465,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,13626,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[547]="PARTIAL\031loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You found it!$B$BAh, I feel so complete with my precious sword back in my hand. Many thanks to you!\030High Executor Darthalia sent me to keep watch of Dun Garok from a distance.  I had set up camp just out of sight.  But when morning came and I had to boil water, I left to gather firewood.$B$BWhen I returned to camp, I discovered my gear was missing.$B$BApparently some dwarven scouts from Dun Garok had passed by and made off with it.  I need my sword!  If you can get it back for me I would be so grateful.  So many dwarves there...it will be quite difficult to find the dirty little thief who stole it.\030Retrieve Deathguard Humbert's sword from Dun Garok and return it to him in Tarren Mill.\030Were you able to retrieve my sword, $N? High Executor Darthalia will hang me from the rafters if she discovers my folly.\030Humbert's Sword\0312,1,75,2,257,1,2419\0302,78,113,2,257,1,2419\0302,116,188,2,257,1,2419\0302,193,250,2,261,1,2419\0302,255,335,2,257,4,2419\0302,338,353,2,259,1,2419\0302,356,408,2,257,4,2419\0302,411,505,2,257,3,2419\0303,1,87,2,384,1,2419\0301,1,13,4,272,1,2419\0301,18,79,4,272,1,2419\0301,81,99,4,304,1,2419\0304,1,39,3,256,2,2419\0304,41,120,3,256,4,2419\0312215,2,1,High Executor Darthalia\0302419,2,9,Deathguard Humbert\03014528,4,11,Precious\0302215,3,14,High Executor Darthalia\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,5,Dun Garok\0302,0,0,9,Dun Garok\0302,0,0,9,Tarren Mill\031\031ITEM,3693,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5481]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031What's this? Gloom weed?! I've no need for gloom weed! That mindless mass of flesh is out there picking daisies and convincing the Lady knows how many dupes like you into doing the same. No offense.$B$BVery well, you're here now and that's all that matters. Since I'm not going to bother to try to explain things to that abomination how about you collect what I really need... doom weed!\030Master want weeds. Us gots big hands and not good at picking. You help us and we not hurt you. Us need gloom weed. Many weeds around here and near road.$B$BWhen you have gloom weed you take to Master Holland in Brill graveyard.\030Collect 3 Gloom Weed and deliver them to Junior Apothecary Holland in the Brill graveyard.\030Where's that useless abomination? Either you have what I need or you'd best get out there and find it.\030Gordo's Task\0312,1,18,2,259,1,10666\0302,20,61,2,257,1,10666\0302,63,94,2,257,1,10666\0302,96,114,2,259,1,10666\0302,116,152,2,257,1,10666\0302,157,227,2,257,1,10666\0303,1,90,2,384,1,10666\0301,1,12,4,272,2,10665\0301,14,25,4,272,2,10665\0301,27,54,4,274,1,10665\0301,56,186,4,272,1,10665\0301,188,198,4,272,1,10665\0301,203,257,4,272,1,10665\0301,259,376,4,274,3,10665\0301,378,387,4,272,1,10665\0304,1,33,3,256,2,10665\0304,35,102,3,258,1,10665\03110665,2,7,Junior Apothecary Holland\03015065,4,11,Lady\0308545,4,14,Abomination\0308545,3,16,Abomination\0312,85,1420,0,\0302,0,0,6,Master Holland\0302,0,0,6,Brill\0302,0,0,7,Junior Apothecary Holland\0302,0,0,7,Brill\0315482,23,5482,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12737,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[5482]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, my doom weed. Excellent!$B$B<Junior Apothecary Holland rubs his hands together greedily.>$B$BThese will come in quite handy. You've done me, uh, the Lady, a fine service today $N. As promised here is the reward that you deserve.\030So you can see the predicament that I'm in, $N. That thing is out there collecting the wrong weeds! I'll make it worth your while to gather what I need. Bring back to me enough doom weed and I'll give you a suitable reward.$B$BIt is my understanding that they like to plague the flora near the mass gravesite, to the north of the Brill graveyard. Hurry and be mindful of the gnolls in the area.\030Collect 10 Doom Weed and deliver them back to Junior Apothecary Holland.$B\030This had better be good. I trust you have all of the doom weed that I require?\030Doom Weed\0312,1,47,2,257,1,10665\0302,49,99,2,257,1,10665\0302,101,152,2,259,1,10665\0302,154,223,2,257,1,10665\0302,228,346,2,261,1,10665\0302,348,394,2,257,1,10665\0303,1,72,2,384,1,10665\0301,1,17,4,272,1,10665\0301,19,28,4,272,1,10665\0301,33,93,4,272,1,10665\0301,98,128,4,272,3,10665\0