on as the head of the key.\030Araj's Scarab\0312,1,67,2,257,1,11057\0302,70,158,2,257,1,11057\0302,161,254,2,259,3,11057\0302,259,366,2,257,1,11057\0302,369,428,2,261,1,11057\0302,433,466,2,257,1,11057\0303,1,108,2,388,1,11057\0301,1,16,4,272,1,11057\0301,23,93,4,272,1,11057\0301,95,180,4,272,1,11057\0301,185,227,4,272,1,11057\0301,229,397,4,272,1,11057\0301,402,434,4,272,1,11057\0304,1,138,3,256,3,11057\0304,140,241,3,256,3,11057\0311852,2,1,Araj the Summoner\0307269,2,3,Scarab\0307269,2,5,Scarab\0301852,2,7,Araj the Summoner\0307269,2,7,Scarab\03011057,2,7,Apothecary Dithers\0307269,4,12,Scarab\0301852,3,14,Araj the Summoner\0307269,3,15,Scarab\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,6,Scholomance\0302,0,0,7,Apothecary Dithers\0302,0,0,7,Bulwark\0315802,19,5802,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305511,23,5511,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,14610,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5805]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You are indeed a special hero, $N. We welcome you to the world of Azeroth, and offer you one of these unique gifts!\030Welcome to the World of Warcraft!$B$BAs special thanks for purchasing the World of Warcraft Collector's Edition, turn in this gift voucher to Merissa Stilwell in Northshire Valley.  You'll then be given a gift: a little companion to join you on your quest for adventure and glory.$B$BThanks again, and enjoy your stay in the World of Warcraft!$B\030Bring the Northshire Gift Voucher to Merissa Stilwell.\030Greetings! It is a pleasure to meet you!$B$BI see you have a special voucher. Give it to me and I will offer you something in exchange.\030Welcome!\0312,1,33,2,257,1,0\0302,38,180,2,257,1,0\0302,183,280,2,257,1,0\0302,285,343,2,257,1,0\0303,1,54,2,384,1,0\0301,1,34,4,272,1,11940\0301,36,115,4,272,1,11940\0304,1,10,3,256,1,11940\0304,12,40,3,256,1,11940\0304,45,77,3,256,1,11940\0304,79,135,3,256,3,11940\03111940,2,2,Merissa Stilwell\03011940,2,5,Merissa Stilwell\0312,24,1429,0,\0302,0,0,1,World of Warcraft\0302,0,0,2,Merissa Stilwell\0302,0,0,2,Northshire Valley\0302,0,0,4,World of Warcraft\0302,0,0,5,Merissa Stilwell\031\031ITEM,14646,STARTER,?,10,",[581]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031These are good tusks, $N. You prove that you have the strength to hunt the Bloodscalps.$B$BAnd that is good, because you are not done hunting them.\030A doom, there is.  A doom on my chief's youngest son, Yenniku.  As is a custom with our people, he was given to the Gurubashi Trolls of Zul'Gurub, but after my tribe, the Darkspear tribe, left with the orc Thrall, poor Yenniku was lost to us.  I was sent from distant Orgrimmar, back to Stranglethorn, to search for my chief's son.$B$BAnd I believe the Bloodscalp tribe has him.$B$BIf you would help me, then hunt the Bloodscalps.  You may find them to the north.  Gather their tusks and return to me.\030Bring 9 Bloodscalp Tusks to Nimboya at the Grom'gol Base Camp.\030$C. Show me you have made prey of the Bloodscalp tribe.$B$BShow me your trophies.\030Hunt for Yenniku\0312,1,17,2,257,1,2497\0302,20,62,2,257,1,2497\0302,65,242,2,261,1,2497\0302,245,331,2,257,1,2497\0302,336,378,2,257,4,2497\0302,383,430,2,257,4,2497\0302,433,463,2,257,1,2497\0302,466,501,2,257,1,2497\0303,1,62,2,384,1,2497\0301,1,25,4,272,1,2497\0301,27,87,4,272,1,2497\0301,92,147,4,274,1,2497\0304,5,55,3,256,1,2497\0304,60,81,3,256,1,2497\0312530,2,2,Yenniku\03015047,2,3,Gurubashi\0304949,2,3,Thrall\0302530,2,3,Yenniku\0302497,2,9,Nimboya\0312,33,1434,0,\0302,0,0,3,Gurubashi Trolls of Zul'Gurub\0302,0,0,4,Stranglethorn\0302,0,0,9,Nimboya\0302,0,0,9,Grom'gol Base Camp\031582,23,582,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3901,OBJECTIVE,9,15,",[582]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, $N. I will inspect these heads to ensure poor Yenniku was spared the headhunter's axe.\030We must find if Yenniku is dead.$B$BSlay the Bloodscalp Headhunters and take from them their Shrunken Heads.  You must gather many, many heads, and I will inspect them to make sure Yenniku's head is not among them.$B$BAnd if Yenniku was killed by the Bloodscalps, then may a 600-year curse fall on the spirit of their chief, Gan'zulah!$B$BGo, $N.  You may find many Headhunters at the ruins of Zuuldaia and Zul'Kunda, along the coast to the north.\030Bring 20 Shrunken Heads to Nimboya at the Grom'gol Base Camp.\030$N. I fear for our chief's son. Do you have the shrunken heads so I may inspect them?\030Headhunting\0312,1,32,2,257,4,2497\0302,37,108,2,257,1,2497\0302,111,214,2,257,3,2497\0302,219,335,2,261,4,2497\0302,349,447,2,321,1,2497\0303,1,61,2,384,1,2497\0301,1,14,4,272,1,2497\0301,16,97,4,274,3,2497\0304,5,31,3,256,1,2497\0304,33,85,3,256,2,2497\0312530,2,1,Yenniku\0302530,2,4,Yenniku\0301061,2,4,Gan'zulah\0302497,2,6,Nimboya\0302530,4,8,Yenniku\0312,33,1434,0,\0302,0,0,6,Nimboya\0302,0,0,6,Grom'gol Base Camp\031581,19,581,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030584,23,584,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,1532,OBJECTIVE,20,15,",[5821]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031You know, it doesn't seem prosperous to be paying the likes of you to guard Gizelton Caravan. $C, if I were a bit taller I could take on a second job and sit kodo-side-saddle with the biggest gun my hands could carry... and I'd show them blasted centaur who's their papa.\030Under normal circumstances, Rigger and I would lead our kodo past the Kolkar Centaur. Every now and then we hear the Centaur war drums, and when we hear those we stop. It's not good for business to be dead!$B$BI'll tell you what $c, if you protect us past the Kolkar village we'll make it worth your while.$B$BIt's just a short distance, all you need to do is keep the caravan intact and you can pick up your reward from Smeed Scrabblescrew - he is down the road a bit. We do a little business together.\030Escort the Gizelton Caravan past the Kolkar Centaur village. Talk with Smeed at Scrabblescrew's Camp for your reward.\030Escort Gizelton Caravan past Kolkar Centaur Village\030Why do I find myself waiting for that blasted caravan?$B$B<Smeed looks enlightened.>$B$BOh yeah, they pay the bills. Have you seen them?\030Bodyguard for Hire\0312,1,85,2,257,4,11625\0302,87,167,2,261,1,11625\0302,169,206,2,257,1,11625\0302,211,306,2,269,4,11625\0302,311,469,2,259,1,11625\0302,471,503,2,257,1,11625\0303,1,60,2,384,1,11625\0303,62,117,2,384,1,11625\0301,1,93,4,272,4,11596\0301,95,219,4,272,4,11596\0301,221,271,4,272,1,11596\0305,1,54,3,256,2,11596\0305,59,84,3,256,1,11596\0305,89,116,3,256,1,11596\0305,118,136,3,256,2,11596\0304,1,51,3,384,1,11625\0314632,2,1,Kolkar Centaur\03093,2,1,Centaur\03093,2,2,Centaur\03011596,2,5,Smeed Scrabblescrew\0304632,2,7,Kolkar Centaur\03093,2,7,Centaur\03093,4,11,Centaur\0304632,3,16,Kolkar Centaur\03093,3,16,Centaur\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,5,Smeed Scrabblescrew\0302,0,0,8,Scrabblescrew's Camp\031\031",[583]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Jolly nice to make your acquaintance, $N. Haven't seen a $C around these parts for some time.$B$BI situated myself with this expedition for one purpose: to hunt a great and elusive beast. Seeing that you're a hero of sorts I am willing to let you take part in the hunt, but you must first prove yourself.$B$BI shall teach the ways of raptor killing to you. Ajeck will train you with tiger hunting. And Sir Erlgadin is a master of panther tracking.$B$BProve your skill and I'll let you in on the big hunt.\030Welcome to Stranglethorn!$B$BPerhaps you're not aware of this, but that dwarf over there is the one and only Hemet Nesingwary, renowned war hero of the Alliance and master big game hunter.  He's not one for welcoming strangers into his camp, but you look like you've seen quite a bit of action in your day, $c.$B$BBeing a veteran of many battles himself, Master Nesingwary has a soft spot for fellow heroes.$B$BGo and speak with him.  Perhaps he can give you some hunting pointers.\030Speak with Hemet Nesingwary\030\030Welcome to the Jungle\0312,1,25,2,257,1,716\0302,30,188,2,261,4,716\0302,191,310,2,257,1,716\0302,315,407,2,257,1,716\0302,412,433,2,257,1,716\0302,436,481,2,257,4,716\0303,1,27,2,384,1,716\0301,1,41,4,272,1,715\0301,43,93,4,272,1,715\0301,98,187,4,272,1,715\0301,189,304,4,272,1,715\0301,309,356,4,272,3,715\0301,358,397,4,272,3,715\0301,399,447,4,272,1,715\0301,452,504,4,272,1,715\031715,2,2,Hemet Nesingwary\0304950,2,4,Spot\030715,2,7,Hemet Nesingwary\030107,4,12,Raptor\030736,4,14,Panther\0312,33,1434,0,\0302,0,0,1,Stranglethorn\031\031",[584]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You place the heads of Gan'zulah and Nezzliok within the cauldron...\030Yenniku was not among the heads, and I thank the Great Serpent for it.  But we are no closer to finding him.$B$BWe must know the truth, and I fear that only the Bloodscalp chief and his witchdoctor know it.  They are the enemies of the Darkspear tribe and will not speak freely, so we must force the truth from their dead lips!$B$BBring me the heads of Gan'zulah and Nezzliok the Dire and place them within this cauldron.$B$BThey are deep within Zul'Kunda.  Bring their heads...we will then make them talk.\030Bring Gan'zulah's Head and Nezzliok's Head to the bubbling cauldron at the Grom'gol Base Camp.\030The greenish broth within the cauldron bubbles.\030Bloodscalp Clan Heads\0312,1,70,2,257,1,2497\0302,73,108,2,257,1,2497\0302,113,206,2,257,1,2497\0302,209,327,2,261,3,2497\0302,332,421,2,257,1,2497\0302,426,456,2,257,1,2497\0302,459,506,2,257,3,2497\0303,1,94,2,384,1,2497\0301,1,68,4,272,1,0\0304,1,47,3,256,1,0\0312530,2,1,Yenniku\0301061,2,5,Gan'zu