ft voucher to Orenthil Whisperwind in Shadowglen.  You'll then be given a gift: a little companion to join you on your quest for adventure and glory.$B$BThanks again, and enjoy your stay in the World of Warcraft!\030Bring the Shadowglen Gift Voucher to Orenthil Whisperwind.\030Greetings! It is a pleasure to meet you!$B$BI see you have a special voucher. Give it to me and I will offer you something in exchange.\030Welcome!\0312,1,33,2,257,1,0\0302,38,177,2,257,1,0\0302,180,277,2,257,1,0\0302,282,340,2,257,1,0\0303,1,58,2,384,1,0\0301,1,34,4,272,1,11942\0301,36,115,4,272,1,11942\0304,1,10,3,256,1,11942\0304,12,40,3,256,1,11942\0304,45,77,3,256,1,11942\0304,79,135,3,256,3,11942\03111942,2,2,Orenthil Whisperwind\03011942,2,5,Orenthil Whisperwind\0312,188,1438,0,\0302,0,0,1,World of Warcraft\0302,0,0,2,Orenthil Whisperwind\0302,0,0,2,Shadowglen\0302,0,0,4,World of Warcraft\0302,0,0,5,Orenthil Whisperwind\031\031ITEM,14648,STARTER,?,10,",[5843]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You are indeed a special hero, $N. We welcome you to the world of Azeroth, and offer you one of these unique gifts!\030Welcome to the World of Warcraft!$B$BAs special thanks for purchasing the World of Warcraft Collector's Edition, turn in this gift voucher to Magga in the Valley of Trials.  You'll then be given a gift: a little companion to join you on your quest for adventure and glory.$B$BThanks again, and enjoy your stay in the World of Warcraft!\030Bring the Valley of Trials Gift Voucher to Magga.\030Hello! It is a pleasure to meet you!$B$BI see you have a special voucher. Give it to me and I will offer you something in exchange.\030Welcome!\0312,1,33,2,257,1,0\0302,38,172,2,257,1,0\0302,175,272,2,257,1,0\0302,277,335,2,257,1,0\0303,1,49,2,384,1,0\0301,1,34,4,272,1,11943\0301,36,115,4,272,1,11943\0304,1,6,3,256,1,11943\0304,8,36,3,256,1,11943\0304,41,73,3,256,1,11943\0304,75,131,3,256,3,11943\03111943,2,2,Magga\03011943,2,5,Magga\0312,363,1411,0,\0302,0,0,1,World of Warcraft\0302,0,0,2,Magga\0302,0,0,2,Valley of Trials\0302,0,0,4,World of Warcraft\0302,0,0,5,Magga\031\031ITEM,14649,STARTER,?,10,",[5844]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You are indeed a special hero, $N. We welcome you to the world of Azeroth, and offer you one of these unique gifts!\030Welcome to the World of Warcraft!$B$BAs special thanks for purchasing the World of Warcraft Collector's Edition, turn in this gift voucher to Vorn Skyseer in Camp Narache.  You'll then be given a gift: a little companion to join you on your quest for adventure and glory.$B$BThanks again, and enjoy your stay in the World of Warcraft!\030Bring the Camp Narache Gift Voucher to Vorn Skyseer.\030Greetings! It is a pleasure to meet you!$B$BI see you have a special voucher. Give it to me and I will offer you something in exchange.\030Welcome!\0312,1,33,2,257,1,0\0302,38,171,2,257,1,0\0302,174,271,2,257,1,0\0302,276,334,2,257,1,0\0303,1,52,2,384,1,0\0301,1,34,4,272,1,11944\0301,36,115,4,272,1,11944\0304,1,10,3,256,1,11944\0304,12,40,3,256,1,11944\0304,45,77,3,256,1,11944\0304,79,135,3,256,3,11944\03111944,2,2,Vorn Skyseer\03011944,2,5,Vorn Skyseer\0312,221,1412,0,\0302,0,0,1,World of Warcraft\0302,0,0,2,Vorn Skyseer\0302,0,0,2,Camp Narache\0302,0,0,4,World of Warcraft\0302,0,0,5,Vorn Skyseer\031\031ITEM,14650,STARTER,?,10,",[5845]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It is as glorious now - even in its tattered state - as the day I looked upon it and took my oath of allegiance.$B$BHis redemption comes and perhaps mine with it...\030The Order of the Silver Hand was utterly decimated when Uther was slain.$B$BThe boy held out for as long as he could. Pushed to the war torn hamlet of Northdale, he made his final stand.$B$BWere any of the Order left alive, he thought - and did it matter?$B$BIt was with that thought that Taelan threw down the standard of the Order and renounced all that he had known. His honor left upon the blood soaked ground of Northdale.$B$BYou must travel to Northdale and recover that symbol of lost honor.\030Travel to Northdale, in the northeastern region of the Eastern Plaguelands, and recover the Symbol of Lost Honor. Return to Tirion Fordring upon completion of your objective.\030My faith will guide you, $N. The Light knows no bounds.\030Of Lost Honor\0312,1,72,2,261,1,1855\0302,77,117,2,257,4,1855\0302,119,186,2,261,1,1855\0302,191,255,2,257,2,1855\0302,260,369,2,257,1,1855\0302,371,427,2,257,1,1855\0302,432,498,2,261,1,1855\0303,1,113,2,388,1,1855\0303,115,174,2,384,1,1855\0301,1,112,4,272,1,1855\0301,117,164,4,272,4,1855\0304,1,28,3,256,3,1855\0304,30,55,3,256,1,1855\0312996,2,3,Torn\0301855,2,9,Tirion Fordring\0312,139,1423,0,\0302,0,0,7,Northdale\0302,0,0,8,Northdale\0302,0,0,9,Tirion Fordring\0315781,19,5781,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305846,23,5846,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,14625,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5846]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031How could I forget? Many of the spirits on this island are cursed to relive their last happy memory before they met their tragic end.$B$BI too am cursed, but not as they - I am one of the few that remembers all...$B$BPerhaps this thing that you ask me is why I haunt these ruins. Perhaps this thing I tell you shall set me free.\030When Taelan was a child, we would oft visit Caer Darrow on family excursions. On our last visit, an artist by the name of Renfray painted a portrait of us poised along the beachside. It is my fondest memory of both Taelan and Karandra. For it was at that moment, with my wife and son in my arms, that I felt a bond of love and family that I would never know again.$B$BIf this painting still exists, you must find it.$B$BTravel to the ruined island of Caer Darrow and see if the painting or the artist remain.\030Travel to island of Caer Darrow, in the south-central region of the Plaguelands, and look for any clues as to the whereabouts of the painting.\030\030Of Love and Family\0312,1,77,2,257,4,1855\0302,79,182,2,257,1,1855\0302,184,235,2,257,1,1855\0302,237,364,2,257,4,1855\0302,369,416,2,257,4,1855\0302,421,508,2,257,4,1855\0303,1,142,2,384,1,1855\0301,1,19,4,272,4,11936\0301,21,133,4,284,1,11936\0301,138,213,4,276,1,11936\0301,218,279,4,336,4,11936\0301,281,328,4,272,4,11936\031\0312,139,1423,0,\0315845,19,5845,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305848,23,5848,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5847]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You are indeed a special hero, $N. We welcome you to the world of Azeroth, and offer you one of these unique gifts!\030Welcome to the World of Warcraft!$B$BAs special thanks for purchasing the World of Warcraft Collector's Edition, turn in this gift voucher to Claire Willower in Deathknell.  You'll then be given a gift: a little companion to join you on your quest for adventure and glory.$B$BThanks again, and enjoy your stay in the World of Warcraft!\030Bring the Deathknell Gift Voucher to Claire Willower in Deathknell.\030Greetings! It is a pleasure to meet you!$B$BI see you have a special voucher. Give it to me and I will offer you something in exchange.\030Welcome!\0312,1,33,2,257,1,0\0302,38,172,2,257,1,0\0302,175,272,2,257,1,0\0302,277,335,2,257,1,0\0303,1,67,2,384,1,0\0301,1,34,4,272,1,11945\0301,36,115,4,272,1,11945\0304,1,10,3,256,1,11945\0304,12,40,3,256,1,11945\0304,45,77,3,256,1,11945\0304,79,135,3,256,3,11945\03111945,2,2,Claire Willower\03011945,2,5,Claire Willower\0312,154,1420,0,\0302,0,0,1,World of Warcraft\0302,0,0,2,Claire Willower\0302,0,0,2,Deathknell\0302,0,0,4,World of Warcraft\0302,0,0,5,Claire Willower\0302,0,0,5,Deathknell\031\031ITEM,14651,STARTER,?,10,",[5848]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Tirion nearly collapses when he sees the painting.>$B$B<He begins to sob in an almost frenetic manner.>\030The painting... It hung on the wall of my workshop - inside the Order's barracks - for years.$B$BAfter Tirion's trial was over, I knew that I could no longer keep the painting visible. I hid it in a place that they would never think to look.$B$BTravel to Stratholme and make your way deep inside what is now the Scarlet Bastion, search for a painting of our twin moons. Chip away at the paint until you uncover my master work, 'Of Love and Family.'$B$BMay the Light guide your actions.\030Travel to Stratholme, in the northern part of the Plaguelands. It is in the Scarlet Bastion that you will find the painting 'Of Love and Family,' hidden behind another painting depicting the twin moons of our world.$B$BReturn the painting to Tirion Fordring.\030The painting, $N. Do you have the painting?\030Of Love and Family\0312,1,15,2,257,1,11936\0302,17,93,2,257,1,11936\0302,98,184,2,257,4,11936\0302,186,241,2,257,4,11936\0302,246,369,2,257,1,11936\0302,371,448,2,257,1,11936\0302,453,485,2,257,1,11936\0303,1,62,2,384,1,11936\0303,64,215,2,384,3,11936\0303,220,258,2,384,1,11936\0301,1,52,4,272,1,1855\0301,57,104,4,272,1,1855\0304,1,17,3,256,1,1855\0304,19,43,3,256,2,1855\0311855,2,10,Tirion Fordring\0312,2017,0,0,\0302,0,0,5,Stratholme\0302,0,0,8,Stratholme\0302,0,0,9,Scarlet Bastion\0302,0,0,10,Tirion Fordring\0315846,19,5846,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305861,23,5861,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,14679,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[585]="PARTIAL\031characters,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes. These will serve me well. When my spirit is freed, I will enter the Nether with three fine servants!$B$BYou are a credit to your $R clan, and you have appeased me.\030<The head of Nezzliok speaks.>$B$BIt is true.  I know where the child of the Darkspears was taken.  You have bested me and bound my spirit, but I will say nothing without appeasement!$B$BThe Bloodscalps war with the Skullsplitters.  To gain my favor, steal from the Skullsplitters 3 of their trophy skulls and place them here with us, so that my spirit will have slaves in the Nether.  One skull must be from their trophy pile in Balia'mah, another from Ziata'jai, and the last from Zul'Mamwe.\030Bring a Balia'mah Trophy, a Ziata'jai Trophy and a Zul'Mamwe Trophy to the Bubbling Cauldron at the Grom'gol Base Camp.\030I await the skulls...\030Speaking with Nezzliok\0312,1,30,2,257,1,0\0302,35,45,2,257,1,0\0302,48,98,2,257,1,0\0302,101,183,2,261,3,0\0302,188,231,2,261,1,0\0302,234,384,2,263,3,0\0302,387,493,2,257,1,0\0303,1,119,2,384,1,0\0301,1,4,4,272,1,0\0301,6,30,4,272,3,0\0301,32,105,4,272,3,0\0301,110,168,4,272,1,0\0304,1,21,3,256,1,0\031\0312,33,1434,0,\0302,0,0,6,Skullsplitters\0302,0,0,6,Nether\0302,0,0,7,Balia'mah\0302,0,0,7,Ziata'jai\0302,0,0,7,Zul'Mamwe\0302,0,0,8,Bubbling Cauldron\0302,0,0,8,Grom'gol Base Camp\031584,19,584,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,2076,GIVER,?,9,Bubbling Cauldron\030OBJECT,2076,FINISHER,?,12,Bubbling Cauldron\030ITEM,3906,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,3907,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,3908,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[586]="PARTIAL\031loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I do not want to believe it, but I cannot deny what you have done. And my rage eases, now that Ana'thek is defeated. $B$BYour might will drive you to great deeds, $N. But one day...I will see you in the Nether and we will again match strength.$B$BI will be waiting.\030<The head of Gan'zulah speaks.>$B$BCurse you!  And curse your ancestors!!$B$BOnly blood and revenge can cool my rage, so if that is your wish, then... do this:$B$BThrow yourself into the heart of the Skullsplitters to the east.  Slay the fiercest among them, and if you survive...then break yourself against their chief, Ana'thek the Cruel.  Hah!  Bring me his shattered armor if you can!$B$BMay he tear off your limbs and leave you to rot and be eaten by carrion.\030Kill 8 Skullsplitter Hunters, 6 Skullsplitter Headhunters, and 4 Skullsplitter Berserkers.$B$BBring the Broken Armor of Ana'thek to the Bubbling Cauldron at the Grom'gol Base Camp.\030Although my own flesh boils off my skull, I can still smell your fear.$B$BHah!  You will never complete my task...\030Speaking with Gan'zulah\0312,1,31,2,257,1,0\0302,36,45,2,261,1,0\0302,48,73,2,261,1,0\0302,78,150,2,259,4,0\0302,152,159,2,257,1,0\0302,164,227,2,257,1,0\0302,230,340,2,265,4,0\0302,343,346,2,257,1,0\0302,349,388,2,257,4,0\0302,393,464,2,257,1,0\0303,1,90,2,384,1,0\0303,95,180,2,384,1,0\0301,1,66,4,272,4,0\0301,68,116,4,304,1,0\0301,122,166,4,272,4,0\0301,168,243,4,272,3,0\0301,248,265,4,272,3,0\0304,1,70,3,256,1,0\0304,75,78,3,256,1,0\0304,81,114,3,256,3,0\0311061,2,1,Gan'zulah\0301059,2,7,Ana'thek the Cruel\0312,33,1434,0,\0302,0,0,12,Bubbling Cauldron\0302,0,0,12,Grom'gol Base Camp\0304,0,0,16,Nether\031584,19,584,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,2076,GIVER,?,9,Bubbling Cauldron\030OBJECT,2076,FINISHER,?,12,Bubbling Cauldron\030NPC,669,OBJECTIVE,8,13,Skullsplitter Hunter\030NPC,781,OBJECTIVE,6,13,Skullsplitter Headhunter\030NPC,783,OBJECTIVE,4,13,Skullsplitter Berserker\030ITEM,3909,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5861]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I was Tirion's most trusted advisor when he held rank as Lord of Mardenholde. I openly dissented the verdict passed by the Order of the Silver Hand and was banished for my insolence.$B$BHe has been through much heart ache and disappointment in his life, $R. Are you prepared to right the wrongs set upon the Fordrings?\030$N, you have done all that I have asked thus far. Only one step remains in your quest of redemption.$B$BYou must deliver the items you have collected to Taelan. Unfortunately, Taelan and his Scarlet Crusaders will attack you on sight.$B$BThere is only one way in which to deliver my message and that is through a guise of deception.$B$BTo the south you will find Uther's tomb. An old and trusted confidant of mine, Myranda, now resides there - seek her out. Show her the items and she will assist you.\030Travel to Uther's Tomb, located in the southern Plaguelands. Show Myranda the Hag Tirion's Gift.\030I knew this day would come.\030Find Myranda\0312,1,49,2,257,1,1855\0302,51,100,2,257,1,1855\0302,105,160,2,257,1,1855\0302,162,234,2,261,3,1855\0302,239,332,2,257,1,1855\0302,337,376,2,257,3,1855\0302,378,457,2,257,1,1855\0302,459,501,2,257,3,1855\0303,1,60,2,384,1,1855\0303,62,96,2,384,1,1855\0301,1,77,4,272,1,11872\0301,79,182,4,272,1,11872\0301,187,257,4,272,1,11872\0301,259,318,4,272,2,11872\0304,1,27,3,256,4,11872\03111872,2,10,Myranda the Hag\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,3,Taelan\0302,0,0,9,Uther's Tomb\0315848,19,5848,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305862,23,5862,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5862]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031What is this, soldier?$B$B<Taelan opens the box and begins to examine its contents.>$B$BThis... this cannot be true. But all that you have shown me...$B$B<Taelan falls to one knee, his heartbeat quickens. The fury of ages is about to be loosed upon this town.>\030I am what you would call, an illusionist. Though I may be able to create an illusion to allow you entry into Hearthglen, be warned; my powers have their limitations.$B$BShould you travel too far from these lands, the effects of the illusion will cease. The spell itself takes a great amount of concentration and power from me, and thus, I can only sustain the effect for a short time.$B$BSpeak to me again when you are ready.\030Speak to Myranda to gain the Scarlet Illusion. Travel to Hearthglen while under the Scarlet Illusion and deliver Tirion's Gift to Highlord Taelan Fordring.$B$BHearthglen is to the north, Taelan should be inside of Mardenholde Keep.\030Are you the reinforcements from Tyr's Hand?\030Scarlet Subterfuge\0312,1,41,2,257,4,11872\0302,43,165,2,257,1,11872\0302,170,252,2,257,3,11872\0302,254,384,2,257,1,11872\0302,389,425,2,257,1,11872\0303,1,46,2,384,1,11872\0303,48,155,2,384,1,11872\0303,160,231,2,384,1,11872\0301,1,22,4,272,2,1842\0301,27,84,4,272,1,1842\0301,89,95,4,272,1,1842\0301,97,116,4,272,1,1842\0301,118,150,4,272,1,1842\0301,155,204,4,272,1,1842\0301,206,260,4,272,1,1842\0304,1,43,3,256,2,1842\0311842,2,7,Highlord Taelan Fordring\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,6,Myranda\0302,0,0,7,Hearthglen\0302,0,0,7,Highlord Taelan Fordring\0303,0,0,16,Tyr's Hand\0315861,19,5861,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305944,23,5944,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5863]="PARTIAL\031consequences,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I'm so glad you were able to do this for me, $N! Thanks for your help!\030Just recently, a large band of nomadic ogres arrived in Tanaris. South of here, they have taken over a large area of the desert and formed a compound. Several smaller bands are currently wandering the desert, some of which have invaded the old troll ruins.$B$BThe Dunemaul Compound must be destroyed! We cannot allow these ogres to build up a force.$B$BThe leader of this band is named Gor'marok the Ravager; I believe that putting an end to his leadership will be the beginning of the end for the ogres.\030Andi Lynn in Gadgetzan wants you to destroy the Dunemaul Compound by killing 10 Dunemaul Brutes, 10 Dunemaul Enforcers, and Gor'marok the Ravager.\030I'm so worried! Please be careful!\030The Dunemaul Compound\0312,1,64,2,257,1,11758\0302,66,150,2,257,1,11758\0302,152,256,2,325,1,11758\0302,261,300,2,261,1,11758\0302,302,349,2,265,1,11758\0302,354,504,2,257,4,11758\0303,1,146,2,390,1,11758\0301,1,48,4,272,1,11758\0301,50,70,4,272,1,11758\0304,1,15,3,256,1,11758\0304,17,34,3,256,1,11758\03112046,2,6,Gor'marok the Ravager\03011758,2,7,Andi Lynn\03012046,2,7,Gor'marok the Ravager\0312,440,1446,0,\0302,0,0,1,Tanaris\0302,0,0,7,Gadgetzan\031\031NPC,5474,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Dunemaul Brute\030NPC,5472,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Dunemaul Enforcer\030NPC,12046,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Gor'marok the Ravager",[587]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Good show, $N! And just before I need to ship out too! Can't thank you enough, old friend.\030Ah, the sea life.  I ain't gonna say it's the good life, but it's my life.$B$BWhen I get into port I like to find me a good bottle of grog and some high quality snuff.  Nasty habits but what's a pirate without his vices, right?$B$BSo you can imagine how heartbroken I was to find out the herbalist here in town has gone and sold out of the stuff.  Says his shipment got hijacked by those damned Bloodsail Raiders.$B$BI bet a fearless $c like you could convince 'em to share the goods, eh?\030Deeg in Booty Bay wants you to bring him 15 shares of Snuff.\030Any luck finding the goods, matey?\030Up to Snuff\0312,1,17,2,257,1,2488\0302,20,74,2,257,1,2488\0302,79,167,2,257,1,2488\0302,170,227,2,257,2,2488\0302,232,346,2,257,1,2488\0302,349,413,2,257,1,2488\0302,418,488,2,257,4,2488\0303,1,60,2,386,1,2488\0301,1,14,4,272,1,2488\0301,16,54,4,274,1,2488\0301,56,90,4,272,1,2488\0304,1,34,3,256,2,2488\0312488,2,8,Deeg\0312,33,1434,0,\0302,0,0,8,Booty Bay\031595,19,595,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3910,OBJECTIVE,15,15,",[588]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Zanzil the Outcast??$B$BIf Yenniku is held by that troll, a vile and powerful witchdoctor, then I fear that only a faint hope remains. Faint. And tiny as the smallest insect.$B$BBut still, it is hope.\030<Nezzliok speaks.>$B$BYou have appeased myself and my chief, so I will tell you that which you seek to discover...$B$BYoung Yenniku is lost to his clan.$B$BHe was taken by the witchdoctor Zanzil the Outcast.  Now Zanzil controls him, body and soul, and only the most potent magic could set him free.$B$BA magic that you do not have, $c.$B$BPerhaps your Darkspear allies can offer a hope of Yenniku's salvation.  But that, I doubt.\030Speak with Kin'weelay.\030\030The Fate of Yenniku\0312,1,18,2,257,1,0\0302,23,114,2,259,3,0\0302,119,152,2,261,1,0\0302,157,207,2,257,1,0\0302,210,299,2,257,4,0\0302,304,336,2,257,1,0\0302,341,410,2,257,4,0\0302,413,430,2,257,1,0\0303,1,22,2,384,1,0\0301,1,20,4,272,2,2519\0301,25,134,4,274,4,2519\0301,136,141,4,272,1,2519\0301,143,174,4,272,1,2519\0301,179,200,4,274,3,2519\0312530,2,3,Yenniku\0302534,2,4,Zanzil the Outcast\0302519,2,9,Kin'weelay\0302534,4,10,Zanzil the Outcast\0302530,4,11,Yenniku\0312,33,1434,0,\031585,21,585,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030586,21,586,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030589,23,589,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,2076,GIVER,?,9,Bubbling Cauldron",[5881]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is great news; I have been sitting here guarding this hunk of wood for too long. Now I can spend some time with my family... Yippee!\030The Horde does well keeping our troops fresh... since the Great War we have been prosperous here in Kalimdor.$B$BI need you to do me a favor, I have a lad by the name of Grish Longrunner protecting the Great Lift in the southern barrens. Give him this letter; the letter will let him know that I have a reserve warrior coming to relieve him of duty so that he can visit his family. He requested this sometime ago and he would be happy to hear the news.\030Maggran wishes you to deliver a letter to Grish Longrunner at the Great Lift in the Barrens.\030You have news from Maggran Earthbinder?\030Calling in the Reserves\0312,1,47,2,257,1,11860\0302,49,109,2,261,1,11860\0302,114,237,2,259,1,11860\0302,239,381,2,259,3,11860\0302,383,452,2,257,4,11860\0303,1,92,2,386,1,11860\0301,1,85,4,272,1,12576\0301,87,129,4,272,1,12576\0301,131,137,4,272,1,12576\0304,1,39,3,256,2,12576\03112576,2,3,Grish Longrunner\03012576,2,6,Grish Longrunner\03011860,3,10,Maggran Earthbinder\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,2,Kalimdor\0302,0,0,6,Grish Longrunner\0302,0,0,6,Great Lift\0302,0,0,6,Barrens\0303,0,0,10,Maggran Earthbinder\031\031",[5882]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very well then, here are your Cenarion plant salves. Scour Felwood for corrupted plants, $n! Wherever they are, use the salve I have given you to purify them.\030\030\030Possessing a Cenarion Beacon allows one to see a corrupted soul shard on those tainted beasts that are put down for the greater good. I grind shards into a usable reagent that goes into making Cenarion plant salve. We will use that salve to turn corrupted plants into healthy ones again.$B$BIn exchange for these shards, I will give you some Cenarion plant salves I have already prepared.\030Salve via Hunting\0311,1,52,4,272,1,9528\0301,54,92,4,276,1,9528\0301,94,158,4,272,1,9528\0304,1,133,3,268,1,9528\0304,135,214,3,256,1,9528\0304,216,287,3,260,3,9528\0304,292,388,3,256,3,9528\031\0312,361,1448,0,\0314101,19,4101,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304103,23,4103,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,11515,OBJECTIVE,6,15,",[5883]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very well then, here's some Cenarion plant salve. If you find more vitriol when you mine in Felwood, remember to hold on to it for me! The more of it you find, the more salve I will be able to make.\030\030\030If you possess a Cenarion beacon while mining in Felwood, you will be able to see tainted vitriol that corrupts a vein of raw metal. I know how to purify that vitriol and turn it into a reagent that goes into making Cenarion plant salve. You will then use that salve on plants you find in the wild that need saving.$B$BIf you have collected any tainted vitriol, I'll give you some Cenarion plant salve I have already prepared.\030Salve via Mining\0311,1,49,4,272,1,9528\0301,51,134,4,272,4,9528\0301,136,198,4,272,3,9528\0304,1,132,3,256,4,9528\0304,134,237,3,256,1,9528\0304,239,315,3,258,3,9528\0304,320,426,3,256,4,9528\031\0312,361,1448,0,\0304,0,0,2,Felwood\0303,0,0,4,Felwood\0314101,19,4101,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304104,23,4104,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,11513,OBJECTIVE,4,15,",[5884]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Excellent work $n - every bit of this, once we purify it, will help us take back Felwood. Here, take some doses of Cenarion plant salve and head into the forest. The reclaiming of the land from the corruption waits for no $r!\030\030\030A Cenarion beacon allows a seasoned herbalist to spot insidious fel creep - a malfeasant product of Felwood's corruption. My work here has taught me the knowledge of purifying fel creep into a cleansing reagent... used in what we now refer to as Cenarion plant salve.$B$BWhen you gather herbs in Felwood, you should encounter the fel creep so long as you have the beacon. In exchange for what you bring to me, I will give you pre-made Cenarion plant salve.\030Salve via Gathering\0311,1,89,4,272,3,9528\0301,91,161,4,272,1,9528\0301,163,225,4,276,1,9528\0304,1,121,3,260,1,9528\0304,123,213,3,256,1,9528\0304,215,267,3,256,1,9528\0304,272,371,3,256,1,9528\0304,373,456,3,256,3,9528\0314950,3,4,Spot\0312,361,1448,0,\0303,0,0,7,Felwood\0314101,19,4101,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304105,23,4105,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,11514,OBJECTIVE,4,15,",[5885]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is exactly what I need. Here - take these plant salves and use them to reclaim Felwood from the corruption. We must persevere, $n!\030\030\030A Cenarion beacon will allow a well-trained skinner to spot patches of tainted skin from bounty gathered in Felwood. I convert these seemingly useless patches into a thick paste that serves as a quickening agent for Cenarion plant salve. When you skin your kills here in Felwood, be sure to have a beacon on you!$B$BWhen you collect tainted patches, bring them to me and I will give you some Cenarion plant salves that I have already made.\030Salve via Skinning\0311,1,28,4,274,1,9528\0301,30,112,4,276,1,9528\0301,114,135,4,272,1,9528\0304,1,116,3,256,3,9528\0304,118,237,3,256,1,9528\0304,239,312,3,256,1,9528\0304,317,439,3,256,3,9528\0314950,3,4,Spot\0312,361,1448,0,\0303,0,0,4,Felwood\0303,0,0,6,Felwood\0314101,19,4101,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304106,23,4106,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,11512,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[5886]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Here are some Cenarion plant salves - I only need one lesser nether essence for this, $n. Essence is by far the most potent item I can make use of to turn swords into plowshares, as it were. If you need more salve, then find me here!\030\030\030The power of a disenchanted magical item is felt by the essence it creates. I've devised a way to turn raw essence used by enchanters into a suitable reagent for creating Cenarion plant salve. You don't need a Cenarion beacon for this; any suitably disenchanted item that yields lesser nether essences will work.$B$BI just need a single lesser nether essence; in exchange, I will give you Cenarion plant salves. The essence is extremely potent - a little definitely goes a long way!\030Salve via Disenchanting\0311,1,89,4,274,1,9528\0301,91,190,4,272,1,9528\0301,192,233,4,274,4,9528\0304,1,75,3,256,1,9528\0304,77,192,3,256,1,9528\0304,194,312,3,256,3,9528\0304,317,411,3,258,3,9528\0304,413,482,3,256,1,9528\031\0312,361,1448,0,\0314101,19,4101,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304107,23,4107,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,11174,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5887]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very well then, here are your Cenarion plant salves. Scour Felwood for corrupted plants, $n! Wherever they are, use the salve I have given you to purify them.\030\030\030Possessing a Cenarion Beacon allows one to see a corrupted soul shard on those tainted beasts that are put down for the greater good. I grind shards into a usable reagent that goes into making Cenarion plant salve. We will use that salve to turn corrupted plants into healthy ones again.$B$BIn exchange for these shards, I will give you some Cenarion plant salves I have already prepared.\030Salve via Hunting\0311,1,52,4,272,1,9529\0301,54,92,4,276,1,9529\0301,94,158,4,272,1,9529\0304,1,133,3,268,1,9529\0304,135,214,3,256,1,9529\0304,216,287,3,260,3,9529\0304,292,388,3,256,3,9529\031\0312,361,1448,0,\0314102,19,4102,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304108,23,4108,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,11515,OBJECTIVE,6,15,",[5888]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very well then, here's some Cenarion plant salve. If you find more vitriol when you mine in Felwood, remember to hold on to it for me! The more of it you find, the more salve I will be able to make.\030\030\030If you possess a Cenarion beacon while mining in Felwood, you will be able to see tainted vitriol that corrupts a vein of raw metal. I know how to purify that vitriol and turn it into a reagent that goes into making Cenarion plant salve. You will then use that salve on plants you find in the wild that need saving.$B$BIf you have collected any tainted vitriol, I'll give you some Cenarion plant salve I have already prepared.\030Salve via Mining\0311,1,49,4,272,1,9529\0301,51,134,4,272,4,9529\0301,136,198,4,272,3,9529\0304,1,132,3,256,4,9529\0304,134,237,3,256,1,9529\0304,239,315,3,258,3,9529\0304,320,426,3,256,4,9529\031\0312,361,1448,0,\0304,0,0,2,Felwood\0303,0,0,4,Felwood\0314102,19,4102,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304109,23,4109,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,11513,OBJECTIVE,4,15,",[5889]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Excellent work $n - every bit of this, once we purify it, will help us take back Felwood. Here, take some doses of Cenarion plant salve and head into the forest. The reclaiming of the land from the corruption waits for no $r!\030\030\030A Cenarion beacon allows a seasoned herbalist to spot insidious fel creep - a malfeasant product of Felwood's corruption. My work here has taught me the knowledge of purifying fel creep into a cleansing reagent... used in what we now refer to as Cenarion plant salve.$B$BWhen you gather herbs in Felwood, you should encounter the fel creep so long as you have the beacon. In exchange for what you bring to me, I will give you pre-made Cenarion plant salve.\030Salve via Gathering\0311,1,89,4,272,3,9529\0301,91,161,4,272,1,9529\0301,163,225,4,276,1,9529\0304,1,121,3,260,1,9529\0304,123,213,3,256,1,9529\0304,215,267,3,256,1,9529\0304,272,371,3,256,1,9529\0304,373,456,3,256,3,9529\0314950,3,4,Spot\0312,361,1448,0,\0303,0,0,7,Felwood\0314102,19,4102,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304110,23,4110,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,11514,OBJECTIVE,4,15,",[589]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have done well, $N. These shards are well formed. Already I hear them sing to me.$B$BAnd while you were gone, I spoke with the spirits of the jungle. I know where the Mind's Eye rests...$B$B...And who guards it.\030Legends tell of a jewel, hidden deep in the heart of Stranglethorn.  We call it the Mind's Eye, and it has great powers.  If you gain this Eye then, perhaps, we can use it to bring lost Yenniku back from the darkness.$B$BI will consult with the spirits of the jungle to find the Mind's Eye.  While I do this, you enter the Crystalvein Mine, southeast of here, and gather Pulsing Blue Shards from Ironjaw Basilisks.  The shards are rare, but we will need their magic to bend the Mind's Eye to our will.\030Bring 3 Pulsing Blue Shards to Kin'weelay at the Grom'gol Base Camp.\030Do you have the shards, $N? They are needed for my final ritual, after we have the Mind's Eye.\030The Singing Crystals\0312,1,67,2,257,1,2519\0302,70,120,2,257,1,2519\0302,123,217,2,261,4,2519\0302,222,290,2,257,3,2519\0302,293,414,2,257,1,2519\0302,417,501,2,259,3,2519\0303,1,68,2,384,1,2519\0301,1,23,4,272,1,2519\0301,25,53,4,272,1,2519\0301,55,85,4,272,1,2519\0301,90,153,4,272,1,2519\0301,155,190,4,272,1,2519\0301,195,215,4,272,1,2519\0304,1,27,3,256,2,2519\0304,29,94,3,256,1,2519\0317903,2,1,Jewel\0302530,2,3,Yenniku\0302519,2,7,Kin'weelay\0312,33,1434,0,\0302,0,0,5,Ironjaw Basilisks\0302,0,0,7,Kin'weelay\0302,0,0,7,Grom'gol Base Camp\031588,19,588,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030591,23,591,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,3911,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[5890]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is exactly what I need. Here - take these plant salves and use them to reclaim Felwood from the corruption. We must persevere, $n!\030\030\030A Cenarion beacon will allow a well-trained skinner to spot patches of tainted skin from bounty gathered in Felwood. I convert these seemingly useless patches into a thick paste that serves as a quickening agent for Cenarion plant salve. When you skin your kills here in Felwood, be sure to have a beacon on you!$B$BWhen you collect tainted patches, bring them to me and I will give you some Cenarion plant salves that I have already made.\030Salve via Skinning\0311,1,28,4,274,1,9529\0301,30,112,4,276,1,9529\0301,114,135,4,272,1,9529\0304,1,116,3,256,3,9529\0304,118,237,3,256,1,9529\0304,239,312,3,256,1,9529\0304,317,439,3,256,3,9529\0314950,3,4,Spot\0312,361,1448,0,\0303,0,0,4,Felwood\0303,0,0,6,Felwood\0314102,19,4102,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304111,23,4111,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,11512,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[5891]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Here are some Cenarion plant salves - I only need one lesser nether essence for this, $n. Essence is by far the most potent item I can make use of to turn swords into plowshares, as it were. If you need more salve, then find me here!\030\030\030The power of a disenchanted magical item is felt by the essence it creates. I've devised a way to turn raw essence used by enchanters into a suitable reagent for creating Cenarion plant salve. You don't need a Cenarion beacon for this; any suitably disenchanted item that yields lesser nether essences will work.$B$BI just need a single lesser nether essence; in exchange, I will give you Cenarion plant salves. The essence is extremely potent - a little definitely goes a long way!\030Salve via Disenchanting\0311,1,89,4,274,1,9529\0301,91,190,4,272,1,9529\0301,192,233,4,274,4,9529\0304,1,75,3,256,1,9529\0304,77,192,3,256,1,9529\0304,194,312,3,256,3,9529\0304,317,411,3,258,3,9529\0304,413,482,3,256,1,9529\031\0312,361,1448,0,\0314102,19,4102,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304112,23,4112,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,11174,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[5892]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done! I'll put these supplies to good use! Thanks, $N!\030Before the fighting started, we stored supplies for Dun Baldar in the Irondeep mine.  The troggs that surfaced there weren't much of a problem when we had spare troops to guard the mine, but now that we're fighting with the Horde we can't maintain control of Irondeep.$B$BWe need the supplies in Irondeep, $N.  Enter the mine and bring me a load of them.\030Bring 10 Irondeep Supplies to the Alliance Quartermaster in Dun Baldar.\030Do you have the supplies, $N? We can never have enough!\030Irondeep Supplies\0312,1,84,2,261,1,12096\0302,87,268,2,261,1,12096\0302,273,309,2,259,1,12096\0302,312,354,2,257,1,12096\0303,1,71,2,384,1,12096\0301,1,10,4,272,1,12096\0301,12,47,4,272,1,12096\0301,49,59,4,272,1,12096\0304,1,29,3,256,2,12096\0304,31,55,3,256,1,12096\031\0312,2597,1459,0,\0302,0,0,1,Irondeep\0302,0,0,3,Irondeep\0302,0,0,5,Alliance Quartermaster\0302,0,0,5,Dun Baldar\031\031ITEM,17522,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[5893]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, you got them. Good work, $N! These supplies are a little musty from sitting in that dark mine for so long, but we'll make use of them nonetheless.$B$BThank you, $N. Your deeds are vital to the maintenance of our fighting forces.\030The Coldtooth mine to the north was once an ideal place to store extra supplies, but now that the fighting with the Stormpikes grows fierce, we do not always have the spare warriors to station at the mine and protect it.  And so, control of the mine often falls to the Alliance, or to underground denizens...$B$BBut we still need our supplies, $N!  Go to the Coldtooth mine and bring me a load of them.  And be wary of enemies as you go; the tides of battle shift quickly in that place...\030Bring 10 Coldtooth Supplies to the Horde Quatermaster in Frostwolf Keep.\030Have you been to the Coldtooth mine, $N? Do you have the supplies I asked for?\030Coldtooth Supplies\0312,1,220,2,269,1,12097\0302,223,308,2,257,1,12097\0302,313,347,2,259,1,12097\0302,350,402,2,257,1,12097\0302,405,488,2,261,1,12097\0303,1,72,2,384,1,12097\0301,1,17,4,272,1,12097\0301,19,32,4,272,1,12097\0301,34,150,4,272,1,12097\0301,155,168,4,272,1,12097\0301,170,232,4,276,1,12097\0304,1,40,3,256,2,12097\0304,42,78,3,256,2,12097\03110981,2,6,Frostwolf\0312,2597,1459,0,\0302,0,0,2,Alliance\0302,0,0,4,Coldtooth\0302,0,0,6,Horde Quatermaster\0302,0,0,6,Frostwolf Keep\0303,0,0,12,Coldtooth\031\031ITEM,17542,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[59]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, thank you for the marker. Please feel free to pick your choice of armor.$B$BLuck to you, brave $C. And may this armor serve you well.\030For your shrewdness and valor, I have a marker here that is good for one piece of armor.  I want you to take it to Sara Timberlain at the Eastvale Logging Camp.  Give her the marker, and she will fashion the armor for you.  And after you receive it, $N, use it in the defense of Elwynn.$B$BThe Eastvale Logging Camp is beyond Guard Thomas' post to the east.\030Give Sara Timberlain the Stormwind Armor Marker.\030I have been commissioned by the Stormwind Army to supply their people with cloth and leather armor.$B$BIf you have a marker for me, then I'd be happy to make you something.\030Cloth and Leather Armor\0312,1,88,2,257,1,240\0302,91,160,2,259,1,240\0302,163,222,2,257,3,240\0302,225,286,2,257,1,240\0302,291,357,2,257,1,240\0303,1,48,2,384,1,240\0301,1,29,4,272,1,278\0301,31,76,4,272,1,278\0301,81,102,4,272,1,278\0301,104,137,4,272,1,278\0304,1,99,3,256,1,278\0304,104,172,3,256,4,278\031278,2,2,Sara Timberlain\030261,2,5,Guard Thomas\030278,2,6,Sara Timberlain\0312,12,1429,0,\0302,0,0,2,Sara Timberlain\0302,0,0,2,Eastvale Logging Camp\03139,19,39,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[590]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Incredible! What skill!$B$BThought you'd be easy prey, $N. Got me good, you did.$B$BHere's the coin I promised... not as much as I said it'd be, but that's on a count o' me lying to ya in the first place.\030What?$B$BWhat?!$B$BYou want money? I don't owe you any money.$B$BLetter? What letter? Oh, you wanna fight then? All right, mate... let's do this! Owe you any money...\030Defeat Calvin Montague in Deathknell.\030Defeat Calvin Montague\030\030A Rogue's Deal\0312,1,5,2,257,2,6784\0302,10,15,2,257,2,6784\0302,20,34,2,259,2,6784\0302,36,61,2,257,1,6784\0302,66,72,2,257,2,6784\0302,74,85,2,257,2,6784\0302,87,111,2,261,2,6784\0302,113,130,2,257,1,6784\0302,132,145,2,257,1,6784\0302,147,166,2,257,1,6784\0303,1,37,2,384,1,6784\0301,1,11,4,272,1,6784\0301,13,23,4,272,1,6784\0301,28,58,4,272,1,6784\0301,60,80,4,272,1,6784\0301,85,113,4,272,1,6784\0301,115,204,4,272,1,6784\0304,1,22,3,384,1,6784\0316784,2,11,Calvin Montague\0306784,3,18,Calvin Montague\0312,154,1420,0,\0302,0,0,11,Deathknell\0318,19,8,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[5901]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031These will do nicely, $N. Thank you.$B$BIf you're ready, we can get on with the next step.\030So, to bring pain and strife to the Scarlet Crusade, I want to take their precious lumber mill from them. I'm sure the loss of such a resource will cause them a great deal of harm in defending and rebuilding the town for their own reasons. Will you help me, $N?$B$BStart by taking this jar to Plaguewood in the Eastern Plaguelands. Fill it with the termites you find in their mounds throughout the woods. Come back when you have enough.\030Use the Empty Termite Jar on the Termite Mounds in Eastern Plaguelands. After you've gathered 100 Plagueland Termites, return to Mickey Levine at the Bulwark in Tirisfal Glades.\030Do you have the termites yet, $N? I am sure it is obvious to a smart $C like yourself.$B$BOnce we have enough of them, we'll make sure no one can use the lumber mill ever again!\030A Plague Upon Thee\0312,1,105,2,259,1,11615\0302,107,239,2,321,3,11615\0302,241,261,2,257,2,11615\0302,266,331,2,257,1,11615\0302,333,404,2,257,1,11615\0302,406,436,2,257,1,11615\0303,1,71,2,384,1,11615\0303,73,177,2,384,1,11615\0301,1,25,4,272,3,11615\0301,27,36,4,272,1,11615\0301,41,90,4,272,4,11615\0304,1,33,3,256,2,11615\0304,35,86,3,256,1,11615\0304,91,177,3,256,1,11615\03114528,2,1,Precious\03011615,2,8,Mickey Levine\0312,85,1420,0,\0302,0,0,1,Scarlet Crusade\0302,0,0,4,Plaguewood\0302,0,0,4,Eastern Plaguelands\0302,0,0,7,Eastern Plaguelands\0302,0,0,8,Mickey Levine\0302,0,0,8,Bulwark\0302,0,0,8,Tirisfal Glades\0315902,23,5902,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,15043,OBJECTIVE,100,15,",[5902]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The termites are obviously getting restless as you place the barrel on top of the crate.\030Now that we have plenty of termites, take this steel reinforced barrel to the Northridge Lumber Mill south of Hearthglen--you'll find it to the west of the road that leads you up to the town.$B$BOnce there, place the barrel in the center of the lumber mill; someplace high, like on a crate or something.$B$BAfter you open it, the rest should take care of itself. Just come back here and I'll reward you for helping me.\030Find someplace suitable in the center of the Northridge Lumber Mill in Western Plaguelands to place the Barrel of Plagueland Termites.\030\030A Plague Upon Thee\0312,1,191,2,257,1,11615\0302,196,303,2,257,1,11615\0302,308,362,2,257,1,11615\0302,364,418,2,257,1,11615\0303,1,134,2,384,1,11615\0301,1,88,4,272,1,0\031\0312,85,1420,0,\0302,0,0,1,Northridge Lumber Mill\0302,0,0,1,Hearthglen--you'll\0302,0,0,5,Western Plaguelands\0315901,19,5901,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306390,23,6390,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,177491,FINISHER,?,12,Termite Barrel",[5903]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031These will do nicely, $N. Thank you.$B$BIf you're ready, we can get on with the next step.\030I've tried many times to rout out the Scarlet Crusade through force alone, but to no avail. So, as an alternative, I've decided to make their lives more difficult.$B$BIf you are willing to help, I want to infest that lumber mill with the most terrible species of termites ever found.$B$BIn Plaguewood, near the once-great Stratholme, there is a breed that survived the plague and the Scourge combined. Find their mounds and fill this jar with them, so we can prepare them to be unleashed on the Crusade.\030Use the Empty Termite Jar on the Termite Mounds in Eastern Plaguelands. After you've gathered 100 Plagueland Termites, return to Nathaniel Dumah at Chillwind Camp in Western Plaguelands.\030Did you find the termite mounds, $N? I've heard they are all over Plaguewood.\030A Plague Upon Thee\0312,1,91,2,257,1,11616\0302,93,163,2,257,1,11616\0302,168,283,2,259,4,11616\0302,288,401,2,325,1,11616\0302,403,503,2,257,1,11616\0303,1,71,2,384,1,11616\0303,73,186,2,384,1,11616\0301,1,25,4,272,3,11616\0301,27,36,4,272,1,11616\0301,41,90,4,272,4,11616\0304,1,36,3,256,2,11616\0304,38,77,3,256,1,11616\03111616,2,7,Nathaniel Dumah\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,6,Eastern Plaguelands\0302,0,0,7,Nathaniel Dumah\0302,0,0,7,Chillwind Camp\0302,0,0,7,Western Plaguelands\0315904,23,5904,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,15043,OBJECTIVE,100,15,",[5904]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The termites are obviously getting restless as you place the barrel on top of the crate.\030Now that we have the termites, take this steel reinforced barrel to the Northridge Lumber Mill south of Hearthglen--you'll find it to the west of the road that leads you up to the town.$B$BOnce there, place the barrel in the center of the lumber mill; find someplace suitable, like on a crate and then open it. The termites should do their work from there and make the mill useless to the Crusade.\030Find someplace suitable in the center of the Northridge Lumber Mill in Western Plaguelands to place the Barrel of Plagueland Termites.\030\030A Plague Upon Thee\0312,1,185,2,257,1,11616\0302,190,310,2,257,1,11616\0302,312,397,2,257,1,11616\0303,1,134,2,384,1,11616\0301,1,88,4,272,1,0\031\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,1,Northridge Lumber Mill\0302,0,0,1,Hearthglen--you'll\0302,0,0,3,Crusade\0302,0,0,4,Western Plaguelands\0315903,19,5903,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306389,23,6389,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,177491,FINISHER,?,12,Termite Barrel",[591]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You retrieved the eye! Your might is the stuff of legends, $N!$B$BAnd in getting the Eye, you must have defeated Mai'Zoth and sent him to the Nether. That is why the spirits would not mention him before.$B$BIt is good that he is gone from the world of flesh and bone, but now that he is in the realm of spirits...I fear he will begin a new reign.$B$BBut that is a worry for another time. Now, I must perform a ritual to bend the Mind's Eye to our needs...\030The Mind's Eye is held by an ogre mage, east of here and deep within the Mosh'Ogg ogre mound.  His name is Mai'Zoth.  I know him from when the Darkspears dwelt in Stranglethorn - he is vicious, and his magic is strong.$B$BAnd if he has the Mind's Eye, then his magic will be stronger still.$B$BYou must face Mai'Zoth and wrest from him the Mind's Eye.  It is a perilous task, but it is the only hope we have of saving Yenniku.\030Bring the Mind's Eye to Kin'weelay at the Grom'gol Base Camp.\030Greetings, $N. The spirits sing praise of your bravery, yet they tell me no tales of your quest against Mai'Zoth.$B$BDo you have the Eye?\030The Mind's Eye\0312,1,93,2,257,1,2519\0302,96,116,2,257,1,2519\0302,119,218,2,257,1,2519\0302,223,290,2,257,4,2519\0302,295,351,2,257,1,2519\0302,354,426,2,259,3,2519\0303,1,61,2