You say you saw my Sully pinned beneath the icy waters? Say it isn't so!$B$BLet me read what he wrote....\030The waterlogged and war-torn envelope dissolves in your hands, leaving you with a few pages of a letter in your grasp, written with painstaking care.$B$BThe letter is addressed to a Mrs. Sara Balloo of Ironforge and begins, \"My dear Sara....\"\030Deliver Sully Balloo's Letter to Sara Balloo.\030You look as though you have traveled a great distance and seen much turmoil in your time, $C. These times we live in are trying on the soul. What news do you bring to me now?\030Sully Balloo's Letter\0312,1,149,2,261,1,0\0302,154,186,2,257,1,0\0302,188,242,2,257,1,0\0303,1,45,2,384,1,0\0301,1,55,4,272,2,2695\0301,57,72,4,272,1,2695\0301,77,105,4,272,1,2695\0304,1,93,3,256,1,2695\0304,95,140,3,256,1,2695\0304,142,174,3,256,2,2695\0312695,2,3,Sara Balloo\0302695,2,4,Sara Balloo\0312,1537,1455,0,\0302,0,0,4,Sara Balloo\031683,23,683,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4433,STARTER,?,10,",[638]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031How you doing, $C? The task set before us by Vol'jin will be a difficult one, and any assistance you might provide will be appreciated and necessary.\030With Thoras Trollbane dead and Stromgarde in ruins, Vol'jin has instructed that we make every effort to spirit the legendary sword Trol'kalar from the humans' hands, so that we might use it in our coming battles against the trolls of Zul'Gurub.$B$BZengu, one of our seasoned hunters, was dispatched to Hammerfall in northeastern Arathi Highlands to oversee its procurement.\030Travel to Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands and speak with Zengu.\030\030Trollbane\0312,1,244,2,323,4,2497\0302,249,373,2,257,1,2497\0303,1,66,2,384,1,2497\0301,1,18,4,272,2,2703\0301,20,149,4,272,4,2703\03110540,2,1,Vol'jin\0302703,2,2,Zengu\0302703,2,3,Zengu\03010540,4,5,Vol'jin\0312,33,1434,0,\0302,0,0,2,Hammerfall\0302,0,0,3,Hammerfall\0302,0,0,3,Arathi Highlands\031639,23,639,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030639,24,639,UNKNOWN\031",[6381]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030requestItems\030title\031This is great victory for the land. In time, other things will come to pass: the Venture Co. will pack up their buzz saws and axes, the angry fire spirits will calm, and the harpies will be pushed out by the land.$B$BOnly then $N, will Stonetalon be truly at peace.$B$BYou have done well $C; take one of these items as thanks for the new life you have created here today.\030As you have seen, $c, though the land is in pain, the cycle of life is a powerful thing. Now we must do our part help it along. You must plant these seeds at the center of the destruction, to the west, in the Charred Vale. Beware, for harpies and angry fire elementals still plague the scarred land.$B$B$N, take these enchanted Gaea seeds and plant them in fertile mounds of soil. The cycle of life must go on!\030Plant 10 Gaea Seeds in Gaea Dirt Mounds, and then return the remaining Enchanted Gaea Seeds to Tammra at Sun Rock Retreat.\030\030Gaea seed planted\030These seeds you plant are strong, resisting corruption, and making a foothold for other life. They will grow and grow, first preventing corruption and healing the scarred land, and then one day, restoring Stonetalon to a lush forest, once again.$B$BHave you planted all of the Gaea seeds?\030New Life\0312,1,88,2,257,1,11864\0302,90,127,2,257,1,11864\0302,129,222,2,257,1,11864\0302,224,299,2,261,1,11864\0302,304,380,2,257,1,11864\0302,382,410,2,257,1,11864\0303,1,122,2,384,1,11864\0301,1,35,4,272,1,11864\0301,37,92,4,272,3,11864\0301,94,213,4,272,3,11864\0301,218,265,4,280,3,11864\0301,270,371,4,272,1,11864\0306,1,93,3,260,1,11864\0306,95,245,3,260,3,11864\0306,250,288,3,256,2,11864\0305,1,17,3,384,1,11864\031\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,3,Charred Vale\0302,0,0,7,Gaea Dirt Mounds\0302,0,0,7,Tammra\0302,0,0,7,Sun Rock Retreat\0316301,19,6301,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,177929,OBJECTIVE,10,14,Gaea Dirt Mound\030SPELL,20269,OBJECTIVE,?,17,",[6382]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Welcome to the new frontier, $N.  Ashenvale is a land of opportunity, one where a young $C like yourself is able to find boundless chances to prove their mettle.  Look around the outpost here, and be sure to travel out to the Zoram Strand, as the Horde has another outpost there as well.$B$BYour presence here tells me that you've come to learn more about the hunt.  Listen close, and I will gladly share with you what you need to know.\030Your strength impresses me, $c.  Your willingness to embrace the hunt gives me confidence that you could move on to bigger game... and bigger challenges.$B$BThe forests of Ashenvale represent a vast untamed wild that the Horde seeks to impose its own will upon, both politically and spiritually.  If you seek to prove yourself in an unproven land, seek the guidance of Senani Thunderheart in Splintertree Post.  The outpost is due north of the path leading from the Barrens.\030Speak with Senani Thunderheart at Splintertree Post, Ashenvale.\030\030The Ashenvale Hunt\0312,1,31,2,257,1,3387\0302,34,130,2,257,4,3387\0302,132,153,2,257,1,3387\0302,158,295,2,259,3,3387\0302,298,410,2,259,4,3387\0302,413,474,2,257,1,3387\0303,1,63,2,384,1,3387\0301,1,32,4,272,1,12696\0301,35,161,4,272,1,12696\0301,164,287,4,272,1,12696\0301,292,365,4,272,1,12696\0301,368,436,4,274,3,12696\03112696,2,5,Senani Thunderheart\0309084,2,5,Thunderheart\03012696,2,7,Senani Thunderheart\0309084,2,7,Thunderheart\0312,17,1413,0,\0302,0,0,5,Splintertree Post\0302,0,0,6,Barrens\0302,0,0,7,Splintertree Post\0304,0,0,10,Zoram Strand\031235,22,235,UNKNOWN\030742,22,742,UNKNOWN\0306383,24,6383,UNKNOWN\031",[6383]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031There are three legendary creatures that make up the Ashenvale Hunt; you may seek them and test yourself against their cunning and might.  In the process, you will hopefully learn something about yourself.  The creatures are: the bear Ursangous, the nightsaber cat Shadumbra, and the hippogryph Sharptalon.$B$BThe creatures of the Ashenvale Hunt are powerful, and you may find that you'll need aid in bringing them down.  If you should best them, bring me proof of your deed.\030\030\030\030The Ashenvale Hunt\0311,1,137,4,274,4,12696\0301,140,205,4,272,3,12696\0301,208,306,4,272,1,12696\0301,311,420,4,274,1,12696\0301,423,475,4,272,4,12696\03112678,4,3,Ursangous\0302042,4,3,Nightsaber\03012677,4,3,Shadumbra\03012676,4,3,Sharptalon\0312,331,1440,0,\031\031",[6384]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh, wonderful! Those are fine cuts! These are from Zargh, are they? That orc sure knows his way into a lady's heart...$B$BOh, I can't wait to cook it. But not too much! Meat is best served rare, don't you think?\030For just a few coins I will have a wind rider bring you to Orgrimmar.  When you get there, you can take Zargh's Meats to Gryshka.  Her inn is in the Valley of Strength, not far from the Skytower, where my wind rider will drop you off.$B$BSpeak with me again when you are ready for the journey.\030Buy a wind rider to Orgrimmar from the wind rider master Devrak, then bring Zargh's Meats to Gryshka in Orgrimmar.\030Something smells good! You don't have raw meat on you, do you?\030Ride to Orgrimmar\0312,1,69,2,257,3,3615\0302,72,129,2,257,1,3615\0302,132,234,2,257,3,3615\0302,239,293,2,257,1,3615\0303,1,114,2,384,1,3615\0301,1,14,4,272,1,6929\0301,16,35,4,272,1,6929\0301,37,67,4,272,2,6929\0301,69,118,4,272,1,6929\0301,123,150,4,272,1,6929\0301,152,168,4,272,1,6929\0301,170,211,4,272,2,6929\0304,1,22,3,256,1,6929\0304,24,62,3,256,2,6929\0312224,2,1,Wind Rider\0302224,2,3,Wind Rider\0302224,2,5,Wind Rider\0303615,2,5,Devrak\0303489,4,8,Zargh\0312,17,1413,0,\0302,0,0,1,Orgrimmar\0302,0,0,2,Gryshka\0302,0,0,3,Valley of Strength\0302,0,0,3,Skytower\0302,0,0,5,Orgrimmar\0302,0,0,5,Gryshka\0302,0,0,5,Orgrimmar\0304,0,0,8,Zargh\0316365,19,6365,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306385,23,6385,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6385]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have to get this to the Crossroads in the Barrens? Yes, I can get you there...\030I've written a letter of thanks to Zargh.  Will you deliver it for me?  If you've already been to the Crossroads and spoken with their wind rider master, then you can fly a wind rider back there.$B$BTake my letter to Doras, the wind rider master of Orgrimmar, and speak with him about transport to the Crossroads.\030Bring Gryshka's Letter to Doras in Orgrimmar.\030Do you need one of my wind riders?\030Doras the Wind Rider Master\0312,1,41,2,257,1,6929\0302,44,70,2,257,2,6929\0302,73,195,2,257,4,6929\0302,200,313,2,257,1,6929\0303,1,45,2,384,1,6929\0301,1,54,4,272,2,3310\0301,56,82,4,272,1,3310\0304,1,34,3,258,2,3310\0313489,2,1,Zargh\0302224,2,3,Wind Rider\0303310,2,4,Doras\0302224,2,4,Wind Rider\0303310,2,5,Doras\0312,17,1413,0,\0302,0,0,1,Zargh\0302,0,0,3,Crossroads\0302,0,0,4,Doras\0302,0,0,4,Crossroads\0302,0,0,5,Doras\0302,0,0,5,Orgrimmar\0304,0,0,6,Crossroads\0304,0,0,6,Barrens\0316384,19,6384,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306386,23,6386,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6386]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hah! I guess she liked it! Nothing brings red to a lady's cheeks like a big, juicy steak!$B$BThank you, $N. You've done me a great service. Here is some money for your trouble, and don't be surprised if I invite you to my wedding!\030My wind riders are trained to fly to many different places, as long as you have already been to that place and spoken with the wind rider master there.$B$BYou have been to the Crossroads and spoken to their wind rider master Devrak, so now you can fly directly to him from here.  Once you're at the Crossroads, you can deliver Gryshka's letter to Zargh.$B$BSpeak with me when you are ready to go.\030Buy a wind rider to the Crossroads from the wind rider master Doras, then bring Gryshka's Letter to Zargh at the Crossroads.\030Have you returned from Orgrimmar? Did Gryshka like the meat I sent her?\030Return to the Crossroads.\0312,1,151,2,257,1,3310\0302,156,278,2,257,1,3310\0302,281,353,2,257,1,3310\0302,358,396,2,257,1,3310\0303,1,124,2,384,1,3310\0301,1,4,4,272,1,3489\0301,6,26,4,272,1,3489\0301,28,89,4,272,1,3489\0301,94,107,4,272,1,3489\0301,109,139,4,272,1,3489\0301,141,230,4,272,4,3489\0304,1,33,3,256,2,3489\0304,35,71,3,256,2,3489\0312224,2,1,Wind Rider\0302224,2,2,Wind Rider\0303615,2,2,Devrak\0303489,2,3,Zargh\0302224,2,5,Wind Rider\0303310,2,5,Doras\0303489,2,5,Zargh\0312,17,1413,0,\0302,0,0,2,Crossroads\0302,0,0,3,Crossroads\0302,0,0,3,Zargh\0302,0,0,5,Crossroads\0302,0,0,5,Zargh\0302,0,0,5,Crossroads\0303,0,0,12,Orgrimmar\0316385,19,6385,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6387]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have to get this to Ironforge, eh? For a small fee I can put you on the back of one of my gryphons, and it'll take you there. How does that sound?\030I see a lot of young dwarves at my door, eager to learn the trade of mining.  And if there's one thing a miner needs more than anything, it's a pick!$B$BI have a list of mining students who scored high in their lessons and earned an honorary pick.  Take my list to Golnir Bouldertoe in Ironforge.  He'll get the picks ready.$B$BThe fastest way to Ironforge is on a gryphon, so bring the list to our gryphon master, Thorgrum Borrelson, and speak with him about transport to Ironforge.\030Bring Brock's List to Thorgrum Borrelson in Thelsamar.\030Have you had your fill of Thelsamar so soon? Are you ready to leave for another city?\030Honor Students\0312,1,76,2,257,1,1681\0302,79,149,2,259,4,1681\0302,154,247,2,257,1,1681\0302,250,296,2,257,1,1681\0302,299,324,2,257,1,1681\0302,329,483,2,257,1,1681\0303,1,54,2,384,1,1681\0301,1,38,4,272,2,1572\0301,40,129,4,272,1,1572\0301,131,150,4,272,2,1572\0304,1,44,3,256,2,1572\0304,46,85,3,256,2,1572\0314256,2,4,Golnir Bouldertoe\0301572,2,6,Thorgrum Borrelson\0301572,2,7,Thorgrum Borrelson\0312,38,1432,0,\0302,0,0,4,Golnir Bouldertoe\0302,0,0,4,Ironforge\0302,0,0,6,Ironforge\0302,0,0,6,Ironforge\0302,0,0,7,Thorgrum Borrelson\0302,0,0,7,Thelsamar\0304,0,0,8,Ironforge\0316391,23,6391,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6388]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have to get these to Thelsamar, eh? That won't be a problem. As long as you've already been to Thelsamar and spoken to Thorgrum Borrelson, then you can take one of my gryphons back to him.\030Here are the honorary picks for Brock's students.  If you've already been to Thelsamar, then you should fly a gryphon back there!$B$BTake the picks to our gryphon master, Gryth Thurden, and speak with him about a ride back to Thelsamar.\030Bring the Honorary Picks to Gryth Thurden in Ironforge.\030You look like you have somewhere to go. Need one of my gryphons?\030Gryth Thurden\0312,1,49,2,257,1,4256\0302,52,129,2,257,4,4256\0302,134,236,2,257,1,4256\0303,1,55,2,384,1,4256\0301,1,39,4,272,2,1573\0301,41,64,4,276,1,1573\0301,66,192,4,272,1,1573\0304,1,39,3,256,1,1573\0304,41,64,3,256,2,1573\0311573,2,3,Gryth Thurden\0301573,2,4,Gryth Thurden\0301572,4,7,Thorgrum Borrelson\0312,38,1432,0,\0302,0,0,2,Thelsamar\0302,0,0,3,Thelsamar\0302,0,0,4,Gryth Thurden\0302,0,0,4,Ironforge\0304,0,0,5,Thelsamar\0304,0,0,7,Thelsamar\0304,0,0,7,Thorgrum Borrelson\0316391,19,6391,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306392,23,6392,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6389]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Haha! Thank you, $N! You've done it! My father's spirit can now rest and I can live in peace.$B$BThank you again. If there is anything I can do for you, please, just ask.\030You look around the lumber mill for something suitable to open the barrel with. You find a crowbar that looks like it will do the trick.$B$BYou set your feet and pray that you'll be able to get out of the mill before the termites get to you.\030Release the Plagueland Termites in the Northridge Lumber Mill, then return with the Barrel of Plagueland Termites to Nathaniel Dumah at Chillwind Camp in Western Plaguelands.\030Have you done it, $N? Have you released the termites? The Light help us if the Scarlet Crusade were able to hold onto both the mill and Hearthglen. They should have neither. They're just capitalizing on the victims of the last war and should be put down like rabid animals!\030A Plague Upon Thee\0312,1,79,2,257,1,0\0302,81,136,2,257,3,0\0302,141,241,2,257,1,0\0303,1,174,2,384,1,0\0301,1,5,4,272,1,11616\0301,7,20,4,272,1,11616\0301,22,36,4,272,1,11616\0301,38,93,4,280,1,11616\0301,98,113,4,272,1,11616\0301,115,170,4,272,4,11616\0304,1,21,3,256,2,11616\0304,23,53,3,256,2,11616\0304,55,147,3,256,4,11616\0304,149,173,3,256,1,11616\0304,175,273,3,260,1,11616\03111616,2,4,Nathaniel Dumah\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,4,Northridge Lumber Mill\0302,0,0,4,Nathaniel Dumah\0302,0,0,4,Chillwind Camp\0302,0,0,4,Western Plaguelands\0315904,19,5904,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,177491,GIVER,?,9,Termite Barrel",[639]="PARTIAL\031consequences\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Excellent, mon. That's a good start to collecting the sigils we'll need to remove Trol'kalar from Trollbane's tomb.\030In ancient times, trolls fought against the Arathorian Empire and our most capable adversary, Lord Ignaeus of Strom, named Trollbane. He rode into battle wielding Trol'kalar--troll slayer, in their ancient tongue.$B$BBut now the sons of Trollbane are weakened, their stronghold brought to ruin.$B$BThe sword is protected by several sigils that were divided among the survivors of Stromgarde, and we must retrieve them.$B$BThe first was taken by the Syndicate, one of their men in Stromgarde should have it.\030Get the Sigil of Strom for Zengu in Hammerfall.\030Have you located the first sigil yet? It is most likely carried on the person of one of the Syndicate agents in Stromgarde.\030Sigil of Strom\0312,1,133,2,321,1,2703\0302,135,213,2,325,1,2703\0302,218,294,2,257,1,2703\0302,299,418,2,265,1,2703\0302,423,506,2,257,1,2703\0303,1,47,2,384,1,2703\0301,1,15,4,272,1,2703\0301,17,115,4,274,1,2703\0304,1,37,3,256,2,2703\0304,39,123,3,256,1,2703\0312703,2,6,Zengu\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,5,Stromgarde\0302,0,0,6,Hammerfall\0304,0,0,8,Trollbane's\0303,0,0,10,Stromgarde\031640,23,640,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4440,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6390]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, $N. Here, take this coin. I'm sorry it's not more, but try to take some joy in helping destroy the Scarlet Crusade's efforts!\030You look around the lumber mill for something suitable to open the barrel with. You find a crowbar that looks like it will do the trick.$B$BYou set your feet and pray that you'll be able to get out of the mill before the termites get to you.\030Release the Plagueland Termites in the Northridge Lumber Mill, then return with the Barrel of Plagueland Termites to Mickey Levine at the Bulwark in Tirisfal Glades.\030Have you done it, $N? Have you released the termites in the lumber mill?$B$BIt was bad enough that my family lost their jobs and lives, but then to see the place where my childhood was spent taken over by those disgusting so-called holy men... pfah!!\030A Plague Upon Thee\0312,1,79,2,257,1,0\0302,81,136,2,257,3,0\0302,141,241,2,257,1,0\0303,1,165,2,384,1,0\0301,1,14,4,272,1,11615\0301,16,36,4,272,1,11615\0301,38,136,4,276,1,11615\0304,1,21,3,256,2,11615\0304,23,72,3,256,2,11615\0304,77,243,3,260,1,11615\0304,245,250,3,256,1,11615\03111615,2,4,Mickey Levine\0312,28,1422,0,\0302,0,0,4,Northridge Lumber Mill\0302,0,0,4,Mickey Levine\0302,0,0,4,Bulwark\0302,0,0,4,Tirisfal Glades\0315902,19,5902,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,177491,GIVER,?,9,Termite Barrel",[6391]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, the lastest list of Brock's best pupils. I have a batch of honorary picks ready to go. I just need to chisel in the names of the students...\030For just a few coins, one of my gryphons will take you to Ironforge.  From there, deliver Brock's list to Golnir Bouldertoe.  You'll find him in the Deep Mountain Mining Guild.  That's in the Great Forge District of Ironforge, which is right where my gryphon will drop you off!$B$BSpeak to me again when you're ready for the journey.\030Buy a gryphon to Ironforge from the gryphon master Thorgrum Borrelson, then bring Brock's List to Golnir Bouldertoe in Ironforge.\030What can I do for you, sir?\030Ride to Ironforge\0312,1,68,2,257,3,1572\0302,71,124,2,257,1,1572\0302,127,176,2,257,1,1572\0302,179,277,2,257,3,1572\0302,282,333,2,257,1,1572\0303,1,129,2,384,1,1572\0301,1,44,4,272,1,4256\0301,46,90,4,272,1,4256\0301,92,144,4,274,1,4256\0304,1,27,3,256,2,4256\0314256,2,2,Golnir Bouldertoe\0301572,2,6,Thorgrum Borrelson\0304256,2,6,Golnir Bouldertoe\0312,38,1432,0,\0302,0,0,1,Ironforge\0302,0,0,2,Golnir Bouldertoe\0302,0,0,3,Deep Mountain Mining Guild\0302,0,0,4,Great Forge District of Ironforge\0302,0,0,6,Ironforge\0302,0,0,6,Golnir Bouldertoe\0302,0,0,6,Ironforge\0316387,19,6387,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306388,23,6388,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6392]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You brought the picks. Great! I'll get these to my mining students. I'm sure they're eager to use them on the ore deposits of Loch Modan.$B$BThank you for your help, $N. I am in your debt, but I hope this money will at least cover your travel costs.\030For a small fee you can buy a gryphon ride to Thelsamar... as long as you've already been there.  Gryphons will only fly you to places you've already been, so be sure to speak with every gryphon master you see so you can fly to him later.$B$BYou've already been to Thorgrum, the gryphon master of Thelsamar, so now you can return to him.  And once in Thelsamar, you can deliver the picks to Brock Stoneseeker.$B$BSpeak with me when you're ready to go.\030Buy a gryphon to Thelsamar from the gryphon master Gryth Thurden, then bring the Honorary Picks to Brock Stoneseeker in Thelsamar.\030Ah, $N. Have you returned from Ironforge?\030Return to Brock\0312,1,58,2,257,1,1573\0302,60,96,2,257,1,1573\0302,99,238,2,257,3,1573\0302,243,337,2,257,1,1573\0302,340,409,2,257,1,1573\0302,414,451,2,257,1,1573\0303,1,130,2,384,1,1573\0301,1,22,4,272,1,1681\0301,24,29,4,272,1,1681\0301,31,67,4,272,1,1681\0301,69,137,4,272,1,1681\0301,142,169,4,272,1,1681\0301,171,249,4,274,3,1681\0304,9,41,3,256,2,1681\0311681,2,5,Brock Stoneseeker\0301573,2,7,Gryth Thurden\0301681,2,7,Brock Stoneseeker\0312,38,1432,0,\0302,0,0,1,Thelsamar\0302,0,0,4,Thorgrum\0302,0,0,5,Thelsamar\0302,0,0,5,Brock Stoneseeker\0302,0,0,7,Thelsamar\0302,0,0,7,Brock Stoneseeker\0302,0,0,7,Thelsamar\0303,0,0,14,Ironforge\0316388,19,6388,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6393]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The water spirits within me bubble with the excitement. $N, you have given me a glorious victory to report to the Tribunal of the Tides.$B$BFor your efforts, I reward you with a choice of my prized possessions.\030The Tribunal of the Tides has sent me to wage war on the fire elementals here in Stonetalon Mountain. Neptulon the Tidehunter, Lord of all water elementals, has taken a personal interest in seeing our fiery cousins extinguished.$B$B$N, you can help me gain favor with the Tribunal by destroying the fire elementals in Charred Vale. When destroyed, the fire elementals leave Incendrites. Return these to me and be rewarded.\030Bring 10 Incendrites to Tsunaman at Sun Rock Retreat.\030The Tribunal of the Tides grows impatient. They seek to end this war that has raged across all dimensions for eons. My brethren are anxious to hear news of the glorious victory over the hated fire elementals. Have you the Incendrites that I require?\030Elemental War\0312,1,101,2,261,1,11862\0302,103,228,2,257,1,11862\0302,233,331,2,261,1,11862\0302,333,386,2,261,1,11862\0302,388,422,2,257,1,11862\0303,1,53,2,384,1,11862\0301,1,55,4,272,1,11862\0301,57,136,4,272,1,11862\0301,141,210,4,272,1,11862\0304,1,42,3,256,1,11862\0304,44,115,3,262,1,11862\0304,117,208,3,256,1,11862\0304,210,249,3,256,2,11862\03111862,2,6,Tsunaman\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,1,Stonetalon Mountain\0302,0,0,3,Charred Vale\0302,0,0,6,Tsunaman\0302,0,0,6,Sun Rock Retreat\0304,0,0,8,Tribunal of the Tides\031\031ITEM,16312,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[6394]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Great, you got it! Thanks a lot, $N. This is my favorite pick! Now if my peons ever finish chopping down these trees, maybe we can find a nice cave to mine!\030$N, you are a dependable $r.  Can I count on you for another task?$B$BSome time ago I was surveying the cave to the north for minerals, and I left my favorite pick behind.  When I later returned to retrieve it I found the cave was filled with vicious beasts!  Will you go into the cave, the Burning Blade Coven, and get my pick?$B$BI left it in a chamber with waterfalls.  My pick has a spell on it so you can see it in the dark, so you won't have to worry about finding it... just what's guarding it!\030Bring Thazz'ril's Pick to Foreman Thazz'ril.\030Have you entered the Burning Blade Coven, $N? Did you find my pick?\030Thazz'ril's Pick\0312,1,28,2,257,1,11378\0302,31,66,2,257,2,11378\0302,71,171,2,257,1,11378\0302,174,258,2,257,1,11378\0302,261,328,2,257,2,11378\0302,333,371,2,257,1,11378\0302,374,476,2,257,1,11378\0302,478,501,2,257,1,11378\0303,1,44,2,384,1,11378\0301,1,18,4,272,1,11378\0301,20,36,4,272,1,11378\0301,38,62,4,272,1,11378\0301,64,156,4,272,4,11378\0304,1,45,3,256,2,11378\0304,47,67,3,256,2,11378\03111378,2,9,Foreman Thazz'ril\0312,363,1411,0,\0302,0,0,9,Foreman Thazz'ril\0315441,19,5441,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,16332,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6395]="PARTIAL\031consequences\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030requestItems\030title\031You have done a good deed today, $N. Although our struggle against the Scourge continues, let us hope that Marla and Samuel will find peace together in their final resting place.\030My friend Marla Fipps lived with her husband Samuel before the plague, but when the plague came Samuel succumbed and joined the Scourge's ranks.$B$BMarla was spared an undeath only to die at the hands of her now mindless husband.  So strong was her love, however, that her last dying wish was to be buried with her beloved Samuel.$B$BSamuel Fipps roams at a ruined camp along the road northeast of Deathknell.  Defeat him and grant Marla's wish: bury him at her grave, in the first row of our graveyard.\030Bring Samuel Fipps' Remains to Marla's Grave, then return to Novice Elreth.\030\030Samuel's Remains Buried\030We must respect our dead, $N. It is one of the ways in which we differ from the Scourge...\030Marla's Last Wish\0312,1,144,2,325,1,1661\0302,149,229,2,257,1,1661\0302,232,330,2,259,3,1661\0302,335,409,2,257,1,1661\0302,412,503,2,257,3,1661\0303,1,75,2,384,1,1661\0301,1,36,4,272,1,1661\0301,38,178,4,346,3,1661\0306,1,29,3,256,1,1661\0306,31,90,3,320,1,1661\0305,1,23,3,384,1,1661\0311919,2,4,Samuel Fipps\0301919,2,6,Samuel Fipps\0301661,2,6,Novice Elreth\0312,154,1420,0,\0302,0,0,6,Marla's Grave\0302,0,0,6,Novice Elreth\0303,0,0,10,Scourge\031376,19,376,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,178090,OBJECTIVE,1,14,Marla's Grave\030SPELL,20364,OBJECTIVE,?,17,",[64]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031My watch! Thank you so much, kind sir! $B$BWe are but poor farmers and we have lost our land but please accept this reward as a token of our appreciation.\030It was horrible!  Verna woke me when she heard a ruckus in the fields.  The fields were full of hooligans.  We left in a rush and I forgot to pack my pocket watch.  Verna's pa gave me that watch on our wedding day and I feel just sick knowing those thieves have it.  I left the pocket watch in the wardrobe at the farmhouse.  Look for the field of pumpkins to the West -- you can't miss it.  If you bring it back to me, I'd sure be grateful!\030Farmer Furlbrow wants you to retrieve his pocket watch from the wardrobe in his farmhouse at the pumpkin farm to the West.\030Don't suppose you were able to get my watch?\030The Forgotten Heirloom\0312,1,16,2,257,1,237\0302,19,70,2,257,1,237\0302,73,106,2,257,1,237\0302,109,163,2,257,1,237\0302,166,265,2,257,1,237\0302,268,324,2,257,1,237\0302,327,390,2,257,1,237\0302,393,441,2,257,4,237\0303,1,122,2,386,1,237\0301,1,9,4,272,1,237\0301,11,38,4,272,1,237\0301,44,154,4,276,1,237\0304,1,44,3,256,2,237\031237,2,9,Farmer Furlbrow\0312,40,1436,0,\0302,0,0,7,West\0302,0,0,9,West\031\031ITEM,841,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[640]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, you need me to reconstruct this sigil? It shouldn't be too difficult... all the pieces seem to be here and the magical structure will be easy to reform.$B$BYou might want to close your eyes.\030Thoras Trollbane's tomb is protected by three sigils--the first of which you retrieved from the Syndicate. The other two will be harder to get, as they're held by the firmly entrenched Stromgarde militia.$B$BThe sigil of Thoradin was divided into five pieces by Thoras' son, Galen, and dispersed among the Stromgarde defenders. Retrieve the pieces and bring them to Tor'gan, the troll shaman, he will be able to bind them into the complete sigil.\030Retrieve the 5 Sigil Fragments from the defenders in Stromgarde, and bring them to Tor'gan in Hammerfall.\030Throm'ka, $c. Zengu informed me that you required my assistance?\030The Broken Sigil\0312,1,106,2,257,1,2703\0302,108,204,2,257,3,2703\0302,209,327,2,257,1,2703\0302,329,446,2,257,3,2703\0303,1,105,2,384,1,2703\0301,1,42,4,274,2,2706\0301,44,75,4,272,1,2706\0301,77,156,4,272,4,2706\0301,161,194,4,274,4,2706\0304,1,13,3,256,1,2706\0304,15,64,3,256,2,2706\0312706,2,4,Tor'gan\0302706,2,5,Tor'gan\0302703,3,11,Zengu\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,1,Syndicate\0302,0,0,4,Tor'gan\0302,0,0,5,Stromgarde\0302,0,0,5,Tor'gan\0302,0,0,5,Hammerfall\031639,19,639,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030641,23,641,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4450,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[6401]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031My goodness, my niece Kaya is alive! That is good news indeed. Thank you, $N.\030Tell Tammra Windfield, Kaya's aunt who's at Sun Rock Retreat, about the good news! Kaya is alive! We had thought she was lost after the brutal attack on our village. Follow the path to the west to get to Sun Rock Retreat.$B$B\030Tell Tammra Windfield in Sun Rock Retreat the good news.$B\030\030Kaya's Alive\0312,1,82,2,257,1,11857\0302,84,97,2,257,1,11857\0302,99,165,2,261,1,11857\0302,167,221,2,257,1,11857\0303,1,56,2,384,1,11857\0301,1,36,4,272,1,11864\0301,38,62,4,272,1,11864\0301,64,77,4,272,1,11864\03111864,2,1,Tammra Windfield\03011864,2,5,Tammra Windfield\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,1,Sun Rock Retreat\0302,0,0,4,Sun Rock Retreat\0302,0,0,5,Sun Rock Retreat the\0316523,19,6523,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6402]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Before we begin, I ask that you first gather an army. We face a dragon, after all!\030You are to meet with Windsor at the gates of Stormwind.$B$BWhat Windsor is about to unveil will shake the very foundation of the kingdom!$B$BDo not attempt to venture there alone, $N. You must amass an army! Gather your compatriots. To arms! $B$B\030Travel to Stormwind City and venture to the city gates. Speak with Squire Rowe so that he may let Marshal Windsor know that you have arrived.\030\030Stormwind Rendezvous\0312,1,55,2,257,1,9560\0302,60,137,2,257,3,9560\0302,142,183,2,257,1,9560\0302,185,207,2,257,1,9560\0302,209,232,2,257,1,9560\0302,234,241,2,257,1,9560\0303,1,55,2,384,1,9560\0303,57,141,2,386,1,9560\0301,1,53,4,282,1,12580\0301,55,82,4,272,1,12580\03117804,2,8,Squire Rowe\0309023,2,8,Marshal Windsor\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,7,Stormwind City\0314322,19,4322,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306403,23,6403,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6403]="PARTIAL\031loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031<Bolvar holds the shattered medallion.>$B$BThe magic held within must be reignited. The dragon's eye must be attuned.$B$BWindsor's sacrifice has freed our Kingdom, but the threat of Onyxia and her kin is ever looming.$B$BThis medallion is what held my mind and body captive. It is also what gave me access to Onyxia's own mind - to her secrets. Albeit the visions are muddled now, some things I do remember.\030It has been quite the adventure, friend. I owe you a great debt of gratitude. Perhaps, when all is said and done...$B$BAs you have no doubt ascertained by now, Lady Prestor is Onyxia: Brood of Deathwing, twin to the tyrant of the Spire, Nefarian.$B$BFor too long she has held our kingdom in her captivating gaze. Even the Highlord is controlled by her trickery - a puppet. It all ends today... The spell will be broken.$B$BWorry not, for together, we shall be victorious!$B$BAre you ready?\030Follow Reginald Windsor through Stormwind. Protect him from harm!\030Reginald's March\030I... I... I was powerless.\030The Great Masquerade\0312,1,40,2,257,1,12580\0302,42,77,2,257,1,12580\0302,79,115,2,257,4,12580\0302,120,246,2,257,1,12580\0302,251,312,2,257,1,12580\0302,314,372,2,257,1,12580\0302,374,393,2,257,1,12580\0302,395,419,2,257,3,12580\0302,424,471,2,257,3,12580\0302,476,489,2,257,2,12580\0303,1,42,2,384,1,12580\0303,44,65,2,396,1,12580\0301,1,39,4,272,1,1748\0301,44,83,4,272,1,1748\0301,85,117,4,272,1,1748\0301,122,217,4,308,1,1748\0301,222,274,4,276,1,1748\0301,276,344,4,272,1,1748\0301,346,407,4,272,1,1748\0305,11,26,3,256,1,1748\0304,1,16,3,384,1,12580\03115065,2,4,Lady\03010184,2,4,Onyxia\03011583,2,4,Nefarian\03012580,2,11,Reginald Windsor\03010184,4,16,Onyxia\0312,1519,1453,0,\0304,0,0,18,Onyxia's\0316402,19,6402,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306501,23,6501,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[641]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031We're halfway to being able to remove Trol'kalar from Trollbane's tomb. We are not exactly sure where the third sigil is, as its holders seem to move around Arathi quite a bit, but I have faith that you'll be able to find it.\030The reconstruction worked flawlessly. The sigil can now be used to unlock the seal on Trollbane's tomb. Return it to Zengu, no doubt he has additional tasks for you to complete.\030Bring the restored Sigil of Thoradin to Zengu in Hammerfall.\030$N! Do you have the second sigil?\030Sigil of Thoradin\0312,1,37,2,257,1,2706\0302,39,103,2,257,1,2706\0302,105,177,2,257,1,2706\0303,1,60,2,384,1,2706\0301,1,71,4,272,1,2703\0301,73,225,4,272,4,2703\0304,5,33,3,256,2,2703\0312703,2,3,Zengu\0302703,2,4,Zengu\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,3,Zengu\0302,0,0,4,Zengu\0302,0,0,4,Hammerfall\0304,0,0,5,Trollbane's\031640,19,640,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030643,23,643,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[642]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah! You activated these shards. Already I feel more myself!$B$BBut alas, I am still far from free...\030My name is Myzrael.  I am a princess of the earth, and my captors, the giants, have trapped me deep beneath the Arathi Highlands.  These crystal shards are the only way I can speak with the surface world.$B$BPlease help me.  Allies of the giants, the Drywhisker Kobolds, have a shard like this one in their Drywhisker Gorge, to the east.  To power the cluster, you must gather Motes of Myzrael from the kobolds and apply them to it.$B$BI beg you, $N, aid me!\030Gather 12 Motes of Myzrael, then bring them to the Iridescent Shards in Drywhisker Gorge.\030This cluster of shards looks much like the Shards of Myzrael.  But the same feeling of security does not pulse through them.\030The Princess Trapped\0312,1,19,2,257,1,0\0302,22,129,2,257,1,0\0302,132,204,2,257,1,0\0302,209,223,2,257,1,0\0302,226,337,2,257,1,0\0302,340,432,2,257,1,0\0302,437,458,2,257,1,0\0303,1,89,2,384,1,0\0301,5,31,4,272,1,0\0301,33,59,4,272,1,0\0301,64,100,4,272,1,0\0304,1,61,3,256,1,0\0304,64,124,3,264,1,0\0312755,2,1,Myzrael\030330,2,2,Princess\0302755,2,6,Myzrael\0302755,2,8,Myzrael\0302755,3,12,Myzrael\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,8,Iridescent Shards\0302,0,0,8,Drywhisker Gorge\031651,23,651,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,138492,GIVER,?,9,Shards of Myzrael\030OBJECT,2701,FINISHER,?,12,Iridescent Shards\030ITEM,4435,OBJECTIVE,12,15,",[6421]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Ah... Yes! That's it; the Resonite crystals have a trace of Earthen magic. The Kobolds must have dug deep uncovering an Earthen.$B$BLegend states that the Earthen are creatures created by the Titans. They were used to create the land our feet walk on. This most definitely is a threat that cannot be ignored.$B$B<Mor'rogal shakes his head.>$B$BPerhaps I can enchant these ore samples to use against this Kobold plot.\030Something is amiss here in Stonetalon. Can you feel the tension in the air, $N?$B$BSoutheast of here lies a deep cave in Boulderslide Ravine. The kobolds there are frantically mining a rare crystal called Resonite. I need you to bring back some ore samples so that I can understand what's happening in that cave.  I also need you to investigate the depth of that cave.$B$BGo young $c, it's imperative I know what evil lurks under these mountains.\030Explore deep into the cave at Boulderslide Ravine and bring back 10 Resonite Crystals for Mor'rogal at Sun Rock Retreat to investigate.\030Investigate Cave in Boulderslide Ravine\030What news have you discovered from Boulderslide Ravine? I recall some legend that deals with Resonite... I just cannot place my hoof on it. Perhaps knowing what lies at the bottom of the cave will illuminate their devious intentions.\030Boulderslide Ravine\0312,1,38,2,257,1,11861\0302,40,79,2,257,2,11861\0302,84,141,2,257,1,11861\0302,143,214,2,257,1,11861\0302,216,312,2,259,1,11861\0302,315,368,2,259,1,11861\0302,373,446,2,257,1,11861\0303,1,135,2,384,1,11861\0301,7,10,4,272,1,11861\0301,12,74,4,272,1,11861\0301,76,128,4,272,1,11861\0301,133,199,4,336,1,11861\0301,201,251,4,272,1,11861\0301,253,308,4,276,1,11861\0301,313,340,4,272,1,11861\0301,345,416,4,272,4,11861\0305,1,55,3,256,2,11861\0305,57,104,3,256,1,11861\0305,106,139,3,256,1,11861\0305,141,233,3,256,4,11861\0304,1,39,3,384,1,11861\03111861,2,8,Mor'rogal\03011861,4,15,Mor'rogal\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,1,Stonetalon\0302,0,0,3,Boulderslide Ravine\0302,0,0,8,Boulderslide Ravine\0302,0,0,8,Sun Rock Retreat\0303,0,0,17,Boulderslide Ravine\0303,0,0,21,Boulderslide Ravine\0316481,23,6481,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,16581,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[643]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Losing their cavalry leader will prove a large blow to the Stromgarde defenders. Better yet, it means that we are only one sigil from being able to have Trol'kalar for ourselves.\030Though they can barely be said to control Stromgarde, let alone the whole of Arathi Highlands, the human prince trots the remnants of his cavalry over the countryside. I can't understand why he does it, but who understands the way the humans think, hm?$B$BWhatever his reasoning, more importantly, he has given one of the sigils to Lieutenant Valorcall, their cavalry leader. Locate him and bring his sigil back to me.\030Retrieve the Sigil of Arathor and return it to Zengu in Hammerfall.\030Valorcall will not be easy to track down, $N. Mounted on horseback, he can cover ground quickly. Nonetheless, we must have his sigil.\030Sigil of Arathor\0312,1,167,2,257,1,2703\0302,169,252,2,257,2,2703\0302,257,375,2,257,1,2703\0302,377,418,2,257,1,2703\0303,1,67,2,384,1,2703\0301,1,80,4,272,3,2703\0301,82,178,4,272,1,2703\0304,1,45,3,256,3,2703\0304,47,96,3,256,1,2703\0304,98,133,3,256,1,2703\0312612,2,3,Lieutenant Valorcall\0302703,2,5,Zengu\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,3,Lieutenant Valorcall\0302,0,0,5,Zengu\0302,0,0,5,Hammerfall\0304,0,0,6,Stromgarde\031641,19,641,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030644,23,644,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4458,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[644]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Quite a day this is, $C. The blood of Trollbane will no longer haunt my people, and the sigils needed to take Trol'kalar are in our possession. Soon, very soon, we will strike against the hated trolls of Zul'Gurub.\030The final of the sigils needed to unlock the tomb of Thoras Trollbane is held by his son personally. He resides deep within Stromgarde, in a chapel in the militia-held districts. Prince Galen is well protected and no slouch of a warrior himself, so this task could prove most difficult.\030Kill Prince Galen Trollbane and bring the Sigil of Trollbane to Zengu in Hammerfall.\030You've returned, $N. Is the line of Ignaeus Trollbane broken?\030Sigil of Trollbane\0312,1,100,2,257,1,2703\0302,102,178,2,257,1,2703\0302,180,286,2,257,4,2703\0303,1,84,2,384,1,2703\0301,1,24,4,272,1,2703\0301,26,143,4,272,3,2703\0301,145,214,4,272,3,2703\0304,1,20,3,256,1,2703\0304,22,61,3,256,2,2703\0312607,2,4,Prince Galen Trollbane\0302703,2,4,Zengu\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,2,Stromgarde\0302,0,0,4,Zengu\0302,0,0,4,Hammerfall\031643,19,643,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030645,23,645,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4466,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6441]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031These are perfect, $N! Thanks for helping me out!$B$BOh, and this is for your time...\030Heya! I've been traveling through Ashenvale, heading towards Ratchet, and decided to make a stop here at Splintertree. I'm always looking for an opportunity, and it seems that satyr horns are in high demand in Ratchet these days.$B$BAfter asking around here, it seems that the satyrs in Night Run, Satyrnaar, and Xavian all have the type of horns I am looking for. I'm no match for those satyrs... but you look like you might be!$B$BTell you what, you collect the horns for me and I'll make it worth your time.\030Collect 16 Satyr Horns for Pixel in Splintertree Post.\030I hope you can be quick about getting those horns, $N. I'm heading back to Ratchet soon!\030Satyr Horns\0312,1,5,2,257,1,12724\0302,7,118,2,257,1,12724\0302,120,229,2,257,4,12724\0302,234,364,2,257,4,12724\0302,366,397,2,257,1,12724\0302,399,429,2,257,4,12724\0302,434,510,2,257,1,12724\0303,1,54,2,384,1,12724\0301,1,22,4,272,1,12724\0301,24,49,4,272,1,12724\0301,54,85,4,272,1,12724\0304,1,54,3,258,3,12724\0304,56,88,3,256,1,12724\03112724,2,8,Pixel\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,2,Splintertree\0302,0,0,3,Ratchet the\0302,0,0,4,Night Run\0302,0,0,8,Splintertree Post\0303,0,0,13,Ratchet\031\031ITEM,5481,OBJECTIVE,16,15,",[6442]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031We could use more of your kind around here, $N. Thank you for your help.\030There is evil lurking here along the coast, $r.$B$BIt is the resting place of the doomed city of Zoram, long destroyed and submerged beneath the seas.  Lost, and nearly forgotten.$B$BNow, the naga have returned, and for what reason we do not know.  But reason matters little; we must defend the land we have worked so hard to claim as our own.$B$BReturn to me with 20 of their heads! Throw the naga back to the depths!\030Bring 20 Wrathtail Heads to Marukai along the Zoram Strand.\030The naga increase in numbers, $n. Please complete this task for me.\030Naga at the Zoram Strand\0312,1,47,2,257,1,12719\0302,52,150,2,261,1,12719\0302,153,179,2,261,1,12719\0302,184,247,2,257,1,12719\0302,250,343,2,269,1,12719\0302,348,383,2,257,1,12719\0302,385,418,2,257,1,12719\0303,1,59,2,384,1,12719\0301,1,47,4,272,4,12719\0301,49,72,4,272,1,12719\0304,1,33,3,256,1,12719\0304,35,67,3,256,1,12719\03112719,2,8,Marukai\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,8,Marukai\031\031ITEM,5490,OBJECTIVE,20,15,",[645]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Matching the lines on the face of Trollbane's tomb with the glowing lines of the Sigil of Ignaeus, a flash of light consumes the Sigil, and the legendary sword Trol'kalar is released from the stone hands' grip.\030What's this? With the four sigils brought together, they have formed together to create one sigil. There can be no doubt that this will be able to break the wardings placed upon Trollbane's tomb.$B$BTrollbane's remains are entombed in the Sanctum behind the chapel in Stromgarde. Retrieve Trol'kalar.\030Retrieve Trol'kalar from Trollbane's tomb in Stromgarde.\030Etchings in the stone upon the face of the tomb of Trollbane match the glowing lines of the Sigil of Ignaeus...\030Trol'kalar\0312,1,12,2,257,2,2703\0302,14,98,2,257,1,2703\0302,100,195,2,257,3,2703\0302,200,279,2,257,1,2703\0302,281,300,2,257,1,2703\0303,1,56,2,384,1,2703\0301,1,210,4,272,1,0\0304,1,111,3,256,1,0\031\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,4,Sanctum\0302,0,0,4,Stromgarde\0302,0,0,6,Trollbane's\0302,0,0,6,Stromgarde\031644,19,644,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030646,23,646,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,2703,FINISHER,?,12,Trollbane's Tomb",[646]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031For generations, the forces of Strom and Arathor ravaged the trolls. Now their greatest weapon is in our hands. Our inching progress in the steamy forests of Zul'Gurub will be no more.$B$BYour assistance has been great, $N, and the Darkspear trolls are indebted to you.$B$BI will be sure that the sword is delivered to Nimboya at Grom'gol.\030The light slowly fades, the sword Trol'kalar, held within a stone sheath has been released.\030Deliver Trol'kalar to Zengu in Hammerfall.\030$N! Have you taken the sword?\030Trol'kalar\0312,1,91,2,257,1,0\0303,1,42,2,384,1,0\0301,1,68,4,272,1,2703\0301,70,111,4,272,1,2703\0301,113,184,4,272,3,2703\0301,189,269,4,272,1,2703\0301,274,339,4,272,3,2703\0304,5,29,3,256,2,2703\0312703,2,2,Zengu\0302497,4,7,Nimboya\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,2,Zengu\0302,0,0,2,Hammerfall\0304,0,0,7,Nimboya\0304,0,0,7,Grom'gol\031645,19,645,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,2703,GIVER,?,9,Trollbane's Tomb",[6461]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Sweet, mon! Good news, perhaps we will have fewer unwanted dinner guests tonight.$b$bMany thanks, $N. We are forever in your debt.\030We Trolls here at Malaka'Jin have prospered from the land; Stonetalon Mountain offers great hunting for us to live on.$B$BLately, we have attracted the wrong dinner guests... the spiders in these mountains have been raiding our camps at night looking to steal our hunt.$B$BIf you were to help us kill off these ghastly beasts we at Malaka'Jin would be in your debt. Spiders are everywhere in Stonetalon - just head north from here and you will see what I am talking about.\030Xen'zilla at Malaka'Jin needs you to kill 10 Deepmoss Creepers and 7 Deepmoss Venomspitters.\030Hey mon, have you slain the hairy blood feeders? I fear none here in Stonetalon but I don't go walking around here at night... if you know what I mean mon!$B$BAs long as I stay off their dinner plate then all is well.$B$BGood luck to you, $C!\030Blood Feeders\0312,1,118,2,257,1,12816\0302,123,174,2,257,1,12816\0302,176,269,2,261,1,12816\0302,274,365,2,257,4,12816\0302,367,472,2,257,3,12816\0303,1,92,2,386,1,12816\0301,1,11,4,272,1,12816\0301,13,81,4,272,4,12816\0301,86,101,4,272,1,12816\0301,103,130,4,272,1,12816\0304,1,48,3,260,2,12816\0304,50,126,3,256,1,12816\0304,128,155,3,256,4,12816\0304,160,217,3,256,1,12816\0304,222,242,3,256,1,12816\03112816,2,6,Xen'Zilla\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,1,Malaka'Jin\0302,0,0,4,Malaka'Jin\0302,0,0,5,Stonetalon\0302,0,0,6,Malaka'Jin\0303,0,0,12,Stonetalon\031\031NPC,4005,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Deepmoss Creeper\030NPC,4007,OBJECTIVE,7,13,Deepmoss Venomspitter",[6462]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You found them! Thank you! Thank you, $N! You do not know how great a thing you have done for me.$B$BA troll without his charm is like an orc without his battle scars...$B$BWorthless.\030My kinfolk were traveling here with many sacred troll charms, but the Thistlefur furbolgs attacked and killed them before they reached Zoram'gar!  Those vile Furbolgs!$B$BI miss my brothers and sisters who were killed, but we will meet again in the afterlife.  However, their troll charms hold great value in this world.  It is an outrage that the furbolgs have them!$B$B$N, you must retrieve the charms!  They are in chests in Thistlefur Hold, a cave at the end of Thistlefur Village, north of Astranaar.\030Bring 8 Troll Charms to Mitsuwa at the Zoram'gar Outpost.\030Did you find the charms, $N?  Every moment the furbolgs possess those sacred items, my blood boils with rage!\030Troll Charm\0312,1,145,2,269,1,12721\0302,148,167,2,257,1,12721\0302,172,259,2,257,3,12721\0302,262,320,2,257,1,12721\0302,323,367,2,257,1,12721\0302,372,404,2,257,1,12721\0302,407,505,2,257,1,12721\0303,1,57,2,384,1,12721\0301,1,15,4,272,1,12721\0301,17,26,4,272,1,12721\0301,28,41,4,272,1,12721\0301,43,97,4,272,1,12721\0301,102,169,4,276,1,12721\0301,174,183,4,272,1,12721\0304,1,28,3,256,2,12721\0304,31,109,3,256,1,12721\03112721,2,8,Mitsuwa\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,7,Thistlefur Hold\0302,0,0,7,Astranaar\0302,0,0,8,Mitsuwa\0302,0,0,8,Zoram'gar Outpost\031\031ITEM,16602,OBJECTIVE,8,15,",[647]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, nothing like Foggy MacKreel's Moonshine to warm you up on a brisk day! And here I was thinking the little bugger was going to be overdue on his bills again. Thank you, friend! Many thanks indeed!\030Had quite a bit of the ol' Moonshine last night!  Longbraid would have my head if he knew that I passed out during my watch.$B$BThe noggin hurts something fierce.  Felt as though a whole brigade of siege engines passed overhead, all that rumbling.$B$BOh my, look at the time! I promised Brewmeister Bilger in Southshore that I'd repay my debt to him by sending some Moonshine.$B$BBut there are just 15 minutes left before I'm overdue!  Take him this batch, would you please?  And hurry!\030Take MacKreel's Moonshine to Brewmeister Bilger in Southshore.\030What's the good word, $R?\030MacKreel's Moonshine\0312,1,48,2,257,1,2696\0302,51,124,2,257,4,2696\0302,129,162,2,257,1,2696\0302,165,247,2,257,1,2696\0302,252,275,2,257,1,2696\0302,277,376,2,257,1,2696\0302,381,434,2,257,1,2696\0302,437,474,2,257,4,2696\0302,477,486,2,257,1,2696\0303,1,62,2,384,1,2696\0301,1,74,4,272,1,2705\0301,76,160,4,272,3,2705\0301,162,179,4,272,1,2705\0301,181,199,4,272,1,2705\0304,1,25,3,256,2,2705\0312705,2,6,Brewmeister Bilger\0302705,2,10,Brewmeister Bilger\0302696,4,11,Foggy MacKreel\0312,11,1437,0,\0302,0,0,6,Southshore\0302,0,0,10,Brewmeister Bilger\0302,0,0,10,Southshore\031\031",[648]="PARTIAL\031conflict,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Oh, YOU'RE the great savior of OOX-17/TN! I cannot even begin to express my thanks for your assistance! My homing robot series needs more developing, but your recovery has saved me countless hours of rebuilding time, as well as many gold pieces in rebinding costs!$B$BPlease, take your choice of any of these items I have. Hopefully, you will make good use of one of them. Thank you again for your generous assistance, my robots and I are in your debt!\030The gnome's voice crackles once again from the robot:$B$B\"I need to move OOX-17/TN to an open, safe place so it can begin a lengthy take-off procedure.  It has built-in cloaking, but I need time on my end to make it operational again.  I need you to escort the robot from its current location to, let's say, Steamwheedle Port!  That should be a perfect place, and long enough, to get things on line!\"$B$B\"Escort it safely to the port, and then come talk to me in Booty Bay!  Oglethorpe Obnoticus - out!\"\030Escort OOX-17/TN to Steamwheedle Port, then report to Oglethorpe Obnoticus in Booty Bay.\030Escort OOX-17/TN to Steamwheedle Port\030\030Rescue OOX-17/TN!\0312,1,53,2,257,1,7784\0302,58,151,2,259,1,7784\0302,154,234,2,259,1,7784\0302,237,326,2,259,1,7784\0302,329,400,2,257,1,7784\0302,405,473,2,257,1,7784\0302,476,503,2,257,1,7784\0303,1,88,2,384,1,7784\0301,1,41,4,272,1,7406\0301,43,103,4,272,1,7406\0301,105,264,4,370,1,7406\0301,269,322,4,272,1,7406\0301,324,372,4,272,3,7406\0301,374,452,4,272,1,7406\0304,1,37,3,384,1,7784\0317406,2,7,Oglethorpe Obnoticus\0307406,2,8,Oglethorpe Obnoticus\0312,440,1446,0,\0302,0,0,6,Booty Bay\0302,0,0,8,Steamwheedle Port\0302,0,0,8,Oglethorpe Obnoticus\0302,0,0,8,Booty Bay\0303,0,0,15,Steamwheedle Port\031351,19,351,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6481]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You bear good news, $C! I fear the possibilities of what an Earthen would mean to Kalimdor.$B$BSlaying Goggeroc was a task for no one less then a hero. You have done well; all of Stonetalon and Kalimdor are indebted to you, noble $C.$B$BAccept this as your reward most honored one.\030You have uncovered a dark threat to the land, $c. The Resonite cask you have found in that cave houses a slumbering Earthen by the name of Goggeroc.$B$BI have changed the mixture of the Resonite crystals that you gathered with my shamanistic powers. Take the enchanted Resonite crystal and smash open the Resonite cask, which houses the Earthen.$B$BWhen awakened, Goggeroc will be weakened... Slay him, $N!\030Open the Resonite cask with the Enchanted Resonite Crystal, and then slay Goggeroc. Return to Mor'rogal with the news and Enchanted Resonite Crystal.\030I fear if we do not dispose of this threat immediately, all of Stonetalon will be lost. The might of an Earthen can not be matched by any means. When awakened, Goggeroc will be weak from his long slumber, this will be the opportunity that you must take advantage of... go now $N!\030Earthen Arise\0312,1,49,2,261,1,11861\0302,51,148,2,257,1,11861\0302,153,249,2,257,1,11861\0302,251,345,2,257,1,11861\0302,350,392,2,257,3,11861\0302,394,406,2,257,1,11861\0303,1,83,2,384,1,11861\0303,85,149,2,384,1,11861\0301,1,23,4,272,1,11861\0301,25,91,4,280,4,11861\0301,96,151,4,272,1,11861\0301,153,233,4,272,1,11861\0301,238,281,4,272,1,11861\0304,1,87,3,268,4,11861\0304,89,144,3,256,4,11861\0304,146,268,3,256,3,11861\0304,270,279,3,256,1,11861\03111920,2,2,Goggeroc\03011920,2,5,Goggeroc\03011920,2,7,Goggeroc\03011861,2,8,Mor'rogal\03011920,4,11,Goggeroc\03011920,3,16,Goggeroc\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,8,Mor'rogal\0304,0,0,10,Kalimdor\0316421,19,6421,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,11920,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Goggeroc",[6482]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031You found my brother!  He was captured by the Thistlefurs?  That is terrible news to hear, for although many Furbolgs are noble creatures, the Thistlefurs are corrupt.$B$BThank you for rescuing my brother, $N.  I do not want to think of how they treated poor Ruul.  He will likely sleep long after this ordeal...\030Eh?  Who are you?$B$B$N?  You're no furbolg.  They are cursed!  They thought I was a bear and captured me, and now they starve me!  My strength is failing...$B$BHelp me escape, then speak with my sister Yama at the Splintertree Post to the east.$B$B$N! I must escape!\030Escort Ruul, then speak with Yama Snowhoof in Splintertree Post.\030Escort Ruul from the Thistlefurs.\030Have you seen my brother Ruul? He walked into the forest days ago and has not returned...\030Freedom to Ruul\0312,6,17,2,257,2,12818\0302,27,44,2,257,1,12818\0302,47,62,2,261,1,12818\0302,65,130,2,269,1,12818\0302,133,157,2,257,1,12818\0302,162,245,2,257,1,12818\0302,254,267,2,257,1,12818\0303,1,64,2,384,1,12818\0301,1,21,4,272,1,12837\0301,24,58,4,272,2,12837\0301,61,167,4,276,1,12837\0301,172,209,4,272,1,12837\0301,212,264,4,274,1,12837\0301,267,312,4,272,3,12837\0305,1,30,3,256,2,12837\0305,32,89,3,256,1,12837\0304,1,33,3,384,1,12818\03131,2,2,Furbolg\03012837,2,8,Yama Snowhoof\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,6,Splintertree Post\0302,0,0,8,Splintertree Post\0303,0,0,17,Thistlefurs\031\031",[649]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh yeah, about the ripple dad wants! He wants to sell the ripple to a tavern here in Orgrimmar, but we'll get more money if it is in its original packaging. I know someone who can do that, and he's in the Hinterlands where the ripple is. But he's, um, a high elf.$B$BWell, he's a good high elf, as he's not a part of the Alliance. Well, he's not so much a good high elf as he is a drunken high elf. He loves, and I mean LOVES the hooch.\030I've got some salvage work for you, and if you're an aficionado of fine ripple like I am, then you'll love this task.  Ripple!$B$BIt's a drink, you dummy.$B$BAn abandoned Horde outpost has a stash of Hinterlands Honey Ripple from when they were in business.  You can't get fine ripple like that anymore!  One of Malton's dummy associates knows the shot, so you'll go out there and bring me a case of packaged ripple, and two for my own collection!  Talk to Malton, he'll fill you in on the details.\030Talk to Malton Droffers in Orgrimmar.\030\030Ripple Recovery\0312,1,117,2,257,4,6986\0302,120,126,2,257,1,6986\0302,131,154,2,257,1,6986\0302,159,257,2,257,1,6986\0302,260,303,2,257,1,6986\0302,306,447,2,257,1,6986\0302,450,498,2,257,1,6986\0303,1,37,2,384,1,6986\0301,1,36,4,274,1,6987\0301,38,156,4,274,4,6987\0301,158,237,4,272,1,6987\0301,239,263,4,272,1,6987\0301,268,330,4,272,1,6987\0301,332,398,4,272,1,6987\0301,400,436,4,272,1,6987\0316987,2,8,Malton Droffers\0312,1637,1454,0,\0302,0,0,7,Malton\0302,0,0,8,Malton Droffers\0302,0,0,8,Orgrimmar\0304,0,0,10,Orgrimmar\0304,0,0,11,Hinterlands\031650,23,650,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[65]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031So, Stoutmantle sent you? Well, I owe him.\030The band of wretches responsible for driving the good people of Westfall from the land call themselves The Defias Brotherhood.  I need you to infiltrate this clan of thugs.  We need to know who heads up the cartel and where they are hiding out.  In Lakeshire, in the inn, there is a rogue by the name of Wiley who owes me a favor.$B$BTravel to Lakeshire in the Redridge Mountains, east of Elwynn, and find out what you can.\030Gryan Stoutmantle wants you to talk to Wiley in Lakeshire.\030\030The Defias Brotherhood\0312,1,126,2,257,1,234\0302,129,172,2,259,1,234\0302,175,244,2,259,1,234\0302,247,330,2,257,1,234\0302,335,423,2,257,1,234\0303,1,58,2,386,1,234\0301,1,25,4,272,2,266\0301,27,42,4,272,1,266\031234,2,6,Gryan Stoutmantle\0312,40,1436,0,\0302,0,0,5,Lakeshire\0302,0,0,5,Redridge Mountains\0302,0,0,5,Elwynn\0302,0,0,6,Wiley\0302,0,0,6,Lakeshire\031132,23,132,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[650]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, so you know Malton? He is an old drinking companion of mine. You see, I have found something that transcends the boundaries of artificial treaties and alliances - alcohol. Were we all to slake our thirsts on its blissful qualities, we all would be in a much better place spiritually.$B$BAlas, something tells me that your visit here is not to learn of alcohol's redeeming values, now is it.\030The elf you will need to talk to is Gilveradin Sunchaser.  He can name any wine, vintage and all, just by smell alone!  He can package up the ripple we need, so you'll need to talk with him.  We need six bottles for packaging, two for dad, and how ever many he'll want... and believe me, he'll want some.  When you've packaged the ripple and got dad's two bottles, come back here!$B$BGilveradin's camp is near some high elf lodge in the Hinterlands, and those high elves are not good.  Trust me.\030Talk to Gilveradin Sunchaser; his camp is located in the Hinterlands.\030\030Ripple Recovery\0312,1,57,2,259,3,6987\0302,60,118,2,257,1,6987\0302,121,190,2,259,1,6987\0302,193,271,2,259,1,6987\0302,273,304,2,259,4,6987\0302,307,380,2,257,1,6987\0302,385,484,2,257,1,6987\0302,487,495,2,257,1,6987\0303,1,69,2,384,1,6987\0301,1,23,4,272,2,7801\0301,25,64,4,272,1,7801\0301,66,175,4,272,1,7801\0301,177,287,4,272,4,7801\0301,292,394,4,272,1,7801\0317801,2,1,Gilveradin Sunchaser\0307801,2,9,Gilveradin Sunchaser\0312,1637,1454,0,\0302,0,0,7,Hinterlands\0302,0,0,9,Gilveradin Sunchaser\0302,0,0,9,Hinterlands\031649,19,649,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\03077,23,77,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6501]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I should have known - a piece of the black dragon brood mother, Onyxia. How revolting...\030A fragment of the shattered medallion is all that I can offer.$B$BYou must find another of dragon blood willing to assist you in forging a new key. Once you secure this key, you must travel to the Wyrmbog in Dustwallow Marsh. It is there that you will find her lair, $N.$B$BWhere to find other flights willing to help? Sadly, I do not know... They are said to exist. Some may even work and live among us, disguised as one of the humanoid races. I wish you luck.$B\030You must search the world for a being capable of restoring the power to the Fragment of the Dragon's Eye. The only information you possess about such a being is that they exist.\030I sense an aura of evil radiating from you, $R. What could you hold that emits such an aura?\030The Dragon's Eye\0312,1,62,2,257,1,1748\0302,67,147,2,257,1,1748\0302,149,225,2,257,1,1748\0302,227,270,2,257,3,1748\0302,275,318,2,257,2,1748\0302,320,342,2,257,1,1748\0302,344,366,2,257,1,1748\0302,368,444,2,257,1,1748\0302,446,461,2,259,3,1748\0303,1,105,2,384,1,1748\0303,107,177,2,384,1,1748\0301,1,71,4,272,1,10929\0301,73,88,4,272,1,10929\0304,1,47,3,256,1,10929\0304,49,92,3,256,4,10929\03110184,4,12,Onyxia\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,3,Wyrmbog\0302,0,0,3,Dustwallow Marsh\0302,0,0,10,Fragment of the Dragon's Eye\0316403,19,6403,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306502,23,6502,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6502]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This amulet will grant you the access that you seek. The lair of Onyxia can be found in Dustwallow Marsh. As long as you hold the amulet, her wards cannot prevent you from entering.$B$BThe Blue Flight wishes you luck, $N.\030It is a piece of the dragon; a scale - enchanted and transformed. Whole, it could have granted access to the beast's lair. Shattered, it is useless.$B$BIt is possible to repair the item, but to do so would require the blood of a black dragon champion. There is one... He is known as General Drakkisath, ruler of the dragonspawn armies of Nefarian. Perhaps you have heard of him?$B$BReturn with his blood, $r, and I shall enchant the fragment into something that will grant you access to Onyxia's lair.\030You must retrieve the Blood of the Black Dragon Champion from General Drakkisath. Drakkisath can be found in his throne room behind the Halls of Ascension in Blackrock Spire.\030The flow of time does not stop or slow, $R. While my life is eternal, yours is not. Waste not the time that you have...\030Drakefire Amulet\0312,1,65,2,257,1,10929\0302,67,122,2,257,4,10929\0302,124,148,2,257,1,10929\0302,153,251,2,257,4,10929\0302,253,267,2,257,1,10929\0302,269,347,2,257,1,10929\0302,349,378,2,257,4,10929\0302,383,501,2,257,3,10929\0303,1,81,2,384,1,10929\0303,83,174,2,384,1,10929\0301,1,52,4,274,3,10929\0301,54,105,4,272,1,10929\0301,107,181,4,280,1,10929\0301,186,221,4,274,1,10929\0304,1,43,3,256,1,10929\0304,45,83,3,256,1,10929\0304,85,119,3,256,1,10929\03110430,2,2,The Beast\03010363,2,6,General Drakkisath\03011583,2,6,Nefarian\03010363,2,9,General Drakkisath\03010184,4,12,Onyxia\0312,1583,0,0,\0302,0,0,8,Onyxia's\0302,0,0,9,General Drakkisath\0302,0,0,10,Blackrock Spire\0304,0,0,12,Dustwallow Marsh\0316501,19,6501,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,16663,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6503]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very good, $N. Your hunting skills are impressive...$B$BThe loss of those outrunners help blind the Alliance, and when they lack intelligence they are less likely to launch attacks.\030We received reports that Ashenvale outrunners left Silverwing Outpost not long ago, and now sneak near our territories in the forest.  We don't want them gathering intelligence on our defenses!$B$BSneak through the forests south of our post here and east of the Alliance outpost of Silverwing.  Find and slay the outrunners, then return to me.\030Kill 9 Ashenvale Outrunners, then return to Kuray'bin at Splintertree Outpost.\030I await reports of your outrunner kills, $N.\030Ashenvale Outrunners\0312,1,133,2,321,1,12867\0302,136,193,2,257,1,12867\0302,198,293,2,257,1,12867\0302,296,343,2,257,1,12867\0303,1,78,2,384,1,12867\0301,1,14,4,272,1,12867\0301,16,52,4,272,1,12867\0301,57,181,4,276,1,12867\0304,1,44,3,256,1,12867\03112867,2,5,Kuray'bin\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,3,Alliance\0302,0,0,5,Kuray'bin\0302,0,0,5,Splintertree Outpost\031\031NPC,12856,OBJECTIVE,9,13,Ashenvale Outrunner",[6504]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Reading isn't my strong point... but now I'll be able to get back to work! Thanks, $N!\030I just picked up this shredder from Ratchet and I was on my way back to the Warsong Lumber Camp, where I am supposed to be on duty. I was given a manual on how to operate the shredder, but on the trip back, a huge gust of wind blew it from my hands. The pages went everywhere, and all I was left with was the cover.$B$BThe pages could be just about anywhere by now, I suppose... but I don't know how to use the shredder without them! Will you find them for me?\030Find the 12 missing pages of the Shredder Operating Manual, and put them together to form Chapters 1, 2, and 3. Return the pages to Gurda Ragescar near Splintertree Post.$B\030I hope you find the pages soon, $N! I really need to get back to work!\030The Lost Pages\0312,1,131,2,257,1,12718\0302,133,249,2,257,1,12718\0302,251,315,2,257,1,12718\0302,320,378,2,257,4,12718\0302,380,433,2,257,1,12718\0302,435,460,2,257,2,12718\0303,1,111,2,388,1,12718\0303,113,170,2,384,1,12718\0301,1,32,4,272,1,12718\0301,34,74,4,272,1,12718\0301,76,86,4,272,1,12718\0304,1,35,3,258,3,12718\0304,37,70,3,258,1,12718\03112718,2,8,Gurda Ragescar\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,1,Ratchet\0302,0,0,1,Warsong Lumber Camp\0302,0,0,8,Gurda Ragescar\0302,0,0,8,Splintertree Post\031\031ITEM,16642,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,16643,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,16644,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[651]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Myzrael speaks through the stone.>$B$BYou have done it! You opened the Stones of Binding! I can feel the shackles about me loosen, and freedom draws ever closer.$B$BYou are a noble $C, $N. My rescuer!\030Four Stones of Binding are scattered throughout Arathi.  These stones keep me pinned beneath the earth.$B$BTo unlock them you must unlock the strongest: the Stone of Inner Binding.  And to do that, you must gather keys from the other three.$B$BThese stones are watched by guardians, but if you are clever, or lucky, you may find ways to banish them.\030Gather the Burning Key, the Cresting Key and the Thundering Key from the Stone of West Binding, the Stone of East Binding and the Stone of Outer Binding.$B$BBring them to the Stone of Inner Binding.\030This is the Stone of Inner Binding. It is the strongest of the binding stones and must be unlocked for the others to open.\030Stones of Binding\0312,1,55,2,261,1,0\0302,58,103,2,257,1,0\0302,108,180,2,261,1,0\0302,183,240,2,257,1,0\0302,245,349,2,257,4,0\0303,1,153,2,388,1,0\0303,158,198,2,388,1,0\0301,1,35,4,272,1,0\0301,40,56,4,272,1,0\0301,58,90,4,276,1,0\0301,92,162,4,280,1,0\0301,167,189,4,272,1,0\0301,191,201,4,272,1,0\0304,1,35,3,260,1,0\0304,37,122,3,260,1,0\0312755,4,8,Myzrael\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,6,Stone of West Binding\0302,0,0,7,Stone of Inner Binding\031642,19,642,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030652,23,652,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,2701,GIVER,?,9,Iridescent Shards\030OBJECT,2702,FINISHER,?,12,Stone of Inner Binding\030ITEM,4483,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,4484,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,4485,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[652]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You place the rod in the keystone. And a shudder is felt beneath you...\030Opening the Stones of Binding loosened much of my confinement, but a lock still holds me chained.  It is the Keystone you see among this circle of stones.  And the key is held by one of my captors, the stone watcher Fozruk.$B$BYou must obtain that key, which the stone watchers call the Rod of Order, from Fozruk and use it to open the Keystone.$B$B$N, you have done so much to aid me.  Just a little more...and my gratitude will shake the very foundations of the earth!\030Find and kill Fozruk.  Bring the Rod of Order to the Keystone in the Arathi Highlands.\030The Keystone is charged with tremendous geomantic energy.\030Breaking the Keystone\0312,1,97,2,261,1,0\0302,100,154,2,257,1,0\0302,157,223,2,257,1,0\0302,228,345,2,257,1,0\0302,350,385,2,257,1,0\0302,388,470,2,257,3,0\0303,1,21,2,384,1,0\0303,24,86,2,384,1,0\0301,1,34,4,272,1,0\0301,36,71,4,272,1,0\0304,1,57,3,256,1,0\0312611,2,3,Fozruk\0302611,2,4,Fozruk\0302611,2,7,Fozruk\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,4,Fozruk\0302,0,0,8,Keystone\0302,0,0,8,Arathi Highlands\031651,19,651,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,2702,GIVER,?,9,Stone of Inner Binding\030OBJECT,2688,FINISHER,?,12,Keystone\030ITEM,4469,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6521]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Good. Well done, $C.$B$BNow that Malcin is dead, we can at least know that the Scourges advances will be halted. The Dark Lady thanks you for your efforts and wishes to reward you with a gift.$B$BAlthough we do not know the extent of the Scourges influence within the Downs, I am sure we will discover their plots soon enough.\030Malcin claims he is outside Razorfen Downs. This ambassador must be slain--his mission a failure in the eyes of the Lich King.$B$BHis presence there does explain much of what we've discovered about the area--some of the quilboar have grown frightfully powerful while showing signs of the Plague in their own way. Truly that must be a sign of some sort of deal they've struck.$B$BFind Malcin and slay him, $N. Return to me after the deed is done.\030Bring Ambassador Malcin's Head to Varimathras in the Undercity.\030Have you found the Ambassador, $N? Is he dead?$B$BWe cannot afford to allow the Scourge to take a foothold on Kalimdor. They are enough of a threat to our own borders to have to deal with them on two fronts.$B$BThe only optimistic sign from the events you've told me about is that the crone seemed uncorrupted. She must know deep in her spirit that the Scourge may bring great power, but that the Barrens would not truly be hers if she were to agree to their deal.\030An Unholy Alliance\0312,1,43,2,257,1,2425\0302,45,126,2,325,1,2425\0302,131,312,2,261,1,2425\0302,314,375,2,257,1,2425\0302,380,408,2,257,1,2425\0302,410,445,2,257,1,2425\0303,1,63,2,384,1,2425\0301,1,5,4,272,1,2425\0301,7,20,4,272,1,2425\0301,25,112,4,272,3,2425\0301,114,192,4,274,1,2425\0301,197,326,4,272,3,2425\0304,1,34,3,256,2,2425\0304,36,46,3,256,2,2425\0304,51,119,3,320,1,2425\0304,121,207,3,260,1,2425\0304,212,310,3,256,1,2425\0304,312,464,3,320,4,2425\03116980,2,2,The Lich King\03012865,2,7,Ambassador Malcin\0302425,2,7,Varimathras\03015065,4,11,Lady\0312,722,0,0,\0302,0,0,1,Razorfen Downs\0302,0,0,7,Varimathras\0302,0,0,7,Undercity\0304,0,0,12,Downs\0316522,19,6522,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,17009,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6522]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I recognize the insignia on this scroll, $N. You found this on that crone who reigns over Razorfen Kraul? Interesting.$B$BThe Scourge aren't content with one continent it seems. This Ambassador Malcin--the one who wrote the note--is one of the Scourge's plagued servants, a human diplomat to the kingdom of Lordaeron before things... changed.$B$BIf the Scourge are trying to gain a foothold in Kalimdor, then it is up to us to act.\030My Lady,$B$BYou know very well what it is we are offering. The opportunity for you to take the Barrens and the lands beyond is a great one. We simply want your aid in return. By aid we mean nothing more than your giving us the freedom to take action in the area.$B$BPlease, allow us to discuss this further. We have great power and are willing to share with those wise enough to join us. I will remain outside Razorfen Downs for the time being.$B$BBest Regards,$BAmbassador Malcin\030Take the Small Scroll to Varimathras in the Undercity.\030What business is it you wish to speak of, $N? You must feel it is important if you continue to pester me.\030An Unholy Alliance\0312,1,8,2,257,1,0\0302,13,58,2,257,1,0\0302,60,139,2,257,1,0\0302,141,174,2,259,1,0\0302,176,262,2,265,1,0\0302,267,307,2,257,1,0\0302,309,387,2,257,1,0\0302,389,444,2,257,3,0\0302,449,461,2,257,1,0\0302,464,480,2,257,1,0\0303,1,54,2,384,1,0\0301,1,44,4,272,1,2425\0301,46,105,4,272,2,2425\0301,107,118,4,272,1,2425\0301,123,177,4,336,4,2425\0301,179,333,4,336,1,2425\0301,335,342,4,272,1,2425\0301,347,431,4,336,4,2425\0304,1,45,3,258,2,2425\0304,47,105,3,256,4,2425\03115065,2,1,Lady\03012865,2,10,Ambassador Malcin\0302425,2,11,Varimathras\03012865,4,16,Ambassador Malcin\0312,722,0,0,\0302,0,0,8,Razorfen Downs\0302,0,0,11,Varimathras\0302,0,0,11,Undercity\0304,0,0,18,Kalimdor\0316521,23,6521,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,17008,STARTER,?,10,",[6523]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Kaya is alive! $N, I have you to thank for rescuing her.\030Thank you for rescuing me! We must leave quickly before they discover that I am free. Please escort me to Camp Aparaje. From there, I know my way.$B$BMy father, Makaba Flathoof, will be desperate to know that I am safe.\030Escort Kaya Flathoof to Camp Aparaje, and then return to Makaba Flathoof near the southeastern edge of Stonetalon.$B\030Kaya Escorted to Camp Aparaje\030\030Protect Kaya\0312,1,26,2,257,1,11856\0302,28,85,2,265,1,11856\0302,87,119,2,257,1,11856\0302,121,146,2,257,1,11856\0302,151,219,2,257,3,11856\0303,1,114,2,384,1,11856\0301,1,14,4,272,1,11857\0301,16,56,4,272,1,11857\0304,1,29,3,384,1,11856\03111857,2,5,Makaba Flathoof\03011856,2,6,Kaya Flathoof\03011857,2,6,Makaba Flathoof\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,3,Camp Aparaje\0302,0,0,6,Camp Aparaje\0302,0,0,6,Makaba Flathoof\0303,0,0,9,Camp Aparaje\0316401,23,6401,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[653]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The Lady told me of your coming, $C. You are welcome in my abode for you, like I, serve a higher cause.\030<Myzrael speaks.>$B$BFree!  I AM FREE!  I am free to gather strength, hidden from my captors.  For if they faced me now they would surely overpower and again imprison me.$B$BBut in time I will confront the giants, and they will regret their wardship of me!$B$BYou are a noble ally, $N.  I will need your help again in time.  When I am ready, I will need you to summon me to the surface.$B$BSpeak with Gerrig Bonegrip.  He is in Ironforge, in a shop of the Forlorn Cavern.  He knows how I can be summoned.\030Speak with Gerrig Bonegrip in the Forlorn Cavern of Ironforge.\030\030Myzrael's Allies\0312,1,17,2,257,1,0\0302,22,26,2,257,1,0\0302,29,38,2,257,1,0\0302,41,93,2,257,1,0\0302,96,170,2,261,4,0\0302,175,256,2,257,3,0\0302,261,285,2,257,1,0\0302,288,323,2,259,3,0\0302,326,386,2,259,3,0\0302,391,417,2,257,1,0\0302,420,471,2,257,1,0\0302,474,504,2,257,1,0\0303,1,62,2,384,1,0\0301,1,36,4,272,1,2786\0301,38,103,4,272,1,2786\0312755,2,1,Myzrael\0302786,2,10,Gerrig Bonegrip\0302786,2,13,Gerrig Bonegrip\03015065,4,14,Lady\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,11,Ironforge\0302,0,0,13,Forlorn Cavern of Ironforge\031652,19,652,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030687,23,687,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,2688,GIVER,?,9,Keystone",[654]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031All right then, it will take me just a second to remove the power source. After that, you can do with it whatever you like now without having to worry about losing the data inside.\030Activating the power source makes the field testing kit start to glow and vibrate.  It would seem to be working as planned.$B$BAccording to Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle, you now have two hours to collect the data you need in the Tanaris desert.  If you do not collect it within two hours, all the data will be lost and you will need to buy another power source from him.$B$BReturn to him when you have completed the task.\030Acquire acceptable samples for 8 basilisks, 8 hyenas, and 8 scorpions.  Bring the testing kit back to Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle in Gadgetzan before the power source runs out.\030Well, did you get everything you needed? If you didn't and the power runs out, everything inside will be ruined and you'll have to start over.$B$BHey, don't look to me for sympathy; I'm all about the Gadgetzan Water Company making a profit, and if that means selling you power sources until we can afford to import water in from the icy springs of Dun Morogh, so be it!\030Tanaris Field Sampling\0312,1,82,2,257,1,0\0302,85,123,2,257,4,0\0302,128,243,2,259,1,0\0302,246,369,2,271,4,0\0302,374,420,2,257,1,0\0303,1,70,2,384,1,0\0303,73,176,2,384,1,0\0301,1,73,4,272,3,7407\0301,75,180,4,272,1,7407\0304,1,40,3,256,2,7407\0304,42,142,3,256,4,7407\0304,147,369,3,256,4,7407\0317407,2,3,Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle\0307407,2,7,Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle\0312,440,1446,0,\0302,0,0,3,Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle\0302,0,0,3,Tanaris\0302,0,0,7,Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle\0302,0,0,7,Gadgetzan\031379,19,379,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030864,23,864,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,8524,STARTER,?,10,\030ITEM,9440,OBJECTIVE,8,15,\030ITEM,9441,OBJECTIVE,8,15,\030ITEM,9438,OBJECTIVE,8,15,\030ITEM,8523,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6541]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ashenvale is a divided land, but our most recent efforts have been very successful. We not only have an outpost at the Zoram Strand, but another just north of here called Splintertree.\030Have you ever been to Ashenvale, to the north? The horde has recently set up an outpost on the Zoram Strand there, and we can always use some new recruits to help defend our new fronts.$B$BIf you think you are up to it, see Kadrak in the northern Barrens, at the watch tower. He is heading up the Ashenvale campaign and can give you further orders.\030Report to Kadrak at the watch tower in northern Barrens.\030\030Report to Kadrak\0312,1,46,2,257,2,3429\0302,48,185,2,269,1,3429\0302,190,275,2,257,4,3429\0302,277,348,2,257,1,3429\0303,1,56,2,384,1,3429\0301,1,83,4,272,1,8582\0301,85,184,4,272,1,8582\0318582,2,3,Kadrak\0308582,2,5,Kadrak\0312,17,1413,0,\0302,0,0,1,Ashenvale\0302,0,0,5,Kadrak\0304,0,0,7,Zoram Strand\0316542,22,6542,UNKNOWN\0306543,23,6543,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6542]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ashenvale is a divided land, but our most recent efforts have been very successful. We not only have an outpost at the Zoram Strand, but another just north of here called Splintertree.\030Have you ever been to Ashenvale, to the north? The horde has recently set up an outpost on the Zoram Strand there, and we can always use some new recruits to help defend our new fronts.$B$BIf you think you are up to it, see Kadrak in the northern Barrens, at the watch tower. He is heading up the Ashenvale campaign and can give you further orders.$B\030Report to Kadrak at the watch tower in northern Barrens.\030\030Report to Kadrak\0312,1,46,2,257,2,11821\0302,48,185,2,269,1,11821\0302,190,275,2,257,4,11821\0302,277,348,2,257,1,11821\0303,1,56,2,384,1,11821\0301,1,83,4,272,1,8582\0301,85,184,4,272,1,8582\0318582,2,3,Kadrak\0308582,2,5,Kadrak\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,1,Ashenvale\0302,0,0,5,Kadrak\0304,0,0,7,Zoram Strand\0316541,22,6541,UNKNOWN\0306543,23,6543,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6543]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I can see that you are one that can be counted on. These updates are crucial to our plans to further our presence in Ashenvale. We can now plan our next move.\030I recently deployed a few scouts into Ashenvale and I need a runner to take them their orders, and bring me back a report of what they have observed.$B$BYour first stop should be the Zoram'gar Outpost, along the coast to the west, at the Zoram Strand, to locate the first runner. You also need to stop at Splintertree Post, to the north, and along the road to the east, near Azshara. You will find a scout and an outrider there.$B$BGive them each a report, and from them, get an update on their findings.\030Open the Bundle of Reports.  Take the Warsong Reports to the Warsong Scout, Warsong Runner, and Warsong Outrider. Bring back the updates they give you to Kadrak at the northern watch tower in the barrens.\030Hurry, $N. They must receive their reports; it is urgent.\030The Warsong Reports\0312,1,149,2,259,1,8582\0302,154,279,2,257,1,8582\0302,281,383,2,259,1,8582\0302,385,428,2,257,3,8582\0302,433,504,2,257,1,8582\0303,1,27,2,384,1,8582\0303,30,113,2,384,1,8582\0303,115,204,2,384,1,8582\0301,1,50,4,272,1,8582\0301,52,127,4,272,1,8582\0301,129,158,4,272,1,8582\0304,1,10,3,256,1,8582\0304,12,57,3,256,1,8582\03112862,2,7,Warsong Scout\03012863,2,7,Warsong Runner\03012864,2,7,Warsong Outrider\0308582,2,8,Kadrak\0312,17,1413,0,\0302,0,0,2,Zoram Strand\0302,0,0,3,Splintertree Post\0302,0,0,3,Azshara\0302,0,0,7,Warsong Scout\0302,0,0,8,Kadrak\0304,0,0,10,Ashenvale\031\031ITEM,16764,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,16763,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,16765,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6544]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031So Torek's attack was successful! Well done, $N. Night elves are decent foes. A little skinny, but strong and fierce! I'm sure the battle was something to see...$B$BAnd I hope you gained a scar or two!\030Hey!  $C!  Come here!$B$BMy raiders and I are about to attack the Silverwing Outpost to the west.  Our target is its leader, Duriel Moonfire.  Scouts report the outpost is defended heavily with sentinels and warriors.  The battle will be glorious!$B$BDo you want to share in the glory, $N, and aid us?  If so, then when it's over you can report our success to my superior, Ertog Ragetusk in Splintertree.$B$BWhat do you say.  Are you with us?\030Escort Torek on his attack against Silverwing Outpost and Duriel Moonfire, then report to Ertog Ragetusk at Splintertree Post.\030Take Silverwing Outpost.\030Torek was sent on a mission against Silverwing Outpost. Was the attack successful?\030Torek's Assault\0312,1,4,2,257,1,12858\0302,12,21,2,257,1,12858\0302,26,97,2,261,1,12858\0302,100,141,2,257,1,12858\0302,144,217,2,257,1,12858\0302,220,247,2,261,3,12858\0302,252,301,2,259,2,12858\0302,304,404,2,257,4,12858\0302,409,424,2,257,1,12858\0302,427,442,2,257,2,12858\0303,1,126,2,388,1,12858\0301,1,33,4,276,1,12877\0301,35,48,4,272,1,12877\0301,50,77,4,272,1,12877\0301,79,117,4,272,1,12877\0301,119,161,4,276,1,12877\0301,166,201,4,274,3,12877\0305,1,55,3,256,1,12877\0305,57,82,3,260,2,12877\0304,1,24,3,384,1,12858\03112860,2,4,Duriel Moonfire\03012877,2,8,Ertog Ragetusk\03012858,2,11,Torek\03012860,2,11,Duriel Moonfire\03012877,2,11,Ertog Ragetusk\03012858,3,18,Torek\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,8,Splintertree\0302,0,0,11,Ertog Ragetusk\0302,0,0,11,Splintertree Post\031\031",[6545]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well, my update will explain all of this to Kadrak. You must return this to him as quickly as possible.\030\030\030So you're here with my orders? Always good to see a new recruit with an exuberant nature and a strong will.$B$BYou'd best learn fast if you expect to keep up here. The threat of the naga grows, $N. I have observed and have taken up defenses against several attacks on this outpost since I arrived here.$B$BBut if you'd like to pitch in with that effort, speak with one of the others here at the outpost.\030Warsong Runner Update\0311,1,51,4,272,3,12863\0301,53,103,4,272,1,12863\0304,1,30,3,256,2,12863\0304,32,107,3,256,3,12863\0304,112,163,3,256,4,12863\0304,165,197,3,260,1,12863\0304,199,302,3,260,1,12863\0304,307,403,3,256,4,12863\0318582,4,1,Kadrak\0312,331,1440,0,\0304,0,0,1,Kadrak\0316543,20,6543,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,16746,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6546]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Take my update to Kadrak. Swiftly, $N.\030\030\030Much danger lies along this path, $N. You'd do best to remember this while traveling in these lands. The threat of the alliance is quite near.$B$BWe are faced by enemies on all fronts. The satyr are a formidable and prevalent force in eastern Ashenvale. I have also discovered that the naga have taken over a large area of the land of Azshara.$B$BIt's good to see that we are still bolstering our numbers -- be ready for what lies ahead, $N.\030Warsong Outrider Update\0311,1,25,4,272,1,12864\0301,27,38,4,272,1,12864\0304,1,37,3,260,1,12864\0304,39,100,3,256,1,12864\0304,102,142,3,260,1,12864\0304,147,184,3,260,1,12864\0304,186,253,3,256,1,12864\0304,255,343,3,256,1,12864\0304,348,441,3,256,1,12864\0318582,4,1,Kadrak\0312,331,1440,0,\0304,0,0,1,Kadrak\0316543,20,6543,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,16746,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6547]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Let Kadrak know of the success we have had here holding off the night elves. Our plans are going well.\030\030\030Keep an eye out, $R. The elves are often hiding in the shadows...$B$BWe must always be watching. We have worked very hard to claim this land, and the elves are looking for a chance to take it from us.$B$BI assume you have my next orders from Kadrak?\030Warsong Scout Update\0311,1,76,4,272,1,12862\0301,78,102,4,272,1,12862\0304,1,20,3,256,1,12862\0304,22,65,3,256,1,12862\0304,70,96,3,256,1,12862\0304,98,200,3,256,1,12862\0304,205,249,3,256,4,12862\0318582,4,1,Kadrak\0308582,3,7,Kadrak\0312,331,1440,0,\0303,0,0,7,Kadrak\0316543,20,6543,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,16746,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6548]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031$N, I thank you... but I will never forget what the Grimtotem have done to my village.\030The Grimtotem Clan raided my village and killed most everyone. I killed all I could, but barely escaped with my life.$B$B$N, all I wish now is that more of them are dead. You will find them just to the west of here.$B$B\030Kill 8 Grimtotem Ruffians and 6 Grimtotem Mercenaries, and then return to Makaba Flathoof near the southeastern edge of Stonetalon.$B\030Have you killed them yet?\030Avenge My Village\0312,1,62,2,257,1,11857\0302,64,117,2,257,4,11857\0302,122,170,2,259,3,11857\0302,172,215,2,257,3,11857\0303,1,131,2,384,1,11857\0301,1,18,4,272,1,11857\0301,20,86,4,272,3,11857\0304,1,25,3,256,2,11857\03111857,2,5,Makaba Flathoof\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,5,Makaba Flathoof\0316629,23,6629,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,11910,OBJECTIVE,8,13,Grimtotem Ruffian\030NPC,11911,OBJECTIVE,6,13,Grimtotem Mercenary",[655]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, Gor'mul you speak of. Yes, from what he says, it seems he has never recovered from the death of Doomhammer.$B$BGor'mul was a captive here when Thrall and Orgrim fought to free the camp, but as the earth shook and our brethren escaped, he was left behind. He wandered alone and lost for years without direction or hope, until we returned to establish ourselves here in Hammerfall.\030It is still clear to me, like yesterday... So many years without hope, with wood and steel to bind me to this terrible place. Then finally, finally! There was the Warchief. Doomhammer in his midnight plate, his warhammer held high.$B$BIt was... too terrible... That the blow of a coward would strike down our greatest hero. From behind he charged on his horse, and then his lance ran him through... I fell to my knees. What hope was there? What hope is there...\030Speak with Tor'gan in Hammerfall.\030\030Hammerfall\0312,1,42,2,257,1,2792\0302,44,125,2,259,3,2792\0302,127,148,2,257,1,2792\0302,150,172,2,257,1,2792\0302,174,231,2,257,1,2792\0302,236,244,2,257,1,2792\0302,246,260,2,257,1,2792\0302,262,323,2,257,4,2792\0302,325,398,2,257,1,2792\0302,400,418,2,257,1,2792\0302,420,439,2,259,2,2792\0302,441,461,2,259,3,2792\0303,1,33,2,384,1,2792\0301,1,25,4,272,1,2706\0301,27,111,4,272,4,2706\0301,116,258,4,276,1,2706\0301,260,383,4,278,3,2706\031385,2,9,Horse\0302706,2,13,Tor'gan\0302792,4,14,Gor'mul\0302792,4,16,Gor'mul\0304949,4,16,Thrall\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,13,Hammerfall\0304,0,0,17,Hammerfall\031672,23,672,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[65593]="MINIMAL\031conclusion,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030\030Bring the hearts of Avelina Lilly and Isaac Pearson to Carendin Halgar in the Temple of the Damned.\030\030Hearts of the Lovers\0313,1,99,2,384,1,0\0315757,2,1,Lilly\0305675,2,1,Carendin Halgar\0312,0,0,1,Carendin Halgar\0302,0,0,1,Temple of the Damned\031\031",[65597]="MINIMAL\031conclusion,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030\030Using the Lovers' Hearts, summon and subdue an incubus, then return the Lovers' Hearts to Carendin Halgar in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity.\030\030The Binding\0313,1,144,2,384,1,0\0315675,2,1,Carendin Halgar\0312,0,0,1,Carendin Halgar\0302,0,0,1,Magic Quarter of the Undercity\031\031",[656]="PARTIAL\031conflict,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031As the eldritch shackles are placed around the Shards, an unhuman wail is heard from far below. The scream is followed by a roar.$B$BThe Shards of Myzrael no longer invoke feelings of warmth and security as they once did. Now they pulse with an open menace... as if the thing beneath them holds ill will toward the surface.\030You must defeat Myzrael before she grows in strength.  If you do not, then once she has gathered enough power she will challenge her captors!  There are some who think they can control her, but if she can be controlled then why did the giants chain her in the first place??$B$BCrazy logic, eh?$B$BTo defeat her, summon her at the Shards of Myzrael where you first spoke with her.  Defeat her and gather her Eldritch Shackles, then bind them to the Shards of Myzrael.$B$BDo that, and she will again be trapped.\030Go to the Shards of Myzrael, summon her and defeat her.$B$BGather her Eldritch Shackles and bind them to the Shards of Myzrael.\030The Shards of Myzrael are now strangely quiet.\030Summoning the Princess\0312,1,53,2,265,1,2785\0302,56,141,2,257,4,2785\0302,144,273,2,257,4,2785\0302,278,293,2,257,2,2785\0302,298,379,2,257,1,2785\0302,382,466,2,257,1,2785\0302,471,509,2,257,3,2785\0303,1,55,2,384,1,2785\0303,60,127,2,384,1,2785\0301,1,95,4,272,1,0\0301,97,129,4,272,1,0\0301,134,221,4,312,1,0\0301,223,259,4,304,1,0\0301,261,323,4,272,4,0\0304,1,46,3,256,1,0\0312755,2,1,Myzrael\0302755,2,5,Myzrael\0302755,2,6,Myzrael\0302755,2,8,Myzrael\0302755,2,9,Myzrael\0302755,4,12,Myzrael\0302755,3,15,Myzrael\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,5,Shards of Myzrael\0302,0,0,6,Shards of Myzrael\0302,0,0,8,Shards of Myzrael\0302,0,0,9,Shards of Myzrael\031692,19,692,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,138492,FINISHER,?,12,Shards of Myzrael\030ITEM,4473,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[65601]="MINIMAL\031conclusion,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030\030Speak with Magar in Orgrimmar.\030\030Love Hurts\0313,1,30,2,384,1,0\0313363,2,1,Magar\0312,0,0,1,Orgrimmar\031\031",[65602]="MINIMAL\031conclusion,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030\030Retrieve the Wooden Figurine and bring it to Gakin the Darkbinder in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind.\030\030What Is Love?\0313,1,99,2,384,1,0\0316122,2,1,Gakin the Darkbinder\0312,0,0,1,Gakin the Darkbinder\0302,0,0,1,Mage Quarter of Stormwind\031\031",[65603]="MINIMAL\031conclusion,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030\030Using the Wooden Figurine, summon and subdue an incubus, then return the Wooden Figurine to Gakin the Darkbinder in the Slaughtered Lamb.\030\030The Binding\0313,1,137,2,384,1,0\0316122,2,1,Gakin the Darkbinder\0312,0,0,1,Gakin the Darkbinder\0302,0,0,1,Slaughtered Lamb\031\031",[65604]="MINIMAL\031conclusion,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030\030Using the Withered Scarf, summon and subdue an incubus, then return the Withered Scarf to Gan'rul Bloodeye in Orgrimmar.\030\030The Binding\0313,1,120,2,384,1,0\0315875,2,1,Gan'rul Bloodeye\0312,0,0,1,Gan'rul Bloodeye\0302,0,0,1,Orgrimmar\031\031",[6561]="PARTIAL\031consequences,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Kelris has eluded the Argent Dawn for some time.$B$BFor some time they considered him dead or missing.$B$BBy ending his reign you have spared the lives of many innocent people, $N.$B$BEarthmother be praised! To sacrifice another to a servant of an Old God for personal gain is beyond disgusting!$B$BYou have done a great thing this day. Kelris was a creature of evil and sought to bring the world back to a time of chaos by worshipping such creatures as the Old Gods. Thank you, $N.\030Strength has left me. Your help is needed!$B$BLong ago this site was a great temple of Elune. But misfortune led to ruin when the corruption of an Old God seeped up from beneath the earth and tainted the sacred Moon Well.$B$BAku'Mai, servant of the Old God, rose from the waters.$B$BThe Twilight's Hammer cultists have allied with the naga to occupy these grounds. The cultists, led by Kelris, sacrifice innocents to Aku'Mai for power.$B$BSlay Kelris and bring his head to Bashana in Thunder Bluff, $N, please.\030Bring the head of Twilight Lord Kelris to Bashana Runetotem in Thunder Bluff.\030May the Earthmother be with you, $N.$B$BPeace between the earth and all her people should be our goal. She has a grand plan for nature, and we all have a role to play in that plan.\030Blackfathom Villainy\0312,1,21,2,257,1,4787\0302,23,42,2,257,1,4787\0302,47,93,2,321,1,4787\0302,95,221,2,261,1,4787\0302,226,279,2,257,1,4787\0302,284,364,2,257,1,4787\0302,366,435,2,257,1,4787\0302,440,510,2,257,1,4787\0303,1,77,2,384,1,4787\0301,1,48,4,272,1,9087\0301,53,102,4,276,1,9087\0301,107,180,4,272,1,9087\0301,185,207,4,272,1,9087\0301,209,295,4,272,1,9087\0301,300,336,4,272,1,9087\0301,338,467,4,336,1,9087\0301,469,482,4,272,1,9087\0304,1,36,3,256,1,9087\0304,41,102,3,266,1,9087\0304,104,180,3,256,1,9087\0314829,2,5,Aku'mai\0304829,2,7,Aku'mai\0304832,2,9,Twilight Lord Kelris\0309087,2,9,Bashana Runetotem\0312,719,0,0,\0302,0,0,7,Aku'Mai\0302,0,0,8,Bashana\0302,0,0,8,Thunder Bluff\0302,0,0,9,Bashana Runetotem\0302,0,0,9,Thunder Bluff\031\031ITEM,5881,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[65610]="MINIMAL\031conclusion,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030\030Investigate Fallen Sky Lake in Ashenvale and report your findings to Gan'rul Bloodeye in Orgrimmar.\030\030Wish You Were Here\0313,1,99,2,384,1,0\0315875,2,1,Gan'rul Bloodeye\0312,0,0,1,Ashenvale\0302,0,0,1,Gan'rul Bloodeye\0302,0,0,1,Orgrimmar\031\031",[6562]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Tsunaman sent you? Excellent. Then we have matters to discuss.\030Je'neu Sancrea is in need of aid. He is at the Zoram'gar Outpost in Ashenvale. The Night elf forest is to the north of the Stonetalon mountains. You can reach it by traveling through Windshear Crag or by heading north through Barrens. Zoram Strand is far to the west of the forest. Be careful, $N. There are forces there that will not take to your presence kindly.\030Speak to Je'neu Sancrea in Ashenvale.\030\030Trouble in the Deeps\0312,1,33,2,259,1,11862\0302,35,78,2,257,1,11862\0302,80,144,2,257,1,11862\0302,146,234,2,257,1,11862\0302,236,281,2,257,1,11862\0302,283,297,2,257,1,11862\0302,299,364,2,257,3,11862\0303,1,37,2,384,1,11862\0301,1,18,4,272,2,12736\0301,20,29,4,272,1,12736\0301,31,62,4,272,1,12736\03112736,2,1,Je'neu Sancrea\03012736,2,8,Je'neu Sancrea\03011862,4,9,Tsunaman\0312,719,0,0,\0302,0,0,2,Zoram'gar Outpost\0302,0,0,2,Ashenvale\0302,0,0,3,Stonetalon\0302,0,0,8,Je'neu Sancrea\0302,0,0,8,Ashenvale\0316563,23,6563,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6563]="PARTIAL\031conflict,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $N. These are the crystals I spoke of. Intriguing...$B$BI can feel the power within them. The spirits of water cling to them. Whatever the naga were going to use these for... well, let us be glad they are no longer in their hands.\030Within the beginning tunnels of Blackfathom Deeps, large sapphire clusters can be found along the cave walls. Recently it was noted that the naga were harvesting the crystals. Until it can be discerned why, I sense we should stop the naga from succeeding. The crystals have great elemental power and if used inappropriately, could make for a powerful arcane component.$B$BWill you help me, $N? Blackfathom Deeps can be found along Zoram Strand to the north of our outpost.\030Bring 20 Sapphires of Aku'Mai to Je'neu Sancrea in Ashenvale.\030How goes your search for the crystals, $N? Have you witnessed the naga harvesting them? I pray to my ancestors we find the reason they are collecting such things.\030The Essence of Aku'Mai\0312,1,109,2,257,1,12736\0302,111,175,2,257,1,12736\0302,177,255,2,257,1,12736\0302,257,368,2,257,4,12736\0302,373,393,2,257,2,12736\0302,395,472,2,257,1,12736\0303,1,61,2,384,1,12736\0301,1,14,4,272,1,12736\0301,16,49,4,272,1,12736\0301,51,63,4,272,1,12736\0301,68,100,4,272,1,12736\0301,102,136,4,272,1,12736\0301,138,185,4,272,3,12736\0301,187,241,4,304,1,12736\0304,1,42,3,256,2,12736\0304,44,87,3,256,2,12736\0304,89,162,3,256,1,12736\0314829,2,7,Aku'mai\03012736,2,7,Je'neu Sancrea\0312,719,0,0,\0302,0,0,7,Je'neu Sancrea\0302,0,0,7,Ashenvale\0316562,19,6562,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,16784,OBJECTIVE,20,15,",[6564]="PARTIAL\031conflict,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is interesting indeed. I am glad you have brought it to my attention.$B$BNow we have a name for our troubles... Lorgus Jett.\030Some poor handwriting is scrawled on the crumpled up note:$B$B\"Yes, tell all the priestesses to bring the crystals to me. The water elemental spirits are strong within them and they will aid our aquamancers greatly in their own summonings.$B$BBy controlling the power within the crystals, we will appease Aku'Mai. One day we will have enough power to bring Aku'Mai back to us and the world will return to its greatest era! An era of rule by the Old Gods!\"\030Bring the Damp Note to Je'neu Sancrea in Ashenvale.\030Yes, $N? What is it you need? There is still much I must learn about the crystals the naga are gathering.\030Allegiance to the Old Gods\0312,1,58,2,257,1,0\0302,63,121,2,257,1,0\0302,123,239,2,257,3,0\0302,244,313,2,257,3,0\0302,315,422,2,257,3,0\0302,424,455,2,321,1,0\0303,1,51,2,384,1,0\0301,1,27,4,272,1,12736\0301,29,74,4,272,1,12736\0301,79,116,4,304,1,12736\0301,118,129,4,272,1,12736\0304,1,8,3,256,2,12736\0304,10,29,3,258,2,12736\0304,31,105,3,256,1,12736\031510,2,3,Water Elemental\0304829,2,4,Aku'mai\0304829,2,5,Aku'mai\03012736,2,7,Je'neu Sancrea\03012902,4,11,Lorgus Jett\0312,719,0,0,\0302,0,0,7,Je'neu Sancrea\0302,0,0,7,Ashenvale\0316565,23,6565,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,16790,STARTER,?,10,",[6565]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very good!! Thank you, $N. We may not have stopped the Twilight's Hammer completely, but at least you have staved off another of their plans to return the Old Gods to power.$B$BWho knows what other plans they have manifesting, but we can rest easy for now.\030This Twilight's Hammer follower cannot be allowed to complete his plan. The Twilight's Hammer do not understand the spirits of nature. They believe in the Old Gods--creatures of chaos and destruction that were long ago defeated. This Lorgus cannot be allowed to succeed. You must stop him, $N. I cannot do it myself--I am too weak.$B$BGo into Blackfathom Deeps, find him, and kill him. Return to me here at Zoram'gar when it's done.\030Kill Lorgus Jett in Blackfathom Deeps and then return to Je'neu Sancrea in Ashenvale.\030Have you found him yet, $N? Lorgus must be stopped!\030Allegiance to the Old Gods\0312,1,71,2,257,1,12736\0302,73,134,2,257,1,12736\0302,136,228,2,321,4,12736\0302,230,270,2,257,1,12736\0302,272,293,2,257,1,12736\0302,295,331,2,257,1,12736\0302,336,385,2,257,1,12736\0302,387,432,2,257,1,12736\0303,1,85,2,384,1,12736\0301,1,11,4,272,1,12736\0301,13,26,4,272,1,12736\0301,28,173,4,336,1,12736\0301,178,256,4,272,1,12736\0304,1,27,3,256,2,12736\0304,29,51,3,256,1,12736\03112902,2,9,Lorgus Jett\03012736,2,9,Je'neu Sancrea\0312,719,0,0,\0302,0,0,3,Old Gods--creatures of\0302,0,0,8,Zoram'gar\0302,0,0,9,Blackfathom Deeps\0302,0,0,9,Je'neu Sancrea\0302,0,0,9,Ashenvale\0316564,19,6564,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,12902,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Lorgus Jett",[6566]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Are you prepared to take on this task?\030It is good to see you again, $N. The wind carries with it news from the Eastern Kingdom.$B$BSit, listen. $B\030Listen to Thrall.\030Thrall's Tale\030Patience, $N. Pay attention!\030What the Wind Carries\0312,1,32,2,257,1,4949\0302,34,88,2,257,1,4949\0302,93,104,2,257,1,4949\0303,1,17,2,384,1,4949\0301,1,38,4,272,2,4949\0305,1,13,3,256,1,4949\0305,15,28,3,256,1,4949\0304,1,13,3,384,1,4949\0314949,2,4,Thrall\0312,1637,1454,0,\0302,0,0,2,Eastern Kingdom\0302,0,0,4,Thrall\0314974,19,4974,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306567,23,6567,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6567]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031There is but one way into the dragon's lair, $R.$B$BYou see, only the strongest of the Black Dragonflight are allowed entry into the lair of the brood mother. Many trials must be passed and the key to enter ceremoniously enchanted by General Drakkisath himself!$B$BSince you are not of black dragonkin, you may have some difficulty in obtaining passage.$B$B<Rexxar grins.>\030I have received word from one of my champions that a way into the lair of the dragon may exist. You are to seek him out.$B$BRexxar wanders the desert wasteland of Desolace, traveling between Stonetalon and Feralas. He awaits your arrival.\030Seek out Rexxar. The Warchief has instructed you as to his whereabouts. Search the paths of Desolace, between the Stonetalon Mountains and Feralas.\030\030The Champion of the Horde\0312,1,95,2,257,1,4949\0302,97,120,2,259,1,4949\0302,125,214,2,257,1,4949\0302,216,238,2,257,1,4949\0303,1,16,2,384,1,4949\0303,18,71,2,384,1,4949\0303,73,147,2,384,1,4949\0301,1,48,4,272,1,10182\0301,53,158,4,272,1,10182\0301,160,261,4,272,1,10182\0301,266,353,4,272,1,10182\0301,358,372,4,272,1,10182\03110182,2,3,Rexxar\03010182,2,5,Rexxar\03010363,4,10,General Drakkisath\03010182,4,12,Rexxar\0312,1637,1454,0,\0316566,19,6566,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306568,23,6568,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6568]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Myranda holds the note, pauses, then smiles.>$B$BHow is he? Rexxar, I mean. Oh, come now, do not look so confused. The letter was left intentionally blank. It carried with it the intentions and thoughts of its creator. Judging from its contents, it is no wonder Rexxar left it as such. Imagine if you were captured or slain and this information discovered!$B$BOh, nevermind! Myranda will help you, $R. I owe the Warchief a favor or two.$B$B<Myranda smiles.>\030Illusion and disguise. That is how you will fool the Black Dragonflight, and gain what you seek.$B$BThough I could teach you something of the skills of deception, you need the help of a master.$B$BI know of one who could do this. In the Western Plaguelands, you will find Myranda the Hag, once a master illusionist of Lordaeron. She has helped us in the past, and if she believes the cause worthy, she may help you.$B$BTake this message to her.\030Deliver Rexxar's Letter to Myranda the Hag in the Western Plaguelands.\030It is not often I see one of the Horde in these parts of Lordaeron. What is it that you have for Myranda?\030The Testament of Rexxar\0312,1,22,2,257,1,10182\0302,24,96,2,259,3,10182\0302,101,193,2,259,4,10182\0302,198,229,2,257,4,10182\0302,231,328,2,257,3,10182\0302,330,415,2,257,4,10182\0302,420,444,2,257,1,10182\0303,1,70,2,384,1,10182\0301,1,46,4,272,1,11872\0301,51,60,4,272,2,11872\0301,62,76,4,272,1,11872\0301,78,115,4,272,1,11872\0301,117,156,4,272,1,11872\0301,158,219,4,272,1,11872\0301,221,286,4,272,1,11872\0301,288,357,4,276,4,11872\0301,362,375,4,272,1,11872\0301,377,402,4,272,3,11872\0301,404,437,4,272,1,11872\0301,442,458,4,272,1,11872\0304,1,67,3,256,1,11872\0304,69,105,3,256,2,11872\03111872,2,5,Myranda the Hag\03011872,2,8,Myranda the Hag\03010182,4,11,Rexxar\03010182,4,15,Rexxar\0312,405,1443,0,\0302,0,0,8,Myranda the Hag\0302,0,0,8,Western Plaguelands\0316567,19,6567,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306569,23,6569,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6569]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Let Myranda have a look, $R.$B$BOh yes, these will do nicely.$B$BWith these reagents, Myranda will create for you a medallion that will grant an illusion capable of fooling the black dragonflight's gatekeeper.\030So the $r wishes to become one of the Black Flight, eh?$B$BThe creation of the illusion you require is trivial, but the components required for the divination are quite difficult to obtain. The Warchief has entrusted you with this mission, so Myranda must assume you as capable.$B$BTravel to the upper citadel of Blackrock Spire and slay enough of the black dragonspawn to fill up one of your packs with their eyes.$B$BReturn to Myranda when you have gathered enough of the reagent.\030Travel to Blackrock Spire and collect 20 Black Dragonspawn Eyes. Return to Myranda the Hag when the task is complete.\030The eyes of that which we wish to mimic are the most important ingredient of any illusion, $N.$B$B<Myranda points to a bag almost overflowing with eyeballs labeled 'Scarlet Crusade.'>$B$B<Myranda laughs.>\030Oculus Illusions\0312,1,55,2,257,2,11872\0302,60,189,2,257,1,11872\0302,191,278,2,257,4,11872\0302,283,415,2,257,1,11872\0302,420,482,2,257,1,11872\0303,1,64,2,384,1,11872\0303,66,117,2,384,1,11872\0301,1,28,4,272,1,11872\0301,33,61,4,272,3,11872\0301,66,209,4,272,3,11872\0304,1,94,3,258,3,11872\0304,99,183,3,256,1,11872\0304,188,204,3,256,1,11872\0317040,2,4,Black Dragonspawn\0307040,2,6,Black Dragonspawn\03011872,2,7,Myranda the Hag\0312,1583,0,0,\0302,0,0,5,Myranda\0302,0,0,6,Blackrock Spire\0302,0,0,7,Myranda the Hag\0316568,19,6568,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306570,23,6570,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,16786,OBJECTIVE,20,15,",[657]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031If it brings Phin peace, I'll destroy every single one of the Forsaken personally. He's done so much for us since the plague. We never thought we'd find friends or family again.$B$BWhen you're prepared, come let me know. We'll get started right away.\030<Quae begins to go through the folder.>$B$BThis IS interesting. Seems Apothecary Jorell has been working on some deadly experiments here at Go'Shek. Not sure what that has to do with Hillsbrad, but Phin wouldn't like it if we let it continue.$B$BWe had a run-in with some orcs while you were gone, and I'm not in good enough shape to help Kinelory. If you're up for it, she's going to need some protection when she goes down to the farm to steal whatever research Jorell still hasn't sent to Tarren Mill.\030Speak to Kinelory.\030\030Hints of a New Plague?\0312,1,39,2,257,1,2712\0302,44,63,2,257,1,2712\0302,65,148,2,257,4,2712\0302,150,242,2,257,4,2712\0302,247,348,2,257,1,2712\0302,350,504,2,263,4,2712\0303,1,18,2,384,1,2712\0301,1,82,4,284,4,2713\0301,84,125,4,276,1,2713\0301,127,177,4,272,1,2713\0301,182,220,4,272,1,2713\0301,222,250,4,272,1,2713\0312712,2,1,Quae\0302733,2,3,Apothecary Jorell\0302713,2,5,Kinelory\0302713,2,7,Kinelory\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,3,Go'Shek\0302,0,0,6,Tarren Mill\0302,0,0,7,Kinelory\031658,19,658,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030660,23,660,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6570]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Have we run so low on able soldiers that Nefarian is sending me whelps? You will never pass my tests, broodling.\030I have attuned this medallion with the magic necessary to create and maintain an illusion within the bounds of the den of Emberstrife.$B$BEmberstrife is an ancient drake; an old gatekeeper of Nefarian, burdened with the duty to test those dragonspawn that would ascend to the rank of elite guard to Onyxia.$B$BTravel to the Wyrmbog of Dustwallow Marsh and enter the lair of Emberstrife. Once there, put on the amulet and follow where your destiny may lead!$B\030Travel to the Wyrmbog in Dustwallow Marsh and seek out Emberstrife's Den. Once inside, wear the Amulet of Draconic Subversion and speak with Emberstrife.$B\030\030Emberstrife\0312,1,134,2,257,1,11872\0302,139,306,2,321,4,11872\0302,311,386,2,257,1,11872\0302,388,456,2,257,1,11872\0303,1,73,2,386,1,11872\0303,75,153,2,384,1,11872\0301,1,71,4,272,2,10321\0301,73,112,4,272,3,10321\03110321,2,1,Emberstrife\03010321,2,2,Emberstrife\03011583,2,2,Nefarian\03010184,2,2,Onyxia\03010321,2,3,Emberstrife\03010321,2,6,Emberstrife\03011583,4,7,Nefarian\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,2,Onyxia\0302,0,0,3,Wyrmbog of Dustwallow Marsh\0302,0,0,5,Wyrmbog\0302,0,0,5,Dustwallow Marsh\0316569,19,6569,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6571]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Excellent, $N. You've saved me a lot of work!$B$BBut don't think that I'm not grateful!\030We are in short supply of a few items at the Warsong lumber camp!$B$BPixel at Splintertree Post has our shipment of saw blades. It'll take a trip to Booty Bay to pick up a crate of axes from Wharfmaster Lozgil.$B$BOur shipment of oil and rope will be more difficult. The rope was pilfered by the Thistlefur and Foulweald furbolgs, and the satyrs intercepted the delivery of the oil and are now using it for detestable rituals in Night Run, Satyrnaar, and Xavian!$B$BCan you help me?\030Collect the Warsong Supplies: Warsong Saw Blades, Logging Rope, Warsong Oil, and the Warsong Axe Shipment for Locke Okarr in Splintertree Post.\030I hope you can come through with the supplies!\030Warsong Supplies\0312,1,65,2,257,1,11820\0302,70,127,2,257,1,11820\0302,129,210,2,257,1,11820\0302,215,266,2,257,3,11820\0302,268,462,2,257,1,11820\0302,467,482,2,257,2,11820\0303,1,143,2,384,1,11820\0301,1,14,4,272,1,11820\0301,16,45,4,272,1,11820\0301,50,87,4,272,1,11820\0304,1,46,3,258,3,11820\03112724,2,2,Pixel\0304631,2,3,Wharfmaster Lozgil\03011820,2,7,Locke Okarr\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,1,Warsong\0302,0,0,2,Splintertree Post\0302,0,0,3,Booty Bay\0302,0,0,3,Wharfmaster Lozgil\0302,0,0,5,Night Run\0302,0,0,7,Splintertree Post\031\031ITEM,16742,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,16745,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,16744,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,16743,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[658]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Excellent!$B$BLet's see what this is about...\030So, Phin sent you to check on us? Not surprised--he worries too much.$B$BWe've been watching the farm for days, and Kin claims she saw a courier come out of that small house to the south not long ago.$B$BShe talks a lot, but I can always trust her senses when we're in dangerous areas.$B$BYou wouldn't happen to be a skilled tracker, would you? We think the courier might be carrying notes to Tarren Mill. If we could get our hands on those documents, it might shed some light on what's happening in Hillsbrad.\030Find the Forsaken Courier and bring back her Sealed Folder to Quae near the Go'Shek Farm.\030We appreciate your help in looking for that courier, $N.$B$BWhile you were gone, Kin saw an apothecary come out of that same house to the south of here. I'm confident that they're up to no good--I just need proof of it before we go off and do something rash.$B$BHave you had any luck yet?\030Hints of a New Plague?\0312,1,33,2,257,2,2712\0302,35,69,2,257,1,2712\0302,74,200,2,321,1,2712\0302,205,285,2,257,1,2712\0302,290,344,2,257,4,2712\0302,346,405,2,257,4,2712\0302,407,510,2,257,4,2712\0303,1,89,2,384,1,2712\0301,1,10,4,272,1,2712\0301,15,45,4,272,1,2712\0304,1,56,3,256,1,2712\0304,61,152,3,256,1,2712\0304,154,258,3,266,1,2712\0304,263,288,3,256,2,2712\0312714,2,8,Forsaken Courier\0302712,2,8,Quae\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,6,Tarren Mill\0302,0,0,7,Hillsbrad\0302,0,0,8,Quae\0302,0,0,8,Go'Shek Farm\031659,19,659,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030657,23,657,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4482,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6581]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,objectives,setup\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is perfect -- just the thing! Well, here's the shipment.\030\030\030Direct from Ratchet, the Warsong saw blades! Yep, I have them right here.$B$B..But what sort of payment do you have for me? You can't just take them, you know! My time isn't cheap!$B$BWhat I really need is a good gun to carry with me on my travels. A girl's gotta protect herself, you know? There's a gun I really like that I'm sure an engineer would have no problem making.$B$BSo, if you bring me a deadly blunderbuss, I'll give you the saw blade shipment. Do we have a deal?\030Warsong Saw Blades\0311,1,34,4,272,1,12724\0301,36,61,4,272,1,12724\0304,1,44,3,256,1,12724\0304,46,73,3,256,1,12724\0304,78,123,3,256,2,12724\0304,125,159,3,256,1,12724\0304,161,180,3,256,1,12724\0304,185,248,3,258,1,12724\0304,250,290,3,268,2,12724\0304,292,374,3,260,4,12724\0304,379,457,3,256,4,12724\0304,459,476,3,256,2,12724\031\0312,331,1440,0,\0303,0,0,3,Ratchet\0316571,20,6571,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4369,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6582]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031One of ssseveral complete...\030We are Deathwing's children, whelp. Our dominance over the lesser Aspects must be enforced.$B$BIf you are truly worthy of ascension, the lesser dragonflight will wilt in your presence.$B$BFind their champions and lay waste to them in the name of our Father!$B$BTravel to Winterspring and track down the mighty blue drake, Scryer. Crush him and any of the Blue Flight that stand in your path. Tear out his skull and return it to me.\030You must find the blue dragonflight drake champion, Scryer, and slay him. Pry his skull from his corpse and return it to Emberstrife.$B$BYou know that Scryer can be found in Winterspring.\030<Emberstrife hisses.>\030The Test of Skulls, Scryer\0312,1,35,2,257,1,10321\0302,37,91,2,257,1,10321\0302,96,184,2,257,4,10321\0302,189,257,2,257,1,10321\0302,262,329,2,257,1,10321\0302,331,391,2,257,1,10321\0302,393,431,2,257,1,10321\0303,1,73,2,384,1,10321\0303,75,133,2,384,1,10321\0303,138,187,2,384,1,10321\0301,1,28,4,272,1,10321\0304,1,21,3,256,1,10321\03110664,2,5,Scryer\03010664,2,8,Scryer\03010321,2,9,Emberstrife\03010664,2,10,Scryer\03010321,3,12,Emberstrife\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,5,Winterspring\0302,0,0,9,Emberstrife\0302,0,0,10,Winterspring\0316570,19,6570,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,16869,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6583]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Another complete...\030Just as our Father crushes the Aspects themselves, so too must we strive to bring chaos and destruction to their children.$B$BYou must test your battle prowess against the sleepless dreamers: The children of the Green Flight.$B$BTravel to the Swamp of Sorrows and track down Somnus, drake champion of the Green Flight. Let flow your hatred; dominate the insect... Return to me with his skull...\030Destroy the drake champion of the Green Flight, Somnus. Take his skull and return it to Emberstrife.\030Do not return here until you have bathed in the blood of our enemies and drank in their suffering.\030The Test of Skulls, Somnus\0312,1,122,2,257,1,10321\0302,127,225,2,261,1,10321\0302,230,318,2,257,1,10321\0302,320,363,2,257,1,10321\0302,365,394,2,257,1,10321\0303,1,55,2,388,1,10321\0303,57,100,2,384,1,10321\0301,1,19,4,272,1,10321\0304,1,98,3,260,1,10321\03112900,2,3,Somnus\03012900,2,6,Somnus\03010321,2,7,Emberstrife\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,3,Swamp of Sorrows\0302,0,0,7,Emberstrife\0316570,19,6570,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,16870,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6584]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The most hated remainsss...\030The time watchers, children of Nozdormu - Lord of the Centuriesss...$B$BIt is three that guard the Caverns of Time, but only one that holds the interests of the Black Flight: The Time Shifter, Chronalis, favored drakeling of Nozdormu.$B$BSsstrike at this champion, a blow to make even the stoic sands of time weep. Return to me with his skull.\030Guarding the Caverns of Time in the Tanaris Desert is Chronalis, child of Nozdormu. Destroy him and return his skull to Emberstrife.\030Ironically, whelp, time is of the essencccce.\030The Test of Skulls, Chronalis\0312,1,68,2,257,1,10321\0302,73,234,2,257,1,10321\0302,239,314,2,257,1,10321\0302,316,343,2,257,1,10321\0303,1,83,2,384,1,10321\0303,85,132,2,388,1,10321\0301,1,27,4,272,1,10321\0304,1,45,3,256,1,10321\0318197,2,2,Chronalis\0308197,2,5,Chronalis\03010321,2,6,Emberstrife\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,5,Tanaris Desert\0302,0,0,6,Emberstrife\0316570,19,6570,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,16871,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6585]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I had doubted your dedication, whelp. You persisted, dominating our enemies, bringing honor to our flight.$B$BI must now prepare the skulls for your ascension.\030It was over the mountains of Grim Batol that our Father raged against the combined might of the Aspects. The cowardly act of the betrayer, Alexstrasza, bought the other Aspects enough time to escape from Father's wrath.$B$BSssuch a shameful act...$B$BThe Red Flight now guards Grim Batol, their lieutenant, Axtroz, must be destroyed. Return the skull of Axtroz to me. For Father, whelp!\030Travel to Grim Batol and track down Axtroz, drake champion of the Red Flight. Destroy him and take his skull. Return the skull to Emberstrife.\030Changesss... I sense them taking place in you, whelp. Pass this test and only ceremony remains.\030The Test of Skulls, Axtroz\0312,1,104,2,257,4,10321\0302,106,219,2,257,1,10321\0302,224,247,2,257,1,10321\0302,252,333,2,261,1,10321\0302,335,367,2,257,1,10321\0302,369,386,2,257,1,10321\0303,1,77,2,384,1,10321\0303,79,109,2,388,1,10321\0303,111,142,2,384,1,10321\0301,1,37,4,272,1,10321\0301,39,106,4,276,1,10321\0301,111,159,4,272,1,10321\0304,1,12,3,256,1,10321\0304,14,53,3,256,1,10321\0304,55,95,3,256,1,10321\03112899,2,4,Axtroz\03012899,2,5,Axtroz\03012899,2,7,Axtroz\03010321,2,9,Emberstrife\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,2,Father's\0302,0,0,7,Grim Batol\0302,0,0,9,Emberstrife\0316582,21,6582,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306583,21,6583,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306584,21,6584,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306601,23,6601,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,16872,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[659]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Try and stay as quiet as possible, traveler.$B$BOrcs don't take too well to being spied on, and there is more to this farm than meets the eye.\030Hail, and well met, $N. I lead a group of adventurers investigating odd happenings in this area.$B$BMy cousin in Hillsbrad recently put down his dog Stanley because the animal mystically grew to an immense size and savagely attacked anyone who came near him.$B$BI believe the undead are involved, and we're looking for signs to prove as much.$B$BTwo of my companions, Quae and Kinelory, headed to the Go'Shek Farm in the Arathi Highlands, and haven't checked in for days. Find them for me? I grow concerned.\030Find Quae and Kinelory near the Go'Shek Farm in the Arathi Highlands.\030\030Hints of a New Plague?\0312,1,23,2,257,1,2711\0302,25,96,2,257,1,2711\0302,101,258,2,263,1,2711\0302,263,342,2,257,4,2711\0302,347,471,2,257,1,2711\0302,473,489,2,257,2,2711\0302,491,507,2,257,1,2711\0303,1,69,2,384,1,2711\0301,1,44,4,272,1,2712\0301,49,142,4,272,1,2712\0312274,2,3,Stanley\0302712,2,5,Quae\0302713,2,5,Kinelory\0302712,2,8,Quae\0302713,2,8,Kinelory\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,3,Hillsbrad\0302,0,0,5,Go'Shek Farm\0302,0,0,5,Arathi Highlands\0302,0,0,8,Go'Shek Farm\0302,0,0,8,Arathi Highlands\031658,23,658,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[66]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah so Madame Eva sent you....\030Last night a horrible disturbance rippled through my veins.  I sensed that my granddaughter, Alyssa, was in great danger.  I consulted the cards and Death stared up at me from the table.$B$BAfter taking a long journey through a dark trance I was able to uncover a clue to this terrifying mystery.  A name came to me, the name of Stalvan.$B$BSeek out the Clerk in the Town Hall and see if you can find out more about this character.  I fear for us all.\030Seek out the Clerk Daltry in the Darkshire Town Hall.\030\030The Legend of Stalvan\0312,1,59,2,257,1,265\0302,62,121,2,261,1,265\0302,124,186,2,257,1,265\0302,191,296,2,257,1,265\0302,299,337,2,257,1,265\0302,342,431,2,257,4,265\0302,434,451,2,257,1,265\0303,1,53,2,384,1,265\0301,1,29,4,272,1,267\031267,2,8,Clerk Daltry\030265,4,9,Madame Eva\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,6,Town Hall\0302,0,0,8,Darkshire Town Hall\03167,23,67,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[660]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031You've done a great service for us, $N. Thank you.$B$BI hope Kin wasn't too much of a handful down there. She's very friendly, but can be just as deadly when you're her enemy.\030All right, $N. I'm ready if you are.$B$BShall we?\030Protect Kinelory until she returns to Quae.\030Protect Kinelory\030The time for talk is done. Protect Kinelory if you care about the people of Hillsbrad at all.\030Hints of a New Plague?\0312,1,14,2,257,1,2713\0302,16,36,2,257,4,2713\0302,41,49,2,257,2,2713\0303,1,43,2,396,1,2713\0301,1,39,4,272,1,2712\0301,41,50,4,272,1,2712\0301,55,105,4,274,3,2712\0301,107,175,4,276,1,2712\0305,1,26,3,256,1,2712\0305,28,93,3,268,4,2712\0304,1,16,3,396,1,2713\0312713,2,4,Kinelory\0302712,2,4,Quae\0302713,3,10,Kinelory\0302713,3,11,Kinelory\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,4,Quae\031657,19,657,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030661,23,661,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6601]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It is merely dragon-talk, $N - more hot air than actual substantive information. Pompous, aggressive behavior is to be expected from their kind.\030From the skulls of our enemies is shaped a medallion. You know this medallion, yesss? You have no doubt seen it worn by your elders.$B$BTake it, whelp. Return to the Spire and present it to General Drakkisath. The General will place the final enchantment upon the medallion, attuning the trinket to your spirit.$B$BYou will wear the finished medallion as a badge of honor, symbolizing your ascension to one of our most guarded ranks: Guardian to the brood mother.$B$BGo!\030It would appear as if the charade is over. You know that the Amulet of Draconic Subversion that Myranda the Hag created for you will not function inside Blackrock Spire. Perhaps you should find Rexxar and explain your predicament. Show him the Dull Drakefire Amulet. Hopefully he will know what to do next.\030Do not panic, $N!\030Ascension...\0312,1,53,2,261,1,10321\0302,55,85,2,257,2,10321\0302,87,132,2,257,1,10321\0302,137,151,2,257,1,10321\0302,153,209,2,257,1,10321\0302,211,311,2,257,3,10321\0302,316,463,2,257,3,10321\0303,1,42,2,384,4,10321\0303,44,169,2,384,3,10321\0303,171,230,2,384,4,10321\0303,232,266,2,384,1,10321\0303,268,306,2,384,3,10321\0301,1,80,4,272,1,10182\0301,82,144,4,272,1,10182\0304,1,17,3,256,1,10182\03110363,2,5,General Drakkisath\03011872,2,9,Myranda the Hag\03010182,2,10,Rexxar\0312,15,1445,0,\0302,0,0,5,Spire\0302,0,0,5,General Drakkisath\0316585,19,6585,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306602,23,6602,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6602]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A victory that will be remembered for many years, $N. The Drakefire Amulet will open Onyxia's lair. Gather your allies and bring victory to the Horde.\030How would you feel about paying a visit to the General? No illusions, this time.$B$BCeremony? A pretty word to describe the bloodletting that amuses the Black Dragonflight.$B$BAll this amulet requires is the blood of General Drakkisath. Primitive security. There are other ways to receive the General's blood.$B$BGo to Blackrock Spire and kill Drakkisath. Return with his blood and I will activate the key to Onyxia's lair.\030Travel to Blackrock Spire and slay General Drakkisath. Gather his blood and return it to Rexxar.\030I don't think I need to tell you that Drakkisath is not to be taken lightly.$B$BI let the thousands dead by his hand do the talking.\030Blood of the Black Dragon Champion\0312,1,55,2,257,4,10182\0302,57,80,2,257,1,10182\0302,85,93,2,257,2,10182\0302,95,172,2,257,1,10182\0302,177,236,2,257,1,10182\0302,238,256,2,265,1,10182\0302,258,309,2,257,1,10182\0302,314,355,2,257,1,10182\0302,357,423,2,257,3,10182\0303,1,54,2,384,1,10182\0303,56,96,2,384,1,10182\0301,1,53,4,272,3,10182\0301,55,99,4,272,3,10182\0301,101,150,4,272,1,10182\0304,1,76,3,258,1,10182\0304,81,132,3,256,1,10182\03110363,2,5,General Drakkisath\03010363,2,10,General Drakkisath\03010182,2,11,Rexxar\0312,1583,0,0,\0302,0,0,1,General\0302,0,0,8,Blackrock Spire\0302,0,0,9,Onyxia's\0302,0,0,10,Blackrock Spire\0302,0,0,11,Rexxar\0304,0,0,14,Horde\0316601,19,6601,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,16663,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6603]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well, hi there! So Meggi told you of the trouble I have found here?\030There's trouble in Winterspring!$B$BWhy, sure, I spend some time out in the wilds and know about these things... I'm always mighty proud to say it. I consider the hours I spend out there in the hills to be golden. Help you cultivate quick reflexes, a cool head and a keen eye...$B$BIt takes judgement, brains and maturity to appreciate the wilderness in the way that I do.$B$BNow, what was I talking about?$B$BAh yes, trouble. See Donova Snowden at the hot springs and she can tell you more.$B$B\030Find Donova Snowden near the hot springs in Winterspring.\030\030Trouble in Winterspring!\0312,1,32,2,257,1,11754\0302,37,112,2,257,1,11754\0302,114,147,2,257,1,11754\0302,149,213,2,257,1,11754\0302,215,278,2,257,1,11754\0302,283,372,2,257,1,11754\0302,377,406,2,257,2,11754\0302,411,426,2,257,1,11754\0302,428,491,2,257,1,11754\0303,1,57,2,384,1,11754\0301,1,15,4,272,1,9298\0301,17,67,4,272,2,9298\0319298,2,9,Donova Snowden\0309298,2,10,Donova Snowden\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,1,Winterspring\0302,0,0,10,Winterspring\0315082,23,5082,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305082,24,5082,UNKNOWN\031",[6604]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Aye, what can I do for you?\030Have you noticed the abandoned camp to the south of here? It looks like the wildkin went crazy and destroyed just about everything they could find!$B$BI heard a rumor that one of the survivors of the attack is resting at Starfall Village, west of here. I'm sure curious about what happened... aren't you?\030Speak with Jaron Stoneshaper at Starfall Village.\030\030Enraged Wildkin\0312,1,57,2,257,2,11755\0302,59,147,2,261,4,11755\0302,152,252,2,269,1,11755\0302,254,292,2,257,1,11755\0302,294,304,2,257,2,11755\0303,1,49,2,384,1,11755\0301,1,27,4,272,2,10301\03110301,2,6,Jaron Stoneshaper\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,3,Starfall Village\0302,0,0,6,Starfall Village\0314861,23,4861,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304861,24,4861,UNKNOWN\031",[6605]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, $C. I see that there is hope yet. Are you here to assist me?\030I just got back from Felwood, $N. On my way through, I stopped at Bloodvenom Post and I met a very odd character... She seemed intent on one thing, and I suppose I could tell you what that is, but I think she'd like to explain it to you herself.$B$BIf you're interested, head to Bloodvenom Post in western Felwood and look for Winna Hazzard.$B$BWho knows, she might need your help...\030Speak with Winna Hazzard in Felwood.\030\030A Strange One\0312,1,33,2,257,1,11755\0302,35,115,2,257,1,11755\0302,117,245,2,257,4,11755\0302,250,341,2,257,4,11755\0302,346,383,2,259,4,11755\0303,1,36,2,384,1,11755\0301,9,37,4,274,3,9996\0301,39,64,4,272,2,9996\0319996,2,4,Winna Hazzard\0309996,2,6,Winna Hazzard\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,1,Felwood\0302,0,0,2,Bloodvenom Post\0302,0,0,4,Bloodvenom Post\0302,0,0,6,Felwood\0314505,23,4505,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0304505,24,4505,UNKNOWN\031",[6606]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, so Harlo be sendin' you? Well, den, who might you be? I s'pose you be wantin' my help?\030We can always use a little luck, eh? A small advantage is all it takes to turn things in your favor...$B$BI happened to make the acquaintance of a rather eccentric witch doctor some time back. She made me a lucky charm... for a price. Believe me, though, it was well worth it!$B$BMaybe you'd be interested in one of your own? Find Witch Doctor Mau'ari in Everlook. I'm not giving mine up!\030Speak with Witch Doctor Mau'ari in Everlook.\030\030A Little Luck\0312,1,36,2,257,2,11755\0302,38,102,2,257,1,11755\0302,107,192,2,257,1,11755\0302,194,221,2,257,1,11755\0302,223,234,2,257,1,11755\0302,236,276,2,257,4,11755\0302,281,325,2,257,4,11755\0302,327,364,2,257,1,11755\0302,366,388,2,257,1,11755\0303,1,44,2,384,1,11755\0301,1,28,4,272,2,10307\0301,30,57,4,272,4,10307\0301,59,90,4,272,2,10307\03110307,2,8,Witch Doctor Mau'ari\03010307,2,10,Witch Doctor Mau'ari\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,8,Everlook\0302,0,0,10,Everlook\031969,23,969,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6607]="PARTIAL\031conflict,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Now that's a fine catch!$B$BCome over here, lemme show you how to set a few lines.\030Can't say I really enjoy fishin' much. Figure I been at it for a good 20 or 30 years now.$B$BI reckon people are driven to do what they do for different reasons.$B$BNow, I'm not saying you need to fish for 30 years or catch every fish in the sea to become a master fisherman. I reckon you just need to be determined - determined enough to sit on your duff for hours at a time, doin' nothin'.$B$BI'll tell you what, catch me a few rare fish and I'll teach you a thing or two. Here's a list:\030Nat Pagle wants you to catch the following fish:$B$BMisty Reed Mahi Mahi from the Misty Reed Strand in the Swamp of Sorrows.$B$BA Sar'theris Striker from the Sar'theris Strand in Desolace.$B$BFeralas Ahi from the Verdantis River of Feralas.$B$BSavage Coast Blue Sailfin from the Savage Coast of Stranglethorn Vale.$B$BReturn to Nat Pagle when you have reeled them all in!\030Anything bitin' today?\030Nat Pagle, Angler Extreme\0312,1,38,2,257,1,12919\0302,40,89,2,257,1,12919\0302,94,161,2,257,1,12919\0302,166,275,2,259,1,12919\0302,277,391,2,259,1,12919\0302,396,474,2,257,1,12919\0302,476,489,2,257,1,12919\0303,1,48,2,386,1,12919\0303,53,124,2,384,1,12919\0303,129,188,2,384,1,12919\0303,193,240,2,384,1,12919\0303,245,314,2,384,1,12919\0303,319,371,2,384,1,12919\0301,1,24,4,304,1,12919\0301,29,82,4,272,1,12919\0304,1,22,3,256,2,12919\03112919,2,8,Nat Pagle\03012919,2,13,Nat Pagle\0312,0,0,9,Misty Reed Strand\0302,0,0,9,Swamp of Sorrows\0302,0,0,10,Sar'theris Strand\0302,0,0,10,Desolace\0302,0,0,11,Verdantis River of Feralas\0302,0,0,12,Savage Coast of Stranglethorn Vale\0302,0,0,13,Nat Pagle\031\031ITEM,16967,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,16970,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,16968,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,16969,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6608]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031'Course, you must be a friend of Lumak's.$B$BFishin'? I can tell you all 'bout fishin'.\030Lumak no can teach $N no more. You too good! Find Lumak friend, Nat Pagle. Is human but no eat! Is Lumak friend! Nat teach you fish gooder.$B$BYou find Nat in Dustwallow Marsh, south of Humie town, Thermorosomethinglikedat. Nat probably fishing. Go now!\030You think Lumak is trying to tell you that he can no longer help you improve your fishing skill. You may want to try to find his friend, Nat Pagle, a human fishing off one of the islands south of Theramore (at least that's what you think Lumak said).\030\030You Too Good.\0312,1,30,2,257,1,3332\0302,32,44,2,257,1,3332\0302,46,74,2,257,1,3332\0302,76,95,2,257,1,3332\0302,97,112,2,257,1,3332\0302,114,139,2,257,1,3332\0302,144,223,2,257,1,3332\0302,225,245,2,257,1,3332\0302,247,253,2,257,1,3332\0303,1,96,2,384,1,3332\0303,98,250,2,386,1,3332\0301,1,41,4,272,1,12919\0301,46,53,4,272,2,12919\0301,55,87,4,272,1,12919\0313332,2,1,Lumak\0303332,2,3,Lumak\03012919,2,3,Nat Pagle\0303332,2,5,Lumak\0303332,2,10,Lumak\03012919,2,11,Nat Pagle\0303332,2,11,Lumak\0312,0,0,7,Dustwallow Marsh\0302,0,0,7,Humie\0302,0,0,11,Theramore\031\031",[6609]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I've always got room on my island for visitors... I reckon...\030I'm a dwarf fer cryin' out loud, $g lad:missy;! I ain't been designed to fish! I mean look at me! I'm practically made outta stone.$B$BI got nothin' left - ye tapped me out. I've taught ye all I know, flipflop!$B$BDon't ye get it? Ah, fine. I got an ol' friend over on Kalimdor who can help ye out. 'Is name be Nat Pagle, a fine lad. Find him on the islands south o' Theramore. Git goin'!\030Travel to Kalimdor, to the coastal city of Theramore. From there you must search for an island, south of the main town. Nat Pagle awaits your arrival!\030\030I Got Nothin' Left!\0312,1,47,2,257,1,5161\0302,49,78,2,257,1,5161\0302,80,97,2,257,1,5161\0302,99,131,2,257,1,5161\0302,136,173,2,257,1,5161\0302,175,210,2,257,1,5161\0302,215,230,2,257,2,5161\0302,232,240,2,257,1,5161\0302,242,298,2,257,1,5161\0302,300,333,2,257,1,5161\0302,335,377,2,257,1,5161\0302,379,388,2,257,1,5161\0303,1,53,2,384,1,5161\0303,55,119,2,384,1,5161\0303,121,150,2,384,1,5161\0301,1,49,4,272,1,12919\0301,51,61,4,272,1,12919\03112919,2,10,Nat Pagle\03012919,2,15,Nat Pagle\0312,0,0,13,Kalimdor\0316607,24,6607,UNKNOWN\031",[661]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031So, the two troublemakers are all right after all? Haha, I'm glad to hear it. I thank you for bringing me news of their whereabouts and status--it pleases me greatly that they are still alive; the two of them are irreplaceable as friends and traveling companions.$B$BBut... it's more important I thank you properly for your help. Here. Take this along with my group's thanks.$B$BWith any luck, we'll figure out what the Forsaken are up to, and put an end to it.\030I've seen Kinelory look way worse after a night in the tavern than she does now. You obviously did a good job protecting her.$B$BThese items she brought back from the farm should at least let Phin get an idea of what's going on out here in Arathi. Just to make sure there's no retaliation after your attack, we're going to stay here for a bit longer. Would you be willing to head back to Southshore and talk to Phin?\030Find Phin Odelic in Southshore.\030\030Hints of a New Plague?\0312,1,80,2,257,1,2712\0302,82,125,2,257,1,2712\0302,130,247,2,257,1,2712\0302,249,350,2,261,3,2712\0302,352,416,2,257,4,2712\0303,1,31,2,384,1,2712\0301,1,50,4,272,2,2711\0301,52,77,4,272,1,2711\0301,79,263,4,272,1,2711\0301,268,273,4,272,1,2711\0301,275,329,4,272,1,2711\0301,331,335,4,272,1,2711\0301,337,375,4,272,1,2711\0301,380,461,4,272,1,2711\0312713,2,1,Kinelory\0302711,2,6,Phin Odelic\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,3,Arathi\0302,0,0,5,Southshore\0302,0,0,5,Phin\0302,0,0,6,Southshore\031660,19,660,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6610]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You are in for a special treat, $N. Watch and learn!$B$B<Dirge begins to prepare clamlette surprise.>\030Ever heard of a clamlette? Of course you haven't! It's my latest and greatest culinary masterpiece. Oh, $N, just thinking about a clamlette makes my mouth water.$B$BUnfortunately, I'm all out of supplies to make any! How about I make you a deal? You gather the supplies I need to make a clamlette and I'll teach you the finer points of exotic cuisine and I'll even throw in a couple of clamlettes to boot! Deal??$B$BHere's what I need:\030Dirge Quikcleave wants you to get the following items:$B$B12 Giant Eggs. You will find those on the Rocs wandering Tanaris or any other species of large bird.$B$B10 pieces of Zesty Clam Meat. You can find those in clams, naturally!$B$B20 pieces of Alterac Swiss. Get thee to a cheesery!$B$BGather all of the items and return to Dirge.\030My cravings are going to be the end of me! Hurry, $N - before I dip into my own supply.\030Clamlette Surprise\0312,1,26,2,257,2,8125\0302,28,49,2,257,1,8125\0302,51,99,2,257,1,8125\0302,101,161,2,257,1,8125\0302,166,216,2,257,1,8125\0302,218,245,2,257,2,8125\0302,247,405,2,259,1,8125\0302,407,412,2,257,2,8125\0302,417,435,2,259,1,8125\0303,1,54,2,386,1,8125\0303,59,72,2,384,1,8125\0303,74,158,2,384,3,8125\0303,163,191,2,384,1,8125\0303,193,231,2,384,1,8125\0303,236,262,2,384,1,8125\0303,264,286,2,384,1,8125\0303,291,334,2,384,1,8125\0301,1,35,4,272,1,8125\0301,37,52,4,272,1,8125\0301,57,101,4,272,1,8125\0304,1,42,3,256,3,8125\0304,44,87,3,256,1,8125\0318125,2,10,Dirge Quikcleave\0312,0,0,17,Dirge\031\031ITEM,12207,OBJECTIVE,12,15,\030ITEM,7974,OBJECTIVE,10,15,\030ITEM,8932,OBJECTIVE,20,15,",[6611]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Dirge spits out some leather sandal bits.>$B$BPfftooey...$B$B<Dirge hacks loudly.>$B$BWhat? I'll have you know that leather is surprisingly high in protein and low in carbohydrates.\030How you expect Zamja teach you anything? You got all of Zamja's cooking mojo and still you crave more!$B$BZamja can't help. Fat $r needs to go to Gadgetzan. You find a little goblin named Dirge there - he help you, fatty.$B$BWhen you become big cook on the block, you come back and teach Zamja, ok? Now go!\030Travel to Gadgetzan in the Tanaris desert and speak with Dirge Quikcleave about advancing your cooking career.\030\030To Gadgetzan You Go!\0312,1,40,2,257,2,3399\0302,42,102,2,257,1,3399\0302,107,123,2,257,1,3399\0302,125,156,2,257,1,3399\0302,158,221,2,257,1,3399\0302,226,298,2,257,2,3399\0302,300,306,2,257,1,3399\0303,1,110,2,384,1,3399\0301,1,43,4,272,1,8125\0301,48,58,4,272,1,8125\0301,63,83,4,272,1,8125\0301,88,92,4,272,2,8125\0301,94,182,4,272,1,8125\0313399,2,1,Zamja\0303399,2,3,Zamja\0303399,2,6,Zamja\0308125,2,8,Dirge Quikcleave\0312,0,0,4,Gadgetzan\0302,0,0,8,Gadgetzan\0302,0,0,8,Tanaris\0316610,23,6610,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306610,24,6610,UNKNOWN\031",[6612]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Dirge spits out leather.>$B$BPfftey...$B$B<Dirge hacks loudly.>$B$BWhat? I'll have you know that leather is surprisingly high in protein and low in carbohydrates, $R.\030I can tell by yer cooking spoon that ye know what yer doin'. Unfortunately, I can't teach ya nothin'.$B$BLuckily fer ye, I know a guy. He's a goblin and probably the best cook on Kalimdor.$B$BAyep, that's the bad news, $g lad:missy; - ye got to travel to Kalimdor. Git to Gadgetzan and find Dirge Quikcleave. He'll set ya straight.$B\030Travel to Gadgetzan in the Tanaris desert and speak with Dirge Quikcleave about advancing your cooking career.$B\030\030I Know A Guy...\0312,1,60,2,257,1,5159\0302,62,101,2,257,1,5159\0302,106,134,2,257,1,5159\0302,136,188,2,257,1,5159\0302,193,264,2,257,1,5159\0302,266,308,2,257,1,5159\0302,310,331,2,257,1,5159\0303,1,110,2,384,1,5159\0301,1,26,4,272,1,8125\0301,31,39,4,272,1,8125\0301,44,64,4,272,1,8125\0301,69,73,4,272,2,8125\0301,75,167,4,272,1,8125\0318125,2,6,Dirge Quikcleave\0308125,2,8,Dirge Quikcleave\0312,0,0,5,Kalimdor\0302,0,0,6,Gadgetzan\0302,0,0,8,Gadgetzan\0302,0,0,8,Tanaris\0316610,23,6610,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306610,24,6610,UNKNOWN\031",[662]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Knowing this information is secure will bring some ease to the command in Booty Bay. Well done, $N.\030O'Breen led the ships into the cove.  We were certain this is where the treasure could be found.  The Harbinger docked safely but as the Maiden's Folly and Spirit of Silverpine approached the tides began to lower.  Strangest thing I've ever seen!$B$BThose two ships ran aground into something... some sort of temple in the reef.  They sank so quickly, was quite a tragedy.$B$BWe need to retrieve their Logs as well as their Charts before we leave.  We can't leave that information behind for prying eyes!\030First Mate Nilzlix wants you to retrieve the Charts and Logs from the Maiden's Folly and the Spirit of Silverpine.\030How goes the search and recovery mission, $n?  We really need to get those Logs and Charts back from the Maiden's Folly and Spirit of Silverpine.$B$BIf the information from those sources were to fall into enemy hands, Fleet Master Seahorn would force us down the plank.$B$BThat is if we ever get out of this mess...\030Deep Sea Salvage\0312,1,36,2,257,1,2767\0302,39,96,2,257,4,2767\0302,99,213,2,257,1,2767\0302,216,246,2,257,1,2767\0302,251,295,2,257,1,2767\0302,297,328,2,257,1,2767\0302,331,372,2,257,1,2767\0302,377,447,2,267,1,2767\0302,450,504,2,257,1,2767\0303,1,114,2,386,1,2767\0301,1,84,4,272,3,2767\0301,86,99,4,272,1,2767\0304,1,45,3,256,2,2767\0304,48,145,3,258,1,2767\0304,150,269,3,260,4,2767\0304,274,315,3,256,4,2767\0312767,2,10,First Mate Nilzlix\0302487,3,15,Fleet Master Seahorn\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,10,Maiden's Folly\0304,0,0,11,Booty Bay\0303,0,0,14,Maiden's Folly\031663,19,663,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4487,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,4489,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,4488,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,4490,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6621]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Good work, $N. Issuing that challenge to the Foulwealds and defeating their leader sends them a strong message:$B$BThe Horde is not to be trifled with.$B$BI don't believe that tribe will be giving us much trouble for a long time.\030$N, another tribe of Furbolgs,  the Foulweald, live southeast of Astranaar.  They are not as many as the Thistlefur, but their ferocity poses a future threat.  With a show of force, we can remove that threat.$B$BTake this banner, go to the Foulweald village and place it on their totem mound.  They will try to destroy the banner, but hold your ground until their chief, Murgut, appears to save face for the tribe.  Bring me the totem he carries.$B$BGather your allies, $N.  This is no task for a single $c.\030Place Karang's Banner on the Foulweald Totem Mound.  Do not let the furbolgs destroy the banner.  Defeat Chief Murgut and bring Murgut's Totem to Karang Amakkar at Zoram'gar.\030Did you defeat Chief Murgut, $N? Did you retrieve his Foulweald Totem?\030King of the Foulweald\0312,1,75,2,257,1,12757\0302,78,158,2,261,1,12757\0302,161,208,2,261,1,12757\0302,213,292,2,257,1,12757\0302,295,414,2,271,3,12757\0302,417,446,2,257,1,12757\0302,451,473,2,257,1,12757\0302,476,507,2,257,1,12757\0303,1,51,2,384,1,12757\0303,54,96,2,388,1,12757\0303,99,174,2,384,1,12757\0301,1,14,4,272,1,12757\0301,16,111,4,272,1,12757\0301,116,151,4,272,1,12757\0301,156,229,4,272,4,12757\0304,1,32,3,256,2,12757\0304,34,70,3,256,2,12757\03112918,2,11,Chief Murgut\03012757,2,11,Karang Amakkar\03012918,3,16,Chief Murgut\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,4,Foulweald\0302,0,0,11,Karang Amakkar\0302,0,0,11,Zoram'gar\0304,0,0,13,Foulwealds\031216,19,216,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,16976,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6622]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Doctor $N, welcome to Horde Trauma.\030Good day, doctor. You will be tested on your ability to triage patients accordingly this afternoon. Should you pass your examination, you will join the prestigious ranks of Horde Trauma.$B$BNow pay attention! The critically injured must be tended to first. After the criticals come the badly injured. The injured should be tended to last. You must save 15 patients to pass this exam. You will fail should 6 of your patients die in triage.$B$BTriage bandages will be supplied.$B$BGood luck, doctor.$B\030Save patients by using Triage Bandages to tend to their wounds. You must save 15 patients before 6 of them die from their injuries.$B$BRemember the order of triage! Critically Injured Soldiers die the fastest followed by Badly Injured Soldiers. Injured Soldiers take the longest to die and should be saved AFTER your Critically Injured and Badly Injured Soldiers have been triaged.\03015 Patients Saved!\030Miraculous work, doctor. Simply miraculous.\030Triage\0312,1,17,2,257,1,12920\0302,19,99,2,257,3,12920\0302,101,186,2,257,3,12920\0302,191,208,2,257,1,12920\0302,210,256,2,257,1,12920\0302,258,300,2,257,1,12920\0302,302,338,2,257,1,12920\0302,340,383,2,265,1,12920\0302,385,438,2,257,3,12920\0302,443,475,2,257,3,12920\0302,480,497,2,257,1,12920\0303,1,63,2,392,1,12920\0303,65,131,2,392,1,12920\0303,136,164,2,384,1,12920\0303,166,244,2,384,1,12920\0303,246,381,2,384,1,12920\0301,1,35,4,272,1,12920\0305,1,24,3,256,1,12920\0305,26,43,3,256,1,12920\0304,1,18,3,384,1,12920\031\0314,0,0,17,Horde Trauma\031\031",[6623]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Wonderful. Put on your scrubs, we are to start at once!\030Doctor $N, I presume. It is a pleasure to see you again.$B$BI have some wonderful news for you! Doctor Gregory Victor, chief physician of Horde Trauma has made a personal request for you to join him at Hammerfall. This could be the opportunity of a lifetime! I would give anything to be given a chance to study under the great Doctor Gregory Victor! Do not squander this opportunity!\030Travel to Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands and speak with Doctor Gregory Victor about joining the ranks of Horde Trauma.$B\030\030Horde Trauma\0312,1,21,2,257,1,3373\0302,23,56,2,257,1,3373\0302,61,95,2,257,1,3373\0302,97,213,2,257,1,3373\0302,215,258,2,257,4,3373\0302,260,349,2,257,4,3373\0302,351,383,2,257,1,3373\0303,1,122,2,384,1,3373\0301,1,10,4,272,1,12920\0301,12,55,4,272,1,12920\03112920,2,4,Doctor Gregory Victor\03012920,2,6,Doctor Gregory Victor\03012920,2,8,Doctor Gregory Victor\0312,0,0,4,Hammerfall\0302,0,0,8,Hammerfall\0302,0,0,8,Arathi Highlands\0316622,23,6622,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306622,24,6622,UNKNOWN\031",[6624]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Doctor $N, welcome to Alliance Trauma.\030Good day, doctor. You will be tested on your ability to triage patients accordingly this afternoon. Should you pass your examination, you will join the prestigious ranks of Alliance Trauma.$B$BNow pay attention! The critically injured must be tended to first. After the criticals come the badly injured. The injured should be tended to last. You must save 15 patients to pass this exam. You will fail should 6 of your patients die in triage.$B$BGood luck, doctor.$B\030Save patients by using Triage Bandages to tend to their wounds. You must save 15 patients before 6 of them die from their injuries.$B$BRemember the order of triage! Critically Injured Soldiers die the fastest followed by Badly Injured Soldiers. Injured Soldiers take the longest to die and should be saved AFTER your Critically Injured and Badly Injured Soldiers have been triaged.\03015 Patients Saved!\030Miraculous work, doctor. Simply miraculous.\030Triage\0312,1,17,2,257,1,12939\0302,19,99,2,257,3,12939\0302,101,189,2,257,3,12939\0302,194,211,2,257,1,12939\0302,213,259,2,257,1,12939\0302,261,303,2,257,1,12939\0302,305,341,2,257,1,12939\0302,343,386,2,265,1,12939\0302,388,441,2,257,3,12939\0302,446,463,2,257,1,12939\0303,1,63,2,392,1,12939\0303,65,131,2,392,1,12939\0303,136,164,2,384,1,12939\0303,166,244,2,384,1,12939\0303,246,381,2,384,1,12939\0301,1,38,4,272,1,12939\0305,1,24,3,256,1,12939\0305,26,43,3,256,1,12939\0304,1,18,3,384,1,12939\031\0314,0,0,16,Alliance Trauma\031\031",[6625]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Wonderful. Put on your scrubs, we are to start at once!\030Doctor $N, I presume. It is a pleasure to see you.$B$BI have some wonderful news for you! Gustaf VanHowzen, chief physician of Alliance Trauma has made a personal request for you to join him at Theramore. This could be the opportunity of a lifetime! I would give anything to be given a chance to study under the great doctor, Gustaf VanHowzen! Do not squander this opportunity, doctor!\030Travel to Theramore in the Dustwallow Marsh and speak with Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen about joining the ranks of Alliance Trauma.\030\030Alliance Trauma\0312,1,21,2,257,1,5150\0302,23,50,2,257,1,5150\0302,55,89,2,257,1,5150\0302,91,204,2,257,1,5150\0302,206,249,2,257,4,5150\0302,251,343,2,257,4,5150\0302,345,385,2,257,1,5150\0303,1,126,2,384,1,5150\0301,1,10,4,272,1,12939\0301,12,55,4,272,1,12939\03112939,2,8,Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen\0312,0,0,4,Theramore\0302,0,0,8,Theramore\0302,0,0,8,Dustwallow Marsh\0316624,23,6624,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306624,24,6624,UNKNOWN\031",[6626]="PARTIAL\031consequences,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, $N! The work you've done will be a great help, I'm sure.$B$BI will continue my study of this diplomat and the rest of the quilboar here. If you seek greater adventure, I'd find a few friends and head into the cave that looks like a great boar maw just over there. I'm sure once you're inside you'll find greater challenges to face.\030The Forsaken do not pass on their... illness... from what I have seen. This diplomat seems to be granting undeath to would-be followers. I am beginning to think he is one of the Scourge.$B$BFor now, my concern is not with him though, it's with the growing ranks around him. They creep from the shadows daily, almost begging him for more power.$B$BI'm not powerful enough to fight them on my own, $N. What do you say? Are you up for some hunting?\030Kill 8 Razorfen Battleguard, 8 Razorfen Thornweavers, and 8 Death's Head Cultists and return to Myriam Moonsinger near the entrance to Razorfen Downs.\030How goes the hunt, $N? Seeing just this small sample of this diplomat's power here removes any doubt I had that the Scourge are one of the greatest threats this world has ever seen.\030A Host of Evil\0312,1,36,2,257,1,12866\0302,38,47,2,257,1,12866\0302,49,70,2,257,1,12866\0302,72,136,2,257,4,12866\0302,138,186,2,321,1,12866\0302,191,273,2,257,1,12866\0302,275,343,2,257,1,12866\0302,348,399,2,261,1,12866\0302,401,416,2,257,2,12866\0302,418,445,2,257,2,12866\0303,1,150,2,384,1,12866\0301,1,14,4,272,1,12866\0301,16,67,4,272,3,12866\0301,72,147,4,272,3,12866\0301,149,274,4,274,4,12866\0301,276,342,4,272,1,12866\0304,1,22,3,256,2,12866\0304,24,181,3,320,1,12866\0317873,2,11,Razorfen Battleguard\03012866,2,11,Myriam Moonsinger\0302809,4,15,Boar\0312,722,0,0,\0302,0,0,11,Myriam Moonsinger\0302,0,0,11,Razorfen Downs\031\031NPC,7873,OBJECTIVE,8,13,Razorfen Battleguard\030NPC,7874,OBJECTIVE,8,13,Razorfen Thornweaver\030NPC,7872,OBJECTIVE,8,13,Death's Head Cultist",[6627]="PARTIAL\031conflict,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $C. You have studied the text I asked you to, and now you have passed another of our tests.\030You have brought me the book, and now it is time for your question. Are you ready?$B$BTime is not an issue, $c, so do not feel pressured. You may take as long as you like to answer.\030Answer Braug Dimspirit's question successfully and then speak to him again. He will remain in Stonetalon Mountains when you are ready.\030Answer Braug Dimspirit's question correctly\030Life is full of questions, $C. You will never be able to answer all of them, but with some time and study, perhaps you will become a little more knowledgeable.\030Test of Lore\0312,1,67,2,257,1,4489\0302,69,82,2,257,2,4489\0302,87,137,2,257,1,4489\0302,139,181,2,257,1,4489\0303,1,75,2,384,1,4489\0303,77,134,2,384,3,4489\0301,1,14,4,272,1,4489\0301,16,102,4,304,1,4489\0305,1,30,3,256,1,4489\0305,32,159,3,256,4,4489\0304,1,43,3,384,1,4489\0314489,2,5,Braug Dimspirit\0304489,3,11,Braug Dimspirit\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,6,Stonetalon Mountains\0311154,19,1154,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301159,23,1159,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6628]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $N. I had my doubts if you studied the text I asked you to get, but you've answered correctly.\030So the time is once again upon us. As a student of lore, you have shown great tenacity by undertaking my task.$B$BAnd so now I offer you your question. If you are ready, speak to me again, and take all the time you need, $N--there is no pressure to answer quickly.\030Answer Parqual Fintallas' question successfully and then speak to him again. He will remain in the Undercity until you are ready.\030Answer Parqual Fintallas' question correctly\030There is only one rule I feel you must know if you wish to survive in this world: the more you know, the more you'll see.$B$BIf you study, if you observe, then you will begin to see things in the world that no other $r will see.\030Test of Lore\0312,1,34,2,257,1,4488\0302,36,110,2,257,1,4488\0302,115,151,2,257,1,4488\0302,153,264,2,259,4,4488\0303,1,76,2,384,1,4488\0303,78,129,2,384,3,4488\0301,1,14,4,272,1,4488\0301,16,105,4,272,4,4488\0305,1,121,3,266,4,4488\0305,126,228,3,256,4,4488\0304,1,44,3,384,1,4488\0314488,2,5,Parqual Fintallas\0304488,3,11,Parqual Fintallas\0312,400,1441,0,\0302,0,0,6,Undercity\0311160,19,1160,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301394,23,1394,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6629]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Grundig Darkcloud is dead! $N, I will always be grateful for what you've done here today.\030$N, you've done a fine job killing Grimtotem. If you dare, Grundig Darkcloud and his personal band of brutes is by far the worst of the lot. He was the one who led the brutal attack on my village.$B$BYou will find him in Grimtotem Post a bit further up the path to the west. Kill him, and I will be forever grateful.$B\030Kill Grundig Darkcloud and 6 Grimtotem Brutes, and return to Makaba Flathoof near the southeastern edge of Stonetalon.$B\030Have you killed Grundig Darkcloud and his personal band of Brutes?\030Kill Grundig Darkcloud\0312,1,45,2,257,1,11857\0302,47,140,2,257,4,11857\0302,142,196,2,261,1,11857\0302,201,274,2,257,3,11857\0302,276,316,2,257,3,11857\0303,1,118,2,384,1,11857\0301,1,26,4,272,1,11857\0301,28,89,4,272,3,11857\0304,1,66,3,256,2,11857\03111858,2,2,Grundig Darkcloud\03011858,2,6,Grundig Darkcloud\03011857,2,6,Makaba Flathoof\03011858,4,7,Grundig Darkcloud\03011858,3,9,Grundig Darkcloud\0312,406,1442,0,\0302,0,0,4,Grimtotem Post\0302,0,0,6,Makaba Flathoof\0316548,19,6548,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,11858,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Grundig Darkcloud\030NPC,11912,OBJECTIVE,6,13,Grimtotem Brute",[663]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ahoy, matey.$B$B'Twas a horrible mess. Seahorn will have my ship if he finds out what went down.$B$BOne of the Professor's contraptions indicated the lost treasure was near this cove. I brought the Harbinger in to dock and signaled for the Spirit of Silverpine and Maiden's Folly to follow suit.$B$BThen the sea rumbled. The tides lowered and the two ships crashed into the reef.$B$BIt's not just a reef. Something's down there....$B$BHelp my crew out and you'll be rewarded handsomely.\030Lolo sees a tiny $r! Always on the lookout, Lolo is!$B$BWelcome to Faldir's Cove.  Captain O'Breen said we'd only be here for a few hours.  Just long enough to gather the treasure and get back to Booty Bay.$B$BBut Lolo thinks we're going to be here a lot longer than that.  We lost the other two ships from our formation.  Poor Spirit of Silverpine and Maiden's Folly.  On the bottom of the sea they rest now!$B$BLolo suggests you talk to Captain O'Breen if you plan on sticking around here.\030Talk to Captain O'Breen in Faldir's Cove.\030\030Land Ho!\0312,1,20,2,257,1,2766\0302,22,52,2,257,1,2766\0302,57,81,2,257,1,2766\0302,84,138,2,257,1,2766\0302,141,206,2,257,1,2766\0302,211,272,2,257,3,2766\0302,275,321,2,261,1,2766\0302,324,368,2,257,1,2766\0302,371,409,2,257,1,2766\0302,414,491,2,257,4,2766\0303,1,41,2,384,1,2766\0301,1,12,4,272,1,2610\0301,17,38,4,272,1,2610\0301,40,96,4,272,4,2610\0301,101,183,4,276,1,2610\0301,185,295,4,272,1,2610\0301,300,320,4,272,1,2610\0301,322,379,4,272,1,2610\0301,384,404,4,272,1,2610\0301,406,431,4,272,1,2610\0301,436,486,4,272,1,2610\031\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,3,Faldir's Cove\0302,0,0,5,Booty Bay\0302,0,0,10,Captain O'Breen\0302,0,0,11,Captain O'Breen\0302,0,0,11,Faldir's Cove\031662,23,662,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[664]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Nice work out there, $N.$B$BThose scum deserved what they got. While nothin' will ever bring me ship or me crew back, the death of those naga gives me some solace.\030Argh, 'tis a horrible life. I should be in a watery grave right now, not sittin' here by the fire, breathin' fresh air.$B$BThe crew tried so hard to save my beautiful Maiden's Folly. Bless the boys, bless their hearts.$B$BO'Breen made it to shore safely but we weren't so lucky. The seas just sank on us, I swear.$B$BOne second we're afloat and the next water is rushin' in. And those beasts! Killed all the survivors. Horrible naga scum. I went black and ended up here, saved.$B$BI want those beasts dead.\030Captain Steelgut in Faldir's Cove wants you to kill 10 Daggerspine Raiders and 3 Daggerspine Sorceresses.\030Bah, maybe I should go kill those naga scum myself. It's obvious you're not goin' to do it.$B$BMaybe I can find some knitting needles so you can keep yourself busy.\030Drowned Sorrows\0312,1,27,2,257,1,2769\0302,29,119,2,257,1,2769\0302,124,182,2,267,1,2769\0302,184,218,2,257,1,2769\0302,223,278,2,257,1,2769\0302,280,313,2,257,1,2769\0302,318,374,2,257,1,2769\0302,376,392,2,257,1,2769\0302,394,418,2,265,1,2769\0302,420,438,2,257,1,2769\0302,440,477,2,257,1,2769\0302,482,506,2,259,1,2769\0303,1,105,2,386,1,2769\0301,1,24,4,272,1,2769\0301,29,62,4,272,1,2769\0301,64,163,4,272,3,2769\0304,1,51,3,256,4,2769\0304,53,91,3,256,1,2769\0304,96,164,3,256,4,2769\0312769,2,13,Captain Steelgut\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,13,Faldir's Cove\031\031NPC,2595,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Daggerspine Raider\030NPC,2596,OBJECTIVE,3,13,Daggerspine Sorceress",[6641]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031I have witnessed many naga attacks since I arrived here. It puts my mind at ease that Vorsha will no longer roam freely.$B$BWe are in your debt, $N.\030Vorsha the Lasher... the fiendish hydra that roams the seas...$B$BShe has attacked our outpost, each time unprovoked, laying waste to anything that falls in her path.$B$BBut I am ready, $N. I have prepared to best the hydra and end these attacks on Zoram'gar.$B$BThe naga honor the wicked nature of this beast with a brazier that remains lit on an island just off the coast. I believe that if we put it out, Vorsha will appear in anger.$B$BWe will need help, so be sure to bring some strong allies.\030Keep Muglash safe as he travels to the brazier. Help him by putting the brazier out, then protect him as you fight against the Naga.$B$BIf you are successful, return to the Zoram'gar Outpost and inform the Warsong Runner of the death of Vorsha the Lasher.\030Defeat Vorsha the Lasher\030\030Vorsha the Lasher\0312,1,20,2,257,1,12717\0302,22,62,2,257,1,12717\0302,67,166,2,261,1,12717\0302,171,189,2,257,1,12717\0302,191,259,2,261,1,12717\0302,264,374,2,257,1,12717\0302,376,436,2,257,4,12717\0302,441,498,2,259,3,12717\0303,1,47,2,384,1,12717\0303,49,132,2,396,1,12717\0303,137,255,2,384,4,12717\0301,1,56,4,276,1,12863\0301,58,120,4,272,3,12863\0301,125,148,4,272,1,12863\0304,1,24,3,384,1,12717\03112940,2,1,Vorsha the Lasher\03012717,2,9,Muglash\03012863,2,11,Warsong Runner\03012940,2,11,Vorsha the Lasher\03012940,3,15,Vorsha the Lasher\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,11,Zoram'gar Outpost\031\031",[6642]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Your offering has been accepted. Favor you have gained. Continue and you shall be allowed access to the ancient trades.\030\030\030Dark Iron, while plentiful in the Depths, is still a valued commodity amongst the Brotherhood. The sacred arms and armaments of Ragnaros favor Dark Iron.$B$BFor every 10 pieces of Dark Iron Ore you offer, favor amongst the Brotherhood you will gain.\030Favor Amongst the Brotherhood, Dark Iron Ore\0311,1,32,4,272,1,12944\0301,34,55,4,272,1,12944\0301,57,119,4,336,3,12944\0304,1,94,3,256,1,12944\0304,96,153,3,256,1,12944\0304,158,249,3,256,3,12944\03111502,3,5,Ragnaros\0312,2717,0,0,\0303,0,0,4,Depths\031\031ITEM,11370,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[6643]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Your offering has been accepted. Favor you have gained. Continue and you shall be allowed access to the ancient trades.\030\030\030Woe unto those that tempt fate inside the Molten Core. Death comes swiftly - the punishment dealt without mercy.$B$BMany of the Brotherhood have been lost in their search for Fiery Cores.$B$BOffer 1 Fiery Core and you shall be granted favor amongst the Brotherhood.\030Favor Amongst the Brotherhood, Fiery Core\0311,1,32,4,272,1,12944\0301,34,55,4,272,1,12944\0301,57,119,4,336,3,12944\0304,1,54,3,256,1,12944\0304,56,112,3,256,1,12944\0304,117,187,3,260,1,12944\0304,192,265,3,256,3,12944\031\0312,2717,0,0,\031\031ITEM,17010,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6644]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Your offering has been accepted. Favor you have gained. Continue and you shall be allowed access to the ancient trades.\030\030\030The Thorium Brotherhood sympathizes with your plight, $R. This is why Lokthos has been empowered to bargain.$B$BOffer 1 Lava Core and you shall be granted favor amongst the Brotherhood.\030Favor Amongst the Brotherhood, Lava Core\0311,1,32,4,272,1,12944\0301,34,55,4,272,1,12944\0301,57,119,4,336,3,12944\0304,1,57,3,256,1,12944\0304,59,108,3,256,1,12944\0304,113,185,3,256,3,12944\031\0312,2717,0,0,\031\031ITEM,17011,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6645]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Your offering has been accepted. Favor you have gained. Continue and you shall be allowed access to the ancient trades.\030\030\030Many of the sacred recipes require the skin from Ragnaros' chosen pets.$B$BOffer 2 Core Leather, skinned from the smoldering corpses of the Core Hounds of the Molten Core and you shall be granted favor amongst the Brotherhood.\030Favor Amongst the Brotherhood, Core Leather\0311,1,32,4,272,1,12944\0301,34,55,4,272,1,12944\0301,57,119,4,336,3,12944\0304,1,71,3,256,1,12944\0304,76,226,3,256,3,12944\031\0312,2717,0,0,\0303,0,0,4,Ragnaros'\031\031ITEM,17012,OBJECTIVE,2,15,",[6646]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Your offering has been accepted. Favor you have gained. Continue and you shall be allowed access to the ancient trades.\030\030\030The tears of the Fire Lord are a rare find indeed.$B$BOffer 1 Blood of the Mountain and you shall be granted favor amongst the Brotherhood.\030Favor Amongst the Brotherhood, Blood of the Mountain\0311,1,32,4,272,1,12944\0301,34,55,4,272,1,12944\0301,57,119,4,336,3,12944\0304,1,50,3,256,1,12944\0304,55,139,3,256,3,12944\031\0312,2717,0,0,\031\031ITEM,11382,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[665]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031The goggles work perfectly now! Well done, $N.\030Now that we are full-fledged Blackwater Raiders it is our job to help Mr. O'Breen locate the lost elven treasure.$B$BIt is next to impossible to find the gems in the dark sea without aid. The doctor has constructed some goggles that will help. He needs the goggles charged with the energy derived from the enchanted stone in the cave just up the hill.$B$BBut the cave is cursed! When we get close, we get ambushed. Defend me and I can harness the energy from the stone into the goggles.\030Escort Professor Phizzlethorpe to the cave and back.\030Defend Professor Phizzlethorpe\030This is no time to talk! The goggles need to be charged with the power of the stone!\030Sunken Treasure\0312,1,73,2,257,1,2768\0302,75,113,2,261,1,2768\0302,118,187,2,257,1,2768\0302,189,243,2,257,3,2768\0302,245,351,2,259,1,2768\0302,356,378,2,261,1,2768\0302,380,414,2,257,1,2768\0302,416,486,2,269,1,2768\0303,1,52,2,384,1,2768\0301,1,31,4,272,1,2774\0301,33,46,4,272,1,2774\0305,1,24,3,256,1,2774\0305,26,84,3,258,1,2774\0304,1,30,3,396,1,2768\0312768,2,9,Professor Phizzlethorpe\0302768,3,14,Professor Phizzlethorpe\0312,45,1417,0,\031666,23,666,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[666]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Most superb, $N! The Captain will be very pleased! And just wait until word gets back to Fleetmaster Seahorn!\030The treasure has been on the sea floor so long that the gems have calcified into thick stone. But the power harnessed in these goggles will allow you to locate them easily.$B$BA little gnomish ingenuity goes a long way!$B$BSo borrow the Goggles of Gem Hunting, $n, and see if you can collect some of the lost treasure for Captain O'Breen.$B$BI'd swim down there myself but...um...well, I have important scientific business to tend to up on the safe, dry land....er, yeah.\030Doctor Draxlegauge in Faldir's Cove wants you to collect 10 Elven Gems and return the Goggles of Gem Hunting once you are done.\030How did the goggles work? Did everything function properly? Adjustments can be made if necessary.$B$BOh, and I'll need those goggles back when you're done. I am sure Captain O'Breen will have many uses for them later on.\030Sunken Treasure\0312,1,93,2,257,1,2774\0302,95,172,2,257,3,2774\0302,177,219,2,257,1,2774\0302,224,338,2,261,4,2774\0302,343,471,2,257,1,2774\0303,1,127,2,386,1,2774\0301,1,16,4,272,1,2774\0301,18,50,4,272,3,2774\0301,52,109,4,272,1,2774\0304,1,25,3,256,2,2774\0304,27,59,3,256,2,2774\0304,61,97,3,256,4,2774\0304,102,155,3,258,1,2774\0304,157,220,3,256,3,2774\0312774,2,6,Doctor Draxlegauge\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,6,Faldir's Cove\0304,0,0,9,Fleetmaster Seahorn\031665,19,665,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030668,23,668,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4492,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[6661]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030requestItems\030title\031These'll werk nicely, matey. Me brother needs em still tickin' and kickin,' else they go sour... Ye don't want to taste no sour rat kabob.\030Avast ye scallywag. Arrrr... Arrrr ye looking fer work? We gots a serious rat problem down here an' not enough hands on the poop deck.$B$BWhat do ye say? All ye needs to do is take this here rat catchin' flute and play the melody around the vermin. They'll follow ye to the ends of the world!$B$BJust capture five of the little buggers and bring em back here. We needs em alive.$B$BArrrrr...\030Capture 5 Deeprun Rats by using the Rat Catcher's Flute. Lead the rats back to Monty. Don't forget to turn in the flute when you're finished.\030\030Rats Captured\030Yarrr... Swabby, what be takin' ye so long?\030Deeprun Rat Roundup\0312,1,19,2,257,1,12997\0302,21,28,2,257,1,12997\0302,30,55,2,257,2,12997\0302,57,134,2,261,1,12997\0302,139,153,2,257,2,12997\0302,155,248,2,259,1,12997\0302,250,292,2,257,1,12997\0302,297,359,2,257,1,12997\0302,361,378,2,259,1,12997\0302,383,391,2,257,1,12997\0303,1,56,2,384,1,12997\0303,58,85,2,384,1,12997\0303,87,141,2,384,1,12997\0301,1,28,4,272,1,12997\0301,30,96,4,274,1,12997\0301,98,138,4,272,1,12997\0306,1,8,3,256,1,12997\0306,10,43,3,256,2,12997\0305,1,13,3,384,1,12997\03112997,2,12,Monty\0312,2257,0,0,\0302,0,0,12,Monty\0316662,23,6662,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,17115,STARTER,?,10,\030NPC,13017,OBJECTIVE,5,13,Enthralled Deeprun Rat",[6662]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Poor Monty. Ever since the Gnomeregan incident, he hasn't been the same. That boy has never seen an ocean in his life, let alone being some kind of pirate.$B$B<Nipsy sighs.>$B$BAt least he keeps the flow of twitching critters coming.\030Me brother, Nipsy, runs a rat kabob operation on the other side of Deeprun. Ye needs to take this here crate o' rats to him before they go bad. Get a move on!$B$BYe have ridden a tram before, aye? It's easy. Just step aboard when she arrives and enjoy the ride. An' keep yer arms and legs inside durin' the ride, lest ye be peglegged fer life.\030Take the Carton of Mystery Meat to Nipsy at the Stormwind Deeprun Tram Depot.\030<Nipsy puts his index finger through one of the air holes in the carton.>$B$BAlive and kicking... and just in time!\030Me Brother, Nipsy\0312,1,75,2,257,1,12997\0302,77,143,2,267,1,12997\0302,145,158,2,257,1,12997\0302,163,196,2,257,2,12997\0302,198,207,2,257,1,12997\0302,209,261,2,257,1,12997\0302,263,343,2,257,1,12997\0303,1,77,2,384,1,12997\0301,1,11,4,272,1,13018\0301,13,72,4,272,1,13018\0301,74,155,4,272,1,13018\0301,160,173,4,272,1,13018\0301,178,233,4,272,1,13018\0304,1,73,3,256,1,13018\0304,78,97,3,256,1,13018\0304,99,115,3,256,1,13018\03113018,2,1,Nipsy\03013018,2,8,Nipsy\03012997,4,9,Monty\03013018,4,12,Nipsy\03013018,3,14,Nipsy\0312,2257,0,0,\0302,0,0,8,Nipsy\0302,0,0,8,Stormwind Deeprun Tram Depot\0316661,19,6661,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,17116,STARTER,?,10,",[667]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031We survived the attack!$B$BWe could not have done it without you, $N.$B$BWe'll be heading out as soon as the tide rises. If you weren't such a promising hero I'd offer you a place on my crew. But I can tell you have bigger fish to fry.$B$BEven if you are a puny $r....\030This is bad. It seems the Daggerspines are amassing for an attack.$B$BNaga are known for their ruthlessness in battle. They will keep attacking until I am dead.$B$BI don't value my own life above that of my crew members, but you must help to defend me. The crew will not be able to make it back to Booty Bay without my knowledge of the seas.$B$BThe naga will be coming from the sea. I need you to remain up here with me to fend off the attack. Man the cannon and drive them back.$B$BAre you ready, $n?\030Protect Shakes O'Breen during the attack.\030Defend Shakes O'Breen\030\030Death From Below\0312,1,12,2,257,1,2610\0302,14,66,2,261,4,2610\0302,71,118,2,261,1,2610\0302,120,160,2,261,3,2610\0302,165,252,2,271,1,2610\0302,254,341,2,257,3,2610\0302,346,382,2,257,3,2610\0302,384,443,2,263,1,2610\0302,445,479,2,257,1,2610\0302,484,501,2,257,2,2610\0303,1,41,2,396,1,2610\0301,1,23,4,276,1,2610\0301,28,69,4,272,4,2610\0301,74,120,4,272,1,2610\0301,122,191,4,272,4,2610\0301,193,235,4,272,1,2610\0301,240,268,4,272,4,2610\0304,1,21,3,396,1,2610\0312610,2,11,Shakes O'Breen\0302610,3,18,Shakes O'Breen\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,6,Booty Bay\031670,19,670,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[668]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031So the little gnomes proved their worth after all? I knew we kept those ankle biters around for a reason!\030Let's not leave Captain O'Breen waiting. He'll want to see these gems first hand. After all, that's why we're here!$B$BAnd after a few weeks of consorting with these pirates, the professor and I have realized the last thing that's good for our health is to be caught hanging on to their treasure.$B$BHere, $n, take these to O'Breen.\030Take the Elven Gems to Captain O'Breen.\030Ahoy, $C. What brings you to the bridge?\030Sunken Treasure\0312,1,40,2,257,1,2774\0302,42,81,2,259,1,2774\0302,83,115,2,257,1,2774\0302,120,296,2,257,1,2774\0302,301,332,2,257,1,2774\0303,1,39,2,384,1,2774\0301,1,50,4,272,2,2610\0301,52,105,4,272,1,2610\0304,1,9,3,256,1,2610\0304,11,40,3,256,2,2610\031\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,5,O'Breen\0302,0,0,6,Captain O'Breen\031666,19,666,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030669,23,669,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6681]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030objectiveLabel3\030requestItems\030title\031Most excellent, young thief.$B$BYou look a bit beaten down, but no worse for the wear.$B$BA long journey awaits you - long and rewarding. Are you prepared to finally embrace your destiny among the masters of Ravenholdt?$B$BSpeak with the guards outside. They will get you started.\030$N,$B$BRavenholdt has taken an interest in you, young thief. We have been watching. Your style is a bit awkward but nothing we couldn't fix.$B$BShould you be prepared to embark on a career as a disciple of Master Ravenholdt and member of the Assassin's League, you have only to bring the Seal of Ravenholdt (attached to this letter) to Ravenholdt Manor.$B$BYour first task is to find the manor, hidden away in the hills of Hillsbrad and demonstrate your cunning.$B$BRegards,$B$BFahrad\030Take the Seal of Ravenholdt to Fahrad at Ravenholdt Manor, hidden away in the hills of Hillsbrad.$B$BYour cunning will be tested along the way. Be prepared.\030\030\030Rite of Cunning\030Did you meet Milton?<Fahrad laughs.>\030The Manor, Ravenholdt\0312,8,60,2,257,1,0\0302,62,83,2,257,1,0\0302,85,140,2,257,1,0\0302,145,353,2,257,1,0\0302,358,462,2,257,1,0\0302,467,474,2,257,1,0\0302,479,484,2,257,1,0\0303,1,97,2,384,1,0\0303,102,143,2,384,3,0\0303,145,156,2,384,1,0\0301,1,28,4,272,1,6707\0301,33,86,4,272,1,6707\0301,91,137,4,272,1,6707\0301,139,219,4,272,2,6707\0301,224,253,4,272,1,6707\0301,255,280,4,272,3,6707\0307,1,36,3,256,2,6707\0306,1,15,3,384,1,0\03113936,2,1,Ravenholdt\03013936,2,4,Ravenholdt\0306707,2,7,Fahrad\03013936,2,8,Ravenholdt\0306707,2,8,Fahrad\03013936,4,14,Ravenholdt\0306707,3,17,Fahrad\0312,0,0,4,Ravenholdt Manor\0302,0,0,8,Fahrad\0302,0,0,8,Ravenholdt Manor\0316701,23,6701,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,17126,STARTER,?,10,\030NPC,13936,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Ravenholdt",[669]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, leave it to good old Shakes O'Breen! I knew that he was the right Captain for the mission!\030Fleet Master Seahorn will want to hear about our find at once.$B$BBut as you can see, we're not in much of a position to get out of here. Not only is the tide too low, but those damned creatures we disrupted are keeping a close eye on our movements.$B$BYou can be of great service to the Blackwater Raiders if you can get word to Fleet Master Seahorn in Booty Bay that we discovered the treasure and are working on extracting more.  Take him this sample as proof.\030Take the Sample Elven Gem to Fleet Master Seahorn in Booty Bay.\030What brings you to Booty Bay, $C?\030Sunken Treasure\0312,1,62,2,259,3,2610\0302,67,137,2,257,1,2610\0302,139,249,2,257,1,2610\0302,254,431,2,257,4,2610\0302,434,463,2,257,1,2610\0303,1,63,2,384,1,2610\0301,1,40,4,272,1,2487\0301,42,94,4,272,1,2487\0304,1,33,3,256,2,2487\0312487,2,1,Fleet Master Seahorn\0302487,2,4,Fleet Master Seahorn\0302487,2,6,Fleet Master Seahorn\0302610,4,7,Shakes O'Breen\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,4,Blackwater Raiders\0302,0,0,4,Fleet Master Seahorn\0302,0,0,4,Booty Bay\0302,0,0,6,Fleet Master Seahorn\0302,0,0,6,Booty Bay\0303,0,0,9,Booty Bay\031668,19,668,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030670,23,670,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[67]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The old footlocker creaks open. . . .\030Stalvan, eh?  Let me check the town registry.$B$BStalvan. . .Stalvan. . .let's see.  Ah, here we go!  I have a record of a Mr. Stalvan Mistmantle.  The last recorded address is the Moonbrook Schoolhouse.  My, talk about outdated!$B$BDo me a favor will you, friend?  If you happen to go out to Moonbrook, let me know if you get any update on this fellow.  I like to keep the records clean.\030Travel to the Moonbrook Schoolhouse and bring back any updated information about Stalvan to Clerk Daltry.\030\030The Legend of Stalvan\0312,1,12,2,257,2,267\0302,15,45,2,257,1,267\0302,50,57,2,257,1,267\0302,61,69,2,257,1,267\0302,73,83,2,257,1,267\0302,86,100,2,257,1,267\0302,103,126,2,257,1,267\0302,128,146,2,257,1,267\0302,149,203,2,257,1,267\0302,206,229,2,257,1,267\0302,234,264,2,257,2,267\0302,267,353,2,257,4,267\0302,356,388,2,257,1,267\0303,1,105,2,384,1,267\0301,1,31,4,272,1,0\031315,2,8,Stalvan Mistmantle\030267,2,14,Clerk Daltry\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,12,Moonbrook\0302,0,0,14,Moonbrook Schoolhouse\0302,0,0,14,Clerk Daltry\03166,19,66,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\03068,23,68,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,3643,FINISHER,?,12,Old Footlocker",[670]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you for making such a long and perilous journey. You have the gratitude of the Blackwater Raiders.\030Say, $n, you seem to be an adventurous type. My fleet is stuck in Booty Bay until we can restock.$B$BThere are some heavy things brewing here and abroad and I need to get some top secret correspondence to Shakes O'Breen who is tied up off the Arathi coast.$B$BCan I trust you to deliver this message safely and in confidence?\030Deliver Seahorn's Letter to Shakes O'Breen in Arathi Highlands.\030So was Seahorn impressed? I bet you his smile reached from Booty Bay to Ratchet.\030Sunken Treasure\0312,1,44,2,257,4,2487\0302,46,97,2,257,1,2487\0302,102,256,2,259,1,2487\0302,261,325,2,257,2,2487\0303,1,63,2,384,1,2487\0301,1,54,4,272,1,2610\0301,56,104,4,272,1,2610\0304,1,25,3,256,2,2610\0304,27,80,3,256,1,2610\0312610,2,3,Shakes O'Breen\0302610,2,5,Shakes O'Breen\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,2,Booty Bay\0302,0,0,3,Shakes O'Breen\0302,0,0,5,Shakes O'Breen\0302,0,0,5,Arathi Highlands\0303,0,0,9,Booty Bay\0303,0,0,9,Ratchet\031669,19,669,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030667,23,667,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6701]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hey, nice work! Keep this up and the other rogues might stop spitting on you.\030\030\030We have been entrenched in a battle with the Syndicate for years. What they lack in skill they make up for in numbers. It's impossible to kill them off fast enough to have any noticeable impact on their population!$B$BWe've found that the best way to deal with their size is to pilfer their emblems. Once an emblem is stolen the shamed member is 'dealt' with internally.$B$BPick their pockets clean and turn the emblems in to me or one of the other guards.$B$BStart at Durnholde, south of here.\030Syndicate Emblems\0311,1,15,4,272,1,6766\0301,17,77,4,272,4,6766\0304,1,65,3,260,1,6766\0304,67,118,3,256,1,6766\0304,120,214,3,256,1,6766\0304,219,299,3,256,1,6766\0304,301,370,3,260,1,6766\0304,375,456,3,256,1,6766\0304,461,494,3,256,1,6766\031\0313,0,0,9,Durnholde\0316681,19,6681,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,17124,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[671]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It will take some time for me to ascertain the true intentions of the Syndicate, but their obvious association with dark, demonic magic troubles me. I will tell you when I know more.\030I have felt a strangeness in the air... a feeling that simmers in my blood. I had my suspicions. I set off to find the source of my unease and discovered to the west, at Northfold Manor, the residual traces of demonic summoning. As I got close, my blood began to boil and the rage within me grew.$B$BOn the ground I spied an amulet of bloodstone, used to assist in demonic summoning. The one I found was depleted, however. I'll need another to examine, but I dare not return to the manor. Can you bring me some?\030Get 10 Bloodstone Amulets for Tor'gan in Hammerfall.\030Once-cursed blood still runs through my veins, $N. If someone... something is summoning demons, it must be stopped.\030Foul Magics\0312,1,39,2,257,1,2706\0302,41,75,2,257,1,2706\0302,77,96,2,257,1,2706\0302,98,228,2,257,1,2706\0302,230,296,2,257,1,2706\0302,301,383,2,257,1,2706\0302,385,422,2,257,1,2706\0302,424,488,2,259,1,2706\0302,490,511,2,257,2,2706\0303,1,52,2,384,1,2706\0301,1,148,4,272,3,2706\0301,150,182,4,272,3,2706\0304,1,50,3,260,1,2706\0304,52,64,3,256,4,2706\0304,66,115,3,256,1,2706\0312706,2,10,Tor'gan\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,4,Northfold Manor\0302,0,0,10,Hammerfall\031673,23,673,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4495,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[672]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Excellent. The spirits of the raptors that gave these eyes will lend strength to the bearer of this amulet.\030We tried to settle him in, cheer him up, telling him stories of our mighty city at Orgrimmar in Kalimdor, but nothing would move him.$B$BTales of our young Warchief, Thrall, who bears the armor and hammer of Orgrim... but, perhaps... Perhaps! A demonstration of our newly found shamanistic magic would give him new hope. It is worth a try!$B$BA small object we could make for him, yes... Bring me some raptor eyes, and I will see what I can do.\030Acquire 10 Highland Raptor Eyes from Highland Striders and Highland Thrashers for Tor'gan in Hammerfall.\030I will create an amulet that will give Gor'mul some of the strength of the raptors. Perhaps that will awaken some flame within him...\030Raising Spirits\0312,1,133,2,257,4,2706\0302,138,217,2,257,1,2706\0302,219,233,2,257,4,2706\0302,235,242,2,257,4,2706\0302,244,320,2,259,4,2706\0302,322,339,2,257,1,2706\0302,344,387,2,257,4,2706\0302,389,444,2,257,3,2706\0303,1,104,2,384,1,2706\0301,1,10,4,272,1,2706\0301,12,107,4,272,3,2706\0304,1,83,3,256,3,2706\0304,85,133,3,256,4,2706\0314949,2,2,Thrall\030107,2,8,Raptor\0301015,2,9,Highland Raptor\030107,2,9,Raptor\0302706,2,9,Tor'gan\0302792,3,12,Gor'mul\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,1,Orgrimmar\0302,0,0,1,Kalimdor\0302,0,0,9,Highland Striders\0302,0,0,9,Hammerfall\031655,19,655,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030674,23,674,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4512,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[6721]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes, it is time, $C.\030Hello, young hunter. You look to me like you are skilled enough to handle a beast and train it as your companion.$B$BYou must see Dazalar in Dolanaar. He can put you on the path to earning a pet of your own.$B\030Speak with Dazalar in Dolanaar.\030\030The Hunter's Path\0312,1,20,2,257,1,5117\0302,22,113,2,257,1,5117\0302,118,150,2,257,1,5117\0302,152,207,2,257,1,5117\0303,1,31,2,384,1,5117\0301,1,20,4,272,1,3601\0313601,2,3,Dazalar\0303601,2,5,Dazalar\0312,0,0,3,Dolanaar\0302,0,0,5,Dolanaar\0316071,22,6071,UNKNOWN\0306072,22,6072,UNKNOWN\0306073,22,6073,UNKNOWN\0306722,22,6722,UNKNOWN\0306063,23,6063,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6722]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes, it is time, $C.\030Hello, young hunter. You look to me like you are skilled enough to handle a beast and train it as your companion.$B$BYou must see Dazalar in Dolanaar. He can put you on the path to earning a pet of your own.\030Speak with Dazalar in Dolanaar.\030\030The Hunter's Path\0312,1,20,2,257,1,5515\0302,22,113,2,257,1,5515\0302,118,150,2,257,1,5515\0302,152,207,2,257,1,5515\0303,1,31,2,384,1,5515\0301,1,20,4,272,1,3601\0313601,2,3,Dazalar\0303601,2,5,Dazalar\0312,0,0,3,Dolanaar\0302,0,0,5,Dolanaar\0316071,22,6071,UNKNOWN\0306072,22,6072,UNKNOWN\0306073,22,6073,UNKNOWN\0306721,22,6721,UNKNOWN\0306063,23,6063,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[673]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031My restless nights will turn to peaceful slumber when I have destroyed this orb. Thank you, $N. It is a chilling reminder of the terrible power the demons held over the orcs before Hellscream released them from their curse.\030There is no doubt in my mind that a powerful warlock resides within the walls of Stromgarde. From time to time, using an arcane magical relic, this warlock has summoned forth terrible demons in large numbers. We must remove the source of his energy.$B$BFind the warlock and kill him. Bring me whatever magical object you find on his person, and I will take steps to destroy it and see that its power is not used to taint this land any longer.\030Retrieve Marez Cowl's Bloodstone Orb and bring it to Tor'gan in Hammerfall.\030The burning in my blood... it grows by the day. The warlock must be stopped.\030Foul Magics\0312,1,92,2,257,1,2706\0302,94,208,2,257,1,2706\0302,210,249,2,257,1,2706\0302,254,283,2,257,1,2706\0302,285,442,2,261,3,2706\0303,1,75,2,384,1,2706\0301,1,80,4,276,3,2706\0301,82,95,4,272,1,2706\0301,97,223,4,276,1,2706\0304,1,26,3,256,1,2706\0304,28,47,3,256,1,2706\0304,49,76,3,256,1,2706\0312783,2,6,Marez Cowl\0302706,2,6,Tor'gan\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,6,Tor'gan\0302,0,0,6,Hammerfall\031671,19,671,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4510,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[674]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031What is this? Polished bone. What use have I for polished bone? Will a trinket restore the Horde to its glory?\030Here, take this amulet to Gor'mul, and see if the raptors' strength can awaken the flame of the warrior that once burned through his veins.\030Give the Raptor Talon Amulet to Gor'mul.\030What hope is there when the hand of a coward can slay the mightiest of the mightiest? What hope, I ask you!\030Raising Spirits\0312,1,139,2,257,4,2706\0303,1,40,2,384,1,2706\0301,1,13,4,272,2,2792\0301,15,28,4,272,1,2792\0301,30,63,4,272,2,2792\0301,65,110,4,272,2,2792\0304,1,85,3,258,2,2792\0304,87,107,3,258,3,2792\0312792,2,1,Gor'mul\030107,2,2,Raptor\0302792,2,2,Gor'mul\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,1,Gor'mul\0302,0,0,2,Gor'mul\031672,19,672,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030675,23,675,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6741]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thanks again, $N. You do the Horde proud...\030\030\030I need more armor scraps, $N! Do you have any?\030More Booty!\0311,1,17,4,272,1,13176\0301,19,43,4,272,1,13176\0304,1,29,3,258,1,13176\0304,31,46,3,256,2,13176\031\0312,2597,1459,0,\0317224,19,7224,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,17422,OBJECTIVE,20,15,",[675]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It did not work, I see. Nonetheless, I feel that showing him the power of the shamans will eventually return Gor'mul to his once proud self. The amulet's power was not great enough to show him our newfound power.\030<Gor'mul tosses the amulet into the ground.>$B$BTor'gan sent you, didn't he? Pah! Why he feels some mercy towards me I would not understand. Mercy was denied me when I was not allowed to die with my Warchief in battle. A cruel blow fate has dealt me...\030Speak with Tor'gan.\030\030Raising Spirits\0312,1,44,2,257,1,2792\0302,49,76,2,257,2,2792\0302,78,81,2,257,1,2792\0302,83,140,2,257,4,2792\0302,142,218,2,261,1,2792\0302,220,252,2,257,1,2792\0303,1,19,2,384,1,2792\0301,1,23,4,272,1,2706\0301,25,140,4,272,3,2706\0301,142,212,4,272,1,2706\0312792,2,1,Gor'mul\0302706,2,2,Tor'gan\0302706,2,7,Tor'gan\0302792,4,9,Gor'mul\0312,45,1417,0,\031674,19,674,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030701,23,701,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[676]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031So, you think you're strong enough to help Hammerfall? So be it.$B$BTallow either sent you to that ogre mound in the hopes that you would kill yourself or he thinks you're strong enough to aid us. Either way, you're here now and I am in need of more soldiers in our fight against the constant attacks.$B$BIf you plan on staying in Hammerfall then get some rest, and come speak to me again when you're ready. There's no shortage of fighting to be had.\030Weaklings... all of them. You, $c, what are you looking at? Think you're something special, huh? Why not prove it?$B$BThe Hammerfall outpost in Arathi's under attack. Unless we send them help soon, their demise is imminent.$B$BBut before you go rushing off, you may want to test your skills first. Northeast of Stromgarde in Arathi is an ogre mound inhabited by the Boulderfist tribe. When you can handle the ogres and enforcers there, then report to Drum Fel in Hammerfall.\030Kill 8 Boulderfist Ogres and 10 Boulderfist Enforcers, then find Drum Fel in the Hammerfall outpost in Arathi Highlands.\030I have not the time to sharpen my axe, let alone leave the outpost to slay those beasts that would try and slay my kin.$B$BYou do not seem to have the experience of a grunt let alone a full-fledged warrior, what do you want, $N?\030The Hammer May Fall\0312,1,12,2,257,1,2770\0302,14,25,2,257,1,2770\0302,27,59,2,257,2,2770\0302,61,96,2,257,2,2770\0302,98,114,2,257,2,2770\0302,119,166,2,261,1,2770\0302,168,223,2,265,4,2770\0302,228,297,2,259,1,2770\0302,299,384,2,257,1,2770\0302,386,474,2,257,1,2770\0303,1,120,2,384,1,2770\0301,1,54,4,272,2,2771\0301,69,196,4,274,4,2771\0301,198,301,4,278,1,2771\0301,306,407,4,272,4,2771\0301,409,450,4,276,1,2771\0304,1,119,3,256,4,2771\0304,124,228,3,258,4,2771\031211,2,9,Ogre\0302771,2,10,Drum Fel\0302771,2,11,Drum Fel\0302770,4,13,Tallow\030211,4,13,Ogre\0312,267,1424,0,\0302,0,0,6,Arathi's\0302,0,0,9,Arathi\0302,0,0,10,Drum Fel\0302,0,0,10,Hammerfall\0302,0,0,11,Hammerfall\0302,0,0,11,Arathi Highlands\0304,0,0,15,Hammerfall the\031677,23,677,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,2562,OBJECTIVE,8,13,Boulderfist Ogre\030NPC,2564,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Boulderfist Enforcer",[6761]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes $C, thank you for coming. I apologize about the misunderstanding... the air is thick with mistrust between the Arch Druid here and Keeper Remulos in Moonglade. Each suspect the other of chicanery, and the fact that strange corruptions of Teldrassil continue unabated are still an issue here. It does little to quell mistrust.$B$BRegardless, our duty to the Cenarion Circle remains... even if those who lead it may disagree with one another.\030I have relegated my second, Mathrengyl Bearwalker, to deal with Moonglade's call for aid.  Speak to him on this matter - NOT me.$B$BLet me give you some... friendly... advice.  It is I who led us out of the darkness - NOT the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade - when all was lost for our race.  Teldrassil gives us all new life!  They would have you believe otherwise, and to believe their propaganda would be a fool's task.$B$BI'll leave it to you to decide whether or not you're a fool.\030Speak with Mathrengyl Bearwalker at the Cenarion Enclave of Darnassus.\030\030The New Frontier\0312,1,89,2,257,1,3516\0302,92,128,2,257,1,3516\0302,133,155,2,257,1,3516\0302,157,167,2,257,1,3516\0302,169,175,2,257,1,3516\0302,178,288,2,325,1,3516\0302,291,323,2,257,1,3516\0302,326,419,2,265,4,3516\0302,424,483,2,257,1,3516\0303,1,70,2,384,1,3516\0301,1,29,4,272,1,4217\0301,31,71,4,272,1,4217\0301,73,163,4,272,1,4217\0301,165,295,4,272,4,4217\0301,297,329,4,272,1,4217\0301,334,387,4,336,1,4217\0301,389,444,4,272,4,4217\0314217,2,1,Mathrengyl Bearwalker\0304217,2,10,Mathrengyl Bearwalker\03011832,4,13,Keeper Remulos\0312,1657,1457,0,\0302,0,0,6,Moonglade\0302,0,0,10,Cenarion Enclave of Darnassus\0304,0,0,13,Moonglade\0304,0,0,16,Cenarion Circle\0311015,19,1015,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306762,23,6762,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6762]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I am Rabine Saturna, and on behalf of Keeper Remulos and all of the denizens of this sacred glade I bid you welcome.$B$BI appreciate your interest and eagerness to assist the Cenarion Circle. I also know that Arch Druid of Darnassus expressed his displeasure to you in your lending us aid. Rest assured that it is for the greater good, and that you will be safe from any ill-conceived repercussions you may be the target of.$B$BYou are among friends here, $N.\030For this task, Keeper Remulos' majordomo in Moonglade - Rabine Saturna - seeks aid in exploring the vast wastelands far to the west of Tanaris... and even further west of Un'Goro.  You should find him in Nighthaven, the main village of Moonglade.$B$BWhile your work will no doubt be of tremendous benefit to us all, I advise you to tread gingerly.  There are tensions between Darnassus and Moonglade... ones that may grow over the course of time.\030Speak with Rabine Saturna in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade.  Moonglade lies between Felwood and Winterspring, accessible through a path out of Timbermaw Hold.\030\030Rabine Saturna\0312,1,145,2,257,1,4217\0302,147,179,2,257,1,4217\0302,182,246,2,257,1,4217\0302,251,347,2,257,3,4217\0302,350,402,2,257,1,4217\0302,404,446,2,257,1,4217\0303,1,66,2,384,1,4217\0303,69,165,2,384,1,4217\0301,1,116,4,272,1,11801\0301,121,191,4,336,1,11801\0301,193,289,4,272,1,11801\0301,291,424,4,280,3,11801\0301,429,459,4,272,1,11801\03111832,2,1,Keeper Remulos\03011801,2,1,Rabine Saturna\03011801,2,7,Rabine Saturna\03011801,4,9,Rabine Saturna\03011832,4,9,Keeper Remulos\0312,1657,1457,0,\0302,0,0,1,Moonglade\0302,0,0,1,Tanaris\0302,0,0,2,Un'Goro\0302,0,0,3,Nighthaven\0316761,19,6761,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301124,23,1124,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[677]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The signs of war are upon your garments, and sweat drips from your brow. Good, very good indeed.\030The Witherbark trolls and Boulderfist ogres of Arathi are working together to rid us from this land, but we shall not meet our fates at their, or anyone else's, hand. We will slay them and show them that we, too, have a home here. $B$BThe trolls turned their backs to us; the ogres would use us for food and bedding if we allowed them to--these things shall not be.$B$BWe start our attack on the Witherbark trolls to the south of here. Slay them in droves, and only return when their camps run thick with blood.\030Slay 10 Witherbark Axe Throwers, 10 Headhunters and 8 Witch Doctors, and return to Drum Fel in the Hammerfall outpost.\030If you have not yet completed my task, then perhaps you are a coward in heart as well as a tyro in war.\030Call to Arms\0312,1,166,2,257,3,2771\0302,168,230,2,257,3,2771\0302,236,365,2,257,4,2771\0302,370,435,2,261,1,2771\0302,437,511,2,257,1,2771\0303,1,118,2,384,1,2771\0301,1,72,4,276,1,2771\0301,74,96,4,272,1,2771\0304,1,103,3,260,4,2771\0312771,2,6,Drum Fel\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,6,Drum Fel\0302,0,0,6,Hammerfall\031676,19,676,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030678,23,678,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,2554,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Witherbark Axe Thrower\030NPC,2556,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Witherbark Headhunter\030NPC,2555,OBJECTIVE,8,13,Witherbark Witch Doctor",[678]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You are as strong as a kodo, and your lust for battle does your people proud.\030Your strength is evident, $N. Now to see how you fare against a real enemy.$B$BThe Boulderfists have a lair to the southwest of here towards the dwarven bridge, and, if I'm not mistaken, the maulers and magi there shall present to you a greater challenge--they have done so to us thus far.$B$BSlay as many as you can and come to me in body when you are successful, or come to me in spirit when you fail. I shall give praise to your tenacity in battle either way.\030Kill 10 Boulderfist Brutes and 4 Boulderfist Magi, and return to Drum Fel in the Hammerfall outpost.\030You hesitate. Why? You have shown great strength thus far, $N. Do not fail me now.\030Call to Arms\0312,1,29,2,257,1,2771\0302,31,75,2,261,1,2771\0302,80,289,2,257,4,2771\0302,294,403,2,257,1,2771\0302,405,462,2,261,3,2771\0303,1,100,2,384,1,2771\0301,1,77,4,276,1,2771\0304,1,13,3,256,1,2771\0304,15,18,3,256,2,2771\0304,20,62,3,256,1,2771\0304,64,82,3,256,1,2771\0312771,2,6,Drum Fel\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,6,Drum Fel\0302,0,0,6,Hammerfall\031677,19,677,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030679,23,679,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,2566,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Boulderfist Brute\030NPC,2567,OBJECTIVE,4,13,Boulderfist Magus",[6781]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031These are some good pieces, $N. I can use them to fashion new equipment for our troops.$B$BIf my supply level gets high enough, then maybe our seasoned fighting units will enter the field!\030\030\030$N, we need more armor scraps to supply our troops!\030More Armor Scraps\0311,1,31,4,272,1,13257\0301,33,87,4,272,1,13257\0301,92,188,4,276,4,13257\0304,1,51,3,258,1,13257\031\0312,2597,1459,0,\0317223,19,7223,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,17422,OBJECTIVE,20,15,",[679]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You do your people proud, $N. The threat has been greatly lessened, and I am sure we will begin to thrive here in the Highlands.\030The head of the beast is ready to be taken off... with great force, $N. You have shown every sign that you are able to help us with this final mighty blow. The leaders of these attacks have made their lair within the ruins of Stromgarde, a glaring symbol of human frailty.$B$BFind and slay those Boulderfist lords and their lackey shaman who would try and drive us from these lands.\030Kill 7 Boulderfist Shaman and 3 Boulderfist Lords and return to Drum Fel in the Hammerfall outpost.\030I see your courage finally wanes. It seems my instincts were correct about you: your strength is nothing compared to your bravado.$B$BReturn to me when the beast's head has been severed, or return never again.\030Call to Arms\0312,1,49,2,257,1,2771\0302,51,71,2,257,1,2771\0302,73,155,2,257,1,2771\0302,157,272,2,325,1,2771\0302,277,382,2,257,4,2771\0303,1,99,2,384,1,2771\0301,1,29,4,272,1,2771\0301,31,128,4,276,3,2771\0304,1,33,3,256,1,2771\0304,35,130,3,256,4,2771\0304,135,209,3,256,1,2771\03110430,2,1,The Beast\0302570,2,6,Boulderfist Shaman\0302771,2,6,Drum Fel\03010430,3,11,The Beast\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,6,Drum Fel\0302,0,0,6,Hammerfall\0304,0,0,8,Highlands\031678,19,678,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,2570,OBJECTIVE,7,13,Boulderfist Shaman\030NPC,2571,OBJECTIVE,3,13,Boulderfist Lord",[68]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Interesting. So the chap did spend some time in Moonbrook after all. It is rather odd the letter never got delivered. Nonetheless, I shall update the registry.\030You find a Dusty Unsent Letter in the old footlocker.\030Take the Dusty Unsent Letter to Clerk Daltry.\030Ah, I remember you. You're the one who was asking about that Stalvan fellow. Did you ever find what you were looking for?\030The Legend of Stalvan\0312,1,53,2,257,1,0\0303,1,45,2,384,1,0\0301,1,12,4,272,1,267\0301,14,68,4,272,1,267\0301,70,117,4,272,1,267\0301,119,159,4,272,3,267\0304,1,19,3,256,1,267\0304,21,76,3,256,1,267\0304,78,121,3,256,2,267\031267,2,2,Clerk Daltry\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,2,Clerk Daltry\0304,0,0,4,Moonbrook\03167,19,67,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\03069,23,69,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,3643,GIVER,?,9,Old Footlocker",[680]="COMPLETE\031\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have done me a great service, $N. Know that my husband's life and the safety of Hammerfall has been protected for another day because of your deeds. Please take this as a reward for your courage.\030You serve my husband well, $c, but he does not know why Hammerfall is under attack.$B$BOr'Kalar, Mug'thol's pawn in Stromgarde, has an intense hatred for my husband, and wishes nothing more than my husband's death for defeating him years ago.$B$BMy auguries tell me that Or'Kalar has laid a trap for my husband, so I have hidden signs of the ogre's presence from him.$B$BMy husband will rush off foolishly if he learns of the ogre's whereabouts and I would ask for your help in slaying the creature.\030Slay Or'Kalar and bring his Head to Korin Fel in the Hammerfall outpost.\030Near the Tower of Arathor--that is where you will find Or'Kalar. His death will stop the attacks on Hammerfall and protect my husband's life.$B$BI see in your eyes that you think me weak--even dishonorable--for my silence. Some day you will learn what it is to love as I do. Perhaps then you will understand a different kind of strength and honor.$B$BIn the meantime, do as I ask, and slay Or'Kalar.\030The Real Threat\0312,1,83,2,261,1,2772\0302,88,242,2,323,1,2772\0302,247,367,2,257,1,2772\0302,372,499,2,257,4,2772\0303,1,72,2,384,1,2772\0301,1,37,4,272,1,2772\0301,39,152,4,314,1,2772\0301,154,199,4,272,1,2772\0304,1,64,3,256,3,2772\0304,66,141,3,268,3,2772\0304,146,222,3,256,1,2772\0304,224,274,3,256,3,2772\0304,276,347,3,256,4,2772\0304,352,399,3,258,1,2772\0312773,2,2,Or'Kalar\0302773,2,3,Or'Kalar\0302773,2,5,Or'Kalar\0302772,2,5,Korin Fel\0302773,3,9,Or'Kalar\0302773,3,14,Or'Kalar\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,2,Stromgarde\0302,0,0,5,Korin Fel\0302,0,0,5,Hammerfall\031678,19,678,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4551,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6801]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The blood of our enemies has been shed. I shall mix this blood with the rest that has been gathered. Once the offering is complete, the Ice Lord shall show these Stormpike dogs the full wrath of the Frostwolf Clan!\030\030\030I come from Thunder Bluff, $r. Cairne himself has seen to it that I assist the Frostwolf Clan in these dire times.$B$BBut let us not waste any more time. You must strike down our enemies and bring to me their blood. Once enough blood has been gathered, the ritual of summoning may begin.$B$BVictory will be assured when the elemental lord is loosed upon the Stormpike army.\030Lokholar the Ice Lord\0311,1,39,4,276,1,13236\0301,41,100,4,272,3,13236\0301,102,214,4,272,3,13236\0304,1,30,3,256,1,13236\0304,32,114,3,256,1,13236\0304,119,153,3,256,1,13236\0304,155,215,3,260,1,13236\0304,217,287,3,256,1,13236\0304,292,373,3,256,3,13236\03110981,4,3,Frostwolf\03010981,3,5,Frostwolf\0312,2597,1459,0,\0303,0,0,4,Thunder Bluff\031\031ITEM,17306,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6804]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have done well, $C. The corrupted elementals you cured were an outrage to all bodies of water. Our strength lies in our purity and if we are to win our war with the others, we must remain strong.\030A force of elemental scouts was sent to the eastern plaguelands of Lordaeron, and the disease of that place twisted and infected them.  The Waterlords cannot allow this affront to our purity!$B$BTake this vial.  In it is a quantity of one aspect of Neptulon.  If used on the plagued elementals it will fight the poison within their bodies and cure them!  But their inner conflict will drive them into a surging madness.$B$BDefeat the discordant surges and bring me their bracers of binding.\030Use the Aspect of Neptulon on poisoned elementals of Eastern Plaguelands.  Bring 12 Discordant Bracers and the Aspect of Neptulon to Duke Hydraxis in Azshara.\030Do you have the bracers?\030Poisoned Water\0312,1,134,2,257,1,13278\0302,137,191,2,265,1,13278\0302,196,210,2,257,1,13278\0302,213,258,2,257,1,13278\0302,261,353,2,261,4,13278\0302,356,419,2,257,3,13278\0302,424,490,2,261,1,13278\0303,1,73,2,388,1,13278\0303,76,158,2,384,1,13278\0301,1,23,4,272,1,13278\0301,25,98,4,276,1,13278\0301,100,199,4,276,4,13278\0304,1,24,3,256,2,13278\03113278,2,9,Duke Hydraxis\0312,16,1447,0,\0302,0,0,9,Duke Hydraxis\0302,0,0,9,Azshara\031\031ITEM,17309,OBJECTIVE,12,15,",[6805]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Your bravery is proven, as is your worth to us.  Perhaps I may have future tasks for you, tasks more befitting a valued ally of the Waterlords.\030We, the elementals of water, wage war with those beings of the lesser elements.  If you are truly our ally in this conflict, then show me your conviction!$B$BFar to the south, in the desert land of Silithus, the servants of air and earth scurry in a corner of rock named the Crystal Vale.  They protect items of power from smaller beings, mortals, and although I do not know why they do this, I wish to foil their efforts.$B$BGo to the Crystal Vale in Silithus and defeat our enemies, then return to me.\030Kill 15 Dust Stormers and 15 Desert Rumblers and then return to Duke Hydraxis in Azshara.\030Cowardice is not a thing we hold in regard, $c.  Go to Silithus and prove your bravery.\030Stormers and Rumblers\0312,1,79,2,261,1,13278\0302,82,154,2,257,4,13278\0302,159,288,2,257,1,13278\0302,291,422,2,271,3,13278\0302,427,503,2,261,1,13278\0303,1,89,2,384,1,13278\0301,1,47,4,272,1,13278\0301,50,143,4,272,4,13278\0304,1,47,3,256,1,13278\0304,50,87,3,256,1,13278\03113278,2,6,Duke Hydraxis\0312,16,1447,0,\0302,0,0,5,Crystal Vale\0302,0,0,5,Silithus\0302,0,0,6,Duke Hydraxis\0302,0,0,6,Azshara\0303,0,0,10,Silithus\031\031NPC,11744,OBJECTIVE,15,13,Dust Stormer\030NPC,11746,OBJECTIVE,15,13,Desert Rumbler",[681]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very good, $N. With the deaths of those Syndicate members we should have an easier time receiving supplies from Southshore.$B$BPerhaps our cause yet has hope.\030We are fighting a war for Stromgarde, and we are losing.  The ogres, the Syndicate and we have divided our once great city, and each faction battles the other into a bloody stalemate.$B$BBut our forces dwindle while our enemy grows.$B$BWe need help from the town of Southshore, but supplies are difficult to receive while the Syndicate holds territory between us.$B$BGo to the Syndicate base in Northfold Manor and slay them.  Then, perhaps, pressure on our supply trains will lessen and more will get through.\030Kill 10 Syndicate Highwaymen and 6 Syndicate Mercenaries.$B$BReturn to Captain Nials at Refuge Pointe.\030$N, with each passing hour our hold on Stromgarde grows more tenuous. You must make haste or our city will surely fall.\030Northfold Manor\0312,1,56,2,261,1,2700\0302,59,183,2,257,1,2700\0302,188,232,2,261,1,2700\0302,237,363,2,259,1,2700\0302,368,425,2,257,1,2700\0302,428,510,2,257,4,2700\0303,1,57,2,384,1,2700\0303,62,102,2,384,1,2700\0301,1,14,4,272,1,2700\0301,16,123,4,272,1,2700\0301,128,158,4,274,4,2700\0304,1,69,3,256,1,2700\0304,71,119,3,256,3,2700\0312700,2,8,Captain Nials\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,5,Syndicate\0302,0,0,5,Northfold Manor\0302,0,0,8,Captain Nials\0302,0,0,8,Refuge Pointe\0304,0,0,10,Southshore\031682,23,682,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,2586,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Syndicate Highwayman\030NPC,2589,OBJECTIVE,6,13,Syndicate Mercenary",[682]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, $N. We will inform the families of these fallen soldiers that they were killed in battle.$B$BIt will be grim news to bear, but it is better than the uncertainty of a missing loved one.\030The Syndicate in Stromgarde do battle with our contingent of militia there. In order to urge the rabble to fight our more disciplined troops, the Syndicate leaders have placed a bounty on our soldiers, awarding gold for each Stromgarde Badge gathered off killed militiamen.$B$BWe want those badges retrieved - we cannot allow the cutthroats to take trophies from our brave fallen!$B$BEnter the Syndicate-controlled area of Stromgarde and hunt them for our badges.\030Bring 7 Stromgarde Badges to Captain Nials at Refuge Pointe.\030Have you retrieved any Stromgarde Badges, $N? The Syndicate must learn they cannot profit from our dead.\030Stromgarde Badges\0312,1,75,2,261,1,2700\0302,77,273,2,263,1,2700\0302,278,380,2,267,1,2700\0302,385,463,2,257,1,2700\0303,1,60,2,384,1,2700\0301,1,14,4,272,1,2700\0301,16,100,4,276,3,2700\0301,105,195,4,276,3,2700\0304,1,45,3,256,2,2700\0304,47,104,3,256,1,2700\0312700,2,5,Captain Nials\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,1,Stromgarde\0302,0,0,5,Captain Nials\0302,0,0,5,Refuge Pointe\031681,19,681,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4506,OBJECTIVE,7,15,",[6821]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, so you do have the strength.  And you have the cunning as well, for Blackrock Spire is more than a match for brute strength alone.$B$BIndeed $N, you may yet prove a valued ally to us...\030You have shown me that you can defeat our enemies and perform missions to further the cause of the Waterlords.  But until now you have only faced lesser foes... if pitted against a powerful enemy, can you prevail?$B$BThat is your new task.$B$BHigh up in Blackrock Spire the orcs have captured a servant of fire, the Pyroguard Emberseer.  Find his place of imprisonment, slay his captors, and then slay the emberseer.  Bring me his eye and it will show me your worth.\030Bring the Eye of the Emberseer to Duke Hydraxis in Azshara.\030Do you have the Eye, $C?  Do you have the strength to enter Blackrock Spire?\030Eye of the Emberseer\0312,1,110,2,261,1,13278\0302,113,160,2,257,1,13278\0302,162,213,2,261,4,13278\0302,218,239,2,257,1,13278\0302,244,336,2,257,1,13278\0302,339,416,2,261,1,13278\0302,419,466,2,257,3,13278\0303,1,59,2,384,1,13278\0301,1,32,4,272,1,13278\0301,35,134,4,272,1,13278\0301,139,189,4,272,1,13278\0304,1,24,3,256,2,13278\0304,27,76,3,256,2,13278\0319816,2,5,Pyroguard Emberseer\03013278,2,8,Duke Hydraxis\0312,16,1447,0,\0302,0,0,5,Blackrock Spire the\0302,0,0,8,Duke Hydraxis\0302,0,0,8,Azshara\0316804,21,6804,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306805,21,6805,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306822,23,6822,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,17322,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6822]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have done what most of your kind would think impossible.  You have faced the beings of the Molten Core, and triumphed!$B$BFor so small a creature, you have displayed great resource.$B$BSome day, perhaps we might strike a true allegiance between your kind and the Waterlords.\030$n, perhaps it is time to give you a real test.  Are you ready?$B$BAt the bottom of Blackrock Depths is a passage to the Molten Core.  This is a stronghold of our enemy, held by the most powerful servants of fire on this world.$B$BGo to the Molten Core, $N.  Show me you have the strength and the will to defeat what you find there.$B$BAnd if you have allies among your people, then rally them.  Nothing short of an army can hope to enter the Molten Core and live.\030Kill 1 Fire Lord, 1 Molten Giant, 1 Ancient Core Hound and 1 Lava Surger, then return to Duke Hydraxis in Azshara.\030Your success in the Molten Core awaits, $N.\030The Molten Core\0312,1,47,2,257,4,13278\0302,50,63,2,257,2,13278\0302,68,133,2,257,1,13278\0302,136,227,2,261,1,13278\0302,232,257,2,257,1,13278\0302,260,332,2,257,3,13278\0302,337,394,2,257,4,13278\0302,397,464,2,259,3,13278\0303,1,114,2,448,1,13278\0301,1,60,4,272,4,13278\0301,63,122,4,272,1,13278\0301,127,185,4,272,1,13278\0301,190,278,4,272,4,13278\0304,1,43,3,256,1,13278\03111658,2,9,Molten Giant\03011673,2,9,Ancient Core Hound\03011671,2,9,Core Hound\03012101,2,9,Lava Surger\03013278,2,9,Duke Hydraxis\0312,16,1447,0,\0302,0,0,3,Molten Core\0302,0,0,5,Molten Core\0302,0,0,9,Duke Hydraxis\0302,0,0,9,Azshara\0303,0,0,14,Molten Core\0316821,19,6821,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306823,23,6823,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,11658,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Molten Giant\030NPC,11668,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Firelord\030NPC,11673,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Ancient Core Hound\030NPC,12101,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Lava Surger",[6823]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Your exploits against our enemies ring through the chambers of the Waterlords, $N.  It was thought by some that your form is too small and fragile to fight in our war, but you have made great gains.  You have earned respect among us, an unbelievable feat.\030If you truly wish an allegiance with us, then I invite you to wage war on our foes, the servants of air and earth and fire.  Each defeat you heap upon them will weaken their foothold here, and further prove your adherence to our cause.$B$BThe campaign will be long, but if you persevere then your glory and honor will be great.\030Earn an Honored faction with the Hydraxian Waterlords, then talk to Duke Hydraxis in Azshara.\030\030Agent of Hydraxis\0312,1,123,2,263,4,13278\0302,126,235,2,257,3,13278\0302,240,327,2,257,4,13278\0303,1,93,2,384,1,13278\0301,1,82,4,276,1,13278\0301,85,198,4,276,1,13278\0301,201,255,4,272,1,13278\03113278,2,4,Duke Hydraxis\0312,16,1447,0,\0302,0,0,4,Duke Hydraxis\0302,0,0,4,Azshara\0316822,19,6822,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306824,23,6824,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031REPUTATION,749,OBJECTIVE,9000,16,",[6824]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have the hands!  You defeated the fire captains!  I would not have thought it possible, had I not known you and what you are capable of.$B$B$N, your exploits are without number, but word of this last feat will send waves among the Waterlords.  Your name may one day be legend to us.$B$BSpeak with me again, $N.  I may have yet another task...\030$N, your service is of great value to us, so we are reluctant to send you on this last mission for we do not want to lose such a useful agent.$B$BBut its success would further our war efforts tremendously and... it was deemed worth risking you.$B$BWe want these captains in the Molten Core destroyed: Lucifron, Sulfuron, Gehennas and Shazzrah.  Kill them and bring me their hands!$B$BThis task will take every resource you possess, $N, but if you can do it then the Firelords will be dealt a terrible blow.\030Bring the Hands of Lucifron, Sulfuron, Gehennas and Shazzrah to Duke Hydraxis in Azshara.\030Have you defeated Lucifron and the others, $N?  Do you have the hands of the enemy?\030Hands of the Enemy\0312,1,142,2,259,1,13278\0302,147,211,2,261,4,13278\0302,213,244,2,257,1,13278\0302,249,343,2,263,1,13278\0302,346,380,2,257,1,13278\0302,385,506,2,257,4,13278\0303,1,89,2,384,1,13278\0301,1,19,4,272,1,13278\0301,22,52,4,272,1,13278\0301,55,140,4,272,4,13278\0301,145,246,4,272,3,13278\0301,249,286,4,272,1,13278\0301,291,314,4,272,1,13278\0301,317,346,4,272,1,13278\0304,1,46,3,256,2,13278\0304,49,83,3,260,2,13278\03112118,2,4,Lucifron\03012259,2,4,Gehennas\03012264,2,4,Shazzrah\03012118,2,7,Lucifron\03012259,2,7,Gehennas\03012264,2,7,Shazzrah\03013278,2,7,Duke Hydraxis\03012118,3,15,Lucifron\0312,16,1447,0,\0302,0,0,4,Molten Core\0302,0,0,7,Duke Hydraxis\0302,0,0,7,Azshara\0316823,19,6823,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0307486,23,7486,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,17332,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,17329,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,17331,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,17330,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6825]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The fleet feeds on their flesh. It consumes the enemy.$B$BFlight is imminent!\030\030\030We must prepare the new fleet of War Riders, $r! My riders are set to make a strike on the central battlefield; but first, I must wet their appetites - preparing them for the assault.$B$BI need enough Stormpike Soldier Flesh to feed a fleet! Hundreds of pounds! Surely you can handle that, yes? Get going!\030Call of Air - Guse's Fleet\0311,1,31,4,272,1,13179\0301,33,54,4,276,1,13179\0301,59,77,4,272,1,13179\0304,1,48,3,260,1,13179\0304,50,183,3,256,1,13179\0304,188,241,3,258,1,13179\0304,243,261,3,256,1,13179\0304,263,294,3,256,2,13179\0304,296,305,3,256,1,13179\031\0312,2597,1459,0,\031\031ITEM,17326,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6826]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031More! More! Bring more for they are soon to be ready!\030\030\030You've worked hard, $n, but we have only just begun!$B$BMy War Riders must taste in the flesh of their targets. This will ensure a surgical strike against our enemies!$B$BMy fleet is the second most powerful in our air command. Thusly, they will strike at the more powerful of our adversaries. For this, then, they need the flesh of the Stormpike Lieutenants.$B$BMake haste, soldier!\030Call of Air - Jeztor's Fleet\0311,1,5,4,272,1,13180\0301,7,11,4,272,1,13180\0301,13,53,4,272,1,13180\0304,1,52,3,256,1,13180\0304,57,111,3,260,1,13180\0304,113,167,3,260,3,13180\0304,172,227,3,256,1,13180\0304,229,293,3,256,3,13180\0304,295,359,3,258,1,13180\0304,364,383,3,256,1,13180\031\0312,2597,1459,0,\031\031ITEM,17327,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6827]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Not enough! I would expect this level of work from an initiate, but you, $N? Come on, soldier! HUSTLE! More flesh is needed!\030\030\030I was locked up in a dwarven hellhole for days. You better believe I want revenge!$B$BWe must plan carefully.$B$BFirst, my war riders need targets to gun for - high priority targets. I'm going to need to feed them the flesh of Stormpike Commanders. Unfortunately, those little buggers are entrenched deep behind enemy lines! You've definitely got your work cut out for you.\030Call of Air - Mulverick's Fleet\0311,1,11,4,272,1,13181\0301,13,76,4,272,4,13181\0301,78,94,4,272,1,13181\0301,96,102,4,272,1,13181\0301,104,124,4,272,1,13181\0304,1,47,3,256,1,13181\0304,49,82,3,258,4,13181\0304,87,109,3,256,1,13181\0304,114,182,3,262,1,13181\0304,184,248,3,258,3,13181\0304,250,324,3,260,1,13181\0304,326,373,3,256,1,13181\031\0312,2597,1459,0,\031\031ITEM,17328,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[683]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It will take but a moment for me to peruse this letter...\030$n, I have but a small request to ask of you.$B$BTake this note I have prepared to our great monarch of Ironforge, King Magni Bronzebeard. 'Tis a small task to ask of one such as yourself, someone who has shown great valor to the cause of the Alliance thus far.$B$BFor me to go before the King in my grief-ridden state would not serve the purpose of my cause.  Surely you understand.\030Take Sara Balloo's note to King Magni Bronzebeard of Ironforge.\030So you are $N the $C? News of your contributions to the Alliance has traveled quite far, you know?$B$BOn what business do you come before me today?\030Sara Balloo's Plea\0312,1,45,2,257,1,2695\0302,50,138,2,257,1,2695\0302,140,261,2,257,1,2695\0302,266,359,2,257,4,2695\0302,362,383,2,257,1,2695\0303,1,63,2,384,1,2695\0301,1,57,4,272,3,2784\0304,1,21,3,256,2,2784\0304,23,98,3,256,2,2784\0304,103,147,3,256,2,2784\0312784,2,2,King Magni Bronzebeard\0302695,2,6,Sara Balloo\0302784,2,6,King Magni Bronzebeard\0312,1537,1455,0,\0302,0,0,6,King Magni Bronzebeard of Ironforge\0303,0,0,9,Alliance\031637,19,637,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030686,23,686,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[684]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You took down Marez Cowl? Well done, $N. Well done indeed!$B$BMarez menaced our Stromgarde defenders, and it is rumored she was an emissary between the Syndicate and some other, darker power. We are glad to see she'll longer ply her powers against us.\030A bounty has been placed on the head of Marez Cowl, a high-level advisor and operative of the Syndicate.  She was last seen within the Syndicate controlled territory of Stromgarde.$B$BBounty may be collected from Captain Nials.$B$BBe warned: Marez is a skilled and cunning Warlock, known for her trafficking with demons.  Extreme caution is advised when hunting her.\030Bring Marez's head to Captain Nials at Refuge Pointe.\030Greetings, $C. You have a report to make?\030Wanted!  Marez Cowl\0312,1,104,2,257,1,0\0302,107,180,2,257,1,0\0302,185,227,2,257,1,0\0302,232,320,2,257,1,0\0302,323,366,2,257,1,0\0303,1,53,2,384,1,0\0301,1,25,4,272,2,2700\0301,27,40,4,272,1,2700\0301,42,58,4,272,1,2700\0301,63,191,4,272,1,2700\0301,193,251,4,272,1,2700\0304,1,14,3,256,1,2700\0304,16,41,3,256,2,2700\0312783,2,1,Marez Cowl\0302700,2,3,Captain Nials\0302700,2,6,Captain Nials\0302783,4,7,Marez Cowl\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,2,Syndicate\0302,0,0,3,Captain Nials\0302,0,0,6,Captain Nials\0302,0,0,6,Refuge Pointe\031\031OBJECT,2713,GIVER,?,9,Wanted Board\030ITEM,4515,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6844]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well great monkey toads! What have you got here? It's sort of book shaped, I guess... I'll try crack this shell on it.$B$BLayo sent you to me from Silithus? I've only heard very hushed rumblings - which I guess aren't all that hushed when you think about it - about the horrors that are going on out there. Couple that with my lack of pleasure for anything bug-like, and you've got the recipe for me needing to stay here with the books!\030There's plenty to do here still, but I think taking this back to the Circle for analysis is key.  Trust me - the work will still be here once this is all said and done.  If it's a journal inside this sticky chitin, then the Circle would finally have a window into the past!$B$BTake this to the Circle's archivist in Nighthaven.  His name is Umber, and the man's brilliant.  Touched, sure, but brilliant nonetheless!  Umber's salvaged tomes in far worse shape than this.  If it can be saved, he can do it.\030Take the Encrusted Silithid Object to Umber - the Cenarion Circle's archivist - in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade.\030Why, hello there! Hrmm...$B$BLet me be a little honest with you, friend... you smell a bit ripe. Whiffy, one might say. Now I'm not making a personal assailment of your being. I'm just saying... in the future, you may want to freshen up a little after coming in from the field. It will make those first impressions a little more positively impressionable!$B$BAnyhoo... what can I do for you?\030Umber, Archivist\0312,1,96,2,257,1,13220\0302,99,168,2,257,3,13220\0302,171,273,2,257,4,13220\0302,278,327,2,257,1,13220\0302,330,372,2,257,1,13220\0302,375,415,2,257,1,13220\0302,418,469,2,257,1,13220\0302,472,504,2,257,4,13220\0303,1,120,2,448,1,13220\0301,1,24,4,272,1,11939\0301,26,48,4,272,2,11939\0301,50,85,4,272,1,11939\0301,87,118,4,272,1,11939\0301,123,156,4,272,2,11939\0301,158,306,4,272,1,11939\0301,308,436,4,272,1,11939\0304,1,17,3,256,1,11939\0304,19,25,3,256,1,11939\0304,30,74,3,256,1,11939\0304,76,96,3,256,1,11939\0304,98,119,3,256,4,11939\0304,121,175,3,256,1,11939\0304,177,194,3,256,1,11939\0304,196,277,3,258,1,11939\0304,279,355,3,256,3,11939\0304,360,368,3,256,1,11939\0304,370,391,3,256,2,11939\03111939,2,5,Umber\03011939,2,9,Umber\0312,1377,1451,0,\0302,0,0,1,Circle\0302,0,0,4,Circle's\0302,0,0,4,Nighthaven\0302,0,0,9,Umber\0304,0,0,14,Silithus\0311126,19,1126,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306845,23,6845,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6845]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, $N - I had hoped you would stop by. I am glad to see you well.$B$BI received notice you would be coming in from the field, and I wanted to personally express the Cenarion Circle's gratitude for the assistance you've given us thus far. No doubt there are more secrets to uncover from Silithus; your delivery to Umber should prove most interesting once uncovered. Please, accept this as a token of our continued appreciation for your aid.$B$BThank you, generous $C.\030Anyway, you should check back with me relatively soon... that is if you want to know what was in here.  As soon as I find out what it is, and if it's indeed a book, I'd be happy to share that information with you.$B$BIn the meantime, I'd check in with the den mother of this little bear camp, Rabine.  No doubt he'll want to know what crazy antics you've been up to.  Never leave the den mother waiting, $N... that is, unless you want to be doused in honey.$B$BIt's happened, trust me.\030Speak with Rabine Saturna in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade.\030\030Uncovering Past Secrets\0312,1,56,2,257,1,11939\0302,58,102,2,259,4,11939\0302,105,213,2,257,4,11939\0302,218,300,2,257,1,11939\0302,303,366,2,259,1,11939\0302,369,409,2,257,1,11939\0302,411,457,2,267,4,11939\0302,462,485,2,257,1,11939\0303,1,66,2,384,1,11939\0301,1,39,4,272,4,11801\0301,41,66,4,272,1,11801\0301,71,238,4,336,4,11801\0301,240,365,4,272,1,11801\0301,367,440,4,272,1,11801\0301,445,467,4,272,1,11801\0316788,2,4,Den Mother\0306788,2,6,Den Mother\03011801,2,9,Rabine Saturna\03011939,4,13,Umber\0312,493,1450,0,\0304,0,0,13,Silithus\0304,0,0,13,Umber\0316844,19,6844,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301185,23,1185,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6846]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, the orders! They say I'm to assault at will, and my will says... now!\030\030\030My troops are supplied and ready to assault.  We just need orders from Noreg Stormpike and I'll send them into the fray!\030Begin the Attack!\0311,1,15,4,272,1,13446\0301,17,68,4,272,3,13446\0301,70,73,4,272,1,13446\0304,1,44,3,256,1,13446\0304,47,120,3,258,1,13446\031\0312,2597,1459,0,\0303,0,0,5,Noreg Stormpike\031\031ITEM,17353,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6847]="PARTIAL\031conclusion,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031\030Your war in the heart of Alterac means nothing to the Syndicate, $c. We will do as we have always done: Wait until a clear victor rises from the ashes and rubble of this madness and then strike.$B$BThat, however, is not why we are here now. The All Seeing Eye has been lost - taken by the Winterax trolls of the region.$B$BRecover the Eye and our services shall be yours - for whatever time remains for your side.$B$BReturn to me once you acquire the eye so that I may examine you.$B$B<Master Ryson grins.>\030Recover Master Ryson's All Seeing Eye from the Winterax caves and return it to Master Ryson.$B$BBe warned, it is said that Master Ryson's All Seeing Eye carries with it a terrible curse!\030Master Ryson's All Seeing Eye Recovered\030\030Master Ryson's All Seeing Eye\0312,1,68,2,261,1,13151\0302,70,194,2,257,3,13151\0302,199,240,2,257,1,13151\0302,242,319,2,261,1,13151\0302,324,413,2,257,3,13151\0302,418,481,2,259,1,13151\0302,486,506,2,257,1,13151\0303,1,92,2,384,1,13151\0303,97,186,2,388,1,13151\0304,1,39,3,384,1,13151\031\0312,2597,1459,0,\0302,0,0,1,Syndicate\0302,0,0,8,Winterax\0302,0,0,8,Master Ryson\031\031",[6848]="PARTIAL\031conclusion,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031\030Your war in the heart of Alterac means nothing to the Syndicate, $c. We will do as we have always done: Wait until a clear victor rises from the ashes and rubble of this madness and then strike.$B$BThat, however, is not why we are here now. The All Seeing Eye has been lost - taken by the Winterax trolls of the region.$B$BRecover the Eye and our services shall be yours - for whatever time remains for your side.$B$BReturn to me once you acquire the eye so that I may examine you.$B$B<Master Ryson grins.>\030Recover Master Ryson's All Seeing Eye from the Winterax caves and return it to Master Ryson.$B$BBe warned, it is said that Master Ryson's All Seeing Eye carries with it a terrible curse!\030Master Ryson's All Seeing Eye Recovered\030\030Master Ryson's All Seeing Eye\0312,1,68,2,261,1,13151\0302,70,194,2,257,3,13151\0302,199,240,2,257,1,13151\0302,242,319,2,261,1,13151\0302,324,413,2,257,3,13151\0302,418,481,2,259,1,13151\0302,486,506,2,257,1,13151\0303,1,92,2,384,1,13151\0303,97,186,2,388,1,13151\0304,1,39,3,384,1,13151\031\0312,2597,1459,0,\0302,0,0,1,Syndicate\0302,0,0,8,Winterax\0302,0,0,8,Master Ryson\031\031",[685]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Falconcrest and Otto? Wonderful!$B$BHere is your reward, $N. I am happy to pay it.\030The Stromgarde Militia has placed bounties on the heads of Lord Falconcrest, and his bodyguard Otto.  Falconcrest heads the Syndicate's efforts in the Arathi Highlands, and his death would cause a major disruption in those efforts.$B$BHis bodyguard Otto, although not a strategic target, is a fierce opponent and has killed dozens of our defenders.$B$BTheir bounties may be collected from Captain Nials.\030Bring Otto's Head and Falconcrest's Head to Captain Nials at Refuge Pointe.\030Hello. Do you have a report to submit?\030Wanted!  Otto and Falconcrest\0312,1,100,2,257,1,0\0302,103,231,2,257,4,0\0302,236,348,2,257,1,0\0302,353,403,2,257,1,0\0303,1,75,2,384,1,0\0301,1,21,4,272,2,2700\0301,23,32,4,272,1,2700\0301,37,60,4,272,1,2700\0301,62,82,4,272,1,2700\0304,1,6,3,256,1,2700\0304,8,38,3,256,2,2700\0312597,2,1,Lord Falconcrest\0302599,2,1,Otto\0302599,2,3,Otto\0302700,2,4,Captain Nials\0302700,2,5,Captain Nials\0302599,4,6,Otto\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,2,Arathi Highlands\0302,0,0,4,Captain Nials\0302,0,0,5,Captain Nials\0302,0,0,5,Refuge Pointe\031\031OBJECT,2713,GIVER,?,9,Wanted Board\030ITEM,4516,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,4517,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[686]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031So King Magni Bronzebeard himself sent ye?$B$BMy, my! This must be important!\030I do not expect good dwarves like Mrs. Balloo to understand why the travesties of war must be endured for the greater good of our people. The loss of her husband, and the loss of every dwarf that fights in the name of the Alliance, weighs heavy on my soul.$B$BWhile I cannot bring her husband back from the Twisting Nether, I can pay tribute to him.$B$BI am going to commission a memorial to Sully Balloo to be built by Grand Mason Marblesten.$B$BSend word to him now, $c. You shall be custodian of my bidding.\030King Magni Bronzebeard wants you to speak with Grand Mason Marblesten.\030\030A King's Tribute\0312,1,38,2,257,1,2784\0302,40,137,2,269,1,2784\0302,139,256,2,257,1,2784\0302,261,349,2,257,1,2784\0302,354,443,2,257,3,2784\0302,448,472,2,257,1,2784\0302,474,510,2,257,3,2784\0303,1,70,2,386,1,2784\0301,1,42,4,272,2,2790\0301,55,77,4,272,1,2790\0312790,2,5,Grand Mason Marblesten\0302784,2,8,King Magni Bronzebeard\0302790,2,8,Grand Mason Marblesten\0302784,4,9,King Magni Bronzebeard\0312,1537,1455,0,\0302,0,0,4,Twisting Nether\0302,0,0,5,Sully Balloo\031683,19,683,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030689,23,689,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6861]="PARTIAL\031conclusion,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030null\030null\030I'm as anxious as you are to try out my portable shredder unit, $r, but before I can make the kit, I'm going to need materials - lots of materials! $B$BTo be exact, I'm going to need a mountain of thorium, mithril, and iron. I will also need one steamsaw per unit. You'll have to get those at the lumber mill. $B$BWhen I was nosing around in here (before my capture) I noticed a pile of steamsaws at the Stormpike lumber camp. $B$BMaster Engineer Zinfizzlex wants you to bring him the following:\030Zinfizzlex's Portable Shredder Unit\0312,1,4,2,257,1,13377\0303,1,4,2,384,1,13377\0304,1,147,3,258,3,13377\0304,153,224,3,258,3,13377\0304,226,264,3,258,3,13377\0304,266,309,3,256,1,13377\0304,315,426,3,256,1,13377\0304,432,495,3,258,1,13377\03113377,3,8,Master Engineer Zinfizzlex\0312,2597,1459,0,\0303,0,0,7,Stormpike\031\031ITEM,12359,OBJECTIVE,30,15,\030ITEM,3860,OBJECTIVE,50,15,\030ITEM,3575,OBJECTIVE,75,15,\030ITEM,17411,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6862]="PARTIAL\031conclusion,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030null\030null\030I'm as anxious as you are to try out my portable shredder unit, $r, but before I can make the kit, I'm going to need materials - lots of materials! $B$BTo be exact, I'm going to need a mountain of thorium, mithril, and iron. I will also need one steamsaw per unit. You'll have to get those at the lumber mill. $B$BWhen I was nosing around in here (before my capture) I noticed a pile of steamsaws at the Stormpike lumber camp. $B$BMaster Engineer Zinfizzlex wants you to bring him the following:\030Zinfizzlex's Portable Shredder Unit\0312,1,4,2,257,1,13377\0303,1,4,2,384,1,13377\0304,1,147,3,258,3,13377\0304,153,224,3,258,3,13377\0304,226,264,3,258,3,13377\0304,266,309,3,256,1,13377\0304,315,426,3,256,1,13377\0304,432,495,3,258,1,13377\03113377,3,8,Master Engineer Zinfizzlex\0312,2597,1459,0,\0303,0,0,7,Stormpike\031\031ITEM,12359,OBJECTIVE,30,15,\030ITEM,3860,OBJECTIVE,50,15,\030ITEM,3575,OBJECTIVE,75,15,\030ITEM,17411,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[687]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hello. Hello, hello hello hello hello HELLO!$B$BI'm sorry - wait, no I'm not! Don't be rude!$B$BOh no...that was crazy talk.$B$BBut...sometimes being crazy is my only solace.\030Theldurin the Lost was once a member of our order, the Twilight's Hammer.  But he lost his mind and scorned our teachings.  And before he fled from us, he stole the scroll of Myzrael!  We could not catch him, but rumors say he hides in the Badlands, gibbering and mad.$B$BTo bring the Lady back to us, you must find the scroll.  And to do that, you must find Theldurin.\030Find Theldurin the Lost.\030\030Theldurin the Lost\0312,1,73,2,261,1,0\0302,76,122,2,261,1,0\0302,125,183,2,265,1,0\0302,186,268,2,257,4,0\0302,273,327,2,257,1,0\0302,330,369,2,257,1,0\0303,1,24,2,388,1,0\0301,1,6,4,272,1,2785\0301,8,44,4,272,1,2785\0301,49,77,4,272,1,2785\0301,79,92,4,272,1,2785\0301,97,124,4,272,1,2785\0301,129,174,4,272,1,2785\0312785,2,1,Theldurin the Lost\0302755,2,3,Myzrael\03015065,2,5,Lady\0302785,2,7,Theldurin the Lost\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,4,Badlands\031692,23,692,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[688]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Welcome, $C. The Lady has informed me of your coming, and if we are to bring her back to the surface then we have much to discuss...\030<Myzrael speaks.>$B$BFree!  I AM FREE!  I am free to gather strength, hidden from my captors.  For if they faced me now they would surely overpower and again imprison me.$B$BBut in time I will confront the giants, and they will regret their wardship of me!$B$BYou are a noble ally, $N.  I will need your help again in time.  When I am ready, I will need you to summon me to the surface$B$BSpeak with Zaruk in Hammerfall.  He knows how I can be summoned.\030Speak with Zaruk in Hammerfall.\030\030Myzrael's Allies\0312,1,17,2,257,1,0\0302,22,26,2,257,1,0\0302,29,38,2,257,1,0\0302,41,93,2,257,1,0\0302,96,170,2,261,4,0\0302,175,256,2,257,3,0\0302,261,285,2,257,1,0\0302,288,323,2,259,3,0\0302,326,385,2,259,3,0\0302,390,420,2,257,1,0\0302,423,453,2,257,1,0\0303,1,31,2,384,1,0\0301,1,12,4,272,1,2787\0301,14,132,4,272,4,2787\0312755,2,1,Myzrael\0302787,2,10,Zaruk\0302787,2,12,Zaruk\03015065,4,14,Lady\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,10,Hammerfall\0302,0,0,12,Hammerfall\031652,19,652,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030687,23,687,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,2688,GIVER,?,9,Keystone",[6881]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $N. I will use the power of this charm to augment the magic that has already been gathered. When enough power has been amassed, I shall focus the collected energies and call upon the Forest Lord to aid our cause.\030\030\030The Frostwolf Clan is protected by a taint of elemental energy. Their shaman meddle in powers that will surely destroy us all if left unchecked.$B$BThe damage has grown too great for the Circle to control! Ivus must be called to our aid.$B$BThe Frostwolf soldiers carry elemental charms called storm crystals. We can use the charms to conjure Ivus. Venture forth and claim the crystals, $n!\030Ivus the Forest Lord\0311,1,14,4,272,1,13442\0301,16,102,4,272,3,13442\0301,104,223,4,272,3,13442\0304,1,63,3,256,1,13442\0304,65,144,3,260,4,13442\0304,149,205,3,256,1,13442\0304,207,237,3,256,1,13442\0304,242,309,3,256,1,13442\0304,311,348,3,256,1,13442\0304,350,390,3,256,1,13442\03110981,3,4,Frostwolf\03010981,3,8,Frostwolf\0312,2597,1459,0,\031\031ITEM,17423,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[689]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Perfect! Better than I could have imagined!$B$BAnd I have quite an imagination you know...\030So our good King would like a memorial built in honor of a soldier named Sully Balloo?  And you say the poor chap died during the Thandol Span tragedy?$B$BBah, will there ever be peace on Azeroth?$B$BNonetheless, any commission from the King is of utmost importance. To build a truly epic and lasting piece I want to work with one of the finest stones available. Travel to Darrow Hill in Hillsbrad and gather for me some Alterac Granite.\030Grand Mason Marblesten of Ironforge wants 5 pieces of Alterac Granite.\030$N, $N, $N! Tell me you have enough Alterac Granite for me to begin my masterpiece in honor of Sully Balloo.\030A King's Tribute\0312,1,86,2,257,4,2790\0302,89,151,2,257,2,2790\0302,156,196,2,265,2,2790\0302,201,266,2,257,1,2790\0302,268,362,2,259,1,2790\0302,364,437,2,257,1,2790\0303,1,70,2,386,1,2790\0301,1,8,4,272,1,2790\0301,10,43,4,272,4,2790\0301,48,90,4,272,1,2790\0304,13,108,3,256,1,2790\0312790,2,7,Grand Mason Marblesten\0312,1537,1455,0,\0302,0,0,4,King\0302,0,0,6,Darrow Hill\0302,0,0,6,Hillsbrad\031686,19,686,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030700,23,700,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4521,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[69]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Stalvan? Sure sounds familiar.\030Oh my!  Must have missed this the first time.  In the registry, right beneath the first address for Stalvan there's another one listed, only partially scratched out.  Looks like he was headed to The Lion's Pride Inn over in Goldshire.  Might want to check there, $N.\030Go to The Lion's Pride Inn to see if anyone there has heard of the name Stalvan.\030\030The Legend of Stalvan\0312,9,45,2,257,1,267\0302,48,165,2,257,1,267\0302,168,234,2,257,1,267\0302,237,266,2,259,4,267\0303,1,80,2,384,4,267\0301,1,8,4,272,2,295\0301,10,30,4,272,1,295\031\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,3,The Lion's Pride Inn\0302,0,0,3,Goldshire\0302,0,0,5,The Lion's Pride Inn\03168,19,68,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\03070,23,70,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[690]="PARTIAL\031consequences\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031So, Malin sent ye? I don't care if Muradin rose up from the dead and whisked ye here on a dragon. I'm busy! Talk to Kryten if you need somethin'.\030Greetings, $N. You have the look of an adventurer about you, and I have a task that needs some tending to.$B$BArchmage Trelane, my original master, fled Stromgarde in the Arathi Highlands not too long ago, and he's asked me to help him in recovering some of the items he left behind.$B$BThe city fell under siege, and he attempted to defend the Tower of Arathor, but to no avail. I have agents in the Highlands already, but they've requested I send more aid. Are you interested?\030Find Skuerto at Refuge Pointe in the Arathi Highlands.\030\030Malin's Request\0312,1,14,2,257,1,2708\0302,16,106,2,259,1,2708\0302,111,283,2,321,1,2708\0302,288,379,2,271,1,2708\0302,381,458,2,257,1,2708\0302,460,478,2,257,2,2708\0303,1,54,2,384,1,2708\0301,1,18,4,272,2,2789\0301,20,97,4,272,4,2789\0301,99,107,4,272,1,2789\0301,109,145,4,274,4,2789\0312789,2,7,Skuerto\0312,1519,1453,0,\0302,0,0,3,Arathi Highlands\0302,0,0,5,Highlands\0302,0,0,7,Refuge Pointe\0302,0,0,7,Arathi Highlands\0304,0,0,11,Kryten\031691,24,691,UNKNOWN\031",[6901]="PARTIAL\031conflict,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It's about time! Now we can show the Alliance their folly in coming to Alterac Valley!\030\030\030\030Launch the Attack!\0311,1,16,4,272,1,13449\0301,18,86,4,304,1,13449\031\0312,2597,1459,0,\0304,0,0,2,Alterac Valley\031\031ITEM,17442,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[691]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Incredible! I can see why Malin asked you to come join us - very well done indeed!$B$BAt this rate, Skuerto and I will be headed back to Stormwind in no time at all.$B$BI believe my dwarven companion is back from scouting Boulderfist Hall; go speak to him when you're ready.$B$BIt looked as though he might have had a bit of a scuffle with the ogres. Don't mention that to him, though; he's very sensitive about criticisms to his skills at scouting.\030Archmage Malin sent Skuerto and I here to collect reagents for him. I was at a loss as to how I was going to collect the items, but now that you're here, I think my problem's solved.$B$BI need the following: Witherbark tusks, Witherbark medicine pouches and a shadow hunter knife.$B$BCould you find those for me? The Witherbark live to the southeast of Arathi.\030Find 10 Witherbark Tusks, 4 Witherbark Medicine Pouches and a Shadow Hunter Knife for Apprentice Kryten at Refuge Pointe.\030Have you had any luck so far, $N?$B$B<Kryten makes some notes in his journal as he reads.>$B$BIf my research is correct, the tusks should come from any Witherbark troll. The medicine pouches come from the Witherbark witch doctors, and the strongest of the Witherbark shadow hunters should carry the special knife given to them after they've completed their rites of passage. There's no way to tell which shadow hunters will have the knife until you do battle.\030Worth Its Weight in Gold\0312,1,67,2,257,1,2788\0302,69,182,2,261,3,2788\0302,187,280,2,259,1,2788\0302,285,312,2,257,4,2788\0302,314,360,2,257,1,2788\0303,1,121,2,384,1,2788\0301,1,11,4,272,1,2788\0301,13,82,4,272,1,2788\0301,87,165,4,272,3,2788\0301,170,274,4,272,4,2788\0301,279,350,4,272,4,2788\0301,352,449,4,272,1,2788\0304,1,33,3,256,2,2788\0304,38,90,3,256,1,2788\0304,95,169,3,256,4,2788\0304,171,374,3,256,1,2788\0304,376,459,3,260,3,2788\0312708,2,1,Archmage Malin\0302789,2,1,Skuerto\0304244,2,3,Shadow\0304244,2,6,Shadow\0302788,2,6,Apprentice Kryten\0302789,4,9,Skuerto\0302552,3,15,Witherbark Troll\0304244,3,16,Shadow\0304244,3,17,Shadow\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,6,Refuge Pointe\0304,0,0,9,Stormwind\0303,0,0,16,Witherbark\031693,23,693,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4503,OBJECTIVE,10,15,\030ITEM,4522,OBJECTIVE,4,15,\030ITEM,5040,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[692]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, you found them! Good work, $N! These might be the only chance we have against the evil of Myzrael!$B$BJust let me find my scrap-ratchet and see if I can re-attach these fragments...\030The Scroll of Myzrael...the Scroll of Myzrael?!  You don't want that!  Its magic can pull Myzrael to the surface world and if you do that, we are in trouble!$B$BOr...maybe it's too late.  Maybe she already is free.  Maybe she's just gathering strength before unleashing herself upon us.  If so, then you'll NEED the scroll!$B$B...too bad it's destroyed.  Enraged elementals stole it and tore it up and now fight over the fragments.$B$BBut if you can gather those fragments, maybe we can fix it...\030Bring the Torn Scroll Fragment, the Crumpled Scroll Fragment and the Singed Scroll Fragment to Theldurin the Lost.\030Did you find those fragments?!?! You'll need the Scroll of Myzrael if you want to trap her again, before it's too late!\030The Lost Fragments\0312,1,47,2,257,2,2785\0302,50,69,2,257,1,2785\0302,72,157,2,257,4,2785\0302,162,186,2,257,4,2785\0302,189,214,2,257,4,2785\0302,217,286,2,257,4,2785\0302,289,323,2,259,4,2785\0302,328,353,2,261,1,2785\0302,356,431,2,261,1,2785\0302,436,496,2,257,4,2785\0303,1,114,2,388,1,2785\0301,1,19,4,272,1,2785\0301,21,34,4,272,1,2785\0301,36,102,4,272,4,2785\0301,107,185,4,272,4,2785\0304,1,32,3,256,2,2785\0304,34,119,3,266,4,2785\0312755,2,1,Myzrael\0302755,2,3,Myzrael\0302996,2,11,Torn\0302785,2,11,Theldurin the Lost\0302755,4,14,Myzrael\0302755,3,17,Myzrael\0312,3,1418,0,\0302,0,0,11,Theldurin the Lost\031687,19,687,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030656,23,656,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4518,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,4519,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,4520,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6921]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is exactly what I need! A fathom core is an incredible well of information that we will be able to draw much good from. Whatever the Twilight's Hammer is up to in there - and believe me when I say it is no good - my comrades and I will now uncover.$B$BYou've done well here today; the Earthen Ring looks upon you warmly for assisting us. You've also helped the Horde as a whole, and for that you should be proud.\030The Twilight's Hammer has moved into the Moonshrine Ruins of Blackfathom Deeps.  Their presence can only serve to coerce the elements into working against us.  If left unchecked, this region will be theirs for good.$B$B$N, go into Blackfathom and find the ruin's fathom stone; it should be somewhere close in the water.  In it is a fathom core - a device that when properly read it will relate a history of all elemental activity.  If I have it, I and the Earthen Ring can maybe do something to stop them!\030Bring the Fathom Core to Je'neu Sancrea at Zoram'gar Outpost, Ashenvale.\030Have you been successful in locating the fathom core?  Without it we'll have no idea what the Twilight's Hammer is exactly up to down there.\030Amongst the Ruins\0312,1,79,2,321,1,12736\0302,82,158,2,257,1,12736\0302,161,215,2,257,4,12736\0302,220,319,2,257,1,12736\0302,322,430,2,321,3,12736\0302,433,505,2,257,4,12736\0303,1,72,2,384,1,12736\0301,1,28,4,274,1,12736\0301,30,124,4,272,3,12736\0301,126,253,4,272,4,12736\0301,258,342,4,272,1,12736\0301,344,417,4,272,1,12736\0304,1,53,3,256,2,12736\0304,56,140,3,256,1,12736\03112736,2,7,Je'neu Sancrea\0312,719,0,0,\0302,0,0,7,Je'neu Sancrea\0302,0,0,7,Zoram'gar Outpost\031\031ITEM,16762,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6922]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This... this is quite the find, $N.$B$BYou acquired this from Baron Aquanis in Blackfathom, you say?  Baron Aquanis has long been thought of as a corrupted elemental power; this globe will prove what exactly had corrupted him.  While it would be no surprise if it turned out to be the Twilight's Hammer, our studies will also show how they did it as well.$B$BYou did well in bringing this to me.  Please - take this, along with the Earthen Ring's warmest regards.\030The defeated water elemental has left behind a strange water globe.  You surmise that the object somehow fed the beast energy.  Inside the globe, a putrid-looking form of water sloshes about.  The globe itself seems impervious to any sort of physical force.$B$BIf anyone can make any sense of this item, it would be Je'neu Sancrea of the Earthen Ring.  He is located at the Horde's Zoram'gar Outpost in Ashenvale.\030Bring the Strange Water Globe to Je'neu Sancrea at Zoram'gar Outpost, Ashenvale.\030Ah, hello again $N.  I was just reading the waves the sea, much like I always do.  What brings you to the outpost?\030Baron Aquanis\0312,1,67,2,257,1,0\0302,70,126,2,257,1,0\0302,129,191,2,257,1,0\0302,194,257,2,257,4,0\0302,262,351,2,257,4,0\0302,354,413,2,257,1,0\0303,1,80,2,384,1,0\0301,1,7,4,272,1,12736\0301,9,35,4,272,1,12736\0301,40,100,4,272,2,12736\0301,103,226,4,276,3,12736\0301,229,355,4,272,4,12736\0301,360,395,4,272,1,12736\0301,398,463,4,272,1,12736\0304,1,19,3,256,1,12736\0304,22,81,3,256,1,12736\0304,84,114,3,256,2,12736\031510,2,1,Water Elemental\03010430,2,2,The Beast\03012736,2,5,Je'neu Sancrea\03012736,2,7,Je'neu Sancrea\03012876,4,10,Baron Aquanis\03012876,4,11,Baron Aquanis\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,6,Horde's Zoram'gar Outpost\0302,0,0,6,Ashenvale\0302,0,0,7,Je'neu Sancrea\0302,0,0,7,Zoram'gar Outpost\0304,0,0,10,Baron Aquanis\0304,0,0,10,Blackfathom\031\031ITEM,16782,STARTER,?,10,",[693]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Brilliant, $N. One item down an' three more to go, based on my list. The other three items are all in Stromgarde.$B$BTake a rest an' get your strength back--the next phase of my plan'll require a little more time an' effort. Come back to me after you've gotten a warm meal an' some rest.\030Hey, $N. Sorry to be so short with ye earlier... and no, that ain't a pun.$B$BI figured out where Trelane's first item ended up: Kor'gresh has it in Boulderfist Hall. An' by the way he was throwing down blasts of ice at his kin to keep them in line, he must be close to figurin' out how to use all of its powers.$B$BBoulderfist Hall's south of here an' then east of Thandol Span. Find the ogre an' get back that wand.$B$BWhile you're gone, I'll figure out what we're gonna do about Stromgarde.\030Find Trelane's Wand of Invocation and return it to Skuerto at Refuge Pointe.\030Our goal is the wand, $N. Focus on that for now.\030Wand over Fist\0312,1,8,2,257,1,2789\0302,10,48,2,257,1,2789\0302,50,74,2,257,1,2789\0302,79,166,2,257,1,2789\0302,168,312,2,257,1,2789\0302,317,379,2,257,1,2789\0302,381,417,2,257,1,2789\0302,422,493,2,257,1,2789\0303,1,76,2,384,1,2789\0301,1,14,4,272,1,2789\0301,16,68,4,272,1,2789\0301,70,113,4,272,1,2789\0301,118,224,4,272,1,2789\0301,226,287,4,272,1,2789\0304,1,25,3,258,1,2789\0304,27,48,3,256,1,2789\031211,2,7,Ogre\0302789,2,9,Skuerto\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,4,Boulderfist Hall\0302,0,0,6,Thandol Span\0302,0,0,9,Skuerto\0302,0,0,9,Refuge Pointe\0304,0,0,12,Stromgarde\031691,19,691,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030694,23,694,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4525,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[694]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You amaze me, $N. Well done again.$B$BGive me a moment to cast the proper spell to enchant the gem, an' you'll be ready.\030All rested?$B$BHere's our next step: there're ogres all around the Tower of Arathor in Stromgarde. We're gonna need to activate the tower's defenses if you're gonna stand a chance against 'em an' still make it to the items alive. To do that, we're gonna need some gems the Boulderfist shaman have taken a liking to. They took 'em from the tower, but they're not gonna stay in their possession for long.$B$BGet one of them gems an' bring 'em to Kryten--he knows the spell to enchant 'em so they'll work as a key.\030Find an Azure Agate and bring it to Apprentice Kryten at Refuge Pointe.\030$N, hello again. Have you found an azure agate yet?\030Trelane's Defenses\0312,1,11,2,257,2,2789\0302,16,98,2,257,1,2789\0302,100,229,2,259,4,2789\0302,231,315,2,259,1,2789\0302,317,402,2,257,1,2789\0302,407,511,2,257,1,2789\0303,1,71,2,384,1,2789\0301,1,17,4,272,1,2788\0301,19,34,4,272,1,2788\0301,39,120,4,272,1,2788\0304,1,16,3,256,1,2788\0304,18,51,3,256,2,2788\0312570,2,4,Boulderfist Shaman\0302788,2,7,Apprentice Kryten\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,2,Stromgarde\0302,0,0,6,Kryten--he\0302,0,0,7,Apprentice Kryten\0302,0,0,7,Refuge Pointe\031693,19,693,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030695,23,695,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4527,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6941]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The flight will be ready soon. Continue your efforts!\030\030\030The elite Frostwolf units that guard the lines must be dealt with, soldier! I'm tasking you with thinning out that herd of savages. Return to me with medals from their lieutenants and legionnaires. When I feel that enough of the riff-raff has been dealt with, I'll deploy the air strike.\030Call of Air - Vipore's Fleet\0311,1,30,4,272,3,13439\0301,32,53,4,272,1,13439\0304,1,75,3,256,1,13439\0304,77,131,3,256,1,13439\0304,133,197,3,256,1,13439\0304,199,287,3,256,1,13439\03110981,3,3,Frostwolf\0312,2597,1459,0,\031\031ITEM,17503,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6942]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Keep em coming, soldier! The Aerie gryphons will be ready to strike in no time at all!\030\030\030My gryphons are poised to strike at the front lines but cannot make the attack until the lines are thinned out.$B$BThe Frostwolf warriors charged with holding the front lines wear medals of service proudly upon their chests. Rip those medals off their rotten corpses and bring them back here.$B$BOnce the front line is sufficiently thinned out, I will make the call to air! Death from above!\030Call of Air - Slidore's Fleet\0311,1,24,4,272,1,13438\0301,26,86,4,272,3,13438\0304,1,111,3,260,1,13438\0304,116,224,3,256,1,13438\0304,226,292,3,256,1,13438\0304,297,373,3,256,3,13438\0304,375,391,3,256,1,13438\03110981,3,4,Frostwolf\0312,2597,1459,0,\031\031ITEM,17502,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6943]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Can you see it? Look at them, soldier! They're coming around... Soon, Ichman's flight will once again strike at the heart of the valley! Stormpike will rule the skies!\030\030\030Their spirits are low, soldier. After our last failed air strike against the Horde, they refuse to fly! It is up to you to bolster their morale.$B$BReturn to the battlefield and strike at the heart of the Frostwolf's command. Take down their commanders and guardians. Return to me with as many of their medals as you can stuff in your pack! I promise you, when my gryphons see the bounty and smell the blood of our enemies, they will fly again! Go now!\030Call of Air - Ichman's Fleet\0311,1,15,4,272,2,13437\0301,17,38,4,272,1,13437\0301,40,63,4,272,1,13437\0301,65,136,4,272,3,13437\0301,138,167,4,272,3,13437\0304,1,31,3,256,1,13437\0304,33,103,3,256,1,13437\0304,105,144,3,256,1,13437\0304,149,225,3,256,1,13437\0304,227,267,3,256,1,13437\0304,269,340,3,256,1,13437\0304,342,444,3,260,3,13437\0304,446,452,3,256,1,13437\031\0312,2597,1459,0,\031\031ITEM,17504,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[695]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Good, good.$B$BIf there are no other delays, how about we get started?\030Here you are, $N. The gem only needs to be pressed against one of the pedestals near the base of the tower to activate its defenses. Use it when you're ready to enter the tower and find Trelane's remaining items. $B$BGood luck to you. I'll be awaiting your return here at the camp. Oh, and speak to Skuerto before you leave. He'll give you the rest of the details you'll need.\030Speak to Skuerto.\030\030An Apprentice's Enchantment\0312,1,17,2,257,1,2788\0302,19,132,2,259,1,2788\0302,134,212,2,257,1,2788\0302,218,234,2,257,1,2788\0302,236,281,2,257,1,2788\0302,283,324,2,257,1,2788\0302,326,376,2,259,1,2788\0303,1,17,2,384,1,2788\0301,1,11,4,272,1,2789\0301,16,70,4,272,4,2789\0312789,2,6,Skuerto\0302789,2,8,Skuerto\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,6,Skuerto\0302,0,0,8,Skuerto\031694,19,694,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030696,23,696,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[696]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Malin couldn't've asked a worthier person to come here an' aid us, $N. You've done a grand job!$B$BHe'll be pleased to see what an overwhelming success our mission's been.\030Here's what your lookin' for: Trelane's phylactery, Trelane's orb, an' Trelane's ember agate.$B$BAll three should be in chests within the tower an' you shouldn't have a problem opening the chests on your own; you just have to be careful of the ogres.$B$BThe tower's defenses won't take care of 'em on their own; you'll need to have your weapons at the ready. Those ogres find out you're there and stealing from 'em, an' they'll be sure to put the hurt on you.$B$BBe careful, an' good luck.\030Find Trelane's Phylactery, Trelane's Orb, and Trelane's Ember Agate, and return them to Skuerto at Refuge Pointe.\030You do this, an' I'm sure Malin'll be more than pleased with you.\030Attack on the Tower\0312,1,93,2,257,1,2789\0302,98,250,2,261,1,2789\0302,255,358,2,259,1,2789\0302,360,459,2,257,1,2789\0302,464,489,2,257,1,2789\0303,1,113,2,384,1,2789\0301,1,70,4,272,1,2789\0301,72,95,4,272,1,2789\0301,100,171,4,272,1,2789\0304,1,65,3,256,1,2789\0317266,2,1,Ember\0307266,2,6,Ember\0302789,2,6,Skuerto\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,6,Skuerto\0302,0,0,6,Refuge Pointe\031695,19,695,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030697,23,697,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4530,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,4531,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,4532,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6961]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ho ho hello.  I am Greatfather Winter, and I - courtesy of the fine folks of Smokywood Pastures... \"Fresh from our farm to your plate, it's Smokywood Pastures wholesome goodness\" - would like to wish you a fantastic Feast of Winter Veil.$B$BIf you've been good this year, maybe you will receive treats from Smokywood Pastures as your treat for the Feast of Winter Veil.  Huzzah.\030Have a wondrous Winter Veil, friend!  Be sure to say hello to Greatfather Winter!  If you've been nice this year, you'll receive wondrous treats on the day of the Feast of Winter Veil.  Be sure to tell him what you hope to get this year!$B$BAlso, be sure to stock up on treats to give those who've been nice this year.  We have a great selection to choose from.  Fresh from our farm to your plate - it's Smokywood Pastures wholesome goodness!\030Speak with Greatfather Winter; he is located near the Smokywood Pastures vendor area in Orgrimmar.\030\030Great-father Winter is Here!\0312,1,36,2,257,1,13418\0302,39,81,2,257,1,13418\0302,84,184,2,257,4,13418\0302,187,237,2,259,3,13418\0302,242,318,2,257,1,13418\0302,321,361,2,257,1,13418\0302,364,442,2,257,1,13418\0303,1,98,2,384,1,13418\0301,1,12,4,272,1,13445\0301,15,98,4,272,1,13445\0301,100,237,4,274,4,13445\0301,242,369,4,272,4,13445\0301,372,378,4,272,1,13445\03113444,2,2,Greatfather Winter\03013444,2,8,Greatfather Winter\03013444,4,10,Greatfather Winter\0312,0,0,2,Greatfather Winter\0302,0,0,8,Smokywood Pastures\0302,0,0,8,Orgrimmar\0304,0,0,12,Smokywood Pastures\031\031",[6962]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You're quite the helper to ol' Great-father Winter there, $N.  Have a great Feast of Winter Veil.$B$BHere's a little something... you know, for the effort.\030Hey, can you do Great-father Winter a favor, um, little $g boy : girl;?$B$BNot to needlessly talk about myself in the third person, but Great-father Winter has been at this all day and he could use a treat himself.  Some gingerbread cookies and ice cold milk to wash them down with would really hit the spot.  Think you could be a friend to the Great-father and fetch some for me?\030Bring 5 Gingerbread Cookies and an Ice Cold Milk to Great-father Winter in Orgrimmar.\030All this talk of treats has given me a hankering for some myself.  Mmmm... gingerbread cookies and milk...\030Treats for Great-father Winter\0312,1,71,2,257,2,13445\0302,76,214,2,257,4,13445\0302,217,308,2,257,4,13445\0302,311,380,2,257,4,13445\0303,1,85,2,384,1,13445\0301,1,61,4,272,1,13445\0301,64,97,4,272,1,13445\0301,102,129,4,272,1,13445\0301,131,155,4,272,1,13445\0304,1,65,3,256,1,13445\0304,68,74,3,256,1,13445\0304,76,106,3,256,1,13445\03113445,2,1,Great-father Winter\030371,2,1,Girl\03013445,2,2,Great-father Winter\0304950,2,3,Spot\03013445,2,5,Great-father Winter\03013445,4,6,Great-father Winter\0312,0,0,4,Great-father\0302,0,0,5,Great-father Winter\0302,0,0,5,Orgrimmar\031\031ITEM,17197,OBJECTIVE,5,15,\030ITEM,1179,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6963]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Y-y-you can h-h-hear me!  Thank the b-b-bottom line!$B$BI'm not really a s-s-snowman - my n-n-name is Sacks, and I w-w-work for the Orgrimmar b-b-branch of Smokywood Pastures... I g-g-got sent out here to look for a m-m-missing package, when I was attacked by a c-c-creature I have never seen b-b-before!$B$BSo v-v-very cold...\030Listen... not to shatter the magic of the season here, but Smokywood Pastures could use some assistance - the kind you adventuring types are known to give.$B$BWe're missing an important shipment of treats that was restocking us for the season, and now we're missing the agent of Smokywood Pastures that we sent out to the field to find it!  Please - the shipment was last reported in the Alterac Mountains, and that's where our man went to look for it.$B$BSee if both are out there, safe and sound!\030Locate the Smokywood Pastures investigator that has gone missing in the snowy regions of the Alterac Mountains.\030\030Stolen Winter Veil Treats\0312,1,9,2,257,1,13418\0302,11,155,2,257,4,13418\0302,160,339,2,261,1,13418\0302,342,452,2,257,1,13418\0302,457,498,2,257,4,13418\0303,1,111,2,388,1,13418\0301,1,24,4,272,1,13636\0301,27,52,4,272,1,13636\0301,57,177,4,272,1,13636\0301,179,304,4,276,1,13636\0301,309,327,4,272,1,13636\031\0312,0,0,4,Alterac Mountains\0316983,23,6983,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6964]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The Feast of Winter Veil, you say?  Alas, in times past it held a more substantial meaning to us tauren.  Nowadays, it seems as though others have turned the legend of this season of renewal into something that helps to sell candies and presents.$B$BIt's no surprise that Furmund is bitter about that sort of change.  He and other tauren like him cling to our past like a banner of war.  While I think a little celebration is always good, it is important to remember the origins of the Feast.\030Gifts, treats, presents... bah, I say!$B$BThose goblins pollute the true meaning of this season - the Feast of Winter Veil.  This is a time of renewal; the land slumbers under a blanket of snow brought forth by Greatfather Winter, who is NOT the bumbling fool over there in the red suit!$B$BIf you're interested in learning what the Feast is all about for yourself, ask Sagorne Creststrider.  I'm sure he'll be surprised that someone cares about history rather than getting presents.\030Speak with Sagorne Creststrider in the Valley of Wisdom of Orgrimmar about the Feast of Winter Veil.\030\030The Reason for the Season\0312,1,26,2,257,1,9550\0302,28,38,2,257,1,9550\0302,43,123,2,257,1,9550\0302,126,287,2,257,1,9550\0302,292,391,2,257,4,9550\0302,394,483,2,321,1,9550\0303,1,100,2,384,1,9550\0301,1,34,4,272,2,13417\0301,37,104,4,272,1,13417\0301,107,246,4,272,4,13417\0301,251,316,4,272,1,13417\0301,319,386,4,276,1,13417\0301,389,492,4,272,1,13417\03113444,2,4,Greatfather Winter\03013417,2,5,Sagorne Creststrider\03013417,2,7,Sagorne Creststrider\0309550,4,11,Furmund\0312,0,0,7,Valley of Wisdom of Orgrimmar\0317061,23,7061,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[697]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Archmage Malin opens the letter, and his eyes grow wide.>$B$BBy the Light, you've done it. How wonderful. Trelane will be so pleased. I'm sure Kryten and Skuerto are just as excited as I am to have them on their way back to Stormwind.$B$BThank you, $N. Please, take this to help you in your journeys.\030Take this letter back to Stormwind and let Malin know that Kryten an' I'll be home soon. He'll reward you well for helping us here, $N, of that I've no doubt.$B$BTravel safely.\030Take the Sealed Letter to Archmage Malin in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind.\030Yes? You look vaguely familiar. I do apologize, but have we met? I get so busy I lose track.\030Malin's Request\0312,1,88,2,257,1,2789\0302,90,158,2,257,1,2789\0302,163,176,2,257,1,2789\0303,1,74,2,384,1,2789\0301,1,58,4,272,1,2708\0301,63,91,4,272,1,2708\0301,93,106,4,272,1,2708\0301,108,134,4,272,3,2708\0301,136,235,4,272,1,2708\0301,240,253,4,272,1,2708\0301,255,301,4,272,1,2708\0304,1,4,3,256,2,2708\0304,6,31,3,256,1,2708\0304,33,64,3,256,2,2708\0304,66,92,3,256,1,2708\0312708,2,4,Archmage Malin\0302708,4,5,Archmage Malin\0302789,4,9,Skuerto\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,1,Stormwind\0302,0,0,4,Archmage Malin\0302,0,0,4,Mage Quarter of Stormwind\0304,0,0,9,Stormwind\031696,19,696,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[698]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah! Wonderful. Fresh meat for the fire tonight. Thank you, $N.$B$BYou've helped make the coming nights more tolerable. The fire burns bright, and our stomachs will be full.$B$BIts a pleasant surprise to have you bring us a shipment; Dar's not the most attractive orc anyone's laid eyes upon, but at least his attitude reeks far less than his smell.\030I'm working on getting some supplies together for our outpost near the beach to the east--Tok'kar does what he can, but between shifts of guard duty and cooking for his soldiers there's not much time left in the day.$B$BThey do enjoy cooking up some sawtooth meat when they can, but I haven't had time to get them another shipment. Would you mind helping them out?$B$BThe young sawtooths aren't as tasty as the older ones, so stay clear of those; give them a year or two to get to full size.\030Bring 8 Unprepared Sawtooth Flanks to Tok'Kar in Swamp of Sorrows.\030Lok'tar, $C. Traveling through the swamps isn't a risk taken lightly. You're brave to test your mettle here.\030Lack of Surplus\0312,1,216,2,257,1,5591\0302,221,331,2,257,1,5591\0302,333,364,2,257,4,5591\0302,369,491,2,257,1,5591\0303,1,66,2,384,1,5591\0301,5,14,4,272,1,5592\0301,16,47,4,272,1,5592\0301,49,62,4,272,1,5592\0301,67,118,4,272,1,5592\0301,120,172,4,272,3,5592\0301,177,348,4,272,1,5592\0304,1,12,3,256,1,5592\0304,14,69,3,264,1,5592\0304,71,108,3,256,1,5592\0315592,2,5,Tok'Kar\03011045,4,10,Burns\0312,8,1435,0,\0302,0,0,5,Tok'Kar\0302,0,0,5,Swamp of Sorrows\031699,23,699,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6169,OBJECTIVE,8,15,",[6981]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Oh... I have never seen anything like this...\030The shard is a brilliant green, and although solid, what looks like smoke swirls just below the surface. You can't help staring into the depths of the crystal; at the same time, you know there is something very disturbing about it.$B$BMaybe you should see if anyone in Ratchet can tell you more about this strange shard.\030Travel to Ratchet to find someone that can tell you more about the glowing shard.$B$BThen, deliver the shard as you are directed.\030Speak with someone in Ratchet about the Glowing Shard\030Hello, $R. What can I do for you?\030The Glowing Shard\0312,1,104,2,257,1,0\0302,106,231,2,257,1,0\0302,236,320,2,257,4,0\0303,1,81,2,384,1,0\0303,86,129,2,384,1,0\0301,7,45,4,272,1,8418\0305,1,10,3,256,1,8418\0305,12,33,3,256,2,8418\0304,1,53,3,384,1,0\031\0312,718,0,0,\0302,0,0,3,Ratchet\0302,0,0,4,Ratchet\0303,0,0,9,Ratchet\031\031ITEM,10441,STARTER,?,10,",[6982]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, you got them. Good work, $N! These supplies are a little musty from sitting in that dark mine for so long, but we'll make use of them nonetheless.$B$BThank you, $N. Your deeds are vital to the maintenance of our fighting forces.\030The Coldtooth mine is a storage depot for the Horde.  I can't stomach the food they give their troops, and the state of their arms and armor is atrocious!  But... in times like these when supplies are so important, we can use what they have.$B$BEnter the Coldtooth mine and bring me back their supplies.  That will help keep the Alliance in fighting shape, and remove much needed equipment from the Horde's warriors.$B$BGood luck, $N.  The mine is to the distant south, deep in Horde territory.\030Bring 10 Coldtooth Supplies to the Alliance Quartermaster in Dun Baldar.\030Have you been to the Coldtooth mine, $N? Do you have the supplies I asked for?\030Coldtooth Supplies\0312,1,52,2,257,1,12096\0302,55,154,2,257,1,12096\0302,157,162,2,257,1,12096\0302,164,241,2,257,1,12096\0302,246,303,2,257,1,12096\0302,306,416,2,261,3,12096\0302,421,434,2,257,1,12096\0302,437,494,2,257,1,12096\0303,1,72,2,384,1,12096\0301,1,17,4,272,1,12096\0301,19,32,4,272,1,12096\0301,34,150,4,272,1,12096\0301,155,168,4,272,1,12096\0301,170,232,4,276,1,12096\0304,1,40,3,256,2,12096\0304,42,78,3,256,2,12096\031\0312,2597,1459,0,\0302,0,0,6,Horde's\0302,0,0,8,Horde\0302,0,0,9,Alliance Quartermaster\0302,0,0,9,Dun Baldar\0303,0,0,15,Coldtooth\031\031ITEM,17542,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[6983]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You found it!  You've saved Smokywood Pasture's Feast of Winter Veil!$B$BPoor Sacks... we'll be sure to send a team out there and figure out a way to unfreeze him.  Hopefully, he'll be back in time for the day of the Feast; he'll need to make up missed time working though.  Still, this wouldn't even be possible if it weren't for you!\030A c-c-creature called \"The Abominable Greench\" is the one w-w-who stole our shipment of t-t-treats, $N.  Be c-c-careful though!  He is t-t-the one who turned me into this s-s-snowy mess!$B$BYou're g-g-gonna need some help in f-f-facing him.  I've seen him w-w-wander all around where the y-y-yeti are; he's s-s-surely here s-s-somewhere!  F-f-find the treats $N, take them b-b-back to Smokywood Pastures in Orgrimmar, and t-t-tell them I n-n-need to be unfrozen!\030Locate and return the Stolen Treats to Kaymard Copperpinch in Orgrimmar.  It was last thought to be in the possession of the Abominable Greench, found somewhere in the snowy regions of the Alterac Mountains.\030$N - our Feast of Winter Veil will be ruined without those treats to restock!  Graccu himself will miss out on sharing his delicious meat pies with all the good boys and girls this season...\030You're a Mean One...\0312,1,103,2,257,1,13636\0302,106,127,2,257,1,13636\0302,130,186,2,257,1,13636\0302,191,240,2,259,1,13636\0302,243,337,2,257,1,13636\0302,340,462,2,257,1,13636\0303,1,72,2,388,1,13636\0303,75,207,2,384,1,13636\0301,1,13,4,272,1,13418\0301,16,69,4,272,1,13418\0301,74,86,4,272,1,13418\0301,88,163,4,272,1,13418\0301,166,273,4,274,3,13418\0301,276,335,4,272,4,13418\0304,1,77,3,256,3,13418\0304,80,190,3,256,3,13418\03113602,2,1,The Abominable Greench\03013418,2,7,Kaymard Copperpinch\03013602,2,8,The Abominable Greench\0312,0,0,6,Smokywood Pastures\0302,0,0,6,Orgrimmar\0302,0,0,7,Kaymard Copperpinch\0302,0,0,7,Orgrimmar\0316963,19,6963,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0306984,23,6984,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,17662,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[6984]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ho ho hello, adventurer!$B$BThe goblins told me that you have earned a special gift this holiday season, and I am pleased to give it to you.  Here you go - have a wondrous Feast of Winter Veil this and every season in the future.\030We at Smokywood Pastures appreciate the recovery of the stolen treats, $N.  For that, we'd like to offer you a special gift... presented by none other than Great-father Winter himself!$B$BPlease, speak with Great-father Winter, and he will give you your Feast of Winter Veil gift from us here at Smokywood Pastures.  From our farm to your plate, it's always Smokywood Pastures wholesome goodness... thanks to you, of course!\030Speak with Great-father Winter in Orgrimmar.\030\030A Smokywood Pastures Thank You!\0312,1,74,2,261,1,13418\0302,77,126,2,257,1,13418\0302,128,184,2,257,1,13418\0302,189,315,2,257,3,13418\0302,318,398,2,257,1,13418\0302,400,424,2,257,1,13418\0303,1,44,2,384,1,13418\0301,1,24,4,272,1,13445\0301,29,140,4,272,1,13445\0301,143,229,4,272,1,13445\03113445,2,3,Great-father Winter\03013445,2,4,Great-father Winter\03013445,2,7,Great-father Winter\0312,0,0,1,Smokywood Pastures\0302,0,0,4,Smokywood Pastures\0302,0,0,7,Orgrimmar\0316983,19,6983,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[6985]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You got them! Nicely done, $N! And I hope you saw a few dwarves during your raid, and shed their blood for the Frostwolves!\030The Stormpike dwarves are using the Irondeep mine as a storage depot.  I want you to raid that mine and bring me its supplies.  This will curtail the Stormpikes' efforts in Alterac Valley, and will provide us with needed equipment!$B$BBe wary, $N.  The Irondeep mine is deep in Alliance territory, and control of the mine is as shifting as the snows of Alterac.\030Bring 10 Irondeep Supplies to the Horde Quartermaster in Frostwolf Keep.\030Did you enter the Irondeep mine, $N? Did you raid its supplies?\030Irondeep Supplies\0312,1,69,2,257,1,12097\0302,72,126,2,259,1,12097\0302,129,231,2,257,3,12097\0302,236,247,2,257,1,12097\0302,250,361,2,257,1,12097\0303,1,72,2,384,1,12097\0301,1,13,4,272,1,12097\0301,15,30,4,272,1,12097\0301,32,123,4,274,3,12097\0304,1,36,3,256,2,12097\0304,38,63,3,256,2,12097\03110981,2,6,Frostwolf\0312,2597,1459,0,\0302,0,0,3,Alterac Valley\0302,0,0,5,Alliance\0302,0,0,6,Horde Quartermaster\0302,0,0,6,Frostwolf Keep\031\031ITEM,17522,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[699]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Glad to see you're alive and well, $N.$B$BThese claws should make do nicely. The more weapons we have at the ready for attacks against us, the better off we'll be.$B$BI'll get started on your weapon as soon as possible. It will only take a short time. I've become quite adept and quick at their production.\030With the threat of murlocs along the coast, we're stationed out here to protect--or warn if the force is too large--of any coming threats to Stonard. It doesn't give us much time for relaxation, and we could use some more help if you're able.$B$BThe sawtooth snappers' claws make for fine weapons when properly prepared. Bring me some of their claws and I'll see you're rewarded with one of our weapons in thanks for the fresh meat and the good company.\030Bring 6 Sawtooth Snapper Claws to Tok'Kar in the Swamp of Sorrows.\030Good mead, a warm fire, an army of orcs and an arsenal of weapons... that's all we really need out here along the coast. I don't regret my position out here safeguarding Stonard, but it would be nice if we could one day get a burrow, or at least a tower.\030Lack of Surplus\0312,1,149,2,271,4,5592\0302,151,242,2,257,4,5592\0302,247,320,2,257,1,5592\0302,322,453,2,257,1,5592\0303,1,66,2,384,1,5592\0301,1,38,4,272,1,5592\0301,43,76,4,272,1,5592\0301,78,163,4,276,1,5592\0301,168,219,4,272,1,5592\0301,221,251,4,272,3,5592\0301,253,306,4,272,1,5592\0304,1,68,3,256,1,5592\0304,70,120,3,258,1,5592\0304,122,254,3,256,4,5592\0311087,2,5,Sawtooth Snapper\0305592,2,5,Tok'Kar\0312,8,1435,0,\0302,0,0,1,Stonard\0302,0,0,5,Tok'Kar\0302,0,0,5,Swamp of Sorrows\031698,19,698,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301422,23,1422,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,6168,OBJECTIVE,6,15,",[7]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, citizen. Those kobolds are thieves and cowards, but in large numbers they pose a threat to us. And the humans of Stormwind do not need another threat.$B$BFor defeating them, you have my gratitude.\030Your first task is one of cleansing, $N.  A clan of kobolds have infested the woods to the north.  Go there and fight the kobold vermin you find.  Reduce their numbers so that we may one day drive them from Northshire.\030Kill 10 Kobold Vermin, then return to Marshal McBride.\030How goes the hunting, $N? Have you found and defeated those vermin?\030Kobold Camp Cleanup\0312,1,40,2,257,1,197\0302,43,97,2,257,1,197\0302,100,145,2,261,1,197\0302,148,218,2,259,1,197\0303,1,54,2,384,1,197\0301,1,19,4,272,1,197\0301,21,105,4,276,1,197\0301,107,161,4,278,1,197\0301,166,207,4,272,1,197\0304,1,25,3,256,2,197\0304,27,67,3,256,2,197\0316,2,3,Kobold Vermin\0306,2,5,Kobold Vermin\030197,2,5,Marshal McBride\0312,9,1429,0,\0302,0,0,4,Northshire\0302,0,0,5,Marshal McBride\031783,19,783,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,6,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Kobold Vermin",[70]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You've got some nerve bringing this here.\030The name Stalvan rings a bell.  I remember now.$B$BMany years back, on a stormy night, a messenger came in, seeking refuge for the night.  Near the stroke of midnight, the man ran down the stairs screaming, his face pale with fear.  Still wearing his bedclothes, he disappeared into the downpour.$B$BIn his haste he forgot his letters in the chest upstairs.  He never returned for them. One remains from that Stalvan fellow, intended for the Canal District in Stormwind.  Help yourself to it.\030Retrieve Stalvan's Undelivered Letter from the chest and deliver it to the Canal District in Stormwind.\030What have ya got there? Let me take a look at that. . .\030The Legend of Stalvan\0312,1,30,2,257,1,295\0302,33,47,2,257,1,295\0302,52,137,2,257,1,295\0302,140,231,2,257,1,295\0302,234,296,2,257,1,295\0302,301,357,2,257,1,295\0302,360,386,2,257,1,295\0302,388,470,2,257,1,295\0302,473,492,2,257,1,295\0303,1,103,2,384,1,295\0301,1,41,4,272,1,297\0304,1,23,3,256,2,297\0304,25,51,3,256,1,297\031\0312,10,1431,0,\0302,0,0,8,Stormwind\0302,0,0,10,Canal District\0302,0,0,10,Stormwind\03169,19,69,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\03072,23,72,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,910,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[700]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The granite seems but a small token compared to a great dwarf's life. But no dwarf shall last on this planet for eternity.$B$BLet us just hope that the memorial stands as a reminder to those who will trod the great Azeroth of the future. Lest we not forget it is for them that brave soldiers such as Sully Balloo so valiantly gave their lives.\030Ah, such fine stone comes from Lordaeron.  Such a shame the land is in such shambles.$B$BBut the Memorial came out quite well! I should think the King will be most pleased with it.$B$BNow if you will, please send word to His Majesty that the Memorial is complete as requested.\030Report to King Magni Bronzebeard.\030\030A King's Tribute\0312,1,41,2,257,1,2790\0302,44,85,2,257,1,2790\0302,90,126,2,257,1,2790\0302,128,180,2,257,3,2790\0302,185,276,2,257,4,2790\0303,1,33,2,384,1,2790\0301,1,69,4,272,4,2784\0301,71,122,4,272,3,2784\0301,127,237,4,274,3,2784\0301,239,343,4,272,1,2784\0312784,2,6,King Magni Bronzebeard\0312,1537,1455,0,\0302,0,0,1,Lordaeron\0302,0,0,5,His Majesty\0302,0,0,6,King Magni Bronzebeard\031689,19,689,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[7001]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031I can only hope that those charged with collecting ram hides are as determined as you, $N.$B$BAt this rate, we will have the stables full in a matter of hours!\030The war in the valley has taken its toll on our soldiers. We must revitalize our forces!$B$BIf we can fill up the stables, the Wolf Riders will once more be able to ride out into the field of battle.$B$BTake this muzzle and track down the frostwolves that inhabit the nearby forest. Once you find a wolf, use the muzzle to tame the beast. Bring the tamed beast back to me so that I may place it in the stable.$B$BWhen we have enough wolves stabled, the Wolf Riders will rejoin their patrol on our front lines.\030Locate a Frostwolf in Alterac Valley. Use the Frostwolf Muzzle when you are near the Frostwolf to 'tame' the beast. Once tamed, the Frostwolf will follow you back to the Frostwolf Stable Master. Speak with the Frostwolf Stable Master to earn credit for the capture.\030Frostwolf Muzzled and Returned\030Without your help, the Frostwolf Wolf Riders would not have mounts to ride into battle. You do us a great service!\030Empty Stables\0312,1,57,2,261,1,13616\0302,59,88,2,257,1,13616\0302,93,199,2,261,4,13616\0302,204,282,2,257,1,13616\0302,284,338,2,257,1,13616\0302,340,409,2,259,1,13616\0302,414,509,2,257,3,13616\0303,1,37,2,384,1,13616\0303,39,115,2,384,1,13616\0303,117,194,2,384,3,13616\0303,196,265,2,384,1,13616\0301,1,90,4,274,3,13616\0301,95,159,4,272,3,13616\0305,1,87,3,260,4,13616\0305,89,114,3,256,1,13616\0304,1,30,3,384,1,13616\03110430,2,5,The Beast\03010981,2,8,Frostwolf\03010981,2,9,Frostwolf\03010430,2,9,The Beast\03010981,2,10,Frostwolf\03013616,2,10,Frostwolf Stable Master\03013616,2,11,Frostwolf Stable Master\03010981,3,14,Frostwolf\03010981,3,16,Frostwolf\0312,2597,1459,0,\0302,0,0,8,Alterac Valley\0302,0,0,9,Frostwolf\0302,0,0,10,Frostwolf Stable Master\031\031",[7002]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, soldier. I will notify you when I have stockpiled enough of the hides.$B$BCarry on!\030While some of our soldiers are busy capturing wolves for the stable master, others must provide for the simple necessities that riding requires. I am speaking of riding harnesses, of course.$B$BYou must strike at the indigenous rams of the region. The very same rams that the Stormpike cavalry uses as mounts!$B$BSlay them and return to me with their hides. Once we have gathered enough hides, we will fashion harnesses for the riders. The Frostwolf Wolf Riders will ride once more!\030null\030Slay them and return to me with their hides. The same rams that the Stormpike cavalry uses as mounts!\030Ram Hide Harnesses\0312,1,144,2,257,1,13441\0302,146,190,2,257,1,13441\0302,195,247,2,257,1,13441\0302,249,309,2,257,1,13441\0302,314,357,2,257,1,13441\0302,359,435,2,257,3,13441\0302,437,482,2,257,3,13441\0303,1,4,2,384,1,13441\0301,1,19,4,272,1,13441\0301,21,81,4,272,3,13441\0301,86,94,4,272,1,13441\0304,1,44,3,256,1,13441\0304,46,101,3,256,1,13441\03110981,2,7,Frostwolf\0312,2597,1459,0,\031\031ITEM,17642,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7003]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Splendifimous!  Not only am I glad to see that you've returned with the residue, but also with all your major appendages intact!  That is, well, there was never any danger in using the Ultra-Shrinker, now was there!$B$BI do appreciate your effort on my behalf, $N.  Truly, you are a friend to goblins everywhere.  Accept this as a token of my appreciation!\030I'm going to have to do something about the giants if I stay out here!  They're certainly not good for business, now are they?$B$BI've been working on a variant of a gnomish shrinking ray, but I'm using superior GOBLIN technological advances in its construction!  In an effort to avoid inconveniences for myself such as death, I'd like for you to try it out on any of the giants in Feralas.  You should find miniaturization residue on them after you shrink them - bring me back some!\030Use Zorbin's Ultra-Shrinker to zap any kind of giant found in Feralas into a more manageable form.  Bring 15 Miniaturization Residues found on the zapped versions of these giants to Zorbin Fandazzle at the docks of the Forgotten Coast, Feralas.\030Miniaturization residue, I assure you, is a valuable commodity when it comes to engineering!  Well, it is valuable in that it helps me make sure the zapper won't do something as disappointing as explode on the user.$B$BOh, I mean for the zappers other than the one I gave you.  Absolutely!\030Zapped Giants\0312,1,70,2,257,4,14637\0302,73,126,2,257,2,14637\0302,131,262,2,257,1,14637\0302,265,390,2,259,1,14637\0302,393,483,2,257,1,14637\0303,1,98,2,384,1,14637\0303,101,244,2,384,1,14637\0301,1,14,4,272,1,14637\0301,17,128,4,272,1,14637\0301,131,215,4,276,1,14637\0301,220,264,4,272,1,14637\0301,267,312,4,272,1,14637\0301,315,356,4,272,1,14637\0304,1,92,3,256,1,14637\0304,95,215,3,256,1,14637\0304,220,276,3,256,1,14637\0304,279,289,3,256,1,14637\03114637,2,7,Zorbin Fandazzle\0312,357,1444,0,\0302,0,0,4,Feralas\0302,0,0,6,Feralas\0302,0,0,7,Zorbin Fandazzle\0317725,23,7725,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,18956,OBJECTIVE,15,15,",[701]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes, these will work perfectly. I will transfer their power and the spirit of the raptors into this orb. This orb will imbue Gor'mul with the fiery strength and intelligence of the raptor.\030With some additional objects, I will be able to create an item that will imbue Gor'mul with the guile of the raptor! With the power of the raptor flowing through him, Gor'mul will know our new power and rediscover the warrior that lies dormant!$B$BI will require raptor hearts to fashion the item and spell.\030Acquire 12 Raptor Hearts from Highland Fleshstalkers for Tor'gan.\030My preparations are made, all I require are the raptor hearts.\030Guile of the Raptor\0312,1,116,2,257,3,2706\0302,118,244,2,257,3,2706\0302,249,307,2,257,3,2706\0303,1,65,2,384,1,2706\0301,1,31,4,272,3,2706\0301,33,104,4,272,3,2706\0301,106,188,4,272,3,2706\0304,1,62,3,256,1,2706\0312792,2,1,Gor'mul\030107,2,1,Raptor\030107,2,2,Raptor\0302792,2,2,Gor'mul\030107,2,3,Raptor\030107,2,4,Raptor\0302706,2,4,Tor'gan\0302792,4,7,Gor'mul\030107,4,7,Raptor\030107,3,8,Raptor\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,4,Highland Fleshstalkers\031675,19,675,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030702,23,702,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4513,OBJECTIVE,12,15,",[702]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031At least it is something interesting you bring to me this time. A strange power it emits...\030Take this orb and use its energy to give Gor'mul the essence of the raptor. Surely this will invigorate his spirit and give him new purpose in life. With him returned to normal, we can explain to him the current state of the Horde, and we will have a great warrior's assistance in our unceasing battles.\030Give Tor'gan's Orb to Gor'mul.\030Returned again have you? Indeed there is nothing more I could wish for now than more of Tor'gan's pity.$B$BWhat have you for me this time? Perhaps a piece of brightly colored string? Or a length of rope to end this misery of mine...\030Guile of the Raptor\0312,1,75,2,257,1,2706\0302,77,148,2,257,3,2706\0302,150,303,2,257,3,2706\0303,1,30,2,384,1,2706\0301,1,63,4,272,1,2792\0301,65,91,4,272,1,2792\0304,1,24,3,256,2,2792\0304,26,103,3,258,4,2792\0304,108,138,3,256,2,2792\0304,140,182,3,256,4,2792\0304,184,232,3,256,1,2792\0312792,2,1,Gor'mul\030107,2,1,Raptor\0302792,2,4,Gor'mul\0312,45,1417,0,\0302,0,0,4,Gor'mul\031701,19,701,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030847,23,847,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[7021]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ho ho hello. I am Greatfather Winter, and I - courtesy of the fine folks of Smokywood Pastures... \"Fresh from our farm to your plate, it's Smokywood Pastures wholesome goodness\" - would like to wish you a fantastic Feast of Winter Veil.$B$BIf you've been good this year, maybe you will receive treats from Smokywood Pastures as your treat for the Feast of Winter Veil. Huzzah.\030Have a wondrous Winter Veil, friend!  Be sure to say hello to Greatfather Winter, who's currently in Orgrimmar!  If you've been nice this year, you'll receive wondrous treats on the day of the Feast of Winter Veil.  Be sure to tell him what you hope to get this year!$B$BAlso, be sure to stock up on treats to give those who've been nice this year.  We have a great selection to choose from.  Fresh from our farm to your plate - it's Smokywood Pastures wholesome goodness!\030Speak with Greatfather Winter; he is located near the Smokywood Pastures vendor area in Orgrimmar.\030\030Great-father Winter is Here!\0312,1,36,2,257,1,13431\0302,39,111,2,257,1,13431\0302,114,214,2,257,4,13431\0302,217,267,2,259,3,13431\0302,272,348,2,257,1,13431\0302,351,391,2,257,1,13431\0302,394,472,2,257,1,13431\0303,1,98,2,384,1,13431\0301,1,12,4,272,1,13444\0301,14,97,4,272,1,13444\0301,99,236,4,274,4,13444\0301,241,368,4,272,4,13444\0301,370,376,4,272,1,13444\03113444,2,2,Greatfather Winter\03013444,2,8,Greatfather Winter\03013444,4,10,Greatfather Winter\0312,0,0,2,Greatfather Winter\0302,0,0,2,Orgrimmar\0302,0,0,8,Smokywood Pastures\0302,0,0,8,Orgrimmar\0304,0,0,12,Smokywood Pastures\0317024,22,7024,UNKNOWN\031",[7022]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ho ho hello. I am Greatfather Winter, and I - courtesy of the fine folks of Smokywood Pastures... \"Fresh from our farm to your plate, it's Smokywood Pastures wholesome goodness\" - would like to wish you a fantastic Feast of Winter Veil.$B$BIf you've been good this year, maybe you will receive treats from Smokywood Pastures as your treat for the Feast of Winter Veil. Huzzah.\030Have a wondrous Winter Veil, friend!  Be sure to say hello to Greatfather Winter!  If you've been nice this year, you'll receive wondrous treats on the day of the Feast of Winter Veil.  Be sure to tell him what you hope to get this year!$B$BAlso, be sure to stock up on treats to give those who've been nice this year.  We have a great selection to choose from.  Fresh from our farm to your plate - it's Smokywood Pastures wholesome goodness!\030Speak with Greatfather Winter; he is located near the