ghter!$B$BSpeak with Voggah Deathgrip.  He is looking for agents for an important mission into the Alliance's stronghold in Alterac Valley!$B$BYou will find Voggah in Frostwolf Keep.\030Speak with Voggah in Frostwolf Keep.\030\030Speak with Voggah Deathgrip\0312,8,12,2,257,1,0\0302,15,52,2,257,1,0\0302,55,176,2,261,1,0\0302,181,208,2,257,1,0\0302,211,309,2,257,1,0\0302,314,352,2,257,3,0\0303,1,36,2,384,1,0\03113817,2,4,Voggah Deathgrip\03010981,2,6,Frostwolf\03010981,2,7,Frostwolf\0312,2597,1459,0,\0302,0,0,2,Alterac\0302,0,0,3,Horde\0302,0,0,5,Alterac Valley\0302,0,0,6,Frostwolf Keep\0302,0,0,7,Frostwolf Keep\0317142,23,7142,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[7223]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031These are some good pieces, $N. I can use them to fashion new equipment for our troops.$B$BIf my supply level gets high enough, then maybe our seasoned fighting units will enter the field!\030Battles rage constantly in Alterac Valley, and the supplies we get from Ironforge are not enough to outfit our experienced troops.$B$BIf you find armor scraps from the battlefield, aid the war effort and bring those scraps to me!\030Bring 20 Armor Scraps to Murgot Deepforge in Dun Baldar.\030Did you bring any armor scraps, $N?\030Armor Scraps\0312,1,130,2,257,1,13257\0302,135,229,2,261,4,13257\0303,1,56,2,384,1,13257\0301,1,31,4,272,1,13257\0301,33,87,4,272,1,13257\0301,92,188,4,276,4,13257\0304,1,35,3,256,2,13257\03113257,2,3,Murgot Deepforge\0312,2597,1459,0,\0302,0,0,1,Alterac Valley\0302,0,0,1,Ironforge\0302,0,0,3,Murgot Deepforge\0302,0,0,3,Dun Baldar\0316781,23,6781,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,17422,OBJECTIVE,20,15,",[7224]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031These will do nicely. I'll melt them down and patch them up and you'll never know they came from those Stormpike cowards!$B$BThanks, $N. And let me polish up that armor of yours...\030When you fight the enemy, gather the scraps of their armor and bring them to me.  I'll use those scraps to make armor for our own troops!\030Bring 20 Armor Scraps to Smith Regzar in Frostwolf Village.\030How goes the hunting, $N. Do you have any armor scraps for me?\030Enemy Booty\0312,1,80,2,261,1,13176\0302,83,137,2,257,1,13176\0303,1,59,2,384,1,13176\0301,1,21,4,272,3,13176\0301,23,121,4,272,1,13176\0301,126,136,4,272,1,13176\0301,138,180,4,272,1,13176\0304,1,25,3,256,1,13176\0304,27,62,3,256,2,13176\03113176,2,3,Smith Regzar\03010981,2,3,Frostwolf\0312,2597,1459,0,\0302,0,0,3,Smith Regzar\0302,0,0,3,Frostwolf Village\0316741,23,6741,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,17422,OBJECTIVE,20,15,",[723]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hammertoe's amulet? I think my spirits were higher when I thought he was dead. Knowin' fer sure only makes the pain worse. This amulet was his life's work. I can't let his death be in vain.\030<Hammertoe holds his wounds and takes a moment to regain his composure before speaking again.>$B$BFind Ryedol, $N. Bring 'im me amulet. <cough cough> He'll... <cough> figure out what to do. He knows I was seeking the origins of our people, and he... <cough>... knows it was also my mission to stop the Shadowforge clan. They must not be allowed to find the scrolls... <cough>\030Take Hammertoe's Amulet to Prospector Ryedol in the Badlands.\030I'd say it was a bad day, but this is the Badlands: every day's a bad day.\030Prospect of Faith\0312,1,94,2,257,1,2909\0302,99,114,2,257,1,2909\0302,116,135,2,257,1,2909\0302,137,158,2,257,1,2909\0302,160,189,2,257,1,2909\0302,191,249,2,257,1,2909\0302,251,260,2,257,1,2909\0302,262,319,2,257,1,2909\0302,321,367,2,265,1,2909\0302,369,375,2,257,1,2909\0303,1,61,2,384,1,2909\0301,1,19,4,272,2,2910\0301,21,78,4,272,1,2910\0301,80,122,4,272,1,2910\0301,124,155,4,272,1,2910\0301,157,189,4,272,1,2910\0304,1,74,3,256,1,2910\0312910,2,11,Prospector Ryedol\0312,3,1418,0,\0302,0,0,11,Prospector Ryedol\0302,0,0,11,Badlands\031722,19,722,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030724,23,724,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[724]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh! Well, this is a different matter entirely. You probably don't realize the gravity of this matter yet, do you?$B$BI care deeply about Hammertoe's demise, but if he sent you here with his amulet, then he understood what's at stake.$B$BWe will have to take time to mourn his death later.$B$BLet me show you one of the reasons this amulet is so valuable.\030Okay, okay... who would know what to do?$B$BHistorian Karnik! That's it!$B$BHe's in Ironforge. He'll be able to help. He and Hammertoe were workin' together to find the lost artifacts in Uldaman.$B$BGuess the Shadowforge found out the two of them knew more than they were lettin' on.$B$BTell Karnik what's happened to Hammertoe and give him the amulet--he'll tell you what needs to be done next.\030Take Hammertoe's Amulet to Historian Karnik in Ironforge.\030Ah, yes. Another traveler seeking something from the dwarves.$B$BMa'am, I'm truly sorry, but I've no time to answer meaningless questions right now.\030Prospect of Faith\0312,1,13,2,257,1,2910\0302,15,40,2,257,4,2910\0302,45,61,2,257,1,2910\0302,63,72,2,257,1,2910\0302,77,94,2,257,1,2910\0302,96,117,2,257,1,2910\0302,119,195,2,261,1,2910\0302,200,283,2,257,1,2910\0302,288,395,2,259,1,2910\0303,1,57,2,384,1,2910\0301,5,46,4,272,1,2916\0301,48,113,4,272,2,2916\0301,118,233,4,280,4,2916\0301,238,288,4,272,3,2916\0301,293,354,4,272,1,2916\0304,1,8,3,256,1,2916\0304,10,61,3,256,1,2916\0304,66,148,3,256,1,2916\0312916,2,3,Historian Karnik\0302916,2,10,Historian Karnik\0312,3,1418,0,\0302,0,0,5,Ironforge\0302,0,0,7,Uldaman\0302,0,0,9,Hammertoe\0302,0,0,10,Historian Karnik\0302,0,0,10,Ironforge\031723,19,723,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030725,23,725,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[7241]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031To become a soldier of Frostwolf, one must first be tested...\030The drums of war sound off in a distant land, $c. The favored clan of your Warchief is under attack from the nefarious Stormpike Guard of Ironforge.$B$BBy the looks of you, I can discern that you are indeed battle hardy and prepared to take on the cause of the Frostwolf.$B$BIt is you who must now take the next step in your evolution.$B$BNorth of Tarren Mill, in Alterac,  you will find the entrance to Alterac Valley. It is there that you will find Warmaster Laggrond. Hurry $c, for the battle is upon us!\030Venture to Alterac Valley, located in the Alterac Mountains. Find and speak with Warmaster Laggrond - who stands outside the tunnel entrance - to begin your career as a soldier of Frostwolf. You will find Alterac Valley north of Tarren Mill at the base of the Alterac Mountains.\030\030In Defense of Frostwolf\0312,1,49,2,261,1,13842\0302,51,148,2,261,1,13842\0302,153,271,2,261,1,13842\0302,276,335,2,257,1,13842\0302,340,419,2,257,3,13842\0302,421,470,2,257,3,13842\0302,472,507,2,261,1,13842\0303,1,60,2,384,1,13842\0303,62,190,2,384,1,13842\0303,192,278,2,384,3,13842\0301,1,61,4,272,1,13840\03110981,2,3,Frostwolf\03013840,2,6,Warmaster Laggrond\03013840,2,9,Warmaster Laggrond\03010981,2,9,Frostwolf\03010981,4,11,Frostwolf\0312,2597,1459,0,\0302,0,0,5,Alterac\0302,0,0,5,Alterac Valley\0302,0,0,8,Alterac Valley\0302,0,0,8,Alterac Mountains\0302,0,0,10,Tarren Mill\031\031",[725]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, word from Historian Karnik. Excellent.$B$BI always have time for his business.$B$B<Advisor Belgrum opens the note and begins to read.>\030$N, run and find Advisor Belgrum as quickly as you can. Tell him what you've witnessed and ask him how he wants us to proceed. This note will explain more to him.$B$BIn the meantime, I will take the time to speak to Hammertoe's spirit. Maybe he knows something that will help us put a stop to those Shadowforge cretins' activities in the Badlands. We can only pray.\030Find Advisor Belgrum and give him his note.\030Hmm? Yes, $C.\030Passing Word of a Threat\0312,1,55,2,257,1,2916\0302,57,126,2,259,1,2916\0302,128,162,2,257,3,2916\0302,167,235,2,257,3,2916\0302,237,347,2,257,4,2916\0302,349,365,2,257,1,2916\0303,1,43,2,384,1,2916\0301,1,31,4,272,1,2918\0301,33,42,4,272,1,2918\0301,47,82,4,272,1,2918\0301,87,138,4,272,1,2918\0304,1,4,3,256,2,2918\0304,6,13,3,256,1,2918\0312918,2,1,Advisor Belgrum\0302915,2,4,Hammertoe's Spirit\0302918,2,7,Advisor Belgrum\0302916,4,8,Historian Karnik\0302918,4,11,Advisor Belgrum\0312,3,1418,0,\0302,0,0,4,Hammertoe's\0302,0,0,5,Badlands\0304,0,0,8,Historian Karnik\031724,19,724,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030726,23,726,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[726]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You're treating this matter with an urgency I'd expect from the king himself, $N.$B$BAll right, then. I know what'll bring the Shadowforge down.$B$BTheir presence in Uldaman can be slowed if we strike them at their base of operations: Angor Fortress.\030<Advisor Belgrum reaches the end of the note, and his eyes widen for a moment.>$B$BOch, these are evil tidings.$B$B$N, please return to Historian Karnik and tell him on the king's authority to act on this information swiftly and decisively. He must halt the Shadowforge's activities in the Badlands.\030Speak to Historian Karnik.\030\030Passing Word of a Threat\0312,1,79,2,257,1,2918\0302,84,111,2,257,1,2918\0302,116,240,2,257,1,2918\0302,242,299,2,257,1,2918\0303,1,26,2,384,1,2918\0301,1,81,4,272,1,2916\0301,86,101,4,272,1,2916\0301,103,144,4,272,1,2916\0301,149,250,4,272,4,2916\0312918,2,1,Advisor Belgrum\0302916,2,3,Historian Karnik\0302916,2,5,Historian Karnik\0312,3,1418,0,\0302,0,0,3,Historian Karnik\0302,0,0,4,Badlands\0302,0,0,5,Historian Karnik\0304,0,0,9,Uldaman\031725,19,725,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030762,23,762,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[7261]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Let's get to work!\030We are fighting a brutal battle in the valleys of Alterac. The cannibalistic Winterax trolls attack us from one side and the savage Frostwolf Clan from the other. Both must be exterminated in the name of King Magni Bronzebeard! The taking, culling, and turning of that land is a sovereign and territorial imperative to the kingdom of Ironforge.$B$BAlas, soldiers do not grow on trees! Report to Lieutenant Haggerdin outside Alterac Valley to begin your tour of duty and honor amongst the Stormpike.\030Travel to Alterac Valley in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Outside of the entrance tunnel, find and speak with Lieutenant Haggerdin.$B$BFor the glory of Bronzebeard!\030\030The Sovereign Imperative\0312,1,58,2,261,1,13843\0302,60,162,2,261,1,13843\0302,164,227,2,257,1,13843\0302,229,344,2,257,1,13843\0302,349,384,2,257,1,13843\0302,386,498,2,257,1,13843\0303,1,52,2,384,1,13843\0303,54,126,2,384,1,13843\0303,131,159,2,384,1,13843\0301,1,18,4,272,1,13841\03110981,2,2,Frostwolf\0302784,2,3,King Magni Bronzebeard\03013841,2,6,Lieutenant Haggerdin\03013841,2,8,Lieutenant Haggerdin\0312,2597,1459,0,\0302,0,0,6,Lieutenant Haggerdin\0302,0,0,6,Alterac Valley\0302,0,0,7,Alterac Valley\0302,0,0,7,Hillsbrad Foothills\031\031",[727]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh. Greetings, brother.$B$BAnd praise to the dwellers beneath.\030The Tablet tells much.  But not enough!  Not nearly enough!$B$BThere is a book, a digest that Yagyin wrote in ages past.  The ... people I fled ... they keep this book in many places.  And their most learned study it.  It holds vast knowledge.  Knowledge to protect us!$B$BGo to Gerrig Bonegrip.  He is in a shop in Ironforge, in the Forlorn Cavern.  Show him this sigil and he'll think you one of them.  Ask him for Yagyin's Digest ... and bring it to me!\030Give the Sigil of the Hammer to Gerrig Bonegrip in the Forlorn Cavern of Ironforge.\030Hello. Welcome to my shop, but watch what you touch.$B$BKnowledge can be deadly.\030To Ironforge for Yagyin's Digest\0312,1,22,2,257,1,2785\0302,25,39,2,257,1,2785\0302,42,59,2,257,1,2785\0302,64,120,2,257,1,2785\0302,123,129,2,257,1,2785\0302,131,147,2,257,1,2785\0302,149,183,2,257,1,2785\0302,186,217,2,257,1,2785\0302,220,243,2,257,1,2785\0302,246,269,2,271,1,2785\0302,274,295,2,257,1,2785\0302,298,349,2,257,1,2785\0302,352,403,2,257,1,2785\0302,406,436,2,257,1,2785\0302,438,456,2,257,1,2785\0303,1,83,2,384,1,2785\0301,5,23,4,272,1,2786\0301,28,62,4,272,1,2786\0304,1,6,3,256,1,2786\0304,8,52,3,256,1,2786\0304,57,80,3,256,1,2786\0312786,2,11,Gerrig Bonegrip\0302786,2,16,Gerrig Bonegrip\0312,3,1418,0,\0302,0,0,11,Gerrig Bonegrip\0302,0,0,12,Ironforge\0302,0,0,12,Forlorn Cavern\0302,0,0,16,Gerrig Bonegrip\0302,0,0,16,Forlorn Cavern of Ironforge\031709,19,709,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030735,23,735,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[728]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Be discrete with your signs, $C. There are those who do not believe the righteousness of our pledge.$B$BAnd there are those who would see us fail if they knew of us.$B$BWe must always be careful. And watchful. And patient.\030The tablet tells much.  But not enough!  Not nearly enough!$B$BThere is a book, a digest that Yagyin wrote in ages past.  The... people I fled from... they keep this book in many places.  And their most learned study it.  It holds vast knowledge.  Knowledge to protect us!$B$BGo to Keeper Bel'dugur in the Undercity of Lordaeron.  Show him this sigil and he'll think you one of them.  Ask him for Yagin's Digest...and bring it to me!\030Bring the Sigil of the Hammer to Keeper Bel'dugur in the Undercity.\030Ah, we have an eager $C, I see. Are you here to learn from my collection? Good!$B$BBut be warned: just as knowledge gives power to the strong...it will drive the weak mad.\030To the Undercity for Yagyin's Digest\0312,1,22,2,257,1,2785\0302,25,39,2,257,1,2785\0302,42,59,2,257,1,2785\0302,64,120,2,257,1,2785\0302,123,128,2,257,1,2785\0302,130,150,2,257,1,2785\0302,152,186,2,257,1,2785\0302,189,220,2,257,1,2785\0302,223,246,2,257,1,2785\0302,249,272,2,271,1,2785\0302,277,329,2,257,1,2785\0302,332,383,2,257,1,2785\0302,386,433,2,257,1,2785\0303,1,67,2,384,1,2785\0301,1,32,4,272,1,2934\0301,34,100,4,272,4,2934\0301,105,165,4,272,4,2934\0301,170,195,4,272,1,2934\0301,197,209,4,272,1,2934\0301,211,222,4,272,1,2934\0304,1,31,3,256,1,2934\0304,33,73,3,256,2,2934\0304,75,79,3,256,1,2934\0304,84,171,3,256,3,2934\0312934,2,11,Keeper Bel'dugur\0302934,2,14,Keeper Bel'dugur\0312,3,1418,0,\0302,0,0,11,Keeper Bel'dugur\0302,0,0,11,Undercity of Lordaeron\0302,0,0,14,Keeper Bel'dugur\0302,0,0,14,Undercity\031709,19,709,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030736,23,736,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[7281]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Your heroics will not go unnoticed, $N.$B$BI must waste no time if he is to be saved. Sylvanas must be contacted!\030Tragic... My brother faces me on the field of battle: A commander for the Stormpike.$B$BOf the four Stormpike Commanders, he is undoubtedly the most dangerous. Perhaps if he is slain, the Banshee Queen could turn him as she did me - show him the error of his ways...$B$BDeep within enemy territory you will find my brother. Slay him and return to me. I trust that you are capable of completing this mission, soldier.$B$BAnd soldier, do not go alone.\030Travel into Stormpike territory and slay Commander Karl Philips. Return to Commander Louis Philips when the task is complete.$B\030How it must pain him to remain as one of the living while his beloved brother has ascended to perfection.\030Brotherly Love\0312,1,9,2,257,1,13154\0302,11,84,2,261,1,13154\0302,89,159,2,257,1,13154\0302,161,266,2,261,4,13154\0302,271,323,2,261,3,13154\0302,325,350,2,257,1,13154\0302,352,416,2,257,1,13154\0302,421,449,2,257,1,13154\0303,1,64,2,384,1,13154\0303,66,125,2,384,1,13154\0301,1,39,4,272,3,13154\0301,44,85,4,272,4,13154\0301,87,113,4,272,1,13154\0304,1,105,3,256,1,13154\03115193,2,4,The Banshee Queen\03013320,2,9,Commander Karl Philips\03013154,2,10,Commander Louis Philips\0312,2597,1459,0,\0302,0,0,10,Commander Louis Philips\031\031NPC,13320,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Commander Karl Philips",[7282]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You did remember to burn the corpse, didn't you?\030He must be put out of his misery, soldier! He knows not what he does. He has become a mindless servant of the dreaded Banshee Queen.$B$BVenture forth, across the Field of Strife, to the depths of Frostwolf territory. Find my brother and destroy him. His torment must come to an end.\030Travel into Frostwolf territory and slay Commander Louis Philips. Return to Commander Karl Philips when the task is complete.$B\030It is with heavy heart that I give such an order, soldier.\030Brotherly Love\0312,1,42,2,257,1,13320\0302,44,69,2,257,1,13320\0302,71,132,2,257,1,13320\0302,137,216,2,257,1,13320\0302,218,249,2,261,1,13320\0302,251,282,2,257,1,13320\0303,1,65,2,384,1,13320\0303,67,125,2,384,1,13320\0301,1,48,4,272,2,13320\0304,1,58,3,256,1,13320\03110981,2,4,Frostwolf\03010981,2,7,Frostwolf\03013154,2,7,Commander Louis Philips\03013320,2,8,Commander Karl Philips\0312,2597,1459,0,\0302,0,0,8,Commander Karl Philips\031\031NPC,13154,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Commander Louis Philips",[729]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hollee. is that you? I need some help chiseling this stone. Hand me my stone brush, I think I see something.$B$BHey, you're not Hollee! Don't suppose you've seen my stone brush?$B$BNever mind that now! I promised the League I'd send the mysterious fossil I found. Where did Hollee go?$B$BSo much work to be done! Now where is that mysterious fossil... and my brush... and Hollee...$B$BAnd who are you... 'tis no matter, so long as you're here to help.$B$BLet me know when you're ready to start looking.\030What an honor it was when Master Greywhisker assigned me to work under the guidance of the great Prospector Remtravel. At the academy in Ironforge everyone knew of Remtravel's great discoveries.$B$BBut the prospector is rather... um... oblivious ...to his surroundings.$B$BWe had uncovered evidence of a great society. Horrible golems sprang forth from the ground and overran the site. Remtravel never seemed to notice. I ran back to Auberdine for help.$B$BPlease travel south and see if the prospector is okay!\030Travel south and check on Prospector Remtravel.\030\030The Absent Minded Prospector\0312,1,118,2,257,1,2913\0302,120,194,2,257,1,2913\0302,199,229,2,257,1,2913\0302,237,269,2,257,1,2913\0302,274,318,2,257,1,2913\0302,320,385,2,257,1,2913\0302,387,419,2,257,1,2913\0302,421,453,2,257,1,2913\0302,458,511,2,257,4,2913\0303,1,47,2,384,1,2913\0301,1,7,4,272,1,2917\0301,9,20,4,272,2,2917\0301,22,59,4,274,1,2917\0301,61,108,4,272,1,2917\0301,113,135,4,272,1,2917\0301,137,177,4,272,2,2917\0301,182,201,4,272,1,2917\0301,203,263,4,272,1,2917\0301,265,284,4,272,2,2917\0301,289,312,4,272,1,2917\0301,314,351,4,272,1,2917\0301,353,367,4,272,1,2917\0301,369,381,4,272,1,2917\0301,386,403,4,272,1,2917\0301,405,451,4,272,1,2917\0301,456,502,4,272,1,2917\0312917,2,1,Prospector Remtravel\0302917,2,10,Prospector Remtravel\0312,148,1439,0,\0302,0,0,2,Ironforge\0302,0,0,8,Auberdine\031731,23,731,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[730]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I'm so glad Chief Archeologist Greywhisker sent for us....\030How nice it is to see a $c interested in the great archeological wonders of our world.$B$BOftentimes our work is dismissed as mere hobby by our friends in the Alliance. But what many fail to realize is that recent discoveries in Khaz Modan have proven that a great and powerful force threatens all of Azeroth, from Lordaeron to Kalimdor.$B$BI am most worried about my crew that I sent to Darkshore. They haven't sent word in weeks.$B$BTravel to Auberdine and look for a clue as to their whereabouts.\030Travel to Auberdine and look for signs of the dwarven excavation team.\030\030Trouble In Darkshore?\0312,1,86,2,257,1,2912\0302,91,168,2,257,1,2912\0302,170,337,2,261,1,2912\0302,342,398,2,257,1,2912\0302,400,431,2,257,1,2912\0302,436,499,2,257,1,2912\0303,1,70,2,384,1,2912\0301,1,58,4,272,1,2913\031\0312,1657,1457,0,\0302,0,0,2,Alliance\0302,0,0,3,Khaz Modan\0302,0,0,3,Lordaeron\0302,0,0,3,Kalimdor\0302,0,0,4,Darkshore\0302,0,0,6,Auberdine\0302,0,0,7,Auberdine\031729,23,729,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030729,24,729,UNKNOWN\031",[7301]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030objectiveLabel3\030objectiveLabel4\030requestItems\030title\031Unbelievable! You did free them, right? Right??? Well at the very least we know where they were held.\030We got them held prisoner, $r. I'm talking about their Wing Commanders. It was a furious battle in the skies but they finally fell! Unfortunately, our best pilots were shot down in a counterattack against Frostwolf Keep. You gotta find out what happened to them.$B$BSearch Tower Point West and Frostwolf Keep. These were their last known locations. Search these areas thoroughly.\030Travel to Frostwolf territory and search for Wing Commander Slidore, Wing Commander Vipore, and Wing Commander Ichman. Return to Commander Duffy should you complete your mission.\030\030Ichman's Location Discovered\030Vipore's Location Discovered\030Slidore's Location Discovered\030Anything I would care to hear?\030Fallen Sky Lords\0312,1,30,2,257,1,13319\0302,32,71,2,257,1,13319\0302,73,131,2,261,1,13319\0302,133,220,2,257,1,13319\0302,222,262,2,257,1,13319\0302,267,309,2,257,1,13319\0302,311,348,2,257,1,13319\0302,350,379,2,257,1,13319\0303,1,118,2,384,1,13319\0303,120,178,2,384,1,13319\0301,1,13,4,272,1,13319\0301,15,39,4,272,2,13319\0301,41,48,4,272,2,13319\0301,50,101,4,272,1,13319\0308,1,30,3,256,4,13319\0305,1,28,3,384,1,13319\0306,1,28,3,384,1,13319\0307,1,29,3,384,1,13319\03110981,2,4,Frostwolf\03010981,2,6,Frostwolf\03010981,2,9,Frostwolf\03013438,2,9,Wing Commander Slidore\03013439,2,9,Wing Commander Vipore\03013437,2,9,Wing Commander Ichman\03013319,2,10,Commander Duffy\0312,2597,1459,0,\0302,0,0,9,Frostwolf\0302,0,0,10,Commander Duffy\031\031NPC,14029,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Trigger Ichman\030NPC,14031,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Trigger Vipore\030NPC,14030,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Trigger Slidore",[7302]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030objectiveLabel3\030objectiveLabel4\030requestItems\030title\031Well done! The information you recovered will be invaluable to our cause.\030Our air support is in shambles, $N. The Wing Commanders were shot down over enemy territory. You must find out what became of them so that we can attempt a rescue!$B$BGuse was last seen flying over the Icewing Bunker. Jeztor's War Rider was spotted near the Stormpike lumber mill. Mulverick... that reckless fool was seen crashing near the Dun'Baldar North Bunker.$B$BThat's all the information I have. Move out! Search through the areas thoroughly.\030Find out what became of Wing Commander Guse, Wing Commander Jeztor, and Wing Commander Mulverick. Return to Commander Mulfort should you complete your mission.\030\030Guse's Location Discovered\030Jeztor's Location Discovered\030Mulverick's Location Discovered\030Status of the hunt, soldier?\030Fallen Sky Lords\0312,1,35,2,257,1,13153\0302,37,92,2,261,1,13153\0302,94,163,2,267,1,13153\0302,168,217,2,257,1,13153\0302,219,280,2,261,1,13153\0302,282,293,2,257,1,13153\0302,295,364,2,257,1,13153\0302,369,402,2,257,1,13153\0302,404,412,2,257,1,13153\0302,414,449,2,257,1,13153\0303,1,97,2,384,1,13153\0303,99,159,2,384,1,13153\0301,1,10,4,272,1,13153\0301,12,73,4,272,3,13153\0308,1,28,3,256,2,13153\0305,1,26,3,384,1,13153\0306,1,28,3,384,1,13153\0307,1,31,3,384,1,13153\03114944,2,5,Jeztor's War Rider\03013178,2,5,War Rider\03013179,2,11,Wing Commander Guse\03013180,2,11,Wing Commander Jeztor\03013181,2,11,Wing Commander Mulverick\03013153,2,12,Commander Mulfort\0312,2597,1459,0,\0302,0,0,5,Stormpike\0302,0,0,7,Dun'Baldar North Bunker\0302,0,0,12,Commander Mulfort\031\031NPC,14026,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Trigger Guse\030NPC,14028,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Trigger Jeztor\030NPC,14027,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Trigger Mulverick",[731]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Thank the stars Prospector Remtravel is safe! I told you he was absent minded. I can't believe he insisted on staying there with all of those horrible creatures lurking about.\030So then, Hollee... oh that's right, you are not Hollee. Where's Hollee?$B$BBah, that's beside the point. We must find that stone brush... I mean the mysterious fossil! We must find that fossil. The Explorers' League in Darnassus will want some indication as to what I've been doing.$B$BLet me know when you are ready and we will hunt down that brush.... I mean fossil! We shall find something in writing to satisfy the League.$B$BSo are you ready yet?\030Protect Prospector Remtravel as he searches for the mysterious fossil, then return to Archaeologist Hollee in Auberdine.\030Escort Prospector Remtravel\030Is the prospector alive?\030The Absent Minded Prospector\0312,1,18,2,257,1,2917\0302,20,55,2,257,1,2917\0302,57,71,2,257,2,2917\0302,76,104,2,257,1,2917\0302,106,137,2,257,1,2917\0302,139,167,2,257,1,2917\0302,169,193,2,257,1,2917\0302,195,282,2,259,3,2917\0302,287,353,2,257,3,2917\0302,355,368,2,257,1,2917\0302,370,426,2,257,3,2917\0302,431,451,2,257,2,2917\0303,1,120,2,396,1,2917\0301,1,45,4,272,1,2913\0301,47,78,4,272,1,2913\0301,80,175,4,272,4,2913\0305,1,24,3,256,2,2913\0304,1,27,3,384,1,2917\0312917,2,13,Prospector Remtravel\0302913,2,13,Archaeologist Hollee\0302917,4,14,Prospector Remtravel\0302917,3,18,Prospector Remtravel\0312,148,1439,0,\0302,0,0,8,Darnassus\0302,0,0,13,Archaeologist Hollee\0302,0,0,13,Auberdine\031729,19,729,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030741,23,741,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[732]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Good tidings you bring bearing the Sign, $N. The Sign of the Earth was created by the Dark Iron dwarves of Angor Fortress to bind two of Deathwing's ruthless lieutenants, the twins Blacklash and Hematus.\030I heard from Sigrun that you have been a great help to him. Perhaps I might enlist your help. I was sent here by my master, Krasus of the Kirin Tor, to put an end to the trouble brewing in Lethlor Ravine.$B$BI cannot divulge the exact nature of my assignment here or the tasks that I must undertake, but be assured it is of vital importance.$B$BA band of wandering ogres, sometimes seen near Camp Boff, stole an object called the Sign of the Earth; I must have it. Bring it to me, and I will tell you more.\030Retrieve the Sign of the Earth for Garek.\030The nomadic band of ogres travels between their camps across the Badlands; heat rising from the dry earth and the swirling winds will make it difficult to track their progress. I have heard that sometimes they travel through Camp Boff. If you are lost, you might try your search there.\030Tremors of the Earth\0312,1,59,2,257,1,2888\0302,61,93,2,257,4,2888\0302,95,204,2,257,1,2888\0302,209,341,2,257,1,2888\0302,346,464,2,257,1,2888\0302,466,506,2,257,3,2888\0303,1,41,2,384,1,2888\0301,1,44,4,272,1,2888\0301,46,203,4,272,1,2888\0304,1,176,3,256,3,2888\0304,178,235,3,256,1,2888\0304,237,285,3,260,4,2888\0312888,2,7,Garek\0302757,4,9,Blacklash\0302759,4,9,Hematus\0312,3,1418,0,\0302,0,0,1,Sigrun\0302,0,0,3,Lethlor Ravine\0302,0,0,5,Camp Boff\031718,19,718,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030717,23,717,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4640,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7321]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031My soothing turtle bisque will keep you warm on a cold night... if you care about that kind of thing.\030Who says that the undead don't know anything about cooking? Take my secret recipe for Turtle Bisque, for example. I've known folks that would come back from the dead just to enjoy a bowl! Heh, heh...$B$BSpeaking of which, I haven't been able to make any lately.  I used to head over to Lake Lordamere myself to hunt snapjaws, the nasty things, but I can't pull myself away from my work here.$B$BIf you bring me some Turtle Meat from the snapjaws and soothing spices, I'll show you how it's done!\030Bring 10 pieces of Turtle Meat and some Soothing Spices to Christoph Jeffcoat in Tarren Mill.\030Any luck finding the ingredients?  I'll tell you, the alliance maggots are far too numerous in this area now... In my opinion, they have come far too close already...\030Soothing Turtle Bisque\0312,1,59,2,257,2,2393\0302,61,113,2,257,1,2393\0302,115,187,2,257,4,2393\0302,189,199,2,257,1,2393\0302,204,261,2,257,1,2393\0302,264,391,2,257,1,2393\0302,396,495,2,257,4,2393\0303,1,93,2,384,1,2393\0301,1,63,4,272,3,2393\0301,65,101,4,272,4,2393\0304,1,33,3,256,2,2393\0304,36,111,3,256,1,2393\0304,113,166,3,256,1,2393\0312393,2,8,Christoph Jeffcoat\0312,0,0,6,Lake Lordamere\0302,0,0,8,Christoph Jeffcoat\0302,0,0,8,Tarren Mill\031\031ITEM,3712,OBJECTIVE,10,15,\030ITEM,3713,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[733]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It's a start, $N, and it'll have to do until we hear word from Ironforge or the Explorers' League.$B$BNow, if only I could find some salt somewhere for my quenching barrel...\030It's going to be tough going here if I can't manage to scrounge up some materials to construct some defenses and other necessities. I've noticed that the ogres in the area seem to be well equipped with scrap metal. Maybe the stories of siege engines in the Badlands weren't so far off after all...$B$BAnyways, the Prospector's been getting worried about the state of our little camp, so I'd like to get working soon if I can.$B$BThe main ogre camp is at Dustbelch Grotto, a good trek to the west of here.\030Get 7 pieces of Scrap Metal for Sigrun.\030Well, I've made do with what I could, but... it's not much. Have you found any more supplies?\030Scrounging\0312,1,131,2,257,4,2860\0302,133,214,2,257,4,2860\0302,216,297,2,257,4,2860\0302,302,425,2,259,4,2860\0302,430,504,2,257,1,2860\0303,1,39,2,384,1,2860\0301,1,98,4,272,1,2860\0301,103,174,4,272,4,2860\0304,1,44,3,256,4,2860\0304,46,59,3,256,1,2860\0304,61,93,3,256,2,2860\031211,2,5,Ogre\0312,3,1418,0,\0302,0,0,3,Badlands\0302,0,0,5,Dustbelch Grotto\0304,0,0,7,Ironforge\031718,19,718,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4630,OBJECTIVE,7,15,",[734]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Cog #5, huh? Yeah, this isn't going to be good.\030Wonderful, wonderful.$B$B<Lotwil looks up at you for a moment before going back to his shackles.>$B$BGo speak to Lucien, $N. I need a cog #5. Bring it to me, will you?\030Speak to Lucien Tosselwrench in the Badlands.\030\030This Is Going to Be Hard\0312,1,21,2,257,1,2921\0302,26,97,2,257,1,2921\0302,102,124,2,257,1,2921\0302,126,141,2,259,1,2921\0302,143,167,2,257,2,2921\0303,1,45,2,384,1,2921\0301,1,12,4,272,2,2920\0301,14,47,4,272,3,2920\0312920,2,6,Lucien Tosselwrench\0312,3,1418,0,\0302,0,0,3,Lucien\0302,0,0,6,Lucien Tosselwrench\0302,0,0,6,Badlands\031712,21,712,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030714,21,714,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030777,23,777,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[7341]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Excellent! I am a Tauren of my word, $r. The arrows are yours.\030\030\030Greetings, $r. I am Kolark, Bounty Hunter from Thunderbluff. Much of the world I have traveled and much I have seen.$B$BMy journeys across the South Seas led to the discovery of these wonderous thorium headed arrows. Alas, I have an endless supply of the arrows but have exhausted my supply of shells. Bah, no self respecting Tauren would ever be caught dead using a flimsy bow. The arrows are useless!$B$BI will offer a trade: An even exchange of thorium shells for my thorium headed arrows. Deal?\030A Fair Trade\0311,1,10,4,272,1,14182\0301,12,40,4,272,1,14182\0301,42,62,4,272,1,14182\0304,1,14,3,256,1,14182\0304,16,60,3,256,1,14182\0304,62,116,3,256,1,14182\0304,121,216,3,256,1,14182\0304,218,301,3,256,1,14182\0304,303,378,3,256,4,14182\0304,380,402,3,256,1,14182\0304,407,492,3,256,3,14182\0304,494,498,3,256,2,14182\031\0312,1637,1454,0,\0303,0,0,5,Thunderbluff\031\031ITEM,15997,OBJECTIVE,200,15,",[7342]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A done deal if I ever saw one! The arrows are yours.\030\030\030Can you believe this rubbish?! The last shipment of ammunition from Kharanos was botched! All we have for ammo now are these flimsy, good for nothing arrows! What in the world am I going to do with 500,000 thorium headed arrows?$B$BI'll tell you what, kid. If you can bring me thorium shells, I'll trade you thorium headed arrows - straight up! Deal?\030Arrows Are For Sissies\0311,1,30,4,272,4,14183\0301,32,52,4,272,1,14183\0304,1,30,3,256,4,14183\0304,32,89,3,256,1,14183\0304,91,157,3,256,1,14183\0304,159,228,3,256,2,14183\0304,233,256,3,256,1,14183\0304,258,344,3,256,4,14183\0304,346,350,3,256,2,14183\031\0312,1537,1455,0,\0303,0,0,4,Kharanos\031\031ITEM,15997,OBJECTIVE,200,15,",[735]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You are resourceful, $C. If it truly is your charge to begin a new chapter of our order, then I believe you will run it well.\030Yagyin's Digest, eh?  Are you starting a new chapter of us, somewhere?  Never mind, it is not my place to ask.$B$BI will help you, for I have an extra copy.  We must aid each other, yes?  That is how we flourish.$B$BI require three items of power.  Bring them to me and I will give you the digest.$B$BI will not speak their names.  Ears may be on us.  But here, I will write them down.\030Return the items on the Bonegrip's Note to Gerrig Bonegrip in Ironforge.\030Do you have the relics for which I asked?\030The Star, the Hand and the Heart\0312,1,20,2,257,2,2786\0302,23,70,2,257,2,2786\0302,73,110,2,257,1,2786\0302,115,156,2,257,3,2786\0302,159,186,2,257,2,2786\0302,189,212,2,257,1,2786\0302,217,247,2,257,1,2786\0302,250,297,2,257,3,2786\0302,302,330,2,257,3,2786\0302,333,350,2,257,1,2786\0302,353,385,2,257,3,2786\0303,1,72,2,384,1,2786\0301,1,24,4,272,1,2786\0301,26,125,4,272,4,2786\0304,1,41,3,256,2,2786\0312786,2,12,Gerrig Bonegrip\0312,3,1418,0,\0302,0,0,12,Gerrig Bonegrip\0302,0,0,12,Ironforge\031727,19,727,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030737,23,737,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4646,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,4641,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,4644,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[736]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I am impressed! You possess great skill, or great fortune, to have gained these relics. Either way, you are an asset to us.\030You need Yagyin's Digest?  Your plan, then, is to gather another flock?  Of course it is...and of course I will help you, $gbrother:sister;.$B$BBut you must help me too.$B$BI require three items of power.  Bring me these and the digest will be yours.$B$BI cannot utter the names of these items, but I will write them down.$B$BGet me the items on this list.  If you can do that, then you are truly worthy of opening your own chapter of our order.\030Bring the items on Bel'dugur's Note to Keeper Bel'dugur in the Undercity.\030How goes your mission, $c.\030The Star, the Hand and the Heart\0312,1,25,2,259,2,2934\0302,28,71,2,257,2,2934\0302,74,140,2,257,3,2934\0302,145,169,2,257,1,2934\0302,174,204,2,257,1,2934\0302,207,250,2,257,3,2934\0302,255,322,2,257,3,2934\0302,327,356,2,257,1,2934\0302,359,445,2,257,4,2934\0303,1,73,2,384,1,2934\0301,1,15,4,272,1,2934\0301,17,87,4,272,1,2934\0301,89,123,4,272,1,2934\0304,1,26,3,256,1,2934\0312934,2,10,Keeper Bel'dugur\0312,1497,1458,0,\0302,0,0,10,Keeper Bel'dugur\0302,0,0,10,Undercity\031728,19,728,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030737,23,737,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4646,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,4641,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,4644,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7361]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031$N, it is but one of thousands. A job well done nonetheless.\030<Najak snarls.>$B$BBefore the night elves existed there was troll. It was from troll that the night elves came.$B$BTheir mutinous attacks against my people will not be tolerated. Staghelm seeks to wipe us out - to leave no trace of those that bore him and his ilk. It will not happen!$B$BFor every night elf that you slay and decapitate, Najak will grant you favor amongst the Darkspear. Word of your deeds will be spread across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms. Go now and serve the Darkspear!\030You have been tasked with slaying opposing night elf players in Alterac Valley.$B$BKill a night elf and return to Najak Hexxen at Frostwolf Keep with a Severed Night Elf Head.\030They seek to exterminate us? It is they who shall be exterminated.\030Favor Amongst the Darkspear\0312,1,15,2,257,1,0\0302,20,66,2,257,1,0\0302,68,111,2,257,1,0\0302,116,178,2,261,3,0\0302,180,264,2,259,1,0\0302,266,284,2,257,3,0\0302,289,387,2,257,3,0\0302,389,463,2,257,3,0\0302,465,495,2,257,1,0\0303,1,79,2,384,1,0\0303,84,175,2,384,1,0\0301,1,31,4,272,1,0\0301,33,60,4,272,1,0\0304,1,28,3,258,2,0\0304,30,66,3,256,3,0\03114185,2,11,Najak Hexxen\03010981,2,11,Frostwolf\0312,2597,1459,0,\0302,0,0,10,Alterac Valley\0302,0,0,11,Najak Hexxen\0302,0,0,11,Frostwolf Keep\031\031ITEM,18142,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7362]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Aye, this is definitely gnome. Well done, $R, but there is more work to be done.\030The Elder Crone has sent me to this warzone to research the other races. More specifically, I am to collect gnome samples. Magatha is primarily interested in their survivability. Aye, the gnomes - while pitifully weak and miniscule - exude great resilience both in and out of combat.$B$BFortunately for you, I am looking for ruffians to do Magatha's bidding. Return to me with tufts of gnome hair and you shall be known to the tauren as an ally.\030You have been tasked with slaying opposing gnome players in Alterac Valley.$B$BKill a gnome and return to Ravak Grimtotem at Frostwolf Keep with a Tuft of Gnome Hair.\030I don't care where the hair comes from, $R.\030Ally of the Tauren\0312,1,72,2,257,1,0\0302,74,122,2,257,1,0\0302,124,178,2,257,1,0\0302,180,283,2,257,1,0\0302,288,358,2,257,1,0\0302,360,445,2,257,3,0\0303,1,75,2,384,1,0\0303,80,166,2,384,1,0\0301,1,30,4,272,1,0\0301,32,80,4,272,1,0\0304,1,43,3,256,1,0\03114186,2,8,Ravak Grimtotem\03010981,2,8,Frostwolf\0312,2597,1459,0,\0302,0,0,7,Alterac Valley\0302,0,0,8,Ravak Grimtotem\0302,0,0,8,Frostwolf Keep\031\031ITEM,18143,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7363]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It would be easier if they just accepted their illness and gave in to your healing touch. It would also probably be less fun. Carry on! We'll cure them, one way or another.\030Humans are so utterly detestable.$B$B<Commander Philips grimaces.>$B$BWhile it is true that I am a soldier of Frostwolf, I remain a servant of Sylvanas.$B$BDuring my tour of duty, I do extra work on the side for the Dark Apothecaries of the Undercity.$B$BI have been tasked with collecting human bone chips that are to be used in curing the human condition.$B$BI am authorized to pass that task on to my subordinates.$B$BFind them. Kill them. Return their bone chips to me.\030You have been tasked with slaying opposing human players in Alterac Valley.$B$BKill a human and return to Commander Louis Philips (who wanders between the front lines and Frostwolf keep) with a  Human Bone Chip.$B$BA cure for the human condition is close at hand!\030Yes, it is true. My brother is a human. Shameful... A stain upon my nearly immaculate record.\030The Human Condition\0312,1,33,2,257,1,0\0302,38,66,2,257,1,0\0302,71,152,2,257,1,0\0302,157,251,2,257,1,0\0302,256,357,2,257,1,0\0302,362,417,2,257,1,0\0302,422,431,2,257,1,0\0302,433,442,2,257,1,0\0302,444,473,2,257,1,0\0303,1,75,2,384,1,0\0303,80,211,2,384,1,0\0303,216,263,2,384,1,0\0301,1,89,4,272,4,0\0301,91,125,4,272,4,0\0301,127,135,4,272,1,0\0301,137,172,4,272,1,0\0304,1,16,3,256,1,0\0304,18,39,3,256,1,0\0304,41,51,3,256,1,0\0304,53,93,3,256,1,0\03110981,2,3,Frostwolf\03013154,2,11,Commander Louis Philips\03010981,2,11,Frostwolf\0312,2597,1459,0,\0302,0,0,10,Alterac Valley\0302,0,0,11,Commander Louis Philips\031\031ITEM,18144,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7364]="PARTIAL\031conclusion,consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030The High Tinkerer himself has sent me to this field of battle to defend my gnomish brothers and sisters. We have received word that the tauren are singling out and slaying gnomes. Worst of all, they are removing tufts of glorious gnome hair from the corpses of the fallen. These atrocities must be stopped. We must reciprocate!$B$BI want them de-hoofed, $c. Bring me their hooves! Show yourself as an ally of the gnomes.\030You have been tasked with slaying opposing tauren players in Alterac Valley.$B$BKill a tauren and return to Dirk Swindle at Dun'Baldar with a  Tauren Hoof.\030\030Gnomeregan Bounty\0312,1,104,2,271,1,0\0302,106,179,2,257,1,0\0302,181,272,2,257,1,0\0302,274,306,2,257,1,0\0302,308,327,2,257,1,0\0302,332,357,2,259,1,0\0302,359,380,2,257,1,0\0302,382,420,2,257,1,0\0303,1,76,2,384,1,0\0303,81,155,2,384,1,0\03114188,2,10,Dirk Swindle\0312,2597,1459,0,\0302,0,0,9,Alterac Valley\0302,0,0,10,Dirk Swindle\0302,0,0,10,Dun'Baldar\031\031ITEM,18145,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7365]="PARTIAL\031conclusion,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030Staghelm has given the order. All trolls on the field of battle must be exterminated. Their preposterous claims of birthing night elves must be met with force and due prejudice.$B$BSlay them and return to me with their mojo. To reiterate: I want you to steal their mojo.\030You have been tasked with slaying opposing troll players in Alterac Valley.$B$BKill a troll and return to Athramanis at Dun'Baldar with Darkspear Troll Mojo.\030\030Staghelm's Requiem\0312,1,29,2,257,1,0\0302,31,85,2,261,1,0\0302,87,177,2,257,1,0\0302,182,224,2,257,1,0\0302,226,270,2,263,1,0\0303,1,75,2,384,1,0\0303,80,157,2,384,1,0\03114187,2,7,Athramanis\0312,2597,1459,0,\0302,0,0,6,Alterac Valley\0302,0,0,7,Athramanis\0302,0,0,7,Dun'Baldar\031\031ITEM,18146,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7366]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Praise be to Benedictus! Another lost soul, soon to be saved by the white hot flames of the Light!$B$BGo ye, oh soldier of Light! More must be saved!\030The Archbishop is as kind as he is wise. For a man to look mercifully on such a wretched lot...$B$B<Commander Philips shakes his head in disbelief.>$B$BToo kind... Just too kind.$B$BThe Archbishop asks that we take pity on the undead and grant them swift and permanent deaths. For this grand display of mercy, we merely require their black, disease ridden hearts.$B$BBring me the hearts of the Forsaken so that they may be ceremoniously incinerated at the Cathedral of Light. Make haste, $N!\030You have been tasked with slaying opposing Forsaken players in Alterac Valley.$B$BKill a Forsaken and return to Commander Karl Philips (who wanders between the lumber mill and the mine) with a Forsaken Heart.\030Benedictus! I am but a speck in the shadow of his grandeur. Praise him!\030The Archbishop's Mercy\0312,1,40,2,257,1,0\0302,42,95,2,257,1,0\0302,100,148,2,257,1,0\0302,153,163,2,257,1,0\0302,165,178,2,257,1,0\0302,183,276,2,257,1,0\0302,278,363,2,257,1,0\0302,368,475,2,259,1,0\0302,477,491,2,257,1,0\0303,1,78,2,384,1,0\0303,83,208,2,384,1,0\0301,1,24,4,272,1,0\0301,26,98,4,276,1,0\0301,103,129,4,272,1,0\0301,131,149,4,272,1,0\0304,1,11,3,256,1,0\0304,13,59,3,256,1,0\0304,61,71,3,256,1,0\03113320,2,11,Commander Karl Philips\0301531,4,13,Lost Soul\0304244,3,17,Shadow\0312,2597,1459,0,\0302,0,0,8,Cathedral of Light\0302,0,0,10,Alterac Valley\0302,0,0,11,Commander Karl Philips\0304,0,0,12,Benedictus\031\031ITEM,18147,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7367]="PARTIAL\031conclusion,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030The Frostwolf have their front lines and bases booby trapped, $c. You have to watch your step when invading enemy territory.$B$BIf you want to make a solid strike against them, you must destroy their source of anti personnel munitions - I'm talking about their explosives expert. If you kill him, you are safe to disarm the mines. As long as he is kept down, the mines will also stay down.$B$BYou will probably find him in a tower near the Iceblood Garrison. Good luck!\030Find the Frostwolf Explosives Expert and kill him. Return to the Stormpike Explosives Expert when the task is complete.\030\030Defusing the Threat\0312,1,65,2,257,1,0\0302,67,124,2,261,1,0\0302,129,279,2,263,4,0\0302,281,330,2,257,4,0\0302,332,389,2,257,3,0\0302,394,458,2,257,3,0\0302,460,469,2,257,1,0\0303,1,50,2,384,1,0\0303,52,119,2,384,1,0\03110981,2,1,Frostwolf\03013597,2,8,Frostwolf Explosives Expert\03013598,2,9,Stormpike Explosives Expert\0312,2597,1459,0,\0302,0,0,6,Iceblood Garrison\0302,0,0,9,Stormpike Explosives Expert\031\031NPC,13597,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Frostwolf Explosives Expert",[7368]="PARTIAL\031conclusion,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030I know all about landmines. I'm the one that lays all the mines on the front lines here, after all.$B$BIf you want to defuse the Stormpike mine fields, all you have to do is kill their explosives expert. That dwarven coward is no doubt hiding in the first tower on the Field of Strife. Take him out and those landmines won't come back after they've been disarmed.$B$BIf you do happen to kill him, come back here and let me know. No good deed should go unrewarded.\030Find the Stormpike Explosives Expert and kill him. Return to the Frostwolf Explosives Expert when the task is complete.\030\030Defusing the Threat\0312,1,27,2,257,1,0\0302,29,99,2,257,1,0\0302,104,203,2,259,4,0\0302,205,285,2,257,1,0\0302,287,363,2,257,1,0\0302,368,428,2,257,4,0\0302,430,463,2,257,1,0\0303,1,50,2,384,1,0\0303,52,119,2,384,1,0\03113598,2,8,Stormpike Explosives Expert\03013597,2,9,Frostwolf Explosives Expert\0312,2597,1459,0,\0302,0,0,9,Frostwolf Explosives Expert\031\031NPC,13598,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Stormpike Explosives Expert",[737]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You got it! Oh, hope glimmers!$B$BYour efforts may yet save us, $N. A monument they should make of you! A shrine they should build! May your name be praised until your grandchildren have grandchildren!$B$BUnless...THEY are freed and rise to the surface.  If that happens then you can forget about children.$B$BIf THEY are freed, then we're all worm food.\030I have the digest for you, $N.  I need not tell you to take great care with it.  And to keep it far from unfriendly hands.  $B$BThis book holds many truths...$B$B...And the truth can burn.\030Bring Yagyin's Digest to Theldurin.\030Ho! You were gone a long time. Did you get the digest?\030Forbidden Knowledge\0312,1,30,2,257,1,0\0302,33,79,2,259,1,0\0302,82,122,2,257,1,0\0302,129,158,2,257,1,0\0302,163,188,2,257,1,0\0303,1,35,2,384,1,0\0301,1,11,4,272,1,2785\0301,13,30,4,272,3,2785\0301,35,67,4,280,1,2785\0301,69,103,4,272,1,2785\0301,105,131,4,272,1,2785\0301,133,201,4,272,1,2785\0301,206,253,4,280,4,2785\0301,256,306,4,272,4,2785\0301,311,354,4,272,4,2785\0304,5,30,3,256,1,2785\0304,32,54,3,256,2,2785\031\0312,3,1418,0,\0302,0,0,6,Theldurin\031\031",[738]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This skeleton must be the unfortunate remains of Agmond. His body is broken and battered, and his bones picked clean.\030Prospector Agmond was in charge of our excavation sites in the Badlands, to the southwest.  I say \"was\" because...well, I haven't heard from him in weeks.  I need you to find Agmond so I can get his report.$B$BLast I heard Agmond was at the southernmost dig site in the Badlands--a tiny operation past the Angor Fortress.  I'd start your search for him there.\030Find Agmond.\030\030Find Agmond\0312,1,90,2,257,1,1344\0302,93,154,2,259,1,1344\0302,157,206,2,259,1,1344\0302,211,321,2,257,1,1344\0302,324,359,2,257,1,1344\0303,1,12,2,384,1,1344\0301,1,56,4,272,1,0\0301,58,117,4,272,1,0\0316412,4,7,Skeleton\0312,3,1418,0,\0302,0,0,1,Badlands\0302,0,0,4,Badlands--a\031707,19,707,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030739,23,739,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,2875,FINISHER,?,12,Battered Dwarven Skeleton",[7381]="PARTIAL\031conclusion,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030While it is true that Korrak has been slain, one question remains: Will he remain dead? Trolls are notorious for their other-worldly tribal magics. I would not be surprised if the fallen leader was raised from the dead to once more rule over his clan.$B$BYou know what to do should this ever occur.$B$B<Warmaster Laggrond makes a cutting motion across his neck with his index finger.>$B$BAnd  this time, I want his skull. Just keep your eyes peeled, soldier.$B$BDismissed!\030Should Korrak the Bloodrager make a return to the Field of Strife, seek him out and destroy him.$B$BReturn the Skull of Korrak to Warmaster Laggrond in the Hillsbrad Foothills.\030\030The Return of Korrak\0312,1,87,2,261,2,0\0302,89,147,2,257,1,0\0302,149,251,2,257,4,0\0302,256,298,2,257,1,0\0302,303,384,2,257,1,0\0302,389,421,2,259,1,0\0302,423,458,2,257,1,0\0302,463,472,2,257,1,0\0303,1,96,2,388,1,0\0303,101,176,2,384,1,0\03113840,2,5,Warmaster Laggrond\03012159,2,9,Korrak the Bloodrager\03013840,2,10,Warmaster Laggrond\0312,2597,1459,0,\0302,0,0,9,Field of Strife\0302,0,0,10,Warmaster Laggrond\0302,0,0,10,Hillsbrad Foothills\031\031ITEM,18148,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7382]="PARTIAL\031conclusion,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030There's something not quite right about all of this... Did anybody think to burn Korrak's corpse? Those trolls will stop at nothing to revive their fallen leader - as blue skinned pagan man-beasts often do.$B$BJust keep your eyes out, $N. Don't be alarmed if Korrak makes a surprise appearance; and if he does, I want him executed - his corpse burned to ashes.$B$BFor good measure, lop off his head and bring me his skull before you ignite the lifeless mass.\030Should Korrak the Bloodrager make a return to the Field of Strife, seek him out and destroy him.$B$BReturn the Skull of Korrak to Lieutenant Haggerdin in the Hillsbrad Foothills.$B\030\030Korrak the Everliving\0312,1,54,2,257,1,0\0302,56,97,2,257,2,0\0302,99,206,2,257,3,0\0302,211,238,2,257,1,0\0302,240,360,2,259,4,0\0302,365,458,2,257,1,0\0303,1,96,2,388,1,0\0303,101,178,2,384,1,0\03112159,2,7,Korrak the Bloodrager\03013841,2,8,Lieutenant Haggerdin\0312,2597,1459,0,\0302,0,0,7,Field of Strife\0302,0,0,8,Lieutenant Haggerdin\0302,0,0,8,Hillsbrad Foothills\031\031ITEM,18148,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7383]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031To be in the presence of the Oracle Tree... it is almost to feel wisdom take form. Let me continue the telling...$B$BWith Teldrassil grown, the Arch Druid approached the dragons for their blessings, as the dragons had placed upon Nordrassil in ancient times. But Nozdormu, Lord of Time, refused to give his blessing, chiding the druid for his arrogance. In agreement with Nozdormu, Alexstrasza also refused Staghelm, and without her blessing, Teldrassil's growth has been flawed and unpredictable...\030All was not well with Teldrassil, however. Staghelm's carefully made plans for the new World Tree had borne out as he had hoped, but there was one small problem, a problem to which many of the troubles on Teldrassil may be attributed.$B$BHowever, I will not get into that yet. You must visit the last moonwell, to the northwest in the Oracle Glade. Under the boughs of the Oracle Tree lies the first and most powerful of our wells. Retrieve a phial of its water and return to me.\030Fill the Amethyst Phial and bring it back to Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar.\030Along with the druids, the Oracle Tree and the Arch Druid have been carefully monitoring the growth of Teldrassil. But though we have a new home, our immortal lives have not been restored.\030Crown of the Earth\0312,1,42,2,257,1,3515\0302,44,234,2,325,1,3515\0302,239,276,2,257,3,3515\0302,278,348,2,257,1,3515\0302,350,431,2,257,1,3515\0302,433,479,2,257,1,3515\0303,1,76,2,384,1,3515\0301,1,43,4,272,1,3515\0301,45,82,4,272,1,3515\0301,84,113,4,272,1,3515\0301,118,258,4,336,1,3515\0301,260,353,4,272,1,3515\0301,355,499,4,272,1,3515\0304,1,114,3,256,1,3515\0304,116,188,3,256,1,3515\0313515,2,7,Corithras Moonrage\0312,141,1438,0,\0302,0,0,4,Oracle Glade\0302,0,0,7,Corithras Moonrage\0302,0,0,7,Dolanaar\031933,19,933,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030935,23,935,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,18151,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7385]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The blood of our enemies has been shed. I shall mix this blood with the rest that has been gathered. Once the offering is complete, the Ice Lord shall show these Stormpike dogs the full wrath of the Frostwolf Clan!\030You have the option of offering larger quantities of the blood taken from our enemies. I will be glad to accept gallon sized offerings, $N.\030null\030You have the option of offering larger quantities of the blood taken from our enemies. I will be glad to accept gallon sized offerings, $N.\030A Gallon of Blood\0312,1,86,2,261,1,13236\0302,88,139,2,257,3,13236\0303,1,4,2,384,1,13236\0301,1,39,4,276,1,13236\0301,41,100,4,272,3,13236\0301,102,214,4,272,3,13236\0304,1,86,3,260,1,13236\0304,88,139,3,256,3,13236\03110981,4,6,Frostwolf\0312,2597,1459,0,\031\031ITEM,17306,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[7386]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $N. I will use the power of these charms to augment the magic that has already been gathered. When enough power has been amassed, I shall focus the collected energies and call upon the Forest Lord to aid our cause.\030There are times which you may be entrenched in battle for days or weeks on end. During those longer periods of activity you may end up collecting large clusters of the Frostwolf's storm crystals.$B$BThe Circle accepts such offerings, $N.\030null\030There are times which you may be entrenched in battle for days or weeks on end. During those longer periods of activity you may end up collecting large clusters of the Frostwolf's storm crystals.$b$bThe Circle accepts such offerings, $N.\030Crystal Cluster\0312,1,79,2,261,1,13442\0302,81,195,2,257,1,13442\0302,200,237,2,257,1,13442\0303,1,4,2,384,1,13442\0301,1,14,4,272,1,13442\0301,16,104,4,272,3,13442\0301,106,225,4,272,3,13442\0304,1,79,3,260,1,13442\0304,81,195,3,256,1,13442\0304,200,237,3,256,1,13442\031\0312,2597,1459,0,\031\031ITEM,17423,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[739]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is sobering news, $N. But Agmond had a strong arm and a fierce hammer-swing, and his skull was as thick as they come! Although he was killed by those cursed troggs I'm sure he took a lot of them down with him.\030Agmond's tracks lead from the west.  It is easy to tell from the bloody smears across rock and sand that the dwarf crawled some distance.$B$BAnd here he died.$B$BUpon close inspection, the word \"Murdaloc\" is roughly scrawled in a patch of Badlands sandstone.$B$BScrawled next to Agmond's dead hand.\030Slay Agmond's killer, Murdaloc.$B$BSlay 12 Stonevault Bonesnappers.$B$BReport to Prospector Ironband in Loch Modan.\030Do you have news of Agmond's fate? Did you find him?\030Murdaloc\0312,1,35,2,257,1,0\0302,38,137,2,257,1,0\0302,142,158,2,257,1,0\0302,163,258,2,257,1,0\0302,263,298,2,257,1,0\0303,1,31,2,384,1,0\0303,36,67,2,384,1,0\0303,72,115,2,384,1,0\0301,1,26,4,272,1,1344\0301,28,122,4,272,1,1344\0301,124,214,4,276,1,1344\0304,1,34,3,256,2,1344\0304,36,52,3,256,2,1344\0312945,2,4,Murdaloc\0302945,2,6,Murdaloc\0301344,2,8,Prospector Ironband\0312,3,1418,0,\0302,0,0,5,Agmond's\0302,0,0,8,Prospector Ironband\0302,0,0,8,Loch Modan\031738,19,738,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030704,23,704,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,2875,GIVER,?,9,Battered Dwarven Skeleton\030NPC,2945,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Murdaloc\030NPC,2893,OBJECTIVE,12,13,Stonevault Bonesnapper",[74]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I can barely make out those letters. But that writing style reminds me of something I once saw before my vision became so poor.\030Inside the crate you find various objects: musty heirlooms, a family portrait, a few hunting trophies and some old books.  Near the bottom, underneath a ceramic vase, you uncover A Torn Journal Page.\030The Torn Journal page you discovered provides your next clue.\030What have you got there? I cannot see. My eyesight is very bad. Put it in my hands.\030The Legend of Stalvan\0312,1,121,2,257,1,0\0302,124,199,2,257,1,0\0303,1,61,2,384,1,0\0301,1,36,4,272,1,294\0301,38,127,4,272,1,294\0304,1,24,3,256,2,294\0304,26,38,3,256,1,294\0304,40,63,3,256,1,294\0304,65,83,3,256,1,294\0312996,2,2,Torn\0302996,2,3,Torn\0312,10,1431,0,\03172,19,72,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\03075,23,75,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,1561,GIVER,?,9,Sealed Crate",[7401]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You now have license to decimate dwarves by the dozen, $C!$B$B<Yazra stares off into the distance for a moment.>$B$BYou never forget your first de-spining...\030By order of Sergeant Yazra Bloodsnarl, all dwarves on the field of battle are to be killed on sight.$B$BShould you slay a dwarf in combat, rip out their spine, leaving a spineless heap of stink and rot to serve as a warning to any and all that dare oppose the might of the Frostwolf.$B$BReturn to Sergeant Yazra Bloodsnarl with proof of your heroics.\030You have been tasked with slaying opposing Dwarf players in Alterac Valley.$B$BKill a Dwarf and rip out their spine. Take the Dwarf Spine to Sergeant Yazra Bloodsnarl at Frostwolf Keep.\030I deal in wholesale irony, soldier.\030Wanted: DWARVES!\0312,1,100,2,261,1,0\0302,105,283,2,257,4,0\0302,288,350,2,257,1,0\0303,1,75,2,384,1,0\0303,80,116,2,384,1,0\0303,118,185,2,384,1,0\0301,1,58,4,272,1,0\0301,63,112,4,272,1,0\0301,117,157,4,272,1,0\0304,1,35,3,256,1,0\03113448,2,1,Sergeant Yazra Bloodsnarl\03010981,2,2,Frostwolf\03013448,2,3,Sergeant Yazra Bloodsnarl\03013448,2,6,Sergeant Yazra Bloodsnarl\03010981,2,6,Frostwolf\0312,2597,1459,0,\0302,0,0,3,Sergeant Yazra Bloodsnarl\0302,0,0,4,Alterac Valley\0302,0,0,6,Sergeant Yazra Bloodsnarl\0302,0,0,6,Frostwolf Keep\0317427,23,7427,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,179438,GIVER,?,9,Wanted: DWARVES!\030ITEM,18206,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7402]="PARTIAL\031conclusion,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030By order of Corporal Noreg Stormpike, all able bodied soldiers of Stormpike are required to slay any opposing orcs that they meet upon the field of battle.$B$BSoldiers are required to remove a tusk or tooth from the maw of the enemy and present said tooth as proof of their accomplishment.$B$BWear protective gloves.\030You have been tasked with slaying opposing Orc players in Alterac Valley.$B$BKill an Orc and take their Orc Tooth back to Corporal Noreg Stormpike at Dun Baldar.\030\030Wanted: ORCS!\0312,1,155,2,261,1,0\0302,160,289,2,261,1,0\0302,294,316,2,257,1,0\0303,1,73,2,384,1,0\0303,78,161,2,384,1,0\03113447,2,1,Corporal Noreg Stormpike\03013447,2,5,Corporal Noreg Stormpike\0312,2597,1459,0,\0302,0,0,4,Alterac Valley\0302,0,0,5,Corporal Noreg Stormpike\0302,0,0,5,Dun Baldar\0317428,23,7428,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,179437,GIVER,?,9,Wanted: ORCS!\030ITEM,18207,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[741]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh my! Leave it to Prospector Remtravel to discover such a find!\030So the prospector wants to send the mysterious fossil to the Explorers' League in Darnassus? I don't feel right leaving Darkshore without him.$B$BHere, $n, deliver the mysterious fossil to Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker in Darnassus.\030Take the mysterious fossil to Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker in Darnassus.\030What can I do for you, $R?\030The Absent Minded Prospector\0312,1,92,2,259,2,2913\0302,94,142,2,257,1,2913\0302,147,234,2,257,1,2913\0303,1,75,2,384,1,2913\0301,8,64,4,272,1,2912\0304,1,26,3,256,2,2912\0312912,2,3,Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker\0302912,2,4,Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker\0302917,4,5,Prospector Remtravel\0312,148,1439,0,\0302,0,0,1,Explorers' League\0302,0,0,1,Darnassus\0302,0,0,3,Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker\0302,0,0,3,Darnassus\0302,0,0,4,Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker\0302,0,0,4,Darnassus\0304,0,0,5,Prospector Remtravel\031731,19,731,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030942,23,942,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[742]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Welcome to the new frontier, $N. Ashenvale is a land of opportunity, one where a young $C like yourself is able to find boundless chances to prove their mettle. Look around the outpost here, and be sure to travel out to the Zoram Strand, as the Horde has another outpost there as well.$B$BYour presence here tells me that you've come to learn more about the hunt. Listen close, and I will gladly share with you what you need to know.\030Attention, young adventurers!  The wilds of Ashenvale await you!$B$BThe Horde has established a strong presence in the lands north of the Barrens.  Our two outposts - Splintertree Post and the Zoram Strand Outpost - strive to bring glory to the Horde!  Those who would prove themselves should seek out guidance there.  Of note: Senani Thunderheart in Splintertree Post, directly north of the Barrens, seeks adventurers willing to take part in a great hunt of Ashenvale!\030Speak with Senani Thunderheart at Splintertree Post, Ashenvale.\030\030The Ashenvale Hunt\0312,1,29,2,257,1,10881\0302,32,64,2,257,1,10881\0302,69,146,2,257,1,10881\0302,149,251,2,257,1,10881\0302,254,317,2,259,4,10881\0302,320,469,2,257,1,10881\0303,1,63,2,384,1,10881\0301,1,32,4,272,1,12696\0301,34,160,4,272,1,12696\0301,162,285,4,272,1,12696\0301,290,363,4,272,1,12696\0301,365,433,4,274,3,12696\03112696,2,6,Senani Thunderheart\0309084,2,6,Thunderheart\03012696,2,7,Senani Thunderheart\0309084,2,7,Thunderheart\0312,1638,1456,0,\0302,0,0,3,Barrens\0302,0,0,4,Horde\0302,0,0,6,Splintertree Post\0302,0,0,6,Barrens\0302,0,0,7,Splintertree Post\0304,0,0,10,Zoram Strand\031235,22,235,UNKNOWN\0306382,22,6382,UNKNOWN\0306383,24,6383,UNKNOWN\031",[7421]="UNRESOLVED\031characters,conclusion,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes,storytellingContext\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030\030\030\030Darkspear Defense\031\031\0312,2597,1459,0,\031\031ITEM,18142,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7422]="UNRESOLVED\031characters,conclusion,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes,storytellingContext\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030\030\030\030Tuft it Out\031\031\0312,2597,1459,0,\031\031ITEM,18143,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7423]="UNRESOLVED\031characters,conclusion,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes,storytellingContext\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030\030\030\030I've Got A Fever For More Bone Chips\031\031\0312,2597,1459,0,\031\031ITEM,18144,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7424]="PARTIAL\031characters,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031*Dirk throws the hoof in a pile behind him.*\030null\030\030Give 'em a limp, $N. They must learn that the gnomish people won't take to being bullied!\030What the Hoof?\0312,1,4,2,257,1,0\0301,1,44,4,272,1,0\0304,1,20,3,256,1,0\0304,22,89,3,256,1,0\031\0312,2597,1459,0,\031\031ITEM,18145,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7425]="UNRESOLVED\031characters,conclusion,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes,storytellingContext\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030\030\030\030Staghelm's Mojo Jamboree\031\031\0312,2597,1459,0,\031\031ITEM,18146,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7426]="UNRESOLVED\031characters,conclusion,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes,storytellingContext\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030\030\030\030One Man's Love\031\031\0312,2597,1459,0,\031\031ITEM,18147,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7427]="UNRESOLVED\031characters,conclusion,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes,storytellingContext\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030\030\030\030Wanted: MORE DWARVES!\031\031\0312,2597,1459,0,\0317401,19,7401,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,18206,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7428]="UNRESOLVED\031characters,conclusion,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes,storytellingContext\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030\030\030\030Wanted: MORE ORCS!\031\031\0312,2597,1459,0,\0317402,19,7402,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,18207,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7429]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh, thank you for freeing me! You - ranked number one. Everyone else - ranked number two or lower.$B$BI knew my life was destined for more than just being an appetizer to some ogre!\030\030\030It's called the Gordok Shackle Key - well, that's what these \"tons o' fun\" keep calling it. I think any of the ogres might have it, but I'm not sure if any specific ones do. Maybe the guards have a better chance of having one...$B$BWhat am I talking about - you have it already, don't you?! Is that it there??!\030Free Knot!\0311,1,29,4,272,1,14338\0301,31,54,4,272,1,14338\0301,56,98,4,272,1,14338\0301,103,181,4,272,1,14338\0304,1,91,3,256,1,14338\0304,93,173,3,256,4,14338\0304,175,228,3,256,4,14338\0304,233,290,3,256,2,14338\0304,292,310,3,256,2,14338\03115554,4,3,Number Two\030211,4,4,Ogre\0312,2557,0,0,\0315525,19,5525,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,18250,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[743]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have done well, $N. You seem well prepared to travel onward. Let the wind always be at your back.\030Thank you for taking the time to speak to me, $N. I am Ruul, warrior and teacher.$B$BYou have obviously reached an age when you must prepare for your trials if you are to adventure much further out of Mulgore.$B$BIf you wish a test of your strength, start by seeking out the Windfury harpies to the southeast. They nestle along the mountain's edges away from the road.$B$BThey are one of our natural enemies here in Mulgore and will be a good gauge of your skill.\030Bring 8 Windfury Talons to Ruul Eagletalon in Bloodhoof Village.\030The Windfuries are deadly foes. Their strength in battle is only rivaled by their desire for fresh meat.\030Dangers of the Windfury\0312,1,49,2,257,1,2985\0302,51,81,2,257,1,2985\0302,86,209,2,257,4,2985\0302,214,309,2,259,4,2985\0302,311,368,2,257,1,2985\0302,373,463,2,261,3,2985\0303,1,64,2,384,1,2985\0301,1,23,4,272,1,2985\0301,25,64,4,272,4,2985\0301,66,101,4,272,1,2985\0304,1,31,3,256,1,2985\0304,33,104,3,262,1,2985\0312985,2,7,Ruul Eagletalon\0312,215,1412,0,\0302,0,0,6,Mulgore\0302,0,0,7,Ruul Eagletalon\0302,0,0,7,Bloodhoof Village\031\031ITEM,4751,OBJECTIVE,8,15,",[744]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you for your help, $N.$B$BMy part in my brother's ceremony is almost complete. Giving him his headdress and witnessing the ceremony are all my duty requires of me.\030$N, my brother soon stands before Chief Bloodhoof, and it is my honor to make his headdress for him.$B$BI want to ask a favor of you while I finish tanning these leather straps. There is not time for me to find enough feathers, and I was wondering, would you gather more for me?$B$BYou can find feathers of the correct size from the harpies residing far to the north and northwest of Thunder Bluff. I need only 6 azure and 6 bronze feathers to complete the design.\030Collect 6 Azure Feathers and 6 Bronze Feathers, and bring them to Eyahn Eagletalon in Thunder Bluff.\030This headdress will certainly be a wonderful gift for my brother.\030Preparation for Ceremony\0312,1,100,2,257,1,2987\0302,105,177,2,259,1,2987\0302,179,278,2,257,4,2987\0302,283,398,2,257,1,2987\0302,400,464,2,259,1,2987\0303,1,100,2,384,1,2987\0301,1,28,4,272,1,2987\0301,33,84,4,272,1,2987\0301,86,169,4,272,1,2987\0304,1,65,3,256,3,2987\0312987,2,6,Eyahn Eagletalon\0312,1638,1456,0,\0302,0,0,6,Eyahn Eagletalon\0302,0,0,6,Thunder Bluff\031\031ITEM,4752,OBJECTIVE,6,15,\030ITEM,4753,OBJECTIVE,6,15,",[7441]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have found it! A curse upon that miserable imp. Alas, my material possessions are meager at best. You may choose from what I have to offer.\030I had let my guard down for only one moment, stranger. In my haste to escape the grip of the fallen Prince, I was robbed. A most foul demon, the imp Pusillin, pilfered my book of incantations and the key to the once great halls of Eldre'Thalas.$B$BI no longer hold interest in the key, as I have exchanged my immortality for freedom, but I desperately need my book of incantations.$B$BFind the imp, Pusillin, and recover my book.$B$BSearch the Warpwood Quarter of Dire Maul for Pusillin.\030Travel to Dire Maul and locate the Imp, Pusillin. Convince Pusillin to give you Azj'Tordin's Book of Incantations through any means necessary.$B$BReturn to Azj'Tordin at the Lariss Pavilion in Feralas should you recover the Book of Incantations.\030I regret nothing, stranger. The Queen has long since passed. The works of the Shen'Dralar have been marred by the madness of Prince Tortheldrin. I seek only freedom... Escape...\030Pusillin and the Elder Azj'Tordin\0312,1,54,2,257,1,14355\0302,56,121,2,257,1,14355\0302,123,244,2,257,1,14355\0302,249,381,2,265,1,14355\0302,386,429,2,257,1,14355\0302,434,487,2,257,1,14355\0303,1,49,2,384,1,14355\0303,51,142,2,384,1,14355\0303,147,245,2,384,1,14355\0301,1,18,4,272,1,14355\0301,20,51,4,276,1,14355\0301,53,101,4,272,1,14355\0301,103,143,4,272,1,14355\0304,1,27,3,256,1,14355\0304,29,60,3,256,1,14355\0304,62,144,3,256,1,14355\0304,146,167,3,266,1,14355\0304,169,177,3,256,1,14355\03114354,2,3,Pusillin\03014354,2,5,Pusillin\03014354,2,6,Pusillin\03014354,2,7,Pusillin\03014354,2,8,Pusillin\03014355,2,9,Azj'Tordin\03011486,3,16,Prince Tortheldrin\0312,2557,0,0,\0302,0,0,7,Dire Maul\0302,0,0,9,Azj'Tordin\0302,0,0,9,Lariss Pavilion\0302,0,0,9,Feralas\031\031ITEM,18261,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[745]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031$N, it is good you've taken my task seriously. Respect of the land and its creatures is important. Death and life are a circle... a necessity. One cannot exist without the other. Take time to ponder this and do well to never forget it.\030$N, there are many conflicts that wound this land. It is my hope that you will not bear witness to as many of them as I have. Yet there is one that I would ask you to seek out. It will give you some sense of how terrible, if left unchecked, even a small threat can be to the land.$B$BPalemane gnolls have settled to the south of Bloodhoof and in a cave to the west. They disrespect our attempts to communicate with them, and they slay the wildlife of Mulgore unbridled.$B$BWords are no longer the answer.\030Kill 10 Palemane Tanners, 8 Palemane Skinners, and 5 Palemane Poachers, then return to Baine Bloodhoof in Bloodhoof Village.\030If the Palemanes had respected the land and its inhabitants more, this conflict would have never occurred.\030Sharing the Land\0312,1,50,2,257,1,2993\0302,52,125,2,259,3,2993\0302,127,176,2,259,4,2993\0302,178,280,2,261,4,2993\0302,285,365,2,257,1,2993\0302,367,469,2,257,1,2993\0302,474,504,2,257,1,2993\0303,1,124,2,384,1,2993\0301,1,46,4,272,1,2993\0301,48,98,4,272,1,2993\0301,100,129,4,272,1,2993\0301,131,142,4,272,1,2993\0301,144,178,4,272,1,2993\0301,180,235,4,272,1,2993\0304,1,106,3,256,4,2993\0312993,2,8,Baine Bloodhoof\0312,215,1412,0,\0302,0,0,5,Bloodhoof\0302,0,0,8,Baine Bloodhoof\0302,0,0,8,Bloodhoof Village\031\031NPC,2949,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Palemane Tanner\030NPC,2950,OBJECTIVE,8,13,Palemane Skinner\030NPC,2951,OBJECTIVE,5,13,Palemane Poacher",[746]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, $N. This will calm the beasts of Mulgore. And, spirits willing, it will teach the dwarves that hollowing the land is not the path to knowledge.\030There are dwarves preparing a dig site to the northwest.  They think secrets lie in the earth, and that is true, but hollowing and defiling the land is no way to earn its teachings.$B$BCollect the dwarven tools of digging, smash them, and return to me with the dwarves' broken tools.$B$BYou can smash the tools at a forge.  You will find one in Thunder Bluff, but any forge -- even a forge at the dwarven camp -- will suffice.\030Collect 5 Prospector's Picks.$B$BAt a forge, smash the Prospector's Picks to create Broken Tools.$B$BBring 5 Broken Tools to Baine Bloodhoof in Bloodhoof Village.\030Hello, $N.  Do you have the Broken Tools?  The dwarves' digging will enrage the kodos of Mulgore.  This defilement must be stopped!\030Dwarven Digging\0312,1,56,2,257,1,2993\0302,59,181,2,257,1,2993\0302,186,283,2,257,1,2993\0302,288,322,2,257,1,2993\0302,325,426,2,257,3,2993\0303,1,29,2,384,1,2993\0303,34,97,2,384,1,2993\0303,102,162,2,384,1,2993\0301,1,14,4,272,1,2993\0301,16,52,4,272,3,2993\0301,54,154,4,272,3,2993\0304,1,10,3,256,1,2993\0304,13,41,3,256,2,2993\0304,44,97,3,256,3,2993\0304,100,131,3,256,1,2993\0312993,2,8,Baine Bloodhoof\0312,215,1412,0,\0302,0,0,5,Thunder Bluff\0302,0,0,8,Baine Bloodhoof\0302,0,0,8,Bloodhoof Village\031\031ITEM,4703,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[7461]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031We thank you, hero.\030Have you heard enough? Are you a $g man:woman; of action?$B$BThis madness must come to an end. The age of the immortals has long since passed. Destroy the guardians surrounding the pylons to lower the force field. When this is done, destroy Immol'thar. With the Prince's power greatly reduced, attack and end him. Lay the spirits of this city to rest, adventurer.\030You must destroy the guardians surrounding the 5 Pylons that power the Prison of Immol'thar. Once the Pylons have powered down, the force field surrounding Immol'thar will have dissipated.$B$BEnter the Prison of Immol'thar and eradicate the foul demon that stands at its heart. Finally, confront Prince Tortheldrin in Athenaeum.$B$BReturn to the Shen'dralar Ancient in the courtyard should you complete this quest.\030Be wary, adventurer. The Prince is... persuasive.\030The Madness Within\0312,1,22,2,257,2,14358\0302,24,57,2,257,2,14358\0302,62,94,2,257,1,14358\0302,96,142,2,257,1,14358\0302,144,213,2,261,1,14358\0302,215,252,2,261,1,14358\0302,254,313,2,261,1,14358\0302,315,363,2,257,1,14358\0303,1,92,2,388,1,14358\0303,94,188,2,384,3,14358\0303,193,277,2,384,1,14358\0303,279,328,2,384,1,14358\0303,333,414,2,448,1,14358\0301,1,19,4,272,1,14358\0304,1,20,3,256,1,14358\0304,22,37,3,256,1,14358\0304,39,49,3,256,1,14358\03111496,2,6,Immol'thar\03011496,2,9,Immol'thar\03011496,2,10,Immol'thar\03011496,2,11,Immol'thar\03011486,2,12,Prince Tortheldrin\03014358,2,13,Shen'dralar Ancient\0312,2557,0,0,\0302,0,0,12,Athenaeum\0302,0,0,13,Shen'dralar Ancient\0317877,23,7877,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,11496,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Immol'thar\030NPC,11486,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Prince Tortheldrin",[7462]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You open the chest to find...\030In the library, Athenaeum, you will find an ancient chest hidden beneath the stairway. Take from it that which you desire.\030Return to the Athenaeum and find the Treasure of the Shen'dralar. Claim your reward!\030\030The Treasure of the Shen'dralar\0312,1,86,2,321,3,14358\0302,88,122,2,259,1,14358\0303,1,65,2,384,1,14358\0303,67,84,2,384,1,14358\0301,1,29,4,272,1,0\031\0312,2557,0,0,\0302,0,0,3,Athenaeum\0317461,19,7461,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,179517,FINISHER,?,12,Treasure of the Shen'dralar",[7463]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Wonderful! Who are you again? Oh it matters not. What was I supposed to give you? Hrm... well you are a $C, perhaps you will find this useful.\030A $r mage! How wonderous. I have not seen one of your kind for... oh what is it going on now? 500 years!$B$BI have something that will quench your thirst, but first you must do a task for me.$B$B<Lydros snickers.>$B$BThere is an anomaly in Eldre'Thalas. A water elemental has taken residence in the east wing. His presence must be catalogued!$B$BVenture to the Warpwood Quarter and extract a portion of the elemental essence of the Hydrospawn. Return it to me and I shall teach you a useful cantrip.\030Travel to the Warpwood Quarter of Dire Maul and slay the water elemental, Hydrospawn. Return to Lorekeeper Lydros in the Athenaeum with the Hydrospawn Essence.\030Yes? Do I know you?\030Arcane Refreshment\0312,1,10,2,257,1,14368\0302,12,25,2,257,1,14368\0302,27,65,2,257,1,14368\0302,67,93,2,257,2,14368\0302,95,104,2,257,1,14368\0302,109,191,2,257,3,14368\0302,196,213,2,257,1,14368\0302,218,253,2,257,1,14368\0302,255,309,2,257,1,14368\0302,311,342,2,257,1,14368\0302,347,443,2,257,1,14368\0302,445,499,2,257,3,14368\0303,1,85,2,384,1,14368\0303,87,159,2,384,1,14368\0301,1,10,4,272,1,14368\0301,12,29,4,272,2,14368\0301,31,48,4,272,1,14368\0301,50,81,4,272,2,14368\0301,83,88,4,272,1,14368\0301,90,142,4,272,4,14368\0304,1,4,3,256,2,14368\0304,6,19,3,256,2,14368\031510,2,9,Water Elemental\03013280,2,11,Hydrospawn\030510,2,13,Water Elemental\03013280,2,13,Hydrospawn\03014368,2,14,Lorekeeper Lydros\03013280,2,14,Hydrospawn\0312,2557,0,0,\0302,0,0,8,Eldre'Thalas\0302,0,0,11,Warpwood Quarter\0302,0,0,13,Warpwood Quarter of Dire Maul\0302,0,0,14,Lorekeeper Lydros\0302,0,0,14,Athenaeum\031\031ITEM,18299,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[747]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The Tauren of Narache thank you, $N. You show much promise.\030You have a promising air about you, and will prove yourself to the tribe. Perhaps someday soon you will be welcomed into the great city of Thunder Bluff. But before that can happen you must prove yourself to my father, Chief Hawkwind.$B$BUp here on Red Cloud Mesa we pride ourselves on keen hunting skills. Tauren hunt out of necessity and for sport. Our supply of meats has run low and we require feathers for clothing. Hunt the nearby plainstriders and prove yourself by resupplying the village.\030Grull Hawkwind in Camp Narache wants you to bring him 7 Plainstrider Feathers and 7 pieces of Plainstrider Meat.\030Providing meat and feathers for the tribe is the first step in proving yourself as a $C before the Chief.\030The Hunt Begins\0312,1,73,2,257,3,2980\0302,75,153,2,257,4,2980\0302,155,234,2,257,1,2980\0302,239,306,2,257,1,2980\0302,308,350,2,257,1,2980\0302,352,420,2,257,1,2980\0302,422,497,2,257,1,2980\0303,1,112,2,386,1,2980\0301,1,36,4,272,1,2980\0301,38,59,4,272,1,2980\0304,1,105,3,256,1,2980\0312981,2,3,Chief Hawkwind\0302980,2,8,Grull Hawkwind\0302955,2,8,Plainstrider\0312,220,1412,0,\0302,0,0,8,Camp Narache\031\031ITEM,4739,OBJECTIVE,7,15,\030ITEM,4740,OBJECTIVE,7,15,",[748]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have done well, $N. I will take these and bind their power into a totem of cleansing.\030Goblins and their servants have tainted our sacred water wells!  We cannot allow this.$B$BTo cleanse each well, I must create a cleansing totem, then you must bring the totem to the well and perform a cleansing ritual.$B$BFirst we will create a cleansing totem for the Winterhoof Water Well.  To do this, the land must offer its aid. Hunt prairie wolves for their paws and adult plainstriders for their talons.  They are to the southwest.$B$BReturn to me with the paws and talons, $N.\030Bring 6 Prairie Wolf Paws and 4 Plainstrider Talons to Mull Thunderhorn in Bloodhoof.\030Do you have the paws and talons, $N?\030Poison Water\0312,1,63,2,257,1,2948\0302,66,86,2,265,1,2948\0302,91,218,2,257,1,2948\0302,223,291,2,257,3,2948\0302,294,333,2,257,1,2948\0302,335,410,2,257,1,2948\0302,413,438,2,257,1,2948\0302,443,484,2,257,1,2948\0303,1,85,2,384,1,2948\0301,1,23,4,272,1,2948\0301,25,89,4,272,3,2948\0304,1,36,3,256,2,2948\0312958,2,9,Prairie Wolf\0302955,2,9,Plainstrider\0302948,2,9,Mull Thunderhorn\0312,215,1412,0,\0302,0,0,9,Mull Thunderhorn\0302,0,0,9,Bloodhoof\031754,23,754,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4758,OBJECTIVE,6,15,\030ITEM,4759,OBJECTIVE,4,15,",[7481]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031A shame... a tragedy. The items are lost you say? No trace of him, eh?\030Several years ago, a lone elven master named Kariel Winthalus fled the devastation of his homeland with several ancient elven artifacts in tow.$B$BOur search for this lost master lead us from the ruins of Quel'Thalas, through the Burning Steppes, across the great expanses of the sea, to Feralas.$B$BWe suspect that the elf sought sanctuary in the halls of Eldre'Thalas (what is now known as Dire Maul).$B$BYou must find him, adventurer. Whether alive or dead, the knowledge he carried must be recovered!\030Search Dire Maul for Kariel Winthalus. Report back to Sage Korolusk at Camp Mojache with whatever information that you may find.\030Master Kariel Winthalus Found\030My associate, the night elf scholar, Runethorn, is recruiting her allies for this task.\030Elven Legends\0312,1,143,2,321,1,14373\0302,148,296,2,325,1,14373\0302,301,403,2,257,4,14373\0302,408,437,2,257,1,14373\0302,439,504,2,257,1,14373\0303,1,38,2,384,1,14373\0303,40,128,2,384,1,14373\0301,1,10,4,272,1,14373\0301,12,21,4,272,1,14373\0301,23,49,4,276,2,14373\0301,51,70,4,272,2,14373\0305,1,87,3,256,1,14373\0304,1,29,3,384,1,14373\03114373,2,7,Sage Korolusk\0312,2557,0,0,\0302,0,0,2,Feralas\0302,0,0,7,Sage Korolusk\0302,0,0,7,Camp Mojache\031\031",[7482]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031A shame... a tragedy. The items are lost you say? No trace of him, eh?\030Several years ago, a lone elven master named Kariel Winthalus fled the devastation of his homeland with several ancient elven artifacts in tow.$B$BOur search for this lost master lead us from the ruins of Quel'Thalas, through the Burning Steppes, across the great expanses of the sea, to Feralas.$B$BWe suspect that the elf sought sanctuary in the halls of Eldre'Thalas (what is now known as Dire Maul).$B$BYou must find him, adventurer. Whether alive or dead, the knowledge he carried must be recovered!\030Search Dire Maul for Kariel Winthalus. Report back to Scholar Runethorn at Feathermoon with whatever information that you may find.\030Master Kariel Winthalus Found\030My associate, the night elf scholar, Runethorn, is recruiting her allies for this task.\030Elven Legends\0312,1,143,2,321,1,14374\0302,148,296,2,325,1,14374\0302,301,403,2,257,4,14374\0302,408,437,2,257,1,14374\0302,439,504,2,257,1,14374\0303,1,38,2,384,1,14374\0303,40,131,2,384,1,14374\0301,1,10,4,272,1,14374\0301,12,21,4,272,1,14374\0301,23,49,4,276,2,14374\0301,51,70,4,272,2,14374\0305,1,87,3,256,1,14374\0304,1,29,3,384,1,14374\03114374,2,7,Scholar Runethorn\0312,2557,0,0,\0302,0,0,2,Feralas\0302,0,0,7,Scholar Runethorn\0302,0,0,7,Feathermoon\031\031",[7483]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Lydros yawns.>$B$BAs promised, the Arcanum of Rapidity. Don't spend it all in once place.$B$B<Lydros snickers.>\030Master Winthalus lost the Libram of Rapidity in the east wing. The Libram will allow for a minor haste cantrip to be placed upon your equipment. Parlor tricks, really...$B$BRegardless, if you are interested, you will need to present the Libram along with some basic reagents.$B$BHrm... I believe it also requires blood of heroes, a pristine black diamond, and large brilliant shards. I could be wrong!$B$B<Lydros shrugs.>\030Bring a Libram of Rapidity, 1 Pristine Black Diamond, 2 Large Brilliant Shards, and 2 Blood of Heroes to Lorekeeper Lydros in Dire Maul to receive an Arcanum of Rapidity.\030What is it? I have much cataloguing to do!\030Libram of Rapidity\0312,1,62,2,261,1,14368\0302,64,144,2,257,3,14368\0302,146,169,2,257,1,14368\0302,174,275,2,259,4,14368\0302,280,285,2,257,1,14368\0302,287,383,2,257,4,14368\0302,385,401,2,257,4,14368\0302,406,421,2,257,1,14368\0303,1,170,2,384,1,14368\0301,1,15,4,272,1,14368\0301,20,56,4,272,1,14368\0301,58,90,4,272,1,14368\0301,95,112,4,272,1,14368\0304,1,11,3,256,2,14368\0304,13,42,3,256,1,14368\03114368,2,9,Lorekeeper Lydros\0312,2557,0,0,\0302,0,0,9,Lorekeeper Lydros\0302,0,0,9,Dire Maul\031\031ITEM,18332,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,18335,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,14344,OBJECTIVE,2,15,\030ITEM,12938,OBJECTIVE,2,15,",[7484]="PARTIAL\031consequences,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Don't hurt yourself when applying the enchantment, $R.\030This libram almost aroused interest in one of the younger Lorekeeper's familiars. Poor thing, it was only a few weeks old.$B$BThose among you who are more magically inclined might find this item interesting.$B$BThe Libram of Focus was lost in this wing. I can only assume one of the Highborne spirits holds it in their possession.$B$BBring the Libram along with some large brilliant shards, skin of shadow, and a pristine black diamond and I shall conjure the Arcanum.\030Bring a Libram of Focus, 1 Pristine Black Diamond, 4 Large Brilliant Shards, and 2 Skin of Shadow to Lorekeeper Lydros in Dire Maul to receive an Arcanum of Focus.\030You again? What could you possibly want now?\030Libram of Focus\0312,1,81,2,257,1,14368\0302,83,122,2,257,1,14368\0302,127,207,2,257,4,14368\0302,212,253,2,261,1,14368\0302,255,330,2,321,4,14368\0302,335,468,2,257,3,14368\0303,1,163,2,384,1,14368\0301,1,54,4,272,1,14368\0304,1,10,3,256,2,14368\0304,12,44,3,258,4,14368\0314244,2,6,Shadow\0304244,2,7,Shadow\03014368,2,7,Lorekeeper Lydros\0312,2557,0,0,\0302,0,0,7,Lorekeeper Lydros\0302,0,0,7,Dire Maul\031\031ITEM,18333,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,18335,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,14344,OBJECTIVE,4,15,\030ITEM,12753,OBJECTIVE,2,15,",[7485]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes, yes... Calm yourself. As promised, here is your Arcanum.\030He wept like an infant at the loss of this libram. Mind you, I myself have wept over texts - there is no greater loss than that of knowledge and history - but to cry over this nearly useless jumbling of incantations? Preposterous! It left me to believe that the Prince was doing him a favor in flaying the flesh from his bones.$B$BBring the Libram along with a pristine black diamond, large brilliant shards, and a frayed abomination stitching and I shall recreate the Arcanum.$B$BOh, and check the north wing.\030Bring a Libram of Protection, 1 Pristine Black Diamond, 2 Large Brilliant Shards, and 1 Frayed Abomination Stitching to Lorekeeper Lydros in Dire Maul to receive an Arcanum of Protection.\030My patience prevents your suffering.\030Libram of Protection\0312,1,50,2,257,1,14368\0302,52,216,2,321,2,14368\0302,218,230,2,257,1,14368\0302,232,327,2,257,4,14368\0302,332,477,2,257,3,14368\0302,482,510,2,257,1,14368\0303,1,187,2,384,1,14368\0301,1,11,4,272,1,14368\0301,13,26,4,272,1,14368\0301,28,61,4,272,1,14368\0304,1,36,3,260,1,14368\0318545,2,5,Abomination\0308545,2,7,Abomination\03014368,2,7,Lorekeeper Lydros\0312,2557,0,0,\0302,0,0,7,Lorekeeper Lydros\0302,0,0,7,Dire Maul\031\031ITEM,18334,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,18335,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,14344,OBJECTIVE,2,15,\030ITEM,12735,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7486]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hydraxis' voice descends from the waters' surface...$B$B\"Choose that which best suits you, $N.  May it protect you against the foes of the Waterlords.\"\030$N, your services to the Warlords surpassed all we could expect from the denizens of this world.$B$BWe do not understand your people's notions of gratitude, or rewarding good works, but in this case... perhaps a reward is warranted.$B$BUnder the surf at the southern base of this island, you will find a coffer.  In it you will find your... reward.$B$BGo, $N.  Claim your reward.\030Claim your reward from Hydraxis' Coffer.\030\030A Hero's Reward\0312,1,96,2,257,4,13278\0302,101,201,2,257,1,13278\0302,203,232,2,257,4,13278\0302,237,311,2,257,3,13278\0302,314,340,2,257,3,13278\0302,342,348,2,257,1,13278\0302,362,379,2,257,1,13278\0303,1,40,2,384,1,13278\0301,1,52,4,272,1,0\0301,57,94,4,272,1,0\0301,97,151,4,284,1,0\031\0312,16,1447,0,\0302,0,0,1,Warlords\0302,0,0,8,Hydraxis' Coffer\0316824,19,6824,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,179551,FINISHER,?,12,Hydraxis' Coffer",[7488]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You retrieved the web!  Well done, $N!  Lethtendris, like many elves of her ilk, are blind to the dangers the abuse of magic can cause to our world.  They believe they are masters of magic; they do not realize that they are slaves to their own addiction.  Her death saddens me, but it was necessary.$B$BThank you, $N.  I will have the energies within the web released safely over a wide area, and then I'll destroy it to prevent future magical exploits.\030The mage Lethtendris, a vicious blood elf whose brutality is matched only by her twisted addiction to magic, has fled into Dire Maul.  She has created a device, a web to ensnare the magical energies of that place and we fear that, if left unchecked, she will cause irreparable damage to our world!$B$BStop her, $N.  Find her and retrieve her web.  She is likely near the satyrs in Warpwood Quarter of Dire Maul.  Bring the web to me so that its power may be released safely back into the wilds...\030Bring Lethtendris' Web to Latronicus Moonspear at the Feathermoon Stronghold in Feralas.\030Do you have the web, $N?  Its concentrated magical energy must be dissipated!\030Lethtendris's Web\0312,1,133,2,257,1,7877\0302,136,297,2,257,4,7877\0302,302,314,2,257,1,7877\0302,317,346,2,257,1,7877\0302,349,411,2,257,1,7877\0302,414,496,2,259,1,7877\0303,1,88,2,384,1,7877\0301,1,22,4,272,1,7877\0301,25,38,4,272,1,7877\0301,41,148,4,272,1,7877\0301,151,254,4,272,4,7877\0301,257,299,4,272,1,7877\0301,304,317,4,272,1,7877\0301,320,453,4,286,3,7877\0304,1,24,3,256,2,7877\0304,27,77,3,256,1,7877\03114327,2,1,Lethtendris\0307877,2,7,Latronicus Moonspear\03014327,4,10,Lethtendris\0312,2557,0,0,\0302,0,0,5,Warpwood Quarter of Dire Maul\0302,0,0,7,Latronicus Moonspear\0302,0,0,7,Feathermoon Stronghold\0302,0,0,7,Feralas\031\031ITEM,18426,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7489]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have done well, $N. This web holds within it vast stores of the magic of Dire Maul, and I fear what damage may be unleashed if those energies were harnessed by one so irresponsible as Lethtendris. I am saddened by her death, but I know that she could never part with her web while alive.$B$BThank you, $N. I will send the web to students of magic more responsible than Lethtendris. They will be the new wardens of its power.\030The blood elf Lethtendris has overstepped her bounds.  So eager was she to gather magical power that she defied her brethren and created a device of insidious design, a web meant to siphon the tainted magical energies of Dire Maul.  Even now she gathers those energies and plans to release them against her enemies.$B$BLethtendris must be stopped.  Find her within the Warpwood Quarter of Dire Maul, defeat her and bring her web to me so that it might be returned to more clear-headed blood elves for study.\030Bring Lethtendris's Web to Talo Thornhoof at Camp Mojache in Feralas.\030$N, do you have Lethtendris's Web?\030Lethtendris's Web\0312,1,53,2,257,1,7776\0302,56,231,2,257,1,7776\0302,234,315,2,261,1,7776\0302,320,347,2,257,1,7776\0302,350,507,2,259,4,7776\0303,1,69,2,384,1,7776\0301,1,23,4,272,1,7776\0301,25,200,4,272,4,7776\0301,202,291,4,272,4,7776\0301,296,309,4,272,1,7776\0301,311,385,4,272,3,7776\0301,387,428,4,272,3,7776\0304,1,34,3,256,2,7776\03114327,2,1,Lethtendris\03014327,2,4,Lethtendris\0307776,2,6,Talo Thornhoof\03014327,4,8,Lethtendris\03014327,4,11,Lethtendris\0312,2557,0,0,\0302,0,0,5,Warpwood Quarter of Dire Maul\0302,0,0,6,Talo Thornhoof\0302,0,0,6,Camp Mojache\0302,0,0,6,Feralas\031\031ITEM,18426,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[749]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031All sides of the crate are stamped with the sign of the Venture Co. Mining Division. Notes printed carefully on the side of the carton indicate that the contents are due for processing at one of their central plants.\030A few days ago, we found a Venture Co. caravan traveling under guard on the northern shore of Stonebull Lake. We'd lost two of our number in an earlier battle, so we were quick to attack and lay waste to the caravan.$B$BWe left their supply crates, thinking that our torches would destroy anything of value, but given that Venture Co. salvagers have been spotted near the burned wagons, maybe we were wrong.$B$BPerhaps you could go to the caravan and examine the contents of the crates.\030Morin Cloudstalker wants you to examine the contents of a supply crate at the Ravaged Caravan.\030\030The Ravaged Caravan\0312,1,38,2,257,1,2988\0302,40,109,2,257,1,2988\0302,111,216,2,261,1,2988\0302,221,334,2,261,4,2988\0302,336,407,2,257,4,2988\0302,412,486,2,257,4,2988\0303,1,94,2,386,1,2988\0301,1,67,4,272,1,0\0301,69,84,4,272,1,0\0301,86,216,4,272,1,0\0312988,2,7,Morin Cloudstalker\0312,215,1412,0,\0302,0,0,7,Ravag