consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Excellent work, $R. Should you find any more tomes, do not hesitate to return them to us.$B$BAs time passes, we tend to change around and even add new rewards for the return of missing tomes.\030The tome carries the mark of the Athenaeum.\030Return the book to its rightful owners.\030You have recovered a tome!\030The Emerald Dream...\0312,1,43,2,257,1,0\0303,1,39,2,384,1,0\0301,1,19,4,272,1,14381\0301,21,89,4,272,1,14381\0301,94,191,4,276,1,14381\0304,1,26,3,256,1,14381\031795,2,1,Mark\0312,2557,0,0,\031\031ITEM,18364,STARTER,?,10,",[7507]="PARTIAL\031loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You could have gotten quite a lot of gold for this book on the black market, $N. Especially since the protective seal has been broken, leaving the secrets of dragon slaying viewable to any with the requisite intellect to consume the knowledge held within the sacred pages.$B$BPerhaps a grand reward is in order... Well, a reward that will require enormous effort to obtain.$B$B<Lydros grins.>\030You have uncovered something of great importance. This book is unlike any that you have seen.$B$BIt would appear as if someone or something has managed to shatter the seal of Athenaeum. The text within is garbled and barely legible.\030Return Foror's Compendium of Dragon Slaying to the Athenaeum.\030Ah, one of our greatest compilations. This one has been missing for ages.\030Foror's Compendium\0312,1,49,2,257,1,0\0302,51,93,2,257,1,0\0302,98,185,2,257,4,0\0302,187,232,2,257,1,0\0303,1,61,2,384,1,0\0301,1,80,4,272,4,14368\0301,82,272,4,304,1,14368\0301,277,313,4,272,4,14368\0301,315,373,4,272,3,14368\0301,378,392,4,272,1,14368\0304,1,37,3,256,1,14368\0304,39,73,3,260,1,14368\031\0312,2557,0,0,\0302,0,0,5,Athenaeum\0317508,23,7508,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,18401,STARTER,?,10,",[7508]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031If you manage to enter the lair of the dragon, heat the blade under her fiery breath, and ultimately temper it in her blood, I shall bind the blade for your use.\030If you wish to take on this task, present Lydros with the dull blade.\030Give the Dull and Flat Elven Blade to Lorekeeper Lydros.\030Excellent, let us begin...\030The Forging of Quel'Serrar\0312,1,69,2,259,4,0\0303,1,56,2,384,1,0\0301,1,161,4,272,4,14368\0304,1,26,3,256,1,14368\03114368,2,2,Lorekeeper Lydros\0312,2557,0,0,\0302,0,0,2,Lorekeeper Lydros\0317507,19,7507,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0307509,23,7509,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,18513,STARTER,?,10,",[7509]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Lydros murmurs something unintelligible.>$B$BAs promised, $C, the blade of Quel'Serrar.\030Take the unfired ancient blade to the lair of Onyxia and engage her in battle.$B$BSome trickery must be utilized for the heating of the blade. While in combat, she will surely try to incinerate you with her fiery breath. You must plant the unfired ancient blade nearby and hope that the fiery breath heats the blade. If you live beyond this, pick up the now heated ancient blade and finish off the dragon.$B$BPlunge the heated ancient blade into her smoldering corpse to fashion the treated ancient blade.\030You must get Onyxia to breathe fire on the Unfired Ancient Blade. Once this is done, pick up the now Heated Ancient Blade. Be warned, a Heated Ancient Blade will not remain heated forever - time is of the essence.$B$BThe last step before returning to me is to slay the beast and drive the Heated Ancient Blade into her corpse.$B$BDo this and Quel'Serrar will be yours.\030Perhaps one day, another will wield the prismatic blade.\030The Forging of Quel'Serrar\0312,1,78,2,325,1,14368\0302,83,142,2,257,1,14368\0302,144,220,2,257,3,14368\0302,222,316,2,323,3,14368\0302,318,405,2,321,4,14368\0302,410,505,2,321,1,14368\0303,1,65,2,448,1,14368\0303,67,122,2,448,1,14368\0303,124,213,2,448,3,14368\0303,218,326,2,448,1,14368\0303,331,368,2,384,3,14368\0301,1,42,4,272,1,14368\0301,47,88,4,272,1,14368\0304,1,56,3,256,4,14368\03110184,2,1,Onyxia\03010184,2,7,Onyxia\03010430,2,10,The Beast\0312,2159,0,0,\0317508,19,7508,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,18492,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[751]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It does indeed appear that the Venture Co. is attempting to rob us of our natural resources. It is good to know this for true, and now it seems, we must do something about it.\030Prying open the lid reveals a tightly packed assortment of ore and minerals, more evidence of the Venture Co.'s mining operation in Mulgore. On the top of the ore and minerals you remove a tightly bound sheaf of papers.$B$BUp in the foothills to the east, you can barely hear the sounds of work, and see smoke rising from a large fire.\030Return the Venture Co. Documents to Morin Cloudstalker near Bloodhoof Village.\030Hail, $N. Have you learned anything new about the Venture Co.'s plans and operations in our homeland?$B$BIf they plan to exploit our lands as they have others, the Outrunners will be quick to put an end to it.\030The Ravaged Caravan\0312,1,140,2,257,1,0\0302,142,219,2,261,1,0\0302,224,335,2,257,1,0\0303,1,22,2,384,1,0\0303,24,78,2,384,1,0\0301,1,42,4,272,1,2988\0301,44,92,4,272,1,2988\0301,94,175,4,272,4,2988\0304,1,9,3,256,1,2988\0304,11,101,3,256,2,2988\0304,106,209,3,256,4,2988\0312988,2,5,Morin Cloudstalker\0312,215,1412,0,\0302,0,0,1,Mulgore\0302,0,0,5,Morin Cloudstalker\0302,0,0,5,Bloodhoof Village\031749,19,749,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,2908,GIVER,?,9,Sealed Supply Crate",[752]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You traveled all this way just to help an old woman? My my, aren't you a keeper?\030All members of the tribe share in the harmony of life. We live together and work together.$B$BOur commitment to one another carries with it a high degree of responsibility. I ask of you now a humble task.$B$BMy mother set out this morning to fetch water from the well to the southeast of Narache. It has been quite some time now. Perhaps you could check on her for me while I attend to tribal matters here?\030Chief Hawkwind wants you to search for his mother near the water well to the southeast of Camp Narache.\030\030A Humble Task\0312,1,54,2,257,1,2981\0302,56,90,2,257,1,2981\0302,95,172,2,257,1,2981\0302,174,204,2,259,1,2981\0302,209,296,2,257,1,2981\0302,298,329,2,257,1,2981\0302,331,406,2,257,4,2981\0303,1,103,2,386,1,2981\0301,1,52,4,272,2,2991\0301,54,80,4,272,2,2991\0312981,2,8,Chief Hawkwind\0312,220,1412,0,\031753,23,753,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[753]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You carried this pitcher back at the Greatmother's bidding, I see.$B$BYour willingness to help others and provide for the tauren of Camp Narache leads me to believe you would make the tribe proud in Thunder Bluff someday.\030I have traveled many paths through life and these old legs lack the vigor they once had. I can still perform my duties to the tribe. Sometimes it just takes an old woman a little longer to do the task.$B$BBut you look like an eager $c. Let's put some of that youthful vitality to the test. Take a water pitcher from the well and bring it to my son, the Chief, in Camp Narache.$B$BRemember that even the most humble task can gain the recognition of elders.\030Take a Water Pitcher from the water well.$B$BReturn the pitcher to Chief Hawkwind in Camp Narache which is northwest from the water well.\030You look as though you have returned from the plains. Do you have any word from Greatmother Hawkwind?\030A Humble Task\0312,1,88,2,257,1,2991\0302,90,132,2,257,1,2991\0302,134,201,2,257,1,2991\0302,206,235,2,257,1,2991\0302,237,289,2,257,1,2991\0302,291,376,2,257,1,2991\0302,381,455,2,257,1,2991\0303,1,41,2,384,1,2991\0303,46,137,2,384,1,2991\0301,1,66,4,272,1,2981\0301,71,221,4,272,4,2981\0304,1,53,3,256,1,2981\0304,55,101,3,256,2,2981\0312981,2,9,Chief Hawkwind\0302991,3,13,Greatmother Hawkwind\0312,220,1412,0,\0302,0,0,6,Camp Narache\0302,0,0,9,Chief Hawkwind\0302,0,0,9,Camp Narache\0304,0,0,10,Greatmother's\0304,0,0,11,Thunder Bluff\0303,0,0,13,Greatmother Hawkwind\031752,19,752,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030755,23,755,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4755,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[754]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031News of your deed reached me moments ago -- already the beasts near the well drink from it eagerly.$B$BYou have done a great thing for the land, $N. And you have done a great thing for the Tauren people.\030I have crafted the totem to cleanse the Winterhoof Water Well.  Now, you must take it to the well and perform a cleansing ritual.  You will find it to the southeast, guarded by foul goblins!$B$BThis will not be an easy task, but you must do it if we are ever to use its waters again.$B$BFortune to you, $N.\030Use the Winterhoof Cleansing Totem at the Winterhoof Water Well, then return to Mull Thunderhorn.\030Cleanse the Winterhoof Water Well\030Do not delay, $N.  The Winterhoof Well's taint must be removed!\030Winterhoof Cleansing\0312,1,62,2,257,1,2948\0302,65,129,2,257,1,2948\0302,132,190,2,257,3,2948\0302,195,283,2,257,4,2948\0302,288,306,2,257,1,2948\0303,1,97,2,384,1,2948\0301,1,99,4,272,1,2948\0301,104,148,4,272,1,2948\0301,150,203,4,272,1,2948\0305,1,17,3,256,1,2948\0305,20,63,3,256,1,2948\0304,1,33,3,384,1,2948\0312948,2,6,Mull Thunderhorn\0312,215,1412,0,\0302,0,0,6,Winterhoof Water Well\0302,0,0,6,Mull Thunderhorn\031748,19,748,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030756,23,756,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[7541]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It will take time for our scholars to study the pendant you brought us.  But for your service to the Horde I would like to offer you a small token.$B$BThank you, $N.  Your acts bring honor to you, and to us.\030\030\030\030Service to the Horde\0311,1,71,4,272,3,4047\0301,74,147,4,274,4,4047\0301,152,165,4,272,1,4047\0301,168,207,4,272,1,4047\031\0312,15,1445,0,\0304,0,0,2,Horde\0311262,19,1262,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[755]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Chief Hawkwind sent you? Embarking on the Rites of the Earthmother is no small task...\030Your willingness to perform a humble task for the tauren of Narache and your eagerness to learn are noble traits, $n. I believe one day you will be heralded in Thunder Bluff as a $c of greatness.$B$BBefore that you must embark on the Rites of the Earthmother, of which there are three.$B$BThe first test is the Rite of Strength. Travel to Seer Graytongue and tell him Chief Hawkwind has sent you.$B$BYou will find the seer's abode directly to the south of Camp Narache, tucked away in the hills.\030Travel to Seer Graytongue who lives in the hills directly south of Camp Narache.\030\030Rites of the Earthmother\0312,1,117,2,257,1,2981\0302,119,195,2,257,4,2981\0302,200,285,2,257,1,2981\0302,290,328,2,257,1,2981\0302,330,396,2,257,1,2981\0302,401,495,2,257,3,2981\0303,1,80,2,384,1,2981\0301,1,24,4,272,2,2982\0301,26,86,4,272,1,2982\0312982,2,5,Seer Graytongue\0302981,2,5,Chief Hawkwind\0302982,2,7,Seer Graytongue\0302981,4,8,Chief Hawkwind\0312,220,1412,0,\0302,0,0,2,Thunder Bluff\0302,0,0,5,Seer Graytongue\0302,0,0,6,Camp Narache\0302,0,0,7,Seer Graytongue\0302,0,0,7,Camp Narache\031753,19,753,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030757,23,757,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[756]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, $N. The purity with which these beasts hunt is vital in the creation of the next cleansing totem.$B$BThe goblins will never learn the difference between contending with the land, and living in harmony with it.\030To create the Thunderhorn Cleansing Totem, you must gather the claws of the predators of the Mulgore plains.  Hunt prairie stalkers for their stalker claws and flatland cougars for their cougar claws, then return to me.$B$BYou will find the prairie stalkers and flatland cougars to the east and west.\030Bring 6 Stalker Claws and 6 Cougar Claws to Mull Thunderhorn.\030$N, do you have the claws I sent you to gather? The Thunderhorn Water Well grows more tainted with each passing hour!\030Thunderhorn Totem\0312,1,108,2,257,1,2948\0302,111,219,2,257,1,2948\0302,224,300,2,257,3,2948\0303,1,61,2,384,1,2948\0301,1,14,4,272,1,2948\0301,16,108,4,272,1,2948\0301,113,220,4,272,3,2948\0304,1,47,3,256,2,2948\0304,49,117,3,256,1,2948\0312948,2,4,Mull Thunderhorn\0312,215,1412,0,\0302,0,0,4,Mull Thunderhorn\031754,19,754,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030758,23,758,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4801,OBJECTIVE,6,15,\030ITEM,4802,OBJECTIVE,6,15,",[7562]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Greetings, $N, and welcome.  Are you here to study near the Altar of Storms as I am, perhaps to harness its energy for some hidden purpose...$B$BOr... are you here to speak with me?  Yes, I believe you are.$B$BYou want to master a dreadsteed?  Such is no easy task.  It will cost you no small amounts of blood, sweat... and of course gold.  But a dreadsteed of Xoroth is a prize well worth winning so if interested, listen on...\030$N, your delvings into the dark arts are deep.  Your mastery over otherworldly denizens has grown so strong... perhaps you are ready to bind to you one of the infamous dreadsteeds.$B$BThe ritual to summon the beast from its home requires great power and resources, but if you desire to dominate that epic mount, then speak with Mor'zul Bloodbringer.  He is camped near the Altar of Storms in the Burning Steppes.$B$BGo, $N.  This quest will be perilous, but a Warlock of your stature does not shy from danger!\030Speak with Mor'zul Bloodbringer in the Burning Steppes.\030\030Mor'zul Bloodbringer\0312,1,46,2,257,1,0\0302,49,110,2,257,1,0\0302,112,180,2,257,4,0\0302,185,349,2,259,4,0\0302,352,412,2,257,1,0\0302,426,509,2,261,3,0\0303,1,55,2,384,1,0\0301,1,27,4,272,1,14436\0301,30,141,4,272,4,14436\0301,152,181,4,272,2,14436\0301,184,206,4,272,4,14436\0301,211,242,4,274,2,14436\0301,245,265,4,272,1,14436\0301,268,319,4,272,3,14436\0301,321,339,4,272,1,14436\0301,342,428,4,272,4,14436\03110430,2,4,The Beast\03014436,2,4,Mor'zul Bloodbringer\03014436,2,7,Mor'zul Bloodbringer\0312,0,0,5,Altar of Storms\0302,0,0,5,Burning Steppes\0302,0,0,7,Burning Steppes\0304,0,0,9,Altar of Storms\0317563,23,7563,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[7563]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, very good. I will have this blood distilled into an ink and use it for the parchment I promised you. And perhaps I will save just a little for myself, as I hear its taste is quite euphoric...\030The dreadsteeds dwell on another world, on the fiery Plains of Xoroth, and to bind one of those famed beasts you must invoke powerful glyphs.  I can scribe the glyphs on a parchment for you, but first I will need a special ink.$B$BIn distant Winterspring there dwells a race of owl beasts.  Once pure creatures, they were turned mad by the demonic emanations of the Darkwhisper Gorge and now roam the snows in a frenzy.$B$BTheir blood is what I need to ink your parchment.  Bring it to me.\030Bring 30 bottles of Raging Beast's Blood to Mor'zul Bloodbringer in the Burning Steppes.\030Have you seen the raging owl beasts, $N? The magic of those creatures is strong, and it concentrates in the blood that flows through their torturted forms.\030Rage of Blood\0312,1,141,2,257,1,14436\0302,144,227,2,259,3,14436\0302,232,289,2,257,1,14436\0302,292,419,2,257,1,14436\0302,424,472,2,259,1,14436\0302,475,489,2,257,1,14436\0303,1,88,2,384,1,14436\0301,1,14,4,272,1,14436\0301,16,104,4,272,3,14436\0301,106,195,4,280,4,14436\0304,1,40,3,256,2,14436\0304,42,155,3,256,1,14436\03114436,2,7,Mor'zul Bloodbringer\0312,0,0,7,Mor'zul Bloodbringer\0302,0,0,7,Burning Steppes\0317562,19,7562,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0307564,23,7564,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,18590,OBJECTIVE,30,15,",[7564]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh, it's blood. It must be from master Mor'zul then. He is so enamored with the stuff, and loves to see it spilled. I, however, prefer it coursing through the veins of a small rodent. It stays warm that way... until you want it.$B$BThis is powerful blood. Mor'zul must be making another parchment to summon a dreadsteed! How exciting!$B$BIf that's true, and you're going to perform the ritual, then... you're going to need a lot more than blood, my friend.\030My servant, Gorzeeki, is an alchemist of some skill.  He can prepare the ink I will need for your parchment.  I gathered together the blood you acquired; take it to Gorzeeki so that he can begin his work.\030Bring the Case of Blood to Gorzeeki Wildeyes in the Burning Steppes.\030You have something for me?  It's not a big, juicy spider, is it?  Or maybe a roach?  I hope it's still alive... I so love chewing on them when they're still alive...\030Wildeyes\0312,1,52,2,257,1,14436\0302,55,108,2,259,3,14436\0302,111,204,2,259,1,14436\0303,1,68,2,384,1,14436\0301,1,15,4,272,1,14437\0301,17,52,4,272,1,14437\0301,54,115,4,