rove that you are a $C of merit. It is good to have you at Bloodhoof Village.\030The swoop is a cunning bird, and difficult to find and hunt.  A collection of Swoop Quills is a badge of cleverness and determination for a hunter.$B$BIf you are willing to take up this task, then enter the plains and hunt the swoop.$B$BBring me their quills, and bring honor to your clan.$B$BThe swoops may be found anywhere in Mulgore, but your eyes must be sharp to spot them, and your hooves must be quick to catch them.\030Bring 8 Trophy Swoop Quills to Harken Windtotem in Bloodhoof Village.\030Have you found the swoops, $N.  Do you have their quills?\030Swoop Hunting\0312,1,60,2,257,1,2947\0302,63,147,2,257,1,2947\0302,152,233,2,257,4,2947\0302,238,289,2,257,1,2947\0302,294,424,2,257,1,2947\0303,1,69,2,384,1,2947\0301,1,60,4,272,1,2947\0301,62,113,4,272,1,2947\0301,115,158,4,272,1,2947\0304,1,30,3,256,1,2947\0304,33,57,3,256,2,2947\0312970,2,1,Swoop\0302970,2,2,Swoop\0302970,2,3,Swoop\0304950,2,5,Spot\0302970,2,6,Swoop\0302947,2,6,Harken Windtotem\0312,215,1412,0,\0302,0,0,5,Mulgore\0302,0,0,6,Harken Windtotem\0302,0,0,6,Bloodhoof Village\0304,0,0,9,Bloodhoof Village\031\031ITEM,4769,OBJECTIVE,8,15,",[76156]="MINIMAL\031characters,conclusion,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030\030Sneak into the Venture Company mine southeast of Thunder Bluff and collect 5 Seaforium Mining Charges from carts of blasting supplies, then return them to Boarton Shadetotem in Thunder Bluff.\030\030Stalk With The Earthmother\0313,1,191,2,384,1,0\031\0312,0,0,1,Boarton Shadetotem\0302,0,0,1,Thunder Bluff\031\031",[76160]="MINIMAL\031conclusion,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030\030Gather 8 Windfury Cones north of Thunder Bluff, use them with the Mortar and Pestle, then return to Boarton Shadetotem in Thunder Bluff with the result.\030\030Stalk With The Earthmother\0313,1,152,2,384,1,0\03116121,2,1,Mortar\0312,0,0,1,Thunder Bluff\0302,0,0,1,Boarton Shadetotem\0302,0,0,1,Thunder Bluff\031\031",[762]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031$N, your dedication to Ironforge and to the dwarven people cannot be refuted. I thank you for your help in this matter.$B$BI shall send word to Historian Karnik informing him that you have succeeded, and I shall also have aid sent to the Badlands as soon as possible to help recover the excavation site. Thank you again.$B$BBefore you go, there is one more thing I would ask of you in the name of King Bronzebeard.\030Ambassador Infernus was sent to Angor Fortress by Ragnaros himself to mind the Shadowforge seeking lost artifacts in Uldaman.$B$BIt has already meant tremendous casualties for our people, but it has obviously grown worse. I hesitate to guess how many artifacts they would be able to find and use against Ironforge.$B$BOur goal is simple, $c. Return to the Badlands and destroy Ambassador Infernus. Once the threat is eliminated, return to Advisor Belgrum with proof of your victory.$B$BIt is in your hands now.\030Kill Ambassador Infernus in Angor Fortress and bring proof of his death to Advisor Belgrum in Ironforge.\030Time is of the essence, $N. Ragnaros will not wait for us to prepare.\030An Ambassador of Evil\0312,1,125,2,261,1,2916\0302,130,221,2,257,1,2916\0302,223,314,2,257,4,2916\0302,319,341,2,259,1,2916\0302,343,397,2,261,1,2916\0302,399,482,2,261,1,2916\0302,487,510,2,257,1,2916\0303,1,104,2,384,1,2916\0301,1,77,4,272,1,2918\0301,79,119,4,272,1,2918\0301,124,303,4,272,3,2918\0301,305,320,4,272,1,2918\0301,325,414,4,272,4,2918\0304,1,27,3,256,1,2918\0304,29,69,3,256,3,2918\0312745,2,1,Ambassador Infernus\03011502,2,1,Ragnaros\0302745,2,5,Ambassador Infernus\0302918,2,6,Advisor Belgrum\0302745,2,8,Ambassador Infernus\0302918,2,8,Advisor Belgrum\0302916,4,11,Historian Karnik\03011502,3,15,Ragnaros\0312,3,1418,0,\0302,0,0,1,Angor Fortress\0302,0,0,1,Uldaman\0302,0,0,5,Badlands\0302,0,0,6,Advisor Belgrum\0302,0,0,8,Angor Fortress\0302,0,0,8,Advisor Belgrum\0302,0,0,8,Ironforge\0304,0,0,9,Ironforge\0304,0,0,11,Historian Karnik\0304,0,0,11,Badlands\031726,19,726,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301139,23,1139,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4621,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7621]="PARTIAL\031consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031$C, you are about to undergo a rigorous series of events which shall test all of your abilities.$B$BI suggest that you listen to the story that I have to tell.$B$BBe warned, you must complete this task alone. It is recommended that your allies remain at a distance. Interference by outside agents will result in a most severe punishment.$B$BDestiny has led you and you alone here. Battle with honor. Harness the Light.\030\030\030\030A Warning\0311,1,96,4,272,3,14494\0301,101,159,4,272,1,14494\0301,164,208,4,272,1,14494\0301,210,265,4,272,1,14494\0301,267,337,4,272,3,14494\0301,342,380,4,272,1,14494\0301,382,399,4,276,1,14494\0301,401,418,4,272,1,14494\031\031\031\031",[7622]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Your tenacity and courage are astounding, $gpriest:priestess;. You have earned the right to hold the Splinter of Nordrassil. Only one task remains: The Eye of Shadow must be recovered. Scour the world.\030You must do what I could not: Save the peasants that were cut down while fleeing from Stratholme.$B$BThey will walk towards the light, you must ensure their survival. Should too many fall, our cursed existence shall continue - you will have failed.$B$BEvery ability, prayer, and spell that you have learned will be tested. May the Light protect you, $N.\030Save 50 Peasants before 15 are slain. Speak with Eris Havenfire should you accomplish this task.$B$BYou may view the Death Post to view how many Peasants have been slain.\030Your tenacity and courage are astounding, $G priest:priestess;. You have earned the right to hold the Splinter of Nordrassil. Only one task remains: The Eye of Shadow must be recovered. Scour the world.\030\030The Balance of Light and Shadow\0312,1,97,2,265,4,14494\0302,102,166,2,265,3,14494\0302,168,248,2,261,3,14494\0302,253,322,2,257,3,14494\0302,324,353,2,269,1,14494\0303,1,37,2,396,1,14494\0303,39,96,2,384,1,14494\0303,101,170,2,388,1,14494\0301,1,62,4,272,1,14494\0301,64,124,4,272,1,14494\0301,126,184,4,272,1,14494\0301,186,201,4,272,1,14494\0304,1,63,3,384,1,14494\0304,65,125,3,384,1,14494\0304,127,185,3,384,1,14494\0304,187,202,3,384,1,14494\03114494,2,7,Eris Havenfire\030112,4,9,Priestess\0304244,4,11,Shadow\030111,3,13,Priest\030112,3,13,Priestess\0304244,3,15,Shadow\0312,0,0,1,Stratholme\031\031",[7623]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031My patience spans the millenia, warlock.  But do not think that allows you more than an instant of my time...\030Mor'zul says that you want to open a portal to Xoroth.  To do that, you'll need Xorothian stardust.  That's not easy to find on Azeroth!$B$BThere is one being who might have some: Lord Banehollow in Jaedenar, the seat of the Shadow Council!  Speak with him and he might part with the stardust.$B$BBut if you're going to Jaedenar, then you'll need to cloak yourself in the Shadow Council's own flavor of evil.  That will require some of my shadowy potions, and that will cost you...\030Purchase Shadowy Potions from Gorzeeki in the Burning Steppes.$B$BUse the potions to travel through Jaedenar, and speak with Lord Banehollow.\030\030Lord Banehollow\0312,1,54,2,259,1,14437\0302,57,99,2,259,1,14437\0302,102,136,2,257,1,14437\0302,141,240,2,257,4,14437\0302,243,293,2,257,4,14437\0302,298,408,2,259,4,14437\0302,411,481,2,257,3,14437\0303,1,62,2,384,1,14437\0303,67,141,2,384,1,14437\0301,1,40,4,272,1,9516\0301,43,109,4,272,1,9516\0319516,2,4,Lord Banehollow\0304244,2,4,Shadow\0304244,2,6,Shadow\0309516,2,9,Lord Banehollow\0312,0,0,1,Xoroth\0302,0,0,4,Jaedenar\0302,0,0,6,Jaedenar\0302,0,0,6,Shadow Council's\0302,0,0,8,Gorzeeki\0302,0,0,8,Burning Steppes\0317624,23,7624,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[7624]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, how splendid!  After rotting a week, this heart will prove a succulent treat!  Perhaps I will send for Ulathek's head and place it before me as I eat...$B$BYou have done me a service, warlock, and so my patience for you has grown.  Marginally.\030You wish to enter my good graces?  Then kill for me.$B$BMy servant, Ulathek, is pathetic how he grovels before me, all the while plotting with Lord Hel'nurath on Xoroth.  Hel'nurath plans to usurp my power here, and Ulathek is his spy...$B$BProve that you serve me and not my rivals.  Confront Ulathek in his quarters, in the Shadow Hold to the west.  Tell him that I know his secret and watch as fear grips him.  Then, bring me the traitor's heart!\030Confront Ulathek, then bring The Traitor's Heart to Lord Banehollow in Jaedenar.\030I can already taste the heart of Ulathek on my lips. So sweet is the flesh of a traitor...\030Ulathek the Traitor\0312,1,33,2,259,2,9516\0302,36,52,2,257,1,9516\0302,57,169,2,257,1,9516\0302,172,237,2,257,1,9516\0302,242,283,2,257,1,9516\0302,286,350,2,257,1,9516\0302,353,412,2,257,1,9516\0302,415,449,2,257,1,9516\0303,1,80,2,384,1,9516\0301,1,17,4,272,1,9516\0301,20,81,4,272,3,9516\0301,84,156,4,272,4,9516\0301,161,234,4,272,1,9516\0301,237,247,4,272,1,9516\0304,1,52,3,256,1,9516\0304,54,90,3,256,1,9516\03114523,2,3,Ulathek\03014506,2,3,Lord Hel'nurath\03014523,2,4,Ulathek\03014523,2,6,Ulathek\0304244,2,6,Shadow\03014523,2,9,Ulathek\0309516,2,9,Lord Banehollow\03014523,3,15,Ulathek\0312,0,0,6,Shadow Hold\0302,0,0,9,Lord Banehollow\0302,0,0,9,Jaedenar\0317623,19,7623,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0307625,23,7625,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,18719,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[76240]="MINIMAL\031characters,conclusion,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030\030Buy or catch a Raw Brilliant Smallfish, then use the Knife Set to fillet it in front of Boarton Shadetotem in Thunder Bluff.\030\030Stalk With The Earthmother\0313,1,124,2,384,1,0\031\0312,0,0,1,Thunder Bluff\031\031",[7625]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031There it is! I can hardly believe you got it! You must have struck a big deal with that Dreadlord or else paid a large sum, or both!$B$BMor'zul will have his ink very soon and then he can finally make the glyph parchment, so you can open a portal to Xoroth and pull through it one of the famed dreadsteeds!\030So you come to me seeking Xorothian stardust?  You wish to open a portal to Xoroth, the domain of Hel'nurath my rival?  Perhaps you plan to steal from him one of his precious dreadsteeds?$B$BVery well.  My servant Ur'dan has a supply of Xorothian stardust.  You may obtain it from him... if you can pay the price.\030Purchase Xorothian Stardust from Ur'dan.  Bring it to Gorzeeki Wildeyes in the Burning Steppes.\030Have you been to Jaedenar, $N? Did you get the stardust from Lord Banehollow?\030Xorothian Stardust\0312,1,45,2,257,2,9516\0302,48,118,2,259,2,9516\0302,121,187,2,261,4,9516\0302,192,201,2,257,1,9516\0302,204,256,2,257,1,9516\0302,259,287,2,257,1,9516\0302,289,313,2,257,4,9516\0303,1,40,2,384,1,9516\0303,43,95,2,384,1,9516\0301,1,12,4,272,1,14437\0301,14,45,4,272,4,14437\0301,47,132,4,272,1,14437\0301,137,306,4,272,3,14437\0304,1,30,3,256,2,14437\0304,32,77,3,256,2,14437\03114528,2,3,Precious\03014522,2,5,Ur'dan\03014522,2,8,Ur'dan\03014437,2,9,Gorzeeki Wildeyes\0308716,4,12,Dreadlord\0309516,3,15,Lord Banehollow\0312,0,0,2,Xoroth\0302,0,0,8,Ur'dan\0302,0,0,9,Gorzeeki Wildeyes\0302,0,0,9,Burning Steppes\0304,0,0,13,Xoroth\0303,0,0,14,Jaedenar\0303,0,0,15,Lord Banehollow\0317624,19,7624,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,18687,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7626]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very good! I hope these elixirs weren't too hard to get. Sometimes alchemists can be so miserly with their creations...$B$BI'll make the bell and keep it until you're ready for your ritual.\030A Bell of Dethmoora, named after the late warlock Dethmoora Darkeyes, is one of the three tools needed to create a Circle of Greater Summoning.  When properly atuned with the Wheel and the Candle, these items conduct vast stores of arcane power.$B$BMy servant Gorzeeki can construct such a bell, but to do so he will need a large supply of elixirs of shadow power.  Procure the elixirs from an alchemist and bring them to Gorzeeki.\030Bring 10 Elixirs of Shadow Power to Gorzeeki Wildeyes in the Burning Steppes.\030You have those elixirs, $N? Mor'zul told me you need a Bell of Dethmoora, and making one of those takes a lot of shadow power!\030Bell of Dethmoora\0312,1,143,2,257,1,14436\0302,146,245,2,257,1,14436\0302,250,364,2,259,3,14436\0302,367,431,2,257,1,14436\0303,1,77,2,384,1,14436\0301,1,10,4,272,1,14437\0301,12,56,4,274,3,14437\0301,58,119,4,272,1,14437\0301,124,189,4,272,1,14437\0304,1,27,3,256,2,14437\0304,29,126,3,258,1,14437\0314244,2,3,Shadow\0304244,2,5,Shadow\03014437,2,5,Gorzeeki Wildeyes\0304244,3,11,Shadow\0312,0,0,4,Gorzeeki\0302,0,0,5,Gorzeeki Wildeyes\0302,0,0,5,Burning Steppes\0317564,19,7564,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,9264,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[7627]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031There they are! I hear that dark iron ore is only found in the depths of Blackrock, and I'm sure these shards weren't easy to find either. I am often awed at the dedication you warlocks have. If you instead bent all that energy into the art of bug catching, oh... such a feast you would enjoy!$B$BSorry, a small digression. I'll create the wheel and keep it for you until you're ready for your ritual.\030A Wheel of the Black March contains and directs the violent energies required for the Circle of Greater Summoning.  For Gozeeki to construct a wheel, he will need both large brilliant shards from an enchanter, and dark iron ore from a master miner.$B$BAcquire these and bring them to my servant.\030Bring 6 Large Brilliant Shards and 25 Dark Iron Ore to Gorzeeki in the Burning Steppes.\030The Wheel of the Black March isn't easy to make, and takes a lot of materials. Have you gathered them yet?\030Wheel of the Black March\0312,1,114,2,257,1,14436\0302,117,248,2,259,3,14436\0302,253,295,2,257,1,14436\0303,1,87,2,384,1,14436\0301,1,15,4,272,1,14437\0301,17,138,4,272,1,14437\0301,140,191,4,272,1,14437\0301,193,263,4,272,4,14437\0301,265,293,4,272,4,14437\0301,298,323,4,272,1,14437\0301,325,401,4,272,1,14437\0304,1,78,3,256,1,14437\0304,80,106,3,256,2,14437\031\0312,0,0,4,Gorzeeki\0302,0,0,4,Burning Steppes\0317564,19,7564,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,14344,OBJECTIVE,6,15,\030ITEM,11370,OBJECTIVE,25,15,",[7628]="PARTIAL\031conflict,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, very good. I'll need these to contain the fires of the candle. Now that I have the scales, I'll make the candle and hold onto it until you're ready to begin your ritual for the Circle of Greater Summoning.\030A Doomsday Candle stores fire and directs it at those who would disrupt your ritual.  When creating your Circle of Greater Summoning, if your candle is lit then any wayward demons will be burned by its flames!$B$BContaining that fire is not easy, and requires the essence within the scales of a black dragon.  Acquire those scales from a skinner and bring them to Gorzeeki Wildeyes.\030Bring 35 Black Dragonscales to Gorzeeki Wildeyes in the Burning Steppes.\030Did you bring the dragonscales, $N? I don't want to start on the candle until I have them... or I might blow up the whole camp!\030Doomsday Candle\0312,1,84,2,257,4,14436\0302,87,209,2,257,4,14436\0302,214,308,2,257,1,14436\0302,311,382,2,257,1,14436\0303,1,72,2,384,1,14436\0301,1,14,4,272,1,14437\0301,16,66,4,274,1,14437\0301,68,209,4,304,1,14437\0304,1,35,3,256,2,14437\0304,37,92,3,256,1,14437\0304,94,127,3,256,4,14437\03114437,2,4,Gorzeeki Wildeyes\03014437,2,5,Gorzeeki Wildeyes\0312,0,0,4,Gorzeeki Wildeyes\0302,0,0,5,Gorzeeki Wildeyes\0302,0,0,5,Burning Steppes\0317564,19,7564,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,15416,OBJECTIVE,35,15,",[7629]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, good. J'eevee created the parchment. How was the Scholomance? Charming, don't you think? And the bugs there... I hear they're delicious!$B$BWell done, $N, and thank you for returning my jar. I've had it for a long time... and it's not for sale!\030There is one more process required for Mor'zul's parchment; I need paper infused with Xorothian stardust.  And... I'm afraid I can't do that here.  I don't have the equipment!$B$BThere is an alchemy lab, however, with everything needed.  It's in the Scholomance, on the isle of Caer Darrow in the Plaguelands.$B$BI can't make the trip, but here - take this jar.  There's an imp inside who is quite clever.  Let him out at the alchemy lab and he'll infuse the parchment.\030Bring the Imp in a Jar to the alchemy lab in the Scholomance.  After the parchment is created, return the jar to Gorzeeki Wildeyes.\030\030Parchment Created\030Have you been to the Scholomance, $N? Has the imp yet infused the parchment with the stardust?\030Imp Delivery\0312,1,105,2,259,1,14437\0302,108,113,2,257,1,14437\0302,115,146,2,257,1,14437\0302,149,175,2,257,1,14437\0302,180,236,2,257,1,14437\0302,239,309,2,257,1,14437\0302,314,361,2,257,1,14437\0302,364,405,2,257,1,14437\0302,408,469,2,257,1,14437\0303,1,61,2,384,1,14437\0303,64,131,2,384,1,14437\0301,1,9,4,272,1,14437\0301,11,40,4,272,1,14437\0301,42,65,4,272,2,14437\0301,67,92,4,272,2,14437\0301,94,114,4,272,1,14437\0301,116,140,4,272,1,14437\0301,145,194,4,272,1,14437\0301,196,225,4,272,1,14437\0301,227,248,4,272,1,14437\0306,1,37,3,256,2,14437\0306,39,94,3,256,2,14437\0305,1,17,3,384,1,14437\03114437,2,11,Gorzeeki Wildeyes\03014500,4,13,J'eevee\0312,0,0,6,Scholomance\0302,0,0,6,Plaguelands\0302,0,0,10,Scholomance\0302,0,0,11,Gorzeeki Wildeyes\0303,0,0,21,Scholomance\0317564,21,7564,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0307625,21,7625,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,14500,OBJECTIVE,1,13,J'eevee",[763]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Word from my good friend, Chief Hawkwind! Ah, I can see by his carvings you are of a special breed.\030For you to continue with the Rites of the Earthmother you must pass two more tests. It is time for you to broaden your experience, $n.$B$BTravel to Bloodhoof Village and seek out the Chief, Baine Bloodhoof, son of Cairne. There you may continue your journey and earn the acceptance of the elders of Thunder Bluff.$B$BTake this totem to Baine. He will recognize my carvings and help you on your path.$B$BFollow the road out of Camp Narache and travel with haste. Do not stray or you will lose your way.\030Take the Totem of Hawkwind to Baine Bloodhoof in Bloodhoof Village. Follow the road out of Camp Narache.\030What brings you to my village, $C?\030Rites of the Earthmother\0312,1,83,2,257,1,2981\0302,85,134,2,257,1,2981\0302,139,221,2,259,1,2981\0302,223,313,2,257,1,2981\0302,318,342,2,257,1,2981\0302,344,399,2,257,3,2981\0302,404,461,2,257,1,2981\0302,463,501,2,257,3,2981\0303,1,67,2,384,1,2981\0303,69,104,2,384,1,2981\0301,1,41,4,272,1,2993\0301,43,99,4,272,1,2993\0304,1,34,3,256,2,2993\0312993,2,3,Baine Bloodhoof\0302993,2,9,Baine Bloodhoof\0302981,4,11,Chief Hawkwind\0312,220,1412,0,\0302,0,0,3,Bloodhoof Village\0302,0,0,5,Baine\0302,0,0,9,Baine Bloodhoof\0302,0,0,9,Bloodhoof Village\031757,19,757,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030767,23,767,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[7630]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You got it! Nicely done! Now I can create the lodestone. When you're finally ready for your ritual to create the Circle of Greater Summoning, you'll want a lodestone to make sure the ritual doesn't fizzle out!\030Now that the Bell, Wheel and Candle are made, I should make a black lodestone.  During your ritual, you'll need that lodestone to maintain the other ritual objects if they should fail.$B$BTo make the lodestone, I require arcanite.  Do you have any?  If not, then... you'll have to get the arcanite from an alchemist.$B$BReturn to me when you have the arcanite, and then I'll make the black lodestone.\030Bring 3 Arcanite Bar to Gorzeeki in the Burning Steppes.\030Do you have the arcanite, $N? Once I have it I can make you the black lodestone.\030Arcanite\0312,1,78,2,257,1,14437\0302,81,184,2,259,4,14437\0302,189,230,2,257,1,14437\0302,233,248,2,257,2,14437\0302,251,265,2,257,4,14437\0302,267,316,2,257,1,14437\0302,321,400,2,257,1,14437\0303,1,56,2,384,1,14437\0301,1,11,4,272,1,14437\0301,13,24,4,272,1,14437\0301,26,56,4,272,1,14437\0301,58,209,4,274,1,14437\0304,1,29,3,256,2,14437\0304,31,80,3,256,1,14437\031\0312,0,0,8,Gorzeeki\0302,0,0,8,Burning Steppes\0317626,21,7626,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0307627,21,7627,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0307628,21,7628,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12360,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[7631]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The Xorothian Dreadsteed's spirit is beaten.  Although rage pulses through its ghostly flanks, you know that the beast's soul is yours...$B$BIt whispers dark magic into your mind and instills within you the knowledge to summon a dreadsteed.\030All the preparations are made.  Now, you must perform the ritual to create a Circle of Greater Summoning, then use the parchment infused with Xorothian stardust... to open a portal to Xoroth.$B$BI have written the instructions for the ritual onto a scroll.  Study it closely, for you must perform each step exactly if you wish to succeed.$B$BFortune to you, $N.  And may the souls of your enemies swiftly find their way into your shard pouch.\030Read Mor'zul's Instructions.  Summon a Xorothian Dreadsteed, defeat it, then bind its spirit to you.\030\030Dreadsteed of Xoroth\0312,1,30,2,257,1,14436\0302,33,163,2,257,1,14436\0302,165,191,2,257,1,14436\0302,196,256,2,257,1,14436\0302,259,338,2,259,4,14436\0302,343,361,2,257,1,14436\0302,364,442,2,261,1,14436\0303,1,28,2,384,1,14436\0303,31,100,2,384,1,14436\0301,1,44,4,272,1,14504\0301,47,137,4,272,1,14504\0301,142,240,4,272,1,14504\03114502,2,9,Xorothian Dreadsteed\03014502,4,10,Xorothian Dreadsteed\03010430,4,11,The Beast\0312,0,0,3,Xoroth\0317629,21,7629,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0307630,21,7630,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,14502,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Xorothian Dreadsteed",[7632]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Of course I recognize my own leaves. Look at that! It's in perfect condition.$B$BHow good of you to return it, $C.$B$BPerhaps you could be of service to us and we to you.\030The epidermis of the leaf glows a bright green. The surface is extremely rugose, exposing several veins and wrinkles.$B$BIf you had to take a guess, you would say this leaf came from something ancient and powerful.$B$BMaybe you should find the original owner of this leaf?\030Find the owner of the Ancient Petrified Leaf. Good luck, $N; It's a big world.\030<Vartrus groans.>\030The Ancient Leaf\0312,1,47,2,257,1,0\0302,49,117,2,257,1,0\0302,122,214,2,321,4,0\0302,219,272,2,257,4,0\0303,1,45,2,448,1,0\0303,47,78,2,384,1,0\0301,1,36,4,272,1,14524\0301,38,50,4,272,1,14524\0301,52,77,4,272,1,14524\0301,82,114,4,272,1,14524\0301,119,170,4,272,4,14524\0304,1,17,3,256,1,14524\031\031\031\031ITEM,18703,STARTER,?,10,",[7633]="PARTIAL\031consequences,locations,motivations,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Your diligence and integrity has been noted, $C.$B$BWe are Ancients: Protectors of this once great forest. Our physical forms were destroyed 10,000 years ago when Archimonde and the Burning Legion marched upon Hyjal. Our spirits, however, remain intact.$B$BThere are tasks that we can offer. Tasks that if completed will open up the secrets of the Ancients to you.$B$BKnow this, should you complete these tasks, merely return to this rock and we shall answer the calling.\030\030\030\030An Introduction\0311,1,48,4,272,1,14524\0301,53,106,4,272,1,14524\0301,108,216,4,340,1,14524\0301,218,253,4,272,1,14524\0301,258,291,4,272,1,14524\0301,293,364,4,272,4,14524\0301,369,471,4,272,3,14524\031\031\031\031",[7634]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031May my leaves provide your arrows protection from harm. May your arrows strike true. May the enemies of our world be smitten.\030Greetings, $c. I am Hastat, Ancient of Lore. I hold knowledge lost eons ago.$B$BWith the proper binding, one of my leaves can serve as a quiver the likes of which has not been seen in 10,000 years. A quiver that when accompanied by a bow of Ancients, could grant untold powers.$B$BReturn here with sinew from an adult blue dragon and this quiver shall be yours.\030Hastat the Ancient has asked that you bring him a Mature Blue Dragon Sinew. Should you find this sinew, return it to Hastat in Felwood.\030Welcome back, young $C.\030Ancient Sinew Wrapped Lamina\0312,1,14,2,257,1,14526\0302,16,44,2,321,1,14526\0302,46,76,2,261,1,14526\0302,81,197,2,261,1,14526\0302,199,277,2,257,4,14526\0302,282,361,2,257,3,14526\0303,1,75,2,448,1,14526\0303,77,135,2,384,1,14526\0301,1,55,4,272,1,14526\0301,57,84,4,272,1,14526\0301,86,125,4,276,1,14526\0304,1,23,3,256,1,14526\0313468,2,2,Ancient of Lore\03014526,2,7,Hastat the Ancient\0312,0,0,8,Hastat\0302,0,0,8,Felwood\0317632,19,7632,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,18704,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7635]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A most foul dragon this one was. The sinew reeks of evil.$B$BGive me a moment to cleanse the filth from this flesh and apply the proper enchantments.\030Vartrus may offer you the stave to create a bow of Ancients but only I can enchant the string required to complete the bow.$B$BIt is a simple task, puny one. Slay a mature black dragon and remove the sinew from its bones. Return that sinew to me and I shall enchant the material into an almost indestructible bow string.\030Stoma the Ancient has asked that you bring him a Mature Black Dragon Sinew. Should you find this sinew, return it to Stoma in Felwood.\030I am certain that you will have little difficulty in finding and slaying a black dragon, $N. Do not waste my time with idle chatter.\030A Proper String\0312,1,123,2,257,1,14525\0302,128,157,2,257,1,14525\0302,159,221,2,257,1,14525\0302,223,320,2,257,3,14525\0303,1,75,2,448,1,14525\0303,77,134,2,384,1,14525\0301,1,32,4,272,1,14525\0301,34,57,4,272,1,14525\0301,62,149,4,272,1,14525\0304,1,92,3,256,3,14525\0304,94,132,3,256,1,14525\03114525,2,5,Stoma the Ancient\030616,3,11,Chatter\0312,0,0,6,Stoma\0302,0,0,6,Felwood\0317632,19,7632,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,18705,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7636]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have served us well, $N! Take this stave and combine it with the bow string that Stoma is able to create. Together, they form a most formidable weapon.\030Agents of the Burning Legion are still active in our world, $c. These agents corrupt all that they touch. Nature wilts and weeps in their presence.$B$BYou must track down these demonic corrupters and destroy them, $N. Be warned, you must engage them by yourself or they will flee. As long as you are alone, they will try and destroy you. You must strike at them, turning their arrogance into misery.$B$BI grant you a piece of my bark, the inscriptions shall lead you to your targets. Retrieve their heads.\030You must find and destroy these four demonic corrupters:$B$BSimone the Seductress.$B$BKlinfran the Crazed.$B$BSolenor the Slayer.$B$BArtorius the Doombringer.$B$BDestroy these creatures and return to Vartrus the Ancient in Felwood with their heads.$B$BRefer to the Petrified Bark in your inventory for clues as to their whereabouts.$B$BYou MUST complete this task by yourself.\030Do not be fooled by their disguises!\030Stave of the Ancients\0312,1,63,2,321,1,14524\0302,65,105,2,261,1,14524\0302,107,147,2,257,1,14524\0302,152,217,2,261,1,14524\0302,219,280,2,257,3,14524\0302,282,337,2,261,3,14524\0302,339,399,2,257,1,14524\0302,404,483,2,257,3,14524\0302,485,505,2,257,1,14524\0303,1,56,2,388,1,14524\0303,61,82,2,384,1,14524\0303,87,106,2,384,1,14524\0303,111,129,2,384,1,14524\0303,134,158,2,384,1,14524\0303,163,248,2,452,1,14524\0303,253,332,2,384,1,14524\0303,337,376,2,384,1,14524\0301,1,28,4,272,1,14524\0301,30,109,4,272,1,14524\0301,111,155,4,272,1,14524\0304,1,36,3,256,1,14524\03114533,2,11,Simone the Seductress\03014534,2,12,Klinfran the Crazed\03014530,2,13,Solenor the Slayer\03014535,2,14,Artorius the Doombringer\03014524,2,15,Vartrus the Ancient\0312,0,0,15,Vartrus the Ancient\0302,0,0,15,Felwood\0302,0,0,16,Petrified Bark\0317632,19,7632,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,18952,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,18953,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,18954,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,18955,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7637]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Blessings onto you, friend $C! Your donation goes far beyond what was needed. Your sacrifice will not only help us recover what we have lost, but also help us to help those most in need here in Ironforge.$B$BNow, let me make sure I've suitably prepared this censer for your future needs...\030In order to prepare yourself for this task, you must first show due sacrifice and judgment... with an emphasis on sacrifice.$B$BYou must acquire High Priest Rohan's exorcism censer for your task.  Even though its use will be for good and just reasons, due compensation must be given for it.$B$BProceed to Ironforge and speak with the High Priest.  By bringing ample coin with you to help offset the loss of his censer, it will show your due sacrifice.$B$BGo now $N, time is of the essence.\030Travel to Ironforge and get High Priest Rohan's Exorcism Censer.  You will need to make a donation of 150 gold in order to secure it.\030Greetings, noble $C! I have prepared my trusted censer with the freshest of incense and blessed it thrice for your use. Your donation will help us in Ironforge not only create a new censer, but also to bolster sagging reserves of food for our needy.\030Emphasis on Sacrifice\0312,1,93,2,259,1,928\0302,95,124,2,257,1,928\0302,129,195,2,257,1,928\0302,198,290,2,257,3,928\0302,295,346,2,257,1,928\0302,349,451,2,257,3,928\0302,456,489,2,257,1,928\0303,1,64,2,384,1,928\0303,67,133,2,386,3,928\0301,1,30,4,272,1,11406\0301,32,77,4,272,1,11406\0301,79,204,4,278,3,11406\0301,209,289,4,274,1,11406\0304,1,20,3,256,1,11406\0304,22,119,3,256,1,11406\0304,121,249,3,256,3,11406\03111406,2,3,High Priest Rohan\030111,2,3,Priest\030111,2,5,Priest\03011406,2,8,High Priest Rohan\030111,2,8,Priest\0312,0,0,5,Ironforge\0302,0,0,8,Ironforge\0304,0,0,12,Ironforge\0303,0,0,16,Ironforge\0317639,23,7639,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[7638]="PARTIAL\031loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I am glad to see you $N. I know that you have awaited word as to how to acquire your charger, and now that time has come.$B$BYou will be surely tested in many different ways, but most importantly in your willingness to rise above numerous obstacles thrust before you. These are not done as a learning exercise - your stature is beyond simple educational tests. You must save your future companion from the clutches of the evil you have spent your life fighting.$B$BTake heed, your time has come!\030The time has come, $N, for you to learn about what it will take for you to acquire something you have no doubt waited on for some time... your charger.$B$BSpeak with Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker here in Stormwind's Cathedral District.  It is he who will guide you not only though the legerdemain of a Paladin's most trusted mount, but the tasks before you to acquire one of your own.$B$BI wish you the best in this trial.  For the Light, noble $G brother : sister;!\030Speak with Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in Stormwind's Cathedral District.\030\030Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker\0312,1,137,2,257,3,6171\0302,139,151,2,257,1,6171\0302,156,232,2,257,1,6171\0302,235,381,2,257,3,6171\0302,386,419,2,259,3,6171\0302,422,463,2,257,1,6171\0303,1,72,2,384,1,6171\0301,1,24,4,272,1,928\0301,26,121,4,304,1,928\0301,126,267,4,272,3,928\0301,269,360,4,272,1,928\0301,362,461,4,284,1,928\0301,466,495,4,272,1,928\031928,2,3,Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker\030928,2,7,Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker\0312,0,0,3,Stormwind's Cathedral District\0302,0,0,7,Stormwind's Cathedral District\031\031",[7639]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes, this will do. You will be called upon more than once during this process to make acts of sacrifice; I am glad to see that you are willing to do just that. Sacrifice is a key component in what it takes to uphold the duties of being a Paladin... but I don't have to lecture you on that.$B$BNow $N, you will need to show due judgment in your actions. To that end, this censer will act as your vessel to dispense such judgment on tortured spirits of lands lost to us.\030With my blessings, take the censer.  I myself have used it in several exorcisms, and it should serve you well for the arduous tasks that lie ahead.$B$BReturn now to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in Stormwind, $N.  Your quest continues with him.\030Return the Exorcism Censer to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in the Cathedral District of Stormwind.\030Welcome back, $N. Have you acquired the exorcism censer?\030To Show Due Judgment\0312,1,35,2,257,1,11406\0302,38,147,2,257,1,11406\0302,152,209,2,257,1,11406\0302,212,241,2,257,1,11406\0303,1,96,2,384,1,11406\0301,1,18,4,272,3,928\0301,20,159,4,272,3,928\0301,161,248,4,272,1,928\0301,250,289,4,272,1,928\0301,294,352,4,274,3,928\0301,354,468,4,276,3,928\0304,1,17,3,256,1,928\0304,19,56,3,256,2,928\031928,2,3,Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker\030928,2,5,Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker\0312,0,0,3,Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker\0302,0,0,3,Stormwind\0302,0,0,5,Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker\0302,0,0,5,Cathedral District of Stormwind\0317637,19,7637,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0307640,23,7640,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[764]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I don't think there could be too much misinterpreting or ignoring of that signal, hm? The Venture Co. will know not to take the tauren lightly, or to be so arrogant as to believe we would allow them to steal the natural resources around us without protest.\030This explains the buildup of Venture Co. employees and equipment we've seen in Mulgore. Those goblins... their company is expanding too quickly for their own good. It's how they say, show a goblin something, and you can hear the scales in the background.$B$BGreedy little things, they are. Unfortunately for their business enterprise, we tauren cannot allow them to conduct their operations in our lands. Go to their mine northeast of the ravaged caravan and send them a message.\030Kill 14 Venture Co. Workers and 6 Venture Co. Supervisors for Morin Cloudstalker at Bloodhoof Village.\030The Venture Co. was refused mining rights here in Mulgore, but it would seem that they do not take no for an answer. We tauren are not ones to mince words, however, and we have other ways of getting our message across.\030The Venture Co.\0312,1,40,2,257,1,2988\0302,42,87,2,257,1,2988\0302,89,104,2,257,1,2988\0302,106,163,2,257,1,2988\0302,165,254,2,257,1,2988\0302,259,289,2,257,1,2988\0302,291,404,2,265,1,2988\0302,406,479,2,257,1,2988\0303,1,19,2,384,1,2988\0303,21,45,2,384,1,2988\0303,47,102,2,384,1,2988\0301,1,85,4,272,4,2988\0301,87,101,4,272,1,2988\0301,103,256,4,276,4,2988\0304,1,15,3,256,1,2988\0304,17,116,3,256,4,2988\0304,118,218,3,256,1,2988\0312988,2,11,Morin Cloudstalker\0312,215,1412,0,\0302,0,0,2,Mulgore\0302,0,0,11,Bloodhoof Village\0303,0,0,16,Mulgore\031751,19,751,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,2978,OBJECTIVE,14,13,Venture Co. Worker\030NPC,2979,OBJECTIVE,6,13,Venture Co. Supervisor",[7640]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $N. To render the judgment of the Light on those that dwell in darkness is a task we must approach with vim and zeal; you have done just that with your sacrifice in Ironforge and your judgments of the spirits in Terrordale.$B$BYour next steps will call on both sacrifice and judgment again as you now strive to reclaim the spirit of a fallen charger who now serves a Death Knight known as Darkreaver.\030I have added a pinch of dirt from the tainted ground of Terrordale in the Eastern Plaguelands to the censer.  You will now use this censer to find areas there that show signs of spiritual turmoil and disturbance.  Look for green auras that permeate the ground as the physical world buckles under the torment of the spirit realm and use the censer to drive out the evil spirits.$B$BWhen you have passed sufficient judgment on the spirits there, you will be ready to proceed.\030Use the Exorcism Censer to drive out the spirits that torment Terrordale.  When you have slain 25 Terrordale Spirits, return to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in the Cathedral District of Stormwind.\030It is good to see you again $N. Is your work done in Terrordale?\030Exorcising Terrordale\0312,1,108,2,257,1,928\0302,111,212,2,257,3,928\0302,215,377,2,257,1,928\0302,382,473,2,257,3,928\0303,1,73,2,384,1,928\0303,76,194,2,388,1,928\0301,1,14,4,272,1,928\0301,16,234,4,272,1,928\0301,239,411,4,272,3,928\0304,1,31,3,256,1,928\0304,33,64,3,256,2,928\031928,2,6,Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker\0312,0,0,1,Eastern Plaguelands\0302,0,0,6,Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker\0302,0,0,6,Cathedral District of Stormwind\0304,0,0,8,Ironforge\0304,0,0,8,Terrordale\0303,0,0,11,Terrordale\0317639,19,7639,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0307641,23,7641,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,14564,OBJECTIVE,25,13,Terrordale Spirit",[7641]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hello there - Lord Shadowbreaker sent me word ahead of time that you'd be coming around this way to see me. I'm willing to make the barding you need, but it won't be either cheap or easy; let's get that out in the open first and foremost.$B$BI will say this much, and Grayson will back me up when I make this claim... you'll not find better barding made anywhere in all of Azeroth than right here.\030A paladin's charger is nothing more than a pack animal without proper barding for it.  The barding used by your charger not only needs to be of the finest materials possible, but because of the circumstances involved it must also be sufficiently attuned to the spirit realm.$B$BFirst things first, $N - let's get your barding made.  In Stormwind's Dwarven District is one of the finest craftsmen living today, Grimand Elmore.  His work will not be cheap, but his quality is what we seek.  Speak with him.\030Speak with Grimand Elmore in Stormwind's Dwarven District.\030\030The Work of Grimand Elmore\0312,1,85,2,257,1,928\0302,88,274,2,259,1,928\0302,279,331,2,257,1,928\0302,334,425,2,257,1,928\0302,428,487,2,259,3,928\0302,490,504,2,257,1,928\0303,1,58,2,384,1,928\0301,1,107,4,272,1,1416\0301,109,238,4,274,1,1416\0301,243,317,4,272,3,1416\0301,319,397,4,272,1,1416\0311416,2,4,Grimand Elmore\0301416,2,7,Grimand Elmore\0312,0,0,7,Stormwind's Dwarven District\0317640,19,7640,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0307642,23,7642,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[7642]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This... well, this is exactly what I needed.  You're quite the resourceful $C, aren't you?$B$BAll right then, let's get this barding finished up for you!\030You'll need four things for the barding - runecloth for the lining, arcanite bars for the plating, Arthas' Tears for the spiritual attunement, and Stratholme holy water for the spiritual imbuement.  Actually, you need five things... gold for my fee.  That fee includes all labor as well as a handcrafted saddle and stirrups.$B$BOnce you've got all that, I'll be able to finish your barding.  Until then, there are some things I can get started on for you while you assemble your collection of goods.\030Bring 40 Runecloth, 6 Arcanite Bars, 10 Arthas' Tears, 5 Stratholme Holy Water vials, and 150 gold to Grimand Elmore in the Dwarven District of Stormwind.\030Ah, $C. I won't be able to finish your barding without the things I mentioned. Have you gotten everything together?\030Collection of Goods\0312,1,197,2,259,1,1416\0302,200,232,2,259,1,1416\0302,234,249,2,257,1,1416\0302,252,324,2,257,1,1416\0302,329,390,2,257,1,1416\0302,393,499,2,257,1,1416\0303,1,154,2,384,1,1416\0301,1,7,4,272,1,1416\0301,9,44,4,272,1,1416\0301,47,90,4,272,2,1416\0301,95,153,4,272,1,1416\0304,9,78,3,256,1,1416\0304,80,115,3,256,2,1416\0311416,2,7,Grimand Elmore\0312,0,0,7,Grimand Elmore\0302,0,0,7,Dwarven District of Stormwind\0317641,19,7641,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,13180,OBJECTIVE,5,15,\030ITEM,8836,OBJECTIVE,10,15,\030ITEM,14047,OBJECTIVE,40,15,\030ITEM,12360,OBJECTIVE,6,15,",[7643]="PARTIAL\031consequences\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The Ancient Equine Spirit accepts the offering of the Manna-Enriched Horse Feed, nuzzling the container as it helps itself to the special oats and grains. After it has eaten a little, it looks at the barding you possess and positions itself as though it wants you to place it upon its back...\030Your barding needs a special form of blessing, one from an appropriate spirit.  In Dire Maul is such a spirit, the Ancient Equine Spirit.  It is currently held by a corrupt treant, Tendris Warpwood.  Pass judgment upon this foul beast, $N.$B$BKnow this - freedom alone is not enough.  You must soothe the spirit before receiving its blessing.  For that, special horse feed is needed.  Travel to Southshore first and speak with Merideth Carlson on this... and prepare for more sacrifice.\030Acquire special horse feed used for feeding a spirit horse.  Merideth Carlson in Southshore apparently is the source for such food.$B$BTravel to the Dire Maul dungeon in Feralas and slay Tendris Warpwood.  Doing so will free the Ancient Equine Spirit.  Feed it the special horse feed, thereby soothing the spirit.  Finally, give it the Arcanite Barding so it may bless it.\030The Ancient Equine Spirit looks at you expectantly, as though it wants something from you.\030Ancient Equine Spirit\0312,1,78,2,259,1,928\0302,81,137,2,321,1,928\0302,140,198,2,261,1,928\0302,201,239,2,257,1,928\0302,244,283,2,265,1,928\0302,286,342,2,257,1,928\0302,345,383,2,257,1,928\0302,386,454,2,257,1,928\0302,456,486,2,257,1,928\0303,1,59,2,384,1,928\0303,62,131,2,384,4,928\0303,136,204,2,384,1,928\0303,207,251,2,448,3,928\0303,254,313,2,384,1,928\0303,316,372,2,384,1,928\0301,1,154,4,336,1,14566\0301,156,292,4,274,1,14566\0304,1,90,3,322,1,14566\03114566,2,2,Ancient Equine Spirit\0301964,2,3,Treant\03011489,2,3,Tendris Warpwood\030385,2,7,Horse\0302357,2,8,Merideth Carlson\030385,2,10,Horse\0302357,2,11,Merideth Carlson\03011489,2,12,Tendris Warpwood\03014566,2,13,Ancient Equine Spirit\030385,2,14,Horse\03014566,4,16,Ancient Equine Spirit\030385,4,16,Horse\03014566,3,18,Ancient Equine Spirit\0312,0,0,8,Southshore\0302,0,0,11,Southshore\0302,0,0,12,Dire Maul\0302,0,0,12,Feralas\0317642,19,7642,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0307644,23,7644,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,18775,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7644]="PARTIAL\031consequences\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You've come far, my friend. Your barding is now suitably prepared for the last task at hand.$B$BYou will be using this barding to harness your charger once the task of redemption is complete. Before that, however, you will have a monumental struggle to overcome. Your time draws near - huzzah!$B$BThere is one last item that needs to be made before we begin this, $N. Hopefully your resourcefulness has not departed you since you had your barding made...\030As the barding rests on the back of the Ancient Equine Spirit, it glows ever so slightly.  The air is thick with power for a brief moment, and then the barding disappears from the back of the horse and is now secure in your backpack.$B$BIt would seem that the barding has been blessed.  As per Lord Shadowbreaker's instructions, you should now return with it to him in Stormwind.\030Return with the Blessed Arcanite Barding to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in the Cathedral District of Stormwind.\030$N, you're back! Were you able to successfully deal with Merideth Carlson and Tendris Warpwood?  Honestly, I'm not sure which one is a greater threat at times...\030Blessed Arcanite Barding\0312,1,89,2,321,1,14566\0302,92,233,2,257,1,14566\0302,238,285,2,257,4,14566\0302,288,379,2,257,1,14566\0303,1,110,2,384,1,14566\0301,1,27,4,272,1,928\0301,29,92,4,272,1,928\0301,97,191,4,272,3,928\0301,193,262,4,272,3,928\0301,264,293,4,272,1,928\0301,298,367,4,282,1,928\0301,369,454,4,272,3,928\0304,1,16,3,256,1,928\0304,18,95,3,256,2,928\0304,98,161,3,260,1,928\03114566,2,1,Ancient Equine Spirit\030385,2,2,Horse\030928,2,5,Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker\0302357,3,14,Merideth Carlson\03011489,3,14,Tendris Warpwood\0312,0,0,4,Stormwind\0302,0,0,5,Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker\0302,0,0,5,Cathedral District of Stormwind\0317643,19,7643,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0307646,23,7646,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[7645]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031YES, NOW WHO - wait - you're giving me the gold too? You weren't the one who called me mad (actually they called me a fruitcake nut-job)... still, you're willing to show sacrifice even for wrongs you've not committed?$B$BI... I misjudged you, $N.  Should you need more horse feed, come see me. I will give it to you free of charge. Thank you... noble $C.$B$BI am going to keep the money though - I'm not that much of a nut-job as to give up a fortune.\030The Silver Hand thought me MAD when I told them that I could make a special horse feed that could nourish spiritual horses.  EVERYONE thought I was mad!  Well, now it's payback time!$B$BI'll make what you need, PALADIN... so-called CHAMPION... but it will cost you.  I need special biscuits - Enriched Manna Biscuits sold only by the Argent Dawn - for this blend.  I also demand, yes DEMAND gold as compensation for the misery I have endured!$B$BShow me the sacrifice you tout so much, PALADIN.\030Retrieve 20 Enriched Manna Biscuits - the key ingredient in making Manna-Enriched Horse Feed - for Merideth Carlson at Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills.  The Argent Dawn is known as the sole purveyor of the biscuits.$B$BYou also need to give her 50 gold to soothe her ruffled sensibilities.\030Yes, I've proved you wrong now, haven't I? I've proved them all wrong! I WAS RIGHT ALL ALONG!!!\030Manna-Enriched Horse Feed\0312,1,123,2,257,4,2357\0302,126,152,2,257,1,2357\0302,155,182,2,257,1,2357\0302,187,221,2,259,1,2357\0302,223,243,2,257,1,2357\0302,245,265,2,257,3,2357\0302,268,363,2,259,1,2357\0302,366,442,2,257,1,2357\0302,447,494,2,257,1,2357\0303,1,157,2,384,1,2357\0303,160,221,2,384,1,2357\0303,226,295,2,386,1,2357\0301,1,52,4,272,2,2357\0301,54,139,4,272,1,2357\0301,141,217,4,272,2,2357\0301,227,246,4,272,1,2357\0301,249,293,4,274,1,2357\0301,295,331,4,272,3,2357\0301,333,344,4,272,1,2357\0301,346,354,4,272,1,2357\0301,359,451,4,272,3,2357\0304,1,42,3,256,2,2357\0304,44,70,3,256,1,2357\0304,72,95,3,256,1,2357\031385,2,1,Horse\030385,2,10,Horse\0302357,2,10,Merideth Carlson\030385,4,17,Horse\0312,0,0,10,Southshore\0302,0,0,10,Hillsbrad Foothills\0317643,20,7643,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,13724,OBJECTIVE,20,15,",[7646]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031These are fine specimens, $N - the final pieces are now in place. At long last, your time has come!$B$BIn the depths of the Great Ossuary of Scholomance are the skeletal remains of many beings. Amongst them is a once-noble charger. The hollowed soul of this charger now serves as the steed for Death Knight Darkreaver. It is he whom you will face, and it is this steed that you will pass judgment upon. Only you, $N, can redeem its soul and save it from the torment of its servitude.\030We now must assemble a Divination Scryer - this will begin the trial that will allow you to redeem the fallen charger.  Your scryer, actually, is almost done.  The exorcism censer used in Terrordale is the catalyst for it, and I will fashion a suitable housing for the device.$B$BThe last components needed, though, are two diamonds.  They must be as juxtaposed in brilliance as they are in purpose - an Azerothian and a Pristine Black.  These two will be the beacon by which the scryer will pierce the shadows!\030Bring an Azerothian Diamond and a Pristine Black Diamond to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in the Cathedral District of Stormwind.\030You have come so very far, $N. Your final act of worldly-item sacrifice will be the genesis for one of your greatest accomplishments. I can feel it in the very fiber of my being!\030The Divination Scryer\0312,1,118,2,257,3,928\0302,121,158,2,257,1,928\0302,161,276,2,257,3,928\0302,281,333,2,257,1,928\0302,336,436,2,257,1,928\0302,439,511,2,257,3,928\0303,1,126,2,384,1,928\0301,1,65,4,272,1,928\0301,67,99,4,272,1,928\0301,104,193,4,272,1,928\0301,195,231,4,272,1,928\0301,233,318,4,272,1,928\0301,320,402,4,272,3,928\0301,404,483,4,280,1,928\0304,1,30,3,256,1,928\0304,32,133,3,256,3,928\0304,135,178,3,256,1,928\03110664,2,1,Scryer\03010664,2,2,Scryer\03010664,2,6,Scryer\030928,2,7,Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker\0305689,4,12,Steed\03014516,4,12,Death Knight Darkreaver\0305689,4,13,Steed\0312,0,0,3,Terrordale\0302,0,0,7,Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker\0302,0,0,7,Cathedral District of Stormwind\0317644,19,7644,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0307647,23,7647,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12800,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,18335,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7647]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A glimmer of life - long vacant from the poor beast - shines in its eyes as you hand its judged soul back to it. You feel a holy rush of power surge around you as you place the barding on its back, having judged the charger redeemed. The charger nuzzles your hand as the burdens of the past are lifted from the beast. You now feel as though you could call upon this beast to serve as your steed, should the need arise.$B$BYou have claimed your epic charger, $C! Congratulations!\030Take this satchel - in it are the items you will need for your task.$B$BUse the divination scryer in the heart of the Great Ossuary's basement to bring forth accursed spirits that must be judged.  Use your judgments wisely during this trial - they will prove more potent than you realize.  After the spirits, the death knight will appear; defeat him and reclaim the lost soul of the charger.  Only then $N, will you be able to redeem it and place your barding upon your new steed!$B$BGood luck!\030Use the Divination Scryer in the heart of the Great Ossuary's basement in the Scholomance.  Doing so will bring forth the spirits you must judge.  Defeating these spirits will summon forth Death Knight Darkreaver.  Defeat him and reclaim the lost soul of the fallen charger.$B$BGive the Charger's Redeemed Soul and the Blessed Enchanted Barding to Darkreaver's Fallen Charger.\030The spirit of the fallen charger looks upon you with a mournful gaze. Sad, almost hollow eyes look at you as though all hope was lost to it.\030Judgment and Redemption\0312,1,68,2,259,3,928\0302,73,195,2,257,1,928\0302,198,288,2,257,3,928\0302,291,391,2,261,3,928\0302,394,480,2,257,3,928\0302,485,494,2,257,1,928\0303,1,90,2,384,1,928\0303,93,145,2,384,3,928\0303,148,213,2,384,3,928\0303,216,274,2,388,1,928\0303,279,376,2,384,1,928\0301,1,112,4,272,1,14568\0301,114,233,4,272,1,14568\0301,235,317,4,272,1,14568\0301,319,418,4,274,4,14568\0301,423,461,4,272,1,14568\0301,463,478,4,272,1,14568\0304,1,69,3,256,1,14568\0304,71,140,3,262,3,14568\03110664,2,2,Scryer\0301531,2,4,Lost Soul\0305689,2,5,Steed\03010664,2,7,Scryer\03014516,2,9,Death Knight Darkreaver\0301531,2,10,Lost Soul\03014568,2,11,Darkreaver's Fallen Charger\03010430,4,14,The Beast\0305689,4,15,Steed\0312,0,0,7,Scholomance\0302,0,0,11,Darkreaver's Fallen Charger\0317646,19,7646,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0307666,23,7666,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,18799,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,18792,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7648]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This is most impressive work. It seems that as Grimand gets older, his craftsmanship continues to improve. That's quite the feat when his work was already some of the finest you'd find anywhere when he made my barding back in the day.$B$BWhile this barding would be a fine addition to any normal steed, we are not dealing with such a mundane beast. You'll need this barding blessed by an appropriate source for it to be worthy of resting on a $C's charger. I'll hold onto it for you until then.\030<Grimand wipes sweat from his brow, beaming with a sense of pride.>$B$BThere you are, my friend.  This is some of my finest work - as good as the barding I personally made for Lord Shadowbreaker when he went for his own charger.  I thank you for your trust in me to provide for you the best.$B$BNo doubt Grayson will want to see the work for himself as well.  Take your barding to him, and give him my thanks for his honorable business.\030Take the Arcanite Barding to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in Stormwind's Cathedral District for his inspection.\030You're progressing along nicely, $N. Once you have made your barding, you'll be well on your way to the next task.\030Grimand's Finest Work\0312,1,67,2,257,1,1416\0302,72,96,2,257,1,1416\0302,99,228,2,257,1,1416\0302,231,291,2,257,1,1416\0302,296,358,2,259,3,1416\0302,361,436,2,257,1,1416\0303,1,109,2,384,1,1416\0301,1,29,4,272,1,928\0301,31,106,4,272,4,928\0301,108,234,4,272,1,928\0301,239,348,4,272,4,928\0301,350,456,4,274,1,928\0301,458,494,4,272,1,928\0304,1,36,3,256,1,928\0304,38,114,3,256,1,928\031928,2,7,Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker\0305689,4,11,Steed\0312,0,0,7,Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker\0302,0,0,7,Stormwind's Cathedral District\0317642,19,7642,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[7649]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, my boy.$B$B<Lorekeeper Lydros tears out a page from the book.>$B$BI am sure you can make use of this recipe.\030The tome carries the mark of the Athenaeum.\030Return the book to its rightful owners.\030You have recovered a tome!\030Enchanted Thorium Platemail: Volume I\0312,1,43,2,257,1,0\0303,1,39,2,384,1,0\0301,1,18,4,272,1,14368\0301,23,73,4,272,1,14368\0301,78,119,4,272,1,14368\0304,1,26,3,256,1,14368\031795,2,1,Mark\03014368,4,4,Lorekeeper Lydros\031\031\031ITEM,18769,STARTER,?,10,",[765]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031My anger is somewhat lessened at the news that the villain Fizsprocket is dead. I will go through his personal effects and see if there is any additional information about what the Venture Co. has planned for the future. Thank you for your efforts, $N.\030According to the documents you salvaged from the caravan, the Venture Co. created many plans to attempt to drive us from our lands here, so that they could have free reign to plunder our lands.$B$BThe depths that they would sink to accomplish their goals disgusts and appalls me. I want the mastermind behind their plans killed. His name is Supervisor Fizsprocket, you will find him at the Venture Co. mine east of the ravaged caravan. Bring me his clipboard, we shall see if we find out anything useful.\030Kill Supervisor Fizsprocket and return his clipboard to Morin Cloudstalker at Bloodhoof Village.\030I seethe with anger at the thought of the atrocities the Venture Co. is willing to perpetrate against us in the name of profit.\030Supervisor Fizsprocket\0312,1,73,2,257,1,2988\0302,75,193,2,259,4,2988\0302,198,279,2,257,4,2988\0302,281,328,2,259,1,2988\0302,330,401,2,257,3,2988\0302,403,435,2,257,1,2988\0302,437,504,2,257,4,2988\0303,1,96,2,384,1,2988\0301,1,79,4,272,1,2988\0301,81,192,4,272,4,2988\0301,194,220,4,272,1,2988\0301,222,252,4,272,1,2988\0304,1,68,3,256,1,2988\0304,70,127,3,256,1,2988\0313051,2,5,Supervisor Fizsprocket\0303051,2,8,Supervisor Fizsprocket\0302988,2,8,Morin Cloudstalker\0312,215,1412,0,\0302,0,0,5,Venture Co\0302,0,0,8,Morin Cloudstalker\0302,0,0,8,Bloodhoof Village\031751,19,751,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4819,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7650]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, my boy.$B$B<Lorekeeper Lydros tears out a page from the book.>$B$BI am sure you can make use of this recipe.\030The tome carries the mark of the Athenaeum.\030Return the book to its rightful owners.\030You have recovered a tome!\030Enchanted Thorium Platemail: Volume II\0312,1,43,2,257,1,0\0303,1,39,2,384,1,0\0301,1,18,4,272,1,14368\0301,23,73,4,272,1,14368\0301,78,119,4,272,1,14368\0304,1,26,3,256,1,14368\031795,2,1,Mark\03014368,4,4,Lorekeeper Lydros\031\031\031ITEM,18770,STARTER,?,10,",[7651]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, my boy.$B$B<Lorekeeper Lydros tears out a page from the book.>$B$BI am sure you can make use of this recipe.\030The tome carries the mark of the Athenaeum.\030Return the book to its rightful owners.\030You have recovered a tome!\030Enchanted Thorium Platemail: Volume III\0312,1,43,2,257,1,0\0303,1,39,2,384,1,0\0301,1,18,4,272,1,14368\0301,23,73,4,272,1,14368\0301,78,119,4,272,1,14368\0304,1,26,3,256,1,14368\031795,2,1,Mark\03014368,4,4,Lorekeeper Lydros\031\031\031ITEM,18771,STARTER,?,10,",[7652]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,objectives,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Aright, mister, I got a hot deal for ya.$B$BI'm lookin' to offload some of these here Imperial plate armor recipes and need someone willing to take on the burden. All I want in exchange is some thorium bars. Sound good?\030\030\030\030A Blue Light Bargain\0311,1,40,4,272,1,14567\0301,45,162,4,274,1,14567\0301,164,207,4,274,1,14567\0301,209,219,4,272,2,14567\031\031\031\031",[7653]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A pleasure doin' business with ya.$B$B$BAnd $N, wipe that look of disgust off yer face.\030\030\030For the belt plans, I'll be needin' 20 thorium bars.\030Imperial Plate Belt\0311,1,34,4,272,1,14567\0301,41,87,4,272,1,14567\0304,1,52,3,256,1,14567\031\031\0317652,19,7652,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12359,OBJECTIVE,20,15,",[7654]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A pleasure doin' business with ya.$B$BAnd $N, wipe that look of disgust off yer face.\030\030\030For the boot plans, I'll be needin' 40 thorium bars. Yep, 40. Are you gonna cry? Would you like a hanky?$B$B<Derotain laughs.>\030Imperial Plate Boots\0311,1,34,4,272,1,14567\0301,39,85,4,272,1,14567\0304,1,52,3,256,1,14567\0304,54,61,3,256,1,14567\0304,63,80,3,256,2,14567\0304,82,104,3,256,4,14567\0304,109,126,3,256,1,14567\031\031\0317652,19,7652,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12359,OBJECTIVE,40,15,",[7655]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031A pleasure doin' business with ya.$B$BAnd $N, wipe that look of disgust off yer face.\030\030\030For the bracer plans, I'll be needin' 20 thorium bars.$B$BAre you alright, sonny? Yer getting' all red.\030Imperial Plate Bracer\0311,1,34,4,272,1,14567\0301,39,85,4,272,1,14567\0304,1,54,3,256,1,14567\0304,59,81,3,256,2,14567\0304,83,103,3,256,1,14567\031\031\0317652,19,7652,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONF