87,4,272,1,14738\0304,1,22,3,256,1,14738\0304,24,79,3,260,1,14738\03114738,2,7,Otho Moji'ko\0302693,2,7,Highvale Marksman\0312,47,1425,0,\0302,0,0,7,Revantusk Village\0302,0,0,7,Hinterlands\0302,0,0,9,Quel'Danil Lodge\0317842,23,7842,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,2692,OBJECTIVE,15,13,Highvale Scout\030NPC,2691,OBJECTIVE,15,13,Highvale Outrunner\030NPC,2694,OBJECTIVE,15,13,Highvale Ranger\030NPC,2693,OBJECTIVE,15,13,Highvale Marksman",[7842]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Oh, mon, this gonna be good. One more step to go and Wildhammer see that they can't mess with troll!\030They say the Wildhammer and gryphon are as close to each other as troll and mate. Disgusting, but we be able to use this to our advantage, mon. We send them another message.$B$BKill all the gryphons you see in the Hinterlands, collect their feathers. From this we make the final message.\030Otho Moji'ko at Revantusk Village in the Hinterlands wants you to bring him 10 Long Elegant Feathers from the gryphons that inhabit the Hinterlands. Return to him once this task is complete.$B$BGryphons are known to inhabit every region of the Hinterlands.\030The last message gonna scare them off for sure. Either that or make them very, very angry.\030Another Message to the Wildhammer\0312,1,81,2,257,1,14738\0302,83,143,2,257,1,14738\0302,145,173,2,257,1,14738\0302,178,250,2,257,1,14738\0302,252,287,2,257,1,14738\0303,1,148,2,386,1,14738\0303,150,190,2,384,1,14738\0303,195,256,2,384,1,14738\0301,1,28,4,272,1,14738\0301,30,100,4,272,1,14738\0304,1,47,3,256,1,14738\0304,49,90,3,256,1,14738\03114738,2,6,Otho Moji'ko\0312,47,1425,0,\0302,0,0,4,Hinterlands\0302,0,0,6,Revantusk Village\0302,0,0,6,Hinterlands\0317841,19,7841,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0307843,23,7843,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4589,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[7843]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031I wish I coulda been there to see the look on their faces, mon. Are they packing up their bags? Leavin' town?$B$BYou done good, $N. Real good. Otho reward you with the big mojo.\030<Otho hands you a long, blood drenched spear, wrapped in several gryphon feathers.>$B$BYou take this, mon. You take this to Aerie Peak, dead center of town by the well. You plant it! Drive it right into the ground! Show those dwarves that troll mean business! Come back when you do this. Hopefully you come back alive.\030Otho Moji'ko at Revantusk Village in the Hinterlands wants you to travel to Aerie Peak in the western region of the Hinterlands and place the Final Message to the Wildhammer by the well in the center of town. Return to him once this task is complete.$B$BBeware of angry Wildhammer dwarves and unruly members of the Alliance.\030Message to the Wildhammer Delivered\030What's the hold up, mon?\030The Final Message to the Wildhammer\0312,1,83,2,257,1,14738\0302,88,106,2,257,1,14738\0302,108,168,2,257,1,14738\0302,170,182,2,257,1,14738\0302,184,214,2,257,1,14738\0302,216,259,2,257,1,14738\0302,261,287,2,257,1,14738\0302,289,318,2,257,3,14738\0303,1,208,2,386,1,14738\0303,210,250,2,384,1,14738\0303,255,324,2,384,1,14738\0301,1,63,4,274,3,14738\0301,65,95,4,272,2,14738\0301,97,109,4,272,2,14738\0301,114,131,4,272,1,14738\0301,133,142,4,272,1,14738\0301,144,177,4,272,1,14738\0305,1,24,3,256,2,14738\0304,1,35,3,384,1,14738\03114738,2,9,Otho Moji'ko\0312,47,1425,0,\0302,0,0,3,Aerie Peak\0302,0,0,9,Revantusk Village\0302,0,0,9,Hinterlands\0302,0,0,9,Aerie Peak\0302,0,0,9,Wildhammer\0303,0,0,19,Wildhammer Delivered\0317842,19,7842,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[7844]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $C. Zul'jin himself could not have done a better job!\030Three different tribes of trolls inhabit the Hinterlands, $N. That is about as far as the similarities between the tribes extends: We are all trolls and we live in the Hinterlands.$B$BThe Vilebranch - aptly named - are a depraved lot; feeding on other trolls and humanoids.$B$BIf Zul'jin were here, he would have destroyed the whole lot of them with a flick of his wrist - alas, Zul'jin has not yet returned and we are left to our own devices.$B$BIt is up to you to destroy the filth of the region!\030Mystic Yayo'jin at Revantusk Village in the Hinterlands wants you to kill 30 Vilebranch Scalpers and 15 Vilebranch Soothsayers. Return to her when this task is complete.$B$BYayo'jin indicated that these trolls could be found near the Shaol'watha and Agol'watha temples in the north by northeastern region of the Hinterlands.\030The Vilebranch Soothsayers and Scalpers inhabit the north by northeast region of the Hinterlands.\030Cannibalistic Cousins\0312,1,61,2,257,1,14739\0302,63,180,2,257,1,14739\0302,185,273,2,257,1,14739\0302,278,443,2,261,4,14739\0302,448,498,2,261,1,14739\0303,1,127,2,386,1,14739\0303,129,169,2,384,1,14739\0303,174,324,2,384,4,14739\0301,1,14,4,272,1,14739\0301,16,64,4,272,4,14739\0304,1,97,3,256,1,14739\03114739,2,6,Mystic Yayo'jin\0312,47,1425,0,\0302,0,0,2,Hinterlands\0302,0,0,6,Revantusk Village\0302,0,0,6,Hinterlands\0302,0,0,8,Shaol'watha\031\031NPC,4466,OBJECTIVE,30,13,Vilebranch Scalper\030NPC,4467,OBJECTIVE,15,13,Vilebranch Soothsayer",[7845]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You must act quickly, $N. Surely the guards have been alerted to your presence.\030My mate was taken by Vilebranch savages in a bold midnight raid on our village. Our spies have told me that he is still alive and being held prisoner atop Jintha'alor. The Vile Priestess Hexx is said to be preparing him for a sacrifice to the faceless blood God, Hakkar.$B$BYou must save him, $N! Our village could not stand a loss this great.\030Primal Torntusk at Revantusk Village in the Hinterlands wants you to rescue her mate, Elder Torntusk, from Jintha'alor.$B$BYou have been told that he is being held prisoner atop Jintha'alor, the Vilebranch capital city located in the southern region of the Hinterlands.\030\030Kidnapped Elder Torntusk!\0312,1,79,2,257,1,14736\0302,81,167,2,257,1,14736\0302,169,270,2,257,1,14736\0302,275,296,2,265,1,14736\0302,298,343,2,257,4,14736\0303,1,119,2,394,1,14736\0303,124,269,2,384,1,14736\0301,1,25,4,272,1,14757\0301,27,79,4,272,1,14757\0317995,2,3,Vile Priestess Hexx\030112,2,3,Priestess\03014834,2,3,Hakkar\03014736,2,6,Primal Torntusk\03014757,2,6,Elder Torntusk\0312,47,1425,0,\0302,0,0,6,Revantusk Village\0302,0,0,6,Hinterlands\0302,0,0,6,Jintha'alor\0317846,23,7846,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[7846]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Freedom at last! Thank you, $N. Revantusk will know your deeds!\030The key to my bindings is held by Hitah'ya the Keeper. She is in the nearby cave. Be careful, $c, for she is guarded well.$B$BKill her and bring the key back to loosen my shackles. Only then will I be free to return home.\030Elder Torntusk at Jintha'alor wants you to kill Hitah'ya the Keeper to get the Shackle Key to his bindings. Return to Elder Torntusk when you have recovered the key.\030You must hurry!\030Recover the Key!\0312,1,54,2,257,1,14757\0302,56,81,2,257,1,14757\0302,83,122,2,257,1,14757\0302,127,180,2,257,1,14757\0302,182,221,2,257,3,14757\0303,1,107,2,386,1,14757\0303,109,165,2,384,1,14757\0301,1,16,4,280,1,14757\0301,18,31,4,272,1,14757\0301,33,63,4,272,3,14757\0304,1,15,3,256,1,14757\03110802,2,1,Hitah'ya the Keeper\03014757,2,6,Elder Torntusk\03010802,2,6,Hitah'ya the Keeper\03014757,2,7,Elder Torntusk\0312,47,1425,0,\0302,0,0,6,Jintha'alor\0302,0,0,7,Elder Torntusk\0317845,19,7845,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0307847,23,7847,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,19064,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7847]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have done the Revantusk a great service, $N! We owe you a great debt of gratitude.\030Return to my mate, Primal Torntusk at Revantusk Village. Tell her that I am coming home! She is sure to reward you.\030Elder Torntusk at Jintha'alor wants you to return to Primal Torntusk at Revantusk Village with news of his rescue.\030\030Return to Primal Torntusk\0312,1,56,2,257,1,14757\0302,58,88,2,257,1,14757\0302,90,115,2,257,1,14757\0303,1,114,2,394,1,14757\0301,1,48,4,272,1,14736\0301,50,86,4,272,1,14736\03114736,2,1,Primal Torntusk\03014757,2,4,Elder Torntusk\03014736,2,4,Primal Torntusk\0312,47,1425,0,\0302,0,0,1,Revantusk Village\0302,0,0,4,Jintha'alor\0302,0,0,4,Primal Torntusk\0302,0,0,4,Revantusk Village\0317846,19,7846,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[7848]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I am now able to transport you to the Molten Core. Ask and it shall be done.\030Rifts stir, tear, and collapse all around us, $r. Not two paces from where I stand is a tear leading through the depths of Blackrock Mountain, into the maw of the Firelord.$B$BSurprised? Pity... The mortal races cannot comprehend that which they cannot see, touch, or feel.$B$BI assure you, the portal is there and access is possible.$B$BI've piqued your interest? Attunement is simple. Venture into Blackrock Depths and retrieve a core fragment. Return it to me and I shall attune your essence with the portal.\030Venture to the Molten Core entry portal in Blackrock Depths and recover a Core Fragment. Return to Lothos Riftwaker in Blackrock Mountain when you have recovered the Core Fragment.\030You must attune your soul with the Molten Core before access is granted.\030Attunement to the Core\0312,1,49,2,257,1,14387\0302,51,172,2,257,1,14387\0302,177,186,2,257,2,14387\0302,188,194,2,257,1,14387\0302,196,273,2,257,1,14387\0302,278,334,2,257,1,14387\0302,339,364,2,257,2,14387\0302,366,386,2,257,1,14387\0302,388,446,2,257,1,14387\0302,448,511,2,257,3,14387\0303,1,88,2,384,1,14387\0303,90,180,2,384,1,14387\0301,1,50,4,272,1,14387\0301,52,76,4,272,3,14387\0304,1,72,3,256,1,14387\03111668,2,2,Firelord\03014387,2,12,Lothos Riftwaker\0312,2717,0,0,\0302,0,0,11,Molten Core\0302,0,0,11,Blackrock Depths\0302,0,0,12,Lothos Riftwaker\0302,0,0,12,Blackrock Mountain\0304,0,0,13,Molten Core\031\031ITEM,18412,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[7849]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031My dearest brother, how I will miss you...$B$BThank you for your assistance, $N. You are truly a hero in my eyes.\030Like many in our village, I too have lost a loved one to the wilds. Alas, it was my twin brother Malkhor - taken in the same raid as Torntusk's mate by the Vilebranch.$B$BSadly, he was not fated to live and was given a swift, brutal execution; his remains fed to the oozes and wolves of the Vilebranch.$B$BIt is too late to save his life but not too late to save his soul. Recover his remains, $N.\030Huntsman Markhor at Revantusk Village in the Hinterlands wants you to recover his twin brother's remains. Find and return Huntsman Malkhor's Skull and Huntsman Malkhor's Bones to Huntsman Markhor.$B$BMarkhor mentioned that his brother's remains were fed to the oozes and wolves of the Vilebranch. He also mentioned that there is a refuse pit filled with oozes in Jintha'alor as well as a wolf den. Both of these places are near the top of the temple.\030When I have his remains, I shall take them to Yayo'jin and have them prepared for a proper burial.\030Separation Anxiety\0312,1,67,2,261,1,14741\0302,69,167,2,257,1,14741\0302,172,302,2,257,1,14741\0302,307,372,2,267,1,14741\0302,374,397,2,257,1,14741\0303,1,105,2,386,1,14741\0303,107,196,2,384,1,14741\0303,201,296,2,384,1,14741\0303,298,397,2,384,1,14741\0303,399,450,2,384,1,14741\0301,1,42,4,272,3,14741\0301,47,80,4,272,1,14741\0301,82,113,4,272,1,14741\0304,1,98,3,256,3,14741\03114741,2,6,Huntsman Markhor\03014741,2,7,Huntsman Markhor\0312,47,1425,0,\0302,0,0,6,Revantusk Village\0302,0,0,6,Hinterlands\0302,0,0,7,Huntsman Markhor\0302,0,0,9,Jintha'alor\0303,0,0,14,Yayo'jin\031\031ITEM,19069,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,19070,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[785]="MINIMAL\031conclusion,conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030\030Seek out Lar Prowltusk on the western flank of Sen'jin Village.\030\030A Strategic Alliance\0313,1,63,2,384,1,0\0313140,2,1,Lar Prowltusk\031\031\031",[7850]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The dark energy that compels the Vilebranch has been lifted - for now. We must remain ever vigilant in our battle against evil, as even if the Vile Priestess is destroyed, another soon takes her place.\030The Vilebranch fight with supernatural ferocity. This is due to the foul magical weavings of the Vile Priestess Hexx.$B$BThroughout Jintha'alor you will find dark vessels of tainted blood. The vessels radiate the foul magic of the faceless blood God, empowering the Vilebranch and also driving them to madness.$B$BSteal those vessels and return them to me so that I may remove the taint and ultimately loosen the grip of the blood God.\030Primal Torntusk at Revantusk Village in the Hinterlands wants you to recover 10 Vessels of Tainted Blood from Jintha'alor. Return to Primal Torntusk when this task is complete.\030Be cautious in battling the Vilebranch, $N. Their minds are clouded - they fight to the death.\030Dark Vessels\0312,1,48,2,261,1,14736\0302,50,117,2,257,1,14736\0302,122,188,2,257,3,14736\0302,190,310,2,257,1,14736\0302,315,435,2,263,1,14736\0303,1,122,2,386,1,14736\0303,124,176,2,384,1,14736\0301,1,70,4,272,1,14736\0301,72,201,4,276,4,14736\0304,1,43,3,256,1,14736\0304,45,94,3,260,1,14736\0317995,2,2,Vile Priestess Hexx\030112,2,2,Priestess\03014736,2,6,Primal Torntusk\03014736,2,7,Primal Torntusk\030112,4,9,Priestess\0312,47,1425,0,\0302,0,0,6,Revantusk Village\0302,0,0,6,Hinterlands\0302,0,0,6,Jintha'alor\0302,0,0,7,Primal Torntusk\031\031ITEM,19071,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[786]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030objectiveLabel3\030objectiveLabel4\030requestItems\030title\031The Horde would surely prevail if the Kolkar centaurs were to attack. But by preventing such an attack. we have spared our mighty warriors unnecessary bloodshed.$B$BAnd as sure as there is sand in the Tanaris desert, we know that there will be blood spilled before these trying times are through.$B$BYou have served your people well, $C.\030Lower your voice, $c. The Kolkar centaurs lie just over the ridge to the west in Kolkar Crag.$B$BLast night while they were raiding, I snuck into their village and discovered that the dirty beasts have a three-tiered attack planned on the trolls and orcs of Durotar.$B$BWe mustn't let their invasion come to fruition. Perhaps you can muster the might needed to infiltrate Kolkar Crag and destroy their attack plans.$B$BLast I saw, they had divided them up amongst three of their leaders.\030Lar Prowltusk outside of Sen'jin Village wants you to destroy the 3 sets of Attack Plans held within Kolkar Crag.\030\030Attack Plan: Valley of Trials destroyed\030Attack Plan: Sen'jin Village destroyed\030Attack Plan: Orgrimmar destroyed\030The centaurs have proven to be a consistent nuisance to the Horde. Their intentions to lay siege to our homeland cannot be tolerated.\030Thwarting Kolkar Aggression\0312,1,21,2,257,1,3140\0302,23,93,2,257,1,3140\0302,98,266,2,261,1,3140\0302,271,317,2,261,1,3140\0302,319,415,2,261,4,3140\0302,420,487,2,257,1,3140\0303,1,113,2,390,1,3140\0301,1,69,4,276,4,3140