ys are neither understood nor appreciated by Zandalar but we are a fair people. Wear this brand around your neck. It shall serve as both a warning to our enemies and a symbol of your friendship to Zandalar.$B$BContinue to serve our people and I will amplify the power of the brand.\030\030\030\030The Heathen's Brand\0311,1,58,4,272,1,14902\0301,60,151,4,272,1,14902\0301,153,185,4,272,1,14902\0301,187,278,4,276,3,14902\0301,283,353,4,272,3,14902\031\0312,1977,0,0,\0304,0,0,4,Zandalar\0318046,23,8046,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[8046]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Do what you must to defeat our enemies, $c. Even if it means channeling the Light.$B$B<Jin'rokh shudders.>\030\030\030I may have been too hasty in my judgement, $c. It seems as if your blind faith in this Light has some value after all.$B$BGive me your brand and I shall amplify its power.\030The Heathen's Brand\0311,1,43,4,276,1,14902\0301,45,82,4,272,4,14902\0301,87,106,4,272,1,14902\0304,1,46,3,256,1,14902\0304,48,118,3,256,4,14902\0304,123,171,3,256,3,14902\031\0312,1977,0,0,\0318045,19,8045,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0308047,23,8047,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,19579,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8047]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Our beliefs differ but our cause is righteous. Strike down our foes, noble $c.\030\030\030I must confess, I did not think you had the resolution to see this cause through, $c. Zandalar now considers you an invaluable ally. Well done, indeed.$B$BGive me your brand and I shall once more amplify its power.\030The Heathen's Brand\0311,1,46,4,272,1,14902\0301,48,78,4,272,1,14902\0304,1,85,3,256,1,14902\0304,87,132,3,256,1,14902\0304,134,151,3,256,1,14902\0304,156,214,3,256,3,14902\031\0312,1977,0,0,\0318046,19,8046,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0308048,23,8048,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,19585,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8048]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Vigilance, honor, loyalty, bravery... You embody all of these traits and so shall your brand.\030\030\030The King has acknowledged your existence, $c. You are the first of your kind to be accepted by Rastakhan as a true ally of Zandalar.$B$BYou will be rewarded greatly for your efforts. Present your brand and I shall apply the final amplification.\030The Hero's Brand\0311,1,37,4,272,1,14902\0301,39,93,4,272,3,14902\0304,1,45,3,256,1,14902\0304,47,132,3,256,1,14902\0304,137,182,3,256,3,14902\0304,184,244,3,256,3,14902\031\0312,1977,0,0,\0318047,19,8047,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,19586,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8049]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Accept this talisman as a token of our appreciation, $c.$B$BThe Eye of Zuldazar will grow in power as your bond with the trolls of Zandalar strengthens. Return to me periodically and I shall imbue the jewel.\030\030\030\030The Eye of Zuldazar\0311,1,56,4,272,1,14903\0301,61,152,4,272,3,14903\0301,154,207,4,272,3,14903\0317903,4,3,Jewel\0312,1977,0,0,\0318050,23,8050,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[805]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hm... your report comes at a bad time. The Burning Blade is not seen here in Sen'jin, but their evil has taken seed off the coast, on the Echo Isles.$B$BThe orcs are friends of the Darkspear Trolls. Honorable friends. We want to help the orcs, but... we need help too.$B\030Your trials against the Burning Blade are finished... here in the Valley.  But I want you to report your findings.$B$BGo to the troll village of Sen'jin and seek out Master Gadrin.  Sen'jin Village is east out of the valley, then right at the fork.$B$BTell Gadrin of the Burning Blade, and that they have reached the Valley of Trials.  Discover from him if they have yet reached Sen'jin.$B$BGo, $N, and be swift.  I fear the evil found in the Burning Blade Coven is but the herald of a larger threat...\030Speak with Master Gadrin in Sen'jin Village.\030\030Report to Sen'jin Village\0312,1,53,2,257,1,3145\0302,55,73,2,257,1,3145\0302,76,114,2,259,1,3145\0302,119,180,2,259,1,3145\0302,183,248,2,257,1,3145\0302,253,334,2,257,1,3145\0302,337,387,2,257,4,3145\0302,392,412,2,257,1,3145\0302,415,502,2,261,1,3145\0303,1,44,2,384,1,3145\0301,7,38,4,272,1,3188\0301,40,149,4,272,1,3188\0301,154,198,4,272,1,3188\0301,200,217,4,272,1,3188\0301,219,250,4,274,1,3188\0301,252,268,4,274,1,3188\0313188,2,4,Master Gadrin\03014848,2,9,Herald\0303188,2,10,Master Gadrin\0312,363,1411,0,\0302,0,0,2,Valley\0302,0,0,9,Burning Blade Coven\0302,0,0,10,Sen'jin Village\0304,0,0,12,Sen'jin\031794,19,794,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[8050]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Be resolute in your endeavors, $n. The Soulflayer will attempt to siphon your will to live.\030\030\030Tales of your battles against the Gurubashi are whispered in the winds, priestess. Even royalty is beginning to talk of your deeds. It is rumored that King Rastakhan even mentioned you by name.$B$BThe time has come to imbue the Eye. Hand me the talisman and I shall perform the service.\030The Eye of Zuldazar\0311,1,34,4,272,1,14903\0301,36,91,4,272,3,14903\0304,1,82,3,256,1,14903\0304,84,131,3,256,1,14903\0304,133,193,3,256,1,14903\0304,198,232,3,256,1,14903\0304,234,286,3,256,3,14903\03111359,4,2,Soulflayer\03015047,3,3,Gurubashi\030112,3,3,Priestess\0312,1977,0,0,\0318049,19,8049,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0308051,23,8051,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,19591,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8051]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Continue in your battle against the Soulflayer and his minions, $n. He must never be permitted to leave the confines of Zul'Gurub.\030\030\030Welcome $c. The Eye of Zuldazar pulses with energy. You are ready to take the next step. Hand me the talisman and I shall perform the imbue.\030The Eye of Zuldazar\0311,1,67,4,276,1,14903\0301,69,130,4,272,1,14903\0304,1,11,3,256,1,14903\0304,13,51,3,256,1,14903\0304,53,88,3,256,1,14903\0304,90,140,3,256,3,14903\03111359,4,1,Soulflayer\0312,1977,0,0,\0318050,19,8050,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0308052,23,8052,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,19592,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8052]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Smite them all and let Hakkar sort them out...\030\030\030If only we had ten-thousand more like you, $n. The armies of Hakkar would be scattered to the wind in the blink of an eye.$B$B<Al'tabim sighs.>$B$BAlas, the Eye is ready to realize its full potential. Give it to me.\030The All-Seeing Eye of Zuldazar\0311,1,46,4,272,1,14903\0304,1,46,3,256,4,14903\0304,48,122,3,256,4,14903\0304,127,143,3,256,1,14903\0304,148,200,3,256,1,14903\0304,202,215,3,256,1,14903\03114834,4,1,Hakkar\03014834,3,3,Hakkar\0312,1977,0,0,\0318051,19,8051,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,19593,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8053]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You do much to honor us.  Your hands drip with the blood of Hakkar's minions.  You are a friend to the tribe.$B$BWear these bracers.  They are the freethinker's armguards.  This is what I mean about real power.\030You are a heathen.  Heathens have a place in the tribe.  Heathens are freethinkers of Zandalar.  Freethinkers do not fear oppression.  Freethinkers die for what they believe in.  We know you would die for what you believe in.  This earns our acknowledgement.  This earns you a chance to prove yourself further.$B$BWe must have the Paragons of Power.  Go to Zul'Gurub.  Kill the minions of Hakkar.  Return when you have what I seek.  Claim the first battle gear of a Zandalar freethinker.$B$BGo.\030Bring Jin'rokh the Breaker Primal Hakkari Bindings.  You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Friendly with the Zandalar Tribe.$B$BJin'rokh the Breaker is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\030You have returned?  Do you have the Paragons of Power?  Are you wasting my time?$B$BI hope not, heathen.\030Paragons of Power: The Freethinker's Armguards\0312,1,18,2,257,1,14902\0302,21,55,2,257,1,14902\0302,58,95,2,257,1,14902\0302,98,133,2,257,1,14902\0302,136,177,2,257,4,14902\0302,180,225,2,257,4,14902\0302,228,258,2,257,1,14902\0302,261,310,2,257,1,14902\0302,315,349,2,257,1,14902\0302,352,367,2,257,1,14902\0302,370,396,2,257,1,14902\0302,399,431,2,259,1,14902\0302,434,487,2,261,1,14902\0303,1,51,2,384,1,14902\0303,54,143,2,384,1,14902\0303,148,215,2,384,1,14902\0301,1,24,4,272,1,14902\0301,27,77,4,272,1,14902\0301,80,109,4,272,1,14902\0301,114,132,4,272,1,14902\0301,135,171,4,272,1,14902\0301,174,210,4,272,1,14902\0304,1,18,3,256,2,14902\0304,21,54,3,256,2,14902\0304,57,80,3,256,2,14902\0304,85,104,3,258,3,14902\03114834,2,11,Hakkar\03014902,2,14,Jin'rokh the Breaker\03014902,2,16,Jin'rokh the Breaker\0312,19,1434,0,\0302,0,0,10,Zul'Gurub\031\031ITEM,19716,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,270,OBJECTIVE,3000,16,",[8054]="PARTIAL\031consequences,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Your honor is assured in the tribe.  You claim many deaths in Zul'Gurub.  Enemies fall before your convictions.  Enemies fall before your power.$B$BThis is the freethinker's belt.  It is a symbol of honor.  It is powerful mojo.  It is now yours.\030Your beliefs are alien to us, heathen.  Ancient Zandalar were once branded as heretics.  This was when the Gurubashi Empire was strong.  Heathens dared to challenge the priest of Hakkar.  Heathens then were hunted and killed as vermin.  Those heathens never wavered in their fight against the Blood God.  We honor the price they paid.  They are the freethinkers.$B$BDestroy the minions of Hakkar in Zul'Gurub.  Bring me the Paragons of Power I seek.  Success will be greatly rewarded.$B$BGo.\030Bring Jin'rokh the Breaker a Primal Hakkari Shawl.  You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Honored with the Zandalar Tribe.$B$BJin'rokh the Breaker is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\030Your presence means victory?  Do you have the Paragons?  Are you dripping in the remains of your enemies?\030Paragons of Power: The Freethinker's Belt\0312,1,38,2,257,1,14902\0302,41,87,2,321,1,14902\0302,90,135,2,257,1,14902\0302,138,186,2,257,1,14902\0302,189,235,2,257,1,14902\0302,238,303,2,261,1,14902\0302,306,334,2,257,1,14902\0302,337,362,2,257,1,14902\0302,367,409,2,261,1,14902\0302,412,449,2,259,1,14902\0302,452,484,2,257,3,14902\0303,1,50,2,384,1,14902\0303,53,141,2,384,1,14902\0303,146,213,2,384,1,14902\0301,1,35,4,272,1,14902\0301,38,72,4,272,1,14902\0301,75,111,4,276,1,14902\0301,114,144,4,276,1,14902\0301,149,179,4,272,1,14902\0301,182,205,4,272,1,14902\0301,208,227,4,272,1,14902\0301,230,245,4,272,1,14902\0304,1,28,3,256,2,14902\0304,31,55,3,256,2,14902\0304,58,105,3,260,2,14902\03115047,2,3,Gurubashi\030111,2,4,Priest\03014834,2,4,Hakkar\03014834,2,9,Hakkar\03014902,2,12,Jin'rokh the Breaker\03014902,2,14,Jin'rokh the Breaker\0312,19,1434,0,\0302,0,0,9,Zul'Gurub\0304,0,0,16,Zul'Gurub\031\031ITEM,19721,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,270,OBJECTIVE,9000,16,",[8055]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have done what few ever could.  You have brought the minions of Hakkar to their knees.  You have shown them what a freethinker can do.  You have shown us how a heretic could be revered in the tribe.  You have more than real power.  You ARE real power.$B$BTake the breastplate, freethinker.  Crush those who oppose you.\030Battle gear gives you power in the tribe.  The freethinkers are honored in this way.  They are zealots.  They imbue their breastplates with powerful mojo.  If their beliefs falter in the face of the enemy, their breastplate will not.$B$BYou must be revered amongst us to possess such a breastplate.  Go to Zul'Gurub.  Take the Paragons of Power I need.  Take the Paragons most painfully from the fools inside.  Bring them to me.  Prove your worth as a freethinker once and for all.\030Bring Jin'rokh the Breaker a Primal Hakkari Tabard.  You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Revered with the Zandalar Tribe.$B$BJin'rokh the Breaker is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\030Do you have the Paragons?  They have mojo inside them.  We must have them.  You will aid us.\030Paragons of Power: The Freethinker's Breastplate\0312,1,41,2,261,1,14902\0302,44,84,2,257,1,14902\0302,87,103,2,257,1,14902\0302,106,154,2,257,1,14902\0302,157,233,2,261,4,14902\0302,238,298,2,257,1,14902\0302,301,316,2,257,1,14902\0302,319,352,2,259,1,14902\0302,355,409,2,257,1,14902\0302,412,428,2,257,1,14902\0302,431,481,2,257,1,14902\0303,1,51,2,384,1,14902\0303,54,142,2,384,1,14902\0303,147,214,2,384,1,14902\0301,1,34,4,272,4,14902\0301,37,90,4,272,1,14902\0301,93,138,4,272,1,14902\0301,141,202,4,272,4,14902\0301,205,234,4,272,1,14902\0301,237,255,4,272,1,14902\0301,260,293,4,272,1,14902\0301,296,322,4,272,1,14902\0304,1,25,3,256,2,14902\0304,28,54,3,256,1,14902\0304,57,74,3,256,1,14902\0304,77,92,3,256,3,14902\03114902,2,12,Jin'rokh the Breaker\03014902,2,14,Jin'rokh the Breaker\03014834,4,16,Hakkar\0312,19,1434,0,\0302,0,0,7,Zul'Gurub\031\031ITEM,19722,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,270,OBJECTIVE,21000,16,",[8056]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It seems ya got a bit of the Zandalar augur in ya.  We know about the deeds you've been doin' in Zul'Gurub on our behalf mon.  These Paragons of Power will go a long way to helpin' out the Zandalar tribe - a tribe, I might add, ya can call upon as friends.  Take these bracers, $N; ya earned them and then some!\030The augurs of our tribe are revered for their gifts of the divine sight, ya mon.  They ain't a witch doctor; they spend their time castin' bones or readin' the leaves for insight - not hexin' people.  As a shaman, you already know somethin' about the power of augury; we Zandalar prize the insight they give to the tribe.$B$BBring me an offerin' of the Paragons of Power from inside Zul'Gurub and prove your worth to us.  Do this for us, and I'll give ya some bracers that our augurs prize above all others!\030Bring Maywiki of Zuldazar a Primal Hakkari Armsplint.  You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Friendly with the Zandalar Tribe.$B$BMaywiki of Zuldazar is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\030Got the Paragons of Power from Zul'Gurub that I need?  These bracers are well worth any effort ya be needin' to make!\030Paragons of Power: The Augur's Bracers\0312,1,80,2,257,1,14904\0302,83,199,2,257,1,14904\0302,202,321,2,257,1,14904\0302,326,420,2,257,1,14904\0302,423,507,2,257,1,14904\0303,1,53,2,384,1,14904\0303,56,145,2,384,1,14904\0303,150,216,2,384,1,14904\0301,1,50,4,272,4,14904\0301,53,125,4,272,1,14904\0301,128,256,4,272,4,14904\0301,259,311,4,272,1,14904\0304,1,53,3,258,2,14904\0304,56,117,3,256,1,14904\03114904,2,6,Maywiki of Zuldazar\03014904,2,8,Maywiki of Zuldazar\0312,19,1434,0,\0304,0,0,10,Zul'Gurub\0303,0,0,13,Zul'Gurub\031\031ITEM,19717,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,270,OBJECTIVE,3000,16,",[8057]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, I can sense the power comin' from these Paragons of Power, $N.  Ya proved to be someone we in the tribe can call \"friend.\"  A deal is a deal, $N... behold the power of the haruspex's bracers!\030A haruspex is a key member of our tribe; you'll be wise to listen to their portents.  By communion with animals and givin' them up to the spirits when needed, they give us divine guidance.  In times past, the haruspex's insight and wisdom gave us an edge in the wars against the splintered tribes of the Gurubashi.$B$BBring me an offerin' of the Paragons of Power from inside Zul'Gurub and prove your worth to us.  Do this, and I'll give ya bracers that any haruspex of the Zandalar would want.\030Bring Maywiki of Zuldazar a Primal Hakkari Stanchion.  You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Friendly with the Zandalar Tribe.$B$BMaywiki of Zuldazar is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\030Have ya got the Paragons of Power from Zul'Gurub?  These bracers are worth the effort, $N.  Trust me mon!\030Paragons of Power: The Haruspex's Bracers\0312,1,84,2,257,1,14904\0302,87,188,2,257,1,14904\0302,191,314,2,257,1,14904\0302,319,413,2,257,1,14904\0302,416,494,2,259,4,14904\0303,1,53,2,384,1,14904\0303,56,145,2,384,1,14904\0303,150,216,2,384,1,14904\0301,1,66,4,272,1,14904\0301,69,151,4,272,1,14904\0301,153,195,4,272,1,14904\0304,1,49,3,256,2,14904\0304,52,90,3,256,1,14904\0304,93,105,3,256,1,14904\03115047,2,3,Gurubashi\03014904,2,6,Maywiki of Zuldazar\03014904,2,8,Maywiki of Zuldazar\0312,19,1434,0,\0303,0,0,12,Zul'Gurub\031\031ITEM,19718,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,270,OBJECTIVE,3000,16,",[8058]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You have wrought much vengeance today.  You have taken on the visage of the vindicator.  You have brought the Blood God's minions to their knees.$B$BTake this.  It will fuel your vengeance for the future.  You are a friend to the Zandalar now.\030Vengeance is power.  The Zandalar vindicator is such power.  The tribe has many enemies.  The vindicator exacts retribution on them.  No crime against us is unpunished.  The vindicator delivers this punishment.  Our enemies fear our vengeance.  They should.  They forever will.$B$BBecome one of our vindicators.  Seek the Paragons of Power inside Zul'Gurub.  Slay the minions of Hakkar and claim vengeance in the tribe's name.  You will be rewarded.\030Bring Jin'rokh the Breaker a Primal Hakkari Armsplint.  You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Friendly with the Zandalar Tribe.$B$BJin'rokh the Breaker is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\030Have you brought the Paragons of Power?  Has vengeance been claimed in the name of the Zandalar?\030Paragons of Power: The Vindicator's Armguards\0312,1,19,2,259,1,14902\0302,22,59,2,257,1,14902\0302,62,88,2,261,1,14902\0302,91,132,2,257,1,14902\0302,135,168,2,257,1,14902\0302,171,210,2,257,1,14902\0302,213,243,2,263,1,14902\0302,246,257,2,257,1,14902\0302,260,277,2,257,3,14902\0302,282,311,2,257,1,14902\0302,314,357,2,257,1,14902\0302,360,426,2,259,1,14902\0302,429,449,2,257,3,14902\0303,1,54,2,384,1,14902\0303,57,146,2,384,1,14902\0303,151,218,2,384,1,14902\0301,1,38,4,274,1,14902\0301,41,87,4,272,1,14902\0301,90,145,4,272,1,14902\0301,150,159,4,272,1,14902\0301,162,204,4,274,3,14902\0301,207,243,4,272,1,14902\0304,1,39,3,256,2,14902\0304,42,96,3,258,2,14902\03114834,2,12,Hakkar\03014902,2,14,Jin'rokh the Breaker\03014902,2,16,Jin'rokh the Breaker\0312,19,1434,0,\0304,0,0,22,Zandalar\031\031ITEM,19717,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,270,OBJECTIVE,3000,16,",[8059]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done... no doubt they were made to pay in excruciating ways before they gave up the Paragons of Power.  Take this - the demoniac's wraps.  Made from powerful mojo used in summoning the demoniac's prey, it is a powerful tool in your acquisition of power.\030Warlocks tread dangerous ground in dealing with demons, but our demoniacs take this one step further.  Through an ancient and arcane ritual, they allow a demon to enter their being.  Rather than let it possess them though, they enslave the demon from the inside, absorbing the power of the beast for their own command.  It is a feat few are ever able to master.$B$BFor you to learn of the power of the demoniac, I must have Paragons of Power from Zul'Gurub.  Go there and retrieve that which we seek.\030Bring Al'tabim the All-Seeing a Primal Hakkari Stanchion.  You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Friendly with the Zandalar Tribe.$B$BAl'tabim the All-Seeing is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\030Have you returned with the Paragons of Power?  By defeating the diabolic minions of the Hakkar, you will not only prove yourself to us, but also your willingness to learn the ways of the demoniac.\030Paragons of Power: The Demoniac's Wraps\0312,1,101,2,257,1,14903\0302,104,181,2,321,1,14903\0302,184,318,2,257,1,14903\0302,321,361,2,257,1,14903\0302,366,457,2,257,1,14903\0302,460,500,2,259,1,14903\0303,1,57,2,384,1,14903\0303,60,149,2,384,1,14903\0303,154,224,2,384,1,14903\0301,1,12,4,272,1,14903\0301,14,107,4,280,1,14903\0301,110,142,4,272,1,14903\0301,145,258,4,272,1,14903\0304,1,45,3,256,2,14903\0304,48,196,3,256,3,14903\03110430,2,3,The Beast\03014903,2,7,Al'tabim the All-Seeing\03014903,2,9,Al'tabim the All-Seeing\03014834,3,15,Hakkar\0312,19,1434,0,\0302,0,0,5,Zul'Gurub\031\031ITEM,19718,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,270,OBJECTIVE,3000,16,",[806]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Aha! You got him!$B$BYou do your clan proud, $N. And because of you, Durotar is free of one more agent of evil.\030We cannot allow the Burning Blade a foothold in Durotar!  We must destroy them before their evil festers!$B$BI have undergone my own investigations and found that a Burning Blade warlock, the goblin Fizzle Darkstorm, has camped within Thunder Ridge to the northwest.  There he and his cultist minions spread chaos.$B$BFind and defeat Fizzle, and bring me his dead claw!\030Bring Fizzle's Claw to Orgnil Soulscar in Razor Hill.\030Did you find Fizzle, $N? He, and rest of the Burning Blade, must be scoured from our lands!\030Dark Storms\0312,1,56,2,265,1,3142\0302,59,105,2,261,1,3142\0302,110,266,2,257,1,3142\0302,269,314,2,257,1,3142\0302,319,369,2,257,1,3142\0303,1,53,2,384,1,3142\0301,1,4,4,272,1,3142\0301,6,17,4,272,1,3142\0301,22,48,4,272,1,3142\0301,50,111,4,274,1,3142\0304,1,24,3,256,2,3142\0304,26,91,3,256,1,3142\0313203,2,3,Fizzle Darkstorm\0303142,2,6,Orgnil Soulscar\0312,14,1411,0,\0302,0,0,1,Durotar\0302,0,0,3,Thunder Ridge\0302,0,0,6,Orgnil Soulscar\0302,0,0,6,Razor Hill\031823,19,823,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030828,23,828,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4869,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8060]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Impressive... could you feel the mojo flowing through them?  The Paragons of Power were used as currency of sorts back when the Gurubashi Empire ruled these lands.  Now we Zandalar will use the latent mojo inside of them to fight the second rise of the Blood God Hakkar!$B$BYou've done well today - consider yourself to have a friend in the Zandalar.  For that, here are the illusionist's wraps I promised!\030Mages in our tribe are known as illusionists.  They employ powerful mojo in their incantations, often befuddling and confusing the tribe's enemies!$B$B<Al'tabim laughs wickedly.>$B$BIt is quite the sight to see a powerful illusionist at work, bringing our enemies to their knees from their own madness!$B$BFor you to know the way of our illusionists, go to Zul'Gurub and bring back to me selected Paragons of Power.  For this, I will give you arm wraps our illusionists use to weave their spells.\030Bring Al'tabim the All-Seeing Primal Hakkari Bindings.  You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Friendly with the Zandalar Tribe.$B$BAl'tabim the All-Seeing is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\030$N - you've returned already?  Were you able to get the Paragons of Power I need?\030Paragons of Power: The Illusionist's Wraps\0312,1,45,2,257,1,14903\0302,48,147,2,261,1,14903\0302,152,178,2,257,1,14903\0302,183,302,2,261,1,14903\0302,307,415,2,257,1,14903\0302,418,496,2,257,3,14903\0303,1,54,2,384,1,14903\0303,57,146,2,384,1,14903\0303,151,221,2,384,1,14903\0301,1,13,4,272,1,14903\0301,15,59,4,272,4,14903\0301,62,163,4,272,1,14903\0301,166,270,4,276,3,14903\0301,275,350,4,272,1,14903\0301,353,406,4,272,1,14903\0304,1,29,3,256,2,14903\0304,32,81,3,258,2,14903\03114903,2,7,Al'tabim the All-Seeing\03014903,2,9,Al'tabim the All-Seeing\03015047,4,12,Gurubashi\03014834,4,13,Hakkar\0312,19,1434,0,\0302,0,0,5,Zul'Gurub\0304,0,0,14,Zandalar\031\031ITEM,19716,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,270,OBJECTIVE,3000,16,",[8061]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Outstanding, $N!  This was no small feat bringing these to me.  No doubt you've acted as our tribe's confessor today in preserving ourselves against the threat of Hakkar.  These wraps are befitting a friend of the tribe such as you!\030We Zandalar invest power in those who speak with the authority of divinity.  Our priests are more than just healers - they are our confessors.  Evil comes both from outside threats - such as Hakkar - and from within the tribe.  Our confessors act as the judges amongst us, preserving us from the same evil that devoured the Gurubashi from inside itself.$B$BGo to Zul'Gurub and bring back the Paragons of Power from the Gurubashi.  Learn what it means to be the confessor, and preserve us from evil.\030Bring Al'tabim the All-Seeing a Primal Hakkari Stanchion.  You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Friendly with the Zandalar Tribe.$B$BAl'tabim the All-Seeing is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\030Back from Zul'Gurub, are you?  Have you succeeded in retrieving the Paragons of Power from the minions of Hakkar?\030Paragons of Power: The Confessor's Wraps\0312,1,75,2,257,1,14903\0302,78,142,2,257,1,14903\0302,145,226,2,257,1,14903\0302,229,353,2,257,1,14903\0302,358,429,2,257,1,14903\0302,432,498,2,257,1,14903\0303,1,57,2,384,1,14903\0303,60,149,2,384,1,14903\0303,154,224,2,384,1,14903\0301,1,16,4,272,1,14903\0301,19,62,4,272,1,14903\0301,65,170,4,276,1,14903\0301,173,232,4,272,1,14903\0304,1,29,3,256,2,14903\0304,32,113,3,256,2,14903\03114834,2,3,Hakkar\03015047,2,4,Gurubashi\03015047,2,5,Gurubashi\03014903,2,7,Al'tabim the All-Seeing\03014903,2,9,Al'tabim the All-Seeing\03014834,4,12,Hakkar\03014834,3,15,Hakkar\0312,19,1434,0,\0302,0,0,5,Zul'Gurub\0302,0,0,5,Gurubashi\0303,0,0,14,Zul'Gurub\031\031ITEM,19718,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,270,OBJECTIVE,3000,16,",[8062]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes... I need no vision to sense the presence of the Paragons of Power.  Your success in Zul'Gurub has impressed many among the tribe.  We not only consider you to be a friend of the Zandalar, but also consider you worthy enough to possess the predator's bracers - powerful items, and a symbol of what it means to be a predator.  Well done, $N.\030In the dark times after the fall of the Gurubashi Empire, Zandalar predators used their prowess to provide sustenance for the tribe.  Hunters claim to be much like our tribe's predators - to seek the hunt is to embody the essence of the predator, yes.  Your hunt in Zul'Gurub, however, will show us how you truly rate amongst our finest predators.$B$BBring to me a sampling of the Paragons of Power from within Zul'Gurub.  Do so, and you'll take first steps in becoming the penultimate predator.\030Bring the following Paragons of Power from Zul'Gurub to Falthir the Sightless: A Primal Hakkari Bindings.  You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Friendly with the Zandalar Tribe.$B$BFalthir the Sightless is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\030Hunt those in Zul'Gurub that would possess the Paragons of Power, $N.  They are your prey; they possess that which we both must have.\030Paragons of Power: The Predator's Bracers\0312,1,132,2,257,1,14905\0302,135,251,2,259,1,14905\0302,254,347,2,257,3,14905\0302,352,421,2,257,1,14905\0302,424,495,2,257,1,14905\0303,1,105,2,384,1,14905\0303,108,197,2,384,1,14905\0303,202,270,2,384,1,14905\0301,1,6,4,272,1,14905\0301,8,71,4,274,1,14905\0301,74,134,4,272,1,14905\0301,137,328,4,272,1,14905\0301,331,344,4,272,1,14905\0304,1,69,3,256,4,14905\0304,72,133,3,256,1,14905\03115047,2,1,Gurubashi\03014905,2,6,Falthir the Sightless\03014905,2,8,Falthir the Sightless\0312,19,1434,0,\0302,0,0,3,Zul'Gurub\0302,0,0,4,Zul'Gurub\0302,0,0,6,Zul'Gurub\0302,0,0,6,Falthir the Sightless\0304,0,0,11,Zul'Gurub\0303,0,0,14,Zul'Gurub\031\031ITEM,19716,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,270,OBJECTIVE,3000,16,",[8063]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $N... your accomplishments in Zul'Gurub have earned you the right to call the Zandalar tribe as a friend.  I will see to the disposition of the Paragons; for your effort please accept this reward!\030The madcaps of Zandalar are similar to rogues, but above all else they embrace madness... chaos... the unpredictability of existence.  A terror to behold on the battlefield, they sowed the seeds of confusion and mayhem amongst our enemies in the savage times after the tribes splintered.  We would not be here today without them.$B$BBring to me the Paragons of Power from Zul'Gurub that I seek, and I will grant you the first of the madcap's prized armors.  Embrace the madness!\030Bring Falthir the Sightless a Primal Hakkari Armsplint.  You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Friendly with the Zandalar Tribe.$B$BFalthir the Sightless is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\030Seek the madness from within Zul'Gurub and overshadow it with your own, $N!  To do so means success, and success means reward!  Let not the Blood God reign supreme again!\030Paragons of Power: The Madcap's Bracers\0312,1,89,2,257,1,14905\0302,91,98,2,257,1,14905\0302,100,133,2,257,1,14905\0302,136,287,2,261,1,14905\0302,290,329,2,257,4,14905\0302,334,456,2,259,3,14905\0302,459,478,2,257,1,14905\0303,1,55,2,384,1,14905\0303,58,147,2,384,1,14905\0303,152,220,2,384,1,14905\0301,1,16,4,272,1,14905\0301,18,116,4,272,1,14905\0301,119,207,4,272,3,14905\0304,1,75,3,256,1,14905\0304,78,126,3,256,1,14905\0304,129,170,3,256,1,14905\03114905,2,8,Falthir the Sightless\03014905,2,10,Falthir the Sightless\0312,19,1434,0,\0302,0,0,6,Zul'Gurub\0304,0,0,12,Zul'Gurub\0303,0,0,14,Zul'Gurub\031\031ITEM,19717,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,270,OBJECTIVE,3000,16,",[8064]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I thank you - the latent power in these items will be treasures unto themselves, you betcha.  Not only have ya done as I've asked of ya, but you've also proven to be honorable to us here in the tribe.  As promised, here is your reward!\030We Zandalar know not of druidic ways; nature is to be shaped by our need, not the other way around.  Still, a haruspex is the one of us most in tune with nature, and rightly so.  To give up the ghost of a beastie is to know what it is to be one of them.  That is the real power of nature.$B$BBring me an offerin' of the Paragons of Power from inside Zul'Gurub, proving yourself to us.  Do this, and I'll give ya a powerful item - a belt used by many of the Zandalar's haruspices.$B$BStrong mojo, ya mon!\030Bring Maywiki of Zuldazar a Primal Hakkari Sash.  Maywiki of Zuldazar is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale. You must also be Honored with Zandalar.\030Got the Paragons of Power from Zul'Gurub I need?  The haruspex's belt will be yours if ya have them.\030Paragons of Power: The Haruspex's Belt\0312,1,99,2,259,1,14904\0302,102,177,2,257,1,14904\0302,180,253,2,257,1,14904\0302,256,288,2,257,1,14904\0302,293,384,2,257,1,14904\0302,387,479,2,257,1,14904\0302,484,503,2,257,1,14904\0303,1,48,2,384,1,14904\0303,51,117,2,384,1,14904\0303,119,157,2,384,1,14904\0301,1,92,4,272,3,14904\0301,95,200,4,272,1,14904\0301,203,235,4,272,1,14904\0304,1,48,3,258,2,14904\0304,51,100,3,256,4,14904\03114904,2,8,Maywiki of Zuldazar\03014904,2,9,Maywiki of Zuldazar\0312,19,1434,0,\0303,0,0,14,Zul'Gurub\031\031ITEM,19720,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,270,OBJECTIVE,9000,16,",[8065]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Impressive... you've successfully collected the required Paragons of Power, $N.  Your accomplishments in Zul'Gurub for the Zandalar are legendary; hence forth, you'll be revered amongst the tribe.  Here is your tunic, mighty $C!\030The ultimate symbol of a haruspex's power is what they wear, $N.  Of these, the tunic symbolizes the connection between themselves and the divine wisdom they seek.  It often weaves parts of the beasties they sacrifice into the tunic; this reminds them of the connection they have to their gifts.$B$BBring me an offerin' of the Paragons of Power from inside Zul'Gurub and prove your worth to us.  Do this, and a tunic seeping with the true power of a haruspex is yours.\030Bring Maywiki of Zuldazar a Primal Hakkari Tabard.  Maywiki of Zuldazar is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale. You must also be Revered with Zandalar.\030Got the necessary Paragons of Power from Zul'Gurub?  The haruspex's tunic is well worth any effort ya be needin' to make.\030Paragons of Power: The Haruspex's Tunic\0312,1,64,2,257,1,14904\0302,67,163,2,259,1,14904\0302,166,295,2,257,1,14904\0302,300,394,2,257,1,14904\0302,397,468,2,257,1,14904\0303,1,50,2,384,1,14904\0303,53,119,2,384,1,14904\0303,121,159,2,384,1,14904\0301,1,13,4,272,1,14904\0301,15,79,4,272,1,14904\0301,82,196,4,272,1,14904\0301,199,228,4,272,1,14904\0304,1,51,3,256,2,14904\0304,54,121,3,256,1,14904\03114904,2,6,Maywiki of Zuldazar\03014904,2,7,Maywiki of Zuldazar\0312,19,1434,0,\0304,0,0,11,Zul'Gurub\0303,0,0,13,Zul'Gurub\031\031ITEM,19722,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,270,OBJECTIVE,21000,16,",[8066]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I sensed your arrival moments before, $N, but none too easily.  What revealed yourself to me were the Paragons of Power you brought.  I can feel the power without needing to see the trinkets; their latent mojo - raw magic, if you will - will continue to fuel our efforts of vanquishing the diabolic schemes of the Blood God Hakkar.$B$BYou are to be commended - and rewarded - for your success.  You are honored amongst the tribe, and you are worthy to wear the predator's belt.\030A predator knows how to stalk their prey, but a successful one knows how to strike at it once they have closed ranks.  You must master both to have any chance of success in Zul'Gurub... and any chance of being like the Zandalar predators.$B$BBring me choice parts of the Paragons of Power from within Zul'Gurub.  My reward will be the power that the trinkets yield, while yours will be the Zandalar predator's belt - equipment well worth the trade.\030Bring the following Paragons of Power from Zul'Gurub to Falthir the Sightless: A Primal Hakkari Shawl.  You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Honored with the Zandalar Tribe.$B$BFalthir the Sightless is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\030Strike at the insane minions of Hakkar in Zul'Gurub - they are the ones that hold the Paragons of Power, $N.  Prove your success to them - and to the tribe - as an aspirant to the predator.\030Paragons of Power: The Predator's Belt\0312,1,117,2,257,1,14905\0302,120,185,2,257,1,14905\0302,187,238,2,257,1,14905\0302,243,311,2,257,1,14905\0302,314,448,2,257,3,14905\0303,1,102,2,384,1,14905\0303,105,193,2,384,1,14905\0303,198,266,2,384,1,14905\0301,1,62,4,272,1,14905\0301,65,132,4,272,1,14905\0301,135,331,4,272,4,14905\0301,336,393,4,272,1,14905\0301,396,477,4,272,1,14905\0304,1,108,3,256,1,14905\0304,111,189,3,256,1,14905\03114905,2,6,Falthir the Sightless\03014905,2,8,Falthir the Sightless\03014834,4,11,Hakkar\03014834,3,14,Hakkar\0312,19,1434,0,\0302,0,0,2,Zul'Gurub\0302,0,0,4,Zul'Gurub\0302,0,0,6,Zul'Gurub\0302,0,0,6,Falthir the Sightless\0303,0,0,14,Zul'Gurub\031\031ITEM,19721,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,270,OBJECTIVE,9000,16,",[8067]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Success... you are to be revered amongst the tribe, $N.  It was no small feat acquiring the Paragons of Power needed for the mantle, but you handled it in the fashion of the deadliest of our predators.  You've earned your place amongst them, and you've certainly earned the right to wear their mantle.\030We Zandalar prize what we wear as a symbol of accomplishment.  You don't need to be able to see what one wears to be able to sense what emanates from it - power transcends sight.  The garments of the Zandalar predator are like this, and most cherished by them is the mantle they wear.  It helps to obfuscate them from view... and to make their presence known when they wish it.$B$BThe Paragons of Power await your retrieval in Zul'Gurub.  Bring me what I seek, and the predator's mantle shall be yours.\030Bring the following Paragons of Power from Zul'Gurub to Falthir the Sightless: A Primal Hakkari Aegis.  You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Revered with the Zandalar Tribe.$B$BFalthir the Sightless is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\030Have your strikes into Zul'Gurub yielded success, $N?  Only when you've brought me what I seek - and proven yourself fully to the tribe - will you earn a mantle second to none amongst the Zandalar.\030Paragons of Power: The Predator's Mantle\0312,1,61,2,257,1,14905\0302,64,178,2,257,1,14905\0302,181,284,2,257,1,14905\0302,287,325,2,257,1,14905\0302,327,377,2,259,3,14905\0302,382,437,2,257,1,14905\0302,440,502,2,259,3,14905\0303,1,102,2,384,1,14905\0303,105,193,2,384,1,14905\0303,198,266,2,384,1,14905\0301,1,10,4,272,1,14905\0301,12,55,4,272,1,14905\0301,58,201,4,272,1,14905\0301,204,301,4,272,1,14905\0304,1,53,3,256,2,14905\0304,56,197,3,258,3,14905\03114905,2,8,Falthir the Sightless\03014905,2,10,Falthir the Sightless\0312,19,1434,0,\0302,0,0,6,Zul'Gurub\0302,0,0,8,Zul'Gurub\0302,0,0,8,Falthir the Sightless\031\031ITEM,19724,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,270,OBJECTIVE,21000,16,",[8068]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Success!  You shall be honored in the tribe from here on!  Zul'Gurub has certainly tasted the might of the Zandalar today, thanks to you $N.$B$BWith the tribe's blessing, take the Zandalar illusionist's mantle.  May it serve you well.\030Magic is a raw, primal force to be shaped by those strong enough to do it.  Mojo is our extension of this power; one such potent manipulation of it is in the form of illusion.  How can one truly hope to win against a foe that is not even really there?  We Zandalar know the power of this, and as such illusionists hold a honored place within the tribe.$B$BTake the needed Paragons of Power from Zul'Gurub - for this, honor from the tribe and a powerful mantle used by our best illusionists will be yours!\030Bring Al'tabim the All-Seeing a Primal Hakkari Shawl.  You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Honored with the Zandalar Tribe.$B$BAl'tabim the All-Seeing is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\030How was your foray into Zul'Gurub?  Did you drive your enemies mad through the power of illusion?  Illusion or not, their deaths - and the Paragons of Power taken from them - will help thwart the rise of Hakkar.\030Paragons of Power: The Illusionist's Mantle\0312,1,74,2,257,1,14903\0302,77,175,2,257,1,14903\0302,178,251,2,259,2,14903\0302,254,352,2,257,1,14903\0302,357,504,2,257,3,14903\0303,1,53,2,384,1,14903\0303,56,144,2,384,1,14903\0303,149,219,2,384,1,14903\0301,1,8,4,272,1,14903\0301,11,57,4,272,3,14903\0301,60,140,4,272,4,14903\0301,145,210,4,272,1,14903\0301,213,234,4,272,1,14903\0304,1,34,3,256,2,14903\0304,37,97,3,260,2,14903\0304,100,211,3,256,3,14903\03114903,2,6,Al'tabim the All-Seeing\03014903,2,8,Al'tabim the All-Seeing\03014834,3,16,Hakkar\0312,19,1434,0,\0302,0,0,5,Zul'Gurub\031\031ITEM,19721,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,270,OBJECTIVE,9000,16,",[8069]="PARTIAL\031consequences,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031At last, someone worthy to wear the illusionist's robe!  Your success in Zul'Gurub has assured your reverences amongst the tribe for ages to come.  Wear it with pride, $N!\030The tribe acknowledges station and power through what we wear.  Our vestments are made from the finest of materials, and interwoven with the mojo we use to make us powerful.  Illusionists are no exception; their robes are said to embody the essence of illusion in their look.  Legend states that their ancient robes never looked the same twice.$B$BI will give you an illusionist's robe, $N... but earn your place of reverence among the tribe first!  Bring me the Paragons of Power from Zul'Gurub!\030Bring Al'tabim the All-Seeing a Primal Hakkari Kossack.  You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Revered with the Zandalar Tribe.$B$BAl'tabim the All-Seeing is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\030Have you returned with the Paragons of Power we need?  I know it will not be easy... but I have long predicted an outsider would come to aid us in our fight against Hakkar.  Let it be you, I say!\030Paragons of Power: The Illusionist's Robes\0312,1,62,2,257,1,14903\0302,65,173,2,257,1,14903\0302,176,275,2,257,1,14903\0302,278,344,2,321,1,14903\0302,349,392,2,257,3,14903\0302,394,448,2,257,1,14903\0302,451,496,2,257,1,14903\0303,1,55,2,384,1,14903\0303,58,146,2,384,1,14903\0303,151,221,2,384,1,14903\0301,1,55,4,272,1,14903\0301,58,146,4,272,1,14903\0301,149,171,4,272,1,14903\0304,1,53,3,258,2,14903\0304,56,84,3,256,3,14903\0304,86,172,3,260,4,14903\0304,175,195,3,256,1,14903\03114903,2,8,Al'tabim the All-Seeing\03014903,2,10,Al'tabim the All-Seeing\03014834,3,16,Hakkar\0312,19,1434,0,\0302,0,0,7,Zul'Gurub\0304,0,0,12,Zul'Gurub\031\031ITEM,19723,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,270,OBJECTIVE,21000,16,",[8070]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Success!  These will go a long way to building up our power against the rise of Hakkar.  With your help, we've taken a significant step in ensuring that the Blood God will not destroy us all.$B$BYou've earned honor with the tribe today, $N.  Take this - the confessor's bindings - as a symbol of our thanks.\030Shortly after the fall of the Gurubashi, we Zandalar almost succumbed to a final defeat from evil within our own tribe.  It was then that the confessors amongst us arose, preserving the tribe by banishing out those who would destroy their own kind.  They not only keep us in tune with the spirits, but they also preserve the flesh.$B$BGo forth into Zul'Gurub and witness first hand the depravity of Hakkar and the Gurubashi.  Wrest the Paragons of Power that we seek from them; success will be rewarded!\030Bring Al'tabim the All-Seeing a Primal Hakkari Sash.  You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Honored with the Zandalar Tribe.$B$BAl'tabim the All-Seeing is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\030The Paragons of Power... do you have them?  Only when we have them will we be able to make use of the latent power stored inside them.  It will be good to turn the tables on the minions of the Blood God...\030Paragons of Power: The Confessor's Bindings\0312,1,119,2,257,1,14903\0302,122,248,2,261,4,14903\0302,251,331,2,257,1,14903\0302,336,424,2,257,1,14903\0302,427,503,2,259,3,14903\0303,1,52,2,384,1,14903\0303,55,143,2,384,1,14903\0303,148,218,2,384,1,14903\0301,1,8,4,272,1,14903\0301,11,87,4,272,3,14903\0301,90,191,4,276,3,14903\0301,196,240,4,272,1,14903\0301,243,307,4,272,1,14903\0304,1,24,3,256,1,14903\0304,26,42,3,256,2,14903\0304,45,134,3,256,3,14903\0304,137,205,3,256,3,14903\03115047,2,1,Gurubashi\03014834,2,4,Hakkar\03015047,2,4,Gurubashi\03014903,2,6,Al'tabim the All-Seeing\03014903,2,8,Al'tabim the All-Seeing\03014834,4,10,Hakkar\0312,19,1434,0,\031\031ITEM,19720,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,270,OBJECTIVE,9000,16,",[8071]="PARTIAL\031loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $N - the minions of Hakkar have surely felt the retribution of the Zandalar today, thanks to you.  Your actions have given you a permanent place of reverence within the tribe.  With our blessing, please take this confessor's mantle as your own!\030The confessors of the Zandalar all wear a distinctive mantle, marking them as the preservers of the tribe.  These mantles are woven with powerful mojo that aids them in judging those who would threaten our tribe.  As a priest, you too must spend your time judging those worthy and not; such a mantle would definitely be a blessing to you.$B$BIn exchange for fighting Hakkar's minions in Zul'Gurub and bringing me the Paragons of Power I seek, I will give you a mantle worthy of our finest confessors.\030Bring Al'tabim the All-Seeing a Primal Hakkari Aegis.  You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Revered with the Zandalar Tribe.$B$BAl'tabim the All-Seeing is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\030Do you have the Paragons of Power from Zul'Gurub?\030Paragons of Power: The Confessor's Mantle\0312,1,106,2,257,1,14903\0302,109,212,2,261,4,14903\0302,215,338,2,257,4,14903\0302,343,500,2,263,3,14903\0303,1,53,2,384,1,14903\0303,56,144,2,384,1,14903\0303,149,219,2,384,1,14903\0301,1,108,4,304,1,14903\0301,111,186,4,272,1,14903\0301,189,255,4,272,1,14903\0304,1,49,3,256,2,14903\031111,2,3,Priest\03014903,2,5,Al'tabim the All-Seeing\03014903,2,7,Al'tabim the All-Seeing\03014834,4,8,Hakkar\0312,19,1434,0,\0302,0,0,4,Zul'Gurub\0303,0,0,11,Zul'Gurub\031\031ITEM,19724,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,270,OBJECTIVE,21000,16,",[8072]="PARTIAL\031loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Victory is ours this day, thanks to the madness you have sowed upon our mutual enemies!  You are to be honored amongst the Zandalar, and there is no better way of showing gratitude for your deeds than by offering you the madcap's mantle!\030One of Zandalar's legendary madcaps was Khar'vaxal the Cracked.  Legend states that when facing the enemies of the tribe for the first time, Kar'xavan used his mantle specifically woven with \"the weave of madness\".  His form was shrouded not only by the mantle, but also with the blinding speed of his twin daggers.  Madcaps today cherish their mantle as a sign of their place in the tribe.$B$BBring to me the Paragons of Power I seek, and such a mantle will be yours to weave madness unto your own enemies.\030Bring Falthir the Sightless a Primal Hakkari Girdle.  You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Honored with the Zandalar Tribe.$B$BFalthir the Sightless is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\030You've returned - do you have the Paragons of Power I need?$B$BThe legend of Khar'vaxal the Cracked serves us today as a reminder that no foe - no matter how great a threat they may be - is impossible to overcome.  Chaos will bring everyone to their knees, that much is certain... and perhaps the most non-chaotic elements of chaos.\030Paragons of Power: The Madcap's Mantle\0312,1,63,2,257,1,14905\0302,66,214,2,261,1,14905\0302,217,315,2,257,1,14905\0302,318,390,2,257,1,14905\0302,395,507,2,263,3,14905\0303,1,52,2,384,1,14905\0303,55,143,2,384,1,14905\0303,148,216,2,384,1,14905\0301,1,87,4,308,1,14905\0301,90,237,4,272,1,14905\0304,1,59,3,258,2,14905\0304,64,213,3,260,1,14905\0304,216,280,3,256,3,14905\0304,282,332,3,256,4,14905\03114905,2,6,Falthir the Sightless\03014905,2,8,Falthir the Sightless\0312,19,1434,0,\031\031ITEM,19719,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,270,OBJECTIVE,9000,16,",[8073]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Impressive... you have accomplished today what few thought was possible.  Your reverence in the tribe is assured for a lifetime, $N.  You have earned the right to don the madcap's tunic - do so with our blessing.\030My eyes failed me long ago, but I do not miss them.  Even in a tribe such as ours - where one's vestments convey station and purpose - the most potent of garb exudes power that simple eyes cannot see.  The prized tunic of the Zandalar madcap is no exception, exuding the raw power of chaos and madness that they are able to channel.$B$BThe Paragons of Power I need lie in Zul'Gurub; bring me what I seek, and I will reward you with your own legendary tunic... one befitting a weaver of madness.\030Bring Falthir the Sightless a Primal Hakkari Aegis.  You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Revered with the Zandalar Tribe.$B$BFalthir the Sightless is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\030Welcome back to the Isle, $N... have you returned triumphantly with the Paragons of Power in tow?\030Paragons of Power: The Madcap's Tunic\0312,1,51,2,321,1,14905\0302,54,200,2,257,1,14905\0302,203,332,2,257,1,14905\0302,337,459,2,259,3,14905\0302,461,494,2,257,1,14905\0303,1,51,2,384,1,14905\0303,54,142,2,384,1,14905\0303,147,215,2,384,1,14905\0301,1,13,4,272,1,14905\0301,15,72,4,272,1,14905\0301,75,132,4,272,1,14905\0301,135,212,4,272,1,14905\0304,1,31,3,256,1,14905\0304,33,97,3,256,2,14905\0315720,2,5,Weaver\03014905,2,6,Falthir the Sightless\03014905,2,8,Falthir the Sightless\0312,19,1434,0,\0302,0,0,4,Zul'Gurub\0303,0,0,13,Isle\031\031ITEM,19724,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,270,OBJECTIVE,21000,16,",[8074]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I can smell the scent of vanquished evil on ya, $N.  It's a sweet smell mon... one I think you know quite well.$B$BI know it's no small feat to have brought me the Paragons of Power required for the belt.  Your deeds have not only honored the tribe, but also honored yourself amongst my tribe.  Here ya are - take the augur's belt and don it as your own!\030Augurs know the mojo of the elements, mon.  They use it as a means to guide the tribe to glory.  In the dark days after the Gurubashi Empire ripped itself up, our augurs led us to our safe haven in the South Seas.  They've also led us back here to the Vale, right back to the heart of evil brewin' in Zul'Gurub.$B$BBring me an offerin' of the Paragons of Power from inside Zul'Gurub and prove your worth to us.  Do it and I'll give ya a belt that our augurs use - one with powerful mojo inside it!\030Bring Maywiki of Zuldazar a Primal Hakkari Girdle.  You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Honored with the Zandalar Tribe.$B$BMaywiki of Zuldazar is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\030The Paragons of Power are what I need mon - we'll tap the power right out of them in our fight against the evil from Zul'Gurub.  Do ya have them for me?\030Paragons of Power: The Augur's Belt\0312,1,42,2,257,1,14904\0302,45,95,2,257,1,14904\0302,98,213,2,257,1,14904\0302,216,311,2,257,1,14904\0302,316,410,2,257,1,14904\0302,413,497,2,257,1,14904\0303,1,50,2,384,1,14904\0303,53,141,2,384,1,14904\0303,146,212,2,384,1,14904\0301,1,51,4,272,1,14904\0301,54,78,4,272,1,14904\0301,80,111,4,272,1,14904\0301,116,204,4,272,1,14904\0301,207,293,4,272,1,14904\0301,296,354,4,272,1,14904\0304,1,127,3,262,1,14904\0304,130,152,3,256,2,14904\03115047,2,3,Gurubashi\03014904,2,7,Maywiki of Zuldazar\03014904,2,9,Maywiki of Zuldazar\0312,19,1434,0,\0302,0,0,3,South Seas\0302,0,0,4,Vale\0302,0,0,4,Zul'Gurub\0303,0,0,16,Zul'Gurub\031\031ITEM,19719,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,270,OBJECTIVE,9000,16,",[8075]="PARTIAL\031conflict,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I know what ya had to go through to bring me the Paragons of Power, $N.  It wasn't easy, mon - defeatin' the evil that seeps out of Zul'Gurub like a foul ooze - but now that it is all said and done, I can easily say that you'll be revered amongst the Zandalar for ages to come!$B$BHere - take the augur's hauberk and wear it with pride!\030The augurs of the Zandalar all wear a distinctive chest piece called a hauberk.  It's fitted with the finest of silks and cloths, interwoven with strong chain.  It's a symbol of not only their divinity, but also of their authority, mon.  It's never wise to cross one whose life is devoted to speakin' with the spirits...$B$BBring me an offerin' of the Paragons of Power from inside Zul'Gurub and prove your worth to us.  Do it and I'll give ya one of the finest hauberks our augurs would ever hope to wear!\030Bring Maywiki of Zuldazar a Primal Hakkari Tabard.  You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Revered with the Zandalar Tribe.$B$BMaywiki of Zuldazar is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\030The Paragons of Power are a key source of magic power - the same kind of power that goes into makin' the augur's hauberk.  Bring me what I need, and I'll be able to share the finest of vestments any Zandalar augur would be wantin' as their own.\030Paragons of Power: The Augur's Hauberk\0312,1,79,2,257,1,14904\0302,82,159,2,257,1,14904\0302,162,236,2,257,1,14904\0302,239,320,2,257,1,14904\0302,325,419,2,257,1,14904\0302,422,506,2,259,4,14904\0303,1,50,2,384,1,14904\0303,53,141,2,384,1,14904\0303,146,212,2,384,1,14904\0301,1,71,4,272,1,14904\0301,74,277,4,304,1,14904\0301,282,336,4,272,1,14904\0304,1,121,3,256,1,14904\0304,124,244,3,258,4,14904\03114904,2,7,Maywiki of Zuldazar\03014904,2,9,Maywiki of Zuldazar\0312,19,1434,0,\031\031ITEM,19722,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,270,OBJECTIVE,21000,16,",[8076]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, $N.  The Paragons of Power from Zul'Gurub should act as a reminder of wasted power.  The Gurubashi were strong at their height, but they allowed themselves to be consumed by it.  A demoniac knows that the game they play is much similar, but the power unleashed is often the very thing needed for survival.$B$BUse this mantle as an honored ally of the Zandalar... it will serve you well.\030The demoniac seeks to embody power outright, not just possess it.  More than one of our demoniacs has lost a fight with a demon; with our enemies threatening us - especially in Zul'Gurub - the power that a demoniac is able to unleash on our foes is worth the sacrifice.  Our survival depends on crushing those who would destroy us; the fall of the Gurubashi Empire taught us this.$B$BTravel to Zul'Gurub and gain the Paragons of Power we need.  Do this, and a valuable demoniac item shall be yours.\030Bring Al'tabim the All-Seeing a Primal Hakkari Sash.  You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Honored with the Zandalar Tribe.$B$BAl'tabim the All-Seeing is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\030Retrieved the Paragons of Power from Zul'Gurub?  While we will take the latent power from these items and make them our own, we will give you your own reward of power should you be successful...\030Paragons of Power: The Demoniac's Mantle\0312,1,65,2,259,1,14903\0302,68,269,2,261,1,14903\0302,272,380,2,269,4,14903\0302,385,443,2,259,1,14903\0302,446,498,2,257,3,14903\0303,1,52,2,384,1,14903\0303,55,143,2,384,1,14903\0303,148,218,2,384,1,14903\0301,1,14,4,272,1,14903\0301,17,94,4,272,1,14903\0301,97,188,4,272,1,14903\0301,191,316,4,280,1,14903\0301,321,373,4,272,1,14903\0301,375,397,4,272,3,14903\0304,1,47,3,256,2,14903\0304,50,194,3,256,3,14903\03115047,2,3,Gurubashi\03014903,2,6,Al'tabim the All-Seeing\03014903,2,8,Al'tabim the All-Seeing\03015047,4,11,Gurubashi\0312,19,1434,0,\0302,0,0,2,Zul'Gurub\0302,0,0,4,Zul'Gurub\0304,0,0,10,Zul'Gurub\0303,0,0,15,Zul'Gurub\031\031ITEM,19720,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,270,OBJECTIVE,9000,16,",[8077]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Impressive - your victory in Zul'Gurub has assured us - nay, the world - that Hakkar will not prevail.  The time may come when you face the Blood God directly... and should this come to pass know that your reverence is assured amongst the Zandalar tribe.$B$BOh, and this simple robe should help out too I think.$B$B<Al'tabim winks knowingly at you.>\030The ultimate symbol of power amongst the tribe is the garb we wear in battle.  A demoniac's robes have fused fine runecloth and devastatingly powerful mojo into a single fabric.  The visage of the robe is said to instill fear into the minds of all who see it... especially the demons that the demoniac will eventually dominate.$B$BFrom Zul'Gurub, you must bring me a very specific set of the Paragons of Power.  It will be difficult... but your success will assure you of acquiring a robe for yourself.\030Bring Al'tabim the All-Seeing a Primal Hakkari Kossack.  You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Revered with the Zandalar Tribe.$B$BAl'tabim the All-Seeing is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\030The Paragons of Power... you have returned with them?  Only once we have them will we share the ultimate symbol of demoniac power with you, $N.\030Paragons of Power: The Demoniac's Robes\0312,1,77,2,261,1,14903\0302,80,177,2,257,1,14903\0302,180,261,2,257,1,14903\0302,263,327,2,257,3,14903\0302,332,410,2,257,1,14903\0302,413,435,2,257,3,14903\0302,437,502,2,257,3,14903\0303,1,55,2,384,1,14903\0303,58,146,2,384,1,14903\0303,151,221,2,384,1,14903\0301,1,102,4,272,3,14903\0301,105,161,4,272,1,14903\0301,163,254,4,272,1,14903\0301,259,311,4,272,1,14903\0301,316,349,4,272,1,14903\0304,1,24,3,256,1,14903\0304,26,53,3,256,2,14903\0304,56,143,3,256,3,14903\03114903,2,8,Al'tabim the All-Seeing\03014903,2,10,Al'tabim the All-Seeing\03014834,4,11,Hakkar\0312,19,1434,0,\0304,0,0,11,Zul'Gurub\031\031ITEM,19723,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,270,OBJECTIVE,21000,16,",[8078]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The way of the vindicator is now known to you.  You have brought honor to the tribe.  You have brought honor to yourself.  You have brought pain to our enemies.$B$BThe vindicator's belt is yours.  You are surely becoming one with the way of the vindicator.\030The ultimate vengeance waits within Zul'Gurub.  Hakkar must not rise again.  Hakkar destroyed the Gurubashi Empire from within.  No sacrifice was enough.  The trolls are a shadow of former glories.  I know this is because of Hakkar.$B$BBecome the vindicator you were meant to be.  Wreak havoc on the minions of evil.  Zul'Gurub must taste Zandalar vengeance.  Bring me proof in the Paragons of Power.  You will receive the vindicator's belt.  You will receive real power.$B$BGo.\030Bring Jin'rokh the Breaker a Primal Hakkari Girdle.  You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Honored with the Zandalar Tribe.$B$BJin'rokh the Breaker is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\030Have you brought the Paragons of Power?  Have you struck down the enemies of the tribe?  Hakkar must know the wrath of the vindicator!\030Paragons of Power: The Vindicator's Belt\0312,1,46,2,259,1,14902\0302,49,75,2,265,1,14902\0302,78,127,2,261,1,14902\0302,130,153,2,257,1,14902\0302,156,197,2,257,1,14902\0302,200,232,2,259,1,14902\0302,237,279,2,257,1,14902\0302,282,316,2,257,1,14902\0302,319,358,2,259,1,14902\0302,361,400,2,257,1,14902\0302,403,441,2,257,3,14902\0302,444,471,2,257,3,14902\0303,1,51,2,384,1,14902\0303,54,142,2,384,1,14902\0303,147,214,2,384,1,14902\0301,1,46,4,272,1,14902\0301,49,84,4,272,1,14902\0301,87,121,4,272,1,14902\0301,124,160,4,276,1,14902\0301,165,195,4,272,1,14902\0301,198,256,4,272,1,14902\0304,1,39,3,256,2,14902\0304,42,87,3,260,2,14902\0304,90,134,3,256,1,14902\03114834,2,2,Hakkar\03014834,2,3,Hakkar\03015047,2,3,Gurubashi\0304244,2,5,Shadow\03014834,2,6,Hakkar\03014902,2,13,Jin'rokh the Breaker\03014902,2,15,Jin'rokh the Breaker\03014834,3,24,Hakkar\0312,19,1434,0,\0302,0,0,1,Zul'Gurub\0302,0,0,10,Paragons of Power\031\031ITEM,19719,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,270,OBJECTIVE,9000,16,",[8079]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You are to be revered for your deeds.  The tribe rewards its heroes.  Zul'Gurub has tasted Zandalar vengeance like never before.$B$BYour deeds will herald the deeds of others to come.  They will look upon you as a sign of real power.  They will look upon you as vengeance personified!\030The vindicator's symbol of power is the breastplate.  It is forged with powerful mojo.  It is trusted only to those we revere.  It is the Zandalar symbol of vengeance.$B$BTo become a vindicator is to become vengeance.  Take the Paragons of Power we need from Zul'Gurub.  Bring them to us.  We will take the mojo stolen from us.  We will make the minions of Hakkar pay.  We will reward you with the vindicator's breastplate.$B$BGo.  Be our vengeance, $N.\030Bring Jin'rokh the Breaker a Primal Hakkari Kossack.  You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Revered with the Zandalar Tribe.$B$BJin'rokh the Breaker is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\030Your presence means victory?  Do you have the Paragons of Power?  Tell me of the vengeance you have wrought today!\030Paragons of Power: The Vindicator's Breastplate\0312,1,52,2,257,1,14902\0302,55,86,2,257,1,14902\0302,89,126,2,257,1,14902\0302,129,167,2,259,1,14902\0302,172,217,2,259,1,14902\0302,220,269,2,259,1,14902\0302,272,288,2,257,1,14902\0302,291,327,2,261,3,14902\0302,330,368,2,257,3,14902\0302,371,423,2,257,3,14902\0302,433,453,2,259,1,14902\0303,1,52,2,384,1,14902\0303,55,143,2,384,1,14902\0303,148,215,2,384,1,14902\0301,1,37,4,272,1,14902\0301,40,68,4,272,1,14902\0301,71,128,4,274,1,14902\0301,133,183,4,272,3,14902\0301,186,233,4,272,3,14902\0301,236,284,4,274,3,14902\0304,1,28,3,256,2,14902\0304,31,64,3,256,2,14902\0304,67,114,3,258,1,14902\03114834,2,9,Hakkar\03014902,2,12,Jin'rokh the Breaker\03014902,2,14,Jin'rokh the Breaker\03014848,4,18,Herald\0312,19,1434,0,\0302,0,0,6,Zul'Gurub\031\031ITEM,19723,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030REPUTATION,270,OBJECTIVE,21000,16,",[808]="PARTIAL\031conflict,loreConnections,motivations,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thank you, $N. You have saved Minshina. You have saved my brother's spirit from slavery!\030I hear the voice of my brother, Minshina, calling to me in my dreams.$B$BHe was taken by Zalazane, the warlock on the Echo Isles to the east. And he is dead.$B$BBut death is not freedom for my brother. Minshina's spirit was trapped within his own skull by Zalazane's magics. In my dreams I see it with other skulls, in a circle of power on the largest Echo Isle. As long as it remains there my brother's soul is doomed.$B$BPlease, $N. Find the circle and retrieve Minshina's skull. Bring it to me.$B$BFree him!\030Retrieve Minshina's skull from the circle of power on the Echo Isles.$B$BBring it to Master Gadrin in Sen'jin Village.\030Do you have my brother's skull, $N? Is he finally free?\030Minshina's Skull\0312,1,69,2,257,1,3188\0302,74,141,2,257,1,3188\0302,143,157,2,257,1,3188\0302,162,201,2,265,1,3188\0302,203,274,2,257,1,3188\0302,276,362,2,257,1,3188\0302,364,419,2,257,1,3188\0302,424,434,2,257,1,3188\0302,436,481,2,257,1,3188\0302,483,497,2,257,1,3188\0302,502,510,2,257,1,3188\0303,1,69,2,384,1,3188\0303,74,118,2,384,1,3188\0301,1,14,4,272,1,3188\0301,16,39,4,304,1,3188\0301,41,88,4,304,1,3188\0304,1,35,3,256,2,3188\0304,37,55,3,256,2,3188\0313205,2,2,Zalazane\0303188,2,13,Master Gadrin\0312,14,1411,0,\0302,0,0,13,Master Gadrin\0302,0,0,13,Sen'jin Village\031\031ITEM,4864,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8080]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You got the resources! Great job! I'll send the resources to our quartermasters, who can quickly disperse them to our troops.$B$BThank you, $N. Indeed, performing successful missions like the one you achieved are how wars are truly won.\030War must be fought with soldiers, any soldier will tell you.  They'll also say that a battle fought with poor gear or on an empty stomach is lost before it starts!$B$BThat is why Arathi Basin is important.  There are key areas in the basin that hold essential resources.  Metals, weapons, food, lumber - all are needed, and all can be gained there.$B$BThat is what I want from you, $N.  Enter Arathi Basin, win the battle by holding more bases than the enemy, and return to me with a crate of resources.\030Win the battle for Arathi Basin, get an Arathi Resource Crate, and return it to Sergeant Maclear at Refuge Pointe.\030Do you have the resource crate, $N? The League of Arathor can't fight a decent battle without them...\030Arathi Basin Resources!\0312,1,60,2,261,3,0\0302,63,163,2,261,1,0\0302,168,205,2,257,1,0\0302,208,270,2,257,1,0\0302,273,348,2,257,1,0\0302,353,385,2,259,1,0\0302,388,503,2,261,1,0\0303,1,114,2,388,1,0\0301,1,22,4,272,1,0\0301,24,33,4,272,1,0\0301,35,125,4,272,1,0\0301,130,143,4,272,1,0\0301,145,236,4,272,1,0\0304,1,35,3,256,2,0\0304,37,101,3,260,1,0\03114984,2,8,Sergeant Maclear\0312,3358,1461,0,\0302,0,0,8,Sergeant Maclear\0302,0,0,8,Refuge Pointe\0318081,22,8081,UNKNOWN\0308154,22,8154,UNKNOWN\0308155,22,8155,UNKNOWN\0308156,22,8156,UNKNOWN\0308157,22,8157,UNKNOWN\0308158,22,8158,UNKNOWN\0308159,22,8159,UNKNOWN\0308297,22,8297,UNKNOWN\0308298,22,8298,UNKNOWN\0308081,23,8081,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,20559,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8081]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very good. I will get these to our quartermasters immediately, and a commendation for your actions will be sent to my superiors.$B$BOnce again, thank you $N. Your contributions to our struggles are noticed by footman and field marshal alike.\030War must be fought with soldiers, any soldier will tell you. They'll also say that a battle fought with poor gear or on an empty stomach is lost before it starts!$B$BThat is why Arathi Basin is important. There are key areas in the basin that hold essential resources. Metals, weapons, food, lumber - all are needed, and all can be gained there.$B$BThat is what I want from you, $N. Enter Arathi Basin, win the battle by holding more bases than the enemy, and return to me with a crate of resources.\030Win the battle for Arathi Basin, get an Arathi Resource Crate, and return it to Sergeant Maclear at Refuge Pointe.\030$N, the League of Arathor has a standing mission for you to reenter Arathi Basin, procure more resource crates and bring them to me.\030More Resource Crates\0312,1,60,2,261,3,0\0302,62,162,2,261,1,0\0302,167,204,2,257,1,0\0302,206,268,2,257,1,0\0302,270,345,2,257,1,0\0302,350,382,2,259,1,0\0302,384,499,2,261,1,0\0303,1,114,2,388,1,0\0301,1,10,4,272,1,0\0301,12,128,4,272,3,0\0301,133,157,4,272,1,0\0301,159,241,4,272,1,0\0304,1,132,3,256,1,0\03114984,2,8,Sergeant Maclear\0312,3358,1461,0,\0302,0,0,8,Sergeant Maclear\0302,0,0,8,Refuge Pointe\0318080,19,8080,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0308080,22,8080,UNKNOWN\0308154,22,8154,UNKNOWN\0308155,22,8155,UNKNOWN\0308156,22,8156,UNKNOWN\0308157,22,8157,UNKNOWN\0308158,22,8158,UNKNOWN\0308159,22,8159,UNKNOWN\0308297,22,8297,UNKNOWN\0308298,22,8298,UNKNOWN\031ITEM,19725,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[809]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Neeru wants the Demon Seed destroyed, does he? Strange...$B$BVery well. If he wishes the seed gone, then I will tell you how to remove it.\030Since the last great war when the Burning Legion was defeated, I have searched for sources of demonic corruption in orc society.  The collar you brought me confirms my fears.$B$BIt belongs to the Burning Blade, a cult that rallies around an item of demonic power.  It is called the Demon Seed, and it resides in the Barrens atop Dreadmist Peak.  It must be destroyed!$B$BGo to Far Watch Post, on the border of the Barrens to the west, and speak with my assistant, Ak'Zeloth.  He will direct you further.\030Speak with Ak'Zeloth in the Barrens.\030\030Ak'Zeloth\0312,1,128,2,325,1,3216\0302,131,174,2,257,1,3216\0302,179,263,2,257,1,3216\0302,266,344,2,257,1,3216\0302,347,367,2,261,1,3216\0302,372,474,2,257,1,3216\0302,477,503,2,257,3,3216\0303,1,36,2,384,1,3216\0301,1,46,4,278,2,3521\0301,48,57,4,272,1,3521\0301,62,71,4,272,1,3521\0301,73,138,4,274,4,3521\0313521,2,6,Ak'Zeloth\0303521,2,8,Ak'Zeloth\0312,14,1411,0,\0302,0,0,3,Burning Blade\0302,0,0,4,Barrens\0302,0,0,6,Far Watch Post\0302,0,0,8,Barrens\031829,19,829,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\030924,23,924,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[81]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well, let's see what's in this barrel!$B$BYes, yes, it looks as though it is all here. Here's your fee for the package, good job on that. I stand to make five times that fee when I sell it to the tavern! Har har!$B$BThese extra bottles of Hinterlands Honey Ripple are going to be set for a special occasion. I think I'll drink some with champagne. I'll call it... champipple.\030I have taken the extra step of securing not only Dran's packaged ripple in the barrel, but also the extra bottles of ripple he is purloining.  While I may not hold Dran very highly, there is nothing worse than jostled ripple.  You're welcome.$B$BNow, deliver yon barrel to Dran Droffers in his salvage emporium in Orgrimmar.  Pray tell, please extend my warmest greetings to Malton; let him know that should he ever thirst for fine drink and finer drinking companions, we would be honored with his visit.\030Deliver the barrel to Dran Droffers in Orgrimmar.\030If you're not here to buy anything, and you're not here to deliver anything, then you're wasting my time! You better have that ripple!\030Ripple Delivery\0312,1,141,2,257,1,7801\0302,144,225,2,257,1,7801\0302,228,242,2,257,1,7801\0302,247,324,2,257,1,7801\0302,327,504,2,257,4,7801\0303,1,49,2,384,1,7801\0301,1,38,4,272,1,6986\0301,43,86,4,272,1,6986\0301,88,137,4,272,1,6986\0301,139,203,4,272,1,6986\0301,205,212,4,272,1,6986\0301,217,307,4,272,3,6986\0301,309,347,4,272,1,6986\0301,349,363,4,272,1,6986\0301,365,375,4,272,1,6986\0304,1,105,3,256,4,6986\0304,107,134,3,256,1,6986\0316986,2,4,Dran Droffers\0306986,2,6,Dran Droffers\0312,1637,1454,0,\0302,0,0,4,Dran Droffers\0302,0,0,4,Orgrimmar\0302,0,0,5,Malton\0302,0,0,6,Dran Droffers\0302,0,0,6,Orgrimmar\03177,19,77,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[8101]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031$R, the pebble held within the frame of this talisman comes from Mount Kajaro in the South Seas. Mount Kajaro is an area plagued by volatility - marked by violent and oftentimes magical volcanic eruptions.$B$BAs your bond with the trolls of Zandalar grows, so too shall the power of this pebble. Harness the power of the pebble to strike down our enemies. Be like the mountain: Quick, explosive, deadly...\030\030\030NULL\030The Pebble of Kajaro\0311,1,96,4,272,1,14903\0301,98,205,4,272,1,14903\0301,210,295,4,272,3,14903\0301,297,355,4,276,1,14903\0301,357,405,4,272,1,14903\0304,1,4,3,256,1,14903\031\0312,1977,0,0,\0304,0,0,1,Mount Kajaro\0304,0,0,1,South Seas\0318102,23,8102,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[8102]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Be unstoppable, like the molten fronts of Kajaro.\030\030\030Welcome back, $c. I can see that the pebble has seen much use. Many of our foes have fallen to your otherworldly abilities. Their suffering has been great. It is time that I enhance the power of the pebble. Give it to me.\030The Pebble of Kajaro\0311,1,49,4,272,1,14903\0304,1,17,3,256,1,14903\0304,19,62,3,256,1,14903\0304,64,123,3,256,1,14903\0304,125,155,3,260,1,14903\0304,157,206,3,256,1,14903\0304,208,221,3,256,1,14903\031\0312,1977,0,0,\0318101,19,8101,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0308103,23,8103,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,19598,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8103]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Continue in your decimation of the trolls of Zul'Gurub. Hakkar must see that the world will not buckle beneath his indomitable will.\030\030\030Hakkari fear you, $n. They speak of horrors they believed that only their faceless God could perpetrate. You have burned them with the force of Kajaro. They now know fear in two places.$B$BIt is time to further strengthen the pebble. Hand me the talisman.\030The Pebble of Kajaro\0311,1,55,4,272,1,14903\0301,57,132,4,272,3,14903\0304,1,21,3,256,1,14903\0304,23,104,3,256,4,14903\0304,106,151,3,256,1,14903\0304,153,185,3,256,1,14903\0304,190,233,3,256,1,14903\0304,235,255,3,256,1,14903\03114834,4,2,Hakkar\0312,1977,0,0,\0318102,19,8102,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0308104,23,8104,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,19599,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8104]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Al'tabim shatters the pebble with a powerful unseen force.>$B$BDo you see? The pebble is what we call a geode. Inside the pebble are powerful crystals that have been soaking in the latent energies from our world. By cutting the pebble in half, I have finally allowed its full potential to be realized. Use it to lay waste to our enemies.\030\030\030Give me the talisman, $n. I must show you something.\030The Jewel of Kajaro\0311,1,60,4,272,1,14903\0301,65,75,4,272,2,14903\0301,77,111,4,272,1,14903\0301,113,213,4,272,1,14903\0301,215,302,4,272,1,14903\0301,304,338,4,276,1,14903\0304,1,25,3,256,1,14903\0304,27,52,3,256,1,14903\0313094,4,1,Unseen\0312,1977,0,0,\0318103,19,8103,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,19600,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8105]="PARTIAL\031conclusion,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030objectiveLabel3\030objectiveLabel4\030objectiveLabel5\030requestItems\030title\031\030$N, the battle for Arathi Basin is a battle for resources and territory.  Key points in the area must be held and operated in order to supply our forces with much needed raw materials and supplies.  I charge you to assault the points farthest from our Arathi Basin base.$B$BAssault the farm, the mine, the lumber mill and the blacksmith when they are controlled by the enemy.  Find the enemy's banner and rip it from its flag post!$B$BWhen you have done this to all four points, return to me.\030Assault the mine, the lumber mill, the blacksmith and the farm, then return to Field Marshal Oslight in Refuge Pointe.\030\030Mine Assaulted\030Lumber Mill Assaulted\030Blacksmith Assaulted\030Farm Assaulted\030\030The Battle for Arathi Basin!\0312,1,72,2,261,1,14983\0302,75,197,2,259,1,14983\0302,200,270,2,257,1,14983\0302,275,375,2,261,1,14983\0302,378,431,2,261,1,14983\0302,436,492,2,257,1,14983\0303,1,118,2,384,1,14983\0305,1,14,3,384,1,14983\0306,1,21,3,384,1,14983\0307,1,20,3,384,1,14983\0308,1,14,3,384,1,14983\03114983,2,7,Field Marshal Oslight\0312,3358,1461,0,\0302,0,0,7,Field Marshal Oslight\0302,0,0,7,Refuge Pointe\0318166,22,8166,UNKNOWN\0308167,22,8167,UNKNOWN\0308168,22,8168,UNKNOWN\031NPC,15005,OBJECTIVE,1,13,PvP ALT-N Credit Marker\030NPC,15004,OBJECTIVE,1,13,PvP ALT-S Credit Marker\030NPC,15002,OBJECTIVE,1,13,PvP Mid Credit Marker\030NPC,15003,OBJECTIVE,1,13,PvP H-Mid Credit Marker",[8106]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Accept this talisman, $c. Accept it and use its power to strike down our mutual enemies.$B$BKnow that around your neck you carry a piece of history. Kezan was once a grand territory of the Zandalar Empire. Alas, the taint of goblin trade princes would force out my proud brothers and sisters.$B$BKezan is now home to the goblin capital of the Undermine; but know that before the taint, it held greatness. Still to this day Kezan is considered sacred land to my people.\030\030\030\030Kezan's Taint\0311,1,25,4,272,1,14903\0301,27,88,4,276,1,14903\0301,93,148,4,336,1,14903\0301,150,205,4,272,1,14903\0301,207,292,4,272,4,14903\0301,297,404,4,272,1,14903\0301,406,468,4,272,1,14903\031\0312,1977,0,0,\0318107,23,8107,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[8107]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Draw from the darkness, $c. Embrace the shadows. Let Kezan's Taint supplement your dark meddling.\030\030\030Honor is earned amongst the Zandalar trolls, $n. With honor comes reward - friendship, alliance...$B$BHand me the talisman so that I may enhance its power.\030Kezan's Taint\0311,1,27,4,272,1,14903\0301,29,48,4,272,1,14903\0301,50,97,4,272,1,14903\0304,1,48,3,256,1,14903\0304,50,98,3,256,1,14903\0304,103,155,3,258,1,14903\031\0312,1977,0,0,\0318106,19,8106,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0308108,23,8108,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,19602,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8108]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031It is only through our combined efforts that we will stop the Soulflayer.\030\030\030I am ready for you, $c. Once more I will enhance your talisman. I only ask that you continue in your destruction of Hakkar and his minions.$B$BGive me the talisman.\030Kezan's Taint\0311,1,73,4,272,3,14903\0304,1,23,3,256,1,14903\0304,25,63,3,256,3,14903\0304,65,139,3,256,1,14903\0304,144,164,3,256,1,14903\03111359,4,1,Soulflayer\03014834,3,4,Hakkar\0312,1977,0,0,\0318107,19,8107,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0308109,23,8109,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,19603,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8109]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Flay the flesh from their corpses. Watch as the shadows consume the Hakkari. Draw power from their fear, $c. Let Kezan's Taint augment this power...\030\030\030Call forth your demons, $c. Let them bask in the energy of Kezan's Taint. Command them on the field of battle! Decimate the enemy!$B$BYes... The time has come to apply the final enhancement to Kezan's Taint. Give me the talisman.\030Kezan's Unstoppable Taint\0311,1,34,4,272,1,14903\0301,36,76,4,272,1,14903\0301,78,108,4,272,1,14903\0301,110,148,4,272,1,14903\0304,1,27,3,256,1,14903\0304,29,73,3,256,1,14903\0304,75,110,3,260,1,14903\0304,112,130,3,260,1,14903\0304,135,140,3,256,1,14903\0304,142,207,3,256,1,14903\0304,209,229,3,256,1,14903\031\0312,1977,0,0,\0303,0,0,10,Kezan's Taint\0318108,19,8108,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,19604,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8110]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031See this here seaweed, mon? It be from the South Seas. We just add a little mojo and a little magic and it takes on the properties most suited to its owner.$B$BYou a $c so it be easy, mon. Just wrap it around your neck and think of nature or squirrels or whatever it be that you people like.\030\030\030NULL\030Enchanted South Seas Kelp\0311,1,27,4,272,2,14904\0301,29,54,4,272,1,14904\0301,56,156,4,272,1,14904\0301,161,188,4,272,1,14904\0301,190,291,4,272,1,14904\0304,1,4,3,256,1,14904\031\0312,1977,0,0,\0304,0,0,2,South Seas\0318111,23,8111,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[8111]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The neck piece not be for smokin', mon! You got to use it to fight evil.\030\030\030Hey mon! It be good to see you again. The tribe be talking about your killin' of the Hakkari and all that. Molthor gave me the word to be adding more mojo to your talisman. Just give it here and Maywiki make it better.\030Enchanted South Seas Kelp\0311,1,39,4,272,1,14904\0301,41,72,4,276,1,14904\0304,1,8,3,256,1,14904\0304,10,37,3,256,1,14904\0304,39,106,3,256,1,14904\0304,108,172,3,256,1,14904\0304,174,218,3,256,1,14904\03114875,3,6,Molthor\0312,1977,0,0,\0318110,19,8110,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0308112,23,8112,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,19610,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8112]="PARTIAL\031conflict,loreConnections,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Now you take the evil trolls in Zul'Gurub and show them what your nature powers can do, mon!\030\030\030How be that talisman, mon? It look like it be time to add a little more magic and mojo to its leaves. It need a little bloom in its wilt. Give it here and Maywiki fix it right up.\030Enchanted South Seas Kelp\0311,1,92,4,304,1,14904\0304,1,26,3,256,2,14904\0304,28,101,3,256,1,14904\0304,103,137,3,258,1,14904\0304,139,179,3,256,1,14904\031\0312,1977,0,0,\0304,0,0,1,Zul'Gurub\0318111,19,8111,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0308113,23,8113,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,19611,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8113]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031$n mon, it been a good journey. Keep on with the killing and suppressing of Hakkar and he minions.\030\030\030$n! It been a long time since I seen you. Did you know that King Rastakhan himself be givin' me the order to add the final bit of mojo and magic to your talisman? It be true, mon! I wouldn't have believed it had I not seen it with me own eyes. Give it here.\030Pristine Enchanted South Seas Kelp\0311,1,31,4,272,1,14904\0301,33,98,4,272,1,14904\0304,5,41,3,256,1,14904\0304,43,162,3,256,2,14904\0304,164,179,3,256,1,14904\0304,181,243,3,256,1,14904\0304,245,257,3,256,1,14904\03114834,4,2,Hakkar\0312,1977,0,0,\0318112,19,8112,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,19612,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8114]="PARTIAL\031conclusion,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031\030$N, you have taken the battle of Arathi Basin to our enemies and earned great honors in that field of battle.  You have shown us your worth as a $c, and you have shown our enemies that we will not submit to their villainy!$B$BBecause of your proven value to us, I have a difficult task for you.  I want you to take and hold at least four of the bases in Arathi Basin.  If you can do that, then we will not only secure critical resources, we will show the Horde our dominance!$B$BGo, $N, and good fortune.\030Enter Arathi Basin, capture and control four bases at the same time, and then return to Field Marshal Oslight at Refuge Pointe.\030Control Four Bases.\030\030Control Four Bases\0312,1,109,2,261,1,14983\0302,112,222,2,261,3,14983\0302,227,294,2,259,1,14983\0302,297,367,2,259,1,14983\0302,370,475,2,257,4,14983\0302,480,504,2,257,1,14983\0303,1,127,2,384,1,14983\0304,1,19,3,384,1,14983\03114983,2,7,Field Marshal Oslight\0312,3358,1461,0,\0302,0,0,4,Arathi Basin\0302,0,0,7,Field Marshal Oslight\0302,0,0,7,Refuge Pointe\031\031",[8115]="PARTIAL\031conclusion,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031\030$N, battling for the resources of Arathi Basin is a bloody undertaking.  Your services to the League of Arathor are as needed as they are appreciated.$B$BAnd we have one more task for you.$B$BThe League wishes to make one strong push against the Defilers' occupation of Arathi Basin.  We want them driven out of every strategic point on the battlefield!$B$BIt will not be easy, but if anyone can get it done, it is you.\030Control 5 bases in Arathi Basin at the same time, then return to Field Marshal Oslight at Refuge Pointe.\030Take Five Bases.\030\030Control Five Bases\0312,1,71,2,257,1,14983\0302,74,150,2,257,1,14983\0302,155,188,2,257,1,14983\0302,193,283,2,259,1,14983\0302,286,353,2,259,1,14983\0302,358,419,2,257,4,14983\0303,1,104,2,384,1,14983\0304,1,16,3,384,1,14983\03114983,2,7,Field Marshal Oslight\0312,3358,1461,0,\0302,0,0,2,League of Arathor\0302,0,0,7,Arathi Basin\0302,0,0,7,Field Marshal Oslight\0302,0,0,7,Refuge Pointe\031\031",[8116]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You and Maywiki have something in common, mon. We both be $c! Although, Maywiki is more of a mystic and you be more of a scrub. Still, we both know what the great spirits bring.$B$BAs a gift I give to you this orb to wear around your neck. Look deep inside and see the village of Voodress in the South Seas! Let it lift your spirits!\030\030\030NULL\030Vision of Voodress\0311,1,46,4,272,1,14904\0301,48,61,4,272,1,14904\0301,63,127,4,272,1,14904\0301,129,177,4,272,1,14904\0301,182,239,4,272,1,14904\0301,241,307,4,272,1,14904\0301,309,333,4,272,1,14904\0304,1,4,3,256,1,14904\031\0312,1977,0,0,\0304,0,0,6,South Seas\0318117,23,8117,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[8117]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Beware the evil Hakkari spirits, mon. Honestly, they be spooky.\030\030\030Good news, $n. Molthor be singin' your praises lately. He say how you be turnin' into a real hero of Zandalar.$B$BHe also say for Maywiki to polish your orb some more! Give it here so Maywiki can brighten the vision.\030Vision of Voodress\0311,1,37,4,272,1,14904\0301,39,63,4,272,1,14904\0304,1,14,3,256,1,14904\0304,16,54,3,256,1,14904\0304,56,110,3,256,1,14904\0304,115,167,3,256,1,14904\0304,169,216,3,256,1,14904\03114875,3,4,Molthor\0312,1977,0,0,\0318116,19,8116,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0308118,23,8118,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,19606,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8118]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Take a look at it now, $n. Voodress come in even clearer now, yea? Let the primal power flow through you, mon.\030\030\030Sha-mon! Maywiki make a joke!$B$B<Maywiki laughs.>$B$BSo, you been using the spirits and elements against our enemies in Zul'Gurub, eh? Spirits be praised!$B$BMaywiki gonna brighten your orb. Give it here, $n.\030Vision of Voodress\0311,1,26,4,272,1,14904\0301,28,66,4,272,2,14904\0301,68,110,4,272,1,14904\0304,1,8,3,256,1,14904\0304,10,29,3,256,1,14904\0304,34,50,3,256,1,14904\0304,55,135,3,260,2,14904\0304,137,155,3,256,1,14904\0304,160,191,3,256,1,14904\0304,