hains,setup,stakes,storytellingContext\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030\030\030\030Mark of Honor\031\031\0312,3277,1460,0,\031\031ITEM,19322,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8297]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You got the resources! Great job! I'll send the resources to our quartermasters, who can quickly disperse them to our troops.$B$BThank you, $N. Indeed, performing successful missions like the one you achieved are how wars are truly won.\030War must be fought with soldiers, any soldier will tell you.  They'll also say that a battle fought with poor gear or on an empty stomach is lost before it starts!$B$BThat is why Arathi Basin is important.  There are key areas in the basin that hold essential resources.  Metals, weapons, food, lumber - all are needed, and all can be gained there.$B$BThat is what I want from you, $N.  Enter Arathi Basin, win the battle by holding more bases than the enemy, and return to me with a crate of resources.\030Win the battle for Arathi Basin, get an Arathi Resource Crate, and return it to Sergeant Maclear at Refuge Pointe.\030Do you have the resource crate, $N? The League of Arathor can't fight a decent battle without them...\030Arathi Basin Resources!\0312,1,60,2,261,3,0\0302,63,163,2,261,1,0\0302,168,205,2,257,1,0\0302,208,270,2,257,1,0\0302,273,348,2,257,1,0\0302,353,385,2,259,1,0\0302,388,503,2,261,1,0\0303,1,114,2,388,1,0\0301,1,22,4,272,1,0\0301,24,33,4,272,1,0\0301,35,125,4,272,1,0\0301,130,143,4,272,1,0\0301,145,236,4,272,1,0\0304,1,35,3,256,2,0\0304,37,101,3,260,1,0\03114984,2,8,Sergeant Maclear\0312,3358,1461,0,\0302,0,0,8,Sergeant Maclear\0302,0,0,8,Refuge Pointe\0318080,22,8080,UNKNOWN\0308081,22,8081,UNKNOWN\0308154,22,8154,UNKNOWN\0308155,22,8155,UNKNOWN\0308156,22,8156,UNKNOWN\0308157,22,8157,UNKNOWN\0308158,22,8158,UNKNOWN\0308159,22,8159,UNKNOWN\0308298,22,8298,UNKNOWN\0308298,23,8298,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,20559,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8298]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very good. I will get these to our quartermasters immediately, and a commendation for your actions will be sent to my superiors.$B$BOnce again, thank you $N. Your contributions to our struggles are noticed by footman and field marshal alike.\030War must be fought with soldiers, any soldier will tell you. They'll also say that a battle fought with poor gear or on an empty stomach is lost before it starts!$B$BThat is why Arathi Basin is important. There are key areas in the basin that hold essential resources. Metals, weapons, food, lumber - all are needed, and all can be gained there.$B$BThat is what I want from you, $N. Enter Arathi Basin, win the battle by holding more bases than the enemy, and return to me with a crate of resources.\030Win the battle for Arathi Basin, get an Arathi Resource Crate, and return it to Sergeant Maclear at Refuge Pointe.\030$N, the League of Arathor has a standing mission for you to reenter Arathi Basin, procure more resource crates and bring them to me.\030More Resource Crates\0312,1,60,2,261,3,0\0302,62,162,2,261,1,0\0302,167,204,2,257,1,0\0302,206,268,2,257,1,0\0302,270,345,2,257,1,0\0302,350,382,2,259,1,0\0302,384,499,2,261,1,0\0303,1,114,2,388,1,0\0301,1,10,4,272,1,0\0301,12,128,4,272,3,0\0301,133,157,4,272,1,0\0301,159,241,4,272,1,0\0304,1,132,3,256,1,0\03114984,2,8,Sergeant Maclear\0312,3358,1461,0,\0302,0,0,8,Sergeant Maclear\0302,0,0,8,Refuge Pointe\0318297,19,8297,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0308080,22,8080,UNKNOWN\0308081,22,8081,UNKNOWN\0308154,22,8154,UNKNOWN\0308155,22,8155,UNKNOWN\0308156,22,8156,UNKNOWN\0308157,22,8157,UNKNOWN\0308158,22,8158,UNKNOWN\0308159,22,8159,UNKNOWN\0308297,22,8297,UNKNOWN\031ITEM,19725,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8299]="PARTIAL\031conclusion,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031\030The League of Arathor is sparing no expense in their move to retake Arathi.  They, and all the races of the Alliance, now stream to this distant region, intent on expanding their hold from Refuge Pointe.  We must stop them, and the best means to stop them is to take their supplies.$B$BYou can help us, $N.  Enter Arathi Basin, known for its rich mines, fertile land and skilled craftsman.  Capture and control every base you can, win the battle, and return to me with the resources you gain.\030Win the battle for Arathi Basin, get an Arathi Resource Crate, and return it to Deathstalker Mortis at Hammerfall.\030\030Cut Arathor Supply Lines\0312,1,75,2,257,1,0\0302,78,203,2,257,1,0\0302,206,282,2,257,1,0\0302,287,306,2,257,1,0\0302,309,389,2,257,1,0\0302,392,492,2,261,1,0\0303,1,114,2,388,1,0\03115022,2,7,Deathstalker Mortis\0312,3358,1461,0,\0302,0,0,2,Refuge Pointe\0302,0,0,7,Deathstalker Mortis\0302,0,0,7,Hammerfall\0318123,22,8123,UNKNOWN\0308124,22,8124,UNKNOWN\0308160,22,8160,UNKNOWN\0308161,22,8161,UNKNOWN\0308162,22,8162,UNKNOWN\0308163,22,8163,UNKNOWN\0308164,22,8164,UNKNOWN\0308165,22,8165,UNKNOWN\0308300,22,8300,UNKNOWN\0308300,23,8300,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,20559,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[83]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, these are nice bandanas, if a little rough...$B$BHere you are!\030The Defias gang in Northshire wears burlap masks, but the Defias in Elwynn wear linen which I can use to make fine linen goods.$B$BBring me red linen bandanas and I'll use them to fashion something for you.$B$BDefias gang members have camps pocketed throughout Elwynn.\030Bring 6 Red Linen Bandanas to Sara Timberlain at the Eastvale Logging Camp.\030I'm running low on linen, $N. Do you have any for me?\030Red Linen Goods\0312,1,127,2,257,1,278\0302,132,206,2,257,1,278\0302,211,268,2,257,1,278\0303,1,75,2,384,1,278\0301,1,49,4,272,4,278\0301,54,66,4,272,1,278\0304,1,29,3,256,1,278\0304,31,53,3,256,2,278\031278,2,4,Sara Timberlain\0312,12,1429,0,\0302,0,0,1,Northshire\0302,0,0,1,Elwynn\0302,0,0,4,Sara Timberlain\0302,0,0,4,Eastvale Logging Camp\031\031ITEM,1019,OBJECTIVE,6,15,",[830]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This does not bode well at all. You were wise to bring this information to my attention.\030You open the aged and weathered envelope and discover an official looking document. You recognize the seal of Admiral Proudmoore.$B$BThis looks important. Perhaps Gar'Thok, the commander of Razor Hill, would be interested in having this information.\030Take Admiral Proudmoore's Orders to Gar'Thok in Razor Hill.\030There is a look of concern on your face, $C. What have you there?\030The Admiral's Orders\0312,1,83,2,257,1,0\0302,85,129,2,257,1,0\0302,134,154,2,257,1,0\0302,156,249,2,257,4,0\0303,1,59,2,384,1,0\0301,1,31,4,272,1,3139\0301,33,88,4,272,1,3139\0304,1,44,3,256,1,3139\0304,46,65,3,256,2,3139\0313139,2,4,Gar'Thok\0303139,2,5,Gar'Thok\0312,14,1411,0,\0302,0,0,5,Gar'Thok\0302,0,0,5,Razor Hill\031831,23,831,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4881,STARTER,?,10,",[8300]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Very good. I will get these to our quartermasters immediately, and a commendation for your actions will be sent to my superiors.$B$BOnce again, thank you $N. Your contributions to our struggles are noticed by grunt and high warlord alike.\030The League of Arathor is sparing no expense in their move to retake Arathi. They, and all the races of the Alliance, now stream to this distant region, intent on expanding their hold from Refuge Pointe. We must stop them, and the best means to stop them is to take their supplies.$B$BYou can help us, $N. Enter Arathi Basin, known for its rich mines, fertile land and skilled craftsman. Capture and control every base you can, win the battle, and return to me with the resources you gain.\030Win the battle for Arathi Basin, get an Arathi Resource Crate, and return it to Deathstalker Mortis at Hammerfall.\030$N, the Defilers has a standing mission for you to reenter Arathi Basin, procure more resource crates and bring them to me.\030More Resource Crates\0312,1,75,2,257,1,0\0302,77,202,2,257,1,0\0302,204,280,2,257,1,0\0302,285,304,2,257,1,0\0302,306,386,2,257,1,0\0302,388,488,2,261,1,0\0303,1,114,2,388,1,0\0301,1,10,4,272,1,0\0301,12,128,4,272,3,0\0301,133,157,4,272,1,0\0301,159,238,4,272,1,0\0304,1,123,3,256,1,0\03115022,2,7,Deathstalker Mortis\0312,3358,1461,0,\0302,0,0,2,Refuge Pointe\0302,0,0,7,Deathstalker Mortis\0302,0,0,7,Hammerfall\0318299,19,8299,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0308123,22,8123,UNKNOWN\0308124,22,8124,UNKNOWN\0308160,22,8160,UNKNOWN\0308161,22,8161,UNKNOWN\0308162,22,8162,UNKNOWN\0308163,22,8163,UNKNOWN\0308164,22,8164,UNKNOWN\0308165,22,8165,UNKNOWN\0308299,22,8299,UNKNOWN\031ITEM,19725,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8301]="PARTIAL\031consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You are not alone, hero. I will now grant you the ability to deputize others to help you in your quest. If you are to be the champion of your people, you will need assistance in your tasks and duties.\030The Brood of Nozdormu are naturally distrusting of the lesser races. While it is true that you have proven to me that you have the potential makings of a hero, the time has come to prove this to my master.$B$BHive'Ashi, Hive'Zora, Hive'Regal: All swarming with activity and all a threat to our existence. Slay silithid at these hives and take from them a fragment of their carapace. When you can carry no more, return to me and I shall strengthen your resolve.\030Collect 200 Silithid Carapace Fragments and return to Baristolth.\030There is much history rooted in their distrust of the mortal races; but alas, such is a tale better left for the Brood to tell when the time is right.\030The Path of the Righteous\0312,1,68,2,257,1,15180\0302,70,205,2,257,1,15180\0302,210,304,2,261,1,15180\0302,306,382,2,257,1,15180\0302,384,460,2,257,3,15180\0303,1,65,2,384,1,15180\0301,1,24,4,272,1,15180\0301,26,103,4,272,3,15180\0301,105,200,4,274,4,15180\0304,1,150,3,320,1,15180\03115185,2,1,Brood of Nozdormu\0312,1377,1451,0,\0302,0,0,6,Baristolth\0318288,19,8288,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,20384,OBJECTIVE,200,15,",[8302]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done, hero. You will now be granted the ability to deputize another Agent of Nozdormu.\030Choose your deputies wisely, mortal. Each time you return with your task complete, a new deputy you will be allowed to choose.$B$BWith that said, I require more of the carapace fragments. Waste no time!\030Collect 200 Silithid Carapace Fragments and return to Baristolth.\030Perhaps one day the whole of Cenarion Hold will be working under your command.\030The Hand of the Righteous\0312,1,36,2,257,1,15180\0302,38,126,2,257,3,15180\0302,131,187,2,257,1,15180\0302,189,202,2,257,1,15180\0303,1,65,2,384,1,15180\0301,1,16,4,272,1,15180\0301,18,91,4,272,3,15180\0304,1,78,3,256,4,15180\031\0312,1377,1451,0,\0302,0,0,5,Baristolth\0318301,19,8301,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,20384,OBJECTIVE,200,15,",[8303]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You are the hope of Kalimdor, $N.\030It is time, $N.$B$BI must apologize for keeping so much in secret. Enemies abound, even under our very noses. Please, read from this tome and learn. Take the knowledge I give to you and seek out our master.\030Seek out Anachronos at the Caverns of Time in Tanaris.\030\030Anachronos\0312,1,15,2,257,1,15180\0302,20,66,2,257,1,15180\0302,68,109,2,261,1,15180\0302,111,148,2,257,1,15180\0302,150,206,2,259,1,15180\0303,1,54,2,384,1,15180\0301,1,33,4,274,3,15192\03115192,2,6,Anachronos\0312,1377,1451,0,\0302,0,0,6,Caverns of Time\0302,0,0,6,Tanaris\0318301,19,8301,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0308305,23,8305,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[8304]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030objectiveLabel3\030requestItems\030title\031<Commander Mar'alith lowers his head in contemplation.>$B$BWhether she is alive or dead, I must do what is right. She must be found. Alas, I am bound by duty to this outpost. Will you help me once more, $N?\030My dear Natalia has gone missing.$B$BTruth be told, she had been acting strangely for weeks leading up to her disappearance. I had caught her talking to herself when no one was around on more than one occasion. She was adamant that everything was ok and that she must be allowed to continue her research.$B$BShe was last seen heading to Bronzebeard's camp to the south.$B$BMy soldiers are spread too thin, $N. I need you to go to Bronzebeard's camp and question those dwarves.\030Commander Mar'alith at Cenarion Hold in Silithus wants you to question the inhabitants of Bronzebeard's Encampment. You will find Bronzebeard's Encampment south of Cenarion Hold.$B$BOnce you have gathered the requested information, return to Commander Mar'alith.\030\030Frankal Questioned\030Rutgar Questioned\030Waste no time, $N!\030Dearest Natalia\0312,1,33,2,261,1,15181\0302,38,124,2,257,1,15181\0302,126,210,2,257,1,15181\0302,212,304,2,257,1,15181\0302,309,369,2,257,1,15181\0302,374,409,2,257,1,15181\0302,411,476,2,259,1,15181\0303,1,115,2,386,1,15181\0303,117,178,2,384,3,15181\0303,183,262,2,384,1,15181\0301,1,55,4,272,1,15181\0301,60,113,4,272,1,15181\0301,115,132,4,272,1,15181\0301,134,174,4,276,1,15181\0301,176,206,4,272,2,15181\0307,1,18,3,256,1,15181\0305,1,18,3,384,1,15181\0306,1,17,3,384,1,15181\03115181,2,8,Commander Mar'alith\03015181,2,10,Commander Mar'alith\03015181,4,11,Commander Mar'alith\0312,1377,1451,0,\0302,0,0,5,Bronzebeard's\0302,0,0,7,Bronzebeard's\0302,0,0,8,Cenarion Hold\0302,0,0,8,Silithus\0302,0,0,9,Cenarion Hold\0302,0,0,10,Commander Mar'alith\0318306,23,8306,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,15221,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Frankal Invisible Trigger\030NPC,15222,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Rutgar Invisible Trigger",[8305]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You can feel a great sorrow revolving around this crystal. The force is so powerful that you feel as if you might collapse and die of sadness.\030In the southern desert of Silithus, near the sacred barrier, exists a single crystalline tear. This tear serves as a symbol of the great losses beset upon us during the War of the Shifting Sands. Locate this tear and gaze into its depths to gain enlightenment.$B\030Locate the Crystalline Tear in Silithus and gaze into its depths.\030\030Long Forgotten Memories\0312,1,94,2,257,1,15192\0302,96,195,2,261,1,15192\0302,197,260,2,257,1,15192\0303,1,65,2,384,1,15192\0301,1,58,4,272,1,0\0301,60,142,4,272,4,0\031\0312,1377,1451,0,\0302,0,0,4,Silithus\0318303,19,8303,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0308519,23,8519,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,180633,FINISHER,?,12,Crystalline Tear",[8306]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030requestItems\030title\031<Commander Mar'alith clutches at his chest.>$B$BC'Thun? WHAT is the meaning of all this? What is C'Thun? How could this fiend have turned my sweet Natalia into the monster that you described?\030I need you to venture into Hive'Regal and find what became of my dearest Natalia, $N. This will be no easy task for you. Before you dive headlong into the maw of madness, make sure that you go back and speak with those dwarves. They might be able to give you some tips on dealing with the silithid that inhabit that hive.$B$BAnd $N, if she truly is as mad as they say... do what you must.$B$B<Commander Mar'alith turns away from you.>$B\030Commander Mar'alith at Cenarion Hold in Silithus wants you to find his beloved Natalia. The information that you gathered points to Hive'Regal in the south as being the area in which you may find Mistress Natalia Mar'alith.$B$BDo not forget to visit the dwarves at Bronzebeard's camp before venturing into the hive. They might have some additional work and advice for you.$B$BAnd $N, remember the Commander's words: \"Do what you must...\"\030\030The Fate of Mistress Natalia Mar'alith\030Natalia?\030Into The Maw of Madness\0312,1,85,2,259,1,15181\0302,87,120,2,257,3,15181\0302,122,227,2,257,1,15181\0302,229,321,2,257,4,15181\0302,326,370,2,257,4,15181\0302,372,388,2,257,1,15181\0302,393,434,2,257,1,15181\0303,1,87,2,386,1,15181\0303,89,223,2,384,1,15181\0303,228,315,2,384,1,15181\0303,317,372,2,384,4,15181\0303,377,437,2,384,1,15181\0301,1,44,4,272,1,15181\0301,49,55,4,272,2,15181\0301,57,88,4,272,2,15181\0301,90,104,4,272,2,15181\0301,106,191,4,272,4,15181\0306,1,8,3,256,2,15181\0305,1,38,3,384,1,15181\03115181,2,7,Commander Mar'alith\03015181,2,8,Commander Mar'alith\03015215,2,9,Mistress Natalia Mar'alith\03015181,4,13,Commander Mar'alith\03015727,4,14,C'Thun\03015727,4,16,C'Thun\03015215,3,19,Mistress Natalia Mar'alith\0312,1377,1451,0,\0302,0,0,8,Cenarion Hold\0302,0,0,8,Silithus\0302,0,0,9,Hive'Regal\0302,0,0,10,Bronzebeard's\0318304,19,8304,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,15215,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Mistress Natalia Mar'alith",[8307]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This book contains several common recipes and a few unusual ones. After browsing through it for a few seconds you spot a recipe that involves sandworm meat.\030Adapting to life in the desert has been difficult to say the least.  Not only do I miss the birds and trees of Auberdine but our food selection is severely limited by this arid environment.  I'm trying to learn about desert herbs, but there aren't many.$B$BI've seen Twilight's Hammer groups from the camp west of here hunt sandworms for food.  Sandworm meat is so bitter though, I can't imagine how they make it palatable.  Keep your eyes open if you go to their camp and let me know if you learn anything.\030Look for information about cooking Sandworm Meat at the Twilight's Hammer camp west of Cenarion Hold.\030\030Desert Recipe\0312,1,67,2,257,1,15174\0302,70,189,2,257,1,15174\0302,192,253,2,257,1,15174\0302,258,343,2,257,1,15174\0302,346,423,2,257,1,15174\0302,426,507,2,257,4,15174\0303,1,101,2,384,1,15174\0301,1,65,4,272,1,0\0301,67,156,4,272,1,0\03117075,2,5,Sandworm\03017075,2,7,Sandworm\0304950,4,9,Spot\03017075,4,9,Sandworm\0312,0,0,7,Twilight's Hammer\0302,0,0,7,Cenarion Hold\0318313,23,8313,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,180503,FINISHER,?,12,Sandy Cookbook",[8308]="PARTIAL\031consequences,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well this explains a lot. If you ever find a way into Ahn'Qiraj, keep an eye out for ol' Brann. I'm afraid that he'll be powerless without his monkey.\030To Whom It May Concern:$B$BIf you're reading this, I'm either dead or soon to be dead. It's hard to say. Most of the crew is dead anyhow.$B$BFound information about a Titan. Great battle between him and an Old God. Yes, a bona fide Old God. Found ancient tunnel leading to Ahn'Qiraj. Taking it.$B$BTake this letter to my old camp. Make sure my monkey is getting adequate food, water, and hugs.$B$B-Brann Bronzebeard, Explorer Extreme$B$BP.S. Watch out for crazy Old God worshipping night elf.\030Take Brann Bronzebeard's Letter to Bronzebeard's Encampment in southern Silithus.\030Oh dear.\030Brann Bronzebeard's Lost Letter\0312,1,23,2,257,1,0\0302,28,86,2,257,4,0\0302,88,104,2,257,1,0\0302,106,137,2,257,1,0\0302,142,173,2,321,1,0\0302,175,214,2,261,1,0\0302,216,240,2,257,1,0\0302,242,283,2,321,1,0\0302,285,294,2,257,1,0\0302,299,330,2,257,1,0\0302,332,393,2,257,1,0\0302,398,433,2,257,1,0\0302,443,492,2,257,1,0\0303,1,81,2,384,1,0\0301,1,25,4,272,1,15170\0301,27,95,4,272,4,15170\0301,97,150,4,272,1,15170\0304,1,8,3,256,1,15170\031\0312,1377,1451,0,\0302,0,0,8,Ahn'Qiraj\0302,0,0,14,Bronzebeard's Encampment\031\031ITEM,20461,STARTER,?,10,",[8309]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I can't make heads or tails of these glyphs. I've never seen anything like it! I hope Frankal's research can shed some light on this mess.\030After our initial foray into the hives and Mistress Mar'alith's subsequent madness the three hives have been spewing out bugs! The increased activity might be tied into the glyphs covering those strange crystals.$B$BWe must get a rubbing from crystals in all three hives. If we can get those rubbings, we might be able to make sense of this madness.$B$BTake this transcription set  and hit those hives, $N. Don't come back until you've gotten copies from each hive.\030Rutgar Glyphshaper at Bronzebeard's Encampment in Silithus wants you to venture to Hive'Ashi, Hive'Zora, and Hive'Regal and recover Glyphed Rubbings from the Glyphed Crystals of each hive.$B$BUse the Geologist's Transcription Kit to make a reasonable facsimile of the ancient glyphs. Return to Rutgar Glyphshaper when you complete this task.\030If you find some crazy night elf lass in one of the hives, be sure to give her a kick in the duff for us.\030Glyph Chasing\0312,1,126,2,257,1,15170\0302,128,212,2,257,4,15170\0302,217,271,2,257,1,15170\0302,273,349,2,257,4,15170\0302,354,406,2,257,1,15170\0302,408,465,2,257,1,15170\0303,1,188,2,386,1,15170\0303,193,283,2,448,1,15170\0303,285,341,2,384,1,15170\0301,1,44,4,272,1,15170\0301,46,78,4,272,1,15170\0301,80,138,4,274,3,15170\0304,1,105,3,256,4,15170\03115170,2,7,Rutgar Glyphshaper\03015170,2,9,Rutgar Glyphshaper\0312,1377,1451,0,\0302,0,0,7,Bronzebeard's Encampment\0302,0,0,7,Silithus\0302,0,0,7,Hive'Ashi\0302,0,0,7,Glyphed Crystals of\0302,0,0,9,Rutgar Glyphshaper\0318304,19,8304,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,20455,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,20454,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,20456,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[831]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Countless times I urged the Warchief not to trust the humans, but personal pride is not what is at stake here.$B$BYou have served the Horde honorably, young $C.$B$BNow excuse me, I must counsel Thrall on these matters at once...\030Humans cannot be trusted. We fought alongside them with a weary heart, knowing they would betray us one day.$B$BAdmiral Proudmoore's death was not enough to stop his legacy of deceit. The human scum had his plans well laid out before he ever met his demise.$B$BHis reign won't even die with Benedict it seems. Who knows how long it will be before the next waves of Proudmoore's men land upon our shores.$B$BWe need to get these orders to Nazgrel in Orgrimmar immediately! He can be found in Thrall's chamber.\030Deliver Admiral Proudmoore's Orders to Nazgrel in Thrall's chamber in Orgrimmar.\030Can you not see that I am busy? This had better be pressing...\030The Admiral's Orders\0312,1,25,2,257,1,3139\0302,27,108,2,257,4,3139\0302,113,183,2,257,1,3139\0302,185,257,2,265,1,3139\0302,262,309,2,257,4,3139\0302,311,403,2,257,3,3139\0302,408,471,2,259,1,3139\0302,473,508,2,257,1,3139\0303,1,80,2,384,1,3139\0301,1,110,4,280,1,3230\0301,115,160,4,272,1,3230\0301,165,228,4,272,1,3230\0304,1,31,3,256,2,3230\0304,33,62,3,256,1,3230\0313230,2,7,Nazgrel\0303230,2,9,Nazgrel\0304949,4,12,Thrall\0312,14,1411,0,\0302,0,0,7,Nazgrel\0302,0,0,7,Orgrimmar\0302,0,0,8,Thrall's\0302,0,0,9,Nazgrel\0302,0,0,9,Thrall's\0302,0,0,9,Orgrimmar\031830,19,830,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[8310]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Outstanding! Don't wander off too far, kid. We might need you to take on another task or two.\030I think I can formulate an elixir that will allow us to more readily decipher the glyphs and language of the silithid and Qiraji! What do I need? Glad you asked! I need brains! More specifically, a brain from each silithid type that inhabit the hives. Bring me brains and Rutgar's work might not be for naught.\030Frankal Stonebridge at Bronzebeard's Encampment in Silithus wants you to recover a Hive'Zora Silithid Brain, Hive'Ashi Silithid Brain, and a Hive'Regal Silithid Brain. Return to Frankal when you have completed this task.\030Go play with the monkey, kid. I don't have time for this.\030Breaking the Code\0312,1,129,2,257,3,15171\0302,131,145,2,259,2,15171\0302,147,161,2,257,1,15171\0302,163,176,2,259,1,15171\0302,178,251,2,257,1,15171\0302,253,310,2,257,4,15171\0303,1,167,2,386,1,15171\0303,169,220,2,384,1,15171\0301,1,12,4,272,1,15171\0301,14,43,4,272,1,15171\0301,45,93,4,274,4,15171\0304,1,29,3,256,1,15171\0304,31,57,3,256,1,15171\03115171,2,7,Frankal Stonebridge\0312,1377,1451,0,\0302,0,0,7,Bronzebeard's Encampment\0302,0,0,7,Silithus\0302,0,0,8,Frankal\0318304,19,8304,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,20457,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,20458,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,20459,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8311]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Wow, you got them all!  You're awesome!$B$BThank you for trick-or-treating for me.  Here, take these pumpkin treats - I think you'll like them a lot!$B$BHappy Hallow's End, $N!\030I want to go trick-or-treating, but I can't because I'm sick.  If you go for me, I'd trade you the candy you get for some I already have!  I think you'd like this candy - it makes you turn into things both funny and scary!$B$BEach of the innkeepers in the big cities have candy they give for Hallow's End - talk to them and do the tricks they ask for!  Also, a little gnome named Talvash in Ironforge is handing out candy as well.  When you have all the candy, bring them back to me here!\030Speak with the innkeepers of Stormwind, Ironforge, and Darnassus, as well as Talvash del Kissel in Ironforge.  Perform the tricks they ask of you in exchange for the treats they offer.$B$BReturn to Jesper at the Stormwind Orphanage with a Darnassus Marzipan, Gnomeregan Gumdrop, Stormwind Nougat, and Ironforge Mint.\030Have you finished trick-or-treating yet?  I'm sad that I can't go because I'm sick, but you helping me out makes me feel a little better...\030Hallow's End Treats for Jesper!\0312,1,61,2,259,1,15310\0302,64,137,2,257,4,15310\0302,140,222,2,257,1,15310\0302,227,351,2,257,1,15310\0302,354,430,2,257,1,15310\0302,433,488,2,257,1,15310\0303,1,109,2,384,1,15310\0303,112,184,2,384,1,15310\0303,189,316,2,384,1,15310\0301,1,22,4,272,1,15310\0301,25,39,4,272,1,15310\0301,44,82,4,272,1,15310\0301,85,149,4,272,1,15310\0301,154,176,4,272,1,15310\0304,1,40,3,256,2,15310\0304,43,139,3,258,1,15310\0316826,2,7,Talvash del Kissel\03015310,2,9,Jesper\0312,0,0,5,Ironforge\0302,0,0,7,Ironforge\0302,0,0,9,Jesper\0302,0,0,9,Stormwind Orphanage\031\031ITEM,20492,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,20494,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,20490,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,20496,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8312]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Wow, you got them all!  You're awesome!$B$BThank you for trick-or-treating for me.  Here, take these pumpkin treats - I think you'll like them a lot!$B$BHappy Hallow's End, $N!\030I want to go trick-or-treating, but I can't because I'm sick.  If you go for me, I'd trade you the candy you get for some I already have!  I think you'd like this candy - it makes you turn into things both funny and scary!$B$BEach of the innkeepers in the big cities have candy they give for Hallow's End - talk to them and do the tricks they ask for!  Also, a troll named Kali Remik in Sen'jin Village is handing out candy as well.  When you have all the candy, bring them back to me here!\030Speak with the innkeepers of Orgrimmar, Undercity, and Thunder Bluff, as well as Kali Remik in Sen'jin Village.  Perform the tricks they ask of you in exchange for the treats they offer.$B$BReturn to Spoops at the Orgrimmar Orphanage with a Thunder Bluff Marzipan, Darkspear Gumdrop, Orgrimmar Nougat, and Undercity Mint.\030Have you finished trick-or-treating yet?  I'm sad that I can't go because I'm sick, but you helping me out makes me feel a little better...\030Hallow's End Treats for Spoops!\0312,1,61,2,259,1,15309\0302,64,137,2,257,4,15309\0302,140,222,2,257,1,15309\0302,227,351,2,257,1,15309\0302,354,432,2,257,1,15309\0302,435,490,2,257,1,15309\0303,1,111,2,384,1,15309\0303,114,186,2,384,1,15309\0303,191,321,2,384,1,15309\0301,1,22,4,272,1,15309\0301,25,39,4,272,1,15309\0301,44,82,4,272,1,15309\0301,85,149,4,272,1,15309\0301,154,176,4,272,1,15309\0304,1,40,3,256,2,15309\0304,43,139,3,258,1,15309\03111814,2,5,Kali Remik\03011814,2,7,Kali Remik\03015309,2,9,Spoops\0312,0,0,5,Sen'jin Village\0302,0,0,7,Sen'jin Village\0302,0,0,9,Spoops\0302,0,0,9,Orgrimmar Orphanage\031\031ITEM,20493,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,20495,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,20491,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,20497,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8313]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Let's have a look at that...$B$BThis seems simple enough.  They have their own names for some of the herbs, but those are simple enough to figure out.  Here, let me show you!\030While the recipe for cooking sandworm meat is legible, it contains references to herbs and spices you've never heard of.  Calandrath might have enough knowledge of the plants that grow in the desert to make sense of it.\030Bring the Torn Recipe Page to Calandrath at the inn in Cenarion Hold.\030Did you learn the recipe?  You won't keep it to yourself, I hope!\030Sharing the Knowledge\0312,1,120,2,257,1,0\0302,123,219,2,257,4,0\0303,1,69,2,384,1,0\0301,1,28,4,272,1,15174\0301,33,57,4,272,4,15174\0301,60,150,4,272,1,15174\0301,153,174,4,272,1,15174\0304,1,25,3,256,2,15174\0304,28,65,3,258,3,15174\03117075,2,1,Sandworm\03015174,2,2,Calandrath\0302996,2,3,Torn\03015174,2,3,Calandrath\0312,0,0,3,Calandrath\0302,0,0,3,Cenarion Hold\0318307,19,8307,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0308317,23,8317,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,180503,GIVER,?,9,Sandy Cookbook",[8314]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The reason the dwarves could not decipher the glyphs is because there is nothing to decipher. The shifting outer layer of the prism must properly align with the inner crystal's markings in order for the message to be transmitted. Clever...$B$BWhile we should be able to translate this data, we must first unlock the code. There is only one clue on the surface of the prism - assuming the rubbings were transferred correctly - and it looks grim.\030We're on the verge of a breakthrough, $N! The rubbings you recovered have allowed us to recreate the glyphs on this crystalline prism. They are apparently a means for the Qiraji and other unknown entities to communicate various messages to the silithid.$B$BUnfortunately, that is all we could get out of the glyphs. We need to find a way to unlock the messages hidden within the crystals.$B$BTake the glyphed crystal prism to Geologist Larksbane at Cenarion Hold.  She might be able to help.\030Rutgar Glyphshaper at Bronzebeard's Encampment wants you to deliver the Glyphed Crystal Prism to Geologist Larksbane at the Cenarion Hold in Silithus.\030Oh my! What do you have there, $N?\030Unraveling the Mystery\0312,1,41,2,257,1,15170\0302,43,134,2,257,1,15170\0302,136,253,2,257,4,15170\0302,258,315,2,257,4,15170\0302,317,388,2,259,1,15170\0302,393,463,2,257,1,15170\0302,466,491,2,257,4,15170\0303,1,150,2,386,1,15170\0301,1,93,4,274,4,15183\0301,95,229,4,272,1,15183\0301,231,239,4,272,1,15183\0301,244,321,4,272,1,15183\0301,323,444,4,272,1,15183\0304,8,34,3,256,2,15183\03115183,2,6,Geologist Larksbane\03015170,2,8,Rutgar Glyphshaper\03015183,2,8,Geologist Larksbane\0312,1377,1451,0,\0302,0,0,6,Geologist Larksbane\0302,0,0,6,Cenarion Hold\0302,0,0,8,Bronzebeard's Encampment\0302,0,0,8,Geologist Larksbane\0302,0,0,8,Cenarion Hold\0302,0,0,8,Silithus\0318309,21,8309,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0308310,21,8310,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0308315,23,8315,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[8315]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I hold 20,000 years of history in my hands, $N!\030The glyphs illustrate an emissary of the Qiraji meeting with three silithid at the bones of a large dragon. Above the glyphs is what I can only assume to be a code of some sort. This code might very well be the key to summoning the emissary.$B$BI will create a copy of the glyph code that you must use in the sand at the Bones of Grakkarond. If I am right, the Overlords will come thinking that new data is ready for transmission. Strike them down and confront the emissary. He holds the key to the crystals...\030Geologist Larksbane at Cenarion Hold in Silithus wants you to recover the Crystal Unlocking Mechanism from the Qiraji Emissary.$B$BYou have been instructed to take the Glyphs of Calling to the Bones of Grakkarond, south of Cenarion Hold, and draw them in the sand. Should the Qiraji Emissary appear, slay it and recover the Crystal Unlocking Mechanism. Return to Geologist Larksbane if you succeed.$B$BAssemble an army for this task, $N!\030You must take the opportunity as it presents itself and strike!\030The Calling\0312,1,107,2,257,1,15183\0302,109,177,2,257,4,15183\0302,179,241,2,257,4,15183\0302,246,341,2,257,3,15183\0302,343,430,2,257,4,15183\0302,432,474,2,257,1,15183\0302,476,510,2,257,1,15183\0303,1,127,2,386,1,15183\0303,132,264,2,384,1,15183\0303,266,352,2,384,1,15183\0303,354,398,2,384,4,15183\0303,403,437,2,384,1,15183\0301,1,47,4,336,1,15183\0304,1,63,3,256,1,15183\03115183,2,8,Geologist Larksbane\03015183,2,11,Geologist Larksbane\0312,1377,1451,0,\0302,0,0,4,Bones of Grakkarond\0302,0,0,8,Cenarion Hold\0302,0,0,8,Silithus\0302,0,0,8,Qiraji Emissary\0302,0,0,9,Bones of Grakkarond\0302,0,0,9,Cenarion Hold\0302,0,0,11,Geologist Larksbane\0318314,19,8314,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,20465,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8316]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031War comes, $N, and with it comes untold horrors. You have done all that could be asked of you and for that you should be rewarded.$B$BShould this... this prophecy ever come to pass...$B$B<Geologist Larksbane turns pale.>$B$BThe future of us all could be at an end.$B$BThese armaments will prove invaluable to your campaign in this desert.\030\030\030\030Armaments of War\0311,1,48,4,276,1,15183\0301,50,130,4,272,4,15183\0301,135,148,4,272,1,15183\0301,150,183,4,272,1,15183\0301,188,220,4,272,1,15183\0301,225,264,4,272,4,15183\0301,269,338,4,272,3,15183\03115183,4,5,Geologist Larksbane\0312,1377,1451,0,\0318315,19,8315,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[8317]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Excellent! You're a life saver. These dumplings turned out to be quite good. Didn't really expect such good taste from the Twilight's Hammer.\030That recipe sure will come in handy.  I'd better get to work so I can have some smoked desert dumplings ready for today.  I could use a hand in making some, I'll make it worth your while.\030Calandrath at Cenarion Hold needs a batch of 10 Smoked Desert Dumplings.\030How are those dumplings coming along?\030Kitchen Assistance\0312,1,36,2,257,3,15174\0302,39,120,2,257,1,15174\0302,123,187,2,257,4,15174\0303,1,72,2,386,1,15174\0301,1,10,4,272,1,15174\0301,12,31,4,272,1,15174\0301,33,76,4,272,1,15174\0301,78,141,4,272,1,15174\0304,1,37,3,256,2,15174\03115174,2,4,Calandrath\0312,0,0,4,Cenarion Hold\0304,0,0,8,Twilight's Hammer\0318313,19,8313,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,20452,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[8318]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Excellent!  I'll stash these away, maybe they'll be useful later.\030Some of the Twilight's Hammer cultists carry around little papers with gibberish written on them.  I want you to bring me a stack of them, $c.$B$BI can't figure out what the gibberish means, but that's not the point!  These papers are how their different groups communicate secretly.  The more texts we take out of circulation, the less they can communicate!\030Bring 10 Encrypted Twilight Texts to Bor Wildmane in Cenarion Hold.\030Did you bring me some texts?\030Secret Communication\0312,1,97,2,257,1,15306\0302,100,142,2,259,1,15306\0302,147,216,2,257,1,15306\0302,219,283,2,257,1,15306\0302,286,358,2,257,1,15306\0303,1,67,2,384,1,15306\0301,1,10,4,272,1,15306\0301,13,65,4,272,4,15306\0304,1,28,3,256,2,15306\03115306,2,6,Bor Wildmane\0312,1377,1451,0,\0302,0,0,6,Bor Wildmane\0302,0,0,6,Cenarion Hold\0318319,23,8319,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,20404,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[8319]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Excellent work!  I'll put a good word in for you.\030\030\030Keep bringing me texts.  We'll soon force the Twilight's Hammer out of Silithus.\030Encrypted Twilight Texts\0311,1,15,4,272,1,15306\0301,18,49,4,272,1,15306\0304,1,23,3,256,1,15306\0304,26,80,3,256,1,15306\031\0312,1377,1451,0,\0318318,19,8318,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,20404,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[832]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031<Examines the Eye of Burning Shadow>$B$BIntriguing. The voice you heard mentioned my name? I am known for hunting down enemies of our Warchief, but...it is strange that I was singled out. Stranger still that the Burning Blade cultists from whom you recovered this pendant have a name so close to my own.$B$BI must study this pendant. I must study and, and must ponder the meaning of its message.$B$BThank you for bringing this to my attention, $N. You have done your people a great service.\030<Words emanate from the pendant and into your mind.>$B$BGazz'uz?$B$BGazz'uz...report!$B$BThere is word of your discovery in Skull Rock.  You must prepare for an attack!$B$BGazz'uz, I order you to speak!  Speak or I will make sure Neeru Fireblade knows of your presence, and he will descend on you with swift brutality.$B$BDo not test your skills against Neeru...$B$B...Gazz'uz, are you there...?\030Take this eye to Neeru Fireblade.\030You have something vital to report. I can sense it behind your eyes.\030Burning Shadows\0312,1,52,2,257,1,0\0302,57,64,2,257,2,0\0302,69,85,2,257,1,0\0302,90,135,2,257,1,0\0302,138,168,2,261,1,0\0302,173,202,2,257,1,0\0302,205,318,2,257,3,0\0302,323,362,2,257,1,0\0302,367,395,2,257,2,0\0303,1,33,2,384,1,0\0301,1,36,4,272,1,3216\0301,41,51,4,272,1,3216\0301,53,90,4,272,2,3216\0301,92,187,4,276,1,3216\0301,189,303,4,272,1,3216\0301,308,333,4,272,1,3216\0301,335,395,4,272,1,3216\0301,400,447,4,272,1,3216\0301,449,490,4,272,1,3216\0304,1,35,3,256,1,3216\0304,37,68,3,256,1,3216\0313204,2,2,Gazz'uz\0303204,2,3,Gazz'uz\0303204,2,6,Gazz'uz\0303216,2,7,Neeru Fireblade\0303204,2,9,Gazz'uz\0303216,2,10,Neeru Fireblade\0304244,4,11,Shadow\0312,14,1411,0,\0302,0,0,4,Skull Rock\0302,0,0,10,Neeru Fireblade\031\031ITEM,4903,STARTER,?,10,",[8320]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031That was a task well performed, $N.  Your slaying of the Twilight geolords must have dealt a grievous blow to the cult.  Let us hope their plans are slowed...\030The Twilight's Hammer, an insane cult bent on destruction, set up camps in Silithus and perform rituals day and night.  We do not yet know their plans, but we do think they are somehow linked to the pulsing red crystals spread across the desert.$B$BAlthough their mystery may one day be solved, we must first deal with their immediate threat.  Go to their camps to the west and seek out Twilight geolords.  They are the heads of these serpents; that is where we must strike!\030Kill 10 Twilight Geolords, then return to Huum Wildmane in Cenarion Hold.\030Enter the desert and find the Twilight geolords, $N. Return to me after they are slain.\030Twilight Geolords\0312,1,118,2,257,1,15270\0302,121,245,2,257,1,15270\0302,250,342,2,261,1,15270\0302,345,405,2,259,1,15270\0302,408,474,2,257,1,15270\0303,1,73,2,384,1,15270\0301,1,35,4,272,1,15270\0301,38,119,4,272,1,15270\0301,122,158,4,274,3,15270\0304,1,52,3,256,1,15270\0304,54,87,3,260,1,15270\03115270,2,6,Huum Wildmane\0312,1377,1451,0,\0302,0,0,1,Silithus\0302,0,0,6,Huum Wildmane\0302,0,0,6,Cenarion Hold\0318321,23,8321,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,11881,OBJECTIVE,10,13,Twilight Geolord",[8321]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You've done it!  Vyral is killed!  This can only mean doom for the Twilight Hammer's operations in Silithus. There may be more of them scurrying about, but the blow you dealt to the cult today is one from which they will not easily recover.\030We have discovered another base of operations for the Twilight's Hammer.  It is called Twilight's Run; it is a cave tucked in the northeast corner of Silithus.  The local leader of the cult, Vyral the Vile, haunts that cave - it is he who you must next defeat.  When you have done this, bring me his signet ring.$B$BFortune to you, $N.  The horrors of Twilight's Run are formidable indeed.\030Bring Vyral's Signet Ring to Huum Wildmane in Cenarion Hold.\030$N, have you yet defeated Vyral the Vile?  Do you have his signet ring?\030Vyral the Vile\0312,1,72,2,257,1,15270\0302,75,159,2,257,1,15270\0302,162,260,2,257,1,15270\0302,263,312,2,257,1,15270\0302,317,335,2,257,1,15270\0302,338,389,2,257,1,15270\0303,1,60,2,384,1,15270\0301,1,15,4,272,1,15270\0301,18,33,4,272,1,15270\0301,36,108,4,272,1,15270\0301,110,240,4,272,3,15270\0304,1,41,3,256,2,15270\0304,44,71,3,256,2,15270\03115202,2,3,Vyral the Vile\03015270,2,7,Huum Wildmane\03015202,3,12,Vyral the Vile\0312,1377,1451,0,\0302,0,0,7,Huum Wildmane\0302,0,0,7,Cenarion Hold\0304,0,0,10,Silithus\0318320,19,8320,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,20466,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8322]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031The keg is filled with ale.$B$BHaving successfully fought your way inside the inn, you now place the eggs inside the keg. You can smell the foul odor permeating the air...\030The humans of Southshore love their ale, and as such they prize the ale served at the Southshore Inn.  With the chaos of Hallow's End now upon them, we can use it to ruin their latest batch of beverages for weeks - if not months to come!$B$BTake these rotten eggs and place them in the main brew keg inside the Southshore Inn.  Your presence alone will cause strife, so be prepared to defend yourself!$B$BOnce you've given Southshore a taste they'll not soon forget, return to me here at the festival!\030Place the Rotten Eggs in the main brew keg located inside the Southshore Inn.\030\030Rotten Eggs\0312,1,101,2,257,1,15197\0302,104,237,2,257,4,15197\0302,242,326,2,257,1,15197\0302,329,401,2,271,3,15197\0302,406,501,2,257,1,15197\0303,1,77,2,384,1,15197\0301,1,27,4,272,1,0\0301,32,121,4,272,1,0\0301,123,171,4,272,1,0\031\0312,0,0,1,Southshore Inn\0318409,23,8409,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031OBJECT,180570,FINISHER,?,12,Keg",[8323]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Excellent!  I will get to decoding these as soon as possible.  If I find anything of interest I'll find some way to get the information to you.\030Now that I have the Twilight Lexicon in my possession, there is a small favor I'd like to ask of you.$B$BMy former organization has a secret encoded bulletin they circulate on a monthly basis.$B$BIf they make any progress searching for me or if they call off the search, word will be published on the True Believer.$B$BAlthough this information is obviously valuable to me, the publication contains other useful information that I can share.  Bring me any encoded texts you find on Twilight's Hammer members.\030Hermit Ortell wants you to bring him 10 Encrypted Twilight Texts\030Did you find any encrypted texts?  I'm quite curious to read this month's True Believer.\030True Believers\0312,1,101,2,259,1,15194\0302,106,192,2,257,1,15194\0302,197,315,2,257,4,15194\0302,320,441,2,257,1,15194\0302,444,508,2,257,1,15194\0303,1,64,2,386,1,15194\0301,1,10,4,272,1,15194\0301,13,61,4,272,3,15194\0301,64,143,4,272,4,15194\0304,1,33,3,256,2,15194\0304,36,88,3,256,1,15194\03115194,2,6,Hermit Ortell\0312,1377,1451,0,\0318279,19,8279,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0308324,23,8324,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,20404,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[8324]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Excellent!  I can't wait to read these. Please do keep bringing the encrypted texts here if you find them.\030\030\030Find any more encrypted texts? Bring me a good batch of them, this decoding work takes some time.\030Still Believing\0311,1,10,4,272,1,15194\0301,13,39,4,272,1,15194\0301,41,106,4,272,4,15194\0304,1,30,3,256,2,15194\0304,32,97,3,256,1,15194\031\0312,1377,1451,0,\0318323,19,8323,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,20404,OBJECTIVE,10,15,",[833]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,questChains\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Well done. You have sent those foul Bristlebacks a clear message. They will think twice before attempting to meddle in this holy spot again.\030Only the most valiant tauren are laid to rest at Red Rocks, our sacred burial ground. It is an honor bestowed upon the great warriors who helped found and defend Thunder Bluff and those who have given their lives for the greater good of their tribes and chieftains.$B$BBut it appears a foul menace has made its way onto our holy land. A band of Bristleback Interlopers is ravaging the grave site and I am too old and past my prime to drive them away.$B$BThey must be driven off with force, $n.\030Lorekeeper Raintotem wants you to kill 8 Bristleback Interlopers at Red Rocks.\030The Bristleback Interlopers must be driven away from our sacred burial ground, $n.\030A Sacred Burial\0312,1,85,2,257,1,3233\0302,87,265,2,269,1,3233\0302,270,334,2,257,1,3233\0302,336,450,2,257,1,3233\0302,455,493,2,257,1,3233\0303,1,78,2,386,1,3233\0301,1,10,4,272,1,3233\0301,12,65,4,272,1,3233\0301,67,140,4,272,3,3233\0304,1,82,3,256,1,3233\0313233,2,6,Lorekeeper Raintotem\0304950,4,9,Spot\0312,215,1412,0,\0302,0,0,1,Red Rocks\0302,0,0,6,Red Rocks\031\031NPC,3232,OBJECTIVE,8,13,Bristleback Interloper",[8331]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031$N, good day. I was told you will pit yourself against the Abyssal Council? If that is so, then listen closely to my next words...\030$N, although we had hoped the Twilight's Hammer's operations in Silithus were slowing... we were, regrettably, mistaken.  Through continued forays against the cult, we have learned that an even darker power, the Abyssal Council, controls the Hammer through the arcane wind stones dotted amongst the cult's camps.  Your next action, $N, will be against the Abyssal Council.$B$BSpeak with the craftsman Aurel Goldleaf, in the eastern section of Cenarion Hold.  Her skill will be needed for this next gambit.\030Speak with Aurel Goldleaf in Cenarion Hold.\030\030Aurel Goldleaf\0312,1,88,2,257,1,15270\0302,90,120,2,257,1,15270\0302,123,312,2,257,1,15270\0302,315,372,2,257,3,15270\0302,377,457,2,257,1,15270\0302,460,505,2,257,3,15270\0303,1,43,2,384,1,15270\0301,1,13,4,272,1,15282\0301,15,75,4,272,2,15282\0301,77,130,4,272,4,15282\03115282,2,5,Aurel Goldleaf\03015282,2,7,Aurel Goldleaf\0312,1377,1451,0,\0302,0,0,1,Silithus\0302,0,0,7,Cenarion Hold\0318332,23,8332,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[8332]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, very good. I've been working on the medallion - now with these last ingredients, I'll be done in just a few moments...$B$BThere we are. Here is the medallion, $N.$B$BYou'll need to wear this when you activate one of the Twilight's Hammer's wind stones. Put this on, along with the rest of the twilight trappings, and the Abyssal Council will see you as one of their cultist underlings.\030We think it is possible to use a wind stone to ambush a duke of the Abyssal Council.  To do this, however, one must commune through the wind stone, and convince the council you are a middle ranked leader of the Twilight's Hammer.  $B$BSuch a gambit requires a replica of the cult's medallion of station.  I can create the medallion, but I will need a large brilliant shard, and crests worn by the Abyssal Templar.$B$BBring these to me and I will do the rest.\030Bring 1 Large Brilliant Shard and 3 Abyssal Crests to Aurel Goldleaf in Cenarion Hold.\030Do you have the shard and the crests, $N? I will need them to make the twilight cultist's medallion of station.\030Dukes of the Council\0312,1,84,2,261,1,15282\0302,87,229,2,257,1,15282\0302,236,303,2,257,1,15282\0302,306,413,2,259,3,15282\0302,418,458,2,257,3,15282\0303,1,86,2,384,1,15282\0301,1,14,4,272,1,15282\0301,16,122,4,272,1,15282\0301,127,139,4,272,1,15282\0301,141,166,4,272,1,15282\0301,171,256,4,274,1,15282\0301,258,389,4,272,3,15282\0304,1,41,3,256,2,15282\0304,43,111,3,258,3,15282\03115282,2,6,Aurel Goldleaf\0312,1377,1451,0,\0302,0,0,6,Aurel Goldleaf\0302,0,0,6,Cenarion Hold\0318331,19,8331,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0308349,23,8349,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,14344,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,20513,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[8333]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Here you are, $N. One more Twilight medallion of station. Use it well, and I wish you luck against the Abyssal Council!\030\030\030If you need another Twilight cultist's medallion of station, then I am happy to oblige. I will, however, need another brilliant shard and some abyssal crests...\030Medallion of Station\0311,1,17,4,272,1,15282\0301,19,57,4,272,1,15282\0301,59,119,4,274,3,15282\0304,1,87,3,258,4,15282\0304,89,160,3,256,3,15282\031\0312,1377,1451,0,\0318332,19,8332,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,14344,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,20513,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[834]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Hey, now isn't that just the thing! You've got our supplies back for us. That's great. I'll be able to get back to work just as soon as I can find someone to haul these sacks for me.\030I'm Rezlak, one of Gazlowe's boys. Boss sent me to help the orcs here in Durotar. Things'd been going good except for the caravans. Can't manage to keep them safe! Makes my job a little harder, you know?$B$BThe last shipment--they promised it'd get through!--was snatched by the Dustwind harpies of...where was it...Razorwind Canyon?$B$BI gotta have those supplies or I'll never get anything done! Follow the big canyon to the south, you'll find the ravine cut right into the west and east sides of the walls.\030Retrieve 5 Sacks of Supplies and return them to Rezlak near Orgrimmar.\030I'm great at what I do, don't get me wrong, but this is ridiculous! What am I supposed to do, build sand castles?\030Winds in the Desert\0312,1,34,2,257,1,3293\0302,36,81,2,257,1,3293\0302,83,131,2,257,1,3293\0302,133,163,2,257,1,3293\0302,165,203,2,257,2,3293\0302,208,333,2,257,2,3293\0302,338,397,2,257,1,3293\0302,399,509,2,257,1,3293\0303,1,70,2,384,1,3293\0301,1,35,4,272,1,3293\0301,37,72,4,272,1,3293\0301,74,86,4,272,1,3293\0301,88,182,4,272,1,3293\0304,1,67,3,256,1,3293\0304,69,113,3,256,2,3293\0313293,2,1,Rezlak\0303293,2,9,Rezlak\0312,14,1411,0,\0302,0,0,2,Durotar\0302,0,0,9,Rezlak\0302,0,0,9,Orgrimmar\031835,23,835,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,4918,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[8341]="PARTIAL\031loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Thanks. Just one moment and I'll have that ring ready for you...$B$BThere it is. Now you're ready.$B$BBe sure to wear this ring, along with a medallion of station and the rest of the twilight trappings, when you activate a greater wind stone. Do that, and the Abyssal Council will think you one of their servants. Then, perhaps you can lure one into an ambush!\030Lords of the Abyssal Council can only be summoned through the greater wind stones, and only the top ranking members of the Twilight's Council may speak to them.  But... I have found a way to upgrade your disguise and fool the Abyssal Lords!$B$BThe disguise calls for a ring of lordship, worn only by the highest members of the cult.  I will craft one for you if you can bring me large brilliant shards and abyssal signets.\030Bring 5 Large Brilliant Shards and 3 Abyssal Signets to Aurel Goldleaf in Cenarion Hold.\030Do you have the shards and the signets, $N? I will need them to create the ring of lordship.\030Lords of the Council\0312,1,160,2,257,1,15282\0302,163,168,2,257,1,15282\0302,170,240,2,257,1,15282\0302,245,332,2,257,1,15282\0302,335,422,2,257,4,15282\0303,1,88,2,384,1,15282\0301,1,7,4,272,1,15282\0301,9,64,4,272,1,15282\0301,69,80,4,272,1,15282\0301,82,98,4,304,1,15282\0301,103,242,4,272,1,15282\0301,244,313,4,272,3,15282\0301,315,360,4,276,4,15282\0304,1,43,3,256,2,15282\0304,45,92,3,258,3,15282\03115282,2,6,Aurel Goldleaf\0312,1377,1451,0,\0302,0,0,6,Aurel Goldleaf\0302,0,0,6,Cenarion Hold\0318351,23,8351,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,14344,OBJECTIVE,5,15,\030ITEM,20514,OBJECTIVE,3,15,",[8342]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,objectives,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Ah, I see your convictions are strong. Not many will face that council of fiends!$B$BHere's your ring, $N. May your will, and your fortune, stand firm.\030\030\030$N, if you plan to go after the Abyssal High Council again, then you'll need another Twilight ring of lordship. Bring me more shards and signets and I'll make one for you.\030Twilight Ring of Lordship\0311,1,38,4,272,1,15282\0301,40,81,4,272,3,15282\0301,86,106,4,272,1,15282\0301,108,151,4,272,3,15282\0304,1,111,3,258,4,15282\0304,113,171,3,256,1,15282\031\0312,1377,1451,0,\0318341,19,8341,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,20514,OBJECTIVE,3,15,\030ITEM,14344,OBJECTIVE,5,15,",[8343]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031What Huum says is true. I believe I know how to summon a lord of the Abyssal Council! Listen on, and I will explain...\030$N, Aurel Goldleaf thinks she's found a way to summon and defeat a ruling member of the Abyssal Council!  Such a task will be dangerous, but you have earned great respect amongst the Cenarion Circle.  We know that if anyone can do it, you can.$B$BMay fortune go with you, $N.  Speak with Aurel when you are ready.\030Speak with Aurel Goldleaf in Cenarion Hold.\030\030Goldleaf's Discovery\0312,1,104,2,257,1,15270\0302,107,199,2,321,3,15270\0302,202,243,2,257,4,15270\0302,248,275,2,257,1,15270\0302,278,313,2,257,1,15270\0303,1,43,2,384,1,15270\0301,1,23,4,272,1,15282\0301,25,85,4,272,4,15282\0301,87,118,4,272,3,15282\03115282,2,1,Aurel Goldleaf\03015282,2,6,Aurel Goldleaf\0312,1377,1451,0,\0302,0,0,6,Cenarion Hold\0318341,23,8341,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[8348]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I knew you were a tough $C the minute I saw you walk into Cenarion Hold. Keep it up!\030Huum tells me you've figured out how to summon the Abyssal Dukes!  That's quite an accomplishment.$B$BYou know what else would be quite the accomplishment?  Smashing up one of those things really good.  That'll cause an impression on their underlings, if you know what I mean.  Bring back its signet as proof of the deed.\030Bring the Abyssal Signet to Bor Wildmane in Cenarion Hold.\030How did it go with the Abyssal Duke? Did it hit hard?\030Signet of the Dukes\0312,1,65,2,257,1,15306\0302,68,98,2,257,1,15306\0302,103,155,2,257,4,15306\0302,158,201,2,257,1,15306\0302,204,276,2,257,4,15306\0302,279,321,2,257,1,15306\0303,1,58,2,384,1,15306\0301,1,72,4,272,1,15306\0301,74,84,4,272,1,15306\0304,1,36,3,256,2,15306\0304,38,53,3,256,2,15306\03115306,2,7,Bor Wildmane\0312,1377,1451,0,\0302,0,0,7,Bor Wildmane\0302,0,0,7,Cenarion Hold\0318349,19,8349,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0308363,23,8363,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,20514,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8349]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Good to see you again, $C! So you had a medallion made? Good -- you'll need that for your next quest...\030Now that you have a medallion and can summon an Abyssal Duke, speak with Bor Wildmane.  He will set you on a task against the Abyssal Council.$B$BGood luck, $N.  And if you ever need more medallions, return to me.\030Speak with Bor Wildmane in Cenarion Hold.\030\030Bor Wildmane\0312,1,86,2,257,1,15282\0302,89,142,2,257,3,15282\0302,147,160,2,257,1,15282\0302,163,213,2,259,4,15282\0303,1,41,2,384,1,15282\0301,1,26,4,272,1,15306\0301,28,55,4,272,2,15306\0301,57,103,4,274,1,15306\03115306,2,1,Bor Wildmane\03015306,2,5,Bor Wildmane\0312,1377,1451,0,\0302,0,0,5,Cenarion Hold\0318332,19,8332,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0308348,23,8348,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[835]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I think I can breathe easy now, knowing that the harpies won't be bothering our supply caravans anymore. And not one moment too soon, either. I hear I'm being sent some fun little toys with the next shipment!$B$BYou're pretty good at what you do, $N, you ought to track down my boss in Ratchet. I'll bet he could find some work for you.$B$BOh, and don't worry, I wouldn't forget to pay you for the service you provided me.\030Gazlowe told me once, \"Rezlak. There's one thing you need to know in life, and that's if you want something done well, do it yourself.\"$B$BI can't deal with losing all our caravans, so I'm just going to take matters into my own hands. Drygulch Ravine lies through the eastern part of Razorwind Canyon. If we kill all the harpies there, the routes will be safe.$B$BOf course, there was one other thing that Gazlowe taught me, and that's \"You can get anything done for a price.\" So, going to help me out, $n?\030Kill 12 Dustwind Savages and 8 Dustwind Storm Witches for Rezlak near Drygulch Ravine.\030You wouldn't think it from a guy like my boss Gazlowe, but he always seemed to know the score. \"Don't be afraid to take that big step\", he said.$B$BHarpies won't stop bothering us and the caravans won't stop being attacked unless we do something about it, eh?\030Securing the Lines\0312,1,30,2,257,1,3293\0302,32,135,2,259,4,3293\0302,140,234,2,257,3,3293\0302,236,301,2,257,1,3293\0302,303,360,2,257,4,3293\0302,365,506,2,257,2,3293\0303,1,86,2,384,1,3293\0301,1,104,4,272,1,3293\0301,106,141,4,272,1,3293\0301,143,208,4,272,1,3293\0301,213,294,4,272,1,3293\0301,296,336,4,272,4,3293\0301,341,422,4,272,1,3293\0304,1,94,3,256,1,3293\0304,96,144,3,256,1,3293\0304,149,259,3,268,4,3293\0313391,2,1,Gazlowe\0303293,2,1,Rezlak\0303391,2,6,Gazlowe\0303293,2,7,Rezlak\0303391,3,14,Gazlowe\0312,14,1411,0,\0302,0,0,7,Drygulch Ravine\0304,0,0,11,Ratchet\031834,19,834,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,3117,OBJECTIVE,12,13,Dustwind Savage\030NPC,3118,OBJECTIVE,8,13,Dustwind Storm Witch",[8351]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Yes, that's right, $N. I have a very tough task ahead...\030Now that you can disguise yourself as a ruling member of the Twilight Council, I am certain Bor Wildmane will want to speak with you.  Go see him, and prepare yourself for a very difficult mission...\030Speak with Bor Wildmane in Cenarion Hold.\030\030Bor Wishes to Speak\0312,1,133,2,259,3,15282\0302,136,199,2,257,1,15282\0303,1,41,2,384,1,15282\0301,1,22,4,272,1,15306\0301,24,56,4,272,1,15306\03115306,2,1,Bor Wildmane\03015306,2,3,Bor Wildmane\0312,1377,1451,0,\0302,0,0,3,Cenarion Hold\0318341,19,8341,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0308352,23,8352,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[8352]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031You... you did it! You did it, $N! Here! Take this. It's the biggest chest we had lying around and I filled it with some of the best stuff we found.\030Huum and I were just talking about you.  He tells me you're just about ready to try your hand at fighting an Abyssal Lord!$B$BI must tell you this is a very dangerous endeavor.  You'd better bring backup.  And I don't mean one or two of your friends, I'm talking about a top-notch, battle-ready fighting force.  If your friends are as good as you, you might even defeat it!$B$BIf you do - and I'll want evidence, as always - I'll give you a truly great reward.\030Bring an Abyssal Scepter to Bor Wildmane in Cenarion Hold.\030Well, how did it go? I'd do anything to leave my post and wrestle one of those things myself!\030Scepter of the Council\0312,1,39,2,257,1,15306\0302,42,122,2,261,1,15306\0302,127,176,2,257,1,15306\0302,179,204,2,257,1,15306\0302,207,310,2,261,1,15306\0302,313,373,2,257,4,15306\0302,378,460,2,259,4,15306\0303,1,58,2,384,1,15306\0301,1,6,4,272,1,15306\0301,8,18,4,272,1,15306\0301,20,34,4,272,1,15306\0301,36,40,4,272,1,15306\0301,42,51,4,272,1,15306\0301,53,148,4,272,1,15306\0304,1,20,3,256,2,15306\0304,22,93,3,256,1,15306\03115306,2,8,Bor Wildmane\0312,1377,1451,0,\0302,0,0,8,Bor Wildmane\0302,0,0,8,Cenarion Hold\0318351,19,8351,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0308364,23,8364,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,20515,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[8353]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Too funny!  Well done, $N! Here's your treat.$B$BHappy Hallow's End!\030Ah, trick-or-treating for a sick child, are we?  I was going to say, you're a little old to be rummaging about for candies...$B$BWell, for my treat - an Ironforge Mint - you will need to... cluck like a chicken!  Yes, chickens love mints... well OK, maybe they don't LOVE them... but I won't give you a mint unless you chicken cluck for me!$B$BWell $c, are you up to the challenge or not?!  Time to earn your treat!\030Do a chicken emote at Innkeeper Firebrew, and in exchange you'll receive an Ironforge Mint!\030Cluck like a chicken for Innkeeper Firebrew\030\030Chicken Clucking for a Mint\0312,1,47,2,257,2,5111\0302,50,125,2,257,3,5111\0302,130,189,2,259,3,5111\0302,191,211,2,257,1,5111\0302,214,240,2,257,1,5111\0302,242,279,2,257,4,5111\0302,281,340,2,265,4,5111\0302,345,389,2,257,2,5111\0302,392,415,2,257,1,5111\0303,1,91,2,384,1,5111\0301,1,10,4,272,1,5111\0301,13,26,4,272,1,5111\0301,28,45,4,272,1,5111\0301,50,68,4,272,1,5111\0304,1,43,3,384,1,5111\031620,2,4,Chicken\030620,2,7,Chicken\030620,2,10,Chicken\0305111,2,10,Innkeeper Firebrew\030620,3,15,Chicken\0305111,3,15,Innkeeper Firebrew\0312,0,0,10,Innkeeper Firebrew\0318311,20,8311,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[8354]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Too funny!  Well done, $N! Here's your treat.$B$BHappy Hallow's End!\030Ah, trick-or-treating for a sick child, are we?  I was going to say, you're a little old to be rummaging about for candies...$B$BWell, for my treat - an Undercity Mint - you will need to... cluck like a chicken!  Yes, chickens love mints... well OK, maybe they don't LOVE them... but I won't give you a mint unless you chicken cluck for me!$B$BWell $c, are you up to the challenge or not?!  Time to earn your treat!\030Do a chicken emote at Innkeeper Norman, and in exchange you'll receive an Undercity Mint!\030Cluck like a chicken for Innkeeper Norman\030\030Chicken Clucking for a Mint\0312,1,47,2,257,2,6741\0302,50,125,2,257,3,6741\0302,130,189,2,259,3,6741\0302,191,211,2,257,1,6741\0302,214,240,2,257,1,6741\0302,242,279,2,257,4,6741\0302,281,340,2,265,4,6741\0302,345,389,2,257,2,6741\0302,392,415,2,257,1,6741\0303,1,89,2,384,1,6741\0301,1,10,4,272,1,6741\0301,13,26,4,272,1,6741\0301,28,45,4,272,1,6741\0301,50,68,4,272,1,6741\0304,1,41,3,384,1,6741\031620,2,4,Chicken\030620,2,7,Chicken\030620,2,10,Chicken\0306741,2,10,Innkeeper Norman\030620,3,15,Chicken\0306741,3,15,Innkeeper Norman\0312,0,0,10,Innkeeper Norman\0318312,20,8312,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[8355]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031Too funny!  Well done, $N! Here's your treat.$B$BHappy Hallow's End!\030A trick-or-treater!  Huzzah!$B$BWell now, even though you're doing something noble and collecting candies for a sick child, I can't let you off the hook that easily.  I have a yummy Gnomeregan Gumdrop to give to the sick child... if you make a train noise for me!  Haha, yes, that'll be the trick!  The price of this gumdrop is one train noise!$B$BChugga-chugga, $c!\030Do a train emote at Talvash del Kissel, and in exchange you'll receive a Gnomeregan Gumdrop!\030Do the \"train\" for Talvash\030Well, go ahead now...\030Incoming Gumdrop\0312,1,19,2,257,1,6826\0302,22,28,2,257,1,6826\0302,33,165,2,257,1,6826\0302,168,229,2,257,1,6826\0302,231,263,2,257,4,6826\0302,266,297,2,257,1,6826\0302,300,344,2,257,1,6826\0302,349,366,2,257,1,6826\0303,1,92,2,384,1,6826\0301,1,10,4,272,1,6826\0301,13,26,4,272,1,6826\0301,28,45,4,272,1,6826\0301,50,68,4,272,1,6826\0305,1,21,3,256,1,6826\0304,1,26,3,384,1,6826\0316826,2,9,Talvash del Kissel\0312,0,0,9,Talvash\0318311,20,8311,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[8356]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031You are truly mighty, haha! Well done, and thanks for being such a good sport. Here's your candy.$B$BHappy Hallow's End, $N!\030That's an... interesting costume you have on.  Even though you're being nice and helping a sick child trick-or-treat this year, I'm afraid I'm going to have to ask you perform a trick for me!$B$BLet's see... you look so strong and buff in that... costume... let's see you flex!  Yes, go on now and flex for me, strong $g man : woman;!$B$BWhen and only when you flex, I'll give you some tasty Stormwind Nougat.  It's a great Hallow's End treat.\030Do a flex emote at Innkeeper Allison, and in exchange you'll receive Stormwind Nougat!$B\030Flex for Innkeeper Allison\030No candy until you flex for me, $N...\030Flexing for Nougat\0312,1,12,2,257,1,6740\0302,14,45,2,257,1,6740\0302,48,191,2,257,3,6740\0302,196,207,2,257,1,6740\0302,209,246,2,257,1,6740\0302,248,257,2,257,1,6740\0302,259,277,2,257,1,6740\0302,280,334,2,257,1,6740\