entenced by High Justice Grimstone and place the banner firmly on the ground in a sign of defiance.$B$BYour victim will not be able to restrain himself and shall enter the fray filled with a desire to fight you.  Once you obtain that which you seek, go back to Anthion.\030Travel to the Ring of the Law in Blackrock Depths and place the Banner of Provocation in its center as you are sentenced by High Justice Grimstone.  Slay Theldren and his gladiators and return to Anthion Harmon in the Eastern Plaguelands with the first piece of Lord Valthalak's amulet.\030\030Theldren's Team Defeated\030You're back, $N!\030The Challenge\0312,1,17,2,257,1,16032\0302,20,129,2,259,3,16032\0302,132,252,2,257,1,16032\0302,257,364,2,261,3,16032\0302,367,422,2,259,1,16032\0303,1,147,2,384,1,16032\0303,150,286,2,384,1,16032\0301,1,43,4,272,2,16016\0306,1,16,3,256,1,16016\0305,1,24,3,384,1,16032\03110096,2,3,High Justice Grimstone\03010096,2,6,High Justice Grimstone\03016059,2,7,Theldren\03016016,2,7,Anthion Harmon\03016042,2,7,Lord Valthalak\0312,1584,0,0,\0302,0,0,2,Blackrock Depths\0302,0,0,5,Anthion\0302,0,0,6,Ring of the Law\0302,0,0,6,Blackrock Depths\0302,0,0,7,Anthion Harmon\0302,0,0,7,Eastern Plaguelands\0318950,19,8950,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,22047,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[9016]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This curse was bestowed upon us but for a mere medallion. Lord Valthalak certainly knows how to hold a grudge.$B$BWe'll endeavor to find the remaining pieces - hopefully before I meet an untimely demise. But before that, let us see about your reward.\030Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet.  In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.$B$BThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the amulet back together.  Return to Mokvar and tell him that Bodley is his only hope for finding the remaining pieces.  Speak to him about any rewards you've arranged for.$B$BI, for once, shall rest in peace.  I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!\030Return to Mokvar in Orgimmar with a set of Wildheart Boots, a Wildheart Kilt and Wildheart Spaulders.$B\030You've returned and I see in your eyes that you've much to tell me, $N.  Let us take care of your reward first.\030Anthion's Parting Words\0312,1,43,2,257,1,16016\0302,46,140,2,261,4,16016\0302,145,218,2,257,1,16016\0302,221,312,2,259,3,16016\0302,315,365,2,257,1,16016\0302,370,402,2,265,3,16016\0302,405,464,2,259,3,16016\0303,1,101,2,384,1,16016\0301,1,57,4,276,1,16012\0301,59,110,4,272,1,16012\0301,115,203,4,272,3,16012\0301,205,250,4,272,1,16012\0304,1,71,3,256,1,16012\0304,74,111,3,256,1,16012\03116012,2,4,Mokvar\03016033,2,4,Bodley\03016012,2,8,Mokvar\03016042,4,10,Lord Valthalak\0312,1637,1454,0,\0302,0,0,4,Mokvar\0302,0,0,8,Mokvar\0302,0,0,8,Orgimmar\0319015,19,9015,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0309032,23,9032,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,16715,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,16719,OBJECTIVE,1,15,\030ITEM,16718,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[9017]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031This curse was bestowed upon us but for a mere medallion. Lord Valthalak certainly knows how to hold a grudge.$B$BWe'll endeavor to find the remaining pieces - hopefully before I meet an untimely demise. But before that, let us see about your reward.\030Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet.  In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.$B$BThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the amulet back together.  Return to Mokvar and tell him that Bodley is his only hope for finding the remaining pieces.  Speak to him about any rewards you've arranged for.$B$BI, for once, shall rest in peace.  I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!\030Return to Mokvar in Orgimmar with a set of Beaststalker's Boots, Beaststalker's Pants and Beas