that makes his residence at the Fire Scar Shrine,  a place of great evil in southwestern Ashenvale.$B$BHe had been little more than an annoyance until now, and I had not dealt with him, but it seems that his time has come.\030Bring Ilkrud Magthrull's Tome to Delgren the Purifier at Maestra's Post.\030You look a bit shaken up, $n. Are you well?\030The Tower of Althalaxx\0312,1,17,2,257,1,3663\0302,19,47,2,257,1,3663\0302,49,176,2,257,1,3663\0302,181,299,2,257,4,3663\0303,1,72,2,384,1,3663\0301,1,39,4,272,1,3663\0301,41,124,4,272,1,3663\0301,129,184,4,272,1,3663\0304,1,29,3,256,1,3663\0304,31,43,3,256,2,3663\0313664,2,1,Ilkrud Magthrull\0303664,2,5,Ilkrud Magthrull\0303663,2,5,Delgren the Purifier\0312,148,1439,0,\0302,0,0,3,Fire Scar Shrine\0302,0,0,5,Delgren the Purifier\0302,0,0,5,Maestra's Post\0304,0,0,8,Ilkrud's\031970,19,970,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0301140,23,1140,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,5533,OBJECTIVE,1,15,",[97326]="MINIMAL\031characters,conclusion,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030requestItems\030title\031\030\030Return 8 Smooth Boulders to Thra behind Grommash Hold.\030\030Smooth Boulder\030\030Rocks to Rests\0313,1,54,2,384,1,0\0305,1,14,3,384,1,0\031\0312,0,0,1,Thra\031\031",[974]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030requestItems\030title\031Yes, I definitely see the correlation here between the temperature of the volcano and the hot springs. I'll have to double-check my equations for accuracy, but it seems like the distance and the rate that the heat is transferred... Hmm...\030The hot springs here are a source of mystery to me. Where does the heat come from?$B$BLooking at how close the pools are to Fire Plume Ridge, I really wonder if the volcano might have something to do with it. I created a thermometer to take readings of the temperatures at the volcano, and I'd like to find the hottest part. It gives the measurements in degrees Kraklenheit!$B$BHere, take it, and take readings of the temperatures at the ridge whenever you see a hot spot!\030Krakle in Un'Goro Crater wants you to find the hottest area of Fire Plume Ridge.$B$BWhenever you find a hot spot, right click the thermometer to check the temperature. Keep looking until you find the hottest one.\030\030Find the hottest area of Fire Plume Ridge\030I'd go there myself, but... I'm a little scared of the fire elementals there!\030Finding the Source\0312,1,51,2,257,1,10302\0302,53,82,2,257,2,10302\0302,87,208,2,257,4,10302\0302,210,324,2,259,1,10302\0302,326,374,2,257,1,10302\0302,379,472,2,257,1,10302\0303,1,80,2,386,1,10302\0303,85,167,2,384,1,10302\0303,169,212,2,384,1,10302\0301,1,102,4,272,1,10302\0301,104,231,4,272,4,10302\0301,233,238,4,272,1,10302\0306,1,27,3,256,1,10302\0306,29,77,3,256,1,10302\0305,1,41,3,384,1,10302\0314950,2,6,Spot\03010302,2,7,Krakle\0304950,2,8,Spot\0312,490,1449,0,\0302,0,0,3,Fire Plume Ridge\0302,0,0,7,Un'Goro Crater\031980,23,980,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031NPC,10541,OBJECTIVE,1,13,Krakle's Thermometer",[97485]="MINIMAL\031conclusion,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030objectiveLabel3\030requestItems\030title\031\030\030Purchase a Bundle of Herbs from Nida the herbalist, a Bundle of Ceder Twigs from Nata the enchanting supplier, and Sinew Thread from Mahu the leatherworking supplier and Ceremonial Flint and Tinder from Naal the cooking supplier.\010\010Combine the items and sprinkle the incense off of Hunter's Rise.\030\030Incense created\030Spread incense\030\030Traditions of the Bluff\0313,1,229,2,384,1,0\0303,232,295,2,384,1,0\0305,1,15,3,384,1,0\0306,1,14,3,384,1,0\0313005,2,1,Mahu\0307583,2,2,Sprinkle\0312,0,0,1,Nida the\0302,0,0,1,Nata the\0302,0,0,1,Mahu the\0302,0,0,1,Naal the\031\031",[975]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Here it is, $N. Remember, ya have ta carry it with you. Why don't ya head back to Winterspring, an' see what ya be findin' there?\030Now, before I give ya dis charm, I better explain how ta use it.$B$BIf you carry da charm with ya, you'll find dat certain items will drop from creatures ya fight. If you don't have da charm with you, you won't find them. Understand?$B$BYou'll know these special items by the name -- they be called E'ko. If you find any of these items, just bring dem to ol' Mau'ari, and she help ya out.$B$BWait here while I fix your charm.\030Speak to Witch Doctor Mau'ari again in a moment to receive the lucky charm.\030\030Cache of Mau'ari\0312,1,64,2,257,1,10307\0302,69,163,2,261,4,10307\0302,165,221,2,257,4,10307\0302,223,233,2,257,2,10307\0302,238,304,2,257,1,10307\0302,306,388,2,257,4,10307\0302,393,425,2,257,1,10307\0303,1,75,2,384,1,10307\0301,1,15,4,272,1,10307\0301,17,55,4,272,1,10307\0301,57,129,4,272,2,10307\03110307,2,8,Witch Doctor Mau'ari\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,8,Witch Doctor Mau'ari\0304,0,0,11,Winterspring\031969,19,969,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[97538]="MINIMAL\031conclusion,conflict,consequences,loreConnections,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030requestItems\030title\031\030\030Tah Winterhoof in Thunder Bluff wants 30 Mirkweed Pods from Mirkfallon Lake.\030\030Mirkweed Pods\030\030Pigments for Paints\0313,1,76,2,386,1,0\0305,1,13,3,384,1,0\0313024,2,1,Tah Winterhoof\0312,0,0,1,Thunder Bluff\0302,0,0,1,Mirkfallon Lake\031\031",[97558]="MINIMAL\031conclusion,conflict,consequences,locations,loreConnections,motivations,questChains,setup,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030objectiveLabel2\030objectiveLabel3\030objectiveLabel4\030requestItems\030title\031\030\030Bring Shelene Rhobart 8 Duskbat Wing Membranes, 6 Darkhound Hides and 3 Vile Fin Murloc Skin.\030\030Duskbat Wing Membrane\030Darkhound Hide\030Vile Fin Murloc Skin\030\030Hides for the Forsaken\0313,1,93,2,384,1,0\0305,1,21,3,384,1,0\0306,1,14,3,384,1,0\0307,1,20,3,384,1,0\0313549,2,1,Shelene Rhobart\0301512,2,1,Duskbat\0301541,2,1,Vile Fin Murloc\030285,2,1,Murloc\0301512,3,2,Duskbat\0301541,3,4,Vile Fin Murloc\030285,3,4,Murloc\031\031\031",[976]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections\031completion\030description\030objective\030objectiveLabel1\030requestItems\030title\031You have done well today, $C. The items we sent to aid Auberdine will be of immediate use in dealing with the dark threats that infest the forest.$B$BTake these with my heartfelt thanks.\030Delgren has asked me to deliver messages and supplies to Sentinel Starbreeze in Auberdine, but I am loathe to leave on my own. Dangerous foes operate in the forest, and I do not wish to risk letting these supplies and information fall into the wrong hands.$B$BIf you and others could act as my guards, I could leave now. With your protection, I have no doubt that we can see these goods safely to Auberdine.\030Speak with Delgren the Purifier at Maestra's Post after seeing Feero safely through Ashenvale Forest.\030Protect Feero Ironhand\030The Sentinels have a great need for supplies to reinforce themselves in Darkshore.\030Supplies to Auberdine\0312,1,126,2,257,1,4484\0302,128,256,2,267,3,4484\0302,261,320,2,257,4,4484\0302,322,407,2,257,1,4484\0303,1,101,2,384,1,4484\0301,1,29,4,272,1,3663\0301,31,146,4,272,3,3663\0301,151,186,4,272,1,3663\0305,1,82,3,258,1,3663\0304,1,22,3,396,1,4484\0313663,2,5,Delgren the Purifier\0304484,3,10,Feero Ironhand\0312,331,1440,0,\0302,0,0,1,Sentinel Starbreeze\0302,0,0,1,Auberdine\0302,0,0,4,Auberdine\0302,0,0,5,Maestra's Post\0303,0,0,9,Darkshore\031973,19,973,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031",[977]="PARTIAL\031consequences,loreConnections,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031I can't wait to show my friends! Now, just wait a moment while I attach these...$B$BPerfect!\030Now that I have what I need to cover the mechanical moving parts, I only need one other thing. Well, actually two. Two horns!$B$BThe ice thistle patriarchs and matriarchs have the largest horns, so of course, those are the ones I want. That type of yeti inhabits a cave to the southeast. There are plenty of them there; you shouldn't have any problem finding them.$B$BRemember, I only want the best looking ones -- no beat up or broken horns, please!\030Collect 2 Pristine Yeti Horns for Umi Rumplesnicker in Everlook.\030I've just about finished attaching the fur, $N. Please, hurry back with those horns!\030Are We There, Yeti?\0312,1,94,2,259,1,10305\0302,96,114,2,257,1,10305\0302,116,125,2,257,1,10305\0302,130,235,2,259,1,10305\0302,237,287,2,257,1,10305\0302,289,364,2,261,1,10305\0302,369,450,2,259,1,10305\0303,1,64,2,384,1,10305\0301,1,32,4,272,1,10305\0301,34,80,4,272,1,10305\0301,85,92,4,272,1,10305\0304,1,47,3,256,1,10305\0304,49,84,3,256,1,10305\03110305,2,8,Umi Rumplesnicker\0312,618,1452,0,\0302,0,0,8,Everlook\0313783,19,3783,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\0305163,23,5163,NO_KNOWN_BRANCH_CONFLICT\031ITEM,12367,OBJECTIVE,2,15,",[978]="PARTIAL\031conflict,consequences,loreConnections,motivations,stakes\031completion\030description\030objective\030requestItems\030title\031Now I can compare the feathers... Let's see...\030Wildkin feathers from the Hinterlands appear to contain traces of magical qualities. These powers... they don't seem to be wielded by the creatures, it's more like they are simply inherent to the species -- part of their very essence.$B$BDuring my studies, I heard that a large population of wildkin inhabit the snowy lands of Winterspring. Could these creatures have the same powers? Please help me find an answer, $N. Go to Winterspring and gather feathers that have dropped to the ground, then return to me.\030Collect 10 Moontouched Feathers